},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A6","text":"Pour l’Être nécessaire, la possibilité implique l’actualité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A7","text":"La réalité des possibilités n’est pas ontologiquement autosuffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX1","text":"Les essences ou possibilités réelles ne sont pas des réalités sans fondement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX2","text":"Les vérités éternelles ne constituent pas un domaine ontologique autonome séparé de tout existant actuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX3","text":"Le fondement ultime n’est pas une simple possibilité non actualisée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX4","text":"L’Être nécessaire n’est pas un être dont l’essence serait extérieure ou indifférente à l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX5","text":"La réalité des possibles ne se suffit pas à elle-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:D1","text":"La réalité des essences, possibilités ou vérités éternelles conduit à poser un fondement existant et actuel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","CH_UCIC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:D2","text":"Le fondement actuel des réalités possibles est identifié à l’Être nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A3","CH_UCIC_P_36:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:D3","text":"L’Être nécessaire est défini par une identité interne entre essence et existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:D4","text":"Dans l’Être nécessaire, l’actualité n’est pas ajoutée à la possibilité par une cause extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SD1","text":"L’ordre des essences et des vérités éternelles dépend d’une ontologie de l’actualité nécessaire plutôt que d’un règne autonome du possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SD2","text":"La distinction entre possible et actuel est radicalement asymétrique : elle vaut pour les réalités fondées, mais se résorbe dans l’Être nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:A6","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SD3","text":"La nécessité métaphysique fonctionne comme principe de stabilisation ontologique des possibilités et des vérités éternelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’un ordre intelligible puisse subsister sans support existant et actuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX2","text":"Il exclut que la possibilité soit le niveau ontologique premier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une pluralité de fondements ultimes indépendants de l’Être nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une séparation durable entre la détermination essentielle et l’existence au niveau du fondement suprême.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX1","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un fondement autonome des vérités éternelles qui ne serait ni existant ni actuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX2","text":"La possibilité d’un réel intelligible sans nécessité actuelle est forclose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX3","text":"Le système rend inadmissible une ontologie où l’existence serait un fait contingent ajouté à l’essence nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS1","text":"Réalité des essences ou possibilités → exigence de fondement → recours à une existence actuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS2","text":"Existence actuelle ultime → identification de l’Être nécessaire → fondement des réalités possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS3","text":"Être nécessaire → essence contenant l’existence → possibilité convertie immédiatement en actualité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS4","text":"Dépendance des possibles → centralité de la nécessité → exclusion d’un ordre modal autosuffisant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:AF1","text":"Réalité possible ou éternelle → besoin d’un fondement → fondement existant et actuel → Être nécessaire → identité de l’essence et de l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:AF2","text":"Possibilité ontologiquement dépendante → nécessité actuelle comme principe ultime → actualité inhérente au nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ME1","text":"Les essences, possibilités et vérités éternelles sont reclassées comme réalités fondées plutôt que comme principes premiers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ME2","text":"L’Être nécessaire devient le point de jonction entre l’ordre modal et l’ordre actuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ME3","text":"La frontière entre possibilité et actualité est déplacée : elle demeure pour les réalités dépendantes, mais disparaît dans le fondement nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ME4","text":"Le champ ontologique est organisé selon une hiérarchie allant du possible fondé à l’actuel nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT1","text":"Surface — La réalité des essences, possibilités ou vérités éternelles est rapportée à un fondement actuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT2","text":"Structural — La dépendance ontologique des réalités modales impose un fondement qui possède l’existence en propre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’argument recadre la question des possibles : il ne faut plus demander seulement ce qui est possible, mais ce qui fonde la réalité du possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’Être nécessaire constitue une actualité non dérivée, dans laquelle l’essence et l’existence coïncident.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement conditionnel de la proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT2","text":"La chaîne dépend de l’acceptation préalable d’une réalité des essences, possibilités ou vérités éternelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT3","text":"Le passage de la nécessité d’un fondement à son identification avec l’Être nécessaire reste comprimé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT4","text":"La cohérence interne repose sur l’assimilation entre fondement ultime, existence actuelle et nécessité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT5","text":"La structure est forte dans la dépendance des possibles, mais sous-détermine la justification complète de l’identité entre essence et existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : condition modale → exigence ontologique → fondement nécessaire → actualité essentielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193421412793Z_66cf0ae0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 44","source_sha256":"1509983b20c1cebcfc6e453cb95af2081d61b818ab1aa043df36a1e43942a7cd","sha256":"17ae06b147e64b9fb3a4fe1046a082a9e1a9b46701184bc5cc6fd34bbca78640","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:34:21.416279+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:AS1","text":"The possible reality of essences, possibilities, or eternal truths requires an ontological foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2","text":"This foundation can only be an existing and actual reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:AS3","text":"The required actual existence refers back to necessary Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:AS4","text":"In necessary Being, essence contains existence; possibility therefore suffices for actuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","text":"Essences, possibilities, and eternal truths can possess reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","text":"Every reality possessing ontological status must be grounded in something.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A3","text":"The ultimate foundation of a reality cannot lack actual existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","text":"Ultimate actual existence belongs to necessary Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","text":"In necessary Being, essence contains existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A6","text":"For necessary Being, possibility entails actuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:A7","text":"The reality of possibilities is not ontologically self-sufficient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX1","text":"Real essences or possibilities are not ungrounded realities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX2","text":"Eternal truths do not constitute an autonomous ontological domain separate from every actual existent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX3","text":"The ultimate foundation is not a mere unactualized possibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX4","text":"Necessary Being is not a being whose essence would be external or indifferent to existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:NX5","text":"The reality of possibles is not self-sufficient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:D1","text":"The reality of essences, possibilities, or eternal truths leads one to posit an existing and actual foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","CH_UCIC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:D2","text":"The actual foundation of possible realities is identified with necessary Being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A3","CH_UCIC_P_36:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:D3","text":"Necessary Being is defined by an internal identity between essence and existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:D4","text":"In necessary Being, actuality is not added to possibility by an external cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SD1","text":"The order of essences and eternal truths depends on an ontology of necessary actuality rather than on an autonomous realm of the possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SD2","text":"The distinction between possible and actual is radically asymmetrical: it applies to grounded realities, but is absorbed in necessary Being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:A6","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SD3","text":"Metaphysical necessity functions as a principle of ontological stabilization for possibilities and eternal truths.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that an intelligible order might subsist without an existing and actual support.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that possibility be the primary ontological level.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX3","text":"It excludes a plurality of ultimate foundations independent of necessary Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX4","text":"It excludes a lasting separation between essential determination and existence at the level of the supreme foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX1","text":"The structuring absence is that of an autonomous foundation of eternal truths that would be neither existing nor actual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX2","text":"The possibility of an intelligible real without actual necessity is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX3","text":"The system renders inadmissible an ontology in which existence would be a contingent fact added to necessary essence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS1","text":"Reality of essences or possibilities → requirement of a foundation → recourse to an actual existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS2","text":"Ultimate actual existence → identification of necessary Being → foundation of possible realities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS3","text":"Necessary Being → essence containing existence → possibility immediately converted into actuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS4","text":"Dependence of possibles → centrality of necessity → exclusion of a self-sufficient modal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:AF1","text":"Possible or eternal reality → need for a foundation → existing and actual foundation → necessary Being → identity of essence and existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:AF2","text":"Ontologically dependent possibility → actual necessity as ultimate principle → actuality inherent in the necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ME1","text":"Essences, possibilities, and eternal truths are reclassified as grounded realities rather than as first principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ME2","text":"Necessary Being becomes the point of junction between the modal order and the actual order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ME3","text":"The boundary between possibility and actuality is displaced: it remains for dependent realities, but disappears in the necessary foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ME4","text":"The ontological field is organized according to a hierarchy extending from grounded possibility to necessary actuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT1","text":"Surface — The reality of essences, possibilities, or eternal truths is referred to an actual foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT2","text":"Structural — The ontological dependence of modal realities requires a foundation that possesses existence in its own right.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument reframes the question of possibles: one must no longer ask only what is possible, but what grounds the reality of the possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Necessary Being constitutes a non-derived actuality, in which essence and existence coincide.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the conditional movement of the proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT2","text":"The chain depends on the prior acceptance of a reality of essences, possibilities, or eternal truths.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT3","text":"The passage from the necessity of a foundation to its identification with necessary Being remains compressed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence rests on the assimilation of ultimate foundation, actual existence, and necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT5","text":"The structure is strong regarding the dependence of possibles, but underdetermines the complete justification of the identity between essence and existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_36:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: modal condition → ontological requirement → necessary foundation → essential actuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_36:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_36@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_36:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 44"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 44","title":"Proposition 44","context":"Chapter 44","original_title":"Proposition 44"},"original_title":"Proposition 44","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 45","order":45,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_37"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_37@R001","sha256":"71af449246a17a4d796f10e1f79920127771f7fcea9abed320a5a68bbfa1cc9d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS1","text":"Le problème consiste à établir l’existence de Dieu comme Être nécessaire à partir de sa possibilité et de l’existence des êtres contingents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS2","text":"L’argument recadre l’existence nécessaire comme une propriété conditionnelle : si l’Être nécessaire est possible, il doit exister.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS3","text":"L’absence de bornes, de négation et de contradiction fonde la possibilité de cet être.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","text":"Deux voies convergentes sont mobilisées : une démonstration a priori par la possibilité et les vérités éternelles, puis une démonstration a posteriori par les êtres contingents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS5","text":"La contingence exige une raison dernière ou suffisante, située dans l’Être nécessaire qui porte en lui-même la raison de son existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A1","text":"Dieu est défini comme l’Être nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A2","text":"L’Être nécessaire possède le privilège d’exister nécessairement s’il est possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A3","text":"Ce qui n’enferme aucune borne, aucune négation et aucune contradiction est possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A4","text":"Rien ne peut empêcher la possibilité d’un être absolument illimité et non contradictoire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A5","text":"La possibilité de l’Être nécessaire suffit à établir son existence a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A6","text":"Les vérités éternelles fournissent une voie indépendante de démonstration de l’existence divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","text":"Des êtres contingents existent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A8","text":"Tout être contingent requiert une raison dernière ou suffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","text":"La raison dernière ou suffisante des êtres contingents réside dans l’Être nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A10","text":"L’Être nécessaire possède en lui-même la raison de son existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX1","text":"L’Être nécessaire n’est limité par aucune borne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX2","text":"L’Être nécessaire n’inclut aucune négation constitutive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX3","text":"L’Être nécessaire n’implique aucune contradiction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX4","text":"L’existence des êtres contingents ne se suffit pas à elle-même comme explication dernière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX5","text":"La raison de l’existence divine ne se trouve pas dans une cause extérieure à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX6","text":"La démonstration de Dieu ne dépend pas exclusivement de l’expérience contingente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D1","text":"Si l’Être nécessaire est possible, son existence ne peut être empêchée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A2","CH_UCIC_P_37:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D2","text":"L’absence de contradiction transforme la possibilité conceptuelle de l’Être nécessaire en condition suffisante de son existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A3","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D3","text":"La possibilité de Dieu constitue une preuve a priori de son existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A2","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D4","text":"Les vérités éternelles établissent une seconde voie rationnelle vers l’existence divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D5","text":"L’existence d’êtres contingents exclut qu’ils soient la raison dernière de leur propre existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D6","text":"L’existence du contingent renvoie nécessairement à un être dont la raison d’existence est interne à lui-même.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A8","CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D7","text":"La démonstration a priori et la démonstration a posteriori convergent vers le même Être nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:D3","CH_UCIC_P_37:D4","CH_UCIC_P_37:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SD1","text":"L’existence divine est à la fois auto-fondée et fondatrice : Dieu n’a pas de raison extérieure et fournit la raison dernière du contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SD2","text":"La possibilité et la contingence sont intégrées dans une même hiérarchie explicative dont le sommet est l’Être nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A2","CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SD3","text":"La rationalité de l’existence s’étend du domaine logique des vérités éternelles au domaine ontologique des êtres contingents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A6","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4","text":"L’Être nécessaire fonctionne comme clôture explicative du réel : toute recherche de raison s’arrête dans un être dont la raison est immanente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A8","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une possibilité non contradictoire demeure sans actualisation lorsque son contenu est celui de l’Être nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’une série d’êtres contingents fournisse par elle-même une raison dernière suffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une causalité régressive sans fondement ontologique ultime.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut que la nécessité divine soit dérivée d’une condition extérieure ou empirique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX5","text":"Le système exclut une séparation entre la cohérence logique des vérités éternelles et l’ordre réel de l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’un réel contingent sans raison suffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX2","text":"Est forclose l’indépendance ontologique du monde contingent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX3","text":"Est forclose l’hypothèse d’un être nécessaire seulement pensé mais non existant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX4","text":"Est forclose une explication ultime qui ne soit ni nécessaire ni auto-fondée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS1","text":"Non-contradiction et absence de bornes → possibilité de l’Être nécessaire → impossibilité d’empêcher son existence → preuve a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS2","text":"Vérités éternelles → fondement rationnel indépendant → confirmation de l’existence divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS3","text":"Existence du contingent → insuffisance explicative du contingent → exigence d’une raison dernière → Être nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS4","text":"Être nécessaire → raison de son existence en lui-même → fondement de la raison des êtres contingents → clôture de l’explication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AF1","text":"Possibilité non contradictoire → nécessité conditionnelle de l’existence → preuve a priori → vérités éternelles comme voie convergente → existence du contingent → exigence d’une raison suffisante → Être nécessaire auto-fondé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ME1","text":"L’existence est reclassée selon deux régimes : nécessité auto-fondée et contingence dépendante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ME2","text":"La possibilité logique devient un opérateur ontologique capable de produire une conclusion d’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ME3","text":"La contingence cesse d’être un fait terminal et devient un indice de dépendance explicative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ME4","text":"Les voies a priori et a posteriori sont cartographiées comme deux accès distincts à une même fondation nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT1","text":"Surface — L’existence de Dieu est démontrée par sa possibilité et par l’existence des êtres contingents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT2","text":"Structural — Le réel est organisé par une relation asymétrique entre l’être contingent, qui requiert une raison, et l’Être nécessaire, qui la possède en lui-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La démonstration est renforcée par la convergence de preuves indépendantes : logique, vérités éternelles et expérience de la contingence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La causalité explicative s’achève dans une nécessité intemporelle qui fonde l’existence sans être elle-même fondée par autre chose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire les deux voies démonstratives et leur convergence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la possibilité de l’Être nécessaire implique effectivement son existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT3","text":"Le point le plus fort est l’articulation entre principe de raison suffisante et distinction du contingent et du nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT4","text":"Le point sous-déterminé est la justification indépendante de la possibilité de l’être absolument illimité et non contradictoire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : possibilité logique → existence nécessaire, puis contingence empirique → raison dernière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT6","text":"La tension résiduelle porte sur le passage de l’absence de contradiction à la possibilité positive, passage affirmé plus que démontré.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193439630441Z_c6fb040c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 45","source_sha256":"71af449246a17a4d796f10e1f79920127771f7fcea9abed320a5a68bbfa1cc9d","sha256":"e966f27c1b70f50a11e16ca97d06f06b693b86c0129779b15503a185645365ca","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:34:39.634160+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS1","text":"The problem consists in establishing the existence of God as a Necessary Being from His possibility and from the existence of contingent beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS2","text":"The argument reframes necessary existence as a conditional property: if the Necessary Being is possible, it must exist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS3","text":"The absence of bounds, negation, and contradiction grounds the possibility of this being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","text":"Two convergent paths are employed: an a priori demonstration through possibility and eternal truths, then an a posteriori demonstration through contingent beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AS5","text":"Contingency requires an ultimate or sufficient reason, situated in the Necessary Being, which bears within itself the reason for its existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A1","text":"God is defined as the Necessary Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A2","text":"The Necessary Being possesses the privilege of existing necessarily if it is possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A3","text":"That which contains no bound, no negation, and no contradiction is possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A4","text":"Nothing can prevent the possibility of an absolutely unlimited and non-contradictory being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A5","text":"The possibility of the Necessary Being suffices to establish its existence a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A6","text":"Eternal truths provide an independent path for demonstrating divine existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","text":"Contingent beings exist.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A8","text":"Every contingent being requires an ultimate or sufficient reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","text":"The ultimate or sufficient reason of contingent beings resides in the Necessary Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:A10","text":"The Necessary Being possesses within itself the reason for its existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX1","text":"The Necessary Being is not limited by any bound.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX2","text":"The Necessary Being includes no constitutive negation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX3","text":"The Necessary Being entails no contradiction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX4","text":"The existence of contingent beings is not sufficient unto itself as an ultimate explanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX5","text":"The reason for divine existence is not found in a cause external to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:NX6","text":"The demonstration of God does not depend exclusively on contingent experience.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D1","text":"If the Necessary Being is possible, its existence cannot be prevented.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A2","CH_UCIC_P_37:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D2","text":"The absence of contradiction transforms the conceptual possibility of the Necessary Being into a sufficient condition for its existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A3","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D3","text":"The possibility of God constitutes an a priori proof of His existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A2","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D4","text":"Eternal truths establish a second rational path toward divine existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D5","text":"The existence of contingent beings excludes their being the ultimate reason for their own existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D6","text":"The existence of the contingent necessarily refers to a being whose reason for existence is internal to itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A8","CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:D7","text":"The a priori demonstration and the a posteriori demonstration converge upon the same Necessary Being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:D3","CH_UCIC_P_37:D4","CH_UCIC_P_37:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SD1","text":"Divine existence is both self-grounded and grounding: God has no external reason and provides the ultimate reason for the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SD2","text":"Possibility and contingency are integrated into one and the same explanatory hierarchy whose summit is the Necessary Being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A2","CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SD3","text":"The rationality of existence extends from the logical domain of eternal truths to the ontological domain of contingent beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A6","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4","text":"The Necessary Being functions as the explanatory closure of reality: every search for a reason comes to rest in a being whose reason is immanent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A8","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a non-contradictory possibility remain unactualized when its content is that of the Necessary Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a series of contingent beings by itself provide a sufficient ultimate reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX3","text":"The system excludes regressive causality without an ultimate ontological foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX4","text":"The system excludes divine necessity being derived from an external or empirical condition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX5","text":"The system excludes a separation between the logical coherence of eternal truths and the real order of existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX1","text":"The possibility of a contingent reality without sufficient reason is ruled out.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX2","text":"The ontological independence of the contingent world is ruled out.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX3","text":"The hypothesis of a necessary being merely thought but not existing is ruled out.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX4","text":"An ultimate explanation that is neither necessary nor self-grounded is ruled out.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS1","text":"Non-contradiction and absence of bounds → possibility of the Necessary Being → impossibility of preventing its existence → a priori proof.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS2","text":"Eternal truths → independent rational foundation → confirmation of divine existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS3","text":"Existence of the contingent → explanatory insufficiency of the contingent → requirement of an ultimate reason → Necessary Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS4","text":"Necessary Being → reason for its existence within itself → foundation of the reason of contingent beings → closure of explanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:AF1","text":"Non-contradictory possibility → conditional necessity of existence → a priori proof → eternal truths as a convergent path → existence of the contingent → requirement of a sufficient reason → self-grounded Necessary Being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ME1","text":"Existence is reclassified according to two regimes: self-grounded necessity and dependent contingency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ME2","text":"Logical possibility becomes an ontological operator capable of producing a conclusion of existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ME3","text":"Contingency ceases to be a terminal fact and becomes an index of explanatory dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ME4","text":"The a priori and a posteriori paths are mapped as two distinct accesses to one and the same necessary foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT1","text":"Surface — The existence of God is demonstrated through His possibility and through the existence of contingent beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT2","text":"Structural — Reality is organized by an asymmetrical relation between the contingent being, which requires a reason, and the Necessary Being, which possesses it within itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The demonstration is reinforced by the convergence of independent proofs: logic, eternal truths, and the experience of contingency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Explanatory causality culminates in a timeless necessity that grounds existence without itself being grounded by anything else.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the two demonstrative paths and their convergence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if the possibility of the Necessary Being effectively entails its existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT3","text":"The strongest point is the articulation between the principle of sufficient reason and the distinction between the contingent and the necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT4","text":"The underdetermined point is the independent justification of the possibility of the absolutely unlimited and non-contradictory being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: logical possibility → necessary existence, then empirical contingency → ultimate reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT6","text":"The residual tension concerns the transition from the absence of contradiction to positive possibility, a transition asserted more than demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_37:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_37@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_37:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 45"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 45","title":"Proposition 45","context":"Chapter 45","original_title":"Proposition 45"},"original_title":"Proposition 45","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 46","order":46,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_38"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_38@R001","sha256":"f6d5469a29d4c99402bd3f9ff493bb502b2ede53f3675dcc8b21c46af64b894d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS1","text":"Le texte corrige l’inférence selon laquelle la dépendance des vérités éternelles à l’égard de Dieu les rendrait arbitraires.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS2","text":"Il distingue les vérités contingentes des vérités nécessaires selon leur principe respectif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS3","text":"Les vérités contingentes procèdent de la convenance ou du choix du meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS4","text":"Les vérités nécessaires dépendent exclusivement de l’entendement divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS5","text":"La nécessité est ainsi fondée dans l’entendement comme lieu interne des vérités, et non dans la volonté comme pouvoir de décision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","text":"Les vérités éternelles dépendent de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","text":"La dépendance à l’égard de Dieu n’implique pas uniformément l’arbitraire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","text":"Les vérités contingentes ont pour principe la convenance ou le choix du meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","text":"Les vérités nécessaires ne reposent pas sur un choix entre plusieurs possibilités.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","text":"Les vérités nécessaires dépendent uniquement de l’entendement divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A6","text":"Les vérités nécessaires sont les objets internes de l’entendement divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A7","text":"La volonté divine détermine le contingent, mais ne constitue pas le fondement des vérités nécessaires.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A8","text":"L’attribution de l’arbitraire aux vérités éternelles résulte d’une confusion entre dépendance divine et dépendance volontaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX1","text":"Les vérités éternelles ne sont pas arbitraires du seul fait qu’elles dépendent de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX2","text":"Les vérités nécessaires ne dépendent pas de la volonté divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX3","text":"Les vérités nécessaires ne procèdent pas de la convenance ou du choix du meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX4","text":"La nécessité n’est pas une propriété instituée par une décision divine contingente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX5","text":"La dépendance divine n’est pas réductible à l’obéissance d’un contenu à un acte de vouloir.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX6","text":"La position attribuée à Des Cartes et à Monsieur Poiret n’est pas retenue lorsqu’elle universalise l’arbitraire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D1","text":"La distinction entre vérités contingentes et nécessaires doit précéder toute détermination de leur dépendance divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D2","text":"La volonté divine intervient dans l’ordre du choix du monde ou du meilleur, non dans la constitution des vérités nécessaires.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D3","text":"L’entendement divin fournit le principe de nécessité sans fonctionner comme une faculté de sélection arbitraire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D4","text":"La dépendance des vérités nécessaires à l’égard de Dieu est une dépendance intellectuelle et non volitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D5","text":"Le fondement divin des vérités nécessaires conserve leur nécessité au lieu de la convertir en contingence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","text":"La dépendance ontologique à l’égard de Dieu se divise en deux régimes : production volontaire du contingent et intelligibilité interne du nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SD2","text":"La nécessité est compatible avec une dépendance divine dès lors que cette dépendance désigne l’appartenance à l’entendement plutôt que l’effet d’une décision.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SD3","text":"La volonté divine est limitée structurellement par un ordre intelligible qu’elle ne produit pas comme choix contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SD4","text":"Le texte substitue à l’alternative « indépendance ou arbitraire » une architecture différenciée de dépendances divines.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une vérité nécessaire puisse être rendue vraie ou fausse par un décret de la volonté divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX2","text":"Il exclut que tout ce qui dépend de Dieu dépende de Dieu selon le même mode causal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une conception de Dieu dans laquelle l’entendement ne ferait qu’enregistrer des vérités choisies par la volonté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX4","text":"Il exclut la réduction de la nécessité à une préférence divine stabilisée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX5","text":"Il exclut une théorie unitaire de la vérité fondée exclusivement sur la liberté de décision divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX1","text":"L’arbitraire divin comme source universelle de vérité est la possibilité forclose autour de laquelle s’organise la correction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX2","text":"L’indépendance des vérités nécessaires à l’égard de toute volonté constituante est l’absence qui permet de maintenir simultanément leur dépendance à Dieu et leur nécessité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX3","text":"Le texte rend impossible une souveraineté divine conçue comme pouvoir de modifier l’intelligible nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX4","text":"Ce qui est structurellement indisponible à la volonté est précisément ce qui définit les vérités nécessaires comme objets internes de l’entendement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS1","text":"Dépendance des vérités éternelles à Dieu → risque d’inférence volontariste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS2","text":"Inférence volontariste → distinction entre vérités contingentes et vérités nécessaires.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS3","text":"Vérités contingentes → convenance et choix du meilleur → dépendance à la volonté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS4","text":"Vérités nécessaires → entendement divin → objet interne → nécessité non arbitraire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS5","text":"Différenciation des modes de dépendance → compatibilité entre dépendance divine et nécessité éternelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AF1","text":"Dépendance divine apparente → dénonciation de l’arbitraire généralisé → distinction des régimes de vérité → séparation volonté / entendement → fondation intellectuelle de la nécessité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ME1","text":"La carte de la dépendance divine est scindée entre une causalité volontaire du contingent et une dépendance intellectuelle du nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ME2","text":"L’opposition entre autonomie des vérités et arbitraire divin s’effondre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ME3","text":"Les vérités nécessaires sont reclassées comme objets internes de l’entendement plutôt que comme produits d’une décision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ME4","text":"La volonté divine cesse d’occuper la position de fondement universel de l’ordre du vrai.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le texte réfute l’idée que les vérités éternelles soient arbitraires parce qu’elles dépendent de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT2","text":"Structural — Il répartit les vérités selon deux principes : choix du meilleur pour le contingent, entendement divin pour le nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Il neutralise une objection théologique en transformant une dépendance indifférenciée en pluralité de modes de dépendance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Il établit un ordre nécessaire, éternel et intelligible qui n’est pas produit par une décision temporelle ou contingente de la volonté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement central : dépendance divine, distinction des vérités, séparation de l’entendement et de la volonté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente : la dépendance à Dieu reçoit deux modalités non équivalentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT3","text":"La force principale du système réside dans l’identification des vérités nécessaires à des objets internes de l’entendement divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT4","text":"Le texte laisse sous-déterminée la manière exacte dont la convenance et le choix du meilleur produisent les vérités contingentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT5","text":"Il ne développe pas davantage le statut de l’entendement divin ni la relation entre son contenu interne et la dépendance à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel, mais la brièveté de l’énoncé oblige à expliciter la distinction entre fondement intelligible et décision volontaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193453680092Z_3a669297","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 46","source_sha256":"f6d5469a29d4c99402bd3f9ff493bb502b2ede53f3675dcc8b21c46af64b894d","sha256":"4918bf042f4b125ec8d7b2180797faf91638e08e7e2fec484fa257a85e549dc8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:34:53.687569+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS1","text":"The text corrects the inference according to which the dependence of eternal truths on God would render them arbitrary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS2","text":"It distinguishes contingent truths from necessary truths according to their respective principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS3","text":"Contingent truths proceed from fitness or the choice of the best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS4","text":"Necessary truths depend exclusively on the divine understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AS5","text":"Necessity is thus grounded in the understanding as the internal locus of truths, and not in the will as the power of decision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","text":"Eternal truths depend on God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","text":"Dependence on God does not uniformly imply arbitrariness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","text":"Contingent truths have as their principle fitness or the choice of the best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","text":"Necessary truths do not rest upon a choice among several possibilities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","text":"Necessary truths depend solely on the divine understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A6","text":"Necessary truths are the internal objects of the divine understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A7","text":"The divine will determines the contingent, but does not constitute the ground of necessary truths.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:A8","text":"The attribution of arbitrariness to eternal truths results from a confusion between divine dependence and voluntary dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX1","text":"Eternal truths are not arbitrary merely because they depend on God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX2","text":"Necessary truths do not depend on the divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX3","text":"Necessary truths do not proceed from fitness or the choice of the best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX4","text":"Necessity is not a property instituted by a contingent divine decision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX5","text":"Divine dependence cannot be reduced to the obedience of a content to an act of willing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:NX6","text":"The position attributed to Des Cartes and Monsieur Poiret is not retained insofar as it universalizes arbitrariness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D1","text":"The distinction between contingent and necessary truths must precede any determination of their divine dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D2","text":"The divine will intervenes in the order of the choice of the world or of the best, not in the constitution of necessary truths.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D3","text":"The divine understanding provides the principle of necessity without functioning as a faculty of arbitrary selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D4","text":"The dependence of necessary truths on God is an intellectual and not a volitional dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:D5","text":"The divine ground of necessary truths preserves their necessity rather than converting it into contingency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","text":"Ontological dependence on God divides into two regimes: voluntary production of the contingent and internal intelligibility of the necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SD2","text":"Necessity is compatible with divine dependence insofar as this dependence denotes belonging to the understanding rather than the effect of a decision.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SD3","text":"The divine will is structurally limited by an intelligible order that it does not produce as a contingent choice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SD4","text":"The text substitutes for the alternative “independence or arbitrariness” a differentiated architecture of divine dependences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a necessary truth may be made true or false by a decree of the divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that everything which depends on God depends on God according to the same causal mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX3","text":"It excludes a conception of God in which the understanding would merely register truths chosen by the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX4","text":"It excludes the reduction of necessity to a stabilized divine preference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX5","text":"It excludes a unitary theory of truth founded exclusively on the freedom of divine decision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX1","text":"Divine arbitrariness as the universal source of truth is the foreclosed possibility around which the correction is organized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX2","text":"The independence of necessary truths from every constituting will is the absence that makes it possible to maintain simultaneously their dependence on God and their necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX3","text":"The text renders impossible a divine sovereignty conceived as the power to modify the necessary intelligible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX4","text":"That which is structurally unavailable to the will is precisely what defines necessary truths as internal objects of the understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS1","text":"Dependence of eternal truths on God → risk of voluntarist inference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS2","text":"Voluntarist inference → distinction between contingent truths and necessary truths.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS3","text":"Contingent truths → fitness and the choice of the best → dependence on the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS4","text":"Necessary truths → divine understanding → internal object → non-arbitrary necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS5","text":"Differentiation of modes of dependence → compatibility between divine dependence and eternal necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:AF1","text":"Apparent divine dependence → denunciation of generalized arbitrariness → distinction of regimes of truth → separation of will / understanding → intellectual grounding of necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ME1","text":"The map of divine dependence is split between a voluntary causality of the contingent and an intellectual dependence of the necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ME2","text":"The opposition between the autonomy of truths and divine arbitrariness collapses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ME3","text":"Necessary truths are reclassified as internal objects of the understanding rather than as products of a decision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ME4","text":"The divine will ceases to occupy the position of universal ground of the order of truth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text refutes the idea that eternal truths are arbitrary because they depend on God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT2","text":"Structural — It distributes truths according to two principles: choice of the best for the contingent, divine understanding for the necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — It neutralizes a theological objection by transforming an undifferentiated dependence into a plurality of modes of dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — It establishes a necessary, eternal, and intelligible order that is not produced by a temporal or contingent decision of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the central movement: divine dependence, distinction of truths, separation of understanding and will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent: dependence on God receives two non-equivalent modalities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT3","text":"The principal strength of the system lies in the identification of necessary truths with internal objects of the divine understanding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT4","text":"The text leaves underdetermined the exact manner in which fitness and the choice of the best produce contingent truths.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT5","text":"It does not further develop the status of the divine understanding or the relation between its internal content and dependence on God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement, but the brevity of the statement requires making explicit the distinction between intelligible ground and voluntary decision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_38:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_38@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_38:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 46"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 46","title":"Proposition 46","context":"Chapter 46","original_title":"Proposition 46"},"original_title":"Proposition 46","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 47","order":47,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_39"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_39@R001","sha256":"3157e0c33b833a8a38ed599685016e0ff3d2e943b37064bfd32e1c412b418d43","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AS1","text":"L’unité originaire de l’être est identifiée à Dieu seul, conçu comme substance simple primitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AS2","text":"Les Monades créées sont recadrées comme des productions dérivatives plutôt que comme des principes autonomes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AS3","text":"Leur production est conçue comme une fulguration divine continuée de moment en moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AS4","text":"La réceptivité limitée de la créature détermine la borne de cette production et fonde son statut dérivé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","text":"Dieu seul est l’unité primitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","text":"Dieu seul est la substance simple originaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","text":"Toute Monade créée est une production divine dérivative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","text":"Les Monades créées naissent par des fulgurations continuelles de la Divinité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","text":"La production divine se renouvelle de moment en moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","text":"La réceptivité de la créature borne la production divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A7","text":"La limitation est essentielle à la créature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX1","text":"Une Monade créée n’est pas une unité primitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX2","text":"Une Monade créée n’est pas une substance simple originaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX3","text":"La créature n’est pas une source autonome de sa propre production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX4","text":"La création n’est pas un événement achevé et indépendant de la continuation divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX5","text":"La créature n’est pas illimitée dans sa réceptivité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","text":"Toute Monade créée dépend ontologiquement de Dieu comme de sa source productive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:D2","text":"L’existence actuelle des Monades créées implique une continuation de l’opération divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:D3","text":"La différence entre Dieu et la créature se manifeste comme différence entre origine simple et production limitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:D4","text":"La pluralité des Monades dérivatives ne supprime pas l’unité primitive dont elles procèdent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SD1","text":"L’ordre des substances est asymétrique : Dieu constitue l’origine unique, tandis que les Monades créées occupent le régime de la dépendance dérivative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2","text":"La continuité de l’être créé est reconduite à une actualisation divine temporellement réitérée plutôt qu’à une auto-maintenance de la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3","text":"La limitation créaturelle fonctionne simultanément comme condition de la distinction entre Dieu et la créature et comme principe de la détermination des productions créées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une ontologie dans laquelle plusieurs substances posséderaient originairement le même statut de principe premier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX2","text":"Il exclut une conception de l’existence créée comme propriété autosuffisante une fois la création accomplie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une réceptivité créaturelle sans borne, qui abolirait la dissymétrie entre origine divine et production créée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une causalité créatrice réduite à un acte initial sans opération actuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SNX1","text":"L’indépendance ontologique de la créature est la possibilité forclose autour de laquelle s’organise tout le dispositif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SNX2","text":"L’existence créée ne peut être pensée en dehors d’une dépendance continue à une source qui ne devient pas elle-même dérivative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SNX3","text":"L’identité entre l’unité divine originaire et la multiplicité créée est rendue impossible par la limitation constitutive de la créature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS1","text":"Unité primitive divine → substance simple originaire → source de toutes les Monades créées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS2","text":"Fulguration divine continuelle → production de moment en moment → maintien de l’existence dérivative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS3","text":"Réceptivité créaturelle limitée → borne de la production → différenciation entre Dieu et la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS4","text":"Source unique illimitée en son statut originaire + réceptivités créées limitées → pluralité dérivative sans autonomie primitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AF1","text":"Multiplicité des Monades créées → recherche de leur principe commun → identification de Dieu comme unité primitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AF2","text":"Identification de l’origine divine → distinction entre substance originaire et substances dérivatives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AF3","text":"Distinction ontologique → recadrage de la création comme fulguration continuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AF4","text":"Production continuelle → limitation par la réceptivité créaturelle → constitution de la dépendance créée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ME1","text":"L’origine de l’être est reclassée : la primitivité appartient exclusivement à Dieu, tandis que toute Monade créée devient dérivative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ME2","text":"La création est déplacée d’un modèle ponctuel vers un modèle d’actualisation continuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ME3","text":"La limitation cesse d’être une simple imperfection accidentelle et devient le principe structurel de la créature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ME4","text":"L’unité et la multiplicité ne sont plus des principes concurrents : la multiplicité monadique est cartographiée comme production de l’unité divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ALT1","text":"Surface — Dieu est posé comme unité primitive et les Monades créées comme productions dérivatives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ALT2","text":"Structural — Le rapport entre origine, production, continuité et réceptivité organise la hiérarchie des substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La question de l’origine est recadrée en question de dépendance productive continue plutôt qu’en simple succession temporelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’être créé est conçu comme une réalité limitée dont l’existence demeure liée à des fulgurations divines renouvelées de moment en moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire l’opposition entre substance primitive et Monades dérivatives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT2","text":"Ils suffisent également à reconstruire le passage d’une création initiale à une production divine continuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT3","text":"La fonction de la réceptivité créaturelle est déterminée, mais son mode précis de limitation reste sous-déterminé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT4","text":"La cohérence interne repose sur l’articulation entre unicité divine, dérivation monadique et limitation créaturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT5","text":"La tension principale demeure entre la dépendance intégrale des Monades et leur statut de substances créées distinctes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : unité originaire → production continuelle → limitation créaturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193506600692Z_5350167c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 47","source_sha256":"3157e0c33b833a8a38ed599685016e0ff3d2e943b37064bfd32e1c412b418d43","sha256":"8d53342accb8ee886eedecad74a8eed966f81d28e4ce09535ae78f991cb9c577","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:35:06.605473+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AS1","text":"The originary unity of being is identified with God alone, conceived as primitive simple substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AS2","text":"Created Monads are reframed as derivative productions rather than as autonomous principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AS3","text":"Their production is conceived as a divine fulguration continued from moment to moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AS4","text":"The creature's limited receptivity determines the bound of this production and grounds its derivative status.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","text":"God alone is the primitive unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","text":"God alone is the originary simple substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","text":"Every created Monad is a derivative divine production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","text":"Created Monads arise through continual fulgurations of the Divinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","text":"Divine production is renewed from moment to moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","text":"The creature's receptivity bounds divine production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:A7","text":"Limitation is essential to the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX1","text":"A created Monad is not a primitive unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX2","text":"A created Monad is not an originary simple substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX3","text":"The creature is not an autonomous source of its own production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX4","text":"Creation is not an accomplished event independent of divine continuation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:NX5","text":"The creature is not unlimited in its receptivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","text":"Every created Monad depends ontologically on God as on its productive source.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:D2","text":"The actual existence of created Monads implies a continuation of divine operation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:D3","text":"The difference between God and the creature manifests itself as the difference between simple origin and limited production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:D4","text":"The plurality of derivative Monads does not suppress the primitive unity from which they proceed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SD1","text":"The order of substances is asymmetrical: God constitutes the unique origin, while created Monads occupy the regime of derivative dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2","text":"The continuity of created being is traced back to a divinely actualized process temporally reiterated rather than to the creature's self-maintenance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3","text":"Creaturely limitation functions simultaneously as the condition for the distinction between God and the creature and as the principle determining created productions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an ontology in which several substances would originally possess the same status of first principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX2","text":"It excludes a conception of created existence as a self-sufficient property once creation has been accomplished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX3","text":"It excludes an unbounded creaturely receptivity that would abolish the asymmetry between divine origin and created production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX4","text":"It excludes a creative causality reduced to an initial act without present operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SNX1","text":"The ontological independence of the creature is the foreclosed possibility around which the entire apparatus is organized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SNX2","text":"Created existence cannot be conceived apart from continuous dependence on a source that does not itself become derivative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:SNX3","text":"The identity between originary divine unity and created multiplicity is rendered impossible by the creature's constitutive limitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS1","text":"Primitive divine unity → originary simple substance → source of all created Monads.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS2","text":"Continual divine fulguration → production from moment to moment → maintenance of derivative existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS3","text":"Limited creaturely receptivity → bound of production → differentiation between God and the creature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS4","text":"Unique source unlimited in its originary status + limited created receptivities → derivative plurality without primitive autonomy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AF1","text":"Multiplicity of created Monads → search for their common principle → identification of God as primitive unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AF2","text":"Identification of divine origin → distinction between originary substance and derivative substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AF3","text":"Ontological distinction → reframing of creation as continual fulguration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:AF4","text":"Continual production → limitation by creaturely receptivity → constitution of created dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ME1","text":"The origin of being is reclassified: primitiveness belongs exclusively to God, while every created Monad becomes derivative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ME2","text":"Creation is displaced from a punctual model toward a model of continual actualization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ME3","text":"Limitation ceases to be a merely accidental imperfection and becomes the structural principle of the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ME4","text":"Unity and multiplicity are no longer competing principles: monadic multiplicity is mapped as a production of divine unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ALT1","text":"Surface — God is posited as primitive unity and created Monads as derivative productions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ALT2","text":"Structural — The relation between origin, production, continuity, and receptivity organizes the hierarchy of substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The question of origin is reframed as a question of continuous productive dependence rather than as mere temporal succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Created being is conceived as a limited reality whose existence remains bound to divine fulgurations renewed from moment to moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the opposition between primitive substance and derivative Monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT2","text":"They likewise suffice to reconstruct the transition from an initial creation to continual divine production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT3","text":"The function of creaturely receptivity is determined, but its precise mode of limitation remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence rests on the articulation between divine uniqueness, monadic derivation, and creaturely limitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT5","text":"The principal tension remains between the integral dependence of the Monads and their status as distinct created substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: originary unity → continual production → creaturely limitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_39:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_39@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_39:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 47"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 47","title":"Proposition 47","context":"Chapter 47","original_title":"Proposition 47"},"original_title":"Proposition 47","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 48","order":48,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_40"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_40@R001","sha256":"7845bfef461b76b4ce765a217abeccffae2e8c6aa7547627201301fb241a3952","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS1","text":"La constitution divine doit être articulée selon trois fonctions fondamentales : produire, connaître et modifier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS2","text":"La Puissance divine fonde l’existence de tout ce qui peut être produit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS3","text":"La Connaissance divine contient le détail des Idées selon lequel les productions sont déterminées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4","text":"La Volonté divine effectue les changements conformément au principe du meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS5","text":"Cette triade possède une correspondance fonctionnelle dans les Monades créées, sous la forme du sujet ou de la base, de la perception et de l’appétition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS6","text":"La différence entre Dieu et les Monades créées tient au degré de perfection : les attributs divins sont absolument infinis, tandis que leurs équivalents créés n’en sont que des imitations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A1","text":"La Puissance est en Dieu la source de tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A2","text":"La Connaissance divine contient le détail des Idées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A3","text":"La Volonté divine produit les changements selon le principe du meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","text":"Les Monades créées comportent une base ou un sujet, une faculté perceptive et une faculté appétitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","text":"Les trois fonctions divines répondent fonctionnellement aux trois facultés des Monades créées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","text":"Les attributs divins sont absolument infinis ou parfaits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","text":"Les facultés des Monades créées sont des imitations des attributs divins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A8","text":"Le degré d’imitation des attributs divins varie avec le degré de perfection de la Monade créée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A9","text":"La structure de la Monade créée peut être désignée comme une Entéléchie ou comme une perfectihabie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX1","text":"Les facultés des Monades créées ne sont pas identiques aux attributs divins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX2","text":"Les Monades créées ne possèdent pas la Puissance, la Connaissance et la Volonté sous une forme absolument infinie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX3","text":"La perception créée n’est pas la Connaissance divine dans son extension totale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX4","text":"L’appétition créée ne constitue pas une Volonté divine absolument parfaite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX5","text":"La production divine n’est pas un changement dépourvu de principe directeur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX6","text":"La hiérarchie des Monades ne repose pas sur une possession uniforme de la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D1","text":"La structure interne d’une Monade créée reproduit à son échelle la structure fonctionnelle de l’action divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D2","text":"La capacité d’une Monade créée à percevoir et à agir dépend du degré de perfection qu’elle réalise.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D3","text":"La Puissance, la Connaissance et la Volonté divines forment les conditions distinctes de la production ordonnée du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A1","CH_UCIC_P_40:A2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D4","text":"La base, la perception et l’appétition ne sont pas trois propriétés isolées, mais les formes créées correspondant aux trois fonctions divines.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D5","text":"La perfection créée est graduelle parce que l’imitation des attributs divins est graduelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SD1","text":"L’ordre des êtres créés est organisé comme une série de degrés d’imitation de la structure divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2","text":"La causalité divine articule simultanément une source de production, une détermination idéale et une orientation normative vers le meilleur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A1","CH_UCIC_P_40:A2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3","text":"Toute Monade créée est définie à la fois par son inscription dans l’ordre productif divin et par la limitation de cette inscription à un degré fini de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SD4","text":"La distinction entre Dieu et les créatures est une différence de degré absolu, et non une différence de fonctions fondamentales.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une séparation radicale entre la structure divine et la structure monadique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX2","text":"Il exclut une conception de la créature comme réalité étrangère aux fonctions de puissance, de connaissance et de volonté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une production du monde qui ne serait ni fondée dans une puissance, ni déterminée par des Idées, ni orientée par le meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une perfection créée indépendante de toute participation ou imitation de la perfection divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX5","text":"Il exclut une lecture purement nominale de la correspondance entre Dieu et les Monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SNX1","text":"L’altérité absolue entre Dieu et les Monades est forclose par la continuité analogique des fonctions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SNX2","text":"L’autonomie ontologique complète des Monades créées est rendue impossible par leur statut d’imitations graduées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SNX3","text":"Une réalité sans ordre rationnel du meilleur est exclue comme possibilité fondamentale du système.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS1","text":"La Puissance divine fournit la source de toute production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS2","text":"La Connaissance divine spécifie les productions possibles par le détail des Idées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS3","text":"La Volonté divine sélectionne et effectue les changements selon le principe du meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS4","text":"La triade divine se réfracte dans la Monade créée comme base, perception et appétition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS5","text":"La perfection de chaque Monade détermine le degré auquel elle imite cette triade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS6","text":"La structure du créé est ainsi engendrée comme imitation graduée d’une causalité divine infinie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AF1","text":"Structure divine triadique → correspondance fonctionnelle avec la Monade → distinction entre infinité divine et imitation créée → hiérarchie graduelle de la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AF2","text":"Source de production → détermination par les Idées → orientation vers le meilleur → constitution analogue des facultés créées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ME1","text":"Dieu et les Monades sont reclassés dans un même espace fonctionnel, différencié par le degré de perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ME2","text":"La Monade créée devient lisible comme une structure dynamique composée d’une base, d’une représentation et d’une tendance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ME3","text":"La production du réel est reconfigurée comme articulation de puissance, d’intelligibilité et de finalité normative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ME4","text":"La gradation des êtres est établie comme gradation de l’imitation divine plutôt que comme simple classement externe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le texte énumère les trois attributs divins et leurs équivalents dans les Monades créées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT2","text":"Structural — Le texte construit une homologie entre la constitution de Dieu et la constitution interne des Monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le texte recadre la différence entre Dieu et les créatures comme variation de perfection au sein d’une même architecture fonctionnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Le réel créé est compris comme une production ordonnée par les Idées et orientée vers le meilleur, tandis que les êtres créés réalisent cette structure selon des degrés finis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes A1 à A8 suffisent à reconstruire la triade divine, sa correspondance monadique et la gradation de la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT2","text":"La reconstruction demeure sous-déterminée quant au rapport précis entre la base monadique et la Puissance divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT3","text":"La correspondance entre les attributs divins et les facultés créées est fonctionnelle et analogique, mais le texte ne formalise pas son mécanisme détaillé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT4","text":"La cohérence interne repose sur la distinction entre infinité divine et imitation créée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT5","text":"La structure est la plus forte dans l’articulation entre triade divine, facultés monadiques et degrés de perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel du texte : décomposition de l’action divine → correspondance monadique → limitation graduelle de la perfection créée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193525179322Z_75cd3034","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 48","source_sha256":"7845bfef461b76b4ce765a217abeccffae2e8c6aa7547627201301fb241a3952","sha256":"5971fefba66363c28486228b9640240b376bd49d878f7576b2b39cfabb98f3d0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:35:25.180829+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS1","text":"The divine constitution must be articulated according to three fundamental functions: producing, knowing, and modifying.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS2","text":"Divine Power grounds the existence of everything that can be produced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS3","text":"Divine Knowledge contains the detail of the Ideas according to which productions are determined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4","text":"Divine Will brings about changes in accordance with the principle of the best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS5","text":"This triad has a functional correspondence in created Monads, in the form of the subject or basis, perception, and appetition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AS6","text":"The difference between God and created Monads lies in the degree of perfection: divine attributes are absolutely infinite, whereas their created equivalents are only imitations thereof.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A1","text":"Power is in God the source of everything.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A2","text":"Divine Knowledge contains the detail of the Ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A3","text":"Divine Will produces changes according to the principle of the best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","text":"Created Monads comprise a basis or a subject, a perceptive faculty, and an appetitive faculty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","text":"The three divine functions correspond functionally to the three faculties of created Monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","text":"Divine attributes are absolutely infinite or perfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","text":"The faculties of created Monads are imitations of divine attributes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A8","text":"The degree of imitation of divine attributes varies with the degree of perfection of the created Monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:A9","text":"The structure of the created Monad may be designated as an Entelechy or as a perfectihabie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX1","text":"The faculties of created Monads are not identical to divine attributes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX2","text":"Created Monads do not possess Power, Knowledge, and Will in an absolutely infinite form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX3","text":"Created perception is not divine Knowledge in its total extension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX4","text":"Created appetition does not constitute an absolutely perfect divine Will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX5","text":"Divine production is not a change devoid of a guiding principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:NX6","text":"The hierarchy of Monads does not rest on a uniform possession of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D1","text":"The internal structure of a created Monad reproduces, at its own scale, the functional structure of divine action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D2","text":"A created Monad's capacity to perceive and act depends on the degree of perfection that it realizes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D3","text":"Divine Power, Knowledge, and Will constitute the distinct conditions of the ordered production of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A1","CH_UCIC_P_40:A2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D4","text":"Basis, perception, and appetition are not three isolated properties, but the created forms corresponding to the three divine functions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:D5","text":"Created perfection is gradual because imitation of divine attributes is gradual.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SD1","text":"The order of created beings is organized as a series of degrees of imitation of the divine structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2","text":"Divine causality simultaneously articulates a source of production, an ideal determination, and a normative orientation toward the best.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A1","CH_UCIC_P_40:A2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3","text":"Every created Monad is defined both by its inscription within the divine productive order and by the limitation of this inscription to a finite degree of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SD4","text":"The distinction between God and creatures is a difference of absolute degree, and not a difference of fundamental functions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX1","text":"The system excludes a radical separation between the divine structure and the monadic structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX2","text":"It excludes a conception of the creature as a reality foreign to the functions of power, knowledge, and will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX3","text":"It excludes a production of the world that would be neither grounded in a power, nor determined by Ideas, nor oriented by the best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX4","text":"It excludes a created perfection independent of any participation in or imitation of divine perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX5","text":"It excludes a purely nominal reading of the correspondence between God and Monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SNX1","text":"Absolute otherness between God and Monads is precluded by the analogical continuity of the functions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SNX2","text":"The complete ontological autonomy of created Monads is rendered impossible by their status as graded imitations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:SNX3","text":"A reality without a rational order of the best is excluded as a fundamental possibility of the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS1","text":"Divine Power provides the source of all production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS2","text":"Divine Knowledge specifies possible productions through the detail of the Ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS3","text":"Divine Will selects and brings about changes according to the principle of the best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS4","text":"The divine triad is refracted in the created Monad as basis, perception, and appetition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS5","text":"The perfection of each Monad determines the degree to which it imitates this triad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS6","text":"The structure of the created is thus generated as a graded imitation of an infinite divine causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AF1","text":"Triadic divine structure → functional correspondence with the Monad → distinction between divine infinity and created imitation → gradual hierarchy of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:AF2","text":"Source of production → determination by Ideas → orientation toward the best → analogous constitution of created faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ME1","text":"God and Monads are reclassified within the same functional space, differentiated by the degree of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ME2","text":"The created Monad becomes legible as a dynamic structure composed of a basis, a representation, and a tendency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ME3","text":"The production of reality is reconfigured as an articulation of power, intelligibility, and normative finality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ME4","text":"The gradation of beings is established as a gradation of divine imitation rather than as a mere external classification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text enumerates the three divine attributes and their equivalents in created Monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT2","text":"Structural — The text constructs a homology between the constitution of God and the internal constitution of Monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text reframes the difference between God and creatures as a variation of perfection within one and the same functional architecture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Created reality is understood as a production ordered by Ideas and oriented toward the best, while created beings realize this structure according to finite degrees.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT1","text":"Axioms A1 to A8 suffice to reconstruct the divine triad, its monadic correspondence, and the gradation of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined as to the precise relation between the monadic basis and divine Power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT3","text":"The correspondence between divine attributes and created faculties is functional and analogical, but the text does not formalize its detailed mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence rests on the distinction between divine infinity and created imitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT5","text":"The structure is strongest in the articulation between the divine triad, monadic faculties, and degrees of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text: decomposition of divine action → monadic correspondence → gradual limitation of created perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_40:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_40@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_40:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 48"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 48","title":"Proposition 48","context":"Chapter 48","original_title":"Proposition 48"},"original_title":"Proposition 48","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 49","order":49,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_41"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_41@R001","sha256":"bb01bffbfe8347436ac1895e9c06e2bcb0fe762e2fe6c8660505d9ce8a366af0","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS1","text":"Le problème consiste à déterminer selon quel critère une créature est dite agir ou pâtir.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS2","text":"L’action et la passion sont recadrées comme des attributions relatives au degré de perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS3","text":"La perfection se manifeste par la distinction des perceptions, tandis que l’imperfection se manifeste par leur confusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS4","text":"La monade est donc dite agir sous le régime de la perception distincte et pâtir sous celui de la perception confuse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS5","text":"Le mouvement argumentatif va de la distinction ontologique entre perfection et imperfection à une qualification différentielle des états perceptifs de la monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A1","text":"Une créature agit au dehors en tant qu’elle possède de la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A2","text":"Une créature pâtit d’une autre en tant qu’elle est imparfaite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","text":"L’action et la passion sont déterminées par le degré de perfection de la créature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A4","text":"La perfection d’une monade se rapporte à la distinction de ses perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A5","text":"L’imperfection d’une monade se rapporte à la confusion de ses perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","text":"L’action est attribuée à la monade sous le rapport de ses perceptions distinctes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A7","text":"La passion est attribuée à la monade sous le rapport de ses perceptions confuses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A8","text":"Une même monade peut être qualifiée différemment selon le régime perceptif considéré.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX1","text":"L’action n’est pas attribuée à la monade indépendamment de la distinction de ses perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX2","text":"La passion n’est pas attribuée à la monade en tant qu’elle possède de la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX3","text":"La perfection n’est pas assimilée à la confusion perceptive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX4","text":"L’imperfection n’est pas définie comme absence totale de perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX5","text":"L’action et la passion ne constituent pas deux propriétés absolues et uniformes de la monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX6","text":"La qualification d’agent ou de patient ne se déduit pas d’une séparation substantielle entre les monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:D1","text":"La distinction perceptive fonde l’attribution de l’action à la monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A4","CH_UCIC_P_41:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:D2","text":"La confusion perceptive fonde l’attribution de la passion à la monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A5","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:D3","text":"L’action et la passion correspondent à deux modalités perceptives d’un même être plutôt qu’à deux natures séparées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7","CH_UCIC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:D4","text":"Le rapport d’une monade à l’action ou à la passion varie avec le degré de clarté de ses perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_41:A4","CH_UCIC_P_41:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SD1","text":"La causalité imputée à une monade est indexée sur son degré interne de perfection perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A1","CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_41:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SD2","text":"La distinction entre agent et patient devient graduelle et réversible selon le niveau de perception considéré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7","CH_UCIC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SD3","text":"La passivité ne désigne pas une pure privation d’activité, mais une activité déterminée par des perceptions confuses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A2","CH_UCIC_P_41:A5","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SD4","text":"L’opposition entre action et passion est reconduite à une différence de perfection plutôt qu’à une opposition ontologique de substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une conception de l’action comme puissance indépendante de tout état perceptif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut une conception de la passion comme événement extérieur dépourvu de corrélat interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une symétrie stricte entre perceptions distinctes et perceptions confuses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut que la relation extérieure suffise à déterminer l’agent et le patient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX5","text":"Le système exclut une conception binaire où chaque monade serait exclusivement active ou exclusivement passive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’une action absolument extérieure à la monade, puisque l’action est rapportée à son régime perceptif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX2","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’une passion purement imposée du dehors, puisque pâtir suppose l’imperfection propre de la monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX3","text":"Est absente l’idée d’un sujet entièrement transparent à lui-même, puisque la confusion perceptive constitue une modalité opératoire de son rapport au monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX4","text":"Est inadmissible une séparation définitive entre activité et passivité au niveau de la créature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS1","text":"Degré de perfection → qualité du rapport de la créature au dehors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS2","text":"Perfection → perceptions distinctes → attribution de l’action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS3","text":"Imperfection → perceptions confuses → attribution de la passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS4","text":"Variation du régime perceptif → variation de la qualification agent/patient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS5","text":"Action et passion → deux déterminations relatives d’une même monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AF1","text":"Créature → degré de perfection → régime perceptif → action ou passion → qualification relationnelle de la monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AF2","text":"Perception distincte → perfection → action au dehors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AF3","text":"Perception confuse → imperfection → passion d’une autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AF4","text":"Même monade → rapports perceptifs différenciés → alternance structurelle entre activité et passivité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ME1","text":"L’agent et le patient sont reclassés comme des positions relatives déterminées par le degré de perfection perceptive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2","text":"L’opposition extérieur/intérieur est redistribuée : l’action au dehors dépend d’une distinction interne des perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ME3","text":"La passivité est requalifiée comme effet d’une perception confuse plutôt que comme simple réception externe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ME4","text":"L’action et la passion cessent d’être des catégories exclusives et deviennent des fonctions variables d’une même monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Le texte distingue l’action et la passion selon que la monade possède des perceptions distinctes ou confuses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Le degré de perfection organise l’attribution différentielle des positions d’agent et de patient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Le texte recadre l’opposition action/passion en opposition graduelle de clarté perceptive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — La monade est conçue comme un être dont le rapport causal varie selon l’état de ses perceptions, sans changement de substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le passage de la perfection à l’action et de l’imperfection à la passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT2","text":"La distinction entre perceptions distinctes et perceptions confuses fournit le mécanisme médiateur indispensable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT3","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si l’action et la passion sont comprises comme des attributions relatives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT4","text":"Le texte sous-détermine le sens précis de « au dehors » et le mode de dépendance entre monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT5","text":"La tension principale réside dans l’articulation entre une action dite extérieure et un critère entièrement formulé en termes perceptifs internes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : perfection/im­perfection → distinction/confusion perceptive → action/passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193542786526Z_9c2550c8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 49","source_sha256":"bb01bffbfe8347436ac1895e9c06e2bcb0fe762e2fe6c8660505d9ce8a366af0","sha256":"bcacbf6fab5248618ae87809932bbd1ca8b80c8972118af6b7ad274d6d9198db","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:35:42.790546+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS1","text":"The problem consists in determining according to which criterion a creature is said to act or to suffer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS2","text":"Action and passion are reframed as attributions relative to the degree of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS3","text":"Perfection manifests itself through the distinctness of perceptions, whereas imperfection manifests itself through their confusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS4","text":"The monad is thus said to act under the regime of distinct perception and to suffer under that of confused perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AS5","text":"The argumentative movement proceeds from the ontological distinction between perfection and imperfection to a differential qualification of the monad's perceptual states.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A1","text":"A creature acts externally insofar as it possesses perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A2","text":"A creature suffers from another insofar as it is imperfect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","text":"Action and passion are determined by the degree of perfection of the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A4","text":"The perfection of a monad pertains to the distinctness of its perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A5","text":"The imperfection of a monad pertains to the confusion of its perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","text":"Action is attributed to the monad with respect to its distinct perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A7","text":"Passion is attributed to the monad with respect to its confused perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:A8","text":"One and the same monad can be qualified differently according to the perceptual regime considered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX1","text":"Action is not attributed to the monad independently of the distinctness of its perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX2","text":"Passion is not attributed to the monad insofar as it possesses perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX3","text":"Perfection is not equated with perceptual confusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX4","text":"Imperfection is not defined as the total absence of perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX5","text":"Action and passion do not constitute two absolute and uniform properties of the monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:NX6","text":"The qualification as agent or patient is not deduced from a substantial separation between monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:D1","text":"Perceptual distinctness grounds the attribution of action to the monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A4","CH_UCIC_P_41:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:D2","text":"Perceptual confusion grounds the attribution of passion to the monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A5","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:D3","text":"Action and passion correspond to two perceptual modalities of the same being rather than to two separate natures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7","CH_UCIC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:D4","text":"A monad's relation to action or passion varies with the degree of clarity of its perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_41:A4","CH_UCIC_P_41:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SD1","text":"The causality imputed to a monad is indexed to its internal degree of perceptual perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A1","CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_41:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SD2","text":"The distinction between agent and patient becomes gradual and reversible according to the level of perception considered.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7","CH_UCIC_P_41:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SD3","text":"Passivity does not designate a pure deprivation of activity, but an activity determined by confused perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A2","CH_UCIC_P_41:A5","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SD4","text":"The opposition between action and passion is traced back to a difference of perfection rather than to an ontological opposition of substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","CH_UCIC_P_41:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX1","text":"The system excludes a conception of action as a power independent of every perceptual state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a conception of passion as an external event devoid of an internal correlate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a strict symmetry between distinct perceptions and confused perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the external relation's being sufficient to determine the agent and the patient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX5","text":"The system excludes a binary conception in which each monad would be exclusively active or exclusively passive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX1","text":"The possibility of an action absolutely external to the monad is foreclosed, since action is related to its perceptual regime.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a passion purely imposed from outside is foreclosed, since suffering presupposes the monad's own imperfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX3","text":"Absent is the idea of a subject entirely transparent to itself, since perceptual confusion constitutes an operative modality of its relation to the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX4","text":"A definitive separation between activity and passivity at the level of the creature is inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS1","text":"Degree of perfection → quality of the creature's relation to the outside.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS2","text":"Perfection → distinct perceptions → attribution of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS3","text":"Imperfection → confused perceptions → attribution of passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS4","text":"Variation in perceptual regime → variation in agent/patient qualification.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS5","text":"Action and passion → two relative determinations of the same monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AF1","text":"Creature → degree of perfection → perceptual regime → action or passion → relational qualification of the monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AF2","text":"Distinct perception → perfection → external action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AF3","text":"Confused perception → imperfection → suffering from another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:AF4","text":"Same monad → differentiated perceptual relations → structural alternation between activity and passivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ME1","text":"The agent and the patient are reclassified as relative positions determined by the degree of perceptual perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2","text":"The external/internal opposition is redistributed: external action depends on an internal distinctness of perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ME3","text":"Passivity is requalified as the effect of a confused perception rather than as mere external reception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ME4","text":"Action and passion cease to be exclusive categories and become variable functions of the same monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — The text distinguishes action and passion according to whether the monad possesses distinct or confused perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The degree of perfection organizes the differential attribution of the positions of agent and patient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The text reframes the action/passion opposition as a gradual opposition of perceptual clarity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — The monad is conceived as a being whose causal relation varies according to the state of its perceptions, without a change of substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage from perfection to action and from imperfection to passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT2","text":"The distinction between distinct perceptions and confused perceptions provides the indispensable mediating mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent if action and passion are understood as relative attributions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT4","text":"The text underdetermines the precise meaning of « au dehors » and the mode of dependence between monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT5","text":"The principal tension lies in the articulation between an action said to be external and a criterion formulated entirely in internal perceptual terms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: perfection/imperfection → perceptual distinctness/confusion → action/passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_41:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_41@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_41:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 49"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 49","title":"Proposition 49","context":"Chapter 49","original_title":"Proposition 49"},"original_title":"Proposition 49","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 50","order":50,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_42"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_42@R001","sha256":"bad5b923a3aced40b00903d0594fe0d536a187cf316e12d65a251d8b7c24626c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AS1","text":"La perfection des créatures est différenciée selon leur capacité à rendre raison de ce qui se passe dans une autre créature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AS2","text":"Cette capacité repose sur la présence d’une raison a priori de l’événement observé dans l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AS3","text":"Le rapport explicatif est converti en rapport d’action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AS4","text":"L’action attribuée à une créature dérive ainsi d’une priorité rationnelle et non d’un mécanisme causal décrit séparément.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A1","text":"Les créatures peuvent être comparées selon des degrés de perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A2","text":"La perfection est ici mesurée par une relation déterminée à une autre créature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A3","text":"Une créature est d’autant plus parfaite qu’elle contient une raison a priori de ce qui se passe dans une autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","text":"Ce qui rend raison a priori d’un événement en constitue le fondement explicatif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A5","text":"Le fondement explicatif a priori autorise l’attribution d’une action à la créature qui le contient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A6","text":"L’action d’une créature sur une autre est définie par le rapport entre son contenu rationnel et l’événement de l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX1","text":"La perfection n’est pas définie ici comme une qualité indépendante de toute relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX2","text":"L’action n’est pas fondée sur une simple succession temporelle entre deux événements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX3","text":"L’action n’est pas rapportée à une force matérielle explicitement décrite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX4","text":"La priorité explicative n’est pas réduite à une constatation empirique de concomitance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX5","text":"Le texte ne pose pas la réciprocité de l’action entre les deux créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:D1","text":"Une créature qui contient la raison a priori d’un événement dans une autre lui est supérieure en perfection relativement à cet événement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A1","CH_UCIC_P_42:A2","CH_UCIC_P_42:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:D2","text":"La relation d’action est produite par la relation de fondation rationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:D3","text":"Dire qu’une créature agit sur une autre revient à désigner sa fonction de raison a priori dans ce qui arrive à l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A5","CH_UCIC_P_42:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:D4","text":"La hiérarchie de perfection et l’ordre d’action peuvent être lus selon une même asymétrie explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SD1","text":"L’action entre créatures est reclassée comme une relation d’intelligibilité fondatrice plutôt que comme une interaction décrite indépendamment de la raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2","text":"La perfection devient une grandeur fonctionnelle : une créature est plus parfaite lorsqu’elle explique davantage ce qui arrive dans une autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A1","CH_UCIC_P_42:A2","CH_UCIC_P_42:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SD3","text":"L’ordre causal entre créatures est implicitement organisé comme une hiérarchie de raisons a priori.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une créature puisse être dite agir sans qu’un rapport de raison a priori relie son contenu à l’événement de l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut une conception de l’action comme événement originairement indépendant de toute structure explicative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut que la perfection soit déterminée sans référence à la capacité d’une créature à fonder l’intelligibilité d’un événement extérieur à elle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX1","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une causalité brute, détachée de toute raison préalable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX2","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’une action dont le sens ne serait pas dérivé d’une asymétrie rationnelle entre les créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX3","text":"Le texte rend inadmissible une séparation complète entre hiérarchie de perfection, ordre des raisons et attribution de l’action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS1","text":"Comparabilité des créatures → critère relationnel de perfection → présence d’une raison a priori.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A1","CH_UCIC_P_42:A2","CH_UCIC_P_42:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS2","text":"Raison a priori d’un événement dans une autre créature → fondement explicatif → attribution d’une action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS3","text":"Supériorité explicative → supériorité de perfection → asymétrie d’action entre les créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D1","CH_UCIC_P_42:D2","CH_UCIC_P_42:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AF1","text":"Comparaison des créatures → définition relationnelle de la perfection → raison a priori → fondement de l’événement → attribution de l’action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ME1","text":"La perfection est déplacée du registre d’une qualité isolée vers celui d’une puissance explicative relative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ME2","text":"L’action est reclassée comme effet d’une priorité rationnelle plutôt que comme donnée causale autonome.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ME3","text":"La relation entre les créatures est cartographiée selon une asymétrie allant de la raison contenue à l’événement expliqué.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ME4","text":"L’ordre de la perfection et l’ordre de l’action deviennent deux expressions d’une même hiérarchie explicative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Une créature est dite agir sur une autre lorsqu’elle contient ce qui rend raison a priori de ce qui arrive à celle-ci.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — La relation intercréaturelle est organisée par une asymétrie de fondation rationnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — L’attribution de l’action est recadrée comme une conséquence du mode d’explication plutôt que comme un constat séparé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — La priorité pertinente est rationnelle et a priori, non une priorité temporelle explicitement posée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage de la comparaison de perfection à l’attribution d’action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT2","text":"Le système reste sous-déterminé quant à la nature exacte de ce qui est « trouvé » dans la créature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT3","text":"Le système ne précise pas si la raison a priori est ontologique, logique ou métaphysique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT4","text":"La cohérence interne repose sur l’identification de l’action à une relation de fondation explicative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT5","text":"La principale tension réside dans le passage non explicité entre « rendre raison » et « agir ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : perfection relative → raison a priori → attribution d’action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193559825526Z_7981e51d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 50","source_sha256":"bad5b923a3aced40b00903d0594fe0d536a187cf316e12d65a251d8b7c24626c","sha256":"1a2e3e6cbb7baf2a01fa748417cda9d2b80b3902aef3915df99f7db02e983484","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:35:59.829437+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AS1","text":"The perfection of creatures is differentiated according to their capacity to give an account of what occurs in another creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AS2","text":"This capacity rests on the presence of an a priori reason for the event observed in the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AS3","text":"The explanatory relation is converted into a relation of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AS4","text":"The action attributed to a creature thus derives from a rational priority and not from a causal mechanism described separately.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A1","text":"Creatures can be compared according to degrees of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A2","text":"Perfection is here measured by a determinate relation to another creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A3","text":"A creature is all the more perfect insofar as it contains an a priori reason for what occurs in another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","text":"That which gives an a priori account of an event constitutes its explanatory ground.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A5","text":"The a priori explanatory ground authorizes the attribution of an action to the creature that contains it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:A6","text":"The action of one creature upon another is defined by the relation between its rational content and the event of the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX1","text":"Perfection is not defined here as a quality independent of every relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX2","text":"Action is not grounded in a mere temporal succession between two events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX3","text":"Action is not referred to an explicitly described material force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX4","text":"Explanatory priority is not reduced to an empirical observation of concomitance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:NX5","text":"The text does not posit the reciprocity of action between the two creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:D1","text":"A creature that contains the a priori reason for an event in another is superior to it in perfection relative to that event.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A1","CH_UCIC_P_42:A2","CH_UCIC_P_42:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:D2","text":"The relation of action is produced by the relation of rational grounding.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:D3","text":"To say that one creature acts upon another amounts to designating its function as an a priori reason in what happens to the other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A5","CH_UCIC_P_42:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:D4","text":"The hierarchy of perfection and the order of action can be read according to one and the same explanatory asymmetry.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SD1","text":"Action between creatures is reclassified as a relation of grounding intelligibility rather than as an interaction described independently of reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2","text":"Perfection becomes a functional magnitude: a creature is more perfect when it explains more of what happens in another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A1","CH_UCIC_P_42:A2","CH_UCIC_P_42:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SD3","text":"The causal order between creatures is implicitly organized as a hierarchy of a priori reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX1","text":"The system excludes that a creature can be said to act without a relation of a priori reason connecting its content to the event of the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a conception of action as an event originally independent of every explanatory structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX3","text":"The system excludes that perfection be determined without reference to a creature's capacity to ground the intelligibility of an event external to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX1","text":"The structuring absence is that of a brute causality, detached from every prior reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX2","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of an action whose meaning would not be derived from a rational asymmetry between creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX3","text":"The text renders inadmissible a complete separation between the hierarchy of perfection, the order of reasons, and the attribution of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS1","text":"Comparability of creatures → relational criterion of perfection → presence of an a priori reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A1","CH_UCIC_P_42:A2","CH_UCIC_P_42:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS2","text":"A priori reason for an event in another creature → explanatory ground → attribution of an action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS3","text":"Explanatory superiority → superiority in perfection → asymmetry of action between creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D1","CH_UCIC_P_42:D2","CH_UCIC_P_42:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:AF1","text":"Comparison of creatures → relational definition of perfection → a priori reason → ground of the event → attribution of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ME1","text":"Perfection is shifted from the register of an isolated quality to that of a relative explanatory power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ME2","text":"Action is reclassified as the effect of a rational priority rather than as autonomous causal data.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ME3","text":"The relation between creatures is mapped according to an asymmetry running from the reason contained to the event explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ME4","text":"The order of perfection and the order of action become two expressions of one and the same explanatory hierarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — A creature is said to act upon another when it contains that which gives an a priori account of what happens to the latter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The inter-creature relation is organized by an asymmetry of rational grounding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The attribution of action is reframed as a consequence of the mode of explanation rather than as a separate observation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — The relevant priority is rational and a priori, not an explicitly posited temporal priority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage from the comparison of perfection to the attribution of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT2","text":"The system remains underdetermined as to the exact nature of what is « found » in the creature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT3","text":"The system does not specify whether the a priori reason is ontological, logical, or metaphysical.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence rests on the identification of action with a relation of explanatory grounding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT5","text":"The principal tension lies in the unexplained passage between « rendre raison » and « agir ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: relative perfection → a priori reason → attribution of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_42:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_42@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_42:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 50"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 50","title":"Proposition 50","context":"Chapter 50","original_title":"Proposition 50"},"original_title":"Proposition 50","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 51","order":51,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_43"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_43@R001","sha256":"69088aabac2118e0449093147766c790913686b310580d4d8221c760d2b27544","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS1","text":"Le problème consiste à expliquer la dépendance d’une monade à l’égard d’une autre sans influence physique directe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS2","text":"L’impossibilité d’une action physique sur l’intérieur d’une monade impose un recadrage de la causalité intermonadique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS3","text":"La relation entre monades simples est reconduite à une influence idéale inscrite dans l’ordre des idées divines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS4","text":"Dieu médiatise cette influence en réglant dès l’origine les autres monades relativement à chacune.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS5","text":"La dépendance entre monades devient ainsi réelle sans devenir une interaction physique interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","text":"Les substances simples sont des monades dont l’intériorité ne peut être physiquement pénétrée par une autre monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A2","text":"Une monade créée ne peut exercer d’influence physique sur l’intérieur d’une autre monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","text":"L’influence entre substances simples est idéale plutôt que physique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A4","text":"L’influence idéale ne produit son effet que par l’intervention de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A5","text":"Les idées divines contiennent la règle selon laquelle chaque monade doit être prise en considération dans le réglage des autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A6","text":"Dieu règle les monades dès le commencement des choses en tenant compte de leurs exigences réciproques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX1","text":"La dépendance entre monades n’est pas une transmission physique d’une intériorité à une autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX2","text":"Une monade ne modifie pas directement l’intérieur d’une autre monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX3","text":"L’influence intermonadique ne procède pas d’une causalité autonome des créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX4","text":"La relation entre monades ne repose pas sur une interaction immédiate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX5","text":"Le commencement des choses n’est pas un état dépourvu de réglage divin préalable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:D1","text":"La causalité intermonadique doit être comprise comme une correspondance réglée plutôt que comme un transfert d’action physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:A2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:D2","text":"Dieu constitue la condition médiatrice de tout effet qu’une monade peut avoir relativement à une autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:D3","text":"La dépendance d’une monade à l’égard d’une autre est fondée dans l’organisation divine préalable des monades.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A4","CH_UCIC_P_43:A5","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:D4","text":"La relation entre monades est réelle au niveau de l’ordre divin, mais non physique au niveau de leur intériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1","text":"L’unité du monde monadique ne résulte pas d’une communication interne entre les substances, mais d’une coordination divine antérieure à leurs états relationnels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2","text":"La causalité créée est convertie en dépendance réglée par Dieu plutôt qu’abolie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3","text":"Le rapport entre monades possède une structure temporelle originaire : ses effets sont déterminés par un réglage effectué dès le commencement des choses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A5","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","text":"L’autonomie intérieure des monades et leur dépendance réciproque deviennent compatibles par séparation entre intériorité physique et coordination idéale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une monade puisse être une cause physique transitive de l’état intérieur d’une autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX2","text":"Il exclut que la relation entre monades puisse être expliquée par un contact causal direct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX3","text":"Il exclut que la cohérence du multiple provienne d’une auto-organisation relationnelle des monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX4","text":"Il exclut que l’ordre des effets puisse être séparé d’un réglage divin originaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX1","text":"L’absence structurelle d’un passage physique entre les intériorités rend impossible toute communauté monadique immédiate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX2","text":"La possibilité d’une interaction sans médiation divine est la possibilité forclose autour de laquelle s’organise l’argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX3","text":"Le système ne laisse subsister aucun espace causal autonome entre les monades et Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1","text":"Intériorité monadique inaccessible → impossibilité de l’influence physique directe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS2","text":"Impossibilité de l’influence physique → substitution d’une influence idéale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS3","text":"Influence idéale → médiation divine nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS4","text":"Médiation divine → réglage originaire des monades selon leurs exigences réciproques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5","text":"Réglage originaire → dépendance intermonadique sans transmission physique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AF1","text":"Dépendance entre monades → impossibilité d’une influence physique → influence idéale → médiation divine → réglage initial → dépendance non physique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1","text":"La causalité est reclassée : elle ne désigne plus une pénétration physique de l’intériorité, mais une dépendance produite par coordination divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2","text":"L’opposition entre autonomie monadique et dépendance relationnelle est dissoute par la distinction entre intériorité et ordre idéal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3","text":"Le commencement des choses devient le lieu structural où se fonde la totalité des relations ultérieures entre monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ME4","text":"Dieu est reclassé comme médiateur constitutif de toute relation intermonadique, et non comme intervention extérieure occasionnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT1","text":"Surface — Une monade dépend d’une autre par une influence idéale, non physique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT2","text":"Structural — L’intériorité close des monades exige une coordination externe à leur causalité propre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le problème de l’interaction est recadré en problème de réglage divin des correspondances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La réalité relationnelle des monades est fondée dans un ordre divin originaire qui précède leurs effets réciproques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le passage : clôture intérieure, impossibilité physique, influence idéale et médiation divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT2","text":"La structure conserve le mouvement de l’impossibilité causale vers la coordination divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT3","text":"Le système est intérieurement cohérent à condition de distinguer influence physique, influence idéale et dépendance réglée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT4","text":"La proposition reste sous-déterminée quant au statut exact de la « demande » de la monade dans les idées divines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT5","text":"La tension principale oppose l’absence d’action physique entre monades à l’affirmation d’une influence qui conserve néanmoins un effet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT6","text":"La résolution dépend de la médiation divine et du réglage initial, dont le mécanisme n’est pas davantage explicité dans la proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193620077383Z_66eb5430","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 51","source_sha256":"69088aabac2118e0449093147766c790913686b310580d4d8221c760d2b27544","sha256":"69c0dc6099ae7f3a70ff4667863e56d82a437d3b0efb0e155549f461dd23c3d4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:36:20.081179+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS1","text":"The problem consists in explaining the dependence of one monad on another without direct physical influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS2","text":"The impossibility of physical action upon the interior of a monad requires a reframing of intermonadic causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS3","text":"The relation between simple monads is referred back to an ideal influence inscribed in the order of divine ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS4","text":"God mediates this influence by ordering the other monads from the origin in relation to each one.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AS5","text":"The dependence between monads thus becomes real without becoming an internal physical interaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","text":"Simple substances are monads whose interiority cannot be physically penetrated by another monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A2","text":"A created monad cannot exert physical influence upon the interior of another monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","text":"Influence between simple substances is ideal rather than physical.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A4","text":"Ideal influence produces its effect only through God's intervention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A5","text":"Divine ideas contain the rule according to which each monad must be taken into consideration in the ordering of the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:A6","text":"God orders the monads from the beginning of things, taking account of their reciprocal requirements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX1","text":"Dependence between monads is not a physical transmission from one interiority to another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX2","text":"One monad does not directly modify the interior of another monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX3","text":"Intermonadic influence does not proceed from an autonomous causality of creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX4","text":"The relation between monads does not rest upon an immediate interaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:NX5","text":"The beginning of things is not a state devoid of prior divine ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:D1","text":"Intermonadic causality must be understood as an ordered correspondence rather than as a transfer of physical action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:A2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:D2","text":"God constitutes the mediating condition of every effect that one monad can have in relation to another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:D3","text":"The dependence of one monad on another is grounded in the prior divine organization of the monads.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A4","CH_UCIC_P_43:A5","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:D4","text":"The relation between monads is real at the level of divine order, but not physical at the level of their interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1","text":"The unity of the monadic world does not result from internal communication between substances, but from a divine coordination prior to their relational states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2","text":"Created causality is converted into dependence ordered by God rather than abolished.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3","text":"The relation between monads possesses an original temporal structure: its effects are determined by an ordering carried out from the beginning of things.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A5","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","text":"The inner autonomy of monads and their reciprocal dependence become compatible through the separation between physical interiority and ideal coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that one monad may be a transitive physical cause of the inner state of another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that the relation between monads may be explained by direct causal contact.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX3","text":"It excludes the possibility that the coherence of the multiple may arise from a relational self-organization of monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX4","text":"It excludes the possibility that the order of effects may be separated from an original divine ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX1","text":"The structural absence of a physical passage between interiorities renders any immediate monadic community impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX2","text":"The possibility of an interaction without divine mediation is the foreclosed possibility around which the argument is organized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX3","text":"The system leaves no autonomous causal space between monads and God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1","text":"Inaccessible monadic interiority → impossibility of direct physical influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS2","text":"Impossibility of physical influence → substitution of an ideal influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS3","text":"Ideal influence → necessary divine mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS4","text":"Divine mediation → original ordering of monads according to their reciprocal requirements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5","text":"Original ordering → intermonadic dependence without physical transmission.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:AF1","text":"Dependence between monads → impossibility of physical influence → ideal influence → divine mediation → initial ordering → non-physical dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1","text":"Causality is reclassified: it no longer designates a physical penetration of interiority, but a dependence produced by divine coordination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2","text":"The opposition between monadic autonomy and relational dependence is dissolved by the distinction between interiority and ideal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3","text":"The beginning of things becomes the structural locus in which the totality of subsequent relations between monads is grounded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ME4","text":"God is reclassified as the constitutive mediator of every intermonadic relation, and not as an occasional external intervention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT1","text":"Surface — One monad depends on another through an ideal, not physical, influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT2","text":"Structural — The closed interiority of monads requires coordination external to their own causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The problem of interaction is reframed as a problem of divine ordering of correspondences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The relational reality of monads is grounded in an original divine order that precedes their reciprocal effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage: inner closure, physical impossibility, ideal influence, and divine mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT2","text":"The structure preserves the movement from causal impossibility toward divine coordination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT3","text":"The system is internally coherent provided that physical influence, ideal influence, and ordered dependence are distinguished.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT4","text":"The proposition remains underdetermined as to the exact status of the monad's « demande » in divine ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT5","text":"The principal tension opposes the absence of physical action between monads to the affirmation of an influence that nevertheless retains an effect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT6","text":"The resolution depends on divine mediation and initial ordering, whose mechanism is not further explicated in the proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_43:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_43@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_43:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 51"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 51","title":"Proposition 51","context":"Chapter 51","original_title":"Proposition 51"},"original_title":"Proposition 51","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 52","order":52,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_44"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_44@R001","sha256":"63536e74ed747a79d305a9561c172198e227e7a35585a7bcaa22fe3b81fbc37e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS1","text":"L’argument cherche à déterminer comment des créatures peuvent entretenir des actions et passions mutuelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS2","text":"La relation entre les créatures est recadrée par la comparaison divine de substances simples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS3","text":"Chaque substance contient des raisons qui rendent nécessaire l’accommodement de l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS4","text":"L’activité et la passivité sont définies relativement au point de considération adopté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS5","text":"L’action correspond à la fonction explicative d’une connaissance distincte, tandis que la passion correspond à la dépendance explicative inverse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS6","text":"Le mouvement argumentatif va de la mutualité des rapports à leur différenciation selon la direction de la raison.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","text":"Entre les créatures, les actions et les passions sont mutuelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A2","text":"Les créatures considérées dans cette relation sont des substances simples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A3","text":"Dieu compare les substances simples deux à deux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","text":"La comparaison divine découvre dans chaque substance des raisons qui obligent à accommoder l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","text":"Une substance est active lorsqu’une connaissance distincte en elle sert à rendre raison de ce qui se passe dans une autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A6","text":"Une substance est passive lorsque la raison de ce qui se passe en elle se trouve dans une connaissance distincte située dans une autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A7","text":"L’activité et la passivité dépendent d’un point de considération déterminé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX1","text":"L’activité n’est pas une propriété absolue et isolable d’une substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX2","text":"La passivité n’est pas une propriété absolue et isolable d’une substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX3","text":"L’action entre créatures n’est pas une relation unilatérale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX4","text":"La mutualité ne signifie pas que chaque substance exerce le même rôle sous le même rapport.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX5","text":"La raison d’un événement dans une substance ne se trouve pas nécessairement dans cette substance seule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:D1","text":"Une même substance peut être active sous un rapport et passive sous un autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6","CH_UCIC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:D2","text":"La direction de l’action ou de la passion est déterminée par la localisation de la raison explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:D3","text":"La mutualité des relations créées n’abolit pas la distinction entre ce qui explique et ce qui est expliqué.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:D4","text":"L’accommodement entre substances constitue la condition de leur détermination réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SD1","text":"Les rapports entre substances sont constitués par une répartition relationnelle des fonctions explicatives plutôt que par une opposition fixe entre agents et patients.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SD2","text":"L’ordre des créatures apparaît comme un système de correspondances où chaque substance peut simultanément contribuer à l’explication d’un autre événement et recevoir l’explication de son propre événement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SD3","text":"La causalité entre créatures est reconduite vers une structure d’intelligibilité réglée par l’accommodement divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A3","CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut un modèle dans lequel l’action et la passion seraient des statuts intrinsèques indépendants de toute comparaison.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut une interaction conçue comme transfert simple d’une force d’une substance vers une autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une explication de l’événement qui ne ferait intervenir qu’une substance prise isolément.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut que la réciprocité relationnelle suffise à déterminer la fonction active ou passive sans référence à la raison distinctement connue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SNX1","text":"Le texte forclôt l’existence d’un point de vue causal unique permettant de distribuer une fois pour toutes les substances entre agents et patients.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SNX2","text":"Le texte rend indisponible une conception de la relation où la mutualité serait une symétrie indifférenciée plutôt qu’une réciprocité structurée par des raisons distinctes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SNX3","text":"L’ordre des créatures ne peut être pensé comme une juxtaposition de substances autosuffisantes et sans accommodation réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS1","text":"Substances simples comparées → découverte de raisons corrélatives dans chacune.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS2","text":"Raisons corrélatives → obligation divine d’accommoder chaque substance à l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS3","text":"Accommodement réciproque → constitution d’actions et de passions mutuelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS4","text":"Localisation de la raison distinctement connue → attribution relative de l’activité ou de la passivité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS5","text":"Variation du point de considération → réversibilité fonctionnelle des positions active et passive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AF1","text":"Mutualité des actions et passions → comparaison divine des substances simples → accommodement réciproque → distribution relationnelle de l’activité et de la passivité → intelligibilité croisée des événements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ME1","text":"L’opposition agent-patient est reclassée comme une différence de fonction explicative selon le rapport considéré.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ME2","text":"La relation entre substances est cartographiée comme un réseau de raisons croisées plutôt que comme une succession de causalités unidirectionnelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ME3","text":"La mutualité cesse de désigner une égalité indifférenciée et devient une structure articulant réciprocité et asymétrie explicative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ME4","text":"L’accommodement divin devient le principe de liaison entre substances simples et événements corrélés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Les créatures exercent et subissent mutuellement des actions et des passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Les positions active et passive résultent de la localisation comparative des raisons explicatives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Le texte déplace l’analyse de la question « qui agit ? » vers la question « dans quelle substance se trouve la raison distinctement connue de l’événement ? ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Les substances simples sont coordonnées par un ordre d’accommodement qui détermine la correspondance de leurs événements sans abolir leur distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage de la mutualité créaturelle à la distinction entre action et passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT2","text":"La reconstruction préserve le rôle générateur de la comparaison divine et de l’accommodement réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT3","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si l’activité et la passivité sont traitées comme des prédicats relatifs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT4","text":"Le texte laisse sous-déterminé le statut exact des « raisons » et le mécanisme précis par lequel Dieu impose l’accommodement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT5","text":"La tension principale oppose la mutualité des actions et passions à l’asymétrie de la raison explicative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction conserve le mouvement réel du texte : mutualité → accommodement divin → détermination relative de l’activité et de la passivité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193634694323Z_8725ac19","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 52","source_sha256":"63536e74ed747a79d305a9561c172198e227e7a35585a7bcaa22fe3b81fbc37e","sha256":"15d1f9f43185688690ffdba9147156e148e0a9298fb9bf1ad790f8c9e4528a46","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:36:34.701023+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS1","text":"The argument seeks to determine how creatures can maintain mutual actions and passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS2","text":"The relation between creatures is reframed through the divine comparison of simple substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS3","text":"Each substance contains reasons that make the accommodation of the other necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS4","text":"Activity and passivity are defined relative to the adopted point of consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS5","text":"Action corresponds to the explanatory function of a distinct knowledge, whereas passion corresponds to the inverse explanatory dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AS6","text":"The argumentative movement proceeds from the mutuality of relations to their differentiation according to the direction of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","text":"Among creatures, actions and passions are mutual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A2","text":"The creatures considered in this relation are simple substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A3","text":"God compares simple substances two by two.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","text":"The divine comparison discovers in each substance reasons that oblige it to accommodate the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","text":"A substance is active when a distinct knowledge in it serves to account for what occurs in another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A6","text":"A substance is passive when the reason for what occurs in it is found in a distinct knowledge situated in another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:A7","text":"Activity and passivity depend on a determinate point of consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX1","text":"Activity is not an absolute and isolable property of a substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX2","text":"Passivity is not an absolute and isolable property of a substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX3","text":"Action among creatures is not a unilateral relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX4","text":"Mutuality does not mean that each substance exercises the same role under the same respect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:NX5","text":"The reason for an event in a substance is not necessarily found in that substance alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:D1","text":"The same substance can be active in one respect and passive in another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6","CH_UCIC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:D2","text":"The direction of action or passion is determined by the location of the explanatory reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:D3","text":"The mutuality of created relations does not abolish the distinction between what explains and what is explained.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:D4","text":"Accommodation between substances constitutes the condition of their reciprocal determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SD1","text":"Relations between substances are constituted by a relational distribution of explanatory functions rather than by a fixed opposition between agents and patients.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SD2","text":"The order of creatures appears as a system of correspondences in which each substance can simultaneously contribute to the explanation of another event and receive the explanation of its own event.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SD3","text":"Causality among creatures is redirected toward a structure of intelligibility governed by divine accommodation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A3","CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX1","text":"The system excludes a model in which action and passion would be intrinsic statuses independent of any comparison.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX2","text":"The system excludes an interaction conceived as the simple transfer of a force from one substance to another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX3","text":"The system excludes an explanation of the event involving only a substance taken in isolation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the possibility that relational reciprocity suffices to determine the active or passive function without reference to the distinctly known reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SNX1","text":"The text forecloses the existence of a single causal point of view allowing substances to be distributed once and for all between agents and patients.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SNX2","text":"The text renders unavailable a conception of relation in which mutuality would be an undifferentiated symmetry rather than a reciprocity structured by distinct reasons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:SNX3","text":"The order of creatures cannot be conceived as a juxtaposition of self-sufficient substances without reciprocal accommodation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS1","text":"Simple substances compared → discovery of correlative reasons in each.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS2","text":"Correlative reasons → divine obligation to accommodate each substance to the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS3","text":"Reciprocal accommodation → constitution of mutual actions and passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS4","text":"Location of the distinctly known reason → relative attribution of activity or passivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS5","text":"Variation of the point of consideration → functional reversibility of active and passive positions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:AF1","text":"Mutuality of actions and passions → divine comparison of simple substances → reciprocal accommodation → relational distribution of activity and passivity → crosswise intelligibility of events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ME1","text":"The agent-patient opposition is reclassified as a difference in explanatory function according to the relation considered.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ME2","text":"The relation between substances is mapped as a network of intersecting reasons rather than as a succession of unidirectional causalities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ME3","text":"Mutuality ceases to designate an undifferentiated equality and becomes a structure articulating reciprocity and explanatory asymmetry.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ME4","text":"Divine accommodation becomes the principle linking simple substances and correlated events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Creatures mutually perform and undergo actions and passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Active and passive positions result from the comparative location of explanatory reasons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The text shifts the analysis from the question “who acts?” to the question “in which substance is the distinctly known reason for the event found?”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Simple substances are coordinated by an order of accommodation that determines the correspondence of their events without abolishing their distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage from creaturely mutuality to the distinction between action and passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction preserves the generative role of divine comparison and reciprocal accommodation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent if activity and passivity are treated as relative predicates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT4","text":"The text leaves underdetermined the exact status of the “reasons” and the precise mechanism by which God imposes accommodation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT5","text":"The principal tension opposes the mutuality of actions and passions to the asymmetry of explanatory reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the text's actual movement: mutuality → divine accommodation → relative determination of activity and passivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_44:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_44@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_44:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 52"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 52","title":"Proposition 52","context":"Chapter 52","original_title":"Proposition 52"},"original_title":"Proposition 52","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 53","order":53,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_45"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_45@R001","sha256":"27fb26ef016b6466224096aa453fa783a5cff49b3c2f8623fc87fd106f95bae5","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AS1","text":"La pluralité infinie des univers possibles dans les Idées de Dieu ouvre un champ de possibilités concurrentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AS2","text":"L’existence actuelle est limitée à un seul univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AS3","text":"Cette sélection exclusive ne peut être dépourvue de raison suffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AS4","text":"La raison suffisante détermine Dieu à choisir un univers plutôt qu’un autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","text":"Les Idées de Dieu contiennent une infinité d’univers possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A2","text":"Un seul univers peut exister actuellement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A3","text":"L’existence d’un univers plutôt que d’un autre constitue un choix.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A4","text":"Tout choix réel requiert une raison suffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A5","text":"Une raison suffisante détermine le choix divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A6","text":"Dieu choisit un univers déterminé parmi les univers possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX1","text":"Tous les univers conçus comme possibles ne deviennent pas réels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX2","text":"Plusieurs univers ne peuvent pas exister simultanément comme univers actuels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX3","text":"Le choix divin n’est pas sans raison suffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX4","text":"Dieu ne choisit pas entre les univers possibles par indifférence absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX5","text":"L’univers actuel n’est pas posé comme une actualisation sans principe de sélection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:D1","text":"La distinction entre possibilité et existence actuelle devient nécessaire pour expliquer la sélection d’un seul univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:D2","text":"L’existence de l’univers actuel appelle une explication qui porte sur sa préférence relativement aux autres possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A2","CH_UCIC_P_45:A3","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:D3","text":"La raison suffisante fonctionne comme principe de détermination du passage d’un ensemble de possibles à une réalité unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5","CH_UCIC_P_45:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:D4","text":"La contingence du choix n’implique pas l’absence de détermination, puisque le choix est rapporté à une raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A3","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SD1","text":"La multiplicité des possibles est subordonnée à une logique d’actualisation unitaire : l’infinité idéelle ne produit pas une infinité existentielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SD2","text":"L’existence de l’univers actuel est intégrée dans une structure de sélection rationnelle plutôt que dans une décision arbitraire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A3","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SD3","text":"La raison suffisante est le mécanisme qui relie l’espace ontologique des possibles à l’ordre effectif du monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5","CH_UCIC_P_45:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SD4","text":"L’unicité du monde actuel exige une hiérarchisation implicite des possibilités, même si le critère précis de cette hiérarchisation demeure indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A2","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX1","text":"Le réel n’est pas l’ensemble exhaustif des possibilités contenues dans les Idées de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX2","text":"L’actualisation ne résulte pas d’une coexistence indifférenciée des univers possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX3","text":"Le choix divin n’est pas un événement premier dépourvu d’explication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX4","text":"La différence entre l’univers actuel et les autres possibles n’est pas laissée au pur hasard.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX5","text":"La possibilité logique ou idéelle ne suffit pas à produire l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’un fait ultime absolument brut dans l’origine de l’univers actuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX2","text":"Est exclue l’équivalence ontologique entre tous les univers possibles : un seul est actualisé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX3","text":"Est rendue inadmissible une volonté divine entièrement indéterminée par toute raison antérieure au choix.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS1","text":"Infinité des possibilités idéelles → restriction de l’actualité à un seul univers → nécessité d’expliquer la préférence → introduction de la raison suffisante → détermination du choix divin → actualisation d’un univers plutôt qu’un autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS2","text":"Possibles multiples + actualité unique → disjonction à résoudre → choix divin → raison suffisante comme opérateur de sélection → monde actuel déterminé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS3","text":"La différence entre possible et actuel produit la question du choix ; la question du choix produit l’exigence d’une raison ; l’exigence d’une raison produit la détermination divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AF1","text":"Infinité des univers possibles → unicité de l’univers existant → problème de la sélection → exigence d’une raison suffisante → détermination du choix divin → actualisation d’un univers particulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ME1","text":"Le champ ontologique est scindé entre une pluralité infinie de possibles et une actualité strictement unitaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ME2","text":"La question de l’existence est déplacée vers la question comparative du choix d’un univers plutôt qu’un autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ME3","text":"L’alternative entre arbitraire et nécessité est reconfigurée en choix déterminé par une raison suffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ME4","text":"La raison suffisante devient le principe de liaison entre contenu idéel, décision divine et réalité effective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT1","text":"Surface — Dieu choisit un univers parmi une infinité d’univers possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT2","text":"Structural — La pluralité des possibilités et l’unicité de l’existence exigent un mécanisme de sélection rationnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’explication de l’univers doit porter sur le principe de préférence qui rend compte de son actualisation exclusive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Le possible précède logiquement l’actuel, tandis que la raison suffisante explique le passage de la possibilité à l’existence déterminée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement de la pluralité possible vers l’actualité unique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la raison suffisante est admise comme condition de tout choix réel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT3","text":"Le texte sous-détermine la nature exacte de la raison qui motive la préférence divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT4","text":"Le rapport précis entre possibilité, perfection et sélection n’est pas développé dans l’énoncé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT5","text":"La tension principale subsiste entre la contingence apparente du choix parmi plusieurs possibles et la détermination imposée par la raison suffisante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : pluralité idéelle → sélection exclusive → exigence explicative → détermination divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193647087972Z_274ab424","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 53","source_sha256":"27fb26ef016b6466224096aa453fa783a5cff49b3c2f8623fc87fd106f95bae5","sha256":"0bd51a72080656dc1b635a744e73aaf321782d006d70c96d9eb1dfeccbf6a43f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:36:47.091045+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AS1","text":"The infinite plurality of possible universes in God's Ideas opens a field of competing possibilities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AS2","text":"Actual existence is limited to a single universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AS3","text":"This exclusive selection cannot be devoid of sufficient reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AS4","text":"Sufficient reason determines God to choose one universe rather than another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","text":"God's Ideas contain an infinity of possible universes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A2","text":"Only one universe can exist actually.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A3","text":"The existence of one universe rather than another constitutes a choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A4","text":"Every real choice requires a sufficient reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A5","text":"A sufficient reason determines the divine choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:A6","text":"God chooses a determinate universe among possible universes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX1","text":"Not all universes conceived as possible become real.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX2","text":"Several universes cannot exist simultaneously as actual universes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX3","text":"The divine choice is not without sufficient reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX4","text":"God does not choose among possible universes through absolute indifference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:NX5","text":"The actual universe is not posited as an actualization without a principle of selection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:D1","text":"The distinction between possibility and actual existence becomes necessary in order to explain the selection of a single universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:D2","text":"The existence of the actual universe calls for an explanation concerning its preference relative to the other possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A2","CH_UCIC_P_45:A3","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:D3","text":"Sufficient reason functions as a principle determining the passage from a set of possibles to a single reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5","CH_UCIC_P_45:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:D4","text":"The contingency of the choice does not imply the absence of determination, since the choice is referred to a sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A3","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SD1","text":"The multiplicity of possibles is subordinated to a logic of unitary actualization: ideal infinity does not produce existential infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SD2","text":"The existence of the actual universe is integrated into a structure of rational selection rather than into an arbitrary decision.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A3","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SD3","text":"Sufficient reason is the mechanism that connects the ontological space of possibles to the effective order of the world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5","CH_UCIC_P_45:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SD4","text":"The uniqueness of the actual world requires an implicit hierarchy of possibilities, even if the precise criterion of this hierarchy remains indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A2","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX1","text":"The real is not the exhaustive set of possibilities contained in God's Ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX2","text":"Actualization does not result from an undifferentiated coexistence of possible universes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX3","text":"The divine choice is not a primary event devoid of explanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX4","text":"The difference between the actual universe and the other possibles is not left to pure chance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX5","text":"Logical or ideal possibility is not sufficient to produce existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1","text":"The possibility of an absolutely brute ultimate fact at the origin of the actual universe is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX2","text":"The ontological equivalence of all possible universes is excluded: only one is actualized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX3","text":"A divine will wholly undetermined by any reason prior to the choice is rendered inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS1","text":"Infinity of ideal possibilities → restriction of actuality to a single universe → necessity of explaining the preference → introduction of sufficient reason → determination of the divine choice → actualization of one universe rather than another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS2","text":"Multiple possibles + unique actuality → disjunction to be resolved → divine choice → sufficient reason as operator of selection → determinate actual world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS3","text":"The difference between possible and actual gives rise to the question of choice; the question of choice gives rise to the requirement of a reason; the requirement of a reason gives rise to divine determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:AF1","text":"Infinity of possible universes → uniqueness of the existing universe → problem of selection → requirement of a sufficient reason → determination of the divine choice → actualization of a particular universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ME1","text":"The ontological field is divided between an infinite plurality of possibles and a strictly unitary actuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ME2","text":"The question of existence is shifted toward the comparative question of the choice of one universe rather than another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ME3","text":"The alternative between arbitrariness and necessity is reconfigured as a choice determined by a sufficient reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ME4","text":"Sufficient reason becomes the principle linking ideal content, divine decision, and effective reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT1","text":"Surface — God chooses one universe among an infinity of possible universes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT2","text":"Structural — The plurality of possibilities and the uniqueness of existence require a mechanism of rational selection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The explanation of the universe must concern the principle of preference that accounts for its exclusive actualization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The possible logically precedes the actual, while sufficient reason explains the passage from possibility to determinate existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from possible plurality toward unique actuality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if sufficient reason is admitted as the condition of every real choice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT3","text":"The text underdetermines the exact nature of the reason motivating the divine preference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT4","text":"The precise relation between possibility, perfection, and selection is not developed in the statement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT5","text":"The principal tension remains between the apparent contingency of the choice among several possibles and the determination imposed by sufficient reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the real movement: ideal plurality → exclusive selection → explanatory requirement → divine determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_45:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_45@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_45:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 53"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 53","title":"Proposition 53","context":"Chapter 53","original_title":"Proposition 53"},"original_title":"Proposition 53","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 54","order":54,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_46"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_46@R001","sha256":"61e732d6dc096ec65ddaccfe97935ed19e544b2797855a801071126e41f72237","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS1","text":"Le texte cherche la raison de l’existence plutôt que l’existence brute des Mondes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS2","text":"La raison est recadrée comme convenance entre les Mondes possibles et les degrés de perfection qu’ils contiennent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS3","text":"La perfection n’est pas uniforme : elle comporte des degrés mesurables ou comparables.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS4","text":"Tout possible possède un droit tendanciel à l’existence, mais ce droit varie selon la perfection enveloppée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS5","text":"L’argument déploie ainsi une métaphysique de la sélection : possible → perfection graduée → prétention proportionnelle à l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A1","text":"Il existe une pluralité de Mondes possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","text":"Chaque possible enveloppe un certain degré de perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A3","text":"Les degrés de perfection sont différenciables.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A4","text":"La raison de l’existence des Mondes réside dans leur convenance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","text":"Chaque possible a droit de prétendre à l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A6","text":"Le droit de prétendre à l’existence est proportionnel au degré de perfection enveloppé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A7","text":"La convenance constitue le principe de détermination entre les possibilités concurrentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX1","text":"La raison de l’existence ne se trouve pas hors de la convenance des Mondes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX2","text":"L’existence n’est pas attribuée uniformément à tous les possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX3","text":"Un possible ne possède pas un droit absolu ou indépendant de sa perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX4","text":"La perfection n’est pas une propriété indifférenciée dépourvue de degrés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX5","text":"L’existence des Mondes n’est pas présentée comme dépourvue de principe de sélection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:D1","text":"Les possibles sont hiérarchisés selon les degrés de perfection qu’ils enveloppent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A3","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:D2","text":"La convenance transforme la pluralité des possibles en problème de détermination ordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A1","CH_UCIC_P_46:A4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:D3","text":"Le droit à l’existence est gradué plutôt que simplement affirmé ou refusé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:D4","text":"La perfection fournit le critère interne selon lequel une possibilité peut prétendre à l’actualisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SD1","text":"L’ontologie des Mondes devient une ontologie sélective où l’actualité se règle par une hiérarchie de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A1","CH_UCIC_P_46:A3","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6","CH_UCIC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SD2","text":"La convenance relie le principe explicatif de l’existence à une comparaison interne entre les possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6","CH_UCIC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SD3","text":"L’existence apparaît comme une prétention réglée par la perfection, et non comme une propriété première de tout possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une possibilité puisse fonder sa prétention à l’existence sans médiation par la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX2","text":"Il exclut une égalité ontologique complète entre tous les possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une explication de l’existence fondée sur une décision sans critère interne de convenance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX4","text":"Il exclut que le possible et l’existant soient séparés par une rupture sans continuité graduelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX1","text":"L’absence d’une existence indifférenciée de tous les possibles rend nécessaire une hiérarchie de perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX2","text":"La possibilité d’un monde sans principe de sélection est structurellement forclose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX3","text":"Ce qui est rendu inadmissible est une existence sans convenance, sans degré et sans proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS1","text":"Pluralité des possibles → attribution à chaque possible d’un degré de perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS2","text":"Différenciation des degrés → comparaison des prétentions à l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS3","text":"Comparaison des prétentions → détermination par convenance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS4","text":"Convenance + perfection graduée → existence conçue comme actualisation proportionnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS5","text":"Actualisation proportionnelle → exclusion de l’existence indifférente ou sans principe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF1","text":"Question de la raison de l’existence → déplacement vers la convenance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF2","text":"Convenance → prise en compte des degrés de perfection contenus dans les Mondes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF3","text":"Degrés de perfection → hiérarchisation des possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF4","text":"Hiérarchisation → droit gradué de prétendre à l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF5","text":"Droit proportionnel → principe de sélection métaphysique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ME1","text":"L’opposition possible/existant est reclassée en continuum de prétention proportionnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ME2","text":"La perfection devient un opérateur de classement ontologique plutôt qu’un simple attribut.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ME3","text":"La raison de l’existence est déplacée d’une cause extérieure vers une relation de convenance entre possibilités.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ME4","text":"La pluralité des Mondes est transformée en espace hiérarchisé de possibilités.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ALT1","text":"Surface — La raison de l’existence des Mondes est rapportée à leur convenance et à leur perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ALT2","text":"Structural — Les possibles sont organisés par une relation graduée entre perfection et droit à l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ALT3","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’existence est conçue comme actualisation sélective de possibilités déjà différenciées par leur perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement allant de la pluralité des possibles à leur sélection proportionnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la perfection peut être graduée et comparée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT3","text":"La notion de convenance reste sous-déterminée : son contenu et son mode de comparaison ne sont pas explicités.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT4","text":"Le rapport exact entre droit de prétendre à l’existence et existence effectivement réalisée demeure elliptique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT5","text":"La force du système repose sur l’identification de la perfection comme critère de sélection des possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : raison de l’existence → convenance → degrés de perfection → prétention proportionnelle à l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193702553960Z_ebc63b57","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 54","source_sha256":"61e732d6dc096ec65ddaccfe97935ed19e544b2797855a801071126e41f72237","sha256":"5849aff755d0a4b4a564db56987254a688f4747533bd1420f00443eccbf00ed3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:37:02.555314+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS1","text":"The text seeks the reason for existence rather than the brute existence of Worlds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS2","text":"Reason is reframed as fitness between possible Worlds and the degrees of perfection they contain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS3","text":"Perfection is not uniform: it comprises measurable or comparable degrees.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS4","text":"Every possible has a tendential right to existence, but this right varies according to the perfection it involves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AS5","text":"The argument thus unfolds a metaphysics of selection: possible → graduated perfection → proportional claim to existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A1","text":"There exists a plurality of possible Worlds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","text":"Each possible involves a certain degree of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A3","text":"Degrees of perfection are differentiable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A4","text":"The reason for the existence of Worlds lies in their fitness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","text":"Each possible has the right to claim existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A6","text":"The right to claim existence is proportional to the degree of perfection involved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:A7","text":"Fitness constitutes the principle of determination among competing possibilities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX1","text":"The reason for existence is not found outside the fitness of Worlds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX2","text":"Existence is not attributed uniformly to all possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX3","text":"A possible does not possess a right that is absolute or independent of its perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX4","text":"Perfection is not an undifferentiated property devoid of degrees.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:NX5","text":"The existence of Worlds is not presented as devoid of a principle of selection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:D1","text":"Possibles are hierarchized according to the degrees of perfection they involve.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A3","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:D2","text":"Fitness transforms the plurality of possibles into a problem of ordered determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A1","CH_UCIC_P_46:A4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:D3","text":"The right to existence is graduated rather than simply affirmed or denied.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:D4","text":"Perfection provides the internal criterion by which a possibility can lay claim to actualization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SD1","text":"The ontology of Worlds becomes a selective ontology in which actuality is governed by a hierarchy of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A1","CH_UCIC_P_46:A3","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6","CH_UCIC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SD2","text":"Fitness connects the explanatory principle of existence to an internal comparison among possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6","CH_UCIC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SD3","text":"Existence appears as a claim governed by perfection, rather than as a primary property of every possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a possibility may ground its claim to existence without mediation through perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX2","text":"It excludes complete ontological equality among all possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX3","text":"It excludes an explanation of existence based on a decision without an internal criterion of fitness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX4","text":"It excludes the possibility that the possible and the existent are separated by a rupture without graduated continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX1","text":"The absence of an undifferentiated existence of all possibles makes a hierarchy of perfection necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a world without a principle of selection is structurally foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX3","text":"What is rendered inadmissible is an existence without fitness, without degree, and without proportion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS1","text":"Plurality of possibles → attribution to each possible of a degree of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS2","text":"Differentiation of degrees → comparison of claims to existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS3","text":"Comparison of claims → determination by fitness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS4","text":"Fitness + graduated perfection → existence conceived as proportional actualization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS5","text":"Proportional actualization → exclusion of indifferent or unprincipled existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF1","text":"Question of the reason for existence → shift toward fitness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF2","text":"Fitness → consideration of the degrees of perfection contained in Worlds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF3","text":"Degrees of perfection → hierarchization of possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF4","text":"Hierarchization → graduated right to claim existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:AF5","text":"Proportional right → principle of metaphysical selection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ME1","text":"The possible/existent opposition is reclassified as a continuum of proportional claim.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ME2","text":"Perfection becomes an operator of ontological classification rather than a simple attribute.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ME3","text":"The reason for existence is shifted from an external cause toward a relation of fitness between possibilities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ME4","text":"The plurality of Worlds is transformed into a hierarchized space of possibilities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ALT1","text":"Surface — The reason for the existence of Worlds is referred to their fitness and their perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ALT2","text":"Structural — Possibles are organized by a graduated relation between perfection and the right to existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:ALT3","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Existence is conceived as the selective actualization of possibilities already differentiated by their perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the plurality of possibles to their proportional selection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if perfection can be graduated and compared.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT3","text":"The notion of fitness remains underdetermined: its content and its mode of comparison are not made explicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT4","text":"The exact relation between the right to claim existence and existence actually realized remains elliptical.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT5","text":"The force of the system rests on the identification of perfection as the criterion for selecting possibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: reason for existence → fitness → degrees of perfection → proportional claim to existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_46:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_46@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_46:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 54"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 54","title":"Proposition 54","context":"Chapter 54","original_title":"Proposition 54"},"original_title":"Proposition 54","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 55","order":55,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_47"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_47@R001","sha256":"928feb4968b5c68adcdaf0ed5614f9507bc692f7f12ad66095b70db99d40eb08","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AS1","text":"L’existence du Meilleur appelle une cause intelligible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AS2","text":"Cette cause est recadrée comme une articulation interne des facultés divines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AS3","text":"La sagesse détermine la connaissance, la bonté la préférence et la puissance la réalisation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AS4","text":"L’argument progresse de la représentation du meilleur à son choix, puis de son choix à son existence produite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","text":"Le Meilleur constitue le contenu ou le terme de la causalité examinée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","text":"La sagesse divine fait connaître le Meilleur à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","text":"La bonté divine fait choisir le Meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A4","text":"La puissance divine fait produire le Meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A5","text":"Connaître, choisir et produire sont trois fonctions distinctes dans l’engendrement de l’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A6","text":"L’existence du Meilleur résulte de la coordination de ces trois fonctions divines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX1","text":"La sagesse n’est pas présentée comme la faculté qui produit directement le Meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX2","text":"La bonté n’est pas présentée comme la faculté qui connaît le Meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX3","text":"La puissance n’est pas présentée comme la faculté qui détermine seule le choix du Meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX4","text":"La production n’est pas séparée de la connaissance et du choix qui la précèdent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX5","text":"L’existence du Meilleur n’est pas attribuée à une causalité indifférenciée de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:D1","text":"L’objet produit doit être préalablement intelligible comme Meilleur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:D2","text":"La production du Meilleur est orientée par une sélection axiologique plutôt que par la seule capacité d’agir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:D3","text":"La connaissance du Meilleur ne suffit pas à son existence ; elle doit être relayée par le choix et la puissance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:D4","text":"La bonté assure la transition entre le meilleur connu et le meilleur voulu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1","text":"La causalité divine est structurée comme une chaîne normative complète : intelligibilité du meilleur, préférence du meilleur, effectuation du meilleur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4","CH_UCIC_P_47:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SD2","text":"L’existence du meilleur est rendue compatible avec une production intentionnelle sans être réduite à une décision arbitraire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3","text":"Les attributs divins forment un système de causalité différenciée plutôt qu’une série de propriétés juxtaposées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4","CH_UCIC_P_47:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une puissance sans orientation rationnelle suffise à expliquer l’existence du Meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’un choix divin soit intelligible sans un objet préalablement connu comme meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une disjonction entre perfection divine et production du monde ou de l’ordre meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut une causalité extérieure qui déterminerait le contenu du Meilleur indépendamment de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX1","text":"L’existence du Meilleur ne peut être expliquée par une force aveugle ou par une préférence sans fondement cognitif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX2","text":"La possibilité d’un meilleur connu mais non choisi, ou choisi mais non produit, est structurellement neutralisée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX3","text":"L’absence d’un écart entre sagesse, bonté et puissance soutient l’unité implicite de la causalité divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS1","text":"Connaissance du Meilleur → orientation par la bonté → choix du Meilleur → actualisation par la puissance → existence du Meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS2","text":"La sagesse fournit le contenu intelligible ; la bonté fournit la détermination préférentielle ; la puissance fournit l’effectivité causale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS3","text":"La cause de l’existence est produite par l’intégration successive de représentation, de volonté et d’effectuation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AF1","text":"Existence du Meilleur → recherche de sa cause → distinction des facultés divines → connaissance → choix → production → existence effectivement fondée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ME1","text":"La causalité divine est reclassée en trois opérations irréductibles : connaître, vouloir et produire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ME2","text":"La production du meilleur est distinguée de la simple possibilité de produire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ME3","text":"Le rapport entre raison, valeur et puissance devient une structure causale ordonnée plutôt qu’une opposition entre nécessité et arbitraire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Le texte attribue l’existence du Meilleur à la sagesse, à la bonté et à la puissance divines selon trois fonctions distinctes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — L’existence est engendrée par l’enchaînement connaissance–choix–production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — L’argument neutralise simultanément l’explication par la force seule et celle par la volonté non fondée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — La structure implique une priorité logique de la connaissance, une médiation de la bonté et une actualisation finale par la puissance, sans établir nécessairement un ordre temporel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire la chaîne fondamentale de l’argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si les trois fonctions divines sont distinguées sans être séparées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT3","text":"Le statut exact du Meilleur reste sous-déterminé : idéal connu, objet choisi ou réalité produite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT4","text":"Le texte ne précise pas si la séquence connaissance–choix–production est temporelle, logique ou seulement conceptuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : intelligibilité du meilleur → préférence du meilleur → effectuation du meilleur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193715088882Z_ec93c0ab","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 55","source_sha256":"928feb4968b5c68adcdaf0ed5614f9507bc692f7f12ad66095b70db99d40eb08","sha256":"1b2e8a669200ed49b56aa6200d9ab410801805ed3f526f493c72d30d97180a65","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:37:15.092617+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AS1","text":"The existence of the Best calls for an intelligible cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AS2","text":"This cause is reframed as an internal articulation of the divine faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AS3","text":"Wisdom determines knowledge, goodness preference, and power realization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AS4","text":"The argument proceeds from the representation of the best to its choice, then from its choice to its produced existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","text":"The Best constitutes the content or the term of the causality under examination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","text":"Divine wisdom makes the Best known to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","text":"Divine goodness makes the Best chosen.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A4","text":"Divine power brings the Best into being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A5","text":"Knowing, choosing, and producing are three distinct functions in the generation of existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:A6","text":"The existence of the Best results from the coordination of these three divine functions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX1","text":"Wisdom is not presented as the faculty that directly produces the Best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX2","text":"Goodness is not presented as the faculty that knows the Best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX3","text":"Power is not presented as the faculty that alone determines the choice of the Best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX4","text":"Production is not separated from the knowledge and choice that precede it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:NX5","text":"The existence of the Best is not attributed to an undifferentiated causality of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:D1","text":"The produced object must first be intelligible as Best.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:D2","text":"The production of the Best is guided by an axiological selection rather than by the mere capacity to act.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:D3","text":"Knowledge of the Best does not suffice for its existence; it must be relayed by choice and power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:D4","text":"Goodness ensures the transition between the best known and the best willed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1","text":"Divine causality is structured as a complete normative chain: intelligibility of the best, preference for the best, actualization of the best.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4","CH_UCIC_P_47:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SD2","text":"The existence of the best is made compatible with intentional production without being reduced to an arbitrary decision.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3","text":"The divine attributes form a system of differentiated causality rather than a series of juxtaposed properties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4","CH_UCIC_P_47:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that power without rational orientation suffices to explain the existence of the Best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a divine choice is intelligible without an object previously known as better.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a disjunction between divine perfection and the production of the world or of the better order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX4","text":"The system excludes an external causality that would determine the content of the Best independently of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX1","text":"The existence of the Best cannot be explained by a blind force or by a preference without cognitive grounding.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a best known but not chosen, or chosen but not produced, is structurally neutralized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX3","text":"The absence of a gap between wisdom, goodness, and power supports the implicit unity of divine causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS1","text":"Knowledge of the Best → orientation by goodness → choice of the Best → actualization by power → existence of the Best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS2","text":"Wisdom provides the intelligible content; goodness provides the preferential determination; power provides causal efficacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS3","text":"The cause of existence is produced through the successive integration of representation, will, and actualization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:AF1","text":"Existence of the Best → search for its cause → distinction of divine faculties → knowledge → choice → production → effectively grounded existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ME1","text":"Divine causality is reclassified into three irreducible operations: knowing, willing, and producing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ME2","text":"The production of the best is distinguished from the mere possibility of producing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ME3","text":"The relation between reason, value, and power becomes an ordered causal structure rather than an opposition between necessity and arbitrariness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — The text attributes the existence of the Best to divine wisdom, goodness, and power according to three distinct functions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Existence is generated by the sequence knowledge–choice–production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The argument simultaneously neutralizes explanation by force alone and that by unfounded will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — The structure entails a logical priority of knowledge, a mediation of goodness, and a final actualization by power, without necessarily establishing a temporal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the fundamental chain of the argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if the three divine functions are distinguished without being separated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT3","text":"The exact status of the Best remains underdetermined: known ideal, chosen object, or produced reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT4","text":"The text does not specify whether the sequence knowledge–choice–production is temporal, logical, or merely conceptual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the real movement: intelligibility of the best → preference for the best → actualization of the best.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_47:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_47@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_47:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 55"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 55","title":"Proposition 55","context":"Chapter 55","original_title":"Proposition 55"},"original_title":"Proposition 55","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 56","order":56,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_48"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_48@R001","sha256":"c6b2d9d1e4fa298fc64a4c6122c1e6509b93d2f3e5d1fc13269cc7fd2ffada5e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AS1","text":"La liaison universelle entre les choses créées rend chaque substance solidaire de toutes les autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AS2","text":"Cette solidarité est recadrée comme un système de rapports exprimés par chaque substance simple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AS3","text":"L’expression de toutes les autres substances constitue la propriété générative de la substance simple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AS4","text":"La substance simple est ainsi déterminée comme miroir vivant et perpétuel de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","text":"Toutes les choses créées sont liées les unes aux autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A2","text":"Chaque chose créée est accommodée à chacune des autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A3","text":"Chaque substance simple entretient des rapports avec toutes les autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A4","text":"Les rapports d’une substance simple expriment les autres substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","text":"L’expression de l’univers par la substance simple est vivante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A6","text":"L’expression de l’univers par chaque substance simple est perpétuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX1","text":"Une substance simple ne se définit pas par l’isolement à l’égard des autres substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX2","text":"L’univers n’est pas constitué d’éléments dépourvus de rapports réciproques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX3","text":"L’expression de l’univers n’est pas une opération occasionnelle ou intermittente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX4","text":"Le rapport entre la substance simple et l’univers n’est pas purement extérieur ou accidentel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX5","text":"Le miroir n’est pas une reproduction inerte, puisqu’il est qualifié de vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:D1","text":"Chaque substance simple porte en elle un rapport structural à la totalité des autres substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","CH_UCIC_P_48:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:D2","text":"La totalité de l’univers devient exprimable à partir de n’importe quelle substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A3","CH_UCIC_P_48:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:D3","text":"L’individualité d’une substance simple implique une relation universelle plutôt qu’une séparation absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A2","CH_UCIC_P_48:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:D4","text":"La représentation de l’univers par une substance simple possède une continuité temporelle indéfinie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1","text":"L’univers est produit comme totalité distribuée : chaque substance simple en exprime la structure depuis sa position singulière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","CH_UCIC_P_48:A3","CH_UCIC_P_48:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2","text":"La pluralité des substances ne fragmente pas l’univers ; elle en multiplie les expressions locales et simultanées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A2","CH_UCIC_P_48:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SD3","text":"La permanence de l’univers est corrélée à la perpétuité de son expression dans chaque substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une ontologie où les substances simples seraient des unités sans accès structurel à la totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut une totalité extérieure à ses éléments et non exprimée par eux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une conception de l’individualité fondée sur l’autosuffisance relationnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut une rupture entre la persistance d’une substance et son rapport continu à l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’un univers qui ne serait présent nulle part dans son intégralité structurale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX2","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’une substance dont l’identité ne serait pas déjà déterminée par son rapport à la totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX3","text":"Est rendue inadmissible toute disjonction radicale entre multiplicité des substances et unité de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS1","text":"Liaison universelle des choses créées → accommodation réciproque des éléments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS2","text":"Accommodation réciproque → rapports de chaque substance simple avec toutes les autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS3","text":"Rapports universels → expression de toutes les autres substances par chaque substance simple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS4","text":"Expression universelle, vivante et perpétuelle → substance simple comme miroir de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS5","text":"Multiplication des substances simples → pluralisation des expressions sans dissolution de la totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AF1","text":"Liaison et accommodement universels → rapports de chaque substance simple à toutes les autres → expression de la totalité → miroir vivant et perpétuel de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1","text":"La substance simple est reclassée : d’unité isolable, elle devient point d’expression de la totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ME2","text":"L’opposition entre unité et totalité est reconfigurée en rapport d’expression distribuée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ME3","text":"L’univers devient cartographiable à partir de chacune de ses substances simples, sans perdre la pluralité de ses points d’expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ME4","text":"La permanence est déplacée du côté d’une activité expressive continue plutôt que d’une simple conservation passive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ALT1","text":"Surface — Chaque substance simple est dite miroir vivant et perpétuel de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ALT2","text":"Structural — L’accommodation réciproque organise un réseau de rapports entre toutes les substances créées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le texte transforme la relation entre partie et totalité en principe d’intelligibilité de la substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’être de la substance simple est relationnel, expressif, vivant et continuellement orienté vers la totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes A1 à A6 suffisent à reconstruire le passage de la liaison universelle à la fonction de miroir.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si l’expression de toutes les autres substances découle effectivement de leur accommodement réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT3","text":"Le texte sous-détermine le mécanisme précis par lequel une substance simple exprime toutes les autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT4","text":"La métaphore du miroir condense une tension entre singularité de chaque substance et expression de la totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : liaison universelle → rapports réciproques → expression totale → miroir vivant et perpétuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193726997045Z_436021f4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 56","source_sha256":"c6b2d9d1e4fa298fc64a4c6122c1e6509b93d2f3e5d1fc13269cc7fd2ffada5e","sha256":"592538cfffe47597cbe34e8edeef188a54f933ec61d297edf7dbc3e9b365b01e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:37:27.000522+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AS1","text":"The universal connection among created things makes each substance interdependent with all the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AS2","text":"This interdependence is reframed as a system of relations expressed by each simple substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AS3","text":"The expression of all the other substances constitutes the generative property of the simple substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AS4","text":"The simple substance is thus determined as a living and perpetual mirror of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","text":"All created things are connected to one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A2","text":"Each created thing is accommodated to each of the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A3","text":"Each simple substance maintains relations with all the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A4","text":"The relations of a simple substance express the other substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","text":"The expression of the universe by the simple substance is living.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:A6","text":"The expression of the universe by each simple substance is perpetual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX1","text":"A simple substance is not defined by isolation from the other substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX2","text":"The universe is not constituted of elements devoid of reciprocal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX3","text":"The expression of the universe is not an occasional or intermittent operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX4","text":"The relation between the simple substance and the universe is not purely external or accidental.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:NX5","text":"The mirror is not an inert reproduction, since it is qualified as living.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:D1","text":"Each simple substance bears within itself a structural relation to the totality of the other substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","CH_UCIC_P_48:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:D2","text":"The totality of the universe becomes expressible from any simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A3","CH_UCIC_P_48:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:D3","text":"The individuality of a simple substance entails a universal relation rather than an absolute separation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A2","CH_UCIC_P_48:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:D4","text":"The representation of the universe by a simple substance possesses indefinite temporal continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1","text":"The universe is produced as a distributed totality: each simple substance expresses its structure from its singular position.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","CH_UCIC_P_48:A3","CH_UCIC_P_48:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2","text":"The plurality of substances does not fragment the universe; it multiplies its local and simultaneous expressions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A2","CH_UCIC_P_48:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SD3","text":"The permanence of the universe is correlated with the perpetuity of its expression in each simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an ontology in which simple substances would be units without structural access to totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a totality external to its elements and not expressed by them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a conception of individuality founded on relational self-sufficiency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a rupture between the persistence of a substance and its continuous relation to the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX1","text":"The possibility of a universe that would be present nowhere in its structural integrity is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a substance whose identity would not already be determined by its relation to totality is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX3","text":"Any radical disjunction between the multiplicity of substances and the unity of the universe is rendered inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS1","text":"Universal connection of created things → reciprocal accommodation of elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS2","text":"Reciprocal accommodation → relations of each simple substance with all the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS3","text":"Universal relations → expression of all the other substances by each simple substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS4","text":"Universal, living, and perpetual expression → simple substance as mirror of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS5","text":"Multiplication of simple substances → pluralization of expressions without dissolution of totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:AF1","text":"Universal connection and accommodation → relations of each simple substance to all the others → expression of totality → living and perpetual mirror of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1","text":"The simple substance is reclassified: from an isolable unit, it becomes a point of expression of totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ME2","text":"The opposition between unity and totality is reconfigured as a relation of distributed expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ME3","text":"The universe becomes mappable from each of its simple substances, without losing the plurality of its points of expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ME4","text":"Permanence is shifted to the side of a continuous expressive activity rather than a mere passive preservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ALT1","text":"Surface — Each simple substance is said to be a living and perpetual mirror of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ALT2","text":"Structural — Reciprocal accommodation organizes a network of relations among all created substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text transforms the relation between part and totality into a principle of intelligibility of substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The being of the simple substance is relational, expressive, living, and continuously oriented toward totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT1","text":"Axioms A1 to A6 suffice to reconstruct the passage from universal connection to the mirror function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if the expression of all the other substances indeed follows from their reciprocal accommodation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT3","text":"The text underdetermines the precise mechanism by which a simple substance expresses all the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT4","text":"The metaphor of the mirror condenses a tension between the singularity of each substance and the expression of totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: universal connection → reciprocal relations → total expression → living and perpetual mirror.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_48:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_48@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_48:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 56"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 56","title":"Proposition 56","context":"Chapter 56","original_title":"Proposition 56"},"original_title":"Proposition 56","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 57","order":57,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_49"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_49@R001","sha256":"27a28b05c878f0f44a343437aa63129cffff3bb7e90870d44fba5586b96fc338","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS1","text":"La diversité apparente d’un même objet provient de la variation des points de vue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2","text":"Cette logique perspectivale est transposée de l’échelle urbaine à l’ordre des substances simples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS3","text":"La multiplicité infinie des Monades produit une pluralité de perspectives universelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS4","text":"Ces univers perspectifs ne constituent pas des réalités indépendantes, mais les expressions différenciées d’un seul univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS5","text":"L’argument procède par analogie structurale : apparence multiple → pluralité des points de vue → unité du réel perspectivement différencié.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A1","text":"Un même objet peut paraître différent selon le côté depuis lequel il est regardé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A2","text":"La variation des points de vue multiplie perspectivement l’apparence d’un même objet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","text":"Il existe une multitude infinie de substances simples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","text":"Chaque substance simple possède un point de vue propre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","text":"Chaque Monade constitue une perspective sur l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A6","text":"La pluralité des univers perspectifs renvoie à un seul univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A7","text":"La différence entre les univers perspectifs est une différence de perspective plutôt qu’une multiplication du réel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1","text":"Les univers perspectifs ne sont pas des univers indépendants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:NX2","text":"La multiplicité des apparences ne constitue pas une pluralité de réalités séparées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A2","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:NX3","text":"La différence entre les Monades n’implique pas l’existence de plusieurs totalités absolues.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:NX4","text":"Le point de vue particulier ne vaut pas comme production d’un monde autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:D1","text":"La multiplicité des Monades engendre une multiplicité de représentations du même univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:D2","text":"La différence entre les univers perspectifs est indexée sur la position représentative de chaque Monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:D3","text":"L’unité de l’univers est compatible avec l’infinité des perspectives qui l’expriment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:D4","text":"La pluralité phénoménale doit être interprétée comme une différenciation perspectivale de l’unité plutôt que comme une division ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A2","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1","text":"L’unité du réel ne supprime pas la pluralité des perspectives ; elle en constitue le référent commun.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SD2","text":"La multiplicité ontologique des substances est convertie en multiplicité épistémique ou représentationnelle des univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3","text":"Aucun point de vue monadique n’épuise à lui seul l’univers dont il est une perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4","text":"La cohérence du système repose sur la coexistence réglée de deux niveaux : pluralité réelle des substances et unité du monde exprimé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une différence de représentation suffise à établir une différence de monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A2","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’un ensemble de perspectives puisse être compris comme une collection de totalités sans unité sous-jacente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX3","text":"Il exclut la séparation absolue entre le sujet perspectif et l’univers représenté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX4","text":"Il exclut l’équivalence entre multiplicité des substances et fragmentation du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX1","text":"Le texte rend inadmissible l’hypothèse d’un réel sans unité commune derrière la diversité des points de vue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX2","text":"Il forclôt la possibilité que la pluralité des perspectives dissolve toute référence à un univers unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3","text":"Il laisse sans place une perspective extérieure et non située qui posséderait le réel indépendamment de toute Monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS1","text":"Objet un → variation du point de vue → apparence différenciée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS2","text":"Substances simples infinies → points de vue monadiques multiples → univers perspectifs multiples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS3","text":"Univers perspectifs multiples → réduction à des perspectives d’un seul univers → unité du réel sous différenciation perspectivale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS4","text":"La multiplicité est maintenue au niveau des expressions, tandis que l’unité est conservée au niveau du référent commun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AF1","text":"Apparence différente d’un même objet → explication par la variation des points de vue → extension de l’analogie aux Monades → pluralité d’univers perspectifs → réaffirmation d’un univers unique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ME1","text":"La pluralité des mondes est reclassée comme pluralité des perspectives sur un monde unique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ME2","text":"L’opposition entre unité et multiplicité est déplacée vers une distinction entre référent commun et modes d’expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ME3","text":"Chaque Monade devient un site de différenciation du réel sans devenir une totalité indépendante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4","text":"La multiplicité infinie cesse d’être un argument contre l’unité et devient son mode de manifestation perspectivale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Une même ville paraît différente selon le côté depuis lequel elle est regardée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Chaque Monade ordonne une perspective singulière sur l’univers, et la multiplicité des Monades produit la multiplicité des expressions du réel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Le texte neutralise l’opposition directe entre pluralité des apparences et unité du monde en la reformulant comme différence de points de vue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Le réel est un, mais il n’est donné qu’à travers une infinité de perspectives substantielles ; la tension porte sur les niveaux de réalité plutôt que sur une succession temporelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes A1 à A7 suffisent à reconstruire le passage de l’analogie urbaine à la structure monadique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la pluralité des univers est comprise comme pluralité de perspectives et non comme pluralité de totalités.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT3","text":"Le point le plus fort du système est l’articulation entre infinité des substances et unité de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT4","text":"Le texte sous-détermine le statut exact de la relation entre une Monade et « son » univers perspectif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT5","text":"Il laisse également implicite le mécanisme qui garantit la commensurabilité des perspectives particulières.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT6","text":"La tension structurale réside dans la coexistence d’une multiplicité dite infinie et d’un univers néanmoins singulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT7","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : analogie de la perspective → généralisation monadique → conversion de la pluralité en expressions d’une unité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193742613825Z_a95b756f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 57","source_sha256":"27a28b05c878f0f44a343437aa63129cffff3bb7e90870d44fba5586b96fc338","sha256":"9813d95010cd384b13bed01ffd14b0893f53350836cf5efbbb2dc506bcd4542b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:37:42.620693+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS1","text":"The apparent diversity of one and the same object arises from the variation of points of view.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2","text":"This perspectival logic is transposed from the urban scale to the order of simple substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS3","text":"The infinite multiplicity of Monads produces a plurality of universal perspectives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS4","text":"These perspectival universes do not constitute independent realities, but differentiated expressions of a single universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AS5","text":"The argument proceeds by structural analogy: multiple appearance → plurality of points of view → unity of reality perspectivally differentiated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A1","text":"One and the same object may appear different depending on the side from which it is viewed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A2","text":"The variation of points of view perspectivally multiplies the appearance of one and the same object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","text":"There exists an infinite multitude of simple substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","text":"Each simple substance possesses its own point of view.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","text":"Each Monad constitutes a perspective on the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A6","text":"The plurality of perspectival universes refers back to a single universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:A7","text":"The difference between perspectival universes is a difference of perspective rather than a multiplication of reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1","text":"Perspectival universes are not independent universes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:NX2","text":"The multiplicity of appearances does not constitute a plurality of separate realities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A2","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:NX3","text":"The difference between Monads does not imply the existence of several absolute totalities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:NX4","text":"The particular point of view does not count as the production of an autonomous world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:D1","text":"The multiplicity of Monads engenders a multiplicity of representations of the same universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:D2","text":"The difference between perspectival universes is indexed to the representative position of each Monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:D3","text":"The unity of the universe is compatible with the infinity of perspectives that express it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:D4","text":"Phenomenal plurality must be interpreted as a perspectival differentiation of unity rather than as an ontological division.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A2","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1","text":"The unity of reality does not suppress the plurality of perspectives; it constitutes their common referent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SD2","text":"The ontological multiplicity of substances is converted into an epistemic or representational multiplicity of universes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3","text":"No monadic point of view exhausts by itself the universe of which it is a perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4","text":"The coherence of the system rests on the regulated coexistence of two levels: real plurality of substances and unity of the world expressed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a difference in representation suffices to establish a difference in world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A2","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that a set of perspectives can be understood as a collection of totalities without underlying unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX3","text":"It excludes the absolute separation between the perspectival subject and the universe represented.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX4","text":"It excludes the equivalence between multiplicity of substances and fragmentation of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX1","text":"The text renders inadmissible the hypothesis of a reality without common unity behind the diversity of points of view.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX2","text":"It forecloses the possibility that the plurality of perspectives dissolves all reference to a single universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3","text":"It leaves no place for an external and non-situated perspective that would possess reality independently of every Monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS1","text":"One object → variation of the point of view → differentiated appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS2","text":"Infinite simple substances → multiple monadic points of view → multiple perspectival universes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS3","text":"Multiple perspectival universes → reduction to perspectives on a single universe → unity of reality under perspectival differentiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS4","text":"Multiplicity is maintained at the level of expressions, while unity is preserved at the level of the common referent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:AF1","text":"Different appearance of one and the same object → explanation through the variation of points of view → extension of the analogy to Monads → plurality of perspectival universes → reaffirmation of a single universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ME1","text":"The plurality of worlds is reclassified as a plurality of perspectives on a single world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ME2","text":"The opposition between unity and multiplicity is displaced toward a distinction between common referent and modes of expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ME3","text":"Each Monad becomes a site of differentiation of reality without becoming an independent totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4","text":"Infinite multiplicity ceases to be an argument against unity and becomes its mode of perspectival manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — One and the same city appears different depending on the side from which it is viewed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Each Monad orders a singular perspective on the universe, and the multiplicity of Monads produces the multiplicity of expressions of reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The text neutralizes the direct opposition between plurality of appearances and unity of the world by reformulating it as a difference of points of view.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Reality is one, but it is given only through an infinity of substantial perspectives; the tension concerns levels of reality rather than a temporal succession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT1","text":"Axioms A1 to A7 suffice to reconstruct the passage from the urban analogy to the monadic structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if the plurality of universes is understood as a plurality of perspectives and not as a plurality of totalities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT3","text":"The system's strongest point is the articulation between infinity of substances and unity of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT4","text":"The text underdetermines the exact status of the relation between a Monad and “its” perspectival universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT5","text":"It likewise leaves implicit the mechanism that guarantees the commensurability of particular perspectives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT6","text":"The structural tension resides in the coexistence of a multiplicity said to be infinite and a universe that is nevertheless singular.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: analogy of perspective → monadic generalization → conversion of plurality into expressions of a unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_49:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_49@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_49:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 57"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 57","title":"Proposition 57","context":"Chapter 57","original_title":"Proposition 57"},"original_title":"Proposition 57","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 58","order":58,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_50"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_50@R001","sha256":"7c94373ea133edcf23b67c30bada6727a0cab7a5987a2d3534e19f34efe05d73","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AS1","text":"L’énoncé cherche à déterminer le moyen d’obtenir une pluralité maximale sans perdre l’organisation d’ensemble.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AS2","text":"Il recadre la variété et l’ordre comme deux dimensions conjointes d’une même opération.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AS3","text":"Il identifie la perfection avec l’optimisation simultanée de ces deux dimensions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AS4","text":"Le mouvement argumentatif va de la combinaison variété–ordre à la définition de la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A1","text":"Une variété maximale est une fin recherchée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A2","text":"Un ordre maximal est une fin recherchée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A3","text":"La variété et l’ordre peuvent être obtenus conjointement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","text":"Le moyen adéquat doit produire simultanément variété et ordre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A5","text":"La perfection correspond au degré maximal conjoint de variété et d’ordre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A6","text":"La possibilité fixe la limite supérieure de la variété et de l’ordre accessibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX1","text":"La variété n’est pas définie comme une dispersion dépourvue d’ordre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX2","text":"L’ordre n’est pas défini comme une réduction de la variété.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX3","text":"La perfection n’est pas assimilée à la seule maximisation de la variété.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX4","text":"La perfection n’est pas assimilée à la seule maximisation de l’ordre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX5","text":"Le moyen recherché n’est pas un choix entre variété et ordre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:D1","text":"La meilleure configuration est celle qui maximise la variété sans diminuer l’ordre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A1","CH_UCIC_P_50:A2","CH_UCIC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:D2","text":"La perfection est produite par une maximisation coordonnée plutôt que par l’excellence isolée d’une seule dimension.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A3","CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CH_UCIC_P_50:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:D3","text":"L’ordre fonctionne comme la condition de conversion d’une variété abondante en perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A2","CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CH_UCIC_P_50:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:D4","text":"Le moyen est évalué selon le degré de perfection qu’il rend possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CH_UCIC_P_50:A5","CH_UCIC_P_50:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SD1","text":"Le système transforme une opposition apparente entre pluralité et organisation en relation de co-production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A1","CH_UCIC_P_50:A2","CH_UCIC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SD2","text":"La perfection devient une propriété relationnelle de la configuration totale, et non une propriété isolée de ses éléments.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A3","CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CH_UCIC_P_50:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SD3","text":"La limite du possible devient simultanément la limite de la variété, de l’ordre et de la perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A5","CH_UCIC_P_50:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut silencieusement qu’une augmentation de la variété constitue en elle-même une augmentation de la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut silencieusement qu’un ordre accru puisse justifier la suppression de la variété.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut un modèle de perfection fondé sur une seule grandeur indépendante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut qu’il existe une perfection au-delà de ce qui est possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX1","text":"La perfection dépend de critères de mesure de la variété et de l’ordre que l’énoncé ne formalise pas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX2","text":"La possibilité est posée comme une frontière ultime sans que soit déterminé ce qui la constitue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX3","text":"La possibilité d’un conflit irréductible entre variété maximale et ordre maximal reste forclose plutôt que démontrée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:FGS1","text":"Espace du possible → extension maximale de la variété.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:FGS2","text":"Variété maximale → exigence d’un ordre maximal concomitant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:FGS3","text":"Variété maximale + ordre maximal → configuration parfaite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:FGS4","text":"Configuration parfaite → borne supérieure de ce qui peut être obtenu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AF1","text":"Recherche d’un moyen → maximisation de la variété → maintien d’un ordre maximal → identification de cette conjonction avec la perfection → limitation par le possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ME1","text":"La variété et l’ordre sont reclassés comme dimensions compatibles d’une même perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ME2","text":"La perfection est déplacée d’un état isolé vers une relation optimale entre multiplicité et organisation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ME3","text":"Le possible devient la carte de mesure commune des degrés de variété, d’ordre et de perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT1","text":"Surface — L’énoncé prescrit l’obtention de la plus grande variété sous la forme du plus grand ordre possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT2","text":"Structural — La perfection repose sur l’articulation systémique de deux maxima conjoints.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le critère d’évaluation est déplacé du choix entre deux fins vers la coordination de leurs conditions de réalisation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Le réel pertinent est implicitement ordonné selon des degrés de possibilité et une limite supérieure d’accomplissement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage de la variété et de l’ordre à la perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT2","text":"La cohérence interne dépend de la compatibilité présupposée entre les deux maximisations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT3","text":"Le point le plus fort du système est l’identification explicite de la perfection avec une combinaison ordonnée de variété et d’ordre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT4","text":"Le point sous-déterminé est le critère permettant de mesurer la variété, l’ordre et leur degré maximal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel de l’énoncé, mais elle ne peut démontrer la compatibilité des maxima au-delà de leur affirmation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193754622270Z_cd4b6e4b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 58","source_sha256":"7c94373ea133edcf23b67c30bada6727a0cab7a5987a2d3534e19f34efe05d73","sha256":"7a571b821886381687ee26ba460f62e08deab69629a12581990cd00e418a7e74","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:37:54.627310+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AS1","text":"The statement seeks to determine the means of obtaining a maximal plurality without losing overall organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AS2","text":"It reframes variety and order as two conjoint dimensions of a single operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AS3","text":"It identifies perfection with the simultaneous optimization of these two dimensions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AS4","text":"The argumentative movement proceeds from the combination of variety and order to the definition of perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A1","text":"Maximal variety is a sought end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A2","text":"Maximal order is a sought end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A3","text":"Variety and order can be obtained conjointly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","text":"The adequate means must simultaneously produce variety and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A5","text":"Perfection corresponds to the conjoint maximal degree of variety and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:A6","text":"Possibility sets the upper limit of accessible variety and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX1","text":"Variety is not defined as dispersion devoid of order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX2","text":"Order is not defined as a reduction of variety.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX3","text":"Perfection is not equated with the maximization of variety alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX4","text":"Perfection is not equated with the maximization of order alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:NX5","text":"The sought means is not a choice between variety and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:D1","text":"The best configuration is that which maximizes variety without diminishing order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A1","CH_UCIC_P_50:A2","CH_UCIC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:D2","text":"Perfection is produced by coordinated maximization rather than by the isolated excellence of a single dimension.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A3","CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CH_UCIC_P_50:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:D3","text":"Order functions as the condition for converting abundant variety into perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A2","CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CH_UCIC_P_50:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:D4","text":"The means is evaluated according to the degree of perfection it makes possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CH_UCIC_P_50:A5","CH_UCIC_P_50:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SD1","text":"The system transforms an apparent opposition between plurality and organization into a relation of co-production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A1","CH_UCIC_P_50:A2","CH_UCIC_P_50:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SD2","text":"Perfection becomes a relational property of the total configuration, rather than an isolated property of its elements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A3","CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CH_UCIC_P_50:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SD3","text":"The limit of the possible becomes simultaneously the limit of variety, order, and perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A5","CH_UCIC_P_50:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:DNX1","text":"The system silently excludes the notion that an increase in variety is in itself an increase in perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:DNX2","text":"The system silently excludes the notion that increased order could justify the suppression of variety.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a model of perfection founded on a single independent magnitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the existence of a perfection beyond what is possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX1","text":"Perfection depends on criteria for measuring variety and order that the statement does not formalize.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX2","text":"Possibility is posited as an ultimate boundary without determining what constitutes it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX3","text":"The possibility of an irreducible conflict between maximal variety and maximal order remains foreclosed rather than demonstrated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:FGS1","text":"Space of the possible → maximal extension of variety.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:FGS2","text":"Maximal variety → requirement of concomitant maximal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:FGS3","text":"Maximal variety + maximal order → perfect configuration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:FGS4","text":"Perfect configuration → upper bound of what can be obtained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:AF1","text":"Search for a means → maximization of variety → maintenance of maximal order → identification of this conjunction with perfection → limitation by the possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ME1","text":"Variety and order are reclassified as compatible dimensions of a single perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ME2","text":"Perfection is shifted from an isolated state to an optimal relation between multiplicity and organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ME3","text":"The possible becomes the common measure of the degrees of variety, order, and perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT1","text":"Surface — The statement prescribes the attainment of the greatest variety in the form of the greatest possible order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT2","text":"Structural — Perfection rests on the systemic articulation of two conjoint maxima.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The criterion of evaluation is shifted from the choice between two ends to the coordination of their conditions of realization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The relevant real is implicitly ordered according to degrees of possibility and an upper limit of accomplishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage from variety and order to perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT2","text":"Internal coherence depends on the presupposed compatibility between the two maximizations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT3","text":"The system's strongest point is the explicit identification of perfection with an ordered combination of variety and order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT4","text":"The underdetermined point is the criterion allowing the measurement of variety, order, and their maximal degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the statement, but it cannot demonstrate the compatibility of the maxima beyond their assertion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_50:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_50@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_50:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 58"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 58","title":"Proposition 58","context":"Chapter 58","original_title":"Proposition 58"},"original_title":"Proposition 58","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 59","order":59,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_51"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_51@R001","sha256":"46a11e0d363e1126b246689e2cd6308d24d0208ba705082679e652a9ebdaad7d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS1","text":"L’hypothèse d’une harmonie universelle constitue le fondement métaphysique de la grandeur divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS2","text":"Chaque substance exprime exactement toutes les autres selon les rapports qu’elle entretient avec elles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS3","text":"Une objection soutient que cette hypothèse attribue à Dieu une puissance excessive, voire impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS4","text":"L’objection ne fournit toutefois aucune raison établissant l’impossibilité de l’harmonie universelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS5","text":"L’argument progresse ainsi de l’hypothèse harmonique à sa fonction théologique, puis de l’objection à l’absence de réfutation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A1","text":"Il existe une hypothèse d’harmonie universelle entre les substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","text":"Toute substance exprime exactement toutes les autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A3","text":"L’expression réciproque des substances est déterminée par les rapports qu’elles entretiennent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A4","text":"Cette harmonie universelle relève correctement la grandeur de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A5","text":"Bayle a formulé une objection selon laquelle cette conception donne trop à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A6","text":"L’objection de Bayle ne fournit aucune raison démontrant que l’harmonie universelle est impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A7","text":"L’hypothèse est présentée comme démontrée, ou du moins comme suffisamment établie pour soutenir la grandeur divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX1","text":"L’harmonie universelle n’est pas tenue pour impossible en raison de son ampleur théologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX2","text":"L’attribution d’une puissance considérable à Dieu n’est pas réfutée par le seul sentiment qu’elle excède le possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX3","text":"L’objection de Bayle ne constitue pas une démonstration d’impossibilité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX4","text":"La pluralité des substances n’implique pas l’absence de rapports expressifs entre elles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX5","text":"La grandeur divine n’est pas définie par une limitation préalable de ce que Dieu peut produire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:D1","text":"Si chaque substance exprime exactement toutes les autres, alors aucune substance n’est métaphysiquement isolée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A1","CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","CH_UCIC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:D2","text":"Si l’harmonie universelle exprime la grandeur de Dieu, alors la richesse des rapports entre substances devient un indice de la puissance divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A1","CH_UCIC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:D3","text":"Si l’objection ne donne aucune raison d’impossibilité, elle ne suffit pas à invalider l’hypothèse harmonique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A5","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:D4","text":"La charge argumentative est déplacée de l’excès apparent de l’attribution divine vers la production d’une preuve d’impossibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A5","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","text":"L’ordre universel n’est pas une addition externe imposée aux substances, mais le résultat de leur expression réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A1","CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","CH_UCIC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SD2","text":"La possibilité d’un ordre intégral entre les substances devient compatible avec une conception maximale de la puissance divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","CH_UCIC_P_51:A4","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SD3","text":"Une objection fondée sur la démesure de la puissance divine reste extérieure au système tant qu’elle ne transforme pas cette démesure en contradiction démontrée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A5","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6","CH_UCIC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SD4","text":"La possibilité logique de l’harmonie universelle suffit ici à maintenir sa fonction apologétique, même si le passage de la non-impossibilité à la démonstration demeure comprimé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A4","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6","CH_UCIC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une apparence d’excès suffise à établir une impossibilité métaphysique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’une substance puisse être conçue indépendamment de l’ensemble des rapports exprimés par elle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:DNX3","text":"Il exclut qu’une objection théologique non démontrée puisse interrompre la construction métaphysique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une conception de Dieu dont la grandeur serait mesurée par la restriction de son pouvoir harmonisateur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SNX1","text":"Le texte forclôt la possibilité que la puissance divine soit limitée par une norme du possible non justifiée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SNX2","text":"Il rend inadmissible un univers composé de substances sans expression mutuelle intégrale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SNX3","text":"Il laisse hors champ une démonstration positive de la possibilité de l’harmonie, en traitant l’absence de preuve d’impossibilité comme suffisante contre l’objection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS1","text":"Multiplicité des substances → rapports réciproques → expression exacte de chaque substance par toutes les autres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS2","text":"Expression universelle → harmonie intégrale → manifestation adéquate de la grandeur divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS3","text":"Objection d’excès divin → demande implicite d’une preuve d’impossibilité → absence d’une telle preuve → maintien de l’hypothèse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS4","text":"Apparence d’impossibilité → distinction entre excès imaginé et contradiction démontrée → neutralisation de l’objection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AF1","text":"Hypothèse d’harmonie universelle → expression exacte de toutes les substances → relèvement de la grandeur de Dieu → objection d’une attribution excessive → absence de raison d’impossibilité → préservation de l’hypothèse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ME1","text":"La relation entre les substances est reclassée comme expression universelle plutôt que comme simple coexistence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ME2","text":"La puissance divine est redéfinie par la capacité de produire une harmonie intégrale entre toutes les substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ME3","text":"L’objection philosophique est déplacée du registre de la plausibilité vers celui de la démonstration de l’impossibilité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ME4","text":"La frontière entre le possible et l’impossible devient dépendante d’une raison démonstrative, non d’une intuition de démesure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ALT1","text":"Surface — Une hypothèse harmonique est défendue contre l’objection qu’elle donne trop à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ALT2","text":"Structural — Les substances forment un réseau d’expression exacte déterminé par leurs rapports réciproques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La réfutation exige une raison d’impossibilité ; l’objection qui n’en fournit aucune est désamorcée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La réalité est conçue comme une totalité relationnelle où chaque substance exprime l’ensemble sans perdre sa distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement principal : harmonie universelle, expression réciproque, grandeur divine, objection, absence de réfutation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si l’on distingue la non-démonstration de l’impossibilité d’une démonstration positive de la possibilité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT3","text":"Le point le plus fort réside dans le déplacement de la charge de la preuve vers l’adversaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT4","text":"Le point sous-déterminé est le statut exact de l’hypothèse : le texte la qualifie de démontrée sans exposer ici sa démonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT5","text":"La tension principale oppose l’affirmation d’une hypothèse démontrée à l’argument local fondé seulement sur l’absence de raison d’impossibilité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel du texte, mais elle ne peut restituer la preuve antérieure à laquelle renvoie l’expression « cette hypothèse ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193809188548Z_85050795","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 59","source_sha256":"46a11e0d363e1126b246689e2cd6308d24d0208ba705082679e652a9ebdaad7d","sha256":"c22bc1a88890a1933343436dede9d6b3c89842a7f62fbe11c1e49384f81531e8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:38:09.193928+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS1","text":"The hypothesis of a universal harmony constitutes the metaphysical foundation of divine greatness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS2","text":"Each substance exactly expresses all the others according to the relations it maintains with them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS3","text":"An objection maintains that this hypothesis attributes to God an excessive, indeed impossible, power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS4","text":"The objection nevertheless provides no reason establishing the impossibility of universal harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AS5","text":"The argument thus proceeds from the harmonic hypothesis to its theological function, then from the objection to the absence of refutation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A1","text":"There exists a hypothesis of universal harmony among substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","text":"Every substance exactly expresses all the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A3","text":"The reciprocal expression of substances is determined by the relations they maintain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A4","text":"This universal harmony properly enhances the greatness of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A5","text":"Bayle formulated an objection according to which this conception gives too much to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A6","text":"Bayle's objection provides no reason demonstrating that universal harmony is impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:A7","text":"The hypothesis is presented as demonstrated, or at least as sufficiently established to support divine greatness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX1","text":"Universal harmony is not held to be impossible by reason of its theological scope.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX2","text":"The attribution of a considerable power to God is not refuted by the mere feeling that it exceeds what is possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX3","text":"Bayle's objection does not constitute a demonstration of impossibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX4","text":"The plurality of substances does not imply the absence of expressive relations among them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:NX5","text":"Divine greatness is not defined by a prior limitation of what God can produce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:D1","text":"If each substance exactly expresses all the others, then no substance is metaphysically isolated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A1","CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","CH_UCIC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:D2","text":"If universal harmony expresses the greatness of God, then the richness of the relations among substances becomes an indication of divine power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A1","CH_UCIC_P_51:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:D3","text":"If the objection gives no reason for impossibility, it does not suffice to invalidate the harmonic hypothesis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A5","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:D4","text":"The argumentative burden is shifted from the apparent excess of the divine attribution to the production of a proof of impossibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A5","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","text":"Universal order is not an external addition imposed upon substances, but the result of their reciprocal expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A1","CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","CH_UCIC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SD2","text":"The possibility of an integral order among substances becomes compatible with a maximal conception of divine power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","CH_UCIC_P_51:A4","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SD3","text":"An objection founded on the excessiveness of divine power remains external to the system so long as it does not transform this excessiveness into a demonstrated contradiction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A5","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6","CH_UCIC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SD4","text":"The logical possibility of universal harmony suffices here to maintain its apologetic function, even if the passage from non-impossibility to demonstration remains compressed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A4","CH_UCIC_P_51:A6","CH_UCIC_P_51:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that an appearance of excess should suffice to establish a metaphysical impossibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that a substance may be conceived independently of the totality of the relations expressed by it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:DNX3","text":"It excludes the possibility that an undemonstrated theological objection may interrupt the metaphysical construction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:DNX4","text":"It excludes a conception of God whose greatness would be measured by the restriction of His harmonizing power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SNX1","text":"The text forecloses the possibility that divine power might be limited by an unjustified norm of the possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SNX2","text":"It renders inadmissible a universe composed of substances without integral mutual expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:SNX3","text":"It leaves outside its scope a positive demonstration of the possibility of harmony, treating the absence of proof of impossibility as sufficient against the objection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS1","text":"Multiplicity of substances → reciprocal relations → exact expression of each substance by all the others.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS2","text":"Universal expression → integral harmony → adequate manifestation of divine greatness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS3","text":"Objection of divine excess → implicit demand for a proof of impossibility → absence of such a proof → maintenance of the hypothesis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS4","text":"Appearance of impossibility → distinction between imagined excess and demonstrated contradiction → neutralization of the objection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:AF1","text":"Hypothesis of universal harmony → exact expression of all substances → enhancement of the greatness of God → objection of an excessive attribution → absence of a reason for impossibility → preservation of the hypothesis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ME1","text":"The relation among substances is reclassified as universal expression rather than as mere coexistence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ME2","text":"Divine power is redefined by the capacity to produce an integral harmony among all substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ME3","text":"The philosophical objection is shifted from the register of plausibility to that of the demonstration of impossibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ME4","text":"The boundary between the possible and the impossible becomes dependent upon a demonstrative reason, not upon an intuition of excessiveness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ALT1","text":"Surface — A harmonic hypothesis is defended against the objection that it gives too much to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ALT2","text":"Structural — Substances form a network of exact expression determined by their reciprocal relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Refutation requires a reason for impossibility; an objection that provides none is defused.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Reality is conceived as a relational totality in which each substance expresses the whole without losing its distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal movement: universal harmony, reciprocal expression, divine greatness, objection, absence of refutation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if one distinguishes the non-demonstration of impossibility from a positive demonstration of possibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT3","text":"The strongest point lies in shifting the burden of proof to the adversary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT4","text":"The underdetermined point is the exact status of the hypothesis: the text characterizes it as demonstrated without setting out its demonstration here.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT5","text":"The principal tension opposes the affirmation of a demonstrated hypothesis to the local argument founded solely on the absence of a reason for impossibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text, but it cannot restore the prior proof to which the expression « cette hypothèse » refers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_51:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_51@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_51:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 59"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 59","title":"Proposition 59","context":"Chapter 59","original_title":"Proposition 59"},"original_title":"Proposition 59","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 60","order":60,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_52"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_52@R001","sha256":"65aa396375b6b8685f71b4cde242e9b9dae6025fa0587d32f439652a34c8de2a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS1","text":"L’argument cherche les raisons a priori pour lesquelles l’ordre des choses ne peut être autrement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS2","text":"L’ordre divin est recadré comme une régulation qui prend en considération chaque partie et chaque monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS3","text":"La nature représentative de la monade implique une représentation de l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS4","text":"L’universalité de la représentation est distinguée de sa clarté : le détail de l’univers reste confus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS5","text":"La limitation ne porte pas sur l’objet représenté, mais sur la modification de la connaissance de cet objet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS6","text":"Les degrés de perception distincte différencient les monades sans supprimer leur orientation commune vers l’infini et le tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A1","text":"Dieu règle l’ensemble en prenant en considération chaque partie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A2","text":"Dieu prend particulièrement en considération chaque monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A3","text":"La nature de la monade est représentative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A4","text":"Une nature représentative ne peut être bornée à ne représenter qu’une partie des choses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","text":"Chaque monade représente l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A6","text":"La représentation de l’univers est confuse dans le détail.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A7","text":"La représentation ne devient distincte que dans une petite partie des choses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A8","text":"La distinction perceptive porte prioritairement sur les choses les plus proches ou les plus grandes relativement à chaque monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A9","text":"La limitation des monades concerne la modification de la connaissance, non l’objet connu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A10","text":"Toutes les monades tendent confusément vers l’infini et vers le tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A11","text":"Les degrés de perception distincte limitent et distinguent les monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A12","text":"Une représentation également distincte de tout ferait de chaque monade une divinité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX1","text":"La monade n’est pas limitée à la représentation d’une partie isolée des choses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX2","text":"La représentation universelle n’est pas une connaissance distincte de chaque détail de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX3","text":"La limitation de la monade ne vient pas d’une limitation de l’objet représenté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX4","text":"Les monades ne sont pas différenciées par des objets totalement séparés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX5","text":"La perception distincte ne s’étend pas uniformément à l’ensemble de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX6","text":"Une monade n’est pas une divinité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D1","text":"Toute monade contient une représentation, au moins confuse, de l’univers entier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A3","CH_UCIC_P_52:A4","CH_UCIC_P_52:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D2","text":"La représentation universelle et la perception distincte sont compatibles parce qu’elles appartiennent à deux degrés différents de connaissance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A6","CH_UCIC_P_52:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D3","text":"Chaque monade possède un champ local de perception distincte à l’intérieur d’une représentation globale confuse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A7","CH_UCIC_P_52:A8","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D4","text":"La différence entre les monades est une différence de degré dans la connaissance distincte plutôt qu’une différence d’étendue de l’objet représenté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A9","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D5","text":"La connaissance distincte de l’univers entier est exclue pour préserver la différence entre monade et divinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A7","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11","CH_UCIC_P_52:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","text":"L’unité de l’univers est inscrite dans chaque monade sous la forme d’une représentation universelle, tandis que la pluralité des monades apparaît comme une modulation différentielle de cette même représentation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A3","CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A9","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SD2","text":"La finitude des monades est épistémique et modale plutôt qu’objectale : rien n’est soustrait à leur représentation, mais tout n’est pas également rendu distinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A6","CH_UCIC_P_52:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SD3","text":"La distinction entre les monades est produite par une cartographie variable de la clarté perceptive, non par une répartition de fragments exclusifs du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A7","CH_UCIC_P_52:A8","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SD4","text":"La structure divine de l’ordre se conserve en maintenant simultanément l’universalité représentative et l’inégalité des degrés de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A1","CH_UCIC_P_52:A2","CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une ontologie dans laquelle chaque monade ne serait qu’un point de vue fermé sur une portion indépendante du réel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut une séparation absolue entre l’objet représenté et les monades qui le représentent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut l’équivalence entre représenter tout et connaître distinctement tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut une égalité parfaite des monades quant à la clarté de leurs perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX5","text":"Le système exclut que la limitation perceptive résulte d’un défaut de l’univers représenté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX6","text":"Le système exclut une connaissance monadique qui abolirait la différence entre créature et Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’une perspective finie qui serait extérieure à l’univers qu’elle représente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX2","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’une totalité immédiatement transparente à une monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX3","text":"Est forclose une individuation fondée sur l’absence de rapport au tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX4","text":"Est forclose l’autonomie absolue de la perception : chaque point de vue reste intérieurement orienté vers l’infini et le tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX5","text":"Est forclose l’identification de la perfection avec la distinction intégrale de toutes les perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS1","text":"Régulation divine de chaque partie et de chaque monade → inscription d’une fonction représentative dans chaque monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS2","text":"Fonction représentative universelle → représentation nécessaire de l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS3","text":"Représentation de l’univers entier → confusion du détail et absence de distinction globale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS4","text":"Distribution inégale de la perception distincte → focalisation sur les choses proches ou grandes relativement à chaque monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS5","text":"Déplacement de la limite vers la modification de la connaissance → maintien de l’universalité de l’objet représenté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS6","text":"Variation des degrés de perception distincte → différenciation des monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS7","text":"Distinction perceptive intégrale → suppression de la différence entre monade et divinité → impossibilité structurelle d’une telle perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AF1","text":"Question de la nécessité de l’ordre → fondement dans la régulation divine → nature représentative de la monade → représentation confuse de l’univers entier → distinction locale selon la proximité ou la grandeur → limitation de la connaissance plutôt que de l’objet → différenciation graduelle des monades → sauvegarde de la différence entre créature et Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME1","text":"L’objet représenté est reclassé comme universel pour toute monade, tandis que la clarté perceptive devient le principe de limitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME2","text":"L’opposition entre totalité et finitude est dissoute : une monade peut représenter le tout sans le connaître distinctement dans toutes ses parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME3","text":"La différence entre les monades est redessinée comme différence de degrés de perception plutôt que comme différence de territoires ontologiques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME4","text":"Le rapport au proche et au grand devient une règle de localisation de la distinction à l’intérieur d’une représentation universelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME5","text":"La divinité est cartographiée comme seuil négatif de la perception distincte intégrale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT1","text":"Surface — Les monades représentent l’univers entier, mais ne le perçoivent distinctement que dans une petite partie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT2","text":"Structural — La limitation monadique est produite par les degrés de perception distincte et non par une restriction de l’objet représenté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’argument recadre la finitude comme modalité de connaissance afin de rendre compatibles universalité représentative, différenciation des monades et ordre divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Chaque monade est une perspective interne au tout, orientée confusément vers l’infini, sans pouvoir atteindre la transparence absolue réservée à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage de la régulation divine à la représentation universelle des monades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT2","text":"La distinction entre objet représenté et modification de la connaissance est indispensable à la cohérence du système.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT3","text":"La coexistence de la représentation du tout et de la perception distincte locale préserve le mouvement réel de l’argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT4","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente tant que la représentation universelle n’est pas assimilée à une connaissance également distincte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT5","text":"La principale tension réside dans l’articulation entre orientation de toutes les monades vers l’infini et limitation nécessaire de leur perception distincte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT6","text":"La limite divine est maintenue par une exclusion structurelle : la distinction intégrale de tout ferait disparaître le statut fini de la monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT7","text":"La reconstruction dépend de la compression du rapport entre proximité, grandeur et degré de perception, que le passage énonce sans en détailler le mécanisme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193826463184Z_8551424c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 60","source_sha256":"65aa396375b6b8685f71b4cde242e9b9dae6025fa0587d32f439652a34c8de2a","sha256":"1c7eca109c15b5e3e6ffdf1d20ec4f617d7e585609b215296e368ae0607a563b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:38:26.466432+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS1","text":"The argument seeks the a priori reasons why the order of things cannot be otherwise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS2","text":"The divine order is reframed as a regulation that takes every part and every monad into consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS3","text":"The representative nature of the monad entails a representation of the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS4","text":"The universality of representation is distinguished from its clarity: the detail of the universe remains confused.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS5","text":"The limitation concerns not the represented object, but the modification of knowledge of that object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AS6","text":"The degrees of distinct perception differentiate the monads without eliminating their common orientation toward infinity and the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A1","text":"God regulates the whole by taking every part into consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A2","text":"God takes each monad particularly into consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A3","text":"The nature of the monad is representative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A4","text":"A representative nature cannot be confined to representing only one part of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","text":"Each monad represents the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A6","text":"The representation of the universe is confused in detail.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A7","text":"Representation becomes distinct only in a small part of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A8","text":"Perceptual distinction applies primarily to the things closest to or greatest relative to each monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A9","text":"The limitation of monads concerns the modification of knowledge, not the known object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A10","text":"All monads tend confusedly toward infinity and toward the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A11","text":"The degrees of distinct perception limit and distinguish the monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:A12","text":"An equally distinct representation of everything would make each monad a divinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX1","text":"The monad is not limited to representing an isolated part of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX2","text":"Universal representation is not distinct knowledge of every detail of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX3","text":"The limitation of the monad does not arise from a limitation of the represented object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX4","text":"The monads are not differentiated by wholly separate objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX5","text":"Distinct perception does not extend uniformly over the whole universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:NX6","text":"A monad is not a divinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D1","text":"Every monad contains a representation, at least confused, of the entire universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A3","CH_UCIC_P_52:A4","CH_UCIC_P_52:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D2","text":"Universal representation and distinct perception are compatible because they belong to two different degrees of knowledge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A6","CH_UCIC_P_52:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D3","text":"Each monad possesses a local field of distinct perception within a confused global representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A7","CH_UCIC_P_52:A8","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D4","text":"The difference between monads is a difference of degree in distinct knowledge rather than a difference in the extent of the represented object.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A9","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:D5","text":"Distinct knowledge of the entire universe is excluded in order to preserve the difference between monad and divinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A7","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11","CH_UCIC_P_52:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","text":"The unity of the universe is inscribed in each monad in the form of a universal representation, while the plurality of monads appears as a differential modulation of that same representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A3","CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A9","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SD2","text":"The finitude of monads is epistemic and modal rather than objectal: nothing is subtracted from their representation, but not everything is rendered equally distinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A6","CH_UCIC_P_52:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SD3","text":"The distinction among monads is produced by a variable mapping of perceptual clarity, not by a distribution of exclusive fragments of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A7","CH_UCIC_P_52:A8","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SD4","text":"The divine structure of order is preserved by maintaining simultaneously representative universality and the inequality of degrees of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A1","CH_UCIC_P_52:A2","CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CH_UCIC_P_52:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an ontology in which each monad would be only a closed point of view upon an independent portion of reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX2","text":"The system excludes an absolute separation between the represented object and the monads that represent it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX3","text":"The system excludes the equivalence between representing everything and knowing everything distinctly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a perfect equality among monads with respect to the clarity of their perceptions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX5","text":"The system excludes perceptual limitation resulting from a defect in the represented universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX6","text":"The system excludes a monadic knowledge that would abolish the difference between creature and God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX1","text":"The possibility of a finite perspective external to the universe it represents is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a totality immediately transparent to a monad is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX3","text":"An individuation founded on the absence of relation to the whole is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX4","text":"The absolute autonomy of perception is foreclosed: every point of view remains inwardly oriented toward infinity and the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX5","text":"The identification of perfection with the integral distinction of all perceptions is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS1","text":"Divine regulation of every part and every monad → inscription of a representative function in each monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS2","text":"Universal representative function → necessary representation of the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS3","text":"Representation of the entire universe → confusion of detail and absence of global distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS4","text":"Unequal distribution of distinct perception → focus upon things close to or great relative to each monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS5","text":"Displacement of the limit toward the modification of knowledge → preservation of the universality of the represented object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS6","text":"Variation in the degrees of distinct perception → differentiation of monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS7","text":"Integral perceptual distinction → suppression of the difference between monad and divinity → structural impossibility of such perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:AF1","text":"Question of the necessity of order → foundation in divine regulation → representative nature of the monad → confused representation of the entire universe → local distinction according to proximity or greatness → limitation of knowledge rather than of the object → gradual differentiation of monads → preservation of the difference between creature and God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME1","text":"The represented object is reclassified as universal for every monad, while perceptual clarity becomes the principle of limitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME2","text":"The opposition between totality and finitude is dissolved: a monad can represent the whole without knowing it distinctly in all its parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME3","text":"The difference between monads is redrawn as a difference of degrees of perception rather than as a difference of ontological territories.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME4","text":"The relation to the close and the great becomes a rule for locating distinction within a universal representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ME5","text":"Divinity is mapped as the negative threshold of integral distinct perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT1","text":"Surface — The monads represent the entire universe, but perceive it distinctly only in a small part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT2","text":"Structural — Monadic limitation is produced by degrees of distinct perception and not by a restriction of the represented object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument reframes finitude as a modality of knowledge in order to render compatible representative universality, differentiation of monads, and divine order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Each monad is a perspective internal to the whole, confusedly oriented toward infinity, without being able to attain the absolute transparency reserved for God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage from divine regulation to the universal representation of monads.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT2","text":"The distinction between represented object and modification of knowledge is indispensable to the coherence of the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT3","text":"The coexistence of representation of the whole and local distinct perception preserves the actual movement of the argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT4","text":"The structure is internally coherent so long as universal representation is not assimilated to equally distinct knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT5","text":"The principal tension lies in the articulation between the orientation of all monads toward infinity and the necessary limitation of their distinct perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT6","text":"The divine limit is maintained by a structural exclusion: the integral distinction of everything would cause the finite status of the monad to disappear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction depends on the compression of the relation among proximity, greatness, and degree of perception, which the passage states without detailing its mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_52:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_52@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_52:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 60"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 60","title":"Proposition 60","context":"Chapter 60","original_title":"Proposition 60"},"original_title":"Proposition 60","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 61","order":61,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_53"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_53@R001","sha256":"82d3b93d7206b973efdafa733fc60adddf9237a16fdd737af877d525432f763b","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS1","text":"La continuité matérielle exige que tout corps soit affecté au-delà du contact immédiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS2","text":"La plénitude transforme chaque interaction locale en communication causale à distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS3","text":"Cette communication universelle inscrit l’état de l’univers dans chaque corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS4","text":"Une intelligence qui voit tout pourrait déchiffrer l’ensemble de l’univers dans chaque corps particulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS5","text":"L’âme ne possède pas cette lisibilité intégrale, parce que ses représentations distinctes sont limitées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS6","text":"L’infinité des replis de l’âme sépare la représentation totale de la perception actuellement explicite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A1","text":"Tout est plein dans la matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A2","text":"La plénitude rend toute la matière liée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A3","text":"Tout mouvement produit un effet sur les corps distants selon leur distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A4","text":"Un corps est affecté par les corps qui le touchent directement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A5","text":"Un corps est affecté indirectement par les corps qui touchent ceux qui le touchent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","text":"La communication des effets se propage à toute distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","text":"Chaque corps porte une représentation de ce qui se fait dans l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A8","text":"Une vision totale permettrait de lire dans le présent ce qui est éloigné selon le lieu et le temps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","text":"L’âme ne lit distinctement en elle-même que ce qui y est représenté distinctement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A10","text":"Les replis de l’âme sont infinis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A11","text":"Une âme finie ne peut pas développer simultanément tous ses replis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX1","text":"La causalité matérielle n’est pas limitée au contact immédiat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX2","text":"Aucun corps n’est isolé des événements éloignés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX3","text":"La représentation universelle n’est pas identique à une perception distincte de tout l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX4","text":"L’âme ne peut pas expliciter d’un seul coup la totalité de son contenu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX5","text":"La proximité spatiale ou temporelle ne constitue pas la limite de la communication des états.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX6","text":"La capacité de contenir une représentation du tout n’implique pas la capacité humaine ou animique de la lire entièrement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D1","text":"Tout corps reçoit, directement ou par chaînes intermédiaires, l’effet de tout ce qui arrive dans l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A3","CH_UCIC_P_53:A4","CH_UCIC_P_53:A5","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D2","text":"Chaque corps constitue un indice local de l’état global de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D3","text":"Le présent de chaque corps contient des marques du passé et des déterminations du futur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","CH_UCIC_P_53:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D4","text":"La lecture intégrale de l’univers dans un corps appartient à une faculté de vision totale plutôt qu’à la perception ordinaire de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A8","CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D5","text":"La distinction perceptive dépend de l’explicitation de certains replis plutôt que de l’absence de leur contenu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD1","text":"La matière forme un réseau sans extérieur causal : chaque événement se répercute dans la totalité du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A1","CH_UCIC_P_53:A2","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD2","text":"L’individualité corporelle ne supprime pas la totalité ; elle en constitue une expression localisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD3","text":"L’ordre universel est simultanément présent dans chaque corps et inaccessible dans sa totalité à une âme finie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:A10","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD4","text":"La limitation de l’âme est une limitation d’actualisation perceptive, non une limitation de la structure représentative qu’elle contient.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:A10","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD5","text":"Le temps et la distance deviennent des degrés de lisibilité d’un ordre déjà communiqué plutôt que des barrières absolues entre les événements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une matière composée de régions causalement indépendantes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX2","text":"Il exclut une transmission qui s’arrêterait au premier corps touché.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une âme dont tout le contenu représentatif serait immédiatement transparent à elle-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une séparation absolue entre présent, passé et futur au niveau des traces inscrites dans les corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX5","text":"Il exclut que l’obscurité perceptive de l’âme provienne d’une absence de représentation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX1","text":"L’impossibilité centrale est celle d’une présence intégralement distincte du tout dans une âme finie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX2","text":"L’argument dépend de l’absence d’un point de vue fini capable de convertir instantanément toute représentation en connaissance explicite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX3","text":"Ce qui demeure indisponible n’est pas la totalité du réel, mais son déploiement simultané sous une forme distincte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX4","text":"Le système forclôt l’idée qu’une limite de connaissance puisse être une rupture de connexion avec l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS1","text":"Plénitude matérielle → liaison universelle → propagation graduée des effets.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS2","text":"Propagation à distance → inscription de chaque événement dans chaque corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS3","text":"Inscription universelle → possibilité d’une lecture du tout dans le particulier par une vision totale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS4","text":"Infinité des replis de l’âme → impossibilité du déploiement simultané de toutes les représentations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS5","text":"Représentation totale implicite + distinction perceptive partielle → écart entre contenir le tout et le connaître distinctement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AF1","text":"Plénitude de la matière → communication causale indirecte → propagation à toute distance → représentation du tout dans chaque corps → lisibilité totale pour une vision absolue → opacité partielle de l’âme finie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME1","text":"Le corps est reclassé d’un objet local en nœud représentatif de l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME2","text":"La distance est reclassée comme une modulation de l’effet et non comme une coupure causale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME3","text":"La perception est dissociée de la représentation : ne pas distinguer un contenu ne signifie pas en être dépourvu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME4","text":"Le présent est reconfiguré comme surface de lecture de déterminations éloignées, antérieures et ultérieures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME5","text":"La limite de l’âme devient une limite de déploiement et non une limitation de son inscription dans l’ordre universel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Les corps s’affectent mutuellement à distance, tandis que l’âme ne distingue qu’une partie de ce qu’elle contient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — La matière constitue un continuum causal où chaque état se transmet par médiations successives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — L’argument recadre l’ignorance comme défaut d’explicitation perceptive plutôt que comme absence de liaison au réel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Chaque entité exprime le tout, et le présent conserve des déterminations relatives à des événements éloignés dans l’espace et le temps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes relatifs à la plénitude, à la propagation des effets et à la représentation universelle suffisent à reconstruire la première moitié de l’argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT2","text":"Les axiomes relatifs aux replis infinis et à la perception distincte suffisent à reconstruire la limitation de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT3","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la représentation universelle est distinguée de l’aperception distincte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT4","text":"La relation exacte entre « symboliser », représenter et lire reste partiellement sous-déterminée par le passage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT5","text":"L’identification d’une vision totale avec un accès au passé et au futur repose sur une formulation théorique condensée plutôt que sur une démonstration développée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : de la continuité causale de la matière à l’écart entre expression universelle et explicitation psychique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193843641955Z_aa16478f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 61","source_sha256":"82d3b93d7206b973efdafa733fc60adddf9237a16fdd737af877d525432f763b","sha256":"04781577e8b84222e39e05e44e40f3e95a0e4ad75dc86bdd7fbcce693d7c69a3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:38:43.647495+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS1","text":"Material continuity requires that every body be affected beyond immediate contact.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS2","text":"Plenitude transforms every local interaction into causal communication at a distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS3","text":"This universal communication inscribes the state of the universe in every body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS4","text":"An intelligence that sees everything could decipher the entirety of the universe in each particular body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS5","text":"The soul does not possess this integral legibility, because its distinct representations are limited.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AS6","text":"The infinity of the soul's folds separates total representation from presently explicit perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A1","text":"Everything is full in matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A2","text":"Plenitude makes all matter connected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A3","text":"Every movement produces an effect on distant bodies according to their distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A4","text":"A body is affected by the bodies that directly touch it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A5","text":"A body is indirectly affected by the bodies that touch those which touch it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","text":"The communication of effects propagates over every distance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","text":"Each body bears a representation of what takes place in the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A8","text":"A total vision would make it possible to read in the present what is distant in place and time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","text":"The soul reads distinctly within itself only what is distinctly represented there.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A10","text":"The folds of the soul are infinite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:A11","text":"A finite soul cannot simultaneously unfold all its folds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX1","text":"Material causality is not limited to immediate contact.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX2","text":"No body is isolated from distant events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX3","text":"Universal representation is not identical with a distinct perception of the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX4","text":"The soul cannot explicate the totality of its content all at once.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX5","text":"Spatial or temporal proximity does not constitute the limit of the communication of states.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:NX6","text":"The capacity to contain a representation of the whole does not imply the human or psychic capacity to read it entirely.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D1","text":"Every body receives, directly or through intermediary chains, the effect of everything that happens in the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A3","CH_UCIC_P_53:A4","CH_UCIC_P_53:A5","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D2","text":"Each body constitutes a local index of the global state of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D3","text":"The present of each body contains marks of the past and determinations of the future.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","CH_UCIC_P_53:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D4","text":"The integral reading of the universe in a body belongs to a faculty of total vision rather than to the ordinary perception of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A8","CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:D5","text":"Perceptual distinction depends on the explication of certain folds rather than on the absence of their content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD1","text":"Matter forms a network without a causal exterior: every event reverberates throughout the entirety of the system.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A1","CH_UCIC_P_53:A2","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD2","text":"Bodily individuality does not eliminate totality; it constitutes a localized expression of it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD3","text":"The universal order is simultaneously present in every body and inaccessible in its totality to a finite soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:A10","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD4","text":"The limitation of the soul is a limitation of perceptual actualization, not a limitation of the representative structure it contains.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:A10","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SD5","text":"Time and distance become degrees of legibility of an order already communicated rather than absolute barriers between events.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX1","text":"The system excludes matter composed of causally independent regions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX2","text":"It excludes a transmission that would stop at the first body touched.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX3","text":"It excludes a soul whose entire representative content would be immediately transparent to itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX4","text":"It excludes an absolute separation between present, past, and future at the level of traces inscribed in bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX5","text":"It excludes the possibility that the perceptual obscurity of the soul derives from an absence of representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX1","text":"The central impossibility is that of an integrally distinct presence of the whole in a finite soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX2","text":"The argument depends on the absence of a finite point of view capable of instantaneously converting every representation into explicit knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX3","text":"What remains unavailable is not the totality of the real, but its simultaneous unfolding in a distinct form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX4","text":"The system forecloses the idea that a limit of knowledge could be a rupture of connection with the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS1","text":"Material plenitude → universal connection → graduated propagation of effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS2","text":"Propagation at a distance → inscription of each event in each body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS3","text":"Universal inscription → possibility of reading the whole in the particular through a total vision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS4","text":"Infinity of the soul's folds → impossibility of the simultaneous unfolding of all representations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS5","text":"Implicit total representation + partial perceptual distinction → gap between containing the whole and knowing it distinctly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:AF1","text":"Plenitude of matter → indirect causal communication → propagation over every distance → representation of the whole in each body → total legibility for an absolute vision → partial opacity of the finite soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME1","text":"The body is reclassified from a local object into a representative node of the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME2","text":"Distance is reclassified as a modulation of effect and not as a causal break.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME3","text":"Perception is dissociated from representation: not distinguishing a content does not mean being devoid of it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME4","text":"The present is reconfigured as a surface for reading distant, prior, and subsequent determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ME5","text":"The limit of the soul becomes a limit of unfolding and not a limitation of its inscription in the universal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Bodies affect one another at a distance, while the soul distinguishes only a part of what it contains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Matter constitutes a causal continuum in which every state is transmitted through successive mediations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The argument reframes ignorance as a defect of perceptual explication rather than as an absence of connection to the real.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Each entity expresses the whole, and the present preserves determinations relating to events distant in space and time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT1","text":"The axioms concerning plenitude, the propagation of effects, and universal representation suffice to reconstruct the first half of the argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT2","text":"The axioms concerning infinite folds and distinct perception suffice to reconstruct the limitation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent if universal representation is distinguished from distinct apperception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT4","text":"The exact relation among « symboliser », representing, and reading remains partially underdetermined by the passage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT5","text":"The identification of a total vision with access to the past and future rests on a condensed theoretical formulation rather than on a developed demonstration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: from the causal continuity of matter to the gap between universal expression and psychic explication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_53:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_53@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_53:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 61"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 61","title":"Proposition 61","context":"Chapter 61","original_title":"Proposition 61"},"original_title":"Proposition 61","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 62","order":62,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_54"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_54@R001","sha256":"2e366430167f9392c2af340c2d0cadd3bef2d27783037c87531d9a3cd101ca1f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS1","text":"La monade créée doit être pensée comme représentation de l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS2","text":"Cette représentation universelle comporte des degrés de distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS3","text":"La monade représente plus distinctement le corps qui lui est particulièrement affecté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS4","text":"La monade est l’entéléchie de ce corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS5","text":"Le corps exprime l’univers parce que toute la matière est reliée dans le plein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS6","text":"L’âme représente donc l’univers en représentant distinctement le corps qui lui appartient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","text":"Toute monade créée représente l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","text":"Une représentation peut être plus ou moins distincte selon son objet privilégié.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","text":"Chaque monade créée est associée à un corps particulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A4","text":"La monade constitue l’entéléchie de son corps particulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","text":"Le corps exprime l’univers par la connexion de toute la matière dans le plein.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A6","text":"L’âme représente l’univers en représentant son corps particulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A7","text":"La représentation du particulier fonctionne comme médiation de la représentation de l’universel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX1","text":"La monade n’est pas une représentation limitée à un fragment isolé de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX2","text":"La représentation universelle n’est pas uniformément distincte en tous ses points.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX3","text":"Le corps particulier n’est pas séparé de l’univers matériel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX4","text":"L’âme n’est pas définie comme une représentation indépendante de son corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX5","text":"Le corps n’est pas une totalité close sur elle-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX6","text":"La particularité d’un corps n’abolit pas son expression de l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D1","text":"La monade possède une perspective singulière sur un univers qu’elle représente néanmoins tout entier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D2","text":"Le corps particulier devient le lieu de concentration de la représentation universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D3","text":"L’entéléchie relie l’activité représentative de la monade à l’organisation de son corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D4","text":"La connexion matérielle transforme l’expression du corps en expression de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D5","text":"La représentation de l’univers par l’âme est indirectement universelle et directement corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","CH_UCIC_P_54:A6","CH_UCIC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SD1","text":"L’universalité de la monade ne supprime pas sa singularité ; elle se réalise à travers une articulation privilégiée à un corps particulier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SD2","text":"Le rapport entre âme et corps est constitutif de la connaissance représentative de l’univers, et non une simple relation entre deux substances juxtaposées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A4","CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","CH_UCIC_P_54:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SD3","text":"Le particulier devient universellement expressif en vertu de la structure relationnelle du plein.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SD4","text":"La distinction des monades provient de la différence de leurs expressions distinctes plutôt que d’une différence de monde représenté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une représentation universelle exige une perception également distincte de toutes les choses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’un corps puisse être défini indépendamment de la totalité matérielle à laquelle il est connecté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut que l’âme accède à l’univers sans la médiation de son incarnation corporelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut que la singularité soit produite par une limitation à un domaine local absolument séparé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX5","text":"Le système exclut une conception purement externe du rapport entre monade, âme et corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’un univers composé de parties sans connexion intégrale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX2","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’une âme dont l’universalité serait indépendante de toute perspective corporelle singulière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX3","text":"Est forclose l’opposition entre totalité universelle et détermination individuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX4","text":"Est rendue inadmissible l’idée d’une représentation sans point d’ancrage particulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS1","text":"Représentation universelle de la monade → différenciation des degrés de distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS2","text":"Différenciation de la distinction → privilège représentatif accordé au corps particulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS3","text":"Affectation d’un corps particulier → constitution de la monade comme entéléchie de ce corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS4","text":"Connexion de toute la matière dans le plein → expression de l’univers par le corps particulier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS5","text":"Expression universelle du corps → représentation de l’univers par l’âme à travers ce corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS6","text":"Universalité représentée par médiation corporelle → unité de l’universel et du singulier dans la monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AF1","text":"Représentation de l’univers entier → distinction différentielle → corps particulièrement affecté → monade comme entéléchie → connexion matérielle du plein → expression universelle du corps → représentation universelle de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME1","text":"Le corps particulier est reclassé comme centre de concentration de l’universel plutôt que comme portion isolée du monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME2","text":"La distinction entre universel et particulier est transformée en différence de degré de représentation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME3","text":"Le rapport âme-corps est cartographié comme une médiation interne de l’expression universelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME4","text":"Le plein matériel est reclassé comme condition d’expressivité réciproque des parties et du tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME5","text":"La singularité monadique devient une perspective déterminée sur la totalité plutôt qu’une restriction ontologique de la totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Une monade représente l’univers, mais représente plus distinctement le corps qui lui est affecté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — La connexion de toute la matière dans le plein fait du corps particulier une expression de l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — La particularité n’est plus traitée comme une limitation concurrente de l’universalité, mais comme son mode de manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — L’être de la monade est défini par une relation constitutive entre représentation, entéléchie, corps et totalité matérielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le passage de la représentation universelle à la représentation corporelle distincte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT2","text":"La structure préserve la médiation décisive du corps entre l’âme et l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT3","text":"La cohérence interne dépend de l’acceptation du plein comme totalité matériellement connectée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT4","text":"Le système reste sous-déterminé quant à la nature exacte de l’« affection » du corps par la monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT5","text":"Le statut précis de l’âme par rapport à la monade n’est pas entièrement explicité dans la proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT6","text":"La force de l’argument réside dans l’enchaînement entre connexion matérielle et expressivité universelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT7","text":"La tension principale oppose la totalité représentée à la distinction privilégiée d’un seul corps sans que cette opposition soit résolue par séparation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT8","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : univers représenté → corps distinctement représenté → univers réexprimé par le corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193900480363Z_0799f8c5","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 62","source_sha256":"2e366430167f9392c2af340c2d0cadd3bef2d27783037c87531d9a3cd101ca1f","sha256":"54407a4d90d767d5c44455dd1abf789885cffea6a5d05f2512eb851b517c80e6","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:39:00.483742+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS1","text":"The created monad must be conceived as a representation of the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS2","text":"This universal representation includes degrees of distinctness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS3","text":"The monad represents more distinctly the body that is particularly affected by it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS4","text":"The monad is the entelechy of this body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS5","text":"The body expresses the universe because all matter is connected in the plenum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AS6","text":"The soul therefore represents the universe by distinctly representing the body that belongs to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","text":"Every created monad represents the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","text":"A representation can be more or less distinct according to its privileged object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","text":"Each created monad is associated with a particular body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A4","text":"The monad constitutes the entelechy of its particular body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","text":"The body expresses the universe through the connection of all matter in the plenum.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A6","text":"The soul represents the universe by representing its particular body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:A7","text":"The representation of the particular functions as mediation of the representation of the universal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX1","text":"The monad is not a representation limited to an isolated fragment of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX2","text":"Universal representation is not uniformly distinct at all its points.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX3","text":"The particular body is not separate from the material universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX4","text":"The soul is not defined as a representation independent of its body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX5","text":"The body is not a totality closed upon itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:NX6","text":"The particularity of a body does not abolish its expression of the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D1","text":"The monad has a singular perspective on a universe that it nevertheless represents in its entirety.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D2","text":"The particular body becomes the locus of concentration of universal representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D3","text":"The entelechy connects the representational activity of the monad to the organization of its body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D4","text":"Material connection transforms the expression of the body into an expression of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:D5","text":"The representation of the universe by the soul is indirectly universal and directly corporeal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","CH_UCIC_P_54:A6","CH_UCIC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SD1","text":"The universality of the monad does not eliminate its singularity; it is realized through a privileged articulation with a particular body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SD2","text":"The relation between soul and body is constitutive of representational knowledge of the universe, and not a mere relation between two juxtaposed substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A4","CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","CH_UCIC_P_54:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SD3","text":"The particular becomes universally expressive by virtue of the relational structure of the plenum.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SD4","text":"The distinction of monads stems from the difference in their distinct expressions rather than from a difference in the world represented.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a universal representation requires an equally distinct perception of all things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a body can be defined independently of the material totality to which it is connected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX3","text":"The system excludes the possibility that the soul gains access to the universe without the mediation of its corporeal incarnation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the possibility that singularity is produced by a limitation to an absolutely separate local domain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX5","text":"The system excludes a purely external conception of the relation among monad, soul, and body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX1","text":"Foreclosed is the possibility of a universe composed of parts without integral connection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX2","text":"Foreclosed is the possibility of a soul whose universality would be independent of every singular corporeal perspective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX3","text":"Foreclosed is the opposition between universal totality and individual determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX4","text":"The idea of a representation without a particular point of anchorage is rendered inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS1","text":"Universal representation of the monad → differentiation of degrees of distinctness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS2","text":"Differentiation of distinctness → representational privilege granted to the particular body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS3","text":"Assignment of a particular body → constitution of the monad as the entelechy of this body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS4","text":"Connection of all matter in the plenum → expression of the universe by the particular body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS5","text":"Universal expression of the body → representation of the universe by the soul through this body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:FGS6","text":"Universality represented through corporeal mediation → unity of the universal and the singular in the monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:AF1","text":"Representation of the entire universe → differential distinctness → particularly affected body → monad as entelechy → material connection of the plenum → universal expression of the body → universal representation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME1","text":"The particular body is reclassified as a center of concentration of the universal rather than as an isolated portion of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME2","text":"The distinction between universal and particular is transformed into a difference in degree of representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME3","text":"The soul-body relation is mapped as an internal mediation of universal expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME4","text":"The material plenum is reclassified as the condition of the reciprocal expressivity of the parts and the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ME5","text":"Monadic singularity becomes a determinate perspective on totality rather than an ontological restriction of totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — A monad represents the universe, but represents more distinctly the body affected by it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The connection of all matter in the plenum makes the particular body an expression of the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Particularity is no longer treated as a limitation competing with universality, but as its mode of manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — The being of the monad is defined by a constitutive relation among representation, entelechy, body, and material totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage from universal representation to distinct corporeal representation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT2","text":"The structure preserves the decisive mediation of the body between the soul and the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence depends on accepting the plenum as a materially connected totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT4","text":"The system remains underdetermined as to the exact nature of the monad’s “affection” of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT5","text":"The precise status of the soul in relation to the monad is not fully made explicit in the proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT6","text":"The force of the argument lies in the sequence between material connection and universal expressivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT7","text":"The principal tension opposes represented totality to the privileged distinctness of a single body, without this opposition being resolved through separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: represented universe → distinctly represented body → universe re-expressed through the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_54:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_54@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_54:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 62"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 62","title":"Proposition 62","context":"Chapter 62","original_title":"Proposition 62"},"original_title":"Proposition 62","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 63","order":63,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_55"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_55@R001","sha256":"5ad150a08443028f636fa81e0b54dd015ad526e95cb6287abdb3055b594ba3bf","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS1","text":"Le texte détermine les compositions ontologiques formées par la monade, son entéléchie ou son âme, et le corps qui lui appartient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS2","text":"La composition du corps avec l’entéléchie produit un vivant, tandis que sa composition avec l’âme produit un animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS3","text":"Le corps du vivant ou de l’animal est nécessairement organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS4","text":"Cette organicité est fondée sur la fonction représentative de toute monade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS5","text":"Parce que l’univers est ordonné, sa représentation dans les perceptions de l’âme doit également comporter un ordre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS6","text":"L’ordre perceptif de l’âme se prolonge dans l’ordre organique du corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A1","text":"Toute monade possède un corps qui lui appartient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","text":"L’entéléchie d’une monade est son âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","text":"Le corps et l’entéléchie constituent un vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A4","text":"Le corps et l’âme constituent un animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","text":"Toute monade est un miroir de l’univers selon son mode propre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","text":"L’univers est réglé selon un ordre parfait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","text":"La représentation monadique de l’univers s’effectue dans les perceptions de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","text":"L’ordre de l’univers doit être représenté par un ordre correspondant dans les perceptions de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A9","text":"L’ordre perceptif de l’âme détermine un ordre dans le corps qui la représente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A10","text":"Le corps appartenant à une monade est organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX1","text":"Le corps d’un vivant ou d’un animal n’est pas une matière dépourvue d’organisation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX2","text":"La représentation monadique n’est pas une reproduction uniforme de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX3","text":"L’ordre du corps n’est pas indépendant de l’ordre des perceptions de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX4","text":"Le vivant n’est pas constitué par le corps seul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX5","text":"L’animal n’est pas défini par le corps séparé de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D1","text":"Le corps reçoit son statut de vivant par son union avec l’entéléchie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D2","text":"Le corps reçoit son statut d’animal par son union avec l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D3","text":"La différence entre vivant et animal est produite par le terme immatériel avec lequel le corps est considéré : entéléchie ou âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D4","text":"La structure organique du corps est la conséquence corporelle de la représentation ordonnée de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D5","text":"L’organicité du corps est expliquée par une continuité entre ordre universel, perception de l’âme et organisation corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SD1","text":"Le vivant est une unité stratifiée dans laquelle l’organisation corporelle dépend d’une structure représentative portée par la monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A1","CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2","text":"L’ordre cosmique se distribue à travers la monade jusqu’à devenir l’ordre perceptif de l’âme et l’ordre organique du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SD3","text":"L’animalité et la vitalité sont des déterminations relationnelles du corps, et non des propriétés isolables du corps matériel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SD4","text":"La pluralité des corps organiques est compatible avec l’unité de l’ordre universel parce que chaque monade le représente selon son mode propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX1","text":"Le système ne peut pas admettre un corps vivant dont l’organisation serait sans rapport avec les perceptions de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX2","text":"Le système ne peut pas admettre une représentation monadique absolument désordonnée de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX3","text":"Le système ne peut pas expliquer l’organicité par la seule composition matérielle du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX4","text":"Le système ne peut pas séparer radicalement l’ordre cosmique, l’ordre perceptif et l’ordre corporel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’un corps organique autosuffisant, dont la structure ne procéderait d’aucune médiation monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX2","text":"Est exclue la possibilité d’un univers ordonné qui ne se prolongerait pas dans les niveaux perceptif et corporel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX3","text":"L’absence structurante du système est celle d’une matière vivante indépendante de toute âme, entéléchie et représentation ordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS1","text":"Monade → miroir modal de l’univers → perception de l’ordre universel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS2","text":"Ordre parfait de l’univers → nécessité d’un ordre dans sa représentation monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS3","text":"Perception ordonnée de l’âme → détermination d’un ordre correspondant dans le corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS4","text":"Ordre corporel → organicité du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS5","text":"Corps + entéléchie → vivant ; corps + âme → animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AF1","text":"Composition du corps avec l’entéléchie ou l’âme → détermination du vivant et de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AF2","text":"Détermination du vivant et de l’animal → exigence d’un corps organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AF3","text":"Corps organique → miroir monadique de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AF4","text":"Ordre parfait de l’univers → ordre des perceptions de l’âme → ordre du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1","text":"Le corps est reclassé comme niveau corporel d’une représentation ordonnée de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ME2","text":"La distinction entre vivant et animal est déplacée du plan matériel vers le plan des relations entre corps, entéléchie et âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ME3","text":"L’organicité n’apparaît plus comme une propriété première, mais comme l’effet d’une correspondance entre ordre cosmique, perception et corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ME4","text":"L’univers, la monade, l’âme et le corps sont cartographiés sur une même chaîne d’ordre représentatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT1","text":"Surface : le corps associé à l’entéléchie ou à l’âme constitue respectivement un vivant ou un animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT2","text":"Structural : l’organicité du corps résulte de l’ordre inscrit dans les perceptions de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic : l’explication se déplace de la constitution matérielle du corps vers la médiation représentative de la monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal : l’ordre universel se reproduit hiérarchiquement dans la monade, la perception et le corps, sans rupture entre les niveaux de réalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire la distinction entre vivant, animal et corps organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A1","CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT2","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage de l’ordre universel à l’ordre corporel par l’intermédiaire des perceptions de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT3","text":"La cohérence interne repose sur l’hypothèse d’une continuité nécessaire entre représentation et organisation corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT4","text":"La relation précise par laquelle l’ordre des perceptions produit l’ordre organique du corps reste sous-déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel de l’argument : composition ontologique → organicité → représentation ordonnée → correspondance corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193916149505Z_77752237","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 63","source_sha256":"5ad150a08443028f636fa81e0b54dd015ad526e95cb6287abdb3055b594ba3bf","sha256":"66cb468ce89055bbdad9e3de0590e4cafce703f416e4d32062dd19ce82beef4f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:39:16.155328+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS1","text":"The text determines the ontological compositions formed by the monad, its entelechy or its soul, and the body that belongs to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS2","text":"The composition of the body with entelechy produces a living being, whereas its composition with the soul produces an animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS3","text":"The body of the living being or of the animal is necessarily organic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS4","text":"This organicity is grounded in the representative function of every monad.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS5","text":"Because the universe is ordered, its representation in the perceptions of the soul must likewise include an order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AS6","text":"The perceptual order of the soul extends into the organic order of the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A1","text":"Every monad possesses a body that belongs to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","text":"The entelechy of a monad is its soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","text":"The body and entelechy constitute a living being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A4","text":"The body and the soul constitute an animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","text":"Every monad is a mirror of the universe according to its own mode.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","text":"The universe is regulated according to a perfect order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","text":"The monadic representation of the universe takes place in the perceptions of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","text":"The order of the universe must be represented by a corresponding order in the perceptions of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A9","text":"The perceptual order of the soul determines an order in the body that represents it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:A10","text":"The body belonging to a monad is organic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX1","text":"The body of a living being or an animal is not matter devoid of organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX2","text":"Monadic representation is not a uniform reproduction of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX3","text":"The order of the body is not independent of the order of the perceptions of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX4","text":"The living being is not constituted by the body alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:NX5","text":"The animal is not defined by the body separated from the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D1","text":"The body receives its status as a living being through its union with entelechy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D2","text":"The body receives its status as an animal through its union with the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D3","text":"The difference between living being and animal is produced by the immaterial term with which the body is considered: entelechy or soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D4","text":"The organic structure of the body is the corporeal consequence of the ordered representation of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:D5","text":"The organicity of the body is explained by a continuity between universal order, perception of the soul, and corporeal organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SD1","text":"The living being is a stratified unity in which corporeal organization depends on a representative structure borne by the monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A1","CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2","text":"Cosmic order is distributed through the monad until it becomes the perceptual order of the soul and the organic order of the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SD3","text":"Animality and vitality are relational determinations of the body, and not isolable properties of the material body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SD4","text":"The plurality of organic bodies is compatible with the unity of universal order because each monad represents it according to its own mode.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX1","text":"The system cannot admit a living body whose organization would bear no relation to the perceptions of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX2","text":"The system cannot admit an absolutely disordered monadic representation of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX3","text":"The system cannot explain organicity by the material composition of the body alone.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX4","text":"The system cannot radically separate cosmic order, perceptual order, and corporeal order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX1","text":"Foreclosed is the possibility of a self-sufficient organic body whose structure would proceed from no monadic mediation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX2","text":"Excluded is the possibility of an ordered universe that would not extend into the perceptual and corporeal levels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX3","text":"The structuring absence of the system is that of living matter independent of every soul, entelechy, and ordered representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS1","text":"Monad → modal mirror of the universe → perception of universal order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS2","text":"Perfect order of the universe → necessity of an order in its monadic representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS3","text":"Ordered perception of the soul → determination of a corresponding order in the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS4","text":"Corporeal order → organicity of the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS5","text":"Body + entelechy → living being; body + soul → animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AF1","text":"Composition of the body with entelechy or the soul → determination of the living being and the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AF2","text":"Determination of the living being and the animal → requirement of an organic body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AF3","text":"Organic body → monadic mirror of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:AF4","text":"Perfect order of the universe → order of the perceptions of the soul → order of the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1","text":"The body is reclassified as the corporeal level of an ordered representation of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ME2","text":"The distinction between living being and animal is shifted from the material plane to the plane of relations among body, entelechy, and soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ME3","text":"Organicity no longer appears as a primary property, but as the effect of a correspondence between cosmic order, perception, and body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ME4","text":"The universe, the monad, the soul, and the body are mapped onto a single chain of representative order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT1","text":"Surface: the body associated with entelechy or the soul constitutes respectively a living being or an animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT2","text":"Structural: the organicity of the body results from the order inscribed in the perceptions of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: the explanation shifts from the material constitution of the body toward the representative mediation of the monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: universal order is hierarchically reproduced in the monad, perception, and body, without rupture between the levels of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the distinction between living being, animal, and organic body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A1","CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4","CH_UCIC_P_55:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT2","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage from universal order to corporeal order by means of the perceptions of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT3","text":"Internal coherence rests on the hypothesis of a necessary continuity between representation and corporeal organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A7","CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT4","text":"The precise relation by which the order of perceptions produces the organic order of the body remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the argument: ontological composition → organicity → ordered representation → corporeal correspondence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_55:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_55@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_55:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 63"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 63","title":"Proposition 63","context":"Chapter 63","original_title":"Proposition 63"},"original_title":"Proposition 63","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 64","order":64,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_56"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_56@R001","sha256":"6461d0bfbe0170f4f30ca8a5f60f47c7a25a0930f3c949f3085556b0b2684f3c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS1","text":"Le problème consiste à distinguer les machines artificielles des corps vivants malgré leur commune détermination machinique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS2","text":"Le texte recadre le vivant comme une machine naturelle ou un automate naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS3","text":"La supériorité du vivant tient à la conservation de la machinicité dans chacune de ses parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS4","text":"L’exemple de la roue artificielle établit que la machine produite par l’art cesse d’être machine dans ses composants ultimes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS5","text":"La machine naturelle maintient au contraire la structure machinique de ses parties jusqu’à l’infini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS6","text":"L’argument progresse ainsi de la comparaison entre artefact et organisme vers une différence structurelle de composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A1","text":"Tout corps organique d’un vivant est une machine naturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A2","text":"Tout corps organique d’un vivant est un automate naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A3","text":"Les machines naturelles surpassent infiniment les automates artificiels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A4","text":"Une machine artificielle n’est pas machine dans chacune de ses parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A5","text":"Les composants ultimes d’une machine artificielle peuvent perdre toute marque de leur fonction machinique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","text":"Les corps vivants restent machines dans leurs moindres parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A7","text":"La machinicité des corps vivants se prolonge jusqu’à l’infini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A8","text":"La différence entre nature et art se détermine par le régime de composition interne des machines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX1","text":"Une machine naturelle n’est pas assimilable à une machine artificielle simplement parce que toutes deux sont des machines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX2","text":"La machine artificielle n’est pas machinique dans chacune de ses parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX3","text":"Une partie matérielle d’un artefact n’est pas nécessairement porteuse de la fonction qui définit l’ensemble.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX4","text":"La réduction du vivant à un assemblage dont les éléments cessent d’être machines est exclue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX5","text":"La supériorité du vivant ne repose pas seulement sur sa fonction globale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX6","text":"L’automate naturel n’est pas un automate artificiel perfectionné par simple augmentation quantitative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D1","text":"La différence entre organisme et artefact porte sur chaque niveau de composition, et non sur la seule organisation globale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A4","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D2","text":"Dans l’artefact, la fonction machinique est interrompue par l’analyse des parties ; dans le vivant, elle est reconduite à chaque niveau.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A5","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D3","text":"L’infinité des structures internes constitue le critère opératoire de la supériorité des machines naturelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A3","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D4","text":"La partie organique conserve une relation machinique avec le vivant auquel elle appartient.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A1","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D5","text":"L’opposition nature-art est transformée en opposition entre une machinicité continue et une machinicité limitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A4","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7","CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SD1","text":"Le vivant est défini comme une organisation sans dernier niveau où la structure machinique s’abolirait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A1","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SD2","text":"La distinction entre naturel et artificiel devient une différence de profondeur compositionnelle plutôt qu’une différence d’opposition entre mécanisme et non-mécanisme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A3","CH_UCIC_P_56:A4","CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SD3","text":"L’organisme impose une conception récursive de la machine : chaque partie reproduit la détermination machinique du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A1","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SD4","text":"L’infini n’est pas ici une absence de structure, mais la continuation indéfinie de la structure dans la matière organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une analyse matérielle puisse atteindre, dans le vivant, une partie absolument dépourvue de machinicité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’une organisation puisse être considérée comme véritablement naturelle si ses éléments cessent d’exprimer l’organisation du tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une hiérarchie où seule la totalité serait organisée et où les parties seraient ontologiquement brutes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une conception de la nature fondée sur des unités ultimes non structurées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX5","text":"Il exclut que la différence entre vivant et artefact soit réductible à la seule origine divine ou humaine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX1","text":"Le texte forclôt l’existence d’un dernier élément matériel simple qui interromprait la continuité de la machine naturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX2","text":"Il rend inadmissible une séparation absolue entre mécanisme du tout et inertie des parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX3","text":"Il traite comme impossible une nature composée d’éléments définitivement extérieurs à toute organisation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX4","text":"Il laisse hors champ une matière organique qui ne serait qu’un support passif de la forme vivante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS1","text":"Corps organique → qualification comme machine naturelle et automate naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS2","text":"Machine artificielle → décomposition en parties → disparition de la machinicité dans les composants ultimes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS3","text":"Machine naturelle → décomposition en parties → maintien de la machinicité dans chaque partie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS4","text":"Maintien récursif de la structure → prolongation jusqu’à l’infini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS5","text":"Continuité machinique infinie → supériorité structurelle de la nature sur l’artifice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AF1","text":"Corps vivant → machine naturelle → comparaison avec l’artefact → défaut de machinicité des parties artificielles → machinicité persistante des parties organiques → supériorité du vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AF2","text":"Fonction globale commune → différence de composition interne → opposition entre interruption artificielle et continuité naturelle → infinité organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ME1","text":"Le vivant est reclassé : il n’est pas seulement organisé, il est une machine dont chaque partie est encore une machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ME2","text":"La différence entre nature et art est déplacée du plan de la fonction vers celui de la profondeur compositionnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ME3","text":"La partie cesse d’être un résidu matériel extérieur à l’organisation et devient un niveau local de la même structure machinique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ME4","text":"L’infini devient un principe de cartographie interne du vivant, et non une simple grandeur attribuée à sa perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le corps organique est déclaré machine divine ou automate naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT2","text":"Structural — La différence décisive réside dans la persistance ou l’interruption de la machinicité à travers les parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La comparaison avec l’artefact sert à déplacer le critère de supériorité vers l’organisation interne plutôt que vers la seule apparence fonctionnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Le vivant est pensé comme une totalité sans dernier niveau de décomposition où l’organisation cesserait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire la distinction entre machine naturelle et machine artificielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT2","text":"La chaîne générative principale est cohérente : organisme → machinicité des parties → infinité de la structure → supériorité naturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT3","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement comparatif qui produit la thèse à partir de l’exemple de la roue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT4","text":"La portée exacte de « jusqu’à l’infini » reste sous-déterminée entre infinité actuelle de la composition et divisibilité sans terme ultime.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT5","text":"La qualification « divine » ajoute une attribution métaphysique dont le mécanisme argumentatif dépend moins que de la continuité machinique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT6","text":"La tension principale oppose l’image de la machine à l’absence d’un élément final qui puisse être identifié comme simple ou non machinique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193933193409Z_c8c89ba7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 64","source_sha256":"6461d0bfbe0170f4f30ca8a5f60f47c7a25a0930f3c949f3085556b0b2684f3c","sha256":"ff14a25709ac6f2c3608c2ecf2b180132915d7ed842dadd30dd76dbd748a2ba3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:39:33.196674+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS1","text":"The problem consists in distinguishing artificial machines from living bodies despite their shared machinic determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS2","text":"The text reframes the living being as a natural machine or a natural automaton.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS3","text":"The superiority of the living being lies in the preservation of machinicity in each of its parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS4","text":"The example of the artificial wheel establishes that the machine produced by art ceases to be a machine in its ultimate components.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS5","text":"The natural machine, by contrast, maintains the machinic structure of its parts to infinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AS6","text":"The argument thus proceeds from the comparison between artifact and organism toward a structural difference of composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A1","text":"Every organic body of a living being is a natural machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A2","text":"Every organic body of a living being is a natural automaton.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A3","text":"Natural machines infinitely surpass artificial automatons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A4","text":"An artificial machine is not a machine in each of its parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A5","text":"The ultimate components of an artificial machine can lose every mark of their machinic function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","text":"Living bodies remain machines in their smallest parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A7","text":"The machinicity of living bodies extends to infinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:A8","text":"The difference between nature and art is determined by the regime of internal composition of machines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX1","text":"A natural machine cannot be assimilated to an artificial machine merely because both are machines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX2","text":"The artificial machine is not machinic in each of its parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX3","text":"A material part of an artifact does not necessarily bear the function that defines the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX4","text":"The reduction of the living being to an assembly whose elements cease to be machines is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX5","text":"The superiority of the living being does not rest solely on its global function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:NX6","text":"The natural automaton is not an artificial automaton perfected through mere quantitative increase.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D1","text":"The difference between organism and artifact concerns every level of composition, and not global organization alone.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A4","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D2","text":"In the artifact, machinic function is interrupted by the analysis of parts; in the living being, it is reiterated at every level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A5","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D3","text":"The infinity of internal structures constitutes the operative criterion of the superiority of natural machines.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A3","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D4","text":"The organic part preserves a machinic relation with the living being to which it belongs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A1","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:D5","text":"The nature-art opposition is transformed into an opposition between continuous machinicity and limited machinicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A4","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7","CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SD1","text":"The living being is defined as an organization without a final level at which the machinic structure would be abolished.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A1","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SD2","text":"The distinction between natural and artificial becomes a difference of compositional depth rather than a difference of opposition between mechanism and non-mechanism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A3","CH_UCIC_P_56:A4","CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SD3","text":"The organism imposes a recursive conception of the machine: each part reproduces the machinic determination of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A1","CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SD4","text":"Infinity is here not an absence of structure, but the indefinite continuation of structure in organic matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A6","CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a material analysis could reach, in the living being, a part absolutely devoid of machinicity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that an organization could be regarded as truly natural if its elements cease to express the organization of the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX3","text":"It excludes a hierarchy in which only the totality would be organized and the parts would be ontologically brute.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX4","text":"It excludes a conception of nature founded on unstructured ultimate units.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX5","text":"It excludes the possibility that the difference between living being and artifact be reducible to divine or human origin alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX1","text":"The text forecloses the existence of a final simple material element that would interrupt the continuity of the natural machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX2","text":"It renders inadmissible an absolute separation between the mechanism of the whole and the inertia of the parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX3","text":"It treats as impossible a nature composed of elements definitively external to every organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX4","text":"It leaves outside its scope an organic matter that would be merely a passive support of living form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS1","text":"Organic body → qualification as natural machine and natural automaton.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS2","text":"Artificial machine → decomposition into parts → disappearance of machinicity in the ultimate components.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS3","text":"Natural machine → decomposition into parts → maintenance of machinicity in each part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS4","text":"Recursive maintenance of structure → extension to infinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS5","text":"Infinite machinic continuity → structural superiority of nature over artifice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AF1","text":"Living body → natural machine → comparison with the artifact → deficiency of machinicity in artificial parts → persistent machinicity of organic parts → superiority of the living being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:AF2","text":"Shared global function → difference of internal composition → opposition between artificial interruption and natural continuity → organic infinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ME1","text":"The living being is reclassified: it is not merely organized; it is a machine each of whose parts is still a machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ME2","text":"The difference between nature and art is displaced from the plane of function to that of compositional depth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ME3","text":"The part ceases to be a material residue external to organization and becomes a local level of the same machinic structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ME4","text":"Infinity becomes a principle of the internal mapping of the living being, rather than a mere magnitude attributed to its perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT1","text":"Surface — The organic body is declared a divine machine or natural automaton.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT2","text":"Structural — The decisive difference lies in the persistence or interruption of machinicity across the parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The comparison with the artifact serves to shift the criterion of superiority toward internal organization rather than mere functional appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The living being is conceived as a totality without a final level of decomposition at which organization would cease.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the distinction between natural machine and artificial machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT2","text":"The principal generative chain is coherent: organism → machinicity of the parts → infinity of structure → natural superiority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT3","text":"The reconstruction preserves the comparative movement that produces the thesis from the example of the wheel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT4","text":"The exact scope of « jusqu’à l’infini » remains underdetermined between the actual infinity of composition and divisibility without an ultimate term.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT5","text":"The qualification « divine » adds a metaphysical attribution on which the argumentative mechanism depends less than on machinic continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT6","text":"The principal tension opposes the image of the machine to the absence of a final element that could be identified as simple or non-machinic.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_56:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_56@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_56:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 64"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 64","title":"Proposition 64","context":"Chapter 64","original_title":"Proposition 64"},"original_title":"Proposition 64","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 65","order":65,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_57"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_57@R001","sha256":"e2ccdf9e9734fd61783dfd7701ca89c920f01c84f6d8512cc651aac8fc5b1833","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AS1","text":"L’expression de l’univers par chaque portion de matière constitue le problème à rendre possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AS2","text":"La divisibilité infinie reconnue par les anciens est recadrée comme une sous-division actuellement réalisée sans fin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AS3","text":"Chaque partie est dotée d’un mouvement propre, ce qui fournit le mécanisme différentiel de l’expression universelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AS4","text":"L’artifice divin devient intelligible par l’articulation entre subdivision actuelle, mouvement propre et expression de tout l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A1","text":"Toute portion de matière est divisible à l’infini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","text":"Toute portion de matière est actuellement sous-divisée sans fin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","text":"Chaque partie de la matière possède un mouvement propre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","text":"Chaque portion de matière exprime tout l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A5","text":"L’expression universelle d’une portion dépend de sa subdivision interne indéfinie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A6","text":"L’ordre matériel est produit par un artifice divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A7","text":"La divisibilité infinie actuelle distingue la structure réelle de la matière d’une simple possibilité logique de division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX1","text":"La matière n’est pas composée de parties ultimes indivisibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX2","text":"La divisibilité de la matière n’est pas seulement potentielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX3","text":"Une portion de matière n’est pas une unité isolée qui existerait indépendamment de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX4","text":"Les parties de la matière ne sont pas dépourvues de mouvement propre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX5","text":"L’expression de l’univers n’est pas possible à partir d’une structure matérielle finie ou simplement juxtaposée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D1","text":"La subdivision actuelle sans fin transforme chaque portion matérielle en multiplicité interne illimitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A1","CH_UCIC_P_57:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D2","text":"Le mouvement propre de chaque partie empêche de réduire la matière à une extension inerte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D3","text":"Chaque portion peut exprimer l’univers parce que sa constitution interne contient une pluralité indéfinie de mouvements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D4","text":"La divisibilité infinie acquiert une fonction expressive et ne demeure pas une propriété géométrique abstraite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A1","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D5","text":"L’impossibilité d’exprimer l’univers sert de critère négatif contre toute conception non actuellement subdivisée de la matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A5","CH_UCIC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1","text":"Toute portion matérielle fonctionne comme un microcosme dynamique dont la structure interne renvoie à la totalité universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SD2","text":"L’unité matérielle est redéfinie comme une unité expressive produite par une pluralité interne illimitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SD3","text":"L’ordre universel n’est pas ajouté extérieurement aux portions de matière, mais rendu présent dans chacune par leur organisation dynamique interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4","text":"La causalité divine opère ici comme principe d’une architecture où la totalité est répétée dans chaque portion sans supprimer leur différenciation propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une ontologie où la matière serait constituée d’éléments simples définitivement séparables.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX2","text":"Il exclut une distinction stricte entre division réelle et division seulement concevable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une conception de l’espace matériel comme totalité sans activité interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une relation extrinsèque entre les portions matérielles et l’univers qu’elles expriment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX5","text":"Il exclut qu’une portion puisse exprimer la totalité sans porter en elle une structure indéfiniment différenciée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SNX1","text":"La possibilité d’un matériau absolument simple est forclose, car elle rendrait impossible l’expression universelle de chaque portion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SNX2","text":"L’absence d’un fond matériel inerte et sans mouvement propre structure silencieusement toute l’argumentation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SNX3","text":"Est rendue inadmissible toute séparation entre la totalité de l’univers et les unités qui la composent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS1","text":"Divisibilité infinie → sous-division actuellement sans fin → pluralité interne de parties → mouvement propre de chaque partie → expression de tout l’univers par chaque portion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS2","text":"Impossibilité d’expression dans une matière finie ou inerte → nécessité d’une subdivision actuelle indéfinie → attribution d’une activité propre aux parties → intelligibilité de l’artifice divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS3","text":"Totalité universelle à exprimer → structure interne illimitée de chaque portion → réinscription de la totalité dans chaque unité matérielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AF1","text":"Problème de l’expression universelle → distinction entre divisibilité potentielle et sous-division actuelle → mouvement propre des parties → possibilité d’expression de l’univers → justification de l’artifice divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ME1","text":"La matière est reclassée d’étendue divisible en réseau de parties actuellement différenciées et mobiles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ME2","text":"L’opposition entre unité matérielle et totalité universelle s’effondre : chaque portion devient un lieu d’expression du tout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ME3","text":"La divisibilité infinie passe du statut de propriété formelle au statut de condition cosmologique de l’expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ME4","text":"La causalité divine est cartographiée comme production d’une structure interne répétitive, dynamique et universellement expressive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT1","text":"Surface — La matière est indéfiniment divisée et chaque partie possède un mouvement propre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT2","text":"Structural — L’expression de l’univers repose sur une organisation interne sans dernier niveau de composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’argument répond à l’objection de l’impossibilité d’une expression universelle en convertissant la divisibilité en mécanisme explicatif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La réalité matérielle est une multiplicité actuelle, dynamique et récursive, non une extension homogène simplement divisible en droit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage : expression universelle, subdivision actuelle, mouvement propre et artifice divin sont tous conservés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si l’expression est rendue dépendante de la composition dynamique de chaque portion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT3","text":"Le mécanisme précis par lequel une partie exprime tout l’univers reste sous-déterminé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT4","text":"La force de l’argument réside dans l’implication conditionnelle : sans sous-division actuelle, l’expression universelle serait impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel du texte, mais laisse ouverte la médiation exacte entre mouvement propre et expression universelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T193946746635Z_56849a7f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 65","source_sha256":"e2ccdf9e9734fd61783dfd7701ca89c920f01c84f6d8512cc651aac8fc5b1833","sha256":"18d143b87225bee16e138fd763c6fef777ae18ea33e50e6c79140e2b0691b045","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:39:46.751575+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AS1","text":"The expression of the universe by each portion of matter constitutes the problem to be rendered possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AS2","text":"The infinite divisibility recognized by the ancients is reframed as an actually realized subdivision without end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AS3","text":"Each part is endowed with its own movement, which provides the differential mechanism of universal expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AS4","text":"The divine artifice becomes intelligible through the articulation between actual subdivision, proper movement, and the expression of the whole universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A1","text":"Every portion of matter is infinitely divisible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","text":"Every portion of matter is actually subdivided without end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","text":"Each part of matter possesses its own movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","text":"Every portion of matter expresses the whole universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A5","text":"The universal expression of a portion depends on its indefinite internal subdivision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A6","text":"The material order is produced by a divine artifice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:A7","text":"Actual infinite divisibility distinguishes the real structure of matter from a mere logical possibility of division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX1","text":"Matter is not composed of ultimate indivisible parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX2","text":"The divisibility of matter is not merely potential.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX3","text":"A portion of matter is not an isolated unit that would exist independently of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX4","text":"The parts of matter are not devoid of their own movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:NX5","text":"The expression of the universe is not possible on the basis of a finite or merely juxtaposed material structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D1","text":"Actual subdivision without end transforms every material portion into an unlimited internal multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A1","CH_UCIC_P_57:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D2","text":"The proper movement of each part prevents matter from being reduced to inert extension.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D3","text":"Each portion can express the universe because its internal constitution contains an indefinite plurality of movements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D4","text":"Infinite divisibility acquires an expressive function and does not remain an abstract geometrical property.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A1","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:D5","text":"The impossibility of expressing the universe serves as a negative criterion against every conception of matter that is not actually subdivided.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A5","CH_UCIC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1","text":"Every material portion functions as a dynamic microcosm whose internal structure refers to the universal totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SD2","text":"Material unity is redefined as an expressive unity produced by an unlimited internal plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SD3","text":"The universal order is not externally added to portions of matter, but made present in each through their internal dynamic organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4","text":"Divine causality operates here as the principle of an architecture in which the totality is repeated in each portion without suppressing their proper differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an ontology in which matter would be constituted of simple elements definitively separable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX2","text":"It excludes a strict distinction between real division and merely conceivable division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX3","text":"It excludes a conception of material space as a totality without internal activity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX4","text":"It excludes an extrinsic relation between material portions and the universe that they express.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX5","text":"It excludes the possibility that a portion might express the totality without bearing within itself an indefinitely differentiated structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SNX1","text":"The possibility of an absolutely simple material is ruled out, for it would render impossible the universal expression of each portion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SNX2","text":"The absence of an inert material ground devoid of proper movement silently structures the entire argumentation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:SNX3","text":"Any separation between the totality of the universe and the units composing it is rendered inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS1","text":"Infinite divisibility → actually endless subdivision → internal plurality of parts → proper movement of each part → expression of the whole universe by each portion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS2","text":"Impossibility of expression in finite or inert matter → necessity of an indefinite actual subdivision → attribution of proper activity to the parts → intelligibility of the divine artifice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS3","text":"Universal totality to be expressed → unlimited internal structure of each portion → reinscription of the totality in each material unit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:AF1","text":"Problem of universal expression → distinction between potential divisibility and actual subdivision → proper movement of the parts → possibility of expressing the universe → justification of the divine artifice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ME1","text":"Matter is reclassified from divisible extension into a network of actually differentiated and mobile parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ME2","text":"The opposition between material unity and universal totality collapses: each portion becomes a site for the expression of the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ME3","text":"Infinite divisibility passes from the status of a formal property to that of a cosmological condition of expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ME4","text":"Divine causality is mapped as the production of an internal repetitive, dynamic, and universally expressive structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT1","text":"Surface — Matter is indefinitely divided and each part possesses its own movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT2","text":"Structural — The expression of the universe rests upon an internal organization with no final level of composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument responds to the objection of the impossibility of universal expression by converting divisibility into an explanatory mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Material reality is an actual, dynamic, and recursive multiplicity, not a homogeneous extension merely divisible in principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage: universal expression, actual subdivision, proper movement, and divine artifice are all preserved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if expression is made dependent on the dynamic composition of each portion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT3","text":"The precise mechanism by which a part expresses the whole universe remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT4","text":"The force of the argument lies in the conditional implication: without actual subdivision, universal expression would be impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the real movement of the text, but leaves open the exact mediation between proper movement and universal expression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_57:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_57@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_57:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 65"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 65","title":"Proposition 65","context":"Chapter 65","original_title":"Proposition 65"},"original_title":"Proposition 65","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 66","order":66,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_58"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_58@R001","sha256":"0d0e8fb8370f4c78071a501d7943d73262ed8418619e60cc2bda9afa250d6996","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AS1","text":"L’énoncé cherche à établir la composition interne de la matière jusque dans sa moindre partie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AS2","text":"La petitesse matérielle est recadrée comme coexistence d’une pluralité de réalités vivantes et animées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AS3","text":"La matière est déterminée par une gradation allant de la créature à l’âme en passant par le vivant, l’animal et l’entéléchie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AS4","text":"La conclusion universelle est introduite comme une visibilité ou une évidence produite par ce recadrage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A1","text":"Toute partie de la matière, y compris la moindre, possède une structure interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","text":"La structure interne de la matière comporte une pluralité de réalités.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","text":"Ces réalités peuvent être ordonnées selon une série comprenant les créatures, les vivants, les animaux, les entéléchies et les âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","text":"La moindre partie de la matière contient un monde plutôt qu’une unité absolument simple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A5","text":"La matière est compatible avec des déterminations vitales, animales et psychiques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A6","text":"L’examen de la moindre partie matérielle suffit à établir une proposition portant sur la matière en général.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX1","text":"La moindre partie de la matière n’est pas une unité vide de toute composition interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX2","text":"La matière n’est pas définie comme une réalité exclusivement inerte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX3","text":"Une partie matérielle n’est pas dépourvue de vivants, d’animaux, d’entéléchies ou d’âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX4","text":"Le petit ne constitue pas une limite au-delà de laquelle toute réalité organisée disparaîtrait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX5","text":"La matière n’est pas réductible à une agrégation sans principe vital ou animique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:D1","text":"La division de la matière ne conduit pas à un terme absolument simple, puisque la moindre partie contient encore une pluralité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A1","CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:D2","text":"La distinction entre matière et vie ne peut pas être posée comme une séparation absolue au niveau des parties matérielles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","CH_UCIC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:D3","text":"La réalité animique ou entéléchique appartient à la structure même de la moindre portion matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","CH_UCIC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:D4","text":"La totalité matérielle peut être conçue comme une pluralité de mondes internes emboîtés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1","text":"La matière est reconfigurée comme un continuum de pluralités organisées plutôt que comme une étendue composée d’unités ultimes inertes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A1","CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SD2","text":"La vie, l’animalité et l’animation ne sont plus des propriétés ajoutées à la matière depuis l’extérieur, mais des niveaux de sa constitution interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","CH_UCIC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SD3","text":"L’infiniment petit devient le lieu d’une densification ontologique maximale : plus la partie est petite, moins elle est dépourvue de monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SD4","text":"La généralisation sur la matière repose sur une règle d’homogénéité structurelle entre la moindre partie et le tout matériel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A1","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX1","text":"Le système dépend de la fausseté d’une conception de la matière comme totalité finalement décomposable en éléments simples et non organisés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX2","text":"Il exclut une frontière ontologique nette entre l’étendue matérielle et les principes de vie ou d’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX3","text":"Il disqualifie l’idée que la réduction d’échelle produise une réduction de réalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX4","text":"Il exclut qu’une analyse physique de la matière puisse éliminer les niveaux entéléchiques ou animiques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’une matière absolument homogène, muette et sans intérieur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX2","text":"Est rendue inadmissible l’existence d’un dernier dehors de la vie au sein de la matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX3","text":"Est exclue la possibilité d’une simplicité matérielle qui interromprait la pluralité des êtres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX4","text":"L’argument tourne autour de l’absence d’un seuil où la matière cesserait d’être porteuse de monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS1","text":"Partie matérielle → examen de son intérieur → découverte d’une pluralité → qualification vitale, animale et animique → constitution d’un monde interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS2","text":"Moindre partie de la matière → refus de la simplicité absolue → emboîtement des êtres → extension de la structure à la matière entière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS3","text":"Réduction d’échelle → non-disparition de l’organisation → densification ontologique → conclusion universelle sur la matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AF1","text":"Moindre partie matérielle → structure interne → pluralité de réalités → gradation du vivant à l’âme → monde de créatures dans la matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AF2","text":"Hypothèse d’une matière simple et inerte → exclusion de cette hypothèse → matière intérieurement peuplée → généralisation ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ME1","text":"La moindre partie est reclassée : elle n’est plus un fragment terminal, mais un monde composé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ME2","text":"La matière et le vivant cessent d’apparaître comme deux domaines séparés par une frontière absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ME3","text":"La petitesse change de fonction conceptuelle : elle ne désigne plus une pauvreté ontologique, mais une concentration de pluralité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ME4","text":"La hiérarchie créature–vivant–animal–entéléchie–âme devient une carte interne de la matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT1","text":"Surface — La moindre partie de la matière contient un monde de créatures, de vivants, d’animaux, d’entéléchies et d’âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT2","text":"Structural — La matière possède une composition interne pluralisée et organisée à toutes les échelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’argument renverse le geste réducteur : descendre vers le plus petit ne simplifie pas le réel, mais révèle sa structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La matière est présupposée comme indéfiniment riche en déterminations internes, sans terme matériel absolument simple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement allant de la moindre partie matérielle à la pluralité des êtres qu’elle contient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT2","text":"La chaîne générative préserve le passage de la petitesse physique à la densité ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT3","text":"Le texte ne précise pas le statut exact des relations entre créatures, vivants, animaux, entéléchies et âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT4","text":"Le rapport logique entre « voir » et conclure n’est pas démontré dans l’énoncé isolé ; il dépend d’un contexte argumentatif antérieur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction est cohérente si la pluralité interne et l’absence d’une matière absolument simple sont admises.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT6","text":"La tension principale réside dans le passage non explicité d’une moindre partie déterminée à une affirmation portant sur toute la matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194001453423Z_ff6d11a1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 66","source_sha256":"0d0e8fb8370f4c78071a501d7943d73262ed8418619e60cc2bda9afa250d6996","sha256":"7fd8456d63bed006d2c6400082efa9953339c74e20f6a5bad44e47631e7ae1f8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:40:01.456867+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AS1","text":"The statement seeks to establish the internal composition of matter down to its smallest part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AS2","text":"Material smallness is reframed as the coexistence of a plurality of living and animate realities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AS3","text":"Matter is determined by a gradation extending from creature to soul by way of the living being, the animal, and entelechy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AS4","text":"The universal conclusion is introduced as a visibility or an evidence produced by this reframing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A1","text":"Every part of matter, including the smallest, possesses an internal structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","text":"The internal structure of matter comprises a plurality of realities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","text":"These realities can be ordered according to a series comprising creatures, living beings, animals, entelechies, and souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","text":"The smallest part of matter contains a world rather than an absolutely simple unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A5","text":"Matter is compatible with vital, animal, and psychic determinations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:A6","text":"The examination of the smallest material part suffices to establish a proposition concerning matter in general.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX1","text":"The smallest part of matter is not a unity devoid of all internal composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX2","text":"Matter is not defined as an exclusively inert reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX3","text":"A material part is not devoid of living beings, animals, entelechies, or souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX4","text":"The small does not constitute a limit beyond which all organized reality would disappear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:NX5","text":"Matter is not reducible to an aggregation without a vital or animic principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:D1","text":"The division of matter does not lead to an absolutely simple term, since the smallest part still contains an internal plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A1","CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:D2","text":"The distinction between matter and life cannot be posited as an absolute separation at the level of material parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","CH_UCIC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:D3","text":"Animic or entelechic reality belongs to the very structure of the smallest material portion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","CH_UCIC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:D4","text":"Material totality can be conceived as a plurality of nested internal worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1","text":"Matter is reconfigured as a continuum of organized pluralities rather than as an extension composed of inert ultimate units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A1","CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SD2","text":"Life, animality, and animation are no longer properties added to matter from outside, but levels of its internal constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","CH_UCIC_P_58:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SD3","text":"The infinitely small becomes the site of maximal ontological densification: the smaller the part, the less it is devoid of world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A2","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SD4","text":"The generalization concerning matter rests on a rule of structural homogeneity between the smallest part and the material whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A1","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX1","text":"The system depends on the falsity of a conception of matter as a totality ultimately decomposable into simple and unorganized elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX2","text":"It excludes a clear ontological boundary between material extension and the principles of life or soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX3","text":"It disqualifies the idea that a reduction of scale produces a reduction of reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX4","text":"It excludes the possibility that a physical analysis of matter could eliminate entelechic or animic levels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX1","text":"The possibility of matter that is absolutely homogeneous, mute, and without interiority is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX2","text":"The existence of a final outside of life within matter is rendered inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX3","text":"The possibility of a material simplicity that would interrupt the plurality of beings is excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX4","text":"The argument turns around the absence of a threshold at which matter would cease to bear a world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS1","text":"Material part → examination of its interior → discovery of a plurality → vital, animal, and animic qualification → constitution of an internal world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS2","text":"Smallest part of matter → rejection of absolute simplicity → nesting of beings → extension of the structure to matter as a whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS3","text":"Reduction of scale → non-disappearance of organization → ontological densification → universal conclusion concerning matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AF1","text":"Smallest material part → internal structure → plurality of realities → gradation from living being to soul → world of creatures in matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:AF2","text":"Hypothesis of simple and inert matter → exclusion of this hypothesis → matter inwardly populated → ontological generalization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ME1","text":"The smallest part is reclassified: it is no longer a terminal fragment, but a composite world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ME2","text":"Matter and the living being cease to appear as two domains separated by an absolute boundary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ME3","text":"Smallness changes conceptual function: it no longer denotes ontological poverty, but a concentration of plurality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ME4","text":"The creature–living being–animal–entelechy–soul hierarchy becomes an internal map of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT1","text":"Surface — The smallest part of matter contains a world of creatures, living beings, animals, entelechies, and souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT2","text":"Structural — Matter possesses an internally pluralized and organized composition at every scale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument reverses the reductive gesture: descending toward the smallest does not simplify reality, but reveals its structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Matter is presupposed as indefinitely rich in internal determinations, without an absolutely simple material term.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the smallest material part to the plurality of beings it contains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT2","text":"The generative chain preserves the transition from physical smallness to ontological density.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT3","text":"The text does not specify the exact status of the relations among creatures, living beings, animals, entelechies, and souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT4","text":"The logical relation between « voir » and concluding is not demonstrated in the isolated statement; it depends on a prior argumentative context.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction is coherent if internal plurality and the absence of absolutely simple matter are admitted.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT6","text":"The principal tension lies in the unexplained transition from a determinate smallest part to an assertion concerning all matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_58:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_58@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_58:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 66"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 66","title":"Proposition 66","context":"Chapter 66","original_title":"Proposition 66"},"original_title":"Proposition 66","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 67","order":67,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_59"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_59@R001","sha256":"2aca32d01db73c8e1e78bb47b811f8086217cf52599101149f9a81b46d5988c0","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS1","text":"Une portion quelconque de la matière est recadrée comme une totalité organisée plutôt que comme une masse indifférenciée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS2","text":"Cette totalité est figurée par deux modèles structuraux : le jardin et l’étang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS3","text":"La même organisation se retrouve dans chaque partie interne de la totalité considérée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS4","text":"La division matérielle ne conduit donc pas d’abord à des éléments simples, mais à des totalités de même structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS5","text":"L’argument procède par réapplication récursive d’un même schème d’organisation à toutes les échelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A1","text":"Toute portion de matière peut être conçue comme un jardin plein de plantes ou comme un étang plein de poissons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","text":"Un jardin ou un étang constitue une totalité composée d’éléments organisés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","text":"Chaque élément interne d’une totalité matérielle possède à son tour une organisation comparable à celle de la totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A4","text":"Un rameau de plante peut être conçu comme un jardin plein de plantes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A5","text":"Un membre d’animal peut être conçu comme un étang plein de poissons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A6","text":"Une goutte des humeurs d’un animal peut être conçue comme un jardin ou un étang.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A7","text":"La structure organisée de la matière se reproduit dans ses parties à des degrés successifs de petitesse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX1","text":"La matière n’est pas définie comme une masse homogène dépourvue d’organisation interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX2","text":"Une portion matérielle n’est pas une unité absolument simple et indivisible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX3","text":"La division d’un tout matériel ne produit pas une partie qui cesserait d’être une totalité organisée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX4","text":"Les parties de la matière ne sont pas des éléments structurellement différents du tout dont elles proviennent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX5","text":"L’échelle macroscopique n’est pas le seul niveau pertinent de composition matérielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:D1","text":"Toute division d’une portion de matière reconduit à une pluralité organisée plutôt qu’à une unité simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A1","CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:D2","text":"La distinction entre totalité et partie devient relative à l’échelle d’observation, puisque chaque partie peut être traitée comme une nouvelle totalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A1","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:D3","text":"La matière apparaît comme une composition emboîtée de structures organisées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:D4","text":"La petitesse d’une partie ne diminue pas en elle-même son caractère de totalité organisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SD1","text":"La matière est structurée par une récursivité interne qui empêche de poser une frontière simple entre le composé et ses composants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A1","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SD2","text":"L’analyse matérielle ne progresse pas vers un fond inorganisé, mais vers des niveaux supplémentaires de composition organisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SD3","text":"L’unité d’un corps ne réside pas dans l’absence de parties, mais dans l’organisation réitérée de parties elles-mêmes composées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX1","text":"Le système ne peut pas reposer sur l’existence de portions matérielles ultimes dont l’intérieur serait dépourvu de structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX2","text":"Il exclut silencieusement une théorie selon laquelle la division successive aboutirait à des unités absolument simples.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une conception de la matière où l’organisation serait seulement ajoutée aux agrégats depuis l’extérieur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une hiérarchie dans laquelle les petites parties seraient ontologiquement moins organisées que les grandes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX1","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un élément matériel dernier, vide de toute composition interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX2","text":"La possibilité d’une matière absolument simple est forclose par la répétition indéfinie du rapport entre partie et totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX3","text":"Ce qui est rendu indisponible est un point final de l’analyse matérielle où toute pluralité organisée disparaîtrait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS1","text":"Portion matérielle → modélisation comme totalité organisée → identification de parties internes → réapplication du même modèle à chaque partie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS2","text":"Tout composé matériel → pluralité organisée → chaque élément comme nouveau composé → récursivité structurelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS3","text":"Division → non-réduction à l’unité simple → multiplication des totalités emboîtées → impossibilité d’un terme matériel homogène.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AF1","text":"Portion matérielle → jardin ou étang → parties internes organisées → répétition du jardin ou de l’étang dans chaque partie → structure matérielle récursive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AF2","text":"Apparente unité du corps → découverte d’une pluralité interne → relativisation du rapport partie/tout → exclusion de l’élément matériel simple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ME1","text":"La matière est reclassée : de substrat homogène, elle devient réseau de totalités organisées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ME2","text":"La distinction entre partie et totalité est transformée en distinction d’échelle plutôt qu’en opposition absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ME3","text":"La division matérielle cesse d’être une voie vers la simplicité et devient une voie vers l’emboîtement structurel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ME4","text":"L’organisation interne devient visible comme propriété répétée de la matière, et non comme trait réservé aux corps pris globalement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT1","text":"Surface — Une portion de matière est conçue comme un jardin plein de plantes ou comme un étang plein de poissons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT2","text":"Structural — Chaque composant matériel contient à son tour une pluralité organisée analogue à celle du composé initial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’analyse doit changer d’échelle sans changer de principe explicatif : le même schème est reconduit à chaque niveau.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La matière est présupposée comme une composition indéfiniment stratifiée, sans terme simple immédiatement accessible dans la division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement de la portion matérielle vers la totalité organisée puis vers la récursivité des parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si les images du jardin et de l’étang sont prises comme modèles d’organisation et non comme identités littérales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT3","text":"Le texte sous-détermine le statut exact de la répétition : il affirme une possibilité de conception sans expliciter ici son régime ontologique complet.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT4","text":"La conclusion d’une composition indéfiniment organisée dépend de l’extension récursive du principe énoncé aux parties internes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : totalité apparente → parties organisées → nouvelles totalités → exclusion du simple matériel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194015565291Z_e01f3ab0","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 67","source_sha256":"2aca32d01db73c8e1e78bb47b811f8086217cf52599101149f9a81b46d5988c0","sha256":"cfa2fbca64e2a20c62756fd0c5cb05e4275f16455a5f4d6257789b1c67668e5a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:40:15.573434+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS1","text":"Any portion of matter is reframed as an organized whole rather than as an undifferentiated mass.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS2","text":"This whole is figured by two structural models: the garden and the pond.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS3","text":"The same organization is found in every internal part of the whole under consideration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS4","text":"Material division therefore does not lead first to simple elements, but to wholes of the same structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AS5","text":"The argument proceeds through the recursive reapplication of the same organizational schema at every scale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A1","text":"Every portion of matter can be conceived as a garden full of plants or as a pond full of fish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","text":"A garden or a pond constitutes a whole composed of organized elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","text":"Each internal element of a material whole in turn possesses an organization comparable to that of the whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A4","text":"A branch of a plant can be conceived as a garden full of plants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A5","text":"An animal limb can be conceived as a pond full of fish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A6","text":"A drop of an animal's humours can be conceived as a garden or a pond.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:A7","text":"The organized structure of matter reproduces itself in its parts at successive degrees of smallness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX1","text":"Matter is not defined as a homogeneous mass devoid of internal organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX2","text":"A material portion is not an absolutely simple and indivisible unit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX3","text":"The division of a material whole does not produce a part that would cease to be an organized whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX4","text":"The parts of matter are not elements structurally different from the whole from which they come.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:NX5","text":"The macroscopic scale is not the sole relevant level of material composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:D1","text":"Every division of a portion of matter leads again to an organized plurality rather than to a simple unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A1","CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:D2","text":"The distinction between whole and part becomes relative to the scale of observation, since each part can be treated as a new whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A1","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:D3","text":"Matter appears as a nested composition of organized structures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:D4","text":"The smallness of a part does not in itself diminish its character as an organized whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SD1","text":"Matter is structured by an internal recursivity that prevents the positing of a simple boundary between the composite and its components.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A1","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SD2","text":"Material analysis does not progress toward an unorganized ground, but toward additional levels of organized composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SD3","text":"The unity of a body does not reside in the absence of parts, but in the reiterated organization of parts themselves composed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A2","CH_UCIC_P_59:A3","CH_UCIC_P_59:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX1","text":"The system cannot rest on the existence of ultimate material portions whose interior would be devoid of structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX2","text":"It silently excludes a theory according to which successive division would result in absolutely simple units.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX3","text":"It excludes a conception of matter in which organization would be added to aggregates only from the outside.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX4","text":"It excludes a hierarchy in which small parts would be ontologically less organized than large ones.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX1","text":"The structuring absence is that of an ultimate material element, empty of all internal composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX2","text":"The possibility of absolutely simple matter is foreclosed by the indefinite repetition of the relation between part and whole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX3","text":"What is rendered unavailable is an endpoint of material analysis at which all organized plurality would disappear.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS1","text":"Material portion → modeling as organized whole → identification of internal parts → reapplication of the same model to each part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS2","text":"Every material composite → organized plurality → each element as a new composite → structural recursivity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS3","text":"Division → non-reduction to simple unity → multiplication of nested wholes → impossibility of a homogeneous material term.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AF1","text":"Material portion → garden or pond → organized internal parts → repetition of the garden or pond in each part → recursive material structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:AF2","text":"Apparent unity of the body → discovery of an internal plurality → relativization of the part/whole relation → exclusion of the simple material element.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ME1","text":"Matter is reclassified: from homogeneous substrate, it becomes a network of organized wholes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ME2","text":"The distinction between part and whole is transformed into a distinction of scale rather than an absolute opposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ME3","text":"Material division ceases to be a path toward simplicity and becomes a path toward structural nesting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ME4","text":"Internal organization becomes visible as a repeated property of matter, and not as a trait reserved for bodies taken globally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT1","text":"Surface — A portion of matter is conceived as a garden full of plants or as a pond full of fish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT2","text":"Structural — Each material component in turn contains an organized plurality analogous to that of the initial composite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Analysis must change scale without changing its explanatory principle: the same schema is carried over at each level.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Matter is presupposed as an indefinitely stratified composition, without a simple term immediately accessible through division.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the material portion to the organized whole and then to the recursivity of the parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if the images of the garden and the pond are taken as models of organization and not as literal identities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT3","text":"The text underdetermines the exact status of the repetition: it asserts a possibility of conception without here making explicit its complete ontological regime.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT4","text":"The conclusion of an indefinitely organized composition depends on the recursive extension of the stated principle to internal parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: apparent whole → organized parts → new wholes → exclusion of the material simple.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_59:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_59@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_59:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 67"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 67","title":"Proposition 67","context":"Chapter 67","original_title":"Proposition 67"},"original_title":"Proposition 67","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 68","order":68,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_60"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_60@R001","sha256":"5fe5a63a9528f9e6a5d06af51498af005fc1b02b0565f35fff350db212c00c87","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS1","text":"Le texte part de milieux interposés entre des êtres naturels distincts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS2","text":"Il dissocie l’absence d’identité de l’absence de contenu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS3","text":"Il pose que les milieux interposés contiennent encore les êtres qu’ils séparent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS4","text":"Il recadre cette présence comme une subtilité généralement imperceptible pour l’être humain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS5","text":"Le mouvement argumentatif va de la distinction visible à la continuité invisible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A1","text":"La terre et l’air interposés entre les plantes ne sont pas eux-mêmes des plantes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A2","text":"L’eau interposée entre les poissons n’est pas elle-même un poisson.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A3","text":"La non-identité du milieu interposé n’exclut pas qu’il contienne encore ce qui est séparé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A4","text":"La terre et l’air interposés entre les plantes contiennent encore les plantes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A5","text":"L’eau interposée entre les poissons contient encore les poissons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A6","text":"Cette contenance est le plus souvent d’une subtilité imperceptible pour nous.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A7","text":"L’imperceptibilité humaine ne supprime pas la présence contenue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:NX1","text":"Le milieu interposé n’est pas identique à l’être qu’il contient.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:NX2","text":"La séparation spatiale n’est pas une absence totale de l’être séparé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:NX3","text":"La présence contenue n’est pas nécessairement perceptible par les sens humains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:NX4","text":"La terre, l’air et l’eau ne sont pas de simples intervalles vides entre les êtres naturels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:D1","text":"La distinction entre contenant et contenu doit être séparée de l’opposition entre présence et absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A1","CH_UCIC_P_60:A2","CH_UCIC_P_60:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:D2","text":"Un milieu apparemment homogène peut porter une présence naturelle qui n’est pas immédiatement identifiable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A4","CH_UCIC_P_60:A5","CH_UCIC_P_60:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:D3","text":"Le visible ne suffit pas à épuiser la composition réelle des milieux naturels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A6","CH_UCIC_P_60:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SD1","text":"La séparation des corps naturels devient une distinction de degré et de manifestation plutôt qu’une rupture ontologique absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A3","CH_UCIC_P_60:A4","CH_UCIC_P_60:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SD2","text":"La perception humaine est constituée comme un seuil épistémique qui laisse subsister des contenus naturels non discernés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A6","CH_UCIC_P_60:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX1","text":"Le texte exclut que l’espace séparateur puisse être défini par la seule vacuité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’une différence de nature immédiatement perceptible équivaille à une discontinuité complète.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX3","text":"Il exclut que l’imperceptible soit assimilé au non-existant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX1","text":"L’absence d’une forme reconnaissable ne constitue pas une absence de présence naturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX2","text":"La possibilité d’un extérieur absolument séparé entre les êtres est structurellement forclose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX3","text":"La perception humaine ne peut servir de mesure ontologique ultime de ce que contiennent les milieux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS1","text":"Être distinct du contenu → être interposé entre les êtres → conserver leur présence dans le milieu → rendre cette présence subtile → la soustraire généralement à la perception humaine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS2","text":"Non-identité visible + contenance invisible → dissociation de la séparation spatiale et de l’absence ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AF1","text":"Milieu interposé → distinction avec les êtres naturels → affirmation d’une contenance persistante → subtilité imperceptible → limitation du critère perceptif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ME1","text":"L’espace interposé est reclassé de vide séparateur en milieu contenant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ME2","text":"La frontière entre présence et absence est déplacée du visible vers une composition plus subtile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ME3","text":"Les êtres naturels sont cartographiés comme présents au-delà de leurs formes immédiatement discernables.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Des milieux distincts des plantes et des poissons en contiennent néanmoins encore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — La séparation spatiale fonctionne comme médiation de la présence plutôt que comme élimination du contenu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Le texte impose de distinguer ce qui est perceptiblement séparé de ce qui est réellement absent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — La réalité naturelle excède la perception actuelle par des contenus subtils déjà présents dans les milieux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le passage de la non-identité à la contenance imperceptible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT2","text":"La structure interne est cohérente : l’imperceptibilité qualifie l’accès humain, non la réalité de la contenance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT3","text":"Le système reste sous-déterminé quant à la nature exacte de ce qui est contenu et au mécanisme de cette contenance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT4","text":"La généralisation repose sur deux configurations analogues : plantes dans terre et air, poissons dans l’eau.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : distinction phénoménale → présence résiduelle → subtilité → limite perceptive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194026237854Z_d35504e6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 68","source_sha256":"5fe5a63a9528f9e6a5d06af51498af005fc1b02b0565f35fff350db212c00c87","sha256":"c5b981ee2b04b3a6b336fc36758122690bb1a17d0e524ad2c592abb89852fb05","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:40:26.243551+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS1","text":"The text begins from media interposed between distinct natural beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS2","text":"It dissociates the absence of identity from the absence of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS3","text":"It posits that the interposed media still contain the beings they separate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS4","text":"It reframes this presence as a subtlety generally imperceptible to the human being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AS5","text":"The argumentative movement proceeds from visible distinction to invisible continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A1","text":"The earth and air interposed between plants are not themselves plants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A2","text":"The water interposed between fish is not itself a fish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A3","text":"The non-identity of the interposed medium does not exclude its still containing what is separated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A4","text":"The earth and air interposed between plants still contain the plants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A5","text":"The water interposed between fish still contains the fish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A6","text":"This containment is most often of a subtlety imperceptible to us.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:A7","text":"Human imperceptibility does not eliminate the contained presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:NX1","text":"The interposed medium is not identical to the being it contains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:NX2","text":"Spatial separation is not a total absence of the separated being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:NX3","text":"Contained presence is not necessarily perceptible to the human senses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:NX4","text":"Earth, air, and water are not merely empty intervals between natural beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:D1","text":"The distinction between container and content must be separated from the opposition between presence and absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A1","CH_UCIC_P_60:A2","CH_UCIC_P_60:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:D2","text":"An apparently homogeneous medium can bear a natural presence that is not immediately identifiable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A4","CH_UCIC_P_60:A5","CH_UCIC_P_60:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:D3","text":"The visible does not suffice to exhaust the real composition of natural media.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A6","CH_UCIC_P_60:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SD1","text":"The separation of natural bodies becomes a distinction of degree and manifestation rather than an absolute ontological rupture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A3","CH_UCIC_P_60:A4","CH_UCIC_P_60:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SD2","text":"Human perception is constituted as an epistemic threshold that allows undiscerned natural contents to subsist.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A6","CH_UCIC_P_60:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX1","text":"The text excludes the possibility that separating space can be defined by vacuity alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that an immediately perceptible difference in nature amounts to complete discontinuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX3","text":"It excludes the possibility that the imperceptible is assimilated to the non-existent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX1","text":"The absence of a recognizable form does not constitute an absence of natural presence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX2","text":"The possibility of an absolutely separate exterior between beings is structurally foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX3","text":"Human perception cannot serve as the ultimate ontological measure of what media contain.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS1","text":"Being distinct from the content → being interposed between beings → retaining their presence in the medium → rendering this presence subtle → generally withdrawing it from human perception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS2","text":"Visible non-identity + invisible containment → dissociation of spatial separation and ontological absence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:AF1","text":"Interposed medium → distinction from natural beings → affirmation of a persistent containment → imperceptible subtlety → limitation of the perceptual criterion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ME1","text":"Interposed space is reclassified from separating void to containing medium.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ME2","text":"The boundary between presence and absence is displaced from the visible toward a subtler composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ME3","text":"Natural beings are mapped as present beyond their immediately discernible forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Media distinct from plants and fish nevertheless still contain them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Spatial separation functions as a mediation of presence rather than as an elimination of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The text requires distinguishing what is perceptibly separate from what is really absent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Natural reality exceeds present perception through subtle contents already present in media.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage from non-identity to imperceptible containment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT2","text":"The internal structure is coherent: imperceptibility qualifies human access, not the reality of containment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT3","text":"The system remains underdetermined as to the exact nature of what is contained and the mechanism of this containment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT4","text":"The generalization rests on two analogous configurations: plants in earth and air, fish in water.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: phenomenal distinction → residual presence → subtlety → perceptual limit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_60:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_60@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_60:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 68"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 68","title":"Proposition 68","context":"Chapter 68","original_title":"Proposition 68"},"original_title":"Proposition 68","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 69","order":69,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_61"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_61@R001","sha256":"27026a2946bca0f6707e3780b9142c2b962ccefb4a56a3b771e840ee47014190","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS1","text":"Le problème est l’écart entre l’apparence de confusion universelle et la structure réelle de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS2","text":"L’apparente stérilité ou mortalité des choses est recadrée comme un défaut de discernement, non comme une propriété de l’être.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS3","text":"L’univers est posé comme intégralement peuplé, actif et différencié.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS4","text":"L’indistinction perceptive provient de la distance ou de la limitation de l’observateur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS5","text":"L’analogie de l’étang convertit le grouillement indiscernable en multiplicité réelle d’êtres déterminés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS6","text":"L’argument procède de l’apparence confuse vers une ontologie de l’ordre et de la différenciation invisibles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A1","text":"Rien dans l’univers n’est inculte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A2","text":"Rien dans l’univers n’est stérile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A3","text":"Rien dans l’univers n’est mort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A4","text":"Il n’existe pas de chaos réel dans l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A5","text":"La confusion appartient à l’apparence plutôt qu’à la structure de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A6","text":"Une perception limitée peut amalgamer une multiplicité réelle en un mouvement indistinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A7","text":"Les éléments indistincts dans la perception demeurent distincts dans la réalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A8","text":"L’éloignement réduit la discernabilité sans supprimer la différenciation des êtres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX1","text":"L’univers n’est pas un domaine de stérilité ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX2","text":"L’univers n’est pas un domaine de mort absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX3","text":"La confusion apparente n’est pas une confusion réelle des choses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX4","text":"Le chaos n’est pas une propriété constitutive de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX5","text":"L’indistinction perceptive ne constitue pas une indistinction ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX6","text":"L’absence de discernement n’est pas l’absence d’êtres déterminés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:D1","text":"Toute apparence de chaos doit être rapportée à une limitation de perception plutôt qu’à une désorganisation de l’être.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A4","CH_UCIC_P_61:A5","CH_UCIC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:D2","text":"Une réalité qui paraît vide ou morte peut contenir une activité multiple que l’observateur ne distingue pas.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A2","CH_UCIC_P_61:A3","CH_UCIC_P_61:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:D3","text":"La confusion sensible fonctionne comme une compression perceptive d’une pluralité ordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A6","CH_UCIC_P_61:A7","CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:D4","text":"La distance épistémique ne modifie pas la structure différenciée de ce qui est perçu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A7","CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SD1","text":"L’univers doit être compris comme une totalité d’activité et de différenciation dont les niveaux de perception ne livrent jamais immédiatement l’organisation complète.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A1","CH_UCIC_P_61:A2","CH_UCIC_P_61:A3","CH_UCIC_P_61:A4","CH_UCIC_P_61:A5","CH_UCIC_P_61:A6","CH_UCIC_P_61:A7","CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SD2","text":"Toute apparence de vacuité devient compatible avec une plénitude ontologique inaccessible à une perception insuffisamment résolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A2","CH_UCIC_P_61:A3","CH_UCIC_P_61:A6","CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SD3","text":"L’opposition entre ordre et chaos est déplacée du niveau de l’être au niveau de l’accès perceptif à l’être.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A4","CH_UCIC_P_61:A5","CH_UCIC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une apparence globale puisse fournir à elle seule une preuve de désordre ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’un être soit réellement sans activité ou sans fécondité du seul fait qu’il n’est pas discerné.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX3","text":"Il exclut l’équivalence entre perception indistincte et réalité indifférenciée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX4","text":"Il exclut qu’une limitation de résolution perceptive puisse atteindre ou abolir la structure interne des choses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX1","text":"La possibilité d’un chaos réel et irréductible est forclose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX2","text":"L’existence d’un vide ontologique, même local ou dissimulé, est rendue inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX3","text":"L’absence d’une connaissance distincte n’est jamais autorisée à devenir une absence d’ordre ou d’être.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX4","text":"Le système se construit autour de l’impossibilité d’une nature véritablement morte, stérile ou inarticulée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS1","text":"Apparence de grouillement indistinct → suspension de l’identification entre indistinction et chaos réel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS2","text":"Limitation perceptive → agrégation phénoménale d’une multiplicité d’êtres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS3","text":"Multiplicité réelle → rétablissement de la différenciation sous-jacente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS4","text":"Différenciation sous-jacente → exclusion de la stérilité, de la mort et du chaos ontologiques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS5","text":"Exclusion du chaos réel → conversion de toute confusion observée en effet de distance ou de discernement insuffisant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AF1","text":"Apparence de chaos → limitation du discernement → multiplicité réelle indistinctement perçue → ordre ontologique → exclusion de la stérilité et de la mort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ME1","text":"Le chaos est reclassé comme phénomène de perception plutôt que comme catégorie de l’être.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ME2","text":"Le vide apparent est reclassé comme plénitude active non discernée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ME3","text":"L’indistinction sensible cesse de s’opposer à la différenciation ontologique et devient son mode d’apparition dégradé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ME4","text":"La distance devient une variable épistémique qui affecte la visibilité, non une cause de désorganisation réelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Le mouvement confus observé à distance est interprété comme l’effet de poissons réels mais indiscernables.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Toute apparence de confusion résulte de l’agrégation perceptive d’une multiplicité différenciée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — L’argument impose de diagnostiquer les apparences globales à partir des limites du discernement plutôt qu’à partir d’une désorganisation supposée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — L’univers est présupposé comme continuellement rempli d’activité, de distinction et de fécondité, sans région véritablement morte ou stérile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage : ils établissent la plénitude ontologique et distinguent apparence perceptive et réalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT2","text":"L’analogie de l’étang fournit le mécanisme de passage entre mouvement indistinct et multiplicité déterminée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT3","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la limitation perceptive est admise comme cause de la confusion apparente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT4","text":"Le texte ne démontre pas indépendamment que toute confusion provient nécessairement d’une perception limitée ; il l’affirme dans le cadre de son ontologie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT5","text":"La tension résiduelle porte sur le rapport entre l’ordre universel affirmé et la possibilité effective de le discerner.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : nier le chaos ontologique, expliquer la confusion par la perception, rétablir la multiplicité ordonnée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194040750309Z_82171938","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 69","source_sha256":"27026a2946bca0f6707e3780b9142c2b962ccefb4a56a3b771e840ee47014190","sha256":"26fbe4b1a5e1e4f6c0b4d810d0f1e1fd2e7161983b7fe1081b8e49d0f1d6df96","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:40:40.753979+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS1","text":"The problem is the gap between the appearance of universal confusion and the real structure of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS2","text":"The apparent sterility or mortality of things is reframed as a defect of discernment, not as a property of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS3","text":"The universe is posited as integrally populated, active, and differentiated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS4","text":"Perceptual indistinction arises from the distance or limitation of the observer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS5","text":"The pond analogy converts indiscernible teeming into a real multiplicity of determinate beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AS6","text":"The argument proceeds from confused appearance toward an ontology of invisible order and differentiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A1","text":"Nothing in the universe is uncultivated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A2","text":"Nothing in the universe is sterile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A3","text":"Nothing in the universe is dead.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A4","text":"There is no real chaos in the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A5","text":"Confusion belongs to appearance rather than to the structure of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A6","text":"Limited perception can amalgamate a real multiplicity into an indistinct movement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A7","text":"Elements indistinct in perception remain distinct in reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:A8","text":"Distance reduces discernibility without eliminating the differentiation of beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX1","text":"The universe is not a domain of ontological sterility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX2","text":"The universe is not a domain of absolute death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX3","text":"Apparent confusion is not a real confusion of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX4","text":"Chaos is not a constitutive property of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX5","text":"Perceptual indistinction does not constitute ontological indistinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:NX6","text":"The absence of discernment is not the absence of determinate beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:D1","text":"Every appearance of chaos must be attributed to a limitation of perception rather than to a disorganization of being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A4","CH_UCIC_P_61:A5","CH_UCIC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:D2","text":"A reality that appears empty or dead may contain multiple activity that the observer does not distinguish.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A2","CH_UCIC_P_61:A3","CH_UCIC_P_61:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:D3","text":"Sensory confusion functions as a perceptual compression of an ordered plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A6","CH_UCIC_P_61:A7","CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:D4","text":"Epistemic distance does not alter the differentiated structure of what is perceived.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A7","CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SD1","text":"The universe must be understood as a totality of activity and differentiation whose levels of perception never immediately disclose its complete organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A1","CH_UCIC_P_61:A2","CH_UCIC_P_61:A3","CH_UCIC_P_61:A4","CH_UCIC_P_61:A5","CH_UCIC_P_61:A6","CH_UCIC_P_61:A7","CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SD2","text":"Every appearance of emptiness becomes compatible with an ontological plenitude inaccessible to insufficiently resolved perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A2","CH_UCIC_P_61:A3","CH_UCIC_P_61:A6","CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SD3","text":"The opposition between order and chaos is shifted from the level of being to the level of perceptual access to being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A4","CH_UCIC_P_61:A5","CH_UCIC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a global appearance could by itself provide proof of ontological disorder.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that a being is truly without activity or fecundity merely because it is not discerned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX3","text":"It excludes the equivalence between indistinct perception and undifferentiated reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX4","text":"It excludes the possibility that a limitation of perceptual resolution could affect or abolish the internal structure of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX1","text":"The possibility of real and irreducible chaos is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX2","text":"The existence of an ontological void, even a local or concealed one, is rendered inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX3","text":"The absence of distinct knowledge is never permitted to become an absence of order or being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX4","text":"The system is constructed around the impossibility of a nature that is truly dead, sterile, or unarticulated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS1","text":"Appearance of indistinct teeming → suspension of the identification between indistinction and real chaos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS2","text":"Perceptual limitation → phenomenal aggregation of a multiplicity of beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS3","text":"Real multiplicity → restoration of underlying differentiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS4","text":"Underlying differentiation → exclusion of ontological sterility, death, and chaos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS5","text":"Exclusion of real chaos → conversion of all observed confusion into an effect of distance or insufficient discernment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:AF1","text":"Appearance of chaos → limitation of discernment → real multiplicity indistinctly perceived → ontological order → exclusion of sterility and death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ME1","text":"Chaos is reclassified as a phenomenon of perception rather than as a category of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ME2","text":"Apparent emptiness is reclassified as undiscerningly perceived active plenitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ME3","text":"Sensory indistinction ceases to oppose ontological differentiation and becomes its degraded mode of appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ME4","text":"Distance becomes an epistemic variable that affects visibility, not a cause of real disorganization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — The confused movement observed at a distance is interpreted as the effect of real but indiscernible fish.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Every appearance of confusion results from the perceptual aggregation of a differentiated multiplicity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The argument requires global appearances to be diagnosed on the basis of the limits of discernment rather than of a supposed disorganization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — The universe is presupposed as continuously filled with activity, distinction, and fecundity, without any truly dead or sterile region.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage: they establish ontological plenitude and distinguish perceptual appearance from reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT2","text":"The pond analogy provides the mechanism of transition between indistinct movement and determinate multiplicity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent if perceptual limitation is admitted as the cause of apparent confusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT4","text":"The text does not independently demonstrate that all confusion necessarily arises from limited perception; it asserts this within the framework of its ontology.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT5","text":"The residual tension concerns the relation between the affirmed universal order and the effective possibility of discerning it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the real movement: deny ontological chaos, explain confusion through perception, restore ordered multiplicity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_61:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_61@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_61:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 69"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 69","title":"Proposition 69","context":"Chapter 69","original_title":"Proposition 69"},"original_title":"Proposition 69","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 70","order":70,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_62"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_62@R001","sha256":"8216b3055b2dd58371680daad48730059ca67fd9feb384d5ab072d6dca51ee47","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AS1","text":"Le problème est de déterminer l’organisation interne du corps vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AS2","text":"Le corps vivant est recadré comme une unité dominée par une entéléchie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AS3","text":"Cette unité contient cependant d’autres vivants, eux-mêmes dotés d’une entéléchie dominante ou d’une âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AS4","text":"L’argument passe ainsi de l’unité organique à une hiérarchie emboîtée de centres vitaux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","text":"Chaque corps vivant possède une entéléchie dominante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A2","text":"Chez l’animal, l’entéléchie dominante est l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A3","text":"Le corps vivant possède des membres constitutifs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","text":"Les membres d’un corps vivant contiennent d’autres êtres vivants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A5","text":"Les vivants contenus peuvent être des plantes ou des animaux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A6","text":"Chaque vivant contenu possède à son tour une entéléchie dominante ou une âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A7","text":"La composition corporelle est compatible avec une pluralité de centres vitaux hiérarchisés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX1","text":"Le corps vivant n’est pas une unité dépourvue de vie interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX2","text":"L’entéléchie dominante ne constitue pas l’unique principe vital présent dans le corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX3","text":"Les membres du corps vivant ne sont pas de simples parties inertes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX4","text":"Le vivant n’est pas limité à un seul niveau d’organisation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX5","text":"L’animal n’est pas séparé de la structure générale des vivants emboîtés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:D1","text":"Un corps vivant est simultanément une unité organique et une multiplicité de vivants subordonnés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A3","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:D2","text":"La domination d’une entéléchie n’abolit pas l’autonomie vitale relative des vivants contenus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A6","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:D3","text":"Chaque niveau du corps vivant peut reproduire la même structure d’unité dominante et de pluralité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:D4","text":"La distinction entre corps et organisme devient relative au niveau d’organisation considéré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SD1","text":"Le vivant est structuré comme une hiérarchie récursive de dominations entéléchiques plutôt que comme une unité simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A6","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SD2","text":"Toute totalité vivante est à la fois dominante par rapport à ses parties et subordonnée à une pluralité de vivants internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SD3","text":"L’identité d’un organisme ne repose pas sur l’exclusion de la multiplicité, mais sur l’organisation hiérarchique de cette multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’un organisme puisse être expliqué par un seul principe vital sans niveaux internes de vie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut une conception atomique du corps vivant composée de parties absolument dépourvues d’intériorité vitale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une séparation absolue entre l’unité du corps et la pluralité de ses membres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut une ontologie plate dans laquelle tous les vivants posséderaient le même statut hiérarchique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX1","text":"Le texte forclôt l’existence d’un niveau corporel ultime qui serait simplement matériel et non vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX2","text":"Le texte laisse structurellement indisponible une limite définitive entre organisme, partie organique et organisme contenu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX3","text":"Le texte rend inadmissible une totalité vivante absolument close sur elle-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS1","text":"Corps vivant → entéléchie dominante → unité organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS2","text":"Unité organique → membres vivants internes → pluralité de plantes et d’animaux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS3","text":"Vivant interne → entéléchie dominante ou âme → répétition récursive de la structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS4","text":"Répétition récursive → hiérarchie de vivants emboîtés → coexistence de plusieurs niveaux d’unité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AF1","text":"Corps vivant → entéléchie dominante → membres constitués d’autres vivants → entéléchies internes → hiérarchie récursive du vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ME1","text":"Le corps est reclassé comme une totalité organique composée de totalités organiques subordonnées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ME2","text":"La relation entre partie et totalité devient une relation de niveaux plutôt qu’une opposition fixe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ME3","text":"La pluralité interne cesse d’être une menace pour l’unité et devient son mode de constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ME4","text":"La distinction entre animal, plante et organisme est redistribuée dans une architecture commune d’entéléchies dominantes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT1","text":"Surface — Chaque corps vivant possède une entéléchie dominante, tandis que ses membres contiennent d’autres vivants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT2","text":"Structural — Le corps est organisé par l’emboîtement de centres vitaux hiérarchisés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’unité du vivant est expliquée par l’intégration ordonnée de la multiplicité plutôt que par sa suppression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Le vivant est conçu comme une série potentiellement récursive de niveaux d’individualité, sans terme ultime explicitement assigné.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le mouvement de l’unité dominante vers la pluralité vivante interne.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT2","text":"La structure est cohérente intérieurement : un corps peut être une totalité et contenir d’autres totalités vivantes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT3","text":"La reconstruction préserve le passage de l’entéléchie dominante à l’emboîtement hiérarchique des vivants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT4","text":"La relation exacte entre l’entéléchie dominante du tout et celles des vivants internes reste sous-déterminée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT5","text":"La portée de la récursion et l’existence éventuelle d’un niveau terminal ne sont pas établies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT6","text":"La tension principale réside dans la coexistence d’une unité dominante et d’une pluralité de centres vitaux relativement autonomes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194053932907Z_1a56d29b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 70","source_sha256":"8216b3055b2dd58371680daad48730059ca67fd9feb384d5ab072d6dca51ee47","sha256":"84079dd86e08035be8ff81d694aaa9a09c909802e33e9c0bf79e2c4c0cee5fc4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:40:53.937825+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AS1","text":"The problem is to determine the internal organization of the living body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AS2","text":"The living body is reframed as a unity governed by an entelechy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AS3","text":"This unity nevertheless contains other living beings, themselves endowed with a dominant entelechy or a soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AS4","text":"The argument thus moves from organic unity to an embedded hierarchy of vital centers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","text":"Every living body possesses a dominant entelechy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A2","text":"In the animal, the dominant entelechy is the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A3","text":"The living body possesses constitutive members.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","text":"The members of a living body contain other living beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A5","text":"The living beings contained may be plants or animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A6","text":"Each contained living being in turn possesses a dominant entelechy or a soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:A7","text":"Bodily composition is compatible with a plurality of hierarchized vital centers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX1","text":"The living body is not a unity devoid of internal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX2","text":"The dominant entelechy does not constitute the sole vital principle present in the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX3","text":"The members of the living body are not merely inert parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX4","text":"The living being is not limited to a single level of organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:NX5","text":"The animal is not separated from the general structure of embedded living beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:D1","text":"A living body is simultaneously an organic unity and a multiplicity of subordinate living beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A3","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:D2","text":"The dominance of an entelechy does not abolish the relative vital autonomy of the contained living beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A6","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:D3","text":"Each level of the living body can reproduce the same structure of dominant unity and internal plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:D4","text":"The distinction between body and organism becomes relative to the level of organization under consideration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SD1","text":"The living being is structured as a recursive hierarchy of entelechial dominations rather than as a simple unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A6","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SD2","text":"Every living whole is at once dominant in relation to its parts and subordinate to a plurality of internal living beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SD3","text":"The identity of an organism rests not on the exclusion of multiplicity, but on the hierarchical organization of that multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1","CH_UCIC_P_62:A4","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that an organism can be explained by a single vital principle without internal levels of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX2","text":"The system excludes an atomic conception of the living body composed of parts absolutely devoid of vital interiority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX3","text":"The system excludes an absolute separation between the unity of the body and the plurality of its members.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a flat ontology in which all living beings would possess the same hierarchical status.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX1","text":"The text forecloses the existence of an ultimate bodily level that would be merely material and non-living.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX2","text":"The text renders structurally unavailable a definitive boundary between organism, organic part, and contained organism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX3","text":"The text renders inadmissible a living whole absolutely closed upon itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS1","text":"Living body → dominant entelechy → organic unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS2","text":"Organic unity → internal living members → plurality of plants and animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS3","text":"Internal living being → dominant entelechy or soul → recursive repetition of the structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS4","text":"Recursive repetition → hierarchy of embedded living beings → coexistence of several levels of unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:AF1","text":"Living body → dominant entelechy → members constituted by other living beings → internal entelechies → recursive hierarchy of the living being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ME1","text":"The body is reclassified as an organic whole composed of subordinate organic wholes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ME2","text":"The relation between part and whole becomes a relation of levels rather than a fixed opposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ME3","text":"Internal plurality ceases to be a threat to unity and becomes its mode of constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ME4","text":"The distinction between animal, plant, and organism is redistributed within a common architecture of dominant entelechies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT1","text":"Surface — Every living body possesses a dominant entelechy, while its members contain other living beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT2","text":"Structural — The body is organized through the embedding of hierarchized vital centers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The unity of the living being is explained by the ordered integration of multiplicity rather than by its suppression.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The living being is conceived as a potentially recursive series of levels of individuality, without an ultimate term being explicitly assigned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the movement from dominant unity toward internal living plurality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent: a body can be a whole and contain other living wholes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT3","text":"The reconstruction preserves the passage from the dominant entelechy to the hierarchical embedding of living beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT4","text":"The exact relation between the dominant entelechy of the whole and those of the internal living beings remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT5","text":"The scope of recursion and the possible existence of a terminal level are not established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT6","text":"The principal tension lies in the coexistence of a dominant unity and a plurality of relatively autonomous vital centers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_62:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_62@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_62:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 70"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 70","title":"Proposition 70","context":"Chapter 70","original_title":"Proposition 70"},"original_title":"Proposition 70","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 71","order":71,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_63"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_63@R001","sha256":"e8484ae2f6f1aeedcd79ef5124d7c7304f9fcf638fa1513841836214601b49de","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS1","text":"Le texte corrige une interprétation erronée de la relation entre l’âme et la matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS2","text":"Cette interprétation attribue à chaque âme une portion matérielle propre et permanente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS3","text":"La permanence matérielle est invalidée par le flux continuel des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS4","text":"L’entrée et la sortie incessantes des parties rendent impossible une possession corporelle fixe et éternelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS5","text":"L’argument progresse ainsi de la mésinterprétation à sa réfutation par une ontologie dynamique des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A1","text":"Tous les corps sont soumis à un flux perpétuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A2","text":"Des parties entrent continuellement dans les corps et d’autres en sortent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A3","text":"Une portion de matière ne peut pas rester éternellement affectée à une même âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A4","text":"Une âme ne possède donc pas de masse corporelle propre et permanente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A5","text":"La possession permanente d’autres vivants inférieurs ne peut pas découler d’une affectation matérielle éternelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A6","text":"L’interprétation corrigée repose sur la mutabilité matérielle plutôt que sur la fixité des compositions corporelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX1","text":"Le corps n’est pas une masse stable définitivement attachée à une âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX2","text":"Une âme n’est pas propriétaire pour toujours d’une portion déterminée de matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX3","text":"Les vivants inférieurs ne sont pas matériellement destinés pour toujours au service d’une âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX4","text":"L’identité corporelle n’est pas fondée sur la permanence de ses parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX5","text":"La relation entre l’âme et le corps n’est pas celle d’une appropriation matérielle immuable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:D1","text":"La composition matérielle d’un corps est nécessairement transitoire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A1","CH_UCIC_P_63:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:D2","text":"Une matière continuellement renouvelée ne peut constituer une propriété corporelle éternellement individualisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A2","CH_UCIC_P_63:A3","CH_UCIC_P_63:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:D3","text":"La possession durable d’autres vivants ne peut être déduite de leur simple inclusion matérielle dans le corps d’une âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A4","CH_UCIC_P_63:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:D4","text":"Le flux des parties dissocie l’identité d’un corps de la conservation permanente de sa matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A1","CH_UCIC_P_63:A2","CH_UCIC_P_63:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SD1","text":"L’âme ne peut pas être pensée comme le centre d’un domaine matériel fermé dont les composantes seraient fixées une fois pour toutes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SD2","text":"Toute conception d’une hiérarchie corporelle fondée sur une servitude matérielle éternelle est rendue incompatible avec le renouvellement continu des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SD3","text":"La persistance d’un corps doit être distinguée de la permanence de la matière qui le compose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SD4","text":"Le flux matériel transforme la relation entre identité et possession : ce qui persiste ne persiste pas comme conservation intégrale de ses parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une ontologie des corps comme agrégats matériellement clos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’une identité corporelle puisse être garantie par la conservation numérique des mêmes parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX3","text":"Il exclut qu’une relation d’appropriation éternelle puisse être fondée sur une composition matérielle constamment modifiée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une correspondance fixe entre chaque âme et un stock déterminé de matière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SNX1","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’un univers matériel distribué en possessions corporelles permanentes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SNX2","text":"L’argument tourne autour de l’impossibilité d’une clôture matérielle définitive autour de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SNX3","text":"Est rendue inadmissible l’idée d’une servitude éternelle inscrite dans la fixation des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS1","text":"Interprétation erronée de l’âme comme détentrice d’une matière propre → attribution permanente d’une masse corporelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS2","text":"Flux universel des corps → entrée et sortie continues des parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS3","text":"Entrée et sortie continues → impossibilité d’une affectation matérielle éternelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS4","text":"Impossibilité d’une affectation éternelle → réfutation de la possession permanente des vivants inférieurs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS5","text":"Réfutation de la fixité matérielle → substitution d’une ontologie corporelle dynamique à une ontologie de la propriété corporelle immuable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AF1","text":"Mésinterprétation de la pensée → attribution d’une matière permanente à chaque âme → hypothèse d’une possession éternelle → flux perpétuel des corps → dissolution de la permanence matérielle → rejet de la servitude corporelle définitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ME1","text":"Le corps est reclassé d’une masse fixe en composition matérielle continuellement renouvelée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ME2","text":"L’âme est dissociée de la possession permanente d’un stock corporel déterminé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ME3","text":"La relation entre corps et vivants inférieurs cesse d’être cartographiée comme une appropriation éternelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ME4","text":"La distinction entre persistance d’un corps et permanence de ses parties devient structurellement nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Une interprétation de la relation entre l’âme, la matière et les vivants inférieurs est explicitement rejetée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Le flux des parties empêche toute fixation durable de la composition corporelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — La correction procède par déplacement du débat : au lieu d’examiner une propriété permanente de l’âme, elle impose le mécanisme matériel du renouvellement corporel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Les corps sont constitués dans un temps de transformation continue, incompatible avec une identité matérielle fondée sur la permanence des parties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire la réfutation de la matière propre et permanente attribuée à chaque âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT2","text":"La structure conserve le mouvement réel : mésinterprétation → flux corporel → impossibilité de la permanence matérielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT3","text":"Le rapport exact entre la persistance de l’âme et celle du corps reste sous-déterminé par ce passage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT4","text":"La conclusion sur la possession des vivants inférieurs dépend de l’inférence entre affectation matérielle permanente et service éternel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT5","text":"La force du système réside dans l’axiome du flux universel ; sa limite se situe dans ce que ce flux suffit ou non à établir au-delà de la seule non-permanence corporelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194109461054Z_f23d8b09","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 71","source_sha256":"e8484ae2f6f1aeedcd79ef5124d7c7304f9fcf638fa1513841836214601b49de","sha256":"d5a44d00d7edb865e4ccce18f5ed7b907714a1a1db20fbdda8849192249d134e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:41:09.467870+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS1","text":"The text corrects an erroneous interpretation of the relation between the soul and matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS2","text":"This interpretation attributes to each soul a proper and permanent material portion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS3","text":"Material permanence is invalidated by the continual flux of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS4","text":"The unceasing entry and exit of parts make a fixed and eternal corporeal possession impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AS5","text":"The argument thus proceeds from misinterpretation to its refutation through a dynamic ontology of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A1","text":"All bodies are subject to perpetual flux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A2","text":"Parts continually enter bodies and others leave them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A3","text":"A portion of matter cannot remain eternally assigned to the same soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A4","text":"A soul therefore does not possess a proper and permanent corporeal mass.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A5","text":"The permanent possession of other inferior living beings cannot result from an eternal material assignment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:A6","text":"The corrected interpretation rests on material mutability rather than on the fixity of corporeal compositions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX1","text":"The body is not a stable mass definitively attached to a soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX2","text":"A soul is not forever the owner of a determinate portion of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX3","text":"Inferior living beings are not materially destined forever for the service of a soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX4","text":"Corporeal identity is not founded on the permanence of its parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:NX5","text":"The relation between soul and body is not that of an immutable material appropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:D1","text":"The material composition of a body is necessarily transitory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A1","CH_UCIC_P_63:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:D2","text":"Continuously renewed matter cannot constitute an eternally individualized corporeal property.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A2","CH_UCIC_P_63:A3","CH_UCIC_P_63:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:D3","text":"The enduring possession of other living beings cannot be deduced from their mere material inclusion in the body of a soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A4","CH_UCIC_P_63:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:D4","text":"The flux of parts dissociates the identity of a body from the permanent preservation of its matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A1","CH_UCIC_P_63:A2","CH_UCIC_P_63:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SD1","text":"The soul cannot be conceived as the center of a closed material domain whose components would be fixed once and for all.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SD2","text":"Any conception of a corporeal hierarchy founded on eternal material servitude is rendered incompatible with the continuous renewal of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SD3","text":"The persistence of a body must be distinguished from the permanence of the matter composing it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SD4","text":"Material flux transforms the relation between identity and possession: what persists does not persist as the integral preservation of its parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an ontology of bodies as materially closed aggregates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that a corporeal identity may be guaranteed by the numerical preservation of the same parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX3","text":"It excludes the possibility that a relation of eternal appropriation may be founded on a constantly modified material composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX4","text":"It excludes a fixed correspondence between each soul and a determinate stock of matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SNX1","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of a material universe distributed into permanent corporeal possessions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SNX2","text":"The argument revolves around the impossibility of a definitive material closure around the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:SNX3","text":"The idea of an eternal servitude inscribed in the fixation of bodies is rendered inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS1","text":"Erroneous interpretation of the soul as holder of its own matter → permanent attribution of a corporeal mass.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS2","text":"Universal flux of bodies → continuous entry and exit of parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS3","text":"Continuous entry and exit → impossibility of an eternal material assignment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS4","text":"Impossibility of an eternal assignment → refutation of the permanent possession of inferior living beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS5","text":"Refutation of material fixity → substitution of a dynamic corporeal ontology for an ontology of immutable corporeal property.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:AF1","text":"Misinterpretation of thought → attribution of permanent matter to each soul → hypothesis of an eternal possession → perpetual flux of bodies → dissolution of material permanence → rejection of definitive corporeal servitude.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ME1","text":"The body is reclassified from a fixed mass into a continuously renewed material composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ME2","text":"The soul is dissociated from the permanent possession of a determinate corporeal stock.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ME3","text":"The relation between bodies and inferior living beings ceases to be mapped as an eternal appropriation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ME4","text":"The distinction between the persistence of a body and the permanence of its parts becomes structurally necessary.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — An interpretation of the relation between the soul, matter, and inferior living beings is explicitly rejected.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The flux of parts prevents any enduring fixation of corporeal composition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The correction proceeds by displacing the debate: instead of examining a permanent property of the soul, it imposes the material mechanism of corporeal renewal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Bodies are constituted in a time of continuous transformation, incompatible with a material identity founded on the permanence of parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the refutation of the proper and permanent matter attributed to each soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT2","text":"The structure preserves the actual movement: misinterpretation → corporeal flux → impossibility of material permanence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT3","text":"The exact relation between the persistence of the soul and that of the body remains underdetermined by this passage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT4","text":"The conclusion concerning the possession of inferior living beings depends on the inference between permanent material assignment and eternal service.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT5","text":"The force of the system lies in the axiom of universal flux; its limit lies in what this flux does or does not suffice to establish beyond mere corporeal non-permanence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_63:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_63@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_63:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 71"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 71","title":"Proposition 71","context":"Chapter 71","original_title":"Proposition 71"},"original_title":"Proposition 71","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 72","order":72,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_64"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_64@R001","sha256":"0da669ec4644c4f7f7cd4e399ea520635add131288adbf607e1f4838f6abe75f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS1","text":"La question porte sur le mode de transformation de l’âme à travers les changements corporels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS2","text":"Le changement véritable est recadré comme une transformation progressive et graduelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS3","text":"La continuité de l’âme est fondée sur la conservation non instantanément supprimée de ses organes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS4","text":"La métamorphose animale est admise, tandis que la métempsychose et la transmigration sont exclues.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS5","text":"L’incorporation demeure la condition des âmes et des génies finis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS6","text":"Dieu constitue l’unique exception à la dépendance corporelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A1","text":"L’âme ne change de corps que peu à peu et par degrés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A2","text":"L’âme n’est jamais dépouillée tout d’un coup de tous ses organes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A3","text":"Les animaux peuvent subir une métamorphose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A4","text":"La métamorphose animale n’est pas une métempsychose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A5","text":"Il n’y a pas de transmigration des âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","text":"Il n’existe pas d’âmes tout à fait séparées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A7","text":"Il n’existe pas de génies sans corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A8","text":"Dieu seul est entièrement détaché d’un corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX1","text":"Le changement d’un corps à un autre n’est pas une rupture instantanée de l’âme avec toute organisation corporelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX2","text":"La métamorphose n’est pas une transmigration de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX3","text":"L’âme ne passe pas librement d’un corps préexistant à un autre corps préexistant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX4","text":"Une âme finie ne peut être entièrement séparée de tout corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX5","text":"Un génie fini ne peut exister sans corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX6","text":"Le détachement absolu du corps n’est pas une propriété des créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:D1","text":"La continuité de l’âme est assurée par une transition organique graduelle plutôt que par une substitution corporelle instantanée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A1","CH_UCIC_P_64:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:D2","text":"La métamorphose conserve une continuité d’être qui empêche de l’identifier à une migration entre sujets corporels distincts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A3","CH_UCIC_P_64:A4","CH_UCIC_P_64:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:D3","text":"Toute âme créée demeure liée à une forme quelconque de corporéité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","CH_UCIC_P_64:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:D4","text":"Le détachement absolu constitue une différence de statut entre Dieu et toutes les âmes ou tous les génies créés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","CH_UCIC_P_64:A7","CH_UCIC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SD1","text":"L’identité de l’âme est définie par la continuité graduelle d’une organisation corporelle, non par l’indépendance à l’égard du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A1","CH_UCIC_P_64:A2","CH_UCIC_P_64:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SD2","text":"La transformation corporelle devient compatible avec la permanence du sujet dès lors qu’elle est conçue comme métamorphose continue plutôt que comme migration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A3","CH_UCIC_P_64:A4","CH_UCIC_P_64:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SD3","text":"La distinction entre créature et Dieu est construite comme une asymétrie ontologique de l’incorporation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","CH_UCIC_P_64:A7","CH_UCIC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une âme puisse conserver son identité indépendamment de toute continuité organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’un changement de corps puisse être expliqué par une rupture totale suivie d’une réinstallation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut un dualisme opposant des âmes séparables à des corps simplement extérieurs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut une égalité ontologique entre Dieu et les substances spirituelles créées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX1","text":"L’absence d’une discontinuité absolue entre les états corporels successifs structure toute possibilité de transformation de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX2","text":"La possibilité d’une âme finie absolument sans corps est traitée comme indisponible au niveau ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX3","text":"La conception d’un sujet spirituel entièrement autonome à l’égard de toute organisation corporelle est forclose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX4","text":"Le seul point où la séparation absolue demeure pensable est réservé à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS1","text":"Corps organisé → transformation par degrés → conservation partielle des organes → continuité de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS2","text":"Métamorphose animale → continuité organique → négation de la métempsychose → négation de la transmigration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS3","text":"Dépendance de l’âme créée au corps → impossibilité de l’âme séparée → impossibilité du génie sans corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS4","text":"Exception divine → détachement entièrement accompli → séparation ontologique entre Dieu et les créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AF1","text":"Changement de corps → gradualité de la transformation → maintien des organes → continuité corporelle de l’âme → exclusion de la transmigration → restriction du détachement absolu à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ME1","text":"La frontière entre changement corporel et changement de sujet est redessinée autour de la continuité organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ME2","text":"La métamorphose est reclassée comme transformation interne d’un être plutôt que comme passage d’une âme entre des corps séparés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ME3","text":"Les âmes et les génies créés sont replacés dans le champ de la corporéité nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ME4","text":"Le détachement absolu est retiré aux créatures et réservé à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT1","text":"Surface — L’âme change de corps progressivement et ne perd jamais simultanément tous ses organes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT2","text":"Structural — La continuité de l’identité dépend d’une organisation corporelle qui se transforme sans rupture totale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Les catégories de métamorphose, métempsychose et transmigration sont séparées afin d’empêcher leur confusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Le temps de l’identité est celui d’une continuité graduelle ; la séparation absolue d’un corps appartient exclusivement à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le mouvement principal : gradualité, continuité organique, métamorphose, exclusion de la transmigration et exception divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la corporéité est comprise comme condition permanente des âmes créées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT3","text":"Le point le plus fort du système est l’articulation entre absence de rupture instantanée et refus de la transmigration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT4","text":"Le texte ne précise pas le mécanisme exact par lequel les organes se transforment ni le critère détaillé d’identité à travers les degrés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT5","text":"La tension résiduelle porte sur la compatibilité entre changement de corps et maintien d’une même âme, seulement affirmée par la gradualité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel du texte, mais laisse sous-déterminée la nature précise du corps auquel l’âme demeure toujours liée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194125328047Z_1dd6212c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 72","source_sha256":"0da669ec4644c4f7f7cd4e399ea520635add131288adbf607e1f4838f6abe75f","sha256":"02e1b78888831862dac45c12c78d965cbc7ef6880132b88b9fe99ec0203d74f9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:41:25.332174+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS1","text":"The question concerns the mode of transformation of the soul through bodily changes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS2","text":"True change is reframed as a progressive and gradual transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS3","text":"The continuity of the soul is grounded in the non-instantaneous removal of its organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS4","text":"Animal metamorphosis is admitted, whereas metempsychosis and transmigration are excluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS5","text":"Embodiment remains the condition of finite souls and genii.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AS6","text":"God constitutes the sole exception to bodily dependence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A1","text":"The soul changes bodies only little by little and by degrees.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A2","text":"The soul is never stripped all at once of all its organs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A3","text":"Animals can undergo a metamorphosis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A4","text":"Animal metamorphosis is not metempsychosis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A5","text":"There is no transmigration of souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","text":"There are no souls entirely separate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A7","text":"There are no genii without bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:A8","text":"God alone is entirely detached from a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX1","text":"The change from one body to another is not an instantaneous rupture of the soul from all bodily organization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX2","text":"Metamorphosis is not a transmigration of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX3","text":"The soul does not freely pass from one pre-existing body to another pre-existing body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX4","text":"A finite soul cannot be entirely separated from every body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX5","text":"A finite genius cannot exist without a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:NX6","text":"Absolute detachment from the body is not a property of creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:D1","text":"The continuity of the soul is ensured by a gradual organic transition rather than by an instantaneous bodily substitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A1","CH_UCIC_P_64:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:D2","text":"Metamorphosis preserves a continuity of being that prevents its identification with a migration between distinct bodily subjects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A3","CH_UCIC_P_64:A4","CH_UCIC_P_64:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:D3","text":"Every created soul remains bound to some form of corporeity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","CH_UCIC_P_64:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:D4","text":"Absolute detachment constitutes a difference in status between God and all created souls or genii.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","CH_UCIC_P_64:A7","CH_UCIC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SD1","text":"The identity of the soul is defined by the gradual continuity of a bodily organization, not by independence with respect to the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A1","CH_UCIC_P_64:A2","CH_UCIC_P_64:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SD2","text":"Bodily transformation becomes compatible with the persistence of the subject insofar as it is conceived as continuous metamorphosis rather than as migration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A3","CH_UCIC_P_64:A4","CH_UCIC_P_64:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SD3","text":"The distinction between creature and God is constructed as an ontological asymmetry of embodiment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","CH_UCIC_P_64:A7","CH_UCIC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a soul might preserve its identity independently of all organic continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a change of body might be explained by a total rupture followed by a reinstallation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a dualism opposing separable souls to merely external bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX4","text":"The system excludes an ontological equality between God and created spiritual substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX1","text":"The absence of an absolute discontinuity between successive bodily states structures every possibility of transformation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a finite soul absolutely without a body is treated as ontologically unavailable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX3","text":"The conception of a spiritual subject entirely autonomous with respect to every bodily organization is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX4","text":"The sole point at which absolute separation remains thinkable is reserved for God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS1","text":"Organized body → transformation by degrees → partial preservation of organs → continuity of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS2","text":"Animal metamorphosis → organic continuity → negation of metempsychosis → negation of transmigration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS3","text":"Dependence of the created soul on the body → impossibility of the separate soul → impossibility of the genius without a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS4","text":"Divine exception → detachment fully accomplished → ontological separation between God and creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:AF1","text":"Change of body → graduality of transformation → retention of organs → bodily continuity of the soul → exclusion of transmigration → restriction of absolute detachment to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ME1","text":"The boundary between bodily change and change of subject is redrawn around organic continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ME2","text":"Metamorphosis is reclassified as an internal transformation of a being rather than as the passage of a soul between separate bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ME3","text":"Created souls and genii are placed back within the domain of necessary corporeity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ME4","text":"Absolute detachment is withdrawn from creatures and reserved for God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT1","text":"Surface — The soul changes bodies progressively and never loses all its organs simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT2","text":"Structural — The continuity of identity depends on a bodily organization that transforms without total rupture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The categories of metamorphosis, metempsychosis, and transmigration are separated in order to prevent their confusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The time of identity is that of a gradual continuity; absolute separation from a body belongs exclusively to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the principal movement: graduality, organic continuity, metamorphosis, exclusion of transmigration, and divine exception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if corporeity is understood as a permanent condition of created souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT3","text":"The system's strongest point is the articulation between the absence of instantaneous rupture and the rejection of transmigration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT4","text":"The text does not specify the exact mechanism by which the organs are transformed, nor the detailed criterion of identity through the degrees.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT5","text":"The residual tension concerns the compatibility between change of body and the maintenance of one and the same soul, affirmed only through graduality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text, but leaves underdetermined the precise nature of the body to which the soul always remains bound.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_64:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_64@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_64:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 72"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 72","title":"Proposition 72","context":"Chapter 72","original_title":"Proposition 72"},"original_title":"Proposition 72","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 73","order":73,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_65"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_65@R001","sha256":"358cab0405d0f9822fad6b9993739b92a81ca7003ab6891d089eb6db57e9a24c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS1","text":"Le problème est de déterminer ce que sont réellement la génération et la mort lorsqu’elles sont prises à la rigueur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS2","text":"L’argument écarte les conceptions de la génération et de la mort comme commencements ou destructions absolus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS3","text":"La génération est recadrée comme développement et accroissement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS4","text":"La mort est recadrée comme enveloppement et diminution, non comme séparation de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS5","text":"Le mouvement argumentatif est métaphysique et définitionnel : il remplace les ruptures absolues par des transformations continues de degré et de configuration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","text":"Il n’existe jamais de génération entière prise à la rigueur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","text":"Il n’existe jamais de mort parfaite prise à la rigueur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A3","text":"La mort parfaite ne consiste pas dans la séparation de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","text":"Ce qui est appelé génération consiste en développement et en accroissement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A5","text":"Ce qui est appelé mort consiste en enveloppement et en diminution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A6","text":"Les termes de génération et de mort désignent des transformations relatives plutôt que des passages absolus entre non-être et être.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX1","text":"La génération n’est pas une production entière ou absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX2","text":"La mort n’est pas une destruction parfaite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX3","text":"La mort n’est pas la séparation de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX4","text":"La génération n’est pas un commencement sans continuité préalable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX5","text":"La mort n’est pas une disparition sans reste ni transformation ultérieure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:D1","text":"Toute génération implique la présence antérieure d’un processus susceptible de développement et d’accroissement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:D2","text":"Toute mort implique la persistance d’un processus sous une forme enveloppée et diminuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5","CH_UCIC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:D3","text":"La génération et la mort sont deux orientations inverses d’une même logique de transformation graduelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:D4","text":"La distinction entre génération et mort porte sur le mode de transformation, non sur l’existence ou la non-existence absolue de ce qui se transforme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SD1","text":"L’ontologie produite par le texte privilégie la continuité des transformations sur les ruptures substantielles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SD2","text":"La mort ne supprime pas nécessairement l’identité du processus ; elle en modifie le degré de manifestation et le mode d’organisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_65:A3","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SD3","text":"Les catégories de génération et de mort fonctionnent comme des découpages relatifs opérés sur une continuité métaphysique sous-jacente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5","CH_UCIC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une ontologie fondée sur des commencements et des fins absolument discontinus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut l’identification de la mort avec l’anéantissement de ce qui possède une âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une conception de la réalité dans laquelle les changements de forme équivalent à des changements absolus d’être.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut la possibilité qu’une transformation soit épuisée par son apparence phénoménale de naissance ou de disparition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX1","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une séparation absolue entre l’être antérieur et l’être postérieur à la génération ou à la mort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX2","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’une mort comme terme métaphysique définitif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX3","text":"Le texte traite comme inadmissible l’idée d’un passage intégral du néant à l’être ou de l’être au néant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS1","text":"Transformation continue → absence de génération entière → génération comme développement et accroissement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS2","text":"Transformation continue → absence de mort parfaite → mort comme enveloppement et diminution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS3","text":"Refus de la séparation de l’âme → maintien d’une continuité ontologique → redéfinition de la mort comme modification plutôt que disparition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS4","text":"Développement/accroissement et enveloppement/diminution → polarisation inverse d’un même processus de transformation → effacement des ruptures absolues.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AF1","text":"Génération et mort conçues comme ruptures → refus de leur caractère entier ou parfait → distinction entre séparation de l’âme et transformation du vivant → définition de la génération par développement et accroissement → définition de la mort par enveloppement et diminution → continuité métaphysique des transformations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ME1","text":"La naissance et la mort sont reclassées comme des degrés opposés d’un processus continu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ME2","text":"L’opposition entre apparition et disparition absolues s’effondre au profit d’une opposition entre développement et enveloppement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ME3","text":"La séparation de l’âme cesse d’être le critère constitutif de la mort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ME4","text":"Le champ métaphysique est redessiné autour de transformations de degré, de forme et de manifestation plutôt qu’autour de ruptures ontologiques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Le texte définit la génération comme développement et accroissement, et la mort comme enveloppement et diminution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Les processus appelés génération et mort sont intégrés à une continuité de transformations réversibles ou graduelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — L’argument recadre les catégories ordinaires en les soumettant à une détermination plus rigoureuse que leur usage phénoménal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — L’être est présupposé comme persistant à travers des modifications de degré et de configuration, sans commencement ni fin absolument entiers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le mouvement central : refus des ruptures absolues, puis redéfinition différentielle de la génération et de la mort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la génération et la mort sont comprises comme des transformations continues.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT3","text":"Le système reste sous-déterminé quant au statut précis de l’âme et au mécanisme par lequel elle persiste à travers l’enveloppement et la diminution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT4","text":"La principale tension réside entre l’affirmation universelle de l’absence de mort parfaite et l’usage ordinaire de la catégorie de mort, que le texte conserve tout en la redéfinissant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel du texte, mais elle dépend de l’ellipse qui transforme une opposition entre génération et mort en deux orientations d’un même processus métaphysique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194139682462Z_8781f2a4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 73","source_sha256":"358cab0405d0f9822fad6b9993739b92a81ca7003ab6891d089eb6db57e9a24c","sha256":"c045656e89dccbafa4732d21606db4a9ea7c97809cd2bae769becb6d6412ff35","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:41:39.686753+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS1","text":"The problem is to determine what generation and death really are when taken strictly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS2","text":"The argument rejects conceptions of generation and death as absolute beginnings or destructions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS3","text":"Generation is reframed as development and increase.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS4","text":"Death is reframed as envelopment and diminution, not as separation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AS5","text":"The argumentative movement is metaphysical and definitional: it replaces absolute ruptures with continuous transformations of degree and configuration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","text":"There is never any complete generation, taken strictly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","text":"There is never any perfect death, taken strictly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A3","text":"Perfect death does not consist in the separation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","text":"What is called generation consists in development and increase.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A5","text":"What is called death consists in envelopment and diminution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:A6","text":"The terms generation and death designate relative transformations rather than absolute passages between non-being and being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX1","text":"Generation is not a complete or absolute production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX2","text":"Death is not a perfect destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX3","text":"Death is not the separation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX4","text":"Generation is not a beginning without prior continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:NX5","text":"Death is not a disappearance without remainder or subsequent transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:D1","text":"Every generation implies the prior presence of a process capable of development and increase.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:D2","text":"Every death implies the persistence of a process in an enveloped and diminished form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5","CH_UCIC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:D3","text":"Generation and death are two inverse orientations of the same logic of gradual transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:D4","text":"The distinction between generation and death concerns the mode of transformation, not the absolute existence or non-existence of what is transformed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SD1","text":"The ontology produced by the text privileges the continuity of transformations over substantial ruptures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SD2","text":"Death does not necessarily abolish the identity of the process; it modifies its degree of manifestation and its mode of organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_65:A3","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SD3","text":"The categories of generation and death function as relative divisions imposed upon an underlying metaphysical continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5","CH_UCIC_P_65:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX1","text":"The system excludes an ontology founded on absolutely discontinuous beginnings and ends.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX2","text":"The system excludes identifying death with the annihilation of that which possesses a soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a conception of reality in which changes of form amount to absolute changes of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a transformation be exhausted by its phenomenal appearance of birth or disappearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX1","text":"The structuring absence is that of an absolute separation between being prior to and being subsequent to generation or death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX2","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of death as a definitive metaphysical terminus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX3","text":"The text treats as inadmissible the idea of an integral passage from nothingness to being or from being to nothingness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS1","text":"Continuous transformation → absence of complete generation → generation as development and increase.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS2","text":"Continuous transformation → absence of perfect death → death as envelopment and diminution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS3","text":"Rejection of the separation of the soul → maintenance of an ontological continuity → redefinition of death as modification rather than disappearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS4","text":"Development/increase and envelopment/diminution → inverse polarization of one and the same process of transformation → effacement of absolute ruptures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:AF1","text":"Generation and death conceived as ruptures → rejection of their complete or perfect character → distinction between separation of the soul and transformation of the living being → definition of generation through development and increase → definition of death through envelopment and diminution → metaphysical continuity of transformations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ME1","text":"Birth and death are reclassified as opposite degrees of a continuous process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ME2","text":"The opposition between absolute appearance and disappearance collapses in favor of an opposition between development and envelopment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ME3","text":"The separation of the soul ceases to be the constitutive criterion of death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ME4","text":"The metaphysical field is redrawn around transformations of degree, form, and manifestation rather than around ontological ruptures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — The text defines generation as development and increase, and death as envelopment and diminution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The processes called generation and death are integrated into a continuity of reversible or gradual transformations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The argument reframes ordinary categories by subjecting them to a more rigorous determination than their phenomenal usage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Being is presupposed as persisting through modifications of degree and configuration, without absolutely complete beginning or end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the central movement: rejection of absolute ruptures, then differential redefinition of generation and death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if generation and death are understood as continuous transformations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT3","text":"The system remains underdetermined regarding the precise status of the soul and the mechanism by which it persists through envelopment and diminution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT4","text":"The principal tension lies between the universal assertion of the absence of perfect death and the ordinary use of the category of death, which the text retains while redefining it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_65:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text, but it depends on the ellipsis that transforms an opposition between generation and death into two orientations of the same metaphysical process.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_65:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_65@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_65:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 73"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 73","title":"Proposition 73","context":"Chapter 73","original_title":"Proposition 73"},"original_title":"Proposition 73","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 74","order":74,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_66"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_66@R001","sha256":"bdb5aca1ab1667d4a5190459f7e5f7fefeb5288771cb7aaa5c732a407e103952","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS1","text":"L’origine des formes organiques constitue le problème initial de l’argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS2","text":"L’observation des organismes conduit à recadrer leur production comme génération à partir de semences préformées plutôt que comme émergence spontanée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS3","text":"La préformation du corps implique celle de l’âme et de l’animal lui-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS4","text":"La conception ne produit donc pas l’animal, mais le dispose à une transformation majeure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS5","text":"Les métamorphoses hors génération étendent ce modèle de transformation continue aux changements d’espèce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","text":"Les corps organiques naturels ne proviennent jamais d’un Chaos ou d’une putréfaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","text":"Les corps organiques naturels sont toujours produits par des semences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","text":"Les semences contiennent une préformation de l’organisme à venir.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","text":"Le corps organique existe avant la conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","text":"Une âme existe déjà dans le corps organique avant la conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","text":"L’animal existe déjà avant la conception comme unité corporelle et animée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","text":"La conception dispose un animal préexistant à une transformation considérable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","text":"La transformation peut conduire un animal à devenir un animal d’une autre espèce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A9","text":"Des transformations analogues à la métamorphose génésique se produisent hors de la génération.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX1","text":"La production organique n’est pas une émergence à partir du Chaos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX2","text":"La production organique n’est pas un effet de la putréfaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX3","text":"La conception n’est pas le commencement absolu du corps organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX4","text":"La conception n’est pas la création initiale de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX5","text":"La conception n’est pas la production ex nihilo de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX6","text":"La métamorphose n’est pas limitée au processus de génération.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D1","text":"La préformation de l’organisme rend nécessaire une continuité entre la semence et l’animal développé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D2","text":"Si le corps existe avant la conception, la conception doit être comprise comme modification d’un organisme antérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D3","text":"Si l’âme existe déjà dans le corps préformé, le développement organique est aussi une transformation de l’animal animé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D4","text":"Le changement d’espèce doit être conçu comme transformation d’une identité animale persistante plutôt que comme apparition d’un nouvel animal sans continuité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D5","text":"Les métamorphoses de vers en mouches et de chenilles en papillons fournissent un modèle non génésique de la transformation organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SD1","text":"Toute génération organique devient un épisode de transformation dans une continuité antérieure, et non un événement inaugural.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2","text":"L’unité de l’animal est étendue à travers les changements de forme, de développement et éventuellement d’espèce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SD3","text":"La théorie de la génération se convertit en théorie générale de la métamorphose organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4","text":"L’explication des formes repose sur la persistance d’une organisation corporelle et animée sous des états successifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’un organisme puisse commencer sans support organique antérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’une forme organique soit une propriété nouvellement produite par la matière en décomposition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut que l’âme apparaisse après le corps ou indépendamment de son organisation organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut une rupture ontologique entre l’animal présent dans la semence et l’animal développé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX5","text":"Le système exclut une conception réduite à un commencement individuel sans préhistoire organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une origine organique absolument première.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX2","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’un animal qui ne serait constitué qu’au moment de sa conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX3","text":"Le système rend inadmissible toute séparation absolue entre génération, développement et métamorphose.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS1","text":"Production organique observée → exclusion du Chaos et de la putréfaction → affirmation de la semence comme support nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS2","text":"Semence → préformation du corps → présence antérieure de l’organisme avant la conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS3","text":"Corps préformé → âme déjà présente → animal déjà constitué.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS4","text":"Animal préexistant → conception comme disposition → transformation vers une autre configuration ou espèce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS5","text":"Métamorphose hors génération → extension du schème de transformation → continuité générale de l’animal à travers ses formes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AF1","text":"Embarras sur l’origine des formes → observation de la production organique → exclusion de la génération spontanée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AF2","text":"Exclusion de la génération spontanée → semence préformée → antériorité du corps et de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AF3","text":"Antériorité du corps et de l’âme → animal déjà présent → conception comme transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AF4","text":"Transformation par génération → métamorphose hors génération → généralisation de la continuité organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ME1","text":"L’origine des formes est reclassée comme problème de continuité organique plutôt que comme problème de création initiale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2","text":"La conception est déplacée du registre de la production vers celui de la disposition et de la transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ME3","text":"Le corps, l’âme et l’animal sont cartographiés comme trois dimensions solidaires d’une même préformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ME4","text":"La frontière entre génération et métamorphose est remplacée par un continuum de transformations organiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT1","text":"Surface : les organismes apparaissent par semences et subissent des transformations de forme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT2","text":"Structural : la semence conserve une organisation corporelle et animée antérieure à la conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic : l’explication doit abandonner le modèle de l’origine absolue au profit d’un modèle de transformation continue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal : l’animal est posé comme antérieur à ses états de développement et persistant à travers leurs transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le passage de l’exclusion de la génération spontanée à la préformation organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT2","text":"Ils suffisent également à reconstruire l’inférence du corps préexistant vers l’âme et l’animal préexistants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT3","text":"La structure reste sous-déterminée quant au statut exact de la préformation et au mécanisme précis de la transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT4","text":"La cohérence interne dépend de l’acceptation d’une identité animale persistante à travers les changements de forme et d’espèce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT5","text":"La formulation « sans doute quelque préformation » introduit une qualification conjecturale dans une chaîne ensuite traitée comme principe explicatif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : embarras sur l’origine → preuve empirique alléguée → préformation → antériorité de l’animal → transformation continue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194156289161Z_f6f32f8e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 74","source_sha256":"bdb5aca1ab1667d4a5190459f7e5f7fefeb5288771cb7aaa5c732a407e103952","sha256":"3e15e6d97a15ac675eda0286b68757cea09dd2a77a9c4388936b9fb7f433841a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:41:56.294841+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS1","text":"The origin of organic forms constitutes the initial problem of the argument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS2","text":"Observation of organisms leads to reframing their production as generation from preformed seeds rather than as spontaneous emergence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS3","text":"The preformation of the body entails that of the soul and of the animal itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS4","text":"Conception therefore does not produce the animal, but disposes it toward a major transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AS5","text":"Metamorphoses outside generation extend this model of continuous transformation to changes of species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","text":"Natural organic bodies never arise from a Chaos or from putrefaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","text":"Natural organic bodies are always produced by seeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","text":"Seeds contain a preformation of the organism to come.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","text":"The organic body exists before conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","text":"A soul already exists in the organic body before conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","text":"The animal already exists before conception as a bodily and animate unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","text":"Conception disposes a pre-existing animal toward a considerable transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","text":"Transformation can lead an animal to become an animal of another species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:A9","text":"Transformations analogous to generative metamorphosis occur outside generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX1","text":"Organic production is not an emergence from Chaos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX2","text":"Organic production is not an effect of putrefaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX3","text":"Conception is not the absolute beginning of the organic body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX4","text":"Conception is not the initial creation of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX5","text":"Conception is not the ex nihilo production of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:NX6","text":"Metamorphosis is not limited to the process of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D1","text":"The preformation of the organism makes continuity between the seed and the developed animal necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D2","text":"If the body exists before conception, conception must be understood as the modification of a prior organism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D3","text":"If the soul already exists in the preformed body, organic development is also a transformation of the animate animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D4","text":"Change of species must be conceived as the transformation of a persistent animal identity rather than as the appearance of a new animal without continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:D5","text":"The metamorphoses of worms into flies and of caterpillars into butterflies provide a non-generative model of organic transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SD1","text":"Every organic generation becomes an episode of transformation within an antecedent continuity, rather than an inaugural event.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2","text":"The unity of the animal is extended across changes of form, development, and possibly species.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SD3","text":"The theory of generation is converted into a general theory of organic metamorphosis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4","text":"The explanation of forms rests on the persistence of a bodily and animate organization through successive states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that an organism can begin without a prior organic support.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that an organic form is a property newly produced by decomposing matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX3","text":"The system excludes the possibility that the soul appears after the body or independently of its organic organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX4","text":"The system excludes an ontological rupture between the animal present in the seed and the developed animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX5","text":"The system excludes a conception reduced to an individual beginning without organic prehistory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1","text":"The structuring absence is that of an absolutely first organic origin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX2","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of an animal that would be constituted only at the moment of its conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX3","text":"The system renders inadmissible any absolute separation between generation, development, and metamorphosis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS1","text":"Observed organic production → exclusion of Chaos and putrefaction → affirmation of the seed as necessary support.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS2","text":"Seed → preformation of the body → prior presence of the organism before conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS3","text":"Preformed body → soul already present → animal already constituted.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS4","text":"Pre-existing animal → conception as disposition → transformation toward another configuration or species.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS5","text":"Metamorphosis outside generation → extension of the schema of transformation → general continuity of the animal through its forms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AF1","text":"Perplexity concerning the origin of forms → observation of organic production → exclusion of spontaneous generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AF2","text":"Exclusion of spontaneous generation → preformed seed → priority of the body and the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AF3","text":"Priority of the body and the soul → animal already present → conception as transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:AF4","text":"Transformation through generation → metamorphosis outside generation → generalization of organic continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ME1","text":"The origin of forms is reclassified as a problem of organic continuity rather than as a problem of initial creation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2","text":"Conception is shifted from the register of production to that of disposition and transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ME3","text":"The body, the soul, and the animal are mapped as three interdependent dimensions of one and the same preformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ME4","text":"The boundary between generation and metamorphosis is replaced by a continuum of organic transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT1","text":"Surface: organisms appear through seeds and undergo transformations of form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT2","text":"Structural: the seed preserves a bodily and animate organization prior to conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: explanation must abandon the model of absolute origin in favor of a model of continuous transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: the animal is posited as prior to its developmental states and as persisting through their transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage from the exclusion of spontaneous generation to organic preformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A1","CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT2","text":"They likewise suffice to reconstruct the inference from the pre-existing body to the pre-existing soul and animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT3","text":"The structure remains underdetermined regarding the exact status of preformation and the precise mechanism of transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT4","text":"Its internal coherence depends on the acceptance of a persistent animal identity across changes of form and species.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT5","text":"The formulation « sans doute quelque préformation » introduces a conjectural qualification into a chain subsequently treated as an explanatory principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: perplexity concerning origin → alleged empirical proof → preformation → priority of the animal → continuous transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_66:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_66@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_66:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 74"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 74","title":"Proposition 74","context":"Chapter 74","original_title":"Proposition 74"},"original_title":"Proposition 74","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 75","order":75,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_67"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_67@R001","sha256":"1db7dd62b237c9710a6030c54f41201e71c51accecfb1d602a9947d763ff5d6d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS1","text":"Le texte cherche à distinguer plusieurs degrés d’existence animale à partir du rapport entre conception, reproduction et transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS2","text":"Il recadre certains animaux comme « spermatiques » lorsqu’ils peuvent être élevés au degré de « plus grands animaux ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS3","text":"Il établit que la permanence dans l’espèce constitue le régime majoritaire de naissance, de multiplication et de destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS4","text":"Il réserve le passage à un « plus grand théâtre » à un petit nombre d’animaux élus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS5","text":"L’argument est classificatoire et hiérarchique : il va de la reproduction ordinaire à l’exception transformatrice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A1","text":"Les animaux peuvent être différenciés selon leur capacité à changer de degré d’existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A2","text":"Certains animaux peuvent être élevés au degré de « plus grands animaux » par le moyen de la conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A3","text":"Les animaux susceptibles de cette élévation peuvent être appelés « spermatiques ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","text":"La plupart des animaux demeurent dans leur espèce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A5","text":"Les animaux qui demeurent dans leur espèce naissent, se multiplient et sont détruits selon le régime des « grands animaux ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A6","text":"Le passage à un degré supérieur concerne seulement un petit nombre d’animaux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A7","text":"Le passage à un degré supérieur est présenté comme une sélection, et non comme le destin commun des animaux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A8","text":"Le degré supérieur est figuré comme un « plus grand théâtre » distinct du régime ordinaire de l’espèce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX1","text":"La reproduction ordinaire ne suffit pas à produire une élévation de degré.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX2","text":"Le fait d’être animal ne signifie pas que tout individu passe à un « plus grand théâtre ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX3","text":"La permanence dans l’espèce n’est pas identifiée au passage à une condition supérieure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX4","text":"L’élévation n’est pas la condition majoritaire de la vie animale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX5","text":"Le régime des animaux demeurant dans leur espèce n’est pas supprimé par l’existence des animaux élus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:D1","text":"Le statut d’animal « spermatique » dépend d’une possibilité de transformation, et non de la seule appartenance présente à une espèce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A1","CH_UCIC_P_67:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:D2","text":"La conception fonctionne comme opérateur de hiérarchisation lorsqu’elle rend possible l’élévation vers le degré des « plus grands animaux ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:D3","text":"Le cycle naissance–multiplication–destruction constitue le régime normal des animaux qui ne franchissent pas le seuil supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:D4","text":"La distinction entre animaux ordinaires et animaux élus est quantitative autant que qualitative : la majorité reste dans l’espèce, tandis qu’une minorité change de théâtre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6","CH_UCIC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","text":"Le devenir animal est organisé selon une structure à deux régimes : reproduction et destruction dans l’espèce d’un côté, élévation et changement de théâtre de l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6","CH_UCIC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","text":"La continuité spécifique apparaît comme la règle de conservation, tandis que l’élévation constitue une exception sélective qui reconfigure l’échelle des êtres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6","CH_UCIC_P_67:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SD3","text":"La conception ne décrit pas seulement une génération : elle devient le lieu où une continuité animale peut être convertie en changement de degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A3","CH_UCIC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une conception de l’évolution animale comme transformation universelle et uniforme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX2","text":"Il exclut que la reproduction de l’espèce soit le signe nécessaire d’un progrès ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX3","text":"Il exclut que l’appartenance à la catégorie animale détermine à elle seule l’accès au degré supérieur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une opposition simple entre existence et destruction : les animaux ordinaires vivent selon un cycle qui inclut structurellement leur destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1","text":"Le texte s’organise autour de l’absence d’un passage généralisé entre les degrés animaux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX2","text":"Le « plus grand théâtre » demeure une possibilité sélective dont les conditions précises ne sont pas exposées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX3","text":"La majorité est structurellement tenue à distance de l’élévation, sans que cette exclusion soit expliquée par une cause détaillée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS1","text":"Possibilité de conception transformatrice → attribution du statut « spermatique ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS2","text":"Absence de passage effectif → maintien dans l’espèce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS3","text":"Maintien dans l’espèce → naissance → multiplication → destruction selon le régime des grands animaux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS4","text":"Sélection minoritaire → élévation au degré de « plus grands animaux ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS5","text":"Élévation → passage vers un « plus grand théâtre ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6","text":"La distribution finale oppose un régime majoritaire de conservation cyclique à un régime minoritaire de transformation théâtrale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AF1","text":"Différenciation des animaux → possibilité d’élévation par la conception → nomination des animaux « spermatiques » → maintien majoritaire dans l’espèce → cycle ordinaire de vie et de destruction → sélection d’un petit nombre → passage à un « plus grand théâtre ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ME1","text":"L’animalité est reclassée selon une capacité différentielle de passage entre degrés, plutôt que selon une catégorie homogène.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ME2","text":"La reproduction est divisée en deux fonctions conceptuelles : reproduction conservatrice de l’espèce et vecteur possible d’élévation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ME3","text":"La majorité statistique devient un régime ontologique ordinaire, tandis que la minorité élue devient l’indice d’une hiérarchie supérieure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ME4","text":"L’espace de l’existence animale est cartographié comme une succession de théâtres, dont l’accès n’est pas également distribué.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le texte distingue les animaux qui demeurent dans leur espèce de ceux qui passent à un degré supérieur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT2","text":"Structural — La conception articule reproduction, conservation spécifique et possibilité de transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le vocabulaire de l’élection et du théâtre transforme une différence de devenir en hiérarchie de trajectoires.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’existence animale est distribuée entre un cycle temporel fermé — naissance, multiplication, destruction — et un passage vers un degré ou un théâtre supérieur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire la distinction entre régime ordinaire et régime d’élévation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente : la majorité demeure dans l’espèce et une minorité seulement la dépasse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT3","text":"Le rôle exact de la « conception » dans l’élévation reste sous-déterminé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT4","text":"Le rapport entre « animaux spermatiques », « grands animaux » et « plus grands animaux » n’est pas entièrement explicité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT5","text":"La sélection des « élus » est affirmée mais non causalement expliquée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : classification → régime majoritaire → exception sélective → changement de théâtre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194211561744Z_5425dcd9","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 75","source_sha256":"1db7dd62b237c9710a6030c54f41201e71c51accecfb1d602a9947d763ff5d6d","sha256":"33bab748799a2f619e7ba15a26a207d6dd9e3b82dfc7858317df0420b2674884","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:42:11.568139+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS1","text":"The text seeks to distinguish several degrees of animal existence on the basis of the relation between conception, reproduction, and transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS2","text":"It recasts certain animals as “spermatic” when they can be raised to the degree of “greater animals.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS3","text":"It establishes that remaining within the species constitutes the predominant regime of birth, multiplication, and destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS4","text":"It reserves passage to a “greater theatre” for a small number of chosen animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AS5","text":"The argument is classificatory and hierarchical: it proceeds from ordinary reproduction to the transformative exception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A1","text":"Animals can be differentiated according to their capacity to change their degree of existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A2","text":"Certain animals can be raised to the degree of “greater animals” by means of conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A3","text":"Animals susceptible to this elevation may be called “spermatic.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","text":"Most animals remain within their species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A5","text":"Animals that remain within their species are born, multiply, and are destroyed according to the regime of “great animals.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A6","text":"Passage to a higher degree concerns only a small number of animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A7","text":"Passage to a higher degree is presented as a selection, rather than as the common destiny of animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:A8","text":"The higher degree is figured as a “greater theatre” distinct from the ordinary regime of the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX1","text":"Ordinary reproduction does not suffice to produce an elevation of degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX2","text":"Being an animal does not mean that every individual passes to a “greater theatre.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX3","text":"Remaining within the species is not identified with passage to a higher condition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX4","text":"Elevation is not the predominant condition of animal life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:NX5","text":"The regime of animals remaining within their species is not abolished by the existence of chosen animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:D1","text":"The status of a “spermatic” animal depends on a possibility of transformation, rather than on present membership in a species alone.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A1","CH_UCIC_P_67:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:D2","text":"Conception functions as an operator of hierarchization when it makes possible elevation toward the degree of “greater animals.”","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:D3","text":"The cycle birth–multiplication–destruction constitutes the normal regime of animals that do not cross the higher threshold.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:D4","text":"The distinction between ordinary animals and chosen animals is quantitative as much as qualitative: the majority remains within the species, while a minority changes theatre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6","CH_UCIC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","text":"Animal becoming is organized according to a two-regime structure: reproduction and destruction within the species on one side, elevation and change of theatre on the other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6","CH_UCIC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","text":"Specific continuity appears as the rule of conservation, while elevation constitutes a selective exception that reconfigures the scale of beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6","CH_UCIC_P_67:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SD3","text":"Conception does not describe generation alone: it becomes the site where an animal continuity can be converted into a change of degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A3","CH_UCIC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1","text":"The system excludes a conception of animal evolution as universal and uniform transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX2","text":"It excludes the notion that reproduction of the species is the necessary sign of ontological progress.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX3","text":"It excludes the notion that membership in the animal category alone determines access to the higher degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX4","text":"It excludes a simple opposition between existence and destruction: ordinary animals live according to a cycle that structurally includes their destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1","text":"The text is organized around the absence of a generalized passage between animal degrees.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX2","text":"The “greater theatre” remains a selective possibility whose precise conditions are not set forth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX3","text":"The majority is structurally kept at a distance from elevation, without this exclusion being explained by a detailed cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS1","text":"Possibility of transformative conception → attribution of “spermatic” status.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS2","text":"Absence of effective passage → remaining within the species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS3","text":"Remaining within the species → birth → multiplication → destruction according to the regime of great animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS4","text":"Minority selection → elevation to the degree of “greater animals.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS5","text":"Elevation → passage toward a “greater theatre.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6","text":"The final distribution contrasts a majority regime of cyclical conservation with a minority regime of theatrical transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:AF1","text":"Differentiation of animals → possibility of elevation through conception → naming of “spermatic” animals → majority remaining within the species → ordinary cycle of life and destruction → selection of a small number → passage to a “greater theatre.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ME1","text":"Animality is reclassified according to a differential capacity for passage between degrees, rather than according to a homogeneous category.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ME2","text":"Reproduction is divided into two conceptual functions: species-conserving reproduction and a possible vector of elevation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ME3","text":"The statistical majority becomes an ordinary ontological regime, while the chosen minority becomes the index of a higher hierarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ME4","text":"The space of animal existence is mapped as a succession of theatres, access to which is not equally distributed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text distinguishes animals that remain within their species from those that pass to a higher degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT2","text":"Structural — Conception articulates reproduction, specific conservation, and the possibility of transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The vocabulary of election and theatre transforms a difference in becoming into a hierarchy of trajectories.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Animal existence is distributed between a closed temporal cycle — birth, multiplication, destruction — and a passage toward a higher degree or theatre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the distinction between the ordinary regime and the regime of elevation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent: the majority remains within the species, and only a minority exceeds it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT3","text":"The exact role of “conception” in elevation remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT4","text":"The relation between “spermatic animals,” “great animals,” and “greater animals” is not fully made explicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT5","text":"The selection of the “chosen” is asserted but not causally explained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: classification → majority regime → selective exception → change of theatre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_67:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_67@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_67:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 75"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 75","title":"Proposition 75","context":"Chapter 75","original_title":"Proposition 75"},"original_title":"Proposition 75","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 76","order":76,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_68"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_68@R001","sha256":"ebd2ff3948e1550cd2de937fc9099cb020dfc196655ac205204e70218f2e56d5","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AS1","text":"L’absence de commencement naturel chez l’animal engage l’examen de son terme naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AS2","text":"Le raisonnement recadre la mort comme autre chose qu’une destruction entière de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AS3","text":"La négation de la génération naturelle s’étend à la négation de la destruction naturelle absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AS4","text":"Une inférence tirée des expériences est déclarée concordante avec des principes établis a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","text":"L’animal ne commence jamais naturellement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A2","text":"Ce qui ne commence pas naturellement ne finit pas naturellement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A3","text":"La génération naturelle n’a pas lieu au sens rigoureux du texte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A4","text":"La destruction entière de l’animal n’a pas lieu naturellement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A5","text":"La mort prise à la rigueur n’est pas une destruction naturelle absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","text":"Les raisonnements tirés des expériences peuvent confirmer des principes déduits a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A7","text":"Les principes a priori mentionnés antérieurement fournissent le cadre explicatif des phénomènes de génération et de mort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX1","text":"L’animal n’est pas un être qui commence naturellement par génération.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX2","text":"La mort n’est pas une destruction entière de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX3","text":"La mort apparente n’est pas la mort prise à la rigueur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX4","text":"La fin observable n’est pas un terme naturel absolu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5","text":"L’expérience ne constitue pas un principe indépendant des principes a priori ; elle leur est accordée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:D1","text":"L’animal doit être pensé comme persistant à travers les transformations qui paraissent constituer sa naissance ou sa mort.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_68:A2","CH_UCIC_P_68:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:D2","text":"La génération et la destruction appartiennent au registre des apparences ou des transformations, non à celui des commencements et anéantissements absolus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_68:A3","CH_UCIC_P_68:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:D3","text":"La notion rigoureuse de mort est séparée de l’événement empirique appelé mort.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A4","CH_UCIC_P_68:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:D4","text":"Les observations expérimentales reçoivent leur portée théorique de leur conformité aux principes a priori.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","CH_UCIC_P_68:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SD1","text":"La continuité naturelle de l’animal exclut simultanément son apparition absolue et son anéantissement absolu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_68:A2","CH_UCIC_P_68:A3","CH_UCIC_P_68:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SD2","text":"Les événements biologiques sont reclassés comme des modifications d’un être persistant plutôt que comme des passages entre être et néant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_68:A4","CH_UCIC_P_68:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SD3","text":"L’accord entre expérience et a priori transforme l’observation d’une absence de génération ou de destruction absolue en confirmation d’une structure métaphysique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","CH_UCIC_P_68:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’un être naturel puisse surgir absolument à partir du non-être.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’un être naturel puisse retourner absolument au non-être.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut que les catégories empiriques de naissance et de mort suffisent à déterminer l’ontologie de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut une opposition simple entre existence et inexistence comme description adéquate des transformations naturelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX1","text":"L’anéantissement naturel absolu est la possibilité forclose qui donne sa portée à la distinction entre mort et mort rigoureuse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX2","text":"Le néant comme origine ou destination naturelle de l’animal est rendu indisponible par la continuité présupposée de son existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX3","text":"La discontinuité ontologique entre génération et destruction est silencieusement remplacée par une permanence sous transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS1","text":"Absence de commencement naturel → principe de non-fin naturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS2","text":"Non-fin naturelle → exclusion de la génération et de la destruction absolues.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS3","text":"Exclusion de la destruction entière → distinction entre mort empirique et mort rigoureuse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS4","text":"Confrontation aux expériences → confirmation des conclusions négatives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5","text":"Concordance avec les principes a priori → fermeture du circuit entre observation et fondement métaphysique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AF1","text":"Commencement naturel refusé → fin naturelle refusée → génération et destruction absolues exclues → mort empirique dissociée de la mort rigoureuse → expérience accordée à l’a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1","text":"La naissance et la mort sont reclassées comme transformations plutôt que comme événements absolus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ME2","text":"La notion d’animal est déplacée d’une identité définie par ses limites temporelles vers une identité maintenue à travers ces limites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ME3","text":"L’expérience cesse d’être le fondement ultime et devient l’instance de vérification d’une structure a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ME4","text":"L’opposition entre vie et mort est remplacée par une distinction entre changement observable et anéantissement rigoureux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le texte nie la génération naturelle, la destruction entière et la mort au sens strict.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT2","text":"Structural — L’animal est défini par une continuité qui traverse les changements qualifiés de naissance ou de mort.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le raisonnement articule une inférence empirique à des principes a priori afin de produire une validation réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’existence naturelle est conçue sans commencement ni fin absolus ; le temps biologique décrit des transformations plutôt que des passages par le néant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le mouvement allant de l’absence de commencement à l’absence de destruction absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT2","text":"La distinction entre mort empirique et mort rigoureuse est nécessaire pour préserver la portée exacte de la conclusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT3","text":"La concordance entre expérience et a priori complète la structure justificative du passage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT4","text":"Le lien entre absence de commencement et absence de fin est affirmé comme principe opératoire plutôt que démontré dans le passage lui-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction reste dépendante de principes a priori antérieurs qui ne sont pas reproduits dans cette proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT6","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente, mais son fondement complet demeure sous-déterminé par l’ellipse des principes précédents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194226632458Z_a602c75c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 76","source_sha256":"ebd2ff3948e1550cd2de937fc9099cb020dfc196655ac205204e70218f2e56d5","sha256":"58b2515f8278de4b9e1b4dadd3d648f7d2027d8b29e5d1119cc886156f70ef0a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:42:26.637519+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AS1","text":"The absence of a natural beginning in the animal entails examination of its natural end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AS2","text":"The reasoning reframes death as something other than the entire destruction of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AS3","text":"The negation of natural generation extends to the negation of absolute natural destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AS4","text":"An inference drawn from experiments is declared concordant with principles established a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","text":"The animal never begins naturally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A2","text":"What does not begin naturally does not end naturally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A3","text":"Natural generation does not occur in the rigorous sense of the text.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A4","text":"The entire destruction of the animal does not occur naturally.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A5","text":"Death taken rigorously is not an absolute natural destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","text":"Reasonings drawn from experiments can confirm principles deduced a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:A7","text":"The a priori principles mentioned previously provide the explanatory framework for the phenomena of generation and death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX1","text":"The animal is not a being that naturally begins through generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX2","text":"Death is not an entire destruction of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX3","text":"Apparent death is not death taken rigorously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX4","text":"The observable end is not an absolute natural term.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5","text":"Experience does not constitute a principle independent of a priori principles; it is accorded with them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:D1","text":"The animal must be thought as persisting through the transformations that appear to constitute its birth or its death.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_68:A2","CH_UCIC_P_68:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:D2","text":"Generation and destruction belong to the register of appearances or transformations, not to that of absolute beginnings and annihilations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_68:A3","CH_UCIC_P_68:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:D3","text":"The rigorous notion of death is separated from the empirical event called death.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A4","CH_UCIC_P_68:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:D4","text":"Experimental observations receive their theoretical import from their conformity with a priori principles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","CH_UCIC_P_68:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SD1","text":"The natural continuity of the animal simultaneously excludes its absolute appearance and its absolute annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_68:A2","CH_UCIC_P_68:A3","CH_UCIC_P_68:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SD2","text":"Biological events are reclassified as modifications of a persisting being rather than as passages between being and nothingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_68:A4","CH_UCIC_P_68:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SD3","text":"The agreement between experience and the a priori transforms the observation of an absence of absolute generation or destruction into confirmation of a metaphysical structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","CH_UCIC_P_68:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a natural being could arise absolutely from non-being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a natural being could return absolutely to non-being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX3","text":"The system excludes that the empirical categories of birth and death suffice to determine the ontology of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a simple opposition between existence and non-existence as an adequate description of natural transformations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX1","text":"Absolute natural annihilation is the foreclosed possibility that gives its import to the distinction between death and rigorous death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX2","text":"Nothingness as the natural origin or destination of the animal is rendered unavailable by the presupposed continuity of its existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX3","text":"The ontological discontinuity between generation and destruction is silently replaced by permanence under transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS1","text":"Absence of natural beginning → principle of non-natural end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS2","text":"Non-natural end → exclusion of absolute generation and destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS3","text":"Exclusion of entire destruction → distinction between empirical death and rigorous death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS4","text":"Confrontation with experiments → confirmation of negative conclusions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5","text":"Concordance with a priori principles → closure of the circuit between observation and metaphysical foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:AF1","text":"Natural beginning refused → natural end refused → absolute generation and destruction excluded → empirical death dissociated from rigorous death → experience accorded with the a priori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1","text":"Birth and death are reclassified as transformations rather than as absolute events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ME2","text":"The notion of animal is shifted from an identity defined by its temporal limits toward an identity maintained through those limits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ME3","text":"Experience ceases to be the ultimate foundation and becomes the instance of verification of an a priori structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ME4","text":"The opposition between life and death is replaced by a distinction between observable change and rigorous annihilation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text denies natural generation, entire destruction, and death in the strict sense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT2","text":"Structural — The animal is defined by a continuity that traverses the changes described as birth or death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The reasoning articulates an empirical inference with a priori principles in order to produce reciprocal validation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Natural existence is conceived without absolute beginning or end; biological time describes transformations rather than passages through nothingness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from the absence of beginning to the absence of absolute destruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT2","text":"The distinction between empirical death and rigorous death is necessary to preserve the exact import of the conclusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT3","text":"The concordance between experience and the a priori completes the justificatory structure of the passage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT4","text":"The link between absence of beginning and absence of end is affirmed as an operative principle rather than demonstrated in the passage itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction remains dependent on prior a priori principles that are not reproduced in this proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT6","text":"The structure is internally coherent, but its complete foundation remains underdetermined by the ellipsis of the preceding principles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_68:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_68@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_68:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 76"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 76","title":"Proposition 76","context":"Chapter 76","original_title":"Proposition 76"},"original_title":"Proposition 76","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 77","order":77,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_69"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_69@R001","sha256":"25676f9ad648604962b2a22abcd3db684ed8d60cd088950df8d38d52933d1b3f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS1","text":"Le problème est de déterminer si la disparition partielle de la machine organique entraîne celle de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS2","text":"L’argument recadre l’animal comme une réalité distincte de la configuration matérielle momentanée de sa machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS3","text":"L’âme est posée comme miroir d’un univers indestructible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS4","text":"De cette indestructibilité de l’âme, l’argument étend l’indestructibilité à l’animal lui-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS5","text":"La périssabilité partielle de la machine et le renouvellement des dépouilles organiques deviennent compatibles avec la permanence de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A1","text":"L’univers dont l’âme est le miroir est indestructible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A2","text":"L’âme est le miroir de cet univers indestructible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","text":"Ce qui possède une âme ne se réduit pas à la matière organique qui compose momentanément sa machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","text":"L’indestructibilité de l’âme implique l’indestructibilité de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","text":"La machine de l’animal peut périr en partie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A6","text":"L’animal peut quitter ou prendre des dépouilles organiques sans cesser d’être le même animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:NX1","text":"L’animal n’est pas identique à l’intégralité actuelle de sa machine organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:NX2","text":"La destruction partielle de la machine n’est pas la destruction de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:NX3","text":"Le changement de dépouilles organiques n’est pas une succession d’animaux entièrement distincts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:NX4","text":"L’indestructibilité de l’animal ne signifie pas l’indestructibilité de chacune de ses parties matérielles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:D1","text":"La permanence de l’animal doit être cherchée dans le principe animé plutôt que dans la conservation intégrale de sa matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","CH_UCIC_P_69:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:D2","text":"La continuité organique peut subsister à travers une variation matérielle partielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:D3","text":"La mort ou la perte d’une partie de la machine ne suffit pas à conclure à la disparition de l’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","CH_UCIC_P_69:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:D4","text":"L’identité de l’animal est découplée de l’identité numérique de ses dépouilles organiques successives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1","text":"Le vivant est défini comme une unité persistante capable d’intégrer la variation matérielle sans être anéantie par elle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SD2","text":"La destruction physique est reclassée comme modification locale de la machine plutôt que comme suppression de l’être animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SD3","text":"La permanence du vivant repose sur une hiérarchie ontologique où l’âme commande l’identité et où la matière organique assure une fonction changeante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A2","CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX1","text":"Le système dépend du rejet de l’hypothèse selon laquelle l’identité d’un animal serait constituée par la conservation de ses mêmes composants matériels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’une machine organique puisse être le principe ultime de l’identité animale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX3","text":"Il disqualifie l’équivalence entre changement matériel et anéantissement ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX4","text":"Il refuse qu’une périssabilité locale produise nécessairement une mortalité absolue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX1","text":"L’argument forclôt la possibilité d’un animal entièrement réductible à son état corporel présent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX2","text":"Il rend indisponible une conception de la mort comme disparition totale de l’unité vivante dès qu’une partie de sa machine périt.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX3","text":"Il laisse hors système une identité animale sans principe interne de continuité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS1","text":"Univers indestructible → âme-miroir → indestructibilité de l’âme → indestructibilité de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS2","text":"Machine organique partiellement périssable → renouvellement des dépouilles → distinction entre support matériel et unité animale → compatibilité entre changement corporel et permanence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS3","text":"Principe animé supra-matériel + matière organique variable → identité persistante de l’animal malgré la transformation de sa machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AF1","text":"Périssabilité partielle de la machine → distinction entre machine et animal → fondation de l’âme dans un univers indestructible → extension de l’indestructibilité à l’animal → permanence à travers les changements organiques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ME1","text":"L’objet « animal » est reclassé d’agrégat matériel en unité persistante portant une machine variable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ME2","text":"La distinction entre destruction locale et disparition totale devient opératoire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ME3","text":"Le renouvellement organique cesse de fonctionner comme preuve de discontinuité individuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4","text":"La matière corporelle devient un support remplaçable plutôt que le critère exhaustif de l’identité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT1","text":"Surface — L’animal demeure indestructible malgré la destruction partielle de sa machine et le changement de ses dépouilles organiques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT2","text":"Structural — L’identité animale est organisée par la dissociation entre principe animé et configuration matérielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’argument neutralise l’objection empirique selon laquelle la transformation ou la perte corporelle abolirait l’unité du vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’animal est une permanence qui traverse une succession de compositions organiques sans être identique à chacune d’elles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement principal : miroir cosmique, indestructibilité de l’âme, extension à l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT2","text":"La distinction entre animal et machine suffit à intégrer la périssabilité partielle du corps dans le système.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT3","text":"Le critère précis de l’identité qui subsiste à travers les dépouilles organiques reste sous-déterminé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT4","text":"Le passage de l’indestructibilité de l’âme à celle de l’animal est affirmé, mais sa médiation démonstrative demeure elliptique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT5","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si l’âme est admise comme principe constitutif de l’animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT6","text":"La tension principale oppose la périssabilité effective de la machine à l’indestructibilité attribuée à l’unité animale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT7","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel, mais dépend de la force d’une implication métaphysique non explicitée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194240287860Z_c7bf05ef","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 77","source_sha256":"25676f9ad648604962b2a22abcd3db684ed8d60cd088950df8d38d52933d1b3f","sha256":"88e3207108e2572beff0e3807b73bc4bf63d5dcb46958329d69cd08582170457","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:42:40.294072+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS1","text":"The problem is to determine whether the partial disappearance of the organic machine entails that of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS2","text":"The argument reframes the animal as a reality distinct from the momentary material configuration of its machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS3","text":"The soul is posited as the mirror of an indestructible universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS4","text":"From this indestructibility of the soul, the argument extends indestructibility to the animal itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AS5","text":"The partial perishability of the machine and the renewal of organic vestments become compatible with the permanence of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A1","text":"The universe of which the soul is the mirror is indestructible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A2","text":"The soul is the mirror of this indestructible universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","text":"What possesses a soul is not reducible to the organic matter that momentarily composes its machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","text":"The indestructibility of the soul entails the indestructibility of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","text":"The animal's machine can perish in part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:A6","text":"The animal can leave or take on organic vestments without ceasing to be the same animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:NX1","text":"The animal is not identical to the present entirety of its organic machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:NX2","text":"The partial destruction of the machine is not the destruction of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:NX3","text":"The change of organic vestments is not a succession of wholly distinct animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:NX4","text":"The indestructibility of the animal does not mean the indestructibility of each of its material parts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:D1","text":"The permanence of the animal must be sought in the animate principle rather than in the integral preservation of its matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","CH_UCIC_P_69:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:D2","text":"Organic continuity can persist through partial material variation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:D3","text":"The death or loss of a part of the machine is not sufficient to conclude that the animal has disappeared.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","CH_UCIC_P_69:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:D4","text":"The identity of the animal is decoupled from the numerical identity of its successive organic vestments.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1","text":"The living being is defined as a persistent unity capable of integrating material variation without being annihilated by it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SD2","text":"Physical destruction is reclassified as a local modification of the machine rather than as the suppression of animal being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SD3","text":"The permanence of the living being rests on an ontological hierarchy in which the soul governs identity and organic matter performs a changing function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A2","CH_UCIC_P_69:A3","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX1","text":"The system depends on rejecting the hypothesis according to which an animal's identity would be constituted by the preservation of its same material components.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that an organic machine could be the ultimate principle of animal identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX3","text":"It disqualifies the equivalence between material change and ontological annihilation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX4","text":"It rejects the notion that local perishability necessarily produces absolute mortality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX1","text":"The argument forecloses the possibility of an animal wholly reducible to its present bodily state.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX2","text":"It renders unavailable a conception of death as the total disappearance of the living unity as soon as a part of its machine perishes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX3","text":"It leaves outside the system an animal identity without an internal principle of continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS1","text":"Indestructible universe → mirror-soul → indestructibility of the soul → indestructibility of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS2","text":"Partially perishable organic machine → renewal of vestments → distinction between material support and animal unity → compatibility between bodily change and permanence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS3","text":"Supra-material animate principle + variable organic matter → persistent identity of the animal despite the transformation of its machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:AF1","text":"Partial perishability of the machine → distinction between machine and animal → grounding of the soul in an indestructible universe → extension of indestructibility to the animal → permanence through organic changes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ME1","text":"The object “animal” is reclassified from a material aggregate into a persistent unity bearing a variable machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ME2","text":"The distinction between local destruction and total disappearance becomes operative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ME3","text":"Organic renewal ceases to function as proof of individual discontinuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4","text":"Bodily matter becomes a replaceable support rather than the exhaustive criterion of identity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT1","text":"Surface — The animal remains indestructible despite the partial destruction of its machine and the change of its organic vestments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT2","text":"Structural — Animal identity is organized by the dissociation between animate principle and material configuration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument neutralizes the empirical objection according to which bodily transformation or loss would abolish the unity of the living being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The animal is a permanence that traverses a succession of organic compositions without being identical to any one of them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal movement: cosmic mirror, indestructibility of the soul, extension to the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT2","text":"The distinction between animal and machine suffices to integrate the partial perishability of the body into the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT3","text":"The precise criterion of the identity that persists through organic vestments remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT4","text":"The transition from the indestructibility of the soul to that of the animal is asserted, but its demonstrative mediation remains elliptical.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT5","text":"The structure is internally coherent if the soul is admitted as the constitutive principle of the animal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT6","text":"The principal tension opposes the effective perishability of the machine to the indestructibility attributed to animal unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement, but depends on the force of an unexplicated metaphysical implication.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_69:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_69@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_69:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 77"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 77","title":"Proposition 77","context":"Chapter 77","original_title":"Proposition 77"},"original_title":"Proposition 77","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 78","order":78,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_70"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_70@R001","sha256":"80944f5a0a0a5cf4364af76cd8786d322ed6df2d2a197cb7beb96172203d5c1f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS1","text":"Le problème est d’expliquer l’union ou la conformité de l’âme et du corps organique sans réduire leurs lois propres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS2","text":"L’argument recadre cette union comme une coordination entre deux ordres autonomes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS3","text":"Chaque ordre suit ses propres lois, mais tous deux appartiennent à l’harmonie préétablie des substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS4","text":"La conformité devient explicable parce que toutes les substances représentent un même univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS5","text":"Le modèle est métaphysique et reconstructif : autonomie locale → harmonie globale → conformité âme-corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","text":"L’âme suit ses propres lois.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","text":"Le corps organique suit ses propres lois.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A3","text":"L’âme et le corps organique constituent deux ordres de détermination distincts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","text":"Une harmonie préétablie existe entre toutes les substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A5","text":"Toutes les substances sont des représentations d’un même univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A6","text":"L’union de l’âme et du corps se manifeste comme une conformité entre leurs développements respectifs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:NX1","text":"L’âme et le corps ne sont pas gouvernés par une loi unique qui abolirait leur hétérogénéité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:NX2","text":"La conformité de l’âme et du corps n’est pas produite par l’abandon des lois propres de chacun.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:NX3","text":"L’union n’est pas définie comme une fusion indifférenciée des deux ordres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:NX4","text":"La rencontre de l’âme et du corps n’est pas rapportée à une coordination locale isolée du système des substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:D1","text":"Deux séries autonomes peuvent être conformes sans perdre leur indépendance légale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","CH_UCIC_P_70:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:D2","text":"L’union âme-corps est expliquée par une correspondance réglée plutôt que par l’identité de leurs opérations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A3","CH_UCIC_P_70:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:D3","text":"La conformité locale de l’âme et du corps dépend d’une structure universelle de représentation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","CH_UCIC_P_70:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:D4","text":"La notion de rencontre désigne l’accord de deux développements coordonnés par avance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","CH_UCIC_P_70:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1","text":"L’unité d’un composé ne requiert pas l’homogénéité de ses principes ; elle résulte de leur inscription dans une même harmonie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","CH_UCIC_P_70:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SD2","text":"Le même univers fonctionne comme principe de commensurabilité entre des substances qui demeurent distinctes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A3","CH_UCIC_P_70:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","text":"La causalité apparente entre l’âme et le corps est reconduite à une synchronisation métaphysique des séries.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","CH_UCIC_P_70:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX1","text":"Le système doit exclure qu’une substance modifie directement les lois propres d’une autre substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX2","text":"Il doit exclure que la conformité âme-corps soit un événement contingent ou ponctuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX3","text":"Il doit exclure qu’un ordre particulier puisse être intelligible indépendamment de la totalité universelle qu’il représente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX4","text":"Il doit exclure une conception de l’union fondée sur une interaction empirique suffisante à elle seule.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX1","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une interaction causale directe entre l’âme et le corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX2","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’une unité fondée sur la fusion ou la transmission d’une même opération entre deux substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX3","text":"Le système rend indisponible toute explication de la conformité qui ne passerait pas par l’ordre total de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS1","text":"Deux ordres distincts sont posés : lois de l’âme / lois du corps organique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS2","text":"Leur séparation est maintenue au niveau local.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS3","text":"Une harmonie préétablie est introduite au niveau global.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS4","text":"La représentation d’un même univers fournit le principe de correspondance entre les ordres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS5","text":"La correspondance globale produit la conformité observable comme union de l’âme et du corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AF1","text":"Union âme-corps → distinction de leurs lois propres → harmonie préétablie → représentation commune de l’univers → conformité coordonnée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1","text":"L’union âme-corps est reclassée : d’un problème d’interaction locale, elle devient un effet d’harmonie systémique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2","text":"L’autonomie des substances cesse d’être une objection à leur conformité et devient sa condition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ME3","text":"Le corps organique et l’âme sont cartographiés comme deux séries distinctes rapportées à une même totalité représentée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ME4","text":"La relation locale est subordonnée à l’architecture universelle des substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT1","text":"Surface — L’âme et le corps organique apparaissent unis ou conformes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT2","text":"Structural — Chacun suit une légalité propre, tandis que leurs séries sont coordonnées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le problème est déplacé de l’interaction entre substances vers la condition de leur accord.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Toutes les substances représentent un même univers selon une harmonie préétablie qui règle d’avance leur correspondance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement : distinction des lois propres, harmonie universelle, conformité locale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT2","text":"La reconstruction reste sous-déterminée quant au mécanisme précis de l’harmonie préétablie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT3","text":"Le système est intérieurement cohérent à condition que la conformité ne soit pas interprétée comme interaction directe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT4","text":"Sa force réside dans la conversion de l’autonomie des substances en principe de coordination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT5","text":"Sa tension principale tient à l’écart entre le vocabulaire de la « rencontre » et l’exclusion implicite d’une causalité réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT6","text":"L’explication dite naturelle dépend d’un présupposé métaphysique global qui n’est pas lui-même dérivé dans la proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194255147115Z_9c5bc6aa","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 78","source_sha256":"80944f5a0a0a5cf4364af76cd8786d322ed6df2d2a197cb7beb96172203d5c1f","sha256":"4f407af90c981f47678560f2f10141422012a5b6e6bf2fff137e1d9e0fa382d7","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:42:55.149149+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS1","text":"The problem is to explain the union or conformity of the soul and the organic body without reducing their proper laws.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS2","text":"The argument reframes this union as a coordination between two autonomous orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS3","text":"Each order follows its own laws, but both belong to the pre-established harmony of substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS4","text":"Conformity becomes explicable because all substances represent one and the same universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AS5","text":"The model is metaphysical and reconstructive: local autonomy → global harmony → soul-body conformity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","text":"The soul follows its own laws.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","text":"The organic body follows its own laws.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A3","text":"The soul and the organic body constitute two distinct orders of determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","text":"A pre-established harmony exists among all substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A5","text":"All substances are representations of one and the same universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:A6","text":"The union of the soul and the body manifests itself as a conformity between their respective developments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:NX1","text":"The soul and the body are not governed by a single law that would abolish their heterogeneity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:NX2","text":"The conformity of the soul and the body is not produced by abandoning the proper laws of each.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:NX3","text":"The union is not defined as an undifferentiated fusion of the two orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:NX4","text":"The encounter of the soul and the body is not attributed to a local coordination isolated from the system of substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:D1","text":"Two autonomous series can be conformable without losing their nomological independence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","CH_UCIC_P_70:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:D2","text":"The soul-body union is explained by a regulated correspondence rather than by the identity of their operations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A3","CH_UCIC_P_70:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:D3","text":"The local conformity of the soul and the body depends on a universal structure of representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","CH_UCIC_P_70:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:D4","text":"The notion of encounter denotes the agreement of two developments coordinated in advance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","CH_UCIC_P_70:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1","text":"The unity of a composite does not require the homogeneity of its principles; it results from their inscription within one and the same harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","CH_UCIC_P_70:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SD2","text":"The same universe functions as a principle of commensurability among substances that remain distinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A3","CH_UCIC_P_70:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","text":"The apparent causality between the soul and the body is traced back to a metaphysical synchronization of the series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2","CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","CH_UCIC_P_70:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX1","text":"The system must exclude the possibility that one substance directly modifies the proper laws of another substance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX2","text":"It must exclude the possibility that soul-body conformity is a contingent or punctual event.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX3","text":"It must exclude the possibility that a particular order can be intelligible independently of the universal totality that it represents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX4","text":"It must exclude a conception of union founded on an empirical interaction sufficient in itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX1","text":"The structuring absence is that of a direct causal interaction between the soul and the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX2","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of a unity founded on the fusion or transmission of one and the same operation between two substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX3","text":"The system renders unavailable any explanation of conformity that would not pass through the total order of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS1","text":"Two distinct orders are posited: laws of the soul / laws of the organic body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS2","text":"Their separation is maintained at the local level.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS3","text":"A pre-established harmony is introduced at the global level.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS4","text":"The representation of one and the same universe provides the principle of correspondence between the orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS5","text":"The global correspondence produces the observable conformity as the union of the soul and the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:AF1","text":"Soul-body union → distinction of their proper laws → pre-established harmony → common representation of the universe → coordinated conformity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1","text":"The soul-body union is reclassified: from a problem of local interaction, it becomes an effect of systemic harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2","text":"The autonomy of substances ceases to be an objection to their conformity and becomes its condition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ME3","text":"The organic body and the soul are mapped as two distinct series related to one and the same represented totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ME4","text":"The local relation is subordinated to the universal architecture of substances.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT1","text":"Surface — The soul and the organic body appear united or conformable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT2","text":"Structural — Each follows its own lawfulness, while their series are coordinated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The problem is displaced from interaction among substances to the condition of their agreement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — All substances represent one and the same universe according to a pre-established harmony that regulates their correspondence in advance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement: distinction of proper laws, universal harmony, local conformity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined with respect to the precise mechanism of the pre-established harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT3","text":"The system is internally coherent provided that conformity is not interpreted as direct interaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT4","text":"Its force lies in the conversion of the autonomy of substances into a principle of coordination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT5","text":"Its principal tension lies in the gap between the vocabulary of the « encounter » and the implicit exclusion of reciprocal causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT6","text":"The so-called natural explanation depends on a global metaphysical presupposition that is not itself derived in the proposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_70:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_70@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_70:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 78"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 78","title":"Proposition 78","context":"Chapter 78","original_title":"Proposition 78"},"original_title":"Proposition 78","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 79","order":79,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_71"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_71@R001","sha256":"5e3c1a9b6ed5c1c0bbc71bdb7edaa174d5ce421ddaf6d57df159b947d5d65d16","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AS1","text":"L’argument distingue deux régimes causaux irréductibles : la finalité pour les âmes et l’efficience pour les corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AS2","text":"Chaque régime reçoit son mode propre d’action : appétitions, fins et moyens d’un côté ; mouvements de l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AS3","text":"La distinction des causalités n’implique pas leur disjonction réelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AS4","text":"L’harmonie entre causes finales et causes efficientes constitue la résolution de leur dualité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","text":"Les âmes agissent selon les lois des causes finales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:A2","text":"L’action des âmes se déploie par appétitions, fins et moyens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:A3","text":"Les corps agissent selon les lois des causes efficientes ou des mouvements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:A4","text":"Le règne des causes finales et le règne des causes efficientes sont harmoniques entre eux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:NX1","text":"L’action des âmes n’est pas définie par les seules causes efficientes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:NX2","text":"L’action des corps n’est pas définie par les seules causes finales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:NX3","text":"La distinction des deux règnes n’est pas une séparation sans relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:NX4","text":"Aucun des deux régimes causaux n’est réduit à l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:D1","text":"L’âme et le corps doivent être expliqués par deux grammaires causales distinctes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A2","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:D2","text":"Les appétitions, les fins et les moyens constituent la médiation interne de l’action des âmes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:D3","text":"Les mouvements constituent la forme opératoire sous laquelle l’action corporelle relève de l’efficience.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:D4","text":"La pluralité des régimes causaux est compatible avec l’unité ordonnée du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3","CH_UCIC_P_71:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","text":"La causalité est stratifiée plutôt qu’univoque : une même réalité ordonnée comporte un registre intentionnel et un registre mécanique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3","CH_UCIC_P_71:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SD2","text":"L’harmonie fonctionne comme principe de coordination entre des causalités qui demeurent distinctes dans leur mode d’action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A2","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3","CH_UCIC_P_71:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX1","text":"Le texte exclut qu’une explication causale unique suffise à rendre compte des âmes et des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX2","text":"Il exclut que la différence entre finalité et efficience produise une incompatibilité ontologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX3","text":"Il exclut que l’harmonie procède d’une confusion des deux régimes causaux.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX1","text":"L’indépendance absolue des deux ordres causaux est forclose : leur coexistence exige une relation d’harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX2","text":"La réduction du réel à la mécanique ou à la téléologie est rendue inadmissible par la distribution parallèle des causalités.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX3","text":"La médiation concrète par laquelle les deux règnes sont harmoniques reste non spécifiée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS1","text":"Différenciation ontologique : âmes ≠ corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS2","text":"Attribution causale : âmes → causes finales ; corps → causes efficientes ou mouvements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS3","text":"Déploiement modal : causes finales → appétitions → fins → moyens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS4","text":"Coordination inter-régionale : causes finales ∥ causes efficientes → harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS5","text":"Clôture systémique : distinction des lois causales + harmonie des règnes → coexistence ordonnée sans réduction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AF1","text":"Distinction des êtres → attribution de lois causales propres → spécification des modes d’action → coordination des deux règnes → harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ME1","text":"Le champ causal est reclassé en deux règnes fonctionnellement distincts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ME2","text":"L’opposition entre finalité et efficience cesse d’être une alternative exclusive et devient une différence compatible avec l’harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ME3","text":"Les âmes et les corps deviennent deux pôles d’une architecture causale coordonnée plutôt que deux domaines causalement isolés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT1","text":"Surface — Les âmes relèvent des causes finales ; les corps relèvent des causes efficientes ou des mouvements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT2","text":"Structural — Le réel est organisé par la coexistence de deux régimes légaux d’action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La dualité causale est recadrée comme coordination harmonique plutôt que comme conflit explicatif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’ordre du réel admet simultanément une causalité orientée par les fins et une causalité déployée dans les mouvements ; leur mode précis de simultanéité demeure indéterminé.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT1","text":"Les quatre axiomes suffisent à reconstruire la distinction des deux règnes, leurs modes d’action et leur harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT2","text":"La chaîne générative préserve le mouvement réel : distinction → attribution → spécification → coordination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT3","text":"Le système est intérieurement cohérent tant que l’harmonie ne signifie ni identité ni réduction des causalités.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT4","text":"La relation concrète entre l’action finale de l’âme et le mouvement corporel reste sous-déterminée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT5","text":"La force du système réside dans la compatibilité posée entre deux causalités distinctes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT6","text":"Sa principale tension réside dans l’affirmation de l’harmonie sans explicitation du mécanisme qui la produit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194310244535Z_4c3bbd53","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 79","source_sha256":"5e3c1a9b6ed5c1c0bbc71bdb7edaa174d5ce421ddaf6d57df159b947d5d65d16","sha256":"25498e2f73903adad68f890d93872957bec3bdb310d48b6a2561ea187e325107","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:43:10.250046+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AS1","text":"The argument distinguishes two irreducible causal regimes: finality for souls and efficiency for bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AS2","text":"Each regime receives its own mode of action: appetitions, ends, and means on one side; motions on the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AS3","text":"The distinction of causalities does not imply their real disjunction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AS4","text":"The harmony between final causes and efficient causes constitutes the resolution of their duality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","text":"Souls act according to the laws of final causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:A2","text":"The action of souls unfolds through appetitions, ends, and means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:A3","text":"Bodies act according to the laws of efficient causes or of motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:A4","text":"The realm of final causes and the realm of efficient causes are harmonious with one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:NX1","text":"The action of souls is not defined by efficient causes alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:NX2","text":"The action of bodies is not defined by final causes alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:NX3","text":"The distinction of the two realms is not a separation without relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:NX4","text":"Neither of the two causal regimes is reduced to the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:D1","text":"Soul and body must be explained by two distinct causal grammars.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A2","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:D2","text":"Appetitions, ends, and means constitute the internal mediation of the action of souls.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:D3","text":"Motions constitute the operative form under which bodily action falls under efficiency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:D4","text":"The plurality of causal regimes is compatible with the ordered unity of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3","CH_UCIC_P_71:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","text":"Causality is stratified rather than univocal: one and the same ordered reality includes an intentional register and a mechanical register.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3","CH_UCIC_P_71:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SD2","text":"Harmony functions as a principle of coordination between causalities that remain distinct in their mode of action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A2","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3","CH_UCIC_P_71:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX1","text":"The text excludes the possibility that a single causal explanation suffices to account for souls and bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that the difference between finality and efficiency produces an ontological incompatibility.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX3","text":"It excludes the possibility that harmony proceeds from a confusion of the two causal regimes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX1","text":"The absolute independence of the two causal orders is foreclosed: their coexistence requires a relation of harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX2","text":"The reduction of reality to mechanics or to teleology is rendered inadmissible by the parallel distribution of causalities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX3","text":"The concrete mediation through which the two realms are harmonious remains unspecified.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS1","text":"Ontological differentiation: souls ≠ bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS2","text":"Causal attribution: souls → final causes; bodies → efficient causes or motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS3","text":"Modal unfolding: final causes → appetitions → ends → means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS4","text":"Inter-regime coordination: final causes ∥ efficient causes → harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:FGS5","text":"Systemic closure: distinction of causal laws + harmony of the realms → ordered coexistence without reduction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:AF1","text":"Distinction of beings → attribution of proper causal laws → specification of modes of action → coordination of the two realms → harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ME1","text":"The causal field is reclassified into two functionally distinct realms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ME2","text":"The opposition between finality and efficiency ceases to be an exclusive alternative and becomes a difference compatible with harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ME3","text":"Souls and bodies become two poles of a coordinated causal architecture rather than two causally isolated domains.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT1","text":"Surface — Souls fall under final causes; bodies fall under efficient causes or motions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT2","text":"Structural — Reality is organized by the coexistence of two law-governed regimes of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Causal duality is reframed as harmonious coordination rather than as explanatory conflict.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The order of reality simultaneously admits a causality oriented by ends and a causality unfolding in motions; their precise mode of simultaneity remains indeterminate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT1","text":"The four axioms suffice to reconstruct the distinction of the two realms, their modes of action, and their harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT2","text":"The generative chain preserves the real movement: distinction → attribution → specification → coordination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT3","text":"The system is internally coherent so long as harmony signifies neither identity nor reduction of causalities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT4","text":"The concrete relation between the final action of the soul and bodily motion remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT5","text":"The strength of the system resides in the posited compatibility between two distinct causalities.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT6","text":"Its principal tension resides in the affirmation of harmony without explication of the mechanism that produces it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_71:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_71@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_71:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 79"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 79","title":"Proposition 79","context":"Chapter 79","original_title":"Proposition 79"},"original_title":"Proposition 79","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 80","order":80,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_72"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_72@R001","sha256":"f3fe3a3711de95b4e5a8fdf8e3be5f8289b8a61b29a05baa2f9dea1aedc921d7","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS1","text":"Le problème porte sur la possibilité attribuée à l’âme de modifier causalement le mouvement des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS2","text":"La conservation de la force exclut que l’âme fournisse une force nouvelle aux corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS3","text":"La conservation de la direction totale exclut également que l’âme réoriente causalement les corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS4","text":"L’erreur cartésienne provient de la connaissance incomplète des lois de la nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS5","text":"La double conservation transforme l’interaction âme-corps en coordination sans causalité transitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS6","text":"La compréhension complète de ces lois conduit nécessairement au système de l’harmonie préétablie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","text":"La matière contient toujours la même quantité totale de force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A2","text":"Une âme ne peut pas donner de force à un corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","text":"La direction totale de la matière se conserve selon une loi de la nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A4","text":"Une modification de la direction d’un corps nécessiterait une intervention causale de l’âme sur ce corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A5","text":"Les lois naturelles de conservation rendent impossible toute production ou modification physique provenant de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A6","text":"La croyance cartésienne en une action de l’âme sur la direction des corps repose sur l’ignorance de la loi de conservation de la direction totale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A7","text":"La reconnaissance complète des lois de conservation conduit à l’harmonie préétablie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX1","text":"L’âme n’est pas une source de force physique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX2","text":"L’âme n’est pas une cause efficiente de la direction des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX3","text":"La conservation de la force ne suffit pas à autoriser une action sur la direction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX4","text":"La direction apparente donnée par l’âme n’est pas une exception aux lois naturelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX5","text":"L’interaction directe entre âme et corps n’est pas compatible avec la conservation physique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX6","text":"L’erreur cartésienne n’est pas une simple erreur descriptive indépendante des lois de la nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D1","text":"Si la force totale est conservée, l’âme ne peut accroître l’énergie physique d’un corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","CH_UCIC_P_72:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D2","text":"Si la direction totale de la matière est conservée, l’âme ne peut réorienter causalement un corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A4","CH_UCIC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D3","text":"L’action de l’âme sur le corps devient une apparence explicable par la coordination plutôt que par le transfert causal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A2","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D4","text":"La seconde conservation complète la première en fermant la possibilité d’une causalité mentale indirecte par changement de direction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D5","text":"La théorie cartésienne devient intenable dès lors que la loi de conservation de la direction est connue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A4","CH_UCIC_P_72:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SD1","text":"Le problème de l’interaction âme-corps est reconstruit comme un problème de compatibilité avec les invariants de la matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SD2","text":"La causalité mentale est remplacée par une correspondance réglée entre séries psychiques et séries corporelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A2","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3","text":"L’harmonie préétablie apparaît comme la conséquence métaphysique d’une clôture complète de la causalité physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A5","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SD4","text":"Le progrès théorique consiste ici à passer d’une causalité supposée à une loi structurelle de coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A6","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’un événement mental puisse modifier la quantité totale de force matérielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’une causalité puisse subsister sous la forme d’une simple réorientation sans production de force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut que l’expérience de l’action volontaire constitue une preuve de l’interaction réelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut une nature physiquement ouverte à des interventions extramatérielles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX5","text":"Le système exclut que l’insuffisance historique d’une théorie puisse être corrigée sans réviser son modèle causal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX1","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’une causalité psychophysique directe qui ne violerait aucune conservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX2","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un transfert causal entre deux ordres de réalité hétérogènes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX3","text":"Le système traite comme inadmissible toute spontanéité physique de l’âme dans le corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX4","text":"Ce qui disparaît derrière l’apparence de l’action est une interaction réelle remplacée par une synchronisation préétablie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS1","text":"Hypothèse d’une action de l’âme sur le corps → application de la conservation de la force → impossibilité d’une production physique par l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS2","text":"Maintien de l’hypothèse sous la forme d’un changement de direction → application de la conservation de la direction totale → impossibilité d’une réorientation causale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS3","text":"Identification de l’ignorance de cette seconde loi comme cause de l’erreur cartésienne → déplacement du problème de la volonté vers la connaissance des lois naturelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS4","text":"Fermeture de toute causalité physique de l’âme → substitution d’une coordination sans interaction → formulation de l’harmonie préétablie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5","text":"Conservation de la force + conservation de la direction → clôture de la causalité matérielle → nécessité du recadrage harmonique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AF1","text":"Interaction supposée → conservation de la force → impossibilité du transfert causal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AF2","text":"Réduction cartésienne de l’interaction au changement de direction → conservation de la direction totale → impossibilité de la réorientation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AF3","text":"Lacune de connaissance → diagnostic de l’erreur → rejet de l’interaction → harmonie préétablie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME1","text":"La distinction entre force et direction cesse d’ouvrir deux modes distincts d’action de l’âme ; les deux sont soumis à des lois de conservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME2","text":"L’interaction âme-corps est reclassée comme apparence phénoménale plutôt que comme mécanisme causal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME3","text":"La connaissance des lois naturelles devient le critère de résolution d’un problème métaphysique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME4","text":"Le champ causal est redistribué : la matière conserve ses invariants, tandis que l’ordre psychique ne produit aucun changement matériel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME5","text":"L’harmonie préétablie devient une solution structurale au lieu d’une hypothèse concurrente sur l’action de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT1","text":"Surface — L’âme est supposée pouvoir donner de la force ou changer la direction des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT2","text":"Structural — Deux lois de conservation ferment successivement les deux formes possibles d’intervention psychophysique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le désaccord métaphysique est recadré comme effet d’une connaissance incomplète des lois naturelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La matière forme un ordre causal autonome et invariant ; l’harmonie désigne la coordination de séries qui ne se causent pas mutuellement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage de l’interaction supposée à l’harmonie préétablie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT2","text":"La distinction entre conservation de la force et conservation de la direction est indispensable à la reconstruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT3","text":"L’attribution à Descartes doit rester différenciée : il rejette le transfert de force mais maintient le changement de direction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4","text":"Le système reste sous-déterminé quant au mécanisme positif de l’harmonie préétablie ; le passage affirme sa nécessité sans l’expliciter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT5","text":"La cohérence interne dépend de l’assimilation entre conservation de la direction totale et impossibilité de toute réorientation locale par l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : concession partielle à Descartes → extension de la loi naturelle → réfutation → conclusion harmonique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194327478938Z_8309072a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 80","source_sha256":"f3fe3a3711de95b4e5a8fdf8e3be5f8289b8a61b29a05baa2f9dea1aedc921d7","sha256":"07f313829481f28e3d9f3f0860d8c7367e2b2cd29a7eaa81fd131f3a870e40af","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:43:27.483174+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS1","text":"The problem concerns the possibility attributed to the soul of causally modifying the movement of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS2","text":"The conservation of force excludes the soul's providing a new force to bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS3","text":"The conservation of total direction likewise excludes the soul's causally reorienting bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS4","text":"The Cartesian error stems from incomplete knowledge of the laws of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS5","text":"The double conservation transforms soul-body interaction into coordination without transitive causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AS6","text":"The complete understanding of these laws necessarily leads to the system of pre-established harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","text":"Matter always contains the same total quantity of force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A2","text":"A soul cannot give force to a body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","text":"The total direction of matter is conserved according to a law of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A4","text":"A modification of the direction of a body would require a causal intervention of the soul upon that body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A5","text":"The natural laws of conservation render impossible any physical production or modification originating from the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A6","text":"The Cartesian belief in an action of the soul upon the direction of bodies rests on ignorance of the law of conservation of total direction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:A7","text":"Complete recognition of the laws of conservation leads to pre-established harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX1","text":"The soul is not a source of physical force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX2","text":"The soul is not an efficient cause of the direction of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX3","text":"The conservation of force does not suffice to authorize an action upon direction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX4","text":"The apparent direction given by the soul is not an exception to the laws of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX5","text":"Direct interaction between soul and body is not compatible with physical conservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:NX6","text":"The Cartesian error is not a mere descriptive error independent of the laws of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D1","text":"If total force is conserved, the soul cannot increase the physical energy of a body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","CH_UCIC_P_72:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D2","text":"If the total direction of matter is conserved, the soul cannot causally reorient a body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A4","CH_UCIC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D3","text":"The action of the soul upon the body becomes an appearance explicable by coordination rather than by causal transfer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A2","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D4","text":"The second conservation completes the first by closing off the possibility of an indirect mental causality through a change of direction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:D5","text":"Cartesian theory becomes untenable as soon as the law of conservation of direction is known.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A4","CH_UCIC_P_72:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SD1","text":"The problem of soul-body interaction is reconstructed as a problem of compatibility with the invariants of matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SD2","text":"Mental causality is replaced by a regulated correspondence between psychic series and bodily series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A2","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3","text":"Pre-established harmony appears as the metaphysical consequence of a complete closure of physical causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A5","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SD4","text":"Theoretical progress here consists in passing from a supposed causality to a structural law of coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A6","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a mental event may modify the total quantity of material force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that causality may subsist in the form of a mere reorientation without production of force.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX3","text":"The system excludes the possibility that the experience of voluntary action constitutes proof of real interaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX4","text":"The system excludes a nature physically open to extra-material interventions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX5","text":"The system excludes the possibility that the historical insufficiency of a theory may be corrected without revising its causal model.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX1","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of a direct psychophysical causality that would violate no conservation law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX2","text":"The structuring absence is that of a causal transfer between two heterogeneous orders of reality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX3","text":"The system treats as inadmissible every physical spontaneity of the soul in the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX4","text":"What disappears behind the appearance of action is a real interaction replaced by a pre-established synchronization.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS1","text":"Hypothesis of an action of the soul upon the body → application of the conservation of force → impossibility of a physical production by the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS2","text":"Maintenance of the hypothesis in the form of a change of direction → application of the conservation of total direction → impossibility of a causal reorientation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS3","text":"Identification of ignorance of this second law as the cause of the Cartesian error → displacement of the problem from the will to knowledge of the laws of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS4","text":"Closure of all physical causality of the soul → substitution of a coordination without interaction → formulation of pre-established harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5","text":"Conservation of force + conservation of direction → closure of material causality → necessity of harmonious reframing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AF1","text":"Supposed interaction → conservation of force → impossibility of causal transfer.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AF2","text":"Cartesian reduction of interaction to a change of direction → conservation of total direction → impossibility of reorientation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:AF3","text":"Gap in knowledge → diagnosis of error → rejection of interaction → pre-established harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME1","text":"The distinction between force and direction no longer opens two distinct modes of action of the soul; both are subject to laws of conservation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME2","text":"Soul-body interaction is reclassified as a phenomenal appearance rather than as a causal mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME3","text":"Knowledge of the laws of nature becomes the criterion for resolving a metaphysical problem.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME4","text":"The causal field is redistributed: matter preserves its invariants, while the psychic order produces no material change.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ME5","text":"Pre-established harmony becomes a structural solution rather than a competing hypothesis concerning the action of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT1","text":"Surface — The soul is supposed capable of giving force to or changing the direction of bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT2","text":"Structural — Two laws of conservation successively close off the two possible forms of psychophysical intervention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The metaphysical disagreement is reframed as an effect of incomplete knowledge of the laws of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Matter forms an autonomous and invariant causal order; harmony designates the coordination of series that do not mutually cause one another.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage from supposed interaction to pre-established harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT2","text":"The distinction between conservation of force and conservation of direction is indispensable to the reconstruction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT3","text":"The attribution to Descartes must remain differentiated: he rejects the transfer of force but maintains the change of direction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4","text":"The system remains underdetermined with respect to the positive mechanism of pre-established harmony; the passage asserts its necessity without making it explicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT5","text":"Internal coherence depends on the assimilation between conservation of total direction and the impossibility of any local reorientation by the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the real movement: partial concession to Descartes → extension of natural law → refutation → harmonious conclusion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_72:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_72@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_72:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 80"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 80","title":"Proposition 80","context":"Chapter 80","original_title":"Proposition 80"},"original_title":"Proposition 80","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 81","order":81,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_73"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_73@R001","sha256":"f43b992dfb2a5080890634d9ab371a6c635088a40faf375e03ede09062e99a01","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS1","text":"Le problème consiste à rendre compte d’une apparence d’influence réciproque entre les corps et les âmes sans poser cette influence comme une interaction effective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS2","text":"Le système recadre séparément l’activité corporelle et l’activité psychique comme si chacune pouvait s’effectuer sans l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS3","text":"Cette séparation opératoire n’abolit cependant pas la concordance observable entre les deux ordres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS4","text":"L’argument soutient ainsi une coordination des apparences plutôt qu’un transfert causal entre corps et âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS5","text":"Le mouvement va de l’indépendance contrefactuelle des deux ordres à l’apparence d’une influence réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A1","text":"Le système détermine le mode d’action des corps et des âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","text":"Les corps agissent comme s’il n’y avait point d’âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","text":"Les âmes agissent comme s’il n’y avait point de corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A4","text":"L’absence de l’autre ordre est posée sous la forme d’un « comme si » contrefactuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","text":"Le contrefactuel de l’absence des âmes ou des corps est déclaré impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A6","text":"Les corps et les âmes agissent néanmoins comme si l’un influait sur l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A7","text":"L’apparence d’influence réciproque coexiste avec l’autonomie opératoire de chaque ordre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX1","text":"Le système n’est pas fondé sur une dépendance explicite des corps à l’égard des âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX2","text":"Le système n’est pas fondé sur une dépendance explicite des âmes à l’égard des corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX3","text":"Le « comme si » ne pose pas directement l’existence d’une influence réelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX4","text":"L’absence effective des âmes n’est pas affirmée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX5","text":"L’absence effective des corps n’est pas affirmée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX6","text":"L’autonomie des deux ordres n’implique pas leur discordance phénoménale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:D1","text":"L’action corporelle peut être expliquée sans introduire une causalité psychique directe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:D2","text":"L’action psychique peut être expliquée sans introduire une causalité corporelle directe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:D3","text":"La corrélation entre les deux ordres ne suffit pas à établir une interaction réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:D4","text":"Le système conserve l’apparence d’une causalité réciproque tout en séparant les lignes d’action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6","CH_UCIC_P_73:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1","text":"La relation entre corps et âmes est reclassée comme concordance réglée plutôt que comme communication causale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6","CH_UCIC_P_73:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SD2","text":"Le système dissocie l’indépendance ontologico-opératoire des ordres et leur liaison phénoménale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A4","CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","CH_UCIC_P_73:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SD3","text":"L’influence réciproque devient un effet de coordination entre deux séries qui n’ont pas besoin d’interagir directement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut silencieusement l’existence d’un point de contact causal nécessaire entre les corps et les âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’une relation apparente exige la transmission d’une force ou d’un contenu d’un ordre à l’autre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX3","text":"Il exclut qu’une autonomie complète des séries produise nécessairement une absence de correspondance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX4","text":"Il exclut la réduction de l’un des deux ordres à l’autre comme condition de leur coordination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX1","text":"Le système se constitue autour de l’impossibilité d’une causalité mixte où corps et âmes formeraient un seul circuit d’action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX2","text":"Il forclôt un modèle dans lequel la réalité de l’influence réciproque serait la condition de la concordance observable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX3","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une médiation commune entre les deux ordres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS1","text":"Deux ordres distincts → autonomie contrefactuelle de chaque ordre → impossibilité de leur séparation absolue → concordance des manifestations → apparence d’influence réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2","text":"Absence d’interaction directe + correspondance des états → causalité apparente sans causalité transitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS3","text":"Le système produit simultanément indépendance opératoire et liaison phénoménale en remplaçant l’influence par une coordination des séries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AF1","text":"Indépendance supposée des corps et des âmes → double contrefactuel d’absence → maintien impossible d’une séparation absolue → apparence d’influence réciproque → coordination sans interaction posée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ME1","text":"La causalité est déplacée du registre de l’influence directe vers celui de la correspondance entre séries autonomes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ME2","text":"La séparation corps-âme cesse d’être l’opposé simple de leur liaison et devient la condition de son apparence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ME3","text":"L’influence réciproque est reclassée comme phénomène à expliquer plutôt que comme mécanisme immédiatement admis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ME4","text":"Le champ conceptuel distingue l’indépendance de production et la dépendance de représentation ou de manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT1","text":"Surface — Les corps, les âmes et leur apparente influence réciproque constituent les objets explicites.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT2","text":"Structural — Le système articule deux ordres d’action séparés mais concordants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’argument remplace la question « comment l’un agit-il sur l’autre ? » par la question « comment deux séries indépendantes produisent-elles l’apparence d’une influence ? ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La réalité est organisée en séries distinctes dont la simultanéité ou la correspondance peut être prise pour une causalité réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le noyau de l’argument : séparation opératoire, impossibilité de l’absence réelle et apparence d’influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT2","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si l’influence est comprise comme apparence et non comme interaction démontrée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT3","text":"Le point de tension central demeure la coexistence d’une autonomie radicale et d’une apparence formulée dans le vocabulaire de l’influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT4","text":"Le texte ne détermine pas le mécanisme précis de la coordination entre les deux ordres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT5","text":"Il ne tranche pas explicitement le statut ontologique de cette coordination ni la nature exacte du « système ».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : indépendance contrefactuelle → impossibilité de la séparation absolue → apparence d’influence réciproque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194342855350Z_62f727d1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 81","source_sha256":"f43b992dfb2a5080890634d9ab371a6c635088a40faf375e03ede09062e99a01","sha256":"a6b0b24900f70c3a674156b02953762543bb0f1c50d44f48a8130c59f0d15754","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:43:42.863298+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS1","text":"The problem consists in accounting for an appearance of reciprocal influence between bodies and souls without positing that influence as an effective interaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS2","text":"The system separately reframes bodily activity and psychic activity as though each could occur without the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS3","text":"This operational separation does not, however, abolish the observable concordance between the two orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS4","text":"The argument thus maintains a coordination of appearances rather than a causal transfer between bodies and souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AS5","text":"The movement proceeds from the counterfactual independence of the two orders to the appearance of reciprocal influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A1","text":"The system determines the mode of action of bodies and souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","text":"Bodies act as if there were no souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","text":"Souls act as if there were no bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A4","text":"The absence of the other order is posited in the form of a counterfactual “as if.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","text":"The counterfactual of the absence of souls or bodies is declared impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A6","text":"Bodies and souls nevertheless act as if one influenced the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:A7","text":"The appearance of reciprocal influence coexists with the operational autonomy of each order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX1","text":"The system is not founded upon an explicit dependence of bodies on souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX2","text":"The system is not founded upon an explicit dependence of souls on bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX3","text":"The “as if” does not directly posit the existence of a real influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX4","text":"The effective absence of souls is not affirmed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX5","text":"The effective absence of bodies is not affirmed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:NX6","text":"The autonomy of the two orders does not imply their phenomenal discordance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:D1","text":"Bodily action can be explained without introducing a direct psychic causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:D2","text":"Psychic action can be explained without introducing a direct bodily causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:D3","text":"The correlation between the two orders is not sufficient to establish a real interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:D4","text":"The system preserves the appearance of a reciprocal causality while separating the lines of action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6","CH_UCIC_P_73:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1","text":"The relation between bodies and souls is reclassified as regulated concordance rather than as causal communication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6","CH_UCIC_P_73:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SD2","text":"The system dissociates the ontologico-operational independence of the orders from their phenomenal connection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A4","CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","CH_UCIC_P_73:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SD3","text":"Reciprocal influence becomes an effect of coordination between two series that do not need to interact directly.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX1","text":"The system silently excludes the existence of a necessary point of causal contact between bodies and souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that an apparent relation requires the transmission of a force or content from one order to the other.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX3","text":"It excludes the possibility that a complete autonomy of the series necessarily produces an absence of correspondence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX4","text":"It excludes the reduction of one of the two orders to the other as a condition of their coordination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX1","text":"The system constitutes itself around the impossibility of a mixed causality in which bodies and souls would form a single circuit of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX2","text":"It forecloses a model in which the reality of reciprocal influence would be the condition of observable concordance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX3","text":"The structuring absence is that of a common mediation between the two orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS1","text":"Two distinct orders → counterfactual autonomy of each order → impossibility of their absolute separation → concordance of manifestations → appearance of reciprocal influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2","text":"Absence of direct interaction + correspondence of states → apparent causality without transitive causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS3","text":"The system simultaneously produces operational independence and phenomenal connection by replacing influence with a coordination of series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:AF1","text":"Supposed independence of bodies and souls → double counterfactual of absence → impossible maintenance of an absolute separation → appearance of reciprocal influence → coordination without posited interaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ME1","text":"Causality is displaced from the register of direct influence to that of correspondence between autonomous series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ME2","text":"The body-soul separation ceases to be the simple opposite of their connection and becomes the condition of its appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ME3","text":"Reciprocal influence is reclassified as a phenomenon to be explained rather than as an immediately admitted mechanism.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ME4","text":"The conceptual field distinguishes independence of production from dependence of representation or manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT1","text":"Surface — Bodies, souls, and their apparent reciprocal influence constitute the explicit objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT2","text":"Structural — The system articulates two separate yet concordant orders of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument replaces the question “how does one act upon the other?” with the question “how do two independent series produce the appearance of an influence?”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Reality is organized into distinct series whose simultaneity or correspondence may be taken for a reciprocal causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the core of the argument: operational separation, impossibility of real absence, and appearance of influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT2","text":"The structure is internally coherent if influence is understood as appearance and not as demonstrated interaction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT3","text":"The central point of tension remains the coexistence of a radical autonomy and an appearance formulated in the vocabulary of influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT4","text":"The text does not determine the precise mechanism of coordination between the two orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT5","text":"It does not explicitly decide the ontological status of this coordination or the exact nature of the “system.”","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: counterfactual independence → impossibility of absolute separation → appearance of reciprocal influence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_73:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_73@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_73:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 81"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 81","title":"Proposition 81","context":"Chapter 81","original_title":"Proposition 81"},"original_title":"Proposition 81","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 82","order":82,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_74"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_74@R001","sha256":"a6574de3f8a2ec3d764a0283e3d6be516940cbe9381a17eff19dd4c7a41e08e1","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS1","text":"Le texte doit articuler la continuité générale du vivant avec la singularité des Esprits ou Âmes raisonnables.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS2","text":"Il recadre la différence entre animaux et humains comme une différence de degré actuel plutôt que comme une rupture de constitution vitale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS3","text":"Les animaux spermatiques possèdent d’abord des âmes sensitives ordinaires.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS4","text":"La conception actuelle de certains d’entre eux produit leur accession à la nature humaine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS5","text":"Cette accession élève l’âme sensitive au degré de la raison et au statut d’Esprit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A1","text":"L’Animal et l’Âme commencent avec le monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A2","text":"L’Animal et l’Âme ne finissent pas avec les individus vivants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A3","text":"Le fond vital des vivants et des animaux est identique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","text":"Les animaux spermatiques existent d’abord comme animaux pourvus d’âmes sensitives.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A5","text":"Une âme sensitive n’est pas encore une âme raisonnable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A6","text":"Certains animaux spermatiques sont destinés à parvenir à la nature humaine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A7","text":"La conception actuelle constitue le seuil d’accession à la nature humaine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A8","text":"L’accession à la nature humaine élève l’âme sensitive au degré de la raison.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A9","text":"Le degré de la raison confère à l’âme la prérogative d’un Esprit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX1","text":"L’animalité n’est pas une réalité qui commence et finit avec chaque individu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX2","text":"L’âme sensitive n’est pas immédiatement une âme raisonnable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX3","text":"La présence d’une âme dans l’animal ne suffit pas à constituer un Esprit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX4","text":"La nature humaine n’est pas donnée à tout animal spermatique dès son existence initiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX5","text":"La différence entre animaux et Esprits n’est pas posée comme une différence de matière vitale fondamentale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX6","text":"La conception actuelle n’est pas un simple changement sans effet sur le statut de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D1","text":"La continuité de l’animalité à travers le commencement et la fin du monde permet de maintenir une identité vitale au-delà des transformations individuelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A1","CH_UCIC_P_74:A2","CH_UCIC_P_74:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D2","text":"Les animaux spermatiques doivent être conçus comme des êtres déjà animés, mais non encore rationnels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","CH_UCIC_P_74:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D3","text":"L’apparition de la raison ne crée pas ex nihilo une âme nouvelle ; elle transforme le degré d’une âme sensitive préexistante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","CH_UCIC_P_74:A7","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D4","text":"La rationalité humaine dépend d’un passage déterminé par la conception actuelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A6","CH_UCIC_P_74:A7","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D5","text":"L’Esprit désigne une âme animale devenue rationnelle, et non une substance étrangère à l’ordre général du vivant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3","CH_UCIC_P_74:A5","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8","CH_UCIC_P_74:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SD1","text":"Le système produit une hiérarchie continue des êtres animés : âme sensitive, nature humaine, raison, Esprit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3","CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8","CH_UCIC_P_74:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SD2","text":"La singularité humaine est une élévation fonctionnelle d’une continuité animale, non une rupture ontologique absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3","CH_UCIC_P_74:A5","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SD3","text":"La survie de l’Animal et de l’Âme à l’échelle du monde fonde la possibilité d’une transformation durable des degrés de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A1","CH_UCIC_P_74:A2","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SD4","text":"Le statut spirituel dépend d’une actualisation de la nature humaine plutôt que de la seule existence biologique initiale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","CH_UCIC_P_74:A6","CH_UCIC_P_74:A7","CH_UCIC_P_74:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une âme raisonnable soit originairement indépendante de toute histoire animale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX2","text":"Il exclut que la raison soit une propriété uniforme de tous les vivants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX3","text":"Il exclut qu’une différence de substance fondamentale soit nécessaire pour distinguer le vivant sensible de l’Esprit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX4","text":"Il exclut que la conception humaine introduise une âme sans continuité avec l’âme sensitive antérieure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX5","text":"Il exclut que la permanence de l’âme implique la permanence inchangée de son degré de faculté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX1","text":"La possibilité d’une discontinuité absolue entre animalité et humanité est forclose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX2","text":"L’origine autonome d’un sujet rationnel séparé de toute genèse animale demeure structurellement indisponible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX3","text":"L’explication du choix des animaux spermatiques « élus » n’est pas fournie ; cette sélection reste une condition opératoire non élucidée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX4","text":"Le mécanisme précis par lequel la conception actuelle élève l’âme sensitive à la raison demeure absent du système explicite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS1","text":"Continuité cosmique du vivant → permanence de l’Animal et de l’Âme au-delà des limites individuelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS2","text":"Animal spermatique → âme sensitive ordinaire sans raison actuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS3","text":"Élection implicite → conception actuelle → accession à la nature humaine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS4","text":"Accession à la nature humaine → élévation de l’âme sensitive → raison → prérogative d’Esprit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS5","text":"Résultat systémique : continuité du vivant + différenciation graduelle des facultés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AF1","text":"Identité fondamentale du vivant → permanence de l’Animal et de l’Âme → limitation initiale à la sensibilité → conception humaine actuelle → élévation rationnelle → constitution de l’Esprit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ME1","text":"La frontière animal/humain est reclassée comme une transition de degré plutôt que comme une opposition de nature vitale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ME2","text":"La conception devient un opérateur de transformation ontologique du statut de l’âme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ME3","text":"L’Esprit est replacé à l’intérieur de la continuité générale du vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ME4","text":"La différence humaine devient visible comme une prérogative acquise par élévation de la sensibilité à la raison.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT1","text":"Surface : les animaux spermatiques possèdent d’abord des âmes sensitives ; certains accèdent ensuite à la raison.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT2","text":"Structural : une même continuité animée supporte plusieurs degrés de faculté, dont le degré spirituel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic : la distinction entre animal et Esprit est recadrée pour éviter une séparation absolue entre les deux ordres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal : l’Animal et l’Âme sont inscrits dans la durée du monde, tandis que la rationalité apparaît comme une actualisation ultérieure liée à la conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire la continuité entre animalité, humanité et spiritualité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT2","text":"La distinction entre âme sensitive et âme raisonnable est conservée comme articulation décisive du système.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT3","text":"Le mouvement réel est préservé : identité vitale → différenciation des degrés → élévation rationnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT4","text":"La reconstruction reste sous-déterminée quant au sens exact de l’« élection » des animaux spermatiques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT5","text":"Elle reste également sous-déterminée quant au mécanisme de l’élévation opérée par la conception actuelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT6","text":"La cohérence interne dépend de l’acceptation d’une transformation de degré sans rupture substantielle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT7","text":"La formulation « pour ainsi dire » signale une qualification analogique ou prudente de l’élection, que la compression ne peut résoudre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194402200001Z_ecf4e5dc","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 82","source_sha256":"a6574de3f8a2ec3d764a0283e3d6be516940cbe9381a17eff19dd4c7a41e08e1","sha256":"bb8585d1e9ad81897c8268bea741b7d992c27d7eb787ae16df4174ebdd38856b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:44:02.201857+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS1","text":"The text must articulate the general continuity of living beings with the singularity of Spirits or rational Souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS2","text":"It reframes the difference between animals and humans as a difference of current degree rather than as a rupture in vital constitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS3","text":"Spermatic animals initially possess ordinary sensitive souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS4","text":"The present conception of some of them produces their accession to human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AS5","text":"This accession elevates the sensitive soul to the degree of reason and to the status of Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A1","text":"Animal and Soul begin with the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A2","text":"Animal and Soul do not end with living individuals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A3","text":"The vital ground of living beings and animals is identical.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","text":"Spermatic animals initially exist as animals endowed with sensitive souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A5","text":"A sensitive soul is not yet a rational soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A6","text":"Certain spermatic animals are destined to attain human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A7","text":"Present conception constitutes the threshold of accession to human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A8","text":"Accession to human nature elevates the sensitive soul to the degree of reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:A9","text":"The degree of reason confers upon the soul the prerogative of a Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX1","text":"Animality is not a reality that begins and ends with each individual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX2","text":"The sensitive soul is not immediately a rational soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX3","text":"The presence of a soul in the animal is not sufficient to constitute a Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX4","text":"Human nature is not given to every spermatic animal from its initial existence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX5","text":"The difference between animals and Spirits is not posited as a difference of fundamental vital matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:NX6","text":"Present conception is not a mere change without effect upon the status of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D1","text":"The continuity of animality through the beginning and end of the world makes it possible to maintain a vital identity beyond individual transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A1","CH_UCIC_P_74:A2","CH_UCIC_P_74:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D2","text":"Spermatic animals must be conceived as beings already animated, but not yet rational.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","CH_UCIC_P_74:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D3","text":"The appearance of reason does not create ex nihilo a new soul; it transforms the degree of a pre-existing sensitive soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","CH_UCIC_P_74:A7","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D4","text":"Human rationality depends on a passage determined by present conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A6","CH_UCIC_P_74:A7","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:D5","text":"Spirit designates an animal soul that has become rational, and not a substance foreign to the general order of living beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3","CH_UCIC_P_74:A5","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8","CH_UCIC_P_74:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SD1","text":"The system produces a continuous hierarchy of animate beings: sensitive soul, human nature, reason, Spirit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3","CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8","CH_UCIC_P_74:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SD2","text":"Human singularity is a functional elevation of an animal continuity, not an absolute ontological rupture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3","CH_UCIC_P_74:A5","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SD3","text":"The survival of Animal and Soul at the scale of the world grounds the possibility of a durable transformation of the degrees of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A1","CH_UCIC_P_74:A2","CH_UCIC_P_74:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SD4","text":"Spiritual status depends upon an actualization of human nature rather than upon biological existence alone at the outset.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A4","CH_UCIC_P_74:A6","CH_UCIC_P_74:A7","CH_UCIC_P_74:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a rational soul might be originally independent of all animal history.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that reason might be a uniform property of all living beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX3","text":"It excludes the possibility that a difference of fundamental substance might be necessary to distinguish sentient living being from Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX4","text":"It excludes the possibility that human conception might introduce a soul without continuity with the preceding sensitive soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX5","text":"It excludes the possibility that the permanence of the soul implies the unchanged permanence of its degree of faculty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX1","text":"The possibility of an absolute discontinuity between animality and humanity is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX2","text":"The autonomous origin of a rational subject separate from all animal genesis remains structurally unavailable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX3","text":"The explanation of the selection of the “elected” spermatic animals is not provided; this selection remains an unelucidated operative condition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX4","text":"The precise mechanism by which present conception elevates the sensitive soul to reason remains absent from the explicit system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS1","text":"Cosmic continuity of living beings → permanence of Animal and Soul beyond individual limits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS2","text":"Spermatic animal → ordinary sensitive soul without present reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS3","text":"Implicit election → present conception → accession to human nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS4","text":"Accession to human nature → elevation of the sensitive soul → reason → prerogative of Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS5","text":"Systemic result: continuity of living beings + gradual differentiation of faculties.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:AF1","text":"Fundamental identity of living beings → permanence of Animal and Soul → initial limitation to sensibility → present human conception → rational elevation → constitution of Spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ME1","text":"The animal/human boundary is reclassified as a transition of degree rather than as an opposition of vital nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ME2","text":"Conception becomes an operator of ontological transformation of the status of the soul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ME3","text":"Spirit is relocated within the general continuity of living beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ME4","text":"Human difference becomes visible as a prerogative acquired through the elevation of sensibility to reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT1","text":"Surface: spermatic animals initially possess sensitive souls; some subsequently accede to reason.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT2","text":"Structural: one and the same animate continuity supports several degrees of faculty, including the spiritual degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic: the distinction between animal and Spirit is reframed to avoid an absolute separation between the two orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal: Animal and Soul are inscribed within the duration of the world, while rationality appears as a later actualization linked to conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the continuity between animality, humanity, and spirituality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT2","text":"The distinction between sensitive soul and rational soul is preserved as a decisive articulation of the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT3","text":"The real movement is preserved: vital identity → differentiation of degrees → rational elevation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT4","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined as to the exact meaning of the “election” of spermatic animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT5","text":"It likewise remains underdetermined as to the mechanism of the elevation effected by present conception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT6","text":"Internal coherence depends upon accepting a transformation of degree without substantial rupture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT7","text":"The formulation « pour ainsi dire » signals an analogical or cautious qualification of election, which compression cannot resolve.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_74:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_74@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_74:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 82"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 82","title":"Proposition 82","context":"Chapter 82","original_title":"Proposition 82"},"original_title":"Proposition 82","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 83","order":83,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_75"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_75@R001","sha256":"976adbc74e79b8ede7a9a7eb47e40a5a1c6e186a63ca192e4a377399238d9291","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS1","text":"La différence entre les âmes ordinaires et les esprits doit être déterminée au-delà des distinctions déjà établies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS2","text":"Les âmes ordinaires représentent l’univers des créatures comme des miroirs vivants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS3","text":"Les esprits ajoutent à cette représentation une relation de ressemblance à la Divinité ou à l’Auteur de la nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS4","text":"Cette ressemblance fonde une capacité cognitive : connaître le système de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS5","text":"Elle fonde également une capacité productive : imiter l’ordre universel par des échantillons architectoniques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS6","text":"L’esprit est ainsi défini comme une puissance divine limitée à son propre département.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","text":"Les âmes en général sont des miroirs vivants de l’univers des créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","text":"Les esprits sont des âmes qui sont en outre des images de la Divinité ou de l’Auteur de la nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","text":"Être image de la Divinité rend l’esprit capable de connaître le système de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","text":"La connaissance du système de l’univers peut se traduire en imitation architectonique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","text":"L’imitation architectonique procède par échantillons plutôt que par reproduction intégrale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","text":"Chaque esprit possède une puissance analogue à celle d’une petite divinité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A7","text":"La puissance divine de chaque esprit est circonscrite à un département propre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX1","text":"Une âme ordinaire n’est pas définie comme image de la Divinité elle-même.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX2","text":"La représentation de l’univers des créatures ne suffit pas à constituer un esprit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX3","text":"La connaissance du système de l’univers n’est pas attribuée indistinctement à toutes les âmes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX4","text":"L’esprit n’est pas présenté comme une divinité sans limitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX5","text":"L’imitation de l’ordre divin n’équivaut pas à la production de l’univers entier.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D1","text":"La différence entre l’âme ordinaire et l’esprit est une différence de degré et de fonction représentative, non une rupture avec la condition d’image de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D2","text":"L’esprit possède une réflexivité supérieure : il ne reflète pas seulement les créatures, mais peut comprendre l’ordre auquel elles appartiennent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D3","text":"La connaissance spirituelle contient une capacité opératoire, puisqu’elle rend possible une imitation architectonique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D4","text":"L’activité créatrice de l’esprit est analogique et locale : elle reproduit des structures sans égaler l’acte originaire de la Divinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D5","text":"La pluralité des esprits implique une pluralité de foyers limités d’intelligence et d’architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SD1","text":"Le système établit une hiérarchie continue entre représentation du monde, compréhension de son système et imitation locale de son principe architectural.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SD2","text":"L’esprit constitue un relais de la causalité divine : il reçoit une ressemblance à l’Auteur et la convertit en capacité de connaissance et de production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SD3","text":"La création spirituelle est conçue comme une participation fragmentaire à l’architectonique divine plutôt que comme une autonomie absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SD4","text":"La limitation départementale empêche la ressemblance divine de se convertir en identité avec la Divinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX1","text":"Le miroir vivant ne suffit pas à produire une conscience architectonique de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX2","text":"La capacité de connaître l’univers ne repose pas sur une connaissance exhaustive ou indifférenciée de toutes ses productions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX3","text":"L’imitation de la Divinité ne peut être comprise comme une duplication de son pouvoir créateur total.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX4","text":"La ressemblance divine n’abolit pas la différence entre l’Auteur de la nature et les esprits qui en reproduisent localement certains traits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SNX1","text":"Le système exclut une égalité ontologique entre l’esprit et la Divinité tout en maintenant une analogie active entre eux.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SNX2","text":"Il exclut une conception purement passive de l’âme : l’image spirituelle doit pouvoir comprendre et produire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SNX3","text":"Il exclut également une conception illimitée de l’activité spirituelle : toute puissance architectonique demeure partielle et située.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS1","text":"Représentation de l’univers des créatures → constitution de l’âme comme miroir vivant.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS2","text":"Ajout de la ressemblance à la Divinité → différenciation de l’esprit par rapport à l’âme ordinaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS3","text":"Ressemblance divine → capacité de connaître le système de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS4","text":"Connaissance systémique → possibilité d’une imitation architectonique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS5","text":"Imitation par échantillons → participation productive mais non totale à l’architecture divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS6","text":"Participation productive limitée → définition de chaque esprit comme petite divinité dans un département propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AF1","text":"Différence entre âmes ordinaires et esprits → distinction entre simple miroir des créatures et image de la Divinité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AF2","text":"Image de la Divinité → connaissance du système de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AF3","text":"Connaissance du système → imitation architectonique par échantillons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AF4","text":"Imitation architectonique limitée → esprit comme petite divinité dans son département.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ME1","text":"La carte des êtres est réorganisée selon un seuil entre représentation du monde et représentation de son principe divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ME2","text":"La connaissance et la production cessent d’être deux fonctions séparées : la connaissance du système devient la condition de son imitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ME3","text":"L’activité créatrice est reclassée comme participation graduée à l’architecture divine, non comme création indépendante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ME4","text":"La multiplicité des esprits est cartographiée comme une distribution de puissances divines locales.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Le texte distingue les âmes ordinaires, miroirs de l’univers créé, des esprits, images supplémentaires de la Divinité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — La différence repose sur le passage d’une fonction représentative à une fonction cognitive et architectonique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Le texte recadre l’esprit comme opérateur local de l’intelligibilité et de la reproduction de l’ordre universel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — L’être spirituel est une puissance dérivée, analogue à la Divinité mais limitée par son domaine d’action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire la distinction entre âme ordinaire et esprit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT2","text":"La chaîne représentation → ressemblance divine → connaissance → imitation → limitation restitue le mouvement génératif du passage.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT3","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la ressemblance divine est comprise comme analogique et départementale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT4","text":"La principale sous-détermination concerne l’étendue exacte des capacités cognitives et architectoniques de chaque esprit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT5","text":"La formule de la petite divinité condense une tension non résolue entre participation à la puissance divine et dépendance à l’égard de l’Auteur de la nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194416274083Z_cb820861","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 83","source_sha256":"976adbc74e79b8ede7a9a7eb47e40a5a1c6e186a63ca192e4a377399238d9291","sha256":"825d1ec6a4bc8a4b3bf5b64aacf2faa0af4900f4ad8870f454bc5610d8268aa2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:44:16.283772+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS1","text":"The difference between ordinary souls and spirits must be determined beyond the distinctions already established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS2","text":"Ordinary souls represent the universe of creatures as living mirrors.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS3","text":"Spirits add to this representation a relation of resemblance to the Divinity or to the Author of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS4","text":"This resemblance grounds a cognitive capacity: to know the system of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS5","text":"It also grounds a productive capacity: to imitate the universal order through architectonic specimens.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AS6","text":"The spirit is thus defined as a divine power limited to its own department.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","text":"Souls in general are living mirrors of the universe of creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","text":"Spirits are souls that are moreover images of the Divinity or of the Author of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","text":"Being an image of the Divinity makes the spirit capable of knowing the system of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","text":"Knowledge of the system of the universe can be translated into architectonic imitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","text":"Architectonic imitation proceeds through specimens rather than through integral reproduction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","text":"Each spirit possesses a power analogous to that of a small divinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:A7","text":"The divine power of each spirit is circumscribed to a proper department.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX1","text":"An ordinary soul is not defined as an image of the Divinity itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX2","text":"The representation of the universe of creatures is not sufficient to constitute a spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX3","text":"Knowledge of the system of the universe is not attributed indiscriminately to all souls.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX4","text":"The spirit is not presented as a divinity without limitation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:NX5","text":"The imitation of divine order is not equivalent to the production of the entire universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D1","text":"The difference between the ordinary soul and the spirit is a difference of degree and representational function, not a break with the condition of being an image of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D2","text":"The spirit possesses a higher reflexivity: it not only reflects creatures, but can understand the order to which they belong.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D3","text":"Spiritual knowledge contains an operative capacity, since it makes architectonic imitation possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D4","text":"The creative activity of the spirit is analogical and local: it reproduces structures without equaling the original act of the Divinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:D5","text":"The plurality of spirits implies a plurality of limited centers of intelligence and architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SD1","text":"The system establishes a continuous hierarchy between representation of the world, understanding of its system, and local imitation of its architectonic principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SD2","text":"The spirit constitutes a relay of divine causality: it receives a resemblance to the Author and converts it into a capacity for knowledge and production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SD3","text":"Spiritual creation is conceived as a fragmentary participation in divine architectonics rather than as an absolute autonomy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SD4","text":"Departmental limitation prevents divine resemblance from being converted into identity with the Divinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX1","text":"The living mirror does not suffice to produce an architectonic consciousness of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX2","text":"The capacity to know the universe does not rest on exhaustive or undifferentiated knowledge of all its productions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX3","text":"The imitation of the Divinity cannot be understood as a duplication of its total creative power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX4","text":"Divine resemblance does not abolish the difference between the Author of nature and the spirits that locally reproduce certain of its features.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SNX1","text":"The system excludes an ontological equality between the spirit and the Divinity while maintaining an active analogy between them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SNX2","text":"It excludes a purely passive conception of the soul: the spiritual image must be able to understand and produce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:SNX3","text":"It also excludes an unlimited conception of spiritual activity: all architectonic power remains partial and situated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS1","text":"Representation of the universe of creatures → constitution of the soul as a living mirror.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS2","text":"Addition of resemblance to the Divinity → differentiation of the spirit from the ordinary soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS3","text":"Divine resemblance → capacity to know the system of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS4","text":"Systemic knowledge → possibility of an architectonic imitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS5","text":"Imitation through specimens → productive but non-total participation in divine architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS6","text":"Limited productive participation → definition of each spirit as a small divinity in a proper department.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AF1","text":"Difference between ordinary souls and spirits → distinction between a mere mirror of creatures and an image of the Divinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AF2","text":"Image of the Divinity → knowledge of the system of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AF3","text":"Knowledge of the system → architectonic imitation through specimens.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:AF4","text":"Limited architectonic imitation → spirit as a small divinity in its department.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ME1","text":"The map of beings is reorganized according to a threshold between representation of the world and representation of its divine principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ME2","text":"Knowledge and production cease to be two separate functions: knowledge of the system becomes the condition of its imitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ME3","text":"Creative activity is reclassified as graduated participation in divine architecture, not as independent creation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ME4","text":"The multiplicity of spirits is mapped as a distribution of local divine powers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — The text distinguishes ordinary souls, mirrors of the created universe, from spirits, additional images of the Divinity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The difference rests on the transition from a representational function to a cognitive and architectonic function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The text reframes the spirit as a local operator of the intelligibility and reproduction of universal order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — The spiritual being is a derived power, analogous to the Divinity but limited by its domain of action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the distinction between ordinary soul and spirit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT2","text":"The chain representation → divine resemblance → knowledge → imitation → limitation restores the generative movement of the passage.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1","CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A3","CH_UCIC_P_75:A4","CH_UCIC_P_75:A5","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent if divine resemblance is understood as analogical and departmental.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2","CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT4","text":"The principal underdetermination concerns the exact extent of the cognitive and architectonic capacities of each spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT5","text":"The formula of the small divinity condenses an unresolved tension between participation in divine power and dependence on the Author of nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6","CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_75:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_75@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_75:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 83"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 83","title":"Proposition 83","context":"Chapter 83","original_title":"Proposition 83"},"original_title":"Proposition 83","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 84","order":84,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_76"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_76@R001","sha256":"e419052381b2fedf0fc08089d47397074a1be67aeb997f39de081047449d966c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AS1","text":"Une condition antérieure rend les esprits capables d’entrer dans une société avec Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AS2","text":"Cette capacité modifie le rapport entre Dieu et les esprits par rapport au rapport entre Dieu et les autres créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AS3","text":"Le rapport divin aux esprits est déterminé par deux modèles relationnels superposés : la souveraineté politique et la filiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AS4","text":"Le texte passe ainsi d’une causalité productive à une relation sociale et familiale avec Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","text":"Les esprits possèdent une capacité qui les rend aptes à entrer dans une société avec Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A2","text":"Dieu est à l’égard des esprits autre chose qu’un inventeur à l’égard de sa machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A3","text":"Le rapport d’invention et de machine caractérise le rapport de Dieu aux autres créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A4","text":"Dieu est à l’égard des esprits ce qu’un prince est à ses sujets.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A5","text":"Dieu est à l’égard des esprits ce qu’un père est à ses enfants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A6","text":"La relation aux esprits comporte simultanément une dimension politique et une dimension familiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A7","text":"La capacité des esprits à entrer en société avec Dieu fonde la différenciation de leur statut relationnel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:NX1","text":"Les esprits ne sont pas définis, à l’égard de Dieu, comme de simples machines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:NX2","text":"Le rapport de Dieu aux esprits n’est pas réduit au seul rapport d’invention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:NX3","text":"Les esprits ne relèvent pas du même régime relationnel que les autres créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:NX4","text":"La relation divine aux esprits n’est pas exclusivement productive ou mécanique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:D1","text":"La capacité d’entrer en société avec Dieu confère aux esprits un statut distinct de celui des autres créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","CH_UCIC_P_76:A3","CH_UCIC_P_76:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:D2","text":"Le rapport entre Dieu et les esprits inclut une forme de gouvernement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","CH_UCIC_P_76:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:D3","text":"Le rapport entre Dieu et les esprits inclut une forme de filiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","CH_UCIC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:D4","text":"La relation aux esprits excède la causalité qui suffit à caractériser le rapport aux autres créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A2","CH_UCIC_P_76:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SD1","text":"Les esprits sont constitués comme des êtres relationnels dont le statut auprès de Dieu est socialement et familialement spécifié.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","CH_UCIC_P_76:A4","CH_UCIC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SD2","text":"La distinction entre esprits et autres créatures est une distinction de régime de relation à Dieu, non seulement de mode de production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A2","CH_UCIC_P_76:A3","CH_UCIC_P_76:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SD3","text":"La société avec Dieu articule dépendance, gouvernement et filiation sans supprimer la relation de production divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A2","CH_UCIC_P_76:A4","CH_UCIC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX1","text":"Le système dépend de la fausseté d’une définition des esprits comme objets entièrement assimilables aux machines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’une causalité d’invention suffise à déterminer le statut des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX3","text":"Il exclut que la différence entre les esprits et les autres créatures soit dépourvue d’effets relationnels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX4","text":"Il disqualifie un modèle où Dieu serait seulement producteur et où les esprits seraient seulement produits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SNX1","text":"La possibilité d’une relation instituée entre Dieu et les esprits est forclose par tout modèle purement mécanique de la création.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SNX2","text":"L’absence structurante du texte est celle d’une réduction du divin à une causalité sans sujet, sans gouvernement et sans paternité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SNX3","text":"Le texte rend inadmissible une ontologie dans laquelle aucune créature ne pourrait être adressée, gouvernée ou engendrée comme enfant par Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS1","text":"Capacité spécifique des esprits → possibilité d’une société avec Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS2","text":"Société avec Dieu → dépassement du modèle inventeur-machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS3","text":"Dépassement du modèle mécanique → double recodage du rapport comme relation prince-sujets et père-enfants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS4","text":"Double recodage → différenciation du statut des esprits par rapport aux autres créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS5","text":"Différenciation relationnelle → coexistence de la dépendance productive, de l’autorité politique et de la filiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AF1","text":"Capacité des esprits → entrée en société avec Dieu → dépassement du rapport machine-inventeur → gouvernement princier et paternité → statut relationnel distinct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ME1","text":"Le champ des créatures est reclassé selon deux régimes : les créatures rapportées à Dieu comme machines et les esprits rapportés à Dieu comme sujets et enfants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ME2","text":"La création est cartographiée simultanément comme production, gouvernement et filiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ME3","text":"La différence entre les esprits et les autres créatures devient une différence de relation instituée à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ME4","text":"La notion de société introduit une dimension collective et statutaire dans le rapport entre Dieu et les esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT1","text":"Surface — Les esprits sont capables d’entrer dans une société avec Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT2","text":"Structural — Cette capacité produit un régime relationnel distinct du rapport mécanique entre inventeur et machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le texte recadre la relation divine en combinant causalité, autorité et filiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Les esprits sont définis comme des créatures susceptibles d’un statut durable de sujets et d’enfants auprès de Dieu, sans que la condition antérieure de cette capacité soit explicitée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement principal : capacité des esprits, société avec Dieu, différenciation relationnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT2","text":"La comparaison avec l’inventeur et la machine suffit à établir le modèle négatif de la relation purement productive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT3","text":"Les figures du prince et du père permettent de reconstruire les deux dimensions positives de la relation divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT4","text":"La proposition antérieure désignée par « C’est ce qui » reste sous-déterminée et ne peut être reconstruite à partir de l’extrait seul.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT5","text":"La coexistence exacte entre le rapport productif, le gouvernement et la paternité demeure non résolue : le texte affirme leur superposition sans en préciser la hiérarchie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel de l’énoncé, mais dépend de la compression de la distinction entre les esprits et les autres créatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194433414002Z_7712487d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 84","source_sha256":"e419052381b2fedf0fc08089d47397074a1be67aeb997f39de081047449d966c","sha256":"9f14acacdeb9d137f2f5af55a2d6aee4ab776b4ec824e8ad4ee27c54a399c673","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:44:33.421492+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AS1","text":"A prior condition renders spirits capable of entering into a society with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AS2","text":"This capacity modifies the relation between God and spirits in comparison with the relation between God and other creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AS3","text":"The divine relation to spirits is determined by two superimposed relational models: political sovereignty and filiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AS4","text":"The text thus moves from productive causality to a social and familial relation with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","text":"Spirits possess a capacity that makes them fit to enter into a society with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A2","text":"God is, with respect to spirits, something other than an inventor with respect to his machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A3","text":"The relation of inventor and machine characterizes God's relation to other creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A4","text":"God is, with respect to spirits, what a prince is to his subjects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A5","text":"God is, with respect to spirits, what a father is to his children.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A6","text":"The relation to spirits simultaneously includes a political dimension and a familial dimension.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:A7","text":"The capacity of spirits to enter into society with God grounds the differentiation of their relational status.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:NX1","text":"Spirits are not defined, with respect to God, as mere machines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:NX2","text":"God's relation to spirits is not reduced to the sole relation of invention.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:NX3","text":"Spirits do not fall under the same relational regime as other creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:NX4","text":"The divine relation to spirits is not exclusively productive or mechanical.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:D1","text":"The capacity to enter into society with God confers upon spirits a status distinct from that of other creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","CH_UCIC_P_76:A3","CH_UCIC_P_76:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:D2","text":"The relation between God and spirits includes a form of government.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","CH_UCIC_P_76:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:D3","text":"The relation between God and spirits includes a form of filiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","CH_UCIC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:D4","text":"The relation to spirits exceeds the causality sufficient to characterize the relation to other creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A2","CH_UCIC_P_76:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SD1","text":"Spirits are constituted as relational beings whose status in relation to God is socially and familially specified.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1","CH_UCIC_P_76:A4","CH_UCIC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SD2","text":"The distinction between spirits and other creatures is a distinction of regime of relation to God, not only of mode of production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A2","CH_UCIC_P_76:A3","CH_UCIC_P_76:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SD3","text":"Society with God articulates dependence, government, and filiation without suppressing the relation of divine production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A2","CH_UCIC_P_76:A4","CH_UCIC_P_76:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX1","text":"The system depends on the falsity of a definition of spirits as objects entirely assimilable to machines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX2","text":"It excludes the sufficiency of a causality of invention to determine the status of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX3","text":"It excludes the possibility that the difference between spirits and other creatures is devoid of relational effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX4","text":"It disqualifies a model in which God would be only producer and spirits would be only produced.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SNX1","text":"The possibility of an instituted relation between God and spirits is foreclosed by every purely mechanical model of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SNX2","text":"The structuring absence of the text is that of a reduction of the divine to a causality without subject, without government, and without paternity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:SNX3","text":"The text renders inadmissible an ontology in which no creature could be addressed, governed, or begotten as a child by God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS1","text":"Specific capacity of spirits → possibility of a society with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS2","text":"Society with God → surpassing of the inventor-machine model.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS3","text":"Surpassing of the mechanical model → double recoding of the relation as a prince-subjects and father-children relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS4","text":"Double recoding → differentiation of the status of spirits in comparison with other creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS5","text":"Relational differentiation → coexistence of productive dependence, political authority, and filiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:AF1","text":"Capacity of spirits → entry into society with God → surpassing of the machine-inventor relation → princely government and paternity → distinct relational status.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ME1","text":"The field of creatures is reclassified according to two regimes: creatures related to God as machines and spirits related to God as subjects and children.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ME2","text":"Creation is mapped simultaneously as production, government, and filiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ME3","text":"The difference between spirits and other creatures becomes a difference of instituted relation to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ME4","text":"The notion of society introduces a collective and statutory dimension into the relation between God and spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT1","text":"Surface — Spirits are capable of entering into a society with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT2","text":"Structural — This capacity produces a relational regime distinct from the mechanical relation between inventor and machine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text reframes the divine relation by combining causality, authority, and filiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Spirits are defined as creatures susceptible to a durable status of subjects and children in relation to God, without the prior condition of this capacity being made explicit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal movement: capacity of spirits, society with God, relational differentiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT2","text":"The comparison with the inventor and the machine suffices to establish the negative model of the purely productive relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT3","text":"The figures of the prince and the father make it possible to reconstruct the two positive dimensions of the divine relation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT4","text":"The prior proposition designated by « C’est ce qui » remains underdetermined and cannot be reconstructed from the excerpt alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT5","text":"The exact coexistence of the productive relation, government, and paternity remains unresolved: the text affirms their superimposition without specifying their hierarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the statement, but depends on the compression of the distinction between spirits and other creatures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_76:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_76@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_76:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 84"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 84","title":"Proposition 84","context":"Chapter 84","original_title":"Proposition 84"},"original_title":"Proposition 84","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 85","order":85,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_77"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_77@R001","sha256":"e4b1b3329b3bf30dfcbad42b64792935bf20a92a7ef18721cbc8da32cd869c9b","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS1","text":"Le texte cherche à déterminer la forme politique résultant de l’assemblage intégral des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS2","text":"Il recadre cet assemblage comme une totalité politique plutôt que comme une simple collection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS3","text":"Cette totalité est identifiée à la Cité de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS4","text":"La Cité de Dieu est définie par le maximum possible de perfection étatique et monarchique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS5","text":"L’argument procède par déduction métaphysico-politique : totalité des esprits → État parfait → gouvernement par le monarque parfait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","text":"L’ensemble de tous les esprits forme une totalité déterminée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","text":"Cette totalité doit composer une cité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A3","text":"La Cité de Dieu est un État.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","text":"La Cité de Dieu constitue le plus parfait État possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","text":"Le plus parfait État est gouverné par un monarque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A6","text":"Le monarque qui gouverne la Cité de Dieu est le plus parfait des monarques.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A7","text":"L’assemblage des esprits entraîne nécessairement la constitution de cet État parfait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:NX1","text":"La totalité des esprits n’est pas laissée comme une pluralité sans forme politique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:NX2","text":"La Cité de Dieu n’est pas un État partiel ou inférieur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:NX3","text":"Le gouvernement de la Cité de Dieu n’est pas confié à un monarque imparfait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:NX4","text":"L’assemblage des esprits n’est pas présenté comme contingent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:D1","text":"La totalité spirituelle reçoit une détermination politique nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:D2","text":"La constitution de la Cité de Dieu est équivalente à l’actualisation de la perfection étatique maximale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A3","CH_UCIC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:D3","text":"La perfection de l’État implique une hiérarchie monarchique au sommet de sa structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:D4","text":"La perfection politique de la totalité spirituelle dépend conjointement de la forme étatique et de la perfection du souverain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SD1","text":"L’unification de tous les esprits est convertie en ordre politique total plutôt qu’en simple unité ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SD2","text":"La perfection maximale est rendue inséparable d’une structure de souveraineté monarchique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SD3","text":"La nécessité métaphysique de l’assemblage fonde une nécessité politique de la constitution étatique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX1","text":"La totalité spirituelle ne peut demeurer une multiplicité sans principe d’unification politique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX2","text":"Un État parfait ne peut être conçu sans souveraineté centralisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX3","text":"La perfection politique ne peut être séparée de la perfection personnelle du gouvernant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’une perfection spirituelle non politique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX2","text":"Est exclue la possibilité d’un ordre parfait fondé sur une pluralité souveraine ou une absence de souverain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS1","text":"Totalité de tous les esprits → assemblage nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS2","text":"Assemblage nécessaire → constitution d’une cité déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS3","text":"Cité déterminée → État.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS4","text":"État → maximisation de la perfection possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS5","text":"Perfection étatique maximale → gouvernement par le monarque maximalement parfait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS6","text":"La perfection de la totalité est donc produite par la composition suivante : totalité spirituelle → État parfait → monarchie parfaite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A3","CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6","CH_UCIC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AF1","text":"Pluralité des esprits → assemblage total → nécessité de composition → Cité de Dieu → État le plus parfait possible → gouvernement par le monarque le plus parfait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ME1","text":"L’objet « tous les esprits » est reclassé comme une unité politique constituée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ME2","text":"La perfection est déplacée du registre abstrait vers une forme étatique déterminée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ME3","text":"La monarchie est établie comme forme politique adéquate à la perfection maximale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ME4","text":"L’ordre spirituel et l’ordre politique sont cartographiés comme deux dimensions d’une même totalité.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT1","text":"Surface — L’assemblage de tous les esprits compose la Cité de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT2","text":"Structural — La totalité spirituelle est organisée comme un État hiérarchique et monarchique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La perfection est obtenue par la conversion d’une totalité dispersée en ordre politique unifié.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La nécessité de l’assemblage implique que la forme politique parfaite appartient à la structure même de la totalité spirituelle, et non à une décision contingente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement principal : totalité des esprits, constitution de la cité, perfection de l’État, perfection du monarque.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT2","text":"La cohérence interne dépend de l’identification implicite entre perfection collective et forme étatique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT3","text":"Le texte sous-détermine la nature exacte de l’assemblage et le fondement de son caractère nécessaire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT4","text":"Le statut du monarque parfait n’est pas démontré ; il est incorporé à la définition de l’État parfait.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel, mais laisse ouverte la médiation entre unité spirituelle et souveraineté monarchique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194448845432Z_7c5d0080","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 85","source_sha256":"e4b1b3329b3bf30dfcbad42b64792935bf20a92a7ef18721cbc8da32cd869c9b","sha256":"57a69e1323e185804925d3671b4afafacb38305e4b7a782434f9fe1d155facbe","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:44:48.848496+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS1","text":"The text seeks to determine the political form resulting from the integral assemblage of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS2","text":"It reframes this assemblage as a political totality rather than as a mere collection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS3","text":"This totality is identified with the City of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS4","text":"The City of God is defined by the greatest possible degree of state and monarchical perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AS5","text":"The argument proceeds by metaphysico-political deduction: totality of spirits → perfect State → government by the perfect monarch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","text":"The set of all spirits forms a determinate totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","text":"This totality must compose a city.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A3","text":"The City of God is a State.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","text":"The City of God constitutes the most perfect possible State.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","text":"The most perfect State is governed by a monarch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A6","text":"The monarch who governs the City of God is the most perfect of monarchs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:A7","text":"The assemblage of spirits necessarily entails the constitution of this perfect State.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:NX1","text":"The totality of spirits is not left as a plurality without political form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:NX2","text":"The City of God is not a partial or inferior State.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:NX3","text":"The government of the City of God is not entrusted to an imperfect monarch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:NX4","text":"The assemblage of spirits is not presented as contingent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:D1","text":"The spiritual totality receives a necessary political determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:D2","text":"The constitution of the City of God is equivalent to the actualization of maximal state perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A3","CH_UCIC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:D3","text":"The perfection of the State entails a monarchical hierarchy at the summit of its structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:D4","text":"The political perfection of the spiritual totality jointly depends on the state form and on the perfection of the sovereign.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SD1","text":"The unification of all spirits is converted into a total political order rather than into a mere ontological unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SD2","text":"Maximal perfection is rendered inseparable from a structure of monarchical sovereignty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SD3","text":"The metaphysical necessity of assemblage grounds a political necessity of state constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX1","text":"The spiritual totality cannot remain a multiplicity without a principle of political unification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX2","text":"A perfect State cannot be conceived without centralized sovereignty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX3","text":"Political perfection cannot be separated from the personal perfection of the ruler.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX1","text":"The possibility of a non-political spiritual perfection is foreclosed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX2","text":"The possibility of a perfect order founded on a sovereign plurality or an absence of sovereign is excluded.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS1","text":"Totality of all spirits → necessary assemblage.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS2","text":"Necessary assemblage → constitution of a determinate city.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS3","text":"Determinate city → State.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS4","text":"State → maximization of possible perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS5","text":"Maximal state perfection → government by the maximally perfect monarch.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS6","text":"The perfection of the totality is therefore produced by the following composition: spiritual totality → perfect State → perfect monarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A3","CH_UCIC_P_77:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6","CH_UCIC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:AF1","text":"Plurality of spirits → total assemblage → necessity of composition → City of God → most perfect possible State → government by the most perfect monarch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ME1","text":"The object “all spirits” is reclassified as a constituted political unity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ME2","text":"Perfection is displaced from the abstract register toward a determinate state form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ME3","text":"Monarchy is established as the political form adequate to maximal perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ME4","text":"The spiritual order and the political order are mapped as two dimensions of one and the same totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT1","text":"Surface — The assemblage of all spirits composes the City of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT2","text":"Structural — The spiritual totality is organized as a hierarchical and monarchical State.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Perfection is attained through the conversion of a dispersed totality into a unified political order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The necessity of assemblage implies that the perfect political form belongs to the very structure of the spiritual totality, and not to a contingent decision.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT1","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the principal movement: totality of spirits, constitution of the city, perfection of the State, perfection of the monarch.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT2","text":"The internal coherence depends on the implicit identification between collective perfection and state form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT3","text":"The text underdetermines the exact nature of the assemblage and the ground of its necessary character.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT4","text":"The status of the perfect monarch is not demonstrated; it is incorporated into the definition of the perfect State.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement, but leaves open the mediation between spiritual unity and monarchical sovereignty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_77:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_77@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_77:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 85"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 85","title":"Proposition 85","context":"Chapter 85","original_title":"Proposition 85"},"original_title":"Proposition 85","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 86","order":86,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_78"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_78@R001","sha256":"ca246c8602227f3d82d8b5f49bb79db523090f43cf2c6852e7aee86dc248512c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS1","text":"Le problème consiste à déterminer dans quelle œuvre divine résident proprement la gloire de Dieu et sa bonté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS2","text":"L’argument recadre la Cité de Dieu comme une monarchie universelle et comme un monde moral inclus dans le monde naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS3","text":"Cette inclusion hiérarchique fait de la Cité divine l’œuvre la plus élevée et la plus divine de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS4","text":"La gloire divine est rapportée à la connaissance et à l’admiration de la grandeur et de la bonté divines par les esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS5","text":"La sagesse et la puissance se manifestent partout, tandis que la bonté reçoit sa détermination propre dans le rapport à la Cité divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A1","text":"La Cité de Dieu est une monarchie véritablement universelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A2","text":"La Cité de Dieu est un monde moral dans le monde naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","text":"Le monde moral constitue l’œuvre la plus élevée et la plus divine de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","text":"La gloire de Dieu dépend de la connaissance et de l’admiration de sa grandeur et de sa bonté par les esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A5","text":"Sans la connaissance et l’admiration spirituelles de la grandeur et de la bonté divines, il n’y aurait pas de gloire divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A6","text":"La sagesse et la puissance de Dieu se manifestent partout.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A7","text":"La bonté de Dieu reçoit sa détermination propre par rapport à la Cité divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:NX1","text":"La gloire divine n’est pas indépendante de toute connaissance ou admiration par les esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:NX2","text":"La bonté divine n’est pas définie ici comme une manifestation uniforme dans tous les ouvrages de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:NX3","text":"La Cité divine n’est pas un élément extérieur au monde naturel ; elle y est incluse comme monde moral.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:NX4","text":"La hiérarchie des attributs divins ne se réduit pas à la seule extension universelle de leurs manifestations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:D1","text":"La Cité divine devient le lieu dans lequel la grandeur et la bonté de Dieu acquièrent leur reconnaissance spirituelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:D2","text":"La gloire divine est une relation accomplie entre les perfections divines et les esprits capables de les connaître et de les admirer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:D3","text":"La supériorité de la Cité divine tient à la fonction morale et cognitive qu’elle remplit, non à une simple extension dans le monde naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:D4","text":"La sagesse et la puissance ont une portée cosmique générale, alors que la bonté est spécifiée par l’ordre de la Cité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A6","CH_UCIC_P_78:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SD1","text":"L’accomplissement du monde naturel dépend d’une organisation morale capable de convertir les perfections divines en gloire reconnue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SD2","text":"La Cité divine fonctionne comme médiation entre l’universalité de l’action divine et la singularité de sa reconnaissance par les esprits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A1","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SD3","text":"La distinction entre sagesse, puissance et bonté produit une cartographie différenciée des attributs divins : manifestation partout pour les deux premières, relation morale privilégiée pour la dernière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A6","CH_UCIC_P_78:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut une conception de la gloire divine comme propriété autosuffisante, indépendante de toute réception spirituelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut une séparation radicale entre ordre naturel et ordre moral.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une conception indifférenciée des attributs divins selon laquelle sagesse, puissance et bonté auraient le même mode de manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut que la bonté divine soit pleinement déterminée par la seule production ou conservation du monde naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’un monde naturel complet sans monde moral destiné à la connaissance et à l’admiration de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX2","text":"Est forclose une gloire divine sans communauté d’esprits, de sorte que la reconnaissance spirituelle devient une condition structurelle de la finalité divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX3","text":"Est absente toute conception de Dieu dont la bonté serait entièrement intelligible sans référence à une cité ou à une communauté morale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS1","text":"Monde naturel → inclusion d’un monde moral → constitution de la Cité de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS2","text":"Cité de Dieu → monarchie universelle et œuvre suprême → concentration de la finalité divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS3","text":"Perfections divines → connaissance et admiration par les esprits → gloire de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS4","text":"Manifestation universelle de la sagesse et de la puissance / détermination relationnelle de la bonté → différenciation des attributs divins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AF1","text":"Monde naturel → monde moral inclus → monarchie universelle → œuvre la plus élevée → reconnaissance spirituelle des perfections → gloire divine → distinction entre bonté relationnelle et sagesse-puissance universelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ME1","text":"Le monde moral est reclassé comme l’instance supérieure d’organisation du monde naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ME2","text":"La gloire divine est déplacée d’une propriété isolée de Dieu vers une relation entre Dieu et les esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ME3","text":"Les attributs divins sont distribués selon deux régimes : manifestation cosmique générale et accomplissement moral dans la Cité divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ME4","text":"La Cité de Dieu devient le point de convergence entre universalité politique, ordre moral et finalité théologique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT1","text":"Surface — La Cité de Dieu est décrite comme monarchie universelle, monde moral et œuvre suprême de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT2","text":"Structural — L’ordre moral est intégré au monde naturel et assure la médiation entre les perfections divines et leur reconnaissance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La hiérarchie des œuvres divines est déterminée par leur capacité à produire une connaissance et une admiration spirituelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La réalité divine est pensée comme accomplie dans une structure relationnelle où la gloire dépend de l’existence d’esprits connaissants et admirants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le mouvement central : monde naturel, monde moral, Cité divine, gloire et différenciation des attributs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT2","text":"La reconstruction reste sous-déterminée quant à la nature exacte des esprits et au mode précis de leur connaissance et admiration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT3","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la gloire est comprise comme une relation et non comme une perfection indépendante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT4","text":"La principale tension réside dans la dépendance de la gloire divine à une reconnaissance créée, alors que les attributs divins sont affirmés comme universellement manifestes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT5","text":"Une seconde tension oppose la bonté, proprement rapportée à la Cité divine, à la portée apparemment générale de l’action divine dans le monde naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT6","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel du texte, mais elle dépend de l’ellipse par laquelle sont établis le statut des esprits et la transition entre connaissance, admiration et gloire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194504014950Z_c62749de","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 86","source_sha256":"ca246c8602227f3d82d8b5f49bb79db523090f43cf2c6852e7aee86dc248512c","sha256":"786ea7dcb48c86e9f75da9b55f87fd1f481c39ac2d6b793744957ee2888eec9e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:45:04.018307+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS1","text":"The problem consists in determining in which divine work God's glory and goodness properly reside.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS2","text":"The argument reframes the City of God as a universal monarchy and as a moral world included within the natural world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS3","text":"This hierarchical inclusion makes the divine City God's highest and most divine work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS4","text":"Divine glory is related to spirits' knowledge and admiration of divine greatness and goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AS5","text":"Wisdom and power are manifested everywhere, whereas goodness receives its proper determination in relation to the divine City.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A1","text":"The City of God is a truly universal monarchy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A2","text":"The City of God is a moral world within the natural world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","text":"The moral world constitutes God's highest and most divine work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","text":"God's glory depends on spirits' knowledge and admiration of His greatness and goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A5","text":"Without spiritual knowledge and admiration of divine greatness and goodness, there would be no divine glory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A6","text":"God's wisdom and power are manifested everywhere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:A7","text":"God's goodness receives its proper determination in relation to the divine City.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:NX1","text":"Divine glory is not independent of all knowledge or admiration by spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:NX2","text":"Divine goodness is not defined here as a uniform manifestation in all God's works.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:NX3","text":"The divine City is not an element external to the natural world; it is included within it as a moral world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:NX4","text":"The hierarchy of divine attributes is not reducible to the universal extension alone of their manifestations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:D1","text":"The divine City becomes the place in which God's greatness and goodness acquire their spiritual recognition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:D2","text":"Divine glory is a fulfilled relation between divine perfections and spirits capable of knowing and admiring them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:D3","text":"The superiority of the divine City lies in the moral and cognitive function it fulfills, not in a mere extension within the natural world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:D4","text":"Wisdom and power have a general cosmic scope, whereas goodness is specified by the order of the divine City.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A6","CH_UCIC_P_78:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SD1","text":"The fulfillment of the natural world depends on a moral organization capable of converting divine perfections into recognized glory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SD2","text":"The divine City functions as a mediation between the universality of divine action and the singularity of its recognition by spirits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A1","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SD3","text":"The distinction between wisdom, power, and goodness produces a differentiated mapping of divine attributes: manifestation everywhere for the first two, privileged moral relation for the last.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A6","CH_UCIC_P_78:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX1","text":"The system excludes a conception of divine glory as a self-sufficient property, independent of all spiritual reception.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX2","text":"The system excludes a radical separation between natural order and moral order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX3","text":"The system excludes an undifferentiated conception of divine attributes according to which wisdom, power, and goodness would have the same mode of manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the possibility that divine goodness be fully determined by the production or preservation of the natural world alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX1","text":"The possibility of a complete natural world without a moral world directed toward the knowledge and admiration of God is precluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX2","text":"A divine glory without a community of spirits is precluded, such that spiritual recognition becomes a structural condition of divine finality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX3","text":"Absent is any conception of God whose goodness would be entirely intelligible without reference to a city or to a moral community.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS1","text":"Natural world → inclusion of a moral world → constitution of the City of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS2","text":"City of God → universal monarchy and supreme work → concentration of divine finality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS3","text":"Divine perfections → knowledge and admiration by spirits → glory of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS4","text":"Universal manifestation of wisdom and power / relational determination of goodness → differentiation of divine attributes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:AF1","text":"Natural world → included moral world → universal monarchy → highest work → spiritual recognition of perfections → divine glory → distinction between relational goodness and universal wisdom-power.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ME1","text":"The moral world is reclassified as the higher instance of organization of the natural world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ME2","text":"Divine glory is displaced from an isolated property of God toward a relation between God and spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ME3","text":"Divine attributes are distributed according to two regimes: general cosmic manifestation and moral fulfillment in the divine City.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ME4","text":"The City of God becomes the point of convergence between political universality, moral order, and theological finality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT1","text":"Surface — The City of God is described as a universal monarchy, a moral world, and God's supreme work.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT2","text":"Structural — The moral order is integrated into the natural world and mediates between divine perfections and their recognition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The hierarchy of divine works is determined by their capacity to produce spiritual knowledge and admiration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Divine reality is conceived as fulfilled in a relational structure in which glory depends on the existence of knowing and admiring spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the central movement: natural world, moral world, divine City, glory, and differentiation of attributes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined as to the exact nature of spirits and the precise mode of their knowledge and admiration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent if glory is understood as a relation and not as an independent perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT4","text":"The principal tension lies in the dependence of divine glory on a created recognition, whereas divine attributes are affirmed as universally manifest.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT5","text":"A second tension opposes goodness, properly related to the divine City, to the apparently general scope of divine action in the natural world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT6","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text, but it depends on the ellipsis through which the status of spirits and the transition between knowledge, admiration, and glory are established.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_78:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_78@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_78:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 86"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 86","title":"Proposition 86","context":"Chapter 86","original_title":"Proposition 86"},"original_title":"Proposition 86","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 87","order":87,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_79"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_79@R001","sha256":"3fc058f09a7805e0b84ec3036989286a986fa327880406261ea018d0636360cf","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AS1","text":"Une harmonie déjà établie entre deux règnes naturels, celui des causes efficientes et celui des causes finales, fournit le fondement de l’inférence suivante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AS2","text":"Le texte recadre cette première harmonie en une correspondance entre le règne physique de la nature et le règne moral de la grâce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AS3","text":"La correspondance repose sur une double considération fonctionnelle de Dieu : architecte de la machine de l’univers et monarque de la cité divine des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AS4","text":"L’argument est analogique et reconstructif : il étend une harmonie causale à une harmonie entre ordre naturel et ordre moral.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A1","text":"Une harmonie parfaite est établie entre deux règnes naturels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A2","text":"Le premier règne naturel relève des causes efficientes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A3","text":"Le second règne naturel relève des causes finales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A4","text":"L’harmonie entre les règnes naturels autorise l’identification d’une autre harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A5","text":"Le règne physique de la nature et le règne moral de la grâce constituent deux ordres distincts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","text":"Dieu peut être considéré comme architecte de la machine de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A7","text":"Dieu peut être considéré comme monarque de la cité divine des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A8","text":"Les deux fonctions divines correspondent respectivement à l’ordre physique et à l’ordre moral.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX1","text":"L’harmonie ne supprime pas la distinction entre les règnes qu’elle relie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX2","text":"Le règne physique de la nature n’est pas réductible au règne moral de la grâce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX3","text":"Dieu n’est pas limité à la seule fonction d’architecte de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX4","text":"Dieu n’est pas limité à la seule fonction de monarque des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX5","text":"Les causes efficientes et les causes finales ne sont pas confondues.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:D1","text":"La distinction entre causes efficientes et causes finales peut être transposée en distinction entre ordre physique et ordre moral.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A2","CH_UCIC_P_79:A3","CH_UCIC_P_79:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:D2","text":"La double fonction divine fournit le principe de correspondance entre la machine de l’univers et la cité divine des esprits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:A7","CH_UCIC_P_79:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:D3","text":"L’existence d’une première harmonie rend légitime l’affirmation d’une seconde harmonie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A1","CH_UCIC_P_79:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:D4","text":"Nature et grâce peuvent être ordonnées ensemble sans être ramenées à un même type de causalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A2","CH_UCIC_P_79:A3","CH_UCIC_P_79:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SD1","text":"L’unité divine se manifeste par la coordination de plusieurs ordres distincts plutôt que par leur indistinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A1","CH_UCIC_P_79:A5","CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SD2","text":"L’ordre physique et l’ordre moral sont intégrés dans une architecture commune où la causalité naturelle et la finalité spirituelle demeurent différenciées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A2","CH_UCIC_P_79:A3","CH_UCIC_P_79:A5","CH_UCIC_P_79:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3","text":"La nature et la grâce sont présentées comme deux domaines corrélés d’une même gouvernementalité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A4","CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une opposition irréconciliable sépare l’ordre physique de l’ordre moral.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’une harmonie exige l’abolition des différences entre les ordres.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut qu’il existe plusieurs principes divins indépendants correspondant séparément à la nature et à la grâce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut que la finalité morale soit extérieure à l’architecture générale de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX1","text":"La possibilité d’une rupture entre machine cosmique et cité divine est forclose.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX2","text":"L’autonomie complète du règne moral par rapport à l’ordre physique est rendue inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX3","text":"La séparation entre causalité naturelle et gouvernement spirituel ne peut être traitée comme une séparation des fondements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS1","text":"Distinction des causes efficientes et finales → établissement d’une harmonie entre deux règnes naturels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS2","text":"Harmonie naturelle établie → extension du principe d’harmonie à deux règnes d’un autre niveau.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS3","text":"Correspondance nature/grâce → distribution des fonctions divines entre architecture cosmique et gouvernement spirituel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS4","text":"Distribution fonctionnelle de Dieu → unité ordonnée du physique et du moral sans suppression de leur distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AF1","text":"Harmonie entre causes efficientes et finales → légitimation d’une nouvelle analogie → correspondance entre nature physique et grâce morale → double détermination de Dieu comme architecte et monarque → intégration des deux règnes dans une harmonie supérieure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ME1","text":"L’opposition entre nature et grâce est reclassée comme une relation d’harmonie entre deux règnes distincts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ME2","text":"La figure divine est cartographiée selon deux fonctions corrélées : construction de l’univers et gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ME3","text":"La distinction entre causalité efficiente et finalité devient le modèle de liaison entre ordre physique et ordre moral.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4","text":"L’univers est reconfiguré comme une structure à la fois machinique et politique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le texte affirme une harmonie entre le règne physique de la nature et le règne moral de la grâce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT2","text":"Structural — Deux types de causalité et deux ordres de réalité sont coordonnés sans être confondus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Une harmonie déjà démontrée est utilisée comme matrice de légitimation pour une nouvelle harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La réalité est conçue comme une totalité ordonnée où la machine cosmique et la cité spirituelle relèvent d’un même principe divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le mouvement de l’argument : harmonie première, extension analogique, correspondance des ordres et double fonction divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT2","text":"La reconstruction dépend de l’acceptation préalable d’une harmonie parfaite entre causes efficientes et causes finales.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3","text":"Le texte sous-détermine le mécanisme précis par lequel l’harmonie entre nature et grâce est réalisée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT4","text":"La cohérence interne repose sur la distinction maintenue entre les règnes et sur leur coordination par un même Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT5","text":"La principale tension réside dans l’articulation entre séparation des ordres et affirmation de leur harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT6","text":"La compression préserve le mouvement réel du texte, mais laisse ouverte la nature exacte de la correspondance entre architecture cosmique et gouvernement moral.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194520005024Z_344a660d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 87","source_sha256":"3fc058f09a7805e0b84ec3036989286a986fa327880406261ea018d0636360cf","sha256":"b8f0972ddb5ab3608c2e6ca83a7c2001a145c57e19edef21e6fc7e4a3252cddf","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:45:20.008847+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AS1","text":"A harmony already established between two natural kingdoms, that of efficient causes and that of final causes, provides the basis for the following inference.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AS2","text":"The text reframes this first harmony as a correspondence between the physical kingdom of nature and the moral kingdom of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AS3","text":"The correspondence rests on a dual functional consideration of God: architect of the machine of the universe and monarch of the divine city of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AS4","text":"The argument is analogical and reconstructive: it extends a causal harmony into a harmony between natural order and moral order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A1","text":"A perfect harmony is established between two natural kingdoms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A2","text":"The first natural kingdom pertains to efficient causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A3","text":"The second natural kingdom pertains to final causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A4","text":"The harmony between the natural kingdoms authorizes the identification of another harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A5","text":"The physical kingdom of nature and the moral kingdom of grace constitute two distinct orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","text":"God can be considered the architect of the machine of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A7","text":"God can be considered the monarch of the divine city of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:A8","text":"The two divine functions correspond respectively to the physical order and the moral order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX1","text":"Harmony does not abolish the distinction between the kingdoms that it connects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX2","text":"The physical kingdom of nature is not reducible to the moral kingdom of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX3","text":"God is not limited to the sole function of architect of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX4","text":"God is not limited to the sole function of monarch of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:NX5","text":"Efficient causes and final causes are not conflated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:D1","text":"The distinction between efficient causes and final causes can be transposed into a distinction between physical order and moral order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A2","CH_UCIC_P_79:A3","CH_UCIC_P_79:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:D2","text":"The dual divine function provides the principle of correspondence between the machine of the universe and the divine city of spirits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:A7","CH_UCIC_P_79:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:D3","text":"The existence of a first harmony legitimizes the affirmation of a second harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A1","CH_UCIC_P_79:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:D4","text":"Nature and grace can be ordered together without being reduced to the same type of causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A2","CH_UCIC_P_79:A3","CH_UCIC_P_79:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SD1","text":"Divine unity manifests itself through the coordination of several distinct orders rather than through their indistinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A1","CH_UCIC_P_79:A5","CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SD2","text":"The physical order and the moral order are integrated into a common architecture in which natural causality and spiritual finality remain differentiated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A2","CH_UCIC_P_79:A3","CH_UCIC_P_79:A5","CH_UCIC_P_79:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3","text":"Nature and grace are presented as two correlated domains of one and the same divine governance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A4","CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that an irreconcilable opposition separates the physical order from the moral order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that harmony requires the abolition of differences between the orders.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX3","text":"The system excludes the possibility that there are several independent divine principles corresponding separately to nature and grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the possibility that moral finality is external to the general architecture of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX1","text":"The possibility of a rupture between the cosmic machine and the divine city is foreclosed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX2","text":"The complete autonomy of the moral kingdom with respect to the physical order is rendered inadmissible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX3","text":"The separation between natural causality and spiritual governance cannot be treated as a separation of foundations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS1","text":"Distinction between efficient and final causes → establishment of a harmony between two natural kingdoms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS2","text":"Natural harmony established → extension of the principle of harmony to two kingdoms at another level.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS3","text":"Nature/grace correspondence → distribution of divine functions between cosmic architecture and spiritual governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS4","text":"Functional distribution of God → ordered unity of the physical and the moral without suppression of their distinction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:AF1","text":"Harmony between efficient and final causes → legitimation of a new analogy → correspondence between physical nature and moral grace → dual determination of God as architect and monarch → integration of the two kingdoms into a higher harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ME1","text":"The opposition between nature and grace is reclassified as a relation of harmony between two distinct kingdoms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ME2","text":"The divine figure is mapped according to two correlated functions: construction of the universe and governance of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ME3","text":"The distinction between efficient causality and finality becomes the model of connection between physical order and moral order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4","text":"The universe is reconfigured as a structure at once mechanical and political.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text affirms a harmony between the physical kingdom of nature and the moral kingdom of grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT2","text":"Structural — Two types of causality and two orders of reality are coordinated without being conflated.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — A harmony already demonstrated is used as a matrix of legitimation for a new harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Reality is conceived as an ordered totality in which the cosmic machine and the spiritual city pertain to one and the same divine principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the movement of the argument: primary harmony, analogical extension, correspondence of orders, and dual divine function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction depends on the prior acceptance of a perfect harmony between efficient causes and final causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3","text":"The text underdetermines the precise mechanism through which the harmony between nature and grace is realized.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence rests on the distinction maintained between the kingdoms and on their coordination by one and the same God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT5","text":"The principal tension lies in the articulation between the separation of the orders and the affirmation of their harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT6","text":"The compression preserves the actual movement of the text, but leaves open the exact nature of the correspondence between cosmic architecture and moral governance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_79:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_79@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_79:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 87"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 87","title":"Proposition 87","context":"Chapter 87","original_title":"Proposition 87"},"original_title":"Proposition 87","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 88","order":88,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_80"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_80@R001","sha256":"673bd69486c3f6a69f8e9fa96a9554d36da0de07c2966cee34d1e4787e5fb2d2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS1","text":"L’harmonie doit expliquer comment les choses conduisent à la Grâce sans sortir des voies de la Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS2","text":"La Nature est recadrée comme le moyen opératoire du gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS3","text":"La destruction et la réparation du globe deviennent des opérations naturelles déterminées par une finalité spirituelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS4","text":"Les événements cosmiques sont distribués selon une économie de châtiment et de récompense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS5","text":"L’argument convertit ainsi une finalité théologique en processus naturel réglé par l’harmonie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","text":"Une harmonie relie les voies de la Nature à la conduite des choses vers la Grâce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A2","text":"La Nature constitue le mode d’exécution du gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A3","text":"Le gouvernement des esprits requiert des transformations cosmiques correspondant aux mérites et aux fautes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A4","text":"Le globe peut être détruit par des voies naturelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A5","text":"Le globe peut être réparé par des voies naturelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A6","text":"Le moment de la destruction ou de la réparation dépend de la demande du gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A7","text":"Le châtiment des uns et la récompense des autres sont des fonctions opératoires de l’ordre cosmique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A8","text":"La finalité spirituelle peut être réalisée par des causes naturelles sans perdre son caractère providentiel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX1","text":"La conduite vers la Grâce n’est pas séparée des voies de la Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX2","text":"La destruction du globe n’est pas posée comme un événement dépourvu de médiation naturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX3","text":"La réparation du globe n’est pas produite par une rupture avec l’ordre naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX4","text":"Le gouvernement des esprits n’est pas indépendant des transformations du monde matériel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX5","text":"Le châtiment et la récompense ne sont pas des conséquences étrangères à la structure cosmique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:D1","text":"La Nature devient l’instrument médiateur par lequel l’harmonie rend effectif l’accès à la Grâce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_80:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:D2","text":"Les changements du globe acquièrent une signification morale parce qu’ils sont ordonnés aux fautes et aux mérites des esprits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A3","CH_UCIC_P_80:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:D3","text":"La destruction et la réparation forment les deux opérations symétriques d’une même économie naturelle de gouvernement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A4","CH_UCIC_P_80:A5","CH_UCIC_P_80:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:D4","text":"Le temps cosmique est subordonné à une décision spirituelle qui détermine le moment des transformations naturelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SD1","text":"L’ordre naturel est totalisé comme l’appareil d’exécution d’une justice spirituelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_80:A2","CH_UCIC_P_80:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","text":"La distinction entre causalité naturelle et finalité théologique est neutralisée par leur intégration dans une même harmonie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_80:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SD3","text":"Le monde physique devient réversible selon les exigences du gouvernement des esprits, sans cesser d’obéir à des voies naturelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A4","CH_UCIC_P_80:A5","CH_UCIC_P_80:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une causalité naturelle puisse être entièrement dépourvue de finalité spirituelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut que la Grâce exige une intervention extérieure ou arbitraire à l’ordre de la Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une séparation durable entre l’ordre moral des esprits et l’état matériel du globe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut un temps cosmique autonome, indépendant des exigences du gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX1","text":"Est forclose la possibilité d’un monde naturel indifférent au destin moral des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX2","text":"Est forclose l’idée d’une Grâce sans médiation cosmique et naturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX3","text":"Est absente la contingence radicale : chaque transformation du globe doit pouvoir être reconduite à une demande du gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS1","text":"Harmonie cosmique → articulation de la Nature et de la Grâce.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS2","text":"Articulation naturelle-spirituelle → instrumentalisation de la Nature par le gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS3","text":"Gouvernement moral → détermination des transformations du globe selon le châtiment et la récompense.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS4","text":"Détermination spirituelle du moment → destruction ou réparation par des voies naturelles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS5","text":"Destruction/réparation naturelles → confirmation d’un ordre cosmique providentiel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AF1","text":"Harmonie → médiation naturelle de la Grâce → gouvernement des esprits → distribution du châtiment et de la récompense → destruction ou réparation du globe → accomplissement providentiel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ME1","text":"La Nature est reclassée de milieu autonome en instrument du gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ME2","text":"La destruction et la réparation sont reclassées comme deux modalités d’une même régulation cosmique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ME3","text":"Le globe devient une surface matérielle où s’inscrivent les rapports moraux entre les esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ME4","text":"La frontière entre événement physique et sanction spirituelle est supprimée au profit d’une causalité harmonique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le globe est détruit ou réparé naturellement au moment requis.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT2","text":"Structural — Les voies naturelles exécutent les décisions du gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’argument recadre les catastrophes et restaurations cosmiques comme des opérations de justice plutôt que comme des anomalies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La réalité naturelle est ordonnée à une finalité spirituelle, et son temps dépend des exigences morales du gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le passage : harmonie, Nature, Grâce, gouvernement des esprits et économie du châtiment et de la récompense sont interdépendants.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT2","text":"La chaîne générative restitue le mouvement de la finalité spirituelle vers l’événement naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT3","text":"La reconstruction reste sous-déterminée quant aux mécanismes précis de destruction et de réparation du globe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT4","text":"La cohérence interne dépend de l’acceptation simultanée d’une causalité naturelle et d’une détermination spirituelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT5","text":"La tension principale demeure la conciliation entre l’autonomie apparente des voies naturelles et leur subordination au gouvernement des esprits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194535367146Z_efb148d7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 88","source_sha256":"673bd69486c3f6a69f8e9fa96a9554d36da0de07c2966cee34d1e4787e5fb2d2","sha256":"3029de873f99acd7fc473d4a65650da5266720005788320e3a13a974d3d0718a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:45:35.373838+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS1","text":"Harmony must explain how things lead to Grace without departing from the ways of Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS2","text":"Nature is reframed as the operative means of the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS3","text":"The destruction and repair of the globe become natural operations determined by a spiritual finality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS4","text":"Cosmic events are distributed according to an economy of punishment and reward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AS5","text":"The argument thus converts a theological finality into a natural process governed by harmony.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","text":"A harmony connects the ways of Nature to the leading of things toward Grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A2","text":"Nature constitutes the mode of execution of the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A3","text":"The government of spirits requires cosmic transformations corresponding to merits and faults.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A4","text":"The globe can be destroyed by natural means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A5","text":"The globe can be repaired by natural means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A6","text":"The moment of destruction or repair depends on the demand of the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A7","text":"The punishment of some and the reward of others are operative functions of the cosmic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:A8","text":"Spiritual finality can be realized through natural causes without losing its providential character.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX1","text":"Leading toward Grace is not separate from the ways of Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX2","text":"The destruction of the globe is not posited as an event devoid of natural mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX3","text":"The repair of the globe is not produced by a rupture with the natural order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX4","text":"The government of spirits is not independent of the transformations of the material world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:NX5","text":"Punishment and reward are not consequences alien to the cosmic structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:D1","text":"Nature becomes the mediating instrument through which harmony makes access to Grace effective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_80:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:D2","text":"Changes in the globe acquire a moral significance because they are ordered to the faults and merits of spirits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A3","CH_UCIC_P_80:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:D3","text":"Destruction and repair form the two symmetrical operations of one and the same natural economy of government.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A4","CH_UCIC_P_80:A5","CH_UCIC_P_80:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:D4","text":"Cosmic time is subordinated to a spiritual decision that determines the moment of natural transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SD1","text":"The natural order is totalized as the apparatus for the execution of a spiritual justice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_80:A2","CH_UCIC_P_80:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","text":"The distinction between natural causality and theological finality is neutralized by their integration into one and the same harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_80:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SD3","text":"The physical world becomes reversible according to the requirements of the government of spirits, without ceasing to obey natural ways.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A4","CH_UCIC_P_80:A5","CH_UCIC_P_80:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a natural causality could be entirely devoid of spiritual finality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that Grace requires an intervention external or arbitrary to the order of Nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a lasting separation between the moral order of spirits and the material state of the globe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX4","text":"The system excludes an autonomous cosmic time, independent of the requirements of the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX1","text":"Foreclosed is the possibility of a natural world indifferent to the moral destiny of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX2","text":"Foreclosed is the idea of a Grace without cosmic and natural mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX3","text":"Radical contingency is absent: every transformation of the globe must be capable of being traced back to a demand of the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS1","text":"Cosmic harmony → articulation of Nature and Grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS2","text":"Natural-spiritual articulation → instrumentalization of Nature by the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS3","text":"Moral government → determination of the transformations of the globe according to punishment and reward.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS4","text":"Spiritual determination of the moment → destruction or repair by natural means.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS5","text":"Natural destruction/repair → confirmation of a providential cosmic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:AF1","text":"Harmony → natural mediation of Grace → government of spirits → distribution of punishment and reward → destruction or repair of the globe → providential fulfillment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ME1","text":"Nature is reclassified from an autonomous milieu into an instrument of the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ME2","text":"Destruction and repair are reclassified as two modalities of one and the same cosmic regulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ME3","text":"The globe becomes a material surface upon which the moral relations between spirits are inscribed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ME4","text":"The boundary between physical event and spiritual sanction is removed in favor of a harmonic causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT1","text":"Surface — The globe is naturally destroyed or repaired at the required moment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT2","text":"Structural — Natural ways execute the decisions of the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument reframes cosmic catastrophes and restorations as operations of justice rather than as anomalies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Natural reality is ordered to a spiritual finality, and its time depends on the moral requirements of the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage: harmony, Nature, Grace, the government of spirits, and the economy of punishment and reward are interdependent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT2","text":"The generative chain restores the movement from spiritual finality to natural event.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT3","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined regarding the precise mechanisms of the destruction and repair of the globe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence depends on the simultaneous acceptance of a natural causality and a spiritual determination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT5","text":"The principal tension remains the reconciliation between the apparent autonomy of natural ways and their subordination to the government of spirits.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_80:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_80@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_80:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 88"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 88","title":"Proposition 88","context":"Chapter 88","original_title":"Proposition 88"},"original_title":"Proposition 88","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 89","order":89,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_81"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_81@R001","sha256":"1254788a27d22c320bd4b8acfd485a8e8263e347ea00da9b940bd0990ac23d7d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AS1","text":"Le problème consiste à rendre compatibles la législation divine et la structure naturelle des événements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AS2","text":"Le texte recadre cette compatibilité comme une adéquation entre Dieu architecte et Dieu législateur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AS3","text":"L’ordre naturel est posé comme une structure mécanique capable de produire les peines et les récompenses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AS4","text":"La sanction du péché et la récompense de l’action belle sont ainsi immanentes aux corps, sans exiger une manifestation immédiate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A1","text":"Dieu exerce à la fois une fonction d’architecte et une fonction de législateur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","text":"Ce que Dieu construit comme architecte satisfait ce qu’il ordonne comme législateur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","text":"La nature possède une structure mécanique ordonnée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","text":"La structure mécanique des choses peut produire des conséquences morales dans l’ordre corporel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","text":"Les péchés portent leur peine avec eux par l’ordre de la nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A6","text":"Les belles actions attirent leurs récompenses par des voies machinales relativement aux corps.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","text":"La production naturelle d’une peine ou d’une récompense n’implique pas son apparition immédiate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:NX1","text":"La justice divine n’est pas séparée de l’architecture naturelle du monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:NX2","text":"La peine du péché n’est pas définie comme une intervention extérieure indépendante de la nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:NX3","text":"La récompense des belles actions n’est pas définie comme un événement nécessairement instantané.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:NX4","text":"L’ordre moral n’est pas conçu comme dépourvu de médiation corporelle et mécanique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:D1","text":"La satisfaction du législateur divin est réalisée par la cohérence de l’ordre naturel construit par l’architecte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A1","CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:D2","text":"La peine du péché est une conséquence interne de la structure naturelle plutôt qu’un ajout extrinsèque à celle-ci.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","CH_UCIC_P_81:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:D3","text":"Les récompenses des belles actions sont engendrées par les mêmes voies mécaniques qui organisent les effets corporels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:D4","text":"L’absence de récompense ou de peine immédiate ne réfute pas leur inscription dans l’ordre naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1","text":"La justice divine est convertie en processus naturel différé plutôt qu’en succession d’actes judiciaires ponctuels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2","text":"La structure corporelle du monde devient le dispositif de traduction mécanique d’une distinction morale entre péché et action belle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","text":"Le délai entre l’action et son effet permet de maintenir simultanément la nécessité de la rétribution et l’absence de sa visibilité immédiate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une justice divine cohérente doive suspendre ou interrompre l’ordre mécanique de la nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX2","text":"Le système exclut qu’une conséquence morale soit réelle seulement lorsqu’elle est immédiatement perceptible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX3","text":"Le système exclut une opposition principielle entre causalité naturelle et finalité morale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX4","text":"Le système exclut que la législation divine soit extérieure aux conditions architecturales du monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX1","text":"L’impossibilité silencieusement forclose est celle d’un monde où le mal pourrait rester structurellement sans conséquence et le bien sans attraction rétributive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX2","text":"L’absence structurante est l’absence d’une justice immédiatement lisible dans chaque situation particulière.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX3","text":"Le texte rend inadmissible un hasard naturel qui dissocierait durablement les qualités morales de leurs effets corporels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS1","text":"Dualité divine architecte/législateur → exigence de concordance entre construction naturelle et loi morale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS2","text":"Concordance → inscription de la loi morale dans la structure mécanique des choses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS3","text":"Inscription mécanique → peine du péché et récompense de l’action belle comme effets corporels naturels.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS4","text":"Non-immédiateté des effets → maintien de la rétribution sans exigence de manifestation instantanée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS5","text":"Rétribution naturelle différée → clôture de la tension entre ordre moral et causalité mécanique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AF1","text":"Distinction entre Dieu architecte et Dieu législateur → affirmation de leur satisfaction réciproque → inscription de la loi dans l’ordre naturel → production mécanique des peines et récompenses corporelles → acceptation de leur manifestation différée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ME1","text":"La frontière entre ordre physique et ordre moral est reclassée comme une continuité mécanique.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ME2","text":"La peine et la récompense deviennent des effets structurels plutôt que des événements simplement ajoutés au monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ME3","text":"L’immédiateté cesse d’être le critère de réalité de la justice naturelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ME4","text":"Le délai temporel est reclassé comme une modalité compatible avec la nécessité rétributive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT1","text":"Surface — Les péchés reçoivent leur peine et les belles actions leurs récompenses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT2","text":"Structural — La nature fonctionne comme une architecture mécanique produisant des conséquences corporelles moralement différenciées.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La difficulté apparente créée par l’absence de rétribution immédiate est neutralisée par le recours au délai naturel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Le réel est ordonné de telle sorte que la causalité mécanique incorpore la normativité morale selon une temporalité non instantanée.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire le passage : dualité divine, ordre naturel, médiation mécanique et non-immédiateté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT2","text":"La reconstruction reste sous-déterminée quant au mécanisme précis par lequel les corps produisent les peines et les récompenses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT3","text":"La structure est intérieurement cohérente si la nature est tenue pour une architecture mécaniquement orientée par la loi divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT4","text":"Le point de tension principal réside dans l’identification d’effets moraux nécessaires à partir de mécanismes corporels dont le texte ne détaille pas la médiation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT5","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel : concordance théologique → naturalisation mécanique de la rétribution → suspension de l’exigence d’immédiateté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194548908307Z_1665aa68","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 89","source_sha256":"1254788a27d22c320bd4b8acfd485a8e8263e347ea00da9b940bd0990ac23d7d","sha256":"c3d87b4feee4f8d6e53c0fbefaeda4ff8b01af4a89b055a69030662542fef962","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:45:48.911379+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AS1","text":"The problem consists in making divine legislation and the natural structure of events compatible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AS2","text":"The text reframes this compatibility as an adequacy between God as architect and God as legislator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AS3","text":"The natural order is posited as a mechanical structure capable of producing punishments and rewards.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AS4","text":"The punishment of sin and the reward of the beautiful action are thus immanent to bodies, without requiring an immediate manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A1","text":"God exercises both a function of architect and a function of legislator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","text":"What God constructs as architect satisfies what he ordains as legislator.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","text":"Nature possesses an ordered mechanical structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","text":"The mechanical structure of things can produce moral consequences in the bodily order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","text":"Sins carry their punishment with them through the order of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A6","text":"Beautiful actions attract their rewards through mechanical pathways with respect to bodies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","text":"The natural production of a punishment or a reward does not imply its immediate appearance.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:NX1","text":"Divine justice is not separate from the natural architecture of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:NX2","text":"The punishment of sin is not defined as an external intervention independent of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:NX3","text":"The reward of beautiful actions is not defined as a necessarily instantaneous event.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:NX4","text":"The moral order is not conceived as devoid of bodily and mechanical mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:D1","text":"The satisfaction of the divine legislator is realized through the coherence of the natural order constructed by the architect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A1","CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:D2","text":"The punishment of sin is an internal consequence of the natural structure rather than an extrinsic addition to it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","CH_UCIC_P_81:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:D3","text":"The rewards of beautiful actions are generated by the same mechanical pathways that organize bodily effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:D4","text":"The absence of immediate reward or punishment does not refute their inscription in the natural order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1","text":"Divine justice is converted into a deferred natural process rather than a succession of discrete judicial acts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2","text":"The bodily structure of the world becomes the apparatus for mechanically translating a moral distinction between sin and beautiful action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","text":"The delay between action and its effect makes it possible simultaneously to maintain the necessity of retribution and the absence of its immediate visibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that coherent divine justice must suspend or interrupt the mechanical order of nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a moral consequence is real only when it is immediately perceptible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a principled opposition between natural causality and moral finality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the possibility that divine legislation is external to the architectural conditions of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX1","text":"The silently foreclosed impossibility is that of a world in which evil could remain structurally without consequence and good without retributive attraction.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX2","text":"The structuring absence is the absence of a justice immediately legible in every particular situation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX3","text":"The text renders inadmissible a natural chance that would durably dissociate moral qualities from their bodily effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS1","text":"Divine architect/legislator duality → requirement of concordance between natural construction and moral law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS2","text":"Concordance → inscription of moral law in the mechanical structure of things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS3","text":"Mechanical inscription → punishment of sin and reward of beautiful action as natural bodily effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS4","text":"Non-immediacy of effects → maintenance of retribution without requiring instantaneous manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS5","text":"Deferred natural retribution → closure of the tension between moral order and mechanical causality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:AF1","text":"Distinction between God as architect and God as legislator → affirmation of their reciprocal satisfaction → inscription of law in the natural order → mechanical production of bodily punishments and rewards → acceptance of their deferred manifestation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ME1","text":"The boundary between physical order and moral order is reclassified as a mechanical continuity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ME2","text":"Punishment and reward become structural effects rather than events simply added to the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ME3","text":"Immediacy ceases to be the criterion of the reality of natural justice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ME4","text":"Temporal delay is reclassified as a modality compatible with retributive necessity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT1","text":"Surface — Sins receive their punishment and beautiful actions their rewards.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT2","text":"Structural — Nature functions as a mechanical architecture producing morally differentiated bodily consequences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The apparent difficulty created by the absence of immediate retribution is neutralized through recourse to natural delay.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The real is ordered in such a way that mechanical causality incorporates moral normativity according to a non-instantaneous temporality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage: divine duality, natural order, mechanical mediation, and non-immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT2","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined as to the precise mechanism by which bodies produce punishments and rewards.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT3","text":"The structure is internally coherent if nature is held to be an architecture mechanically oriented by divine law.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT4","text":"The principal point of tension lies in identifying necessary moral effects from bodily mechanisms whose mediation the text does not detail.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT5","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement: theological concordance → mechanical naturalization of retribution → suspension of the requirement of immediacy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_81:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_81@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_81:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 89"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 89","title":"Proposition 89","context":"Chapter 89","original_title":"Proposition 89"},"original_title":"Proposition 89","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82","layer":"CH","title":"Proposition 90","order":90,"parents":["RAW_UCIC_P_82"],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_82@R001","sha256":"3a71e9f7d462ba7375870782db3537b1c0385a6b814fcb59e7f943ae5478e44e","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS1","text":"Le problème est de déterminer la condition d’un ordre gouvernemental parfaitement juste et intégralement orienté vers le bien.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS2","text":"Le recadrage consiste à subordonner la réussite humaine à l’ordre providentiel plutôt qu’à l’apparence immédiate des événements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS3","text":"La justice de cet ordre exige une correspondance universelle entre action morale, récompense, faute et châtiment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS4","text":"La conduite vertueuse combine l’accomplissement du devoir, l’adhésion confiante à la Providence et l’amour imitatif de l’Auteur du bien.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS5","text":"L’action humaine doit viser la volonté divine présomptive, tandis que l’acceptation porte sur la volonté divine secrète et effective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS6","text":"La limitation de la connaissance humaine fonde l’optimité nécessaire de l’ordre universel et l’identification de Dieu comme cause efficiente, cause finale, maître et source du bonheur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A1","text":"Un gouvernement parfait ne laisse aucune bonne action sans récompense ni aucune mauvaise action sans châtiment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A2","text":"L’ordre providentiel fait concourir toute chose au bien de ceux qui lui sont adéquatement attachés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A3","text":"Les bons sont ceux qui accomplissent leur devoir et ne se constituent pas en mécontents de l’ordre divin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","text":"La confiance en la Providence est compatible avec l’obligation préalable d’agir conformément au devoir.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A5","text":"Le pur amour consiste à prendre plaisir à la félicité de ce que l’on aime.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A6","text":"Aimer Dieu correctement implique d’aimer et d’imiter l’Auteur de tout bien.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","text":"La volonté humaine doit poursuivre ce qui paraît conforme à la volonté divine présomptive ou antécédente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A8","text":"La volonté humaine doit se contenter de ce que la volonté divine secrète, conséquente et décisive fait effectivement arriver.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A9","text":"L’ordre de l’univers excède les souhaits des plus sages lorsqu’il est considéré dans son ensemble véritable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A10","text":"L’univers ne peut être rendu meilleur, ni en général ni pour l’individu correctement attaché à Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A11","text":"Dieu est à la fois l’Architecte et la cause efficiente de l’être humain, ainsi que son Maître et sa cause finale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A12","text":"Le bonheur humain dépend ultimement de Dieu comme fin de la volonté.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX1","text":"Le gouvernement parfait n’est pas un ordre où le bien resterait sans récompense ou le mal sans châtiment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX2","text":"La bonté n’est pas définie par le mécontentement envers l’ordre providentiel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX3","text":"La confiance en Dieu ne dispense pas de l’accomplissement du devoir.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX4","text":"La volonté humaine ne se confond pas avec la volonté divine secrète qui détermine effectivement les événements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX5","text":"La sagesse humaine ne possède pas une compréhension suffisante de l’ordre universel pour en corriger le plan.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX6","text":"Le bonheur ne relève pas d’une fin indépendante de Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D1","text":"Toute action morale s’inscrit dans une économie de rétribution qui garantit sa réussite ultime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A1","CH_UCIC_P_82:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D2","text":"La vertu exige simultanément l’action conforme au devoir et l’acceptation de l’issue effective des événements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D3","text":"La non-révolte contre l’ordre divin devient un critère constitutif de la bonté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A2","CH_UCIC_P_82:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D4","text":"Le pur amour transforme la perfection divine en principe de motivation pour l’action humaine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A5","CH_UCIC_P_82:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D5","text":"L’écart entre volonté présomptive et volonté conséquente permet de maintenir ensemble responsabilité pratique et acceptation providentielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D6","text":"L’impossibilité d’améliorer l’univers découle de l’insuffisance cognitive humaine et de la perfection de l’ordre divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A9","CH_UCIC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D7","text":"La finalité de la volonté humaine est hétéronome, puisque son bonheur dépend de la causalité finale divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A11","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SD1","text":"La Providence convertit l’échec apparent en bien ultime sans abolir l’obligation d’agir selon ce qui paraît juste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2","text":"Le système produit une subjectivité doublement réglée : active dans la poursuite du devoir, passive dans l’acceptation du résultat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SD3","text":"La perfection du monde devient indissociable d’une limitation structurelle du jugement humain sur le monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SD4","text":"L’ordre moral et l’ordre ontologique sont unifiés par la fonction finale de Dieu, qui ordonne simultanément les événements, les devoirs et le bonheur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX1","text":"Le système exclut qu’une perspective humaine locale puisse constituer une mesure suffisante de la perfection universelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX2","text":"Il exclut qu’une action humaine puisse produire par elle-même son accomplissement final ou son bonheur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX3","text":"Il exclut une opposition durable entre le bien individuel correctement ordonné et le bien total de l’univers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX4","text":"Il exclut une autonomie de la volonté qui déterminerait seule sa propre fin.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX5","text":"Il exclut qu’une critique de l’ordre effectif puisse prévaloir sur l’intelligibilité supposée de la totalité divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX1","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’un monde objectivement améliorable par un jugement humain adéquat.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX2","text":"L’absence structurante est l’absence d’accès humain immédiat à l’ordre complet des causes et des fins.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX3","text":"Le système rend inadmissible toute fin humaine qui ne serait pas reçue de Dieu comme cause finale du bonheur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS1","text":"Gouvernement parfait → rétribution universelle → convergence du devenir vers le bien des sujets adéquatement ordonnés.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS2","text":"Obligation humaine → recherche de la volonté divine présomptive → action vertueuse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS3","text":"Limitation cognitive → distinction entre volonté présomptive et volonté secrète → acceptation de l’événement effectif.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS4","text":"Compréhension totale supposée de l’ordre → constat de son optimalité → impossibilité d’une amélioration humaine du monde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS5","text":"Dieu comme cause efficiente et finale → subordination de la volonté humaine → bonheur comme accomplissement théocentré.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AF1","text":"Gouvernement parfait → rétribution des actions → définition du bon sujet → articulation devoir–amour–confiance → distinction des volontés divine présomptive et conséquente → limitation du jugement humain → optimalité de l’univers → Dieu comme fin exclusive du bonheur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ME1","text":"La distinction entre volonté divine présomptive et volonté divine conséquente reconfigure l’opposition entre action et résignation en complémentarité fonctionnelle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ME2","text":"La catégorie du mécontentement est reclassée : elle ne désigne plus une simple humeur, mais une position incompatible avec la bonté correctement définie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ME3","text":"Le monde est cartographié comme un ordre déjà optimal, de sorte que l’action vertueuse vise la conformité locale plutôt que la refonte globale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ME4","text":"Le bonheur est déplacé du registre d’un résultat autonome vers celui d’une relation finale avec Dieu.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le gouvernement parfait distribue récompenses et châtiments et fait concourir les événements au bien des bons.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT2","text":"Structural — L’ordre moral repose sur l’articulation entre devoir humain, rétribution providentielle et distinction des deux volontés divines.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Le sujet doit agir comme si la volonté divine pouvait être présumée tout en renonçant à juger négativement la volonté divine effective.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Dieu fonde à la fois l’existence, la finalité et le bonheur ; l’ordre total est antérieur et supérieur à toute appréciation humaine locale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT1","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire la chaîne gouvernement parfait–rétribution–vertu–Providence–bonheur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT2","text":"La distinction entre volonté présomptive et volonté conséquente est indispensable pour préserver simultanément l’action et l’acceptation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT3","text":"La reconstruction reste sous-déterminée quant au mécanisme précis de la récompense et du châtiment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT4","text":"La cohérence interne dépend de l’acceptation conjointe de l’optimité du monde et de l’insuffisance cognitive humaine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5","text":"La tension principale oppose l’injonction à transformer activement la conduite à l’interdiction implicite de juger transformable l’ordre total.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT6","text":"Une tension secondaire subsiste entre la définition du bon par l’absence de mécontentement et la qualification morale indépendante du devoir.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT7","text":"La reconstruction préserve le mouvement réel du texte, mais elle dépend de l’identification non démontrée entre perfection divine, optimalité cosmique et bonheur individuel.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194610837735Z_0b2f20e5","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Proposition 90","source_sha256":"3a71e9f7d462ba7375870782db3537b1c0385a6b814fcb59e7f943ae5478e44e","sha256":"143a15ae07097d853a183ed9a87560b2e9a2e205d9d75cfb65f174adccadee27","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:46:10.843923+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS1","text":"The problem is to determine the condition of a governmental order that is perfectly just and wholly oriented toward the good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS2","text":"The reframing consists in subordinating human success to providential order rather than to the immediate appearance of events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS3","text":"The justice of this order requires a universal correspondence between moral action, reward, fault, and punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS4","text":"Virtuous conduct combines the fulfilment of duty, trusting adherence to Providence, and imitative love of the Author of the good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS5","text":"Human action must aim at the presumptive divine will, whereas acceptance bears upon the secret and effective divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AS6","text":"The limitation of human knowledge grounds the necessary optimality of the universal order and the identification of God as efficient cause, final cause, master, and source of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A1","text":"A perfect government leaves no good action without reward and no bad action without punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A2","text":"Providential order makes all things concur for the good of those who are adequately attached to it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A3","text":"The good are those who fulfil their duty and do not make themselves discontented with the divine order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","text":"Trust in Providence is compatible with the prior obligation to act in accordance with duty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A5","text":"Pure love consists in taking pleasure in the felicity of what one loves.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A6","text":"Loving God properly entails loving and imitating the Author of every good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","text":"The human will must pursue what appears to conform to the presumptive or antecedent divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A8","text":"The human will must be content with what the secret, consequent, and decisive divine will effectively brings about.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A9","text":"The order of the universe exceeds the wishes of the wisest when it is considered in its true entirety.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A10","text":"The universe cannot be made better, either in general or for the individual properly attached to God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A11","text":"God is both the Architect and the efficient cause of the human being, as well as his Master and final cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:A12","text":"Human happiness ultimately depends on God as the end of the will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX1","text":"Perfect government is not an order in which good would remain without reward or evil without punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX2","text":"Goodness is not defined by discontent with providential order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX3","text":"Trust in God does not dispense one from fulfilling duty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX4","text":"The human will is not identical with the secret divine will that effectively determines events.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX5","text":"Human wisdom does not possess a sufficient understanding of the universal order to correct its plan.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:NX6","text":"Happiness does not depend on an end independent of God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D1","text":"Every moral action belongs within an economy of retribution that guarantees its ultimate success.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A1","CH_UCIC_P_82:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D2","text":"Virtue simultaneously requires action in accordance with duty and acceptance of the effective outcome of events.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D3","text":"Non-revolt against the divine order becomes a constitutive criterion of goodness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A2","CH_UCIC_P_82:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D4","text":"Pure love transforms divine perfection into a principle of motivation for human action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A5","CH_UCIC_P_82:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D5","text":"The gap between presumptive will and consequent will makes it possible to maintain together practical responsibility and providential acceptance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D6","text":"The impossibility of improving the universe follows from human cognitive insufficiency and the perfection of the divine order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A9","CH_UCIC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:D7","text":"The finality of the human will is heteronomous, since its happiness depends on divine final causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A11","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SD1","text":"Providence converts apparent failure into ultimate good without abolishing the obligation to act according to what appears just.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2","text":"The system produces a doubly regulated subjectivity: active in the pursuit of duty, passive in the acceptance of the result.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SD3","text":"The perfection of the world becomes inseparable from a structural limitation of human judgment concerning the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SD4","text":"The moral order and the ontological order are unified by God's final function, which simultaneously orders events, duties, and happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX1","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a local human perspective could constitute a sufficient measure of universal perfection.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX2","text":"It excludes the possibility that a human action could by itself produce its final fulfilment or its happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX3","text":"It excludes a lasting opposition between properly ordered individual good and the total good of the universe.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX4","text":"It excludes an autonomy of the will that would alone determine its own end.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX5","text":"It excludes the possibility that a critique of the effective order could prevail over the assumed intelligibility of the divine totality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX1","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of a world objectively improvable by adequate human judgment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX2","text":"The structuring absence is the absence of immediate human access to the complete order of causes and ends.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX3","text":"The system renders inadmissible every human end that would not be received from God as the final cause of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS1","text":"Perfect government → universal retribution → convergence of becoming toward the good of adequately ordered subjects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS2","text":"Human obligation → pursuit of the presumptive divine will → virtuous action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS3","text":"Cognitive limitation → distinction between presumptive will and secret will → acceptance of the effective event.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS4","text":"Assumed total understanding of the order → recognition of its optimality → impossibility of a human improvement of the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS5","text":"God as efficient and final cause → subordination of the human will → happiness as theocentred fulfilment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:AF1","text":"Perfect government → retribution of actions → definition of the good subject → articulation of duty–love–trust → distinction between presumptive and consequent divine wills → limitation of human judgment → optimality of the universe → God as the exclusive end of happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ME1","text":"The distinction between presumptive divine will and consequent divine will reconfigures the opposition between action and resignation into functional complementarity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ME2","text":"The category of discontent is reclassified: it no longer designates a mere mood, but a position incompatible with properly defined goodness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ME3","text":"The world is mapped as an already optimal order, such that virtuous action aims at local conformity rather than global refashioning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ME4","text":"Happiness is displaced from the register of an autonomous result to that of a final relation with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT1","text":"Surface — Perfect government distributes rewards and punishments and makes events concur for the good of the good.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT2","text":"Structural — The moral order rests on the articulation between human duty, providential retribution, and the distinction of the two divine wills.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The subject must act as though the divine will could be presumed while renouncing negatively judging the effective divine will.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — God grounds existence, finality, and happiness alike; the total order is prior and superior to every local human appraisal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the chain perfect government–retribution–virtue–Providence–happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT2","text":"The distinction between presumptive will and consequent will is indispensable for preserving action and acceptance simultaneously.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT3","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined as to the precise mechanism of reward and punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT4","text":"Internal coherence depends on the joint acceptance of the optimality of the world and human cognitive insufficiency.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5","text":"The principal tension opposes the injunction actively to transform conduct to the implicit prohibition against judging the total order transformable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0001","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_UCIC_P_82:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT6","text":"A secondary tension persists between the definition of the good by the absence of discontent and the independent moral qualification of duty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text, but it depends on the undemonstrated identification between divine perfection, cosmic optimality, and individual happiness.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_UCIC_P_82@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_UCIC_P_82:v1","source_language_code":"fr","original_title":"Proposition 90"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 90","title":"Proposition 90","context":"Chapter 90","original_title":"Proposition 90"},"original_title":"Proposition 90","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 01–03","order":1,"parents":["CH_UCIC_PRO1","CH_UCIC_PRO2","CH_UCIC_PRO3"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_01@R001","sha256":"cda9996d8b856b773cea95376cdaeff90ddd25ae301f92400c4d525d2102f901","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-01","text":"Le problème central consiste à expliquer la constitution des composés sans faire d’un composé le terme ultime de l’explication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-02","text":"Le composé est recadré comme agrégat dérivé, dont l’analyse doit remonter vers des constituants qui ne soient pas eux-mêmes composés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-03","text":"Les trois propositions convergent vers une même condition terminale : une substance simple, sans parties, nécessaire à la clôture de l’analyse compositionnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-04","text":"La simplicité reçoit une détermination négative cumulative qui exclut l’étendue, la figure et la divisibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-05","text":"L’atome naturel est ainsi déplacé du registre de la petitesse corporelle vers celui de l’unité non spatiale qui constitue les choses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-06","text":"La clôture produite est ontologique plutôt que mécaniste : la nécessité des éléments simples est établie, mais leur mode d’entrée dans les composés demeure indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La monade est une substance simple qui ne contient aucune composition interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La simplicité signifie l’absence de parties et non une simple réduction quantitative de la grandeur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Le composé est un agrégat dérivé qui ne peut constituer par lui-même le terme ultime de l’analyse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","text":"[Terminal] L’analyse compositionnelle doit atteindre des constituants simples afin d’éviter une régression sans terme ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La même unité simple est à la fois terme terminal de l’analyse et condition constituante des composés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] L’absence de parties se transforme d’une définition logique de la simplicité en exclusion des déterminations spatiales et géométriques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] L’atome véritable de la nature n’est pas une particule étendue mais une unité indivisible dont procèdent les choses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Le fondement de la nature est déplacé de la composition des parties vers l’unité sans parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] L’unité des composés est dérivée et relationnelle, tandis que l’unité simple est posée comme primitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] La fonction constituante ne requiert pas que l’élément fondamental possède lui-même une structure composée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-01","text":"La simplicité revient d’abord comme propriété de la monade, puis comme condition de clôture de toute analyse des agrégats.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-02","text":"Le composé passe du statut d’objet donné à celui de réalité dérivée, puis devient le point de départ méthodologique d’une remontée vers ses conditions constituantes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-03","text":"L’absence de parties migre d’une négation structurelle vers une détermination naturelle excluant étendue, figure et divisibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-04","text":"Le terme « atome » inverse sa fonction : il ne désigne plus la plus petite portion d’un corps, mais l’élément naturel qui échappe à la division.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-05","text":"Le terme « élément » est absorbé dans une architecture ontologique : il ne nomme plus seulement une composante, mais le niveau premier de constitution des choses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Escalating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-06","text":"Le mécanisme d’union disparaît après avoir accompli sa fonction négative : il suffit d’établir la nécessité des éléments simples, non d’expliquer leur liaison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-07","text":"La monade conserve sa fonction constituante, mais cette fonction est recodée comme dépendance ontologique plutôt que comme composition interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-01","text":"La définition de la monade comme substance simple reste locale à la première machine lorsqu’elle ne détermine que son statut et sa simplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-02","text":"La déduction de l’absence d’étendue, de figure et de divisibilité reste locale à la troisième machine lorsqu’elle n’est pas reliée à la constitution des composés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-03","text":"Le changement d’échelle apparaît lorsque l’argument part simultanément du composé vers le simple et du simple vers la fonction constituante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-04","text":"La relation entre monade, substance simple, atome naturel et élément des choses constitue la liaison propre au cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-05","text":"La conception de l’atome comme objet corporel devient obsolète à cette échelle, car l’atomicité est recodée comme indivisibilité non spatiale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-06","text":"La distinction entre constituant et composé cesse d’être une simple opposition de niveaux et devient une asymétrie entre unité primitive et totalité dérivée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’un composé, un agrégat ou une totalité divisible puisse être le fondement ultime de sa propre constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut que l’unité naturelle première soit une étendue, une figure géométrique ou une portion corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut qu’une régression indéfinie de parties puisse fournir une explication complète de la composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que la simplicité soit une propriété dérivée d’un agrégat ou une simple limite quantitative de la divisibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut l’identification immédiate de l’élément naturel avec l’objet corporel mesurable et figuré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, il faut que le niveau des agrégats observables ne soit pas toute la réalité ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-02","text":"Il faut que la composition ne puisse pas s’expliquer par une composition antérieure indéfiniment reconduite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-03","text":"Il faut que l’espace, la figure et la division soient des déterminations dérivées plutôt que les conditions ultimes de la nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-04","text":"Le système disqualifie silencieusement une ontologie dans laquelle toute unité serait seulement une composition ultérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-05","text":"Il ne peut admettre que la fonction constituante d’un élément implique une composition interne du constituant lui-même.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSA-01","text":"L’architecture rend indisponible la possibilité d’un fondement entièrement spatial, divisible et composé de la nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSA-02","text":"Elle contourne la possibilité d’une union explicable par les seules relations de parties, sans fournir de mécanisme concurrent déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSA-03","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un terme intermédiaire entre l’unité simple et le composé : la nécessité du fondement est établie, mais son mode de liaison reste indisponible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSA-04","text":"Le système traite comme ontologiquement inadmissible un monde où la simplicité ne serait qu’une abstraction produite par la division.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-01","text":"La simplicité n’est pas seulement le terme où s’arrête l’analyse des composés ; elle est aussi la condition qui rend leur constitution intelligible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-02","CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PRO2:D2","CH_UCIC_PRO1:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-02","text":"La convergence des trois unités transforme l’absence de parties en opérateur général de déspatialisation de l’élément naturel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-02","CL_UCIC_01:GA-06","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-03","text":"Le composé acquiert un statut ontologique dérivé parce que son existence déclenche une remontée vers des unités dont l’existence ne dépend pas d’une composition antérieure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PRO2:A1","CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-04","text":"La fonction d’élément et l’absence de parties produisent une notion de constitution qui n’est ni une composition interne ni une simple relation spatiale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CL_UCIC_01:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PRO1:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-05","text":"L’argumentation fonctionne dans deux directions complémentaires : le composé exige le simple, tandis que le simple reçoit une fonction dans le composé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PRO2:D1","CH_UCIC_PRO1:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-06","text":"La notion d’atome naturel résulte de l’intersection entre la clôture logique de l’analyse et la négation physique de l’étendue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-06","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO3:D2","CH_UCIC_PRO3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est reclassé selon une architecture asymétrique où les totalités composées dépendent d’unités simples sans que l’inverse soit établi.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","CL_UCIC_01:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PRO2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-02","text":"L’élémentarité cesse d’être une propriété géométrique de la plus petite partie et devient une condition ontologique de non-composition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-06","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-03","text":"La stratégie explicative est inversée : au lieu de réduire le simple au composé, elle réduit l’intelligibilité du composé à l’exigence du simple.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-04","text":"Le cluster produit une clôture de nécessité mais non une théorie de l’union : il détermine ce qui doit exister sans déterminer comment les éléments composent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT2","CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-05","text":"La priorité du simple sur le composé est ontologique et explicative, mais son mode exact de priorité reste non spécifié.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PRO1:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-06","text":"L’analyse transforme un donné empirique ou descriptif en indice d’une condition qui n’est ni observable comme agrégat ni reconstruisible par division.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-01","text":"Composé → agrégat → constituants → substances simples → éléments des choses → retour fonctionnel dans les composés : la boucle ferme l’analyse sans expliquer l’union.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-02","text":"Absence de parties → absence d’étendue, de figure et de divisibilité → atome naturel → élément : la négation répétée se convertit en détermination positive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-03","text":"La répétition du simple change de phase lorsqu’il passe de propriété de la monade à condition de toute constitution naturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est l’unité sans parties : elle absorbe les fonctions de substance, de constituant, d’atome et d’élément.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-05","text":"L’escalade va de la définition nominale de la monade à la reclassification de la nature entière comme ordre dépendant d’unités non composées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B01","text":"Un composé donné est traité comme un agrégat ; l’agrégat est déclaré dérivé ; l’analyse cherche alors ses constituants ultimes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B02","text":"La recherche des constituants rencontre une condition de clôture : les éléments ultimes ne peuvent être eux-mêmes des agrégats.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B03","text":"La condition de clôture est identifiée à la monade, substance simple sans parties, dont la fonction constituante ne dérive pas d’une composition interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B04","text":"L’absence de parties est amplifiée en absence d’étendue, de figure et de divisibilité ; la monade devient ainsi l’atome véritable de la nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B05","text":"La machine produit une ontologie stratifiée : l’élément simple fonde le composé, tandis que le passage effectif de l’un à l’autre demeure une limite interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AFM-B01","text":"Composé donné → agrégat dérivé → remontée vers les constituants → clôture par la substance simple → négation de l’espace et de la divisibilité → atome naturel non spatial → élément des choses → constitution réaffirmée sans mécanisme d’union.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AFM-B02","text":"L’argument passe d’une demande d’explication compositionnelle à une reclassification ontologique de l’élément, puis transforme cette reclassification en limite critique contre toute ontologie spatiale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AFM-B03","text":"La clôture terminale est asymétrique : la nécessité des éléments simples est atteinte, mais la relation constitutive qui les unit aux composés reste ouverte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-01","text":"La carte ontologique distingue désormais trois fonctions d’une même unité : substance simple, constituant des composés et élément naturel non spatial.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-02","text":"La distinction partie/totalité est remplacée par la distinction unité sans parties/agrégat, ce qui dissocie élémentarité et extension.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-03","text":"La fausse opposition entre atome et composé s’effondre : l’atome n’est plus le plus petit composé matériel, mais la condition non composée du composé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-04","text":"La question stratégique n’est plus « de quelles parties le composé est-il fait ? », mais « quelle unité rend possible qu’il y ait composition ? ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-05","text":"Une méthode d’analyse ascendante devient disponible : partir du composé manifeste pour atteindre une condition ontologique qui ne peut être observée comme composé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-06","text":"Le champ conceptuel est redessiné autour d’une asymétrie : les agrégats sont explicativement secondaires, tandis que les unités simples sont ontologiquement premières.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B01","text":"Au niveau de surface, des composés et des choses sont pris comme données dont il faut expliquer la constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B02","text":"Au niveau structural, le composé est distribué comme agrégat dépendant de constituants simples, tandis que la monade fonctionne sans composition interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B03","text":"Au niveau métastratégique, l’argument remplace l’acceptation descriptive du composé par une remontée vers ses conditions de possibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B04","text":"Au niveau ontologique et temporel, les monades sont posées comme unités antérieures à la composition, sans que cette antériorité soit déterminée comme succession temporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B05","text":"Au niveau méthodologique, la forme de l’argument accomplit sa propre thèse : elle part d’un agrégat et produit une condition non agrégée comme terme d’explication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FL-01","text":"La monade doit entrer dans les composés tout en étant dépourvue de parties ; la fonction constituante est donc affirmée sans être assimilée à une composition interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FL-02","text":"La nécessité des substances simples est plus fortement établie que leur mode d’union aux composés, ce qui crée une dissymétrie entre fondation et constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FL-03","text":"Le terme « atome » oscille entre analogie conceptuelle et détermination physique ; le cluster exploite cette oscillation sans la résoudre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation survient lorsque « simple » cesse de désigner seulement une structure sans parties et devient le critère d’un élément naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MP-02","text":"Le second point de mutation survient lorsque l’atome est soustrait au régime de la mesure, de la figure et de la divisibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation survient lorsque l’insuffisance d’une régression compositionnelle devient une architecture positive de fondements simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FL-04","text":"La clôture de l’analyse compositionnelle peut être lue comme démonstration ontologique ou comme exigence méthodologique ; le texte ne tranche pas entièrement entre ces deux statuts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:HSI-01","text":"La réalité apparaît implicitement comme une architecture à deux régimes : des agrégats dérivés à la surface et des unités non composées à leur fondement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet théorique devient une instance de remontée : il part du composé, traverse ses dépendances et atteint une unité que la division ne peut produire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:HSI-03","text":"Le temps implicite du système n’est pas celui d’une génération chronologique, mais celui d’un ordre de priorité ontologique entre l’élément et le composé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:HSI-04","text":"La forme de navigation disponible est une remontée analytique : sortir du régime des parties et des corps pour atteindre l’unité qui rend leur composition pensable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre noyaux : le composé comme agrégat, la simplicité comme absence de parties, la clôture par les substances simples et la détermination non spatiale de l’atome naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B02","text":"Ces noyaux suffisent à restituer le mouvement réel : donnée composée → analyse régressive → fondement simple → exclusion de l’étendue → élément naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B03","text":"La compression laisse indéterminés le nombre des monades, leur nature exacte, leur mode d’union et le statut physique ou analogique de l’atome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence est suffisante tant que la fonction constituante n’est pas confondue avec la possession de parties ; cette distinction est indispensable à toute reconstruction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B05","text":"La zone de force du système est la convergence entre nécessité logique et négation spatiale ; sa zone d’instabilité est l’absence d’une théorie de la liaison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B06","text":"Toute reconstruction qui conserve les monades comme éléments mais réintroduit un fondement corporel, une régression infinie ou une composition interne manque l’architecture du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194643930587Z_49e8885b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 01–03","source_sha256":"cda9996d8b856b773cea95376cdaeff90ddd25ae301f92400c4d525d2102f901","sha256":"04f543f05b9ef5cb8d97b3165a07cc2f4030e03f93c551b1c6cc58dcaf8c5e32","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:46:43.934201+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-01","text":"The central problem consists in explaining the constitution of composites without making a composite the ultimate term of explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-02","text":"The composite is reframed as a derived aggregate, whose analysis must ascend toward constituents that are not themselves composites.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-03","text":"The three propositions converge toward the same terminal condition: a simple substance, without parts, necessary for the closure of compositional analysis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-04","text":"Simplicity receives a cumulative negative determination that excludes extension, figure, and divisibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-05","text":"The natural atom is thus displaced from the register of corporeal smallness toward that of the non-spatial unity that constitutes things.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AS-06","text":"The closure produced is ontological rather than mechanistic: the necessity of simple elements is established, but their mode of entry into composites remains indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The monad is a simple substance that contains no internal composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Simplicity means the absence of parts and not a mere quantitative reduction of magnitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] The composite is a derived aggregate that cannot itself constitute the ultimate term of analysis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","text":"[Terminal] Compositional analysis must reach simple constituents in order to avoid a regression without an ontological term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The same simple unity is both the terminal term of analysis and the constitutive condition of composites.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] The absence of parts is transformed from a logical definition of simplicity into an exclusion of spatial and geometrical determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The true atom of nature is not an extended particle but an indivisible unity from which things proceed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] The foundation of nature is displaced from the composition of parts toward unity without parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] The unity of composites is derived and relational, whereas simple unity is posited as primitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] The constitutive function does not require that the fundamental element itself possess a composite structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-01","text":"Simplicity first recurs as a property of the monad, then as the condition of closure of every analysis of aggregates.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-02","text":"The composite passes from the status of a given object to that of a derived reality, then becomes the methodological point of departure for an ascent toward its constitutive conditions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-03","text":"The absence of parts migrates from a structural negation toward a natural determination excluding extension, figure, and divisibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-04","text":"The term « atom » reverses its function: it no longer designates the smallest portion of a body, but the natural element that escapes division.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-05","text":"The term « element » is absorbed into an ontological architecture: it no longer names merely a component, but the primary level of the constitution of things.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Escalating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-06","text":"The mechanism of union disappears after having fulfilled its negative function: it suffices to establish the necessity of simple elements, not to explain their connection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RMD-07","text":"The monad retains its constitutive function, but this function is recoded as ontological dependence rather than as internal composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-01","text":"The definition of the monad as a simple substance remains local to the first machine when it determines only its status and its simplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-02","text":"The deduction of the absence of extension, figure, and divisibility remains local to the third machine when it is not connected to the constitution of composites.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-03","text":"The change of scale appears when the argument proceeds simultaneously from the composite toward the simple and from the simple toward the constitutive function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-04","text":"The relation among monad, simple substance, natural atom, and element of things constitutes the connection proper to the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-05","text":"The conception of the atom as a corporeal object becomes obsolete at this scale, since atomicity is recoded as non-spatial indivisibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:CGD-06","text":"The distinction between constituent and composite ceases to be a mere opposition of levels and becomes an asymmetry between primitive unity and derived totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a composite, an aggregate, or a divisible totality can be the ultimate foundation of its own constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that the primary natural unity is an extension, a geometrical figure, or a corporeal portion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that an indefinite regression of parts can provide a complete explanation of composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that simplicity is a property derived from an aggregate or a mere quantitative limit of divisibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the immediate identification of the natural element with the measurable and figured corporeal object.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, the level of observable aggregates must not be the whole of ontological reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-02","text":"Composition must not be explicable by an indefinitely repeated prior composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-03","text":"Space, figure, and division must be derived determinations rather than the ultimate conditions of nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-04","text":"The system silently disqualifies an ontology in which every unity would be merely a further composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:DBN-05","text":"It cannot admit that the constitutive function of an element entails an internal composition of the constituent itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSA-01","text":"The architecture renders unavailable the possibility of an entirely spatial, divisible, and composite foundation of nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSA-02","text":"It bypasses the possibility of a union explicable by relations of parts alone, without providing a determinate competing mechanism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSA-03","text":"The structuring absence is that of an intermediate term between simple unity and the composite: the necessity of the foundation is established, but its mode of connection remains unavailable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSA-04","text":"The system treats as ontologically inadmissible a world in which simplicity would be only an abstraction produced by division.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-01","text":"Simplicity is not only the term at which the analysis of composites stops; it is also the condition that renders their constitution intelligible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-02","CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PRO2:D2","CH_UCIC_PRO1:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-02","text":"The convergence of the three units transforms the absence of parts into a general operator of the despatialization of the natural element.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-02","CL_UCIC_01:GA-06","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-03","text":"The composite acquires a derived ontological status because its existence triggers an ascent toward unities whose existence does not depend on a prior composition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PRO2:A1","CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-04","text":"The function of element and the absence of parts produce a notion of constitution that is neither internal composition nor a mere spatial relation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CL_UCIC_01:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PRO1:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-05","text":"The argumentation operates in two complementary directions: the composite requires the simple, while the simple receives a function in the composite.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PRO2:D1","CH_UCIC_PRO1:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:XD-06","text":"The notion of the natural atom results from the intersection between the logical closure of analysis and the physical negation of extension.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-06","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO3:D2","CH_UCIC_PRO3:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-01","text":"Reality is reclassified according to an asymmetrical architecture in which composite totalities depend on simple unities without the converse being established.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-05","CL_UCIC_01:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PRO2:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-02","text":"Elementarity ceases to be a geometrical property of the smallest part and becomes an ontological condition of non-composition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-06","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-03","text":"The explanatory strategy is reversed: instead of reducing the simple to the composite, it reduces the intelligibility of the composite to the requirement of the simple.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-04","text":"The cluster produces a closure of necessity but not a theory of union: it determines what must exist without determining how elements compose.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT2","CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-05","text":"The priority of the simple over the composite is ontological and explanatory, but its exact mode of priority remains unspecified.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-04","CL_UCIC_01:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PRO1:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:BSD-06","text":"The analysis transforms an empirical or descriptive given into an indication of a condition that is neither observable as an aggregate nor reconstructible by division.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03","CL_UCIC_01:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-01","text":"Composite → aggregate → constituents → simple substances → elements of things → functional return into composites: the loop closes the analysis without explaining union.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-02","text":"Absence of parts → absence of extension, figure, and divisibility → natural atom → element: repeated negation converts into positive determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-03","text":"The repetition of the simple changes phase when it passes from being a property of the monad to being a condition of all natural constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-04","text":"The conceptual attractor is unity without parts: it absorbs the functions of substance, constituent, atom, and element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:RLE-05","text":"The escalation proceeds from the nominal definition of the monad to the reclassification of the whole of nature as an order dependent on non-composite unities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B01","text":"A given composite is treated as an aggregate; the aggregate is declared derived; analysis then seeks its ultimate constituents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B02","text":"The search for constituents encounters a condition of closure: ultimate elements cannot themselves be aggregates.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B03","text":"The condition of closure is identified with the monad, a simple substance without parts, whose constitutive function does not derive from an internal composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B04","text":"The absence of parts is amplified into absence of extension, figure, and divisibility; the monad thus becomes the true atom of nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B05","text":"The machine produces a stratified ontology: the simple element grounds the composite, while the effective passage from one to the other remains an internal limit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AFM-B01","text":"Given composite → derived aggregate → ascent toward constituents → closure through simple substance → negation of space and divisibility → non-spatial natural atom → element of things → constitution reaffirmed without a mechanism of union.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AFM-B02","text":"The argument passes from a demand for compositional explanation to an ontological reclassification of the element, then transforms this reclassification into a critical limit against every spatial ontology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:AFM-B03","text":"The terminal closure is asymmetrical: the necessity of simple elements is reached, but the constitutive relation that unites them to composites remains open.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-01","text":"The ontological map henceforth distinguishes three functions of the same unity: simple substance, constituent of composites, and non-spatial natural element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-02","text":"The part/totality distinction is replaced by the distinction between unity without parts and aggregate, which dissociates elementarity from extension.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-03","text":"The false opposition between atom and composite collapses: the atom is no longer the smallest material composite, but the non-composite condition of the composite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-04","text":"The strategic question is no longer « of what parts is the composite made? », but « what unity makes it possible for composition to exist? ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-05","text":"A method of ascending analysis becomes available: beginning from the manifest composite in order to reach an ontological condition that cannot be observed as a composite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MME-06","text":"The conceptual field is redrawn around an asymmetry: aggregates are explanatorily secondary, whereas simple unities are ontologically primary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, composites and things are taken as givens whose constitution must be explained.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, the composite is distributed as an aggregate dependent on simple constituents, whereas the monad functions without internal composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the argument replaces the descriptive acceptance of the composite with an ascent toward its conditions of possibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, monads are posited as unities prior to composition, without this priority being determined as temporal succession.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological level, the form of the argument accomplishes its own thesis: it begins from an aggregate and produces a non-aggregated condition as the term of explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FL-01","text":"The monad must enter into composites while being devoid of parts; its constitutive function is therefore affirmed without being assimilated to an internal composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FL-02","text":"The necessity of simple substances is more strongly established than their mode of union with composites, which creates a dissymmetry between foundation and constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FL-03","text":"The term « atom » oscillates between conceptual analogy and physical determination; the cluster exploits this oscillation without resolving it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MP-01","text":"The first point of mutation occurs when « simple » ceases to designate only a structure without parts and becomes the criterion of a natural element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MP-02","text":"The second point of mutation occurs when the atom is removed from the regime of measure, figure, and divisibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MP-03","text":"The third point of mutation occurs when the insufficiency of a compositional regression becomes a positive architecture of simple foundations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:FL-04","text":"The closure of compositional analysis can be read as an ontological demonstration or as a methodological requirement; the text does not entirely decide between these two statuses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as an architecture with two regimes: derived aggregates at the surface and non-composite unities at their foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:HSI-02","text":"The theoretical subject becomes an instance of ascent: it begins from the composite, traverses its dependencies, and reaches a unity that division cannot produce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:HSI-03","text":"The implicit time of the system is not that of chronological generation, but that of an order of ontological priority between element and composite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:HSI-04","text":"The available form of navigation is an analytical ascent: leaving the regime of parts and bodies in order to reach the unity that renders their composition thinkable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four cores: the composite as aggregate, simplicity as absence of parts, closure through simple substances, and the non-spatial determination of the natural atom.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B02","text":"These cores suffice to restore the actual movement: composite given → regressive analysis → simple foundation → exclusion of extension → natural element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B03","text":"The compression leaves indeterminate the number of monads, their exact nature, their mode of union, and the physical or analogical status of the atom.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO2:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence is sufficient so long as the constitutive function is not confused with the possession of parts; this distinction is indispensable to every reconstruction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO1:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B05","text":"The system's zone of strength is the convergence between logical necessity and spatial negation; its zone of instability is the absence of a theory of connection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B06","text":"Every reconstruction that retains monads as elements but reintroduces a corporeal foundation, an infinite regression, or an internal composition misses the architecture of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_01:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 01–03","context":"Proposition 1 · Proposition 2 · Proposition 3"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 04–06","order":2,"parents":["CH_UCIC_PRO4","CH_UCIC_PRO5","CH_UCIC_PRO6"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_02@R001","sha256":"f616943414fd1fe33c491d9339d93630921339a8ae803fa0a5faf0012320d15d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-01","text":"Le problème central est de déterminer comment la simplicité règle les conditions de commencement, de fin et de transformation naturelle d’une entité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-02","text":"La simplicité est recadrée comme absence de parties, puis comme exclusion des opérations compositionnelles et décompositionnelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-03","text":"Le contraste entre simple et composé devient une différence entre deux régimes de causalité et de temporalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-04","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif : une impossibilité locale de dissolution s’étend à la genèse, puis à l’architecture ontologique des transitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-05","text":"La clôture ne fournit pas une conservation positive universelle, mais une frontière négative entre transformations partitives et événements instantanés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Une entité simple ne possède pas de parties dont la séparation puisse constituer sa dissolution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La dissolution et la décomposition présupposent une structure composée susceptible d’être désagrégée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] L’absence de composition interdit le commencement naturel lorsque celui-ci est défini par une formation composée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Les composés commencent et finissent par des opérations portant sur leurs parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Pour une entité simple, les limites existentielles ne peuvent être partitives et sont rapportées à la création et à l’annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La distinction entre simplicité et composition produit deux régimes temporels incompatibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-07","text":"[Terminal] La création et l’annihilation de l’entité simple sont des événements instantanés plutôt que des processus graduels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Aucun mécanisme naturel concevable de genèse ou de destruction ne peut être attribué à l’entité simple comme telle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:SD1","CH_UCIC_PRO4:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-01","text":"L’absence de parties conserve sa fonction négative à travers les unités : elle exclut d’abord la dissolution, puis la composition et enfin la transition partitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-02","text":"La simplicité mute d’une propriété de composition en contrainte sur la genèse et sur les limites temporelles de l’entité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-03","text":"La négation de la dissolution s’inverse en détermination positive du régime monadique par la création et l’annihilation instantanées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-04","text":"La question du périssement est absorbée dans une ontologie des opérations admissibles sur les parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-05","text":"La prétention à une conservation absolue disparaît au profit d’une conclusion limitée aux mécanismes naturels concevables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-01","text":"La non-dissolution d’une substance simple reste une proposition locale ; au niveau courant, elle devient un cas d’une exclusion générale des transitions partitives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-02","text":"L’absence de parties change d’échelle lorsqu’elle devient un principe de cartographie des modes possibles de destruction et de génération.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-03","text":"Les unités se relient lorsqu’elles font dépendre le commencement et la fin du même critère structurel : simplicité ou composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-04","text":"La transition majeure consiste à convertir l’impossibilité de médiation partitive en création et annihilation instantanées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-05","text":"Le modèle uniforme de génération et de corruption devient obsolète dès lors que les régimes simple et composé sont séparés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut la dissolution naturelle comme mode de périssement d’une entité simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut que la simplicité puisse être produite ou détruite par assemblage et séparation de parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut les commencements et les fins graduels pour les entités dépourvues de parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut toute destruction naturelle dont le mécanisme interne resterait indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut la catégorie d’un commencement ou d’une fin identique pour les composés et les entités simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:DBN-01","text":"Le système ne reconnaît une explication naturelle du périssement qu’à condition qu’un mécanisme concevable soit spécifié.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:DBN-02","text":"Il disqualifie le modèle selon lequel une substance simple pourrait recevoir son être initial d’une composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:DBN-03","text":"Il disqualifie l’application d’un modèle unique de transition à toutes les entités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:DBN-04","text":"Il interdit de traiter création, annihilation et transformation composée comme des opérations ontologiquement continues.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSA-01","text":"L’absence la plus profonde est celle d’une démonstration positive de la conservation absolue : la permanence n’est établie que par exclusion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’un commencement ou d’une fin de l’entité simple qui ne relèverait ni de la composition ni d’un événement instantané.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSA-03","text":"Le système traite comme inadmissible l’assimilation de l’entité simple au devenir ordinaire des réalités composées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-01","text":"La simplicité devient, par interaction des unités, le principe commun qui interdit à la fois la genèse compositionnelle et la destruction par désagrégation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-01","CL_UCIC_02:GA-02","CL_UCIC_02:GA-03","CH_UCIC_PRO4:A1","CH_UCIC_PRO5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-02","text":"La distinction simple-composé ne classe pas seulement des structures ; elle distribue les opérations causales et les temporalités qui leur sont accessibles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-04","CL_UCIC_02:GA-05","CL_UCIC_02:GA-06","CH_UCIC_PRO6:A3","CH_UCIC_PRO6:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-03","text":"L’exclusion d’un mode particulier de destruction et l’exclusion du commencement naturel produisent ensemble une délimitation bilatérale du statut de l’entité simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:D3","CH_UCIC_PRO5:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-04","text":"La composition cesse d’être une simple description et devient le critère qui détermine le régime ontologique d’une entité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-03","CL_UCIC_02:GA-06","CH_UCIC_PRO5:ME1","CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-05","text":"L’introduction de la création et de l’annihilation excède les seules exclusions naturelles et laisse indéterminée la causalité externe qui les produit.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-05","CL_UCIC_02:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PRO5:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-01","text":"L’ontologie est organisée par les opérations qu’une structure rend admissibles, et non par une loi uniforme de génération et de corruption.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-02","text":"Le temps devient une propriété différentielle des régimes ontologiques : continuité partitive pour les composés, discontinuité aux limites pour les entités simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-03","text":"La validité de l’argument dépend d’un principe épistémique : une possibilité naturelle non spécifiable par mécanisme ne peut porter la conclusion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-04","text":"La survie de l’entité simple est une conséquence négative, bornée par l’impossibilité de spécifier son anéantissement naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-05","text":"La méthode transforme une réfutation locale en reclassification générale des catégories de commencement, de fin et de transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale répète l’absence de parties sous des fonctions successives : impossibilité de dissolution, impossibilité de genèse composée, puis distinction ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RLE-02","text":"L’escalade suit le trajet simplicité → exclusion de la composition → privation du mode de formation → impossibilité du commencement naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RLE-03","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est l’opposition entre deux régimes de transition, l’un partitif et l’autre instantané.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RLE-04","text":"La clôture récursive survient lorsque l’absence de médiation partitive appelle les seules opérations restantes : création et annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B01","text":"Une structure composée possède des parties ; les opérations de commencement et de fin peuvent donc être rapportées à leur modification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B02","text":"Une structure simple ne possède pas de parties ; toute transition partitive lui est donc retirée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B03","text":"Le retrait de la médiation partitive produit une temporalité discontinue aux deux limites de l’existence simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B04","text":"La différenciation des opérations produit une distinction ontologique entre entités simples et composées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B05","text":"La machine se ferme par négation : elle établit un régime d’existence sans fournir une cause positive de conservation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:AFM-B01","text":"Menace de dissolution → absence de parties → exclusion de la composition → impossibilité du commencement naturel → distinction entre transitions partitives et événements instantanés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:AF1","CH_UCIC_PRO5:AF1","CH_UCIC_PRO6:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:AFM-B02","text":"Négation d’un mécanisme uniforme → reclassification des commencements et des fins → séparation de deux temporalités ontologiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MME-01","text":"La dissolution est reclassée comme un processus applicable aux composés, non comme une possibilité générale de périssement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MME-02","text":"Le commencement et la fin cessent d’être des catégories uniformes et deviennent fonction du statut structurel de l’entité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MME-03","text":"La transformation par parties est cartographiée comme un régime régional, tandis que création et annihilation définissent ses limites extérieures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MME-04","text":"Une nouvelle méthode de lecture devient disponible : tester chaque possibilité naturelle par la concevabilité de son mécanisme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B01","text":"**Surface level** — Les problèmes explicites de dissolution et de commencement sont résolus par l’absence de parties et l’impossibilité de la composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B02","text":"**Structural level** — La dissolution est comprise comme désagrégation interne présupposant une composition ; la structure détermine donc les opérations accessibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B03","text":"**Metastrategic level** — L’argument neutralise les modèles concurrents en exigeant un mécanisme concevable plutôt qu’une affirmation directe de conservation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B04","text":"**Ontological / Temporal level** — La simplicité produit une temporalité discontinue à ses limites, tandis que la composition autorise des transitions partitives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B05","text":"**Methodological / Performative level** — La forme argumentative accomplit sa thèse en remplaçant progressivement les explications positives par des exclusions mécanistes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FL-01","text":"Le commencement naturel est identifié à une formation par composition, tandis que la création est ensuite posée comme seul commencement de l’entité simple ; la relation entre création et nature reste instable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:A3","CH_UCIC_PRO6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FL-02","text":"La structure affirme des événements instantanés tout en laissant sous-déterminée leur causalité externe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FL-03","text":"L’équivalence fonctionnelle entre monade et substance simple est requise par la dérivation, mais l’unité fournie n’en établit pas explicitement l’identité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MP-01","text":"La simplicité mute d’une description de structure en contrainte générale sur la genèse, la destruction et la temporalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MP-02","text":"La négation des processus de composition et de décomposition se transforme en soustraction de l’entité simple au modèle général de génération et de corruption.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MP-03","text":"La négation devient une opération classificatoire : les limites existentielles sont reclassées selon la simplicité ou la composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:HSI-01","text":"Le réel est implicitement une machine différentielle où chaque structure n’autorise que certaines opérations sur ses parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:HSI-02","text":"L’entité simple devient une borne ontologique : elle n’est ni un agrégat transformable ni un objet soumis au devenir composé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système est bifurqué entre une continuité partitive des composés et deux seuils instantanés pour les entités simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:HSI-04","text":"Les seules opérations compatibles avec la limite simple sont des événements externes de création et d’annihilation, dont l’agent reste indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B01","text":"Le noyau axiomatique suffit à reconstruire la distinction entre entités simples et composées ainsi que leurs régimes de transition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction reste indéterminée quant à la nature et à l’agent de la création et de l’annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B03","text":"La cohérence dépend de l’identification implicite entre absence de parties, simplicité et statut monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B04","text":"La fidélité au mouvement réel exige de conserver le passage de la négation locale à la classification de deux régimes temporels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B05","text":"La réduction ne peut pas décider si l’exclusion des mécanismes naturels implique une permanence absolue ou seulement l’absence de périssement naturel concevable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194710003835Z_ac2f0fa3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 04–06","source_sha256":"f616943414fd1fe33c491d9339d93630921339a8ae803fa0a5faf0012320d15d","sha256":"f563c6249543d65f29bc66c11ce0684fce7b318369368fd261859955f588a0c9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:47:10.005321+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-01","text":"The central problem is to determine how simplicity governs the conditions of an entity's beginning, end, and natural transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-02","text":"Simplicity is reframed as absence of parts, then as exclusion of compositional and decompositional operations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-03","text":"The contrast between simple and composite becomes a difference between two regimes of causality and temporality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-04","text":"The movement is cumulative: a local impossibility of dissolution extends to genesis, then to the ontological architecture of transitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BAS-05","text":"The conclusion does not provide a universal positive preservation, but a negative boundary between partitive transformations and instantaneous events.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A simple entity possesses no parts whose separation could constitute its dissolution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Dissolution and decomposition presuppose a composite structure liable to be disaggregated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The absence of composition precludes natural beginning when the latter is defined by composite formation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Composites begin and end through operations affecting their parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] For a simple entity, existential limits cannot be partitive and are referred to creation and annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] The distinction between simplicity and composition produces two incompatible temporal regimes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-07","text":"[Terminal] The creation and annihilation of the simple entity are instantaneous events rather than gradual processes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] No conceivable natural mechanism of genesis or destruction can be attributed to the simple entity as such.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:SD1","CH_UCIC_PRO4:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-01","text":"The absence of parts retains its negative function across the units: it first excludes dissolution, then composition, and finally partitive transition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-02","text":"Simplicity mutates from a property of composition into a constraint on genesis and on the entity's temporal limits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-03","text":"The negation of dissolution is reversed into a positive determination of the monadic regime through instantaneous creation and annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-04","text":"The question of perishing is absorbed into an ontology of admissible operations on parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RMD-05","text":"The claim to absolute preservation disappears in favor of a conclusion limited to conceivable natural mechanisms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-01","text":"The non-dissolution of a simple substance remains a local proposition; at the current level, it becomes a case of a general exclusion of partitive transitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-02","text":"The absence of parts changes scale when it becomes a principle for mapping the possible modes of destruction and generation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-03","text":"The units connect when they make beginning and end depend on the same structural criterion: simplicity or composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-04","text":"The major transition consists in converting the impossibility of partitive mediation into instantaneous creation and annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:CGD-05","text":"The uniform model of generation and corruption becomes obsolete once the simple and composite regimes are separated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes natural dissolution as a mode of perishing for a simple entity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that simplicity could be produced or destroyed by the assembly and separation of parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-03","text":"It excludes gradual beginnings and ends for entities devoid of parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-04","text":"It excludes every natural destruction whose internal mechanism would remain indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the category of a beginning or an end identical for composites and simple entities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:DBN-01","text":"The system recognizes a natural explanation of perishing only on condition that a conceivable mechanism is specified.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:DBN-02","text":"It disqualifies the model according to which a simple substance could receive its initial being from a composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:DBN-03","text":"It disqualifies the application of a single model of transition to all entities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:DBN-04","text":"It prohibits treating creation, annihilation, and composite transformation as ontologically continuous operations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSA-01","text":"The deepest absence is that of a positive demonstration of absolute preservation: permanence is established only through exclusion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSA-02","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of a beginning or an end of the simple entity that would pertain neither to composition nor to an instantaneous event.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSA-03","text":"The system treats as inadmissible the assimilation of the simple entity to the ordinary becoming of composite realities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-01","text":"Through the interaction of the units, simplicity becomes the common principle that precludes both compositional genesis and destruction by disaggregation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-01","CL_UCIC_02:GA-02","CL_UCIC_02:GA-03","CH_UCIC_PRO4:A1","CH_UCIC_PRO5:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-02","text":"The simple-composite distinction does not merely classify structures; it distributes the causal operations and temporalities accessible to them.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-04","CL_UCIC_02:GA-05","CL_UCIC_02:GA-06","CH_UCIC_PRO6:A3","CH_UCIC_PRO6:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-03","text":"The exclusion of a particular mode of destruction and the exclusion of natural beginning together produce a bilateral delimitation of the status of the simple entity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:D3","CH_UCIC_PRO5:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-04","text":"Composition ceases to be a mere description and becomes the criterion determining an entity's ontological regime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-03","CL_UCIC_02:GA-06","CH_UCIC_PRO5:ME1","CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:XD-05","text":"The introduction of creation and annihilation exceeds natural exclusions alone and leaves indeterminate the external causality that produces them.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-05","CL_UCIC_02:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PRO5:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-01","text":"Ontology is organized by the operations that a structure renders admissible, rather than by a uniform law of generation and corruption.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-02","text":"Time becomes a differential property of ontological regimes: partitive continuity for composites, discontinuity at the limits for simple entities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-03","text":"The validity of the argument depends on an epistemic principle: a natural possibility not specifiable by a mechanism cannot support the conclusion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-04","text":"The survival of the simple entity is a negative consequence, bounded by the impossibility of specifying its natural annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:BSD-05","text":"The method transforms a local refutation into a general reclassification of the categories of beginning, end, and transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop repeats the absence of parts under successive functions: impossibility of dissolution, impossibility of composite genesis, then ontological distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RLE-02","text":"The escalation follows the path simplicity → exclusion of composition → deprivation of the mode of formation → impossibility of natural beginning.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RLE-03","text":"The conceptual attractor is the opposition between two regimes of transition, one partitive and the other instantaneous.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:RLE-04","text":"Recursive closure occurs when the absence of partitive mediation calls for the only remaining operations: creation and annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B01","text":"A composite structure possesses parts; the operations of beginning and end can therefore be referred to their modification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B02","text":"A simple structure possesses no parts; every partitive transition is therefore withdrawn from it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B03","text":"The withdrawal of partitive mediation produces a discontinuous temporality at the two limits of simple existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B04","text":"The differentiation of operations produces an ontological distinction between simple and composite entities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B05","text":"The machine closes through negation: it establishes a regime of existence without providing a positive cause of preservation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:AFM-B01","text":"Threat of dissolution → absence of parts → exclusion of composition → impossibility of natural beginning → distinction between partitive transitions and instantaneous events.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:AF1","CH_UCIC_PRO5:AF1","CH_UCIC_PRO6:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:AFM-B02","text":"Negation of a uniform mechanism → reclassification of beginnings and ends → separation of two ontological temporalities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MME-01","text":"Dissolution is reclassified as a process applicable to composites, not as a general possibility of perishing.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MME-02","text":"Beginning and end cease to be uniform categories and become functions of the entity's structural status.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MME-03","text":"Transformation through parts is mapped as a regional regime, while creation and annihilation define its outer limits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MME-04","text":"A new method of reading becomes available: testing every natural possibility by the conceivability of its mechanism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B01","text":"**Surface level** — The explicit problems of dissolution and beginning are resolved by the absence of parts and the impossibility of composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B02","text":"**Structural level** — Dissolution is understood as internal disaggregation presupposing composition; structure therefore determines the accessible operations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B03","text":"**Metastrategic level** — The argument neutralizes competing models by requiring a conceivable mechanism rather than a direct assertion of preservation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B04","text":"**Ontological / Temporal level** — Simplicity produces a discontinuous temporality at its limits, whereas composition permits partitive transitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:ALT-B05","text":"**Methodological / Performative level** — The argumentative form accomplishes its thesis by progressively replacing positive explanations with mechanistic exclusions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FL-01","text":"Natural beginning is identified with formation through composition, while creation is subsequently posited as the sole beginning of the simple entity; the relation between creation and nature remains unstable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:A3","CH_UCIC_PRO6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FL-02","text":"The structure asserts instantaneous events while leaving their external causality underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:FL-03","text":"The functional equivalence between monad and simple substance is required by the derivation, but the supplied unit does not explicitly establish their identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MP-01","text":"Simplicity mutates from a description of structure into a general constraint on genesis, destruction, and temporality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MP-02","text":"The negation of the processes of composition and decomposition is transformed into the subtraction of the simple entity from the general model of generation and corruption.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MP-03","text":"Negation becomes a classificatory operation: existential limits are reclassified according to simplicity or composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a differential machine in which each structure permits only certain operations on its parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:HSI-02","text":"The simple entity becomes an ontological bound: it is neither a transformable aggregate nor an object subject to composite becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:HSI-03","text":"The system's time bifurcates between a partitive continuity of composites and two instantaneous thresholds for simple entities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:HSI-04","text":"The only operations compatible with the simple limit are external events of creation and annihilation, whose agent remains indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B01","text":"The axiomatic core suffices to reconstruct the distinction between simple and composite entities, as well as their regimes of transition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction remains indeterminate as to the nature and agent of creation and annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B03","text":"Coherence depends on the implicit identification between absence of parts, simplicity, and monadic status.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B04","text":"Fidelity to the actual movement requires retaining the passage from local negation to the classification of two temporal regimes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO6:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_02:MRT-B05","text":"The reduction cannot determine whether the exclusion of natural mechanisms implies absolute permanence or merely the absence of conceivable natural perishing.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO5:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_02:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 04–06","context":"Proposition 4 · Proposition 5 · Proposition 6"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 07–09","order":3,"parents":["CH_UCIC_PRO7","CH_UCIC_PRO8","CH_UCIC_PRO9"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_03@R001","sha256":"0a15d8dae044588d8608789f5dfd7d52b47a8ef926cd56c4472b08254b3db1f6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-01","text":"Le problème central est de déterminer comment une pluralité de Monades peut être à la fois ontologiquement fermée, qualitativement différenciée et capable de produire un changement discernable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-02","text":"Le système recadre la causalité : une Monade ne reçoit rien de l’extérieur, tandis que la différence et le changement doivent être fondés dans ses déterminations propres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-03","text":"La distinction entre composés et substances simples déplace le régime du changement des relations entre parties vers les différences internes entre unités simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-04","text":"La qualité devient le principe conjoint de l’être, de la distinction individuelle et de la discernabilité des états composés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-05","text":"L’interaction des trois unités transforme l’absence d’ouverture en condition d’une différenciation interne plutôt qu’en simple négation de l’influence extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:AS3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-06","text":"La pluralité naturelle ne peut donc être une répétition d’unités interchangeables : chaque Monade doit porter une différence constitutive qui interdit la duplication parfaite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:AS3","CH_UCIC_PRO9:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-07","text":"Le mouvement argumental est cumulatif et mutationnel : fermeture négative, différenciation qualitative, individuation intrinsèque, puis reconstruction d’un ordre où le changement ne provient pas d’un transfert.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Une Monade ne peut être directement altérée par une autre créature ni recevoir une entité venue de l’extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La Monade est dépourvue de fenêtres, de parties transférables et d’accidents autonomes susceptibles de circuler.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Une Monade doit posséder des qualités, faute de quoi elle ne serait ni un être discernable ni une unité différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Les composés ne contiennent que ce qui provient de leurs ingrédients simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Le changement, d’abord distingué des relations entre parties, est ensuite rapporté aux différences qualitatives internes des substances simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] L’opposition intérieur/extérieur cesse de désigner seulement une limite d’accès et devient une distinction entre fondement intrinsèque et dénomination extrinsèque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La discernabilité du devenir exige une pluralité qualitative réelle au niveau des unités simples, et non une simple permutation de positions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] La pluralité naturelle implique que chaque Monade soit intrinsèquement différente de toute autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Sont exclues à la fois l’altération externe directe et la duplication parfaite d’un être naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] La différenciation interne constitue l’attracteur qui unifie fermeture ontologique, qualité monadique, discernabilité du changement et individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-01","text":"La fermeture monadique revient d’abord comme impossibilité de pénétration, puis comme condition positive d’une détermination qui ne peut être importée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-02","text":"L’absence de transfert conserve son identité apophatique, mais sa fonction se déplace : elle ne suffit plus à définir la Monade et doit être complétée par une différenciation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PRO8:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-03","text":"La notion de partie est limitée aux composés ; elle est remplacée, au niveau simple, par celle de qualité ou de détermination interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:A4","CH_UCIC_PRO8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-04","text":"La qualité migre du statut de propriété requise vers celui de principe ontologique assurant simultanément être, différence et devenir discernable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-05","text":"Le mouvement est recodé : il ne vaut plus comme transport suffisant, mais comme changement seulement intelligible lorsqu’une différence qualitative réelle existe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-06","text":"L’individualité se déplace d’une distinction numérique ou positionnelle vers une détermination intrinsèque non substituable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-07","text":"Les accidents circulants et la duplication parfaite sont absorbés dans une exclusion plus vaste : aucune différence réelle ne peut être purement externe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:NX4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-01","text":"La prohibition locale de l’intrusion extérieure reste une thèse propre à la clôture monadique ; au niveau du cluster, elle devient une condition de la théorie générale de l’individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-02","text":"L’argument local sur les qualités ne vaut pas seulement pour la constitution des Monades : il relie la différence interne à la possibilité de discerner le changement dans les composés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-03","text":"L’interdiction de deux êtres parfaitement semblables catalyse le passage d’une ontologie fermée à une ontologie structurée par des différences intrinsèques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-04","text":"La distinction entre monade et composé est locale lorsqu’elle oppose absence de parties et relations entre parties ; elle change d’échelle lorsqu’elle organise deux régimes généraux du changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-05","text":"La circulation autonome des accidents devient secondaire au niveau courant : son travail est absorbé par l’exclusion générale de toute différence produite uniquement de l’extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-06","text":"Ce qui émerge entre les unités est une structure absente de chacune prise isolément : la fermeture ne supprime pas la différenciation, elle en détermine le lieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME2","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-01","text":"Le système rejette toute conception de la causalité comme pénétration d’un agent extérieur dans l’intériorité d’une unité simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut l’intériorité conçue comme assemblage, réceptacle ou circulation de parties et d’accidents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PRO7:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-03","text":"Il refuse une nature composée d’unités sans qualité, indifférenciées et néanmoins capables de produire des états discernables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que la position, la quantité, la nomination extérieure ou la substitution spatiale suffisent à fonder l’individualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-05","text":"L’apophatisme converge vers un seul rejet : aucune différence réelle ne peut être entièrement extrinsèque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’hypothèse d’un monde où le changement serait une simple permutation d’éléments indiscernables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également disqualifier l’idée que le composé puisse produire une différence absente de ses ingrédients simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:DBN-03","text":"Le système exclut silencieusement un modèle relationnel dans lequel l’identité des êtres serait constituée après coup par leurs positions ou leurs rapports externes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:DBN-04","text":"L’architecture négative interdit donc simultanément la pénétrabilité de l’unité, l’indifférenciation de ses qualités et l’extrinsécité de son individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PRO8:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité indisponible qui donne sa force au système est celle d’une pluralité obtenue par duplication exacte d’une même unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSA-02","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un intérieur sans détermination propre : un tel intérieur serait à la fois indiscernable, substituable et incapable de fonder un changement réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSA-03","text":"Est ontologiquement inadmissible un monde où l’ouverture à l’extérieur, la position ou la nomination suffiraient à produire l’individualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:DNX4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-01","text":"La fermeture de la Monade n’est pas un déficit de relation : elle impose que toute différence pertinente soit recherchée dans sa détermination propre.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-01","CL_UCIC_03:GA-02","CH_UCIC_PRO7:D4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-02","text":"La qualité devient le relais structurel entre l’unité simple fermée et la pluralité composée discernable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-03","CL_UCIC_03:GA-04","CL_UCIC_03:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-03","text":"L’absence de transfert extérieur et l’exigence de qualités différenciées convergent vers une théorie du changement sans importation ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-01","CL_UCIC_03:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PRO7:NX3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-04","text":"La différence individuelle et la discernabilité du changement sont deux effets d’une même exigence : les unités simples doivent être réellement déterminées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-03","CL_UCIC_03:GA-08","CL_UCIC_03:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-05","text":"Le composé ne constitue pas le lieu originaire de la différence ; il en distribue les effets à partir de ses ingrédients simples.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-04","CL_UCIC_03:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME4","CH_UCIC_PRO8:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-06","text":"La clôture et la différenciation produisent une inversion du modèle causal : ce qui apparaît comme changement relationnel au composé doit être fondé dans la pluralité qualitative des simples.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-05","CL_UCIC_03:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme multiplicité d’unités closes dont les états sont différenciés sans être constitués par une pénétration extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-02","text":"La causalité directe entre substances est remplacée par une architecture où l’ordre du changement dépend de déterminations internes et de leur composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-03","text":"Le temps devient intelligible non comme succession de permutations, mais comme série d’états différenciables parce que les unités qui les composent ne sont pas indifférentes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-04","text":"Le sujet monadique n’est pas un réceptacle ouvert aux influences ; il est une unité déterminée dont la différence précède toute comparaison extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-05","text":"La pluralité cesse d’être une collection de positions et devient un ordre de différences intrinsèques non substituables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-06","text":"La méthode du système consiste à établir positivement une structure par accumulation d’exclusions : ce qui ne peut entrer, circuler ou se répéter révèle le lieu de la détermination réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-01","text":"Le système boucle de la fermeture vers la différenciation : l’absence d’échange extérieur renvoie à la nécessité d’une détermination interne, laquelle rend la fermeture conceptuellement productive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS5","CH_UCIC_PRO8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-02","text":"Une seconde boucle relie qualité et changement : la qualité rend les Monades discernables, puis la discernabilité du changement confirme la nécessité de la qualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:AF1","CH_UCIC_PRO8:AF6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-03","text":"Une troisième boucle relie pluralité et individuation : plusieurs êtres exigent des différences réelles, et ces différences transforment la pluralité en ordre intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-04","text":"L’escalade va de l’impossibilité locale d’une intrusion à l’impossibilité globale d’un monde d’unités parfaitement substituables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD3","CH_UCIC_PRO9:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est la détermination intrinsèque : chaque ligne négative y converge, tandis que chaque ligne positive en déploie une fonction nouvelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:D3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B01","text":"Unité simple sans parties → impossibilité du transfert interne ou de l’intrusion extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B02","text":"Absence de transfert → nécessité de chercher le principe du changement dans les déterminations propres de l’unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B03","text":"Suppression des qualités → indistinguabilité des Monades → impossibilité de discerner les états composés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PRO8:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B04","text":"Impossibilité de la parfaite ressemblance → exigence d’une différence interne ou intrinsèque pour chaque être.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PRO9:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B05","text":"Différence interne + composition à partir des simples → discernabilité du changement sans importation d’entités extérieures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:AS4","CH_UCIC_PRO8:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B06","text":"Fermeture ontologique + différenciation qualitative + individuation intrinsèque → pluralité réelle d’unités closes et non substituables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS5","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:AFM-B01","text":"Altération externe problématique → exclusion du transfert → fermeture ontologique → nécessité de qualités internes → discernabilité du changement → exclusion de l’indifférenciation → individuation intrinsèque → pluralité non substituable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:AF1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-01","text":"La frontière de la Monade devient une limite ontologique, tandis que sa différence interne devient le principe positif de son individualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME2","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-02","text":"L’opposition entre intérieur et extérieur est redessinée : l’extérieur ne pénètre pas l’unité, mais la pluralité des unités rend possible un ordre de différences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:ME2","CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-03","text":"La différence entre mouvement et permutation devient une distinction centrale : seul un changement porté par des qualités différenciées est discernable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-04","text":"La fausse opposition entre unité simple et devenir s’effondre : la fermeture n’abolit pas le changement, elle exclut seulement son explication par transfert.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PRO7:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-05","text":"La carte stratégique de l’explication passe d’une recherche d’agents transmetteurs à une analyse des régimes de détermination interne et de composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B01","text":"**Surface level** — Sont visés l’altération d’une Monade, la discernabilité du changement et la possibilité de deux êtres parfaitement semblables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B02","text":"**Structural level** — Le système articule absence de parties, absence d’ouvertures, qualités monadiques, composition et différences intrinsèques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B03","text":"**Metastrategic level** — L’argument remplace les modèles d’influence, de permutation et de désignation extérieure par une architecture de clôture et de détermination interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PRO9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B04","text":"**Ontological / Temporal level** — Le réel est pensé comme une pluralité qualitative dont les états successifs restent discernables sans être produits par importation extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B05","text":"**Methodological / Performative level** — Le système accomplit sa thèse par négations successives : il établit positivement la détermination interne en éliminant les modèles de pénétration, d’indifférenciation et de répétition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FL-01","text":"La clôture interdit l’altération externe, mais les unités fournies ne déterminent pas positivement le mécanisme interne du changement ; la fermeture est donc plus établie que sa dynamique propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PRO8:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FL-02","text":"La qualité fonde la discernabilité et l’individuation, mais sa nature positive reste indéterminée ; le concept porte plus de fonctions qu’il ne reçoit de contenu explicite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PRO9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FL-03","text":"La différence interne et la dénomination intrinsèque sont rapprochées sans être entièrement identifiées, ce qui laisse une tension entre fondement ontologique et description logique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FL-04","text":"Le système affirme une fermeture des Monades tout en rapportant leurs états à des composés ; il doit donc distinguer soigneusement dépendance de composition et influence causale directe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:A3","CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MP-01","text":"Le concept de changement mute lorsqu’il passe des relations entre parties à la différenciation qualitative des substances simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MP-02","text":"Le concept de frontière mute d’une limite spatiale à une limite ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MP-03","text":"Le concept d’individualité mute d’une différence de position ou de nombre à une détermination intrinsèque non substituable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MP-04","text":"La contradiction productive oppose la fermeture causale de la Monade à la nécessité d’expliquer une succession d’états ; elle force le déplacement vers la différenciation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une architecture de chambres ontologiquement closes, différenciées de l’intérieur et composées sans transfert direct entre leurs unités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une unité non pénétrable mais qualitativement déterminée, dont l’identité ne dépend ni d’une position ni d’une duplication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:D2","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est une série de différences discernables, non une permutation de contenus équivalents ; la lutte conceptuelle porte contre l’indifférenciation, la pénétration et la substituabilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:AF5","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre axiomes : fermeture de la Monade, qualités internes, composition à partir des simples et différence intrinsèque de chaque unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PRO8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B02","text":"Ces axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement d’ensemble : impossibilité du transfert, déplacement du changement vers la qualité, puis exclusion de la duplication parfaite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT6","CH_UCIC_PRO9:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B03","text":"La compression reste fidèle parce qu’elle conserve la mutation fonctionnelle de la fermeture, de la qualité et de la différence, au lieu de les traiter comme des répétitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne surtout le mécanisme positif du changement interne et le rapport exact entre différence interne et dénomination intrinsèque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PRO9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B05","text":"La cohérence du cluster dépend de la distinction entre influence causale directe, composition des simples et discernabilité des états ; sans cette distinction, fermeture et devenir paraissent incompatibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT2","CH_UCIC_PRO8:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B06","text":"La structure minimale suffisante est donc : unité close → détermination qualitative → pluralité intrinsèquement différenciée → changement discernable sans transfert externe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194743441238Z_cd778390","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 07–09","source_sha256":"0a15d8dae044588d8608789f5dfd7d52b47a8ef926cd56c4472b08254b3db1f6","sha256":"3b5773f611b9f0ef338a07045a7bc6a3440b94ec8fa3df570cfd8c64ed92f216","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:47:43.442615+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-01","text":"The central problem is to determine how a plurality of Monads can be both ontologically closed, qualitatively differentiated, and capable of producing discernible change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-02","text":"The system reframes causality: a Monad receives nothing from outside, while difference and change must be grounded in its own determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-03","text":"The distinction between composites and simple substances shifts the regime of change from relations between parts to internal differences between simple units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-04","text":"Quality becomes the joint principle of being, individual distinction, and the discernibility of composite states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-05","text":"The interaction of the three units transforms the absence of openness into a condition of internal differentiation rather than a mere negation of external influence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:AS3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-06","text":"Natural plurality therefore cannot be a repetition of interchangeable units: each Monad must bear a constitutive difference that precludes perfect duplication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:AS3","CH_UCIC_PRO9:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BAS-07","text":"The argumentative movement is cumulative and mutational: negative closure, qualitative differentiation, intrinsic individuation, then reconstruction of an order in which change does not arise from a transfer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A Monad cannot be directly altered by another creature or receive an entity coming from outside.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The Monad is devoid of windows, transferable parts, and autonomous accidents liable to circulate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] A Monad must possess qualities, failing which it would be neither a discernible being nor a differentiated unit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Composites contain only what comes from their simple ingredients.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Change, initially distinguished from relations between parts, is subsequently referred to the internal qualitative differences of simple substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] The interior/exterior opposition ceases to designate merely a limit of access and becomes a distinction between intrinsic ground and extrinsic denomination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The discernibility of becoming requires a real qualitative plurality at the level of simple units, and not a mere permutation of positions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Natural plurality entails that each Monad is intrinsically different from every other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Both direct external alteration and the perfect duplication of a natural being are excluded.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Internal differentiation constitutes the attractor that unifies ontological closure, monadic quality, the discernibility of change, and individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-01","text":"Monadic closure first recurs as the impossibility of penetration, then as the positive condition of a determination that cannot be imported.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-02","text":"The absence of transfer retains its apophatic identity, but its function shifts: it no longer suffices to define the Monad and must be supplemented by internal differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PRO8:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-03","text":"The notion of part is restricted to composites; at the simple level, it is replaced by that of quality or internal determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:A4","CH_UCIC_PRO8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-04","text":"Quality migrates from the status of a required property to that of an ontological principle simultaneously ensuring being, difference, and discernible becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-05","text":"Motion is recoded: it no longer counts as sufficient transport, but as change intelligible only when a real qualitative difference exists.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-06","text":"Individuality shifts from a numerical or positional distinction to a non-substitutable intrinsic determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RMD-07","text":"Circulating accidents and perfect duplication are absorbed into a broader exclusion: no real difference can be purely external.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:NX4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-01","text":"The local prohibition of external intrusion remains a thesis proper to monadic closure; at the cluster level, it becomes a condition of the general theory of individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-02","text":"The local argument concerning qualities applies not only to the constitution of Monads: it connects internal difference to the possibility of discerning change in composites.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-03","text":"The prohibition of two perfectly similar beings catalyzes the passage from a closed ontology to an ontology structured by intrinsic differences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-04","text":"The distinction between monad and composite is local when it opposes absence of parts to relations between parts; it changes scale when it organizes two general regimes of change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-05","text":"The autonomous circulation of accidents becomes secondary at the current level: its work is absorbed by the general exclusion of any difference produced solely from outside.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:CGD-06","text":"What emerges between the units is a structure absent from each taken in isolation: closure does not suppress differentiation; it determines its locus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME2","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects every conception of causality as the penetration of an external agent into the interiority of a simple unit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-02","text":"It excludes interiority conceived as an assemblage, receptacle, or circulation of parts and accidents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PRO7:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-03","text":"It rejects a nature composed of quality-less, undifferentiated units that are nonetheless capable of producing discernible states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that position, quantity, external denomination, or spatial substitution suffice to ground individuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:GNX-05","text":"Apophaticism converges upon a single rejection: no real difference can be entirely extrinsic.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the hypothesis of a world in which change would be a mere permutation of indiscernible elements must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:DBN-02","text":"The idea that the composite could produce a difference absent from its simple ingredients must likewise be disqualified.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:DBN-03","text":"The system silently excludes a relational model in which the identity of beings would be constituted after the fact by their positions or external relations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:DBN-04","text":"The negative architecture therefore simultaneously prohibits the penetrability of the unit, the indifferentiation of its qualities, and the extrinsicality of its individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PRO8:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSA-01","text":"The unavailable possibility that gives the system its force is that of a plurality obtained through the exact duplication of one and the same unit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSA-02","text":"The structuring absence is that of an interior without its own determination: such an interior would be at once indiscernible, substitutable, and incapable of grounding real change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSA-03","text":"Ontologically inadmissible is a world in which openness to the exterior, position, or denomination would suffice to produce individuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:DNX4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-01","text":"The closure of the Monad is not a deficit of relation: it requires that every relevant difference be sought in its own determination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-01","CL_UCIC_03:GA-02","CH_UCIC_PRO7:D4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-02","text":"Quality becomes the structural relay between the closed simple unit and discernible composite plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-03","CL_UCIC_03:GA-04","CL_UCIC_03:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-03","text":"The absence of external transfer and the requirement of differentiated qualities converge toward a theory of change without ontological importation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-01","CL_UCIC_03:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PRO7:NX3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-04","text":"Individual difference and the discernibility of change are two effects of the same requirement: simple units must be really determined.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-03","CL_UCIC_03:GA-08","CL_UCIC_03:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-05","text":"The composite does not constitute the original locus of difference; it distributes its effects on the basis of its simple ingredients.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-04","CL_UCIC_03:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME4","CH_UCIC_PRO8:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:XD-06","text":"Closure and differentiation produce an inversion of the causal model: what appears as relational change in the composite must be grounded in the qualitative plurality of simples.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-05","CL_UCIC_03:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-01","text":"The real is reclassified as a multiplicity of closed units whose states are differentiated without being constituted by external penetration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-02","text":"Direct causality between substances is replaced by an architecture in which the order of change depends on internal determinations and their composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-03","text":"Time becomes intelligible not as a succession of permutations, but as a series of differentiable states because the units composing them are not indifferent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-04","text":"The monadic subject is not a receptacle open to influences; it is a determined unit whose difference precedes every external comparison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-05","text":"Plurality ceases to be a collection of positions and becomes an order of non-substitutable intrinsic differences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:BSD-06","text":"The method of the system consists in positively establishing a structure through an accumulation of exclusions: what cannot enter, circulate, or be repeated reveals the locus of real determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-01","text":"The system loops from closure to differentiation: the absence of external exchange refers back to the necessity of an internal determination, which renders closure conceptually productive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS5","CH_UCIC_PRO8:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-02","text":"A second loop connects quality and change: quality renders Monads discernible, then the discernibility of change confirms the necessity of quality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:AF1","CH_UCIC_PRO8:AF6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-03","text":"A third loop connects plurality and individuation: several beings require real differences, and these differences transform plurality into an intelligible order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-04","text":"The escalation proceeds from the local impossibility of an intrusion to the global impossibility of a world of perfectly substitutable units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD3","CH_UCIC_PRO9:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is intrinsic determination: every negative line converges upon it, while every positive line unfolds a new function of it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:D3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B01","text":"Simple unit without parts → impossibility of internal transfer or external intrusion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B02","text":"Absence of transfer → necessity of seeking the principle of change in the unit's own determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B03","text":"Removal of qualities → indistinguishability of Monads → impossibility of discerning composite states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PRO8:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B04","text":"Impossibility of perfect resemblance → requirement of an internal or intrinsic difference for each being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PRO9:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B05","text":"Internal difference + composition from simples → discernibility of change without importation of external entities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:AS4","CH_UCIC_PRO8:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B06","text":"Ontological closure + qualitative differentiation + intrinsic individuation → real plurality of closed and non-substitutable units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS5","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:AFM-B01","text":"Problematic external alteration → exclusion of transfer → ontological closure → necessity of internal qualities → discernibility of change → exclusion of indifferentiation → intrinsic individuation → non-substitutable plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:AF1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-01","text":"The boundary of the Monad becomes an ontological limit, while its internal difference becomes the positive principle of its individuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME2","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-02","text":"The opposition between interior and exterior is redrawn: the exterior does not penetrate the unit, but the plurality of units makes possible an order of differences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:ME2","CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-03","text":"The difference between motion and permutation becomes a central distinction: only change borne by differentiated qualities is discernible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-04","text":"The false opposition between simple unity and becoming collapses: closure does not abolish change; it merely excludes its explanation through transfer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PRO7:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MME-05","text":"The strategic map of explanation shifts from a search for transmitting agents to an analysis of regimes of internal determination and composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B01","text":"**Surface level** — The alteration of a Monad, the discernibility of change, and the possibility of two perfectly similar beings are at issue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B02","text":"**Structural level** — The system articulates absence of parts, absence of openings, monadic qualities, composition, and intrinsic differences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B03","text":"**Metastrategic level** — The argument replaces models of influence, permutation, and external designation with an architecture of closure and internal determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PRO9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B04","text":"**Ontological / Temporal level** — The real is conceived as a qualitative plurality whose successive states remain discernible without being produced by external importation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B05","text":"**Methodological / Performative level** — The system accomplishes its thesis through successive negations: it positively establishes internal determination by eliminating models of penetration, indifferentiation, and repetition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME4","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FL-01","text":"Closure prohibits external alteration, but the units provided do not positively determine the internal mechanism of change; closure is therefore more established than its proper dynamics.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PRO8:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FL-02","text":"Quality grounds discernibility and individuation, but its positive nature remains undetermined; the concept bears more functions than it receives explicit content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PRO9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FL-03","text":"Internal difference and intrinsic denomination are brought together without being fully identified, leaving a tension between ontological ground and logical description.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:FL-04","text":"The system affirms the closure of Monads while relating their states to composites; it must therefore carefully distinguish compositional dependence from direct causal influence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:A3","CH_UCIC_PRO7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MP-01","text":"The concept of change mutates when it passes from relations between parts to the qualitative differentiation of simple substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MP-02","text":"The concept of boundary mutates from a spatial limit into an ontological limit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MP-03","text":"The concept of individuality mutates from a difference of position or number into a non-substitutable intrinsic determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MP-04","text":"The productive contradiction opposes the causal closure of the Monad to the necessity of explaining a succession of states; it forces the shift toward internal differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PRO7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is an architecture of ontologically closed chambers, internally differentiated and composed without direct transfer between their units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes an impenetrable but qualitatively determined unit, whose identity depends neither on a position nor on a duplication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO9:D2","CH_UCIC_PRO9:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:HSI-03","text":"Time is a series of discernible differences, not a permutation of equivalent contents; the conceptual struggle is against indifferentiation, penetration, and substitutability.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:AF5","CH_UCIC_PRO8:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four axioms: closure of the Monad, internal qualities, composition from simples, and the intrinsic difference of each unit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PRO8:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B02","text":"These axioms suffice to reconstruct the overall movement: impossibility of transfer, displacement of change toward quality, then exclusion of perfect duplication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT6","CH_UCIC_PRO9:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B03","text":"The compression remains faithful because it preserves the functional mutation of closure, quality, and difference, rather than treating them as repetitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO8:ME1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B04","text":"The remaining indeterminacy chiefly concerns the positive mechanism of internal change and the exact relation between internal difference and intrinsic denomination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PRO9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B05","text":"The coherence of the cluster depends on the distinction between direct causal influence, composition of simples, and the discernibility of states; without this distinction, closure and becoming appear incompatible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:MRT2","CH_UCIC_PRO8:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B06","text":"The minimally sufficient structure is therefore: closed unit → qualitative determination → intrinsically differentiated plurality → discernible change without external transfer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PRO7:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PRO9:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_03@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_03:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 07–09","context":"Proposition 7 · Proposition 8 · Proposition 9"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 10–12","order":4,"parents":["CH_UCIC_PR_2","CH_UCIC_PR_3","CH_UCIC_PR_4"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_04@R001","sha256":"e0e0424f73f874e33755a55a19bd21dc1f39c89a60817267460046b64df115f9","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-01","text":"Le problème consiste à expliquer comment une monade créée peut être continuellement changeante tout en demeurant causalement fermée à l’extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-02","text":"Le système recadre la mutabilité comme condition universelle de l’ordre créé plutôt que comme propriété exceptionnelle de certaines substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-03","text":"La clôture de l’intériorité exclut la causalité externe et déplace l’explication du changement vers un principe immanent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-04","text":"L’intériorité ne suffit toutefois pas comme principe abstrait : elle doit comporter un détail déterminé de ce qui change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-05","text":"La pluralité des substances simples est ainsi produite par la différenciation interne d’un même régime général du changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-06","text":"Le mouvement argumentatif va de la mutabilité universelle à l’autonomie causale, puis de l’autonomie à la spécification différentielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-07","text":"L’architecture est cumulative et récursive : chaque exclusion rend nécessaire une détermination plus précise du principe conservé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-08","text":"La clôture produite n’est pas l’immobilité, mais une pluralité de processus internes continuellement différenciés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Tout être créé est sujet au changement, et aucune monade créée n’est exemptée de cette condition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Le changement dans l’ordre créé n’est pas ponctuel : il affecte continuellement chaque être créé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Les changements naturels d’une monade requièrent un principe déterminant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Une cause externe ne peut pas influer dans l’intériorité de la monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] La mutabilité passe d’une propriété générale de l’être créé à une production interne du changement naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Le principe général du changement ne suffit pas à déterminer une substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Toute substance simple reçoit sa détermination d’un détail propre de ce qui change en elle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] La pluralité qualitative des substances simples résulte de la différenciation interne du changement, non d’une causalité extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Le système converge vers la figure d’une unité dynamique, causalement close et qualitativement différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] L’identité substantielle ne peut être reconduite à un état fixe ou à une simplicité dépourvue de contenu interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] L’unité du principe et la pluralité des substances ne s’excluent qu’à condition de séparer principe et détermination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-01","text":"La mutabilité revient avec une identité stable comme condition de tout être créé, mais sa fonction se déplace ensuite vers la définition interne de la monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-02","text":"Le changement récurrent passe d’un statut ontologique général à une fonction causale : il devient l’effet d’un principe interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-03","text":"L’intériorité conserve son rôle de lieu du changement, mais mute d’espace fermé en structure productrice de déterminations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-04","text":"Le principe du changement persiste comme invariant, tandis que son insuffisance entraîne l’introduction d’un détail différentiel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-05","text":"La simplicité est inversée : elle ne signifie plus absence de contenu, mais concentration d’une détermination qualitative dans une unité non composée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-06","text":"La diversité ne provient plus d’une différence de principe, mais de variations dans la détermination de ce qui change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-07","text":"La causalité externe disparaît comme explication directe après avoir accompli un travail de délimitation, mais son exclusion rend nécessaire la causalité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-08","text":"La récurrence du changement cesse d’être redondante lorsqu’elle devient le mécanisme qui relie universalité, autonomie et individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-01","text":"[Local] L’inclusion de la Monade dans la classe des êtres créés établit une conséquence locale : elle est soumise à la mutabilité générale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-02","text":"[Local] L’impossibilité d’une influence externe établit localement la clôture causale de chaque monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-03","text":"[Scale-shift] L’interaction des deux machines transforme la clôture causale en principe général d’explication de la dynamique créée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-04","text":"[Cross-unit] La nécessité d’un détail différentiel relie la dynamique interne à la pluralité des substances simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-05","text":"[Catalytic] L’insuffisance du principe général catalyse le passage d’une ontologie du changement à une théorie de l’individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-06","text":"[Recoded] La différence entre intérieur et extérieur n’est plus seulement spatiale ou relationnelle : elle devient la différence entre principe effectif et cause impossible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-07","text":"[Obsolète] Un modèle où la pluralité résulterait d’actions externes ou d’un principe abstrait indifférencié est dépassé par la structure interne du changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut l’immutabilité comme caractéristique générale d’un être créé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut que la création constitue une exemption à la mutabilité ou à la temporalité du changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut une conception du changement comme événement ponctuel sans continuité constitutive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX3","CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut la causalité externe comme mécanisme de transformation de l’intériorité monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut que le changement en général suffise à définir une substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut une pluralité purement numérique de substances indiscernables par leur détermination interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-07","text":"Il exclut la séparation entre la forme générale du changement et le contenu concret de ce qui change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit faux le modèle d’un être créé achevé et définitivement stabilisé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que soit faux le modèle d’une monade réceptive à des causes pénétrant son intériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:DNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie toute explication où les rapports externes suffiraient à produire les transformations internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-04","text":"Il disqualifie aussi l’indifférenciation comme explication de la pluralité : un principe unique doit recevoir des déterminations distinctes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-05","text":"La simplicité sans contenu différentiel est inadmissible, car elle rendrait impossible toute identité qualitative des substances simples.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-06","text":"La négation accumulée prépare positivement une ontologie de processus autonomes, différenciés de l’intérieur et continuellement transformés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSA-01","text":"Le système contourne toute ontologie où l’être créé pourrait posséder une stabilité indépendante de tout changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSA-02","text":"Il rend indisponible l’idée d’un dehors causal capable de pénétrer l’unité substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSA-03","text":"Il rend également indisponible une unité qui ne serait qu’abstraction : toute unité réelle doit être spécifiée par un contenu de changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSA-04","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un principe externe d’individuation ; sa suppression oblige le système à produire la différence depuis l’intérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-01","text":"La mutabilité universelle et la clôture causale ne s’opposent pas : l’impossibilité de l’influence externe convertit le changement en production interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-01","CL_UCIC_04:GA-04","CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-02","text":"La monade est simultanément incluse dans un ordre universel du changement et constituée comme unité autonome dans la production de ses transformations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-02","CL_UCIC_04:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-03","text":"Le principe interne ne produit pas encore l’individuation complète : il doit être spécifié par le détail de ce qui change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-03","CL_UCIC_04:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PR_3:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-04","text":"L’identité substantielle devient le profil déterminé d’un processus interne plutôt qu’une propriété ajoutée à une unité déjà constituée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-05","CL_UCIC_04:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-05","text":"L’unité du système et la pluralité des substances deviennent compatibles parce que l’unité principielle se différencie sans se fragmenter.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-06","CL_UCIC_04:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-06","text":"La négation de la causalité externe devient constructive : ce qui ne peut pas produire le changement détermine la nécessité d’une cause immanente.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-04","CL_UCIC_04:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-07","text":"Une tension productive oppose la clôture causale de chaque monade à son appartenance commune à l’ordre créé ; cette tension est résolue par la différenciation interne du même régime dynamique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-01","CL_UCIC_04:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-01","text":"L’ontologie globale devient une ontologie de processus autonomes : être signifie être continuellement transformé selon une détermination interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-02","text":"L’individuation ne repose plus sur l’opposition entre entités déjà constituées, mais sur la différence qualitative de leurs devenirs internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-03","text":"La causalité est reclassée : l’extérieur peut appartenir à l’ordre décrit, mais il ne constitue pas le principe explicatif immédiat des modifications internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-04","text":"La temporalité n’est pas un cadre ajouté aux substances ; elle est inscrite dans la continuité du changement qui les constitue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-05","text":"L’unité et la pluralité cessent d’être des termes concurrents : la pluralité est l’effet interne de la différenciation d’un principe commun.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-06","text":"La méthode du système est apophatico-constructive : elle retire successivement les modèles impossibles afin de faire apparaître la structure positive requise.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-07","text":"La conséquence terminale est une théorie de la substance comme unité dynamique, close quant à sa causalité et ouverte seulement comme succession interne de déterminations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-01","text":"L’ordre récursif est : création → mutabilité universelle → changement continuel → exigence d’un principe → détermination interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-02","text":"L’exclusion de la cause externe produit une première clôture, mais cette clôture réouvre immédiatement la question du contenu du principe interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-03","text":"L’insuffisance du principe général déclenche une seconde boucle : principe commun → détail déterminé → spécification substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-04","text":"La répétition du changement signale un changement de phase : il cesse d’être un prédicat général et devient le mécanisme d’identité des substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est la monade comme processus interne : toute la chaîne converge vers une unité qui produit et différencie son propre devenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-06","text":"La boucle finale retourne à la mutabilité initiale, mais sous une forme enrichie : le changement est désormais continu, interne et qualitativement spécifié.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B01","text":"L’appartenance à l’ordre créé impose la mutabilité à toute substance créée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B02","text":"La mutabilité continuelle transforme la substance créée en processus plutôt qu’en état achevé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B03","text":"La recherche du principe du processus rencontre l’impossibilité d’une causalité externe pénétrant l’intériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B04","text":"L’exclusion de l’extérieur force la localisation du principe dans la monade elle-même.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B05","text":"L’intériorité ainsi obtenue reste trop générale pour expliquer la pluralité ; elle requiert un détail de ce qui change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B06","text":"Le détail différentiel spécifie chaque substance et convertit l’unité dynamique en pluralité qualitative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B07","text":"Le schéma complet est donc : mutabilité universelle → clôture causale → principe interne → détail différentiel → pluralité substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B01","text":"Être créé → être continuellement mutable → rechercher le principe du changement → exclure l’influence externe → localiser le principe dans l’intériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AF1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B02","text":"Clôture causale → insuffisance du principe abstrait → exigence d’un détail déterminé → spécification de la substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PR_4:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B03","text":"Spécification interne → différenciation qualitative → pluralité des substances simples → compatibilité de l’unité et de la variété.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B04","text":"Universalisation de la mutabilité → fermeture de la causalité externe → intériorisation du principe → différenciation du devenir → unité dynamique plurielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-01","text":"La carte ontologique reclasse tous les êtres créés sous la mutabilité continue et retire à la Monade tout statut d’exception statique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-02","text":"La carte causale déplace le lieu explicatif de l’interaction externe vers la production interne des changements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-03","text":"La carte de l’individuation remplace la différence entre entités par la différence entre déterminations internes du changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-04","text":"La fausse opposition entre unité et pluralité s’effondre : la pluralité devient l’effet structuré d’un principe commun différencié.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-05","text":"La simplicité est reclassée comme concentration d’une structure qualitative, et non comme absence de médiation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-06","text":"La méthode de lecture requise doit suivre les déplacements de fonction du changement : catégorie générale, principe causal, puis opérateur d’individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level : la Monade créée change continuellement et chaque substance simple possède un détail propre de ce qui change en elle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ALT1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level : l’ordre créé est organisé par la mutabilité universelle, la clôture causale interne et la différenciation du changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level : l’argument neutralise successivement l’exception monadique, la causalité externe et l’indifférenciation abstraite pour imposer une explication immanente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level : l’être créé est produit comme processus continu, et l’identité substantielle dépend de la détermination interne de ce devenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level : la forme de l’argument accomplit ce qu’elle établit en transformant chaque exclusion en exigence structurale positive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-01","text":"La monade appartient à l’ordre universel du changement, mais aucune cause extérieure ne peut influer dans son intérieur ; l’universalité porte donc sur la condition, non sur une interaction causale directe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-02","text":"Le principe interne explique l’origine du changement, mais il reste insuffisant pour expliquer la diversité sans l’introduction d’un détail différentiel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-03","text":"La continuité du changement définit la dynamique de la substance, tandis que la substance doit rester assez déterminée pour être distinguée des autres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-04","text":"La clôture causale risque d’isoler chaque monade, mais la différenciation par un cadre commun maintient une unité ontologique du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-05","text":"Le terme de « principe » oscille entre règle universelle du changement et détermination effective d’une substance singulière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation survient lorsque la mutabilité cesse d’être seulement universelle et devient causalement interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MP-02","text":"Le second point de mutation survient lorsque le principe interne est déclaré insuffisant sans le détail de ce qui change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation transforme la simplicité en forme de détermination qualitative plutôt qu’en absence de composition interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MP-04","text":"La ligne de faille productive oppose l’autonomie causale de chaque monade à la nécessité d’un régime commun de différenciation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de processus internes : chaque unité change continuellement selon une causalité qui ne vient pas du dehors.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:HSI-02","text":"La monade devient une unité auto-déterminante dont l’identité n’est pas la fixité, mais la trajectoire qualitative de ses changements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:HSI-03","text":"Le temps supposé par le système est un devenir continu, non une série d’états achevés reliés par une cause extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée disponible n’est pas une sortie hors du changement, mais une différenciation interne du mode de changer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre éléments : mutabilité universelle, clôture causale, principe interne et détail différentiel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B02","text":"Ces éléments suffisent à reconstruire le passage de l’être créé à la pluralité qualitative des substances simples sans réintroduire une causalité externe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne la nature précise du principe interne, du détail différentiel et de leur mode de liaison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B04","text":"La reconstruction ne doit pas prétendre expliquer les relations entre plusieurs monades, question explicitement laissée ouverte par la couche fournie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B05","text":"La fidélité structurelle dépend de la conservation de l’ordre mutationnel : universalité du changement, intériorisation de la cause, puis différenciation substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B06","text":"Le système est donc reconstructible à cette échelle comme une ontologie dynamique de substances causalement closes, dont la pluralité procède de la spécification interne du changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194821089238Z_490baee6","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 10–12","source_sha256":"e0e0424f73f874e33755a55a19bd21dc1f39c89a60817267460046b64df115f9","sha256":"6780bd8adbcee08ca7abf9a8b61df72bb001178df85923eb3731e7dffafc56fa","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:48:21.092865+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-01","text":"The problem consists in explaining how a created monad can be continuously changing while remaining causally closed to the outside.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-02","text":"The system reframes mutability as a universal condition of the created order rather than as an exceptional property of certain substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-03","text":"The closure of interiority excludes external causality and shifts the explanation of change toward an immanent principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-04","text":"Interiority is nevertheless insufficient as an abstract principle: it must comprise a determinate detail of what changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-05","text":"The plurality of simple substances is thus produced by the internal differentiation of one and the same general regime of change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-06","text":"The argumentative movement proceeds from universal mutability to causal autonomy, then from autonomy to differential specification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-07","text":"The architecture is cumulative and recursive: each exclusion makes necessary a more precise determination of the retained principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AS-08","text":"The closure produced is not immobility, but a plurality of continuously differentiated internal processes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every created being is subject to change, and no created monad is exempt from this condition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Change in the created order is not punctual: it continuously affects every created being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] The natural changes of a monad require a determining principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] An external cause cannot exert influence within the interiority of the monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Mutability passes from a general property of created being to an internal production of natural change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] The general principle of change is insufficient to determine a simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Every simple substance receives its determination from a distinctive detail of what changes within it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] The qualitative plurality of simple substances results from the internal differentiation of change, not from an external causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] The system converges toward the figure of a dynamic, causally closed, and qualitatively differentiated unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Substantial identity cannot be reduced to a fixed state or to a simplicity devoid of internal content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] The unity of the principle and the plurality of substances exclude one another only on condition that principle and determination are separated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-01","text":"Mutability recurs with stable identity as the condition of every created being, but its function subsequently shifts toward the internal definition of the monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-02","text":"Recurrent change passes from a general ontological status to a causal function: it becomes the effect of an internal principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-03","text":"Interiority retains its role as the locus of change, but mutates from closed space into a structure productive of determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-04","text":"The principle of change persists as an invariant, while its insufficiency entails the introduction of a differential detail.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-05","text":"Simplicity is inverted: it no longer signifies absence of content, but the concentration of a qualitative determination in an uncompounded unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-06","text":"Diversity no longer arises from a difference of principle, but from variations in the determination of what changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-07","text":"External causality disappears as a direct explanation after having performed a delimiting function, but its exclusion makes internal causality necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RMD-08","text":"The recurrence of change ceases to be redundant when it becomes the mechanism linking universality, autonomy, and individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The inclusion of the Monad within the class of created beings establishes a local consequence: it is subject to general mutability.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-02","text":"[Local] The impossibility of an external influence locally establishes the causal closure of each monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-03","text":"[Scale-shift] The interaction of the two machines transforms causal closure into a general principle for explaining created dynamics.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-04","text":"[Cross-unit] The necessity of a differential detail links internal dynamics to the plurality of simple substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-05","text":"[Catalytic] The insufficiency of the general principle catalyzes the passage from an ontology of change to a theory of individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-06","text":"[Recoded] The difference between interior and exterior is no longer merely spatial or relational: it becomes the difference between an effective principle and an impossible cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:CGD-07","text":"[Obsolète] A model in which plurality would result from external actions or from an undifferentiated abstract principle is superseded by the internal structure of change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes immutability as a general characteristic of a created being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the notion that creation constitutes an exemption from mutability or from the temporality of change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_2:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-03","text":"It excludes a conception of change as a punctual event without constitutive continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX3","CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-04","text":"It excludes external causality as a mechanism for transforming monadic interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the notion that change in general suffices to define a simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-06","text":"It excludes a purely numerical plurality of substances indiscernible by their internal determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:GNX-07","text":"It excludes the separation between the general form of change and the concrete content of what changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the model of a completed and definitively stabilized created being must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_2:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-02","text":"The model of a monad receptive to causes penetrating its interiority must likewise be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:DNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies every explanation in which external relations would suffice to produce internal transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-04","text":"It also disqualifies undifferentiation as an explanation of plurality: a single principle must receive distinct determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-05","text":"Simplicity without differential content is inadmissible, for it would render impossible any qualitative identity of simple substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:DBN-06","text":"The accumulated negation positively prepares an ontology of autonomous processes, differentiated from within and continuously transformed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSA-01","text":"The system bypasses every ontology in which created being could possess a stability independent of all change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSA-02","text":"It renders unavailable the idea of a causal outside capable of penetrating substantial unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSA-03","text":"It likewise renders unavailable a unity that would be mere abstraction: every real unity must be specified by a content of change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSA-04","text":"The structuring absence is that of an external principle of individuation; its removal compels the system to produce difference from within.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-01","text":"Universal mutability and causal closure are not opposed: the impossibility of external influence converts change into internal production.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-01","CL_UCIC_04:GA-04","CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-02","text":"The monad is simultaneously included in a universal order of change and constituted as an autonomous unity in the production of its transformations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-02","CL_UCIC_04:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-03","text":"The internal principle does not yet produce complete individuation: it must be specified by the detail of what changes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-03","CL_UCIC_04:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PR_3:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-04","text":"Substantial identity becomes the determinate profile of an internal process rather than a property added to an already constituted unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-05","CL_UCIC_04:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-05","text":"The unity of the system and the plurality of substances become compatible because principial unity differentiates itself without fragmenting.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-06","CL_UCIC_04:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-06","text":"The negation of external causality becomes constructive: that which cannot produce change determines the necessity of an immanent cause.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-04","CL_UCIC_04:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:XD-07","text":"A productive tension opposes the causal closure of each monad to its common belonging to the created order; this tension is resolved by the internal differentiation of the same dynamic regime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GA-01","CL_UCIC_04:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_2:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-01","text":"Global ontology becomes an ontology of autonomous processes: to be means to be continuously transformed according to an internal determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-02","text":"Individuation no longer rests on the opposition between already constituted entities, but on the qualitative difference of their internal becomings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-03","text":"Causality is reclassified: the exterior may belong to the order described, but it does not constitute the immediate explanatory principle of internal modifications.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-04","text":"Temporality is not a framework added to substances; it is inscribed in the continuity of change that constitutes them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-05","text":"Unity and plurality cease to be competing terms: plurality is the internal effect of the differentiation of a common principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-06","text":"The method of the system is apophatic-constructive: it successively removes impossible models in order to make the required positive structure appear.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:BSD-07","text":"The terminal consequence is a theory of substance as a dynamic unity, closed with respect to its causality and open only as an internal succession of determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-01","text":"The recursive order is: creation → universal mutability → continual change → requirement of a principle → internal determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-02","text":"The exclusion of the external cause produces a first closure, but this closure immediately reopens the question of the content of the internal principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-03","text":"The insufficiency of the general principle triggers a second loop: common principle → determinate detail → substantial specification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-04","text":"The repetition of change signals a phase change: it ceases to be a general predicate and becomes the mechanism of the identity of substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is the monad as internal process: the whole chain converges toward a unity that produces and differentiates its own becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:RLE-06","text":"The final loop returns to initial mutability, but in an enriched form: change is henceforth continuous, internal, and qualitatively specified.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B01","text":"Belonging to the created order imposes mutability on every created substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_2:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B02","text":"Continual mutability transforms created substance into a process rather than a completed state.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_2:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B03","text":"The search for the principle of the process encounters the impossibility of an external causality penetrating interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B04","text":"The exclusion of the exterior forces the localization of the principle within the monad itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_3:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B05","text":"The interiority thus obtained remains too general to explain plurality; it requires a detail of what changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B06","text":"The differential detail specifies each substance and converts dynamic unity into qualitative plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B07","text":"The complete schema is therefore: universal mutability → causal closure → internal principle → differential detail → substantial plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B01","text":"To be created → to be continuously mutable → to seek the principle of change → to exclude external influence → to locate the principle in interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AF1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B02","text":"Causal closure → insufficiency of the abstract principle → requirement of a determinate detail → specification of the simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PR_4:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B03","text":"Internal specification → qualitative differentiation → plurality of simple substances → compatibility of unity and variety.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B04","text":"Universalization of mutability → closure of external causality → internalization of the principle → differentiation of becoming → plural dynamic unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-01","text":"The ontological map reclassifies all created beings under continuous mutability and removes from the Monad every status of static exception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_2:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-02","text":"The causal map shifts the explanatory locus from external interaction to the internal production of changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-03","text":"The map of individuation replaces the difference between entities with the difference between internal determinations of change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-04","text":"The false opposition between unity and plurality collapses: plurality becomes the structured effect of a differentiated common principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-05","text":"Simplicity is reclassified as the concentration of a qualitative structure, and not as the absence of internal mediation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MME-06","text":"The required method of reading must follow the functional displacements of change: general category, causal principle, then operator of individuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level: the created Monad changes continuously and each simple substance possesses a distinctive detail of what changes within it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ALT1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level: the created order is organized by universal mutability, internal causal closure, and the differentiation of change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level: the argument successively neutralizes the monadic exception, external causality, and abstract undifferentiation in order to impose an immanent explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level: created being is produced as a continuous process, and substantial identity depends on the internal determination of this becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level: the form of the argument accomplishes what it establishes by transforming each exclusion into a positive structural requirement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-01","text":"The monad belongs to the universal order of change, but no external cause can exert influence within its interior; universality thus bears upon the condition, not upon a direct causal interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-02","text":"The internal principle explains the origin of change, but remains insufficient to explain diversity without the introduction of a differential detail.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-03","text":"The continuity of change defines the dynamic character of substance, whereas substance must remain sufficiently determinate to be distinguished from others.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-04","text":"Causal closure risks isolating each monad, but differentiation through a common framework maintains an ontological unity of the system.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:FL-05","text":"The term “principle” oscillates between a universal rule of change and the effective determination of a singular substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point occurs when mutability ceases to be merely universal and becomes causally internal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point occurs when the internal principle is declared insufficient without the detail of what changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point transforms simplicity into a form of qualitative determination rather than an absence of internal composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MP-04","text":"The productive fault line opposes the causal autonomy of each monad to the necessity of a common regime of differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a machine of internal processes: each unity changes continuously according to a causality that does not come from outside.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_3:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:HSI-02","text":"The monad becomes a self-determining unity whose identity is not fixity, but the qualitative trajectory of its changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:HSI-03","text":"The time presupposed by the system is a continuous becoming, not a series of completed states connected by an external cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:HSI-04","text":"The only available escape is not an exit from change, but an internal differentiation of the mode of changing.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_4:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four elements: universal mutability, causal closure, internal principle, and differential detail.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B02","text":"These elements suffice to reconstruct the passage from created being to the qualitative plurality of simple substances without reintroducing an external causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the precise nature of the internal principle, the differential detail, and their mode of connection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT3","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B04","text":"The reconstruction must not claim to explain the relations among several monads, a question explicitly left open by the supplied layer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_3:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B05","text":"Structural fidelity depends on preserving the mutational order: universality of change, internalization of the cause, then substantial differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PR_4:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B06","text":"The system is thus reconstructible at this scale as a dynamic ontology of causally closed substances, whose plurality proceeds from the internal specification of change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_2:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_4:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_04@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_04:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 10–12","context":"Proposition 10 · Proposition 11 · Proposition 12"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 13–15","order":5,"parents":["CH_UCIC_PR_5","CH_UCIC_PR_6","CH_UCIC_PR_7"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_05@R001","sha256":"d31de852b43347afb19fdbc55f90c2c1314781f8ea9ae8ecc895ee65fcbbe6e5","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-01","text":"Le système affronte la difficulté de penser une multitude interne sans dissoudre l’unité simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-02","text":"Il recadre cette difficulté par une théorie graduelle du changement, où variation et permanence coexistent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-03","text":"La multitude devient ensuite le contenu représenté d’un état passager de la substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-04","text":"Le passage d’une perception à une autre est produit par un principe interne orienté, nommé appétition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-05","text":"L’orientation n’exige pas l’accomplissement complet de son terme, car son efficacité se mesure à la production d’une nouveauté perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-06","text":"Le mouvement global transforme donc la simplicité en unité différenciée, représentative et auto-modificatrice plutôt qu’en indifférenciation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-07","text":"L’argument est cumulatif et récursif : la pluralité exige une représentation, la représentation une transition, et la transition reconduit une nouvelle pluralité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-08","text":"Sa clôture est dynamique plutôt que terminale : chaque accomplissement partiel devient la condition d’une perception nouvelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] L’unité substantielle n’est pas composée de parties, mais cette absence de parties n’exclut pas une pluralité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La pluralité pertinente est constituée d’affections, de rapports et de contenus représentés plutôt que de composants substantiels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Tout changement implique la coexistence d’une modification et d’une permanence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] La gradualité du changement se transforme en succession de configurations perceptives sans perdre le support unitaire qui les porte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La perception est l’état passager qui enveloppe et représente une multitude dans une unité substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La représentation est une opération interne d’unification de la pluralité, non une réception passive ou un rapport extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Le passage perceptif possède une source dynamique interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] L’appétition oriente le devenir vers une perception déterminée sans garantir la coïncidence entre le terme visé et le résultat obtenu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] L’accomplissement partiel fonctionne comme une efficacité réelle parce qu’il produit nécessairement une perception nouvelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Chaque transition se convertit en nouvelle configuration perceptive, ce qui ferme localement un état tout en relançant le devenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-01","text":"La simplicité revient d’abord comme absence de parties, puis comme capacité de contenir et de représenter une multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-02","text":"La pluralité migre du registre des affections et des rapports vers celui du contenu représenté, puis vers celui de la nouveauté produite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-03","text":"Le changement passe de la gradualité naturelle à la transition perceptive, puis devient une dynamique orientée par l’appétition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-04","text":"La permanence ne désigne plus un état immobile ; elle devient la continuité de l’unité à travers des modifications successives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-05","text":"L’intériorité se déplace de la différenciation sans parties vers une causalité interne productrice de transitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-06","text":"L’état passager, d’abord définition de la perception, devient le moment local d’une série auto-transformative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-07","text":"L’inachèvement cesse d’être une simple limitation et devient le mécanisme qui maintient la production du nouveau.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-01","text":"La proposition locale selon laquelle la substance simple possède des affections sans parties établit une condition ontologique, mais ne suffit pas à expliquer la perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_5:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-02","text":"La définition locale de la perception comme état représentatif devient, à l’échelle du cluster, une médiation entre pluralité interne et devenir temporel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-03","text":"L’appétition n’est pas seulement un principe local de changement : elle fournit le mécanisme qui relie représentation, orientation et production de nouveauté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-04","text":"L’interaction des unités recode la simplicité : elle passe d’une propriété négative à une architecture positive de différenciation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-05","text":"Les distinctions locales entre changement, perception et appétition deviennent les trois moments d’une seule machine de transformation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-06","text":"La recherche d’une substance sans pluralité, d’une perception immobile ou d’une tendance sans effet est dépassée par l’architecture cumulative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut que l’unité soit synonyme d’indifférenciation ou que la pluralité exige une composition en parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut une perception conçue comme substance séparée, multitude autonome ou faculté indépendante de son support unitaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut un changement sans degrés, sans permanence ou sans principe interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut l’équivalence entre orientation et accomplissement intégral, ainsi que l’alternative entre succès total et absence d’effet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une causalité extérieure qui produirait la nouveauté sans orientation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’idée selon laquelle toute multiplicité réelle est une division de l’unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:DNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également écarter le modèle d’une substance simple sans contenu, sans modification et sans représentation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:DNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie une ontologie où permanence et devenir s’excluraient mutuellement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:DBN-04","text":"Il disqualifie enfin une causalité évaluée seulement par l’atteinte de son terme, car l’effet partiel constitue déjà une production réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:DNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSA-01","text":"L’indistinction absolue est rendue ontologiquement inadmissible : une unité qui ne différerait en rien ne pourrait ni percevoir ni changer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSA-02","text":"La composition est privée de son monopole explicatif sur la multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSA-03","text":"Une substance sans devenir interne est exclue du régime de la perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSA-04","text":"L’absence structurante du système est celle d’un dehors causal autonome : la nouveauté doit être produite depuis l’unité elle-même.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-01","text":"La pluralité interne devient perceptive lorsqu’elle est organisée comme représentation successive par une unité qui demeure identique à travers ses modifications.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-01","CL_UCIC_05:GA-04","CL_UCIC_05:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PR_5:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_6:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-02","text":"La perception n’est pas seulement un contenu de la substance simple ; elle est le mode temporel selon lequel cette substance conserve son unité en changeant.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-03","CL_UCIC_05:GA-05","CL_UCIC_05:GA-06","CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-03","text":"L’appétition transforme la représentation en puissance de transition : ce qui est représenté devient une orientation vers une configuration nouvelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-06","CL_UCIC_05:GA-07","CL_UCIC_05:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-04","text":"L’inachèvement est productif parce que la non-coïncidence entre perception visée et perception obtenue ouvre la séquence suivante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-08","CL_UCIC_05:GA-09","CL_UCIC_05:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-05","text":"La simplicité, la perception et l’appétition forment une seule structure : support unitaire, représentation pluralisante et poussée de transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-01","CL_UCIC_05:GA-05","CL_UCIC_05:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-06","text":"La continuité du changement devient une continuité générative : chaque état conserve le support tout en reconfigurant son contenu perceptif.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-03","CL_UCIC_05:GA-04","CL_UCIC_05:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PR_5:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-07","text":"Le système substitue à l’opposition entre unité et multiplicité une boucle où l’unité produit, représente et relance la multiplicité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-01","CL_UCIC_05:GA-06","CL_UCIC_05:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D5","CH_UCIC_PR_6:FGS4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-01","text":"L’unité substantielle devient un opérateur de différenciation interne plutôt qu’un substrat inerte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-02","text":"L’identité n’est plus la répétition d’un même état, mais la persistance d’une capacité de transformation orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-03","text":"La causalité est redéfinie comme production partielle et continuée plutôt que comme réalisation exhaustive d’un terme prédéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-04","text":"Le temps acquiert une fonction constitutive : il n’enregistre pas seulement les états, il articule la conservation du support et la production du nouveau.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-05","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme série de configurations internes orientées, et non comme collection d’états indépendants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-06","text":"L’agentivité minimale ne réside pas dans la maîtrise du terme, mais dans la capacité à transformer effectivement l’état présent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-01","text":"Pluralité interne → représentation unifiante → modification de l’état → nouvelle perception → pluralité reconfigurée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:FGS4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-02","text":"Permanence du support → orientation interne → accomplissement partiel → déplacement perceptif → confirmation de la permanence dynamique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-03","text":"La perception devient une machine lorsqu’elle cesse d’être seulement représentation et produit elle-même la transition vers une autre perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-04","text":"L’inachèvement agit comme attracteur : aucun terme n’épuise la dynamique, mais chaque terme partiel maintient la continuité productive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-05","text":"La répétition de la nouveauté signale un changement de phase : la perception devient le vecteur d’une auto-transformation sérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-06","text":"L’attracteur global est une unité capable de contenir la multiplicité sans la supprimer et de la renouveler sans se composer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B01","text":"Unité simple sans parties + pluralité interne → nécessité d’une différenciation non compositionnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_5:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B02","text":"Changement graduel + coexistence du changement et de la permanence → pluralité d’affections et de rapports dans une même substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B03","text":"Pluralité interne + état passager → enveloppement et représentation → perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B04","text":"Perception représentative + succession d’états → nécessité d’un principe interne de transition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B05","text":"Principe interne + orientation vers une perception déterminée → appétition sans garantie d’accomplissement complet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B06","text":"Accomplissement partiel + effet réel → perception nouvelle → relance du processus perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B07","text":"La machine totale produit une unité dynamique : elle conserve son identité en générant continuellement des différences internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B01","text":"Difficulté de la multitude dans l’unité → distinction entre pluralité et composition → unité simple différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_5:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B02","text":"Unité différenciée → multitude représentée dans un état passager → perception comme opération interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B03","text":"Perception successive → principe interne → appétition orientée → accomplissement partiel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B04","text":"Effet partiel → perception nouvelle → intensification récursive → unité comme générateur de multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-01","text":"L’opposition unité/multiplicité est remplacée par la distinction unité composée/unité différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-02","text":"La perception est reclassée comme modification dynamique d’une substance, et non comme faculté séparée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-03","text":"La représentation devient une opération interne, ce qui neutralise le modèle d’un sujet séparé d’un objet extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-04","text":"L’échec partiel est reclassé comme moteur de production plutôt que comme défaut de causalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-05","text":"La temporalité devient une structure ontologique de l’identité, et non une simple succession extrinsèque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME4","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-06","text":"La méthode de lecture doit suivre les déplacements fonctionnels d’un même concept : simplicité, perception et appétition changent de rôle en s’intégrant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Une substance simple contient une multitude d’affections et de rapports, puis la représente dans des états perceptifs successifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] La machine articule support unitaire, contenu multiple, représentation interne et transition orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] La contradiction entre unité et multiplicité est déplacée vers une distinction entre composition et différenciation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PR_5:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] L’identité est une continuité transformante : elle persiste en traversant une série de modifications orientées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La structure argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle affirme en faisant passer chaque définition locale vers une dynamique qui la dépasse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FL-01","text":"La simplicité doit rester non composée tout en accueillant assez de différenciation pour produire représentation et changement ; cette compatibilité n’est pas davantage fondée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_6:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FL-02","text":"L’« enveloppement » et la « représentation » restent fonctionnellement nécessaires mais leur mécanisme exact demeure indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:MRT3","CH_UCIC_PR_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FL-03","text":"L’appétition est à la fois orientation vers un terme et production d’un résultat différent ; la tension entre visée et effet soutient la dynamique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MP-01","text":"La simplicité mute lorsqu’elle cesse de désigner seulement l’absence de parties et devient capacité de représentation multiple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MP-02","text":"Le changement mute lorsqu’il passe d’une transition graduelle à une série de transformations perceptives produites de l’intérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MP-03","text":"L’inachèvement mute en principe positif lorsque l’effet partiel devient la condition nécessaire d’une perception nouvelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de condensation : une unité sans parties contient, représente et reconfigure une multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet n’est pas un observateur extérieur, mais un foyer interne de représentation et de transformation orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est une spirale de configurations : chaque état conserve une continuité et produit une différence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée possible n’est pas la sortie hors de l’unité, mais la production interne d’une nouvelle perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage de l’unité simple à la pluralité interne, puis de la pluralité à la perception et à l’appétition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction conserve la dépendance décisive entre unité substantielle, représentation interne et transition perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:MRT2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B03","text":"Le point de force du système est la conversion de la limitation en efficacité : le résultat incomplet suffit à relancer le devenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne le mécanisme exact de l’enveloppement, de la représentation et le rapport précis entre principe interne et appétition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:MRT3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B05","text":"La compression est fidèle au mouvement réel : unité non composée → pluralité représentée → transition interne → effet partiel → perception nouvelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194855573040Z_31650726","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 13–15","source_sha256":"d31de852b43347afb19fdbc55f90c2c1314781f8ea9ae8ecc895ee65fcbbe6e5","sha256":"7d2ff4456d898d21d2e0fc7839f88fc96e3c1d5916d8cb5b6c4d717d3ba3f860","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:48:55.577609+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-01","text":"The system confronts the difficulty of thinking an internal multitude without dissolving simple unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-02","text":"It reframes this difficulty through a gradual theory of change, in which variation and permanence coexist.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-03","text":"The multitude subsequently becomes the represented content of a transient state of the simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-04","text":"The passage from one perception to another is produced by an internally directed principle, called appetition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-05","text":"Orientation does not require the complete attainment of its terminus, for its efficacy is measured by the production of a perceptual novelty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-06","text":"The overall movement thus transforms simplicity into a differentiated, representative, and self-modifying unity rather than into undifferentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-07","text":"The argument is cumulative and recursive: plurality requires representation, representation a transition, and transition brings forth a new plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AS-08","text":"Its closure is dynamic rather than terminal: each partial accomplishment becomes the condition of a new perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Substantial unity is not composed of parts, but this absence of parts does not exclude an internal plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The relevant plurality consists of affections, relations, and represented contents rather than substantial components.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Every change entails the coexistence of a modification and a permanence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] The graduality of change is transformed into a succession of perceptual configurations without losing the unitary support that bears them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Perception is the transient state that enfolds and represents a multitude in a substantial unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Representation is an internal operation of unifying plurality, not a passive reception or an external relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Perceptual passage possesses an internal dynamic source.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Appetition directs becoming toward a determinate perception without guaranteeing the coincidence between the intended terminus and the result obtained.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Partial accomplishment functions as a real efficacy because it necessarily produces a new perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Each transition is converted into a new perceptual configuration, which locally closes one state while relaunching becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-01","text":"Simplicity first recurs as absence of parts, then as the capacity to contain and represent a multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-02","text":"Plurality migrates from the register of affections and relations to that of represented content, then to that of produced novelty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-03","text":"Change passes from natural graduality to perceptual transition, then becomes a dynamic directed by appetition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-04","text":"Permanence no longer designates an immobile state; it becomes the continuity of unity through successive modifications.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-05","text":"Interiority shifts from differentiation without parts to an internal causality productive of transitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-06","text":"The transient state, initially the definition of perception, becomes the local moment of a self-transformative series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RMD-07","text":"Incompleteness ceases to be a mere limitation and becomes the mechanism that sustains the production of the new.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-01","text":"The local proposition according to which simple substance possesses affections without parts establishes an ontological condition, but does not suffice to explain perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_5:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-02","text":"The local definition of perception as a representative state becomes, at the scale of the cluster, a mediation between internal plurality and temporal becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-03","text":"Appetition is not merely a local principle of change: it provides the mechanism linking representation, orientation, and the production of novelty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-04","text":"The interaction of the units recodes simplicity: it passes from a negative property to a positive architecture of internal differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-05","text":"The local distinctions between change, perception, and appetition become the three moments of a single machine of internal transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:CGD-06","text":"The search for a substance without plurality, an immobile perception, or a tendency without effect is surpassed by the cumulative architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes unity being synonymous with undifferentiation or plurality requiring composition into parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a perception conceived as a separate substance, autonomous multitude, or faculty independent of its unitary support.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-03","text":"It excludes change without degrees, without permanence, or without an internal principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the equivalence between orientation and integral accomplishment, as well as the alternative between total success and absence of effect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:GNX-05","text":"It excludes an external causality that would produce novelty without internal orientation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the idea according to which every real multiplicity is a division of unity must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:DNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:DBN-02","text":"The model of a simple substance without content, modification, or representation must likewise be set aside.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:DNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies an ontology in which permanence and becoming would mutually exclude one another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:DNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:DBN-04","text":"Finally, it disqualifies a causality evaluated solely by the attainment of its terminus, for the partial effect already constitutes a real production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:DNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSA-01","text":"Absolute indistinction is rendered ontologically inadmissible: a unity differing in nothing could neither perceive nor change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSA-02","text":"Composition is deprived of its explanatory monopoly over multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSA-03","text":"A substance without internal becoming is excluded from the regime of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSA-04","text":"The system's structuring absence is that of an autonomous causal outside: novelty must be produced from unity itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-01","text":"Internal plurality becomes perceptual when it is organized as successive representation by a unity that remains identical through its modifications.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-01","CL_UCIC_05:GA-04","CL_UCIC_05:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PR_5:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_6:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-02","text":"Perception is not merely a content of simple substance; it is the temporal mode according to which this substance preserves its unity while changing.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-03","CL_UCIC_05:GA-05","CL_UCIC_05:GA-06","CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-03","text":"Appetition transforms representation into a power of transition: what is represented becomes an orientation toward a new configuration.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-06","CL_UCIC_05:GA-07","CL_UCIC_05:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-04","text":"Incompleteness is productive because the non-coincidence between intended perception and obtained perception opens the following sequence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-08","CL_UCIC_05:GA-09","CL_UCIC_05:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-05","text":"Simplicity, perception, and appetition form a single structure: unitary support, pluralizing representation, and impetus of transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-01","CL_UCIC_05:GA-05","CL_UCIC_05:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-06","text":"The continuity of change becomes a generative continuity: each state preserves the support while reconfiguring its perceptual content.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-03","CL_UCIC_05:GA-04","CL_UCIC_05:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PR_5:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:XD-07","text":"The system substitutes for the opposition between unity and multiplicity a loop in which unity produces, represents, and relaunches multiplicity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-01","CL_UCIC_05:GA-06","CL_UCIC_05:GA-10","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D5","CH_UCIC_PR_6:FGS4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-01","text":"Substantial unity becomes an operator of internal differentiation rather than an inert substrate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-02","text":"Identity is no longer the repetition of one and the same state, but the persistence of a capacity for directed transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-03","text":"Causality is redefined as partial and continued production rather than as exhaustive realization of a predetermined terminus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-04","text":"Time acquires a constitutive function: it does not merely record states; it articulates the preservation of support and the production of the new.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-05","text":"The real is reclassified as a series of directed internal configurations, and not as a collection of independent states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:BSD-06","text":"Minimal agency lies not in mastery of the terminus, but in the capacity effectively to transform the present state.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-01","text":"Internal plurality → unifying representation → modification of the state → new perception → reconfigured plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:FGS4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-02","text":"Permanence of the support → internal orientation → partial accomplishment → perceptual displacement → confirmation of dynamic permanence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-03","text":"Perception becomes a machine when it ceases to be merely representation and itself produces the transition toward another perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-04","text":"Incompleteness acts as an attractor: no terminus exhausts the dynamic, but each partial terminus sustains productive continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-05","text":"The repetition of novelty signals a phase change: perception becomes the vector of a serial self-transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:RLE-06","text":"The global attractor is a unity capable of containing multiplicity without suppressing it and of renewing it without becoming composite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B01","text":"Simple unity without parts + internal plurality → necessity of a non-compositional differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_5:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B02","text":"Gradual change + coexistence of change and permanence → plurality of affections and relations in one and the same substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_5:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B03","text":"Internal plurality + transient state → enfolding and representation → perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B04","text":"Representative perception + succession of states → necessity of an internal principle of transition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B05","text":"Internal principle + orientation toward a determinate perception → appetition without guarantee of complete accomplishment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B06","text":"Partial accomplishment + real effect → new perception → relaunching of the perceptual process.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A6","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B07","text":"The total machine produces a dynamic unity: it preserves its identity by continually generating internal differences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B01","text":"Difficulty of multitude within unity → distinction between plurality and composition → differentiated simple unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_5:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B02","text":"Differentiated unity → multitude represented in a transient state → perception as internal operation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B03","text":"Successive perception → internal principle → directed appetition → partial accomplishment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B04","text":"Partial effect → new perception → recursive intensification → unity as generator of multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AF5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-01","text":"The unity/multiplicity opposition is replaced by the distinction between composite unity and differentiated unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-02","text":"Perception is reclassified as the dynamic modification of a substance, and not as a separate faculty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-03","text":"Representation becomes an internal operation, which neutralizes the model of a subject separate from an external object.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-04","text":"Partial failure is reclassified as a motor of production rather than as a defect of causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-05","text":"Temporality becomes an ontological structure of identity, and not a mere extrinsic succession.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME4","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MME-06","text":"The method of reading must follow the functional displacements of a single concept: simplicity, perception, and appetition change roles as they become integrated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] A simple substance contains a multitude of affections and relations, then represents it in successive perceptual states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:AS4","CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] The machine articulates unitary support, multiple content, internal representation, and directed transition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The contradiction between unity and multiplicity is displaced toward a distinction between composition and internal differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PR_5:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Identity is a transforming continuity: it persists by passing through a series of directed modifications.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative structure accomplishes what it asserts by moving each local definition toward a dynamic that surpasses it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:AS5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FL-01","text":"Simplicity must remain non-composite while admitting enough differentiation to produce representation and change; this compatibility is not further grounded.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_6:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FL-02","text":"“Enfolding” and “representation” remain functionally necessary, but their exact mechanism remains indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:MRT3","CH_UCIC_PR_5:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:FL-03","text":"Appetition is both orientation toward a terminus and production of a different result; the tension between aim and effect sustains the dynamic.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:NX4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MP-01","text":"Simplicity mutates when it ceases to designate only the absence of parts and becomes the capacity for multiple representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MP-02","text":"Change mutates when it passes from gradual transition to a series of perceptual transformations produced from within.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MP-03","text":"Incompleteness mutates into a positive principle when the partial effect becomes the necessary condition of a new perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a machine of condensation: a unity without parts contains, represents, and reconfigures a multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_5:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:HSI-02","text":"The subject is not an external observer, but an internal focus of representation and directed transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:HSI-03","text":"Time is a spiral of configurations: each state preserves a continuity and produces a difference.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:SD3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:HSI-04","text":"The only possible escape is not an exit from unity, but the internal production of a new perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_7:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage from simple unity to internal plurality, then from plurality to perception and appetition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction preserves the decisive dependency between substantial unity, internal representation, and perceptual transition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:MRT2","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B03","text":"The system's strength lies in the conversion of limitation into efficacy: the incomplete result suffices to relaunch becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_7:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B04","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the exact mechanism of enfolding, of representation, and the precise relation between internal principle and appetition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_6:MRT3","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B05","text":"The compression is faithful to the real movement: non-composite unity → represented plurality → internal transition → partial effect → new perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_5:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PR_7:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_05@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_05:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 13–15","context":"Proposition 13 · Proposition 14 · Proposition 15"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 16–18","order":6,"parents":["CH_UCIC_PR_8","CH_UCIC_PR_9","CH_UCIC_P_10"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_06@R001","sha256":"ddc49a3a4d596a1be529ee6cbd5f131da0b5eaa1c09b4312de5907042a635182","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-01","text":"Le problème global est de rendre compatible la simplicité non composée de la substance avec une multiplicité interne, une perception différenciée et une activité autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-02","text":"Le système recadre la simplicité : elle n’est pas une homogénéité vide, mais une unité capable d’envelopper une variété.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-03","text":"La pensée consciente fournit le premier indice d’une structure interne plus riche que l’unité apparente de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-04","text":"L’examen de la machine mécanique produit une négation cumulative : ni la figure, ni le mouvement, ni l’agrégation des parties ne suffisent à expliquer la perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-05","text":"L’agrandissement imaginaire de la machine transforme l’inspection mécanique en démonstration de l’absence d’un principe perceptif dans les parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-06","text":"La perception est alors déplacée du composé vers la substance simple, où elle devient le régime propre de l’activité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-07","text":"La perfection de la Monade est reconduite en suffisance interne, puis en production autonome de ses actions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-08","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et mutationnel : l’unité simple passe de support de multiplicité à centre perceptif, puis à source active et automate incorporel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La substance simple n’a pas de parties composantes, mais cette absence de composition ne supprime pas sa détermination interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] La multiplicité pertinente est enveloppée dans l’unité ; elle ne consiste pas en une pluralité de supports substantiels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Toute pensée consciente possède un objet dont la structure comporte une variété différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_8:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] La perception convertit une donnée phénoménale en indice de structure ontologique interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Les figures, les mouvements et les interactions entre parties ne constituent pas une explication suffisante de la perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] L’augmentation de l’échelle ne produit pas une perception mécanique ; elle rend plus manifeste l’absence d’un principe perceptif dans la machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La substance simple devient le lieu ontologique de la perception et de ses changements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] L’action interne de la substance simple consiste en une succession de perceptions et de modifications perceptives, non en un déplacement de parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:A9","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] La perfection d’une Monade implique une suffisance qui la rend source de ses actions internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:A3","CH_UCIC_P_10:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] L’automatisme est détaché de la corporéité et redéfini comme spontanéité d’une unité dont le principe d’action est interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] La simplicité désigne finalement une unité non composée, perceptive, différenciée et auto-active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D1","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] La mécanique est reléguée au régime des relations entre parties, tandis que la perception et l’action interne relèvent de la substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-01","text":"La simplicité persiste comme prémisse, mais sa fonction mute : d’abord propriété de l’âme, elle devient ensuite condition d’une activité interne autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A1","CH_UCIC_P_10:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-02","text":"La multiplicité revient d’abord comme variété de l’objet pensé, puis comme régime général des perceptions internes de la Monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-03","text":"La machine passe d’un modèle prétendument explicatif à un dispositif apophatique qui expose l’absence de perception dans la composition mécanique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AS3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-04","text":"La perception migre du statut de phénomène à expliquer vers celui de contenu constitutif de l’activité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-05","text":"L’action interne se déplace de la poussée entre parties vers la variation successive des perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-06","text":"L’automate subit une inversion fonctionnelle : il ne désigne plus principalement un mécanisme corporel, mais une source incorporelle d’action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-07","text":"L’objection de Bayle reste locale et disparaît après avoir servi à stabiliser la compatibilité entre simplicité et multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX5","CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-01","text":"La référence à Bayle reste locale : elle désigne une difficulté interprétative précise, non une composante nécessaire de l’architecture générale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-02","text":"La pensée minimale est une machine argumentative locale ; à l’échelle du cluster, elle devient le premier opérateur de passage du phénoménal à l’ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-03","text":"L’agrandissement de la machine est une expérience mentale locale qui change d’échelle et devient une procédure générale de disqualification du réductionnisme mécanique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-04","text":"La distinction entre composé et substance simple relie les unités : l’échec de la mécanique appelle la détermination positive d’un centre perceptif et actif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-05","text":"À l’échelle courante, la simplicité n’est plus une propriété isolée ; elle devient la forme commune d’une multiplicité enveloppée et d’une causalité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-06","text":"La perfection cesse d’être une qualification statique et devient le mécanisme par lequel la Monade produit ses actions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D2","CH_UCIC_P_10:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-07","text":"Les noms « Entéléchie » et « Automate incorporel » sont recodés comme deux expressions terminales d’une même structure d’auto-activité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D4","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut l’équivalence entre simplicité et absence de toute multiplicité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une multiplicité exige une pluralité de substances ou une composition de parties substantielles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_8:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut que la perception soit produite par la seule configuration matérielle, par le mouvement ou par l’accumulation des interactions mécaniques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que l’inspection détaillée d’un mécanisme puisse transformer une relation de poussée en intériorité perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut que l’action interne soit une réception passive ou une conséquence d’une constitution corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_10:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-06","text":"L’exclusion s’intensifie jusqu’au rejet d’une causalité entièrement externe comme modèle suffisant de l’activité substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que la composition spatiale ne soit pas le niveau ultime de toute réalité active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-02","text":"Il faut que l’intériorité ne soit pas identifiable à une structure inspectable, même lorsque cette structure est décrite avec une précision illimitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-03","text":"Il faut que la simplicité puisse contenir de la différenciation sans devenir une totalité composée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-04","text":"Il faut que la perfection possède une efficacité causale ; sinon la transition vers la suffisance et l’automatisme s’effondre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-05","text":"Le rival silencieux du système est une ontologie où seuls les corps composés expliqueraient l’action, la perception et l’intériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSA-01","text":"Le système rend inadmissible un réel dont toute unité serait soit vide de multiplicité, soit composée de parties extérieures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSA-02","text":"Il contourne la possibilité d’une intériorité entièrement réductible à des relations spatiales observables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSA-03","text":"Il refuse la possibilité d’une action dont la source serait toujours extérieure à l’unité agissante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSA-04","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un principe perceptif localisable dans la mécanique : cette absence force l’invention ontologique de la Monade active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-01","text":"L’unité simple n’est pas seulement compatible avec la multiplicité ; elle devient le support nécessaire d’une multiplicité qui ne peut être expliquée par composition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-01","CL_UCIC_06:GA-02","CL_UCIC_06:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PR_8:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-02","text":"L’échec de la mécanique ne laisse pas un vide explicatif indéterminé : il requalifie la substance simple comme régime propre de la perception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-05","CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-03","text":"La perception et la suffisance interne se combinent pour faire de la Monade une unité à la fois réceptive, différenciée et productrice de ses changements.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","CL_UCIC_06:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-04","text":"La notion d’automatisme est inversée : l’absence de corps ne supprime pas l’autonomie, mais permet de la définir par l’intériorité de l’action.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","CL_UCIC_06:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_10:D3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-05","text":"La négation de la perception mécanique et l’affirmation de la perception monadique produisent une division de la causalité en deux régimes irréductibles : poussée externe et modification interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-05","CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-06","text":"La simplicité, la perception et la perfection convergent vers un attracteur unique : une unité non composée dont l’activité interne est auto-produite et perceptive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-01","CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","CL_UCIC_06:GA-09","CL_UCIC_06:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_10:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-01","text":"L’ontologie est stratifiée : les corps expliquent des interactions entre parties, tandis que les substances simples expliquent l’intériorité perceptive et l’activité propre.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:XD-02","CL_UCIC_06:XD-05","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-02","text":"La simplicité change de statut ontologique : elle ne marque plus un déficit de structure, mais une capacité supérieure d’enveloppement et d’auto-détermination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:XD-01","CL_UCIC_06:XD-06","CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-03","text":"La causalité interne n’est plus conçue comme transmission de mouvement, mais comme série de modifications perceptives produites depuis l’unité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","CL_UCIC_06:XD-05","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-04","text":"Le sujet métaphysique devient une unité qui contient de la diversité, perçoit cette diversité et produit ses changements sans devenir un assemblage.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-02","CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","CL_UCIC_06:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_10:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-05","text":"Le temps interne est reconstruit comme succession de perceptions et de changements perceptifs plutôt que comme déplacement de parties.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-06","text":"La méthode du cluster est une négation stratifiée : chaque échec explicatif mécanique prépare une détermination positive de la Monade.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_06:XD-02","CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-07","text":"L’« automate incorporel » constitue la clôture conceptuelle du mouvement : l’autonomie n’est plus le contraire de la simplicité, mais son expression active.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-10","CL_UCIC_06:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_10:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-01","text":"L’inspection mécanique produit l’absence de perception ; cette absence déplace l’explication vers la substance simple ; la substance simple redéfinit ensuite l’action comme perception et changement perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AF1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-02","text":"La pensée révèle une variété ; la variété menace l’unité seulement si celle-ci est conçue comme homogénéité ; le recodage de la simplicité en unité enveloppante résout la menace à un niveau supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-03","text":"La perfection produit la suffisance, la suffisance produit l’action interne, et l’action interne reconduit la perfection comme puissance active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-04","text":"L’agrandissement de la machine intensifie la visibilité des mécanismes et, par cette intensification même, intensifie l’absence d’un principe perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est la Monade comme unité simple, multiple en ses perceptions, autonome dans ses changements et incorporelle dans son automatisme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B01","text":"Unité simple + pensée consciente → objet de pensée différencié → variété enveloppée dans l’unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B02","text":"Variété enveloppée + simplicité non composée → multiplicité interne qui ne se convertit pas en pluralité de substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_8:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B03","text":"Machine perceptive supposée + agrandissement + inspection des parties → poussées mécaniques visibles → absence d’explication perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B04","text":"Absence d’un principe perceptif dans la mécanique → disjonction du composé et de la substance simple → localisation de la perception dans l’unité simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B05","text":"Perception + changements de perception → définition de l’action interne comme modification qualitative plutôt que comme mouvement de parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B06","text":"Perfection interne → suffisance → source des actions → automatisme incorporel → Entéléchie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B07","text":"Les trois voies convergent : multiplicité enveloppée, perception non mécanique et perfection active produisent la Monade comme centre autonome d’activité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B01","text":"Simplicité apparemment homogène → pensée minimale → variété enveloppée → compatibilité entre unité et multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B02","text":"Modèle mécanique de la perception → agrandissement inspectif → visibilité des poussées → échec de la réduction mécanique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AF1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B03","text":"Échec mécanique → substance simple comme lieu de perception → perception et changements comme actions internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AF2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B04","text":"Perfection interne → suffisance → auto-production de l’action → Entéléchie et Automate incorporel → clôture de l’unité simple active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-01","text":"L’opposition entre unité et multiplicité s’effondre et est remplacée par celle entre composition externe et multiplicité enveloppée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-02","text":"Le composé matériel perd le statut de principe explicatif ultime ; il reste un régime de relations mécaniques entre parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-03","text":"L’expérience interne devient un instrument de classification ontologique, non une simple donnée psychologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-04","text":"L’action interne est séparée de la causalité mécanique et reclassée comme variation perceptive auto-produite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-05","text":"L’automatisme devient une catégorie transcorporelle : il désigne toute unité dont l’action procède de son propre principe interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-06","text":"La méthode disponible change d’échelle : il ne faut plus accroître indéfiniment la description mécanique, mais changer de niveau ontologique lorsque l’intériorité demeure absente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets explicites sont l’âme simple, la pensée consciente, la machine perceptive et les Monades créées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_10:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Le système distribue les fonctions : les corps transmettent des mouvements entre parties ; les substances simples enveloppent des perceptions et produisent leurs changements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Les objections et les expériences mentales servent à déplacer la question du degré de complexité mécanique vers le niveau ontologique pertinent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel comporte des unités simples dont le temps interne est la succession de perceptions et de modifications perceptives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — La négation répétée de la mécanique ne reste pas négative : elle performe la construction d’un régime positif d’intériorité autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FL-01","text":"La multiplicité enveloppée est affirmée comme compatible avec la simplicité, mais la transition exacte entre variété phénoménale et multitude ontologique reste partiellement sous-déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FL-02","text":"L’autonomie interne de la Monade est fortement affirmée, tandis que son rapport aux déterminations et interactions externes demeure explicitement non développé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FL-03","text":"La distinction entre mécanique et intériorité est productive, mais elle laisse ouverte la manière dont les structures mécaniques se rapportent aux perceptions monadiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FL-04","text":"L’analogie de l’Automate incorporel accomplit une fonction structurante, mais sa portée exacte reste moins démontrée que la définition de la Monade comme source interne d’action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MP-01","text":"La simplicité mute lorsqu’elle cesse de signifier seulement l’absence de parties et devient capacité d’envelopper une multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MP-02","text":"La mécanique mute de modèle explicatif en opérateur apophatique qui révèle le besoin d’un autre régime de causalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MP-03","text":"La perception mute de contenu phénoménal à principe ontologique de l’action interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MP-04","text":"L’automatisme mute de mécanisme corporel en nom de l’auto-production incorporelle, clôturant la série de déplacements conceptuels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une architecture à deux régimes : des mécanismes composés à l’extérieur et des centres simples d’intériorité active à l’intérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une unité non composée qui contient une multiplicité, la transforme en perceptions et produit ses propres changements internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_10:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système n’est pas d’abord celui du déplacement spatial, mais celui de la succession interne des perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D5","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:HSI-04","text":"La lutte conceptuelle oppose la capture mécanique de l’explication à l’échappée vers une causalité interne, perceptive et incorporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre axiomes : simplicité non composée, multiplicité enveloppée, insuffisance de la mécanique pour expliquer la perception et suffisance interne de la Monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A5","CH_UCIC_P_10:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B02","text":"Ces axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement de la pensée consciente vers la multiplicité, de l’échec mécanique vers la perception simple, puis de la perfection vers l’automatisme incorporel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B03","text":"La compression reste fidèle parce qu’elle conserve la négation progressive de la mécanique et la reconstruction positive d’une unité perceptive et active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination résiduelle concerne le passage exact du contenu phénoménal à la structure monadique et le rapport entre activité interne et déterminations externes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B05","text":"La structure courante est suffisante comme architecture générative, mais elle ne résout pas les médiations qu’elle a délibérément séparées : perception et mécanique, intériorité et extérieur, analogie et démonstration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT7","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T194932753579Z_4f5283f7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 16–18","source_sha256":"ddc49a3a4d596a1be529ee6cbd5f131da0b5eaa1c09b4312de5907042a635182","sha256":"0646a6378eab323bffff99281e7499c08957508d7d3419dacdd8e82e15d296d2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:49:32.756946+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-01","text":"The overall problem is to make the uncompounded simplicity of substance compatible with an internal multiplicity, differentiated perception, and autonomous activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-02","text":"The system reframes simplicity: it is not empty homogeneity, but a unity capable of enveloping a variety.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-03","text":"Conscious thought provides the first indication of an internal structure richer than the apparent unity of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-04","text":"Examination of the mechanical machine produces a cumulative negation: neither figure, nor movement, nor the aggregation of parts suffices to explain perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-05","text":"The imaginary enlargement of the machine transforms mechanical inspection into a demonstration of the absence of a perceptive principle in the parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-06","text":"Perception is then displaced from the composite to simple substance, where it becomes the proper regime of internal activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-07","text":"The perfection of the Monad is traced back to internal sufficiency, then to the autonomous production of its actions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AS-08","text":"The movement is cumulative and mutational: the simple unity passes from being the support of multiplicity to a perceptive center, then to an active source and incorporeal automaton.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Simple substance has no constituent parts, but this absence of composition does not eliminate its internal determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] The relevant multiplicity is enveloped within unity; it does not consist in a plurality of substantial supports.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Every conscious thought has an object whose structure includes a differentiated variety.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A3","CH_UCIC_PR_8:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Perception converts a phenomenal datum into an indication of internal ontological structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Figures, movements, and interactions among parts do not constitute a sufficient explanation of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:A1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] An increase in scale does not produce mechanical perception; it makes more manifest the absence of a perceptive principle in the machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AS2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Simple substance becomes the ontological locus of perception and its changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] The internal action of simple substance consists in a succession of perceptions and perceptive modifications, not in a displacement of parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:A9","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] The perfection of a Monad entails a sufficiency that makes it the source of its internal actions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:A3","CH_UCIC_P_10:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Automatism is detached from corporeality and redefined as the spontaneity of a unity whose principle of action is internal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Simplicity ultimately designates an uncompounded, perceptive, differentiated, and self-active unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D1","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Mechanics is relegated to the regime of relations among parts, while perception and internal action belong to simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-01","text":"Simplicity persists as a premise, but its function mutates: initially a property of the soul, it subsequently becomes the condition of autonomous internal activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A1","CH_UCIC_P_10:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-02","text":"Multiplicity first returns as a variety of the object thought, then as the general regime of the Monad's internal perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-03","text":"The machine passes from a purportedly explanatory model to an apophatic device that exposes the absence of perception in mechanical composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AS3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-04","text":"Perception migrates from the status of a phenomenon to be explained to that of constitutive content of internal activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-05","text":"Internal action shifts from the pushing among parts to the successive variation of perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-06","text":"The automaton undergoes a functional inversion: it no longer primarily designates a bodily mechanism, but an incorporeal source of action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RMD-07","text":"Bayle's objection remains local and disappears after serving to stabilize the compatibility between simplicity and multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX5","CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-01","text":"The reference to Bayle remains local: it designates a specific interpretive difficulty, not a necessary component of the general architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A7","CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-02","text":"Minimal thought is a local argumentative machine; at the scale of the cluster, it becomes the first operator of passage from the phenomenal to the ontological.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-03","text":"The enlargement of the machine is a local thought experiment that changes scale and becomes a general procedure for disqualifying mechanical reductionism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-04","text":"The distinction between composite and simple substance connects the units: the failure of mechanics calls for the positive determination of a perceptive and active center.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-05","text":"At the current scale, simplicity is no longer an isolated property; it becomes the common form of an enveloped multiplicity and internal causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-06","text":"Perfection ceases to be a static qualification and becomes the mechanism through which the Monad produces its actions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D2","CH_UCIC_P_10:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:CGD-07","text":"The names “Entéléchie” and “Automate incorporel” are recoded as two terminal expressions of one and the same structure of self-activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:D4","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the equivalence between simplicity and the absence of all internal multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the claim that a multiplicity requires a plurality of substances or a composition of substantial parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX2","CH_UCIC_PR_8:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the claim that perception is produced by material configuration alone, by movement, or by the accumulation of mechanical interactions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:NX1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that detailed inspection of a mechanism could transform a relation of pushing into perceptive interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the claim that internal action is passive reception or a consequence of bodily constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_10:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:GNX-06","text":"The exclusion intensifies to the rejection of an entirely external causality as a sufficient model of substantial activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, spatial composition must not be the ultimate level of all active reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-02","text":"Interiority must not be identifiable with an inspectable structure, even when that structure is described with unlimited precision.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-03","text":"Simplicity must be able to contain differentiation without becoming a composite whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-04","text":"Perfection must possess causal efficacy; otherwise the transition to sufficiency and automatism collapses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:DBN-05","text":"The silent rival of the system is an ontology in which only composite bodies would explain action, perception, and interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSA-01","text":"The system renders inadmissible a reality in which every unity would be either devoid of multiplicity or composed of external parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSA-02","text":"It avoids the possibility of an interiority entirely reducible to observable spatial relations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSA-03","text":"It rejects the possibility of an action whose source would always be external to the acting unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSA-04","text":"The structuring absence is that of a perceptive principle locatable in mechanics: this absence compels the ontological invention of the active Monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-01","text":"Simple unity is not merely compatible with multiplicity; it becomes the necessary support of a multiplicity that cannot be explained by composition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-01","CL_UCIC_06:GA-02","CL_UCIC_06:GA-05","CH_UCIC_PR_8:D3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-02","text":"The failure of mechanics does not leave an indeterminate explanatory void: it requalifies simple substance as the proper regime of perception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-05","CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-03","text":"Perception and internal sufficiency combine to make the Monad a unity at once receptive, differentiated, and productive of its changes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","CL_UCIC_06:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-04","text":"The notion of automatism is inverted: the absence of a body does not eliminate autonomy, but makes it possible to define it through the interiority of action.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","CL_UCIC_06:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_10:D3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-05","text":"The negation of mechanical perception and the affirmation of monadic perception produce a division of causality into two irreducible regimes: external pushing and internal modification.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-05","CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:XD-06","text":"Simplicity, perception, and perfection converge toward a single attractor: an uncompounded unity whose internal activity is self-produced and perceptive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-01","CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","CL_UCIC_06:GA-09","CL_UCIC_06:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_10:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-01","text":"Ontology is stratified: bodies explain interactions among parts, whereas simple substances explain perceptive interiority and proper activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:XD-02","CL_UCIC_06:XD-05","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-02","text":"Simplicity changes ontological status: it no longer marks a deficit of structure, but a superior capacity for enveloping and self-determination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:XD-01","CL_UCIC_06:XD-06","CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-03","text":"Internal causality is no longer conceived as the transmission of movement, but as a series of perceptive modifications produced from the unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","CL_UCIC_06:XD-05","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-04","text":"The metaphysical subject becomes a unity that contains diversity, perceives that diversity, and produces its changes without becoming an assemblage.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-02","CL_UCIC_06:GA-07","CL_UCIC_06:GA-09","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_10:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-05","text":"Internal time is reconstructed as a succession of perceptions and perceptive changes rather than as a displacement of parts.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-08","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-06","text":"The method of the cluster is a stratified negation: each mechanical explanatory failure prepares a positive determination of the Monad.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_06:XD-02","CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:BSD-07","text":"The “incorporeal automaton” constitutes the conceptual closure of the movement: autonomy is no longer the opposite of simplicity, but its active expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-10","CL_UCIC_06:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_10:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-01","text":"Mechanical inspection produces the absence of perception; this absence shifts explanation toward simple substance; simple substance then redefines action as perception and perceptive change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AF1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-02","text":"Thought reveals a variety; variety threatens unity only if the latter is conceived as homogeneity; the recoding of simplicity as enveloping unity resolves the threat at a higher level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-03","text":"Perfection produces sufficiency, sufficiency produces internal action, and internal action restores perfection as active power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-04","text":"The enlargement of the machine intensifies the visibility of mechanisms and, through that very intensification, intensifies the absence of a perceptive principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is the Monad as a simple unity, multiple in its perceptions, autonomous in its changes, and incorporeal in its automatism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B01","text":"Simple unity + conscious thought → differentiated object of thought → variety enveloped in unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B02","text":"Enveloped variety + uncompounded simplicity → internal multiplicity that does not convert into a plurality of substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_8:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B03","text":"Supposed perceptive machine + enlargement + inspection of parts → visible mechanical pushes → absence of perceptive explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B04","text":"Absence of a perceptive principle in mechanics → disjunction of composite and simple substance → localization of perception in simple unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B05","text":"Perception + changes of perception → definition of internal action as qualitative modification rather than movement of parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B06","text":"Internal perfection → sufficiency → source of actions → incorporeal automatism → Entéléchie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B07","text":"The three paths converge: enveloped multiplicity, non-mechanical perception, and active perfection produce the Monad as an autonomous center of activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B01","text":"Apparently homogeneous simplicity → minimal thought → enveloped variety → compatibility between unity and multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B02","text":"Mechanical model of perception → inspectory enlargement → visibility of pushes → failure of mechanical reduction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AF1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B03","text":"Mechanical failure → simple substance as locus of perception → perception and changes as internal actions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:AF2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B04","text":"Internal perfection → sufficiency → self-production of action → Entéléchie and Automate incorporel → closure of active simple unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-01","text":"The opposition between unity and multiplicity collapses and is replaced by that between external composition and enveloped multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-02","text":"The material composite loses the status of ultimate explanatory principle; it remains a regime of mechanical relations among parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-03","text":"Internal experience becomes an instrument of ontological classification, not a mere psychological datum.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-04","text":"Internal action is separated from mechanical causality and reclassified as self-produced perceptive variation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-05","text":"Automatism becomes a transcorporeal category: it designates every unity whose action proceeds from its own internal principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_10:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MME-06","text":"The available method changes scale: one must no longer indefinitely increase mechanical description, but change ontological level when interiority remains absent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit objects are the simple soul, conscious thought, the perceptive machine, and created Monads.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_10:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — The system distributes functions: bodies transmit movements among parts; simple substances envelop perceptions and produce their changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Objections and thought experiments serve to shift the question from the degree of mechanical complexity to the relevant ontological level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ALT3","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Reality includes simple unities whose internal time is the succession of perceptions and perceptive modifications.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ALT4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The repeated negation of mechanics does not remain negative: it performs the construction of a positive regime of autonomous interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FL-01","text":"Enveloped multiplicity is affirmed as compatible with simplicity, but the exact transition between phenomenal variety and ontological multitude remains partially underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT5","CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FL-02","text":"The Monad's internal autonomy is strongly affirmed, while its relation to external determinations and interactions remains explicitly undeveloped.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FL-03","text":"The distinction between mechanics and interiority is productive, but it leaves open the manner in which mechanical structures relate to monadic perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:FL-04","text":"The analogy of the Automate incorporel fulfills a structuring function, but its exact scope remains less demonstrated than the definition of the Monad as an internal source of action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MP-01","text":"Simplicity mutates when it ceases to signify merely the absence of parts and becomes the capacity to envelop a multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:ME1","CH_UCIC_PR_8:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MP-02","text":"Mechanics mutates from an explanatory model into an apophatic operator that reveals the need for another regime of causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ME2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MP-03","text":"Perception mutates from phenomenal content into an ontological principle of internal action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:SD2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MP-04","text":"Automatism mutates from a bodily mechanism into the name of incorporeal self-production, closing the series of conceptual displacements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_10:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_10:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:HSI-01","text":"Implicit reality is an architecture with two regimes: composite mechanisms externally and simple centers of active interiority internally.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:FGS4","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes an uncompounded unity that contains a multiplicity, transforms it into perceptions, and produces its own internal changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_10:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:HSI-03","text":"The system's time is not primarily that of spatial displacement, but that of the internal succession of perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:D5","CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:HSI-04","text":"The conceptual struggle opposes the mechanical capture of explanation to the escape toward an internal, perceptive, and incorporeal causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_9:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_10:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four axioms: uncompounded simplicity, enveloped multiplicity, the insufficiency of mechanics to explain perception, and the Monad's internal sufficiency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:A2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:A5","CH_UCIC_P_10:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B02","text":"These axioms suffice to reconstruct the movement from conscious thought toward multiplicity, from mechanical failure toward simple perception, then from perfection toward incorporeal automatism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT1","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B03","text":"The compression remains faithful because it preserves the progressive negation of mechanics and the positive reconstruction of a perceptive and active unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT2","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B04","text":"Residual indeterminacy concerns the exact passage from phenomenal content to monadic structure and the relation between internal activity and external determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B05","text":"The current structure is sufficient as a generative architecture, but it does not resolve the mediations that it has deliberately separated: perception and mechanics, interiority and exteriority, analogy and demonstration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_PR_8:MRT7","CH_UCIC_PR_9:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_10:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_06@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_06:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 16–18","context":"Proposition 16 · Proposition 17 · Proposition 18"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 19–21","order":7,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_11","CH_UCIC_P_12","CH_UCIC_P_13"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_07@R001","sha256":"380788ba0ce567657a319b30bce50f8b558e8fc1093cf66f2c01fa62cafe8ba8","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-01","text":"Le problème global consiste à déterminer si l’âme se définit par ses manifestations perceptives actuelles ou par une structure de capacités qui les excède.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-02","text":"L’extension générale du terme « âme » est conservée comme possibilité logique, puis resserrée par une distinction entre perception, sentiment, perception distincte et mémoire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_11:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-03","text":"La simple substance fournit le genre commun, tandis que les degrés de perception et la mémoire organisent une différenciation terminologique interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_11:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-04","text":"L’expérience de l’absence de souvenir et de perception distincte met cette classification en crise en rendant momentanément l’âme indiscernable d’une simple Monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A2","CH_UCIC_P_12:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-05","text":"La crise est recodée par la temporalité et par la persistance d’affections perceptives indistinctes : l’absence de distinction n’est pas une absence de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D2","CH_UCIC_P_13:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-06","text":"Le mouvement produit une architecture où l’identité de l’âme dépend moins d’un état phénoménal que de la continuité d’une capacité perceptive graduée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-07","text":"La clôture ne supprime pas la différence entre âme et Monade : elle la déplace du registre de l’apparition immédiate vers celui de la disposition, de la succession et de la classification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_12:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Une substance simple ne peut ni périr ni subsister sans affection, et cette affection est une perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A1","CH_UCIC_P_13:A2","CH_UCIC_P_13:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La perception n’est pas identique à la perception distincte : elle peut subsister sous une forme multiple, petite et indistincte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A4","CH_UCIC_P_13:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] La simplicité substantielle constitue un genre commun qui ne suffit pas à fixer la dénomination particulière de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A1","CH_UCIC_P_11:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Le terme « âme » passe d’une extension générale applicable aux substances simples à une désignation restreinte des formes de perception plus distinctes accompagnées de mémoire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A2","CH_UCIC_P_11:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] La mémoire passe du statut de marqueur classificatoire manifeste à celui de capacité dont l’absence actuelle ne détruit pas l’identité de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A7","CH_UCIC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La distinction entre l’âme et la simple Monade est temporelle et dispositionnelle plutôt que constamment phénoménale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D2","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] L’indistinction perceptive est une modalité interne de la perception et non un degré zéro de l’activité substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:D2","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Aucun état d’évanouissement, de sommeil sans songe ou de mort temporaire ne suffit à conclure à la destruction de la substance ou à l’abolition de toute perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A3","CH_UCIC_P_13:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Le système converge vers la dissociation entre l’existence métaphysique d’une substance, l’accessibilité phénoménale de ses perceptions et l’usage gradué des termes qui la désignent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_13:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] La réalité de l’âme ne se laisse pas épuiser par ce qui est actuellement distingué, mémorisé ou conscient.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_12:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-01","text":"La perception revient comme propriété générique de la substance simple, puis comme continuum différencié dont la distinction consciente ne constitue qu’un degré local.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-02","text":"La distinction perceptive conserve sa fonction de critère terminologique, mais perd sa fonction de critère ontologique exhaustif lorsque l’état présent devient indistinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_13:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-03","text":"La mémoire revient d’abord comme condition de l’appellation restreinte « âme », puis devient une capacité dont l’interruption temporaire révèle le caractère non actuel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-04","text":"La Monade passe de catégorie ontologique générale à terme-limite de comparaison lorsque l’âme, privée momentanément de distinction, lui devient phénoménalement indiscernable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D2","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-05","text":"L’absence de perception distincte migre d’une apparence de privation vers une forme de perception comprimée par la multiplicité des petites affections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_13:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-06","text":"Le sommeil, l’évanouissement et la mort temporaire cessent d’être des preuves de perte et deviennent des cas-limites servant à tester la continuité de la substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_13:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-01","text":"La détermination lexicale des usages respectifs de « Monades », « Entéléchies » et « Ames » reste locale à la première unité inférieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_11:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-02","text":"L’exemple humain de la défaillance ou du sommeil sans songe reste local comme scène empirique, mais devient à ce niveau un test de l’insuffisance des états actuels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A3","CH_UCIC_P_12:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-03","text":"L’analogie animale de la mort temporaire reste une illustration locale, mais acquiert une fonction inter-unités en dissociant disparition phénoménale et destruction substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A7","CH_UCIC_P_13:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-04","text":"Le changement d’échelle consiste à relier la classification terminologique, la continuité temporelle et la microstructure perceptive dans une seule architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-05","text":"La transition majeure est catalysée par l’interaction entre deux thèses qui ne peuvent être maintenues séparément : la mémoire classe l’âme, mais son absence actuelle ne l’abolit pas.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-06","text":"L’opposition simple entre âme et non-âme devient obsolète et est remplacée par une architecture à plusieurs niveaux de perception, de mémoire et de persistance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_13:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-01","text":"Le système rejette l’identification de l’âme avec l’ensemble de ses manifestations perceptives actuellement accessibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut que la perception simple, la perception indistincte ou l’absence de mémoire suffisent isolément à fixer le sens restreint d’« âme ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-03","text":"Il refuse de convertir une indiscernabilité phénoménale en identité ontologique avec une simple Monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_12:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que l’évanouissement ou la mort temporaire constituent des preuves directes d’une destruction de la substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_13:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-05","text":"Il disqualifie toute frontière conceptuelle fondée sur l’alternative perception totale ou absence totale de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit faux le modèle d’une substance simple absolument dépourvue de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_13:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que soit faux le modèle selon lequel un état phénoménal isolé révélerait immédiatement le statut ontologique complet de la substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie une taxonomie fixe où la possession ou l’absence actuelle de mémoire suffirait à séparer définitivement les Ames des Monades.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_12:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:DBN-04","text":"Il rend inadmissible la coupure entre existence substantielle et affection perceptive, même lorsque cette affection n’est ni distincte ni consciente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_13:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSA-01","text":"L’absence absolue de perception est la possibilité ontologique que l’architecture contourne et forclôt simultanément.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSA-02","text":"Le système ne peut admettre une transparence phénoménale complète : ce qui n’est pas distingué peut néanmoins constituer l’affection réelle de la substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_13:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSA-03","text":"L’absence qui structure tout le dispositif est l’absence de distinction, laquelle devient productive précisément parce qu’elle ne coïncide jamais avec le néant perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSA-04","text":"L’impossibilité ultime est celle d’une identité entièrement donnée dans un instant : l’âme exige une continuité de transformations qui excède chaque état local.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-01","text":"La classification graduée des substances simples devient dynamique lorsque l’expérience de l’indistinction montre qu’un même sujet peut traverser plusieurs positions fonctionnelles sans changer de substance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-03","CL_UCIC_07:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_11:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-02","text":"La mémoire fonctionne comme critère de nomination plutôt que comme condition permanente de l’identité, parce que son interruption est compatible avec la reprise d’une capacité supérieure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-04","CL_UCIC_07:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_11:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-03","text":"L’indistinction perceptive fournit le mécanisme qui réconcilie la permanence de l’affection avec l’absence de perception distincte dans l’expérience.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-01","CL_UCIC_07:GA-02","CH_UCIC_P_13:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_13:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-04","text":"La différence entre âme et Monade devient une différence de trajectoire et de disposition, non une différence phénoménale immédiatement présente dans chaque instant.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-06","CL_UCIC_07:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_12:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-05","text":"La négation répétée de la perception zéro produit positivement un modèle de réalité comme champ continu d’affections à degrés variables de distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-01","CL_UCIC_07:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-06","text":"La tension entre la définition restreinte de l’âme et l’absence temporaire de ses marqueurs manifestes force la distinction entre identité ontologique et classement terminologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-04","CL_UCIC_07:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_12:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-01","text":"L’identité substantielle devient une propriété temporelle de continuité capable de traverser des interruptions phénoménales sans se réduire à la présence constante d’un contenu distinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_12:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-02","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme une échelle de micro-affections dont les états conscients et distincts ne sont que des configurations locales.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_13:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-03","text":"L’épistémologie du système devient indirecte : la différence ontologique se déduit de la succession et de la capacité de transformation plutôt que d’une observation statique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-04","text":"Le vocabulaire ontologique cesse de simplement nommer des espèces fixes et devient un instrument de cartographie des degrés opératoires de la perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_11:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-05","text":"La négation de l’absence perceptive absolue engendre une ontologie positive de la continuité, dans laquelle l’inconscience est une compression de l’activité plutôt qu’un dehors de l’activité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_13:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-06","text":"Le sujet n’est plus l’unité d’un état transparent, mais le parcours d’une substance dont les capacités excèdent périodiquement leur manifestation actuelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D3","CH_UCIC_P_12:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-01","text":"Extension générale de l’âme → resserrement terminologique → crise produite par l’absence de mémoire → recodage temporel → maintien d’une identité excédant l’état présent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D1","CH_UCIC_P_12:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-02","text":"Absence de distinction → apparence d’absence de perception → rappel de l’affection persistante → modèle des petites perceptions → conversion de l’indistinction en mode perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_13:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-03","text":"Le terme « âme » devient d’abord une catégorie, puis un problème de classement, puis un nom pour une capacité de reprise à travers l’interruption.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A2","CH_UCIC_P_12:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-04","text":"La répétition des cas d’évanouissement, de sommeil et de mort temporaire signale un changement de phase : l’absence phénoménale devient preuve négative de la non-réduction ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel du cluster est la différence entre perception comme affection toujours présente et perception distincte comme régime local d’accessibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A3","CH_UCIC_P_13:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B01","text":"Poser la perception et l’appétit comme base générale de la substance simple, puis réserver l’âme à une différenciation de la perception accompagnée de mémoire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A1","CH_UCIC_P_11:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B02","text":"Introduire un état sans souvenir ni perception distincte afin de produire une indiscernabilité locale entre âme et Monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B03","text":"Exploiter la non-durabilité de cet état pour faire apparaître une capacité qui ne se confond pas avec sa manifestation momentanément suspendue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A5","CH_UCIC_P_12:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B04","text":"Requalifier l’absence de distinction comme multiplicité de petites perceptions et maintenir ainsi une affection substantielle continue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_13:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B05","text":"Produire la synthèse suivante : une âme peut être terminologiquement définie par des opérations supérieures sans être ontologiquement détruite lorsque ces opérations cessent d’être manifestes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:AFM-B01","text":"Extension générale de l’âme → différenciation par perception et mémoire → indiscernabilité phénoménale → temporalisation de la différence → recodage de l’indistinction en perception persistante → séparation entre identité substantielle et classement terminologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_13:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:AFM-B02","text":"Apparence d’absence → négation de la perception zéro → recours aux petites perceptions → continuité de l’affection → clôture sur une identité dispositionalement excédentaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:AF2","CH_UCIC_P_13:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-01","text":"La frontière pertinente n’oppose plus perception et non-perception, mais perception distincte et perception indistincte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_13:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-02","text":"Les états d’inconscience sont reclassés comme modifications internes de la perception et non comme sorties de l’ordre perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_13:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-03","text":"L’objet d’analyse se déplace de l’état mental isolé vers la trajectoire des états et vers la capacité de transformation qui les relie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-04","text":"La terminologie devient une carte à deux axes : genre ontologique des substances simples et degré fonctionnel de leurs opérations perceptives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-05","text":"Une opposition prétendument absolue entre âme et non-âme s’effondre au profit d’une architecture graduée, temporelle et dispositionnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B01","text":"**Surface level** — Les objets explicites sont les termes « Monades », « Entéléchies » et « Ames », ainsi que les états de sommeil, d’évanouissement et de mort temporaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_12:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B02","text":"**Structural level** — Le mécanisme central est une distribution en degrés de perception, de distinction et de mémoire, soutenue par la continuité de l’affection substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_13:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B03","text":"**Metastrategic level** — La preuve doit être déplacée de l’état présent vers la transition entre états, et de l’apparence phénoménale vers la capacité dispositionnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_12:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B04","text":"**Ontological / Temporal level** — L’identité est conçue comme une continuité capable de traverser l’interruption perceptive sans perdre toute affection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_13:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B05","text":"**Methodological / Performative level** — Le système accomplit sa thèse en transformant chaque apparence de privation en opération de distinction entre absence manifeste et persistance cachée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_13:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FL-01","text":"La mémoire est posée comme condition de l’âme au sens restreint, mais son absence actuelle est compatible avec la persistance de l’âme ; la distinction entre critère de classement et condition d’identité reste indispensable et partiellement sous-déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FL-02","text":"L’âme est affirmée comme plus qu’une simple Monade alors qu’elle peut lui être momentanément indiscernable ; la différence ontologique repose donc sur une preuve indirecte et non sur une distinction actuellement observable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A4","CH_UCIC_P_12:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FL-03","text":"La permanence métaphysique de la perception est établie par la nécessité d’une affection, mais la nature exacte de cette perception indistincte demeure moins déterminée que sa fonction architecturale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_11:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MP-01","text":"Le concept de « perception » mute d’une capacité générale à un continuum interne dont la perception distincte devient un degré, et non la définition exhaustive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A3","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MP-02","text":"Le concept d’« âme » mute d’un genre extensible en nom d’une trajectoire disposant d’une capacité de reprise après l’interruption phénoménale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D1","CH_UCIC_P_12:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MP-03","text":"L’inconscience mute d’un indice apparent de privation en opérateur théorique qui révèle la différence entre affection réelle et accessibilité consciente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:HSI-01","text":"La réalité apparaît implicitement comme un champ continu d’affections perceptives, où la distinction consciente est une modulation locale plutôt qu’une condition de l’existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une trajectoire substantielle capable de traverser des régimes d’indistinction, de reprendre certaines opérations et de demeurer identique à travers leurs interruptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est le milieu qui transforme une apparente perte de l’âme en suspension transitoire d’une manifestation, puis en indice d’une capacité excédentaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D2","CH_UCIC_P_12:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:HSI-04","text":"La voie d’échappée du système ne consiste pas à sortir de la perception, mais à passer d’un régime indistinct à un régime plus distinct sans abolir la continuité qui les relie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_13:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre axiomes : toute substance simple persiste, toute persistance implique une affection perceptive, la distinction n’est qu’un degré de perception, et l’âme excède ses manifestations actuelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A1","CH_UCIC_P_13:A2","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MRT-B02","text":"Ces axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le passage de la classification terminologique à la continuité temporelle, puis de l’indistinction phénoménale à la persistance perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_13:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante porte sur le statut exact du sentiment, sur la relation entre perception distincte et mémoire et sur la nature de l’excédent désigné par « quelque chose de plus ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_12:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MRT-B04","text":"La compression reste fidèle au mouvement réel parce qu’elle conserve la boucle décisive : privation apparente → indistinction → affection persistante → différence dispositionnelle ; elle ne peut toutefois remplacer les cas-limites qui donnent à cette boucle sa force probatoire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_13:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195007059152Z_655d6dbd","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 19–21","source_sha256":"380788ba0ce567657a319b30bce50f8b558e8fc1093cf66f2c01fa62cafe8ba8","sha256":"c71f649779b257bfe2e15d16fd48486838bc43ae94cfcc993ff845c7a2556737","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:50:07.063739+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-01","text":"The overall problem consists in determining whether the soul is defined by its current perceptual manifestations or by a structure of capacities that exceeds them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-02","text":"The general extension of the term « soul » is preserved as a logical possibility, then narrowed by a distinction between perception, feeling, distinct perception, and memory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_11:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-03","text":"Simple substance provides the common genus, while degrees of perception and memory organize an internal terminological differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_11:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-04","text":"The experience of the absence of recollection and distinct perception throws this classification into crisis by momentarily rendering the soul indiscernible from a simple Monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A2","CH_UCIC_P_12:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-05","text":"The crisis is recoded through temporality and the persistence of indistinct perceptual affections: the absence of distinction is not an absence of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D2","CH_UCIC_P_13:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-06","text":"The movement produces an architecture in which the identity of the soul depends less on a phenomenal state than on the continuity of a graded perceptual capacity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BS-07","text":"The closure does not eliminate the difference between soul and Monad: it displaces it from the register of immediate appearance to that of disposition, succession, and classification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_12:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A simple substance can neither perish nor subsist without affection, and this affection is a perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A1","CH_UCIC_P_13:A2","CH_UCIC_P_13:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Perception is not identical with distinct perception: it may subsist in a multiple, minute, and indistinct form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A4","CH_UCIC_P_13:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Substantial simplicity constitutes a common genus that is insufficient to establish the particular designation of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A1","CH_UCIC_P_11:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] The term « soul » passes from a general extension applicable to simple substances to a restricted designation of more distinct forms of perception accompanied by memory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A2","CH_UCIC_P_11:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Memory passes from the status of a manifest classificatory marker to that of a capacity whose current absence does not destroy the identity of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A7","CH_UCIC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] The distinction between the soul and the simple Monad is temporal and dispositional rather than constantly phenomenal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D2","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Perceptual indistinction is an internal modality of perception and not a zero degree of substantial activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:D2","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] No state of fainting, dreamless sleep, or temporary death suffices to conclude either the destruction of the substance or the abolition of all perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A3","CH_UCIC_P_13:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] The system converges toward the dissociation between the metaphysical existence of a substance, the phenomenal accessibility of its perceptions, and the graded use of the terms that designate it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_13:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] The reality of the soul cannot be exhausted by what is currently distinguished, remembered, or conscious.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_12:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-01","text":"Perception recurs as a generic property of simple substance, then as a differentiated continuum of which conscious distinction constitutes only a local degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-02","text":"Perceptual distinction retains its function as a terminological criterion, but loses its function as an exhaustive ontological criterion when the present state becomes indistinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_13:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-03","text":"Memory first recurs as a condition of the restricted appellation « soul », then becomes a capacity whose temporary interruption reveals its non-current character.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-04","text":"The Monad passes from a general ontological category to a limiting term of comparison when the soul, momentarily deprived of distinction, becomes phenomenally indiscernible from it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D2","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-05","text":"The absence of distinct perception migrates from an appearance of privation toward a form of perception compressed by the multiplicity of minute affections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_13:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RMD-06","text":"Sleep, fainting, and temporary death cease to be proofs of loss and become limiting cases serving to test the continuity of substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_13:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-01","text":"The lexical determination of the respective uses of « Monads », « Entelechies », and « Souls » remains local to the first lower unit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_11:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-02","text":"The human example of fainting or dreamless sleep remains local as an empirical scene, but at this level becomes a test of the insufficiency of current states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A3","CH_UCIC_P_12:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-03","text":"The animal analogy of temporary death remains a local illustration, but acquires an inter-unit function by dissociating phenomenal disappearance from substantial destruction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A7","CH_UCIC_P_13:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-04","text":"The change of scale consists in linking terminological classification, temporal continuity, and perceptual microstructure within a single architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-05","text":"The major transition is catalyzed by the interaction between two theses that cannot be maintained separately: memory classifies the soul, but its current absence does not abolish it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:CGD-06","text":"The simple opposition between soul and non-soul becomes obsolete and is replaced by an architecture of multiple levels of perception, memory, and persistence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_13:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects the identification of the soul with the totality of its currently accessible perceptual manifestations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that simple perception, indistinct perception, or the absence of memory alone suffice to establish the restricted meaning of « soul ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_12:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-03","text":"It refuses to convert phenomenal indiscernibility into ontological identity with a simple Monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_12:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that fainting or temporary death constitute direct proofs of a destruction of simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_13:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:GNX-05","text":"It disqualifies every conceptual boundary founded on the alternative of total perception or total absence of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the model of a simple substance absolutely devoid of perception must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_13:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:DBN-02","text":"The model according to which an isolated phenomenal state would immediately reveal the complete ontological status of the substance must likewise be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies a fixed taxonomy in which the possession or current absence of memory would suffice definitively to separate Souls from Monads.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_12:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:DBN-04","text":"It renders inadmissible the division between substantial existence and perceptual affection, even when this affection is neither distinct nor conscious.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_13:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSA-01","text":"The absolute absence of perception is the ontological possibility that the architecture simultaneously circumvents and forecloses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSA-02","text":"The system cannot admit complete phenomenal transparency: what is not distinguished may nevertheless constitute the real affection of the substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_13:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSA-03","text":"The absence that structures the entire apparatus is the absence of distinction, which becomes productive precisely because it never coincides with perceptual nothingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSA-04","text":"The ultimate impossibility is that of an identity wholly given in an instant: the soul requires a continuity of transformations that exceeds every local state.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-01","text":"The graded classification of simple substances becomes dynamic when the experience of indistinction shows that one and the same subject can pass through several functional positions without changing substance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-03","CL_UCIC_07:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_11:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-02","text":"Memory functions as a criterion of naming rather than as a permanent condition of identity, because its interruption is compatible with the resumption of a higher capacity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-04","CL_UCIC_07:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_11:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-03","text":"Perceptual indistinction provides the mechanism that reconciles the permanence of affection with the absence of distinct perception in experience.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-01","CL_UCIC_07:GA-02","CH_UCIC_P_13:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_13:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-04","text":"The difference between soul and Monad becomes a difference of trajectory and disposition, not a phenomenal difference immediately present in every instant.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-06","CL_UCIC_07:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_12:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-05","text":"The repeated negation of zero perception positively produces a model of reality as a continuous field of affections with variable degrees of distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-01","CL_UCIC_07:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_13:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:XD-06","text":"The tension between the restricted definition of the soul and the temporary absence of its manifest markers compels the distinction between ontological identity and terminological classification.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-04","CL_UCIC_07:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_12:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-01","text":"Substantial identity becomes a temporal property of continuity capable of passing through phenomenal interruptions without being reduced to the constant presence of a distinct content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_12:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-02","text":"The real is reclassified as a scale of micro-affections, of which conscious and distinct states are only local configurations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_13:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-03","text":"The epistemology of the system becomes indirect: ontological difference is deduced from succession and the capacity for transformation rather than from static observation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-04","text":"Ontological vocabulary ceases merely to name fixed species and becomes an instrument for mapping the operative degrees of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_11:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-05","text":"The negation of absolute perceptual absence generates a positive ontology of continuity, in which unconsciousness is a compression of activity rather than an outside of activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_13:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:BSD-06","text":"The subject is no longer the unity of a transparent state, but the trajectory of a substance whose capacities periodically exceed their current manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D3","CH_UCIC_P_12:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-01","text":"General extension of the soul → terminological narrowing → crisis produced by the absence of memory → temporal recoding → maintenance of an identity exceeding the present state.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D1","CH_UCIC_P_12:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-02","text":"Absence of distinction → appearance of absence of perception → reminder of persistent affection → model of small perceptions → conversion of indistinction into a perceptual mode.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_13:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-03","text":"The term « soul » first becomes a category, then a problem of classification, then a name for a capacity of resumption through interruption.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A2","CH_UCIC_P_12:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-04","text":"The repetition of cases of fainting, sleep, and temporary death signals a phase change: phenomenal absence becomes negative proof of ontological non-reduction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor of the cluster is the difference between perception as an always present affection and distinct perception as a local regime of accessibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A3","CH_UCIC_P_13:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B01","text":"Posit perception and appetite as the general basis of simple substance, then reserve the soul for a differentiation of perception accompanied by memory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A1","CH_UCIC_P_11:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B02","text":"Introduce a state without recollection or distinct perception in order to produce a local indiscernibility between soul and Monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_12:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B03","text":"Exploit the non-durability of this state to make appear a capacity that is not identical with its momentarily suspended manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A5","CH_UCIC_P_12:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B04","text":"Requalify the absence of distinction as a multiplicity of small perceptions and thus maintain a continuous substantial affection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_13:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FGS-B05","text":"Produce the following synthesis: a soul may be terminologically defined by higher operations without being ontologically destroyed when these operations cease to be manifest.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:AFM-B01","text":"General extension of the soul → differentiation through perception and memory → phenomenal indiscernibility → temporalization of the difference → recoding of indistinction as persistent perception → separation between substantial identity and terminological classification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_13:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:AFM-B02","text":"Appearance of absence → negation of zero perception → recourse to small perceptions → continuity of affection → closure upon a dispositionally exceeding identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:AF2","CH_UCIC_P_13:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-01","text":"The relevant boundary no longer opposes perception and non-perception, but distinct perception and indistinct perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_13:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-02","text":"States of unconsciousness are reclassified as internal modifications of perception and not as departures from the perceptual order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_13:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-03","text":"The object of analysis shifts from the isolated mental state to the trajectory of states and to the capacity for transformation that links them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-04","text":"Terminology becomes a map with two axes: the ontological genus of simple substances and the functional degree of their perceptual operations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_11:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MME-05","text":"A supposedly absolute opposition between soul and non-soul collapses in favor of a graded, temporal, and dispositional architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B01","text":"**Surface level** — The explicit objects are the terms « Monads », « Entelechies », and « Souls », as well as the states of sleep, fainting, and temporary death.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_12:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B02","text":"**Structural level** — The central mechanism is a distribution into degrees of perception, distinction, and memory, supported by the continuity of substantial affection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_13:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B03","text":"**Metastrategic level** — Proof must be displaced from the present state to the transition between states, and from phenomenal appearance to dispositional capacity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_12:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B04","text":"**Ontological / Temporal level** — Identity is conceived as a continuity capable of passing through perceptual interruption without losing all affection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_13:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B05","text":"**Methodological / Performative level** — The system accomplishes its thesis by transforming every appearance of privation into an operation of distinction between manifest absence and hidden persistence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_13:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FL-01","text":"Memory is posited as a condition of the soul in the restricted sense, but its current absence is compatible with the persistence of the soul; the distinction between criterion of classification and condition of identity remains indispensable and partially underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D4","CH_UCIC_P_12:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FL-02","text":"The soul is asserted to be more than a simple Monad while it may be momentarily indiscernible from it; ontological difference thus rests on indirect proof and not on a currently observable distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:A4","CH_UCIC_P_12:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:FL-03","text":"The metaphysical permanence of perception is established by the necessity of an affection, but the exact nature of this indistinct perception remains less determined than its architectural function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_11:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MP-01","text":"The concept of « perception » mutates from a general capacity into an internal continuum of which distinct perception becomes a degree, and not the exhaustive definition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:A3","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MP-02","text":"The concept of « soul » mutates from an extensible genus into the name of a trajectory possessing a capacity for resumption after phenomenal interruption.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:D1","CH_UCIC_P_12:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MP-03","text":"Unconsciousness mutates from an apparent index of privation into a theoretical operator that reveals the difference between real affection and conscious accessibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:HSI-01","text":"Reality implicitly appears as a continuous field of perceptual affections, in which conscious distinction is a local modulation rather than a condition of existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a substantial trajectory capable of passing through regimes of indistinction, resuming certain operations, and remaining identical through their interruptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:HSI-03","text":"Time is the medium that transforms an apparent loss of the soul into a transitory suspension of a manifestation, then into an index of an exceeding capacity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:D2","CH_UCIC_P_12:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:HSI-04","text":"The system's path of escape does not consist in leaving perception, but in passing from an indistinct regime to a more distinct regime without abolishing the continuity that links them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_13:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four axioms: every simple substance persists, every persistence implies a perceptual affection, distinction is only a degree of perception, and the soul exceeds its current manifestations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:A1","CH_UCIC_P_13:A2","CH_UCIC_P_13:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_12:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MRT-B02","text":"These axioms suffice to reconstruct the passage from terminological classification to temporal continuity, then from phenomenal indistinction to perceptual persistence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_13:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the exact status of feeling, the relation between distinct perception and memory, and the nature of the excess designated by « something more ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_11:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_12:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_07:MRT-B04","text":"The compression remains faithful to the real movement because it preserves the decisive loop: apparent privation → indistinction → persistent affection → dispositional difference; it nevertheless cannot replace the limiting cases that give this loop its probative force.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_13:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_13:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_07@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_07:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 19–21","context":"Proposition 19 · Proposition 20 · Proposition 21"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 22–24","order":8,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_14","CH_UCIC_P_15","CH_UCIC_P_16"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_08@R001","sha256":"97f54bef6c726f8bb790807d77ae777133d05dc6595662829d445ab7f2c7f9a3","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-01","text":"Le cluster reconstruit l’unité substantielle non comme immobilité, mais comme continuité interne d’états successifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-02","text":"Cette continuité temporelle devient le modèle d’une continuité perceptive où toute perception actuelle possède une antécédence naturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-03","text":"L’aperception ne produit pas la perception ; elle rend visible une activité perceptive déjà en cours.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-04","text":"La perception est ensuite différenciée par degrés de distinction et d’élévation qualitative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-05","text":"L’étourdissement désigne ainsi une perception persistante mais insuffisamment distinguée, et non un néant mental.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-06","text":"Le mouvement génératif va de l’état séquentiel à la perception latente, puis de la perception latente au seuil d’aperception et à la hiérarchie qualitative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-07","text":"L’architecture est cumulative et récursive : chaque état conserve une antécédence, porte une virtualité et peut devenir le support d’une différenciation ultérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-08","text":"La clôture produite à cette échelle est une ontologie de la continuité différentielle : il n’y a ni présent isolé, ni perception sans genèse, ni distinction sans degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Un état présent n’est intelligible qu’à partir d’un état antérieur dont il constitue la suite naturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La substance se maintient par une succession interne orientée, et non par une identité séparée du devenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La virtualité de l’avenir transforme le présent en opérateur de transition plutôt qu’en simple résultat conservé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Une perception peut exister sans être aperçue ; l’inaperception ne constitue donc pas une absence perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Le réveil est une élévation de visibilité au sein d’une continuité perceptive, non une production perceptive ex nihilo.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Une perception actuelle provient naturellement d’une perception antérieure de même ordre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] La perception n’est pas binaire : elle comporte des degrés de distinction, de relief et de qualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] L’étourdissement est un régime perceptif inférieur, caractérisé par l’insuffisance de distinction plutôt que par l’absence de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Les monades « toutes nues » désignent le seuil inférieur d’une échelle perceptive, non une vacuité ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] L’identité de l’unité simple est finalement recodée comme trajectoire temporelle et perceptive différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Toute l’architecture converge vers une continuité sans vide initial, sans rupture absolue et sans homogénéité perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-01","text":"La succession revient d’abord comme relation entre états substantiels, puis comme chaîne de perceptions ; sa fonction passe de la temporalité de l’être à la genèse de l’expérience.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-02","text":"La continuité interne persiste, mais son domaine s’étend de la substance à la perception et à l’aperception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-03","text":"La virtualité de l’avenir mute en latence perceptive : ce qui n’est pas encore aperçu n’est pas pour autant absent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-04","text":"L’absence est recodée successivement comme absence d’état isolé, absence d’aperception, puis absence de distinction perceptive ; elle cesse de signifier le néant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-05","text":"Le réveil déplace la notion de commencement : il devient une transition de visibilité plutôt qu’un début absolu de la vie mentale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-06","text":"La simplicité substantielle et la nudité monadique sont absorbées dans une structure différentielle : l’unité demeure, mais elle se définit par le régime de ses états.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-07","text":"La causalité de même ordre persiste et s’étend : elle vaut d’abord pour les états, puis pour les perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-08","text":"L’identité statique disparaît après avoir servi de point de départ ; elle est remplacée par une continuité générative orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-01","text":"La dépendance du présent envers l’état précédent reste locale lorsqu’elle décrit uniquement la séquence interne d’une substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-02","text":"Le réveil reste un cas local lorsqu’il sert seulement à montrer qu’une perception peut être aperçue après avoir existé sans aperception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-03","text":"Les monades « toutes nues » restent une détermination locale tant qu’elles désignent seulement l’absence de perceptions distinguées et relevées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-04","text":"Au niveau du cluster, ces machines locales convergent vers une même règle : tout état actuel est une modulation d’une activité antérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-05","text":"La distinction entre perception, aperception et relève qualitative devient une articulation transversale reliant temporalité, causalité et hiérarchie des états.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-06","text":"Les modèles de l’instant isolé, du surgissement ex nihilo, de la conscience binaire et de l’identité immobile sont dépassés par une architecture de seuils continus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut le présent sans profondeur temporelle et la substance définie par une identité immobile.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut l’apparition d’une perception consciente sans antécédent perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut l’assimilation de l’inaperception à une vacuité mentale absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut l’équivalence entre percevoir et percevoir distinctement, puisque la perception est structurée par des degrés qualitatifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une causalité extérieure ou hétérogène qui interromprait la génération interne des états et des perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, le temps ne doit pas être une juxtaposition d’instants sans liaison générative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-02","text":"La conscience ne peut pas constituer un domaine séparé de la réalité perceptive dont elle dépend.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-03","text":"Une ontologie de la perception purement quantitative est disqualifiée : la distinction et le relief introduisent une hiérarchie qualitative irréductible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-04","text":"Le système ne peut admettre une rupture entre unité substantielle et devenir temporel ; leur séparation détruirait le principe de continuité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-05","text":"Le modèle total rival silencieusement exclu est celui d’une réalité faite d’états indépendants, de perceptions sans genèse et de seuils sans gradation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSA-01","text":"L’absence la plus structurante est celle d’un néant perceptif initial à partir duquel surgirait l’aperception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité indisponible est celle d’un avenir absolument extérieur au présent et sans inscription virtuelle dans son état.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSA-03","text":"Le système contourne l’idée d’un commencement absolu en faisant de tout présent une phase déjà engagée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSA-04","text":"Il traite comme ontologiquement inadmissible une réalité sans différences de degré, où toute perception aurait la même visibilité et la même valeur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-01","text":"La continuité temporelle de la substance et la continuité perceptive imposent ensemble qu’aucun état actuel ne commence à partir d’un zéro naturel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-01","CL_UCIC_08:GA-04","CL_UCIC_08:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_15:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-02","text":"Le présent devient simultanément rétention d’un état antérieur et support d’une visibilité perceptive ultérieure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-03","CL_UCIC_08:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_14:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_15:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-03","text":"L’unité simple ne se définit plus par l’homogénéité, mais par la conservation d’une continuité à travers des degrés de différenciation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-02","CL_UCIC_08:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_14:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_16:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-04","text":"Le réveil et la sortie de l’étourdissement sont deux formes d’un même opérateur : une élévation de distinction au sein d’une activité persistante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-05","CL_UCIC_08:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_15:D2","CH_UCIC_P_16:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-05","text":"La perception latente et la monade « toute nue » convergent vers une figure de seuil : l’insuffisance de distinction ne supprime pas l’activité perceptive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-04","CL_UCIC_08:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_16:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_16:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-06","text":"Le principe de causalité homogène s’étend des transitions substantielles aux transitions perceptives, unifiant les deux séries sous une même logique générative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-02","CL_UCIC_08:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_15:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_14:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-07","text":"La distinction perceptive donne une forme opératoire à la virtualité temporelle : l’avenir d’un état est ce qui peut devenir plus distinct dans la série.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-03","CL_UCIC_08:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_14:D3","CH_UCIC_P_16:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-08","text":"Une tension demeure entre l’orientation virtuelle du futur et la sous-détermination du mécanisme exact de son émergence perceptive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-03","CL_UCIC_08:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_15:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-01","text":"L’unité substantielle devient une trajectoire de transformations internes dont la cohésion dépend de la continuité plutôt que de l’immobilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-02","text":"La conscience est reclassée comme événement de visibilité et de degré, non comme naissance d’un contenu mental autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-03","text":"Le temps et la perception partagent une même ontologie : chacun est une série ordonnée où le présent conserve une antécédence et ouvre une possibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-04","text":"La causalité devient une production interne et homogène de différences successives plutôt qu’une intervention extérieure dans une série passive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-05","text":"Le degré inférieur n’est pas le néant mais une puissance insuffisamment relevée ; la privation devient une position structurée dans le champ.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-06","text":"La méthode adéquate consiste à reconstruire les réalités à partir de leurs transitions, de leurs seuils et de leurs antécédences, non à partir d’états isolés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-01","text":"État antérieur → état présent → virtualité de l’avenir → nouvel état : la temporalité se reproduit comme génération récursive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-02","text":"Perception non aperçue → perception actuelle → aperception → extension régressive vers une perception antérieure : la conscience reconduit la chaîne qu’elle rend visible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-03","text":"Indistinction → étourdissement → exigence de distinction → sortie partielle de l’étourdissement : le manque de relief devient moteur de différenciation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-04","text":"La temporalité fournit le modèle de la continuité perceptive, tandis que la perception fournit le modèle gradué de la différenciation temporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est une continuité sans rupture : toute tentative d’introduire un vide initial est réabsorbée dans une série antérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-06","text":"L’escalade générale va de la séquence à la latence, de la latence au seuil, du seuil à une ontologie différentielle des unités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B01","text":"État antérieur + succession naturelle → état présent déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B02","text":"État présent + virtualité d’avenir → continuité temporelle orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B03","text":"Perception existante + absence d’aperception → perception latente plutôt que néant perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B04","text":"Perception latente + seuil d’aperception → réveil comme élévation de visibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B05","text":"Perception + degré de distinction + degré de relief → position qualitative de l’unité perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B06","text":"Continuité temporelle + continuité perceptive + gradation qualitative → unité dynamique sans rupture ni homogénéité absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B01","text":"Présent isolé → rapport nécessaire à l’antécédence → succession interne → présent porteur d’avenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B02","text":"Perception aperçue → perception antérieure non aperçue → continuité causale → exclusion du surgissement perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B03","text":"Perception indistincte → étourdissement → différenciation qualitative → monade située dans une échelle perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B04","text":"Continuité substantielle + continuité perceptive + hiérarchie des degrés → ontologie de la transition différentielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-01","text":"Le présent est reclassé comme nœud de conservation et de production virtuelle, non comme unité temporelle autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-02","text":"La substance et la perception sont cartographiées selon une même logique de série interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-03","text":"L’opposition perception/non-perception est remplacée par la distinction perception/aperception et par une hiérarchie de degrés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-04","text":"L’étourdissement devient un régime inférieur mais réel, ce qui rend pensable une continuité mentale sous le seuil de la conscience explicite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-05","text":"La frontière entre substance et devenir s’effondre : le devenir devient le mode de maintien de l’unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-06","text":"La lecture adéquate doit suivre les transitions, les seuils et les changements de degré plutôt que des catégories binaires d’existence et d’absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level : les objets explicites sont l’état présent, le réveil, la perception non aperçue et l’étourdissement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level : ces objets sont organisés par des séries internes, des causalités homogènes et des degrés de distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level : l’analyse doit déplacer son attention des commencements apparents vers les continuités et les seuils qui les rendent possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level : être, devenir, perception et conscience sont produits comme phases d’une même orientation séquentielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level : la forme argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle affirme en remontant chaque état manifeste vers une condition antérieure et en refusant tout commencement isolé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FL-01","text":"La simplicité de l’unité doit accueillir une multiplicité d’états successifs ; la simplicité devient donc structure de déploiement plutôt qu’absence de composition temporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FL-02","text":"La virtualité de l’avenir oriente le présent sans déterminer entièrement le degré exact de ce qui adviendra.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FL-03","text":"La perception peut être réelle sans être aperçue, mais le critère précis qui fait passer de la latence à l’aperception reste indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FL-04","text":"La continuité perceptive n’entraîne pas automatiquement la distinction perceptive : l’activité peut persister sous forme d’étourdissement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MP-01","text":"Le présent mute d’un état déterminé en opérateur biface qui conserve le passé et prépare l’avenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MP-02","text":"Le réveil mute d’un événement apparent en changement de degré d’aperception au sein d’une série déjà active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MP-03","text":"La perception mute d’une occurrence mentale en échelle qualitative structurée par la distinction et le relief.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MP-04","text":"La monade mute d’une unité simplement donnée en position différentielle dans un régime perceptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une machine de séquences internes où chaque état est à la fois dépôt, transition et réserve de transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient un seuil de visibilité dans un champ perceptif qui le précède et l’excède.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas une ligne d’instants, mais une orientation cumulative où le présent condense une rétention et une virtualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:HSI-04","text":"La lutte ou l’échappée ne consistent pas à sortir de la continuité, mais à produire davantage de distinction et de relève à l’intérieur d’elle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes de continuité temporelle, de perception latente et de gradation qualitative suffisent à reconstruire l’architecture générative du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction est cohérente si la « suite » désigne une dépendance interne et si l’inaperception n’est pas assimilée à l’absence de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne le mécanisme précis de l’élévation perceptive et le degré de détermination de l’avenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B04","text":"La force structurale du cluster réside dans la convergence de trois exclusions : le présent isolé, le néant perceptif et la perception homogène.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_16:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B05","text":"La réduction demeure fidèle tant qu’elle conserve le mouvement réel : antécédence, génération interne, latence, relève et différenciation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195041152085Z_012d387d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 22–24","source_sha256":"97f54bef6c726f8bb790807d77ae777133d05dc6595662829d445ab7f2c7f9a3","sha256":"48b1d587683fcc0325f22d32d6681ba762412088e52547ace058f4951fc46a74","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:50:41.156661+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-01","text":"The cluster reconstructs substantial unity not as immobility, but as the internal continuity of successive states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-02","text":"This temporal continuity becomes the model of a perceptual continuity in which every current perception has a natural antecedence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-03","text":"Apperception does not produce perception; it makes visible a perceptual activity already under way.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-04","text":"Perception is then differentiated by degrees of distinction and qualitative elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-05","text":"Dizziness thus denotes a persistent but insufficiently distinct perception, and not a mental nothingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-06","text":"The generative movement proceeds from the sequential state to latent perception, then from latent perception to the threshold of apperception and to qualitative hierarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-07","text":"The architecture is cumulative and recursive: each state retains an antecedence, bears a virtuality, and can become the support of a subsequent differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AS-08","text":"The closure produced at this scale is an ontology of differential continuity: there is neither an isolated present, nor perception without genesis, nor distinction without degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A present state is intelligible only from an antecedent state of which it constitutes the natural continuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Substance is maintained through an oriented internal succession, and not through an identity separate from becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The virtuality of the future transforms the present into an operator of transition rather than a mere preserved result.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] A perception can exist without being apperceived; inapperception therefore does not constitute a perceptual absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Awakening is an elevation of visibility within a perceptual continuity, not a perceptual production ex nihilo.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] A current perception naturally proceeds from an antecedent perception of the same order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Perception is not binary: it comprises degrees of distinction, salience, and quality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Dizziness is an inferior perceptual regime, characterized by insufficient distinction rather than by the absence of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] “Entirely bare” monads designate the lower threshold of a perceptual scale, not an ontological emptiness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] The identity of the simple unity is ultimately recoded as a differentiated temporal and perceptual trajectory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] The entire architecture converges toward a continuity without initial void, absolute rupture, or perceptual homogeneity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-01","text":"Succession first recurs as a relation between substantial states, then as a chain of perceptions; its function shifts from the temporality of being to the genesis of experience.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-02","text":"Internal continuity persists, but its domain extends from substance to perception and apperception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-03","text":"The virtuality of the future mutates into perceptual latency: what is not yet apperceived is not thereby absent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-04","text":"Absence is successively recoded as the absence of an isolated state, the absence of apperception, then the absence of perceptual distinction; it ceases to signify nothingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-05","text":"Awakening displaces the notion of beginning: it becomes a transition of visibility rather than an absolute beginning of mental life.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-06","text":"Substantial simplicity and monadic bareness are absorbed into a differential structure: unity remains, but it is defined by the regime of its states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-07","text":"Same-order causality persists and expands: it applies first to states, then to perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RMD-08","text":"Static identity disappears after having served as a point of departure; it is replaced by an oriented generative continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-01","text":"The dependence of the present upon the preceding state remains local when it describes only the internal sequence of a substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-02","text":"Awakening remains a local case when it serves only to show that a perception can be apperceived after having existed without apperception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-03","text":"“Entirely bare” monads remain a local determination so long as they designate only the absence of distinct and elevated perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-04","text":"At the level of the cluster, these local machines converge toward one and the same rule: every current state is a modulation of an antecedent activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-05","text":"The distinction between perception, apperception, and qualitative elevation becomes a transversal articulation linking temporality, causality, and the hierarchy of states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:CGD-06","text":"The models of the isolated instant, ex nihilo emergence, binary consciousness, and immobile identity are surpassed by an architecture of continuous thresholds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the present without temporal depth and substance defined by an immobile identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the appearance of a conscious perception without a perceptual antecedent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the assimilation of inapperception to an absolute mental emptiness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the equivalence between perceiving and perceiving distinctly, since perception is structured by qualitative degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:GNX-05","text":"It excludes an external or heterogeneous causality that would interrupt the internal generation of states and perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, time must not be a juxtaposition of instants without generative connection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-02","text":"Consciousness cannot constitute a domain separate from the perceptual reality upon which it depends.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-03","text":"An ontology of perception that is purely quantitative is disqualified: distinction and salience introduce an irreducible qualitative hierarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-04","text":"The system cannot admit a rupture between substantial unity and temporal becoming; their separation would destroy the principle of continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:DBN-05","text":"The silently excluded rival total model is that of a reality made of independent states, perceptions without genesis, and thresholds without gradation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSA-01","text":"The most structuring absence is that of an initial perceptual nothingness from which apperception would arise.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSA-02","text":"The unavailable possibility is that of a future absolutely external to the present and without virtual inscription in its state.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSA-03","text":"The system circumvents the idea of an absolute beginning by making every present an already engaged phase.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSA-04","text":"It treats as ontologically inadmissible a reality without differences of degree, in which every perception would have the same visibility and the same value.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-01","text":"The temporal continuity of substance and perceptual continuity jointly require that no current state begin from a natural zero.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-01","CL_UCIC_08:GA-04","CL_UCIC_08:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_14:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_15:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-02","text":"The present becomes simultaneously the retention of an antecedent state and the support of a subsequent perceptual visibility.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-03","CL_UCIC_08:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_14:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_15:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-03","text":"Simple unity is no longer defined by homogeneity, but by the preservation of a continuity across degrees of differentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-02","CL_UCIC_08:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_14:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_16:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-04","text":"Awakening and emergence from dizziness are two forms of one and the same operator: an elevation of distinction within a persistent activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-05","CL_UCIC_08:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_15:D2","CH_UCIC_P_16:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-05","text":"Latent perception and the “entirely bare” monad converge toward a threshold figure: insufficient distinction does not suppress perceptual activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-04","CL_UCIC_08:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_16:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_16:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-06","text":"The principle of homogeneous causality extends from substantial transitions to perceptual transitions, unifying the two series under one and the same generative logic.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-02","CL_UCIC_08:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_15:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_14:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-07","text":"Perceptual distinction gives an operative form to temporal virtuality: the future of a state is what can become more distinct in the series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-03","CL_UCIC_08:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_14:D3","CH_UCIC_P_16:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:XD-08","text":"A tension remains between the virtual orientation of the future and the underdetermination of the exact mechanism of its perceptual emergence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-03","CL_UCIC_08:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_15:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-01","text":"Substantial unity becomes a trajectory of internal transformations whose cohesion depends on continuity rather than immobility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-02","text":"Consciousness is reclassified as an event of visibility and degree, not as the birth of autonomous mental content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-03","text":"Time and perception share the same ontology: each is an ordered series in which the present retains an antecedence and opens a possibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-04","text":"Causality becomes an internal and homogeneous production of successive differences rather than an external intervention in a passive series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-05","text":"The lower degree is not nothingness but an insufficiently elevated power; privation becomes a structured position in the field.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:BSD-06","text":"The adequate method consists in reconstructing realities from their transitions, their thresholds, and their antecedences, not from isolated states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-01","text":"Antecedent state → present state → virtuality of the future → new state: temporality reproduces itself as recursive generation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-02","text":"Unapperceived perception → current perception → apperception → regressive extension toward an antecedent perception: consciousness reinstates the chain that it makes visible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-03","text":"Indistinction → dizziness → requirement of distinction → partial emergence from dizziness: the lack of salience becomes the motor of differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-04","text":"Temporality provides the model of perceptual continuity, while perception provides the graduated model of temporal differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is a continuity without rupture: every attempt to introduce an initial void is reabsorbed into an antecedent series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:RLE-06","text":"The general escalation proceeds from sequence to latency, from latency to threshold, from threshold to a differential ontology of unities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B01","text":"Antecedent state + natural succession → determined present state.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B02","text":"Present state + virtuality of the future → oriented temporal continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B03","text":"Existing perception + absence of apperception → latent perception rather than perceptual nothingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B04","text":"Latent perception + threshold of apperception → awakening as elevation of visibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B05","text":"Perception + degree of distinction + degree of salience → qualitative position of the perceptual unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B06","text":"Temporal continuity + perceptual continuity + qualitative gradation → dynamic unity without rupture or absolute homogeneity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B01","text":"Isolated present → necessary relation to antecedence → internal succession → present bearing the future.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B02","text":"Apperceived perception → antecedent unapperceived perception → causal continuity → exclusion of perceptual emergence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B03","text":"Indistinct perception → dizziness → qualitative differentiation → monad situated within a perceptual scale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B04","text":"Substantial continuity + perceptual continuity + hierarchy of degrees → ontology of differential transition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-01","text":"The present is reclassified as a node of conservation and virtual production, not as an autonomous temporal unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-02","text":"Substance and perception are mapped according to one and the same logic of internal series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-03","text":"The opposition perception/non-perception is replaced by the distinction perception/apperception and by a hierarchy of degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-04","text":"Dizziness becomes an inferior but real regime, making conceivable a mental continuity below the threshold of explicit consciousness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-05","text":"The boundary between substance and becoming collapses: becoming becomes the mode of maintenance of unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MME-06","text":"The adequate reading must follow transitions, thresholds, and changes of degree rather than binary categories of existence and absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level: the explicit objects are the present state, awakening, unapperceived perception, and dizziness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level: these objects are organized by internal series, homogeneous causalities, and degrees of distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level: analysis must shift its attention from apparent beginnings toward the continuities and thresholds that make them possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level: being, becoming, perception, and consciousness are produced as phases of one and the same sequential orientation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level: the argumentative form accomplishes what it asserts by tracing each manifest state back to an antecedent condition and refusing every isolated beginning.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FL-01","text":"The simplicity of unity must accommodate a multiplicity of successive states; simplicity thus becomes a structure of deployment rather than an absence of temporal composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FL-02","text":"The virtuality of the future orients the present without entirely determining the exact degree of what will occur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FL-03","text":"Perception can be real without being apperceived, but the precise criterion that effects the transition from latency to apperception remains indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:FL-04","text":"Perceptual continuity does not automatically entail perceptual distinction: activity can persist in the form of dizziness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MP-01","text":"The present mutates from a determined state into a two-sided operator that preserves the past and prepares the future.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MP-02","text":"Awakening mutates from an apparent event into a change in the degree of apperception within an already active series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MP-03","text":"Perception mutates from a mental occurrence into a qualitative scale structured by distinction and salience.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MP-04","text":"The monad mutates from a merely given unity into a differential position within a perceptual regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a machine of internal sequences in which each state is at once deposit, transition, and reserve of transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a threshold of visibility within a perceptual field that precedes and exceeds it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_15:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:HSI-03","text":"Time is not a line of instants, but a cumulative orientation in which the present condenses a retention and a virtuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:HSI-04","text":"Struggle or escape does not consist in leaving continuity, but in producing more distinction and elevation within it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms of temporal continuity, latent perception, and qualitative gradation suffice to reconstruct the generative architecture of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction is coherent if “continuation” designates an internal dependence and if inapperception is not assimilated to the absence of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indetermination concerns the precise mechanism of perceptual elevation and the degree of determination of the future.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_16:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B04","text":"The structural force of the cluster lies in the convergence of three exclusions: the isolated present, perceptual nothingness, and homogeneous perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_15:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_16:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B05","text":"The reduction remains faithful so long as it preserves the real movement: antecedence, internal generation, latency, elevation, and differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_14:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_08@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_08:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 22–24","context":"Proposition 22 · Proposition 23 · Proposition 24"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 25–27","order":9,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_17","CH_UCIC_P_18","CH_UCIC_P_19"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_09@R001","sha256":"7eb619f74a6d1217c58b8e9ccf407173aaea02db5f66a3e014b9794eb3dd489d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-01","text":"Le problème commun consiste à expliquer comment une organisation animale produit des effets perceptifs, mémoriels et imaginatifs qui paraissent ordonnés sans relever nécessairement d’une raison réflexive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_18:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-02","text":"Le système recadre la perception comme une composition active : l’organe rassemble une pluralité de stimuli et la convertit en efficacité perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_17:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-03","text":"Cette logique de composition se déplace ensuite vers la mémoire, où une perception présente réactive une liaison passée et produit une attente orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_18:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-04","text":"L’imagination généralise encore cette architecture en faisant converger l’intensité instantanée et l’accumulation temporelle vers un même effet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_19:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-05","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et mutationnel : la pluralité physique devient unité organique, l’unité organique devient représentation, puis la représentation devient anticipation, affect et intensité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A8","CH_UCIC_P_18:A7","CH_UCIC_P_19:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-06","text":"L’architecture ne réduit pas ces mécanismes à la raison : elle produit des conduites et des effets fonctionnellement ordonnés sans leur attribuer une origine rationnelle nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_18:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-07","text":"La clôture obtenue est une clôture ouverte : le principe de composition s’étend aux sens inconnus, tandis que le rapport entre organe, mémoire, imagination et âme demeure partiellement différé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A7","CH_UCIC_P_17:A9","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] L’efficacité perceptive provient de la composition d’une pluralité de stimuli plutôt que de l’action isolée d’un stimulus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_17:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’organe perceptif est une structure active de rassemblement et d’amplification, non un récepteur passif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A2","CH_UCIC_P_17:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] L’opération corporelle et son effet psychique sont liés par représentation sans être identifiés immédiatement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A8","CH_UCIC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Le principe de composition conserve son identité en s’étendant de la vision à d’autres modalités sensorielles et à des sens encore inconnus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A5","CH_UCIC_P_17:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] La mémoire fournit une consécution fonctionnelle qui imite l’ordre rationnel sans être la raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A1","CH_UCIC_P_18:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Une perception présente peut réactiver une perception antérieure et la liaison qui lui était associée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_18:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La réactivation mémorielle transforme le passé représenté en attente d’un événement futur et en conduite orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_18:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] L’affect constitue le relais entre représentation mémorielle, anticipation et comportement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_18:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] La force imaginative peut provenir soit de la grandeur d’une perception, soit de la multitude des perceptions antérieures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_19:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Une impression forte peut condenser instantanément l’effet normalement produit par une habitude prolongée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] La répétition de perceptions médiocres peut atteindre l’effet d’une impression fortement impressionnante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] Un même effet présent peut être produit par des genèses perceptives différentes, de sorte que l’effet ne révèle pas à lui seul sa cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:D4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-13","text":"[Attractor] L’architecture générale est une théorie de la médiation : toute efficacité supérieure résulte d’une organisation, d’une liaison ou d’une accumulation antérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-01","text":"[Stable identity] La composition revient comme invariant transversal : elle rassemble d’abord des stimuli, puis des perceptions passées et enfin des intensités accumulées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:A6","CH_UCIC_P_19:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] Le rassemblement organique se déplace d’une fonction d’amplification perceptive vers une fonction de production d’unité psychique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A3","CH_UCIC_P_17:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-03","text":"[Escalation] La représentation, d’abord requise pour relier organe et âme, devient dans la mémoire le mécanisme qui convertit le passé en attente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A8","CH_UCIC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-04","text":"[Displacement] La consécution quitte le domaine de la raison pour devenir une propriété fonctionnelle de la mémoire et de l’affect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-05","text":"[Reversal] L’ordre comportemental, qui pourrait être pris pour un indice de rationalité, devient la preuve d’une organisation non rationnelle suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-06","text":"[Mutation] L’intensité cesse d’indiquer une cause unique : elle devient le résultat commun d’un choc instantané ou d’une accumulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-07","text":"[Absorption] Les différences entre organes, mémoire et imagination sont absorbées dans une architecture supérieure de médiation, sans que leurs fonctions locales soient abolies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-08","text":"[Terminal transformation] L’effet présent conserve une histoire de production, mais cette histoire devient indécidable à partir de l’effet seul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-01","text":"[Local] Le rassemblement de rayons lumineux ou d’ondulations de l’air reste une description locale du fonctionnement d’organes particuliers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_17:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-02","text":"[Local] La réactivation d’une perception semblable, l’attente animale et la répétition de perceptions médiocres sont des mécanismes inférieurs spécialisés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A5","CH_UCIC_P_18:A7","CH_UCIC_P_19:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-03","text":"[Changement d’échelle] À l’échelle du cluster, ces mécanismes deviennent les variantes d’un seul opérateur : transformer une multiplicité antérieure en unité actuelle efficace.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:D1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-04","text":"[Reliaison] Les unités se raccordent par la fonction commune de la médiation : l’organe compose, la mémoire associe, l’imagination condense.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-05","text":"[Catalyse] La distinction entre imitation de la raison et raison réelle permet de généraliser l’ordre animal sans lui attribuer une faculté rationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A3","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-06","text":"[Recodage] Le récepteur passif, le comportement mécaniquement opposé au comportement rationnel et la mesure univoque de l’intensité deviennent des modèles insuffisants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_19:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une perception relevée soit produite par un stimulus isolé sans opération de rassemblement organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_17:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une conduite ordonnée soit immédiatement imputée à la raison, à une décision réflexive ou à une compréhension conceptuelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_18:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut qu’une imagination forte soit expliquée par la seule grandeur, la seule répétition ou une seule forme temporelle de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_19:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_19:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut l’identification entre processus organique et représentation psychique, en maintenant entre eux une relation de correspondance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une taxonomie close des sens et une origine immédiatement lisible des effets perceptifs, mémoriels ou imaginatifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_19:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, doit être faux le modèle d’une réception passive où l’effet serait proportionnel au stimulus pris isolément.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:DBN-02","text":"Doit également être faux le modèle selon lequel tout comportement orienté manifeste une raison présente et consciente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie toute causalité unique de l’intensité : choc, durée, nombre et grandeur peuvent converger sans être équivalents comme genèses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:DBN-04","text":"Il ne peut admettre une transparence complète du rapport entre corps, âme, mémoire et imagination, puisque chaque niveau conserve une médiation propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité la plus profondément forclose est celle d’une continuité simple entre ordre fonctionnel, intention rationnelle et conscience de la cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSA-02","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un accès immédiat à l’origine réelle des effets : l’effet peut être présent alors que son histoire causale reste indécidable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSA-03","text":"Le système contourne l’idée d’une totalité sensorielle connaissable, en maintenant l’inconnu comme extension interne du mécanisme plutôt que comme extérieur absolu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-01","text":"La perception, la mémoire et l’imagination forment une même architecture de conversion : une pluralité antérieure est organisée pour produire une unité présente efficace.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A3","CH_UCIC_P_18:D2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2","CL_UCIC_09:GA-01","CL_UCIC_09:GA-06","CL_UCIC_09:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-02","text":"L’animal peut produire de l’ordre sans posséder l’opération qui, dans un autre registre, serait appelée raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:D3","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD1","CL_UCIC_09:GA-05","CL_UCIC_09:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-03","text":"La temporalité animale n’est pas ajoutée de l’extérieur aux mécanismes perceptifs : elle est produite par la réactivation du passé et son orientation vers l’avenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:D2","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CL_UCIC_09:GA-06","CL_UCIC_09:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-04","text":"La même intensité actuelle peut être le résultat d’une condensation instantanée ou d’une accumulation progressive, ce qui dissocie puissance de l’effet et forme de la genèse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:D2","CH_UCIC_P_19:D3","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4","CL_UCIC_09:GA-10","CL_UCIC_09:GA-11","CL_UCIC_09:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-05","text":"La composition organique, la liaison mémorielle et l’accumulation imaginative constituent trois régimes distincts d’une même stratégie anti-réductionniste.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT3","CL_UCIC_09:GA-01","CL_UCIC_09:GA-06","CL_UCIC_09:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-06","text":"Plus l’architecture devient générale, plus elle rend impossible une explication immédiate : elle gagne en extension ce qu’elle perd en détermination locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A7","CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT4","CL_UCIC_09:GA-04","CL_UCIC_09:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-01","text":"La cognition animale est reclassée comme une architecture de médiations successives plutôt que comme la manifestation d’une faculté centrale unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD1","CL_UCIC_09:XD-01","CL_UCIC_09:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-02","text":"Le temps animal est produit par des opérations de composition : le présent perceptif porte une histoire passée et ouvre une attente future.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD3","CL_UCIC_09:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-03","text":"La raison perd le monopole de l’ordre pratique : une conduite peut être orientée, répétable et affectivement structurée sans déduction consciente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME4","CL_UCIC_09:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-04","text":"La causalité est redéfinie comme convergence de voies hétérogènes vers un même effet, et non comme correspondance simple entre une cause et sa puissance apparente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:DNX4","CL_UCIC_09:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-05","text":"L’agentivité animale apparaît comme une orientation produite par des médiations organiques, mémorielles et affectives plutôt que comme une initiative réflexive originaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A9","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX4","CL_UCIC_09:GA-07","CL_UCIC_09:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-06","text":"La méthode adéquate consiste à reconstruire les chaînes de production et les histoires perceptives, puisque l’effet seul ne permet pas d’identifier son origine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:D4","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME3","CL_UCIC_09:GA-12","CL_UCIC_09:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-01","text":"Stimuli multiples → rassemblement organique → unité perceptive → perception relevée ; la perception supérieure est produite par resserrement d’une multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_17:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-02","text":"Perception présente → réactivation d’une liaison passée → attente → affect → comportement ; le passé revient comme mécanisme d’orientation du présent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_18:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_18:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-03","text":"Impression forte ou perceptions faibles répétées → même intensité imaginative ; la répétition signale ici un changement de phase où durée et instantanéité deviennent fonctionnellement équivalentes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:A4","CH_UCIC_P_19:A5","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-04","text":"Apparence de raison → attribution à la mémoire → distinction de la raison → reconnaissance d’un ordre non rationnel ; l’imitation devient la voie d’escalade qui dissout l’opposition mécanique/rationnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur global est la médiation compositive : chaque niveau transforme une pluralité antérieure en effet unifié, puis réinjecte cet effet dans une nouvelle chaîne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B01","text":"Multiplicité physique → rassemblement organique → amplification perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B02","text":"Perception présente semblable → représentation d’une liaison antérieure → attente de l’événement associé → affect réactivé → conduite orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B03","text":"Grandeur singulière ou multitude cumulative → force imaginative → frappe et émotion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B04","text":"Impression forte → condensation instantanée d’une habitude ; perceptions médiocres répétées → accumulation → effet équivalent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B05","text":"Composition organique → représentation psychique → liaison mémorielle → anticipation affective → intensité imaginative ; la médiation produit une série récursive d’unités supérieures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B06","text":"Effet fonctionnel ordonné ≠ raison nécessaire ; effet intense ≠ genèse unique ; principe général ≠ taxonomie sensorielle close.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AFM-B01","text":"Stimulus isolé insuffisant → composition organique → amplification perceptive → représentation psychique → mémoire comme consécution → attente affective → comportement orienté sans raison → imagination comme équivalence entre choc et accumulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_17:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_18:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_19:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AFM-B02","text":"Réception passive → médiation active → pluralité organisée → temporalité pratique → intensité à genèses multiples → indécidabilité de l’origine → architecture ouverte des facultés animales.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-01","text":"La distinction entre perception, mémoire et imagination est remplacée par une carte des opérations de composition, de liaison et de condensation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-02","text":"L’opposition entre mécanique et rationnel s’effondre au profit d’un troisième régime : l’ordre fonctionnel produit par mémoire et affect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-03","text":"L’opposition entre instantanéité et durée est reclassée comme différence de genèse produisant potentiellement une même puissance d’effet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-04","text":"Le présent psychique devient lisible comme résultat comprimé d’une histoire organique, perceptive ou mémorielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-05","text":"La méthode de lecture doit suivre les transformations de fonction d’un même terme plutôt que les identités nominales : composition, consécution et intensité changent d’échelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Des stimuli sont rassemblés, des perceptions antérieures sont réactivées et des expériences accumulées produisent des effets présents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Les effets résultent de médiations distribuées qui convertissent multiplicité, répétition et liaison en unité opératoire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Le système remplace les attributions immédiates de raison, de passivité ou de cause unique par une analyse des chaînes de production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le présent n’est pas autonome : il est produit par la composition corporelle, la réactivation du passé et la condensation d’une histoire perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — La forme argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle établit : elle part de cas sensoriels distincts, en extrait un invariant, puis le généralise sans fermer le champ des cas possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-01","text":"La relation entre processus organique et représentation psychique est affirmée comme structurante alors que son mécanisme explicatif est explicitement différé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A9","CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-02","text":"La mémoire imite la raison tout en devant en être distinguée ; l’analogie fonctionnelle produit l’ordre qu’elle interdit d’attribuer à la raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_18:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-03","text":"L’imagination forte peut être expliquée par une perception immense ou par une accumulation de perceptions faibles, mais le texte ne fournit pas de critère pour départager les genèses à partir de l’effet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:D4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-04","text":"Le principe cherche une généralité transmodale tout en conservant une réserve sur les sens inconnus et sur la nature exacte de la composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_17:A7","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-05","text":"La synthèse supérieure unifie les mécanismes sans abolir leurs différences : toute réduction à un seul mécanisme détruirait la médiation propre de chaque niveau.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:D3","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation survient lorsque le stimulus cesse d’être l’unité explicative et devient le matériau d’une composition organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MP-02","text":"Le deuxième point de mutation survient lorsque la perception présente devient le signe d’une liaison passée et acquiert une fonction temporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:D5","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation survient lorsque l’intensité cesse d’être indexée sur une seule cause et devient une convergence d’histoires perceptives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MP-04","text":"Le point d’absorption final transforme les mécanismes locaux en variantes d’une médiation générale, sans résoudre l’indétermination de leurs rapports exacts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:HSI-01","text":"La réalité animale apparaît implicitement comme une machine de rassemblement : elle convertit des pluralités physiques, perceptives et temporelles en unités d’action et d’effet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:D2","CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet animal devient un nœud de médiations où l’affect et le comportement sont produits par des liaisons antérieures plutôt que commandés par une transparence réflexive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:D4","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système est un temps de compression : le passé revient dans le présent sous forme d’attente, d’habitude ou d’intensité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:HSI-04","text":"Les formes d’échappée ne consistent pas en une sortie hors du mécanisme, mais dans la possibilité de reclasser ses voies, ses niveaux et ses genèses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire une architecture unique de médiation : composition organique, liaison mémorielle, orientation affective et condensation imaginative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_18:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante pour expliquer le mouvement inter-unités, mais elle ne détermine pas le mécanisme exact de la représentation psychique ni la nature des sens inconnus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B03","text":"La cohérence dépend d’une compression contrôlée : les différences entre perception, mémoire et imagination doivent être conservées comme fonctions locales puis intégrées comme variantes d’un même opérateur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:D6","CH_UCIC_P_18:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B04","text":"Le système ne peut être reconstruit fidèlement par une séquence linéaire, car chaque niveau réinterprète le précédent en modifiant la fonction de composition, de représentation ou d’intensité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_18:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B05","text":"L’indétermination restante n’est pas un défaut périphérique : elle constitue la condition d’ouverture du système, qui généralise son principe sans fermer son domaine d’application.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME5","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B06","text":"La reconstruction minimale est donc : pluralité organisée → médiation → représentation ou liaison → orientation présente → effet supérieur → genèse partiellement indécidable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195116952750Z_5b8e2cca","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 25–27","source_sha256":"7eb619f74a6d1217c58b8e9ccf407173aaea02db5f66a3e014b9794eb3dd489d","sha256":"a4c48b23cc1083f99f68b2737068d3316a6459874ff69aa712853eabd6a89832","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:51:16.955791+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-01","text":"The common problem consists in explaining how an animal organization produces perceptual, memorial, and imaginative effects that appear ordered without necessarily falling under reflective reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_18:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-02","text":"The system reframes perception as an active composition: the organ gathers a plurality of stimuli and converts it into perceptual efficacy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_17:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-03","text":"This logic of composition then shifts to memory, where a present perception reactivates a past connection and produces an oriented expectation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_18:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-04","text":"Imagination further generalizes this architecture by making instantaneous intensity and temporal accumulation converge toward one and the same effect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_19:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-05","text":"The movement is cumulative and mutational: physical plurality becomes organic unity, organic unity becomes representation, and representation then becomes anticipation, affect, and intensity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A8","CH_UCIC_P_18:A7","CH_UCIC_P_19:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-06","text":"The architecture does not reduce these mechanisms to reason: it produces functionally ordered conduct and effects without assigning them a necessarily rational origin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_18:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AS-07","text":"The closure achieved is an open closure: the principle of composition extends to unknown senses, while the relation among organ, memory, imagination, and soul remains partially deferred.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A7","CH_UCIC_P_17:A9","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Perceptual efficacy arises from the composition of a plurality of stimuli rather than from the isolated action of one stimulus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_17:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The perceptual organ is an active structure of gathering and amplification, not a passive receiver.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A2","CH_UCIC_P_17:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Bodily operation and its psychic effect are linked through representation without being immediately identified.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A8","CH_UCIC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] The principle of composition retains its identity as it extends from vision to other sensory modalities and to senses still unknown.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A5","CH_UCIC_P_17:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Memory supplies a functional succession that imitates rational order without being reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A1","CH_UCIC_P_18:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] A present perception can reactivate an earlier perception and the connection associated with it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_18:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Memorial reactivation transforms the represented past into an expectation of a future event and into oriented conduct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_18:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Affect constitutes the relay between memorial representation, anticipation, and behavior.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_18:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Imaginative force may arise either from the magnitude of a perception or from the multitude of prior perceptions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_19:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] A strong impression can instantaneously condense the effect normally produced by a prolonged habit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-11","text":"[Mutating] The repetition of mediocre perceptions can attain the effect of a strongly impressive impression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-12","text":"[Emergent] One and the same present effect may be produced by different perceptual geneses, such that the effect alone does not reveal its cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:D4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GA-13","text":"[Attractor] The general architecture is a theory of mediation: every higher efficacy results from a prior organization, connection, or accumulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-01","text":"[Stable identity] Composition recurs as a transversal invariant: it first gathers stimuli, then past perceptions, and finally accumulated intensities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:A6","CH_UCIC_P_19:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] Organic gathering shifts from a function of perceptual amplification to a function of producing psychic unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A3","CH_UCIC_P_17:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-03","text":"[Escalation] Representation, initially required to connect organ and soul, becomes in memory the mechanism that converts the past into expectation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A8","CH_UCIC_P_18:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-04","text":"[Displacement] Succession leaves the domain of reason to become a functional property of memory and affect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-05","text":"[Reversal] Behavioral order, which might be taken as an indication of rationality, becomes proof of a sufficient non-rational organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-06","text":"[Mutation] Intensity ceases to indicate a single cause: it becomes the common result of an instantaneous shock or an accumulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-07","text":"[Absorption] The differences among organs, memory, and imagination are absorbed into a higher architecture of mediation, without their local functions being abolished.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RMD-08","text":"[Terminal transformation] The present effect retains a history of production, but this history becomes undecidable from the effect alone.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The gathering of rays of light or undulations of air remains a local description of the functioning of particular organs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_17:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-02","text":"[Local] The reactivation of a similar perception, animal expectation, and the repetition of mediocre perceptions are specialized lower mechanisms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A5","CH_UCIC_P_18:A7","CH_UCIC_P_19:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-03","text":"[Change of scale] At the scale of the cluster, these mechanisms become variants of a single operator: transforming a prior multiplicity into an efficacious present unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:D1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-04","text":"[Relinking] The units are connected by the common function of mediation: the organ composes, memory associates, imagination condenses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-05","text":"[Catalysis] The distinction between imitation of reason and actual reason makes it possible to generalize animal order without attributing a rational faculty to it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A3","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:CGD-06","text":"[Recoding] The passive receiver, behavior mechanically opposed to rational behavior, and the univocal measure of intensity become insufficient models.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_19:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that an elevated perception is produced by an isolated stimulus without an operation of organic gathering.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_17:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that ordered conduct is immediately imputed to reason, to a reflective decision, or to conceptual understanding.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_18:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that strong imagination is explained by magnitude alone, repetition alone, or a single temporal form of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_19:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_19:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the identification of organic process with psychic representation, maintaining between them a relation of correspondence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_17:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:GNX-05","text":"It excludes a closed taxonomy of the senses and an immediately legible origin of perceptual, memorial, or imaginative effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_19:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, the model of passive reception in which the effect would be proportional to the stimulus taken in isolation must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:DBN-02","text":"The model according to which all oriented behavior manifests a present and conscious reason must likewise be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies every single causality of intensity: shock, duration, number, and magnitude can converge without being equivalent as geneses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:DBN-04","text":"It cannot admit complete transparency in the relation among body, soul, memory, and imagination, since each level retains its own mediation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSA-01","text":"The possibility most deeply foreclosed is that of a simple continuity among functional order, rational intention, and consciousness of the cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSA-02","text":"The structuring absence is that of immediate access to the real origin of effects: the effect may be present while its causal history remains undecidable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSA-03","text":"The system bypasses the idea of a knowable sensory totality, maintaining the unknown as an internal extension of the mechanism rather than as an absolute exterior.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-01","text":"Perception, memory, and imagination form one and the same architecture of conversion: a prior plurality is organized in order to produce an efficacious present unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A3","CH_UCIC_P_18:D2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2","CL_UCIC_09:GA-01","CL_UCIC_09:GA-06","CL_UCIC_09:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-02","text":"The animal can produce order without possessing the operation that, in another register, would be called reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:D3","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD1","CL_UCIC_09:GA-05","CL_UCIC_09:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-03","text":"Animal temporality is not added from outside to perceptual mechanisms: it is produced by the reactivation of the past and its orientation toward the future.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:D2","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CL_UCIC_09:GA-06","CL_UCIC_09:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-04","text":"The same current intensity may result from an instantaneous condensation or a progressive accumulation, which dissociates the power of the effect from the form of its genesis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:D2","CH_UCIC_P_19:D3","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4","CL_UCIC_09:GA-10","CL_UCIC_09:GA-11","CL_UCIC_09:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-05","text":"Organic composition, memorial connection, and imaginative accumulation constitute three distinct regimes of one and the same anti-reductionist strategy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT3","CL_UCIC_09:GA-01","CL_UCIC_09:GA-06","CL_UCIC_09:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:XD-06","text":"The more general the architecture becomes, the more it makes immediate explanation impossible: it gains in extension what it loses in local determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A7","CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT4","CL_UCIC_09:GA-04","CL_UCIC_09:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-01","text":"Animal cognition is reclassified as an architecture of successive mediations rather than as the manifestation of a single central faculty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD1","CL_UCIC_09:XD-01","CL_UCIC_09:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-02","text":"Animal time is produced by operations of composition: the perceptual present bears a past history and opens onto a future expectation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD3","CL_UCIC_09:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-03","text":"Reason loses its monopoly over practical order: conduct may be oriented, repeatable, and affectively structured without conscious deduction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME4","CL_UCIC_09:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-04","text":"Causality is redefined as the convergence of heterogeneous paths toward one and the same effect, rather than as a simple correspondence between a cause and its apparent power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:DNX4","CL_UCIC_09:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-05","text":"Animal agency appears as an orientation produced by organic, memorial, and affective mediations rather than as an originary reflective initiative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A9","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX4","CL_UCIC_09:GA-07","CL_UCIC_09:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:BSD-06","text":"The appropriate method consists in reconstructing chains of production and perceptual histories, since the effect alone does not make it possible to identify its origin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:D4","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME3","CL_UCIC_09:GA-12","CL_UCIC_09:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-01","text":"Multiple stimuli → organic gathering → perceptual unity → elevated perception; higher perception is produced by the tightening of a multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_17:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-02","text":"Present perception → reactivation of a past connection → expectation → affect → behavior; the past returns as a mechanism orienting the present.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_18:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_18:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-03","text":"Strong impression or repeated weak perceptions → same imaginative intensity; repetition here signals a phase change in which duration and instantaneity become functionally equivalent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:A4","CH_UCIC_P_19:A5","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-04","text":"Appearance of reason → attribution to memory → distinction from reason → recognition of a non-rational order; imitation becomes the path of escalation that dissolves the mechanical/rational opposition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:RLE-05","text":"The global attractor is compositional mediation: each level transforms a prior plurality into a unified effect, then reinjects that effect into a new chain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B01","text":"Physical multiplicity → organic gathering → perceptual amplification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B02","text":"Similar present perception → representation of a prior connection → expectation of the associated event → reactivated affect → oriented conduct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B03","text":"Singular magnitude or cumulative multitude → imaginative force → impact and emotion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B04","text":"Strong impression → instantaneous condensation of a habit; repeated mediocre perceptions → accumulation → equivalent effect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B05","text":"Organic composition → psychic representation → memorial connection → affective anticipation → imaginative intensity; mediation produces a recursive series of higher unities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FGS-B06","text":"Ordered functional effect ≠ necessary reason; intense effect ≠ single genesis; general principle ≠ closed sensory taxonomy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AFM-B01","text":"Insufficient isolated stimulus → organic composition → perceptual amplification → psychic representation → memory as succession → affective expectation → oriented conduct without reason → imagination as equivalence between shock and accumulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_17:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_18:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_19:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:AFM-B02","text":"Passive reception → active mediation → organized plurality → practical temporality → intensity with multiple geneses → undecidability of origin → open architecture of animal faculties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-01","text":"The distinction among perception, memory, and imagination is replaced by a map of operations of composition, connection, and condensation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-02","text":"The opposition between mechanical and rational collapses in favor of a third regime: functional order produced by memory and affect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-03","text":"The opposition between instantaneity and duration is reclassified as a difference of genesis potentially producing the same power of effect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-04","text":"The psychic present becomes legible as the compressed result of an organic, perceptual, or memorial history.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MME-05","text":"The method of reading must follow the transformations of function of one and the same term rather than nominal identities: composition, succession, and intensity change scale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Stimuli are gathered, prior perceptions are reactivated, and accumulated experiences produce present effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Effects result from distributed mediations that convert multiplicity, repetition, and connection into operative unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The system replaces immediate attributions of reason, passivity, or single cause with an analysis of chains of production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The present is not autonomous: it is produced by bodily composition, the reactivation of the past, and the condensation of a perceptual history.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The argumentative form accomplishes what it establishes: it begins with distinct sensory cases, extracts an invariant from them, then generalizes it without closing the field of possible cases.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_17:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-01","text":"The relation between organic process and psychic representation is affirmed as structuring while its explanatory mechanism is explicitly deferred.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:A9","CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-02","text":"Memory imitates reason while having to be distinguished from it; functional analogy produces the order that it forbids attributing to reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:A2","CH_UCIC_P_18:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_18:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-03","text":"Strong imagination may be explained by an immense perception or by an accumulation of weak perceptions, but the text provides no criterion for distinguishing the geneses on the basis of the effect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:D4","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-04","text":"The principle seeks transmodal generality while retaining a reservation regarding unknown senses and the exact nature of composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_17:A7","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:FL-05","text":"The higher synthesis unifies the mechanisms without abolishing their differences: any reduction to a single mechanism would destroy the proper mediation of each level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:D3","CH_UCIC_P_18:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point occurs when the stimulus ceases to be the explanatory unit and becomes the material of an organic composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point occurs when present perception becomes the sign of a past connection and acquires a temporal function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:D5","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point occurs when intensity ceases to be indexed to a single cause and becomes a convergence of perceptual histories.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_19:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MP-04","text":"The final absorption point transforms local mechanisms into variants of a general mediation, without resolving the indeterminacy of their exact relations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:HSI-01","text":"Animal reality implicitly appears as a machine of gathering: it converts physical, perceptual, and temporal pluralities into unities of action and effect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:D2","CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:HSI-02","text":"The animal subject becomes a node of mediations in which affect and behavior are produced by prior connections rather than commanded by reflective transparency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:D4","CH_UCIC_P_18:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system is a time of compression: the past returns in the present in the form of expectation, habit, or intensity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_19:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:HSI-04","text":"The forms of escape do not consist in an exit from the mechanism, but in the possibility of reclassifying its paths, levels, and geneses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_18:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_19:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct a single architecture of mediation: organic composition, memorial connection, affective orientation, and imaginative condensation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_18:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient to explain inter-unit movement, but it does not determine the exact mechanism of psychic representation or the nature of unknown senses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B03","text":"Coherence depends on controlled compression: the differences among perception, memory, and imagination must be retained as local functions and then integrated as variants of one and the same operator.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:D6","CH_UCIC_P_18:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B04","text":"The system cannot be faithfully reconstructed through a linear sequence, because each level reinterprets the preceding one by modifying the function of composition, representation, or intensity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_18:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B05","text":"The remaining indeterminacy is not a peripheral defect: it constitutes the condition of the system's openness, which generalizes its principle without closing its domain of application.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_17:ME5","CH_UCIC_P_19:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_09:MRT-B06","text":"The minimal reconstruction is therefore: organized plurality → mediation → representation or connection → present orientation → higher effect → partially undecidable genesis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_17:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_18:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_19:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_09@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_09:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 25–27","context":"Proposition 25 · Proposition 26 · Proposition 27"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 28–30","order":10,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_20","CH_UCIC_P_21","CH_UCIC_P_22"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_10@R001","sha256":"49e00f06bbf6981d96c2ba58799d328fc89b0a5993ed933f57058d24773e1f2f","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-01","text":"Le cluster part d’une action humaine dont l’efficacité peut provenir d’une liaison mémorielle des perceptions sans connaissance de sa raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_20:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-02","text":"Il recadre ensuite la différence entre l’humain et l’animal comme différence de régime cognitif plutôt que comme séparation biologique absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_21:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-03","text":"La régularité cesse d’être une simple répétition lorsqu’elle reçoit une fondation théorique et devient connaissance de vérités nécessaires et éternelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A7","CH_UCIC_P_21:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-04","text":"Cette fondation produit la Raison et les sciences, puis les réoriente vers la connaissance de soi et de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A4","CH_UCIC_P_21:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-05","text":"L’abstraction des vérités nécessaires déclenche une seconde escalade : la connaissance devient réflexion sur le Moi et sur les contenus présents en nous.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-06","text":"La réflexion sur le Moi ouvre une continuité générative vers l’Être, la substance, les distinctions ontologiques et Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A6","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-07","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et récursif : la mémoire produit l’habitude, la théorie requalifie la régularité, puis la réflexion requalifie le sujet qui connaît.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D5","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-08","text":"La clôture du cluster nomme cette trajectoire Ame raisonnable ou Esprit, tout en laissant sous-déterminée la médiation exacte entre finitude humaine et infinité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La conduite dépend du mode selon lequel les perceptions successives sont reliées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La mémoire peut produire une conduite efficace sans fournir la théorie de la régularité qui la guide.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A5","CH_UCIC_P_20:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La distinction entre animalité et humanité se déplace de l’espèce vers le fondement effectif de l’action et de la connaissance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Les vérités nécessaires et éternelles constituent le critère d’un régime humain supérieur à la simple répétition empirique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A1","CH_UCIC_P_21:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] La Raison et les sciences procèdent de cet accès aux vérités nécessaires et orientent le savoir vers le soi et Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A4","CH_UCIC_P_21:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] La connaissance des vérités nécessaires se transforme en abstraction, puis en actes réflexifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La réflexivité n’est pas seulement connaissance du sujet : elle engendre les catégories ontologiques qui organisent le raisonnement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A9","CH_UCIC_P_22:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Le Moi fonctionne comme point de passage entre une connaissance intérieure limitée et la pensée de l’Être, de la substance et de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:D2","CH_UCIC_P_22:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] La limitation humaine devient la position à partir de laquelle l’infinité divine est conçue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Ame raisonnable ou Esprit désigne le principe humain produit par cette trajectoire de connaissance, plutôt qu’un simple nom indépendant de ses opérations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Le cluster converge vers une continuité opératoire entre connaissance, réflexivité, ontologie et théologie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_21:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-01","text":"La liaison des perceptions persiste comme mécanisme général, mais sa fonction se déplace de la mémoire pratique vers la fondation théorique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A1","CH_UCIC_P_20:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-02","text":"La régularité revient d’abord comme habitude reproductible, puis comme objet dont il faut connaître la raison, enfin comme vérité nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A4","CH_UCIC_P_21:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-03","text":"L’analogie entre l’homme et la bête conserve une fonction critique, mais elle est absorbée par une cartographie des régimes cognitifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-04","text":"La raison change de statut : elle est d’abord une spécialisation minoritaire de l’action, puis le principe qui engendre les sciences et définit la capacité humaine supérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_21:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-05","text":"La connaissance nécessaire migre de la théorie des régularités vers une opération réflexive portant sur le sujet connaissant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-06","text":"Le Moi cesse d’être un terme terminal : il devient un opérateur de généralisation vers l’être, la substance et Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-07","text":"La limitation ne disparaît pas dans l’infini ; elle est conservée comme point de départ et inversée en support de l’élévation divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_22:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-08","text":"Le terme Esprit absorbe les fonctions précédemment dispersées entre théorie, raison, science, réflexivité et orientation théologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:D4","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-01","text":"Restent locales les scènes de conduite empirique, l’attente du lendemain et la figure de l’astronome comme exemple de conversion de l’habitude en théorie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D2","CH_UCIC_P_20:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-02","text":"Restent également locales la mesure rhétorique de la majorité empirique et la sous-détermination du principe rationnel de l’astronome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-03","text":"Change d’échelle la différence homme-animal : elle cesse d’être une comparaison de comportements pour devenir une théorie de la capacité à connaître le nécessaire et l’éternel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:D2","CH_UCIC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-04","text":"Relie les unités la transformation de la régularité en connaissance, puis de la connaissance en réflexivité et en ontologie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:D1","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-05","text":"Catalyse la transition majeure le passage d’une liaison perceptive efficace à une liaison fondée par un principe théorique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D4","CH_UCIC_P_20:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-06","text":"Deviennent obsolètes comme explications totales la mémoire seule, la simple appartenance biologique et l’intériorité autosuffisante du sujet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une action réussie soit par elle-même une action rationnellement fondée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D1","CH_UCIC_P_20:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut que la répétition d’une régularité passée donne accès à la raison de cette régularité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_20:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut que l’animalité, la mémoire ou l’expérience empirique suffisent à définir l’humain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SNX4","CH_UCIC_P_21:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que le savoir humain soit limité aux contenus contingents, périssables ou immédiatement donnés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut que la réflexion sur le Moi reste enfermée dans la psychologie intérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut une séparation radicale entre connaissance de soi, ontologie et théologie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que la régularité observée ne contienne pas spontanément sa propre explication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_20:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que l’homme ne soit ni un animal simplement continué, ni un être rationnel dans chacune de ses actions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_21:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-03","text":"Le sujet doit être assez réflexif pour ouvrir l’ontologie, mais assez limité pour ne pas constituer une totalité autosuffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-04","text":"Le passage de la connaissance à l’ontologie suppose que la fonction cognitive de la réflexion soit déjà ontologiquement productive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_22:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-05","text":"Le système ne peut admettre que Dieu soit une simple répétition quantitative des limites humaines.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_22:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSA-01","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une médiation pleinement explicitée entre la finitude humaine et l’infinité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSA-02","text":"Est rendue indisponible une théorie où la mémoire, l’expérience, la raison et l’esprit formeraient un continuum homogène sans seuil de fondation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SNX4","CH_UCIC_P_21:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSA-03","text":"Est également indisponible une connaissance qui resterait sans réflexivité, sans portée ontologique et sans orientation théologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSA-04","text":"Le système contourne la question du mécanisme précis par lequel les vérités nécessaires deviennent accessibles à un sujet fini.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-01","text":"La distinction entre empirisme et rationalité devient une échelle de transformation de l’action, allant de la répétition efficace à la connaissance fondée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-02","CL_UCIC_10:GA-03","CL_UCIC_10:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_20:D4","CH_UCIC_P_21:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-02","text":"Les vérités nécessaires ne remplacent pas simplement la mémoire : elles convertissent la régularité en objet de théorie, puis en principe de réflexivité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-04","CL_UCIC_10:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_20:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_22:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-03","text":"La Raison et les sciences forment le dispositif intermédiaire par lequel une différence cognitive devient connaissance de soi et connaissance de Dieu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-04","CL_UCIC_10:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_21:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_21:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-04","text":"La réflexivité constitue le mécanisme de raccord entre l’épistémologie des vérités nécessaires et l’ontologie de l’Être, de la substance et de Dieu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-06","CL_UCIC_10:GA-07","CL_UCIC_10:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-05","text":"La limitation humaine acquiert une double fonction : elle marque une insuffisance cognitive et fournit la position de départ pour penser l’infini.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-08","CL_UCIC_10:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-06","text":"Le nom Ame raisonnable ou Esprit clôt nominalement la chaîne sans résoudre le principe de son fonctionnement interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-10","CL_UCIC_10:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-07","text":"La frontière humain-animal, d’abord déplacée vers la rationalité, est finalement absorbée dans une architecture plus vaste de connaissance, réflexivité et élévation ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-03","CL_UCIC_10:GA-07","CL_UCIC_10:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-01","text":"L’humain n’est plus défini par une propriété fixe, mais par sa position dans une série de conversions allant de la mémoire à la théorie, puis de la théorie à la réflexivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-02","text":"La rationalité devient une opération de fondation et de transformation, non une possession uniforme attribuable à toute action humaine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_20:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-03","text":"Le sujet connaissant devient un relais génératif : il ne produit pas seulement des représentations, il ouvre les catégories selon lesquelles le réel est pensé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-04","text":"Le temps est requalifié par contraste entre le futur anticipé à partir du passé et l’éternité nécessaire qui prétend fournir la raison de cette anticipation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_21:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-05","text":"L’ontologie et la théologie apparaissent comme des effets d’une opération épistémique intérieure plutôt que comme des domaines séparés du savoir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-06","text":"La méthode implicite consiste à suivre le fondement d’une liaison perceptive jusqu’à la structure de vérité et au statut du sujet qui la connaît.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-07","text":"La clôture par l’Esprit transforme une série d’opérations cognitives en principe anthropologique et ontologique, mais conserve l’indétermination de leur médiation ultime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:D4","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-01","text":"La boucle empirique est : régularité observée → mémoire → répétition de la conduite → efficacité pratique → renforcement de la mémoire, sans production de théorie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_20:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-02","text":"La voie d’escalade est : régularité → fondation rationnelle → vérités nécessaires → Raison et sciences → connaissance de soi et de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_21:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-03","text":"La voie réflexive est : abstraction → actes réflexifs → Moi → Être et substance → distinctions ontologiques → Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-04","text":"Une boucle de rétroaction se forme lorsque les actes réflexifs deviennent les objets principaux du raisonnement qui les a produits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A9","CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur intermédiaire est la vérité nécessaire et éternelle ; l’attracteur terminal est la continuité entre Moi, Être, substance et Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A1","CH_UCIC_P_22:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-06","text":"La nomination comme Ame raisonnable ou Esprit ferme la chaîne conceptuelle tout en laissant ouverte la mécanique du passage de la finitude à l’infini.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B01","text":"Liaison perceptive par mémoire → conduite répétée → efficacité empirique sans connaissance de la raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A2","CH_UCIC_P_20:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B02","text":"Insuffisance de la répétition → exigence d’un principe distinct → jugement rationnel fondant la régularité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_20:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B03","text":"Principe rationnel → connaissance des vérités nécessaires et éternelles → production conjointe de la Raison et des sciences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A1","CH_UCIC_P_21:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B04","text":"Vérités nécessaires abstraites → actes réflexifs → pensée du Moi et identification de contenus présents en nous.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B05","text":"Moi réflexif → généralisation vers l’Être et la substance → différenciation du simple, du composé et de l’immatériel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:D2","CH_UCIC_P_22:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B06","text":"Limitation reconnue en nous → transposition sans bornes en Dieu → élévation ontologico-théologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B07","text":"Réflexivité devenue principe du raisonnement → absorption de la trajectoire sous le nom d’Ame raisonnable ou d’Esprit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A9","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AFM-B01","text":"Action efficace sans théorie → recadrage de la différence humain-animal → distinction mémoire/raison → fondation par les vérités nécessaires → production de la Raison et des sciences → réflexivité du Moi → généralisation ontologique → pensée de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D1","CH_UCIC_P_21:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AFM-B02","text":"La chaîne se clôt par la nomination de l’Esprit, mais sa force dépend d’une médiation non explicitée entre limitation humaine et infinité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-01","text":"L’action humaine est cartographiée selon son mode de fondation plutôt que selon l’appartenance à l’espèce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_21:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-02","text":"La mémoire, l’empirisme et la raison deviennent des niveaux fonctionnels d’une même architecture de liaison entre perception et action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-03","text":"La différence humain-animal cesse d’être une opposition stable et devient une différence de capacité à accéder au nécessaire, à l’éternel et à la réflexivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_21:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-04","text":"La frontière entre épistémologie, ontologie et théologie est redessinée comme une continuité générative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-05","text":"Le Moi est reclassé comme opérateur de passage et non comme objet psychologique terminal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-06","text":"La finitude humaine devient une position productive pour penser l’infini, au lieu d’être seulement une limite négative du savoir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-07","text":"Une nouvelle méthode de lecture s’impose : suivre les mutations fonctionnelles d’un concept plutôt que conserver son identité nominale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D5","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets explicites sont la conduite empirique, la connaissance des vérités nécessaires, le Moi, l’Être, la substance et Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_22:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Le mécanisme central est une distribution des fonctions de liaison : mémoire, théorie, abstraction, réflexivité et généralisation ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Le texte déplace la question « l’homme est-il rationnel ? » vers « quel principe relie effectivement ses perceptions, ses actions et ses connaissances ? ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_20:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le passé produit une anticipation pratique du futur, tandis que l’éternel fournit la norme d’une connaissance qui dépasse la succession empirique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_21:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — Le texte accomplit sa propre thèse en faisant passer le lecteur d’une distinction pratique à une reclassification réflexive des catégories qui rendent cette distinction pensable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-01","text":"La majorité de l’action humaine est empirique, mais la définition supérieure de l’humain repose sur l’accès à la raison et aux vérités nécessaires ; le cluster conserve cette dissymétrie sans la résoudre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A6","CH_UCIC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-02","text":"Les vérités nécessaires sont posées comme connaissables, mais le mécanisme de leur connaissance demeure sous-déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A2","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-03","text":"La limitation humaine est le point de départ de la pensée de Dieu, mais le passage à l’infinité ne peut être une simple amplification quantitative de cette limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-04","text":"Ame raisonnable et Esprit sont traités comme des noms équivalents, alors que leur fonction de principe humain reste conceptuellement non différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-05","text":"Le sujet est l’accès à l’ontologie, mais il ne peut être une totalité autosuffisante ; la réflexivité exige donc une ouverture qu’elle ne théorise pas entièrement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-01","text":"L’analogie homme-bête mute en distinction de régimes : la continuité comportementale est conservée, mais la différence décisive devient la fondation cognitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_20:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-02","text":"La régularité mute de répétition mémorielle en objet théorique, puis en vérité nécessaire susceptible d’abstraction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_22:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-03","text":"La connaissance mute en réflexivité : elle ne vise plus seulement une régularité, mais le sujet et les contenus qui rendent toute généralisation possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A3","CH_UCIC_P_22:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-04","text":"La réflexivité mute en production ontologique lorsque le Moi devient le point de départ des catégories de l’être.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:D2","CH_UCIC_P_22:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-05","text":"La raison mute d’une pratique spécialisée, illustrée par l’astronome, en principe générateur de la Raison, des sciences et de l’Esprit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A8","CH_UCIC_P_21:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de liaisons hiérarchisées : elle va de la succession perceptive à l’habitude, de l’habitude à la théorie, puis de la théorie à la réflexivité ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient un relais fini capable de convertir ses propres limitations en accès conceptuel à des déterminations plus générales et à l’infini divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est supposé comme succession empirique à dépasser par la nécessité éternelle, non comme simple ligne homogène de répétitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_21:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-04","text":"La navigation possible consiste à modifier le régime de liaison qui guide l’action : quitter la mémoire répétitive pour la fondation théorique, puis convertir cette fondation en réflexivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-05","text":"L’échappée n’est pas une sortie hors du sujet, mais une traversée du sujet vers l’Être, la substance et Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_22:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire la chaîne complète : liaison mémorielle, empirisme, fondation rationnelle, vérités nécessaires, réflexivité, ontologie et théologie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B02","text":"La compression conserve le mouvement génératif réel, qui n’est pas linéaire mais récursif : chaque niveau requalifie le principe du niveau précédent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B03","text":"La reconstruction reste indéterminée sur le mécanisme de connaissance des vérités nécessaires et sur le passage exact de la limitation humaine à l’infini divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence du cluster dépend d’une opposition stable entre répétition mémorielle et fondation rationnelle, puis d’une continuité opératoire entre réflexivité et ontologie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B05","text":"La réduction est suffisante tant qu’elle conserve trois éléments irréductibles : la mutation de la rationalité, la centralité du Moi comme relais et la clôture incomplète par l’Esprit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195154281313Z_8d9e2a37","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 28–30","source_sha256":"49e00f06bbf6981d96c2ba58799d328fc89b0a5993ed933f57058d24773e1f2f","sha256":"1f013cc26174beac7cff3a165c7dae6e2ef8261bcc38e8df66e1886b271010ba","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:51:54.285384+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-01","text":"The cluster begins from a human action whose efficacy may derive from a mnemonic linkage of perceptions without knowledge of its reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_20:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-02","text":"It then reframes the difference between human and animal as a difference of cognitive regime rather than as an absolute biological separation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_21:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-03","text":"Regularity ceases to be mere repetition when it receives a theoretical foundation and becomes knowledge of necessary and eternal truths.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A7","CH_UCIC_P_21:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-04","text":"This foundation produces Reason and the sciences, then reorients them toward knowledge of the self and of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A4","CH_UCIC_P_21:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-05","text":"The abstraction of necessary truths initiates a second escalation: knowledge becomes reflection upon the Self and upon the contents present within us.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-06","text":"Reflection upon the Self opens a generative continuity toward Being, substance, ontological distinctions, and God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A6","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-07","text":"The movement is cumulative and recursive: memory produces habit, theory requalifies regularity, then reflection requalifies the knowing subject.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D5","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AS-08","text":"The closure of the cluster names this trajectory rational Soul or Spirit, while leaving underdetermined the exact mediation between human finitude and divine infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Conduct depends on the mode according to which successive perceptions are linked.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Memory can produce effective conduct without providing the theory of the regularity that guides it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A5","CH_UCIC_P_20:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The distinction between animality and humanity shifts from species to the effective foundation of action and knowledge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Necessary and eternal truths constitute the criterion of a human regime superior to mere empirical repetition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A1","CH_UCIC_P_21:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Reason and the sciences proceed from this access to necessary truths and direct knowledge toward the self and God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A4","CH_UCIC_P_21:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Knowledge of necessary truths transforms into abstraction, then into reflexive acts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Reflexivity is not merely knowledge of the subject: it engenders the ontological categories that organize reasoning.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A9","CH_UCIC_P_22:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] The Self functions as a point of passage between limited inner knowledge and the thought of Being, substance, and God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:D2","CH_UCIC_P_22:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Human limitation becomes the position from which divine infinity is conceived.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Rational Soul or Spirit designates the human principle produced by this trajectory of knowledge, rather than a mere name independent of its operations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_21:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] The cluster converges toward an operative continuity between knowledge, reflexivity, ontology, and theology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_21:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-01","text":"The linkage of perceptions persists as a general mechanism, but its function shifts from practical memory toward theoretical foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A1","CH_UCIC_P_20:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-02","text":"Regularity returns first as reproducible habit, then as an object whose reason must be known, and finally as necessary truth.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A4","CH_UCIC_P_21:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-03","text":"The analogy between man and beast retains a critical function, but it is absorbed into a mapping of cognitive regimes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-04","text":"Reason changes status: it is first a minority specialization of action, then the principle that engenders the sciences and defines superior human capacity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_21:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-05","text":"Necessary knowledge migrates from the theory of regularities toward a reflexive operation bearing upon the knowing subject.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-06","text":"The Self ceases to be a terminal term: it becomes an operator of generalization toward being, substance, and God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-07","text":"Limitation does not disappear into infinity; it is retained as a point of departure and inverted into a support for divine elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_22:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RMD-08","text":"The term Spirit absorbs the functions previously dispersed among theory, reason, science, reflexivity, and theological orientation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:D4","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-01","text":"The scenes of empirical conduct, the expectation of the morrow, and the figure of the astronomer as an example of the conversion of habit into theory remain local.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D2","CH_UCIC_P_20:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-02","text":"Likewise remaining local are the rhetorical measure of the empirical majority and the underdetermination of the astronomer's rational principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-03","text":"The human-animal difference changes scale: it ceases to be a comparison of behaviors in order to become a theory of the capacity to know the necessary and the eternal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:D2","CH_UCIC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-04","text":"What links the units is the transformation of regularity into knowledge, then of knowledge into reflexivity and ontology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:D1","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-05","text":"The major transition is catalyzed by the passage from an effective perceptual linkage to a linkage founded by a theoretical principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D4","CH_UCIC_P_20:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:CGD-06","text":"Memory alone, mere biological membership, and the self-sufficient interiority of the subject become obsolete as total explanations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a successful action is, in itself, a rationally founded action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D1","CH_UCIC_P_20:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that repetition of a past regularity gives access to the reason for that regularity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_20:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that animality, memory, or empirical experience suffice to define the human.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SNX4","CH_UCIC_P_21:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that human knowledge is limited to contingent, perishable, or immediately given contents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the possibility that reflection upon the Self remains enclosed within inner psychology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:GNX-06","text":"It excludes a radical separation between self-knowledge, ontology, and theology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, observed regularity must not spontaneously contain its own explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_20:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-02","text":"It is also necessary that man be neither an animal merely continued nor a rational being in each of his actions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_21:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-03","text":"The subject must be reflexive enough to open ontology, but limited enough not to constitute a self-sufficient totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-04","text":"The passage from knowledge to ontology presupposes that the cognitive function of reflection is already ontologically productive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_22:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:DBN-05","text":"The system cannot admit that God is a mere quantitative repetition of human limits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_22:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSA-01","text":"The structuring absence is that of a fully explicated mediation between human finitude and divine infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSA-02","text":"Unavailable is a theory in which memory, experience, reason, and spirit would form a homogeneous continuum without a threshold of foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SNX4","CH_UCIC_P_21:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSA-03","text":"Also unavailable is a knowledge that would remain without reflexivity, without ontological scope, and without theological orientation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSA-04","text":"The system bypasses the question of the precise mechanism by which necessary truths become accessible to a finite subject.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-01","text":"The distinction between empiricism and rationality becomes a scale of transformation of action, extending from effective repetition to founded knowledge.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-02","CL_UCIC_10:GA-03","CL_UCIC_10:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_20:D4","CH_UCIC_P_21:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-02","text":"Necessary truths do not merely replace memory: they convert regularity into an object of theory, then into a principle of reflexivity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-04","CL_UCIC_10:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_20:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_22:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-03","text":"Reason and the sciences form the intermediate apparatus through which a cognitive difference becomes self-knowledge and knowledge of God.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-04","CL_UCIC_10:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_21:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_21:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-04","text":"Reflexivity constitutes the mechanism of connection between the epistemology of necessary truths and the ontology of Being, substance, and God.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-06","CL_UCIC_10:GA-07","CL_UCIC_10:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-05","text":"Human limitation acquires a double function: it marks a cognitive insufficiency and provides the starting position for thinking infinity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-08","CL_UCIC_10:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-06","text":"The name rational Soul or Spirit nominally closes the chain without resolving the principle of its internal functioning.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-10","CL_UCIC_10:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:XD-07","text":"The human-animal boundary, first displaced toward rationality, is ultimately absorbed into a broader architecture of knowledge, reflexivity, and ontological elevation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-03","CL_UCIC_10:GA-07","CL_UCIC_10:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-01","text":"The human is no longer defined by a fixed property, but by its position in a series of conversions proceeding from memory to theory, then from theory to reflexivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-02","text":"Rationality becomes an operation of foundation and transformation, not a uniform possession attributable to every human action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_20:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-03","text":"The knowing subject becomes a generative relay: it does not merely produce representations, it opens the categories according to which the real is thought.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-04","text":"Time is requalified through the contrast between the future anticipated from the past and the necessary eternity that claims to provide the reason for this anticipation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_21:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-05","text":"Ontology and theology appear as effects of an inner epistemic operation rather than as separate domains of knowledge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-06","text":"The implicit method consists in following the foundation of a perceptual linkage through to the structure of truth and the status of the subject who knows it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:BSD-07","text":"Closure through Spirit transforms a series of cognitive operations into an anthropological and ontological principle, but retains the indeterminacy of their ultimate mediation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:D4","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-01","text":"The empirical loop is: observed regularity → memory → repetition of conduct → practical efficacy → reinforcement of memory, without production of theory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_20:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-02","text":"The escalation path is: regularity → rational foundation → necessary truths → Reason and sciences → self-knowledge and knowledge of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_21:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-03","text":"The reflexive path is: abstraction → reflexive acts → Self → Being and substance → ontological distinctions → God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-04","text":"A feedback loop forms when reflexive acts become the principal objects of the reasoning that produced them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A9","CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-05","text":"The intermediate attractor is necessary and eternal truth; the terminal attractor is the continuity between Self, Being, substance, and God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A1","CH_UCIC_P_22:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:RLE-06","text":"Naming as rational Soul or Spirit closes the conceptual chain while leaving open the mechanics of the passage from finitude to infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B01","text":"Perceptual linkage through memory → repeated conduct → empirical efficacy without knowledge of the reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A2","CH_UCIC_P_20:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B02","text":"Insufficiency of repetition → requirement of a distinct principle → rational judgment founding regularity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_20:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B03","text":"Rational principle → knowledge of necessary and eternal truths → joint production of Reason and the sciences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A1","CH_UCIC_P_21:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B04","text":"Abstract necessary truths → reflexive acts → thought of the Self and identification of contents present within us.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B05","text":"Reflexive Self → generalization toward Being and substance → differentiation of the simple, the composite, and the immaterial.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:D2","CH_UCIC_P_22:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B06","text":"Limitation recognized within us → unbounded transposition into God → ontologico-theological elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B07","text":"Reflexivity become the principle of reasoning → absorption of the trajectory under the name rational Soul or Spirit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A9","CH_UCIC_P_21:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AFM-B01","text":"Effective action without theory → reframing of the human-animal difference → distinction between memory and reason → foundation through necessary truths → production of Reason and the sciences → reflexivity of the Self → ontological generalization → thought of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D1","CH_UCIC_P_21:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:AFM-B02","text":"The chain closes with the naming of Spirit, but its force depends on an unexplicated mediation between human limitation and divine infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-01","text":"Human action is mapped according to its mode of foundation rather than according to membership in the species.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_21:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-02","text":"Memory, empiricism, and reason become functional levels of one and the same architecture of linkage between perception and action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-03","text":"The human-animal difference ceases to be a stable opposition and becomes a difference in the capacity to access the necessary, the eternal, and reflexivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_21:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-04","text":"The boundary between epistemology, ontology, and theology is redrawn as a generative continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-05","text":"The Self is reclassified as an operator of passage and not as a terminal psychological object.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_22:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-06","text":"Human finitude becomes a productive position for thinking infinity, instead of being merely a negative limit of knowledge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MME-07","text":"A new method of reading imposes itself: follow the functional mutations of a concept rather than preserve its nominal identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D5","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit objects are empirical conduct, knowledge of necessary truths, the Self, Being, substance, and God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_22:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — The central mechanism is a distribution of linkage functions: memory, theory, abstraction, reflexivity, and ontological generalization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The text shifts the question “is man rational?” toward “what principle effectively links his perceptions, his actions, and his knowledge?”.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_20:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The past produces a practical anticipation of the future, whereas the eternal provides the norm of a knowledge that exceeds empirical succession.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_21:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The text performs its own thesis by moving the reader from a practical distinction to a reflexive reclassification of the categories that render this distinction thinkable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-01","text":"The majority of human action is empirical, but the higher definition of the human rests on access to reason and necessary truths; the cluster retains this dissymmetry without resolving it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A6","CH_UCIC_P_21:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-02","text":"Necessary truths are posited as knowable, but the mechanism of their knowledge remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A2","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-03","text":"Human limitation is the point of departure for the thought of God, but the passage to infinity cannot be a mere quantitative amplification of this limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-04","text":"Rational Soul and Spirit are treated as equivalent names, whereas their function as human principle remains conceptually undifferentiated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:A8","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:FL-05","text":"The subject is access to ontology, but it cannot be a self-sufficient totality; reflexivity therefore requires an openness that it does not fully theorize.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_22:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-01","text":"The man-beast analogy mutates into a distinction of regimes: behavioral continuity is retained, but the decisive difference becomes cognitive foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_20:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-02","text":"Regularity mutates from mnemonic repetition into a theoretical object, then into a necessary truth susceptible to abstraction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_22:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-03","text":"Knowledge mutates into reflexivity: it no longer concerns merely a regularity, but the subject and the contents that make every generalization possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:A3","CH_UCIC_P_22:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-04","text":"Reflexivity mutates into ontological production when the Self becomes the point of departure for the categories of being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:D2","CH_UCIC_P_22:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MP-05","text":"Reason mutates from a specialized practice, illustrated by the astronomer, into a principle generating Reason, the sciences, and Spirit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:A8","CH_UCIC_P_21:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a machine of hierarchical linkages: it proceeds from perceptual succession to habit, from habit to theory, then from theory to ontological reflexivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_22:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a finite relay capable of converting its own limitations into conceptual access to more general determinations and to divine infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_22:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-03","text":"Time is presupposed as empirical succession to be exceeded by eternal necessity, not as a mere homogeneous line of repetitions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_21:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-04","text":"The possible navigation consists in modifying the regime of linkage that guides action: leaving repetitive memory for theoretical foundation, then converting this foundation into reflexivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:HSI-05","text":"The escape is not an exit from the subject, but a passage through the subject toward Being, substance, and God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_22:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the complete chain: mnemonic linkage, empiricism, rational foundation, necessary truths, reflexivity, ontology, and theology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B02","text":"The compression preserves the real generative movement, which is not linear but recursive: each level requalifies the principle of the preceding level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_22:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction remains indeterminate concerning the mechanism of knowledge of necessary truths and the exact passage from human limitation to divine infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B04","text":"The coherence of the cluster depends on a stable opposition between mnemonic repetition and rational foundation, then on an operative continuity between reflexivity and ontology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_20:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B05","text":"The reduction is sufficient insofar as it preserves three irreducible elements: the mutation of rationality, the centrality of the Self as relay, and incomplete closure through Spirit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_22:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_21:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_10@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_10:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 28–30","context":"Proposition 28 · Proposition 29 · Proposition 30"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 31–33","order":11,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_23","CH_UCIC_P_24","CH_UCIC_P_25"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_11@R001","sha256":"8053938f58f2c2b92799d3572c95176f68d04ca856c63b774740f9f1ada22f9c","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-01","text":"Le cluster traite la possibilité d’un jugement rationnel qui ne repose ni sur la contradiction ni sur une absence de fondement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-02","text":"Il recadre cette possibilité par un double régime : exclusion du contradictoire et recherche d’une raison expliquant pourquoi une chose est ainsi plutôt qu’autrement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-03","text":"La contradiction fournit l’opérateur négatif qui sépare le faux du vrai par opposition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-04","text":"La raison suffisante fournit l’opérateur positif qui rattache les faits, l’existence et les vérités à un fondement explicatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-05","text":"La distinction entre vérités nécessaires et vérités contingentes transforme ensuite cette architecture en système modal réglé par la possibilité ou l’impossibilité de l’opposé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-06","text":"La nécessité reçoit une procédure de justification régressive qui décompose les propositions jusqu’aux idées et vérités primitives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-07","text":"L’interaction des unités fait émerger une architecture où toute vérité doit être à la fois protégée contre la contradiction, fondée par une raison et située selon son régime modal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-08","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et mutationnel : un critère de fausseté devient une théorie relationnelle de la vérité, puis une machine de fondation, de classification et d’analyse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-09","text":"La clôture est asymétrique : les vérités nécessaires tendent vers les primitives, tandis que les vérités de fait conservent une ouverture explicative et modale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Une proposition contradictoire ne peut recevoir le statut de vérité dans le régime de jugement établi.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La vérité n’est pas autonome : elle est déterminée par son opposition au faux et par la relation qui la fonde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Aucun fait, aucune existence et aucune énonciation véritable ne sont admis sans raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Une raison suffisante explique la détermination d’une chose plutôt qu’une autre, passant du statut de fondement des faits à celui de principe général de sélection rationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] L’inaccessibilité humaine d’une raison ne supprime pas sa réalité ni sa nécessité objective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Le système distingue deux régimes de vérité selon le statut modal de leur opposé : impossibilité pour le nécessaire, possibilité pour le contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A3","CH_UCIC_P_25:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] La nécessité n’est pas seulement une propriété modale ; elle devient une propriété démontrable par analyse régressive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] L’analyse des vérités nécessaires converge vers des idées et vérités primitives qui fonctionnent comme limites internes de la justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] La rationalité globale se constitue par la composition de trois opérations : exclure la contradiction, fonder la détermination et distribuer les vérités selon leur modalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:D3","CH_UCIC_P_25:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] La question « pourquoi ainsi plutôt qu’autrement » attire les faits, les vérités et les analyses vers un même champ de justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-01","text":"La contradiction revient d’abord comme critère de fausseté, puis comme impossibilité de l’opposé dans le régime des vérités nécessaires. Sa fonction s’étend sans conserver son seul rôle classificatoire initial.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_25:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-02","text":"L’opposition migre du couple vrai/faux vers le couple nécessaire/contingent : elle ne sépare plus seulement des valeurs de jugement, elle règle l’espace des possibilités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:D2","CH_UCIC_P_25:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-03","text":"La raison suffisante revient comme fondement des faits, de l’existence et de la vérité, puis se resserre en procédure d’explication analytique pour les vérités nécessaires.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A4","CH_UCIC_P_25:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-04","text":"L’ignorance change de fonction : elle n’est plus un indice possible d’absence de raison, mais une limite épistémique compatible avec un ordre rationnel objectif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:D3","CH_UCIC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-05","text":"La clôture analytique par les primitives absorbe la demande de justification pour les vérités nécessaires, mais ne s’étend pas explicitement au régime des vérités de fait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A8","CH_UCIC_P_25:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-06","text":"L’incomplétude initiale du fondement ne disparaît pas ; elle est déplacée vers la différence entre une raison objective, une raison connaissable et une raison définitivement analysée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_24:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-01","text":"Reste local le fait que deux principes sont annoncés alors qu’un seul, celui de la Contradiction, est explicitement formulé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-02","text":"Change d’échelle l’exigence de raison suffisante, qui n’est plus seulement une règle de jugement mais une condition commune de la vérité, de l’existence et de la détermination factuelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-03","text":"Relie les unités la correspondance entre l’opposé impossible, l’opposé possible et la procédure d’analyse, qui transforme une classification modale en méthode de justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:D1","CH_UCIC_P_25:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-04","text":"Catalyse la transition majeure la dissociation entre fondement objectif et connaissance humaine, car elle empêche l’ignorance de devenir une réfutation de la rationalité du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A5","CH_UCIC_P_24:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-05","text":"Est recodée au niveau courant l’opposition vrai/faux : elle devient une première couche d’une architecture qui ajoute fondement explicatif, modalité et profondeur analytique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_25:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une contradiction puisse demeurer compatible avec le statut de vérité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut le fait brut, l’existence autojustifiée et la vérité réduite à une simple assertion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_24:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut l’indistinction entre nécessité et contingence en assignant à chacune une modalité opposée propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que l’inexplicable pour nous soit automatiquement l’infondé en soi.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une justification analytique sans terme de réduction, mais laisse ouverte la nature exacte des primitives qui terminent cette réduction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, il faut que soit faux tout modèle dans lequel un fait constitue un terme final de l’explication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:DBN-02","text":"Le système disqualifie un modèle subjectiviste où la limite de la connaissance humaine déterminerait la limite de l’ordre rationnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:DBN-03","text":"Il disqualifie un espace modal indifférencié dans lequel les vérités nécessaires et les vérités de fait recevraient le même régime de preuve.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:DBN-04","text":"Il ne peut admettre une analyse nécessaire qui se prolongerait sans limite et ne produirait jamais de primitives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSA-01","text":"L’absence la plus profonde est celle d’un fondement ultime explicitement fourni pour les vérités de fait : leur contingence est reconnue, mais leur régime complet de justification demeure indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité forclose est celle d’un réel ultimement dépourvu de pourquoi.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSA-03","text":"Le système contourne sans la résoudre entièrement la possibilité d’une clôture explicative accessible à l’entendement humain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSA-04","text":"Il traite comme ontologiquement inadmissible une vérité qui serait vraie sans relation au faux, sans raison suffisante ou sans position modale déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-01","text":"La vérité est produite par une double opération : une proposition doit éviter la contradiction et recevoir une détermination qui la distingue du faux.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_23:D3","CL_UCIC_11:GA-01","CL_UCIC_11:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-02","text":"Le principe de raison suffisante convertit la séparation logique du vrai et du faux en exigence ontologique : être vrai ou exister implique être déterminé par une raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A1","CH_UCIC_P_24:A4","CL_UCIC_11:GA-02","CL_UCIC_11:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-03","text":"La modalité de l’opposé fournit le lien opératoire entre la classification logique et la justification analytique : l’impossibilité de l’opposé déclenche la recherche de raisons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A3","CH_UCIC_P_25:A6","CL_UCIC_11:GA-06","CL_UCIC_11:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-04","text":"L’ignorance humaine ne suspend pas l’architecture ; elle déplace le problème de la vérité vers la différence entre fondement réel et accès cognitif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A5","CH_UCIC_P_24:D3","CL_UCIC_11:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-05","text":"La contradiction et la raison suffisante forment deux seuils successifs plutôt qu’un seul principe : le premier interdit certaines propositions, le second exige une explication pour celles qui restent admissibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_24:D1","CL_UCIC_11:GA-01","CL_UCIC_11:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-06","text":"La clôture des vérités nécessaires produit une asymétrie structurelle : l’analyse peut atteindre un terme primitif, tandis que le régime des vérités de fait demeure explicitement moins déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A8","CH_UCIC_P_25:DNX5","CL_UCIC_11:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-01","text":"Le système transforme la vérité en trajectoire de validation : exclusion de la contradiction, fondation par une raison, détermination modale, puis analyse si la nécessité est en jeu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_25:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-02","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme ordre rationnel stratifié plutôt que comme collection de faits immédiatement donnés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-03","text":"Le sujet connaissant perd le rôle de mesure de la rationalité objective et devient l’agent limité d’une reconstruction dont les raisons peuvent excéder son accès.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-04","text":"Le temps de la connaissance est séparé de la structure du fondement : une raison peut être réelle avant d’être découverte, ou rester inaccessible sans devenir inexistante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-05","text":"La méthode pertinente n’est ni la simple constatation ni l’assertion, mais une descente contrôlée du complexe vers le simple et le primitif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale est : proposition → test de contradiction → exclusion du faux → exigence de raison → détermination de la vérité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-02","text":"La boucle modale est : vérité nécessaire → opposé impossible → recherche de la raison → analyse successive → primitives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-03","text":"La boucle épistémique est : raison inaccessible → distinction entre ignorance et absence de raison → maintien de l’ordre objectif → reprise de la recherche.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est la détermination d’une différence : chaque « ainsi » appelle le pourquoi de sa sélection contre un « autrement ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-05","text":"Le point de changement de phase apparaît lorsque la contradiction cesse d’être seulement un défaut à éliminer et devient un opérateur de cartographie modale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B01","text":"Une proposition candidate entre dans le système par un test d’exclusion : contradiction enveloppée → fausseté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B02","text":"Une proposition non exclue est soumise à l’exigence de fondement : fait, existence ou vérité → raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B03","text":"La raison doit expliquer une sélection : détermination donnée → pourquoi ainsi plutôt qu’autrement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B04","text":"Le statut modal organise la suite : opposé impossible → nécessité et analyse ; opposé possible → contingence et maintien de l’ouverture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B05","text":"L’analyse nécessaire se resserre récursivement jusqu’aux primitives, tandis que l’inaccessibilité des raisons bloque seulement la connaissance, non la structure rationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B06","text":"La machine totale produit ainsi une rationalité à trois filtres : non-contradiction, fondement suffisant, fermeture ou ouverture modale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AFM-B01","text":"Contradiction possible → classement du faux → opposition au faux → exigence d’une raison → différenciation de l’ainsi et de l’autrement → classification nécessaire/contingente → analyse vers les primitives ou maintien de l’ouverture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AFM-B02","text":"Fait apparemment brut → refus de l’absence de pourquoi → raison objective mais parfois inaccessible → réorganisation du réel comme champ explicatif stratifié.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-01","text":"Le champ de la vérité est redessiné selon deux axes conjoints : relation au faux et disponibilité d’une raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-02","text":"La différence entre vérité nécessaire et vérité contingente devient une différence de procédure, non seulement de contenu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-03","text":"L’opposition « connu/inconnu » cesse de recouvrir l’opposition « fondé/infondé ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-04","text":"La justification est cartographiée comme une profondeur : constatation, fondement, modalité, analyse et primitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-05","text":"La fausse opposition entre nécessité et analyse s’effondre : la nécessité devient précisément ce qui peut être reconstruit par analyse jusqu’à une limite primitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B01","text":"Au niveau de surface, le système porte sur des propositions jugées vraies ou fausses, sur des faits, des existants et des énonciations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B02","text":"Au niveau structurel, ces objets sont distribués par des opérations de contradiction, de fondement explicatif et de classification modale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B03","text":"Au niveau métastratégique, la validité est déplacée des conclusions particulières vers les principes qui rendent leur jugement possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B04","text":"Au niveau ontologique et temporel, le réel est présupposé comme rationnellement structuré, tandis que l’accès humain à cette structure reste situé et différé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B05","text":"Au niveau méthodologique et performatif, la forme de l’argument accomplit ce qu’elle affirme : elle classe, décompose, remonte vers les conditions et refuse les termes ultimes non fondés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FL-01","text":"La vérité est définie par opposition au faux, mais elle exige simultanément une raison suffisante ; la relation différentielle ne suffit donc pas à elle seule comme fondement complet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:A3","CH_UCIC_P_24:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FL-02","text":"Les vérités nécessaires disposent d’une clôture analytique, alors que le régime de justification des vérités de fait reste explicitement sous-déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A8","CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FL-03","text":"L’universalité de la raison suffisante entre en tension avec l’inaccessibilité fréquente des raisons, sans que cette tension soit résolue par une théorie de leur connaissance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MP-01","text":"Le second principe annoncé dans la fondation initiale est fonctionnellement rejoint par l’exigence de raison suffisante, sans être textuellement identifié à elle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MP-02","text":"La contradiction mute d’un opérateur négatif de classement en opérateur modal qui règle la possibilité de l’opposé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_25:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MP-03","text":"L’ignorance change de statut : d’obstacle apparent à la rationalité, elle devient frontière méthodologique interne à un ordre rationnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:HSI-01","text":"L’image minimale du système est celle d’une machine de filtrage et de fondation : une porte logique exclut la contradiction, un moteur explicatif fonde la détermination, un routeur modal distingue nécessité et contingence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient un opérateur de reconstruction limité, capable de suivre certaines raisons mais non de mesurer par son ignorance la rationalité du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système est régressif et stratifié : il remonte du complexe vers le simple, tandis que les raisons peuvent précéder leur découverte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_24:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:HSI-04","text":"La navigation rationnelle consiste à passer du fait apparent à sa raison, puis à déterminer si cette raison ferme l’opposé ou maintient une possibilité contingente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre noyaux : exclusion de la contradiction, raison suffisante, différenciation modale et analyse régressive des vérités nécessaires.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B02","text":"Ces noyaux suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement courant, car ils préservent le passage du jugement logique à la fondation ontologique puis à la procédure analytique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante porte sur l’identité exacte du second principe, la nature des raisons suffisantes, le statut des primitives et la justification complète des vérités de fait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence maximale se situe dans la chaîne nécessaire–opposé impossible–analyse–primitives ; la zone la plus instable est le passage entre rationalité universelle et contingence non entièrement analysée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B05","text":"Aucune unité inférieure ne produit seule l’architecture complète : la première fournit l’exclusion logique, la seconde l’exigence de fondement et la troisième la différenciation modale ainsi que la clôture analytique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:A1","CH_UCIC_P_24:A7","CH_UCIC_P_25:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B06","text":"Le système est donc reconstructible comme une machine de rationalisation stratifiée, mais non comme une clôture absolue : ses propres principes maintiennent une ouverture au niveau des vérités contingentes et du fondement initial incomplet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_24:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195227067014Z_7c3be277","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 31–33","source_sha256":"8053938f58f2c2b92799d3572c95176f68d04ca856c63b774740f9f1ada22f9c","sha256":"4226c928b86dda16edbc2958283db98d1c62cba14f03954b546cd32a65ef106e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:52:27.071284+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-01","text":"The cluster addresses the possibility of a rational judgment that rests neither on contradiction nor on an absence of foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-02","text":"It reframes this possibility through a dual regime: exclusion of contradiction and the search for a reason explaining why a thing is thus rather than otherwise.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-03","text":"Contradiction provides the negative operator that separates the false from the true by opposition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-04","text":"Sufficient reason provides the positive operator that connects facts, existence, and truths to an explanatory foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-05","text":"The distinction between necessary truths and contingent truths then transforms this architecture into a modal system governed by the possibility or impossibility of the opposite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-06","text":"Necessity is given a regressive procedure of justification that decomposes propositions down to primitive ideas and truths.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-07","text":"The interaction of the units brings forth an architecture in which every truth must be both protected against contradiction, founded by a reason, and situated according to its modal regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-08","text":"The movement is cumulative and mutational: a criterion of falsity becomes a relational theory of truth, then a machine of foundation, classification, and analysis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AS-09","text":"The closure is asymmetrical: necessary truths tend toward primitives, whereas truths of fact retain an explanatory and modal openness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A contradictory proposition cannot be granted the status of truth within the established regime of judgment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Truth is not autonomous: it is determined by its opposition to the false and by the relation that grounds it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] No fact, no existence, and no true statement are admitted without sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] A sufficient reason explains the determination of one thing rather than another, shifting from the status of foundation of facts to that of a general principle of rational selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] The human inaccessibility of a reason does not eliminate either its reality or its objective necessity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] The system distinguishes two regimes of truth according to the modal status of their opposite: impossibility for the necessary, possibility for the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A3","CH_UCIC_P_25:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Necessity is not merely a modal property; it becomes a property demonstrable through regressive analysis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] The analysis of necessary truths converges upon primitive ideas and truths that function as internal limits of justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Global rationality is constituted through the composition of three operations: excluding contradiction, grounding determination, and distributing truths according to their modality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:D3","CH_UCIC_P_25:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The question “why thus rather than otherwise” draws facts, truths, and analyses into a single field of justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-01","text":"Contradiction first recurs as a criterion of falsity, then as the impossibility of the opposite in the regime of necessary truths. Its function expands without retaining only its initial classificatory role.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_25:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-02","text":"Opposition migrates from the true/false pair to the necessary/contingent pair: it no longer merely separates values of judgment; it governs the space of possibilities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:D2","CH_UCIC_P_25:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-03","text":"Sufficient reason recurs as the foundation of facts, existence, and truth, then narrows into a procedure of analytical explanation for necessary truths.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A4","CH_UCIC_P_25:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-04","text":"Ignorance changes function: it is no longer a possible indication of the absence of reason, but an epistemic limit compatible with an objective rational order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:D3","CH_UCIC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-05","text":"Analytical closure through primitives absorbs the demand for justification for necessary truths, but does not explicitly extend to the regime of truths of fact.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A8","CH_UCIC_P_25:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RMD-06","text":"The initial incompleteness of the foundation does not disappear; it is displaced onto the difference between an objective reason, a knowable reason, and a definitively analyzed reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_24:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-01","text":"What remains local is the fact that two principles are announced whereas only one, that of Contradiction, is explicitly formulated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-02","text":"The requirement of sufficient reason changes scale, no longer being merely a rule of judgment but a condition common to truth, existence, and factual determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-03","text":"What connects the units is the correspondence between the impossible opposite, the possible opposite, and the procedure of analysis, which transforms a modal classification into a method of justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:D1","CH_UCIC_P_25:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-04","text":"The dissociation between objective foundation and human knowledge catalyzes the major transition, because it prevents ignorance from becoming a refutation of the rationality of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A5","CH_UCIC_P_24:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:CGD-05","text":"The true/false opposition is recoded at the current level: it becomes a first layer of an architecture that adds explanatory foundation, modality, and analytical depth.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_25:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a contradiction might remain compatible with the status of truth.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the brute fact, self-justified existence, and truth reduced to a mere assertion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_24:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the indistinction between necessity and contingency by assigning each its own opposing modality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the notion that what is inexplicable to us is automatically unfounded in itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:GNX-05","text":"It excludes analytical justification without a term of reduction, but leaves open the exact nature of the primitives that terminate this reduction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, every model in which a fact constitutes a final term of explanation must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:DBN-02","text":"The system disqualifies a subjectivist model in which the limit of human knowledge would determine the limit of rational order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:DBN-03","text":"It disqualifies an undifferentiated modal space in which necessary truths and truths of fact would receive the same regime of proof.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:DBN-04","text":"It cannot admit a necessary analysis that would continue without limit and never produce primitives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSA-01","text":"The deepest absence is that of an ultimate foundation explicitly provided for truths of fact: their contingency is recognized, but their complete regime of justification remains undetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSA-02","text":"The foreclosed possibility is that of a real ultimately devoid of a why.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSA-03","text":"The system circumvents, without fully resolving, the possibility of an explanatory closure accessible to human understanding.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSA-04","text":"It treats as ontologically inadmissible a truth that would be true without relation to the false, without sufficient reason, or without determined modal position.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-01","text":"Truth is produced through a double operation: a proposition must avoid contradiction and receive a determination that distinguishes it from the false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_23:D3","CL_UCIC_11:GA-01","CL_UCIC_11:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-02","text":"The principle of sufficient reason converts the logical separation of true and false into an ontological requirement: to be true or to exist implies being determined by a reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A1","CH_UCIC_P_24:A4","CL_UCIC_11:GA-02","CL_UCIC_11:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-03","text":"The modality of the opposite provides the operative link between logical classification and analytical justification: the impossibility of the opposite initiates the search for reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A3","CH_UCIC_P_25:A6","CL_UCIC_11:GA-06","CL_UCIC_11:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-04","text":"Human ignorance does not suspend the architecture; it displaces the problem of truth onto the difference between real foundation and cognitive access.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A5","CH_UCIC_P_24:D3","CL_UCIC_11:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-05","text":"Contradiction and sufficient reason form two successive thresholds rather than a single principle: the first prohibits certain propositions, the second requires an explanation for those that remain admissible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_24:D1","CL_UCIC_11:GA-01","CL_UCIC_11:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:XD-06","text":"The closure of necessary truths produces a structural asymmetry: analysis can reach a primitive term, whereas the regime of truths of fact remains explicitly less determined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A8","CH_UCIC_P_25:DNX5","CL_UCIC_11:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-01","text":"The system transforms truth into a trajectory of validation: exclusion of contradiction, foundation by a reason, modal determination, then analysis if necessity is at issue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_25:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-02","text":"The real is reclassified as a stratified rational order rather than as a collection of immediately given facts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-03","text":"The knowing subject loses the role of measure of objective rationality and becomes the limited agent of a reconstruction whose reasons may exceed its access.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-04","text":"The time of knowledge is separated from the structure of foundation: a reason may be real before being discovered, or remain inaccessible without becoming nonexistent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:BSD-05","text":"The relevant method is neither simple observation nor assertion, but a controlled descent from the complex toward the simple and the primitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop is: proposition → test of contradiction → exclusion of the false → requirement of reason → determination of truth.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-02","text":"The modal loop is: necessary truth → impossible opposite → search for reason → successive analysis → primitives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-03","text":"The epistemic loop is: inaccessible reason → distinction between ignorance and absence of reason → maintenance of objective order → resumption of the search.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-04","text":"The conceptual attractor is the determination of a difference: every “thus” calls for the why of its selection against an “otherwise.”","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:RLE-05","text":"The point of phase change appears when contradiction ceases to be merely a defect to eliminate and becomes an operator of modal mapping.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B01","text":"A candidate proposition enters the system through a test of exclusion: enclosed contradiction → falsity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B02","text":"A proposition not excluded is subjected to the requirement of foundation: fact, existence, or truth → sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B03","text":"The reason must explain a selection: given determination → why thus rather than otherwise.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B04","text":"Modal status organizes what follows: impossible opposite → necessity and analysis; possible opposite → contingency and maintenance of openness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B05","text":"Necessary analysis narrows recursively down to primitives, whereas the inaccessibility of reasons blocks only knowledge, not rational structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_24:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B06","text":"The total machine thus produces a rationality with three filters: non-contradiction, sufficient foundation, modal closure or openness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AFM-B01","text":"Possible contradiction → classification of the false → opposition to the false → requirement of a reason → differentiation of thus and otherwise → necessary/contingent classification → analysis toward primitives or maintenance of openness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:AFM-B02","text":"Apparently brute fact → refusal of the absence of a why → objective but sometimes inaccessible reason → reorganization of the real as a stratified explanatory field.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-01","text":"The field of truth is redrawn along two joint axes: relation to the false and availability of a sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-02","text":"The difference between necessary truth and contingent truth becomes a difference of procedure, not merely of content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-03","text":"The opposition “known/unknown” ceases to overlap with the opposition “grounded/ungrounded.”","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-04","text":"Justification is mapped as a depth: observation, foundation, modality, analysis, and primitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MME-05","text":"The false opposition between necessity and analysis collapses: necessity becomes precisely that which can be reconstructed by analysis down to a primitive limit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the system concerns propositions judged true or false, facts, existents, and statements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, these objects are distributed through operations of contradiction, explanatory foundation, and modal classification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, validity is displaced from particular conclusions to the principles that make their judgment possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, the real is presupposed as rationally structured, while human access to this structure remains situated and deferred.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the form of the argument accomplishes what it asserts: it classifies, decomposes, ascends toward conditions, and rejects unfounded ultimate terms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FL-01","text":"Truth is defined by opposition to the false, but it simultaneously requires a sufficient reason; the differential relation therefore does not suffice by itself as a complete foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:A3","CH_UCIC_P_24:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FL-02","text":"Necessary truths have analytical closure, whereas the regime of justification for truths of fact remains explicitly underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:A8","CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:FL-03","text":"The universality of sufficient reason enters into tension with the frequent inaccessibility of reasons, without this tension being resolved by a theory of their knowledge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MP-01","text":"The second principle announced in the initial foundation is functionally joined by the requirement of sufficient reason, without being textually identified with it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_24:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MP-02","text":"Contradiction mutates from a negative operator of classification into a modal operator governing the possibility of the opposite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_25:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MP-03","text":"Ignorance changes status: from an apparent obstacle to rationality, it becomes a methodological boundary internal to a rational order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:HSI-01","text":"The minimal image of the system is that of a machine of filtering and foundation: a logical gate excludes contradiction, an explanatory engine grounds determination, and a modal router distinguishes necessity and contingency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a limited operator of reconstruction, capable of following certain reasons but not of measuring by its ignorance the rationality of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system is regressive and stratified: it ascends from the complex toward the simple, while reasons may precede their discovery.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_24:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:HSI-04","text":"Rational navigation consists in passing from the apparent fact to its reason, then determining whether that reason closes off the opposite or maintains a contingent possibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B01","text":"Minimal reconstruction requires four cores: exclusion of contradiction, sufficient reason, modal differentiation, and regressive analysis of necessary truths.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B02","text":"These cores suffice to reconstruct the current movement, because they preserve the passage from logical judgment to ontological foundation and then to analytical procedure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indetermination concerns the exact identity of the second principle, the nature of sufficient reasons, the status of primitives, and the complete justification of truths of fact.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_24:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B04","text":"Maximum coherence lies in the chain necessary–impossible opposite–analysis–primitives; the most unstable zone is the passage between universal rationality and contingency not fully analyzed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_25:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B05","text":"No lower unit alone produces the complete architecture: the first provides logical exclusion, the second the requirement of foundation, and the third modal differentiation as well as analytical closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:A1","CH_UCIC_P_24:A7","CH_UCIC_P_25:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B06","text":"The system is therefore reconstructible as a machine of stratified rationalization, but not as an absolute closure: its own principles maintain an openness at the level of contingent truths and the incomplete initial foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_23:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_24:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_11@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_11:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 31–33","context":"Proposition 31 · Proposition 32 · Proposition 33"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 34–36","order":12,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_26","CH_UCIC_P_27","CH_UCIC_P_28"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_12@R001","sha256":"cee5a6cf8d56615c1e58fd65c6690eeae7ca10e0ee2bf8334777850bae7350bf","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-01","text":"Le système part d’une pluralité de productions mathématiques et cherche la condition commune qui rend leur diversité intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_26:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-02","text":"L’analyse transforme cette diversité en une hiérarchie de dépendances, d’abord reconduite aux Définitions, Axiomes et Demandes, puis aux limites primitives de la définition et de la preuve.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-03","text":"La primitivité ne clôt toutefois pas uniformément le système : elle fournit des arrêts locaux, tandis que les vérités contingentes exigent une raison distribuée dans une série sans terme particulier ultime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:D2","CH_UCIC_P_28:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-04","text":"Le mouvement génératif passe ainsi d’une réduction fondationnelle à une rationalité sérielle qui maintient la suffisance de la raison sans produire de clôture finie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-05","text":"La clôture produite à ce niveau n’est pas un dernier élément, mais la conservation d’une exigence de fondation à travers la mutation du terme final en ordre total de déterminations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Toute production intelligible doit pouvoir être rapportée à des conditions constitutives, même lorsque cette relation ne prend pas la forme d’une preuve ou d’une définition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A2","CH_UCIC_P_27:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La différence entre spéculation, pratique, idée simple, principe primitif et vérité contingente modifie le régime d’intelligibilité sans abolir l’exigence de fondation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A5","CH_UCIC_P_28:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Le terminus de l’analyse se déplace d’un socle explicite de principes vers des seuils non définissables ou non démontrables, puis vers une série infinie qui ne possède aucun terme particulier final.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A4","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] La non-dérivabilité n’est pas assimilée à l’illégitimité : elle peut signaler une idée simple, un principe primitif ou une identité logique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:A5","CH_UCIC_P_27:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La légitimité logique est distribuée entre plusieurs formes de clôture : simplicité conceptuelle, primitivité axiomatique, contradiction de l’opposé et suffisance de l’ordre sériel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La raison suffisante s’étend aux vérités contingentes sans leur imposer une explication locale, finie ou isolée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_28:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Un événement présent est intelligible comme convergence de déterminations corporelles efficientes et de déterminations psychiques finales.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_28:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] L’attracteur du système est une fondation sans arbitraire : aucune contingence n’est abandonnée au hasard, mais aucune explication locale ne suffit à elle seule.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] La clôture locale est abandonnée au profit d’une clôture fonctionnelle : l’analyse s’achève non dans un dernier fait, mais dans la structure qui maintient la raison à travers l’infinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-01","text":"L’analyse revient comme opération de réduction, mais sa fonction mute : elle passe d’une reconduction vers des principes premiers à un parcours d’une série dont l’extension empêche tout arrêt particulier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A3","CH_UCIC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-02","text":"Le fondement revient d’abord comme triade explicite, puis comme idée simple ou principe primitif, enfin comme ordre total des déterminations contingentes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-03","text":"La non-dérivabilité change de statut : elle désigne successivement un point d’arrêt définitionnel, un point d’arrêt démonstratif et l’absence de terme final dans une série pourtant rationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:D4","CH_UCIC_P_28:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-04","text":"La différence entre théorie et pratique est absorbée dans une architecture commune, puis relayée par la différence entre causalité efficiente et causalité finale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D4","CH_UCIC_P_28:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-05","text":"La contradiction, d’abord propriété d’une énonciation identique, devient par déplacement un mécanisme de limitation des prétentions à la clôture et à l’explication univoque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-06","text":"Le concept de raison persiste en changeant d’échelle : d’un critère de reconstruction locale, il devient une propriété de la distribution sérielle elle-même.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-01","text":"Les théorèmes de spéculation, les canons de pratique, les idées simples, les principes primitifs et l’exemple de l’écriture restent des machines locales ; leur fonction commune n’apparaît qu’au niveau de la fondation distribuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A1","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-02","text":"La distinction locale entre spéculation et pratique devient au niveau courant une différence de régime dans une même architecture de justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D1","CH_UCIC_P_26:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-03","text":"La distinction locale entre indéfinissabilité et indémontrabilité devient une théorie générale des seuils de fondation, sans se réduire à l’un ou l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:D1","CH_UCIC_P_27:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-04","text":"La proposition locale selon laquelle les principes premiers arrêtent l’analyse est recodée : pour le contingent, l’intelligibilité exige au contraire une propagation indéfinie des raisons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-05","text":"Ce qui devient obsolète à l’échelle du cluster est l’idée qu’une fondation adéquate doive être un terme singulier, fini et immédiatement identifiable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’un théorème, un canon, une idée ou un événement constitue par lui-même le niveau ultime de justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_28:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une absence de définition ou de preuve soit automatiquement une déficience, comme il exclut qu’une contingence soit automatiquement une absence de raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut l’explication par facteur unique : la validité, l’action et la contingence dépendent de relations constitutives distribuées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GNX-04","text":"La limite externe stable du système est l’impossibilité d’une clôture analytique locale qui abolirait la profondeur des dépendances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit faux le modèle d’une connaissance entièrement dérivée, dans laquelle chaque élément devrait recevoir définition et preuve à partir d’un élément antérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_27:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que soit faux le modèle d’une contingence brute, séparée de toute raison parce que sa série explicative ne possède pas de terme fini.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie ainsi deux totalités rivales : la clôture axiomatique entièrement locale et la chaîne causale finie entièrement linéaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSA-01","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un dernier fondement particulier qui permettrait de convertir toute raison en objet simple, fini et définitivement isolable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_28:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSA-02","text":"Le système rend ontologiquement inadmissible une réalité composée soit d’unités matérielles indivisibles, soit d’événements psychiques détachés de toute histoire corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSA-03","text":"La possibilité indisponible qui donne sa force à l’ensemble est une explication sans terme final local : la raison doit subsister sans devenir une chose ultime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-01","text":"L’analyse fondationnelle ne disparaît pas devant l’infini ; elle change d’objet, en passant de la recherche d’un principe terminal à la cartographie des dépendances qui rendent un événement intelligible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-01","CL_UCIC_12:GA-03","CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_26:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-02","text":"Les limites primitives de la définition et de la preuve fournissent le modèle formel d’une clôture non locale : ce qui fonde n’est pas nécessairement un élément dérivable, mais une condition qui arrête ou distribue la régression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-04","CL_UCIC_12:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_27:D2","CH_UCIC_P_27:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-03","text":"L’extension de la raison suffisante aux vérités contingentes transforme la fondation en problème d’échelle : ce qui ne peut être conclu dans un terme particulier peut être intelligible dans l’ordre de la série.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","CL_UCIC_12:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_28:D1","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-04","text":"La distinction entre fondation théorique et pratique est relayée par une dualité interne de l’événement : l’efficience corporelle et la finalité psychique sont deux distributions coordonnées plutôt que deux domaines séparés.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-02","CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_26:D1","CH_UCIC_P_28:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-05","text":"La clôture logique par contradiction et la rationalité infinie du contingent produisent une même conséquence : la nécessité n’exige pas la finitude du parcours explicatif.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-04","CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","CL_UCIC_12:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_27:D3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-01","text":"La rationalité passe d’un modèle architectural fondé sur des principes premiers à un modèle topologique fondé sur la position d’un élément dans un réseau de dépendances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:XD-01","CL_UCIC_12:XD-03","CH_UCIC_P_26:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_28:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-02","text":"Le temps du système n’est ni une simple succession ni une régression sans structure : le présent condense une multiplicité de déterminations passées et actuelles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","CL_UCIC_12:XD-04","CH_UCIC_P_28:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-03","text":"La causalité devient une opération de coordination entre séries hétérogènes, et non la transmission linéaire d’une force depuis une origine isolée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","CL_UCIC_12:XD-04","CH_UCIC_P_28:A8","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-04","text":"Le sujet n’est plus l’origine simple de son action : il est le point de convergence de dispositions psychiques, d’états corporels et de déterminations antérieures.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_28:A7","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-05","text":"La méthode adéquate devient une reconstruction récursive des conditions, capable de maintenir la suffisance rationnelle sans la convertir en explication finie.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-01","CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","CL_UCIC_12:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_26:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale est : production dérivée → analyse → principe constitutif → nouvelle question sur le statut du principe → déplacement vers un seuil primitif ou une série plus profonde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D2","CH_UCIC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-02","text":"La voie d’escalade est : diversité des résultats → fondation commune → limites primitives → raison suffisante du contingent → infinité des déterminations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_28:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-03","text":"La répétition de la réduction signale un changement de phase : elle ne conduit plus à un principe dernier, mais à la reconnaissance que la série elle-même porte l’intelligibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est la raison suffisante, qui absorbe successivement la fondation mathématique, la primitivité logique et la causalité contingente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-05","text":"La boucle finale est : absence de terme fini → risque d’arbitraire → maintien de la raison par l’ordre total → impossibilité d’un terme fini comme condition de la cohérence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B01","text":"Pluralité de productions → opération analytique commune → réduction aux conditions constitutives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_26:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B02","text":"Conditions constitutives → distinction entre éléments définissables, idées simples, propositions démontrables et principes primitifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:D1","CH_UCIC_P_27:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B03","text":"Limites de définition et de preuve → fondation par primitivité ou identité logique plutôt que par dérivation universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_27:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B04","text":"Extension de la raison aux contingences → série créée indéfinie → impossibilité d’un terme particulier final.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B05","text":"Série infinie → convergence des causalités corporelle et psychique → clôture structurelle par maintien de la raison, non par arrêt de l’analyse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AFM-B01","text":"Diversité des productions → analyse commune → réduction fondationnelle → distinction des seuils primitifs → extension aux vérités contingentes → série infinie des raisons → convergence efficiente et finale → clôture non locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_28:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AFM-B02","text":"Recherche d’un principe premier → découverte de limites primitives → déplacement vers l’ordre des dépendances → reclassification du présent comme nœud causal distribué.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_28:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-01","text":"La carte du savoir est réorganisée selon les régimes de fondation et non selon la simple opposition entre théorie et pratique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_26:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-02","text":"La distinction entre « non prouvé » et « non légitime » s’effondre pour les principes primitifs, tandis que la distinction entre « non fini » et « non rationnel » s’effondre pour les séries contingentes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-03","text":"La cause est reclassée comme distribution sérielle, et l’événement comme intersection de lignes corporelles, psychiques, passées et présentes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-04","text":"L’objet de l’analyse devient moins le résultat isolé que la profondeur de ses médiations et la forme de leur coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-05","text":"Une méthode nouvelle devient disponible : suivre les dépendances sans exiger qu’elles convergent vers un dernier élément, tout en refusant l’hypothèse d’une contingence sans raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:D2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets explicites sont des théorèmes, des canons, des idées, des principes et une action présente dont l’écriture sert de cas de détermination multiple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Ces objets sont reclassés comme productions, seuils et événements pris dans des architectures de dépendance, de non-dérivabilité et de causalité distribuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Comprendre consiste à reconstruire les conditions constitutives, mais cette reconstruction doit accepter plusieurs formes de clôture et l’absence de terme local.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le présent est produit par l’interférence d’une infinité de déterminations, et le réel n’est pas une collection d’unités matérielles ultimement indivisibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:A5","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — La forme de l’argument accomplit ce qu’elle affirme : elle descend vers les conditions, rencontre des limites, puis transforme l’échec d’une clôture finie en structure explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FL-01","text":"La tension centrale oppose l’exigence d’une raison suffisante à l’impossibilité d’achever la résolution des raisons particulières dans un terme fini.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_28:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FL-02","text":"Une seconde tension oppose la clôture par principes premiers à la nécessité, pour le contingent, d’une série sans borne ; la première reste valide localement mais cesse d’être universalisable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FL-03","text":"Une troisième tension réside dans le statut de la raison suffisante : elle doit unifier la série sans être présentée comme un élément particulier supplémentaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation survient lorsque la réduction aux Définitions, Axiomes et Demandes devient une théorie générale des seuils de fondation plutôt qu’une clôture unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_27:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MP-02","text":"Le second point de mutation survient lorsque l’absence de preuve cesse d’être un manque et devient le signe d’une primitivité légitime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_27:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation survient lorsque l’infinité, au lieu de dissoudre la rationalité, devient le mode même selon lequel la contingence reçoit une raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une architecture stratifiée de dépendances, où les éléments ne valent pas seulement par leur contenu mais par leur position dans une chaîne ou un réseau de raisons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient un nœud de convergence : son action est produite par l’articulation de dispositions psychiques et de déterminations corporelles qui le précèdent et l’accompagnent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:A7","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est une profondeur active : le présent condense une multiplicité indéfinie de mouvements, figures, inclinations et dispositions plutôt qu’il ne commence à partir de lui-même.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_28:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:HSI-04","text":"La lutte théorique possible n’est pas la recherche d’un dernier élément, mais la reconstruction des médiations qui empêchent à la fois l’arbitraire et la clôture prématurée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B01","text":"L’ensemble est reconstructible à partir de cinq opérations : différencier les productions, réduire leurs prétentions autonomes, distinguer les seuils primitifs, étendre la raison au contingent et convertir l’infinité en structure d’intelligibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction est cohérente si la fondation n’est pas identifiée à un terme unique : les principes primitifs arrêtent certaines régressions, tandis que l’ordre sériel porte les autres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne le statut exact de la raison qui unifie une série infinie et la relation précise entre identité logique, primitivité et suffisance sérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B04","text":"La compression préserve le mouvement génératif réel : une fondation d’abord conçue comme réduction vers des premiers éléments devient une architecture récursive où la raison subsiste sans clôture analytique locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195257458321Z_bb1e057e","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 34–36","source_sha256":"cee5a6cf8d56615c1e58fd65c6690eeae7ca10e0ee2bf8334777850bae7350bf","sha256":"acca57842b63f267b046a08ad2acdcba20a98358c460c84472adec6cbc7001fa","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:52:57.462232+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-01","text":"The system begins from a plurality of mathematical productions and seeks the common condition that renders their diversity intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_26:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-02","text":"Analysis transforms this diversity into a hierarchy of dependencies, first traced back to Definitions, Axioms and Postulates, then to the primitive limits of definition and proof.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-03","text":"Primitivity does not, however, uniformly close the system: it provides local stopping points, whereas contingent truths require a reason distributed throughout a series with no ultimate particular term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:D2","CH_UCIC_P_28:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-04","text":"The generative movement thus proceeds from foundational reduction to a serial rationality that maintains the sufficiency of reason without producing finite closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AS-05","text":"The closure produced at this level is not a final element, but the preservation of a requirement of foundation through the mutation of the final term into a total order of determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every intelligible production must be capable of being related to constitutive conditions, even where this relation does not take the form of a proof or a definition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A2","CH_UCIC_P_27:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The difference between speculation, practice, simple idea, primitive principle, and contingent truth modifies the regime of intelligibility without abolishing the requirement of foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A5","CH_UCIC_P_28:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The terminus of analysis shifts from an explicit foundation of principles toward indefinable or indemonstrable thresholds, then toward an infinite series that possesses no final particular term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A4","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Non-derivability is not equated with illegitimacy: it may indicate a simple idea, a primitive principle, or a logical identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:A5","CH_UCIC_P_27:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Logical legitimacy is distributed among several forms of closure: conceptual simplicity, axiomatic primitivity, contradiction of the opposite, and sufficiency of serial order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Sufficient reason extends to contingent truths without imposing upon them a local, finite, or isolated explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_28:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] A present event is intelligible as the convergence of efficient bodily determinations and final psychic determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_28:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] The system's attractor is a foundation without arbitrariness: no contingency is abandoned to chance, but no local explanation suffices on its own.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Local closure is abandoned in favor of functional closure: analysis concludes not in a final fact, but in the structure that maintains reason through infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-01","text":"Analysis recurs as an operation of reduction, but its function mutates: it passes from tracing back to first principles to traversing a series whose extension prevents any particular stopping point.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A3","CH_UCIC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-02","text":"Foundation recurs first as an explicit triad, then as a simple idea or primitive principle, finally as the total order of contingent determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-03","text":"Non-derivability changes status: it successively designates a definitional stopping point, a demonstrative stopping point, and the absence of a final term in a nonetheless rational series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:D4","CH_UCIC_P_28:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-04","text":"The difference between theory and practice is absorbed into a common architecture, then relayed by the difference between efficient causality and final causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D4","CH_UCIC_P_28:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-05","text":"Contradiction, initially a property of an identical statement, becomes through displacement a mechanism for limiting claims to closure and univocal explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RMD-06","text":"The concept of reason persists while changing scale: from a criterion of local reconstruction, it becomes a property of serial distribution itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-01","text":"The theorems of speculation, the canons of practice, simple ideas, primitive principles, and the example of writing remain local machines; their common function appears only at the level of distributed foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A1","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-02","text":"The local distinction between speculation and practice becomes at the current level a difference of regime within one and the same architecture of justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D1","CH_UCIC_P_26:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-03","text":"The local distinction between indefinability and indemonstrability becomes a general theory of thresholds of foundation, without reducing itself to either one.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:D1","CH_UCIC_P_27:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-04","text":"The local proposition according to which first principles halt analysis is recoded: for the contingent, intelligibility instead requires an indefinite propagation of reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:CGD-05","text":"What becomes obsolete at the scale of the cluster is the idea that an adequate foundation must be a singular, finite, and immediately identifiable term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a theorem, a canon, an idea, or an event might in itself constitute the ultimate level of justification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_28:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that an absence of definition or proof is automatically a deficiency, just as it excludes the possibility that contingency is automatically an absence of reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GNX-03","text":"It excludes explanation by a single factor: validity, action, and contingency depend on distributed constitutive relations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:GNX-04","text":"The stable external limit of the system is the impossibility of a local analytical closure that would abolish the depth of dependencies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the model of an entirely derived knowledge must be false, a model in which every element would have to receive definition and proof from an earlier element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_27:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:DBN-02","text":"The model of a brute contingency, separated from all reason because its explanatory series possesses no finite term, must likewise be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:DBN-03","text":"The system thus disqualifies two rival totalities: entirely local axiomatic closure and the entirely linear finite causal chain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSA-01","text":"The structuring absence is that of a final particular foundation that would make it possible to convert every reason into a simple, finite, and definitively isolable object.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_28:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSA-02","text":"The system renders ontologically inadmissible a reality composed either of indivisible material units or of psychic events detached from all bodily history.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSA-03","text":"The unavailable possibility that gives the whole its force is an explanation without a local final term: reason must subsist without becoming an ultimate thing.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-01","text":"Foundational analysis does not disappear before infinity; it changes its object, passing from the search for a terminal principle to the mapping of dependencies that render an event intelligible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-01","CL_UCIC_12:GA-03","CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_26:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_28:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-02","text":"The primitive limits of definition and proof provide the formal model of a non-local closure: what founds is not necessarily a derivable element, but a condition that halts or distributes regress.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-04","CL_UCIC_12:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_27:D2","CH_UCIC_P_27:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-03","text":"The extension of sufficient reason to contingent truths transforms foundation into a problem of scale: what cannot be concluded in a particular term can be intelligible in the order of the series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","CL_UCIC_12:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_28:D1","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-04","text":"The distinction between theoretical and practical foundation is relayed by an internal duality of the event: bodily efficiency and psychic finality are two coordinated distributions rather than two separate domains.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-02","CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_26:D1","CH_UCIC_P_28:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:XD-05","text":"Logical closure through contradiction and the infinite rationality of contingency produce the same consequence: necessity does not require the finitude of the explanatory course.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-04","CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","CL_UCIC_12:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_27:D3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-01","text":"Rationality passes from an architectural model founded on first principles to a topological model founded on the position of an element within a network of dependencies.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:XD-01","CL_UCIC_12:XD-03","CH_UCIC_P_26:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_28:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-02","text":"The time of the system is neither a simple succession nor a regression without structure: the present condenses a multiplicity of past and present determinations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","CL_UCIC_12:XD-04","CH_UCIC_P_28:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-03","text":"Causality becomes an operation of coordination among heterogeneous series, rather than the linear transmission of a force from an isolated origin.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","CL_UCIC_12:XD-04","CH_UCIC_P_28:A8","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-04","text":"The subject is no longer the simple origin of its action: it is the point of convergence of psychic dispositions, bodily states, and prior determinations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_28:A7","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:BSD-05","text":"The adequate method becomes a recursive reconstruction of conditions, capable of maintaining rational sufficiency without converting it into a finite explanation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-01","CL_UCIC_12:GA-06","CL_UCIC_12:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_26:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop is: derived production → analysis → constitutive principle → new question concerning the status of the principle → displacement toward a primitive threshold or a deeper series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:D2","CH_UCIC_P_27:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-02","text":"The escalation path is: diversity of results → common foundation → primitive limits → sufficient reason of contingency → infinity of determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_28:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-03","text":"The repetition of reduction signals a phase change: it no longer leads to a final principle, but to the recognition that the series itself bears intelligibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-04","text":"The conceptual attractor is sufficient reason, which successively absorbs mathematical foundation, logical primitivity, and contingent causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:RLE-05","text":"The final loop is: absence of a finite term → risk of arbitrariness → maintenance of reason through total order → impossibility of a finite term as a condition of coherence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B01","text":"Plurality of productions → common analytical operation → reduction to constitutive conditions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_26:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B02","text":"Constitutive conditions → distinction between definable elements, simple ideas, demonstrable propositions, and primitive principles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:D1","CH_UCIC_P_27:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B03","text":"Limits of definition and proof → foundation through primitivity or logical identity rather than through universal derivation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_27:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B04","text":"Extension of reason to contingencies → indefinite created series → impossibility of a final particular term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B05","text":"Infinite series → convergence of bodily and psychic causalities → structural closure through maintenance of reason, not through the halting of analysis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AFM-B01","text":"Diversity of productions → common analysis → foundational reduction → distinction of primitive thresholds → extension to contingent truths → infinite series of reasons → efficient and final convergence → non-local closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_28:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:AFM-B02","text":"Search for a first principle → discovery of primitive limits → displacement toward the order of dependencies → reclassification of the present as a distributed causal node.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_28:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-01","text":"The map of knowledge is reorganized according to regimes of foundation rather than according to the simple opposition between theory and practice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_26:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-02","text":"The distinction between « unproven » and « illegitimate » collapses for primitive principles, while the distinction between « non-finite » and « non-rational » collapses for contingent series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-03","text":"Cause is reclassified as serial distribution, and the event as the intersection of bodily, psychic, past, and present lines.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-04","text":"The object of analysis becomes less the isolated result than the depth of its mediations and the form of their coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MME-05","text":"A new method becomes available: following dependencies without requiring them to converge toward a final element, while refusing the hypothesis of a contingency without reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:D2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit objects are theorems, canons, ideas, principles, and a present action for which writing serves as a case of multiple determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — These objects are reclassified as productions, thresholds, and events caught within architectures of dependency, non-derivability, and distributed causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Understanding consists in reconstructing constitutive conditions, but this reconstruction must accept several forms of closure and the absence of a local term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The present is produced by the interference of an infinity of determinations, and the real is not a collection of ultimately indivisible material units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:A5","CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The form of the argument performs what it affirms: it descends toward conditions, encounters limits, then transforms the failure of finite closure into explanatory structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FL-01","text":"The central tension opposes the requirement of sufficient reason to the impossibility of completing the resolution of particular reasons in a finite term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_28:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FL-02","text":"A second tension opposes closure through first principles to the necessity, for contingency, of a boundless series; the former remains locally valid but ceases to be universally applicable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:A6","CH_UCIC_P_28:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:FL-03","text":"A third tension lies in the status of sufficient reason: it must unify the series without being presented as an additional particular element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point occurs when reduction to Definitions, Axioms and Postulates becomes a general theory of thresholds of foundation rather than a single closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_27:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point occurs when the absence of proof ceases to be a lack and becomes the sign of a legitimate primitivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_27:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point occurs when infinity, instead of dissolving rationality, becomes the very mode by which contingency receives a reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a stratified architecture of dependencies, in which elements count not only by their content but by their position in a chain or network of reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a node of convergence: its action is produced by the articulation of psychic dispositions and bodily determinations that precede and accompany it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:A7","CH_UCIC_P_28:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:HSI-03","text":"Time is an active depth: the present condenses an indefinite multiplicity of movements, figures, inclinations, and dispositions rather than beginning from itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_28:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:HSI-04","text":"The possible theoretical struggle is not the search for a final element, but the reconstruction of mediations that prevent both arbitrariness and premature closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_28:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_28:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B01","text":"The whole is reconstructible from five operations: differentiating productions, reducing their autonomous claims, distinguishing primitive thresholds, extending reason to contingency, and converting infinity into a structure of intelligibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction is coherent if foundation is not identified with a single term: primitive principles halt certain regressions, whereas serial order bears the others.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the exact status of the reason that unifies an infinite series and the precise relation between logical identity, primitivity, and serial sufficiency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_27:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_28:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B04","text":"The compression preserves the real generative movement: a foundation first conceived as reduction toward first elements becomes a recursive architecture in which reason subsists without local analytical closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_26:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_28:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_12@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_12:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 34–36","context":"Proposition 34 · Proposition 35 · Proposition 36"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 37–39","order":13,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_29","CH_UCIC_P_30","CH_UCIC_P_31"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_13@R001","sha256":"2a084489c923531d01b967c17d3e488db0acb6a5162ccd7322aa1905087d9039","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-01","text":"La contingence renvoie toujours à une autre contingence et ne produit donc jamais, par simple prolongation analytique, une raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-02","text":"La régression infinie conserve le statut contingent de chacun de ses termes et échoue ainsi à devenir une clôture explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-03","text":"L’insuffisance interne de la série impose une rupture de niveau entre les choses à expliquer et la raison qui rend leur explication possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-04","text":"Cette rupture est recodée comme l’existence d’une substance nécessaire qui contient éminemment les changements sans se confondre avec leur détail.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-05","text":"La totalité du détail devient explicable lorsqu’elle est saisie comme un ensemble lié dépendant d’une raison unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-06","text":"Le mouvement est donc régressif, cumulatif et mutationnel : il transforme une demande de fondement en hiérarchie ontologique, puis cette hiérarchie en unicité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-07","text":"La clôture est produite par la suffisance attribuée à un Dieu unique, mais le passage de la nécessité à cette dénomination demeure partiellement posé plutôt que démontré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Une série composée uniquement de contingences ne peut porter en elle-même sa raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Chaque explication contingente reconduit la demande d’une analyse supplémentaire au lieu de la satisfaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] L’infinité de la régression augmente l’étendue de la dépendance sans transformer cette dépendance en fondement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] La demande d’une raison dernière exige un changement de registre entre l’ordre contingent et son principe explicatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] La raison dernière doit être portée par une substance nécessaire et non par une substance contingente supplémentaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] L’extériorité d’abord exigée comme condition de la raison devient une source ontologique des changements particuliers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Les changements sont contenus éminemment dans leur source, ce qui établit une relation de fondation sans identité détaillée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Le détail n’est explicable comme totalité que s’il est présupposé comme intégralement lié.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] La substance nécessaire est identifiée comme Dieu, ce qui convertit une structure explicative en désignation théologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] La suffisance d’un Dieu unique ferme la recherche d’un principe divin ou explicatif additionnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-01","text":"[Persistent] La contingence revient comme dépendance successive : dans la première unité elle forme une série régressive, puis elle reste le statut inférieur des changements rapportés à une source nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A1","CH_UCIC_P_30:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-02","text":"[Mutating] La régression passe d’une procédure d’analyse à une preuve négative de l’insuffisance de toute clôture interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-03","text":"[Displaced] La raison suffisante migre d’une exigence encore indéterminée vers une substance nécessaire, puis vers un principe nommé Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_30:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-04","text":"[Mutating] L’extériorité cesse d’être une simple position hors de la série et devient une relation de source à effets dérivés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A6","CH_UCIC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-05","text":"[Reversal] Le détail, d’abord signe de dispersion et d’insuffisance, devient ensuite une totalité liée qui rend possible l’unité du principe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_31:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-06","text":"[Absorption] L’infini perd sa fonction de solution et est absorbé comme simple propriété non concluante de la série contingente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-07","text":"[Terminal Transformation] La pluralité des phénomènes est conservée, mais la pluralité des principes est supprimée par la suffisance d’une source unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-01","text":"[Local] La simple constatation qu’un contingent renvoie à d’autres contingents appartient à la machine régressive locale et ne constitue pas encore l’architecture du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-02","text":"[Scale-Shift] Au niveau courant, la répétition de la régression devient le mécanisme qui force le passage vers une raison extérieure à la série.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-03","text":"[Cross-Unit] La substance nécessaire relie l’exigence apophatique d’une extériorité à la détermination positive d’une source des changements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-04","text":"[Catalytic] La présence éminente catalyse le passage entre fondation et manifestation sans réduire la multiplicité à une identité détaillée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-05","text":"[Emergent] La liaison universelle du détail n’est pas une propriété locale d’un changement : elle rend possible l’unicité de la raison pour l’ensemble du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-06","text":"[Recoded] La conclusion théologique ne se contente pas d’ajouter un terme à la série ; elle recode la série entière comme dépendante d’un principe suffisant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-07","text":"[Obsolete] Une explication obtenue par simple ajout de contingences devient obsolète dès que la question porte sur la raison du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une analyse plus détaillée produise à elle seule une explication dernière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut que l’antériorité d’un terme dans la série lui confère le statut de fondement ultime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut que l’infini transforme une succession de dépendances en raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que la raison dernière soit une substance contingente ou un changement particulier parmi les autres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_30:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut que la totalité des phénomènes exige une pluralité irréductible de principes premiers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut enfin qu’un second principe soit nécessaire pour compléter la suffisance du premier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-01","text":"Le système doit rendre fausse l’hypothèse selon laquelle une série infinie pourrait se clore par sa seule prolongation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-02","text":"Il doit également disqualifier l’idée qu’une totalité de raisons conditionnées devienne inconditionnée par simple totalisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-03","text":"Il ne peut admettre que la source nécessaire soit composée de détails changeants, car la source perdrait alors sa fonction de fondement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-04","text":"Il ne peut admettre que le réel soit sans raison totale, puisque la liaison du détail est mobilisée pour établir l’unité explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-05","text":"La distinction entre principe et conséquence doit rester irréductible à l’intérieur de l’ordre temporel des changements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSA-01","text":"L’absence la plus profonde est celle d’un terme interne capable de porter en lui-même la raison de toute la série contingente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSA-02","text":"Le système forclôt la possibilité d’un réel dont la liaison générale ne conduirait à aucune raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSA-03","text":"Il rend ontologiquement inadmissible l’idée que l’infini puisse remplacer le fondement ou qu’un second principe doive compléter le premier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_31:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-01","text":"La régression contingente ne produit pas seulement une insuffisance locale : elle engendre la nécessité d’un principe appartenant à un autre ordre que la série.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-01","CL_UCIC_13:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_29:D4","CH_UCIC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-02","text":"L’extériorité exigée par l’analyse est déterminée par l’unité suivante comme une substance nécessaire plutôt que comme une abstraction hors série.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-04","CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","CL_UCIC_13:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_29:A6","CH_UCIC_P_30:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-03","text":"La présence éminente fournit le médiateur conceptuel entre une source séparée du détail et une source qui en contient pourtant la détermination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-06","CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_30:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-04","text":"La liaison intégrale du détail transforme la substance nécessaire en principe unique de l’ensemble plutôt qu’en simple fondement d’une partie des changements.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","CL_UCIC_13:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_31:A2","CH_UCIC_P_31:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-05","text":"L’unicité divine résulte de l’articulation entre totalité liée et suffisance explicative, non d’une simple suppression numérique de la pluralité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-08","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_31:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_31:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-06","text":"La clôture finale est structurellement productive mais demeure tendue, car l’identification de la substance nécessaire à Dieu est affirmée sans médiation démonstrative équivalente.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","CL_UCIC_13:GA-09","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_31:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-01","text":"Le système convertit une demande épistémique de raison en hiérarchie ontologique entre contingence dérivée et nécessité fondatrice.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-01","CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_29:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_30:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-02","text":"L’infini cesse d’être une profondeur explicative et devient le nom d’une dépendance qui ne change pas de nature.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-02","CL_UCIC_13:GA-03","CH_UCIC_P_29:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-03","text":"La relation entre source et manifestation établit une asymétrie fondamentale : la source explique les changements, tandis que les changements ne peuvent expliquer la source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_30:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-04","text":"La liaison universelle du détail permet de comprimer une multiplicité phénoménale en dépendance ordonnée à un principe unique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-08","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_31:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-05","text":"La clôture explicative ne supprime pas la diversité des choses ; elle en déplace le statut, de principes possibles vers des manifestations dérivées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_30:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-06","text":"Le statut terminal de Dieu est produit comme effet de fermeture de la recherche, tandis que la nature positive de la raison dernière reste partiellement indéterminée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-09","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-01","text":"La boucle primaire est contingence → analyse → nouvelle contingence : chaque tentative de fondation interne reconduit le point de départ sous une forme plus détaillée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-02","text":"La répétition change de phase lorsque l’échec de chaque clôture interne devient la preuve cumulative qu’un changement de niveau est requis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-03","text":"La voie d’escalade est série contingente → extériorité → substance nécessaire → source éminente → raison unique → Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-04","text":"Une boucle de totalisation s’établit entre le détail lié qui appelle une raison unique et la raison unique qui requalifie le détail comme dépendance ordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est une substance nécessaire, unique et suffisante, capable de fermer l’explication sans être réintégrée dans la série qu’elle explique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-06","text":"Le point de mutation terminal survient lorsque la raison dernière cesse d’être une fonction abstraite et reçoit le nom de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B01","text":"Soit une multiplicité de contingences dont chaque terme renvoie à un autre terme : la série produit une dépendance récursive sans fondement interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B02","text":"Pour toute extension finie ou infinie de la série, chaque terme demeure contingent ; l’extension ne modifie donc pas le statut explicatif de l’ensemble.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B03","text":"Si la série ne peut produire sa raison, alors une coupure de niveau est posée entre l’ordre des contingences et une raison extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B04","text":"La raison extérieure est déterminée comme substance nécessaire, puis comme source éminente des changements particuliers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B05","text":"Si le détail total est lié, sa dépendance peut être rapportée à une seule substance suffisante plutôt qu’à plusieurs principes irréductibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B06","text":"L’unité de la raison explicative est finalement identifiée à l’unicité divine, laquelle clôt la recherche d’un fondement supplémentaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AFM-B01","text":"Contingence détaillée → régression homogène → insuffisance de l’infini → rupture de niveau → substance nécessaire → présence éminente → totalité liée → raison unique → unicité divine → clôture explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_30:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_31:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-01","text":"Le champ explicatif est divisé entre une série interne de dépendances et une raison externe qui n’appartient pas au même régime ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-02","text":"L’infini est reclassé : de solution potentielle de la régression, il devient une propriété incapable de produire la clôture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-03","text":"La pluralité phénoménale et la pluralité des principes sont séparées, de sorte que la première peut subsister sous l’unité de la seconde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-04","text":"Le détail est redessiné comme totalité intelligiblement liée plutôt que comme agrégat dispersé de faits indépendants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-05","text":"La méthode explicative disponible n’est plus l’accumulation de raisons locales, mais l’identification du niveau capable de rendre raison de leur série entière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-06","text":"La clôture du champ est obtenue par suffisance et unicité, non par épuisement descriptif du détail.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les changements particuliers et les contingences détaillées sont traités comme des réalités qui exigent une raison au-delà de leur succession.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Le système organise ces réalités en chaîne de dépendances, puis en hiérarchie entre source nécessaire et effets dérivés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] La question est déplacée de l’explication d’un terme particulier vers la détermination de la raison de la série entière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] La succession, l’antériorité et l’infinité appartiennent à l’ordre contingent, tandis que la nécessité est posée comme fondement d’un autre ordre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme régressive accomplit son propre dépassement : elle prolonge l’analyse jusqu’au point où l’analyse interne doit être abandonnée au profit d’une fondation externe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FL-01","text":"[Tension] L’insuffisance de la série établit la nécessité d’une sortie, mais ne démontre pas à elle seule que cette sortie doive être une substance nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FL-02","text":"[Tension] La présence éminente relie source et changements, mais son mode exact reste indéterminé et oscille entre métaphore de la source et contenu ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FL-03","text":"[Tension] Le passage de la substance nécessaire à l’appellation « Dieu » fonctionne comme fermeture argumentative, sans démonstration supplémentaire de l’identité ainsi posée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FL-04","text":"[Tension] La liaison universelle du détail rend plausible une raison unique, mais le lien entre suffisance et unicité divine reste affirmé plus que déduit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MP-01","text":"[Mutation] L’infinité passe du statut de possibilité de la série à celui de preuve de son incapacité à se clore.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MP-02","text":"[Mutation] La raison suffisante passe d’une demande laissée ouverte à une substance nécessaire qui devient la source des changements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MP-03","text":"[Mutation] Le détail passe d’un ensemble régressif de contingences à une totalité liée qui autorise l’unité du principe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MP-04","text":"[Mutation] L’extériorité passe d’une limite négative de la série à une détermination positive nommée Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une machine à niveaux : ses éléments inférieurs se conditionnent réciproquement, mais leur ensemble ne peut produire son propre principe de suffisance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet connaissant devient l’opérateur d’une montée de niveau : il suit la régression jusqu’à ce que la poursuite du même type d’explication cesse d’être pertinente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est représenté comme succession contingente incapable de porter le fondement ; la nécessité occupe une position hors de cette temporalité dérivée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée systémique consiste à quitter la chaîne des dépendances, tandis que la capture terminale consiste à reconduire toute la multiplicité vers une source unique et suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B01","text":"Un noyau minimal de quatre propositions suffit à reconstruire le cluster : la contingence renvoie, l’infini ne fonde pas, la raison doit être nécessaire et la totalité liée dépend d’un principe unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A3","CH_UCIC_P_30:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B02","text":"Ce noyau préserve le mouvement génératif complet, depuis la régression négative jusqu’à la clôture par suffisance divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B03","text":"La reconstruction reste indéterminée quant au contenu positif de la nécessité, au sens exact de la présence éminente et à la justification du nom « Dieu ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B04","text":"La liaison universelle du détail est indispensable : sans elle, le passage d’une substance suffisante à l’unicité divine ne peut être reconstruit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B05","text":"La compression élimine les détails locaux de la régression, mais conserve la machine entière : insuffisance interne, changement de niveau, source nécessaire, totalisation et clôture unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195328511691Z_bd415857","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 37–39","source_sha256":"2a084489c923531d01b967c17d3e488db0acb6a5162ccd7322aa1905087d9039","sha256":"5207ed2e87f69418af24347e167c7a02995ec59d236c3377d29e3e10169554f2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:53:28.515282+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-01","text":"Contingency always refers back to another contingency and therefore never produces, through mere analytical prolongation, a sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-02","text":"Infinite regress preserves the contingent status of each of its terms and thus fails to become an explanatory closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-03","text":"The internal insufficiency of the series imposes a break in level between the things to be explained and the reason that makes their explanation possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-04","text":"This break is recoded as the existence of a necessary substance that contains changes eminently without being identical with their detail.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-05","text":"The totality of detail becomes explicable when it is grasped as a connected whole dependent on a single reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-06","text":"The movement is therefore regressive, cumulative, and mutational: it transforms a demand for a foundation into an ontological hierarchy, then that hierarchy into divine uniqueness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AS-07","text":"Closure is produced by the sufficiency attributed to a unique God, but the passage from necessity to this designation remains partly posited rather than demonstrated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A series composed solely of contingencies cannot bear within itself its sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Each contingent explanation renews the demand for further analysis instead of satisfying it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The infinity of regress increases the extent of dependence without transforming that dependence into a foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The demand for an ultimate reason requires a change of register between the contingent order and its explanatory principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] The ultimate reason must be borne by a necessary substance and not by an additional contingent substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Exteriority, initially required as the condition of reason, becomes an ontological source of particular changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Changes are contained eminently in their source, which establishes a relation of foundation without detailed identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Detail is explicable as a totality only if it is presupposed as integrally connected.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] The necessary substance is identified as God, thereby converting an explanatory structure into a theological designation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The sufficiency of a unique God closes the search for an additional divine or explanatory principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-01","text":"[Persistent] Contingency recurs as successive dependence: in the first unit it forms a regressive series, then it remains the inferior status of changes referred to a necessary source.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A1","CH_UCIC_P_30:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-02","text":"[Mutating] Regress shifts from a procedure of analysis to a negative proof of the insufficiency of every internal closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-03","text":"[Displaced] Sufficient reason migrates from a still indeterminate requirement toward a necessary substance, then toward a principle named God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_30:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-04","text":"[Mutating] Exteriority ceases to be a mere position outside the series and becomes a relation of source to derived effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A6","CH_UCIC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-05","text":"[Reversal] Detail, initially a sign of dispersion and insufficiency, subsequently becomes a connected totality that makes the unity of the principle possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_31:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-06","text":"[Absorption] Infinity loses its function as a solution and is absorbed as a merely non-conclusive property of the contingent series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RMD-07","text":"[Terminal Transformation] The plurality of phenomena is preserved, but the plurality of principles is eliminated by the sufficiency of a unique source.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The mere observation that one contingent refers to other contingents belongs to the local regressive mechanism and does not yet constitute the architecture of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-02","text":"[Scale-Shift] At the current level, the repetition of regress becomes the mechanism that compels the passage toward a reason external to the series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-03","text":"[Cross-Unit] The necessary substance connects the apophatic requirement of an exteriority to the positive determination of a source of changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-04","text":"[Catalytic] Eminent presence catalyzes the passage between foundation and manifestation without reducing multiplicity to detailed identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-05","text":"[Emergent] The universal connectedness of detail is not a local property of a change: it makes possible the uniqueness of the reason for the whole of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-06","text":"[Recoded] The theological conclusion does not merely add a term to the series; it recodes the entire series as dependent on a sufficient principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:CGD-07","text":"[Obsolete] An explanation obtained by the mere addition of contingencies becomes obsolete as soon as the question concerns the reason for the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a more detailed analysis alone could produce an ultimate explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that the priority of a term in the series confers upon it the status of ultimate foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that infinity transforms a succession of dependencies into a sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that the ultimate reason is a contingent substance or a particular change among others.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_30:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the possibility that the totality of phenomena requires an irreducible plurality of first principles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:GNX-06","text":"Finally, it excludes the possibility that a second principle is necessary to complete the sufficiency of the first.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-01","text":"The system must render false the hypothesis according to which an infinite series could close through its own internal prolongation alone.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-02","text":"It must also disqualify the idea that a totality of conditioned reasons becomes unconditioned through mere totalization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-03","text":"It cannot admit that the necessary source is composed of changing details, for the source would then lose its function as foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-04","text":"It cannot admit that reality is without a total reason, since the connectedness of detail is mobilized to establish explanatory unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:DBN-05","text":"The distinction between principle and consequence must remain irreducible within the temporal order of changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSA-01","text":"The deepest absence is that of an internal term capable of bearing within itself the reason for the entire contingent series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSA-02","text":"The system forecloses the possibility of a reality whose general connectedness would lead to no sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSA-03","text":"It renders ontologically inadmissible the idea that infinity could replace the foundation or that a second principle should complete the first.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_31:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-01","text":"Contingent regress produces not merely a local insufficiency: it generates the necessity of a principle belonging to an order other than that of the series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-01","CL_UCIC_13:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_29:D4","CH_UCIC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-02","text":"The exteriority required by analysis is determined by the following unit as a necessary substance rather than as an abstraction outside the series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-04","CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","CL_UCIC_13:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_29:A6","CH_UCIC_P_30:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-03","text":"Eminent presence supplies the conceptual mediator between a source separate from detail and a source that nevertheless contains its determination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-06","CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_30:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_30:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-04","text":"The integral connectedness of detail transforms the necessary substance into the unique principle of the whole rather than a mere foundation of a part of the changes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","CL_UCIC_13:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_31:A2","CH_UCIC_P_31:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-05","text":"Divine uniqueness results from the articulation between connected totality and explanatory sufficiency, not from a mere numerical suppression of plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-08","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_31:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_31:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:XD-06","text":"Final closure is structurally productive but remains strained, for the identification of the necessary substance with God is affirmed without equivalent demonstrative mediation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","CL_UCIC_13:GA-09","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_31:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-01","text":"The system converts an epistemic demand for reason into an ontological hierarchy between derived contingency and founding necessity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-01","CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_29:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_30:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-02","text":"Infinity ceases to be an explanatory depth and becomes the name of a dependence that does not change in nature.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-02","CL_UCIC_13:GA-03","CH_UCIC_P_29:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-03","text":"The relation between source and manifestation establishes a fundamental asymmetry: the source explains changes, whereas changes cannot explain the source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-05","CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_30:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-04","text":"The universal connectedness of detail makes it possible to compress a phenomenal multiplicity into ordered dependence on a unique principle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-08","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_31:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-05","text":"Explanatory closure does not eliminate the diversity of things; it displaces their status, from possible principles to derived manifestations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-07","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_30:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:BSD-06","text":"The terminal status of God is produced as an effect of the closure of inquiry, while the positive nature of the ultimate reason remains partly indeterminate.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GA-09","CL_UCIC_13:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-01","text":"The primary loop is contingency → analysis → new contingency: every attempt at internal foundation returns to the starting point in a more detailed form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-02","text":"Repetition changes phase when the failure of every internal closure becomes the cumulative proof that a change of level is required.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-03","text":"The escalation path is contingent series → exteriority → necessary substance → eminent source → unique reason → God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-04","text":"A loop of totalization is established between connected detail that calls for a unique reason and the unique reason that requalifies detail as ordered dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is a necessary, unique, and sufficient substance, capable of closing explanation without being reintegrated into the series it explains.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:RLE-06","text":"The terminal mutation point occurs when the ultimate reason ceases to be an abstract function and receives the name of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B01","text":"Let there be a multiplicity of contingencies, each term of which refers to another term: the series produces a recursive dependence without internal foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B02","text":"For every finite or infinite extension of the series, each term remains contingent; the extension therefore does not modify the explanatory status of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B03","text":"If the series cannot produce its reason, then a break in level is posited between the order of contingencies and an external reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B04","text":"The external reason is determined as a necessary substance, then as the eminent source of particular changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B05","text":"If total detail is connected, its dependence can be referred to a single sufficient substance rather than to several irreducible principles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B06","text":"The unity of explanatory reason is ultimately identified with divine uniqueness, which closes the search for an additional foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:AFM-B01","text":"Detailed contingency → homogeneous regress → insufficiency of infinity → break in level → necessary substance → eminent presence → connected totality → unique reason → divine uniqueness → explanatory closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_30:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_31:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-01","text":"The explanatory field is divided between an internal series of dependencies and an external reason that does not belong to the same ontological regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-02","text":"Infinity is reclassified: from a potential solution to regress, it becomes a property incapable of producing closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-03","text":"Phenomenal plurality and plurality of principles are separated, such that the former can subsist under the unity of the latter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-04","text":"Detail is redrawn as an intelligibly connected totality rather than as a dispersed aggregate of independent facts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-05","text":"The available explanatory method is no longer the accumulation of local reasons, but the identification of the level capable of accounting for their entire series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MME-06","text":"Closure of the field is obtained through sufficiency and uniqueness, not through descriptive exhaustion of detail.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Particular changes and detailed contingencies are treated as realities requiring a reason beyond their succession.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] The system organizes these realities into a chain of dependencies, then into a hierarchy between necessary source and derived effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The question is displaced from the explanation of a particular term toward the determination of the reason for the entire series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Succession, priority, and infinity belong to the contingent order, while necessity is posited as the foundation of another order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The regressive form performs its own overcoming: it prolongs analysis to the point at which internal analysis must be abandoned in favor of an external foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FL-01","text":"[Tension] The insufficiency of the series establishes the necessity of an exit, but does not by itself demonstrate that this exit must be a necessary substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FL-02","text":"[Tension] Eminent presence connects source and changes, but its exact mode remains indeterminate and oscillates between a metaphor of source and ontological content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FL-03","text":"[Tension] The passage from necessary substance to the appellation « God » functions as argumentative closure, without further demonstration of the identity thus posited.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:FL-04","text":"[Tension] The universal connectedness of detail makes a unique reason plausible, but the link between sufficiency and divine uniqueness remains asserted more than deduced.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MP-01","text":"[Mutation] Infinity shifts from the status of a possibility of the series to that of proof of its incapacity to close.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MP-02","text":"[Mutation] Sufficient reason shifts from an open demand to a necessary substance that becomes the source of changes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MP-03","text":"[Mutation] Detail shifts from a regressive set of contingencies to a connected totality that authorizes the unity of the principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MP-04","text":"[Mutation] Exteriority shifts from a negative limit of the series to a positive determination named God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a machine of levels: its lower elements condition one another reciprocally, but their whole cannot produce its own principle of sufficiency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:HSI-02","text":"The knowing subject becomes the operator of an ascent in level: it follows the regress until the continuation of the same type of explanation ceases to be relevant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:HSI-03","text":"Time is represented as contingent succession incapable of bearing the foundation; necessity occupies a position outside this derived temporality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:HSI-04","text":"The only systemic escape consists in leaving the chain of dependencies, while terminal capture consists in leading all multiplicity back to a unique and sufficient source.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B01","text":"A minimal core of four propositions suffices to reconstruct the cluster: contingency refers onward, infinity does not found, reason must be necessary, and the connected totality depends on a unique principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:A3","CH_UCIC_P_30:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B02","text":"This core preserves the complete generative movement, from negative regress to closure through divine sufficiency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_30:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction remains indeterminate regarding the positive content of necessity, the exact meaning of eminent presence, and the justification of the name « God ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B04","text":"The universal connectedness of detail is indispensable: without it, the passage from a sufficient substance to divine uniqueness cannot be reconstructed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_31:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_13:MRT-B05","text":"Compression eliminates the local details of regress, but preserves the entire mechanism: internal insufficiency, change of level, necessary source, totalization, and unique closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_29:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_13@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_13:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 37–39","context":"Proposition 37 · Proposition 38 · Proposition 39"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 40–42","order":14,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_32","CH_UCIC_P_33","CH_UCIC_P_34"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_14@R001","sha256":"12523f58d6c66ba241a556c707c66a333bd97bbbbfaeae01e262a8d3a9cdc3bb","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-01","text":"Le système cherche à déterminer comment une réalité suprême peut être à la fois unique, nécessaire, illimitée et pleinement réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-02","text":"Il recadre la perfection comme grandeur de réalité positive dégagée de toute borne plutôt que comme accumulation de qualités finies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-03","text":"L’absence d’extérieur indépendant transforme l’unité suprême en totalité ontologique autosuffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-04","text":"La non-limitation divine devient le principe de l’infinité absolue et de la plénitude du réel possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-05","text":"La perfection créée est ensuite distribuée asymétriquement : reçue quant à ses déterminations positives, mais limitée par la nature propre de la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-06","text":"La finitude n’est donc pas une privation accidentelle, mais le principe interne de l’imperfection créaturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-07","text":"L’inertie corporelle matérialise cette structure en convertissant une limitation ontologique en propriété physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-08","text":"Le mouvement général est cumulatif et descendant : propriétés suprêmes, exclusion de l’extérieur, infinité, différenciation créaturelle, puis manifestation physique de la finitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS6","CH_UCIC_P_34:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Une substance suprême existe comme principe de l’architecture ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’unicité, l’universalité et la nécessité de la substance suprême excluent la coexistence de principes indépendants concurrents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Rien d’indépendant ne subsiste hors de la substance suprême ; l’altérité ontologique extérieure est donc forclose.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Le rapport de la substance suprême à l’être possible est simple et interne plutôt que composé ou externe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] La perfection se mesure par la grandeur de la réalité positive, abstraction faite des bornes qui la restreignent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-06","text":"[Terminal] L’absence de toute borne convertit la perfection en infinité absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Les perfections créaturelles sont reçues de l’influence divine, mais cette réception ne supprime pas la limitation propre de la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A1","CH_UCIC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] La finitude appartient constitutivement à la nature créaturelle et non à une simple déficience contingente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A3","CH_UCIC_P_34:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] La différence entre Dieu et les créatures est une différence de régime ontologique : illimitation d’un côté, limitation constitutive de l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A4","CH_UCIC_P_34:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] La limite fonctionne comme opérateur de différenciation : exclue au niveau suprême, elle devient constitutive au niveau créaturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_34:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-01","text":"La récurrence de l’absence de limites change de fonction : elle fonde d’abord la plénitude divine, puis sert de critère négatif pour définir la finitude créaturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_34:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-02","text":"La perfection migre d’une propriété de la substance suprême vers une détermination reçue par les créatures, sans devenir pour autant leur principe autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A4","CH_UCIC_P_34:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-03","text":"La notion de nature passe d’un rapport simple à l’être possible à une source interne d’imperfection et de limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A6","CH_UCIC_P_34:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-04","text":"L’extérieur indépendant est supprimé au sommet, tandis que la différence créaturelle est conservée sous la forme d’une limite interne non indépendante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A5","CH_UCIC_P_34:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-05","text":"L’unité ne reste pas une simple singularité numérique : elle se transforme en totalité intensive contenant la réalité possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_32:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-06","text":"L’imperfection passe d’une négation abstraite à une manifestation corporelle déterminée par l’inertie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A5","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-07","text":"La négation de la limite produit finalement une positivité maximale, tandis que la limite créaturelle devient le mode d’existence de la négativité ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-01","text":"Les affirmations locales sur l’unicité, l’infinité ou l’inertie ne portent pas isolément au niveau du cluster ; elles deviennent opératoires lorsqu’elles sont intégrées à une économie commune de la limite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A2","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-02","text":"La distinction d’échelle majeure consiste à passer d’une propriété divine particulière à une architecture générale de distribution entre réalité suprême et réalité créée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-03","text":"Le pont inter-unitaire est fourni par la notion de borne : son exclusion définit le suprême, son intériorisation définit la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-04","text":"La transition théologique vers le physique est catalysée par l’identification de l’inertie comme manifestation d’une structure ontologique antérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-05","text":"Le modèle d’une perfection limitée devient obsolète au niveau courant, car la perfection est recodée comme réalité positive sans restriction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_33:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-06","text":"Le modèle d’une créature auto-fondée est dépassé : la créature dépend de Dieu pour ses perfections, mais non pour le principe de ses imperfections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-01","text":"Le système rejette toute substance suprême dépendante d’un principe extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut une pluralité de réalités nécessaires et indépendantes pouvant limiter ou concurrencer la substance suprême.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_32:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-03","text":"Il refuse que l’être possible demeure un domaine autonome extérieur à la substance suprême.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-04","text":"Il disqualifie un Dieu fini ou déterminé par une borne interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A4","CH_UCIC_P_33:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-05","text":"Il refuse que l’imperfection corporelle soit un accident sans rapport avec la nature créaturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-06","text":"Il interdit enfin d’identifier la créature à Dieu ou de lui attribuer une perfection auto-fondée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_34:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-01","text":"Le système ne peut tenir que si la substance suprême ne reçoit aucune détermination fondamentale d’un dehors indépendant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-02","text":"Il doit être faux que plusieurs réalités nécessaires puissent coexister sans être reconduites à une unité supérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-03","text":"Il doit être faux que le possible excède la substance suprême comme totalité autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-04","text":"Il doit être faux que la finitude soit le régime ultime de toute réalité ; elle ne vaut que comme détermination créaturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A6","CH_UCIC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-05","text":"Il doit être faux que l’imperfection créaturelle soit directement produite par l’influence divine plutôt que par la nature limitée de la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_34:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSA-01","text":"L’extérieur indépendant constitue la possibilité indisponible autour de laquelle se ferme toute l’architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSA-02","text":"Le système ne laisse subsister aucun reste de réalité positive qui excéderait la substance suprême sans relever d’elle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSA-03","text":"Une créature absolument auto-suffisante est ontologiquement inadmissible, car la perfection lui vient d’une influence extérieure tandis que sa limitation lui appartient en propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSA-04","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une altérité indépendante : la différence Dieu-créature est maintenue sans devenir séparation de deux absolus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_34:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-01","text":"L’exclusion de tout extérieur indépendant, jointe à la définition positive de la perfection, transforme l’infinité en propriété de clôture ontologique plutôt qu’en simple grandeur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_33:SD2","CL_UCIC_14:GA-03","CL_UCIC_14:GA-05","CL_UCIC_14:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-02","text":"La différence entre Dieu et la créature n’est pas une opposition entre plénitude et néant, mais entre plénitude illimitée et réception limitée de déterminations positives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_34:D1","CL_UCIC_14:GA-05","CL_UCIC_14:GA-07","CL_UCIC_14:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-03","text":"La finitude créaturelle permet de conserver une hiérarchie ontologique sans réintroduire un principe extérieur indépendant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A5","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2","CL_UCIC_14:GA-03","CL_UCIC_14:GA-08","CL_UCIC_14:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-04","text":"La perfection divine et l’imperfection créaturelle forment deux régimes corrélés de la limite : suppression au sommet, constitution à la base.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:D3","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2","CL_UCIC_14:GA-06","CL_UCIC_14:GA-08","CL_UCIC_14:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-05","text":"L’inertie corporelle devient la preuve phénoménale que la négativité de la finitude possède une efficacité structurelle et n’est pas une simple absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A6","CH_UCIC_P_34:D4","CL_UCIC_14:GA-08","CL_UCIC_14:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-06","text":"La totalité suprême n’abolit pas la différence des créatures ; elle l’absorbe comme différenciation interne de la réalité possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_34:DNX4","CL_UCIC_14:GA-03","CL_UCIC_14:GA-04","CL_UCIC_14:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-07","text":"L’attribution séparée des perfections et des imperfections fonctionne comme dispositif de sauvegarde de la plénitude divine : ce qui limite la créature n’est pas imputé à la source de ses perfections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1","CL_UCIC_14:GA-07","CL_UCIC_14:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme totalité différenciée : aucune réalité indépendante ne demeure extérieure, mais des régimes internes de limitation persistent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_32:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-02","text":"La causalité devient asymétrique : la source suprême explique la positivité des perfections, tandis que la nature propre explique la négativité des limites.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-03","text":"La négation acquiert une fonction productive : supprimer la borne ne conduit pas au vide, mais à la maximisation de la réalité positive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_33:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-04","text":"La limite change de statut épistémique : elle n’est plus une propriété neutre, mais l’indice permettant d’identifier un régime créaturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-05","text":"Le corps devient une interface de lecture ontologique : un phénomène physique révèle la constitution finie de la réalité qui le porte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-06","text":"Le sujet connaissant doit lire les phénomènes par attribution différentielle plutôt que rapporter indistinctement toute détermination à la cause suprême.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-07","text":"Le cluster produit une ontologie de la plénitude interne, où la transcendance est obtenue par clôture de l’extérieur et la différence par limitation immanente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-01","text":"L’exclusion de l’extérieur produit la totalité ; la totalité exige l’illimitation ; l’illimitation requalifie toute limite comme différence interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_32:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-02","text":"La définition de la perfection par la réalité positive conduit à l’abstraction des bornes, laquelle reconduit la perfection à l’infinité absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-03","text":"L’infinité suprême produit son envers structurel : une créature ne peut être définie que par sa capacité constitutive à ne pas être sans bornes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-04","text":"La réception des perfections et la production interne des imperfections forment une boucle d’asymétrie causale qui protège simultanément la dépendance et la distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_34:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-05","text":"La finitude passe de principe ontologique à manifestation physique ; cette manifestation reconduit ensuite le phénomène physique à son fondement ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-06","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel du cluster est la limite, alternativement supprimée, déplacée, intériorisée et matérialisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-07","text":"La répétition de la structure limite/illimitation signale un changement de phase : d’abord critère de perfection, elle devient ensuite principe de différenciation ontologique et physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B01","text":"Unicité + universalité + nécessité → exclusion de tout extérieur indépendant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_32:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B02","text":"Absence d’extérieur indépendant + rapport simple au possible → immanence de l’être possible dans la substance suprême.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B03","text":"Réalité positive − bornes → définition de la perfection absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A1","CH_UCIC_P_33:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B04","text":"Absence de bornes → infinité absolue → plénitude du réel possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A5","CH_UCIC_P_32:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B05","text":"Plénitude divine + nature créée limitée → perfection reçue et imperfection propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:D1","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B06","text":"Imperfection originelle + corps fini → inertie comme manifestation physique de la limitation ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A5","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:AFM-B01","text":"Propriétés suprêmes → fermeture de l’extérieur → immanence du possible → redéfinition positive de la perfection → infinité sans borne → distribution asymétrique des perfections et imperfections → finitude constitutive → manifestation corporelle → clôture ontologique différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_34:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:AFM-B02","text":"Le mouvement n’est pas linéaire au sens simple : il descend vers le corps tout en reconduisant chaque manifestation locale à l’architecture de la limite qui l’a produite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-01","text":"L’opposition entre transcendance et immanence est reconfigurée : la transcendance de la substance suprême est produite par l’absence d’un dehors, non par sa séparation d’avec le possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-02","text":"L’unité cesse d’être une singularité minimale et devient une totalité maximale de réalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-03","text":"La perfection relative et la perfection absolue sont distinguées par le régime de la limite plutôt que par une simple différence de degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_33:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-04","text":"La créature est reclassée comme réalité dérivée mais non purement déficiente : elle reçoit des perfections et produit elle-même la forme de ses imperfections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:D1","CH_UCIC_P_34:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-05","text":"Le corps devient un objet ontologiquement lisible, puisque son inertie est interprétée comme indice de finitude et non comme phénomène isolé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-06","text":"La méthode d’analyse disponible est une méthode d’attribution différentielle : séparer ce qui procède de l’influence divine de ce qui procède de la nature limitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont la substance suprême, la perfection divine, les créatures et l’inertie des corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont organisés par une distribution causale entre influence divine, nature propre, limite et manifestation physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] L’argument déplace la preuve de la perfection vers l’exclusion de la dépendance externe et déplace l’explication de l’imperfection vers la nature créaturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] La limite est originelle pour la créature, tandis que l’infinité appartient à la constitution ontologique de la substance suprême et non à un devenir quantitatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] Le texte accomplit sa propre clôture en répétant la négation de l’extérieur jusqu’à produire une architecture positive de totalité, puis en réinscrivant la négativité dans la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_34:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-01","text":"La plénitude de toute réalité possible dans la substance suprême entre en tension avec l’attribution de l’imperfection à la nature propre des créatures ; la tension est productive parce qu’elle transforme l’imperfection en différenciation interne plutôt qu’en reste extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-02","text":"Le passage de l’absence de limites à une infinité positive est affirmé avec force mais demeure logiquement sous-démontré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-03","text":"Le concept de « suite simple » porte une ambiguïté structurelle : il doit exprimer à la fois l’immanence du possible et l’absence de composition sans préciser leur articulation logique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_32:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-04","text":"L’inertie est traitée comme manifestation de l’imperfection, mais le mécanisme reliant directement constitution ontologique et propriété physique reste indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-05","text":"La source divine des perfections et la nature créaturelle des imperfections forment une asymétrie explicative qui évite l’imputation divine, mais ne fournit pas une théorie complète de la causalité intermédiaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MP-01","text":"La notion de limite mute lorsqu’elle passe de propriété exclue de la substance suprême à principe constitutif de la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MP-02","text":"La perfection mute d’une grandeur ontologique absolue en perfection reçue, sans perdre son origine dans la plénitude suprême.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_34:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MP-03","text":"La négativité mute en indice positif : l’inertie rend perceptible la structure finie de la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MP-04","text":"La totalité mute en système différentiel : absorber le possible ne supprime pas ses formes finies, mais les requalifie comme déterminations internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_32:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une totalité sans dehors, dont les différences ne sont pas des substances indépendantes mais des régimes internes de détermination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:HSI-02","text":"La substance suprême est l’image d’une plénitude auto-contenue ; la créature est l’image d’une réalité dérivée qui porte en elle la règle de sa propre limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_34:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas le lieu d’une production progressive de l’infini : l’infinité est donnée comme structure, tandis que les manifestations corporelles en sont les expressions limitées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:HSI-04","text":"La navigation conceptuelle consiste à suivre la limite : la supprimer pour penser le suprême, l’intérioriser pour penser la créature, puis la lire dans les phénomènes corporels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre noyaux : substance suprême sans extérieur indépendant, perfection comme réalité positive non bornée, créature limitée par sa nature propre, inertie comme manifestation corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_33:A1","CH_UCIC_P_34:A3","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B02","text":"Ces noyaux suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement du cluster, depuis la clôture ontologique jusqu’à la différenciation physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B03","text":"La cohérence dépend de l’interprétation de la perfection comme positivité sans borne et de la finitude comme propriété constitutive plutôt que comme manque accidentel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B04","text":"Restent indéterminés le statut exact de la « suite simple », la déduction de l’infinité à partir de la non-limitation et le mécanisme précis de passage vers l’inertie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_33:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B05","text":"La compression est fidèle si elle conserve la double économie de la limite : exclue dans la substance suprême, constitutive dans la créature, phénoménalisée dans le corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_34:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195404592761Z_13ca4f2c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 40–42","source_sha256":"12523f58d6c66ba241a556c707c66a333bd97bbbbfaeae01e262a8d3a9cdc3bb","sha256":"c998067fb26e636806731e7712a098fa30ca95e147be7ede735645ecd2ac7613","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:54:04.596994+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-01","text":"The system seeks to determine how a supreme reality can be at once unique, necessary, unlimited, and fully real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-02","text":"It reframes perfection as a magnitude of positive reality freed from every bound rather than as an accumulation of finite qualities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-03","text":"The absence of an independent exterior transforms supreme unity into a self-sufficient ontological totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-04","text":"Divine non-limitation becomes the principle of absolute infinity and of the fullness of the possible real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-05","text":"Created perfection is then distributed asymmetrically: received with respect to its positive determinations, but limited by the creature's own nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-06","text":"Finitude is therefore not an accidental privation, but the internal principle of creaturely imperfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-07","text":"Bodily inertia materializes this structure by converting an ontological limitation into a physical property.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:SP-08","text":"The general movement is cumulative and descending: supreme properties, exclusion of the exterior, infinity, creaturely differentiation, then physical manifestation of finitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS6","CH_UCIC_P_34:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A supreme substance exists as the principle of the ontological architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The uniqueness, universality, and necessity of the supreme substance exclude the coexistence of competing independent principles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Nothing independent subsists outside the supreme substance; external ontological otherness is therefore foreclosed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The relation of the supreme substance to possible being is simple and internal rather than composite or external.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Perfection is measured by the magnitude of positive reality, abstracting from the bounds that restrict it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-06","text":"[Terminal] The absence of every bound converts perfection into absolute infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Creaturely perfections are received from divine influence, but this reception does not suppress the creature's own limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A1","CH_UCIC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Finitude belongs constitutively to creaturely nature and not to a mere contingent deficiency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A3","CH_UCIC_P_34:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] The difference between God and creatures is a difference of ontological regime: unlimitedness on one side, constitutive limitation on the other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A4","CH_UCIC_P_34:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The limit functions as an operator of differentiation: excluded at the supreme level, it becomes constitutive at the creaturely level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_34:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-01","text":"The recurrence of the absence of limits changes function: it first grounds divine fullness, then serves as a negative criterion for defining creaturely finitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_34:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-02","text":"Perfection migrates from a property of the supreme substance to a determination received by creatures, without thereby becoming their autonomous principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A4","CH_UCIC_P_34:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-03","text":"The notion of nature shifts from a simple relation to possible being to an internal source of imperfection and limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A6","CH_UCIC_P_34:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-04","text":"The independent exterior is eliminated at the summit, while creaturely difference is retained in the form of a non-independent internal limit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A5","CH_UCIC_P_34:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-05","text":"Unity does not remain a mere numerical singularity: it becomes an intensive totality containing possible reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_32:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-06","text":"Imperfection shifts from an abstract negation to a bodily manifestation determined by inertia.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A5","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RMD-07","text":"The negation of the limit ultimately produces maximal positivity, whereas the creaturely limit becomes the mode of existence of ontological negativity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-01","text":"Local assertions concerning uniqueness, infinity, or inertia do not independently carry weight at the cluster level; they become operative when integrated into a shared economy of the limit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A2","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-02","text":"The major distinction of scale consists in moving from a particular divine property to a general architecture of distribution between supreme reality and created reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-03","text":"The inter-unit bridge is provided by the notion of bound: its exclusion defines the supreme, its internalization defines the creature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-04","text":"The theological transition to the physical is catalyzed by the identification of inertia as the manifestation of a prior ontological structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-05","text":"The model of a limited perfection becomes obsolete at the current level, because perfection is recoded as positive reality without restriction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_33:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:CGD-06","text":"The model of a self-grounded creature is superseded: the creature depends on God for its perfections, but not for the principle of its imperfections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects any supreme substance dependent on an external principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a plurality of necessary and independent realities capable of limiting or competing with the supreme substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_32:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-03","text":"It rejects the possibility that possible being should remain an autonomous domain external to the supreme substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-04","text":"It disqualifies a finite God or one determined by an internal bound.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A4","CH_UCIC_P_33:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-05","text":"It rejects the possibility that bodily imperfection might be an accident unrelated to creaturely nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:GNX-06","text":"Finally, it prohibits identifying the creature with God or attributing to it a self-grounded perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_34:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-01","text":"The system can hold only if the supreme substance receives no fundamental determination from an independent outside.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that several necessary realities can coexist without being referred back to a higher unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that the possible exceeds the supreme substance as an autonomous totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that finitude is the ultimate regime of all reality; it holds only as a creaturely determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A6","CH_UCIC_P_34:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:DBN-05","text":"It must be false that creaturely imperfection is directly produced by divine influence rather than by the creature's limited nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_34:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSA-01","text":"The independent exterior constitutes the unavailable possibility around which the entire architecture closes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSA-02","text":"The system leaves no remainder of positive reality that would exceed the supreme substance without depending on it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSA-03","text":"An absolutely self-sufficient creature is ontologically inadmissible, for its perfection comes to it from an external influence while its limitation belongs to it properly.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSA-04","text":"The structuring absence is that of an independent otherness: the God-creature difference is maintained without becoming the separation of two absolutes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_34:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-01","text":"The exclusion of every independent exterior, joined to the positive definition of perfection, transforms infinity into a property of ontological closure rather than a mere magnitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_33:SD2","CL_UCIC_14:GA-03","CL_UCIC_14:GA-05","CL_UCIC_14:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-02","text":"The difference between God and the creature is not an opposition between fullness and nothingness, but between unlimited fullness and the limited reception of positive determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_34:D1","CL_UCIC_14:GA-05","CL_UCIC_14:GA-07","CL_UCIC_14:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-03","text":"Creaturely finitude makes it possible to preserve an ontological hierarchy without reintroducing an independent external principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:A5","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2","CL_UCIC_14:GA-03","CL_UCIC_14:GA-08","CL_UCIC_14:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-04","text":"Divine perfection and creaturely imperfection form two correlated regimes of the limit: suppression at the summit, constitution at the base.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:D3","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2","CL_UCIC_14:GA-06","CL_UCIC_14:GA-08","CL_UCIC_14:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-05","text":"Bodily inertia becomes the phenomenal proof that the negativity of finitude possesses structural efficacy and is not a mere absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A6","CH_UCIC_P_34:D4","CL_UCIC_14:GA-08","CL_UCIC_14:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-06","text":"The supreme totality does not abolish the difference of creatures; it absorbs it as an internal differentiation of possible reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_34:DNX4","CL_UCIC_14:GA-03","CL_UCIC_14:GA-04","CL_UCIC_14:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:XD-07","text":"The separate attribution of perfections and imperfections functions as a device safeguarding divine fullness: what limits the creature is not imputed to the source of its perfections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1","CL_UCIC_14:GA-07","CL_UCIC_14:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-01","text":"The real is reclassified as a differentiated totality: no independent reality remains external, but internal regimes of limitation persist.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_32:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-02","text":"Causality becomes asymmetrical: the supreme source explains the positivity of perfections, while proper nature explains the negativity of limits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-03","text":"Negation acquires a productive function: removing the bound does not lead to emptiness, but to the maximization of positive reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_33:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-04","text":"The limit changes epistemic status: it is no longer a neutral property, but the indicator allowing identification of a creaturely regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-05","text":"The body becomes an interface for ontological reading: a physical phenomenon reveals the finite constitution of the reality that bears it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-06","text":"The knowing subject must read phenomena through differential attribution rather than indiscriminately referring every determination to the supreme cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:BSD-07","text":"The cluster produces an ontology of internal fullness, in which transcendence is obtained through closure of the exterior and difference through immanent limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-01","text":"The exclusion of the exterior produces totality; totality requires unlimitedness; unlimitedness requalifies every limit as internal difference.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_32:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-02","text":"The definition of perfection by positive reality leads to abstraction from bounds, which in turn brings perfection back to absolute infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-03","text":"Supreme infinity produces its structural reverse: a creature can be defined only by its constitutive capacity not to be without bounds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-04","text":"The reception of perfections and the internal production of imperfections form a loop of causal asymmetry that simultaneously protects dependence and distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_34:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-05","text":"Finitude passes from ontological principle to physical manifestation; this manifestation then refers the physical phenomenon back to its ontological foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-06","text":"The conceptual attractor of the cluster is the limit, alternately suppressed, displaced, internalized, and materialized.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:RLE-07","text":"The repetition of the limit/unlimitedness structure signals a phase change: first a criterion of perfection, it subsequently becomes a principle of ontological and physical differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B01","text":"Uniqueness + universality + necessity → exclusion of every independent exterior.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_32:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B02","text":"Absence of an independent exterior + simple relation to the possible → immanence of possible being in the supreme substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_32:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B03","text":"Positive reality − bounds → definition of absolute perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A1","CH_UCIC_P_33:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B04","text":"Absence of bounds → absolute infinity → fullness of the possible real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:A5","CH_UCIC_P_32:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B05","text":"Divine fullness + limited created nature → received perfection and proper imperfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:D1","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B06","text":"Original imperfection + finite body → inertia as physical manifestation of ontological limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:A5","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:AFM-B01","text":"Supreme properties → closure of the exterior → immanence of the possible → positive redefinition of perfection → infinity without bound → asymmetrical distribution of perfections and imperfections → constitutive finitude → bodily manifestation → differentiated ontological closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_34:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:AFM-B02","text":"The movement is not linear in the simple sense: it descends toward the body while referring each local manifestation back to the architecture of the limit that produced it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-01","text":"The opposition between transcendence and immanence is reconfigured: the transcendence of the supreme substance is produced by the absence of an outside, not by its separation from the possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-02","text":"Unity ceases to be a minimal singularity and becomes a maximal totality of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-03","text":"Relative perfection and absolute perfection are distinguished by the regime of the limit rather than by a mere difference of degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_33:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-04","text":"The creature is reclassified as a derived but not purely deficient reality: it receives perfections and itself produces the form of its imperfections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:D1","CH_UCIC_P_34:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-05","text":"The body becomes an ontologically legible object, since its inertia is interpreted as an indicator of finitude and not as an isolated phenomenon.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MME-06","text":"The available method of analysis is a method of differential attribution: separating what proceeds from divine influence from what proceeds from limited nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are the supreme substance, divine perfection, creatures, and the inertia of bodies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are organized by a causal distribution among divine influence, proper nature, limit, and physical manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The argument shifts the proof of perfection toward the exclusion of external dependence and shifts the explanation of imperfection toward creaturely nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The limit is original for the creature, whereas infinity belongs to the ontological constitution of the supreme substance and not to a quantitative becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The text accomplishes its own closure by repeating the negation of the exterior until it produces a positive architecture of totality, then by reinscribing negativity in the creature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_34:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-01","text":"The fullness of all possible reality in the supreme substance enters into tension with the attribution of imperfection to the creatures' own nature; the tension is productive because it transforms imperfection into internal differentiation rather than an external remainder.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_34:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-02","text":"The passage from the absence of limits to a positive infinity is asserted forcefully but remains logically under-demonstrated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-03","text":"The concept of « suite simple » bears a structural ambiguity: it must express both the immanence of the possible and the absence of composition without specifying their logical articulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_32:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-04","text":"Inertia is treated as a manifestation of imperfection, but the mechanism directly linking ontological constitution and physical property remains indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:FL-05","text":"The divine source of perfections and the creaturely nature of imperfections form an explanatory asymmetry that avoids divine imputation, but does not provide a complete theory of intermediate causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MP-01","text":"The notion of limit mutates when it passes from a property excluded from the supreme substance to a constitutive principle of the creature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MP-02","text":"Perfection mutates from an absolute ontological magnitude into received perfection, without losing its origin in supreme fullness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_34:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MP-03","text":"Negativity mutates into a positive indicator: inertia makes the finite structure of the creature perceptible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MP-04","text":"Totality mutates into a differential system: absorbing the possible does not suppress its finite forms, but requalifies them as internal determinations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_32:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a totality without an outside, whose differences are not independent substances but internal regimes of determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_32:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:HSI-02","text":"The supreme substance is the image of a self-contained fullness; the creature is the image of a derived reality that bears within itself the rule of its own limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_34:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:HSI-03","text":"Time is not the site of a progressive production of the infinite: infinity is given as structure, whereas bodily manifestations are its limited expressions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_34:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:HSI-04","text":"Conceptual navigation consists in following the limit: suppressing it in order to think the supreme, internalizing it in order to think the creature, then reading it in bodily phenomena.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_34:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four cores: supreme substance without an independent exterior, perfection as unbounded positive reality, creature limited by its own nature, inertia as bodily manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_33:A1","CH_UCIC_P_34:A3","CH_UCIC_P_34:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B02","text":"These cores suffice to reconstruct the movement of the cluster, from ontological closure to physical differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B03","text":"Coherence depends on interpreting perfection as positivity without bound and finitude as a constitutive property rather than as an accidental lack.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_33:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_34:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B04","text":"The exact status of « suite simple », the deduction of infinity from non-limitation, and the precise mechanism of passage toward inertia remain indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_32:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_33:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_14:MRT-B05","text":"The compression is faithful if it preserves the double economy of the limit: excluded in the supreme substance, constitutive in the creature, phenomenalized in the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_34:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_34:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_14@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_14:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 40–42","context":"Proposition 40 · Proposition 41 · Proposition 42"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 43–45","order":15,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_35","CH_UCIC_P_36","CH_UCIC_P_37"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_15@R001","sha256":"2c99cce27487b0dc4f65818e527b7481d328d97be4596708c8da7a36cdb37b36","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-01","text":"Le problème commun consiste à déterminer si le fondement divin porte seulement sur l’existence actuelle ou sur la réalité même du possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_36:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-02","text":"Le système recadre progressivement la causalité divine comme fondement conjoint des existences, des essences réelles et des possibilités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_35:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-03","text":"L’entendement divin fournit d’abord la médiation intelligible par laquelle les vérités éternelles et les essences possibles acquièrent une réalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_35:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-04","text":"Cette médiation est ensuite stabilisée par l’exigence d’un fondement existant et actuel, identifié à l’Être nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_36:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-05","text":"La possibilité de l’Être nécessaire et l’existence des êtres contingents deviennent deux voies convergentes vers une même clôture explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-06","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif : fondation intellectuelle du possible, stabilisation ontologique par le nécessaire, puis justification rationnelle du contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-07","text":"L’architecture se définit négativement par l’exclusion successive d’un possible autonome, d’un fondement simplement potentiel et d’un contingent autosuffisant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_36:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_37:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-08","text":"La clôture produite est un Être nécessaire auto-fondé, source simultanée de la réalité modale et de la raison dernière du contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Toute réalité modale qui possède un statut ontologique requiert un fondement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","CH_UCIC_P_36:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Le fondement divin s’étend de la production des existences à la constitution réelle des essences et des possibilités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:A1","CH_UCIC_P_35:A2","CH_UCIC_P_35:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] La possibilité réelle n’est pas une réalité autonome indépendante de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:A6","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] La réalité du possible exige à la fois une condition intelligible dans l’entendement divin et un fondement ontologique actuel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] L’Être nécessaire constitue le fondement actuel ultime des réalités possibles et contingentes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] La distinction entre essence et existence demeure pour les réalités dépendantes, mais se résorbe dans l’Être nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Les voies a priori et a posteriori convergent vers une même fondation nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] L’existence contingente requiert une raison dernière ou suffisante qui ne peut être fournie par le contingent lui-même.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] L’explication s’achève dans un être dont la raison d’existence est interne et qui fonde à son tour la raison du contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Toute l’architecture converge vers l’indissociabilité d’un fondement divin, d’une réalité modale et d’une actualité nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D4","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-01","text":"[Persistent → Mutating] La causalité divine persiste comme principe de fondation, mais migre de l’existence actuelle vers la structure même du pensable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D1","CH_UCIC_P_35:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-02","text":"[Mutating] Le possible passe d’un contenu intelligible dans l’entendement divin à une réalité fondée, puis à un opérateur de démonstration ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_37:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-03","text":"[Mutating] Les vérités éternelles passent d’une région de l’entendement divin à une voie rationnelle indépendante vers l’existence divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:A4","CH_UCIC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-04","text":"[Reversal] La possibilité, d’abord subordonnée à l’entendement divin, devient dans le cas de l’Être nécessaire une condition suffisante de l’actualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A6","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-05","text":"[Absorption] La distinction entre essence et existence est conservée comme différence locale, puis absorbée par l’identité interne de l’Être nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-06","text":"[Mutation] La contingence cesse d’être un simple fait à expliquer et devient l’indice positif d’une dépendance envers le nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-07","text":"[Escalation] La négation de Dieu passe de la suppression des existences et des possibles à l’impossibilité d’une raison ultime du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-08","text":"[Terminal Transformation] L’idée de fondement absorbe finalement l’ordre intelligible, l’ordre modal, l’ordre actuel et l’ordre explicatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-01","text":"La fonction précise de l’entendement divin comme région des idées et des vérités éternelles reste une machine locale de la couche inférieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-02","text":"L’identité entre essence et existence dans l’Être nécessaire est une détermination locale qui devient ici le mécanisme de stabilisation du possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-03","text":"La démonstration a priori par la possibilité et la démonstration a posteriori par la contingence sont des voies locales qui deviennent au niveau courant des accès convergents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-04","text":"L’interaction des trois unités reclassifie leurs machines comme les étapes d’une seule architecture de fondation : intelligibilité, actualité nécessaire, clôture explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-05","text":"Le lien inter-unités apparaît lorsque la réalité du possible exige simultanément une médiation intellectuelle et un support existant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D2","CH_UCIC_P_36:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-06","text":"L’idée d’un ordre autonome des vérités éternelles devient obsolète : elle est recodée comme dépendance à l’entendement et à l’actualité nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_36:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-07","text":"La différence entre possible et actuel cesse d’être une opposition absolue et devient une différence de régime à l’intérieur d’une hiérarchie fondée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_37:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-01","text":"Le système rejette une possibilité réelle qui subsisterait indépendamment de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_35:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut un domaine des vérités éternelles extérieur ou antérieur à l’entendement divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_35:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-03","text":"Il refuse qu’un fondement ultime soit une simple possibilité dépourvue d’existence actuelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-04","text":"Il refuse que l’existence soit un ajout contingent à l’essence de l’Être nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-05","text":"Il refuse que les êtres contingents constituent la raison dernière de leur propre existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_37:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-06","text":"Il refuse une régression explicative qui ne déboucherait ni sur une nécessité auto-fondée ni sur une raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’hypothèse d’un réel intelligible disponible sans intellect divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que soit fausse l’hypothèse selon laquelle la possibilité constituerait le niveau ontologique premier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie une séparation durable entre l’ordre logique des vérités et l’ordre réel de l’existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_35:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-04","text":"Il ne peut admettre plusieurs fondements ultimes indépendants, car la fonction de raison dernière exige une asymétrie terminale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-05","text":"Le modèle rival silencieusement exclu est celui d’un monde dont les formes, les possibles et les raisons seraient autoportants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSA-01","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un réel qui conserverait une structure modale après la disparition de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_35:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSA-02","text":"Le système rend indisponible la possibilité d’une intelligibilité sans source intellectuelle et sans actualité nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSA-03","text":"Il traite comme inadmissible un monde contingent qui existerait sans raison suffisante ni orientation vers un terme explicatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSA-04","text":"Sa force provient de l’impossibilité de dissocier totalement être, possibilité, intelligibilité et raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_35:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-01","text":"La réalité du possible reçoit une double détermination : elle est intelligible dans l’entendement divin et fondée dans une actualité qui ne dépend pas d’une autre cause.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-02","CL_UCIC_15:GA-04","CL_UCIC_15:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_35:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-02","text":"Le possible n’est donc ni une pure représentation ni une réalité séparée : il devient un niveau dépendant d’une fondation à la fois intellectuelle et ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-03","CL_UCIC_15:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_35:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_36:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-03","text":"L’identité de l’essence et de l’existence dans l’Être nécessaire transforme la fondation du possible en mécanisme de conversion de la possibilité en actualité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-05","CL_UCIC_15:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-04","text":"Les vérités éternelles et les êtres contingents sont réunis dans une même économie rationnelle : les premières ouvrent l’accès logique, les seconds imposent l’exigence d’une raison dernière.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-07","CL_UCIC_15:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_37:A6","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-05","text":"La hiérarchie globale est asymétrique : les possibles dépendent du nécessaire, tandis que le contingent dépend d’un être qui porte en lui-même sa propre raison.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-05","CL_UCIC_15:GA-08","CL_UCIC_15:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-06","text":"La convergence des voies a priori et a posteriori ne produit pas seulement une preuve cumulative ; elle ferme les deux directions principales de la recherche de fondement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-07","CL_UCIC_15:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_37:D7","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-07","text":"La structure demeure tendue parce que l’absence de contradiction est utilisée comme possibilité positive, alors que la justification indépendante de cette possibilité reste sous-déterminée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-04","CL_UCIC_15:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_37:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-01","text":"L’ontologie et la modalité cessent d’être deux domaines parallèles : elles deviennent deux expressions d’une même dépendance envers le fondement divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_35:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-02","text":"La possibilité devient un opérateur ontologique seulement lorsqu’elle est ordonnée à une actualité nécessaire capable de la fonder et de l’actualiser.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-03","text":"Le statut de Dieu se déplace de cause du monde à condition de détermination de tout ordre ontologique et de toute explication suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-04","text":"La priorité logique du possible ne signifie pas son indépendance ontologique : le possible peut précéder conceptuellement l’actuel tout en dépendant du nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_35:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-05","text":"La rationalité métaphysique est organisée par convergence : logique, vérités éternelles et expérience de la contingence convergent vers une même clôture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-06","text":"Le réel ne possède aucun niveau pleinement autosuffisant : ni l’essence, ni le possible, ni le contingent ne terminent par eux-mêmes l’explication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale suit le trajet existence → essence réelle → vérité éternelle → possibilité → fondement nécessaire → raison de l’existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_35:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-02","text":"Le système réinjecte la conclusion ontologique dans le problème modal : le fondement trouvé pour l’existence devient la condition de réalité du possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D4","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-03","text":"Une seconde boucle convertit la possibilité de l’Être nécessaire en existence, puis cette existence en fondement de toutes les possibilités dépendantes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-04","text":"La voie a priori et la voie a posteriori partent de directions opposées mais se referment sur le même attracteur nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-05","text":"La négation s’intensifie par paliers : absence de Dieu, absence d’existants, absence de possibilités réelles, puis absence de raison dernière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_35:A8","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-06","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est l’Être nécessaire, qui devient successivement fondement modal, actualité non dérivée et clôture explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B01","text":"La réalité des essences et des possibilités est posée comme un contenu qui ne peut rester ontologiquement sans fondement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","CH_UCIC_P_36:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B02","text":"L’exigence de fondement déplace l’analyse vers une existence actuelle, puisque le fondement ultime ne peut être seulement possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B03","text":"L’existence actuelle ultime est identifiée à l’Être nécessaire, dont l’essence contient l’existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B04","text":"La non-contradiction et l’absence de limites rendent possible l’Être nécessaire, dont la possibilité implique alors l’actualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B05","text":"L’existence des contingents introduit une seconde exigence : tout ce qui n’a pas en soi sa raison doit renvoyer au nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B06","text":"Les voies modale, intelligible et contingente convergent vers un être dont la raison est interne et dont la fonction est fondatrice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:D7","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B07","text":"La machine se ferme lorsque le même Être nécessaire fonde à la fois la réalité du possible, l’actualité du contingent et l’arrêt de la régression explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AFM-B01","text":"Le mouvement suit la chaîne : Réalité modale → Exigence de fondement → Entendement divin → Actualité nécessaire → Possibilité convertie en existence → Contingence renvoyée à une raison suffisante → Clôture explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AFM-B02","text":"La trajectoire négative correspondante est : Rejet du possible autonome → Rejet du fondement simplement potentiel → Rejet du contingent autosuffisant → Affirmation d’un nécessaire auto-fondé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-01","text":"Le champ divin est reclassé comme structure comprenant les existences actuelles, les essences réelles, les vérités éternelles et les possibilités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_35:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-02","text":"La séparation entre ontologie et modalité s’effondre au niveau du fondement, même si elle demeure comme distinction conceptuelle locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_35:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-03","text":"Les vérités éternelles sont déplacées du statut de principes autonomes vers celui de réalités dépendantes d’une intelligence et d’une nécessité fondatrices.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_36:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-04","text":"La possibilité logique est reclassée comme opérateur ontologique, mais seulement dans le cadre d’un Être dont l’essence contient l’existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_36:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-05","text":"La contingence est redessinée comme position dépendante dans une hiérarchie explicative plutôt que comme terme ultime du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_36:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-06","text":"La méthode disponible devient une double remontée : des structures intelligibles vers leur fondement et des existences contingentes vers leur raison dernière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B01","text":"Au niveau de surface, les objets explicites sont les essences, les possibilités, les vérités éternelles, l’Être nécessaire et les êtres contingents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","CH_UCIC_P_37:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B02","text":"Au niveau structural, ces objets sont organisés par des relations de dépendance, de fondation, d’actualisation et de raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B03","text":"Au niveau métastratégique, la question est déplacée de « ce qui est possible » vers « ce qui rend réelle la possibilité » et « ce qui fonde l’existence contingente ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_35:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B04","text":"Au niveau ontologique et temporel, la possibilité possède une priorité logique sans indépendance ontologique, tandis que l’Être nécessaire constitue une actualité non dérivée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B05","text":"Au niveau méthodologique et performatif, la démonstration reproduit ce qu’elle affirme : plusieurs voies sont distribuées, puis reconduites vers un unique terme explicatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FL-01","text":"La médiation de l’entendement divin semble maintenir une distinction entre Dieu et les vérités éternelles, tandis que l’Être nécessaire tend vers une fondation plus immédiate et auto-identique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FL-02","text":"Le passage de la possibilité non contradictoire à la possibilité positive de l’Être nécessaire est affirmé comme décisif, mais reste insuffisamment justifié.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A3","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FL-03","text":"Les vérités éternelles paraissent conserver une indépendance logique alors que leur réalité est déclarée ontologiquement dépendante de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FL-04","text":"La convergence des preuves renforce la clôture du système, mais peut aussi masquer le passage non démontré entre cohérence conceptuelle et existence effective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:D2","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MP-01","text":"Le possible mute de contenu intelligible en réalité ontologiquement fondée, puis en condition suffisante de l’existence nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D3","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MP-02","text":"Le fondement mute de cause des existences en condition de possibilité du pensable, puis en clôture explicative du contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MP-03","text":"La négation cesse d’être seulement destructive et produit positivement une hiérarchie : supprimer Dieu revient à supprimer les niveaux mêmes du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D5","CH_UCIC_P_35:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une machine hiérarchique de dépendances, centrée sur une source qui fonde à la fois l’intelligibilité, l’actualité et la raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet connaissant devient un opérateur de remontée : il reconstruit le réel en suivant les dépendances du possible vers le nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas le principe ultime de l’explication : la priorité décisive est logique et ontologique, tandis que la nécessité demeure non dérivée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée admise n’est pas une autonomie du possible, mais la remontée vers le fondement qui rend possible toute détermination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante si elle conserve quatre fonctions : l’entendement divin comme médiation, l’Être nécessaire comme actualité, le possible comme réalité dépendante et le contingent comme indice de raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B02","text":"Le système reste cohérent à condition de distinguer la priorité conceptuelle du possible de sa dépendance ontologique envers le nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_35:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination résiduelle porte principalement sur la justification de la possibilité positive de l’Être absolument illimité et sur le statut exact des vérités éternelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B04","text":"La compression demeure fidèle au mouvement génératif : existence → essence réelle → vérité éternelle → possibilité → nécessité → fondement du contingent ; elle ne doit pas réduire cette séquence à une simple preuve d’existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195439479025Z_d3601626","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 43–45","source_sha256":"2c99cce27487b0dc4f65818e527b7481d328d97be4596708c8da7a36cdb37b36","sha256":"fa8e0380508c17ef2a3a25842ead50ea21168ba32687f528adeca186737b5bff","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:54:39.482277+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-01","text":"The common problem consists in determining whether the divine foundation bears only on actual existence or on the very reality of the possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_36:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-02","text":"The system progressively reframes divine causality as the joint foundation of existences, real essences, and possibilities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_35:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-03","text":"The divine understanding first provides the intelligible mediation through which eternal truths and possible essences acquire reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_35:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-04","text":"This mediation is then stabilized by the requirement of an existing and actual foundation, identified with the necessary Being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_36:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-05","text":"The possibility of the necessary Being and the existence of contingent beings become two convergent paths toward one and the same explanatory closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-06","text":"The movement is cumulative: intellectual foundation of the possible, ontological stabilization by the necessary, then rational justification of the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-07","text":"The architecture is negatively defined by the successive exclusion of an autonomous possible, a merely potential foundation, and a self-sufficient contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_36:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_37:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AS-08","text":"The closure produced is a self-founded necessary Being, the simultaneous source of modal reality and of the ultimate reason for the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every modal reality possessing ontological status requires a foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","CH_UCIC_P_36:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] The divine foundation extends from the production of existences to the real constitution of essences and possibilities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:A1","CH_UCIC_P_35:A2","CH_UCIC_P_35:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Real possibility is not an autonomous reality independent of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:A6","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The reality of the possible requires both an intelligible condition in the divine understanding and an actual ontological foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] The necessary Being constitutes the ultimate actual foundation of possible and contingent realities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] The distinction between essence and existence remains for dependent realities, but is absorbed in the necessary Being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The a priori and a posteriori paths converge toward one and the same necessary foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Contingent existence requires an ultimate or sufficient reason that cannot be supplied by the contingent itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Explanation culminates in a being whose reason for existence is internal and which in turn grounds the reason for the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A9","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The whole architecture converges toward the inseparability of a divine foundation, a modal reality, and a necessary actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D4","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-01","text":"[Persistent → Mutating] Divine causality persists as a principle of foundation, but migrates from actual existence to the very structure of the thinkable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D1","CH_UCIC_P_35:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-02","text":"[Mutating] The possible shifts from intelligible content in the divine understanding to a founded reality, then to an operator of ontological demonstration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_37:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-03","text":"[Mutating] Eternal truths shift from a region of the divine understanding to an independent rational path toward divine existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:A4","CH_UCIC_P_37:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-04","text":"[Reversal] Possibility, initially subordinated to the divine understanding, becomes in the case of the necessary Being a sufficient condition of actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A6","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-05","text":"[Absorption] The distinction between essence and existence is retained as a local difference, then absorbed by the internal identity of the necessary Being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-06","text":"[Mutation] Contingency ceases to be a mere fact to be explained and becomes the positive indication of a dependence upon the necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-07","text":"[Escalation] The negation of God shifts from the suppression of existences and possibilities to the impossibility of an ultimate reason for the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RMD-08","text":"[Terminal Transformation] The idea of foundation ultimately absorbs the intelligible order, the modal order, the actual order, and the explanatory order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-01","text":"The precise function of the divine understanding as the region of ideas and eternal truths remains a local mechanism of the lower layer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_35:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-02","text":"The identity between essence and existence in the necessary Being is a local determination that here becomes the mechanism for stabilizing the possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-03","text":"The a priori demonstration by possibility and the a posteriori demonstration by contingency are local paths that become convergent accesses at the current level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-04","text":"The interaction of the three units reclassifies their mechanisms as the stages of a single architecture of foundation: intelligibility, necessary actuality, explanatory closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-05","text":"The inter-unit link appears when the reality of the possible simultaneously requires intellectual mediation and an existing support.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D2","CH_UCIC_P_36:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-06","text":"The idea of an autonomous order of eternal truths becomes obsolete: it is recoded as dependence on the understanding and on necessary actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_36:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:CGD-07","text":"The difference between possible and actual ceases to be an absolute opposition and becomes a difference of regime within a founded hierarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_37:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects a real possibility that would subsist independently of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_35:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a domain of eternal truths external or prior to the divine understanding.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_35:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-03","text":"It rejects an ultimate foundation that would be a mere possibility deprived of actual existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-04","text":"It rejects existence as a contingent addition to the essence of the necessary Being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-05","text":"It rejects contingent beings as constituting the ultimate reason for their own existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_37:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:GNX-06","text":"It rejects an explanatory regress that would lead neither to a self-founded necessity nor to a sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, the hypothesis of an intelligible real available without divine intellect must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-02","text":"The hypothesis according to which possibility would constitute the primary ontological level must likewise be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies a lasting separation between the logical order of truths and the real order of existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_35:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-04","text":"It cannot admit several independent ultimate foundations, for the function of ultimate reason requires a terminal asymmetry.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:DBN-05","text":"The silently excluded rival model is that of a world whose forms, possibilities, and reasons would be self-supporting.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSA-01","text":"The structuring absence is that of a real that would retain a modal structure after the disappearance of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_35:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSA-02","text":"The system renders unavailable the possibility of an intelligibility without an intellectual source and without necessary actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSA-03","text":"It treats as inadmissible a contingent world that would exist without sufficient reason or orientation toward an explanatory terminus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSA-04","text":"Its force derives from the impossibility of completely dissociating being, possibility, intelligibility, and reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_35:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-01","text":"The reality of the possible receives a double determination: it is intelligible in the divine understanding and founded in an actuality that does not depend on another cause.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-02","CL_UCIC_15:GA-04","CL_UCIC_15:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_35:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-02","text":"The possible is therefore neither a pure representation nor a separate reality: it becomes a level dependent on a foundation that is both intellectual and ontological.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-03","CL_UCIC_15:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_35:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_36:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-03","text":"The identity of essence and existence in the necessary Being transforms the foundation of the possible into a mechanism for converting possibility into actuality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-05","CL_UCIC_15:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_36:A5","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-04","text":"Eternal truths and contingent beings are united in one and the same rational economy: the former open logical access, the latter impose the requirement of an ultimate reason.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-07","CL_UCIC_15:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_37:A6","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-05","text":"The overall hierarchy is asymmetrical: possibilities depend on the necessary, whereas the contingent depends on a being that bears within itself its own reason.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-05","CL_UCIC_15:GA-08","CL_UCIC_15:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-06","text":"The convergence of the a priori and a posteriori paths does not merely produce a cumulative proof; it closes off the two principal directions of the search for foundation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-07","CL_UCIC_15:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_37:D7","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:XD-07","text":"The structure remains strained because absence of contradiction is used as positive possibility, whereas the independent justification of this possibility remains underdetermined.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-04","CL_UCIC_15:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_37:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-01","text":"Ontology and modality cease to be two parallel domains: they become two expressions of one and the same dependence upon the divine foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_35:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-02","text":"Possibility becomes an ontological operator only when it is ordered to a necessary actuality capable of grounding and actualizing it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-03","text":"The status of God shifts from cause of the world to condition of determination of every ontological order and every sufficient explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-04","text":"The logical priority of the possible does not signify its ontological independence: the possible may conceptually precede the actual while depending on the necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_35:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-05","text":"Metaphysical rationality is organized by convergence: logic, eternal truths, and the experience of contingency converge toward one and the same closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:BSD-06","text":"The real possesses no fully self-sufficient level: neither essence, nor the possible, nor the contingent terminates explanation by itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop follows the path existence → real essence → eternal truth → possibility → necessary foundation → reason for existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_35:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-02","text":"The system reinjects the ontological conclusion into the modal problem: the foundation found for existence becomes the condition of reality of the possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D4","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-03","text":"A second loop converts the possibility of the necessary Being into existence, then this existence into the foundation of all dependent possibilities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-04","text":"The a priori path and the a posteriori path begin from opposite directions but close upon the same necessary attractor.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-05","text":"Negation intensifies in stages: absence of God, absence of existents, absence of real possibilities, then absence of ultimate reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_35:A8","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:RLE-06","text":"The conceptual attractor is the necessary Being, which successively becomes modal foundation, underived actuality, and explanatory closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B01","text":"The reality of essences and possibilities is posited as content that cannot remain ontologically without foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","CH_UCIC_P_36:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B02","text":"The requirement of foundation shifts the analysis toward an actual existence, since the ultimate foundation cannot be merely possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_36:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B03","text":"Ultimate actual existence is identified with the necessary Being, whose essence contains existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A4","CH_UCIC_P_36:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B04","text":"Non-contradiction and the absence of limits make the necessary Being possible, whose possibility then entails actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_36:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B05","text":"The existence of contingents introduces a second requirement: everything that does not have its reason in itself must refer back to the necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A7","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B06","text":"The modal, intelligible, and contingent paths converge toward a being whose reason is internal and whose function is foundational.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:D7","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B07","text":"The mechanism closes when the same necessary Being grounds at once the reality of the possible, the actuality of the contingent, and the cessation of explanatory regress.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_37:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AFM-B01","text":"The movement follows the chain: Modal reality → Requirement of foundation → Divine understanding → Necessary actuality → Possibility converted into existence → Contingency referred to a sufficient reason → Explanatory closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_36:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_37:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:AFM-B02","text":"The corresponding negative trajectory is: Rejection of the autonomous possible → Rejection of the merely potential foundation → Rejection of the self-sufficient contingent → Affirmation of a self-founded necessary being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_36:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-01","text":"The divine field is reclassified as a structure comprising actual existences, real essences, eternal truths, and possibilities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_35:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-02","text":"The separation between ontology and modality collapses at the level of foundation, even if it remains as a local conceptual distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_35:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-03","text":"Eternal truths are displaced from the status of autonomous principles to that of realities dependent on a founding intelligence and necessity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_36:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-04","text":"Logical possibility is reclassified as an ontological operator, but only within the framework of a Being whose essence contains existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_36:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-05","text":"Contingency is redrawn as a dependent position within an explanatory hierarchy rather than as the ultimate term of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_36:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MME-06","text":"The available method becomes a double ascent: from intelligible structures toward their foundation and from contingent existences toward their ultimate reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the explicit objects are essences, possibilities, eternal truths, the necessary Being, and contingent beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A1","CH_UCIC_P_37:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, these objects are organized by relations of dependence, foundation, actualization, and sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:A2","CH_UCIC_P_37:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, the question is shifted from « what is possible » toward « what makes possibility real » and « what grounds contingent existence ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_35:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, possibility possesses logical priority without ontological independence, while the necessary Being constitutes an underived actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the demonstration reproduces what it affirms: several paths are distributed, then led back toward a single explanatory terminus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_37:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FL-01","text":"The mediation of the divine understanding seems to maintain a distinction between God and eternal truths, whereas the necessary Being tends toward a more immediate and self-identical foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:A5","CH_UCIC_P_36:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FL-02","text":"The transition from non-contradictory possibility to the positive possibility of the necessary Being is asserted as decisive, but remains insufficiently justified.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:A3","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FL-03","text":"Eternal truths seem to retain a logical independence while their reality is declared ontologically dependent on God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:FL-04","text":"The convergence of proofs reinforces the closure of the system, but may also conceal the undemonstrated transition between conceptual coherence and effective existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_37:D2","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MP-01","text":"The possible mutates from intelligible content into an ontologically founded reality, then into a sufficient condition of necessary existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D3","CH_UCIC_P_37:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MP-02","text":"The foundation mutates from cause of existences into condition of possibility of the thinkable, then into explanatory closure of the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MP-03","text":"Negation ceases to be merely destructive and positively produces a hierarchy: to suppress God is to suppress the very levels of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:D5","CH_UCIC_P_35:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a hierarchical mechanism of dependencies, centered on a source that grounds intelligibility, actuality, and reason alike.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_37:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:HSI-02","text":"The knowing subject becomes an operator of ascent: it reconstructs the real by following the dependencies of the possible toward the necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:HSI-03","text":"Time is not the ultimate principle of explanation: decisive priority is logical and ontological, while necessity remains underived.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_37:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:HSI-04","text":"The only admitted escape is not an autonomy of the possible, but the ascent toward the foundation that makes every determination possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_36:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B01","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves four functions: the divine understanding as mediation, the necessary Being as actuality, the possible as dependent reality, and the contingent as an indication of sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_36:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B02","text":"The system remains coherent provided that the conceptual priority of the possible is distinguished from its ontological dependence upon the necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_35:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B03","text":"The residual indeterminacy concerns principally the justification of the positive possibility of the absolutely unlimited Being and the exact status of eternal truths.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B04","text":"The compression remains faithful to the generative movement: existence → real essence → eternal truth → possibility → necessity → foundation of the contingent; it must not reduce this sequence to a mere proof of existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_35:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_37:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_15@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_15:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 43–45","context":"Proposition 43 · Proposition 44 · Proposition 45"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 46–48","order":16,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_38","CH_UCIC_P_39","CH_UCIC_P_40"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_16@R001","sha256":"4566f2767ebba52ecc3547a63f7d6ad1942ba2bca079788f4d8a428d2214b719","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-01","text":"Le cluster résout le problème d’une dépendance divine qui semblerait soit arbitraire, soit incompatible avec l’autonomie relative des vérités et des créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-02","text":"Il recadre cette dépendance comme une différenciation de régimes : l’entendement fonde le nécessaire, la volonté détermine le contingent, et la puissance soutient la production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-03","text":"L’unité divine demeure la source primitive, tandis que les Monades créées sont produites, maintenues et structurées selon des degrés finis d’imitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-04","text":"La création passe d’un événement initial à une actualisation continuée, bornée par la réceptivité créaturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_39:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-05","text":"La structure divine se réfracte fonctionnellement dans la Monade sous forme de base, perception et appétition, sans abolir la différence d’infinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-06","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et analogique : la distinction des vérités devient distinction des modes de production, puis hiérarchie des êtres et des facultés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-07","text":"La clôture du cluster n’est pas une autonomie de la créature, mais une architecture de dépendance différenciée où l’activité créée est une imitation finie de l’ordre divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La dépendance à Dieu ne possède pas un mode unique : elle se distribue entre fondement intellectuel, production volontaire et actualisation ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Les vérités nécessaires dépendent de l’entendement divin plutôt que d’un décret de la volonté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La volonté divine détermine le contingent selon la convenance et le meilleur, mais ne constitue pas la nécessité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Dieu seul est l’unité primitive et la substance originaire à partir de laquelle les substances créées reçoivent leur existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Toute Monade créée est dérivative et dépend d’une production divine renouvelée de moment en moment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] La limitation de la réceptivité créaturelle est constitutive de la différence entre Dieu et les créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La causalité divine est triadique : puissance de produire, connaissance qui spécifie et volonté qui oriente les changements vers le meilleur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] La Monade créée reproduit cette triade sous forme de base, perception et appétition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] La différence entre Dieu et les Monades est une différence de degré de perfection dans une architecture fonctionnelle commune, non une séparation de fonctions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8","CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Le cluster converge vers une dépendance productive, intelligible et analogique qui exclut à la fois l’arbitraire universel et l’autonomie primitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-01","text":"La dépendance divine revient d’abord comme problème de fondement de la vérité, puis comme condition de l’existence créée et enfin comme structure interne des facultés monadiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D4","CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-02","text":"La volonté change de fonction : elle est d’abord exclue du fondement du nécessaire, puis réinscrite comme puissance de sélection et d’orientation du contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-03","text":"L’entendement se déplace du lieu des vérités nécessaires vers le dispositif qui contient les Idées déterminant les productions possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-04","text":"L’unité divine conserve son identité de principe originaire, mais mute en source productive, normative et structurante de la multiplicité créée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-05","text":"La création passe du modèle d’un acte achevé au modèle d’une fulguration continuée, ce qui transforme le temps en condition de maintien ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-06","text":"La limitation, d’abord négation de l’illimitation divine, devient principe positif de différenciation et de gradation des êtres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A7","CH_UCIC_P_39:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-07","text":"La Monade n’est plus seulement une substance produite : elle devient une structure dynamique qui reçoit, perçoit et tend selon un degré d’imitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-08","text":"L’opposition entre nécessité et contingence est absorbée dans une architecture plus vaste où l’entendement spécifie, la volonté choisit et la puissance actualise.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D2","CH_UCIC_P_40:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-01","text":"La correction de l’arbitraire des vérités éternelles reste locale lorsqu’elle porte seulement sur la distinction entre entendement et volonté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-02","text":"La fulguration continuelle reste locale lorsqu’elle sert seulement à expliquer la dépendance actuelle des Monades créées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-03","text":"La triade puissance-connaissance-volonté reste locale lorsqu’elle décrit seulement les attributs divins et leurs équivalents monadiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-04","text":"À l’échelle du cluster, ces machines locales se relient en une théorie unique des modes de dépendance : intelligible, productive, temporelle et analogique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-05","text":"La distinction entre vérités nécessaires et contingentes change d’échelle lorsqu’elle devient distinction entre ordre intelligible, choix du meilleur et production du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-06","text":"La limitation cesse d’être une simple borne locale de la créature et devient le mécanisme commun qui traduit l’infini divin en différences de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-07","text":"L’autonomie primitive, la dépendance uniforme et la séparation radicale sont recodées comme modèles inférieurs incapables de rendre compte de l’architecture distribuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-01","text":"Le cluster exclut qu’une dépendance divine implique uniformément l’arbitraire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une vérité nécessaire soit constituée par une décision volontaire contingente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut que la créature soit une unité originaire, une source autosuffisante ou une substance indépendante après sa production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_39:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut une création ponctuelle qui rendrait l’existence actuelle indépendante d’une opération divine continuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une coupure absolue entre les fonctions divines et les facultés créées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut une réalité sans ordre rationnel du meilleur et sans articulation entre puissance, intelligibilité et orientation normative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_40:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’hypothèse d’un mode unique de dépendance divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-02","text":"Le cluster disqualifie silencieusement un modèle où la volonté serait la source universelle du vrai, du possible et du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_38:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-03","text":"Il disqualifie également un modèle où la création serait une émission initiale suivie d’une auto-maintenance des substances créées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-04","text":"L’autonomie créaturelle complète est incompatible avec la fois la fulguration continuelle et l’imitation graduée des attributs divins.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-05","text":"Une séparation entre Dieu et les créatures qui serait une différence de nature fonctionnelle détruirait l’analogie constitutive du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité la plus profondément forclose est celle d’un réel dont l’existence, l’intelligibilité et l’orientation seraient séparées de toute source divine différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSA-02","text":"Le système rend indisponible une souveraineté divine conçue comme pouvoir de modifier à volonté le nécessaire, le possible et la structure du vrai.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSA-03","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une créature qui pourrait se maintenir, se déterminer et se perfectionner sans participation dérivative à l’ordre divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSA-04","text":"Ce que le cluster traite comme ontologiquement inadmissible est une multiplicité de principes premiers : toute pluralité doit être produite, soutenue et différenciée à partir de l’unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-01","text":"La distinction entre nécessité et contingence devient une différenciation générale des opérations divines : l’entendement spécifie ce qui est nécessaire, tandis que la volonté oriente ce qui peut être autrement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3","CL_UCIC_16:GA-02","CL_UCIC_16:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-02","text":"La continuation de la création et l’analogie fonctionnelle des Monades impliquent qu’exister signifie simultanément être soutenu de l’extérieur et être structuré de l’intérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3","CL_UCIC_16:GA-05","CL_UCIC_16:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-03","text":"L’unité primitive de Dieu et la gradation des imitations transforment la hiérarchie des êtres en distribution de degrés d’une même architecture, plutôt qu’en juxtaposition de substances premières.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:D4","CH_UCIC_P_39:ME4","CL_UCIC_16:GA-04","CL_UCIC_16:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-04","text":"Le principe du meilleur relie l’ordre des vérités contingentes à l’ordre de la production cosmique : choisir le monde et effectuer ses changements relèvent d’une même orientation normative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS3","CL_UCIC_16:GA-03","CL_UCIC_16:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-05","text":"La limitation créaturelle fonctionne comme opérateur de traduction : elle convertit la puissance, la connaissance et la volonté infinies en facultés finies mais homologues.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5","CL_UCIC_16:GA-06","CL_UCIC_16:GA-08","CL_UCIC_16:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-06","text":"La dépendance devient stratifiée : dépendance sémantique des vérités, dépendance ontologique de l’existence et dépendance fonctionnelle des facultés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D4","CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:D4","CL_UCIC_16:GA-01","CL_UCIC_16:GA-02","CL_UCIC_16:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-07","text":"L’activité des Monades n’abolit pas leur dépendance : elle est précisément la forme finie sous laquelle la causalité divine devient perception, appétition et tendance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS4","CL_UCIC_16:GA-05","CL_UCIC_16:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-08","text":"Le cluster remplace le choix entre transcendance divine et autonomie créée par une continuité asymétrique où l’analogie augmente la dépendance au lieu de la supprimer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3","CL_UCIC_16:GA-09","CL_UCIC_16:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-01","text":"L’ordre du réel n’est ni un décret arbitraire ni une nécessité indépendante : il est une architecture à plusieurs régimes de dépendance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-02","text":"La causalité est reclassée comme articulation de trois fonctions irréductibles : rendre possible, déterminer intelligiblement et orienter vers le meilleur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D3","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-03","text":"Le temps devient une dimension ontologique de la création, puisque l’être créé doit être continuellement reconduit sans cesser d’être une substance distincte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-04","text":"Le sujet créé n’est pas un principe premier, mais une unité dérivative capable de reproduire intérieurement, à degré fini, la structure de la source divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:D3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-05","text":"La hiérarchie ontologique devient une cartographie des capacités d’imitation : plus la perfection augmente, plus la structure divine est réalisée sous une forme finie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-06","text":"La souveraineté divine est redéfinie comme maîtrise différenciée des régimes de production, et non comme indifférence à l’égard de toute structure intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-07","text":"La conséquence méthodologique est une lecture par correspondances fonctionnelles et mutations de régime, plutôt que par identités simples entre Dieu et créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D4","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale est : dépendance divine → risque d’arbitraire → différenciation des modes de dépendance → dépendance plus structurée de la créature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-02","text":"Une seconde boucle convertit la création en maintien : production divine → existence dérivative → renouvellement temporel → impossibilité d’une autonomie ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-03","text":"Une troisième boucle convertit l’infini en gradation : attribut divin → imitation créée → limitation de la réceptivité → degré différencié de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-04","text":"Le terme volonté oscille entre pouvoir exclu du nécessaire et pouvoir requis pour le contingent ; cette oscillation devient un mécanisme de différenciation plutôt qu’une incohérence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel du cluster est la dépendance différenciée : chaque tentative de produire une autonomie simple réintroduit un niveau de dépendance plus profond.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-06","text":"La trajectoire d’escalade va de la théorie de la vérité à l’ontologie de la création, puis à une théorie interne de l’activité monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B01","text":"Dépendance divine indifférenciée → soupçon d’arbitraire → séparation du nécessaire et du contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B02","text":"Vérité nécessaire → entendement divin ; vérité contingente → volonté, convenance et choix du meilleur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B03","text":"Unité divine primitive → production des Monades → fulguration continuelle → existence dérivative maintenue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B04","text":"Réceptivité limitée → borne de la production → distinction Dieu/créature → gradation de la perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B05","text":"Puissance, connaissance, volonté → production, détermination idéale, orientation normative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B06","text":"Triade divine → base, perception, appétition → imitation finie et fonctionnellement analogue dans chaque Monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B07","text":"Négation de l’arbitraire universel + négation de l’autonomie primitive + analogie graduée → architecture de dépendance productive et intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AFM-B01","text":"Dépendance divine indifférenciée → risque d’arbitraire → distinction nécessaire/contingent → séparation entendement/volonté → unité divine comme source primitive → création comme fulguration continuelle → limitation de la réceptivité → triade divine réfractée dans la Monade → hiérarchie des imitations → clôture par dépendance différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_39:AF4","CH_UCIC_P_40:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-01","text":"La dépendance divine est reclassée d’une relation unique en une carte à plusieurs régimes : logique, ontologique, temporel et fonctionnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_40:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-02","text":"La fausse opposition entre autonomie des vérités et arbitraire divin s’effondre avec la distinction entre entendement et volonté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-03","text":"La création ponctuelle est remplacée par une carte temporelle de l’actualisation continue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-04","text":"La limitation est reclassée comme opérateur de différenciation productive, et non comme simple déficit ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-05","text":"La hiérarchie des êtres devient une hiérarchie d’imitation et de capacité fonctionnelle, non un classement externe de substances isolées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-06","text":"Le terrain stratégique de la lecture se déplace de l’opposition Dieu/créature vers l’analyse des traductions finies de fonctions divines infinies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_40:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont les vérités éternelles, Dieu, les Monades créées, leurs facultés et leur différence de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_40:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont organisés par des distributions de dépendance : entendement/volonté, origine/production, puissance/connaissance/orientation et infinité/limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] La stratégie consiste à dissoudre les alternatives globales en distinguant les fonctions et en convertissant les objections en changements de régime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] L’être créé est une production continuellement reconduite, finie dans sa réceptivité et analogue dans sa structure interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit sa thèse en remplaçant progressivement les oppositions binaires par des distinctions fonctionnelles emboîtées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_40:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_40:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FL-01","text":"La dépendance intégrale des Monades menace leur statut de substances distinctes, tandis que leur activité interne empêche de les réduire à de simples effets passifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FL-02","text":"L’analogie fonctionnelle rapproche Dieu et les créatures, mais l’infinité divine et la limitation créaturelle empêchent toute identité substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FL-03","text":"La volonté est simultanément subordonnée à l’ordre intelligible du nécessaire et indispensable à la détermination du contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FL-04","text":"La création continuelle intensifie la dépendance temporelle sans dissoudre la stabilité de l’identité monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MP-01","text":"Le passage de la dépendance des vérités à la dépendance de l’existence transforme une distinction logique en ontologie de la production continuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MP-02","text":"Le passage de la limitation comme borne à la limitation comme degré d’imitation convertit une négation en principe positif de hiérarchie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MP-03","text":"Le passage de la triade divine à la structure monadique produit une analogie opératoire, et non une simple ressemblance doctrinale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MP-04","text":"Le passage de l’unité primitive à la multiplicité graduée établit la créature comme répétition limitée de la source plutôt que comme second principe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une machine de production continuée : une source simple y distribue des effets différenciés selon la réceptivité de ce qui les reçoit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet créé devient une micro-architecture de puissance limitée, de représentation partielle et de tendance orientée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas un simple cadre des événements : il est le rythme de reconduction de l’existence dérivative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée disponible n’est pas une indépendance absolue, mais une augmentation du degré d’imitation et de perfection au sein de la dépendance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le noyau du cluster : dépendance différenciée, unité divine primitive, création continuée, triade fonctionnelle et imitation graduée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction reste cohérente parce que le nécessaire, le contingent, l’existence créée et l’activité monadique sont assignés à des fonctions distinctes mais coordonnées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:D3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B03","text":"La compression ne peut toutefois pas déterminer entièrement le mécanisme précis qui relie l’entendement divin aux Idées ni celui qui relie la base monadique à la puissance divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B04","text":"La zone de force du système est l’articulation entre limitation, analogie et dépendance continuée ; sa zone instable est le maintien simultané de la dérivation et de l’activité propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B05","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante au niveau Cluster : elle restitue l’escalade générative sans réduire les trois unités à leurs machines locales, mais elle laisse ouverte la détermination détaillée des médiations internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195515720071Z_662ed8ba","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 46–48","source_sha256":"4566f2767ebba52ecc3547a63f7d6ad1942ba2bca079788f4d8a428d2214b719","sha256":"5296e488fc84d8f56ec767ed269e19e619ce0c15b9f321858782fabece82cd4d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:55:15.722875+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-01","text":"The cluster resolves the problem of a divine dependence that would seem either arbitrary or incompatible with the relative autonomy of truths and creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-02","text":"It reframes this dependence as a differentiation of regimes: the understanding grounds the necessary, the will determines the contingent, and power sustains production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-03","text":"Divine unity remains the primitive source, while created Monads are produced, maintained, and structured according to finite degrees of imitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-04","text":"Creation shifts from an initial event to a continued actualization, bounded by creaturely receptivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_39:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-05","text":"The divine structure is functionally refracted in the Monad as base, perception, and appetition, without abolishing the difference of infinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-06","text":"The movement is cumulative and analogical: the distinction of truths becomes a distinction of modes of production, then a hierarchy of beings and faculties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AS-07","text":"The closure of the cluster is not an autonomy of the creature, but an architecture of differentiated dependence in which created activity is a finite imitation of the divine order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Dependence on God does not possess a single mode: it is distributed among intellectual foundation, voluntary production, and ontological actualization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Necessary truths depend on the divine understanding rather than on a decree of the will.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The divine will determines the contingent according to fittingness and the best, but does not constitute necessity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] God alone is the primitive unity and the original substance from which created substances receive their existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Every created Monad is derivative and depends on a divine production renewed from moment to moment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The limitation of creaturely receptivity is constitutive of the difference between God and creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Divine causality is triadic: power to produce, knowledge that specifies, and will that directs changes toward the best.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] The created Monad reproduces this triad as base, perception, and appetition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] The difference between God and Monads is a difference in degree of perfection within a common functional architecture, not a separation of functions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8","CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The cluster converges upon a productive, intelligible, and analogical dependence that excludes both universal arbitrariness and primitive autonomy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-01","text":"Divine dependence first recurs as a problem of the foundation of truth, then as a condition of created existence, and finally as the internal structure of monadic faculties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D4","CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-02","text":"The will changes function: it is first excluded from the foundation of the necessary, then reinscribed as a power of selection and direction of the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-03","text":"The understanding shifts from the locus of necessary truths toward the apparatus that contains the Ideas determining possible productions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_38:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-04","text":"Divine unity retains its identity as original principle, but mutates into the productive, normative, and structuring source of created multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-05","text":"Creation shifts from the model of a completed act to the model of a continued flash, which transforms time into a condition of ontological maintenance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_39:A4","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-06","text":"Limitation, initially the negation of divine unlimitedness, becomes a positive principle of differentiation and gradation of beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A7","CH_UCIC_P_39:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-07","text":"The Monad is no longer merely a produced substance: it becomes a dynamic structure that receives, perceives, and tends according to a degree of imitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RMD-08","text":"The opposition between necessity and contingency is absorbed into a broader architecture in which the understanding specifies, the will chooses, and power actualizes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D2","CH_UCIC_P_40:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-01","text":"The correction of the arbitrariness of eternal truths remains local when it bears only on the distinction between understanding and will.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-02","text":"Continual flashing remains local when it serves only to explain the current dependence of created Monads.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-03","text":"The power-knowledge-will triad remains local when it describes only divine attributes and their monadic equivalents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-04","text":"At the scale of the cluster, these local machines are joined into a single theory of modes of dependence: intelligible, productive, temporal, and analogical.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-05","text":"The distinction between necessary and contingent truths changes scale when it becomes a distinction between intelligible order, choice of the best, and production of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-06","text":"Limitation ceases to be a simple local boundary of the creature and becomes the common mechanism that translates divine infinity into differences of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:CGD-07","text":"Primitive autonomy, uniform dependence, and radical separation are recoded as inferior models incapable of accounting for the distributed architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-01","text":"The cluster excludes that divine dependence uniformly entails arbitrariness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-02","text":"It excludes that a necessary truth is constituted by a contingent voluntary decision.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-03","text":"It excludes that the creature is an original unity, a self-sufficient source, or an independent substance after its production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_39:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-04","text":"It excludes a punctual creation that would render present existence independent of a continued divine operation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-05","text":"It excludes an absolute break between divine functions and created faculties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:GNX-06","text":"It excludes a reality without a rational order of the best and without an articulation between power, intelligibility, and normative orientation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_40:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the hypothesis of a single mode of divine dependence must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-02","text":"The cluster silently disqualifies a model in which the will would be the universal source of the true, the possible, and the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_38:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-03","text":"It likewise disqualifies a model in which creation would be an initial emission followed by the self-maintenance of created substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-04","text":"Complete creaturely autonomy is incompatible both with continual flashing and with the graded imitation of divine attributes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:DBN-05","text":"A separation between God and creatures that would be a difference of functional nature would destroy the constitutive analogy of the system.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSA-01","text":"The possibility most deeply foreclosed is that of a real whose existence, intelligibility, and orientation would be separated from every differentiated divine source.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSA-02","text":"The system renders unavailable a divine sovereignty conceived as the power to modify at will the necessary, the possible, and the structure of truth.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSA-03","text":"The structuring absence is that of a creature that could maintain, determine, and perfect itself without derivative participation in the divine order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSA-04","text":"What the cluster treats as ontologically inadmissible is a multiplicity of first principles: every plurality must be produced, sustained, and differentiated from unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-01","text":"The distinction between necessity and contingency becomes a general differentiation of divine operations: the understanding specifies what is necessary, while the will directs what can be otherwise.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D2","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3","CL_UCIC_16:GA-02","CL_UCIC_16:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-02","text":"The continuation of creation and the functional analogy of Monads imply that to exist means simultaneously to be sustained from without and structured from within.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3","CL_UCIC_16:GA-05","CL_UCIC_16:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-03","text":"The primitive unity of God and the gradation of imitations transform the hierarchy of beings into a distribution of degrees of one and the same architecture, rather than a juxtaposition of primary substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:D4","CH_UCIC_P_39:ME4","CL_UCIC_16:GA-04","CL_UCIC_16:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-04","text":"The principle of the best connects the order of contingent truths to the order of cosmic production: choosing the world and effecting its changes fall under the same normative orientation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS3","CL_UCIC_16:GA-03","CL_UCIC_16:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-05","text":"Creaturely limitation functions as an operator of translation: it converts infinite power, knowledge, and will into finite but homologous faculties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5","CL_UCIC_16:GA-06","CL_UCIC_16:GA-08","CL_UCIC_16:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-06","text":"Dependence becomes stratified: semantic dependence of truths, ontological dependence of existence, and functional dependence of faculties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D4","CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:D4","CL_UCIC_16:GA-01","CL_UCIC_16:GA-02","CL_UCIC_16:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-07","text":"The activity of Monads does not abolish their dependence: it is precisely the finite form under which divine causality becomes perception, appetition, and tendency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS4","CL_UCIC_16:GA-05","CL_UCIC_16:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:XD-08","text":"The cluster replaces the choice between divine transcendence and created autonomy with an asymmetric continuity in which analogy increases dependence instead of suppressing it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3","CL_UCIC_16:GA-09","CL_UCIC_16:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-01","text":"The order of the real is neither an arbitrary decree nor an independent necessity: it is an architecture with several regimes of dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-02","text":"Causality is reclassified as an articulation of three irreducible functions: making possible, determining intelligibly, and directing toward the best.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D3","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-03","text":"Time becomes an ontological dimension of creation, since created being must be continually renewed without ceasing to be a distinct substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-04","text":"The created subject is not a first principle, but a derivative unity capable of reproducing inwardly, to a finite degree, the structure of the divine source.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:D3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-05","text":"Ontological hierarchy becomes a cartography of capacities for imitation: the more perfection increases, the more the divine structure is realized in a finite form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D5","CH_UCIC_P_40:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-06","text":"Divine sovereignty is redefined as differentiated mastery of the regimes of production, and not as indifference with regard to every intelligible structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_38:SNX4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:BSD-07","text":"The methodological consequence is a reading through functional correspondences and mutations of regime, rather than through simple identities between God and creature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D4","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop is: divine dependence → risk of arbitrariness → differentiation of modes of dependence → more structured dependence of the creature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_38:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-02","text":"A second loop converts creation into maintenance: divine production → derivative existence → temporal renewal → impossibility of ontological autonomy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-03","text":"A third loop converts infinity into gradation: divine attribute → created imitation → limitation of receptivity → differentiated degree of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-04","text":"The term will oscillates between a power excluded from the necessary and a power required for the contingent; this oscillation becomes a mechanism of differentiation rather than an incoherence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7","CH_UCIC_P_40:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor of the cluster is differentiated dependence: every attempt to produce a simple autonomy reintroduces a deeper level of dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_39:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:RLE-06","text":"The escalation trajectory goes from the theory of truth to the ontology of creation, then to an internal theory of monadic activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B01","text":"Undifferentiated divine dependence → suspicion of arbitrariness → separation of the necessary and the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_38:A2","CH_UCIC_P_38:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B02","text":"Necessary truth → divine understanding; contingent truth → will, fittingness, and choice of the best.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_38:A3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B03","text":"Primitive divine unity → production of Monads → continual flashing → maintained derivative existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B04","text":"Limited receptivity → boundary of production → God/creature distinction → gradation of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B05","text":"Power, knowledge, will → production, ideal determination, normative orientation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_40:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B06","text":"Divine triad → base, perception, appetition → finite and functionally analogous imitation in each Monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B07","text":"Negation of universal arbitrariness + negation of primitive autonomy + graded analogy → architecture of productive and intelligible dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:AFM-B01","text":"Undifferentiated divine dependence → risk of arbitrariness → necessary/contingent distinction → understanding/will separation → divine unity as primitive source → creation as continual flashing → limitation of receptivity → divine triad refracted in the Monad → hierarchy of imitations → closure through differentiated dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_39:AF4","CH_UCIC_P_40:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-01","text":"Divine dependence is reclassified from a single relation into a map with several regimes: logical, ontological, temporal, and functional.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_40:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-02","text":"The false opposition between the autonomy of truths and divine arbitrariness collapses with the distinction between understanding and will.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-03","text":"Punctual creation is replaced by a temporal map of continuous actualization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-04","text":"Limitation is reclassified as an operator of productive differentiation, and not as a simple ontological deficit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-05","text":"The hierarchy of beings becomes a hierarchy of imitation and functional capacity, not an external ranking of isolated substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MME-06","text":"The strategic terrain of the reading shifts from the God/creature opposition toward the analysis of finite translations of infinite divine functions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_40:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are eternal truths, God, created Monads, their faculties, and their difference in perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_39:A3","CH_UCIC_P_40:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are organized by distributions of dependence: understanding/will, origin/production, power/knowledge/orientation, and infinity/limitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The strategy consists in dissolving global alternatives by distinguishing functions and converting objections into changes of regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Created being is a continually renewed production, finite in its receptivity and analogous in its internal structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form accomplishes its thesis by progressively replacing binary oppositions with nested functional distinctions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_40:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_40:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FL-01","text":"The integral dependence of Monads threatens their status as distinct substances, while their internal activity prevents their reduction to mere passive effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_40:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FL-02","text":"Functional analogy brings God and creatures closer together, but divine infinity and creaturely limitation prevent every substantial identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_40:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FL-03","text":"The will is simultaneously subordinate to the intelligible order of the necessary and indispensable to the determination of the contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_38:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:FL-04","text":"Continual creation intensifies temporal dependence without dissolving the stability of monadic identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MP-01","text":"The transition from the dependence of truths to the dependence of existence transforms a logical distinction into an ontology of continued production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MP-02","text":"The transition from limitation as boundary to limitation as degree of imitation converts a negation into a positive principle of hierarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A6","CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MP-03","text":"The transition from the divine triad to monadic structure produces an operative analogy, and not a mere doctrinal resemblance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MP-04","text":"The transition from primitive unity to graded multiplicity establishes the creature as a limited repetition of the source rather than as a second principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_39:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a machine of continued production: a simple source distributes differentiated effects according to the receptivity of that which receives them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_39:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:HSI-02","text":"The created subject becomes a micro-architecture of limited power, partial representation, and directed tendency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:A4","CH_UCIC_P_40:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:HSI-03","text":"Time is not a mere framework of events: it is the rhythm of the renewal of derivative existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:A5","CH_UCIC_P_40:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:HSI-04","text":"The only available escape is not an absolute independence, but an increase in the degree of imitation and perfection within dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_40:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the core of the cluster: differentiated dependence, primitive divine unity, continued creation, functional triad, and graded imitation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_39:A1","CH_UCIC_P_40:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction remains coherent because the necessary, the contingent, created existence, and monadic activity are assigned to distinct but coordinated functions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:D1","CH_UCIC_P_40:D3","CH_UCIC_P_40:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B03","text":"Compression cannot, however, entirely determine the precise mechanism that connects the divine understanding to Ideas, nor that which connects the monadic base to divine power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B04","text":"The system's area of strength is the articulation between limitation, analogy, and continued dependence; its unstable area is the simultaneous maintenance of derivation and proper activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_39:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_40:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient at the Cluster level: it restores the generative escalation without reducing the three units to their local machines, but it leaves open the detailed determination of internal mediations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_38:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_39:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_40:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_16@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_16:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 46–48","context":"Proposition 46 · Proposition 47 · Proposition 48"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 49–51","order":17,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_41","CH_UCIC_P_42","CH_UCIC_P_43"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_17@R001","sha256":"7b12069a769d28576d65e4960e48ce60ae30f9709ce379128d91a786facc947d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-01","text":"Le système cherche à déterminer comment une créature peut être dite active ou passive alors que son rapport aux autres créatures ne repose pas sur une transmission physique directe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_43:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-02","text":"Il recadre d’abord l’action et la passion comme des fonctions graduelles du régime perceptif, puis comme des positions dans une hiérarchie de raisons explicatives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_42:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-03","text":"La causalité se déplace ainsi d’une distinction interne entre perceptions vers une asymétrie rationnelle entre créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_42:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-04","text":"L’impossibilité d’une influence physique ne détruit pas la dépendance intermonadique ; elle la reconstruit comme influence idéale médiatisée par Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-05","text":"Le mouvement est récursif et mutationnel : le critère de l’activité est internalisé, rendu relationnel, puis absorbé dans un ordre divin originaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-06","text":"L’architecture obtenue conserve simultanément la clôture intérieure des monades, l’asymétrie de l’action et la réalité d’une dépendance réciproque non physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_43:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-07","text":"La clôture du cluster n’est pas une causalité matérielle retrouvée, mais une topologie de coordination dans laquelle agir signifie expliquer, régler ou correspondre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] L’action et la passion ne sont pas des propriétés absolues de la substance ; elles sont des attributions relatives à un régime de détermination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] La perfection conserve une fonction directrice, mais elle passe de la distinction perceptive interne à la capacité de rendre raison de ce qui arrive ailleurs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","text":"[Emergent] L’action devient une priorité explicative : agit ce qui contient la raison a priori de l’événement attribué à l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] La monade possède une intériorité qui ne peut être physiquement pénétrée par une autre monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La relation intermonadique réelle est produite par une coordination idéale plutôt que par une communication matérielle des intériorités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] La causalité créée n’est pas supprimée mais convertie en dépendance réglée par une médiation divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] La séparation entre intériorité physique et ordre relationnel permet de rendre compatibles autonomie monadique et dépendance réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] L’ordre causal ultime est un ordre de correspondance originaire, non de transfert d’un état intérieur vers un autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] L’action et la passion restent asymétriques, mais cette asymétrie devient graduelle, explicative et dépendante d’un ordre plus vaste.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_42:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-01","text":"[Persistance fonctionnelle] L’opposition action/passion revient à travers les trois unités, mais cesse d’être une opposition de natures pour devenir une différence de régime perceptif, d’explication et de coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D3","CH_UCIC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] La perfection se déplace d’un degré interne de clarté vers une supériorité relationnelle dans l’ordre des raisons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D4","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-03","text":"[Escalade] La distinction perceptive devient fondement de l’action, puis l’action devient fonction de l’intelligibilité, avant d’être intégrée à une coordination divine préalable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D1","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-04","text":"[Inversion] L’influence intermonadique est d’abord affirmée comme action sur l’autre, puis refusée comme influence physique et conservée sous forme idéale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-05","text":"[Absorption] L’agent et le patient, d’abord distingués par leur perfection relative, sont finalement absorbés dans un système de réglage qui précède leurs effets particuliers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D4","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-06","text":"[Transformation terminale] Dieu passe d’une condition non explicitée de l’action à la médiation constitutive de toute relation intermonadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:D2","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-07","text":"[Disparition productive] La causalité physique disparaît comme modèle explicatif autonome après avoir rendu nécessaire la distinction entre intériorité close et coordination idéale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-01","text":"[Local] La distinction entre perceptions distinctes et perceptions confuses reste une machine propre à l’analyse de l’activité interne de la monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A4","CH_UCIC_P_41:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-02","text":"[Local] La présence d’une raison a priori dans une créature reste d’abord un critère local de supériorité explicative entre deux créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-03","text":"[Changement d’échelle] L’interaction des deux critères transforme l’action en continuité entre clarté perceptive, intelligibilité et dépendance relationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D2","CH_UCIC_P_43:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-04","text":"[Catalyseur] L’impossibilité d’une influence physique contraint la synthèse à reclasser toute action comme coordination plutôt que comme transmission.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-05","text":"[Recodage] La formule « agir sur l’autre » n’est plus comprise comme contact causal ; elle devient le nom d’une priorité rationnelle inscrite dans un ordre divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-06","text":"[Obsolescence] L’idée d’une action ou d’une passion exclusivement attachée à une monade devient insuffisante dès lors que les positions sont graduelles et coordonnées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A8","CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut une action indépendante de toute détermination perceptive, explicative ou relationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut une passion conçue comme pure réception extérieure, sans corrélat interne ni degré propre d’imperfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut la causalité brute, la succession temporelle comme explication suffisante et la force matérielle comme fondement autonome de l’action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut qu’une monade puisse pénétrer physiquement l’intériorité d’une autre ou produire seule la cohérence du multiple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une séparation définitive entre agent et patient, ainsi qu’une réciprocité symétrique de l’action entre créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_42:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’idée selon laquelle une relation causale peut être intelligible sans fondement interne ou rationnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que soit fausse l’hypothèse d’une communauté immédiate entre les monades, car leur clôture physique rend nécessaire un ordre médiateur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie tout modèle total fondé sur l’auto-organisation relationnelle des substances ou sur une causalité créée autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:DBN-04","text":"Il ne peut admettre une symétrie causale entre les créatures, puisque l’ordre de l’action est construit comme asymétrie de raison et de réglage.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D4","CH_UCIC_P_42:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSA-01","text":"Le système contourne la possibilité d’un monde où les substances communiqueraient directement leurs états intérieurs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_43:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité indisponible qui donne sa force à l’ensemble est celle d’une action réelle sans médiation rationnelle ou divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSA-03","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un extérieur causal indépendant de l’intériorité, de l’explication et du réglage originaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSA-04","text":"Est ontologiquement inadmissible un sujet qui serait soit entièrement transparent à lui-même, soit absolument séparé de tout ordre relationnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-01","text":"L’action est progressivement dématérialisée : elle commence comme attribution liée à la perception, devient priorité explicative et s’achève comme coordination idéale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_43:D1","CL_UCIC_17:GA-01","CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-02","text":"La perfection n’est pas un contenu fixe mais une fonction d’ordonnancement : elle mesure d’abord la distinction, puis la capacité à fonder l’intelligibilité d’un autre événement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2","CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-03","text":"L’intériorité close ne supprime pas la relation ; elle impose que la relation soit reconstruite comme correspondance préétablie entre séries internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-04","text":"La causalité intermonadique devient une causalité sans transfert : l’effet demeure réel, mais sa réalité réside dans l’ordre de coordination qui le rend possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:D4","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05","CL_UCIC_17:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-05","text":"L’asymétrie entre agent et patient est conservée tout en changeant de support : elle passe de la clarté perceptive à la priorité rationnelle, puis au réglage divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS4","CL_UCIC_17:GA-01","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_17:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-06","text":"[Tension] Le même vocabulaire d’influence doit désigner à la fois une action reconnue et une action physique interdite ; cette contradiction produit la distinction entre influence idéale et transmission matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A5","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT5","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05","CL_UCIC_17:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-01","text":"Le réel intermonadique est reclassé comme un ordre d’intelligibilité coordonnée plutôt que comme un réseau de transmissions entre intériorités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-02","text":"Le sujet monadique devient une entité causalement close mais structurellement lisible à travers les raisons et les correspondances qui l’ordonnent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-03","text":"Le temps causal est déplacé de la succession des interactions vers le commencement originaire où les relations futures sont réglées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3","CL_UCIC_17:GA-06","CL_UCIC_17:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-04","text":"La causalité devient une hiérarchie de fondations : ce qui agit est ce qui explique, et ce qui explique est lui-même inscrit dans un ordre de coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_43:D3","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-05","text":"La distinction entre autonomie et dépendance cesse d’être une opposition : l’autonomie désigne la clôture de l’intériorité, tandis que la dépendance désigne son inscription dans l’ordre idéal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1","CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-06","text":"La méthode générée par le cluster consiste à remplacer toute causalité supposée par la recherche de son niveau de fondation : perceptif, rationnel ou divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS3","CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_17:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale est : perception distincte → perfection → action → priorité explicative → coordination idéale → redétermination de l’action comme correspondance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-02","text":"Chaque fois que l’action semble exiger un dehors causal, le système reconduit ce dehors vers une structure interne, rationnelle ou divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-03","text":"La séquence d’escalade est : état perceptif → degré de perfection → hiérarchie de raisons → impossibilité physique → médiation divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_42:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_43:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est la compatibilité entre clôture monadique et dépendance réelle, obtenue par séparation des niveaux de causalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-05","text":"La répétition de l’action ne signale pas une redondance : elle marque trois changements de phase, de l’activité perceptive à l’explication puis au réglage originaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D1","CH_UCIC_P_42:D3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-06","text":"La clôture distribuée est produite lorsque la causalité extérieure est successivement absorbée par la perception, la raison et l’ordre divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B01","text":"Une différence de clarté perceptive produit une différence de perfection, laquelle produit une différence d’activité ou de passivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B02","text":"La différence de perfection est ensuite convertie en asymétrie explicative : ce qui contient la raison a priori de l’événement est dit agir sur l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B03","text":"L’hypothèse d’une transmission physique est supprimée, ce qui force la dissociation entre effet réel et pénétration de l’intériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_43:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B04","text":"L’influence restante est élevée au niveau idéal, puis subordonnée à une médiation divine qui règle les monades dès l’origine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B05","text":"La machine complète transforme donc la causalité en chaîne de fondation : perception → perfection → raison → coordination → dépendance non physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B06","text":"La conclusion positive n’est pas une interaction retrouvée, mais une architecture de correspondances qui conserve l’action en supprimant son modèle matériel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:D1","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B01","text":"Attribution problématique de l’action et de la passion → recadrage perceptif de la perfection → détermination relative de l’agent et du patient.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_41:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B02","text":"Hiérarchie perceptive → hiérarchie de raisons → conversion de l’action en priorité explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D4","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B03","text":"Clôture physique des monades → impossibilité de l’influence directe → substitution d’une influence idéale médiatisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B04","text":"Réglage divin originaire → dépendance intermonadique non physique → compatibilité terminale entre autonomie intérieure et coordination universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-01","text":"L’agent et le patient sont reclassés comme des positions variables dans une hiérarchie de perception, d’explication et de coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_41:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-02","text":"L’opposition entre intérieur et extérieur s’effondre comme opposition simple : l’action au dehors dépend d’une organisation interne ou d’un ordre qui la préconfigure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-03","text":"L’opposition entre causalité et intelligibilité devient une fausse opposition, puisque l’action est définie par la fonction de rendre raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D3","CH_UCIC_P_42:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-04","text":"Le commencement des choses devient une infrastructure causale : il ne désigne plus seulement une origine temporelle, mais le réglage des relations ultérieures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-05","text":"Une nouvelle méthode de lecture devient disponible : suivre le déplacement d’un même terme entre plusieurs niveaux plutôt que lui attribuer une fonction stable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D3","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-06","text":"Le terrain stratégique est redessiné autour de la question suivante : quel ordre rend une relation possible lorsque le contact causal est exclu ?","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont l’action, la passion, la perfection, la perception et la dépendance d’une monade à l’égard d’une autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont organisés par des distributions de clarté, des asymétries de raison et une coordination qui remplace la transmission physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Le système recadre chaque attribution causale en demandant quel régime de perception, de fondation rationnelle ou de réglage la rend possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est conçu comme un ordre de dépendances non physiques établi dans un commencement qui règle les relations sans modifier les substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle affirme : elle retire progressivement le contact causal et reconstruit une cohérence par déplacement de niveau.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FL-01","text":"[Ligne de faille] L’action est dite orientée vers l’extérieur alors que son critère demeure interne à la perception de la monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FL-02","text":"[Ligne de faille] Le passage de « rendre raison » à « agir » n’est pas démontré par un mécanisme indépendant ; il constitue le pont décisif de l’architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FL-03","text":"[Ligne de faille] La notion d’influence conserve un effet réel tout en excluant toute action physique, ce qui maintient une ambiguïté productive entre causalité et correspondance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FL-04","text":"[Ligne de faille] La médiation divine résout la contradiction entre clôture et dépendance, mais son mécanisme exact reste sous-déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MP-01","text":"[Point de mutation] La perfection cesse d’être seulement un degré de qualité interne lorsqu’elle devient capacité d’expliquer un événement extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MP-02","text":"[Point de mutation] L’action change de fonction lorsqu’elle passe d’un état perceptif à une relation de fondation rationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D1","CH_UCIC_P_42:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MP-03","text":"[Point de mutation] La causalité change définitivement de registre lorsque l’impossibilité physique produit l’influence idéale au lieu d’abolir toute dépendance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MP-04","text":"[Point de mutation] Le commencement des choses devient le lieu où une pluralité de substances closes reçoit une cohérence relationnelle sans communication interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de correspondances stratifiées : chaque état monadique exprime un ordre qui le dépasse sans être physiquement pénétré par lui.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une chambre intérieure causalement close, mais positionnée dans une architecture de raisons, de degrés et de réglages.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas principalement une succession d’actions ; il est une origine de réglage qui préconfigure les dépendances ultérieures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:HSI-04","text":"La lutte ou la navigation possibles consistent moins à transmettre une force qu’à occuper une position d’intelligibilité, de perfection relative ou de correspondance dans l’ordre réglé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre axiomes : la relativité de l’action et de la passion, la mutation relationnelle de la perfection, la clôture physique des monades et la médiation divine de leur coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B02","text":"Ces axiomes suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement complet, car ils engendrent successivement l’action perceptive, la priorité explicative et la dépendance idéale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne le statut exact de la raison a priori, la nature de la demande monadique et le mécanisme précis du réglage divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence ne dépend pas d’un séquençage linéaire, mais du retour récursif d’un même problème : comment maintenir une action réelle sans admettre une transmission physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B05","text":"La compression est suffisante lorsque la causalité est reconstruite comme chaîne de perception, raison et coordination ; tout ajout qui réintroduirait une force matérielle autonome détruirait la logique du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B06","text":"La proposition indispensable qui résiste à toute réduction est la suivante : la dépendance réelle entre monades ne peut être conservée qu’en changeant de niveau ontologique et explicatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:D4","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195546940607Z_5135a766","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 49–51","source_sha256":"7b12069a769d28576d65e4960e48ce60ae30f9709ce379128d91a786facc947d","sha256":"6b40eb647449b7653d903cf991dbeacfb29b145cdcfb1a0b6ec1cfd57920137f","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:55:46.944374+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-01","text":"The system seeks to determine how a creature can be said to be active or passive when its relation to other creatures does not rest on direct physical transmission.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_43:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-02","text":"It first reframes action and passion as gradual functions of the perceptual regime, then as positions in a hierarchy of explanatory reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_42:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-03","text":"Causality thus shifts from an internal distinction between perceptions to a rational asymmetry between creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_42:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-04","text":"The impossibility of physical influence does not destroy intermonadic dependence; it reconstructs it as ideal influence mediated by God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-05","text":"The movement is recursive and mutational: the criterion of activity is internalized, made relational, then absorbed into an originating divine order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-06","text":"The resulting architecture simultaneously preserves the inner closure of monads, the asymmetry of action, and the reality of a reciprocal non-physical dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_43:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:SP-07","text":"The closure of the cluster is not a recovered material causality, but a topology of coordination in which acting means explaining, regulating, or corresponding.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Action and passion are not absolute properties of substance; they are attributions relative to a regime of determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Perfection retains a guiding function, but it shifts from internal perceptual distinction to the capacity to give a reason for what happens elsewhere.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","text":"[Emergent] Action becomes explanatory priority: that acts which contains the a priori reason for the event attributed to the other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A4","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The monad possesses an interiority that cannot be physically penetrated by another monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The real intermonadic relation is produced by ideal coordination rather than by material communication between interiorities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A3","CH_UCIC_P_43:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Created causality is not suppressed but converted into dependence regulated by a divine mediation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] The separation between physical interiority and relational order makes it possible to reconcile monadic autonomy and reciprocal dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] The ultimate causal order is an order of originating correspondence, not of transfer from one inner state to another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Action and passion remain asymmetrical, but this asymmetry becomes gradual, explanatory, and dependent on a broader order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_42:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-01","text":"[Functional persistence] The opposition between action and passion recurs across the three units, but ceases to be an opposition of natures in order to become a difference of perceptual, explanatory, and coordinative regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D3","CH_UCIC_P_42:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] Perfection shifts from an internal degree of clarity to relational superiority in the order of reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D4","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-03","text":"[Escalation] Perceptual distinction becomes the foundation of action, then action becomes a function of intelligibility, before being integrated into a prior divine coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D1","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-04","text":"[Inversion] Intermonadic influence is first affirmed as action upon the other, then rejected as physical influence and preserved in ideal form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-05","text":"[Absorption] Agent and patient, initially distinguished by their relative perfection, are ultimately absorbed into a system of regulation that precedes their particular effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D4","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-06","text":"[Terminal transformation] God shifts from an unexplicated condition of action to the constitutive mediation of every intermonadic relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:D2","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RMD-07","text":"[Productive disappearance] Physical causality disappears as an autonomous explanatory model after having made necessary the distinction between closed interiority and ideal coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The distinction between distinct perceptions and confused perceptions remains a mechanism proper to the analysis of the monad's internal activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A4","CH_UCIC_P_41:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-02","text":"[Local] The presence of an a priori reason in one creature remains initially a local criterion of explanatory superiority between two creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-03","text":"[Change of scale] The interaction of the two criteria transforms action into a continuity between perceptual clarity, intelligibility, and relational dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D2","CH_UCIC_P_43:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-04","text":"[Catalyst] The impossibility of physical influence compels the synthesis to reclassify all action as coordination rather than transmission.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-05","text":"[Recoding] The phrase « agir sur l’autre » is no longer understood as causal contact; it becomes the name of a rational priority inscribed in a divine order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:CGD-06","text":"[Obsolescence] The idea of an action or passion attached exclusively to one monad becomes insufficient once the positions are gradual and coordinated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A8","CH_UCIC_P_41:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes an action independent of every perceptual, explanatory, or relational determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a passion conceived as pure external reception, without an internal correlate or a proper degree of imperfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-03","text":"It excludes brute causality, temporal succession as a sufficient explanation, and material force as an autonomous foundation of action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that one monad can physically penetrate the interiority of another or by itself produce the coherence of multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:GNX-05","text":"It excludes a definitive separation between agent and patient, as well as a symmetrical reciprocity of action between creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_42:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the idea that a causal relation can be intelligible without an internal or rational foundation must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:DBN-02","text":"The hypothesis of an immediate community between monads must likewise be false, for their physical closure makes a mediating order necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies every total model founded on the relational self-organization of substances or on an autonomous created causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:DBN-04","text":"It cannot admit a causal symmetry between creatures, since the order of action is constructed as an asymmetry of reason and regulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D4","CH_UCIC_P_42:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSA-01","text":"The system circumvents the possibility of a world in which substances would directly communicate their inner states.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_43:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSA-02","text":"The unavailable possibility that gives the whole its force is that of a real action without rational or divine mediation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSA-03","text":"The structuring absence is that of a causal exterior independent of interiority, explanation, and originating regulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSA-04","text":"Ontologically inadmissible is a subject that would be either wholly transparent to itself or absolutely separated from every relational order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-01","text":"Action is progressively dematerialized: it begins as an attribution linked to perception, becomes explanatory priority, and ends as ideal coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A6","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_43:D1","CL_UCIC_17:GA-01","CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-02","text":"Perfection is not a fixed content but an ordering function: it first measures distinction, then the capacity to ground the intelligibility of another event.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2","CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-03","text":"Closed interiority does not suppress relation; it requires relation to be reconstructed as a pre-established correspondence between internal series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:A1","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-04","text":"Intermonadic causality becomes causality without transfer: the effect remains real, but its reality lies in the order of coordination that makes it possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:D4","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05","CL_UCIC_17:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-05","text":"The asymmetry between agent and patient is preserved while changing its support: it shifts from perceptual clarity to rational priority, then to divine regulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS4","CL_UCIC_17:GA-01","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_17:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:XD-06","text":"[Tension] The same vocabulary of influence must designate both a recognized action and a prohibited physical action; this contradiction produces the distinction between ideal influence and material transmission.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:A5","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT5","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05","CL_UCIC_17:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-01","text":"The intermonadic real is reclassified as an order of coordinated intelligibility rather than as a network of transmissions between interiorities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-02","text":"The monadic subject becomes a causally closed entity but structurally legible through the reasons and correspondences that order it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-03","text":"Causal time is displaced from the succession of interactions to the originating beginning in which future relations are regulated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3","CL_UCIC_17:GA-06","CL_UCIC_17:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-04","text":"Causality becomes a hierarchy of foundations: what acts is what explains, and what explains is itself inscribed in an order of coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_43:D3","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_17:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-05","text":"The distinction between autonomy and dependence ceases to be an opposition: autonomy designates the closure of interiority, whereas dependence designates its inscription in the ideal order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1","CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:BSD-06","text":"The method generated by the cluster consists in replacing every supposed causality with the search for its level of foundation: perceptual, rational, or divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS3","CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_17:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop is: distinct perception → perfection → action → explanatory priority → ideal coordination → redetermination of action as correspondence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-02","text":"Whenever action seems to require a causal exterior, the system redirects that exterior toward an internal, rational, or divine structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_42:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-03","text":"The escalation sequence is: perceptual state → degree of perfection → hierarchy of reasons → physical impossibility → divine mediation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_42:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_43:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-04","text":"The conceptual attractor is the compatibility between monadic closure and real dependence, achieved through the separation of levels of causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-05","text":"The repetition of action does not indicate redundancy: it marks three phase changes, from perceptual activity to explanation and then to originating regulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D1","CH_UCIC_P_42:D3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:RLE-06","text":"Distributed closure is produced when external causality is successively absorbed by perception, reason, and divine order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B01","text":"A difference in perceptual clarity produces a difference in perfection, which produces a difference in activity or passivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B02","text":"The difference in perfection is then converted into explanatory asymmetry: that which contains the a priori reason for the event is said to act upon the other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B03","text":"The hypothesis of a physical transmission is removed, which compels the dissociation between real effect and penetration of interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_43:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B04","text":"The remaining influence is elevated to the ideal level, then subordinated to a divine mediation that regulates the monads from the origin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B05","text":"The complete mechanism thus transforms causality into a chain of foundations: perception → perfection → reason → coordination → non-physical dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B06","text":"The positive conclusion is not a recovered interaction, but an architecture of correspondences that preserves action while suppressing its material model.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:D1","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B01","text":"Problematic attribution of action and passion → perceptual reframing of perfection → relative determination of agent and patient.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_41:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B02","text":"Perceptual hierarchy → hierarchy of reasons → conversion of action into explanatory priority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D4","CH_UCIC_P_42:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B03","text":"Physical closure of monads → impossibility of direct influence → substitution of mediated ideal influence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B04","text":"Originating divine regulation → non-physical intermonadic dependence → terminal compatibility between inner autonomy and universal coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-01","text":"Agent and patient are reclassified as variable positions in a hierarchy of perception, explanation, and coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_41:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-02","text":"The opposition between interior and exterior collapses as a simple opposition: action outward depends on an internal organization or on an order that preconfigures it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-03","text":"The opposition between causality and intelligibility becomes a false opposition, since action is defined by the function of giving a reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:D3","CH_UCIC_P_42:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-04","text":"The beginning of things becomes a causal infrastructure: it no longer designates merely a temporal origin, but the regulation of subsequent relations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-05","text":"A new method of reading becomes available: tracing the displacement of one and the same term across several levels rather than assigning it a stable function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D3","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MME-06","text":"The strategic terrain is redrawn around the following question: what order makes a relation possible when causal contact is excluded?","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are action, passion, perfection, perception, and the dependence of one monad with respect to another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are organized by distributions of clarity, asymmetries of reason, and a coordination that replaces physical transmission.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The system reframes every causal attribution by asking what regime of perception, rational foundation, or regulation makes it possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_42:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The real is conceived as an order of non-physical dependencies established in a beginning that regulates relations without modifying substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form performs what it asserts: it progressively withdraws causal contact and reconstructs coherence through a displacement of level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FL-01","text":"[Fault line] Action is said to be directed outward even though its criterion remains internal to the monad's perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_41:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FL-02","text":"[Fault line] The transition from « rendre raison » to « agir » is not demonstrated by an independent mechanism; it constitutes the decisive bridge of the architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_42:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FL-03","text":"[Fault line] The notion of influence preserves a real effect while excluding all physical action, thereby sustaining a productive ambiguity between causality and correspondence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_43:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:FL-04","text":"[Fault line] Divine mediation resolves the contradiction between closure and dependence, but its exact mechanism remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MP-01","text":"[Mutation point] Perfection ceases to be solely a degree of internal quality when it becomes the capacity to explain an external event.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:A3","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MP-02","text":"[Mutation point] Action changes function when it shifts from a perceptual state to a relation of rational foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:D1","CH_UCIC_P_42:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MP-03","text":"[Mutation point] Causality definitively changes register when physical impossibility produces ideal influence rather than abolishing all dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MP-04","text":"[Mutation point] The beginning of things becomes the place where a plurality of closed substances receives relational coherence without internal communication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a mechanism of stratified correspondences: each monadic state expresses an order that exceeds it without being physically penetrated by it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a causally closed inner chamber, but positioned within an architecture of reasons, degrees, and regulations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:HSI-03","text":"Time is not primarily a succession of actions; it is an originating regulation that preconfigures subsequent dependencies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_43:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:HSI-04","text":"Possible struggle or navigation consists less in transmitting a force than in occupying a position of intelligibility, relative perfection, or correspondence within the regulated order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_43:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four axioms: the relativity of action and passion, the relational mutation of perfection, the physical closure of monads, and the divine mediation of their coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_42:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_43:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B02","text":"These axioms suffice to reconstruct the complete movement, because they successively generate perceptual action, explanatory priority, and ideal dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_41:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the exact status of the a priori reason, the nature of monadic demand, and the precise mechanism of divine regulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_42:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence does not depend on linear sequencing, but on the recursive return of one and the same problem: how to maintain a real action without admitting a physical transmission.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_43:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B05","text":"The compression is sufficient when causality is reconstructed as a chain of perception, reason, and coordination; any addition that would reintroduce an autonomous material force would destroy the logic of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_43:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B06","text":"The indispensable proposition that resists every reduction is the following: real dependence between monads can be preserved only by changing ontological and explanatory level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_43:D4","CH_UCIC_P_43:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_17@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_17:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 49–51","context":"Proposition 49 · Proposition 50 · Proposition 51"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 52–54","order":18,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_44","CH_UCIC_P_45","CH_UCIC_P_46"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_18@R001","sha256":"470e8cd14bdbf87e731a1429dad517f937d5e4212e0653dc7cd1f64a1b279b49","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B01","text":"Le système cherche à déterminer comment des réalités distinctes peuvent être coordonnées et déterminées sans que leur ordre repose sur une relation brute, unilatérale ou indifférenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B02","text":"Le problème est recadré : la détermination n’est jamais une propriété isolée, mais l’effet d’une comparaison, d’une raison explicative ou d’une convenance entre possibilités concurrentes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A7","CH_UCIC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B03","text":"Le fondement de l’argument est une ontologie relationnelle où l’accommodement des substances et la sélection des Mondes procèdent d’une même exigence de raison suffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D4","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B04","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et mutationnel : la mutualité locale devient asymétrie explicative, puis la raison explicative devient principe de sélection ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_45:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B05","text":"L’architecture progresse de la coordination des événements à la hiérarchisation des possibles, en remplaçant les statuts absolus par des fonctions comparatives et graduées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_46:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B06","text":"La clôture produite est une actualité sélectionnée et intelligible : un seul ordre est réalisé, mais il demeure inscrit dans un champ de possibilités différenciées par leur convenance et leur perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Toute détermination effective exige une raison qui exclut le fait brut et l’indifférence absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A4","CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Les statuts d’activité, de passivité, de possibilité et d’actualité ne sont intelligibles qu’à partir d’un rapport comparatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A7","CH_UCIC_P_45:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La relation est d’abord un accommodement entre substances, puis elle devient une convenance organisant la sélection entre Mondes possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Le réel est produit à partir d’une pluralité préalable de possibilités, et non identifié sans reste à l’unique ordre actuel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] La raison explicative localisée dans une substance se généralise en raison suffisante déterminant le choix d’un univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La détermination est différentielle : elle distribue des fonctions, des degrés de perfection et des prétentions à l’existence plutôt qu’elle ne pose des identités fixes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] L’existence devient une actualisation proportionnelle à une convenance et à un degré de perfection, non une propriété uniforme du possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] La réciprocité n’abolit jamais l’asymétrie fonctionnelle : plusieurs réalités peuvent se déterminer mutuellement sans exercer la même fonction sous le même rapport.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_44:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] La convenance fonctionne comme opérateur d’unification entre correspondance relationnelle, raison suffisante, hiérarchie des possibles et actualisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A4","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] L’actualité est le résultat d’une sélection déterminée au sein du possible, tandis que le champ des possibles demeure irréductible à ce qui est réalisé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-01","text":"La raison revient d’abord comme localisation de l’explication dans une substance, puis comme principe suffisant de la sélection d’un univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_45:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-02","text":"L’accommodement migre de la coordination de substances particulières vers la convenance globale entre Mondes possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-03","text":"La mutualité conserve sa structure de réciprocité, mais sa fonction se déplace vers une asymétrie explicative et une hiérarchie de détermination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-04","text":"La comparaison divine passe d’un dispositif de coordination intersubstantielle à un dispositif de classement des possibilités selon leur perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A3","CH_UCIC_P_46:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-05","text":"Le droit à l’existence transforme le possible : d’une simple alternative logique, il devient une prétention graduée soumise à la convenance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-06","text":"L’opposition agent-patient ne disparaît pas ; elle est absorbée dans une théorie plus vaste des positions relatives au sein d’un réseau de raisons croisées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D1","CH_UCIC_P_44:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-01","text":"La distinction entre activité et passivité des créatures demeure locale à la couche inférieure lorsqu’elle concerne seulement le point de considération d’une substance particulière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-02","text":"La pluralité des univers et l’unicité de l’actualité restent locales lorsqu’elles ne produisent que le problème initial du choix divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-03","text":"Au niveau courant, ces machines locales sont reliées par une même grammaire : une pluralité de termes est convertie en ordre par comparaison, raison et différenciation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D3","CH_UCIC_P_45:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-04","text":"La transition majeure consiste à faire passer la raison du statut d’explication locale d’un événement au statut d’opérateur global de sélection du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D2","CH_UCIC_P_45:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-05","text":"Les modèles de l’agent isolé, du patient absolu, du possible indifférent et du choix arbitraire deviennent obsolètes à l’échelle du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_45:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-01","text":"Le système rejette toute activité ou passivité conçue comme propriété intrinsèque indépendante d’un rapport de considération.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_44:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut une causalité unilatérale où une substance transférerait simplement une force à une autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-03","text":"Il refuse que tous les possibles deviennent réels ou que l’existence actuelle soit la coexistence indifférenciée de leurs contenus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_45:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-04","text":"Il récuse une actualisation sans principe de préférence, de raison suffisante ou de convenance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_46:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-05","text":"Il délimite le réel contre toute autosuffisance : aucun événement ni aucun Monde ne se suffit à lui-même comme principe explicatif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, il faut que soit faux le modèle d’un réel composé d’unités autosuffisantes et causalement closes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:DBN-02","text":"Le système disqualifie une ontologie plate où la possibilité, la perfection et l’actualité auraient le même statut.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:DBN-03","text":"Il ne peut admettre une décision première sans raison, car l’unicité de l’actualité deviendrait alors un fait ultime et inexplicable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:DBN-04","text":"Il ne peut séparer la hiérarchie des possibles de la convenance qui la rend opératoire ; une sélection sans critère détruirait la logique du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSA-01","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un fondement non relationnel, absolument brut et extérieur à toute comparaison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_46:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité inadmissible est celle d’un monde où tous les possibles posséderaient une prétention égale et simultanément réalisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_46:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSA-03","text":"Le système contourne la possibilité d’une actualité qui ne serait qu’un choix sans architecture de préférence, sans degré et sans convenance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSA-04","text":"Ce qui donne sa force à l’ensemble est l’impossibilité d’un passage immédiat du possible au réel : toute actualisation doit traverser une structure comparative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-01","text":"La coordination des substances et la sélection des Mondes sont deux régimes d’une même opération : convertir une multiplicité de termes en ordre par localisation ou hiérarchisation de raisons.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-03","CL_UCIC_18:GA-05","CL_UCIC_18:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_44:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-02","text":"L’asymétrie explicative entre substances réapparaît à l’échelle des Mondes comme asymétrie de perfection et de prétention à l’existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-06","CL_UCIC_18:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_44:D2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-03","text":"L’action et l’actualité sont parallèlement reclassées : l’une n’est plus un pouvoir absolu, l’autre n’est plus une propriété brute, toutes deux résultant d’un rapport déterminant.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-02","CL_UCIC_18:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_44:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_45:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-04","text":"La raison qui explique un événement dans une substance fournit le modèle fonctionnel de la raison suffisante qui explique la préférence d’un univers.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-05","CL_UCIC_18:GA-01","CH_UCIC_P_44:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_45:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-05","text":"La mutualité et la hiérarchie ne sont pas contradictoires : la première décrit la réciprocité du champ, la seconde distribue les fonctions explicatives et les degrés de réalisation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-06","CL_UCIC_18:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_44:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-01","text":"L’ontologie est transformée en système de sélection relationnelle : être réel signifie occuper une position déterminée dans un ordre de raisons, de correspondances et de degrés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-02","text":"La causalité et la création cessent d’être deux problèmes séparés : elles deviennent deux échelles d’une même logique d’intelligibilité distribuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_45:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-03","text":"Le possible n’est plus un réservoir neutre et l’actuel n’est plus une donnée première ; tous deux sont les pôles d’une opération de classement et d’actualisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-04","text":"La nécessité ne porte pas sur une identité fixe, mais sur la contrainte de produire une détermination proportionnée aux raisons disponibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_45:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-05","text":"L’ordre effectif conserve en lui la trace active des alternatives non réalisées : l’exclusion des possibles n’abolit pas leur fonction de contraste et de mesure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-01","text":"La pluralité produit l’exigence d’une raison ; la raison produit une comparaison ; la comparaison produit une sélection ; la sélection reconstitue un ordre relationnel qui relance la question de la détermination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_45:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-02","text":"La mutualité engendre une asymétrie explicative, laquelle exige l’accommodement ; l’accommodement reconduit ensuite la mutualité sous une forme structurée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-03","text":"La négation du fait brut force l’introduction de la raison suffisante, qui interdit à son tour toute sélection indifférente ou sans critère.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-04","text":"La convenance est l’attracteur conceptuel vers lequel convergent l’accommodement, la raison suffisante, la perfection graduée et l’actualisation proportionnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A7","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-05","text":"Le point de considération local devient un changement de phase lorsqu’il se généralise en point de comparaison entre Mondes possibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B01","text":"Une pluralité de substances et de Mondes est posée comme champ initial de possibilités distinctes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B02","text":"La comparaison rend visibles des raisons corrélatives, des fonctions explicatives et des degrés de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B03","text":"Les raisons corrélatives imposent un accommodement ; les degrés de perfection ordonnent les prétentions concurrentes à l’existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B04","text":"L’accommodement et la convenance convertissent la multiplicité en détermination relative, puis en sélection d’un ordre actuel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B05","text":"L’ordre sélectionné réintroduit une pluralité de relations où chaque terme peut être simultanément source d’explication et objet d’explication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B06","text":"La machine se ferme en excluant toute identité absolue, toute symétrie plate et toute actualité sans raison, tout en conservant le possible comme horizon de comparaison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AFM-B01","text":"Mutualité des relations → localisation comparative des raisons → accommodation réciproque → exigence d’une raison suffisante → hiérarchisation par convenance et perfection → sélection d’un univers actuel → réentrée dans un réseau d’événements mutuellement déterminés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_45:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AFM-B02","text":"Rejet des statuts absolus → relationalisation des fonctions → transformation du possible en prétention graduée → actualisation sélective → architecture globale de correspondances explicatives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-01","text":"L’opposition possible/existant est reconfigurée en continuum hiérarchisé de prétentions, de convenances et de degrés de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-02","text":"L’opposition agent-patient est reclassée comme une distribution relative de fonctions explicatives dans un réseau réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-03","text":"La causalité intercréaturelle et la sélection cosmologique apparaissent comme deux manifestations d’une même cartographie des raisons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_45:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-04","text":"La divinité est fonctionnellement reclassée : elle n’est pas seulement cause ou choix, mais principe de comparaison, d’accommodement et de sélection ordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-05","text":"Le terrain stratégique de l’analyse se déplace de la recherche d’un agent premier vers l’identification des rapports qui rendent une détermination intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_45:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B01","text":"**Surface level** — Des substances agissent et pâtissent mutuellement, tandis que plusieurs Mondes sont possibles et un seul devient actuel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B02","text":"**Structural level** — Les positions, les événements et les Mondes sont organisés par la localisation de raisons, la comparaison des termes et la hiérarchisation des degrés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B03","text":"**Metastrategic level** — L’analyse remplace les questions d’identité absolue par des questions de rapport, de fonction explicative, de préférence et de convenance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B04","text":"**Ontological / Temporal level** — Le possible précède logiquement l’actuel, et l’actualité est produite comme sélection déterminée plutôt que comme commencement sans condition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B05","text":"**Methodological / Performative level** — La forme argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle affirme : elle part d’une pluralité indifférenciée, introduit des distinctions négatives, puis reconstruit un ordre par raisons et proportions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FL-01","text":"La mutualité des rapports entre créatures demeure en tension avec l’asymétrie de la raison explicative : la réciprocité du champ ne produit pas l’égalité des fonctions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FL-02","text":"Le choix entre plusieurs Mondes paraît contingent, mais il est simultanément déterminé par une raison suffisante ; cette tension soutient la différence entre contingence et arbitraire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:D4","CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FL-03","text":"Le droit de chaque possible à prétendre à l’existence ne garantit pas son actualisation, ce qui laisse ouverte la relation exacte entre mérite ontologique et réalisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MP-01","text":"Le concept d’action mute lorsqu’il cesse de désigner un pouvoir intrinsèque et devient une fonction relative à la localisation de la raison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MP-02","text":"Le concept de possibilité mute lorsqu’il devient une prétention graduée à l’existence, mesurée par la perfection et la convenance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A6","CH_UCIC_P_46:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MP-03","text":"Le concept d’accommodement mute lorsqu’il passe de la coordination de substances à l’opérateur cosmologique de sélection des Mondes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_46:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une machine comparative : elle transforme une pluralité de termes en ordre par distribution de raisons, de fonctions et de degrés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:HSI-02","text":"Toute substance ou tout Monde est un nœud relationnel plutôt qu’un centre autonome ; son statut dépend de ce qu’il explique, reçoit, contient ou prétend réaliser.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système est principalement logique : le possible précède l’actuel comme espace de comparaison, puis l’actualité résulte d’une sélection proportionnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:HSI-04","text":"La navigation dans cette réalité ne consiste pas à sortir du réseau, mais à reclasser les positions selon les raisons qui les déterminent et les degrés qu’elles enveloppent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_46:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale est suffisante si elle conserve quatre opérateurs : pluralité des possibles, comparaison des termes, raison suffisante et actualisation proportionnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B02","text":"La cohérence dépend du maintien des deux échelles : la fonction active ou passive reste locale, tandis que la raison suffisante et la convenance produisent l’architecture du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination résiduelle concerne le contenu exact des raisons, le mécanisme de comparaison divine, la mesure de la perfection et le passage du droit à l’existence à l’existence effective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B04","text":"La compression reste fidèle au mouvement réel si elle préserve la tension entre réciprocité et asymétrie, ainsi que le passage de la mutualité relationnelle à la sélection métaphysique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B05","text":"Toute reconstruction qui supprimerait la négation du fait brut, l’échelle des degrés ou la fonction de la convenance réduirait le système à une simple théorie de la relation et manquerait sa clôture sélective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195617124137Z_c602b82f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 52–54","source_sha256":"470e8cd14bdbf87e731a1429dad517f937d5e4212e0653dc7cd1f64a1b279b49","sha256":"b8218a98f5c316f060c5218b2c013701967dca05463bcc364a6aeba8ada4d665","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:56:17.128115+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B01","text":"The system seeks to determine how distinct realities can be coordinated and determined without their order resting on a brute, unilateral, or undifferentiated relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_45:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B02","text":"The problem is reframed: determination is never an isolated property, but the effect of a comparison, an explanatory reason, or a fittingness among competing possibilities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A7","CH_UCIC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B03","text":"The foundation of the argument is a relational ontology in which the accommodation of substances and the selection of Worlds proceed from one and the same requirement of sufficient reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D4","CH_UCIC_P_45:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B04","text":"The movement is cumulative and mutational: local mutuality becomes explanatory asymmetry, then explanatory reason becomes a principle of ontological selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_45:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B05","text":"The architecture progresses from the coordination of events to the hierarchization of possibles, replacing absolute statuses with comparative and graded functions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_46:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AS-B06","text":"The closure produced is a selected and intelligible actuality: a single order is realized, but it remains inscribed within a field of possibilities differentiated by their fittingness and their perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every effective determination requires a reason that excludes brute fact and absolute indifference.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A4","CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The statuses of activity, passivity, possibility, and actuality are intelligible only on the basis of a comparative relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A7","CH_UCIC_P_45:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The relation is initially an accommodation among substances, then it becomes a fittingness organizing selection among possible Worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The real is produced from a prior plurality of possibilities, and is not identified without remainder with the sole actual order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] The explanatory reason localized in a substance becomes generalized into sufficient reason determining the choice of a universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Determination is differential: it distributes functions, degrees of perfection, and claims to existence rather than positing fixed identities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Existence becomes an actualization proportionate to a fittingness and to a degree of perfection, not a uniform property of the possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Reciprocity never abolishes functional asymmetry: several realities can determine one another mutually without exercising the same function under the same respect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_44:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Fittingness functions as an operator of unification among relational correspondence, sufficient reason, the hierarchy of possibles, and actualization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A4","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Actuality is the result of a determined selection within the possible, while the field of possibles remains irreducible to what is realized.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-01","text":"Reason first recurs as the localization of explanation in a substance, then as the sufficient principle of the selection of a universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_45:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-02","text":"Accommodation migrates from the coordination of particular substances toward global fittingness among possible Worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-03","text":"Mutuality retains its structure of reciprocity, but its function shifts toward explanatory asymmetry and a hierarchy of determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-04","text":"Divine comparison passes from an apparatus of intersubstantial coordination to an apparatus for ranking possibilities according to their perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A3","CH_UCIC_P_46:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-05","text":"The right to existence transforms the possible: from a mere logical alternative, it becomes a graded claim subject to fittingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RMD-06","text":"The agent-patient opposition does not disappear; it is absorbed into a broader theory of relative positions within a network of intersecting reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D1","CH_UCIC_P_44:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-01","text":"The distinction between the activity and passivity of creatures remains local to the lower layer when it concerns only the point of consideration of a particular substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_44:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-02","text":"The plurality of universes and the uniqueness of actuality remain local when they yield only the initial problem of divine choice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:A1","CH_UCIC_P_45:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-03","text":"At the current level, these local mechanisms are connected by the same grammar: a plurality of terms is converted into order through comparison, reason, and differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D3","CH_UCIC_P_45:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-04","text":"The major transition consists in shifting reason from the status of local explanation of an event to that of a global operator of selection of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:D2","CH_UCIC_P_45:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:CGD-05","text":"The models of the isolated agent, the absolute patient, the indifferent possible, and arbitrary choice become obsolete at the scale of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_45:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects all activity or passivity conceived as an intrinsic property independent of a relation of consideration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_44:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a unilateral causality in which one substance would simply transfer a force to another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-03","text":"It refuses that all possibles become real or that actual existence be the undifferentiated coexistence of their contents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_45:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-04","text":"It rejects an actualization without a principle of preference, sufficient reason, or fittingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_46:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:GNX-05","text":"It delimits the real against every self-sufficiency: no event and no World suffices unto itself as an explanatory principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, the model of a real composed of self-sufficient and causally closed units must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:DBN-02","text":"The system disqualifies a flat ontology in which possibility, perfection, and actuality would have the same status.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:DBN-03","text":"It cannot admit a first decision without reason, for the uniqueness of actuality would then become an ultimate and inexplicable fact.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:DBN-04","text":"It cannot separate the hierarchy of possibles from the fittingness that renders it operative; a selection without criterion would destroy the logic of the system.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSA-01","text":"The structuring absence is that of a non-relational foundation, absolutely brute and external to every comparison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_46:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSA-02","text":"The inadmissible possibility is that of a world in which all possibles would possess an equal and simultaneously realized claim.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_46:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSA-03","text":"The system circumvents the possibility of an actuality that would be merely a choice without an architecture of preference, without degree, and without fittingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_46:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSA-04","text":"What gives the whole its force is the impossibility of an immediate passage from the possible to the real: every actualization must pass through a comparative structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-01","text":"The coordination of substances and the selection of Worlds are two regimes of the same operation: converting a multiplicity of terms into order through the localization or hierarchization of reasons.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-03","CL_UCIC_18:GA-05","CL_UCIC_18:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_44:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-02","text":"The explanatory asymmetry among substances reappears at the scale of Worlds as asymmetry of perfection and of claim to existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-06","CL_UCIC_18:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_44:D2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-03","text":"Action and actuality are reclassified in parallel: the former is no longer an absolute power, the latter is no longer a brute property; both result from a determining relation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-02","CL_UCIC_18:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_44:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_45:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-04","text":"The reason that explains an event in a substance provides the functional model of the sufficient reason that explains the preference for a universe.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-05","CL_UCIC_18:GA-01","CH_UCIC_P_44:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_45:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:XD-05","text":"Mutuality and hierarchy are not contradictory: the former describes the reciprocity of the field, the latter distributes explanatory functions and degrees of realization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-06","CL_UCIC_18:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_44:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-01","text":"Ontology is transformed into a system of relational selection: to be real means to occupy a determined position in an order of reasons, correspondences, and degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-02","text":"Causality and creation cease to be two separate problems: they become two scales of the same logic of distributed intelligibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_45:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-03","text":"The possible is no longer a neutral reservoir and the actual is no longer a primary datum; both are the poles of an operation of ranking and actualization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-04","text":"Necessity does not bear upon a fixed identity, but upon the constraint to produce a determination proportionate to the available reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_45:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:BSD-05","text":"The effective order retains within itself the active trace of unrealized alternatives: the exclusion of possibles does not abolish their function of contrast and measure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-01","text":"Plurality produces the requirement of a reason; reason produces a comparison; comparison produces a selection; selection reconstitutes a relational order that relaunches the question of determination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_45:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-02","text":"Mutuality generates explanatory asymmetry, which requires accommodation; accommodation then brings mutuality back under a structured form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-03","text":"The negation of brute fact compels the introduction of sufficient reason, which in turn forbids every indifferent or criterionless selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-04","text":"Fittingness is the conceptual attractor toward which accommodation, sufficient reason, graded perfection, and proportionate actualization converge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A7","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:RLE-05","text":"The local point of consideration becomes a phase change when it is generalized into a point of comparison among possible Worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B01","text":"A plurality of substances and Worlds is posited as the initial field of distinct possibilities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A2","CH_UCIC_P_46:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B02","text":"Comparison renders visible correlative reasons, explanatory functions, and degrees of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A4","CH_UCIC_P_46:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B03","text":"Correlative reasons impose an accommodation; degrees of perfection order competing claims to existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B04","text":"Accommodation and fittingness convert multiplicity into relative determination, then into selection of an actual order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B05","text":"The selected order reintroduces a plurality of relations in which each term can be simultaneously a source of explanation and an object of explanation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B06","text":"The mechanism closes by excluding every absolute identity, every flat symmetry, and every actuality without reason, while retaining the possible as a horizon of comparison.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_45:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AFM-B01","text":"Mutuality of relations → comparative localization of reasons → reciprocal accommodation → requirement of a sufficient reason → hierarchization by fittingness and perfection → selection of an actual universe → re-entry into a network of mutually determined events.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_45:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:AFM-B02","text":"Rejection of absolute statuses → relationalization of functions → transformation of the possible into a graded claim → selective actualization → global architecture of explanatory correspondences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-01","text":"The possible/existent opposition is reconfigured into a hierarchized continuum of claims, fittingnesses, and degrees of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-02","text":"The agent-patient opposition is reclassified as a relative distribution of explanatory functions within a reciprocal network.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-03","text":"Intercreaturely causality and cosmological selection appear as two manifestations of one and the same cartography of reasons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_45:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-04","text":"Divinity is functionally reclassified: it is not merely cause or choice, but a principle of comparison, accommodation, and ordered selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_45:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MME-05","text":"The strategic terrain of analysis shifts from the search for a first agent toward the identification of the relations that render a determination intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_45:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B01","text":"**Surface level** — Substances act upon and undergo one another mutually, while several Worlds are possible and only one becomes actual.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B02","text":"**Structural level** — Positions, events, and Worlds are organized through the localization of reasons, comparison of terms, and hierarchization of degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B03","text":"**Metastrategic level** — Analysis replaces questions of absolute identity with questions of relation, explanatory function, preference, and fittingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B04","text":"**Ontological / Temporal level** — The possible logically precedes the actual, and actuality is produced as determined selection rather than as an unconditioned beginning.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_46:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B05","text":"**Methodological / Performative level** — The argumentative form accomplishes what it asserts: it begins from an undifferentiated plurality, introduces negative distinctions, then reconstructs an order through reasons and proportions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FL-01","text":"The mutuality of relations among creatures remains in tension with the asymmetry of explanatory reason: the reciprocity of the field does not produce equality of functions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A1","CH_UCIC_P_44:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FL-02","text":"The choice among several Worlds appears contingent, yet it is simultaneously determined by a sufficient reason; this tension sustains the difference between contingency and arbitrariness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:D4","CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:FL-03","text":"The right of each possible to claim existence does not guarantee its actualization, leaving open the exact relation between ontological merit and realization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A5","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MP-01","text":"The concept of action mutates when it ceases to designate an intrinsic power and becomes a function relative to the localization of reason.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:A5","CH_UCIC_P_44:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MP-02","text":"The concept of possibility mutates when it becomes a graded claim to existence, measured by perfection and fittingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_46:A6","CH_UCIC_P_46:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MP-03","text":"The concept of accommodation mutates when it passes from the coordination of substances to the cosmological operator of selection of Worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_46:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a comparative machine: it transforms a plurality of terms into order through the distribution of reasons, functions, and degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_46:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:HSI-02","text":"Every substance or World is a relational node rather than an autonomous center; its status depends on what it explains, receives, contains, or claims to realize.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_46:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system is primarily logical: the possible precedes the actual as a space of comparison, then actuality results from a proportionate selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_46:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:HSI-04","text":"Navigation in this reality does not consist in leaving the network, but in reclassifying positions according to the reasons that determine them and the degrees they encompass.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_46:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction is sufficient if it retains four operators: plurality of possibles, comparison of terms, sufficient reason, and proportionate actualization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B02","text":"Coherence depends on maintaining the two scales: the active or passive function remains local, while sufficient reason and fittingness produce the architecture of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B03","text":"Residual indetermination concerns the exact content of reasons, the mechanism of divine comparison, the measure of perfection, and the passage from the right to existence to effective existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B04","text":"Compression remains faithful to the real movement if it preserves the tension between reciprocity and asymmetry, as well as the passage from relational mutuality to metaphysical selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_44:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B05","text":"Any reconstruction that removed the negation of brute fact, the scale of degrees, or the function of fittingness would reduce the system to a mere theory of relation and miss its selective closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_45:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_46:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_18@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_18:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 52–54","context":"Proposition 52 · Proposition 53 · Proposition 54"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 55–57","order":19,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_47","CH_UCIC_P_48","CH_UCIC_P_49"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_19@R001","sha256":"0a7585cdc80a1f2cc428a32ccf91af5ac02db8c45c68df0caf0c32ed21364560","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-01","text":"L’existence du meilleur exige une cause intelligible, différenciée et non arbitraire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-02","text":"La causalité divine est recadrée comme l’articulation de trois fonctions : connaître, préférer et produire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_47:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-03","text":"Cette différenciation causale fournit le modèle d’un réel dont l’unité ne supprime pas la pluralité des modes d’expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-04","text":"La substance simple cesse d’être une unité isolée et devient un site relationnel exprimant la totalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","CH_UCIC_P_48:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-05","text":"L’expression universelle transforme le rapport partie-totalité en principe constitutif de l’individualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A4","CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-06","text":"La multiplicité des substances est ensuite convertie en pluralité de perspectives sur un univers unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-07","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et mutationnel : une distinction interne de la cause devient une distribution ontologique de l’expression, puis une différenciation perspectivale du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-08","text":"La clôture produite n’est pas une réduction de la multiplicité, mais sa réinscription dans une unité commune qui ne peut être saisie depuis un point de vue extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Le meilleur constitue le contenu normatif de la causalité examinée et son terme d’effectuation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La causalité opérante distingue la connaissance, la préférence et la production sans les séparer dans le résultat final.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] La sagesse fournit l’intelligibilité, la bonté la sélection axiologique et la puissance l’effectivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Les choses créées sont liées par une accommodation réciproque qui interdit de penser les substances comme des unités autosuffisantes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","CH_UCIC_P_48:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Chaque substance simple entretient un rapport structurel à toutes les autres substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] L’expression de la totalité par chaque substance est vivante et perpétuelle, non occasionnelle ni inerte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] L’individualité passe du statut d’unité séparée à celui de position expressive dans un réseau universel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_48:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] L’univers n’est pas seulement une totalité commune : il est produit comme totalité distribuée dans ses expressions singulières.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Un même réel peut apparaître différemment selon le point de vue sans devenir plusieurs réalités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] La multiplicité des substances devient une multiplicité de perspectives, tandis que l’unité demeure le référent commun.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D1","CH_UCIC_P_49:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] La pluralité phénoménale est maintenue au niveau des expressions et neutralisée comme fragmentation ontologique du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D4","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] L’unité différenciée constitue l’architecture minimale qui relie causalité, substance, expression et perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-01","text":"La distinction fonctionnelle entre les facultés divines revient à un niveau supérieur comme distinction entre modes d’expression, et non comme séparation de substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-02","text":"Le meilleur migre d’un objet produit par la causalité divine vers un attracteur général d’intelligibilité et d’ordre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-03","text":"La fonction de production se transforme en fonction d’expression : ce qui est d’abord actualisé est ensuite présent dans chaque position singulière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A4","CH_UCIC_P_48:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-04","text":"La relation passe d’une coordination interne de la cause à une accommodation universelle entre substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_48:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-05","text":"Le miroir vivant est recodé en perspective : la totalité n’est plus seulement reflétée, elle est différenciée selon une position.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-06","text":"L’unité persiste, mais sa fonction change : unité de la causalité au premier niveau, unité de l’univers exprimé au niveau terminal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-07","text":"La multiplicité cesse d’être un problème à résoudre et devient le mécanisme par lequel l’unité se manifeste sans se fragmenter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-08","text":"La causalité divine comme opération explicite disparaît après avoir fourni la matrice structurale de l’ordre distribué et perspectival.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-01","text":"La triade sagesse-bonté-puissance reste locale lorsqu’elle décrit directement les facultés divines et leur ordre d’action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-02","text":"Le miroir vivant reste local lorsqu’il désigne la substance simple comme image perpétuelle de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-03","text":"L’analogie de la ville observée selon plusieurs côtés reste locale comme dispositif d’exposition, mais change d’échelle lorsqu’elle devient théorie de la perspective monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-04","text":"Le niveau courant relie les trois machines inférieures par une même forme : une unité est rendue effective par différenciation interne, distribuée puis perspectivale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-05","text":"Le passage de la causalité à l’expression constitue la première transition majeure : l’ordre ne reste plus dans la cause, il se distribue dans ses effets.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-06","text":"Le passage de l’expression à la perspective constitue la seconde transition : l’unité distribuée devient unité différenciée selon des positions singulières.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-07","text":"Les modèles d’une puissance aveugle, d’une substance isolée et de mondes indépendants deviennent obsolètes à l’échelle du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une puissance non orientée puisse expliquer à elle seule l’existence du meilleur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une substance simple soit définie par l’isolement ou par l’absence de rapports universels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_48:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut qu’une expression de l’univers soit inerte, intermittente ou extérieure à la substance qui l’exprime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_48:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut qu’une différence de point de vue produise une différence de monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut que la multiplicité des substances équivaille à une fragmentation du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut une totalité extérieure à ses expressions et une perspective extérieure aux positions qui la constituent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-07","text":"Les limites du système sont ainsi définies par double répudiation : ni indifférenciation de la cause, ni pluralisation absolue du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, doit être faux le modèle d’une causalité réduite à la capacité d’agir sans intelligibilité ni sélection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_47:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-02","text":"Doit également être faux le modèle d’une individualité sans inscription dans une totalité exprimée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-03","text":"Doit être faux le modèle d’un univers qui existerait indépendamment de toute expression locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-04","text":"Doit être faux le relativisme perspectival qui convertirait chaque point de vue en totalité autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-05","text":"Doit être faux l’idéal d’une connaissance absolue située hors de toute perspective monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSA-01","text":"Le système contourne la possibilité d’un réel sans principe commun, sans la traiter comme une hypothèse symétriquement disponible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSA-02","text":"Il rend indisponible une extériorité pure qui pourrait connaître ou posséder l’univers sans être située dans une relation expressive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSA-03","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un écart entre unité et expression : aucune totalité ne subsiste sans être distribuée dans des perspectives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSA-04","text":"La possibilité ontologiquement inadmissible est celle d’un monde qui serait soit indifférencié, soit composé de totalités séparées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-01","text":"La différenciation interne de la cause et la différenciation externe des perspectives sont deux régimes d’une même production ordonnée de l’unité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-02","CL_UCIC_19:GA-09","CL_UCIC_19:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_47:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-02","text":"Ce qui est produit par une causalité différenciée devient ensuite présent comme totalité distribuée dans une pluralité de substances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-03","CL_UCIC_19:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-03","text":"La substance simple n’est ni un effet passif ni un sujet fermé : elle est le point où une totalité déjà ordonnée devient perspective singulière.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-05","CL_UCIC_19:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_48:D1","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-04","text":"L’unité du réel ne précède pas simplement la multiplicité ; elle est conservée par la multiplication réglée de ses expressions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-08","CL_UCIC_19:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_49:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-05","text":"La pluralité perspectivale ne peut devenir pluralité de mondes qu’en rompant simultanément l’expression universelle et le référent commun.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-06","CL_UCIC_19:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-06","text":"La continuité expressive et la singularité perspectivale produisent une tension constitutive : chaque substance exprime le tout sans pouvoir l’épuiser.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-06","CL_UCIC_19:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-07","text":"L’architecture transforme une théorie de la causalité en théorie de la commensurabilité : les perspectives diffèrent parce qu’elles expriment un même ordre.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-03","CL_UCIC_19:GA-09","CL_UCIC_19:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_47:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est requalifié comme unité distribuée : il n’existe pas hors de ses expressions, mais aucune expression locale ne le constitue seule.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-02","text":"La causalité n’est ni mécanique ni arbitraire ; elle est normative lorsqu’elle sélectionne le meilleur et expressive lorsqu’elle le rend présent dans la totalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-03","text":"Le statut du sujet se transforme : il devient une position locale de manifestation du tout plutôt qu’un observateur placé devant lui.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:D3","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-04","text":"Le temps reçoit deux régimes distincts : priorité logique de la connaissance sur la production et perpétuité non nécessairement temporelle de l’expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_48:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-05","text":"L’épistémologie devient intrinsèquement perspectivale : connaître le réel exige de rapporter chaque expression à l’unité qu’elle différencie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-06","text":"La méthode adéquate n’oppose plus totalité et point de vue ; elle reconstruit la totalité par la relation entre les points de vue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-07","text":"L’individuation devient une opération de localisation expressive : être singulier signifie occuper une position dans l’ordre universel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale est : meilleur intelligible → meilleur choisi → meilleur produit → totalité exprimée → perspectives différenciées → unité reconnue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-02","text":"La distinction initiale des facultés devient une machine générale de différenciation, puis revient comme distinction entre positions expressives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-03","text":"La boucle partie-totalité fonctionne ainsi : chaque substance exprime l’univers, et l’univers n’est accessible qu’à travers la pluralité de ces expressions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:D2","CH_UCIC_P_48:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-04","text":"La boucle unité-multiplicité convertit chaque menace de fragmentation en nouvelle forme de différenciation du même réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D4","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-05","text":"L’analogie du point de vue franchit un seuil lorsqu’elle cesse d’illustrer le réel et devient le principe ontologique de sa pluralisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-06","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est l’unité différenciée : toute distinction valide doit produire davantage de structure sans produire une réalité séparée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D3","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-07","text":"La négation prépare positivement le système en éliminant successivement l’arbitraire, l’isolement, l’inertie, le relativisme et l’extériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B01","text":"Différencier la cause en intelligibilité, préférence et effectuation afin d’empêcher que l’existence du meilleur soit attribuée à une force indéterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B02","text":"Intégrer ces fonctions dans une chaîne unique où la connaissance oriente le choix et où le choix reçoit une effectivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B03","text":"Distribuer l’ordre ainsi produit dans une multiplicité de substances liées et accommodées les unes aux autres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B04","text":"Convertir chaque substance en opérateur d’expression de la totalité plutôt qu’en unité autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B05","text":"Perspectiviser cette expression : la totalité devient différente selon les positions sans cesser d’être une.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B06","text":"Recomposer la multiplicité des perspectives comme manifestation distribuée d’un seul univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B07","text":"Stabiliser la reconstruction par exclusion de toute extériorité absolue, de toute substance isolée et de toute pluralité de mondes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B08","text":"Produire comme résultat une unité qui ne vaut qu’en tant qu’elle est différenciée, exprimée et perspectivement distribuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B01","text":"Existence du meilleur → exigence d’une cause intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B02","text":"Cause intelligible → différenciation de la connaissance, de la préférence et de la puissance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B03","text":"Causalité différenciée → ordre relationnel entre les choses créées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_48:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B04","text":"Ordre relationnel → expression de la totalité par chaque substance simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A3","CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B05","text":"Expression de la totalité → pluralité de perspectives situées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B06","text":"Pluralité des perspectives → reclassification de la multiplicité comme différenciation d’un seul réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B07","text":"Unité différenciée → clôture sans point de vue extérieur et sans dissolution de la multiplicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-01","text":"La causalité est reclassée comme architecture à plusieurs opérations plutôt que comme puissance homogène.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-02","text":"La substance est reclassée comme nœud d’expression de la totalité plutôt que comme atome ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-03","text":"La totalité devient cartographiable depuis une pluralité de positions sans qu’aucune carte locale n’en devienne la totalité absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-04","text":"L’opposition unité-multiplicité s’effondre et laisse place à la distinction entre référent commun et modes d’expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-05","text":"L’individualité est redéfinie par la relation à la totalité, non par la séparation à son égard.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-06","text":"La lecture adéquate doit suivre les migrations fonctionnelles d’un concept, notamment le passage de production à expression puis à perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-07","text":"Le terrain conceptuel ne permet plus de choisir entre unité et pluralité : il impose d’analyser leur co-production structurale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont le meilleur, les substances simples, leurs rapports et les perspectives monadiques sur l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Le mécanisme actif est une distribution ordonnée : distinction des fonctions, liaison universelle, expression totale et différenciation des points de vue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] L’argument neutralise les alternatives rivales en les reclassant comme formes incomplètes : force sans raison, unité sans différence, perspective sans référent commun.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est un mais différencié, et l’ordre de connaissance, de choix et de production est logique plutôt que nécessairement temporel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit son contenu en passant elle-même de la distinction à l’intégration, puis de la pluralité à l’unité structurée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-01","text":"[Tension] La priorité logique de la connaissance et la perpétuité de l’expression ne suffisent pas à établir un ordre temporel univoque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-02","text":"[Tension] L’unité de l’univers coexiste avec la formulation de perspectives comme « différents univers », ce qui exige une distinction stricte entre apparence et ontologie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-03","text":"[Tension] L’expression universelle est affirmée sans que soit déterminé le mécanisme précis par lequel une substance exprime toutes les autres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-04","text":"[Tension] Le miroir vivant oscille entre métaphore de représentation et description ontologique de l’activité substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-05","text":"[Tension] Le meilleur est à la fois objet connu, terme choisi et réalité produite ; son statut exact demeure sous-déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MP-01","text":"[Mutating] Le meilleur passe d’un contenu de causalité divine à un attracteur d’ordre pour l’architecture entière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MP-02","text":"[Mutating] La distinction des attributs divins devient une logique transposable de différenciation sans séparation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MP-03","text":"[Mutating] La substance simple passe du statut de miroir à celui de position perspectivale active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MP-04","text":"[Mutating] L’analogie urbaine franchit le seuil de l’illustration pour devenir une règle de construction ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine d’unification différentielle : elle produit l’ordre en distinguant ses fonctions, ses substances et ses perspectives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient un miroir vivant situé, c’est-à-dire une opération locale par laquelle la totalité se rend présente sans devenir transparente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système est double : succession logique des fonctions causales et continuité perpétuelle de l’expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_48:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée disponible n’est pas une sortie hors du système, mais une reconfiguration de la position depuis laquelle le même univers est exprimé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes suffisent à reconstruire la chaîne minimale : causalité différenciée → liaison universelle → expression totale → perspectives multiples → unité du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B02","text":"La compression conserve la mutation des fonctions : production, expression et perspective ne sont pas traitées comme des synonymes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B03","text":"La reconstruction reste indéterminée sur le mécanisme exact de l’expression universelle et sur le statut ontologique complet du meilleur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence dépend du maintien simultané de deux niveaux : pluralité réelle des substances et unité du monde exprimé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_49:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B05","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante à l’échelle du cluster parce qu’elle restitue le mouvement génératif, les exclusions structurantes, l’attracteur d’unité différenciée et les tensions non résolues.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195654872475Z_dbf06575","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 55–57","source_sha256":"0a7585cdc80a1f2cc428a32ccf91af5ac02db8c45c68df0caf0c32ed21364560","sha256":"735929d822907f6b36f33f9f8cb5dda77e29cef45d17f33c358eef46b9a1a21a","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:56:54.876842+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-01","text":"The existence of the best requires an intelligible, differentiated, and non-arbitrary cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-02","text":"Divine causality is reframed as the articulation of three functions: knowing, preferring, and producing.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_47:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-03","text":"This causal differentiation provides the model of a real whose unity does not abolish the plurality of modes of expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-04","text":"The simple substance ceases to be an isolated unity and becomes a relational site expressing the totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","CH_UCIC_P_48:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-05","text":"Universal expression transforms the part-whole relation into a constitutive principle of individuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A4","CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-06","text":"The multiplicity of substances is then converted into a plurality of perspectives on a single universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-07","text":"The movement is cumulative and mutational: an internal distinction of the cause becomes an ontological distribution of expression, then a perspectival differentiation of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AS-08","text":"The closure produced is not a reduction of multiplicity, but its reinscription within a common unity that cannot be grasped from an external point of view.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The best constitutes the normative content of the causality under examination and its term of actualization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Operative causality distinguishes knowledge, preference, and production without separating them in the final result.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Wisdom provides intelligibility, goodness axiological selection, and power effectiveness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A2","CH_UCIC_P_47:A3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Created things are connected by a reciprocal accommodation that precludes conceiving substances as self-sufficient unities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A1","CH_UCIC_P_48:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Each simple substance maintains a structural relation to all other substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The expression of the totality by each substance is living and perpetual, neither occasional nor inert.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Individuality passes from the status of separate unity to that of expressive position in a universal network.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_48:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] The universe is not merely a common totality: it is produced as a totality distributed in its singular expressions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] One and the same real can appear differently according to the point of view without becoming several realities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] The multiplicity of substances becomes a multiplicity of perspectives, while unity remains the common referent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D1","CH_UCIC_P_49:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Phenomenal plurality is maintained at the level of expressions and neutralized as ontological fragmentation of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D4","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Differentiated unity constitutes the minimal architecture connecting causality, substance, expression, and perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-01","text":"The functional distinction among the divine faculties recurs at a higher level as a distinction among modes of expression, and not as a separation of substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-02","text":"The best migrates from an object produced by divine causality to a general attractor of intelligibility and order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-03","text":"The function of production is transformed into a function of expression: what is initially actualized is subsequently present in each singular position.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A4","CH_UCIC_P_48:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-04","text":"The relation passes from an internal coordination of the cause to a universal accommodation among substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_48:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-05","text":"The living mirror is recoded as perspective: the totality is no longer merely reflected; it is differentiated according to a position.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-06","text":"Unity persists, but its function changes: unity of causality at the first level, unity of the expressed universe at the terminal level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-07","text":"Multiplicity ceases to be a problem to be solved and becomes the mechanism by which unity manifests itself without fragmenting.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RMD-08","text":"Divine causality as an explicit operation disappears after having supplied the structural matrix of distributed and perspectival order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-01","text":"The wisdom-goodness-power triad remains local when it directly describes the divine faculties and their order of action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-02","text":"The living mirror remains local when it designates the simple substance as a perpetual image of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-03","text":"The analogy of the city observed from several sides remains local as a device of exposition, but changes scale when it becomes a theory of monadic perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-04","text":"The current level connects the three lower machines through one and the same form: a unity is made effective through internal, distributed, then perspectival differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-05","text":"The passage from causality to expression constitutes the first major transition: order no longer remains in the cause; it is distributed in its effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-06","text":"The passage from expression to perspective constitutes the second transition: distributed unity becomes unity differentiated according to singular positions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:CGD-07","text":"The models of blind power, isolated substance, and independent worlds become obsolete at the scale of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that unoriented power could by itself explain the existence of the best.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that a simple substance be defined by isolation or by the absence of universal relations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_48:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that an expression of the universe be inert, intermittent, or external to the substance expressing it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_48:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that a difference of point of view produce a difference of world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the possibility that the multiplicity of substances amount to a fragmentation of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-06","text":"It excludes a totality external to its expressions and a perspective external to the positions constituting it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:GNX-07","text":"The limits of the system are thus defined by a double repudiation: neither indifferentiation of the cause nor absolute pluralization of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, the model of a causality reduced to the capacity to act without intelligibility or selection must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_47:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-02","text":"The model of an individuality without inscription within an expressed totality must likewise be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-03","text":"The model of a universe that would exist independently of every local expression must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-04","text":"The perspectival relativism that would convert each point of view into an autonomous totality must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:DBN-05","text":"The ideal of an absolute knowledge situated outside every monadic perspective must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSA-01","text":"The system bypasses the possibility of a real without a common principle, without treating it as a symmetrically available hypothesis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSA-02","text":"It renders unavailable a pure exteriority that could know or possess the universe without being situated in an expressive relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSA-03","text":"The structuring absence is that of a gap between unity and expression: no totality subsists without being distributed in perspectives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSA-04","text":"The ontologically inadmissible possibility is that of a world that would be either undifferentiated or composed of separate totalities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-01","text":"The internal differentiation of the cause and the external differentiation of perspectives are two regimes of one and the same ordered production of unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-02","CL_UCIC_19:GA-09","CL_UCIC_19:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_47:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-02","text":"What is produced by a differentiated causality subsequently becomes present as a totality distributed in a plurality of substances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-03","CL_UCIC_19:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-03","text":"The simple substance is neither a passive effect nor a closed subject: it is the point at which an already ordered totality becomes singular perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-05","CL_UCIC_19:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_48:D1","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-04","text":"The unity of the real does not simply precede multiplicity; it is preserved through the regulated multiplication of its expressions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-08","CL_UCIC_19:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_49:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-05","text":"Perspectival plurality can become a plurality of worlds only by simultaneously breaking universal expression and the common referent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-06","CL_UCIC_19:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-06","text":"Expressive continuity and perspectival singularity produce a constitutive tension: each substance expresses the whole without being able to exhaust it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-06","CL_UCIC_19:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_48:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:XD-07","text":"The architecture transforms a theory of causality into a theory of commensurability: perspectives differ because they express one and the same order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-03","CL_UCIC_19:GA-09","CL_UCIC_19:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_47:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-01","text":"The real is requalified as distributed unity: it does not exist outside its expressions, but no local expression alone constitutes it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-02","text":"Causality is neither mechanical nor arbitrary; it is normative when it selects the best and expressive when it renders it present in the totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_48:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-03","text":"The status of the subject is transformed: it becomes a local position of manifestation of the whole rather than an observer placed before it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:D3","CH_UCIC_P_49:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-04","text":"Time receives two distinct regimes: the logical priority of knowledge over production and the not necessarily temporal perpetuity of expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_48:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-05","text":"Epistemology becomes intrinsically perspectival: knowing the real requires relating each expression to the unity it differentiates.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-06","text":"The adequate method no longer opposes totality and point of view; it reconstructs totality through the relation among points of view.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:BSD-07","text":"Individuation becomes an operation of expressive localization: to be singular means to occupy a position in the universal order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop is: intelligible best → chosen best → produced best → expressed totality → differentiated perspectives → recognized unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-02","text":"The initial distinction of the faculties becomes a general machine of differentiation, then returns as a distinction among expressive positions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-03","text":"The part-whole loop thus functions: each substance expresses the universe, and the universe is accessible only through the plurality of these expressions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:D2","CH_UCIC_P_48:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-04","text":"The unity-multiplicity loop converts every threat of fragmentation into a new form of differentiation of the same real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D4","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-05","text":"The analogy of the point of view crosses a threshold when it ceases to illustrate the real and becomes the ontological principle of its pluralization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-06","text":"The conceptual attractor is differentiated unity: every valid distinction must produce more structure without producing a separate reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:D3","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:RLE-07","text":"Negation positively prepares the system by successively eliminating arbitrariness, isolation, inertia, relativism, and exteriority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B01","text":"Differentiate the cause into intelligibility, preference, and actualization in order to prevent the existence of the best from being attributed to an indeterminate force.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B02","text":"Integrate these functions into a single chain in which knowledge guides choice and choice receives effectiveness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B03","text":"Distribute the order thus produced across a multiplicity of substances connected and accommodated to one another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B04","text":"Convert each substance into an operator of expression of the totality rather than into an autonomous unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B05","text":"Perspectivize this expression: the totality becomes different according to positions without ceasing to be one.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B06","text":"Recompose the multiplicity of perspectives as the distributed manifestation of a single universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B07","text":"Stabilize the reconstruction by excluding every absolute exteriority, every isolated substance, and every plurality of worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B08","text":"Produce as a result a unity that holds only insofar as it is differentiated, expressed, and perspectivally distributed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B01","text":"Existence of the best → requirement of an intelligible cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B02","text":"Intelligible cause → differentiation of knowledge, preference, and power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B03","text":"Differentiated causality → relational order among created things.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_48:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B04","text":"Relational order → expression of the totality by each simple substance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A3","CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B05","text":"Expression of the totality → plurality of situated perspectives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B06","text":"Plurality of perspectives → reclassification of multiplicity as differentiation of a single real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B07","text":"Differentiated unity → closure without an external point of view and without dissolution of multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-01","text":"Causality is reclassified as an architecture involving several operations rather than as homogeneous power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-02","text":"Substance is reclassified as a node of expression of the totality rather than as an ontological atom.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-03","text":"The totality becomes mappable from a plurality of positions without any local map becoming its absolute totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-04","text":"The unity-multiplicity opposition collapses and gives way to the distinction between common referent and modes of expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-05","text":"Individuality is redefined by its relation to the totality, not by separation from it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-06","text":"An adequate reading must follow the functional migrations of a concept, notably the passage from production to expression and then to perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MME-07","text":"The conceptual terrain no longer allows a choice between unity and plurality: it requires analyzing their structural co-production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are the best, simple substances, their relations, and monadic perspectives on the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","CH_UCIC_P_49:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] The active mechanism is an ordered distribution: distinction of functions, universal connection, total expression, and differentiation of points of view.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_48:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The argument neutralizes rival alternatives by reclassifying them as incomplete forms: force without reason, unity without difference, perspective without common referent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The real is one but differentiated, and the order of knowledge, choice, and production is logical rather than necessarily temporal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form accomplishes its content by itself passing from distinction to integration, then from plurality to structured unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_49:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-01","text":"[Tension] The logical priority of knowledge and the perpetuity of expression are insufficient to establish a univocal temporal order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-02","text":"[Tension] The unity of the universe coexists with the formulation of perspectives as « différents univers », which requires a strict distinction between appearance and ontology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-03","text":"[Tension] Universal expression is affirmed without determining the precise mechanism by which one substance expresses all the others.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-04","text":"[Tension] The living mirror oscillates between a metaphor of representation and an ontological description of substantial activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:FL-05","text":"[Tension] The best is at once a known object, a chosen term, and a produced reality; its exact status remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_47:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MP-01","text":"[Mutating] The best passes from a content of divine causality to an attractor of order for the entire architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:A1","CH_UCIC_P_47:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MP-02","text":"[Mutating] The distinction among divine attributes becomes a transposable logic of differentiation without separation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MP-03","text":"[Mutating] The simple substance passes from the status of mirror to that of active perspectival position.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A6","CH_UCIC_P_49:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MP-04","text":"[Mutating] The urban analogy crosses the threshold of illustration to become a rule of ontological construction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_49:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a machine of differential unification: it produces order by distinguishing its functions, its substances, and its perspectives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a situated living mirror, that is, a local operation through which the totality renders itself present without becoming transparent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:A5","CH_UCIC_P_49:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system is double: logical succession of causal functions and perpetual continuity of expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_48:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:HSI-04","text":"The only available escape is not an exit outside the system, but a reconfiguration of the position from which the same universe is expressed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:A4","CH_UCIC_P_49:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms suffice to reconstruct the minimal chain: differentiated causality → universal connection → total expression → multiple perspectives → unity of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B02","text":"The compression preserves the mutation of functions: production, expression, and perspective are not treated as synonyms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_48:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_49:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction remains indeterminate concerning the exact mechanism of universal expression and the complete ontological status of the best.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_48:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence depends on the simultaneous maintenance of two levels: real plurality of substances and unity of the expressed world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_49:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_49:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient at the scale of the cluster because it restores the generative movement, the structuring exclusions, the attractor of differentiated unity, and the unresolved tensions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_47:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_49:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_19@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_19:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 55–57","context":"Proposition 55 · Proposition 56 · Proposition 57"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 58–60","order":20,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_50","CH_UCIC_P_51","CH_UCIC_P_52"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_20@R001","sha256":"17960f618db69816d14ec8d90d5f038f31043c163e9342e5980b6e4592b0f9a8","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-01","text":"Le problème central consiste à produire une pluralité maximale sans dissoudre l’organisation qui la rend intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-02","text":"Le système recadre variété et ordre comme deux dimensions conjointes d’une même opération de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-03","text":"Cette opération se déplace d’une optimisation locale vers une architecture relationnelle où chaque élément exprime le tout selon un degré déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-04","text":"L’harmonie universelle transforme la pluralité des substances en réseau d’expressions réciproques plutôt qu’en juxtaposition d’unités isolées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-05","text":"La monade réalise cette architecture sous une forme perspectivale : elle représente l’univers entier, mais n’en distingue localement qu’une faible partie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-06","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et récursif : maximisation, harmonisation, universalisation de la représentation, différenciation des degrés, puis clôture par les limites du possible et de la divinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La variété et l’ordre ne sont porteurs qu’à condition d’être maximisés conjointement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A3","CL_UCIC_20:SP-01","CL_UCIC_20:SP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La perfection est une propriété de configuration totale, non une qualité isolée d’un seul élément ou d’une seule grandeur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:D2","CL_UCIC_20:SP-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] L’ordre universel se réalise comme expression réciproque des substances plutôt que comme arrangement externe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","CL_UCIC_20:SP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] La pluralité n’est pas un dehors de l’ordre : elle constitue le médium par lequel l’ordre devient intégral.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Chaque monade représente l’univers entier, même lorsque cette représentation demeure confuse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CL_UCIC_20:SP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] La finitude porte sur le degré de distinction de la connaissance, non sur l’étendue de l’objet représenté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Les monades se différencient par des degrés de perception distincte à l’intérieur d’une orientation commune vers le tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] La limite du possible borne simultanément la variété, l’ordre et la perfection accessibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A6","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] La distinction intégrale de toutes les perceptions abolirait la différence entre monade et divinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A12","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Le système converge vers une totalité interne où chaque perspective contient le tout sans devenir transparente au tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-01","text":"La maximisation revient d’abord comme combinaison de variété et d’ordre, puis comme architecture universelle d’expressions réciproques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-02","text":"L’ordre conserve son identité fonctionnelle, mais il cesse d’être une contrainte appliquée à la pluralité et devient le produit interne de ses rapports.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-03","text":"L’harmonie migre du registre théologique vers une ontologie relationnelle où toute substance est liée à toutes les autres par expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:D1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-04","text":"La totalité représentée ne signifie plus transparence totale : elle se transforme en champ universel modulé par des degrés de clarté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:D2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-05","text":"La limitation se déplace de l’objet connu vers la modification de la connaissance, recodant la finitude comme modulation épistémique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AS5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-06","text":"La perfection terminale n’est pas une transparence absolue, mais une différenciation maximale compatible avec l’unité du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-01","text":"La recherche d’un moyen produisant simultanément variété et ordre reste locale tant qu’elle ne devient pas une théorie de la totalité relationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-02","text":"Le niveau courant relie la perfection configurationnelle, l’harmonie universelle et la représentation monadique dans une seule structure de co-production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-03","text":"La proposition locale selon laquelle chaque monade représente l’univers devient ici le principe de différenciation de toute la pluralité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-04","text":"L’objection théologique locale est recodée en règle méthodologique générale : une apparence d’excès ne vaut pas preuve d’impossibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:D4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-05","text":"Le modèle d’une distribution territoriale du réel devient obsolète au niveau courant, remplacé par une distribution graduelle de la clarté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ME3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-01","text":"Le système rejette une variété qui serait dispersion et un ordre qui serait réduction de la pluralité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:NX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une objection fondée sur l’excès apparent puisse interrompre la construction sans démonstration d’impossibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:NX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-03","text":"Il refuse une monade limitée à une région indépendante du réel ou extérieure à l’univers qu’elle représente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:NX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-04","text":"Il sépare représenter tout, connaître distinctement tout et être divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut la perfection fondée sur une grandeur unique, qu’il s’agisse de la variété, de l’ordre ou de la clarté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:NX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que la pluralité ne soit jamais une extériorité absolue à l’unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:DBN-02","text":"Il faut que la totalité puisse être représentée sans devenir entièrement distincte, faute de quoi la hiérarchie entre créature et Dieu s’effondrerait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX6","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie silencieusement tout modèle où la finitude proviendrait d’un défaut de l’objet plutôt que d’un degré de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:DBN-04","text":"Il ne peut admettre un conflit irréductible entre variété maximale et ordre maximal sans perdre son principe de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSA-01","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un point de vue extérieur à l’univers : toute perspective est déjà prise dans le tout qu’elle représente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité indisponible est une transparence intégrale où chaque perspective connaîtrait distinctement chaque détail sans devenir divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSA-03","text":"Le système contourne la question d’un critère formel de mesure de la variété, de l’ordre et de leur compatibilité maximale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-01","text":"La perfection devient une coordination de maxima parce que la pluralité n’est pleinement productive qu’inscrite dans un ordre qui ne la supprime pas.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CH_UCIC_P_50:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-02","text":"L’harmonie universelle fournit à la pluralité une forme d’unité interne : les substances ne sont pas ordonnées depuis l’extérieur, elles s’expriment mutuellement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-03","text":"La structure monadique généralise la logique de la perfection : le tout est conservé dans chaque unité, tandis que la différence se déplace vers le degré de clarté.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_52:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-04","text":"La défense de l’harmonie et la théorie des monades reposent sur une même stratégie : maintenir l’intégralité du système en localisant la limite dans le degré plutôt que dans l’objet.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_52:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-05","text":"La perfection est relationnelle à l’échelle globale parce qu’aucune unité ne possède un domaine ontologique exclusif ni une position extérieure à la totalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-06","text":"La limite du possible fonctionne à la fois comme borne métaphysique et comme point non résolu du système, puisque sa constitution n’est pas formalisée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est reconfiguré comme totalité relationnelle interne : chaque unité porte le tout, mais aucune unité ne l’épuise par une transparence intégrale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-02","text":"Le sujet fini n’est plus une entité séparée du réel, mais une modulation locale d’un champ universel qu’il exprime confusément.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-03","text":"L’ordre cesse d’être une loi imposée à une matière distincte : il devient l’effet distribué de rapports d’expression réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-04","text":"La méthode du système transforme l’objection en test de contradiction démontrée, substituant la preuve d’impossibilité au sentiment de démesure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:ME3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-05","text":"La perfection ne désigne pas l’abolition des différences, mais leur intégration maximale dans une totalité ordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:ME1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-06","text":"La causalité générative du système est distribuée : l’unité du tout produit les différences locales, et les différences locales rendent manifeste l’unité du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale suit la séquence variété maximale → ordre maximal → perfection → borne du possible, puis reconduit la mesure de la variété et de l’ordre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AF1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-02","text":"La boucle apologétique transforme l’excès apparent en demande de preuve d’impossibilité, puis utilise l’absence de cette preuve pour préserver l’hypothèse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-03","text":"La boucle monadique part de la représentation du tout, produit la confusion du détail, localise la distinction, puis reconduit chaque monade vers le tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AF1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-04","text":"La répétition de la totalité sous des degrés différents constitue un changement de phase : l’identité du tout devient le moteur de la différence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est une totalité maximale mais non transparente, où l’intégration augmente avec la différenciation sans atteindre l’égalité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A12","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B01","text":"Poser une pluralité maximale sans la laisser devenir dispersion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B02","text":"Ajouter à cette pluralité un ordre maximal conçu comme condition de sa perfection plutôt que comme sa négation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B03","text":"Transformer l’ordre en harmonie universelle par l’expression réciproque de toutes les substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B04","text":"Inscrire l’univers entier dans chaque monade, puis distribuer la différence selon les degrés de perception distincte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B05","text":"Déplacer toute limitation de l’objet vers la clarté de sa connaissance afin de maintenir l’universalité représentative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B06","text":"Fermer le système par deux seuils : le possible borne la perfection, et la transparence intégrale est réservée à Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B07","text":"La forme générale est donc : pluralité maximale → ordre immanent → expression universelle → perception graduée → totalité non transparente → perfection bornée par le possible et la divinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:AFM-B01","text":"Problème de la pluralité organisée → recadrage de variété et d’ordre comme maxima conjoints → perfection configurationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:AFM-B02","text":"Perfection configurationnelle → harmonie universelle → expression réciproque des substances → neutralisation de l’objection par déplacement vers la preuve d’impossibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:AFM-B03","text":"Ordre universel → représentation du tout dans chaque monade → distinction locale et graduée → exclusion de la transparence divine → totalité relationnelle non extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-01","text":"La variété et l’ordre sont reclassés comme dimensions co-productives d’une seule architecture de perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:ME1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-02","text":"La relation entre substances devient plus fondamentale que leur séparation : l’individu est cartographié comme nœud d’expression du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:ME1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-03","text":"L’opposition entre totalité et finitude s’effondre : une unité finie peut représenter le tout sans le distinguer intégralement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ME2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-04","text":"Les différences entre monades sont redessinées comme gradients de clarté et non comme frontières entre territoires ontologiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ME3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-05","text":"La divinité devient le seuil cartographique de la perception intégralement distincte, non un simple degré supérieur parmi les autres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ME5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level : le système traite la production d’une pluralité ordonnée et la représentation de l’univers par chaque monade.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level : la cohérence repose sur une distribution de l’expression universelle et des degrés de perception distincte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level : le système remplace le choix entre pluralité et ordre par la coordination de conditions qui se renforcent mutuellement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level : chaque monade est une perspective interne au tout, mais aucune temporalité générative autonome n’est explicitement constituée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level : l’argument accomplit son principe en transformant les limites apparentes en degrés internes d’une architecture plus vaste.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FL-01","text":"La compatibilité entre variété maximale et ordre maximal est constitutive du système, mais elle est affirmée plus qu’elle n’est démontrée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FL-02","text":"L’hypothèse d’une harmonie démontrée repose localement sur l’absence de preuve d’impossibilité, créant un décalage entre statut revendiqué et fondement exposé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FL-03","text":"L’universalité de la représentation entre en tension productive avec la limitation nécessaire de la perception distincte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MP-01","text":"Le concept d’ordre mute lorsqu’il passe d’une fin coordonnée à une relation immanente entre substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MP-02","text":"La finitude mute d’une limitation possible de l’objet en modulation graduelle de la connaissance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MP-03","text":"La limite divine mute d’une borne extérieure en fonction terminale qui empêche la perception intégrale de devenir identité avec Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:D5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine d’expression récursive : chaque unité contient le schème du tout et le tout se manifeste par la différenciation des unités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une perspective finie sans dehors, définie par la modulation locale d’une représentation universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas l’opérateur principal de la machine ; la dynamique décisive est modale et graduelle, organisée par le possible et les degrés de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A6","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:HSI-04","text":"Aucune échappée ne consiste à sortir du tout : la seule marge consiste à modifier le degré de distinction depuis lequel le tout est exprimé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B01","text":"Un noyau suffisant comprend quatre opérations : maximiser variété et ordre, convertir leur rapport en harmonie, inscrire le tout dans chaque monade et différencier la clarté sans réduire l’objet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction reste cohérente seulement si la représentation universelle n’est pas assimilée à une connaissance également distincte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B03","text":"Le point de force est la transformation de la totalité en principe de différenciation plutôt qu’en abolition des différences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination principale concerne le critère de mesure des maxima et la démonstration effective de leur compatibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B05","text":"La réduction préserve le mouvement génératif, mais elle ne restitue pas la preuve antérieure invoquée pour soutenir l’harmonie universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT6","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B06","text":"L’architecture minimale est donc suffisante pour reconstruire le cluster, tandis que ses zones de force dépendent d’une compatibilité postulée et ses zones de faille d’une formalisation incomplète du possible, de la mesure et de la preuve.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195724663964Z_b9b888d9","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 58–60","source_sha256":"17960f618db69816d14ec8d90d5f038f31043c163e9342e5980b6e4592b0f9a8","sha256":"9dcdb84c095d675b0d55c387109f4f748e6526f62147b7e518a32d7445d12ffa","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:57:24.668036+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-01","text":"The central problem consists in producing a maximal plurality without dissolving the organization that renders it intelligible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-02","text":"The system reframes variety and order as two conjoint dimensions of one and the same operation of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-03","text":"This operation shifts from local optimization toward a relational architecture in which each element expresses the whole according to a determinate degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-04","text":"Universal harmony transforms the plurality of substances into a network of reciprocal expressions rather than a juxtaposition of isolated units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-05","text":"The monad realizes this architecture in a perspectival form: it represents the entire universe, but distinguishes only a small part of it locally.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:SP-06","text":"The movement is cumulative and recursive: maximization, harmonization, universalization of representation, differentiation of degrees, then closure through the limits of the possible and of divinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Variety and order are productive only on condition that they are jointly maximized.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A3","CL_UCIC_20:SP-01","CL_UCIC_20:SP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Perfection is a property of total configuration, not an isolated quality of a single element or a single magnitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:D2","CL_UCIC_20:SP-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Universal order is realized as reciprocal expression of substances rather than as external arrangement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A2","CL_UCIC_20:SP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Plurality is not an outside of order: it constitutes the medium through which order becomes integral.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Each monad represents the entire universe, even when this representation remains confused.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5","CL_UCIC_20:SP-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Finitude concerns the degree of distinctness of knowledge, not the extent of the represented object.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Monads are differentiated by degrees of distinct perception within a common orientation toward the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] The limit of the possible simultaneously bounds accessible variety, order, and perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A6","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] The integral distinctness of all perceptions would abolish the difference between monad and divinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A12","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The system converges toward an internal totality in which each perspective contains the whole without becoming transparent to the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-01","text":"Maximization first recurs as a combination of variety and order, then as a universal architecture of reciprocal expressions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-02","text":"Order retains its functional identity, but it ceases to be a constraint applied to plurality and becomes the internal product of its relations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-03","text":"Harmony migrates from the theological register toward a relational ontology in which every substance is linked to all the others by expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:D1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-04","text":"Represented totality no longer signifies total transparency: it is transformed into a universal field modulated by degrees of clarity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:D2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-05","text":"Limitation shifts from the known object toward the modification of knowledge, recoding finitude as epistemic modulation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AS5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RMD-06","text":"Terminal perfection is not absolute transparency, but maximal differentiation compatible with the unity of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-01","text":"The search for a means simultaneously producing variety and order remains local so long as it does not become a theory of relational totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-02","text":"The current level links configurational perfection, universal harmony, and monadic representation within a single structure of co-production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-03","text":"The local proposition according to which each monad represents the universe here becomes the principle of differentiation of all plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-04","text":"The local theological objection is recoded as a general methodological rule: an appearance of excess does not constitute proof of impossibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:D4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:CGD-05","text":"The model of a territorial distribution of the real becomes obsolete at the current level, replaced by a graduated distribution of clarity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ME3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects a variety that would be dispersion and an order that would be a reduction of plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:NX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that an objection founded on apparent excess could interrupt the construction without a demonstration of impossibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:NX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-03","text":"It rejects a monad limited to an independent region of the real or external to the universe it represents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:NX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-04","text":"It separates representing everything, knowing everything distinctly, and being divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:GNX-05","text":"It excludes perfection founded on a single magnitude, whether variety, order, or clarity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:NX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, plurality must never be an absolute exteriority to unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:DBN-02","text":"Totality must be capable of being represented without becoming wholly distinct, failing which the hierarchy between creature and God would collapse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX6","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:DBN-03","text":"The system silently disqualifies every model in which finitude would stem from a defect of the object rather than from a degree of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:DNX5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:DBN-04","text":"It cannot admit an irreducible conflict between maximal variety and maximal order without losing its principle of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSA-01","text":"The structuring absence is that of a point of view external to the universe: every perspective is already caught within the whole it represents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSA-02","text":"The unavailable possibility is an integral transparency in which each perspective would know every detail distinctly without becoming divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSA-03","text":"The system sidesteps the question of a formal criterion for measuring variety, order, and their maximal compatibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-01","text":"Perfection becomes a coordination of maxima because plurality is fully productive only when inscribed within an order that does not suppress it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CH_UCIC_P_50:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-02","text":"Universal harmony provides plurality with a form of internal unity: substances are not ordered from the outside; they mutually express one another.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-03","text":"The monadic structure generalizes the logic of perfection: the whole is preserved in each unit, while difference shifts toward the degree of clarity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_52:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-04","text":"The defense of harmony and the theory of monads rest on one and the same strategy: maintaining the integrity of the system by locating the limit in degree rather than in the object.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_52:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-05","text":"Perfection is relational on the global scale because no unit possesses an exclusive ontological domain or a position external to totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:XD-06","text":"The limit of the possible functions both as a metaphysical bound and as an unresolved point of the system, since its constitution is not formalized.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-01","text":"The real is reconfigured as an internal relational totality: each unit bears the whole, but no unit exhausts it through integral transparency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-02","text":"The finite subject is no longer an entity separate from the real, but a local modulation of a universal field that it expresses confusedly.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-03","text":"Order ceases to be a law imposed upon distinct matter: it becomes the distributed effect of relations of reciprocal expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-04","text":"The method of the system transforms objection into a test of demonstrated contradiction, substituting proof of impossibility for the feeling of disproportion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:ME3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-05","text":"Perfection does not designate the abolition of differences, but their maximal integration within an ordered totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:ME1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:BSD-06","text":"The system's generative causality is distributed: the unity of the whole produces local differences, and local differences make manifest the unity of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop follows the sequence maximal variety → maximal order → perfection → bound of the possible, then returns to the measure of variety and order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AF1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-02","text":"The apologetic loop transforms apparent excess into a demand for proof of impossibility, then uses the absence of this proof to preserve the hypothesis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:FGS3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-03","text":"The monadic loop begins with the representation of the whole, produces confusion of detail, localizes distinctness, then returns each monad to the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AF1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-04","text":"The repetition of totality under different degrees constitutes a phase change: the identity of the whole becomes the motor of difference.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is a maximal but non-transparent totality, in which integration increases with differentiation without attaining divine equality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A12","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B01","text":"Posit a maximal plurality without allowing it to become dispersion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B02","text":"Add to this plurality a maximal order conceived as the condition of its perfection rather than as its negation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B03","text":"Transform order into universal harmony through the reciprocal expression of all substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B04","text":"Inscribe the entire universe in each monad, then distribute difference according to degrees of distinct perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B05","text":"Shift every limitation from the object to the clarity of its knowledge in order to maintain representational universality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B06","text":"Close the system through two thresholds: the possible bounds perfection, and integral transparency is reserved for God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B07","text":"The general form is therefore: maximal plurality → immanent order → universal expression → graduated perception → non-transparent totality → perfection bounded by the possible and divinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:FGS7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:AFM-B01","text":"Problem of organized plurality → reframing of variety and order as joint maxima → configurational perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:AFM-B02","text":"Configurational perfection → universal harmony → reciprocal expression of substances → neutralization of the objection through displacement toward proof of impossibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:AFM-B03","text":"Universal order → representation of the whole in each monad → local and graduated distinctness → exclusion of divine transparency → non-external relational totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-01","text":"Variety and order are reclassified as co-productive dimensions of a single architecture of perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:ME1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-02","text":"The relation among substances becomes more fundamental than their separation: the individual is mapped as a node of expression of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:ME1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-03","text":"The opposition between totality and finitude collapses: a finite unit can represent the whole without distinguishing it integrally.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ME2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-04","text":"Differences among monads are redrawn as gradients of clarity and not as boundaries between ontological territories.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ME3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MME-05","text":"Divinity becomes the cartographic threshold of integrally distinct perception, not a mere higher degree among others.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ME5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level: the system addresses the production of an ordered plurality and the representation of the universe by each monad.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level: coherence rests on a distribution of universal expression and degrees of distinct perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level: the system replaces the choice between plurality and order with the coordination of conditions that mutually reinforce one another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:ALT3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level: each monad is a perspective internal to the whole, but no autonomous generative temporality is explicitly constituted.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level: the argument enacts its principle by transforming apparent limits into internal degrees of a broader architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:ALT3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FL-01","text":"Compatibility between maximal variety and maximal order is constitutive of the system, but it is asserted more than demonstrated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:SNX3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FL-02","text":"The hypothesis of a demonstrated harmony relies locally on the absence of proof of impossibility, creating a discrepancy between claimed status and stated foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:FL-03","text":"The universality of representation enters into productive tension with the necessary limitation of distinct perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MP-01","text":"The concept of order mutates when it passes from a coordinated end to an immanent relation among substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MP-02","text":"Finitude mutates from a possible limitation of the object into a graduated modulation of knowledge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD2","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MP-03","text":"The divine limit mutates from an external bound into a terminal function that prevents integral perception from becoming identity with God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:D5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:HSI-01","text":"Implicit reality is a machine of recursive expression: each unit contains the schema of the whole, and the whole manifests itself through the differentiation of units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SD1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a finite perspective without an outside, defined by the local modulation of a universal representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:HSI-03","text":"Time is not the principal operator of the machine; the decisive dynamic is modal and graduated, organized by the possible and degrees of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:A6","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:HSI-04","text":"No escape consists in leaving the whole: the only margin consists in modifying the degree of distinctness from which the whole is expressed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:SNX1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B01","text":"A sufficient core comprises four operations: maximize variety and order, convert their relation into harmony, inscribe the whole in each monad, and differentiate clarity without reducing the object.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT1","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction remains coherent only if universal representation is not assimilated to an equally distinct knowledge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B03","text":"The point of strength is the transformation of totality into a principle of differentiation rather than into an abolition of differences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_52:MRT3","CL_UCIC_20:GA-05","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B04","text":"The principal indeterminacy concerns the criterion for measuring the maxima and the effective demonstration of their compatibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT4","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B05","text":"The reduction preserves the generative movement, but it does not restore the prior proof invoked to support universal harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_51:MRT6","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B06","text":"The minimal architecture is therefore sufficient to reconstruct the cluster, while its zones of strength depend on a postulated compatibility and its fault zones on an incomplete formalization of the possible, measurement, and proof.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_50:MRT5","CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-03","CL_UCIC_20:GA-08","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_20@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_20:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 58–60","context":"Proposition 58 · Proposition 59 · Proposition 60"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 61–63","order":21,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_53","CH_UCIC_P_54","CH_UCIC_P_55"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_21@R001","sha256":"58430ed5f2cef9b9a2c0ae1cc758fa59fbc544c031e6ec91cc4f4fa05dcf08ae","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-01","text":"Le problème central est de penser comment une totalité universellement connectée devient présente dans des entités particulières sans abolir leur différence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-02","text":"La continuité matérielle transforme chaque corps en indice local d’un ordre qui le dépasse et l’affecte à distance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-03","text":"La monade convertit cette connexion universelle en représentation différenciée, dont le corps propre constitue le foyer de distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-04","text":"L’universalité ne devient donc accessible qu’à travers une perspective incarnée, et non par une saisie homogène de toutes les choses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-05","text":"La chaîne représentative se prolonge dans l’organisation corporelle : l’ordre perçu par l’âme devient l’ordre organique du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-06","text":"Le vivant et l’animal apparaissent ainsi comme des compositions relationnelles plutôt que comme des propriétés autonomes de la matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-07","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et stratifié : plénitude matérielle, représentation monadique, perspective corporelle, perception ordonnée, organicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-08","text":"La clôture produite est une ontologie de l’expression incarnée, maintenue par l’écart entre contenir le tout et le rendre distinctement lisible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AS6","CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La matière pleine forme un continuum causal dans lequel aucun corps n’est séparé des effets produits ailleurs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A1","CH_UCIC_P_53:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Toute entité corporelle exprime l’état global de l’univers selon la position et la structure de ses connexions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","CH_UCIC_P_53:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La représentation universelle ne vaut pas comme lisibilité uniforme, mais comme distribution différentielle de la distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_54:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] La monade représente l’univers entier à partir d’un corps particulier qui lui sert de centre de concentration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_54:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La particularité corporelle devient le mode nécessaire par lequel l’universalité représentative acquiert une perspective déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A6","CH_UCIC_P_54:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] L’entéléchie ou l’âme ne s’ajoute pas extérieurement au corps : elle détermine son statut de vivant ou d’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] L’organicité du corps est l’effet d’une continuité entre ordre cosmique, perception monadique et organisation corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_55:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] La limite de l’âme porte sur l’actualisation distincte de ses représentations, non sur son inscription dans la totalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Le corps propre est à la fois un nœud causal, une perspective représentative et un organisme ordonné.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] L’unité de l’univers se conserve à travers la pluralité des modes d’expression monadiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] La totalité universelle n’aboutit pas à une connaissance finie intégralement explicite, mais à une expression corporelle toujours perspectivée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] L’architecture converge vers la correspondance réglée entre ordre universel, perception de l’âme et organisation du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-01","text":"La plénitude revient d’abord comme propagation causale, puis comme condition d’expressivité réciproque entre le particulier et le tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-02","text":"La représentation du tout se déplace d’une inscription diffuse dans chaque corps vers une perspective monadique centrée sur le corps propre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","CH_UCIC_P_54:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-03","text":"La distinction perceptive, d’abord limite épistémique de l’âme, devient ensuite principe de différenciation entre les monades.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-04","text":"Le corps passe du statut d’objet affecté à distance à celui de médiateur actif de l’expression universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A4","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-05","text":"L’entéléchie se déplace d’un principe associé au corps vers une fonction qui confère au corps son statut de vivant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_55:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-06","text":"L’ordre cosmique, initialement condition de représentation, devient principe de structuration organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-07","text":"L’opacité perceptive n’est pas supprimée par l’universalité de la représentation ; elle est absorbée dans une théorie graduée de l’expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_54:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-01","text":"La propagation d’un effet d’un corps à l’autre reste une machine locale ; au niveau courant, elle devient la condition générale d’une expressivité sans extérieur causal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A3","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-02","text":"La limitation de l’âme à ses perceptions distinctes reste locale tant qu’elle concerne la lisibilité ; elle devient structurelle lorsqu’elle règle le rapport entre universalité et perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_54:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-03","text":"L’association d’une monade à un corps particulier change d’échelle lorsqu’elle devient le principe de médiation entre totalité représentée et singularité vécue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-04","text":"La distinction entre vivant et animal est locale dans sa terminologie, mais devient au niveau courant un modèle général de détermination relationnelle du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:D1","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-05","text":"L’organicité ne demeure pas une propriété attribuée au corps : elle devient le résultat d’une chaîne cosmique, perceptive et corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:D4","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-06","text":"Les formulations locales sur la communication, la représentation et la composition sont absorbées dans une architecture unique de correspondances graduées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut une matière composée de régions causalement indépendantes ou isolables par le seul contact immédiat.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une représentation universelle soit identique à une perception également distincte de tous les contenus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut une monade dont l’universalité serait indépendante d’un point d’ancrage corporel singulier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut un corps vivant dont l’organisation procéderait de la seule composition matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une séparation radicale entre ordre cosmique, ordre perceptif et ordre corporel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-06","text":"La singularité n’est donc ni une clôture locale ni une rupture avec le tout, mais une modulation de sa manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_54:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut disqualifier l’idée qu’une connexion réelle exige une présence spatiale ou temporelle immédiate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_53:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également exclure une transparence intégrale de la représentation à la conscience finie, faute de quoi la différence entre totalité et perspective disparaîtrait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A11","CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie un univers dont les parties seraient seulement juxtaposées, car aucune expression universelle ne pourrait alors traverser les niveaux.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_54:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-04","text":"Il refuse une conception externe de l’âme et du corps : la représentation doit être corporelle, et l’organisation corporelle représentative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_55:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-05","text":"L’architecture ne peut admettre une organicité sans médiation monadique, parce que l’ordre du corps doit prolonger l’ordre de la perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSA-01","text":"L’impossibilité la plus profonde est celle d’un point de vue fini qui convertirait instantanément l’expression universelle en connaissance distincte du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSA-02","text":"Le système contourne la possibilité d’une matière vivante autosuffisante, indépendante de toute âme, entéléchie ou structure représentative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSA-03","text":"Ce qui demeure indisponible n’est pas la présence du tout dans chaque entité, mais sa conversion totale en présence distincte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSA-04","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un extérieur ontologique : aucun niveau de l’architecture ne peut être défini par soustraction au réseau universel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-01","text":"La causalité universelle devient une théorie de l’expression : ce qui affecte chaque corps ne le traverse pas seulement, mais s’y inscrit selon un degré de distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-01","CL_UCIC_21:GA-02","CL_UCIC_21:GA-03","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-02","text":"Le corps propre n’est pas simplement le terme privilégié d’une chaîne causale ; il est le dispositif qui convertit la totalité représentée en perspective monadique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-04","CL_UCIC_21:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_54:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_54:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-03","text":"L’universalité de la monade et la limitation de l’âme ne sont compatibles qu’à condition de distinguer possession représentative et explicitation perceptive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-03","CL_UCIC_21:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_53:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-04","text":"L’organicité apparaît comme le point de jonction où la structure universelle cesse d’être seulement représentée et devient forme corporelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CL_UCIC_21:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-05","text":"Le vivant et l’animal sont deux codages d’une même opération : la détermination du corps par une fonction immatérielle de représentation et d’ordre.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-06","CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-06","text":"La différence entre totalité et singularité est reconduite comme différence de degré, de foyer et de fonction plutôt que comme opposition de substances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-04","CL_UCIC_21:GA-05","CL_UCIC_21:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-07","text":"L’ordre organique fournit la preuve interne que l’expression universelle n’est pas une métaphore distributive, mais une détermination des niveaux corporels.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CL_UCIC_21:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_55:D4","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est requalifié comme un continuum d’expressions emboîtées où chaque niveau traduit l’ordre des niveaux supérieurs sans les reproduire uniformément.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-02","text":"Le sujet monadique devient une capacité finie de focalisation plutôt qu’un réceptacle séparé du monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:D1","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-03","text":"Le corps devient simultanément archive causale, miroir perspectif et réalisation organique d’un ordre universel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-04","text":"Le temps et la distance cessent d’être des barrières absolues et deviennent des degrés de présence, de propagation et de lisibilité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SD5","CH_UCIC_P_53:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-05","text":"La causalité n’est plus un transfert linéaire entre unités séparées, mais une modulation distribuée qui produit des formes locales d’organisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D1","CH_UCIC_P_55:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-06","text":"La connaissance doit être pensée comme déploiement graduel d’une inscription déjà présente, et non comme acquisition d’un contenu extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D5","CH_UCIC_P_53:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-07","text":"L’ontologie entière est orientée vers une production de correspondances : le cosmique devient perceptif, le perceptif devient organique, et le local réexprime le global.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-01","text":"La boucle fondamentale est : plénitude → propagation universelle → inscription dans chaque corps → représentation → nouvelle expression de la totalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-02","text":"Une seconde boucle transforme la représentation en organisation : univers ordonné → perception ordonnée → corps ordonné → preuve corporelle de l’ordre représenté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-03","text":"L’escalade conceptuelle va de l’effet distant à la forme organique : la causalité diffuse devient structure du vivant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur de l’ensemble est l’expression universelle incarnée : chaque niveau reconduit la totalité sous une forme plus déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-05","text":"La répétition de la totalité ne produit jamais une identité simple ; elle produit une série de focalisations, de médiations et de degrés de distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-06","text":"La tension entre contenu total et perception partielle agit comme moteur récursif : l’opacité locale confirme la profondeur de l’inscription universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B01","text":"Plénitude matérielle → connexion causale sans extérieur → affectation graduée de chaque corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A1","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B02","text":"Affectation universelle → inscription de l’état du tout dans chaque corps → possibilité d’une expression locale de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_53:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B03","text":"Expression locale → représentation monadique universelle → différenciation selon le corps particulièrement affecté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","CH_UCIC_P_54:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B04","text":"Corps privilégié → entéléchie ou âme du corps → constitution relationnelle du vivant et de l’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A4","CH_UCIC_P_55:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B05","text":"Univers ordonné → perceptions ordonnées → ordre correspondant du corps → organicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B06","text":"Infinité des replis → impossibilité d’une explicitation totale → distinction entre représentation intégrale et perception finie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A10","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B07","text":"Expression universelle incarnée + explicitation partielle → architecture stable d’un tout présent dans chaque corps mais jamais épuisé par une perspective finie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AFM-B01","text":"Plénitude matérielle → causalité à distance → inscription universelle dans les corps → représentation monadique du tout → privilège du corps propre → composition du vivant et de l’animal → organicité perceptivement ordonnée → opacité finie de l’explicitation → expression universelle incarnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_54:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AFM-B02","text":"Le mouvement global remplace l’opposition entre universel et particulier par une circulation graduée entre totalité, perspective, perception et organisme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-01","text":"Le corps est reclassé comme nœud où se croisent causalité distribuée, représentation universelle et organisation organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-02","text":"La singularité n’est plus cartographiée comme exclusion du tout, mais comme foyer de concentration et de modulation du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_54:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-03","text":"La perception est séparée de la représentation sans être séparée de la réalité : l’inconscient perceptif devient une forme de présence implicite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-04","text":"L’organisme est cartographié comme une traduction corporelle de l’ordre représentatif, non comme un assemblage matériel autosuffisant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-05","text":"L’âme et le corps cessent d’être deux domaines juxtaposés et deviennent deux régimes coordonnés d’une même expression monadique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-06","text":"La méthode pertinente n’est plus l’analyse d’unités isolées, mais le suivi des correspondances entre niveaux d’expression et degrés de distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les corps s’affectent à distance, les monades représentent l’univers, et les corps associés à l’entéléchie ou à l’âme constituent des vivants ou des animaux.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A4","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Un continuum causal et représentatif distribue l’ordre du tout à travers la monade, la perception, le corps et l’organicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] L’explication est déplacée de l’isolement des substances vers l’analyse des médiations par lesquelles le tout devient localement distinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est supposé continu, le présent conserve des déterminations éloignées, et chaque entité exprime le tout selon une temporalité non isolante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme de l’argument accomplit sa propre thèse en faisant passer une même structure par des niveaux successifs de causalité, représentation et organisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FL-01","text":"La totalité est présente dans chaque corps, mais aucune âme finie ne peut la rendre simultanément distincte ; cette contradiction est constitutive et non déficiente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FL-02","text":"La monade représente l’univers entier tout en privilégiant un seul corps ; la perspective singulière doit donc être comprise comme mode d’universalité, non comme réduction locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:D1","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FL-03","text":"L’ordre des perceptions est déclaré producteur de l’ordre organique, mais le mécanisme précis de cette conversion demeure sous-déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FL-04","text":"La différence entre entéléchie et âme organise des statuts distincts du corps, sans que leur rapport conceptuel soit entièrement résolu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MP-01","text":"Le passage de la causalité matérielle à la représentation monadique constitue le premier point de mutation : l’effet devient inscription.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D1","CH_UCIC_P_53:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MP-02","text":"Le passage de la représentation au corps organique constitue le second point de mutation : l’expression devient architecture corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:D4","CH_UCIC_P_55:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MP-03","text":"Le passage de la totalité représentée à la perception partielle constitue le point de compression final : la limitation produit la perspective au lieu de l’annuler.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est un réseau plein de miroirs incarnés, où chaque corps reçoit, conserve et réexprime des déterminations du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_55:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une ouverture corporelle focalisée : il n’est ni extérieur au monde ni capable de le déployer entièrement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_54:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est un régime de traces et de degrés de lisibilité, non une succession qui isolerait absolument passé, présent et futur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D3","CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:HSI-04","text":"La lutte ou la navigation possibles ne consistent pas à sortir du réseau, mais à modifier le degré d’explicitation d’une expression déjà intégralement connectée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ME5","CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante si elle conserve quatre opérations : connexion causale universelle, expression monadique, médiation corporelle et conversion de l’ordre perceptif en organicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B02","text":"La distinction entre représentation implicite et perception distincte est indispensable ; sans elle, l’universalité monadique et la finitude de l’âme deviennent incompatibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_53:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B03","text":"La distinction entre âme, entéléchie, vivant et animal reste partiellement indéterminée, mais cette indétermination n’empêche pas de reconstruire la fonction générale de médiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B04","text":"La relation exacte par laquelle l’ordre perceptif produit l’ordre organique demeure le principal point de compression théorique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B05","text":"Le noyau minimal fidèle est donc : totalité sans extérieur → perspective corporelle → représentation graduée → organisation du vivant → explicitation finie et inachevable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195759028788Z_a0126279","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 61–63","source_sha256":"58430ed5f2cef9b9a2c0ae1cc758fa59fbc544c031e6ec91cc4f4fa05dcf08ae","sha256":"5d76db98e9a03e80ffa06d83b44dc834b8449fe71b1edad250c26ef461a60ead","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:57:59.032706+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-01","text":"The central problem is to think how a universally connected totality becomes present in particular entities without abolishing their difference.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-02","text":"Material continuity transforms each body into a local index of an order that exceeds it and affects it at a distance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-03","text":"The monad converts this universal connection into differentiated representation, of which the proper body constitutes the focal point of distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_54:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-04","text":"Universality thus becomes accessible only through an embodied perspective, and not through a homogeneous apprehension of all things.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-05","text":"The representative chain extends into bodily organization: the order perceived by the soul becomes the organic order of the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A8","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-06","text":"The living being and the animal thus appear as relational compositions rather than as autonomous properties of matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-07","text":"The movement is cumulative and stratified: material plenitude, monadic representation, bodily perspective, ordered perception, organicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AS-08","text":"The resulting closure is an ontology of embodied expression, sustained by the gap between containing the whole and rendering it distinctly legible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AS6","CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Full matter forms a causal continuum in which no body is separated from effects produced elsewhere.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A1","CH_UCIC_P_53:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Every corporeal entity expresses the global state of the universe according to the position and structure of its connections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","CH_UCIC_P_53:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Universal representation does not amount to uniform legibility, but to a differential distribution of distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_54:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The monad represents the entire universe from a particular body that serves it as a center of concentration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_54:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Bodily particularity becomes the necessary mode through which representative universality acquires a determinate perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A6","CH_UCIC_P_54:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Entelechy or soul is not added externally to the body: it determines its status as a living being or animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_55:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The organicity of the body is the effect of a continuity between cosmic order, monadic perception, and bodily organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_55:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] The limitation of the soul concerns the distinct actualization of its representations, not its inscription in the totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] The proper body is at once a causal node, a representative perspective, and an ordered organism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] The unity of the universe is preserved through the plurality of modes of monadic expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Universal totality does not culminate in an entirely explicit finite knowledge, but in an always perspectivized bodily expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] The architecture converges toward regulated correspondence between universal order, the soul's perception, and the organization of the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-01","text":"Plenitude first recurs as causal propagation, then as the condition of reciprocal expressivity between the particular and the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-02","text":"The representation of the whole shifts from a diffuse inscription in every body to a monadic perspective centered on the proper body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A7","CH_UCIC_P_54:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-03","text":"Perceptual distinction, initially an epistemic limit of the soul, subsequently becomes a principle of differentiation among monads.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A9","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-04","text":"The body passes from the status of an object affected at a distance to that of an active mediator of universal expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A4","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-05","text":"Entelechy shifts from a principle associated with the body to a function that confers upon the body its status as a living being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_55:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-06","text":"Cosmic order, initially a condition of representation, becomes a principle of organic structuring.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RMD-07","text":"Perceptual opacity is not removed by the universality of representation; it is absorbed into a graded theory of expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_54:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-01","text":"The propagation of an effect from one body to another remains a local mechanism; at the current level, it becomes the general condition of an expressivity without causal exteriority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A3","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-02","text":"The limitation of the soul to its distinct perceptions remains local insofar as it concerns legibility; it becomes structural when it regulates the relation between universality and perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_54:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-03","text":"The association of a monad with a particular body changes scale when it becomes the principle of mediation between represented totality and lived singularity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A3","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-04","text":"The distinction between living being and animal is local in its terminology, but at the current level becomes a general model of the relational determination of the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:D1","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-05","text":"Organicity does not remain a property attributed to the body: it becomes the result of a cosmic, perceptual, and bodily chain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:D4","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:CGD-06","text":"Local formulations concerning communication, representation, and composition are absorbed into a single architecture of graded correspondences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes matter composed of causally independent regions or regions isolable by immediate contact alone.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a universal representation identical with an equally distinct perception of all contents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-03","text":"It excludes a monad whose universality would be independent of a singular bodily point of anchorage.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-04","text":"It excludes a living body whose organization would proceed from material composition alone.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-05","text":"It excludes a radical separation between cosmic order, perceptual order, and bodily order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:GNX-06","text":"Singularity is thus neither a local closure nor a rupture with the whole, but a modulation of its manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_54:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the idea that a real connection requires immediate spatial or temporal presence must be disqualified.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_53:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-02","text":"It is likewise necessary to exclude an integral transparency of representation to finite consciousness, failing which the difference between totality and perspective would disappear.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A11","CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies a universe whose parts would be merely juxtaposed, for no universal expression could then traverse the levels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_54:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-04","text":"It rejects an external conception of soul and body: representation must be bodily, and bodily organization representative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_55:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:DBN-05","text":"The architecture cannot admit an organicity without monadic mediation, because the order of the body must extend the order of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSA-01","text":"The deepest impossibility is that of a finite point of view that would instantaneously convert universal expression into distinct knowledge of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSA-02","text":"The system circumvents the possibility of self-sufficient living matter, independent of any soul, entelechy, or representative structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_55:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSA-03","text":"What remains unavailable is not the presence of the whole in each entity, but its total conversion into distinct presence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSA-04","text":"The structuring absence is that of an ontological exterior: no level of the architecture can be defined by subtraction from the universal network.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-01","text":"Universal causality becomes a theory of expression: what affects each body does not merely pass through it, but is inscribed in it according to a degree of distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-01","CL_UCIC_21:GA-02","CL_UCIC_21:GA-03","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-02","text":"The proper body is not simply the privileged term of a causal chain; it is the apparatus that converts represented totality into monadic perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-04","CL_UCIC_21:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_54:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_54:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-03","text":"The universality of the monad and the limitation of the soul are compatible only on condition of distinguishing representative possession from perceptual explication.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-03","CL_UCIC_21:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_53:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_53:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-04","text":"Organicity appears as the junction point at which universal structure ceases to be merely represented and becomes bodily form.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CL_UCIC_21:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_55:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_55:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-05","text":"The living being and the animal are two codings of one and the same operation: the determination of the body by an immaterial function of representation and order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-06","CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3","CH_UCIC_P_55:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-06","text":"The difference between totality and singularity is recast as a difference of degree, focal point, and function rather than as an opposition of substances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-04","CL_UCIC_21:GA-05","CL_UCIC_21:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_54:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:XD-07","text":"Organic order provides internal proof that universal expression is not a distributive metaphor, but a determination of bodily levels.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CL_UCIC_21:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_55:D4","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Direct","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-01","text":"The real is requalified as a continuum of nested expressions in which each level translates the order of higher levels without reproducing them uniformly.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-02","text":"The monadic subject becomes a finite capacity for focalization rather than a receptacle separated from the world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:D1","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-03","text":"The body becomes simultaneously a causal archive, a perspectival mirror, and the organic realization of a universal order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-04","text":"Time and distance cease to be absolute barriers and become degrees of presence, propagation, and legibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SD5","CH_UCIC_P_53:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-05","text":"Causality is no longer a linear transfer between separate units, but a distributed modulation that produces local forms of organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D1","CH_UCIC_P_55:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-06","text":"Knowledge must be thought as the gradual unfolding of an inscription already present, and not as the acquisition of an external content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D5","CH_UCIC_P_53:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:BSD-07","text":"The entire ontology is oriented toward a production of correspondences: the cosmic becomes perceptual, the perceptual becomes organic, and the local re-expresses the global.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-01","text":"The fundamental loop is: plenitude → universal propagation → inscription in each body → representation → renewed expression of totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-02","text":"A second loop transforms representation into organization: ordered universe → ordered perception → ordered body → bodily proof of the represented order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-03","text":"The conceptual escalation proceeds from distant effect to organic form: diffuse causality becomes the structure of the living being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-04","text":"The attractor of the whole is embodied universal expression: each level reintroduces totality in a more determinate form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A5","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-05","text":"The repetition of totality never produces a simple identity; it produces a series of focalizations, mediations, and degrees of distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:RLE-06","text":"The tension between total content and partial perception acts as a recursive motor: local opacity confirms the depth of universal inscription.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX5","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B01","text":"Material plenitude → causal connection without exteriority → graded affection of each body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A1","CH_UCIC_P_53:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B02","text":"Universal affection → inscription of the state of the whole in each body → possibility of a local expression of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_53:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B03","text":"Local expression → universal monadic representation → differentiation according to the particularly affected body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A1","CH_UCIC_P_54:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B04","text":"Privileged body → entelechy or soul of the body → relational constitution of the living being and the animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:A4","CH_UCIC_P_55:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B05","text":"Ordered universe → ordered perceptions → corresponding order of the body → organicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A6","CH_UCIC_P_55:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B06","text":"Infinity of folds → impossibility of a total explication → distinction between integral representation and finite perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A10","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B07","text":"Embodied universal expression + partial explication → stable architecture of a whole present in each body but never exhausted by a finite perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AFM-B01","text":"Material plenitude → causality at a distance → universal inscription in bodies → monadic representation of the whole → privilege of the proper body → composition of the living being and the animal → perceptually ordered organicity → finite opacity of explication → embodied universal expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_54:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:AFM-B02","text":"The overall movement replaces the opposition between universal and particular with a graded circulation between totality, perspective, perception, and organism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-01","text":"The body is reclassified as a node at which distributed causality, universal representation, and organic organization intersect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_55:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-02","text":"Singularity is no longer mapped as exclusion from the whole, but as a focal point of concentration and modulation of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_54:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-03","text":"Perception is separated from representation without being separated from reality: the perceptual unconscious becomes a form of implicit presence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-04","text":"The organism is mapped as a bodily translation of representative order, not as a self-sufficient material assemblage.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_55:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-05","text":"Soul and body cease to be two juxtaposed domains and become two coordinated regimes of one and the same monadic expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MME-06","text":"The pertinent method is no longer the analysis of isolated units, but the tracking of correspondences between levels of expression and degrees of distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Bodies affect one another at a distance, monads represent the universe, and bodies associated with entelechy or soul constitute living beings or animals.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:A4","CH_UCIC_P_55:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] A causal and representative continuum distributes the order of the whole through the monad, perception, the body, and organicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Explanation is shifted from the isolation of substances to the analysis of the mediations through which the whole becomes locally distinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The real is presumed continuous, the present preserves distant determinations, and each entity expresses the whole according to a non-isolating temporality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_53:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The form of the argument performs its own thesis by moving one and the same structure through successive levels of causality, representation, and organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_55:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FL-01","text":"Totality is present in every body, but no finite soul can render it simultaneously distinct; this contradiction is constitutive and not deficient.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_53:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FL-02","text":"The monad represents the entire universe while privileging a single body; the singular perspective must therefore be understood as a mode of universality, not as a local reduction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:D1","CH_UCIC_P_54:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FL-03","text":"The order of perceptions is declared productive of organic order, but the precise mechanism of this conversion remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:FL-04","text":"The difference between entelechy and soul organizes distinct statuses of the body, without their conceptual relation being entirely resolved.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:A2","CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MP-01","text":"The passage from material causality to monadic representation constitutes the first mutation point: effect becomes inscription.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D1","CH_UCIC_P_53:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MP-02","text":"The passage from representation to the organic body constitutes the second mutation point: expression becomes bodily architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:D4","CH_UCIC_P_55:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MP-03","text":"The passage from represented totality to partial perception constitutes the final compression point: limitation produces perspective instead of annulling it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_54:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:HSI-01","text":"Implicit reality is a network full of embodied mirrors, in which each body receives, preserves, and re-expresses determinations of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_55:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a focused bodily opening: it is neither external to the world nor capable of fully unfolding it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_54:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:HSI-03","text":"Time is a regime of traces and degrees of legibility, not a succession that would absolutely isolate past, present, and future.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:D3","CH_UCIC_P_53:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:HSI-04","text":"Possible struggle or navigation does not consist in leaving the network, but in modifying the degree of explication of an expression already integrally connected.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:ME5","CH_UCIC_P_53:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B01","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves four operations: universal causal connection, monadic expression, bodily mediation, and conversion of perceptual order into organicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B02","text":"The distinction between implicit representation and distinct perception is indispensable; without it, monadic universality and the finitude of the soul become incompatible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_53:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B03","text":"The distinction between soul, entelechy, living being, and animal remains partially indeterminate, but this indeterminacy does not prevent reconstruction of the general function of mediation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_54:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_55:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B04","text":"The exact relation by which perceptual order produces organic order remains the principal point of theoretical compression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B05","text":"The faithful minimal core is therefore: totality without exteriority → bodily perspective → graded representation → organization of the living being → finite and unfinishable explication.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_53:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_55:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_21@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_21:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 61–63","context":"Proposition 61 · Proposition 62 · Proposition 63"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 64–66","order":22,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_56","CH_UCIC_P_57","CH_UCIC_P_58"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_22@R001","sha256":"eaaad468b048539d3a8004fcc64f261306fb40e88e5bea6b62b133f641dc3832","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-01","text":"Le problème commun consiste à déterminer comment une matière entièrement machinique peut néanmoins se distinguer d’un artefact et exprimer une totalité universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-02","text":"Le vivant est recadré comme une machine naturelle dont la structure se conserve dans chacune de ses parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-03","text":"La différence entre nature et art ne porte plus sur la présence de mécanisme, mais sur la continuité du mécanisme à travers la composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-04","text":"La divisibilité infinie est transformée d’une propriété abstraite en une subdivision actuelle, dynamique et expressive de chaque portion matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-05","text":"La moindre partie n’est pas un terme de réduction, mais un monde interne où se concentrent plusieurs niveaux de réalité organisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-06","text":"Le mouvement génératif va de la machinicité récursive à l’expression universelle, puis de l’expression universelle à la densification ontologique de la matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-07","text":"La clôture produite est négative et récursive : aucune analyse matérielle ne rencontre un dernier élément simple, inerte ou extérieur à l’organisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La matière organique est machinique jusque dans ses parties les plus petites.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La nature se distingue de l’artifice par une continuité interne de la machinicité, et non par l’absence de mécanisme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La divisibilité infinie devient une sous-division actuellement réalisée, dotée d’une fonction architecturale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Chaque partie matérielle possède un mouvement propre qui empêche de réduire la matière à une extension inerte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Chaque portion matérielle exprime l’univers parce que sa composition interne demeure indéfiniment différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La moindre partie de la matière contient une pluralité de réalités organisées plutôt qu’une unité ultime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] La vie, l’animalité, l’entéléchie et l’âme deviennent des niveaux internes de la constitution matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] L’analyse ne peut atteindre une matière absolument simple, homogène, muette ou dépourvue d’intérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Le système converge vers une image de la matière comme multiplicité de mondes emboîtés, chaque niveau reconduisant l’organisation du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] L’infini fonctionne comme principe de continuité structurale, d’expression et de densification ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-01","text":"La machinicité revient d’abord comme critère de distinction entre organisme et artefact, puis comme modèle général de la matière organisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:D5","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-02","text":"La récursivité migre de la conservation de la machine dans les parties vers la subdivision actuelle et enfin vers l’emboîtement des mondes matériels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-03","text":"L’infini change de fonction : d’abord profondeur compositionnelle du vivant, il devient ensuite condition d’expression universelle, puis absence d’un seuil ontologique terminal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:D3","CH_UCIC_P_57:D4","CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-04","text":"La partie cesse d’être un composant subordonné et devient successivement relais machinique, unité expressive et monde intérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:D4","CH_UCIC_P_58:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-05","text":"Le mouvement propre des parties est absorbé dans une théorie plus vaste où l’activité interne fonde l’expression du tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-06","text":"L’opposition nature-art perd sa fonction terminale lorsque la matière entière est redéfinie comme continuum de structures organisées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Absorption","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-07","text":"La hiérarchie créature–vivant–animal–entéléchie–âme ne constitue pas un nouvel inventaire indépendant, mais le codage interne de la pluralité matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","CH_UCIC_P_58:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Absorption","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-01","text":"L’exemple de la roue artificielle reste local : il illustre l’interruption de la machinicité sans constituer à lui seul l’architecture du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-02","text":"La qualification divine du vivant demeure une attribution métaphysique locale, tandis que la continuité machinique fournit le mécanisme transversal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_56:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-03","text":"La liste des êtres contenus dans la moindre partie est locale dans son lexique, mais devient à l’échelle courante une carte de la stratification matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-04","text":"Le mouvement propre de chaque partie et l’expression de l’univers sont reliés au niveau courant comme deux fonctions d’une même architecture dynamique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-05","text":"La distinction entre artefact et organisme change d’échelle lorsqu’elle devient une distinction entre matière interrompue et matière intérieurement illimitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:D2","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-06","text":"Le mécanisme exact reliant mouvement propre, expression universelle et vie animique reste sous-déterminé et ne peut être traité comme un axiome courant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-01","text":"Le système rejette toute machine dont les parties ultimes cesseraient d’être elles-mêmes machinées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-02","text":"Il rejette une matière divisée seulement en droit, sans subdivision actuelle ni activité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-03","text":"Il rejette l’unité matérielle isolée qui existerait indépendamment de l’univers qu’elle exprime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-04","text":"Il rejette une matière dont l’analyse réduirait progressivement la réalité jusqu’à un élément inorganisé et sans monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-05","text":"Il rejette la séparation absolue entre matière, vie, animalité et âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-06","text":"Il rejette une conception où l’organisation appartiendrait au tout tandis que les parties resteraient ontologiquement brutes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_58:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, doit être fausse l’existence d’unités matérielles ultimes, simples et définitivement séparables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-02","text":"Doit être fausse l’idée que la réduction spatiale ou matérielle produise une réduction de l’organisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-03","text":"Doit être fausse l’opposition stricte entre mécanisme et vie, puisque la machinicité constitue la continuité interne du vivant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-04","text":"Doit être fausse l’idée que la totalité universelle soit extérieure à chaque portion matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-05","text":"Doit être fausse toute ontologie de l’inerte comme fond absolu sur lequel des formes vivantes seraient ajoutées de l’extérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX4","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSA-01","text":"Le système contourne la possibilité d’un dehors matériel absolument simple où la structure, la vie et l’expression cesseraient simultanément.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSA-02","text":"La force de l’architecture dépend de l’absence d’un seuil où la matière ne serait plus porteuse de monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSA-03","text":"Est ontologiquement inadmissible une réalité dont le tout serait organisé mais dont chaque partie serait muette, inerte et extérieure à l’organisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSA-04","text":"Le système ne peut admettre une matière purement homogène sans perdre à la fois la récursivité de la machine et l’expression universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-01","text":"La continuité machinique du vivant fournit le modèle structurel selon lequel chaque portion matérielle peut exprimer l’univers sans devenir identique au tout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-01","CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_56:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-02","text":"La subdivision actuelle convertit la partie organique en unité expressive : ce qui conservait d’abord la machine conserve désormais une relation active avec l’univers entier.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-03","CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_57:D1","CH_UCIC_P_57:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-03","text":"La moindre partie devient un monde interne parce que l’infinité de composition, le mouvement propre et la pluralité des êtres sont une seule architecture à plusieurs fonctions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-03","CL_UCIC_22:GA-04","CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_58:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-04","text":"La descente vers le plus petit n’est pas une opération de simplification, mais une escalade vers une matière plus riche en organisation et en expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","CL_UCIC_22:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-05","text":"La différence entre nature et art est finalement absorbée dans une différence entre composition interrompue et composition qui reconduit indéfiniment le monde dans ses parties.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-02","CL_UCIC_22:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_56:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-06","text":"L’expression universelle exige simultanément une différenciation interne et une non-séparation du tout et de la partie.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-04","CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_57:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-07","text":"Le cluster produit une ontologie où l’organisation n’est ni une propriété globale ni une addition locale, mais une propagation récursive sans terme final.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-01","CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","CL_UCIC_22:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-01","text":"La matière devient un continuum de médiations internes plutôt qu’un support homogène composé d’unités ultimes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-02","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme une totalité distribuée dans ses parties, où chaque unité possède une perspective structurelle sur l’ensemble sans abolir sa différenciation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-03","text":"La causalité n’est plus principalement une transmission externe : elle devient l’effet d’une organisation interne qui rend chaque portion expressive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-04","text":"L’histoire de la composition matérielle est remplacée par une profondeur sans dernier niveau, où chaque analyse reconduit la structure au lieu de l’épuiser.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-05","text":"Le sujet connaissant ne découvre pas un fond simple en descendant dans la matière ; il rencontre une prolifération de niveaux organisés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-06","text":"La stratégie conceptuelle consiste à déplacer toute objection réductrice vers un niveau où elle devient une preuve supplémentaire de la complexité interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-01","text":"Partie machinique → subdivision interne → mouvement propre → expression du tout → nouvelle qualification de la partie comme monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-02","text":"Chaque tentative de réduire la matière à une unité terminale relance la découverte d’une pluralité organisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-03","text":"La récursion change de phase lorsque la machine naturelle cesse d’être seulement un modèle du vivant et devient le schème de toute matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est la totalité distribuée : le tout est présent dans les parties, mais seulement sous forme de différenciations internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-05","text":"L’infini agit comme opérateur d’escalade : chaque niveau supprimé laisse apparaître un niveau plus profond de composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-06","text":"La boucle terminale transforme l’absence de terme ultime en résultat positif : ne pas trouver de dehors de l’organisation confirme la continuité du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B01","text":"Poser un corps organisé comme machine naturelle plutôt que comme artefact perfectionné.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B02","text":"Décomposer la machine et distinguer l’interruption artificielle de la conservation organique de la machinicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B03","text":"Étendre cette conservation à la matière en remplaçant la divisibilité potentielle par une sous-division actuelle sans fin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B04","text":"Attribuer à chaque partie un mouvement propre afin que la subdivision ne produise pas une multiplicité inerte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B05","text":"Convertir la multiplicité interne en puissance expressive : chaque portion devient un lieu de présence de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:D3","CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B06","text":"Généraliser cette structure jusqu’à la moindre partie, où la multiplicité devient monde, vie, animalité, entéléchie et âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B07","text":"Produire une ontologie sans élément simple, sans matière inerte terminale et sans séparation stable entre totalité et partie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:AFM-B01","text":"Artifice fonctionnel → analyse des parties → interruption de la machinicité → recadrage du vivant comme machine naturelle récursive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:AFM-B02","text":"Machine récursive → matière actuellement subdivisée → mouvement propre → expression universelle de chaque portion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:AFM-B03","text":"Expression universelle → monde interne dans la moindre partie → densification ontologique → exclusion de toute simplicité matérielle terminale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_58:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-01","text":"La frontière nature-art est remplacée par une cartographie des régimes de composition interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-02","text":"La matière est reclassée comme réseau dynamique de parties, et non comme étendue homogène simplement divisible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-03","text":"La partie devient une échelle complète d’analyse : composant, organisme local, unité expressive et monde interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_58:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-04","text":"La petitesse est requalifiée comme densification ontologique plutôt que comme diminution de réalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-05","text":"L’infini devient une méthode de cartographie structurale : il désigne la poursuite des niveaux plutôt qu’une simple grandeur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_57:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-06","text":"La fausse opposition entre unité et totalité s’effondre au profit d’une totalité répétée différentiellement dans chaque unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont le corps vivant, la machine artificielle, la portion matérielle et la moindre partie contenant un monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Le mécanisme déterminant est la conservation récursive de l’organisation, articulée à la subdivision actuelle et au mouvement propre des parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] L’argument neutralise toute réduction en transformant l’analyse des parties en démonstration de leur richesse organisationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est une multiplicité actuelle, dynamique et sans dernier niveau de composition, où le temps ne conduit pas à une clôture matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit sa thèse en répétant le même geste : descendre vers la partie et produire davantage de structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FL-01","text":"L’expression universelle est posée comme conséquence de la subdivision et du mouvement, mais la médiation précise entre ces fonctions reste non démontrée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FL-02","text":"L’infinité actuelle de la composition oscille entre une thèse ontologique forte et une divisibilité sans terme ultime dont le statut demeure sous-déterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FL-03","text":"La qualification divine fournit une garantie métaphysique, mais l’architecture fonctionne surtout par continuité machinique et organisation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FL-04","text":"Le passage d’une moindre partie déterminée à une affirmation sur toute la matière constitue un pont généralisant qui n’est pas entièrement explicité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MP-01","text":"La machine naturelle devient le schème général de la matière lorsque la machinicité cesse de caractériser seulement le vivant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MP-02","text":"La divisibilité passe d’une propriété géométrique à une condition dynamique de l’expression universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MP-03","text":"La partie passe de composant organique à microcosme matériel, ce qui inverse la fonction conceptuelle de la petitesse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_58:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MP-04","text":"La négation de l’élément simple se transforme en proposition positive : toute absence de terme ultime devient une production de mondes internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une machine récursive sans extérieur matériel, dont chaque partie reproduit une organisation sans se confondre avec le tout.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une position locale dans une totalité distribuée, confrontée non à un fond simple mais à une prolifération de mondes internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas une progression vers un dernier niveau : il est la reconduction indéfinie de la structure à travers les parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:HSI-04","text":"La navigation conceptuelle consiste à suivre les niveaux de composition, tandis que l’échappée hors du système est rendue impossible par l’absence d’un dehors inerte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes courants suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement complet : machinicité récursive, subdivision actuelle, mouvement propre, expression universelle et monde interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction conserve la mutation d’échelle par laquelle le vivant sert d’abord de cas exemplaire, puis de modèle pour toute la matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_57:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne principalement la médiation entre mouvement propre, expression universelle, entéléchie et âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence dépend d’une double lecture de l’infini : continuation actuelle de la composition et absence d’un terme matériel simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B05","text":"La compression est suffisante si elle préserve l’attracteur central : toute réduction de la matière reconduit une organisation plus profonde au lieu de produire un élément brut.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_58:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195829897248Z_a257f7b2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 64–66","source_sha256":"eaaad468b048539d3a8004fcc64f261306fb40e88e5bea6b62b133f641dc3832","sha256":"0d8b15a69d5dc4fc6c5ddc84c20589cbb38294424bfa02af0c5f89db617aada7","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:58:29.901095+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-01","text":"The common problem consists in determining how a wholly machinic matter can nevertheless be distinguished from an artefact and express a universal totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-02","text":"The living is reframed as a natural machine whose structure is preserved in each of its parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-03","text":"The difference between nature and art no longer concerns the presence of mechanism, but the continuity of mechanism throughout composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-04","text":"Infinite divisibility is transformed from an abstract property into an actual, dynamic, and expressive subdivision of each material portion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-05","text":"The smallest part is not a term of reduction, but an internal world in which several levels of organized reality are concentrated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-06","text":"The generative movement proceeds from recursive machinicity to universal expression, then from universal expression to the ontological densification of matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:SP-07","text":"The closure produced is negative and recursive: no material analysis encounters a final element that is simple, inert, or external to organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Organic matter is machinic down to its smallest parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Nature is distinguished from artifice by an internal continuity of machinicity, and not by the absence of mechanism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Infinite divisibility becomes an actually realized subdivision endowed with an architectural function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Each material part possesses a movement of its own that prevents matter from being reduced to inert extension.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Each material portion expresses the universe because its internal composition remains indefinitely differentiated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] The smallest part of matter contains a plurality of organized realities rather than an ultimate unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Life, animality, entelechy, and soul become internal levels of material constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Analysis cannot reach matter that is absolutely simple, homogeneous, mute, or devoid of interiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] The system converges toward an image of matter as a multiplicity of nested worlds, each level reproducing the organization of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The infinite functions as a principle of structural continuity, expression, and ontological densification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-01","text":"Machinicity first returns as a criterion for distinguishing organism from artefact, then as a general model of organized matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:D5","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-02","text":"Recursivity migrates from the preservation of the machine in the parts to actual subdivision and finally to the nesting of material worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-03","text":"The infinite changes function: first the compositional depth of the living, it subsequently becomes the condition of universal expression, then the absence of a terminal ontological threshold.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:D3","CH_UCIC_P_57:D4","CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-04","text":"The part ceases to be a subordinate component and successively becomes a machinic relay, an expressive unit, and an inner world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:D4","CH_UCIC_P_58:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-05","text":"The proper movement of the parts is absorbed into a broader theory in which internal activity grounds the expression of the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-06","text":"The nature-art opposition loses its terminal function when all matter is redefined as a continuum of organized structures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Absorption","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RMD-07","text":"The hierarchy creature–living being–animal–entelechy–soul does not constitute a new independent inventory, but the internal coding of material plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A3","CH_UCIC_P_58:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Absorption","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-01","text":"The example of the artificial wheel remains local: it illustrates the interruption of machinicity without by itself constituting the architecture of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-02","text":"The divine qualification of the living remains a local metaphysical attribution, whereas machinic continuity provides the transversal mechanism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_56:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-03","text":"The list of beings contained in the smallest part is local in its lexicon, but at the current scale it becomes a map of material stratification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-04","text":"The proper movement of each part and the expression of the universe are connected at the current level as two functions of one and the same dynamic architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3","CH_UCIC_P_57:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-05","text":"The distinction between artefact and organism changes scale when it becomes a distinction between interrupted matter and inwardly unlimited matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:D2","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:CGD-06","text":"The exact mechanism linking proper movement, universal expression, and soul-life remains underdetermined and cannot be treated as a current axiom.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects every machine whose ultimate parts would cease to be themselves machined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-02","text":"It rejects matter divided only in principle, without actual subdivision or internal activity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-03","text":"It rejects the isolated material unity that would exist independently of the universe it expresses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-04","text":"It rejects matter whose analysis would progressively reduce reality to an unorganized and worldless element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-05","text":"It rejects the absolute separation between matter, life, animality, and soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:GNX-06","text":"It rejects a conception in which organization would belong to the whole while the parts remained ontologically raw.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_58:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the existence of ultimate, simple, and definitively separable material units must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-02","text":"The idea that spatial or material reduction produces a reduction of organization must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-03","text":"The strict opposition between mechanism and life must be false, since machinicity constitutes the internal continuity of the living.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-04","text":"The idea that universal totality is external to each material portion must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:DBN-05","text":"Any ontology of the inert as an absolute ground upon which living forms would be added from the outside must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX4","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSA-01","text":"The system circumvents the possibility of an absolutely simple material outside where structure, life, and expression would simultaneously cease.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSA-02","text":"The force of the architecture depends on the absence of a threshold at which matter would no longer be world-bearing.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSA-03","text":"A reality whose whole would be organized but whose every part would be mute, inert, and external to organization is ontologically inadmissible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSA-04","text":"The system cannot admit purely homogeneous matter without losing both the recursivity of the machine and universal expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-01","text":"The machinic continuity of the living provides the structural model according to which each material portion can express the universe without becoming identical to the whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-01","CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_56:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-02","text":"Actual subdivision converts the organic part into an expressive unit: what first preserved the machine now preserves an active relation with the entire universe.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-03","CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_57:D1","CH_UCIC_P_57:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-03","text":"The smallest part becomes an internal world because infinity of composition, proper movement, and the plurality of beings are a single architecture with several functions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-03","CL_UCIC_22:GA-04","CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_58:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-04","text":"The descent toward the smallest is not an operation of simplification, but an ascent toward matter richer in organization and expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","CL_UCIC_22:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-05","text":"The difference between nature and art is ultimately absorbed into a difference between interrupted composition and composition that indefinitely reproduces the world in its parts.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-02","CL_UCIC_22:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_56:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-06","text":"Universal expression simultaneously requires internal differentiation and the non-separation of whole and part.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-04","CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_57:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:XD-07","text":"The cluster produces an ontology in which organization is neither a global property nor a local addition, but a recursive propagation without a final term.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-01","CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","CL_UCIC_22:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-01","text":"Matter becomes a continuum of internal mediations rather than a homogeneous substrate composed of ultimate units.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-02","text":"The real is reclassified as a totality distributed in its parts, in which each unit possesses a structural perspective on the whole without abolishing its differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-03","text":"Causality is no longer primarily an external transmission: it becomes the effect of an internal organization that renders each portion expressive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_57:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-04","text":"The history of material composition is replaced by a depth without a final level, where each analysis reproduces the structure instead of exhausting it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-05","text":"The knowing subject does not discover a simple ground by descending into matter; it encounters a proliferation of organized levels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:BSD-06","text":"The conceptual strategy consists in displacing every reductive objection to a level at which it becomes further proof of internal complexity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-01","text":"Machinic part → internal subdivision → proper movement → expression of the whole → new qualification of the part as world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-02","text":"Every attempt to reduce matter to a terminal unit renews the discovery of an organized plurality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-03","text":"Recursion changes phase when the natural machine ceases to be merely a model of the living and becomes the schema of all matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-04","text":"The conceptual attractor is distributed totality: the whole is present in the parts, but only in the form of internal differentiations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-05","text":"The infinite acts as an operator of escalation: each removed level reveals a deeper level of composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:RLE-06","text":"The terminal loop transforms the absence of an ultimate term into a positive result: not finding an outside of organization confirms the continuity of the system.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B01","text":"Posit an organized body as a natural machine rather than as a perfected artefact.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B02","text":"Decompose the machine and distinguish artificial interruption from the organic preservation of machinicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B03","text":"Extend this preservation to matter by replacing potential divisibility with endless actual subdivision.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A2","CH_UCIC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B04","text":"Attribute to each part a movement of its own so that subdivision does not produce an inert multiplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B05","text":"Convert internal multiplicity into expressive power: each portion becomes a site of the presence of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:D3","CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B06","text":"Generalize this structure down to the smallest part, where multiplicity becomes world, life, animality, entelechy, and soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:A4","CH_UCIC_P_58:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B07","text":"Produce an ontology without a simple element, without terminal inert matter, and without a stable separation between totality and part.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:AFM-B01","text":"Functional artefact → analysis of parts → interruption of machinicity → reframing of the living as a recursive natural machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:AFM-B02","text":"Recursive machine → actually subdivided matter → proper movement → universal expression of each portion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_57:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:AFM-B03","text":"Universal expression → internal world in the smallest part → ontological densification → exclusion of all terminal material simplicity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_58:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-01","text":"The nature-art boundary is replaced by a mapping of regimes of internal composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-02","text":"Matter is reclassified as a dynamic network of parts, rather than as homogeneous extension that is merely divisible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-03","text":"The part becomes a complete scale of analysis: component, local organism, expressive unit, and internal world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_58:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-04","text":"Smallness is requalified as ontological densification rather than as a diminution of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-05","text":"The infinite becomes a method of structural mapping: it designates the continuation of levels rather than mere magnitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_57:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MME-06","text":"The false opposition between unity and totality collapses in favor of a totality differentially repeated in each unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are the living body, the artificial machine, the material portion, and the smallest part containing a world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] The determining mechanism is the recursive preservation of organization, articulated with actual subdivision and the proper movement of the parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The argument neutralizes every reduction by transforming the analysis of parts into a demonstration of their organizational richness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The real is an actual, dynamic multiplicity without a final level of composition, in which time does not lead to material closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_56:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form performs its thesis by repeating the same gesture: descend toward the part and produce more structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_58:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FL-01","text":"Universal expression is posited as a consequence of subdivision and movement, but the precise mediation between these functions remains undemonstrated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FL-02","text":"The actual infinity of composition oscillates between a strong ontological thesis and a divisibility without an ultimate term whose status remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_57:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FL-03","text":"The divine qualification provides a metaphysical guarantee, but the architecture operates above all through machinic continuity and internal organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:FL-04","text":"The passage from a determinate smallest part to an assertion concerning all matter constitutes a generalizing bridge that is not fully explicated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MP-01","text":"The natural machine becomes the general schema of matter when machinicity ceases to characterize only the living.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_58:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MP-02","text":"Divisibility passes from a geometric property to a dynamic condition of universal expression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MP-03","text":"The part passes from organic component to material microcosm, which reverses the conceptual function of smallness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_58:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Mutating","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MP-04","text":"The negation of the simple element is transformed into a positive proposition: every absence of an ultimate term becomes a production of internal worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_58:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a recursive machine without a material outside, each part reproducing an organization without being conflated with the whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a local position in a distributed totality, confronted not with a simple ground but with a proliferation of internal worlds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:HSI-03","text":"Time is not a progression toward a final level: it is the indefinite reproduction of structure through the parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_57:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:HSI-04","text":"Conceptual navigation consists in following the levels of composition, while escape from the system is rendered impossible by the absence of an inert outside.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_56:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B01","text":"The current axioms suffice to reconstruct the complete movement: recursive machinicity, actual subdivision, proper movement, universal expression, and internal world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction preserves the mutation of scale whereby the living first serves as an exemplary case, then as a model for all matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_57:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indeterminacy principally concerns the mediation between proper movement, universal expression, entelechy, and soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_57:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence depends on a double reading of the infinite: the actual continuation of composition and the absence of a simple material term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_56:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_58:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B05","text":"Compression is sufficient if it preserves the central attractor: every reduction of matter reproduces a deeper organization instead of producing a raw element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_58:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_58:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_22@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_22:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 64–66","context":"Proposition 64 · Proposition 65 · Proposition 66"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 67–69","order":23,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_59","CH_UCIC_P_60","CH_UCIC_P_61"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_23@R001","sha256":"07df026b7ee950f35387a730fa33caa52904d370f99f8d21808c254ee8be6ac6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-01","text":"Le cluster part de l’écart entre l’apparence d’une matière confuse ou vide et une structure réelle composée, active et différenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-02","text":"Il recadre toute portion matérielle comme une totalité organisée dont les parties reproduisent le principe d’organisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-03","text":"La relation entre partie et totalité devient une relation d’échelle plutôt qu’une opposition ontologique stable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-04","text":"Les milieux séparateurs sont ensuite réinscrits dans la continuité matérielle : leur non-identité avec les êtres ne supprime pas leur contenance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-05","text":"L’imperceptibilité est déplacée du statut d’absence vers celui de seuil épistémique déterminant la visibilité d’une présence réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-06","text":"L’apparence de chaos est finalement produite par une perception insuffisamment résolue qui agrège des êtres pourtant distincts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-07","text":"Le mouvement est récursif et cumulatif : organisation interne, contenance invisible et compression perceptive convergent vers une ontologie de plénitude organisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-08","text":"La clôture locale consiste à rendre indisponibles la matière simple, le milieu vide et le chaos réel sans fournir un terme positif ultime à l’analyse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Toute portion de matière peut être comprise comme une totalité organisée, et non comme une masse indifférenciée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’organisation interne se reproduit dans les parties de la totalité à des degrés successifs de petitesse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La distinction entre partie et totalité cesse d’être absolue dès lors que chaque partie peut devenir une totalité de même type.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Un milieu interposé n’est pas un être identique à ce qu’il sépare, mais il n’est pas pour autant vide de ce contenu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] La présence réelle peut subsister sous une forme imperceptible pour l’observateur humain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] La perception indistincte doit être interprétée comme une compression d’une multiplicité réelle plutôt que comme la preuve d’une indistinction ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] L’univers n’est ni stérile, ni mort, ni réellement chaotique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] La matière forme un plénum d’activités différenciées dont les niveaux d’organisation excèdent toute perception immédiate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] La division matérielle ne conduit jamais, dans le cadre courant, à un élément absolument simple ou dépourvu de structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Le système converge vers une image de plénitude organisée où toute apparence de vide ou de chaos est reconduite à une résolution perceptive insuffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-01","text":"La récursivité revient d’abord comme répétition de l’organisation dans les parties, puis mute en principe général de continuité du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-02","text":"Le jardin et l’étang sont des modèles locaux qui sont absorbés dans une structure plus abstraite : toute portion matérielle devient un composé organisé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-03","text":"La relation partie-totalité se déplace vers la relation contenant-contenu, où la séparation spatiale conserve une présence interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-04","text":"L’imperceptibilité passe d’une propriété des contenus subtils à une théorie générale de la perception comme seuil de résolution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-05","text":"La confusion inverse sa valence : d’apparence possible du monde, elle devient effet produit par la limitation du discernement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-06","text":"La petitesse ne diminue plus seulement l’importance d’une partie ; elle devient compatible avec une totalité organisée et ontologiquement pleine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-07","text":"Les notions de stérilité, de mort et de chaos disparaissent comme descriptions du réel après avoir été recodées en erreurs d’apparence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-01","text":"[Local] Les images du jardin, de l’étang, des plantes et des poissons restent des dispositifs exemplaires de visualisation et ne constituent pas, à elles seules, l’architecture courante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-02","text":"[Local] Les exemples de terre, d’air et d’eau spécifient des milieux particuliers, mais leur fonction courante est de démontrer qu’un intervalle apparent peut contenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-03","text":"[Scale-shift] La répétition de l’organisation dans les parties change d’échelle lorsqu’elle devient la condition d’une matière sans terme simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-04","text":"[Relational] La non-identité du milieu et de son contenu devient une médiation entre séparation phénoménale et continuité ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-05","text":"[Catalytic] La limitation perceptive relie les deux machines précédentes : elle rend invisible la structure récursive et transforme la plénitude en confusion apparente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-06","text":"[Absorbed] Les oppositions simples entre partie et tout, vide et présence, ordre et chaos sont dépassées par une architecture de niveaux et de seuils.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut une matière homogène dont les parties seraient dépourvues d’organisation interne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une division matérielle produise une unité absolument simple et indivisible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut que l’espace interposé soit un intervalle vide entre les êtres naturels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que l’imperceptible puisse être assimilé au non-existant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut que la confusion sensible, la distance ou le manque de discernement constituent des preuves de désordre ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut enfin toute région véritablement morte, stérile ou inarticulée de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’hypothèse d’un élément matériel dernier dont l’intérieur serait homogène.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-02","text":"Elle disqualifie un modèle dans lequel l’organisation serait ajoutée extérieurement à des agrégats primitivement inorganisés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-03","text":"Elle disqualifie un modèle où la séparation spatiale aurait pour conséquence une absence réelle du contenu séparé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-04","text":"Elle disqualifie une épistémologie qui ferait de la perception humaine la mesure ultime de la composition naturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-05","text":"Elle disqualifie enfin l’équivalence entre indistinction phénoménale et indifférenciation réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSA-01","text":"L’absence la plus profonde est celle d’un dehors matériel absolument vide, séparé ou dépourvu de contenu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité indisponible est celle d’un point final où la pluralité organisée disparaîtrait dans une matière simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSA-03","text":"Le système contourne une ontologie où l’ordre serait local, la vie discontinue et la confusion irréductiblement réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSA-04","text":"Sa force dépend de l’absence d’un critère perceptif capable de coïncider immédiatement avec la structure totale du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-01","text":"La récursivité des parties et la contenance des milieux produisent une continuité matérielle où aucune séparation locale ne suffit à établir un dehors ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-02","CL_UCIC_23:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_59:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-02","text":"La matière ne se contente pas d’être composée de parties organisées ; elle conserve ses organisations à travers les milieux qui semblent les interrompre.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-02","CL_UCIC_23:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_59:D3","CH_UCIC_P_60:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-03","text":"La perception confuse est l’effet commun de deux limites : elle ne résout ni l’emboîtement matériel ni la présence subtile des êtres dans leurs milieux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-05","CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_60:D3","CH_UCIC_P_61:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-04","text":"L’apparence de chaos devient ainsi le mode phénoménal d’une plénitude trop finement différenciée pour être immédiatement décomposée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","CL_UCIC_23:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_61:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_61:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-05","text":"La distinction entre ordre et chaos est déplacée vers la qualité de l’accès perceptif sans être supprimée au niveau ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","CL_UCIC_23:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_61:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-06","text":"L’exclusion simultanée de l’élément simple, du milieu vide et du chaos réel transforme une série de négations locales en théorie positive de la plénitude organisée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-08","CL_UCIC_23:GA-09","CL_UCIC_23:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-01","text":"La matière devient un continuum de compositions emboîtées dont les frontières sont des changements d’échelle plutôt que des coupures absolues.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-02","text":"Le réel est ontologiquement plus riche que toute scène perceptive qui le présente comme homogène, vide ou chaotique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-03","text":"La perception n’est pas une fenêtre neutre sur la structure ; elle opère une réduction de résolution qui convertit la différenciation en mouvement indistinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-04","text":"L’ordre n’est pas ajouté à une matière première désorganisée ; il est présupposé comme propriété récursive de toute composition matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-05","text":"La causalité descriptive se renverse : ce qui semblait être chaos ou vacuité doit être expliqué par les limites de l’accès plutôt que par un défaut du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-06","text":"Le statut du sujet devient celui d’un observateur structurellement situé sous le niveau de résolution nécessaire pour totaliser ce qu’il perçoit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-01","text":"Portion matérielle → totalité organisée → parties organisées → nouvelles totalités → impossibilité d’un terme simple.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-02","text":"Milieu interposé → contenu non identique → présence subtile → imperceptibilité → maintien de la présence au-delà du visible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-03","text":"Apparence confuse → limitation perceptive → compression d’une multiplicité → différenciation réelle → exclusion du chaos ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-04","text":"La répétition du même schème ne ramène pas à une identité fixe : elle augmente la portée du principe, de la partie matérielle à l’univers entier.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est une plénitude organisée qui absorbe successivement la matière, les milieux et les apparences perceptives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-06","text":"La boucle terminale reconduit toute apparence négative à une insuffisance de discernement, puis reconduit cette insuffisance à une structure réelle plus fine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B01","text":"Toute portion est posée comme totalité organisée ; toute partie de cette totalité est ensuite traitée selon le même principe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B02","text":"La récursivité interdit que la division fournisse un terme simple et convertit l’analyse en approfondissement de la composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B03","text":"Les milieux interposés sont introduits comme des séparations non vides, où la présence persiste sous une forme subtile.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B04","text":"La faible résolution perceptive agrège les compositions et les présences en une apparence de chaos ou de vacuité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B05","text":"La reconstruction positive rétablit une multiplicité ordonnée et transforme les négations successives en ontologie de plénitude organisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AFM-B01","text":"Apparence de matière homogène ou de chaos → recadrage en totalité organisée → récursivité des parties → contenance des milieux → imperceptibilité structurale → compression perceptive → plénitude différenciée → exclusion de la matière simple, du vide et du chaos réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-01","text":"La matière est reclassée comme réseau de totalités organisées plutôt que comme substrat homogène.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-02","text":"L’espace interposé est reclassé comme milieu contenant, ce qui effondre l’opposition entre séparation spatiale et absence ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-03","text":"Le visible devient un niveau de résolution parmi d’autres et cesse de fournir la carte complète de la composition naturelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-04","text":"Le chaos est déplacé de la carte de l’être vers la carte des conditions de perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-05","text":"La distinction partie-totalité, présence-absence et ordre-chaos est remplacée par une cartographie de niveaux, de médiations et de seuils de discernement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les plantes, les poissons, la terre, l’air et l’eau servent de configurations visibles pour exposer une composition et une contenance qui débordent leur apparence immédiate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] La structure courante articule emboîtement matériel, médiation des milieux et agrégation perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] L’analyse doit changer de résolution sans changer de principe explicatif : le même schème d’organisation est réappliqué aux parties et aux apparences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est supposé continuellement organisé, rempli et différencié, sans terme simple ni région véritablement morte.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] Le texte accomplit son propre principe en reconduisant des analogies locales vers une architecture générale sans abandonner la récursivité qui les a produites.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FL-01","text":"La plénitude ontologique est affirmée comme universelle alors que la structure exacte des contenus imperceptibles reste sous-déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FL-02","text":"Le système dépend d’une extension récursive du principe d’organisation qui est structurellement requise mais non démontrée à chaque niveau.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FL-03","text":"Les modèles du jardin et de l’étang doivent être suffisamment littéraux pour porter l’argument, mais suffisamment analogiques pour ne pas être pris comme identités matérielles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FL-04","text":"La distinction entre ordre réel et confusion perceptive est productive, mais elle rend le système dépendant d’une ontologie que la perception ne peut vérifier directement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MP-01","text":"La partie mute en totalité lorsqu’elle reçoit le même statut organisationnel que le composé dont elle provient.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MP-02","text":"Le milieu mute d’intervalle séparateur en médiation contenant lorsque la non-identité cesse d’impliquer l’absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MP-03","text":"La confusion mute de propriété apparente du monde en effet de compression perceptive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MP-04","text":"La négation du chaos mute en principe positif : tout défaut de discernement renvoie à une différenciation réelle plus profonde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une machine d’emboîtement où chaque totalité contient des organisations supplémentaires et où aucune frontière matérielle ne clôt définitivement la composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient un observateur à résolution limitée, placé devant une plénitude dont il ne perçoit que des agrégats, des seuils et des effets de distance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système n’est pas celui d’une genèse depuis le chaos, mais celui d’une différenciation continue d’un réel toujours déjà rempli.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée méthodologique consiste à augmenter la résolution conceptuelle sans attendre qu’une perception immédiate fournisse un terme final.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige trois axiomes : toute matière est organisée, toute séparation peut conserver une présence, et toute confusion peut provenir d’une résolution perceptive insuffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B02","text":"Ces axiomes suffisent à produire le mouvement du composé vers ses parties, des parties vers les milieux, puis des milieux vers la perception du chaos.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B03","text":"La reconstruction reste indéterminée quant au statut exact de la répétition et au mécanisme précis de la contenance subtile.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence courante dépend de la non-confusion entre modèle analogique et identité littérale, ainsi que de l’extension récursive du principe aux niveaux non observés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B05","text":"La compression demeure fidèle tant qu’elle conserve la double opération génératrice : produire une plénitude organisée et déplacer toute apparence négative vers les limites de la perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195858006296Z_78e3131b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 67–69","source_sha256":"07df026b7ee950f35387a730fa33caa52904d370f99f8d21808c254ee8be6ac6","sha256":"5cc0ea6462c32c5f02774d227ce2e0e7d10e57d71c870ae3724464576c1b4627","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:58:58.010428+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-01","text":"The cluster begins from the gap between the appearance of confused or empty matter and a real structure that is composite, active, and differentiated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-02","text":"It reframes every material portion as an organized whole whose parts reproduce the principle of organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-03","text":"The relation between part and whole becomes a relation of scale rather than a stable ontological opposition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-04","text":"Separating media are then reinscribed within material continuity: their non-identity with beings does not eliminate their containment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-05","text":"Imperceptibility is shifted from the status of absence to that of an epistemic threshold determining the visibility of a real presence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-06","text":"The appearance of chaos is ultimately produced by insufficiently resolved perception that aggregates beings which are nevertheless distinct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-07","text":"The movement is recursive and cumulative: internal organization, invisible containment, and perceptual compression converge toward an ontology of organized plenitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AS-08","text":"The local closure consists in rendering unavailable simple matter, the empty medium, and real chaos without providing an ultimate positive term for analysis.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every portion of matter can be understood as an organized whole, and not as an undifferentiated mass.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Internal organization reproduces itself in the parts of the whole at successive degrees of smallness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The distinction between part and whole ceases to be absolute insofar as each part can become a whole of the same type.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] An interposed medium is not a being identical to what it separates, but is not thereby empty of that content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Real presence can subsist in a form imperceptible to the human observer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Indistinct perception must be interpreted as a compression of a real multiplicity rather than as proof of ontological indistinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] The universe is neither sterile, nor dead, nor truly chaotic.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Matter forms a plenum of differentiated activities whose levels of organization exceed all immediate perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Material division never leads, within the present framework, to an absolutely simple or structureless element.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The system converges toward an image of organized plenitude in which every appearance of emptiness or chaos is traced back to insufficient perceptual resolution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-01","text":"Recursivity first returns as repetition of organization in the parts, then mutates into a general principle of the continuity of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-02","text":"The garden and the pond are local models absorbed into a more abstract structure: every material portion becomes an organized composite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-03","text":"The part-whole relation shifts toward the container-content relation, in which spatial separation preserves an internal presence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-04","text":"Imperceptibility passes from a property of subtle contents to a general theory of perception as a threshold of resolution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-05","text":"Confusion reverses its valence: from a possible appearance of the world, it becomes an effect produced by the limitation of discernment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-06","text":"Smallness no longer merely diminishes the importance of a part; it becomes compatible with an organized and ontologically full whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RMD-07","text":"The notions of sterility, death, and chaos disappear as descriptions of reality after having been recoded as errors of appearance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The images of the garden, the pond, plants, and fish remain exemplary devices of visualization and do not by themselves constitute the current architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-02","text":"[Local] The examples of earth, air, and water specify particular media, but their current function is to demonstrate that an apparent interval can contain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-03","text":"[Scale-shift] The repetition of organization in the parts changes scale when it becomes the condition of matter without a simple term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-04","text":"[Relational] The non-identity of the medium and its content becomes a mediation between phenomenal separation and ontological continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-05","text":"[Catalytic] Perceptual limitation connects the two preceding machines: it renders recursive structure invisible and transforms plenitude into apparent confusion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:CGD-06","text":"[Absorbed] Simple oppositions between part and whole, emptiness and presence, order and chaos are surpassed by an architecture of levels and thresholds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes homogeneous matter whose parts would lack internal organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that material division produces an absolutely simple and indivisible unit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that interposed space is an empty interval between natural beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that the imperceptible can be assimilated to the non-existent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the possibility that sensible confusion, distance, or lack of discernment constitute evidence of ontological disorder.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:GNX-06","text":"Finally, it excludes every truly dead, sterile, or unarticulated region of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, the hypothesis of a final material element whose interior would be homogeneous must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-02","text":"It disqualifies a model in which organization would be added externally to primitively unorganized aggregates.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-03","text":"It disqualifies a model in which spatial separation would result in a real absence of the separated content.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-04","text":"It disqualifies an epistemology that would make human perception the ultimate measure of natural composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:DBN-05","text":"Finally, it disqualifies the equivalence between phenomenal indistinction and real undifferentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSA-01","text":"The deepest absence is that of an absolutely empty, separate, or contentless material outside.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSA-02","text":"The unavailable possibility is that of an endpoint at which organized plurality would disappear into simple matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSA-03","text":"The system avoids an ontology in which order would be local, life discontinuous, and confusion irreducibly real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSA-04","text":"Its force depends on the absence of a perceptual criterion capable of immediately coinciding with the total structure of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-01","text":"The recursivity of parts and the containment of media produce a material continuity in which no local separation suffices to establish an ontological outside.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-02","CL_UCIC_23:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_59:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-02","text":"Matter is not merely composed of organized parts; it preserves its organizations through the media that seem to interrupt them.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-02","CL_UCIC_23:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_59:D3","CH_UCIC_P_60:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-03","text":"Confused perception is the common effect of two limits: it resolves neither material nesting nor the subtle presence of beings in their media.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-05","CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_60:D3","CH_UCIC_P_61:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-04","text":"The appearance of chaos thus becomes the phenomenal mode of a plenitude too finely differentiated to be immediately decomposed.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","CL_UCIC_23:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_61:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_61:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-05","text":"The distinction between order and chaos is shifted toward the quality of perceptual access without being eliminated at the ontological level.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","CL_UCIC_23:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_61:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:XD-06","text":"The simultaneous exclusion of the simple element, the empty medium, and real chaos transforms a series of local negations into a positive theory of organized plenitude.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-08","CL_UCIC_23:GA-09","CL_UCIC_23:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_61:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-01","text":"Matter becomes a continuum of nested compositions whose boundaries are changes of scale rather than absolute breaks.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-02","text":"Reality is ontologically richer than any perceptual scene that presents it as homogeneous, empty, or chaotic.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-03","text":"Perception is not a neutral window onto structure; it performs a reduction of resolution that converts differentiation into indistinct movement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-04","text":"Order is not added to disorganized prime matter; it is presupposed as a recursive property of every material composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-05","text":"Descriptive causality is reversed: what seemed to be chaos or emptiness must be explained by the limits of access rather than by a defect of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:BSD-06","text":"The status of the subject becomes that of an observer structurally situated below the level of resolution necessary to totalize what it perceives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-01","text":"Material portion → organized whole → organized parts → new wholes → impossibility of a simple term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-02","text":"Interposed medium → non-identical content → subtle presence → imperceptibility → maintenance of presence beyond the visible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-03","text":"Confused appearance → perceptual limitation → compression of a multiplicity → real differentiation → exclusion of ontological chaos.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-04","text":"The repetition of the same schema does not return to a fixed identity: it increases the scope of the principle, from the material part to the entire universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is an organized plenitude that successively absorbs matter, media, and perceptual appearances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:RLE-06","text":"The terminal loop traces every negative appearance back to an insufficiency of discernment, then traces this insufficiency back to a finer real structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B01","text":"Every portion is posited as an organized whole; every part of this whole is then treated according to the same principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B02","text":"Recursivity prevents division from supplying a simple term and converts analysis into a deepening of composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B03","text":"Interposed media are introduced as non-empty separations, in which presence persists in a subtle form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B04","text":"Low perceptual resolution aggregates compositions and presences into an appearance of chaos or emptiness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FGS-B05","text":"Positive reconstruction restores an ordered multiplicity and transforms successive negations into an ontology of organized plenitude.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:AFM-B01","text":"Appearance of homogeneous matter or chaos → reframing as organized whole → recursivity of parts → containment of media → structural imperceptibility → perceptual compression → differentiated plenitude → exclusion of simple matter, emptiness, and real chaos.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-01","text":"Matter is reclassified as a network of organized wholes rather than as a homogeneous substrate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-02","text":"Interposed space is reclassified as a containing medium, which collapses the opposition between spatial separation and ontological absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-03","text":"The visible becomes one level of resolution among others and ceases to provide the complete map of natural composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-04","text":"Chaos is shifted from the map of being to the map of the conditions of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MME-05","text":"The distinction part-whole, presence-absence, and order-chaos is replaced by a cartography of levels, mediations, and thresholds of discernment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Plants, fish, earth, air, and water serve as visible configurations for setting forth a composition and containment that exceed their immediate appearance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] The current structure articulates material nesting, mediation by media, and perceptual aggregation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Analysis must change resolution without changing explanatory principle: the same schema of organization is reapplied to parts and appearances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Reality is assumed to be continuously organized, full, and differentiated, without a simple term or a truly dead region.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The text performs its own principle by tracing local analogies back to a general architecture without abandoning the recursivity that produced them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FL-01","text":"Ontological plenitude is affirmed as universal while the exact structure of imperceptible contents remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FL-02","text":"The system depends on a recursive extension of the principle of organization that is structurally required but not demonstrated at every level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FL-03","text":"The models of the garden and the pond must be sufficiently literal to carry the argument, but sufficiently analogical not to be taken as material identities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:FL-04","text":"The distinction between real order and perceptual confusion is productive, but it makes the system dependent on an ontology that perception cannot directly verify.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MP-01","text":"The part mutates into a whole when it receives the same organizational status as the composite from which it derives.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MP-02","text":"The medium mutates from a separating interval into a containing mediation when non-identity ceases to imply absence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_60:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MP-03","text":"Confusion mutates from an apparent property of the world into an effect of perceptual compression.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MP-04","text":"The negation of chaos mutates into a positive principle: every deficiency of discernment refers back to a deeper real differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a machine of nesting in which every whole contains additional organizations and in which no material boundary definitively closes composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes an observer of limited resolution, placed before a plenitude of which it perceives only aggregates, thresholds, and effects of distance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system is not that of a genesis from chaos, but that of a continuous differentiation of a reality always already full.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:HSI-04","text":"The only methodological escape consists in increasing conceptual resolution without awaiting immediate perception to provide a final term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B01","text":"Minimal reconstruction requires three axioms: all matter is organized, every separation can preserve a presence, and every confusion can result from insufficient perceptual resolution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B02","text":"These axioms suffice to produce the movement from the composite to its parts, from the parts to the media, then from the media to the perception of chaos.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction remains indeterminate as to the exact status of repetition and the precise mechanism of subtle containment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B04","text":"Current coherence depends on not confusing analogical model and literal identity, as well as on the recursive extension of the principle to unobserved levels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_59:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B05","text":"The compression remains faithful so long as it preserves the double generative operation: producing an organized plenitude and shifting every negative appearance toward the limits of perception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_61:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_23@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_23:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 67–69","context":"Proposition 67 · Proposition 68 · Proposition 69"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 70–72","order":24,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_62","CH_UCIC_P_63","CH_UCIC_P_64"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_24@R001","sha256":"95f4678ef4db830a8890a79f4f520a422fa2b98d69240fa46efe483e01b49a50","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-01","text":"Le problème courant consiste à déterminer comment une unité vivante peut demeurer une totalité tout en contenant plusieurs centres vitaux et en subissant un renouvellement matériel permanent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_62:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-02","text":"L’unité organique est recadrée comme une hiérarchie récursive de vivants subordonnés, non comme une totalité simple composée de parties inertes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_62:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-03","text":"Le flux continuel des parties interdit de fonder l’identité sur la possession permanente d’une matière déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A1","CH_UCIC_P_63:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-04","text":"La continuité du vivant est alors déplacée vers l’organisation et la transformation graduelle plutôt que vers la conservation numérique de ses composants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:D4","CH_UCIC_P_64:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-05","text":"Le mouvement global produit une ontologie dynamique où pluralité interne, flux matériel et identité persistante deviennent des dimensions compatibles d’un même processus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_64:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-06","text":"La clôture produite n’est pas une matière ultime, mais la limite ontologique qui sépare la corporéité nécessaire des créatures du détachement absolu réservé à Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","CH_UCIC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Toute totalité vivante possède une entéléchie dominante sans supprimer la vitalité de ses constituants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Les membres d’un vivant sont eux-mêmes susceptibles de constituer des vivants relativement autonomes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La domination entéléchique désigne un principe d’organisation hiérarchique plutôt qu’un droit de propriété sur une matière fixe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Aucun corps ne conserve définitivement une portion matérielle affectée à une âme déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Tous les corps sont soumis à un flux perpétuel d’entrée et de sortie des parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] L’identité corporelle repose sur la continuité d’une organisation plutôt que sur l’identité permanente de la matière composée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] La continuité de l’âme est produite par une transformation graduelle qui ne supprime pas instantanément toute organisation corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Toute âme créée demeure liée à une forme de corporéité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Le détachement absolu du corps constitue une exception réservée à Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Chaque niveau du vivant peut reproduire la structure d’une unité dominante contenant une pluralité de vivants subordonnés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-01","text":"La récurrence de l’entéléchie passe d’un principe interne d’unité à une fonction de hiérarchisation récursive des niveaux du vivant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-02","text":"La pluralité des centres vitaux conserve sa fonction, mais cesse d’impliquer une possession matérielle stable lorsque le flux corporel devient déterminant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:D2","CH_UCIC_P_63:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-03","text":"Le corps migre du statut de masse ou de contenant vers celui de processus matériel continuellement renouvelé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-04","text":"La persistance de l’identité se déplace de la conservation des parties vers la continuité organique de leur transformation graduelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_64:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-05","text":"La métamorphose absorbe la fonction explicative du changement corporel tandis que la transmigration est éliminée comme modèle concurrent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_64:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-06","text":"La séparation absolue ne disparaît pas, mais devient une transformation terminale de la structure : elle est retirée aux créatures et conservée comme attribut divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:D4","CH_UCIC_P_64:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-01","text":"La distinction explicite entre plantes et animaux reste locale ; au niveau courant, elle est absorbée dans une architecture commune de vivants emboîtés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-02","text":"La réfutation d’une interprétation particulière de la matière propre à l’âme est locale ; son effet courant est la disqualification générale de toute identité fondée sur la fixité matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-03","text":"La gradualité du changement corporel est locale dans sa formulation, mais devient au niveau courant le mécanisme temporel de compatibilité entre flux et persistance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-04","text":"L’exception divine demeure une limite particulière, mais elle stabilise à l’échelle courante la frontière entre l’ontologie des créatures incorporées et celle d’un être absolument détaché.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A8","CH_UCIC_P_64:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-05","text":"La structure de niveau courant relie les trois machines inférieures : hiérarchie des vivants, flux de la matière et continuité graduelle de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-06","text":"Le modèle du corps comme stock matériel fixe devient obsolète, car il ne peut rendre compte simultanément de la récursivité vitale et du renouvellement corporel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_63:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une unité vivante soit une totalité simple composée de parties absolument inertes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une âme soit propriétaire pour toujours d’une portion matérielle déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut qu’une identité corporelle soit garantie par la conservation numérique des mêmes parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut qu’une âme créée puisse être entièrement séparée de toute organisation corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut de confondre métamorphose progressive et transfert instantané d’une âme entre des corps distincts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’idée d’un organisme expliqué par un principe vital unique opérant sur des parties sans intériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que soit fausse toute ontologie des corps comme agrégats matériellement clos et durablement individualisés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie le dualisme qui ferait de l’âme un sujet autonome et du corps une enveloppe extérieure remplaçable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:DBN-04","text":"Il rend impossible une ontologie plate où tous les vivants auraient le même statut et où aucune asymétrie d’organisation ne pourrait apparaître.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSA-01","text":"Le système contourne la possibilité d’une clôture matérielle définitive autour d’un sujet vivant : toute totalité reste ouverte par ses parties et par leur renouvellement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_63:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSA-02","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un corps ultime qui serait simplement matériel, inerte et extérieur à toute autre vie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSA-03","text":"La possibilité ontologiquement indisponible est celle d’une âme finie sans corps, autonome à l’égard de toute organisation et libre de migrer entre des sujets.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-01","text":"La hiérarchie des vivants ne peut fonctionner comme une hiérarchie de propriétés fixes ; elle devient une hiérarchie de fonctions organisatrices traversée par le flux matériel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-01","CL_UCIC_24:GA-02","CL_UCIC_24:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7","CH_UCIC_P_63:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-02","text":"Le renouvellement matériel ne détruit pas l’unité du vivant parce que cette unité est transférée de la matière possédée vers la continuité de l’organisation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-04","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_63:D2","CH_UCIC_P_63:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-03","text":"La pluralité interne cesse d’être une menace pour l’identité dès lors que chaque changement de niveau est réglé par une continuité graduelle plutôt que par une substitution de sujet.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-02","CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_62:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_64:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-04","text":"Le refus de la transmigration est produit par la conjonction de deux exclusions : aucune âme créée n’est sans corps et aucun changement corporel n’est une rupture totale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_64:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-05","text":"La distinction entre créature et Dieu devient la borne terminale d’une architecture où l’incorporation est universelle pour les êtres finis mais non pour l’être divin.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","CL_UCIC_24:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_64:D3","CH_UCIC_P_64:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-06","text":"L’unité du vivant est finalement définie comme une coordination récursive de multiplicités en transformation, et non comme l’identité simple d’un substrat.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-01","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_62:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-01","text":"Le vivant devient un processus récursif d’individuation : chaque totalité est une unité organisatrice, une multiplicité interne et un niveau subordonné d’une totalité possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-01","CL_UCIC_24:GA-02","CL_UCIC_24:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_62:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_62:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-02","text":"L’identité n’est plus une conservation de matière, mais une persistance fonctionnelle à travers le remplacement progressif de ses supports corporels.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-05","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_63:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_63:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-03","text":"Le sujet vivant est reclassé comme une trajectoire organique continue plutôt que comme une âme transportable entre des corps préexistants.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_64:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-04","text":"Le temps pertinent du vivant est un temps de mutation graduelle, où la continuité est produite par l’absence de rupture instantanée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-05","text":"La méthode d’identification doit suivre les relations d’organisation, de transformation et de subordination plutôt que rechercher un matériau invariant ou un sujet désincarné.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-03","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-01","text":"Entéléchie dominante → membres vivants → entéléchies internes → nouvelle unité dominante : la structure se reproduit à chaque niveau sans atteindre de terme matériel ultime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-02","text":"Flux matériel → impossibilité de possession fixe → déplacement vers l’organisation → nécessité d’une continuité graduelle : la non-fixité renforce l’architecture au lieu de la dissoudre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-03","text":"Métamorphose → conservation organique → refus de la transmigration → maintien de l’incorporation : le changement devient le mécanisme même de la persistance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-04","text":"La répétition du motif unité-multiplicité change de phase lorsqu’elle rencontre le flux : elle passe d’une hiérarchie statique à une hiérarchie processuelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_63:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est une totalité vivante ouverte, récursive et incorporée, dont l’unité ne cesse d’être produite par la transformation de ses composants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B01","text":"Poser une unité vivante dominée par une entéléchie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B02","text":"Déployer cette unité en membres qui sont eux-mêmes des vivants dotés de principes internes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B03","text":"Introduire le flux perpétuel des parties afin d’interdire toute fermeture matérielle de l’unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B04","text":"Remplacer la permanence du substrat par la persistance d’une organisation traversant la transformation graduelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B05","text":"Déduire que la métamorphose conserve l’identité tandis que la transmigration est exclue comme rupture sans continuité organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B06","text":"Produire une architecture où toute créature finie est incorporée, où toute totalité contient une multiplicité et où seul Dieu constitue la limite du détachement absolu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AFM-B01","text":"Unité organique → pluralité de vivants internes → flux matériel → impossibilité de la possession fixe → continuité organisationnelle → transformation graduelle → exclusion de la transmigration → incorporation universelle des créatures → exception divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_64:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AFM-B02","text":"La trajectoire réelle va d’une théorie de l’unité à une ontologie de la persistance processuelle, puis d’une critique de la matière fixe à une hiérarchie récursive des modes d’incorporation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-01","text":"Le corps est reclassé comme une totalité de totalités organiques, et non comme un agrégat matériel contenant une âme extérieure à ses parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-02","text":"La frontière partie-totalité devient une différence de niveau fonctionnel plutôt qu’une opposition ontologique fixe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-03","text":"La distinction entre persistance et conservation matérielle devient indispensable pour penser toute identité corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-04","text":"La frontière entre changement de corps et changement de sujet est redessinée autour de la continuité organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-05","text":"La métamorphose est rendue pensable comme transformation interne d’un être, tandis que la transmigration devient une catégorie sans fonction explicative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_64:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont le corps vivant, ses membres, l’âme, les organes et les transformations animales.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont distribués dans une architecture d’emboîtement vital, de flux des parties et de continuité organisationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Le système reformule l’identité en abandonnant la propriété matérielle, la séparation âme-corps et la migration au profit de relations de niveau et de transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel vivant est un continuum de formes corporelles graduelles, sans âme finie absolument séparée et sans terme matériel ultime explicitement assigné.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit sa thèse en corrigeant les catégories de propriété, de séparation et de migration par une série d’exclusions qui reconstruit positivement la continuité organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_64:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FL-01","text":"L’unité dominante doit organiser les vivants internes sans les réduire à des parties inertes, ce qui maintient une tension constitutive entre domination et autonomie relative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_62:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FL-02","text":"L’identité doit persister alors que la matière qui la compose est continuellement remplacée ; la solution organisationnelle est affirmée, mais son critère exact demeure partiellement indéterminé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FL-03","text":"La continuité graduelle rend compatible le changement de corps et la permanence de l’âme, mais elle ne spécifie pas entièrement la nature du corps conservé à travers la transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FL-04","text":"La limite divine stabilise l’architecture tout en introduisant une asymétrie qui ne se déduit pas du seul mécanisme général de l’incorporation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation survient lorsque la multiplicité interne cesse d’être une objection à l’unité et devient son mode de constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MP-02","text":"Le second point de mutation survient lorsque le flux matériel force à dissocier l’identité corporelle de la permanence de ses parties.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation transforme le changement corporel en métamorphose continue et rend la transmigration conceptuellement excédentaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:D2","CH_UCIC_P_64:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:HSI-01","text":"La réalité vivante est implicitement une machine d’emboîtement où chaque unité est simultanément centre organisateur, totalité composée et composant d’une totalité supérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une trajectoire organique incorporée, capable de persister par transformation mais incapable, s’il est fini, de s’extraire absolument de toute corporéité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système est un temps continu de renouvellement et de métamorphose, non une succession de ruptures entre supports corporels séparés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A2","CH_UCIC_P_64:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:HSI-04","text":"Les seules formes d’échappée sont relatives : transformation graduelle, déplacement des niveaux d’organisation et, à la limite, détachement absolu réservé à Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale est suffisante si elle conserve quatre opérations : emboîter des vivants, faire circuler la matière, maintenir l’identité par transformation graduelle et réserver le détachement absolu à Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MRT-B02","text":"La cohérence du système dépend de la conversion de l’unité substantielle en unité organisationnelle ; sans cette conversion, la pluralité interne et le flux matériel deviennent incompatibles avec la persistance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_63:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne la relation précise entre l’entéléchie dominante et les centres vitaux internes, ainsi que le critère détaillé de leur continuité à travers les degrés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MRT-B04","text":"La compression reste fidèle au mouvement courant : la récursivité fournit la forme, le flux fournit la négation de la fixité, la gradualité fournit la continuité et l’exception divine fournit la borne terminale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_64:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195924167320Z_72f85fca","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 70–72","source_sha256":"95f4678ef4db830a8890a79f4f520a422fa2b98d69240fa46efe483e01b49a50","sha256":"9b552e1f2926da3c8674f04aecd7e90530664952028e86eb6a1bb2ea0cba3cb9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:59:24.171461+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-01","text":"The governing problem consists in determining how a living unity can remain a whole while containing several vital centers and undergoing permanent material renewal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_62:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-02","text":"Organic unity is reframed as a recursive hierarchy of subordinate living beings, not as a simple whole composed of inert parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_62:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-03","text":"The continual flux of parts precludes grounding identity in the permanent possession of determinate matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A1","CH_UCIC_P_63:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-04","text":"The continuity of the living being is then shifted toward organization and gradual transformation rather than toward the numerical preservation of its components.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:D4","CH_UCIC_P_64:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-05","text":"The overall movement produces a dynamic ontology in which internal plurality, material flux, and persistent identity become compatible dimensions of one and the same process.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_64:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AS-06","text":"The closure produced is not an ultimate matter, but the ontological limit that separates the necessary corporeality of creatures from the absolute detachment reserved for God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6","CH_UCIC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every living whole possesses a dominant entelechy without suppressing the vitality of its constituents.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The members of a living being are themselves capable of constituting relatively autonomous living beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Entelechial domination designates a principle of hierarchical organization rather than a right of ownership over fixed matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] No body permanently retains a material portion assigned to a determinate soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] All bodies are subject to a perpetual flux of the entry and exit of parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Bodily identity rests on the continuity of an organization rather than on the permanent identity of the matter composing it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] The continuity of the soul is produced by a gradual transformation that does not instantaneously suppress all bodily organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Every created soul remains bound to a form of corporeality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Absolute detachment from the body constitutes an exception reserved for God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Each level of the living being can reproduce the structure of a dominant unity containing a plurality of subordinate living beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-01","text":"The recurrence of entelechy shifts from an internal principle of unity to a function of recursive hierarchization of the levels of the living being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-02","text":"The plurality of vital centers retains its function, but ceases to imply stable material possession when bodily flux becomes determinative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:D2","CH_UCIC_P_63:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-03","text":"The body migrates from the status of mass or container to that of a continually renewed material process.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-04","text":"The persistence of identity shifts from the preservation of parts to the organic continuity of their gradual transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_64:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-05","text":"Metamorphosis absorbs the explanatory function of bodily change, while transmigration is eliminated as a competing model.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_64:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RMD-06","text":"Absolute separation does not disappear, but becomes a terminal transformation of the structure: it is withdrawn from creatures and retained as a divine attribute.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:D4","CH_UCIC_P_64:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-01","text":"The explicit distinction between plants and animals remains local; at the current level, it is absorbed into a common architecture of nested living beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-02","text":"The refutation of a particular interpretation of matter proper to the soul is local; its current effect is the general disqualification of every identity grounded in material fixity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-03","text":"The gradualness of bodily change is local in its formulation, but at the current level becomes the temporal mechanism of compatibility between flux and persistence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-04","text":"The divine exception remains a particular limit, but at the current scale it stabilizes the boundary between the ontology of embodied creatures and that of an absolutely detached being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:A8","CH_UCIC_P_64:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-05","text":"The current-level structure connects the three lower machines: hierarchy of living beings, flux of matter, and gradual continuity of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:CGD-06","text":"The model of the body as a fixed material stock becomes obsolete, because it cannot simultaneously account for vital recursivity and bodily renewal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_63:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a living unity is a simple whole composed of absolutely inert parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that a soul is forever the owner of a determinate material portion.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that a bodily identity is guaranteed by the numerical preservation of the same parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that a created soul can be entirely separated from every bodily organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the conflation of progressive metamorphosis with the instantaneous transfer of a soul between distinct bodies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the idea of an organism explained by a single vital principle operating upon parts without interiority must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:DBN-02","text":"Likewise, every ontology of bodies as materially closed and durably individuated aggregates must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_63:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies the dualism that would make the soul an autonomous subject and the body a replaceable external envelope.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:DBN-04","text":"It renders impossible a flat ontology in which all living beings would have the same status and in which no organizational asymmetry could emerge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSA-01","text":"The system bypasses the possibility of definitive material closure around a living subject: every whole remains open through its parts and their renewal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_63:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSA-02","text":"The structuring absence is that of an ultimate body that would be simply material, inert, and external to every other life.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSA-03","text":"The ontologically unavailable possibility is that of a finite soul without a body, autonomous with regard to every organization and free to migrate between subjects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-01","text":"The hierarchy of living beings cannot function as a hierarchy of fixed properties; it becomes a hierarchy of organizing functions traversed by material flux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-01","CL_UCIC_24:GA-02","CL_UCIC_24:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_62:A7","CH_UCIC_P_63:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-02","text":"Material renewal does not destroy the unity of the living being because that unity is transferred from possessed matter to the continuity of organization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-04","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_63:D2","CH_UCIC_P_63:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-03","text":"Internal plurality ceases to be a threat to identity insofar as every change of level is governed by gradual continuity rather than by a substitution of subject.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-02","CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_62:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_64:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-04","text":"The rejection of transmigration is produced by the conjunction of two exclusions: no created soul is without a body, and no bodily change is a total rupture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_64:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-05","text":"The distinction between creature and God becomes the terminal bound of an architecture in which embodiment is universal for finite beings but not for the divine being.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","CL_UCIC_24:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_64:D3","CH_UCIC_P_64:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:XD-06","text":"The unity of the living being is ultimately defined as a recursive coordination of multiplicities in transformation, and not as the simple identity of a substrate.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-01","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_62:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-01","text":"The living being becomes a recursive process of individuation: every whole is an organizing unity, an internal multiplicity, and a subordinate level of a possible whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-01","CL_UCIC_24:GA-02","CL_UCIC_24:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_62:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_62:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-02","text":"Identity is no longer a preservation of matter, but a functional persistence through the progressive replacement of its bodily supports.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-05","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_63:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_63:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-03","text":"The living subject is reclassified as a continuous organic trajectory rather than as a soul transportable between pre-existing bodies.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_64:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-04","text":"The relevant time of the living being is a time of gradual mutation, in which continuity is produced by the absence of instantaneous rupture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:BSD-05","text":"The method of identification must follow relations of organization, transformation, and subordination rather than seek an invariant material or a disembodied subject.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-03","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-01","text":"Dominant entelechy → living members → internal entelechies → new dominant unity: the structure reproduces itself at each level without reaching an ultimate material term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-02","text":"Material flux → impossibility of fixed possession → shift toward organization → necessity of gradual continuity: non-fixity reinforces the architecture instead of dissolving it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-03","text":"Metamorphosis → organic preservation → rejection of transmigration → maintenance of embodiment: change becomes the very mechanism of persistence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-04","text":"The repetition of the unity-multiplicity pattern changes phase when it encounters flux: it passes from a static hierarchy to a processual hierarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_63:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is an open, recursive, and embodied living whole, whose unity is continually produced by the transformation of its components.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B01","text":"Posit a living unity dominated by an entelechy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B02","text":"Unfold this unity into members that are themselves living beings endowed with internal principles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B03","text":"Introduce the perpetual flux of parts in order to preclude every material closure of unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B04","text":"Replace the permanence of the substrate with the persistence of an organization traversing gradual transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B05","text":"Deduce that metamorphosis preserves identity, while transmigration is excluded as a rupture without organic continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FGS-B06","text":"Produce an architecture in which every finite creature is embodied, every whole contains a multiplicity, and God alone constitutes the limit of absolute detachment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AFM-B01","text":"Organic unity → plurality of internal living beings → material flux → impossibility of fixed possession → organizational continuity → gradual transformation → exclusion of transmigration → universal embodiment of creatures → divine exception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_64:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:AFM-B02","text":"The actual trajectory proceeds from a theory of unity to an ontology of processual persistence, then from a critique of fixed matter to a recursive hierarchy of modes of embodiment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-01","text":"The body is reclassified as a whole of organic wholes, and not as a material aggregate containing a soul external to its parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-02","text":"The part-whole boundary becomes a difference of functional level rather than a fixed ontological opposition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-03","text":"The distinction between persistence and material preservation becomes indispensable for thinking any bodily identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-04","text":"The boundary between change of body and change of subject is redrawn around organic continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MME-05","text":"Metamorphosis is rendered thinkable as the internal transformation of a being, while transmigration becomes a category without explanatory function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_64:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are the living body, its members, the soul, organs, and animal transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are distributed within an architecture of vital nesting, flux of parts, and organizational continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The system reformulates identity by abandoning material property, soul-body separation, and migration in favor of relations of level and transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Living reality is a continuum of gradual bodily forms, without an absolutely separated finite soul and without an explicitly assigned ultimate material term.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_64:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form accomplishes its thesis by correcting the categories of property, separation, and migration through a series of exclusions that positively reconstructs organic continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_64:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FL-01","text":"The dominant unity must organize the internal living beings without reducing them to inert parts, which sustains a constitutive tension between domination and relative autonomy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_62:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FL-02","text":"Identity must persist while the matter composing it is continually replaced; the organizational solution is affirmed, but its exact criterion remains partially indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FL-03","text":"Gradual continuity makes change of body and permanence of soul compatible, but it does not fully specify the nature of the body preserved through transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:FL-04","text":"The divine limit stabilizes the architecture while introducing an asymmetry that cannot be deduced from the general mechanism of embodiment alone.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_64:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point occurs when internal multiplicity ceases to be an objection to unity and becomes its mode of constitution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point occurs when material flux forces bodily identity to be dissociated from the permanence of its parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point transforms bodily change into continuous metamorphosis and renders transmigration conceptually superfluous.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:D2","CH_UCIC_P_64:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:HSI-01","text":"Living reality is implicitly a machine of nesting in which every unity is simultaneously an organizing center, a composite whole, and a component of a higher whole.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes an embodied organic trajectory, capable of persisting through transformation but incapable, if finite, of absolutely extracting itself from every corporeality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:HSI-03","text":"The time of the system is a continuous time of renewal and metamorphosis, not a succession of ruptures between separate bodily supports.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_63:A2","CH_UCIC_P_64:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:HSI-04","text":"The only forms of escape are relative: gradual transformation, displacement of levels of organization, and, at the limit, absolute detachment reserved for God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves four operations: nesting living beings, circulating matter, maintaining identity through gradual transformation, and reserving absolute detachment for God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MRT-B02","text":"The coherence of the system depends on the conversion of substantial unity into organizational unity; without this conversion, internal plurality and material flux become incompatible with persistence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_63:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the precise relation between the dominant entelechy and the internal vital centers, as well as the detailed criterion of their continuity across degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_64:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_24:MRT-B04","text":"The compression remains faithful to the governing movement: recursivity provides the form, flux provides the negation of fixity, graduality provides continuity, and the divine exception provides the terminal bound.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_62:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_64:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_24@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_24:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 70–72","context":"Proposition 70 · Proposition 71 · Proposition 72"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 73–75","order":25,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_65","CH_UCIC_P_66","CH_UCIC_P_67"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_25@R001","sha256":"3afc0e89e7c1e83bb5ab5085658b84b7ec29485000759f55f5ee8c481c2cec21","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-01","text":"Le problème central consiste à déterminer comment génération, mort, formation organique et changement de degré peuvent être pensés sans recourir à des ruptures absolues.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-02","text":"Le système recadre les commencements et les fins comme des transformations continues, puis étend ce recadrage à la formation des organismes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-03","text":"La préformation de l’organisme déplace l’origine vers une antériorité du corps, de l’âme et de l’animal relativement à la conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-04","text":"La conception cesse alors d’être une production inaugurale et devient une opération de disposition, de développement ou de transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-05","text":"La continuité organique ne produit pas une homogénéité des trajectoires : elle se distribue entre maintien dans l’espèce et élévation sélective vers un degré supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-06","text":"Le mouvement argumentatif est cumulatif et mutationnel : négation des ruptures, affirmation d’une continuité, extension organique, puis différenciation hiérarchique des devenirs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_67:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-07","text":"La clôture ne réside pas dans une théorie uniforme de la transformation, mais dans une architecture à deux régimes : conservation cyclique et passage exceptionnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Les générations et les morts ne sont jamais des événements entiers ou parfaits au sens absolu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Génération et mort désignent deux orientations inverses d’une transformation continue : développement et accroissement d’un côté, enveloppement et diminution de l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Les formes organiques proviennent de semences qui portent une préformation de l’organisme à venir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Le corps, l’âme et l’animal sont antérieurs à la conception comme événement individuel de formation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] La conception est une disposition ou une transformation d’un organisme préexistant, non une production ex nihilo.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] La continuité organique s’étend au-delà de la génération vers la métamorphose et le changement d’espèce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La continuité animale se scinde entre un régime majoritaire de permanence dans l’espèce et un régime minoritaire d’élévation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] La conception devient un opérateur de hiérarchisation lorsqu’elle rend possible le passage vers un degré supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] La persistance sous transformation constitue le principe d’unification qui relie ontologie, biologie et hiérarchie des devenirs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] La continuité n’abolit pas les différences de trajectoire : elle produit une bifurcation entre cycle ordinaire et changement de théâtre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-01","text":"[Recurrence] Le refus de l’origine absolue revient d’abord pour la génération et la mort, puis pour la formation organique et enfin pour le passage entre degrés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] La génération passe du statut de commencement refusé à celui d’épisode de développement, puis à celui de transformation organique potentiellement élévatrice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-03","text":"[Mutation] La mort conserve sa fonction de terme phénoménal mais perd son statut d’anéantissement métaphysique ; la destruction devient un régime local dans une continuité plus vaste.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-04","text":"[Expansion] La continuité d’abord métaphysique devient continuité du corps, de l’âme et de l’animal, puis continuité différentielle des espèces et des degrés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-05","text":"[Reversal] La conception, d’abord soustraite au registre de la création, réapparaît comme lieu possible d’une élévation ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_67:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-06","text":"[Absorption] La métamorphose absorbe la génération comme cas particulier d’une théorie générale des transformations organiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-07","text":"[Terminal Transformation] La continuité cesse d’être seulement un principe de conservation lorsqu’elle devient le support de trajectoires inégalement distribuées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:D4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-01","text":"Les exclusions du Chaos, de la putréfaction et de la génération spontanée restent locales à la machine explicative de la production organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-02","text":"Les exemples de vers, de mouches, de chenilles et de papillons servent localement de modèles, mais leur fonction courante est d’étendre la transformation au-delà de la génération.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D5","CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-03","text":"Le vocabulaire des animaux « spermatiques », des « grands animaux » et du « plus grand théâtre » appartient à la couche classificatoire inférieure, mais il révèle au niveau courant une distribution hiérarchique des devenirs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-04","text":"La proposition courante relie les unités en transformant la continuité métaphysique en principe commun de formation, de métamorphose et de différenciation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:D3","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-05","text":"La conception catalyse le changement d’échelle : elle passe de la disposition d’un organisme préformé à l’opérateur d’un possible changement de degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D2","CH_UCIC_P_67:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-06","text":"L’idée d’une naissance comme commencement absolu est recodée en reconfiguration d’un processus antérieur ; l’idée d’une reproduction simplement conservatrice est recodée en bifurcation potentielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-07","text":"Les mécanismes précis de la préformation et de la sélection restent locaux et sous-déterminés ; le niveau courant n’en retient que leur fonction structurale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut les commencements et les fins absolument discontinus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_65:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut la production organique à partir du Chaos, de la putréfaction ou d’une matière dépourvue de support formel antérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut que la conception crée séparément le corps, l’âme ou l’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que toute reproduction conduise à une élévation de degré ou à un changement de théâtre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut l’équivalence entre permanence dans l’espèce et progrès ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut également une homogénéisation des trajectoires : la continuité admet la conservation cyclique, la métamorphose et l’élévation sélective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_67:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, doit être fausse l’idée qu’un être commence ou cesse intégralement au moment où une forme apparaît ou disparaît.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-02","text":"Doit être fausse l’hypothèse selon laquelle l’identité d’un organisme se réduit à son état phénoménal présent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-03","text":"Doit être fausse l’idée d’une évolution uniforme où tout animal suivrait la même trajectoire vers un degré supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-04","text":"Le modèle rival silencieusement exclu est celui d’un monde composé d’entités séparées, produites à neuf et distribuées selon une seule loi de devenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-05","text":"Le système ne peut admettre que la destruction ordinaire suffise à définir une mort métaphysiquement parfaite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSA-01","text":"L’absence la plus profonde est celle d’une origine absolument première : aucune forme organique, aucun animal et aucun degré ne surgissent sans antériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSA-02","text":"Le système rend indisponible la possibilité d’une mort comme terme ontologique définitif, même lorsque la destruction demeure un événement du régime ordinaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSA-03","text":"Il traite comme inadmissible l’idée que la continuité impose une trajectoire unique et égalitaire à tous les êtres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSA-04","text":"La possibilité structurellement absente est celle d’une explication complète de la sélection : l’élévation est affirmée, mais ses conditions causales restent hors champ.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-01","text":"La négation conjointe de la génération absolue, de la production ex nihilo et de l’élévation universelle transforme la continuité en règle différentielle : tout devenir procède d’un antérieur, mais tous les antérieurs n’ouvrent pas le même avenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1","CL_UCIC_25:GA-01","CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","CL_UCIC_25:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-02","text":"La conception remplit une fonction commune dans les deux machines organiques : elle ne crée pas l’animal, mais elle peut convertir une organisation préexistante en nouvelle configuration ou en degré supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_67:D2","CL_UCIC_25:GA-05","CL_UCIC_25:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-03","text":"La métamorphose et l’élévation montrent que la persistance n’est pas synonyme d’identité statique : elle autorise une conservation de l’animal à travers une modification de forme, d’espèce ou de degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","CL_UCIC_25:GA-06","CL_UCIC_25:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-04","text":"La mort parfaite étant exclue tandis que la destruction appartient au cycle des animaux ordinaires, la destruction doit être comprise comme une transformation terminale locale plutôt que comme anéantissement absolu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5","CL_UCIC_25:GA-01","CL_UCIC_25:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-05","text":"La continuité organique ne conduit pas à abolir la hiérarchie ; elle fournit au contraire le support commun à partir duquel des régimes de conservation et d’élévation peuvent être distingués.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","CL_UCIC_25:GA-06","CL_UCIC_25:GA-07","CL_UCIC_25:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-06","text":"L’architecture apophatique interdit simultanément deux extrêmes : l’organisme sans préhistoire et l’élévation sans sélection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1","CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","CL_UCIC_25:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-07","text":"La répétition de la continuité à plusieurs échelles produit une nouvelle distinction : la persistance explique l’existence des formes, tandis que la sélection explique leur distribution inégale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME3","CL_UCIC_25:GA-09","CL_UCIC_25:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-01","text":"L’ontologie courante privilégie des processus organisés et persistants sur des substances séparées par des seuils absolus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-02","text":"Le temps est reconstruit comme profondeur d’antériorité : chaque état observable renvoie à une organisation, une âme ou un animal déjà présents sous une autre configuration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-03","text":"La génération, la mort, la conception et la reproduction cessent d’être des catégories d’origine et deviennent des opérateurs de transformation, de disposition ou de classement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-04","text":"Le changement d’espèce et le changement de degré sont rendus pensables par la même structure de persistance sous modification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D4","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-05","text":"La continuité ne supprime pas la hiérarchie : elle rend possible une politique conceptuelle des trajectoires, distinguant la conservation majoritaire de l’élévation minoritaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:D4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-06","text":"La méthode de connaissance consiste à remonter des apparences de naissance, de mort ou de changement vers les structures persistantes qu’elles recouvrent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-01","text":"Apparition d’une forme → hypothèse d’un commencement → exclusion du commencement absolu → découverte d’une antériorité → nouvelle forme à expliquer : la négation de l’origine relance récursivement l’enquête.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-02","text":"Semence préformée → corps antérieur → âme déjà présente → animal préexistant → conception comme disposition : la conception revient comme transformation d’un processus déjà engagé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-03","text":"Développement et accroissement → métamorphose organique → changement d’espèce → changement de degré : la continuité s’escalade d’une théorie du développement vers une cartographie des devenirs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_67:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-04","text":"La continuité est l’attracteur conceptuel principal, mais elle se reconfigure à chaque échelle : continuité métaphysique, continuité organique, continuité spécifique, puis continuité hiérarchisée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-05","text":"Le cycle naissance–multiplication–destruction réintroduit localement la mort que l’architecture globale avait désabsolutisée ; cette contradiction produit une stratification des sens de la mort.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-06","text":"La trajectoire du système converge vers une bifurcation : la persistance devient soit conservation de l’espèce, soit passage sélectif vers un autre théâtre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B01","text":"Rupture supposée entre apparition et disparition → exclusion de la génération entière et de la mort parfaite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B02","text":"Exclusion des ruptures absolues → transformation continue comme forme ontologique de base.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:D3","CH_UCIC_P_65:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B03","text":"Transformation continue → préformation de l’organisme → antériorité du corps, de l’âme et de l’animal à la conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B04","text":"Antériorité de l’animal → conception comme disposition → extension de la transformation à la métamorphose et au changement d’espèce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B05","text":"Transformation organique généralisée → différenciation des capacités de devenir → distinction entre permanence spécifique et élévation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A1","CH_UCIC_P_67:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B06","text":"Continuité persistante + distribution inégale des capacités → architecture à deux régimes : cycle ordinaire et changement sélectif de théâtre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B01","text":"Ruptures supposées → négation de la génération entière et de la mort parfaite → recodage en transformations continues → préformation organique → antériorité du corps, de l’âme et de l’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_66:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B02","text":"Animal préexistant → conception comme disposition → métamorphose hors génération → changement d’espèce → différenciation des degrés d’existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:AF3","CH_UCIC_P_67:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B03","text":"Continuité organique → maintien majoritaire dans l’espèce → cycle naissance–multiplication–destruction → sélection minoritaire → passage vers un « plus grand théâtre ».","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B04","text":"Position terminale : aucune origine ni fin n’est absolue, mais la continuité produit des trajectoires différenciées plutôt qu’un devenir commun.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-01","text":"Le champ métaphysique est déplacé des ruptures d’être vers les transformations de degré, de forme et de manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-02","text":"La naissance et la mort sont reclassées comme des positions locales dans une continuité, non comme des seuils ontologiques absolus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_65:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-03","text":"La génération est absorbée dans une théorie plus vaste de la métamorphose, qui inclut développement, changement d’espèce et changement de degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-04","text":"La conception est cartographiée comme un seuil opératoire à double fonction : conservation transformée d’un organisme préexistant et possibilité d’élévation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-05","text":"L’animalité cesse d’être une catégorie homogène et devient une distribution différentielle de capacités de transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-06","text":"La majorité statistique acquiert une fonction ontologique : elle définit le régime ordinaire, tandis que l’exception révèle une échelle supérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-07","text":"La fausse opposition entre conservation et transformation s’effondre : la conservation est elle-même une transformation cyclique, et l’élévation une transformation sélectionnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets explicites sont la génération, la mort, la semence, le corps, l’âme, l’animal, l’espèce et le degré supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Ces objets sont reliés par des mécanismes de préformation, persistance, développement, enveloppement, métamorphose, conservation spécifique et élévation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — L’argument remplace les catégories ordinaires d’origine et de disparition par une lecture différentielle des transformations et des trajectoires.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel est posé comme persistance organisée à travers des états successifs ; le temps devient une profondeur d’antériorité et une distribution inégale des devenirs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — La forme de l’argument accomplit ce qu’elle affirme : elle détruit progressivement les commencements absolus et reconstruit la réalité comme série de transformations reliées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-01","text":"La continuité universalisée par la théorie de la génération et de la métamorphose entre en tension avec l’élévation réservée à une minorité d’animaux.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-02","text":"La mort est désabsolutisée au niveau métaphysique, mais la destruction demeure constitutive du cycle ordinaire de certains animaux.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-03","text":"L’identité persistante de l’animal doit soutenir à la fois la continuité et le changement d’espèce ; le système ne précise pas entièrement le seuil où l’identité change de statut.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D4","CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-04","text":"La préformation est introduite avec une qualification conjecturale, puis mobilisée comme fondement explicatif d’une chaîne plus déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-05","text":"Le vocabulaire de l’élection et du théâtre fournit une hiérarchie forte sans exposer la causalité de la sélection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation survient lorsque génération et mort cessent de désigner des ruptures et deviennent des orientations d’un même processus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:D3","CH_UCIC_P_65:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MP-02","text":"Le deuxième point de mutation survient lorsque la conception passe de l’événement reproductif à l’opérateur de transformation d’un organisme déjà constitué.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D2","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation survient lorsque la continuité organique est convertie en hiérarchie de trajectoires et en accès différentiel aux degrés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A1","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MP-04","text":"Le point de compression final est l’articulation instable entre une ontologie de la continuité et une structure de sélection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de transformations stratifiées où aucune forme n’est première et où chaque état manifeste une organisation antérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:HSI-02","text":"L’animal devient une unité persistante mais modulable, capable de conserver son organisation, de changer de forme ou d’accéder exceptionnellement à un autre degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:HSI-03","text":"Le temps supposé par le système n’est ni linéaire ni inaugural : il est composé de strates d’antériorité, de reprises, de développements et de passages sélectifs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:HSI-04","text":"La possibilité d’action interne au système ne consiste pas à créer à partir de rien, mais à transformer une continuité donnée et, dans certains cas, à franchir un degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B01","text":"Un noyau minimal suffit à reconstruire l’ensemble : absence de génération et de mort absolues, préformation organique, conception comme disposition, métamorphose, puis différenciation entre permanence spécifique et élévation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_67:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction est cohérente si la continuité est comprise comme persistance sous transformation et non comme identité statique ou trajectoire uniforme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne le mécanisme exact de la préformation, les conditions de l’élévation et le statut précis de l’identité à travers le changement d’espèce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B04","text":"La compression doit conserver la tension entre continuité et sélection ; la réduire à une simple théorie de la conservation ferait disparaître la clôture hiérarchique du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B05","text":"La dépendance au séquençage est faible pour les principes globaux, mais le mouvement mutationnel doit être préservé : désabsolutisation, préformation, transformation, puis distribution inégale des devenirs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_67:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B06","text":"La reconstruction minimale est suffisante à condition de maintenir l’absence d’une origine première, l’absence d’une mort parfaite et l’absence d’un passage universel vers le degré supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T195958309601Z_630d7c5a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 73–75","source_sha256":"3afc0e89e7c1e83bb5ab5085658b84b7ec29485000759f55f5ee8c481c2cec21","sha256":"c0d90feff26ab519eb73de9c55aedbf7e4e55f5392aa5015e828171adbe521f5","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T19:59:58.313165+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-01","text":"The central problem is to determine how generation, death, organic formation, and change of degree can be conceived without recourse to absolute ruptures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-02","text":"The system reframes beginnings and ends as continuous transformations, then extends this reframing to the formation of organisms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-03","text":"The preformation of the organism displaces origin toward a prior existence of the body, soul, and animal relative to conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-04","text":"Conception thus ceases to be an inaugural production and becomes an operation of disposition, development, or transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-05","text":"Organic continuity does not produce a homogeneity of trajectories: it is distributed between persistence within the species and selective elevation toward a higher degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-06","text":"The argumentative movement is cumulative and mutational: negation of ruptures, affirmation of a continuity, organic extension, then hierarchical differentiation of becomings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_67:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:SP-07","text":"The closure lies not in a uniform theory of transformation, but in a two-regime architecture: cyclical conservation and exceptional passage.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Generations and deaths are never whole or perfect events in the absolute sense.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Generation and death designate two inverse orientations of a continuous transformation: development and increase on one side, envelopment and diminution on the other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_65:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Organic forms arise from seeds that bear a preformation of the organism to come.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A2","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The body, soul, and animal precede conception as an individual event of formation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A5","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Conception is a disposition or transformation of a pre-existing organism, not a production ex nihilo.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Organic continuity extends beyond generation toward metamorphosis and change of species.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Animal continuity divides between a majority regime of persistence within the species and a minority regime of elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A4","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Conception becomes an operator of hierarchization when it makes passage toward a higher degree possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Persistence under transformation constitutes the unifying principle linking ontology, biology, and the hierarchy of becomings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Continuity does not abolish differences of trajectory: it produces a bifurcation between ordinary cycle and change of theatre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-01","text":"[Recurrence] The rejection of absolute origin returns first for generation and death, then for organic formation, and finally for passage between degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] Generation passes from the status of rejected beginning to that of an episode of development, then to that of potentially elevating organic transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-03","text":"[Mutation] Death retains its function as phenomenal term but loses its status as metaphysical annihilation; destruction becomes a local regime within a broader continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-04","text":"[Expansion] Initially metaphysical continuity becomes continuity of body, soul, and animal, then differential continuity of species and degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-05","text":"[Reversal] Conception, initially removed from the register of creation, reappears as a possible site of ontological elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_67:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-06","text":"[Absorption] Metamorphosis absorbs generation as a particular case of a general theory of organic transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RMD-07","text":"[Terminal Transformation] Continuity ceases to be merely a principle of conservation when it becomes the support of unequally distributed trajectories.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:D4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-01","text":"The exclusions of Chaos, putrefaction, and spontaneous generation remain local to the explanatory mechanism of organic production.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-02","text":"The examples of worms, flies, caterpillars, and butterflies serve locally as models, but their current function is to extend transformation beyond generation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D5","CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-03","text":"The vocabulary of “spermatic” animals, “great animals,” and the “greater theatre” belongs to the lower classificatory layer, but at the current level it reveals a hierarchical distribution of becomings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-04","text":"The current proposition links the units by transforming metaphysical continuity into a common principle of formation, metamorphosis, and differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:D3","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-05","text":"Conception catalyzes the change of scale: it passes from the disposition of a preformed organism to the operator of a possible change of degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D2","CH_UCIC_P_67:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-06","text":"The idea of birth as an absolute beginning is recoded as the reconfiguration of a prior process; the idea of merely conservative reproduction is recoded as a potential bifurcation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:CGD-07","text":"The precise mechanisms of preformation and selection remain local and underdetermined; the current level retains only their structural function.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes absolutely discontinuous beginnings and ends.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_65:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-02","text":"It excludes organic production from Chaos, putrefaction, or matter devoid of prior formal support.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that conception separately creates the body, soul, or animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_66:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that every reproduction leads to elevation of degree or change of theatre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the equivalence between persistence within the species and ontological progress.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:GNX-06","text":"It also excludes a homogenization of trajectories: continuity admits cyclical conservation, metamorphosis, and selective elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_67:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the idea that a being begins or ceases integrally at the moment when a form appears or disappears must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-02","text":"The hypothesis according to which the identity of an organism is reduced to its present phenomenal state must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-03","text":"The idea of a uniform evolution in which every animal would follow the same trajectory toward a higher degree must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-04","text":"The silently excluded rival model is that of a world composed of separate entities, produced anew and distributed according to a single law of becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:DBN-05","text":"The system cannot admit that ordinary destruction suffices to define a metaphysically perfect death.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSA-01","text":"The deepest absence is that of an absolutely first origin: no organic form, animal, or degree arises without prior existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSA-02","text":"The system renders unavailable the possibility of death as a definitive ontological term, even when destruction remains an event of the ordinary regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSA-03","text":"It treats as inadmissible the idea that continuity imposes a single and egalitarian trajectory on all beings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSA-04","text":"The structurally absent possibility is that of a complete explanation of selection: elevation is affirmed, but its causal conditions remain outside the field.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-01","text":"The joint negation of absolute generation, production ex nihilo, and universal elevation transforms continuity into a differential rule: every becoming proceeds from a prior state, but not all prior states open onto the same future.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_66:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1","CL_UCIC_25:GA-01","CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","CL_UCIC_25:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-02","text":"Conception fulfills a common function in the two organic mechanisms: it does not create the animal, but it can convert a pre-existing organization into a new configuration or a higher degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_67:D2","CL_UCIC_25:GA-05","CL_UCIC_25:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-03","text":"Metamorphosis and elevation show that persistence is not synonymous with static identity: it permits the conservation of the animal through a modification of form, species, or degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","CL_UCIC_25:GA-06","CL_UCIC_25:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-04","text":"Since perfect death is excluded while destruction belongs to the cycle of ordinary animals, destruction must be understood as a local terminal transformation rather than as absolute annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A5","CL_UCIC_25:GA-01","CL_UCIC_25:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-05","text":"Organic continuity does not lead to abolishing hierarchy; on the contrary, it provides the common support from which regimes of conservation and elevation can be distinguished.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","CL_UCIC_25:GA-06","CL_UCIC_25:GA-07","CL_UCIC_25:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-06","text":"The apophatic architecture simultaneously prohibits two extremes: the organism without prehistory and elevation without selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1","CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","CL_UCIC_25:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:XD-07","text":"The repetition of continuity at several scales produces a new distinction: persistence explains the existence of forms, whereas selection explains their unequal distribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME3","CL_UCIC_25:GA-09","CL_UCIC_25:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-01","text":"The current ontology privileges organized and persistent processes over substances separated by absolute thresholds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-02","text":"Time is reconstructed as a depth of prior existence: every observable state refers to an organization, a soul, or an animal already present under another configuration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-03","text":"Generation, death, conception, and reproduction cease to be categories of origin and become operators of transformation, disposition, or classification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-04","text":"Change of species and change of degree are rendered thinkable by the same structure of persistence under modification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D4","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-05","text":"Continuity does not suppress hierarchy: it makes possible a conceptual politics of trajectories, distinguishing majority conservation from minority elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:D4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:BSD-06","text":"The method of knowledge consists in ascending from appearances of birth, death, or change toward the persistent structures they cover over.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-01","text":"Appearance of a form → hypothesis of a beginning → exclusion of absolute beginning → discovery of a prior existence → new form to explain: the negation of origin recursively relaunches inquiry.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-02","text":"Preformed seed → prior body → soul already present → pre-existing animal → conception as disposition: conception returns as transformation of an already initiated process.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-03","text":"Development and increase → organic metamorphosis → change of species → change of degree: continuity escalates from a theory of development toward a cartography of becomings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A4","CH_UCIC_P_66:A8","CH_UCIC_P_67:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-04","text":"Continuity is the principal conceptual attractor, but it is reconfigured at each scale: metaphysical continuity, organic continuity, specific continuity, then hierarchized continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-05","text":"The birth–multiplication–destruction cycle locally reintroduces the death that the global architecture had de-absolutized; this contradiction produces a stratification of the meanings of death.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:RLE-06","text":"The system's trajectory converges toward a bifurcation: persistence becomes either conservation of the species or selective passage toward another theatre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B01","text":"Supposed rupture between appearance and disappearance → exclusion of whole generation and perfect death.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A1","CH_UCIC_P_65:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B02","text":"Exclusion of absolute ruptures → continuous transformation as basic ontological form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:D3","CH_UCIC_P_65:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B03","text":"Continuous transformation → preformation of the organism → prior existence of body, soul, and animal before conception.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B04","text":"Prior existence of the animal → conception as disposition → extension of transformation to metamorphosis and change of species.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_66:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B05","text":"Generalized organic transformation → differentiation of capacities for becoming → distinction between specific persistence and elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A1","CH_UCIC_P_67:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B06","text":"Persistent continuity + unequal distribution of capacities → two-regime architecture: ordinary cycle and selective change of theatre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B01","text":"Supposed ruptures → negation of whole generation and perfect death → recoding as continuous transformations → organic preformation → prior existence of body, soul, and animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_66:AF2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B02","text":"Pre-existing animal → conception as disposition → metamorphosis outside generation → change of species → differentiation of degrees of existence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:AF3","CH_UCIC_P_67:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B03","text":"Organic continuity → majority persistence within the species → birth–multiplication–destruction cycle → minority selection → passage toward a “greater theatre.”","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B04","text":"Terminal position: no origin or end is absolute, but continuity produces differentiated trajectories rather than a common becoming.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-01","text":"The metaphysical field is displaced from ruptures of being toward transformations of degree, form, and manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-02","text":"Birth and death are reclassified as local positions within a continuity, not as absolute ontological thresholds.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_65:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-03","text":"Generation is absorbed into a broader theory of metamorphosis, which includes development, change of species, and change of degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-04","text":"Conception is mapped as an operative threshold with a double function: transformed conservation of a pre-existing organism and possibility of elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_67:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-05","text":"Animality ceases to be a homogeneous category and becomes a differential distribution of capacities for transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-06","text":"The statistical majority acquires an ontological function: it defines the ordinary regime, while the exception reveals a higher scale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MME-07","text":"The false opposition between conservation and transformation collapses: conservation is itself a cyclical transformation, and elevation a selected transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit objects are generation, death, seed, body, soul, animal, species, and higher degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — These objects are connected by mechanisms of preformation, persistence, development, envelopment, metamorphosis, specific conservation, and elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The argument replaces ordinary categories of origin and disappearance with a differential reading of transformations and trajectories.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Reality is posited as organized persistence through successive states; time becomes a depth of prior existence and an unequal distribution of becomings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The form of the argument accomplishes what it affirms: it progressively destroys absolute beginnings and reconstructs reality as a series of connected transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_65:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-01","text":"Continuity universalized by the theory of generation and metamorphosis comes into tension with elevation reserved for a minority of animals.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-02","text":"Death is de-absolutized at the metaphysical level, but destruction remains constitutive of the ordinary cycle of certain animals.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A2","CH_UCIC_P_67:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-03","text":"The persistent identity of the animal must support both continuity and change of species; the system does not fully specify the threshold at which identity changes status.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D4","CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-04","text":"Preformation is introduced with a conjectural qualification, then mobilized as the explanatory foundation of a more determinate chain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:FL-05","text":"The vocabulary of election and theatre provides a strong hierarchy without setting out the causality of selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point occurs when generation and death cease to designate ruptures and become orientations of a single process.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:D3","CH_UCIC_P_65:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point occurs when conception passes from the reproductive event to the operator of transformation of an already constituted organism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:D2","CH_UCIC_P_66:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point occurs when organic continuity is converted into a hierarchy of trajectories and differential access to degrees.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:A1","CH_UCIC_P_67:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MP-04","text":"The final compression point is the unstable articulation between an ontology of continuity and a structure of selection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a machine of stratified transformations in which no form is first and in which each state manifests a prior organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:HSI-02","text":"The animal becomes a persistent but modifiable unit, capable of preserving its organization, changing form, or exceptionally gaining access to another degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:HSI-03","text":"The time presupposed by the system is neither linear nor inaugural: it is composed of strata of prior existence, repetitions, developments, and selective passages.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_67:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:HSI-04","text":"The possibility of action internal to the system consists not in creating from nothing, but in transforming a given continuity and, in certain cases, crossing a degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:A7","CH_UCIC_P_67:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B01","text":"A minimal core suffices to reconstruct the whole: absence of absolute generation and death, organic preformation, conception as disposition, metamorphosis, then differentiation between specific persistence and elevation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:A6","CH_UCIC_P_66:A3","CH_UCIC_P_67:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction is coherent if continuity is understood as persistence under transformation and not as static identity or uniform trajectory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the exact mechanism of preformation, the conditions of elevation, and the precise status of identity through change of species.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B04","text":"The compression must preserve the tension between continuity and selection; reducing it to a mere theory of conservation would cause the system's hierarchical closure to disappear.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_67:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_67:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B05","text":"Dependence on sequencing is low for global principles, but the mutational movement must be preserved: de-absolutization, preformation, transformation, then unequal distribution of becomings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_66:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_67:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B06","text":"The minimal reconstruction is sufficient provided that the absence of a first origin, the absence of a perfect death, and the absence of a universal passage toward the higher degree are maintained.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_65:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_66:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_67:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_25@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_25:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 73–75","context":"Proposition 73 · Proposition 74 · Proposition 75"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 76–78","order":26,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_68","CH_UCIC_P_69","CH_UCIC_P_70"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_26@R001","sha256":"edf4d03d17bd5568052e67c944fd0997bb671f69d6638e9fc745f0831ffa0a4d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-01","text":"Le problème central est de déterminer comment un animal peut être dit naître, mourir ou changer sans que ces événements impliquent son apparition ou son anéantissement absolus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_69:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-02","text":"Le système recadre l’animal comme une unité persistante distincte de la configuration matérielle momentanée de sa machine organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_69:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-03","text":"La permanence est d’abord établie négativement, par l’exclusion d’un commencement et d’une fin naturels absolus, puis positivement, par l’indestructibilité du principe animé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_69:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-04","text":"La variation ou la destruction partielle de la machine organique devient compatible avec la continuité de l’animal parce que l’identité ne réside pas dans la conservation de ses parties matérielles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","CH_UCIC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-05","text":"L’union de l’âme et du corps est ensuite déplacée du registre de l’interaction locale vers celui de deux séries autonomes coordonnées par une harmonie universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_70:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-06","text":"Le mouvement est récursif : une négation ontologique produit une distinction structurelle, celle-ci appelle une architecture métaphysique, puis l’expérience revient confirmer le cadre a priori.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_70:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-07","text":"La clôture obtenue n’est pas une démonstration empirique autonome mais une fermeture systémique entre permanence, distinction des ordres, harmonie et validation a priori.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] L’animal naturel n’est pas posé comme surgissant absolument du non-être.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’absence de commencement naturel est prolongée par l’absence de fin naturelle absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Génération et mort sont reclassées comme transformations d’un être persistant plutôt que comme passages entre être et néant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:D2","CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] L’animal n’est pas identique à la totalité actuelle de sa machine organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] L’âme est rapportée à un univers indestructible dont elle constitue le miroir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A1","CH_UCIC_P_69:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] L’indestructibilité attribuée à l’âme est étendue à l’animal comme unité, sans être étendue à chacune de ses parties matérielles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","CH_UCIC_P_69:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] La machine organique peut périr partiellement, changer de dépouille et demeurer subordonnée au principe d’identité animale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] L’âme et le corps organique suivent chacun leurs lois propres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] L’autonomie des deux ordres n’abolit pas leur conformité, mais en constitue la condition locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A3","CH_UCIC_P_70:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Une harmonie préétablie coordonne les développements distincts de l’âme et du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] La représentation commune d’un même univers fournit le principe de commensurabilité entre des substances qui restent hétérogènes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A5","CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] L’unité véritable est une persistance à travers la différence, la variation matérielle et l’autonomie des séries.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] La causalité directe entre l’âme et le corps est remplacée par une synchronisation métaphysique de leurs développements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-01","text":"La négation du commencement revient comme négation de la fin, puis se transforme en principe positif de permanence sous transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_68:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-02","text":"La mort migre d’un événement biologique apparent vers une distinction ontologique entre perte locale de matière et disparition de l’unité animale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_69:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-03","text":"La continuité d’abord attribuée à l’animal en général se spécifie ensuite comme continuité du principe animé à travers des dépouilles variables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:D1","CH_UCIC_P_69:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-04","text":"La machine organique passe du statut de constituant apparent de l’identité à celui de support périssable et remplaçable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_69:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-05","text":"L’autonomie, d’abord formulée comme séparation des lois de l’âme et du corps, devient le mécanisme même de leur conformité systémique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-06","text":"La notion de rencontre change de fonction : elle ne désigne plus une interaction causale mais l’accord réglé de deux développements indépendants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_70:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-07","text":"L’expérience est déplacée du statut de fondement vers celui d’instance de confirmation d’un cadre a priori.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-01","text":"Les arguments relatifs à l’absence de génération naturelle restent locaux lorsqu’ils établissent seulement la non-absoluité de la naissance ou de la mort.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A3","CH_UCIC_P_68:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-02","text":"La distinction entre animal et machine change d’échelle lorsqu’elle relie la permanence ontologique à la variation corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:D2","CH_UCIC_P_69:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-03","text":"La distinction entre lois propres de l’âme et du corps devient une structure de niveau courant lorsqu’elle explique l’union par une harmonie globale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-04","text":"Le pont entre les unités est l’idée d’une identité qui ne dépend ni d’un commencement absolu, ni d’une matière inchangée, ni d’une interaction directe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-05","text":"Les apparences de naissance, de mort et de rencontre deviennent obsolètes comme descriptions ultimes, mais sont conservées comme effets locaux d’une architecture supérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-01","text":"Le système rejette l’idée qu’un animal puisse surgir absolument à partir du non-être.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-02","text":"Il rejette également le retour absolu de l’animal au non-être et distingue la destruction locale de l’anéantissement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-03","text":"Il récuse l’identification de l’animal avec la conservation numérique de ses composants organiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut qu’une conformité entre âme et corps résulte d’une loi unique, d’une fusion ou d’une interaction ponctuelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-05","text":"Il subordonne l’expérience à des principes a priori et refuse qu’elle fonde seule l’ontologie des transformations naturelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que l’opposition simple entre existence et inexistence soit inadéquate pour décrire les transformations naturelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que la machine organique ne soit pas le principe ultime de l’identité animale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:DBN-03","text":"Le modèle rival silencieusement exclu est celui d’un vivant réductible à son état corporel présent et à ses interactions observables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:DBN-04","text":"La conformité locale ne peut être intelligible qu’en étant rapportée à la totalité universelle représentée par les substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSA-01","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un néant naturel pouvant servir simultanément d’origine et de destination à l’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSA-02","text":"Le système rend indisponible une identité sans principe interne de continuité et sans inscription dans un ordre universel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSA-03","text":"L’unité n’est admissible qu’à condition de ne pas être une fusion : elle doit être produite par la coordination de différences irréductibles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-01","text":"La permanence de l’animal est construite par la convergence de trois exclusions : pas de commencement absolu, pas d’anéantissement absolu et pas de réduction à la machine organique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX2","CL_UCIC_26:GA-01","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-02","text":"Le principe animé devient le point de médiation entre la permanence ontologique de l’animal et la variabilité de ses supports matériels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:D1","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:GA-06","CL_UCIC_26:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-03","text":"La distinction entre âme et corps ne produit pas une simple dualité : elle devient la condition formelle d’une unité coordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:D1","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1","CL_UCIC_26:GA-08","CL_UCIC_26:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-04","text":"La représentation d’un même univers convertit l’hétérogénéité des substances en commensurabilité sans supprimer leur autonomie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-05","text":"L’union âme-corps est une causalité apparente produite par la synchronisation de séries distinctes, non par une transmission réciproque d’opérations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX1","CL_UCIC_26:GA-10","CL_UCIC_26:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-06","text":"L’expérience ne réfute pas la structure métaphysique parce qu’elle est réinscrite dans celle-ci comme confirmation de ses effets observables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_68:ME3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-07","text":"Le vocabulaire de la rencontre conserve une apparence interactive tout en désignant, à l’échelle du cluster, une coordination déjà réglée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:D4","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT5","CL_UCIC_26:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-01","text":"L’être naturel n’est plus défini par un instant d’apparition ou de disparition, mais par une trajectoire persistante qui absorbe ses propres transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT4","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02","text":"Le corps devient une infrastructure variable de l’identité, tandis que l’identité se déplace vers un principe animé et relationnel de continuité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:GA-06","CL_UCIC_26:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-03","text":"La causalité locale est reclassée comme effet phénoménal d’une architecture de correspondances préétablies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-10","CL_UCIC_26:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-04","text":"L’ordre temporel biologique décrit des changements internes à une permanence plutôt qu’un passage ontologique entre être et néant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-05","text":"L’ordre épistémique est hiérarchisé : l’expérience rend visibles des effets, mais les principes a priori déterminent leur portée ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:D4","CH_UCIC_P_68:SD3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-06","text":"La méthode du système consiste à produire une reconstruction positive par accumulation d’exclusions plutôt qu’à partir d’une description empirique immédiate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS4","CL_UCIC_26:GA-01","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-01","text":"L’absence de commencement appelle l’absence de fin, laquelle transforme la mort apparente en modification d’un être persistant.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-02","text":"La périssabilité de la machine déclenche la séparation entre support et unité, puis cette séparation reconduit l’indestructibilité de l’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-03","text":"La séparation des lois de l’âme et du corps produit le besoin d’une harmonie, qui transforme ensuite cette séparation en condition de l’union.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-04","text":"La représentation commune de l’univers sert d’attracteur intermédiaire : elle absorbe les différences locales dans une correspondance globale sans les annuler.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-05","text":"Le circuit épistémique va des phénomènes aux principes, puis des principes à la requalification des phénomènes comme confirmations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-06","text":"L’attracteur terminal est une unité persistante définie non par l’identité de ses composants, mais par la continuité réglée de ses transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_69:ME3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B01","text":"Négation du commencement naturel → négation de la fin naturelle → exclusion de la génération et de la destruction absolues.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B02","text":"Transformation apparente → distinction entre événement empirique et statut ontologique → persistance de l’animal à travers le changement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:D3","CH_UCIC_P_68:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B03","text":"Périssabilité de la machine → dissociation du support et de l’unité → fondation de l’identité dans le principe animé.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_69:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B04","text":"Âme-miroir d’un univers indestructible → indestructibilité du principe animé → extension de la permanence à l’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_69:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B05","text":"Lois propres de l’âme et du corps → séparation des séries → harmonie préétablie → conformité sans interaction directe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B06","text":"Représentation commune de l’univers → commensurabilité des substances → reclassification de l’union comme effet systémique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B07","text":"Expérience observable → vérification d’un principe a priori → fermeture récursive entre fondement métaphysique et phénomènes biologiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AFM-B01","text":"Apparence de naissance et de mort → refus de l’origine et de l’anéantissement absolus → distinction entre animal et machine → permanence du principe animé → autonomie des séries → harmonie universelle → conformité sans causalité directe → confirmation empirique de l’architecture a priori.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_70:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AFM-B02","text":"La clôture terminale remplace l’opposition vie/mort par une structure de transformation, puis remplace l’opposition âme/corps par une coordination de séries distinctes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-01","text":"La naissance et la mort cessent d’être des frontières ontologiques et deviennent des transformations internes à une continuité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_68:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-02","text":"L’objet « animal » est cartographié comme une unité persistante portant une machine variable, non comme un agrégat matériel stable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-03","text":"La destruction locale et la disparition totale sont séparées comme deux catégories de portée ontologique différente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_69:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-04","text":"L’union âme-corps est déplacée du champ des interactions locales vers celui de la coordination métaphysique globale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-05","text":"L’autonomie et la conformité ne sont plus des opposés : l’autonomie locale devient le mécanisme de la conformité universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_70:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-06","text":"L’expérience est reclassée comme surface de vérification d’une structure a priori plutôt que comme source ultime de l’ontologie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_68:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les phénomènes explicites sont la génération, la mort, la périssabilité de la machine et la conformité apparente de l’âme et du corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces phénomènes sont distribués entre une unité animale persistante, un support matériel variable et deux séries autonomes coordonnées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Le système neutralise les objections empiriques en changeant le niveau auquel elles doivent être interprétées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le temps naturel décrit une succession de transformations dans une existence sans commencement ni fin absolus.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle affirme : elle nie successivement les absolus pour faire apparaître une architecture positive de coordination et de permanence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FL-01","text":"La non-finitude naturelle est opératoire mais demeure affirmée à partir de l’absence de commencement plutôt que démontrée dans le passage.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FL-02","text":"Le passage de l’indestructibilité de l’âme à celle de l’animal reste une implication métaphysique dont la médiation n’est pas entièrement explicitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FL-03","text":"Le terme de rencontre conserve une tonalité interactionnelle alors que le système exclut la causalité réciproque directe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FL-04","text":"L’expérience est présentée comme concordante avec l’a priori, mais cette concordance ne constitue pas une fondation indépendante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MP-01","text":"La mort opère un changement de phase lorsqu’elle cesse de signifier destruction et devient distinction entre transformation corporelle et permanence animale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MP-02","text":"La machine organique change de fonction lorsqu’elle passe de critère apparent de l’identité à support matériel remplaçable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MP-03","text":"L’autonomie des substances change de valence lorsqu’elle passe d’un risque de séparation à la condition de leur conformité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MP-04","text":"La causalité change de statut lorsqu’elle est conservée comme apparence phénoménale mais retirée de l’ordre des opérations réciproques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de correspondances stratifiées où des séries autonomes représentent un même univers sans agir directement les unes sur les autres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A5","CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet animal devient une unité de continuité capable de survivre au renouvellement de ses supports et à la variation de ses configurations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A6","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas une ligne allant de l’être au néant, mais une série de transformations ordonnées à l’intérieur d’une permanence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:HSI-04","text":"La navigation possible consiste à distinguer les apparences locales des structures qui les coordonnent, tandis que l’échappée hors du système serait une réduction au néant ou à l’identité matérielle, toutes deux interdites.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes sont suffisants pour reconstruire la trajectoire principale : absence de commencement, absence d’anéantissement, distinction entre animal et machine, puis permanence sous transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B02","text":"La structure de l’union requiert en outre la distinction des lois propres, l’harmonie préétablie et la représentation commune de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B03","text":"La reconstruction reste dépendante de principes a priori antérieurs et du mécanisme non explicité par lequel l’âme transmet son indestructibilité à l’animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence du système dépend du maintien simultané de deux écarts : machine et animal ne sont pas identiques, âme et corps ne sont pas causalement fusionnés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_70:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B05","text":"La compression est suffisante si elle conserve la boucle négation–distinction–coordination–confirmation ; elle devient insuffisante si elle réduit les contradictions de médiation à de simples identités.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B06","text":"Le noyau minimal du cluster est une ontologie de la permanence différentielle : un animal persiste non malgré les transformations de ses supports et de ses relations, mais à travers elles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200030999393Z_b8fb7a07","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 76–78","source_sha256":"edf4d03d17bd5568052e67c944fd0997bb671f69d6638e9fc745f0831ffa0a4d","sha256":"570c9cfbcefc4dbde4d2dcdb1679fcb4746793ef4adc6baefed2cfc35ea4fafe","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:00:31.003900+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-01","text":"The central problem is to determine how an animal can be said to be born, die, or change without these events entailing its absolute appearance or annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_69:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-02","text":"The system reframes the animal as a persistent unity distinct from the momentary material configuration of its organic machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_69:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-03","text":"Permanence is first established negatively, through the exclusion of an absolute natural beginning and end, then positively, through the indestructibility of the animate principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1","CH_UCIC_P_69:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-04","text":"Variation or partial destruction of the organic machine becomes compatible with the continuity of the animal because identity does not reside in the preservation of its material parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","CH_UCIC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-05","text":"The union of soul and body is then shifted from the register of local interaction to that of two autonomous series coordinated by a universal harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_70:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-06","text":"The movement is recursive: an ontological negation produces a structural distinction, this calls for a metaphysical architecture, and experience then returns to confirm the a priori framework.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_70:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AS-07","text":"The closure obtained is not an autonomous empirical demonstration but a systemic closure between permanence, distinction of orders, harmony, and a priori validation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The natural animal is not posited as arising absolutely from non-being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The absence of a natural beginning is extended by the absence of an absolute natural end.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Generation and death are reclassified as transformations of a persistent being rather than as passages between being and nothingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:D2","CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The animal is not identical with the current totality of its organic machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] The soul is related to an indestructible universe of which it constitutes the mirror.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A1","CH_UCIC_P_69:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] The indestructibility attributed to the soul is extended to the animal as a unity, without being extended to each of its material parts.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A4","CH_UCIC_P_69:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] The organic machine can partially perish, change its covering, and remain subordinated to the principle of animal identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A5","CH_UCIC_P_69:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] The soul and the organic body each follow their own laws.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A1","CH_UCIC_P_70:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] The autonomy of the two orders does not abolish their conformity, but constitutes its local condition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A3","CH_UCIC_P_70:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] A pre-established harmony coordinates the distinct developments of soul and body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A4","CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] The common representation of one and the same universe provides the principle of commensurability between substances that remain heterogeneous.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A5","CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] True unity is persistence through difference, material variation, and the autonomy of series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Direct causality between soul and body is replaced by a metaphysical synchronization of their developments.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-01","text":"The negation of the beginning recurs as negation of the end, then becomes a positive principle of permanence under transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_68:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-02","text":"Death migrates from an apparent biological event to an ontological distinction between local loss of matter and disappearance of animal unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_69:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-03","text":"Continuity, first attributed to the animal in general, is subsequently specified as continuity of the animate principle through variable coverings.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:D1","CH_UCIC_P_69:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-04","text":"The organic machine passes from the status of apparent constituent of identity to that of perishable and replaceable support.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_69:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-05","text":"Autonomy, first formulated as the separation of the laws of soul and body, becomes the very mechanism of their systemic conformity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-06","text":"The notion of encounter changes function: it no longer denotes a causal interaction but the regulated agreement of two independent developments.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:NX4","CH_UCIC_P_70:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RMD-07","text":"Experience is shifted from the status of foundation to that of an instance confirming an a priori framework.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-01","text":"Arguments concerning the absence of natural generation remain local when they establish only the non-absoluteness of birth or death.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A3","CH_UCIC_P_68:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-02","text":"The distinction between animal and machine changes scale when it links ontological permanence to bodily variation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:D2","CH_UCIC_P_69:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-03","text":"The distinction between the proper laws of soul and body becomes a current-level structure when it explains union through a global harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-04","text":"The bridge between the units is the idea of an identity that depends neither on an absolute beginning, nor on unchanged matter, nor on a direct interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:CGD-05","text":"The appearances of birth, death, and encounter become obsolete as ultimate descriptions, but are retained as local effects of a higher architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects the idea that an animal can arise absolutely from non-being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-02","text":"It likewise rejects the animal's absolute return to non-being and distinguishes local destruction from annihilation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-03","text":"It rejects the identification of the animal with the numerical preservation of its organic components.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that a conformity between soul and body results from a single law, a fusion, or a punctual interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:GNX-05","text":"It subordinates experience to a priori principles and refuses to let it alone found the ontology of natural transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the simple opposition between existence and non-existence must be inadequate for describing natural transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:DBN-02","text":"It must also be the case that the organic machine is not the ultimate principle of animal identity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:DBN-03","text":"The silently excluded rival model is that of a living being reducible to its present bodily state and its observable interactions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:DBN-04","text":"Local conformity can be intelligible only insofar as it is related to the universal totality represented by substances.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSA-01","text":"The structuring absence is that of a natural nothingness capable of serving simultaneously as the animal's origin and destination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSA-02","text":"The system renders unavailable an identity without an internal principle of continuity and without inscription within a universal order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSA-03","text":"Unity is admissible only on condition that it not be a fusion: it must be produced by the coordination of irreducible differences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-01","text":"The permanence of the animal is constructed through the convergence of three exclusions: no absolute beginning, no absolute annihilation, and no reduction to the organic machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_69:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX2","CL_UCIC_26:GA-01","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-02","text":"The animate principle becomes the point of mediation between the ontological permanence of the animal and the variability of its material supports.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:D1","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:GA-06","CL_UCIC_26:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-03","text":"The distinction between soul and body does not produce a mere duality: it becomes the formal condition of a coordinated unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:D1","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1","CL_UCIC_26:GA-08","CL_UCIC_26:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-04","text":"The representation of one and the same universe converts the heterogeneity of substances into commensurability without suppressing their autonomy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-05","text":"The soul-body union is an apparent causality produced by the synchronization of distinct series, not by a reciprocal transmission of operations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX1","CL_UCIC_26:GA-10","CL_UCIC_26:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-06","text":"Experience does not refute the metaphysical structure because it is reinscribed within it as confirmation of its observable effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_68:ME3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:XD-07","text":"The vocabulary of encounter retains an interactive appearance while designating, at the scale of the cluster, an already regulated coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:D4","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT5","CL_UCIC_26:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-01","text":"Natural being is no longer defined by an instant of appearance or disappearance, but by a persistent trajectory that absorbs its own transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT4","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02","text":"The body becomes a variable infrastructure of identity, while identity shifts toward an animate and relational principle of continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:GA-06","CL_UCIC_26:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-03","text":"Local causality is reclassified as a phenomenal effect of an architecture of pre-established correspondences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-10","CL_UCIC_26:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-04","text":"Biological temporal order describes changes internal to a permanence rather than an ontological passage between being and nothingness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-05","text":"The epistemic order is hierarchical: experience makes effects visible, but a priori principles determine their ontological scope.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:D4","CH_UCIC_P_68:SD3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:BSD-06","text":"The system's method consists in producing a positive reconstruction through an accumulation of exclusions rather than from an immediate empirical description.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS4","CL_UCIC_26:GA-01","CL_UCIC_26:GA-02","CL_UCIC_26:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-01","text":"The absence of a beginning calls forth the absence of an end, which transforms apparent death into modification of a persistent being.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-02","text":"The perishability of the machine triggers the separation between support and unity, then this separation reaffirms the indestructibility of the animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-03","text":"The separation of the laws of soul and body produces the need for a harmony, which subsequently transforms this separation into the condition of union.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-04","text":"The common representation of the universe serves as an intermediate attractor: it absorbs local differences into a global correspondence without cancelling them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-05","text":"The epistemic circuit proceeds from phenomena to principles, then from principles to the requalification of phenomena as confirmations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:RLE-06","text":"The terminal attractor is a persistent unity defined not by the identity of its components, but by the regulated continuity of its transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_69:ME3","CL_UCIC_26:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B01","text":"Negation of the natural beginning → negation of the natural end → exclusion of absolute generation and destruction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B02","text":"Apparent transformation → distinction between empirical event and ontological status → persistence of the animal through change.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:D3","CH_UCIC_P_68:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B03","text":"Perishability of the machine → dissociation of support and unity → grounding of identity in the animate principle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_69:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B04","text":"Soul-mirror of an indestructible universe → indestructibility of the animate principle → extension of permanence to the animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_69:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B05","text":"Proper laws of soul and body → separation of series → pre-established harmony → conformity without direct interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B06","text":"Common representation of the universe → commensurability of substances → reclassification of union as a systemic effect.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B07","text":"Observable experience → verification of an a priori principle → recursive closure between metaphysical foundation and biological phenomena.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AFM-B01","text":"Appearance of birth and death → refusal of absolute origin and annihilation → distinction between animal and machine → permanence of the animate principle → autonomy of series → universal harmony → conformity without direct causality → empirical confirmation of the a priori architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_70:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:AFM-B02","text":"The terminal closure replaces the life/death opposition with a structure of transformation, then replaces the soul/body opposition with a coordination of distinct series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-01","text":"Birth and death cease to be ontological boundaries and become transformations internal to a continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_68:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-02","text":"The object “animal” is mapped as a persistent unity bearing a variable machine, not as a stable material aggregate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-03","text":"Local destruction and total disappearance are separated as two categories of different ontological scope.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_69:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-04","text":"The soul-body union is shifted from the field of local interactions to that of global metaphysical coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-05","text":"Autonomy and conformity are no longer opposites: local autonomy becomes the mechanism of universal conformity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_70:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MME-06","text":"Experience is reclassified as a surface of verification for an a priori structure rather than as the ultimate source of ontology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_68:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit phenomena are generation, death, the perishability of the machine, and the apparent conformity of soul and body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These phenomena are distributed among a persistent animal unity, a variable material support, and two coordinated autonomous series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The system neutralizes empirical objections by changing the level at which they must be interpreted.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Natural time describes a succession of transformations within an existence without absolute beginning or end.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form accomplishes what it affirms: it successively negates absolutes in order to make appear a positive architecture of coordination and permanence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_68:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FL-01","text":"Natural non-finitude is operative but remains asserted from the absence of a beginning rather than demonstrated in the passage.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FL-02","text":"The passage from the indestructibility of the soul to that of the animal remains a metaphysical implication whose mediation is not fully explicated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FL-03","text":"The term encounter retains an interactional tone although the system excludes direct reciprocal causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_70:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:FL-04","text":"Experience is presented as concordant with the a priori, but this concordance does not constitute an independent foundation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:A6","CH_UCIC_P_68:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MP-01","text":"Death effects a phase change when it ceases to signify destruction and becomes a distinction between bodily transformation and animal permanence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MP-02","text":"The organic machine changes function when it passes from an apparent criterion of identity to replaceable material support.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_69:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MP-03","text":"The autonomy of substances changes valence when it passes from a risk of separation to the condition of their conformity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MP-04","text":"Causality changes status when it is retained as phenomenal appearance but removed from the order of reciprocal operations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a machine of stratified correspondences in which autonomous series represent one and the same universe without acting directly upon one another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:A5","CH_UCIC_P_70:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:HSI-02","text":"The animal subject becomes a unity of continuity capable of surviving the renewal of its supports and the variation of its configurations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:A6","CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:HSI-03","text":"Time is not a line running from being to nothingness, but a series of ordered transformations within a permanence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_69:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:HSI-04","text":"Possible navigation consists in distinguishing local appearances from the structures that coordinate them, while escape from the system would be a reduction to nothingness or to material identity, both prohibited.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_69:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the principal trajectory: absence of beginning, absence of annihilation, distinction between animal and machine, then permanence under transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B02","text":"The structure of union further requires the distinction of proper laws, pre-established harmony, and the common representation of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_70:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction remains dependent on prior a priori principles and on the unexplicated mechanism by which the soul transmits its indestructibility to the animal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B04","text":"The coherence of the system depends on the simultaneous maintenance of two gaps: machine and animal are not identical, soul and body are not causally fused.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_70:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B05","text":"The compression is sufficient if it preserves the negation–distinction–coordination–confirmation loop; it becomes insufficient if it reduces the contradictions of mediation to mere identities.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_68:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_70:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B06","text":"The minimal core of the cluster is an ontology of differential permanence: an animal persists not despite the transformations of its supports and relations, but through them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_69:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_70:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_26@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_26:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 76–78","context":"Proposition 76 · Proposition 77 · Proposition 78"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 79–81","order":27,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_71","CH_UCIC_P_72","CH_UCIC_P_73"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_27@R001","sha256":"23cd66ca438e00db8c10354464279d37881b03a876a68bc4b1738a3fe29288a6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-01","text":"Le problème est celui de la coexistence entre deux régimes causaux hétérogènes, l’un orienté par les fins et l’autre par les mouvements matériels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-02","text":"La distinction initiale des causalités est maintenue, mais elle est progressivement soumise à la clôture des invariants physiques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-03","text":"La conservation de la force interdit que l’âme ajoute une détermination énergétique au corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_72:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-04","text":"La conservation de la direction interdit que l’âme produise une réorientation corporelle qui échapperait à l’ordre matériel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_72:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-05","text":"L’interaction supposée est ainsi recodée en coordination de séries autonomes plutôt qu’en transmission causale entre elles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-06","text":"L’autonomie des corps et des âmes demeure opératoire, tandis que leur concordance phénoménale produit l’apparence d’une influence réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-07","text":"Le mouvement argumentatif va de la pluralité des causalités à la fermeture de l’interaction, puis de cette fermeture à l’harmonie préétablie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-08","text":"La clôture produite n’est pas une réduction de la finalité à la mécanique, mais une architecture de correspondance sans causalité transitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Les âmes et les corps relèvent de régimes causaux distincts, respectivement final et efficient.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’action des âmes se déploie par appétitions, fins et moyens plutôt que par mouvement matériel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] L’action corporelle relève des causes efficientes et des mouvements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] La distinction des régimes n’implique ni leur séparation absolue ni leur réduction l’un à l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_71:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] La matière conserve une quantité totale de force qui ferme toute production physique par l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","CH_UCIC_P_72:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] La direction totale de la matière se conserve selon une loi indépendante de l’action psychique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La double conservation ferme successivement les deux formes possibles d’intervention psychophysique : ajout de force et changement de direction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:D4","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] L’âme ne peut être une cause efficiente de la modification corporelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_72:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Les corps et les âmes opèrent comme s’ils pouvaient être expliqués indépendamment l’un de l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] La concordance observable est produite par une coordination de séries autonomes, non par une interaction transitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] L’harmonie préétablie constitue la forme métaphysique de la clôture complète de la causalité physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-01","text":"La distinction entre finalité et efficience persiste comme architecture de base, mais sa fonction se déplace d’une simple classification causale vers la justification d’une autonomie coordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-02","text":"L’harmonie passe d’une compatibilité générale entre règnes à une solution déterminée par l’impossibilité de l’interaction physique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-03","text":"La force puis la direction forment une séquence de fermeture : la seconde conservation absorbe la possibilité résiduelle laissée par la première.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:D4","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-04","text":"Le « comme si » mute d’un dispositif d’indépendance contrefactuelle en mécanisme expliquant l’apparence d’une influence réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-05","text":"L’interaction âme-corps n’est pas simplement rejetée : elle est absorbée dans une correspondance réglée entre séries séparées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-06","text":"La causalité mentale conserve son effet phénoménal, mais perd sa fonction de production physique et devient un effet de coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:D3","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-07","text":"L’erreur cartésienne se déplace d’une erreur sur l’interaction vers une erreur de connaissance des lois de conservation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-08","text":"L’indétermination du mécanisme harmonique persiste après la clôture causale et devient la limite terminale du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-01","text":"La distinction locale entre âmes et corps constitue une grammaire causale inférieure ; au niveau courant, elle devient une architecture de régimes parallèles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D1","CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-02","text":"Les lois particulières de conservation appartiennent à la machine physique locale ; leur interaction produit ici la clôture générale de l’intervention psychophysique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:D1","CH_UCIC_P_72:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-03","text":"Le « comme si » est localement un contrefactuel d’absence, mais devient au niveau courant la forme logique d’une causalité apparente sans transmission.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-04","text":"Les trois machines inférieures convergent vers une même opération : préserver la concordance tout en excluant le contact causal.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-05","text":"Les notions de force, de direction et d’absence deviennent subordonnées à la distinction courante entre production causale et correspondance phénoménale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_73:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-06","text":"Le mécanisme précis de l’harmonie reste localement sous-déterminé, mais cette lacune devient au niveau courant une condition de fermeture plutôt qu’un simple manque descriptif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une grammaire causale unique puisse expliquer simultanément l’action des âmes et celle des corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_71:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une âme puisse produire de la force ou réorienter matériellement un corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_72:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut qu’une différence de direction puisse préserver une causalité mentale indirecte après la conservation de la direction totale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut qu’une apparence de corrélation suffise à établir une interaction réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:D3","CH_UCIC_P_73:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut que l’autonomie des séries entraîne leur discordance phénoménale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut simultanément la réduction mécanique du réel et la réduction téléologique de la matière.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_71:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’idée d’un circuit causal commun aux âmes et aux corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-02","text":"Le système disqualifie le modèle selon lequel l’expérience de l’action volontaire prouverait une intervention physique réelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-03","text":"Il disqualifie une nature matérielle ouverte à des exceptions extramatérielles qui ne modifieraient ni force ni direction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-04","text":"Il refuse que la concordance observable soit la preuve immédiate d’une communication ontologique entre les ordres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-05","text":"Il rend inadmissible l’idée que l’harmonie puisse résulter d’une confusion des causalités plutôt que de leur coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_71:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSA-01","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une médiation commune capable de convertir une détermination psychique en modification matérielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité indisponible est celle d’une causalité psychophysique directe qui respecterait néanmoins les invariants matériels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSA-03","text":"Le système contourne l’idée d’une simultanéité ontologiquement active : la simultanéité ne vaut que comme concordance de séries.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSA-04","text":"Ce qui est traité comme ontologiquement inadmissible n’est pas la liaison phénoménale, mais la production transitive d’un ordre par l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-01","text":"La distinction entre causalité finale et causalité efficiente devient, sous l’effet des lois de conservation, une distinction entre deux séries coordonnées mais causalement closes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","CL_UCIC_27:GA-05","CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-02","text":"La conservation de la force et celle de la direction ne réfutent pas deux interactions différentes ; elles ferment ensemble l’espace logique de l’intervention psychophysique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-05","CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_72:D4","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-03","text":"L’harmonie préétablie apparaît comme le nom donné à la concordance qui subsiste après l’élimination successive de toutes les formes de causalité transitive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-07","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CL_UCIC_27:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-04","text":"Le « comme si » transforme l’impossibilité de l’interaction en condition de l’apparence d’influence, de sorte que la négation causale produit une liaison phénoménale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-09","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6","CH_UCIC_P_73:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-05","text":"La matière et l’âme ne sont pas seulement deux domaines distincts : elles deviennent deux régimes dont la coordination explique pourquoi leur séparation ne se manifeste pas comme rupture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_73:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-06","text":"Le problème métaphysique de l’interaction est déplacé vers une théorie de la compatibilité structurelle entre ordres causalement autonomes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:GA-07","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-07","text":"La connaissance des lois naturelles ne fournit pas le mécanisme positif de l’harmonie ; elle rend seulement l’interaction impossible et la coordination nécessaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01","text":"La causalité n’est plus un transfert entre agents, mais une distribution de fonctions entre séries hétérogènes dont la concordance est réglée à un autre niveau.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-02","text":"Le sujet volontaire perd le statut de producteur d’effets corporels et devient le point phénoménal où une série autonome est vécue comme action.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-08","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-03","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme coexistence de séries causalement fermées dont l’unité ne provient pas d’une médiation commune.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-04","text":"Le temps causal cesse d’être conçu comme une chaîne d’influences croisées et devient une simultanéité ordonnée de développements parallèles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-09","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-05","text":"La résolution métaphysique procède par élimination : chaque conservation retire une forme d’intervention jusqu’à ce que la coordination apparaisse comme unique issue systémique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-05","CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-06","text":"La connaissance complète des lois naturelles ne produit pas une maîtrise causale accrue du sujet ; elle réduit son pouvoir d’intervention et augmente la lisibilité de la structure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-01","text":"La boucle centrale est : distinction des régimes → recherche d’une interaction → conservation → impossibilité de l’interaction → retour à l’harmonie comme coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-02","text":"La première conservation ferme l’ajout de force ; la seconde ferme la réorientation ; la répétition du schème transforme une réfutation locale en clôture globale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-03","text":"L’autonomie contrefactuelle de chaque ordre revient sous une forme mutée comme apparence d’influence réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est une harmonie qui doit expliquer la concordance sans réintroduire l’interaction qu’elle remplace.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-05","text":"Le système spirale autour d’une absence : plus la concordance est affirmée, plus la médiation commune doit être exclue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-06","text":"La répétition de la coordination signale un changement de phase : elle cesse d’être une propriété entre deux ordres et devient le principe organisateur du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B01","text":"Deux régimes causaux distincts sont posés : finalité des âmes et efficience des corps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B02","text":"Chaque régime reçoit son mode opératoire propre sans que la distinction produise encore une séparation ontologique absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_71:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B03","text":"L’hypothèse d’une intervention de l’âme dans le corps est testée contre la conservation de la force.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_72:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B04","text":"La possibilité résiduelle d’une modification de direction est testée contre la conservation de la direction totale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_72:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B05","text":"La fermeture des deux voies d’intervention recode l’interaction en coordination de séries autonomes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B06","text":"L’autonomie est reformulée par le double « comme si » : chaque ordre agit indépendamment, mais la concordance rend cette indépendance phénoménalement invisible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B07","text":"La structure terminale est une harmonie préétablie : liaison observable, absence de transmission, mécanisme positif non spécifié.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B01","text":"Régimes causaux distincts → harmonie encore indéterminée → hypothèse d’intervention psychophysique → conservation de la force → conservation de la direction → clôture de l’interaction → autonomie parallèle → apparence d’influence → coordination sans transmission → harmonie préétablie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_73:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B02","text":"Le mouvement réel va d’une dualité causale à une unité structurelle non réductrice : la coordination remplace l’action croisée sans supprimer la concordance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D4","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-01","text":"Le champ causal est reclassé en production interne des séries et en correspondance inter-séries, au lieu d’être organisé par transfert d’influences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_73:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-02","text":"La distinction entre finalité et efficience cesse d’être une alternative exclusive et devient une différence fonctionnelle compatible avec l’unité du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-03","text":"L’interaction âme-corps est reclassée comme phénomène à expliquer plutôt que comme mécanisme à présupposer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-04","text":"La conservation physique devient un opérateur de reclassification métaphysique : elle transforme une question sur la volonté en question sur la structure des lois.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-05","text":"L’autonomie et la liaison ne sont plus des contraires simples : l’autonomie des séries devient la condition de la liaison phénoménale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-06","text":"Une nouvelle méthode d’analyse apparaît : tester toute prétendue interaction contre les invariants du régime auquel elle prétend appartenir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont les âmes, les corps, la force, la direction et l’apparence d’une influence réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Le système distribue l’action entre deux ordres autonomes et fait de la conservation l’opérateur de leur clôture respective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] La question « comment l’un agit-il sur l’autre ? » est remplacée par celle de la production d’une apparence d’influence entre séries indépendantes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_73:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est pensé comme simultanéité ordonnée de séries dont l’autonomie n’empêche pas la concordance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] L’argument accomplit sa thèse par exclusions successives : il ne démontre pas un mécanisme harmonique, il rend l’interaction de plus en plus impossible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AF3","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FL-01","text":"Le système affirme une harmonie entre causalités distinctes sans expliciter la médiation concrète qui rend cette harmonie effective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FL-02","text":"Il parle d’influence réciproque pour décrire un phénomène dont sa propre architecture interdit la causalité réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FL-03","text":"L’autonomie radicale des séries et leur liaison phénoménale sont compatibles dans le système, mais leur compatibilité reste structurellement sous-déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FL-04","text":"La conservation de la direction totale est utilisée pour exclure toute réorientation locale, ce qui constitue le point le plus compressé de l’inférence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_72:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MP-01","text":"La causalité passe d’une relation entre agents à une distribution parallèle de fonctions entre séries.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MP-02","text":"La conservation de la force mute en principe métaphysique lorsqu’elle cesse seulement de mesurer la matière et commence à exclure l’action de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MP-03","text":"Le « comme si » mute d’une hypothèse contrefactuelle en forme positive de la coordination phénoménale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MP-04","text":"L’harmonie cesse d’être une propriété ajoutée aux deux règnes et devient l’attracteur qui organise leur séparation, leur clôture et leur concordance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine à séries parallèles : chaque ordre produit son propre développement sans transmettre d’énergie ni de direction à l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient le lieu phénoménal où une coordination préétablie est vécue comme volonté, influence ou action réciproque.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:HSI-03","text":"Le temps du système n’est pas celui d’une transmission croisée, mais celui de développements simultanés dont la concordance est antérieure à l’interaction apparente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:HSI-04","text":"La lutte théorique consiste à distinguer l’apparence d’influence du mécanisme causal et à maintenir la concordance sans réintroduire le contact exclu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre noyaux : distinction des causalités, conservation de la force, conservation de la direction et coordination des séries autonomes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D1","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B02","text":"Ces noyaux suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement de la dualité causale vers l’harmonie sans interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B03","text":"La reconstruction perdrait sa fidélité si elle supprimait la différence entre transfert de force et changement de direction, car cette différence constitue l’escalade réfutative.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination restante porte sur le mécanisme positif de l’harmonie et non sur la clôture négative de l’interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B05","text":"Le système est cohérent à condition de maintenir la distinction entre concordance phénoménale et causalité transitive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B06","text":"La compression conserve l’architecture générative : pluralité causale → fermeture des invariants → autonomie parallèle → apparence d’influence → harmonie coordinatrice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_73:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B07","text":"L’élément irréductible est la tension entre une harmonie affirmée comme nécessité et une médiation laissée non spécifiée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200101224075Z_7adbefd7","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 79–81","source_sha256":"23cd66ca438e00db8c10354464279d37881b03a876a68bc4b1738a3fe29288a6","sha256":"47528675a7e0d8cd6e7f3b16d5f610ac93ceb76fc373a2e905a3ed98540beb28","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:01:01.227323+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-01","text":"The problem is that of the coexistence of two heterogeneous causal regimes, one oriented by ends and the other by material movements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-02","text":"The initial distinction between causalities is maintained, but it is progressively subjected to the closure of physical invariants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-03","text":"The conservation of force prohibits the soul from adding an energetic determination to the body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_72:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-04","text":"The conservation of direction prohibits the soul from producing a bodily reorientation that would escape the material order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_72:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-05","text":"The supposed interaction is thus recoded as coordination of autonomous series rather than as causal transmission between them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-06","text":"The autonomy of bodies and souls remains operative, while their phenomenal concordance produces the appearance of reciprocal influence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-07","text":"The argumentative movement proceeds from the plurality of causalities to the closure of interaction, then from this closure to pre-established harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AS-08","text":"The closure produced is not a reduction of finality to mechanics, but an architecture of correspondence without transitive causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Souls and bodies belong to distinct causal regimes, final and efficient respectively.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The action of souls unfolds through appetitions, ends, and means rather than through material movement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Bodily action pertains to efficient causes and movements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] The distinction of regimes implies neither their absolute separation nor their reduction to one another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_71:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Matter conserves a total quantity of force that precludes any physical production by the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A1","CH_UCIC_P_72:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The total direction of matter is conserved according to a law independent of psychic action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The double conservation successively closes off the two possible forms of psychophysical intervention: addition of force and change of direction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:D4","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] The soul cannot be an efficient cause of bodily modification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_72:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Bodies and souls operate as if they could be explained independently of one another.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Observable concordance is produced by a coordination of autonomous series, not by transitive interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Pre-established harmony constitutes the metaphysical form of the complete closure of physical causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_72:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-01","text":"The distinction between finality and efficiency persists as a basic architecture, but its function shifts from a simple causal classification toward the justification of a coordinated autonomy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-02","text":"Harmony shifts from a general compatibility between realms to a solution determined by the impossibility of physical interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-03","text":"Force and then direction form a sequence of closure: the second conservation absorbs the residual possibility left by the first.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:D4","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-04","text":"The “as if” mutates from a device of counterfactual independence into a mechanism explaining the appearance of reciprocal influence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-05","text":"Soul-body interaction is not simply rejected: it is absorbed into a regulated correspondence between separate series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-06","text":"Mental causality retains its phenomenal effect, but loses its function of physical production and becomes an effect of coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:D3","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-07","text":"The Cartesian error shifts from an error concerning interaction to an error in knowledge of the laws of conservation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_72:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RMD-08","text":"The indeterminacy of the harmonic mechanism persists after causal closure and becomes the terminal limit of the system.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-01","text":"The local distinction between souls and bodies constitutes a lower causal grammar; at the current level, it becomes an architecture of parallel regimes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D1","CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-02","text":"The particular laws of conservation belong to the local physical machine; their interaction here produces the general closure of psychophysical intervention.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:D1","CH_UCIC_P_72:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-03","text":"The “as if” is locally a counterfactual of absence, but at the current level becomes the logical form of an apparent causality without transmission.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-04","text":"The three lower machines converge toward one operation: preserving concordance while excluding causal contact.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-05","text":"The notions of force, direction, and absence become subordinate to the current distinction between causal production and phenomenal correspondence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_73:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:CGD-06","text":"The precise mechanism of harmony remains locally underdetermined, but this gap becomes, at the current level, a condition of closure rather than a simple descriptive lack.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a single causal grammar could simultaneously explain the action of souls and that of bodies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_71:NX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that a soul could produce force or materially reorient a body.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_72:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that a difference in direction could preserve an indirect mental causality after the conservation of total direction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that an appearance of correlation could suffice to establish a real interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:D3","CH_UCIC_P_73:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the possibility that the autonomy of the series entails their phenomenal discordance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:NX6","CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:GNX-06","text":"It simultaneously excludes the mechanical reduction of reality and the teleological reduction of matter.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_71:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the idea of a causal circuit common to souls and bodies must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-02","text":"The system disqualifies the model according to which the experience of voluntary action would prove a real physical intervention.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-03","text":"It disqualifies a material nature open to extramaterial exceptions that would modify neither force nor direction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-04","text":"It rejects the claim that observable concordance is immediate proof of ontological communication between the orders.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:DBN-05","text":"It renders inadmissible the idea that harmony could result from a confusion of causalities rather than from their coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_71:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSA-01","text":"The structuring absence is that of a common mediation capable of converting a psychic determination into a material modification.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSA-02","text":"The unavailable possibility is that of a direct psychophysical causality that would nevertheless respect material invariants.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSA-03","text":"The system bypasses the idea of an ontologically active simultaneity: simultaneity has value only as concordance of series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSA-04","text":"What is treated as ontologically inadmissible is not phenomenal connection, but the transitive production of one order by the other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-01","text":"The distinction between final causality and efficient causality becomes, under the effect of the laws of conservation, a distinction between two coordinated yet causally closed series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","CL_UCIC_27:GA-05","CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-02","text":"The conservation of force and that of direction do not refute two different interactions; together, they close the logical space of psychophysical intervention.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-05","CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_72:D4","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-03","text":"Pre-established harmony appears as the name given to the concordance that remains after the successive elimination of all forms of transitive causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-07","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CL_UCIC_27:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-04","text":"The “as if” transforms the impossibility of interaction into the condition of the appearance of influence, such that causal negation produces a phenomenal connection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-09","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6","CH_UCIC_P_73:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-05","text":"Matter and soul are not merely two distinct domains: they become two regimes whose coordination explains why their separation does not manifest itself as rupture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_73:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-06","text":"The metaphysical problem of interaction is displaced toward a theory of structural compatibility between causally autonomous orders.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:GA-07","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:XD-07","text":"Knowledge of natural laws does not provide the positive mechanism of harmony; it merely renders interaction impossible and coordination necessary.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01","text":"Causality is no longer a transfer between agents, but a distribution of functions among heterogeneous series whose concordance is regulated at another level.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-02","text":"The willing subject loses the status of producer of bodily effects and becomes the phenomenal point at which an autonomous series is experienced as action.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-08","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-03","text":"Reality is reclassified as the coexistence of causally closed series whose unity does not derive from a common mediation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-04","text":"Causal time ceases to be conceived as a chain of cross-influences and becomes an ordered simultaneity of parallel developments.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-09","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-05","text":"The metaphysical resolution proceeds through elimination: each conservation removes a form of intervention until coordination appears as the sole systemic outcome.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-05","CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:BSD-06","text":"Complete knowledge of natural laws does not produce increased causal mastery by the subject; it reduces its power of intervention and increases the legibility of structure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_72:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-01","text":"The central loop is: distinction of regimes → search for an interaction → conservation → impossibility of interaction → return to harmony as coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-02","text":"The first conservation closes off the addition of force; the second closes off reorientation; repetition of the schema transforms a local refutation into a global closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-03","text":"The counterfactual autonomy of each order returns in a mutated form as the appearance of reciprocal influence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-04","text":"The conceptual attractor is a harmony that must explain concordance without reintroducing the interaction it replaces.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-05","text":"The system spirals around an absence: the more concordance is affirmed, the more common mediation must be excluded.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:RLE-06","text":"The repetition of coordination signals a phase change: it ceases to be a property between two orders and becomes the organizing principle of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B01","text":"Two distinct causal regimes are posited: the finality of souls and the efficiency of bodies.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A1","CH_UCIC_P_71:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B02","text":"Each regime receives its own mode of operation without the distinction yet producing an absolute ontological separation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_71:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B03","text":"The hypothesis of an intervention of the soul in the body is tested against the conservation of force.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_72:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B04","text":"The residual possibility of a modification of direction is tested against the conservation of total direction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_72:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B05","text":"The closure of the two avenues of intervention recodes interaction as coordination of autonomous series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B06","text":"Autonomy is reformulated through the double “as if”: each order acts independently, but concordance renders this independence phenomenally invisible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A2","CH_UCIC_P_73:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B07","text":"The terminal structure is a pre-established harmony: observable connection, absence of transmission, unspecified positive mechanism.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B01","text":"Distinct causal regimes → harmony still indeterminate → hypothesis of psychophysical intervention → conservation of force → conservation of direction → closure of interaction → parallel autonomy → appearance of influence → coordination without transmission → pre-established harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_73:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B02","text":"The real movement proceeds from a causal duality to a non-reductive structural unity: coordination replaces cross-action without eliminating concordance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D4","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-01","text":"The causal field is reclassified into internal production of series and inter-series correspondence, instead of being organized by the transfer of influences.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_73:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-02","text":"The distinction between finality and efficiency ceases to be an exclusive alternative and becomes a functional difference compatible with the unity of reality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-03","text":"Soul-body interaction is reclassified as a phenomenon to be explained rather than as a mechanism to be presupposed.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-04","text":"Physical conservation becomes an operator of metaphysical reclassification: it transforms a question about the will into a question about the structure of laws.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-05","text":"Autonomy and connection are no longer simple opposites: the autonomy of the series becomes the condition of phenomenal connection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MME-06","text":"A new method of analysis appears: test every purported interaction against the invariants of the regime to which it claims to belong.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are souls, bodies, force, direction, and the appearance of reciprocal influence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] The system distributes action between two autonomous orders and makes conservation the operator of their respective closure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The question “how does one act upon the other?” is replaced by that of producing an appearance of influence between independent series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_73:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Reality is conceived as an ordered simultaneity of series whose autonomy does not prevent concordance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_71:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argument performs its thesis through successive exclusions: it does not demonstrate a harmonic mechanism; it renders interaction increasingly impossible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:AF3","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FL-01","text":"The system affirms a harmony between distinct causalities without making explicit the concrete mediation that renders this harmony effective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_71:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FL-02","text":"It speaks of reciprocal influence to describe a phenomenon whose reciprocal causality its own architecture prohibits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_73:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FL-03","text":"The radical autonomy of the series and their phenomenal connection are compatible in the system, but their compatibility remains structurally underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_73:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:FL-04","text":"The conservation of total direction is used to exclude every local reorientation, which constitutes the most compressed point of the inference.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_72:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MP-01","text":"Causality passes from a relation between agents to a parallel distribution of functions among series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_73:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MP-02","text":"The conservation of force mutates into a metaphysical principle when it ceases merely to measure matter and begins to exclude the action of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MP-03","text":"The “as if” mutates from a counterfactual hypothesis into a positive form of phenomenal coordination.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:A5","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MP-04","text":"Harmony ceases to be a property added to the two realms and becomes the attractor that organizes their separation, their closure, and their concordance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:A4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a machine of parallel series: each order produces its own development without transmitting energy or direction to the other.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes the phenomenal site where a pre-established coordination is experienced as will, influence, or reciprocal action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_72:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:HSI-03","text":"The system's time is not that of cross-transmission, but that of simultaneous developments whose concordance precedes apparent interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_72:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:HSI-04","text":"The theoretical struggle consists in distinguishing the appearance of influence from the causal mechanism and in maintaining concordance without reintroducing the excluded contact.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_73:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four nuclei: distinction of causalities, conservation of force, conservation of direction, and coordination of autonomous series.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:D1","CH_UCIC_P_72:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B02","text":"These nuclei suffice to reconstruct the movement from causal duality toward harmony without interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction would lose its fidelity if it suppressed the difference between transfer of force and change of direction, because this difference constitutes the refutative escalation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B04","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the positive mechanism of harmony and not the negative closure of interaction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_72:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B05","text":"The system is coherent provided that the distinction between phenomenal concordance and transitive causality is maintained.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_73:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B06","text":"The compression preserves the generative architecture: causal plurality → closure of invariants → parallel autonomy → appearance of influence → coordinating harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_73:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B07","text":"The irreducible element is the tension between a harmony affirmed as necessity and a mediation left unspecified.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_71:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_73:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_27@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_27:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 79–81","context":"Proposition 79 · Proposition 80 · Proposition 81"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 82–84","order":28,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_74","CH_UCIC_P_75","CH_UCIC_P_76"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_28@R001","sha256":"a192960fa444924d4e2db64cf021a9cc729927d3d62e294bd04ac80498f17b9d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-01","text":"Le système doit articuler la continuité générale du vivant avec l’émergence d’un statut spirituel qui ne soit ni une rupture substantielle ni une simple propriété biologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-02","text":"La différence entre animalité et spiritualité est d’abord recadrée comme une variation de degré, puis comme une transformation de fonction et de régime relationnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-03","text":"Le fond vital commun rend possible une différenciation progressive des facultés sans supprimer la continuité de l’âme à travers les transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-04","text":"La conception fonctionne comme seuil d’actualisation de la raison, mais son interaction avec les capacités cognitives et sociales de l’esprit déplace ce seuil vers une architecture plus vaste de participation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-05","text":"L’esprit n’est pas seulement une âme vivante plus élevée : il devient une image de la Divinité capable de saisir l’ordre dont il participe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-06","text":"La connaissance spirituelle se convertit en production architectonique locale, de sorte que connaître l’ordre signifie pouvoir en reproduire certains principes.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-07","text":"Cette puissance architectonique produit une capacité d’entrée en société avec Dieu, faisant passer le système de la causalité productive à la relation politique et familiale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-08","text":"Le mouvement terminal est une reclassification du vivant en réseau de puissances spirituelles locales, analogues à la Divinité mais limitées, adressables et gouvernables.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Le vivant forme une continuité fondamentale dans laquelle l’animalité et l’âme ne sont pas épuisées par les limites individuelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’âme conserve une identité transindividuelle tout en pouvant changer de degré de faculté et de statut.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La distinction entre âme sensitive et âme raisonnable ne sépare pas deux substances, mais deux régimes fonctionnels d’une continuité animée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] La conception constitue un opérateur de passage par lequel une âme sensitive peut accéder à la raison et au statut d’Esprit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Toute âme représente l’univers créé, mais l’esprit ajoute à cette représentation une relation d’image à la Divinité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La ressemblance divine produit une capacité réflexive qui connaît l’ordre de l’univers et non seulement la multiplicité de ses créatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] La connaissance spirituelle se réalise comme imitation architectonique par échantillons, dans un domaine propre et limité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] L’esprit est défini par une capacité à entrer en société avec Dieu, ce qui excède le régime de la machine produite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] La relation à Dieu combine gouvernement princier et filiation paternelle sans se réduire à l’un ou à l’autre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] La forme accomplie de l’esprit est celle d’une puissance divine locale, dérivée et relationnelle, plutôt que celle d’une divinité autonome ou d’une machine passive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-01","text":"La continuité du vivant revient d’abord comme identité du fond vital, puis comme condition de transformations durables du degré de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-02","text":"La permanence de l’âme cesse de signifier conservation inchangée : elle devient la capacité de traverser une mutation fonctionnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-03","text":"La conception se déplace d’un seuil biologique d’humanisation vers la condition d’accès à une forme supérieure de cognition, de production et de relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-04","text":"Le miroir vivant revient sous une forme mutée : il ne reflète plus seulement les créatures, mais devient image de leur principe d’ordre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-05","text":"La représentation devient connaissance systémique, puis la connaissance devient capacité architectonique ; le concept de miroir est ainsi absorbé dans une machine productive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-06","text":"La production divine, d’abord opposée au rapport des machines, est recodée en gouvernement et en filiation dès que l’esprit devient un sujet adressable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-07","text":"La figure de la petite divinité perd sa fonction si elle est isolée ; elle devient opératoire seulement lorsqu’elle est réinscrite dans une société de puissances limitées.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-01","text":"La distinction entre animaux spermatiques et humains demeure locale à la couche inférieure ; au niveau courant, elle devient le premier cas d’une théorie générale de la différenciation graduelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-02","text":"L’élection de certains animaux et le mécanisme précis de l’élévation par la conception restent des sous-déterminations locales ; ils ne constituent pas l’architecture globale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-03","text":"La représentation de l’univers par les âmes ordinaires est locale ; à l’échelle du cluster, elle devient le substrat d’une montée vers la réflexivité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-04","text":"L’imitation par échantillons n’est pas la thèse totale, mais le mécanisme local par lequel une puissance spirituelle limitée participe à l’architecture universelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-05","text":"Les figures du prince et du père sont des modèles relationnels locaux ; leur interaction produit au niveau courant un régime mixte de gouvernement et de filiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-06","text":"Le rapport machine-inventeur est un modèle négatif inférieur ; au niveau courant, il sert à délimiter une ontologie relationnelle de l’esprit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-07","text":"La frontière animal-humain, le miroir créaturel et la relation sociale sont absorbés dans une seule structure : l’actualisation graduelle d’une puissance vivante et architectonique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut une rupture ontologique absolue entre animalité et spiritualité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une âme soit spirituelle par sa seule présence dans un vivant ou par sa seule capacité de représentation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut qu’une connaissance de l’univers produise automatiquement une puissance illimitée : toute imitation reste locale et échantillonnaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que la relation divine aux esprits soit adéquatement décrite par la seule invention d’une machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une autonomie absolue de l’esprit : la puissance divine locale reste dérivée, limitée et inscrite dans une relation de dépendance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-01","text":"Le système ne peut tenir que si l’origine de l’esprit n’est ni une création ex nihilo d’une substance séparée ni une simple conservation de l’animalité sensible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-02","text":"Il disqualifie simultanément le matérialisme de la machine et le spiritualisme d’une puissance sans genèse, en imposant une transformation continue de la vie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-03","text":"Il rend inadmissible une cognition purement contemplative : connaître l’ordre doit ouvrir une capacité de le reproduire localement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-04","text":"Il rend également inadmissible une création spirituelle indépendante : l’architectonique locale demeure une participation à un ordre auteur et supérieur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-05","text":"Le modèle total rival silencieusement exclu est celui d’un univers composé soit de machines sans société, soit de divinités sans limitation ni hiérarchie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSA-01","text":"Le système rend indisponible l’idée d’un sujet rationnel originairement séparé de toute continuité animale, productive et relationnelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSA-02","text":"Il ne peut admettre un réel sans ordre imitable, car la connaissance spirituelle n’existe qu’en tant qu’elle peut se convertir en architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSA-03","text":"Il contourne sans la résoudre la question du mécanisme exact qui transforme une âme sensitive en esprit capable de raison, d’architecture et de société.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSA-04","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une relation divine purement causale : le système exige un Dieu qui puisse être auteur, prince et père.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-01","text":"La continuité vitale et la différenciation des degrés produisent une conception de l’esprit comme transformation interne du vivant plutôt que comme ajout substantiel extérieur.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-01","CL_UCIC_28:GA-02","CL_UCIC_28:GA-03","CH_UCIC_P_74:D3","CH_UCIC_P_74:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-02","text":"La fonction de miroir, jointe à l’image divine, convertit la représentation du monde en réflexivité sur le système qui l’organise.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-05","CL_UCIC_28:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_75:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-03","text":"La connaissance systémique et l’imitation architectonique font de l’esprit un agent productif sans lui conférer une causalité originaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-06","CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_75:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-04","text":"L’opposition entre machine et esprit, combinée à la limitation départementale, institue un régime médian entre passivité mécanique et autonomie divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_76:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-05","text":"La capacité architectonique devient une capacité sociale : l’esprit ne se contente plus de reproduire un ordre, il peut être inscrit dans l’ordre relationnel de son Auteur.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_76:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-06","text":"La limitation des puissances spirituelles rend compatible la pluralité des esprits avec une unité supérieure de gouvernement et de filiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_75:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-07","text":"L’interaction des trois unités produit une figure nouvelle : une vie graduée qui devient localement architectonique, puis politiquement et familialement adressable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-03","CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_76:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-01","text":"Ontologiquement, l’esprit n’est pas une substance isolée mais un mode supérieur d’organisation du vivant, défini par la convergence de la raison, de l’architecture et de la relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-02","text":"Épistémiquement, connaître ne signifie plus seulement représenter : la connaissance valide est celle qui saisit une structure et peut en produire des échantillons.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-03","text":"Stratégiquement, la puissance spirituelle est distribuée en départements locaux plutôt que concentrée dans une faculté globale ou une souveraineté autonome.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-04","text":"Politiquement, l’univers est reclassé comme un ordre de sujets et d’enfants gouvernés par un Auteur, et non comme une collection d’objets fabriqués.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05","text":"Temporellement, la permanence de l’âme autorise une histoire des transformations de faculté : l’identité persiste en changeant de régime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-06","text":"Méthodologiquement, le système se reconstruit par déplacements successifs d’une opposition : animal contre esprit, miroir contre image, machine contre sujet, production contre société.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-07","text":"Le statut du sujet devient celui d’un agent dérivé capable de reproduire localement l’ordre qui le produit et de participer à la relation qui le gouverne.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale va de la continuité vitale à la différenciation spirituelle, puis de la spiritualité à une requalification supérieure de la continuité elle-même.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-02","text":"Le miroir devient image, l’image devient connaissance, la connaissance devient architecture, et l’architecture revient comme preuve d’une ressemblance divine active.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-03","text":"La puissance locale appelle une limitation de domaine ; cette limitation rend possible la pluralité des esprits, qui appelle à son tour une structure commune de gouvernement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-04","text":"L’exclusion de la machine pure force l’escalade vers le sujet, puis vers le citoyen ou l’enfant d’un ordre divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur conceptuel est une société de puissances analogues : chacune reproduit localement l’architecture divine sans pouvoir se substituer à son Auteur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-06","text":"La répétition de la limitation ne réduit pas la puissance ; elle la transforme en condition de relation, de distribution et de coexistence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B01","text":"Continuité du vivant → permanence transindividuelle de l’âme → possibilité d’une différenciation sans rupture substantielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B02","text":"Âme sensitive → seuil de conception → actualisation de la raison → constitution graduelle de l’Esprit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B03","text":"Miroir des créatures → image de la Divinité → connaissance du système de l’univers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B04","text":"Connaissance systémique → imitation par échantillons → puissance architectonique locale et limitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B05","text":"Puissance locale → capacité d’entrer en société → dépassement du modèle inventeur-machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B06","text":"Dépassement du mécanisme → gouvernement princier + filiation paternelle → esprit comme sujet dérivé dans une architecture divine distribuée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B01","text":"Continuité vitale → transformation graduelle des facultés → émergence de la raison → image divine → connaissance architectonique → puissance locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B02","text":"Puissance architectonique limitée → capacité sociale → reclassification du rapport à Dieu → gouvernement + filiation → statut spirituel relationnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B03","text":"L’ensemble se clôt sur une convergence systémique : la continuité du vivant est conservée, mais elle est désormais organisée comme une pluralité de puissances locales participant à un ordre divin commun.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-01","text":"La carte ontologique cesse d’opposer simplement animal et humain ; elle distingue des régimes successifs de sensibilité, de raison, de représentation et de participation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-02","text":"La conception est reclassée comme opérateur de transformation ontologique, et non comme simple événement biologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-03","text":"La connaissance et la production sont réunies dans une même fonction architectonique : comprendre l’ordre implique pouvoir en reproduire localement la forme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-04","text":"La création est cartographiée selon plusieurs régimes simultanés : production, gouvernement et filiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-05","text":"La multiplicité des esprits devient une distribution de puissances divines locales, chacune limitée par son département et intégrée à une société supérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-06","text":"La fausse opposition entre dépendance et activité s’effondre : l’esprit est actif précisément parce que sa puissance reste dérivée et située.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les animaux spermatiques, les âmes sensitives, les esprits et les relations de société fournissent les objets explicites du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Ces objets sont organisés par une chaîne de médiations : continuité vitale, degrés de faculté, représentation, ressemblance divine, architecture et statut relationnel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — La stratégie consiste à remplacer chaque opposition statique par une séquence de recodages fonctionnels : l’animal devient esprit, le miroir devient architecte, la créature devient sujet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel est pensé comme une continuité durable capable de produire des mutations de statut sans perdre l’identité de l’âme.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — La forme argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle décrit : elle procède par élévations successives, chaque négation d’un modèle insuffisant ouvrant un régime relationnel plus riche.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FL-01","text":"La continuité du vivant fonde la singularité spirituelle, mais cette singularité introduit une hiérarchie qui ne peut être réduite à une simple différence de degré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FL-02","text":"La figure de la petite divinité augmente l’agentivité de l’esprit tout en maintenant sa dépendance à l’égard de l’Auteur ; la tension est constitutive et non résolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FL-03","text":"Le rapport machine-inventeur reste une condition productive de l’existence des créatures, mais il est déclaré insuffisant dès qu’il s’agit des esprits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FL-04","text":"Le gouvernement princier et la filiation paternelle décrivent deux formes de dépendance qui se superposent sans que leur hiérarchie soit explicitée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation est le passage de la permanence de l’âme à la mobilité de son degré : conserver l’identité devient pouvoir changer de faculté.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MP-02","text":"Le second point de mutation est le passage du miroir à l’image divine : la représentation du monde devient représentation de son principe d’organisation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation est la conversion de la connaissance en imitation architectonique, qui transforme la cognition en agentivité locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MP-04","text":"Le quatrième point de mutation est le passage de la puissance architectonique à la société avec Dieu : l’agent local devient sujet d’un ordre politique et familial.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une architecture vivante à degrés, capable de conserver ses unités tout en les faisant passer d’un régime de sensibilité à un régime de participation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient une puissance locale qui reflète, comprend, imite et reproduit partiellement l’ordre dont elle dépend.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas une simple succession d’états : il est le milieu d’une élévation fonctionnelle qui transforme le statut sans abolir la continuité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:HSI-04","text":"La lutte ou l’échappée possibles ne consistent pas à sortir de l’ordre, mais à changer de degré, de département et de régime relationnel à l’intérieur d’une architecture supérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige quatre invariants : continuité du vivant, mobilité des degrés de l’âme, ressemblance divine productive et relation sociale avec Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B02","text":"La chaîne minimale reste suffisante si elle conserve le mouvement réel : identité vitale → différenciation → élévation → architecture → société.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B03","text":"La reconstruction demeure sous-déterminée quant au mécanisme de l’élection, de la conception et de l’élévation, mais ces lacunes n’empêchent pas d’identifier la machine générative du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence dépend de l’acceptation d’une transformation de degré sans rupture substantielle, puis d’une participation divine sans autonomie absolue.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B05","text":"La compression est fidèle si elle conserve la tension entre continuité et privilège, activité et dépendance, puissance locale et ordre supérieur ; toute réduction supprimant ces tensions détruit l’architecture courante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200137816944Z_646e11e1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 82–84","source_sha256":"a192960fa444924d4e2db64cf021a9cc729927d3d62e294bd04ac80498f17b9d","sha256":"3e33d777a5cb0be6ab2b14497acb92217641caf9aab0f06d8629d40903ee732d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:01:37.819164+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-01","text":"The system must articulate the general continuity of living beings with the emergence of a spiritual status that is neither a substantial rupture nor a mere biological property.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-02","text":"The difference between animality and spirituality is first reframed as a variation in degree, then as a transformation of function and relational regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-03","text":"The common vital ground makes possible a progressive differentiation of faculties without suppressing the continuity of the soul across transformations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-04","text":"Conception functions as a threshold for the actualization of reason, but its interaction with the cognitive and social capacities of the mind shifts this threshold toward a broader architecture of participation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-05","text":"The mind is not merely a higher living soul: it becomes an image of the Divinity, capable of grasping the order in which it participates.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-06","text":"Spiritual knowledge is converted into local architectonic production, such that knowing the order means being able to reproduce some of its principles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-07","text":"This architectonic power produces a capacity to enter into society with God, moving the system from productive causality to political and familial relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AS-08","text":"The terminal movement is a reclassification of living beings into a network of local spiritual powers, analogous to the Divinity but limited, addressable, and governable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Living beings form a fundamental continuity in which animality and soul are not exhausted by individual limits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The soul retains a transindividual identity while being able to change in degree of faculty and status.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The distinction between sensitive soul and rational soul does not separate two substances, but two functional regimes of an animate continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Conception constitutes an operator of passage through which a sensitive soul can gain access to reason and to the status of Spirit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Every soul represents the created universe, but the mind adds to this representation a relation of image to the Divinity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Divine likeness produces a reflexive capacity that knows the order of the universe and not merely the multiplicity of its creatures.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] Spiritual knowledge is realized as architectonic imitation by samples, within a proper and limited domain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] The mind is defined by a capacity to enter into society with God, which exceeds the regime of the produced machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] The relation to God combines princely government and paternal filiation without being reducible to either one.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] The accomplished form of the mind is that of a local, derived, and relational divine power, rather than that of an autonomous divinity or a passive machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-01","text":"The continuity of living beings first recurs as identity of the vital ground, then as the condition of enduring transformations in the degree of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-02","text":"The permanence of the soul ceases to mean unchanged preservation: it becomes the capacity to undergo a functional mutation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-03","text":"Conception shifts from a biological threshold of humanization toward the condition of access to a higher form of cognition, production, and relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-04","text":"The living mirror recurs in a mutated form: it no longer reflects creatures alone, but becomes the image of their principle of order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-05","text":"Representation becomes systemic knowledge, then knowledge becomes architectonic capacity; the concept of the mirror is thus absorbed into a productive machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-06","text":"Divine production, initially opposed to the relation of machines, is recoded as government and filiation as soon as the mind becomes an addressable subject.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RMD-07","text":"The figure of the little divinity loses its function if it is isolated; it becomes operative only when reinscribed within a society of limited powers.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-01","text":"The distinction between spermatic animals and humans remains local to the lower layer; at the current level, it becomes the first case of a general theory of gradual differentiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-02","text":"The election of certain animals and the precise mechanism of elevation through conception remain local underdeterminations; they do not constitute the global architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-03","text":"The representation of the universe by ordinary souls is local; at the scale of the cluster, it becomes the substrate of an ascent toward divine reflexivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-04","text":"Imitation by samples is not the total thesis, but the local mechanism through which a limited spiritual power participates in universal architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-05","text":"The figures of the prince and the father are local relational models; their interaction produces, at the current level, a mixed regime of government and filiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-06","text":"The machine-inventor relation is an inferior negative model; at the current level, it serves to delimit a relational ontology of the mind.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:CGD-07","text":"The animal-human boundary, the creaturely mirror, and social relation are absorbed into a single structure: the gradual actualization of a living and architectonic power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes an absolute ontological rupture between animality and spirituality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that a soul is spiritual solely by its presence in a living being or solely by its capacity for representation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that knowledge of the universe automatically produces unlimited power: every imitation remains local and sample-based.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that the divine relation to minds is adequately described by the mere invention of a machine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:GNX-05","text":"It excludes an absolute autonomy of the mind: local divine power remains derived, limited, and inscribed within a relation of dependence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-01","text":"The system can hold only if the origin of the mind is neither an ex nihilo creation of a separate substance nor a mere preservation of sensitive animality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-02","text":"It simultaneously disqualifies the materialism of the machine and the spiritualism of a power without genesis, by imposing a continuous transformation of life.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-03","text":"It renders inadmissible a purely contemplative cognition: knowing the order must open a capacity to reproduce it locally.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-04","text":"It likewise renders inadmissible an independent spiritual creation: local architectonics remains a participation in an authorial and superior order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:DBN-05","text":"The silently excluded rival total model is that of a universe composed either of machines without society or of divinities without limitation or hierarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSA-01","text":"The system makes unavailable the idea of a rational subject originally separate from all animal, productive, and relational continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSA-02","text":"It cannot admit a reality without an imitable order, for spiritual knowledge exists only insofar as it can be converted into architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSA-03","text":"Without resolving it, it circumvents the question of the exact mechanism that transforms a sensitive soul into a mind capable of reason, architecture, and society.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSA-04","text":"The structuring absence is that of a purely causal divine relation: the system requires a God who can be author, prince, and father.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-01","text":"Vital continuity and the differentiation of degrees produce a conception of the mind as an internal transformation of living beings rather than as an external substantial addition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-01","CL_UCIC_28:GA-02","CL_UCIC_28:GA-03","CH_UCIC_P_74:D3","CH_UCIC_P_74:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-02","text":"The mirror function, joined to the divine image, converts representation of the world into reflexivity upon the system that organizes it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-05","CL_UCIC_28:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_75:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-03","text":"Systemic knowledge and architectonic imitation make the mind a productive agent without conferring upon it an originating causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-06","CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_75:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-04","text":"The opposition between machine and mind, combined with departmental limitation, institutes an intermediate regime between mechanical passivity and divine autonomy.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_76:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-05","text":"Architectonic capacity becomes a social capacity: the mind no longer merely reproduces an order; it can be inscribed within the relational order of its Author.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:GA-08","CH_UCIC_P_76:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-06","text":"The limitation of spiritual powers makes the plurality of minds compatible with a higher unity of government and filiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_75:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:XD-07","text":"The interaction of the three units produces a new figure: a graded life that becomes locally architectonic, then politically and familially addressable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-03","CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_76:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-01","text":"Ontologically, the mind is not an isolated substance but a higher mode of organization of living beings, defined by the convergence of reason, architecture, and relation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-02","text":"Epistemically, knowing no longer means merely representing: valid knowledge is that which grasps a structure and can produce samples of it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-03","text":"Strategically, spiritual power is distributed among local departments rather than concentrated in a global faculty or autonomous sovereignty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-04","text":"Politically, the universe is reclassified as an order of subjects and children governed by an Author, and not as a collection of fabricated objects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05","text":"Temporally, the permanence of the soul authorizes a history of transformations of faculty: identity persists by changing regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-06","text":"Methodologically, the system is reconstructed through successive displacements of an opposition: animal against mind, mirror against image, machine against subject, production against society.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:BSD-07","text":"The status of the subject becomes that of a derived agent capable of locally reproducing the order that produces it and of participating in the relation that governs it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop proceeds from vital continuity to spiritual differentiation, then from spirituality to a higher requalification of continuity itself.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-02","text":"The mirror becomes image, image becomes knowledge, knowledge becomes architecture, and architecture returns as proof of an active divine likeness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-03","text":"Local power calls for a limitation of domain; this limitation makes possible the plurality of minds, which in turn calls for a common structure of government.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-04","text":"The exclusion of the pure machine forces an escalation toward the subject, then toward the citizen or child of a divine order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-05","text":"The conceptual attractor is a society of analogous powers: each locally reproduces divine architecture without being able to substitute itself for its Author.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:RLE-06","text":"The repetition of limitation does not diminish power; it transforms it into a condition of relation, distribution, and coexistence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B01","text":"Continuity of living beings → transindividual permanence of the soul → possibility of differentiation without substantial rupture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B02","text":"Sensitive soul → threshold of conception → actualization of reason → gradual constitution of Spirit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B03","text":"Mirror of creatures → image of the Divinity → knowledge of the system of the universe.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B04","text":"Systemic knowledge → imitation by samples → local and limited architectonic power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B05","text":"Local power → capacity to enter into society → surpassing of the inventor-machine model.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B06","text":"Surpassing of mechanism → princely government + paternal filiation → mind as derived subject within a distributed divine architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B01","text":"Vital continuity → gradual transformation of faculties → emergence of reason → divine image → architectonic knowledge → local power.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B02","text":"Limited architectonic power → social capacity → reclassification of the relation to God → government + filiation → relational spiritual status.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B03","text":"The whole concludes in a systemic convergence: the continuity of living beings is preserved, but it is henceforth organized as a plurality of local powers participating in a common divine order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-01","text":"The ontological map ceases simply to oppose animal and human; it distinguishes successive regimes of sensibility, reason, representation, and participation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-02","text":"Conception is reclassified as an operator of ontological transformation, and not as a mere biological event.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-03","text":"Knowledge and production are united in one and the same architectonic function: understanding the order entails being able locally to reproduce its form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-04","text":"Creation is mapped according to several simultaneous regimes: production, government, and filiation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-05","text":"The multiplicity of minds becomes a distribution of local divine powers, each limited by its department and integrated into a higher society.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MME-06","text":"The false opposition between dependence and activity collapses: the mind is active precisely because its power remains derived and situated.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Spermatic animals, sensitive souls, minds, and relations of society provide the explicit objects of the system.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — These objects are organized by a chain of mediations: vital continuity, degrees of faculty, representation, divine likeness, architecture, and relational status.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The strategy consists in replacing each static opposition with a sequence of functional recodings: the animal becomes mind, the mirror becomes architect, the creature becomes subject.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Reality is conceived as an enduring continuity capable of producing mutations of status without losing the identity of the soul.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The argumentative form accomplishes what it describes: it proceeds through successive elevations, each negation of an insufficient model opening a richer relational regime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FL-01","text":"The continuity of living beings grounds spiritual singularity, but this singularity introduces a hierarchy that cannot be reduced to a mere difference of degree.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FL-02","text":"The figure of the little divinity increases the agency of the mind while maintaining its dependence upon the Author; the tension is constitutive and unresolved.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FL-03","text":"The machine-inventor relation remains a productive condition of the existence of creatures, but it is declared insufficient as soon as minds are concerned.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:FL-04","text":"Princely government and paternal filiation describe two forms of dependence that overlap without their hierarchy being made explicit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point is the passage from the permanence of the soul to the mobility of its degree: preserving identity becomes being able to change faculty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point is the passage from the mirror to the divine image: representation of the world becomes representation of its principle of organization.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point is the conversion of knowledge into architectonic imitation, which transforms cognition into local agency.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MP-04","text":"The fourth mutation point is the passage from architectonic power to society with God: the local agent becomes a subject of a political and familial order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_76:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a graded living architecture, capable of preserving its units while making them pass from a regime of sensibility to a regime of participation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a local power that reflects, understands, imitates, and partially reproduces the order upon which it depends.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:HSI-03","text":"Time is not a mere succession of states: it is the medium of a functional elevation that transforms status without abolishing continuity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:HSI-04","text":"Possible struggle or escape does not consist in leaving the order, but in changing degree, department, and relational regime within a higher architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction requires four invariants: continuity of living beings, mobility of the degrees of the soul, productive divine likeness, and social relation with God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B02","text":"The minimal chain remains sufficient if it preserves the real movement: vital identity → differentiation → elevation → architecture → society.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction remains underdetermined with respect to the mechanism of election, conception, and elevation, but these gaps do not prevent the identification of the generative machine of the cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence depends on accepting a transformation of degree without substantial rupture, then a divine participation without absolute autonomy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_74:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B05","text":"The compression is faithful if it preserves the tension between continuity and privilege, activity and dependence, local power and higher order; any reduction that removes these tensions destroys the current architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_75:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_28@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_28:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 82–84","context":"Proposition 82 · Proposition 83 · Proposition 84"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 85–87","order":29,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_77","CH_UCIC_P_78","CH_UCIC_P_79"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_29@R001","sha256":"5fcb59818f8ce48b15ee3cbc03026bf15045d99e1f6518a447cfb462d23c02d8","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-01","text":"Le problème central consiste à convertir l’unité spirituelle en une forme politique capable d’organiser simultanément la perfection collective et la reconnaissance de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_78:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-02","text":"La totalité des esprits est recadrée comme une cité universelle, c’est-à-dire comme un monde moral inclus dans le monde naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-03","text":"La thèse globale identifie la perfection maximale à l’État parfait, à la monarchie parfaite et à une communauté spirituelle capable de connaître et d’admirer les perfections divines.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-04","text":"L’argument combine déduction métaphysico-politique, détermination théologique de la gloire et analogie reconstructive entre les ordres causal, naturel et moral.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_79:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-05","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif : la pluralité spirituelle devient totalité, la totalité devient État, l’État devient monarchie, puis la monarchie devient médiation de l’ordre moral et de la gloire divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_78:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-06","text":"La clôture n’est pas une fusion des ordres, mais leur coordination sous une double fonction divine : architecture de l’univers et gouvernement des esprits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] L’ensemble des esprits forme une totalité déterminée dont l’unité reçoit nécessairement une configuration politique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] La totalité spirituelle ne reste pas une unité abstraite : elle se convertit en cité, puis en État.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] La forme politique adéquate à cette totalité est le plus parfait État possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] La perfection étatique se ferme sur une souveraineté monarchique exercée par le monarque le plus parfait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La Cité de Dieu devient simultanément monarchie universelle et monde moral inclus dans le monde naturel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A1","CH_UCIC_P_78:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La gloire divine n’est accomplie que dans la relation entre les perfections divines et des esprits capables de les connaître et de les admirer.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Les attributs divins sont différenciés selon leurs régimes de manifestation : sagesse et puissance se montrent partout, tandis que la bonté reçoit sa détermination propre dans la Cité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A6","CH_UCIC_P_78:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Les causes efficientes et les causes finales constituent deux ordres distincts dont l’harmonie rend possible une architecture plus vaste.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A1","CH_UCIC_P_79:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Une harmonie déjà établie autorise l’extension analogique du rapport entre causalité naturelle et finalité vers le rapport entre nature et grâce.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A4","CH_UCIC_P_79:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] Dieu est distribué selon deux fonctions corrélées : architecte de la machine universelle et monarque de la cité des esprits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] L’unité supérieure est produite par la coordination de plusieurs ordres distincts et non par leur indistinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] La perfection devient une architecture gouvernementale qui coordonne unité spirituelle, organisation politique, reconnaissance morale et ordre cosmique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-01","text":"La totalité revient avec une fonction mutée : d’agrégat des esprits, elle devient sujet politique, puis condition de la gloire divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:D1","CH_UCIC_P_78:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-02","text":"La perfection se déplace d’un maximum étatique vers une fonction médiatrice capable de transformer les perfections divines en reconnaissance spirituelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:D2","CH_UCIC_P_78:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-03","text":"La monarchie conserve sa forme souveraine mais change de portée : elle passe du gouvernement de l’État parfait à la médiation de l’ordre moral universel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-04","text":"L’harmonie migre du rapport entre causes efficientes et finales vers la correspondance entre nature physique et grâce morale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:D1","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-05","text":"La figure divine se dédouble fonctionnellement sans se diviser : l’architecte et le monarque deviennent les opérateurs complémentaires d’une même gouvernementalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:D2","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-06","text":"Les causes efficientes et finales sont absorbées comme échafaudage analogique dans une structure supérieure de coordination entre physique, moral et théologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-01","text":"La déduction de la totalité spirituelle vers l’État monarchique reste une machine locale ; au niveau courant, elle devient le premier moment d’une architecture théologico-politique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-02","text":"La description de la gloire comme connaissance et admiration devient, à l’échelle du cluster, la fonction relationnelle de la Cité universelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:D1","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-03","text":"L’analogie entre causes, nature et grâce cesse d’être un simple procédé local et devient le pont génératif qui relie machine cosmique et cité morale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-04","text":"Les détails sur la nature exacte de l’assemblage, des esprits et du mécanisme de la grâce demeurent locaux et sous-déterminés ; ils ne sont pas promus au rang d’axiomes globaux.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-05","text":"La distinction entre sagesse, puissance et bonté est conservée, mais recodée comme distribution fonctionnelle des régimes de manifestation divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une totalité spirituelle demeure une pluralité sans forme politique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’un État parfait puisse être fondé sur une pluralité souveraine ou sur l’absence de souverain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut une gloire divine autosuffisante, indépendante de toute connaissance et admiration spirituelles.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut un monde naturel achevé qui ne comporterait pas de monde moral capable de recevoir une finalité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut à la fois la confusion des ordres et leur séparation absolue : l’harmonie exige leur distinction coordonnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut que nature et grâce relèvent de principes divins indépendants ou de fondements totalement séparés.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, une unité ontologique sans gouvernement doit être tenue pour insuffisante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-02","text":"Un modèle de perfection qui ne serait ni institutionnel ni monarchique est silencieusement disqualifié.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_77:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-03","text":"Un Dieu dont la gloire et la bonté seraient pleinement intelligibles sans communauté morale est rendu inadmissible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-04","text":"Un naturalisme fermé sur la seule production ou conservation du monde naturel ne peut fournir la détermination complète de la bonté divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-05","text":"Une harmonisation par indistinction est exclue : l’unité supérieure ne peut être obtenue qu’en maintenant les différences de régime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSA-01","text":"Le système rend ontologiquement indisponible une perfection spirituelle non politique et non gouvernementale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSA-02","text":"Il rend indisponible une transcendance divine qui n’aurait pas besoin d’être reconnue par une communauté d’esprits.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSA-03","text":"Il rend impossible un monde naturel autosuffisant, séparé d’un ordre moral qui en révèle la finalité supérieure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSA-04","text":"Il ne peut admettre plusieurs principes ultimes correspondant séparément à la nature, à la grâce, à l’architecture et au gouvernement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-01","text":"La Cité de Dieu accomplit une double opération : elle donne une forme politique à la totalité spirituelle et fournit le milieu où les perfections divines deviennent gloire reconnue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:D1","CH_UCIC_P_78:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-02","text":"La monarchie universelle n’est pas seulement le sommet de l’État parfait ; elle devient la forme institutionnelle de la médiation entre Dieu, les esprits et le monde moral.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-03","text":"La gloire divine et la gouvernementalité monarchique se renforcent réciproquement : la communauté qui reconnaît Dieu légitime la structure qui l’organise.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:D2","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-04","text":"L’harmonie naturelle sert de matrice probatoire à l’harmonie morale ; l’analogie ne décrit donc pas seulement le système, elle autorise son extension.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:D3","CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-05","text":"L’unité divine se manifeste comme coordination de fonctions et de domaines différenciés, non comme réduction du physique au moral ou du moral au physique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-06","text":"La perfection politique devient le dispositif qui articule une perfection ontologique, une finalité morale et une reconnaissance épistémique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_78:D3","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-01","text":"La politique n’est pas une application extérieure de la métaphysique : elle constitue la forme d’actualisation de la totalité spirituelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-02","text":"La gloire divine est produite comme relation collective de connaissance et d’admiration, ce qui rend la communauté morale structurellement nécessaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:D2","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-03","text":"Le cosmos est reclassé comme une totalité à double régime : une machine physique gouvernée selon l’efficience et une cité morale gouvernée selon la finalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-04","text":"La perfection cesse d’être une propriété isolée et devient un opérateur de coordination entre forme politique, réception spirituelle et ordre cosmique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05","text":"La souveraineté acquiert une portée ontologique : elle ne règle pas seulement une collectivité, elle donne à la totalité son mode d’existence achevé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_77:D3","CH_UCIC_P_77:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-06","text":"La méthode générale du système consiste à prolonger une harmonie locale jusqu’à une architecture totale, sans abolir les distinctions qui rendent cette prolongation possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:D3","CH_UCIC_P_79:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale convertit la totalité en gouvernement, le gouvernement en communauté morale, puis la communauté reconnaissante en confirmation de la totalité organisée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-02","text":"L’escalade analogique suit le trajet causes efficientes et finales → nature physique et grâce morale → architecte et monarque → unité supérieure des ordres.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-03","text":"La Cité de Dieu est l’attracteur conceptuel vers lequel convergent État parfait, monarchie universelle, monde moral, gloire et harmonie cosmique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-04","text":"La répétition de la monarchie signale un changement de phase : de forme politique locale, elle devient principe de totalisation théologique et cosmologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_78:A1","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-05","text":"La clôture distribuée se produit lorsque les trois opérations — totaliser politiquement, médiatiser théologiquement, harmoniser analogiquement — convergent dans une même architecture de gouvernement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_79:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B01","text":"Une multiplicité spirituelle est posée comme totalité déterminée, mais cette totalité reste incomplète tant qu’elle n’est pas convertie en composition politique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B02","text":"La composition politique produit une cité ; la cité est maximisée en État parfait ; l’État parfait se ferme sur la monarchie parfaite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B03","text":"L’État monarchique est élevé au rang de monde moral inclus dans le monde naturel, ce qui transforme la structure politique en œuvre suprême de Dieu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B04","text":"La communauté morale convertit les perfections divines en connaissance et admiration ; cette conversion produit la gloire et spécifie la bonté.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B05","text":"L’harmonie des causes efficientes et finales est réutilisée comme opérateur de passage vers l’harmonie entre nature et grâce.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B06","text":"La machine de l’univers et la cité des esprits sont réunies par la double fonction divine d’architecte et de monarque, sans devenir un seul ordre indifférencié.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B01","text":"Pluralité spirituelle → totalité déterminée → composition politique → État parfait → monarchie parfaite.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B02","text":"Monde naturel → monde moral inclus → monarchie universelle → communauté connaissante et admirante → gloire divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B03","text":"Harmonie des causes → analogie étendue → correspondance nature/grâce → architecte et monarque → coordination supérieure des ordres.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B04","text":"Les trois trajectoires convergent vers une totalité politique, morale et cosmologique où l’unité est produite par gouvernement différencié plutôt que par fusion.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-01","text":"L’objet « tous les esprits » est reclassé : d’une totalité ontologique, il devient une unité politique constituée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CH_UCIC_P_77:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_77:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-02","text":"La perfection est déplacée du registre abstrait vers une institution monarchique, morale et relationnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_78:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-03","text":"La Cité de Dieu devient le point de convergence entre politique universelle, reconnaissance spirituelle et finalité théologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-04","text":"Dieu est cartographié comme opérateur biface : constructeur de la machine cosmique et souverain de la cité morale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-05","text":"L’opposition nature/grâce est remplacée par une distinction coordonnée entre deux régimes d’une même gouvernementalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-06","text":"Les catégories de causalité deviennent une méthode de cartographie inter-domaines reliant structure physique, finalité morale et souveraineté divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B01","text":"Au niveau Surface level, l’assemblage des esprits, la Cité de Dieu, la monarchie universelle et la gloire divine sont les objets explicites du système.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B02","text":"Au niveau Structural level, ces objets sont organisés par les médiations entre totalité, État, monde moral, causalité et gouvernement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B03","text":"Au niveau Metastrategic level, une totalité dispersée est rendue pensable par conversion politique, puis une harmonie locale est utilisée pour légitimer une harmonie supérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B04","text":"Au niveau Ontological / Temporal level, la forme politique parfaite est inscrite dans la structure de la totalité ; la dimension temporelle reste toutefois sous-déterminée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B05","text":"Au niveau Methodological / Performative level, le système accomplit ce qu’il affirme : il transforme une harmonie locale en principe de liaison globale par analogie et récurrence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_79:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FL-01","text":"La perfection collective est présentée comme dépendante d’une souveraineté monarchique, alors que la gloire divine dépend d’une communauté d’esprits capables de reconnaissance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FL-02","text":"La gloire semble dépendre d’une réception créée, tandis que la sagesse et la puissance divines sont affirmées comme manifestes partout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FL-03","text":"L’harmonie exige simultanément la séparation des ordres et leur intégration, ce qui fait de la distinction une condition de l’unité plutôt qu’un obstacle à celle-ci.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_79:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FL-04","text":"L’extension analogique est structurellement productive mais ne démontre pas le mécanisme précis par lequel nature et grâce sont effectivement harmonisées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MP-01","text":"La totalité spirituelle mute en totalité politique lorsque l’assemblage cesse d’être une simple pluralité et devient constitution d’une cité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CH_UCIC_P_77:D1","CH_UCIC_P_77:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MP-02","text":"La monarchie mute d’une forme de gouvernement en opérateur de médiation entre ordre moral, gloire divine et universalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MP-03","text":"L’harmonie mute d’une relation entre causes en une architecture de correspondance entre nature et grâce.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:D1","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MP-04","text":"La bonté mute d’un attribut divin parmi d’autres en fonction relationnelle spécifiée par la Cité et par la reconnaissance des esprits.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:A7","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:HSI-01","text":"La réalité apparaît comme une machine cosmique enchâssant une cité morale, les deux étant coordonnées par un même principe divin.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient un esprit gouverné, membre d’une totalité monarchique et agent de la connaissance et de l’admiration qui produisent la gloire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:HSI-03","text":"Le temps n’est pas construit comme une dynamique autonome ; l’architecture privilégie l’ordre établi, la perfection possible et la coordination des régimes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:HSI-04","text":"La navigation interne ne consiste pas à sortir du système, mais à maintenir la distinction des ordres tout en les reconduisant vers leur gouvernement commun.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B01","text":"Une reconstruction minimale suffisante conserve cinq opérations : totaliser les esprits, politiser la totalité, monarchiser la perfection, moraliser le monde naturel et harmoniser nature et grâce.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B02","text":"La cohérence dépend de l’identification entre perfection collective et forme étatique, ainsi que de l’acceptation d’une gloire conçue comme relation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B03","text":"Restent indéterminés la nature des esprits, le mécanisme de leur assemblage, la médiation de la grâce et le statut démonstratif du monarque parfait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B04","text":"La synthèse serait infidèle si elle supprimait l’analogie, la distinction des attributs ou la tension entre séparation et harmonie des ordres.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B05","text":"Le système courant est reconstructible sans séquençage détaillé parce que son attracteur est stable : une totalité spirituelle doit devenir une cité monarchique qui médiatise la gloire et coordonne le cosmos.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS6","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200212415105Z_cfe1c823","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 85–87","source_sha256":"5fcb59818f8ce48b15ee3cbc03026bf15045d99e1f6518a447cfb462d23c02d8","sha256":"e0fe67e4f645fc50b953adaf1a7cf02dc973c6aa5486513232d4abc1df60981b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:02:12.420531+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-01","text":"The central problem consists in converting spiritual unity into a political form capable of organizing simultaneously collective perfection and the recognition of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_78:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-02","text":"The totality of spirits is reframed as a universal city, that is, as a moral world included within the natural world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-03","text":"The overall thesis identifies maximal perfection with the perfect State, perfect monarchy, and a spiritual community capable of knowing and admiring divine perfections.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-04","text":"The argument combines metaphysico-political deduction, theological determination of glory, and reconstructive analogy among the causal, natural, and moral orders.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_79:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-05","text":"The movement is cumulative: spiritual plurality becomes totality, totality becomes State, State becomes monarchy, and monarchy then becomes mediation of the moral order and divine glory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_78:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AS-06","text":"The closure is not a fusion of orders, but their coordination under a dual divine function: architecture of the universe and government of spirits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The ensemble of spirits forms a determinate totality whose unity necessarily receives a political configuration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Spiritual totality does not remain an abstract unity: it is converted into a city, then into a State.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A2","CH_UCIC_P_77:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] The political form adequate to this totality is the most perfect possible State.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] State perfection culminates in a monarchical sovereignty exercised by the most perfect monarch.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A5","CH_UCIC_P_77:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The City of God becomes simultaneously universal monarchy and a moral world included within the natural world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A1","CH_UCIC_P_78:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Divine glory is fulfilled only in the relation between divine perfections and spirits capable of knowing and admiring them.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_78:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Divine attributes are differentiated according to their regimes of manifestation: wisdom and power are displayed everywhere, whereas goodness receives its proper determination in the divine City.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:A6","CH_UCIC_P_78:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Efficient causes and final causes constitute two distinct orders whose harmony makes a more extensive architecture possible.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A1","CH_UCIC_P_79:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] An already established harmony authorizes the analogical extension of the relation between natural causality and finality toward the relation between nature and grace.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A4","CH_UCIC_P_79:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","text":"[Persistent] God is distributed according to two correlated functions: architect of the universal machine and monarch of the city of spirits.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] Higher unity is produced by the coordination of several distinct orders and not by their indistinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Perfection becomes a governmental architecture that coordinates spiritual unity, political organization, moral recognition, and cosmic order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS4","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-01","text":"Totality recurs with a mutated function: from an aggregate of spirits, it becomes a political subject, then a condition of divine glory.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:D1","CH_UCIC_P_78:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-02","text":"Perfection shifts from a State maximum toward a mediating function capable of transforming divine perfections into spiritual recognition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:D2","CH_UCIC_P_78:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-03","text":"Monarchy retains its sovereign form but changes in scope: it passes from governing the perfect State to mediating the universal moral order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-04","text":"Harmony migrates from the relation between efficient and final causes toward the correspondence between physical nature and moral grace.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:D1","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-05","text":"The divine figure is functionally doubled without being divided: architect and monarch become the complementary operators of one and the same governmentality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:D2","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RMD-06","text":"Efficient and final causes are absorbed as analogical scaffolding into a higher structure of coordination among the physical, the moral, and the theological.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-01","text":"The deduction from spiritual totality toward the monarchical State remains a local machine; at the current level, it becomes the first moment of a theologico-political architecture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-02","text":"The description of glory as knowledge and admiration becomes, at the scale of the cluster, the relational function of the universal City.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:D1","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-03","text":"The analogy among causes, nature, and grace ceases to be a mere local procedure and becomes the generative bridge connecting the cosmic machine and the moral city.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-04","text":"The details concerning the exact nature of the assembly, spirits, and the mechanism of grace remain local and underdetermined; they are not elevated to the rank of global axioms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:CGD-05","text":"The distinction among wisdom, power, and goodness is retained, but recoded as a functional distribution of regimes of divine manifestation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes a spiritual totality remaining a plurality without political form.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a perfect State that could be founded upon a sovereign plurality or upon the absence of a sovereign.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-03","text":"It excludes a self-sufficient divine glory, independent of all spiritual knowledge and admiration.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-04","text":"It excludes a completed natural world that would not contain a moral world capable of receiving a divine finality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-05","text":"It excludes both the confusion of orders and their absolute separation: harmony requires their coordinated distinction.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:GNX-06","text":"It excludes nature and grace being dependent upon independent divine principles or upon totally separate foundations.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, an ontological unity without government must be regarded as insufficient.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-02","text":"A model of perfection that would be neither institutional nor monarchical is silently disqualified.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_77:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-03","text":"A God whose glory and goodness would be fully intelligible without a moral community is rendered inadmissible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-04","text":"A naturalism closed upon the sole production or preservation of the natural world cannot provide the complete determination of divine goodness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:DBN-05","text":"Harmonization through indistinction is excluded: higher unity can be obtained only by maintaining differences of regime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSA-01","text":"The system renders ontologically unavailable a spiritual perfection that is non-political and non-governmental.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CH_UCIC_P_77:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSA-02","text":"It renders unavailable a divine transcendence that would not need to be recognized by a community of spirits.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_78:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSA-03","text":"It makes impossible a self-sufficient natural world, separated from a moral order that reveals its higher finality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSA-04","text":"It cannot admit several ultimate principles corresponding separately to nature, grace, architecture, and government.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_79:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-01","text":"The City of God performs a dual operation: it gives political form to spiritual totality and provides the milieu in which divine perfections become recognized glory.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:D1","CH_UCIC_P_78:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-02","text":"Universal monarchy is not merely the summit of the perfect State; it becomes the institutional form of mediation among God, spirits, and the moral world.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-03","text":"Divine glory and monarchical governmentality reinforce each other reciprocally: the community that recognizes God legitimates the structure that organizes it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:D2","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-04","text":"Natural harmony serves as an evidentiary matrix for moral harmony; analogy therefore does not merely describe the system, it authorizes its extension.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:D3","CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-05","text":"Divine unity manifests itself as coordination of differentiated functions and domains, not as reduction of the physical to the moral or of the moral to the physical.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:XD-06","text":"Political perfection becomes the apparatus that articulates an ontological perfection, a moral finality, and an epistemic recognition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_78:D3","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-01","text":"Politics is not an external application of metaphysics: it constitutes the form of actualization of spiritual totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-02","text":"Divine glory is produced as a collective relation of knowledge and admiration, which renders the moral community structurally necessary.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:D2","CH_UCIC_P_78:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-03","text":"The cosmos is reclassified as a dual-regime totality: a physical machine governed according to efficiency and a moral city governed according to finality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-04","text":"Perfection ceases to be an isolated property and becomes an operator of coordination among political form, spiritual reception, and cosmic order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05","text":"Sovereignty acquires an ontological scope: it does not merely regulate a collectivity, it gives totality its completed mode of existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_77:D3","CH_UCIC_P_77:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:BSD-06","text":"The system's general method consists in extending a local harmony into a total architecture, without abolishing the distinctions that make this extension possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:D3","CH_UCIC_P_79:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop converts totality into government, government into moral community, and then the recognizing community into confirmation of organized totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-02","text":"Analogical escalation follows the path efficient and final causes → physical nature and moral grace → architect and monarch → higher unity of orders.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-03","text":"The City of God is the conceptual attractor toward which the perfect State, universal monarchy, moral world, glory, and cosmic harmony converge.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME4","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-04","text":"The repetition of monarchy signals a change of phase: from a local political form, it becomes a principle of theological and cosmological totalization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_78:A1","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:RLE-05","text":"Distributed closure occurs when the three operations—politically totalizing, theologically mediating, analogically harmonizing—converge in one and the same architecture of government.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_79:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B01","text":"A spiritual multiplicity is posited as a determinate totality, but this totality remains incomplete so long as it is not converted into political composition.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:A1","CH_UCIC_P_77:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B02","text":"Political composition produces a city; the city is maximized into a perfect State; the perfect State culminates in perfect monarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B03","text":"The monarchical State is elevated to the rank of a moral world included within the natural world, which transforms the political structure into God's supreme work.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CH_UCIC_P_78:A3","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B04","text":"The moral community converts divine perfections into knowledge and admiration; this conversion produces glory and specifies goodness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B05","text":"The harmony of efficient and final causes is reused as an operator of passage toward the harmony between nature and grace.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B06","text":"The machine of the universe and the city of spirits are united by the dual divine function of architect and monarch, without becoming a single undifferentiated order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B01","text":"Spiritual plurality → determinate totality → political composition → perfect State → perfect monarchy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B02","text":"Natural world → included moral world → universal monarchy → knowing and admiring community → divine glory.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_78:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_78:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B03","text":"Harmony of causes → extended analogy → nature/grace correspondence → architect and monarch → higher coordination of orders.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_79:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B04","text":"The three trajectories converge toward a political, moral, and cosmological totality in which unity is produced by differentiated government rather than by fusion.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-01","text":"The object “all spirits” is reclassified: from an ontological totality, it becomes a constituted political unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CH_UCIC_P_77:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_77:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-02","text":"Perfection is displaced from the abstract register toward a monarchical, moral, and relational institution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_78:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-03","text":"The City of God becomes the point of convergence among universal politics, spiritual recognition, and theological finality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-04","text":"God is mapped as a two-faced operator: builder of the cosmic machine and sovereign of the moral city.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-05","text":"The nature/grace opposition is replaced by a coordinated distinction between two regimes of one and the same governmentality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MME-06","text":"The categories of causality become a method of inter-domain mapping linking physical structure, moral finality, and divine sovereignty.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B01","text":"At the Surface level, the assembly of spirits, the City of God, universal monarchy, and divine glory are the explicit objects of the system.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B02","text":"At the Structural level, these objects are organized by mediations among totality, State, moral world, causality, and government.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_78:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B03","text":"At the Metastrategic level, a dispersed totality is rendered thinkable through political conversion, then a local harmony is used to legitimate a higher harmony.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B04","text":"At the Ontological / Temporal level, the perfect political form is inscribed in the structure of totality; the temporal dimension nevertheless remains underdetermined.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B05","text":"At the Methodological / Performative level, the system accomplishes what it asserts: it transforms a local harmony into a principle of global linkage through analogy and recurrence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_79:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FL-01","text":"Collective perfection is presented as dependent upon a monarchical sovereignty, whereas divine glory depends upon a community of spirits capable of recognition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_77:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FL-02","text":"Glory appears to depend upon a created reception, whereas divine wisdom and power are asserted to be manifest everywhere.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FL-03","text":"Harmony simultaneously requires the separation of orders and their integration, which makes distinction a condition of unity rather than an obstacle to it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_79:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:FL-04","text":"Analogical extension is structurally productive but does not demonstrate the precise mechanism by which nature and grace are effectively harmonized.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MP-01","text":"Spiritual totality mutates into political totality when the assembly ceases to be a mere plurality and becomes the constitution of a city.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CH_UCIC_P_77:D1","CH_UCIC_P_77:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MP-02","text":"Monarchy mutates from a form of government into an operator of mediation among moral order, divine glory, and universality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MP-03","text":"Harmony mutates from a relation among causes into an architecture of correspondence between nature and grace.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_79:D1","CH_UCIC_P_79:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MP-04","text":"Goodness mutates from one divine attribute among others into a relational function specified by the City and by the recognition of spirits.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CH_UCIC_P_78:A7","CH_UCIC_P_78:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a cosmic machine embedding a moral city, both coordinated by one and the same divine principle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:A6","CH_UCIC_P_79:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a governed spirit, a member of a monarchical totality and an agent of the knowledge and admiration that produce glory.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_78:A4","CH_UCIC_P_77:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:HSI-03","text":"Time is not constructed as an autonomous dynamic; the architecture privileges established order, possible perfection, and the coordination of regimes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:HSI-04","text":"Internal navigation does not consist in exiting the system, but in maintaining the distinction of orders while leading them back toward their common government.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_79:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B01","text":"A sufficient minimal reconstruction retains five operations: totalizing spirits, politicizing totality, monarchizing perfection, moralizing the natural world, and harmonizing nature and grace.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B02","text":"Coherence depends upon the identification between collective perfection and State form, as well as upon the acceptance of a glory conceived as relation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-03","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B03","text":"The nature of spirits, the mechanism of their assembly, the mediation of grace, and the demonstrative status of the perfect monarch remain indeterminate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_77:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B04","text":"The synthesis would be unfaithful if it removed analogy, the distinction of attributes, or the tension between separation and harmony of orders.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CH_UCIC_P_78:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_79:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B05","text":"The current system is reconstructible without detailed sequencing because its attractor is stable: a spiritual totality must become a monarchical city that mediates glory and coordinates the cosmos.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-12","CH_UCIC_P_77:FGS6","CH_UCIC_P_79:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_29@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_29:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 85–87","context":"Proposition 85 · Proposition 86 · Proposition 87"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 88–90","order":30,"parents":["CH_UCIC_P_80","CH_UCIC_P_81","CH_UCIC_P_82"],"revision":"CL_UCIC_30@R001","sha256":"ac11d67f847b834ea5ab32f56c16eecb0c1d82e0fdb14a736df7c022d21daee6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-01","text":"Le problème central est de rendre continue la relation entre finalité spirituelle, causalité naturelle, rétribution morale et conduite humaine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_81:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-02","text":"La thèse globale recode la Nature comme l’architecture opératoire d’une Providence qui inscrit la justice dans les corps, les événements et le temps.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_81:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-03","text":"Le système ne juxtapose pas théologie, mécanique et éthique : il les convertit en niveaux d’une même économie de gouvernement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-04","text":"Le mouvement est cumulatif et mutationnel : la Nature passe de médiation de la Grâce à mécanisme rétributif, puis à condition de la conduite vertueuse.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:D1","CH_UCIC_P_81:D2","CH_UCIC_P_82:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-05","text":"L’interaction des unités transforme la catastrophe cosmique, le délai corporel et l’acceptation providentielle en variantes d’une même temporalité de la rétribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_82:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-06","text":"La contradiction entre agir et accepter n’est pas supprimée mais fonctionnellement distribuée entre la volonté présomptive et la volonté secrète.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D5","CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-07","text":"La clôture produite est une subjectivité active dans le devoir, passive devant l’issue effective et incapable de réviser l’ordre total.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-08","text":"Le système cherche finalement à générer une Providence immanente : un ordre où la justice divine paraît produite par les mécanismes mêmes du monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La Nature ne constitue jamais un dehors autonome de la finalité spirituelle ou morale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_81:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] La Nature conserve sa fonction d’exécution tout en mutant de voie harmonique de la Grâce en architecture mécanique de rétribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-03","text":"[Emergent] La construction naturelle et la législation divine deviennent deux descriptions coordonnées d’un seul ordre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A1","CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CL_UCIC_30:GA-01","CL_UCIC_30:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] La peine et la récompense sont des effets internes à l’ordre naturel plutôt que des interventions extrinsèques.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] La rétribution devient progressivement cosmique, corporelle, différée puis gouvernementale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A7","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La responsabilité humaine exige une double orientation : poursuivre le bien présumé et consentir à l’événement effectivement produit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] Un gouvernement parfait implique qu’aucun bien ne reste sans récompense et qu’aucun mal ne demeure sans châtiment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A1","CH_UCIC_P_82:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] L’ordre universel est déclaré non améliorable depuis une perspective humaine locale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A9","CH_UCIC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] Dieu fonctionne simultanément comme origine efficiente, architecte, maître, cause finale et source du bonheur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A11","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] La bonté converge vers une conduite qui combine devoir, imitation du bien, confiance et absence de révolte contre l’ordre effectif.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_82:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-01","text":"La Grâce revient d’abord comme destination spirituelle, puis se déplace vers une structure cosmique et devient finalement l’arrière-plan final du bonheur humain.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-02","text":"La Nature conserve une fonction médiatrice stable, mais sa fonction mute : elle ne conduit plus seulement vers la Grâce, elle encode la loi et produit la rétribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:D1","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-03","text":"Le châtiment et la récompense passent d’opérations cosmiques à des effets corporels différés, puis à une règle universelle du gouvernement parfait.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A7","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_82:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-04","text":"Le temps cesse d’être un simple cadre : il devient d’abord l’instrument du moment cosmique, ensuite le délai de la rétribution, enfin la séparation entre présomption et effectivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:D4","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-05","text":"L’harmonie revient comme principe de liaison, puis se transforme en concordance architecte-législateur et en unification du moral et de l’ontologique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_81:D1","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-06","text":"Le sujet passe de bénéficiaire ou victime d’un ordre cosmique à opérateur du devoir, puis à agent limité par l’impossibilité de juger la totalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-07","text":"Le globe local est absorbé dans le corps, puis dans l’univers total : l’objet matériel de la justice s’élargit jusqu’à devenir l’ordre entier du réel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_82:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-01","text":"La destruction et la réparation du globe restent locales lorsqu’elles décrivent des opérations cosmiques particulières sans déterminer la structure générale de la rétribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A4","CH_UCIC_P_80:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-02","text":"La distinction entre Dieu architecte et Dieu législateur est locale dans sa formulation, mais devient structurante lorsqu’elle unifie construction naturelle et loi morale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A1","CH_UCIC_P_81:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-03","text":"Le pur amour et l’imitation de l’Auteur du bien demeurent des prescriptions éthiques locales, sauf lorsqu’ils sont intégrés à la structure générale de la subjectivité providentielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A5","CH_UCIC_P_82:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-04","text":"Le délai de la peine ou de la récompense change d’échelle : de difficulté théologique locale, il devient principe général de temporalisation de la justice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:D4","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-05","text":"La distinction entre volonté présomptive et volonté conséquente relie les unités en convertissant une tension doctrinale en protocole général d’action et d’acceptation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-06","text":"Les mécanismes précis de destruction, de réparation, de récompense et de châtiment restent inférieurs et deviennent indéterminés au niveau du cluster.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-07","text":"La révolte contre l’ordre divin cesse d’être un simple comportement local et devient, à l’échelle courante, l’exclusion d’une position critique envers la totalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut une Nature indifférente, autonome ou séparée de la finalité spirituelle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut une justice qui interromprait les mécanismes naturels ou dépendrait d’ajouts judiciaires extérieurs.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_81:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut l’immédiateté comme critère de réalité de la peine, de la récompense ou de la justice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut une séparation durable entre ordre physique, ordre moral et ordre providentiel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut enfin la possibilité d’une amélioration humaine de la totalité ou d’un bonheur indépendant de Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, il faut que soit fausse l’hypothèse d’une causalité naturelle sans portée morale ultime.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-02","text":"Il faut également que soit fausse l’hypothèse d’une intervention providentielle extérieure aux conditions architecturales du monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-03","text":"Le système disqualifie un temps autonome qui pourrait retarder, suspendre ou contredire définitivement la rétribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-04","text":"Il disqualifie la perspective humaine comme mesure souveraine du bien, de la perfection et de l’améliorabilité du monde.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-05","text":"Le modèle rival silencieusement exclu est celui d’une autonomie morale où l’action humaine produirait seule sa fin et son bonheur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSA-01","text":"Le système contourne sans l’admettre pleinement la possibilité d’un monde naturel non rétributif, où la distribution du bien et du mal resterait contingente.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSA-02","text":"Son absence structurante est l’absence d’un accès humain complet aux causes et aux fins qui ordonnent les événements.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_82:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSA-03","text":"La possibilité inadmissible est celle d’un jugement humain capable de corriger l’ordre universel sans se placer hors de la Providence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSA-04","text":"Le système traite comme ontologiquement impossible une fin du bonheur qui ne serait pas déjà inscrite dans la causalité divine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-01","text":"La Providence n’est pas seulement appliquée au monde depuis l’extérieur : elle est reconstruite comme l’intelligibilité interne de ses mécanismes naturels, corporels et temporels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_81:D2","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD4","CL_UCIC_30:GA-01","CL_UCIC_30:GA-02","CL_UCIC_30:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-02","text":"Le délai rétributif permet de faire fonctionner la même structure comme explication cosmique, mécanique et éthique sans exiger une manifestation immédiate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS4","CL_UCIC_30:GA-04","CL_UCIC_30:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-03","text":"La distinction entre action selon le devoir et acceptation de l’issue effective convertit une incompatibilité apparente en division fonctionnelle du sujet.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D2","CH_UCIC_P_82:D5","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT2","CL_UCIC_30:GA-06","CL_UCIC_30:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-04","text":"L’identité entre architecte et législateur rend possible une justice qui ne juge pas le monde après coup mais le construit déjà comme rétribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:D1","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS1","CL_UCIC_30:GA-03","CL_UCIC_30:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-05","text":"L’optimalité du monde et la limitation cognitive du sujet se renforcent mutuellement : l’impossibilité de juger la totalité devient la preuve pratique de sa supériorité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D6","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT4","CL_UCIC_30:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-06","text":"La rétribution universelle absorbe la différence entre catastrophe, conséquence corporelle et résultat moral en les subordonnant à une même règle de gouvernement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS1","CL_UCIC_30:GA-05","CL_UCIC_30:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-07","text":"La non-révolte ne désigne plus seulement une attitude religieuse : elle devient la condition subjective de la cohérence entre devoir local et perfection globale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D3","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT6","CL_UCIC_30:GA-06","CL_UCIC_30:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-01","text":"La causalité naturelle acquiert une normativité interne : elle ne décrit plus seulement ce qui arrive, mais la manière dont la justice arrive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-02","text":"Le temps devient une technologie de compatibilisation : il différencie l’action humaine, l’effet naturel et la révélation de la justice sans rompre leur unité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_82:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-03","text":"Le sujet humain est produit comme agent de transformation locale et récepteur de décisions globales qu’il ne peut totaliser.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-04","text":"La critique du monde est neutralisée non par réfutation empirique, mais par déplacement de l’autorité du jugement vers la totalité providentielle.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-05","text":"L’architecture transforme l’opposition entre mécanique et téléologie en circuit fermé où la mécanique devient le mode visible de la téléologie.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-06","text":"Le bonheur cesse d’être une fin que le sujet pourrait produire et devient l’effet terminal d’une orientation vers une cause finale déjà donnée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D7","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-01","text":"Finalité spirituelle → Nature médiatrice → mécanisme rétributif → confirmation d’une finalité spirituelle : la causalité naturelle revient comme preuve de la Providence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-02","text":"Action morale → effet différé → absence de visibilité immédiate → maintien de la rétribution nécessaire : le délai protège simultanément la causalité et la croyance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:D4","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-03","text":"Devoir local → volonté présomptive → événement effectif → acceptation de la volonté secrète → retour au devoir : le sujet est pris dans une boucle d’activation et de dessaisissement.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-04","text":"La rétribution s’escalade du globe aux corps, des corps à l’univers et de l’univers à la formation du sujet moral.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur du système est une Providence immanente qui absorbe toute différence entre ordre naturel, loi divine, justice, temps et bonheur.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-06","text":"La répétition de la concordance ne produit pas une identité statique : elle intensifie progressivement la capture du naturel par le spirituel, puis du spirituel par la conduite humaine.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_82:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B01","text":"Une finalité spirituelle est posée comme exigence d’harmonie entre la Grâce et les voies de la Nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B02","text":"L’exigence d’harmonie recode la Nature en dispositif d’exécution du gouvernement divin.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A2","CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03","text":"La construction du monde et sa législation sont identifiées, de sorte que la loi morale devient une propriété de l’architecture mécanique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B04","text":"La propriété mécanique produit des peines et des récompenses corporelles dont la manifestation peut être différée.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:D2","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B05","text":"La rétribution différée est généralisée en gouvernement parfait garantissant la correspondance universelle entre faute, mérite, châtiment et récompense.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A1","CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B06","text":"La limitation cognitive impose au sujet de poursuivre le bien présumé tout en acceptant l’ordre effectif comme non améliorable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B07","text":"La boucle se ferme lorsque l’action, l’événement naturel, la rétribution et le bonheur sont rapportés à Dieu comme cause finale unique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A11","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12","CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:AFM-B01","text":"Disjonction entre nature et finalité → recodage de la Nature comme médiation → concordance architecte-législateur → inscription mécanique de la rétribution → temporalisation du jugement → division active/passive du sujet → optimalité non améliorable de la totalité → bonheur théocentré.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_81:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_82:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-01","text":"La Nature est reclassée de milieu autonome en appareil de traduction de la loi et de la justice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-02","text":"La catastrophe cosmique, la peine corporelle et l’échec apparent deviennent des formes lisibles d’une même économie rétributive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-03","text":"La distinction entre agir et subir est remplacée par une complémentarité entre orientation pratique et consentement à l’effectivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-04","text":"Le délai devient une catégorie positive de la justice et non un défaut de manifestation ou une objection à la Providence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-05","text":"La carte stratégique interdit la refonte globale du monde et réduit l’intervention légitime à la conformité locale au devoir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont le globe, les corps, les actions belles, les péchés, les catastrophes et les récompenses.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont distribués par une architecture commune où Nature, mécanique, Providence et rétribution sont médiations d’un même ordre.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Le système remplace la critique de l’événement par l’examen de la position subjective qui le juge, puis disqualifie le mécontentement envers la totalité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est produit comme ordre finalisé et le temps comme différenciation entre causalité, rétribution et accès humain à leur sens.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle affirme : elle reconduit chaque séparation vers une unité supérieure sans supprimer les tensions qui rendent cette reconduction nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FL-01","text":"La causalité naturelle paraît autonome dans ses voies, mais elle est simultanément déclarée entièrement subordonnée à une finalité spirituelle ; cette contradiction fonde la médiation plutôt qu’elle ne la détruit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FL-02","text":"L’obligation de transformer la conduite coexiste avec l’interdiction implicite de juger transformable l’ordre universel.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FL-03","text":"La définition du bon par l’absence de mécontentement entre en tension avec une normativité indépendante du devoir et de l’action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_82:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FL-04","text":"L’optimalité du monde dépend d’une limitation cognitive qui ne peut être démontrée depuis la perspective humaine sans mobiliser l’ordre qu’elle cherche à établir.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D6","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MP-01","text":"La Nature mute de milieu de médiation en machine de rétribution lorsque la finalité théologique est absorbée par la structure mécanique.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:D1","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MP-02","text":"Le délai mute d’objection potentielle en mécanisme positif de compatibilisation entre justice nécessaire et absence de visibilité immédiate.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:D4","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MP-03","text":"La subjectivité mute lorsque la volonté se scinde entre recherche active du bien présumé et consentement au bien effectivement produit.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D5","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine providentielle auto-rétributive où les mécanismes naturels exécutent une législation morale sans intervention extérieure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet devient un opérateur local de la Providence : il agit dans l’incertitude, puis reçoit l’issue comme expression d’un ordre qu’il ne peut totaliser.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est une distribution différée de la justice, assez lent pour masquer la rétribution, mais assez ordonné pour la rendre nécessaire.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée admise n’est pas une sortie hors du système, mais une orientation correcte du désir : agir selon le devoir, aimer le bien et consentir à l’effectivité.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_82:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige cinq noyaux : Nature finalisée, mécanique rétributive, temporalité différée, gouvernement parfait et subjectivité active-passive.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B02","text":"La chaîne est suffisante pour reconstruire le mouvement du cluster, depuis la naturalisation de la Providence jusqu’à la subordination du bonheur à Dieu.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination restante concerne les mécanismes précis par lesquels les corps, le globe et les événements produisent leurs effets moraux.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence dépend de l’acceptation simultanée d’une causalité naturelle réelle, d’une finalité divine déterminante et d’une connaissance humaine structurellement insuffisante.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B05","text":"La ligne de force est la conversion de toute séparation en médiation ; la ligne de faille est l’écart persistant entre cette conversion et l’autonomie apparente des mécanismes naturels.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B06","text":"Le système ne peut être reconstruit fidèlement sans conserver la tension entre devoir de transformation locale et impossibilité de transformation globale.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200247142464Z_a5060b93","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 88–90","source_sha256":"ac11d67f847b834ea5ab32f56c16eecb0c1d82e0fdb14a736df7c022d21daee6","sha256":"f125931743f649fe28186f2e9c4009cd1cfd6e438e0c2249f8f746cc312dfc7d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:02:47.244507+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-01","text":"The central problem is to render continuous the relation between spiritual finality, natural causality, moral retribution, and human conduct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_81:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-02","text":"The overall thesis recodes Nature as the operational architecture of a Providence that inscribes justice in bodies, events, and time.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS2","CH_UCIC_P_81:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-03","text":"The system does not juxtapose theology, mechanics, and ethics: it converts them into levels of one and the same economy of governance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-04","text":"The movement is cumulative and mutational: Nature passes from mediation of Grace to a retributive mechanism, then to a condition of virtuous conduct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:D1","CH_UCIC_P_81:D2","CH_UCIC_P_82:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-05","text":"The interaction of the units transforms cosmic catastrophe, bodily delay, and providential acceptance into variants of one and the same temporality of retribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS3","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_82:AS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-06","text":"The contradiction between acting and accepting is not removed but functionally distributed between presumptive will and secret will.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D5","CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-07","text":"The closure produced is an active subjectivity in duty, passive before the effective outcome, and incapable of revising the total order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BAS-08","text":"The system ultimately seeks to generate an immanent Providence: an order in which divine justice appears to be produced by the very mechanisms of the world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Nature never constitutes an autonomous outside of spiritual or moral finality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_81:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Nature retains its function of execution while mutating from a harmonious way of Grace into a mechanical architecture of retribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-03","text":"[Emergent] Natural construction and divine legislation become two coordinated descriptions of a single order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A1","CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CL_UCIC_30:GA-01","CL_UCIC_30:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Punishment and reward are effects internal to the natural order rather than extrinsic interventions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A5","CH_UCIC_P_81:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Retribution progressively becomes cosmic, bodily, deferred, and then governmental.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A7","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Human responsibility requires a double orientation: to pursue the presumed good and to consent to the event actually produced.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] Perfect governance entails that no good remain without reward and no evil remain without punishment.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A1","CH_UCIC_P_82:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] The universal order is declared unimprovable from a local human perspective.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A9","CH_UCIC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-09","text":"[Persistent] God functions simultaneously as efficient origin, architect, master, final cause, and source of happiness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A11","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Goodness converges toward a conduct that combines duty, imitation of the good, trust, and absence of revolt against the effective order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_82:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-01","text":"Grace first recurs as a spiritual destination, then shifts toward a cosmic structure and ultimately becomes the final background of human happiness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-02","text":"Nature retains a stable mediating function, but its function mutates: it no longer leads only toward Grace; it encodes law and produces retribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:D1","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-03","text":"Punishment and reward pass from cosmic operations to deferred bodily effects, then to a universal rule of perfect governance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A7","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_82:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-04","text":"Time ceases to be a mere framework: it first becomes the instrument of the cosmic moment, then the delay of retribution, and finally the separation between presumption and actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:D4","CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-05","text":"Harmony recurs as a principle of connection, then is transformed into architect-legislator concordance and into the unification of the moral and the ontological.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_81:D1","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-06","text":"The subject passes from beneficiary or victim of a cosmic order to operator of duty, then to an agent limited by the impossibility of judging totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RMD-07","text":"The local globe is absorbed into the body, then into the total universe: the material object of justice expands until it becomes the entire order of the real.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_82:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-01","text":"The destruction and repair of the globe remain local when they describe particular cosmic operations without determining the general structure of retribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A4","CH_UCIC_P_80:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-02","text":"The distinction between God as architect and God as legislator is local in its formulation, but becomes structuring when it unifies natural construction and moral law.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A1","CH_UCIC_P_81:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-03","text":"Pure love and imitation of the Author of the good remain local ethical prescriptions, except when they are integrated into the general structure of providential subjectivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A5","CH_UCIC_P_82:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-04","text":"The delay of punishment or reward changes scale: from a local theological difficulty, it becomes a general principle for the temporalization of justice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:D4","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-05","text":"The distinction between presumptive will and consequent will links the units by converting a doctrinal tension into a general protocol of action and acceptance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-06","text":"The precise mechanisms of destruction, repair, reward, and punishment remain subordinate and become indeterminate at the cluster level.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:CGD-07","text":"Revolt against divine order ceases to be a merely local behavior and becomes, at the current scale, the exclusion of a critical position toward totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:NX2","CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes a Nature indifferent, autonomous, or separate from spiritual finality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a justice that would interrupt natural mechanisms or depend on external judicial additions.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_81:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-03","text":"It excludes immediacy as a criterion of the reality of punishment, reward, or justice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:NX3","CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-04","text":"It excludes a lasting separation between physical order, moral order, and providential order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX3","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:GNX-05","text":"Finally, it excludes the possibility of a human improvement of totality or of a happiness independent of God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the hypothesis of a natural causality without ultimate moral import must be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-02","text":"The hypothesis of a providential intervention external to the architectural conditions of the world must likewise be false.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_81:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-03","text":"The system disqualifies an autonomous time that could indefinitely delay, suspend, or contradict retribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:DNX4","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-04","text":"It disqualifies the human perspective as the sovereign measure of the good, perfection, and the improvability of the world.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX1","CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:DBN-05","text":"The silently excluded rival model is that of a moral autonomy in which human action alone would produce its end and its happiness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX2","CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSA-01","text":"Without fully admitting it, the system sidesteps the possibility of a non-retributive natural world, in which the distribution of good and evil would remain contingent.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_81:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSA-02","text":"Its structuring absence is the absence of complete human access to the causes and ends that order events.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX2","CH_UCIC_P_82:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSA-03","text":"The inadmissible possibility is that of a human judgment capable of correcting the universal order without placing itself outside Providence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX1","CH_UCIC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSA-04","text":"The system treats as ontologically impossible an end of happiness that would not already be inscribed in divine causality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:SNX3","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-01","text":"Providence is not merely applied to the world from outside: it is reconstructed as the internal intelligibility of its natural, bodily, and temporal mechanisms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD1","CH_UCIC_P_81:D2","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD4","CL_UCIC_30:GA-01","CL_UCIC_30:GA-02","CL_UCIC_30:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-02","text":"Retributive delay allows the same structure to function as a cosmic, mechanical, and ethical explanation without requiring immediate manifestation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS4","CL_UCIC_30:GA-04","CL_UCIC_30:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-03","text":"The distinction between action according to duty and acceptance of the effective outcome converts an apparent incompatibility into a functional division of the subject.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D2","CH_UCIC_P_82:D5","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT2","CL_UCIC_30:GA-06","CL_UCIC_30:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-04","text":"The identity between architect and legislator makes possible a justice that does not judge the world after the fact but already constructs it as retribution.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:D1","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS1","CL_UCIC_30:GA-03","CL_UCIC_30:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-05","text":"The optimality of the world and the cognitive limitation of the subject mutually reinforce one another: the impossibility of judging totality becomes the practical proof of its superiority.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D6","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT4","CL_UCIC_30:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-06","text":"Universal retribution absorbs the difference between catastrophe, bodily consequence, and moral result by subordinating them to one and the same rule of governance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS1","CL_UCIC_30:GA-05","CL_UCIC_30:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:XD-07","text":"Non-revolt no longer denotes merely a religious attitude: it becomes the subjective condition of coherence between local duty and global perfection.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D3","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT6","CL_UCIC_30:GA-06","CL_UCIC_30:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-01","text":"Natural causality acquires an internal normativity: it no longer merely describes what happens, but the manner in which justice happens.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A4","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-02","text":"Time becomes a technology of compatibilization: it differentiates human action, natural effect, and the revelation of justice without breaking their unity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_82:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-03","text":"The human subject is produced as an agent of local transformation and recipient of global decisions that it cannot totalize.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-04","text":"Critique of the world is neutralized not through empirical refutation, but through displacement of the authority of judgment toward providential totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:NX5","CH_UCIC_P_82:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-05","text":"The architecture transforms the opposition between mechanics and teleology into a closed circuit in which mechanics becomes the visible mode of teleology.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:BSD-06","text":"Happiness ceases to be an end that the subject could produce and becomes the terminal effect of an orientation toward an already given final cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D7","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-01","text":"Spiritual finality → mediating Nature → retributive mechanism → confirmation of a spiritual finality: natural causality returns as proof of Providence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS1","CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-02","text":"Moral action → deferred effect → absence of immediate visibility → maintenance of necessary retribution: delay simultaneously protects causality and belief.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:D4","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD3","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-03","text":"Local duty → presumptive will → effective event → acceptance of secret will → return to duty: the subject is caught in a loop of activation and dispossession.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS3","CH_UCIC_P_82:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-04","text":"Retribution escalates from the globe to bodies, from bodies to the universe, and from the universe to the formation of the moral subject.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-05","text":"The system's attractor is an immanent Providence that absorbs every difference between natural order, divine law, justice, time, and happiness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:NX1","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD4","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:RLE-06","text":"The repetition of concordance does not produce a static identity: it progressively intensifies the capture of the natural by the spiritual, then of the spiritual by human conduct.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:AS5","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS2","CH_UCIC_P_82:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B01","text":"A spiritual finality is posited as a requirement of harmony between Grace and the ways of Nature.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A1","CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B02","text":"The requirement of harmony recodes Nature as an apparatus for the execution of divine governance.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:A2","CH_UCIC_P_80:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03","text":"The construction of the world and its legislation are identified, such that moral law becomes a property of mechanical architecture.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A2","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B04","text":"The mechanical property produces bodily punishments and rewards whose manifestation may be deferred.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:D2","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B05","text":"Deferred retribution is generalized into perfect governance guaranteeing the universal correspondence between fault, merit, punishment, and reward.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A1","CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B06","text":"Cognitive limitation requires the subject to pursue the presumed good while accepting the effective order as unimprovable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A7","CH_UCIC_P_82:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B07","text":"The loop closes when action, natural event, retribution, and happiness are referred to God as a single final cause.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A11","CH_UCIC_P_82:A12","CH_UCIC_P_82:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:AFM-B01","text":"Disjunction between nature and finality → recoding of Nature as mediation → architect-legislator concordance → mechanical inscription of retribution → temporalization of judgment → active/passive division of the subject → unimprovable optimality of totality → theocentered happiness.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:AS1","CH_UCIC_P_81:AF1","CH_UCIC_P_82:AF1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-01","text":"Nature is reclassified from an autonomous milieu into an apparatus for translating law and justice.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-02","text":"Cosmic catastrophe, bodily punishment, and apparent failure become legible forms of one and the same retributive economy.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ME2","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-03","text":"The distinction between acting and undergoing is replaced by a complementarity between practical orientation and consent to actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:ME1","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-04","text":"Delay becomes a positive category of justice rather than a defect of manifestation or an objection to Providence.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MME-05","text":"The strategic map forbids the global remaking of the world and reduces legitimate intervention to local conformity with duty.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:ME3","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are the globe, bodies, beautiful actions, sins, catastrophes, and rewards.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT1","CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are distributed by a common architecture in which Nature, mechanics, Providence, and retribution are mediations of one and the same order.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT2","CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The system replaces critique of the event with examination of the subjective position that judges it, then disqualifies discontent toward totality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT3","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The real is produced as a finalized order and time as a differentiation between causality, retribution, and human access to their meaning.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:ALT4","CH_UCIC_P_81:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form accomplishes what it affirms: it returns every separation to a higher unity without removing the tensions that make this return necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FL-01","text":"Natural causality appears autonomous in its ways, but is simultaneously declared entirely subordinate to a spiritual finality; this contradiction founds mediation rather than destroying it.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FL-02","text":"The obligation to transform conduct coexists with the implicit prohibition against judging the universal order transformable.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_82:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FL-03","text":"The definition of the good by the absence of discontent comes into tension with an independent normativity of duty and action.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT6","CH_UCIC_P_82:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:FL-04","text":"The optimality of the world depends on a cognitive limitation that cannot be demonstrated from the human perspective without mobilizing the order it seeks to establish.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D6","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MP-01","text":"Nature mutates from a milieu of mediation into a machine of retribution when theological finality is absorbed by mechanical structure.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:D1","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MP-02","text":"Delay mutates from a potential objection into a positive mechanism of compatibilization between necessary justice and the absence of immediate visibility.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:D4","CH_UCIC_P_81:FGS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MP-03","text":"Subjectivity mutates when the will splits between active pursuit of the presumed good and consent to the good actually produced.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:D5","CH_UCIC_P_82:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a self-retributive providential machine in which natural mechanisms execute moral legislation without external intervention.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A3","CH_UCIC_P_81:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:HSI-02","text":"The subject becomes a local operator of Providence: it acts in uncertainty, then receives the outcome as the expression of an order it cannot totalize.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:A4","CH_UCIC_P_82:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:HSI-03","text":"Time is a deferred distribution of justice, slow enough to conceal retribution, yet sufficiently ordered to render it necessary.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_81:A7","CH_UCIC_P_81:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:HSI-04","text":"The only admitted escape is not an exit from the system, but a correct orientation of desire: to act according to duty, love the good, and consent to actuality.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:AS4","CH_UCIC_P_82:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B01","text":"Minimal reconstruction requires five nuclei: finalized Nature, retributive mechanics, deferred temporality, perfect governance, and active-passive subjectivity.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT1","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B02","text":"The chain is sufficient to reconstruct the movement of the cluster, from the naturalization of Providence to the subordination of happiness to God.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B03","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the precise mechanisms through which bodies, the globe, and events produce their moral effects.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT2","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence depends on the simultaneous acceptance of a real natural causality, a determining divine finality, and structurally insufficient human knowledge.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT3","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B05","text":"The line of force is the conversion of every separation into mediation; the fault line is the persistent gap between this conversion and the apparent autonomy of natural mechanisms.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_80:SD2","CH_UCIC_P_81:MRT4","CH_UCIC_P_80:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B06","text":"The system cannot be faithfully reconstructed without retaining the tension between the duty of local transformation and the impossibility of global transformation.","refs":["CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT5","CH_UCIC_P_82:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_UCIC_30@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_UCIC_30:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Chapters 88–90","context":"Proposition 88 · Proposition 89 · Proposition 90"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L1 01","order":1,"parents":["CL_UCIC_01","CL_UCIC_02","CL_UCIC_03","CL_UCIC_04"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_01@R001","sha256":"2648999fe1339ec0aa565613139ec20283ffb12dd91c3c0b3bf11a9eb86c0892","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B01","text":"Le système part de l’insuffisance ontologique du composé et reconduit toute constitution vers des unités simples non spatiales, sans parties et irréductibles à l’agrégation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:AS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B02","text":"Cette simplicité cesse d’être une propriété statique : elle distribue les opérations admissibles, soustrait la monade aux transformations partitives et impose des seuils existentiels non graduels.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B03","text":"La clôture causale ne produit pas une immobilité, mais déplace le changement, l’identité et la différence vers les déterminations internes de chaque unité simple.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:AS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B04","text":"Le mouvement général est récursif : chaque exclusion — composition interne, étendue, dissolution, pénétration extérieure, indifférenciation — rend nécessaire une fonction positive plus déterminée de la monade.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B05","text":"L’argument produit une ontologie asymétrique où les composés dépendent des simples, les changements visibles dépendent de déterminations immanentes, et la pluralité dépend de différences intrinsèques.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B06","text":"Sa clôture est productive mais incomplète : le système établit la nécessité du simple, de son dynamisme et de sa différenciation, sans déterminer pleinement l’union des composés ni le mécanisme positif du changement interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Le composé ne possède qu’une unité dérivée ; il ne peut être le terme ultime de l’explication de sa propre constitution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La monade est une unité simple sans parties, dont la simplicité ne désigne ni petitesse quantitative ni réduction spatiale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] L’absence de parties passe d’une négation de la composition à une exclusion de l’étendue, de la dissolution, de la pénétration et des transitions partitives.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-04","text":"[Terminal] Les commencements et fins des unités simples ne peuvent relever des opérations qui gouvernent les composés ; ils forment des limites instantanées plutôt que des processus graduels.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Aucun changement naturel d’une monade ne peut être expliqué par l’importation d’une cause, d’une partie ou d’un accident depuis l’extérieur.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La fermeture causale rend nécessaire une détermination interne capable de porter le changement sans que celui-ci devienne transfert ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La qualité interne est la condition commune de l’individuation, de la discernabilité du changement et de la pluralité non substituable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] La simplicité ne signifie pas absence de contenu : elle concentre une dynamique qualitative propre dans une unité non composée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] La monade est l’attracteur qui absorbe les fonctions de fondement, d’élément non spatial, de borne existentielle, de foyer causal et de principe d’individuation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] La pluralité réelle ne résulte ni de positions externes ni d’une répétition numérique, mais de trajectoires internes qualitativement différenciées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-01","text":"La simplicité conserve son identité comme absence de parties, mais sa fonction migre du fondement compositionnel vers une grammaire des opérations, de la temporalité et de la causalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-02","text":"Le composé passe du statut de donné analytique à celui d’effet dérivé : il n’est plus le lieu originaire de l’unité, de la différence ou du changement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-03","text":"L’atome subit une inversion durable : de la plus petite portion corporelle, il devient l’unité naturelle non spatiale qui rend les corps intelligibles sans leur ressembler.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-04","text":"La frontière monadique se déplace d’une clôture négative contre l’intrusion à une condition positive de localisation du principe de changement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-05","text":"La qualité cesse d’être un attribut requis parmi d’autres et devient le relais entre identité individuelle, pluralité réelle et changement discernable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-06","text":"Le changement est successivement recodé comme problème de dissolution, limite des opérations partitives, différence qualitative interne, puis profil constitutif de l’identité substantielle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-07","text":"La création et l’annihilation apparaissent comme résidus terminaux de l’exclusion des transitions naturelles, mais leur causalité positive demeure non spécifiée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-01","text":"La définition de la monade comme substance sans parties demeure locale tant qu’elle ne règle que son statut ; elle devient globale lorsqu’elle ordonne constitution, causalité, temporalité et individuation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-02","text":"L’exclusion de l’étendue reste locale comme déspatialisation de l’atome ; au niveau courant, elle devient la condition d’une causalité et d’une identité irréductibles au modèle corporel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-03","text":"La non-dissolution reste locale comme impossibilité de désagrégation ; elle change d’échelle lorsqu’elle sépare deux régimes de transition, l’un partitif et l’autre instantané.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-04","text":"La fermeture à l’influence extérieure devient transversale lorsqu’elle cesse de décrire une limite et impose la recherche de toute différence effective dans l’intériorité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-05","text":"Le détail interne du changement est le catalyseur qui transforme une théorie de la mutabilité générale en théorie de la pluralité qualitative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-06","text":"Le modèle d’unité purement numérique, corporelle ou positionnelle devient obsolète, car il ne peut produire ni différence réelle ni changement discernable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’un agrégat, une totalité divisible ou une relation de parties puisse constituer le fondement ultime de l’être composé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut que l’unité première soit étendue, figurée, mesurable ou définissable comme une portion de matière.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut que la monade puisse commencer, finir ou se transformer par les mécanismes de composition et de décomposition propres aux corps composés.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que la causalité soit pénétration, transfert, réception d’accidents ou modification imposée depuis un dehors.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut qu’une pluralité réelle puisse être fondée sur la duplication parfaite, la position, la nomination ou une différence seulement extrinsèque.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut enfin l’image d’une simplicité immobile et vide, car une unité simple doit porter une détermination propre de son changement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, le domaine des composés observables ne doit pas être toute la réalité ; l’observable doit dépendre de conditions qui ne se donnent pas elles-mêmes comme agrégats.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-02","text":"Toute ontologie où l’unité serait elle-même une composition indéfiniment reconduite est disqualifiée, car elle rendrait impossible une clôture explicative non circulaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-03","text":"Un monde dans lequel les différences seraient produites après coup par les rapports externes est incompatible avec l’exigence d’individuation intrinsèque.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-04","text":"Un être créé achevé, stable et soustrait au changement est également exclu ; la stabilité ne peut être l’identité primitive de la substance créée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-05","text":"Le système requiert que l’absence de causalité externe ne soit pas une privation pure, mais le principe négatif qui oblige à localiser l’explication dans l’unité elle-même.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:XD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité la plus profondément forclose est celle d’un réel entièrement spatial, composé, transférentiel et explicable par les seules relations entre parties.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-02","text":"Le système rend indisponible un extérieur causal qui pénétrerait la substance simple et produirait directement son identité ou ses changements.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-03","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une unité indifférenciée : une monade sans détermination propre serait simultanément sans individuation, sans devenir discernable et sans pluralité réelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-04","text":"L’autre absence structurante est celle d’un mécanisme explicite d’union entre simples et composés, ou d’un mécanisme positif de production interne suffisamment déterminé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-01","text":"La déspatialisation de l’élément et l’intériorisation de la causalité convergent : ce qui fonde le réel n’est ni une particule corporelle ni un point de réception d’influences, mais une unité non composée porteuse de ses déterminations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-08","CL_UCIC_01:XD-02","CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-02","text":"Les exclusions de dissolution et d’altération extérieure forment une même loi : aucune transition constitutive de la monade ne peut être décrite comme réarrangement ou intrusion de parties.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-05","CL_UCIC_02:XD-01","CL_UCIC_03:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-03","text":"La qualité interne devient nécessaire non seulement pour distinguer les monades, mais aussi pour empêcher que le changement soit réduit à un déplacement externe d’éléments identiques.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-10","CL_UCIC_03:XD-04","CL_UCIC_03:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-04","text":"Le système transforme une régression compositionnelle et une interdiction causale en une même exigence constructive : le fondement doit être simple, et son devenir doit être intrinsèquement déterminé.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-08","CL_UCIC_01:XD-03","CL_UCIC_04:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-05","text":"La distinction entre unité et pluralité est reconfigurée : l’unité simple n’est pas opposée à la diversité, puisque la diversité procède de spécifications qualitatives internes sans fragmentation de la substance.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-10","CL_UCIC_04:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-06","text":"L’architecture atteint une tension irréductible : elle détermine que le changement est interne sans fournir un contenu positif équivalent pour son principe, sa causalité ou sa liaison aux composés.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-09","CL_UCIC_03:FL-01","CL_UCIC_04:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme une architecture de dépendance non réductible à la matière : les composés manifestent, mais ne fondent pas, l’ordre des unités simples dynamiques.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-02","text":"La causalité change de statut : elle n’est plus transmission entre substances, mais nécessité structurale selon laquelle toute modification doit être imputable à une détermination immanente.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-03","text":"Le temps est différencié à deux niveaux : les composés relèvent de transformations partitives, tandis que la substance simple est définie par une continuité interne bordée de seuils non processuels.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-04","text":"L’identité substantielle cesse d’être fixité ou substrat vide ; elle devient cohérence d’une trajectoire qualitative interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-05","text":"La méthode d’explication se transforme en méthode de soustraction : éliminer les opérations impossibles fait apparaître les conditions positives minimales de l’unité, du changement et de la pluralité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-06","text":"La monade devient le point de passage entre ontologie et épistémologie : elle n’est pas directement donnée comme objet composé, mais exigée comme condition de l’intelligibilité de ce qui apparaît.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-01","text":"Composé → agrégat → simple → élément non spatial → condition du composé : la première boucle reconduit le donné vers son fondement tout en laissant ouverte la médiation de l’union.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-02","text":"Absence de parties → retrait des transitions partitives → seuils instantanés d’existence : la simplicité devient une machine de sélection des opérations admissibles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-03","text":"Fermeture extérieure → nécessité de détermination interne → qualité → individuation → pluralité non substituable : la négation de l’influence devient la production de la différence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-04","text":"Mutabilité universelle → principe interne → insuffisance du principe abstrait → détail différentiel → identité dynamique : le changement repasse de prédicat à opérateur d’individuation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur général est l’unité simple qualitativement déterminée : elle absorbe substance, atome, élément, sujet causal, borne temporelle et individu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B01","text":"Composé donné → déclaration de dérivation → impossibilité d’une régression de compositions → exigence d’un constituant simple.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B02","text":"Simple sans parties → retrait de l’étendue, de la figure, de la divisibilité et de la dissolution → constitution de l’élément comme non spatial.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B03","text":"Retrait des transitions partitives → séparation des régimes temporels → limitation du commencement et de la fin de la monade à des seuils instantanés.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B04","text":"Retrait de l’influence extérieure → localisation du changement dans l’intériorité → nécessité d’un principe monadique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B05","text":"Principe interne abstrait → insuffisance explicative → détail qualitatif déterminé → spécification individuelle de chaque substance simple.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B06","text":"Différences internes des simples → discernabilité des états composés → pluralité réelle sans duplication, transfert ni fondement positionnel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B07","text":"La machine entière produit une ontologie apophatico-constructive : chaque impossibilité retire un faux mécanisme et impose une fonction positive de la monade.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AFM-B01","text":"Composé manifeste → agrégat dérivé → nécessité du simple → déspatialisation de l’élément → retrait des transformations partitives → clôture causale → intériorisation du changement → différenciation qualitative → pluralité non substituable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AFM-B02","text":"Régression analytique → fondement non composé → exclusion des mécanismes corporels → reclassification des temporalités → rejet du transfert externe → individuation par le détail du devenir.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AFM-B03","text":"Négation cumulative → nécessité ontologique → dynamique immanente → détermination qualitative → fermeture partielle par une pluralité de monades, avec persistance d’une lacune sur l’union et la causalité positive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-01","text":"La distinction pertinente n’est plus partie/totalité, mais unité sans parties/agrégat dérivé ; l’élémentarité est ainsi dissociée de toute extension.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-02","text":"La causalité est redessinée comme problème de détermination interne plutôt que comme circulation d’éléments entre substances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-03","text":"Le changement est reclassé : une permutation, un déplacement ou une désagrégation ne suffisent plus à rendre compte du devenir ; il requiert des différences qualitatives effectives.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-04","text":"L’individuation devient pensable sans position, quantité ou désignation externe, parce que l’identité est rapportée au contenu différentiel du changement interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-05","text":"Une lecture méthodique devient disponible : tester toute explication par les opérations que la structure de son objet autorise ou interdit.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-06","text":"La fausse opposition entre simplicité et dynamisme s’effondre : la simplicité n’est plus immobilité, mais concentration non composée d’une trajectoire qualitative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les problèmes explicites sont la constitution des composés, la dissolution, le commencement, l’altération monadique, le changement et la différence entre plusieurs substances simples.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — L’architecture articule agrégats dérivés, unités simples, absence de parties, clôture causale, déterminations qualitatives et pluralité intrinsèquement différenciée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — L’argument substitue aux explications par corps, transfert, position ou indifférenciation une remontée vers les conditions structurelles de l’unité et du devenir.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel est formé d’unités simples dont la priorité sur les composés est ontologique, dont les limites existentielles sont discontinues et dont l’identité se déploie comme devenir interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — La forme démonstrative accomplit sa thèse en produisant positivement la monade par accumulation d’impossibilités relatives à la composition, à l’influence et à l’indifférenciation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FL-01","text":"La nécessité des simples est plus fortement établie que leur mode d’union aux composés ; la fondation ontologique dépasse la théorie effectivement disponible de la constitution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FL-02","text":"Le système affirme que le changement est interne, mais laisse sous-déterminés le mécanisme de cette production, la nature des qualités et le rapport entre différence interne et dénomination intrinsèque.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FL-03","text":"La création et l’annihilation sont posées comme limites de l’existence simple sans que soit déterminé l’agent, la causalité ou le statut exact de ces événements à l’égard de la nature.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FL-04","text":"La clôture monadique doit coexister avec la composition des états et avec l’ordre commun des êtres créés ; la distinction entre dépendance, composition et influence demeure décisive et fragile.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation convertit la simplicité de condition logique de clôture en détermination ontologique non spatiale de l’élément naturel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MP-02","text":"Le second point de mutation convertit l’absence de parties en différenciation des régimes de commencement, de fin et de temporalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation convertit la fermeture causale en exigence positive de déterminations internes et de qualités différentielles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MP-04","text":"Le quatrième point de mutation reconçoit l’identité : elle ne désigne plus une persistance fixe, mais le profil qualitatif d’un changement continu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine stratifiée : les agrégats visibles sont des effets dérivés d’unités non composées dont les déterminations internes distribuent le changement et la différence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-02","text":"La monade est une chambre ontologique close, non comme isolement inerte, mais comme foyer de transformation interne qualitativement spécifiée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-03","text":"Le sujet théorique devient une instance de remontée et de discrimination : il doit reconduire les phénomènes composés vers leurs conditions non composées, puis distinguer causalité, composition et différence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-04","text":"Le temps est double : le temps des composés est celui des réarrangements possibles, tandis que le temps monadique est la continuité qualitative d’un devenir intérieurement déterminé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-05","text":"La seule navigation conceptuelle disponible consiste à abandonner les explications par transfert et à suivre la conversion des exclusions en conditions internes de possibilité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale requiert six noyaux : dérivation du composé, simplicité sans parties, déspatialisation de l’élément, exclusion des transitions partitives, clôture causale et différenciation qualitative interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B02","text":"Ces noyaux suffisent à restituer le mouvement méta-cluster : du composé donné vers le simple, du simple vers la clôture causale, puis de cette clôture vers l’identité dynamique et la pluralité non substituable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B03","text":"La compression doit conserver la différence entre trois rapports souvent confondus : composition des simples dans les agrégats, influence causale directe entre substances et discernabilité qualitative des états.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination irréductible concerne le mécanisme de liaison entre simples et composés, le contenu positif du principe interne, ainsi que l’agent et le statut de la création et de l’annihilation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B05","text":"La reconstruction échoue si elle réintroduit un fondement corporel, une causalité pénétrante, une identité immobile ou une pluralité obtenue par simple répétition numérique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B06","text":"La force de la machine réside dans la conversion récursive de ses négations en exigences positives ; sa limite réside dans le fait que cette conversion détermine plus sûrement les impossibilités que les mécanismes effectifs.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200324760588Z_8afaaecc","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L1 01","source_sha256":"2648999fe1339ec0aa565613139ec20283ffb12dd91c3c0b3bf11a9eb86c0892","sha256":"1bf9f0cdbd0e2c349c642cd68092286fa36b47c910a9ca4c3bb749750a30a2bb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:03:24.764311+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B01","text":"The system begins from the ontological insufficiency of the composite and traces every constitution back to simple non-spatial units, without parts and irreducible to aggregation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:AS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B02","text":"This simplicity ceases to be a static property: it distributes admissible operations, removes the monad from partitive transformations, and imposes non-gradual existential thresholds.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B03","text":"Causal closure does not produce immobility, but relocates change, identity, and difference into the internal determinations of each simple unit.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:AS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B04","text":"The general movement is recursive: each exclusion—internal composition, extension, dissolution, external penetration, indifferentiation—renders necessary a more determinate positive function of the monad.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B05","text":"The argument produces an asymmetrical ontology in which composites depend on simples, visible changes depend on immanent determinations, and plurality depends on intrinsic differences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B06","text":"Its closure is productive but incomplete: the system establishes the necessity of the simple, its dynamism, and its differentiation, without fully determining the union of composites or the positive mechanism of internal change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The composite possesses only derived unity; it cannot be the ultimate term of the explanation of its own constitution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The monad is a simple unit without parts, whose simplicity denotes neither quantitative smallness nor spatial reduction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The absence of parts passes from a negation of composition to an exclusion of extension, dissolution, penetration, and partitive transitions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-04","text":"[Terminal] The beginnings and ends of simple units cannot fall under the operations governing composites; they constitute instantaneous limits rather than gradual processes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] No natural change of a monad can be explained by the importation of a cause, a part, or an accident from outside.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Causal closure renders necessary an internal determination capable of bearing change without its becoming ontological transfer.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Internal quality is the common condition of individuation, the discernibility of change, and non-substitutable plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Simplicity does not mean absence of content: it concentrates a proper qualitative dynamism within a non-composite unit.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] The monad is the attractor that absorbs the functions of foundation, non-spatial element, existential limit, causal focus, and principle of individuation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Real plurality results neither from external positions nor from numerical repetition, but from qualitatively differentiated internal trajectories.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-01","text":"Simplicity retains its identity as absence of parts, but its function migrates from compositional foundation toward a grammar of operations, temporality, and causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-02","text":"The composite passes from the status of an analytical given to that of a derived effect: it is no longer the original locus of unity, difference, or change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-03","text":"The atom undergoes a lasting inversion: from the smallest corporeal portion, it becomes the non-spatial natural unit that renders bodies intelligible without resembling them.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-04","text":"The monadic boundary shifts from negative closure against intrusion to a positive condition for locating the principle of change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-05","text":"Quality ceases to be one required attribute among others and becomes the relay between individual identity, real plurality, and discernible change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-06","text":"Change is successively recoded as a problem of dissolution, a limit of partitive operations, internal qualitative difference, and then the constitutive profile of substantial identity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-07","text":"Creation and annihilation appear as terminal residues of the exclusion of natural transitions, but their positive causality remains unspecified.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-01","text":"The definition of the monad as a substance without parts remains local so long as it regulates only its status; it becomes global when it orders constitution, causality, temporality, and individuation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-02","text":"The exclusion of extension remains local as the despatialization of the atom; at the current level, it becomes the condition of a causality and identity irreducible to the corporeal model.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-03","text":"Non-dissolution remains local as the impossibility of disaggregation; it changes scale when it separates two regimes of transition, one partitive and the other instantaneous.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-04","text":"Closure to external influence becomes transversal when it ceases to describe a limit and imposes the search for every effective difference within interiority.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-05","text":"The internal detail of change is the catalyst that transforms a theory of general mutability into a theory of qualitative plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-06","text":"The model of purely numerical, corporeal, or positional unity becomes obsolete, because it can produce neither real difference nor discernible change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that an aggregate, a divisible totality, or a relation of parts could constitute the ultimate foundation of composite being.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that primary unity be extended, figured, measurable, or definable as a portion of matter.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that the monad can begin, end, or transform itself through the mechanisms of composition and decomposition proper to composite bodies.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that causality be penetration, transfer, reception of accidents, or modification imposed from without.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the possibility that real plurality can be founded on perfect duplication, position, naming, or a merely extrinsic difference.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-06","text":"Finally, it excludes the image of an immobile and empty simplicity, for a simple unit must bear a proper determination of its change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, the domain of observable composites must not be all of reality; the observable must depend on conditions that do not themselves present as aggregates.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-02","text":"Every ontology in which unity would itself be an indefinitely repeated composition is disqualified, since it would render a non-circular explanatory closure impossible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-03","text":"A world in which differences were produced retrospectively by external relations is incompatible with the requirement of intrinsic individuation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-04","text":"A created being that is complete, stable, and removed from change is likewise excluded; stability cannot be the primitive identity of created substance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-05","text":"The system requires that the absence of external causality not be pure privation, but the negative principle compelling the location of explanation within unity itself.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:XD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-01","text":"The possibility most deeply foreclosed is that of a real entirely spatial, composite, transferential, and explicable through relations among parts alone.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-02","text":"The system renders unavailable an external causality that would penetrate simple substance and directly produce its identity or its changes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-03","text":"The structuring absence is that of an undifferentiated unity: a monad without proper determination would simultaneously lack individuation, discernible becoming, and real plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-04","text":"The other structuring absence is that of an explicit mechanism of union between simples and composites, or of a sufficiently determinate positive mechanism of internal production.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-01","text":"The despatialization of the element and the internalization of causality converge: what grounds the real is neither a corporeal particle nor a point receiving influences, but a non-composite unit bearing its determinations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-08","CL_UCIC_01:XD-02","CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-02","text":"The exclusions of dissolution and external alteration form one and the same law: no constitutive transition of the monad can be described as rearrangement or intrusion of parts.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-05","CL_UCIC_02:XD-01","CL_UCIC_03:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-03","text":"Internal quality becomes necessary not only for distinguishing monads, but also for preventing change from being reduced to an external displacement of identical elements.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-10","CL_UCIC_03:XD-04","CL_UCIC_03:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-04","text":"The system transforms a compositional regress and a causal prohibition into a single constructive requirement: the foundation must be simple, and its becoming must be intrinsically determined.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-08","CL_UCIC_01:XD-03","CL_UCIC_04:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-05","text":"The distinction between unity and plurality is reconfigured: simple unity is not opposed to diversity, since diversity proceeds from internal qualitative specifications without fragmentation of substance.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-10","CL_UCIC_04:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:XD-06","text":"The architecture reaches an irreducible tension: it determines that change is internal without providing an equivalent positive content for its principle, causality, or connection to composites.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-09","CL_UCIC_03:FL-01","CL_UCIC_04:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-01","text":"The real is reclassified as an architecture of dependence irreducible to matter: composites manifest, but do not ground, the order of dynamic simple units.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-02","text":"Causality changes status: it is no longer transmission between substances, but the structural necessity according to which every modification must be attributable to an immanent determination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-03","text":"Time is differentiated at two levels: composites fall under partitive transformations, whereas simple substance is defined by an internal continuity bounded by non-processual thresholds.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-04","text":"Substantial identity ceases to be fixity or an empty substratum; it becomes the coherence of an internal qualitative trajectory.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-05","text":"The method of explanation transforms into a method of subtraction: eliminating impossible operations reveals the minimal positive conditions of unity, change, and plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-06","text":"The monad becomes the point of passage between ontology and epistemology: it is not directly given as a composite object, but required as the condition of the intelligibility of what appears.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-01","text":"Composite → aggregate → simple → non-spatial element → condition of the composite: the first loop returns the given to its foundation while leaving open the mediation of union.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-02","text":"Absence of parts → withdrawal of partitive transitions → instantaneous thresholds of existence: simplicity becomes a machine for selecting admissible operations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-03","text":"External closure → necessity of internal determination → quality → individuation → non-substitutable plurality: the negation of influence becomes the production of difference.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-04","text":"Universal mutability → internal principle → insufficiency of the abstract principle → differential detail → dynamic identity: change passes again from predicate to operator of individuation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:RLE-05","text":"The general attractor is the qualitatively determined simple unity: it absorbs substance, atom, element, causal subject, temporal limit, and individual.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B01","text":"Given composite → declaration of derivation → impossibility of a regress of compositions → requirement of a simple constituent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B02","text":"Simple without parts → withdrawal of extension, figure, divisibility, and dissolution → constitution of the element as non-spatial.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B03","text":"Withdrawal of partitive transitions → separation of temporal regimes → limitation of the beginning and end of the monad to instantaneous thresholds.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B04","text":"Withdrawal of external influence → location of change in interiority → necessity of a monadic principle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B05","text":"Abstract internal principle → explanatory insufficiency → determinate qualitative detail → individual specification of each simple substance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B06","text":"Internal differences of simples → discernibility of composite states → real plurality without duplication, transfer, or positional foundation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FGS-B07","text":"The entire machine produces an apophatic-constructive ontology: each impossibility removes a false mechanism and imposes a positive function of the monad.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AFM-B01","text":"Manifest composite → derived aggregate → necessity of the simple → despatialization of the element → withdrawal of partitive transformations → causal closure → internalization of change → qualitative differentiation → non-substitutable plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AFM-B02","text":"Analytical regress → non-composite foundation → exclusion of corporeal mechanisms → reclassification of temporalities → rejection of external transfer → individuation through the detail of becoming.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:AFM-B03","text":"Cumulative negation → ontological necessity → immanent dynamism → qualitative determination → partial closure through a plurality of monads, with persistence of a gap concerning union and positive causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-01","text":"The relevant distinction is no longer part/whole, but unit without parts/derived aggregate; elementarity is thus dissociated from all extension.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-02","text":"Causality is redrawn as a problem of internal determination rather than as the circulation of elements between substances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-03","text":"Change is reclassified: a permutation, displacement, or disaggregation no longer suffices to account for becoming; it requires effective qualitative differences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-04","text":"Individuation becomes thinkable without position, quantity, or external designation, because identity is related to the differential content of internal change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-05","text":"A methodical reading becomes available: test every explanation by the operations that the structure of its object authorizes or forbids.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MME-06","text":"The false opposition between simplicity and dynamism collapses: simplicity is no longer immobility, but the non-composite concentration of a qualitative trajectory.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit problems are the constitution of composites, dissolution, beginning, monadic alteration, change, and difference among several simple substances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — The architecture articulates derived aggregates, simple units, absence of parts, causal closure, qualitative determinations, and intrinsically differentiated plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The argument substitutes for explanations by bodies, transfer, position, or indifferentiation a return to the structural conditions of unity and becoming.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The real is formed of simple units whose priority over composites is ontological, whose existential limits are discontinuous, and whose identity unfolds as internal becoming.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The demonstrative form accomplishes its thesis by positively producing the monad through the accumulation of impossibilities concerning composition, influence, and indifferentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FL-01","text":"The necessity of simples is more strongly established than their mode of union with composites; ontological foundation exceeds the actually available theory of constitution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FL-02","text":"The system affirms that change is internal, but leaves underdetermined the mechanism of this production, the nature of qualities, and the relation between internal difference and intrinsic denomination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FL-03","text":"Creation and annihilation are posited as limits of simple existence without determining the agent, causality, or exact status of these events with respect to nature.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:FL-04","text":"Monadic closure must coexist with the composition of states and with the common order of created beings; the distinction between dependence, composition, and influence remains decisive and fragile.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point converts simplicity from a logical condition of closure into a non-spatial ontological determination of the natural element.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point converts the absence of parts into differentiation of the regimes of beginning, end, and temporality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point converts causal closure into a positive requirement for internal determinations and differential qualities.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MP-04","text":"The fourth mutation point reconceives identity: it no longer denotes fixed persistence, but the qualitative profile of a continuous change.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-01","text":"Implicit reality is a stratified machine: visible aggregates are derived effects of non-composite units whose internal determinations distribute change and difference.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-02","text":"The monad is a closed ontological chamber, not as inert isolation, but as the focus of qualitatively specified internal transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-03","text":"The theoretical subject becomes an instance of return and discrimination: it must trace composite phenomena back to their non-composite conditions, then distinguish causality, composition, and difference.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-04","text":"Time is double: the time of composites is that of possible rearrangements, whereas monadic time is the qualitative continuity of an internally determined becoming.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-05","text":"The only available conceptual navigation consists in abandoning explanations by transfer and following the conversion of exclusions into internal conditions of possibility.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B01","text":"Minimal reconstruction requires six nuclei: derivation of the composite, simplicity without parts, despatialization of the element, exclusion of partitive transitions, causal closure, and internal qualitative differentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B02","text":"These nuclei suffice to restore the meta-cluster movement: from the given composite toward the simple, from the simple toward causal closure, then from that closure toward dynamic identity and non-substitutable plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B03","text":"Compression must preserve the difference among three relations often confused: composition of simples in aggregates, direct causal influence between substances, and qualitative discernibility of states.","refs":["CL_UCIC_03:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B04","text":"The irreducible indetermination concerns the mechanism of connection between simples and composites, the positive content of the internal principle, as well as the agent and status of creation and annihilation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_04:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B05","text":"Reconstruction fails if it reintroduces a corporeal foundation, penetrative causality, an immobile identity, or a plurality obtained through mere numerical repetition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_01:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B06","text":"The strength of the machine lies in the recursive conversion of its negations into positive requirements; its limit lies in the fact that this conversion determines impossibilities more reliably than effective mechanisms.","refs":["CL_UCIC_02:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L1_01:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L1 01","context":"Chapters 01–12 · Proposition 1 · Proposition 2 · Proposition 3 · Proposition 4 · Proposition 5 · Proposition 6 · Proposition 7 · Proposition 8 · Proposition 9 · Proposition 10 · Proposition 11 · Proposition 12"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L2 01","order":1,"parents":["MC_UCIC_L1_01","MC_UCIC_L1_02","MC_UCIC_L1_03","MC_UCIC_L1_04"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L2_01@R001","sha256":"5113c1dc08dd86f934591c3c33cf36587fea9f2d1245bb7ca798d81798c8f20d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-01","text":"Le système retire au composé la capacité de se fonder lui-même et reconduit toute réalité dérivée vers des unités non composées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-02","text":"La simplicité cesse d’être une borne négative lorsqu’elle devient la concentration active d’une différence, d’une perception et d’une trajectoire internes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-03","text":"La pluralité est reclassée comme contenu interne qualitativement différencié plutôt que comme juxtaposition de parties ou de substances externes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-04","text":"L’autonomie du présent est dissoute : tout état, fait, action ou vérité résulte de médiations antérieures et engage une orientation ultérieure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-05","text":"La raison suffisante généralise la clôture monadique en exigence d’intelligibilité pour les vérités, les faits, les possibles et les déterminations contingentes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-06","text":"L’échec de l’auto-fondation contingente produit une coupure de niveau vers une nécessité qui ne relève pas du régime dépendant qu’elle rend possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-07","text":"Le mouvement total est régressif vers le fondement, descendant vers la différenciation créée et récursif parce que chaque effet reconduit sa dépendance vers une source plus profonde.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-08","text":"La clôture obtenue est une architecture de dépendance différenciée, tendue entre activité interne réelle, absence d’autonomie ontologique et unité sans dehors.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Le composé n’est jamais un fondement ultime : son unité dépend de réalités non composées dont il ne peut dériver les principes par agrégation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] La simplicité passe de l’absence de parties à une puissance de concentration qui autorise détermination, perception, changement et individuation sans composition.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Aucun changement constitutif ne peut être expliqué comme pénétration, transfert ou importation depuis un dehors immédiatement causal.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] La pluralité réelle provient de différences qualitatives et perceptives internes, non de position, répétition numérique ou juxtaposition spatiale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] La perception et l’appétition convertissent la différence interne en succession orientée : l’identité subsiste en produisant des états nouveaux.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La raison suffisante étend l’interdiction du fait auto-explicatif à tous les régimes de vérité, de causalité, de possibilité et d’existence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] L’activité créée est réelle sans être primitive : elle opère intérieurement comme dépendance productive d’une source qu’elle ne possède pas.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Le nécessaire est le point où raison suffisante, possibilité, perfection, intelligibilité et causalité deviennent coextensives sans former des opérations homogènes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] L’identité est la cohérence d’une trajectoire qualitative et temporelle, non l’immobilité d’un substrat ni la permanence d’une conscience transparente.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Aucun dehors ne peut fonctionner comme principe premier indépendant, qu’il soit matière, cause externe, possible autonome ou second absolu.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-01","text":"La simplicité conserve l’identité d’absence de parties, mais migre du fondement anti-compositionnel vers une fonction positive d’enveloppement, de perception et de génération interne.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-02","text":"La négativité de la simplicité est renversée : ce qui excluait l’étendue devient la condition d’une intériorité riche sans division substantielle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-03","text":"La pluralité se déplace de la distribution externe des corps vers la différenciation de qualités, de perceptions, de degrés et de limitations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-04","text":"La perception mute d’état représentatif en principe de causalité interne, puis en continuum où mémoire, aperception et indistinction ne sont que des seuils fonctionnels.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-05","text":"La médiation demeure un invariant, mais ses supports changent : organe, mémoire, analyse, raison, série causale et dépendance divine deviennent des régimes non réductibles d’un même opérateur.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-06","text":"La raison suffisante passe d’une demande de fondement pour le contingent à une matrice qui distribue les rapports entre nécessité, possibilité, intelligibilité et création.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-07","text":"Le possible cesse d’être un contenu abstrait disponible indépendamment du réel et devient un régime dépendant de l’actualité nécessaire.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-01","text":"Les exclusions locales de l’étendue, de la dissolution ou de l’intrusion deviennent globales lorsqu’elles redistribuent simultanément causalité, temporalité, individuation et fondation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-02","text":"Les scènes de sommeil, d’évanouissement et de réveil cessent d’être des cas psychologiques : elles testent l’impossibilité d’un vide perceptif dans une substance active.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-03","text":"La distinction entre ordre fonctionnel et raison fondatrice devient le catalyseur qui convertit les mécanismes effectifs en objets de justification.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-04","text":"La distinction entendement/volonté/puissance, locale au niveau théologique, devient une matrice générale des régimes du nécessaire, du contingent et de l’existence produite.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-05","text":"Les modèles du possible autonome, de la causalité uniforme, de la création ponctuelle et de la créature auto-fondée deviennent obsolètes parce qu’ils confondent dépendance, activité et fondation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut que l’agrégat, la totalité divisible ou la relation de parties puissent produire leur propre unité explicative.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut une causalité conçue comme pénétration, réception, transport ou échange immédiat de déterminations entre substances.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut qu’absence d’aperception, de mémoire ou de distinction équivaille à absence de perception, d’activité ou d’être.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut le fait brut, l’existence autojustifiée et l’effet présent considéré comme la totalité de ses propres conditions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut tout dehors principiel : aucune matière, possibilité, altérité ou cause ne peut subsister comme fondement indépendant du nécessaire.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, l’être ne peut être une composition indéfiniment reconduite : une régression de constituants composés détruirait toute clôture explicative.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-02","text":"Pour que la raison reste opératoire, aucun fondement local — organe, sujet, primitive, série ou créature — ne peut universaliser seul son régime de justification.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-03","text":"Le système requiert une médiation objectivement effective mais jamais intégralement accessible au sujet fini, faute de quoi la différence entre ordre rationnel et possession de la raison s’effondrerait.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-04","text":"La différence réelle ne peut être fondée par un second absolu : elle doit être produite comme différenciation dérivée sans autonomie principielle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité la plus profondément refusée est celle d’un réel intelligible, actif et modal après retrait de toute source nécessaire.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-02","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’un extérieur causal qui pourrait constituer directement l’identité, le changement ou la différence d’une substance simple.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-03","text":"Le système interdit tout reste positif non fondé : admettre une réalité indépendante qui excéderait la raison suffisante détruirait l’unité de la fondation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-01","text":"La clôture monadique et la raison suffisante sont deux échelles d’une même interdiction : ni l’état interne ni le fait objectif ne peuvent être laissés sans détermination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-02","text":"La multiplicité interne et la dépendance productive convergent vers une activité créée qui produit réellement ses transitions sans devenir une source ontologiquement primitive.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-03","text":"La modalité et la causalité divine composent une cartographie de fonctions hétérogènes : comprendre, sélectionner, actualiser et soutenir ne sont pas une seule opération.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-04","text":"La continuité temporelle devient une double structure : succession interne des perceptions et reconduction actuelle de l’existence dérivée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-05","text":"L’intériorité causale ne signifie pas indépendance : elle désigne le site propre de l’opération créée à l’intérieur d’une dépendance ontologique continuellement reconduite.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme une hiérarchie sans extérieur, composée de foyers finis d’activité interne, de médiations distribuées et d’une fondation nécessaire non dérivée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-02","text":"Le sujet devient un nœud de perceptions, de mémoires, de raisons et de dépendances capable de reconstruire des médiations sans jamais posséder leur totalité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-03","text":"Le temps devient une profondeur opératoire : il est simultanément transition perceptive, accumulation de médiations et maintien actuel du dérivé.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-04","text":"La causalité est définitivement multi-régime : constituer, percevoir, orienter, justifier, actualiser et soutenir relèvent de fonctions articulées mais non homogénéisables.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-05","text":"La méthode du système est apophatico-constructive : la négation des faux mécanismes contraint l’apparition de fonctions positives minimales.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-01","text":"Composé dérivé → simple non composé → détermination interne → raison suffisante → nécessité fondatrice → différenciation créée : la régression ontologique revient comme distribution des dépendances.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-02","text":"Multiplicité interne → perception → appétition → transition → différence reconfigurée : l’unité se maintient uniquement en produisant des variations qui ne la divisent pas.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-03","text":"Effet orienté → insuffisance explicative → exclusion de la contradiction → demande de raison → clôture analytique ou série infinie : chaque réponse redéfinit le régime de fondation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur terminal est la dépendance différenciée : les tentatives d’autonomie du composé, de la perception, du possible, du sujet ou de la créature y sont réabsorbées comme dépendances de niveau.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B01","text":"Composé donné → insuffisance de l’agrégat → nécessité d’une unité simple non composée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B02","text":"Unité simple → exclusion de l’importation causale → localisation du changement dans une détermination interne.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B03","text":"Différenciation interne non spatiale → perception unifiante → succession qualitative sans division de substance.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B04","text":"Succession perceptive et médiation des effets → exigence de raison suffisante → différenciation modale des régimes de clôture.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B05","text":"Contingence, possibilité et intelligibilité non auto-fondées → nécessité actuelle → absorption de leurs conditions dans une source sans dehors.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B06","text":"Nécessité fondatrice → limitation réceptrice → activité créée intérieure, réelle et dérivative → monde de dépendances différenciées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AFM-B01","text":"Composé manifeste → simple non spatial → clôture causale → différence qualitative interne → perception successive → identité dynamique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AFM-B02","text":"Perception continue → appétition orientée → médiation des effets → insuffisance de l’ordre empirique → raison suffisante.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AFM-B03","text":"Raison suffisante → différence entre nécessité et contingence → refus du fondement local terminal → intelligibilité sérielle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AFM-B04","text":"Contingence dépendante → nécessité auto-fondée → plénitude sans dehors → limitation créaturelle → activité monadique dérivative.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-01","text":"L’opposition unité/multiplicité est remplacée par la distinction entre composition externe, différenciation interne et dépendance hiérarchique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-02","text":"La causalité cesse d’être un modèle unique de transmission et devient une carte de fonctions : produire, représenter, expliquer, actualiser et soutenir.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-03","text":"L’opposition identité/devenir s’effondre : l’identité est reclassée comme continuité différenciée d’une trajectoire interne et dépendante.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-04","text":"Le sujet perd le statut de principe transparent et gagne celui d’un nœud fini d’opérations, de traces et de raisons partiellement reconstructibles.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets explicites sont le composé, la monade, le corps, la perception, la mémoire, l’action, la vérité contingente, le possible et Dieu.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — L’architecture articule unités simples, multiplicité enveloppée, médiations causales, raison suffisante, limitation et dépendance productive.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — La propriété apparente d’un sujet, d’un fait ou d’un effet est remplacée par l’analyse du régime de liaison et de fondation qui le produit.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel est une stratification de dépendances où le temps conjoint succession interne, profondeur médiatrice et reconduction de l’existence finie.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — La forme argumentative accomplit son objet en convertissant chaque exclusion structurale en exigence positive de fondement, de différence ou de fonction.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-01","text":"L’activité intérieure de la monade est requise pour éviter le passivisme, mais la création continuée radicalise sa dépendance au point de fragiliser le statut exact de son autonomie opératoire.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-02","text":"L’exigence universelle de raison suffisante entre en tension avec l’impossibilité de fournir pour chaque contingent une raison finie, accessible et localement terminale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-03","text":"Une totalité divine sans dehors doit produire de la limitation réelle sans pouvoir attribuer cette limitation à la perfection de sa source.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MP-01","text":"La simplicité change de phase lorsqu’elle cesse d’être seulement absence de parties et devient capacité d’enveloppement, de représentation et de production de différences.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MP-02","text":"L’intériorité monadique change de fonction lorsqu’elle est distinguée de l’indépendance : elle devient activité propre à l’intérieur d’une dépendance fondatrice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est une machine hiérarchique de foyers internes, de médiations stratifiées et de dépendances sans extérieur principiel.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-02","text":"La monade est une chambre ontologique active : elle ne reçoit pas son devenir comme intrusion, mais déploie intérieurement une différence qui demeure dérivative dans son être.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-03","text":"La navigation admissible ne consiste pas à sortir du système, mais à distinguer les régimes de causalité, de médiation, de dépendance et de relève réflexive.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante si elle conserve le composé dérivé, la simplicité active, la perception successive, la raison suffisante, la nécessité sans dehors et la dépendance productive créée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B02","text":"L’indétermination irréductible porte sur le mécanisme positif de l’enveloppement perceptif, l’articulation entre activité interne et dépendance continue, ainsi que le passage de la plénitude au fini.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B03","text":"La compression demeure fidèle seulement si elle préserve la différence entre composition, causalité, médiation, fondation et dépendance, sans les résoudre dans une causalité uniforme.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200749334810Z_c774f291","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L2 01","source_sha256":"5113c1dc08dd86f934591c3c33cf36587fea9f2d1245bb7ca798d81798c8f20d","sha256":"f98fbb766e1d8e319d7c375a24581b7fa58ce41b44c2d2ef8481d5f10f7453d0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:07:49.338346+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-01","text":"The system deprives the composite of the capacity to ground itself and refers all derived reality back to non-composite units.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-02","text":"Simplicity ceases to be a negative limit when it becomes the active concentration of an internal difference, perception, and trajectory.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-03","text":"Plurality is reclassified as qualitatively differentiated internal content rather than as a juxtaposition of parts or external substances.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-04","text":"The autonomy of the present is dissolved: every state, fact, action, or truth results from prior mediations and entails a subsequent orientation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-05","text":"Sufficient reason generalizes monadic closure into a requirement of intelligibility for truths, facts, possibilities, and contingent determinations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-06","text":"The failure of contingent self-grounding produces a break in level toward a necessity that does not belong to the dependent regime that it makes possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-07","text":"The overall movement is regressive toward the ground, descending toward created differentiation, and recursive because each effect refers its dependence back to a deeper source.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-08","text":"The closure attained is an architecture of differentiated dependence, stretched between real internal activity, the absence of ontological autonomy, and unity without an outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The composite is never an ultimate ground: its unity depends on non-composite realities from which it cannot derive its principles by aggregation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Simplicity shifts from the absence of parts to a power of concentration that permits determination, perception, change, and individuation without composition.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] No constitutive change can be explained as penetration, transfer, or importation from an immediately causal outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Real plurality arises from internal qualitative and perceptual differences, not from position, numerical repetition, or spatial juxtaposition.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Perception and appetition convert internal difference into oriented succession: identity persists by producing new states.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Sufficient reason extends the prohibition of the self-explanatory fact to all regimes of truth, causality, possibility, and existence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] Created activity is real without being primitive: it operates inwardly as the productive dependence of a source that it does not possess.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] The necessary is the point at which sufficient reason, possibility, perfection, intelligibility, and causality become coextensive without forming homogeneous operations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Identity is the coherence of a qualitative and temporal trajectory, not the immobility of a substratum nor the permanence of a transparent consciousness.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] No outside can function as an independent first principle, whether it be matter, external cause, autonomous possibility, or second absolute.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-01","text":"Simplicity retains the identity of absence of parts, but migrates from an anti-compositional ground toward a positive function of enfolding, perception, and internal generation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-02","text":"The negativity of simplicity is reversed: what excluded extension becomes the condition of a rich interiority without substantial division.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-03","text":"Plurality shifts from the external distribution of bodies toward the differentiation of qualities, perceptions, degrees, and limitations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-04","text":"Perception mutates from a representative state into a principle of internal causality, then into a continuum in which memory, apperception, and indistinction are only functional thresholds.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-05","text":"Mediation remains an invariant, but its supports change: organ, memory, analysis, reason, causal series, and divine dependence become irreducible regimes of one and the same operator.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-06","text":"Sufficient reason shifts from a demand for a ground for the contingent to a matrix that distributes the relations among necessity, possibility, intelligibility, and creation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-07","text":"The possible ceases to be an abstract content available independently of the real and becomes a regime dependent on necessary actuality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-01","text":"Local exclusions of extension, dissolution, or intrusion become global when they simultaneously redistribute causality, temporality, individuation, and grounding.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-02","text":"The scenes of sleep, fainting, and awakening cease to be psychological cases: they test the impossibility of a perceptual void in an active substance.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-03","text":"The distinction between functional order and grounding reason becomes the catalyst that converts effective mechanisms into objects of justification.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-04","text":"The understanding/will/power distinction, local at the theological level, becomes a general matrix of the regimes of the necessary, the contingent, and produced existence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-05","text":"The models of autonomous possibility, uniform causality, punctual creation, and the self-grounded creature become obsolete because they confuse dependence, activity, and grounding.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that the aggregate, the divisible whole, or the relation of parts could produce their own explanatory unity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-02","text":"It excludes a causality conceived as penetration, reception, transport, or immediate exchange of determinations between substances.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that the absence of apperception, memory, or distinction is equivalent to the absence of perception, activity, or being.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the brute fact, self-justified existence, and the present effect considered as the totality of its own conditions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-05","text":"It excludes every principial outside: no matter, possibility, otherness, or cause can subsist as a ground independent of the necessary.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, being cannot be an indefinitely continued composition: a regression of composite constituents would destroy all explanatory closure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-02","text":"For reason to remain operative, no local ground—organ, subject, primitive, series, or creature—can alone universalize its regime of justification.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-03","text":"The system requires mediation that is objectively effective but never wholly accessible to the finite subject, failing which the difference between rational order and possession of reason would collapse.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-04","text":"Real difference cannot be grounded by a second absolute: it must be produced as derived differentiation without principial autonomy.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-01","text":"The possibility most deeply refused is that of an intelligible, active, and modal real after the withdrawal of every necessary source.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-02","text":"The structuring absence is that of a causal exterior that could directly constitute the identity, change, or difference of a simple substance.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-03","text":"The system prohibits every ungrounded positive remainder: to admit an independent reality exceeding sufficient reason would destroy the unity of grounding.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-01","text":"Monadic closure and sufficient reason are two scales of the same prohibition: neither the internal state nor the objective fact can be left undetermined.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-02","text":"Internal multiplicity and productive dependence converge toward a created activity that genuinely produces its transitions without becoming an ontologically primitive source.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-03","text":"Modality and divine causality compose a mapping of heterogeneous functions: understanding, selecting, actualizing, and sustaining are not a single operation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-04","text":"Temporal continuity becomes a double structure: internal succession of perceptions and the present renewal of derived existence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-05","text":"Causal interiority does not mean independence: it designates the proper site of created operation within an ontological dependence continuously renewed.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-01","text":"The real is reclassified as a hierarchy without an outside, composed of finite centers of internal activity, distributed mediations, and a necessary non-derived ground.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-02","text":"The subject becomes a node of perceptions, memories, reasons, and dependencies capable of reconstructing mediations without ever possessing their totality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-03","text":"Time becomes an operative depth: it is simultaneously perceptual transition, accumulation of mediations, and present maintenance of the derived.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-04","text":"Causality is definitively multi-regime: constituting, perceiving, orienting, justifying, actualizing, and sustaining belong to articulated but non-homogenizable functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-05","text":"The method of the system is apophatic-constructive: the negation of false mechanisms constrains the emergence of minimal positive functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-01","text":"Derived composite → non-composite simple → internal determination → sufficient reason → grounding necessity → created differentiation: ontological regression returns as a distribution of dependencies.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-02","text":"Internal multiplicity → perception → appetition → transition → reconfigured difference: unity is maintained only by producing variations that do not divide it.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-03","text":"Oriented effect → explanatory insufficiency → exclusion of contradiction → demand for reason → analytic closure or infinite series: each response redefines the regime of grounding.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-04","text":"The terminal attractor is differentiated dependence: attempts at autonomy by the composite, perception, the possible, the subject, or the creature are therein reabsorbed as level-dependencies.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B01","text":"Given composite → insufficiency of the aggregate → necessity of a simple non-composite unity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B02","text":"Simple unity → exclusion of causal importation → localization of change in an internal determination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B03","text":"Non-spatial internal differentiation → unifying perception → qualitative succession without division of substance.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B04","text":"Perceptual succession and mediation of effects → requirement of sufficient reason → modal differentiation of regimes of closure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B05","text":"Ungrounded contingency, possibility, and intelligibility → present necessity → absorption of their conditions into a source without an outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B06","text":"Grounding necessity → receptive limitation → internal, real, and derivative created activity → world of differentiated dependencies.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AFM-B01","text":"Manifest composite → non-spatial simple → causal closure → internal qualitative difference → successive perception → dynamic identity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AFM-B02","text":"Continuous perception → oriented appetition → mediation of effects → insufficiency of the empirical order → sufficient reason.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AFM-B03","text":"Sufficient reason → difference between necessity and contingency → refusal of the terminal local ground → serial intelligibility.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:AFM-B04","text":"Dependent contingency → self-grounded necessity → plenitude without an outside → creaturely limitation → derivative monadic activity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-01","text":"The unity/multiplicity opposition is replaced by the distinction between external composition, internal differentiation, and hierarchical dependence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-02","text":"Causality ceases to be a single model of transmission and becomes a map of functions: producing, representing, explaining, actualizing, and sustaining.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-03","text":"The identity/becoming opposition collapses: identity is reclassified as the differentiated continuity of an internal and dependent trajectory.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-04","text":"The subject loses the status of a transparent principle and gains that of a finite node of operations, traces, and partially reconstructible reasons.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit objects are the composite, the monad, the body, perception, memory, action, contingent truth, the possible, and God.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — The architecture articulates simple units, enfolded multiplicity, causal mediations, sufficient reason, limitation, and productive dependence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The apparent property of a subject, fact, or effect is replaced by analysis of the regime of linkage and grounding that produces it.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The real is a stratification of dependencies in which time conjoins internal succession, mediating depth, and the renewal of finite existence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The argumentative form accomplishes its object by converting each structural exclusion into a positive requirement of grounding, difference, or function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-01","text":"The monad's internal activity is required to avoid passivism, but continued creation radicalizes its dependence to the point of weakening the exact status of its operative autonomy.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-02","text":"The universal requirement of sufficient reason is in tension with the impossibility of providing, for each contingent, a finite, accessible, and locally terminal reason.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-03","text":"A divine totality without an outside must produce real limitation without being able to attribute that limitation to the perfection of its source.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MP-01","text":"Simplicity changes phase when it ceases to be merely the absence of parts and becomes a capacity for enfolding, representation, and the production of differences.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MP-02","text":"Monadic interiority changes function when it is distinguished from independence: it becomes an activity proper within a grounding dependence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-01","text":"Reality is a hierarchical machine of internal centers, stratified mediations, and dependencies without a principial outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-02","text":"The monad is an active ontological chamber: it does not receive its becoming as an intrusion, but inwardly unfolds a difference that remains derivative in its being.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-03","text":"Admissible navigation does not consist in leaving the system, but in distinguishing the regimes of causality, mediation, dependence, and reflexive supersession.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B01","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves the derived composite, active simplicity, successive perception, sufficient reason, necessity without an outside, and created productive dependence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B02","text":"Irreducible indeterminacy concerns the positive mechanism of perceptual enfolding, the articulation between internal activity and continuous dependence, and the passage from plenitude to the finite.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_01:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B03","text":"Compression remains faithful only if it preserves the difference between composition, causality, mediation, grounding, and dependence, without resolving them into uniform causality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L2_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L2_01:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L2 01","context":"Chapters 01–48 · Proposition 1 · Proposition 2 · Proposition 3 · Proposition 4 · Proposition 5 · Proposition 6 · Proposition 7 · Proposition 8 · Proposition 9 · Proposition 10 · Proposition 11 · Proposition 12 · Proposition 13 · Proposition 14 · Proposition 15 · Proposition 16 · Proposition 17 · Proposition 18 · Proposition 19 · Proposition 20 · Proposition 21 · Proposition 22 · Proposition 23 · Proposition 24 · Proposition 25 · Proposition 26 · Proposition 27 · Proposition 28 · Proposition 29 · Proposition 30 · Proposition 31 · Proposition 32 · Proposition 33 · Proposition 34 · Proposition 35 · Proposition 36 · Proposition 37 · Proposition 38 · Proposition 39 · Proposition 40 · Proposition 41 · Proposition 42 · Proposition 43 · Proposition 44 · Proposition 45 · Proposition 46 · Proposition 47 · Proposition 48"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L1 02","order":2,"parents":["CL_UCIC_05","CL_UCIC_06","CL_UCIC_07","CL_UCIC_08"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_02@R001","sha256":"125b366b23312a67c00fc41592444bc0dd9ba95b4fdc924453f8163d78b2a6e4","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-01","text":"Le problème directeur consiste à penser une unité simple qui demeure non composée tout en portant une diversité réelle d’affections, de perceptions et de transformations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-02","text":"Le recadrage décisif substitue à l’opposition unité/multiplicité une différenciation interne : la pluralité ne divise pas la substance, elle en constitue le contenu représenté et successivement modulé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-03","text":"L’argument dissocie deux régimes de causalité : les corps composés organisent des relations de parties, tandis que la substance simple produit des transitions perceptives depuis son propre principe.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:AS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-04","text":"La perception devient la médiation générale entre multiplicité, identité et devenir ; l’aperception, la mémoire et la distinction n’en sont que des degrés ou des manifestations localement relevées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-05","text":"Le mouvement est récursif et cumulatif : toute perception provient d’une antécédence, porte une orientation interne, produit une configuration nouvelle et reconduit ainsi la continuité de l’unité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-06","text":"La clôture est non terminale : l’identité substantielle ne survit pas au changement malgré lui, mais se maintient comme capacité d’envelopper, différencier et relancer ses propres états.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Une substance simple ne comporte pas de parties substantielles, mais son absence de composition spatiale n’implique ni homogénéité ni vacuité interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La multiplicité pertinente est une pluralité d’affections, de rapports et de perceptions enveloppés dans l’unité, non un assemblage de supports indépendants.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La perception passe du statut de représentation interne de la multitude à celui de régime général de l’activité substantielle, incluant ses formes indistinctes, latentes et distinctes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] La continuité temporelle et la continuité perceptive relèvent d’une même loi : aucun état actuel n’est isolé, car toute manifestation prolonge une activité antérieure et prépare une modulation ultérieure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] L’inaperception, l’absence de mémoire et l’indistinction ne désignent pas le néant perceptif, mais des régimes de visibilité ou de distinction inférieurs.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] L’appétition cesse d’être seulement une orientation vers un terme et devient la puissance par laquelle une perception se convertit effectivement en transition vers une autre perception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La critique de la mécanique ne supprime pas le mécanisme ; elle le limite au régime des relations externes et réserve l’intériorité perceptive à la causalité monadique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] L’identité ne désigne ni la répétition d’un même état ni la transparence continue de la conscience, mais la persistance d’une trajectoire perceptive capable de variations graduées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] L’autonomie substantielle est définie comme auto-production successive de modifications perceptives plutôt que comme indépendance d’un devenir ou maîtrise intégrale de ses résultats.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Le réel est constitué d’unités différenciées de l’intérieur, dont chaque degré perceptif est simultanément dépôt d’une histoire, seuil de visibilité et réserve de transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-01","text":"La simplicité persiste comme non-composition, mais mute en capacité positive d’enveloppement, de représentation, de continuité et d’auto-activité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-02","text":"La pluralité se déplace des affections internes vers la variété représentée, puis vers une échelle de perceptions graduées où l’indistinction devient une modalité productive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-03","text":"La perception se transforme d’état passager en principe de causalité interne, puis en continuum dont l’aperception et la mémoire ne marquent que des seuils locaux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-04","text":"La mémoire conserve une fonction classificatoire, mais perd sa prétention à fixer l’identité ontologique lorsque l’interruption manifeste devient compatible avec la reprise d’une capacité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-05","text":"La mécanique subit une inversion : d’explication candidate de la perception, elle devient le dispositif négatif qui rend visible l’irréductibilité de l’intériorité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-01","text":"Les scènes locales de sommeil, d’évanouissement, de réveil et d’étourdissement ne sont plus des exemples psychologiques séparés ; elles deviennent des tests d’une ontologie sans vide perceptif.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-02","text":"L’agrandissement de la machine reste une procédure locale de réfutation, mais devient à cette échelle une règle de changement de niveau : une description externe accrue ne produit pas l’intériorité absente.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-03","text":"La distinction locale entre perception et aperception est absorbée dans une architecture plus générale de degrés, reliant conscience, mémoire, temporalité et identité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-04","text":"L’appétition cesse d’être un principe local du passage perceptif et devient l’opérateur transversal qui articule continuité, orientation, inachèvement et génération de nouveauté.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-05","text":"Les taxonomies fixes de l’âme, de la Monade et de l’Entéléchie deviennent secondaires devant une cartographie dispositionnelle où les termes nomment des positions fonctionnelles dans une trajectoire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut que l’unité simple soit indifférenciation, que la multiplicité soit nécessairement composition et que le changement détruise la permanence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut que les figures, mouvements et interactions mécaniques suffisent à engendrer ou expliquer une perception intérieure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut l’équivalence entre absence d’aperception, absence de mémoire ou indistinction, d’une part, et abolition de l’affection perceptive, d’autre part.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut le présent isolé, le commencement perceptif absolu et l’avenir absolument extérieur à l’état qui le prépare.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut enfin une causalité évaluée uniquement par l’accomplissement complet, puisque l’effet partiel est déjà une production réelle de différence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:DBN-01","text":"Le système ne peut tenir si toute multiplicité réelle doit être spatiale, composée ou inspectable depuis l’extérieur.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:DBN-02","text":"Il ne peut tenir si un état phénoménal actuel épuise le statut ontologique de la substance qui le porte.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:DBN-03","text":"Il ne peut tenir si l’intériorité est une propriété émergente d’une accumulation de mouvements externes plutôt qu’un régime propre de causalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:DBN-04","text":"Il ne peut tenir si le temps est une juxtaposition d’instants indépendants plutôt qu’une succession générative d’états corrélés.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSA-01","text":"L’impossibilité structurante est celle d’une substance absolument vide de perception : une unité sans affection ne pourrait ni persister comme trajectoire ni se différencier.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité indisponible est celle d’un dehors causal autonome qui produirait la nouveauté sans être repris dans l’activité interne de l’unité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSA-03","text":"L’architecture forclôt une identité entièrement donnée dans l’instant, puisque toute identité substantielle excède ce qui est actuellement distingué, remémoré ou aperçu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-01","text":"La Monade est reconstruite comme une unité à double irréductibilité : elle n’est ni divisée par sa multiplicité interne ni expliquée par l’agrégation mécanique externe.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-07","CL_UCIC_06:XD-01","CL_UCIC_06:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-02","text":"La continuité perceptive transforme l’inconscience en problème de seuil : ce qui disparaît phénoménalement demeure ontologiquement actif sous une modalité moins distincte.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-08","CL_UCIC_07:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_08:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-03","text":"La causalité interne possède une structure temporalisée : chaque état conserve une antécédence, oriente un passage et produit un résultat qui relance la série sans l’épuiser.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-09","CL_UCIC_05:XD-06","CL_UCIC_08:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-04","text":"L’autonomie ne signifie pas séparation absolue d’avec tout changement ; elle signifie que le changement constitutif de l’unité provient d’une succession de modifications perceptives internes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-09","CL_UCIC_06:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-05","text":"L’inachèvement devient productif parce que l’écart entre perception orientée et résultat obtenu ne marque pas un défaut extrinsèque, mais le mécanisme de la relance perceptive.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-09","CL_UCIC_05:XD-04","CL_UCIC_05:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-06","text":"La distinction entre âme et Monade est reclassée : elle ne sépare plus deux substances visibles dans un instant, mais deux régimes de capacité et de relève au sein d’un même champ perceptif.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-08","CL_UCIC_07:XD-04","CL_UCIC_07:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-01","text":"L’ontologie est stratifiée sans être dualiste : les corps et les substances simples ne sont pas deux réalités isolées, mais deux régimes explicatifs hétérogènes de l’extériorité relationnelle et de l’intériorité perceptive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-02","text":"Le temps devient la forme opératoire de l’identité : persister signifie intégrer un passé perceptif, traverser une variation présente et maintenir une virtualité de différenciation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-03","text":"Le sujet métaphysique n’est ni un observateur séparé ni une conscience continûment transparente ; il est un foyer de perceptions dont les capacités excèdent périodiquement l’accessibilité phénoménale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-04","text":"La causalité est reclassée comme production interne de différences successives : elle ne transporte pas seulement un effet, elle convertit la persistance même en génération.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-05","text":"L’infériorité perceptive ne constitue pas une privation ontologique, mais une position structurée dans une hiérarchie de relief, de distinction et d’aperception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-06","text":"La méthode adéquate devient généalogique et différentielle : expliquer un état exige de remonter vers son antécédence, d’identifier son degré perceptif et de suivre sa puissance de mutation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-01","text":"Multiplicité interne → représentation perceptive → appétition orientée → transformation de l’état → multiplicité reconfigurée : l’unité se conserve en produisant ses propres différences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-02","text":"Inspection mécanique accrue → visibilité accrue des parties → intensification de l’absence de perception → déplacement vers la causalité monadique : la négation de la mécanique devient une construction positive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-03","text":"Indistinction perceptive → apparence de privation → reconnaissance d’affections persistantes → relèvement possible : la latence est la boucle qui relie inconscience et continuité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-04","text":"État antérieur → état présent → virtualité de l’avenir → nouvel état : la temporalité s’auto-reproduit comme série interne sans commencement absolu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur global est une unité simple qui ne se soustrait pas à la multiplicité, mais l’enveloppe, la hiérarchise et la transforme sans devenir composée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B01","text":"Non-composition substantielle + multiplicité d’affections → différenciation interne non spatiale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B02","text":"Différenciation interne + état représentatif → perception comme enveloppement unifiant de la pluralité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B03","text":"Perception successive + continuité de la substance → nécessité d’un principe interne de transition et d’orientation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B04","text":"Orientation interne + accomplissement non exhaustif → effet partiel réel → production d’une perception nouvelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B05","text":"Perception non aperçue + absence de mémoire ou de distinction → latence perceptive, non abolition de l’affection substantielle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B06","text":"Continuité des états + gradation perceptive + auto-production interne → Monade comme trajectoire différentielle, perceptive et active.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B01","text":"Simplicité non composée → pluralité interne non spatiale → perception comme représentation unifiante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B02","text":"Perception représentative → critique de l’explication mécanique → distinction entre poussée externe et modification perceptive interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B03","text":"Modification perceptive interne → appétition orientée → accomplissement partiel → relance de la succession.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B04","text":"Indistinction, sommeil ou évanouissement → refus de la perception zéro → continuité d’affections latentes → identité dispositionnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B05","text":"Continuité temporelle → seuils d’aperception → différenciation qualitative → unité comme trajectoire active sans rupture ni homogénéité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-01","text":"L’opposition unité/multiplicité est définitivement remplacée par la distinction entre composition externe et différenciation interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-02","text":"L’opposition perception/non-perception est remplacée par une carte de degrés : perception indistincte, aperception, mémoire, distinction et relève qualitative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-03","text":"L’opposition identité/devenir s’effondre : le devenir interne est le mode même par lequel l’unité maintient sa cohésion.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-04","text":"L’opposition mécanique/spirituel est déplacée vers une différenciation méthodique des niveaux d’explication, plutôt que maintenue comme conflit entre deux ensembles d’objets.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-05","text":"Les états de faible conscience deviennent des objets ontologiquement lisibles, car ils manifestent une activité réelle sans exiger de transparence réflexive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets explicites sont la substance simple, la machine, l’âme, la mémoire, le sommeil, l’évanouissement, le réveil et l’étourdissement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Le système articule une substance non composée, une multiplicité enveloppée, une série perceptive, une orientation interne et une hiérarchie de degrés.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — La méthode déplace systématiquement l’analyse des apparences isolées vers les conditions de continuité, de transition et de classement qui les rendent possibles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel est une pluralité d’unités dont le temps interne est la succession générative de perceptions à degrés variables de distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — L’argument accomplit son ontologie en refusant chaque commencement apparent, chaque absence présumée et chaque identité statique au profit de leur genèse interne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FL-01","text":"La simplicité doit contenir assez de différenciation pour produire perception, mémoire, orientation et succession sans devenir une composition ; le mécanisme exact de cette compatibilité demeure sous-déterminé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FL-02","text":"L’autonomie interne de la Monade est affirmée, mais son articulation avec les déterminations externes et les structures mécaniques reste ouverte.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FL-03","text":"La perception indistincte est structurellement indispensable pour éviter le néant perceptif, mais sa nature positive demeure moins déterminée que sa fonction argumentative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-01","text":"La simplicité mute d’une détermination négative, l’absence de parties, en puissance affirmative d’enveloppement et de représentation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-02","text":"La mécanique mute d’un modèle explicatif concurrent en opérateur apophatique qui force le passage à un autre régime de causalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-03","text":"L’inconscience mute d’une apparence de privation en indice d’une activité perceptive qui persiste sous le seuil de la distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une architecture de foyers non composés où chaque unité condense une multiplicité, l’ordonne en perceptions et la reconfigure sans sortie hors d’elle-même.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet est une trajectoire de visibilité variable, non une conscience fixe : il demeure actif à travers les régimes d’indistinction, de mémoire interrompue et de relève perceptive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est une spirale de rétention et de virtualité dans laquelle le présent n’existe qu’en prolongeant un passé et en préparant une différenciation future.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée possible n’est pas une sortie de la continuité, mais une élévation de distinction à l’intérieur d’une activité perceptive qui ne cesse jamais absolument.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MRT-B01","text":"Les axiomes de non-composition, multiplicité interne, perception continue, causalité interne et gradation qualitative suffisent à reconstruire l’architecture de ce méta-cluster.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MRT-B02","text":"La reconstruction conserve le mouvement génératif décisif : unité non composée → pluralité représentée → succession perceptive → latence ou distinction → transformation orientée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MRT-B03","text":"La force de compression réside dans l’intégration de trois exclusions : la composition comme modèle unique de multiplicité, le néant perceptif et le présent sans antécédence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination irréductible concerne le mécanisme positif de l’enveloppement, le seuil exact de l’aperception et le rapport entre activité interne monadique et ordre mécanique externe.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200359769911Z_28f55527","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L1 02","source_sha256":"125b366b23312a67c00fc41592444bc0dd9ba95b4fdc924453f8163d78b2a6e4","sha256":"ea0adcd54eb64c6ac227459a6744fb6801460417597c4f0ef5ce9c40e7c69097","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:03:59.774434+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-01","text":"The guiding problem consists in thinking a simple unity that remains non-composite while bearing a real diversity of affections, perceptions, and transformations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-02","text":"The decisive reframing replaces the opposition unity/multiplicity with an internal differentiation: plurality does not divide substance; it constitutes its represented and successively modulated content.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-03","text":"The argument dissociates two regimes of causality: composite bodies organize relations of parts, whereas simple substance produces perceptual transitions from its own principle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:AS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-04","text":"Perception becomes the general mediation between multiplicity, identity, and becoming; apperception, memory, and distinction are only degrees or locally elevated manifestations thereof.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-05","text":"The movement is recursive and cumulative: every perception comes from an antecedence, bears an internal orientation, produces a new configuration, and thus renews the continuity of unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AS-06","text":"The closure is non-terminal: substantial identity does not survive change in spite of itself, but is maintained as the capacity to envelop, differentiate, and relaunch its own states.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] A simple substance contains no substantial parts, but its lack of spatial composition implies neither homogeneity nor internal emptiness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The relevant multiplicity is a plurality of affections, relations, and perceptions enveloped in unity, not an assemblage of independent supports.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Perception passes from the status of internal representation of the multitude to that of a general regime of substantial activity, including its indistinct, latent, and distinct forms.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Temporal continuity and perceptual continuity fall under the same law: no present state is isolated, for every manifestation prolongs a prior activity and prepares a subsequent modulation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Inapperception, absence of memory, and indistinction do not designate perceptual nothingness, but lower regimes of visibility or distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Appetition ceases to be merely an orientation toward a term and becomes the power by which one perception is effectively converted into a transition toward another perception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The critique of mechanics does not suppress mechanism; it limits it to the regime of external relations and reserves perceptual interiority for monadic causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Identity designates neither the repetition of one and the same state nor the continuous transparency of consciousness, but the persistence of a perceptual trajectory capable of gradual variations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Substantial autonomy is defined as the successive self-production of perceptual modifications rather than as independence from becoming or complete mastery of its results.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The real is constituted by units differentiated from within, each perceptual degree of which is simultaneously the deposit of a history, a threshold of visibility, and a reserve of transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-01","text":"Simplicity persists as non-composition, but mutates into the positive capacity for enveloping, representation, continuity, and self-activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-02","text":"Plurality shifts from internal affections to represented variety, then to a scale of graduated perceptions in which indistinction becomes a productive modality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-03","text":"Perception transforms from a passing state into a principle of internal causality, then into a continuum of which apperception and memory mark only local thresholds.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-04","text":"Memory retains a classificatory function, but loses its claim to fix ontological identity when manifest interruption becomes compatible with the resumption of a capacity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RMD-05","text":"Mechanics undergoes an inversion: from a candidate explanation of perception, it becomes the negative apparatus that makes the irreducibility of interiority visible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-01","text":"The local scenes of sleep, fainting, awakening, and dizziness are no longer separate psychological examples; they become tests of an ontology without perceptual emptiness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-02","text":"The enlargement of the machine remains a local procedure of refutation, but at this scale becomes a rule of level-change: an increased external description does not produce the absent interiority.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-03","text":"The local distinction between perception and apperception is absorbed into a more general architecture of degrees, linking consciousness, memory, temporality, and identity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-04","text":"Appetition ceases to be a local principle of perceptual passage and becomes the transversal operator articulating continuity, orientation, incompletion, and the generation of novelty.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:CGD-05","text":"Fixed taxonomies of the soul, the Monad, and the Entelechy become secondary before a dispositional mapping in which terms name functional positions within a trajectory.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the notions that simple unity is undifferentiation, that multiplicity is necessarily composition, and that change destroys permanence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the notion that mechanical figures, movements, and interactions suffice to generate or explain an inner perception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the equivalence between absence of apperception, absence of memory, or indistinction, on the one hand, and the abolition of perceptual affection, on the other.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the isolated present, the absolute perceptual beginning, and the future as absolutely external to the state that prepares it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:GNX-05","text":"Finally, it excludes a causality assessed solely by complete accomplishment, since the partial effect is already a real production of difference.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:DBN-01","text":"The system cannot hold if every real multiplicity must be spatial, composite, or inspectable from the outside.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:DBN-02","text":"It cannot hold if a current phenomenal state exhausts the ontological status of the substance that bears it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:DBN-03","text":"It cannot hold if interiority is an emergent property of an accumulation of external movements rather than a proper regime of causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:DBN-04","text":"It cannot hold if time is a juxtaposition of independent instants rather than a generative succession of correlated states.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSA-01","text":"The structuring impossibility is that of a substance absolutely devoid of perception: a unity without affection could neither persist as a trajectory nor differentiate itself.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSA-02","text":"The unavailable possibility is that of an autonomous causal outside that would produce novelty without being taken up into the internal activity of unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSA-03","text":"The architecture forecloses an identity wholly given in the instant, since every substantial identity exceeds what is presently distinguished, remembered, or apperceived.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-01","text":"The Monad is reconstructed as a unity with a double irreducibility: it is neither divided by its internal multiplicity nor explained by external mechanical aggregation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-07","CL_UCIC_06:XD-01","CL_UCIC_06:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-02","text":"Perceptual continuity transforms unconsciousness into a problem of threshold: what disappears phenomenally remains ontologically active under a less distinct modality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-08","CL_UCIC_07:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_08:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-03","text":"Internal causality possesses a temporalized structure: each state retains an antecedence, orients a passage, and produces a result that relaunches the series without exhausting it.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-09","CL_UCIC_05:XD-06","CL_UCIC_08:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-04","text":"Autonomy does not mean absolute separation from all change; it means that the change constitutive of unity proceeds from a succession of internal perceptual modifications.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-09","CL_UCIC_06:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_06:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-05","text":"Incompletion becomes productive because the gap between oriented perception and the result obtained does not mark an extrinsic defect, but the mechanism of perceptual relaunching.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-09","CL_UCIC_05:XD-04","CL_UCIC_05:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:XD-06","text":"The distinction between soul and Monad is reclassified: it no longer separates two substances visible in an instant, but two regimes of capacity and elevation within the same perceptual field.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_02:GA-08","CL_UCIC_07:XD-04","CL_UCIC_07:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-01","text":"Ontology is stratified without being dualist: bodies and simple substances are not two isolated realities, but two heterogeneous explanatory regimes of relational exteriority and perceptual interiority.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-02","text":"Time becomes the operative form of identity: to persist means integrating a perceptual past, passing through a present variation, and maintaining a virtuality of differentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-03","text":"The metaphysical subject is neither a separate observer nor a continuously transparent consciousness; it is a focus of perceptions whose capacities periodically exceed phenomenal accessibility.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-04","text":"Causality is reclassified as the internal production of successive differences: it does not merely convey an effect; it converts persistence itself into generation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-05","text":"Perceptual inferiority does not constitute an ontological privation, but a structured position in a hierarchy of salience, distinction, and apperception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:BSD-06","text":"The adequate method becomes genealogical and differential: explaining a state requires tracing back to its antecedence, identifying its perceptual degree, and following its power of mutation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-01","text":"Internal multiplicity → perceptual representation → oriented appetition → transformation of the state → reconfigured multiplicity: unity preserves itself by producing its own differences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-02","text":"Increased mechanical inspection → increased visibility of parts → intensification of the absence of perception → shift toward monadic causality: the negation of mechanics becomes a positive construction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-03","text":"Perceptual indistinction → appearance of privation → recognition of persistent affections → possible elevation: latency is the loop linking unconsciousness and continuity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-04","text":"Prior state → present state → virtuality of the future → new state: temporality self-reproduces as an internal series without absolute beginning.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:RLE-05","text":"The global attractor is a simple unity that does not withdraw from multiplicity, but envelops, hierarchizes, and transforms it without becoming composite.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B01","text":"Substantial non-composition + multiplicity of affections → non-spatial internal differentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B02","text":"Internal differentiation + representative state → perception as unifying enveloping of plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B03","text":"Successive perception + continuity of substance → necessity of an internal principle of transition and orientation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B04","text":"Internal orientation + non-exhaustive accomplishment → real partial effect → production of a new perception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B05","text":"Unapperceived perception + absence of memory or distinction → perceptual latency, not abolition of substantial affection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FGS-B06","text":"Continuity of states + perceptual gradation + internal self-production → Monad as differential, perceptual, and active trajectory.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B01","text":"Non-composite simplicity → non-spatial internal plurality → perception as unifying representation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B02","text":"Representative perception → critique of mechanical explanation → distinction between external impulse and internal perceptual modification.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B03","text":"Internal perceptual modification → oriented appetition → partial accomplishment → relaunching of succession.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:AFM-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B04","text":"Indistinction, sleep, or fainting → rejection of zero perception → continuity of latent affections → dispositional identity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:AFM-B05","text":"Temporal continuity → thresholds of apperception → qualitative differentiation → unity as an active trajectory without rupture or homogeneity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-01","text":"The opposition unity/multiplicity is definitively replaced by the distinction between external composition and internal differentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-02","text":"The opposition perception/non-perception is replaced by a map of degrees: indistinct perception, apperception, memory, distinction, and qualitative elevation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-03","text":"The opposition identity/becoming collapses: internal becoming is the very mode by which unity maintains its cohesion.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-04","text":"The mechanical/spiritual opposition is displaced toward a methodical differentiation of levels of explanation, rather than maintained as a conflict between two sets of objects.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MME-05","text":"States of low consciousness become ontologically legible objects, because they manifest a real activity without requiring reflexive transparency.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit objects are simple substance, the machine, the soul, memory, sleep, fainting, awakening, and dizziness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — The system articulates a non-composite substance, an enveloped multiplicity, a perceptual series, an internal orientation, and a hierarchy of degrees.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The method systematically shifts analysis from isolated appearances toward the conditions of continuity, transition, and classification that make them possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The real is a plurality of units whose internal time is the generative succession of perceptions at varying degrees of distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The argument performs its ontology by rejecting every apparent beginning, every presumed absence, and every static identity in favor of their internal genesis.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FL-01","text":"Simplicity must contain enough differentiation to produce perception, memory, orientation, and succession without becoming a composition; the exact mechanism of this compatibility remains underdetermined.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FL-02","text":"The Monad's internal autonomy is affirmed, but its articulation with external determinations and mechanical structures remains open.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:FL-03","text":"Indistinct perception is structurally indispensable for avoiding perceptual nothingness, but its positive nature remains less determined than its argumentative function.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-01","text":"Simplicity mutates from a negative determination, the absence of parts, into an affirmative power of enveloping and representation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-02","text":"Mechanics mutates from a competing explanatory model into an apophatic operator that compels the passage to another regime of causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MP-03","text":"Unconsciousness mutates from an appearance of privation into an indication of a perceptual activity persisting below the threshold of distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is an architecture of non-composite foci in which each unity condenses a multiplicity, orders it into perceptions, and reconfigures it without exiting itself.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a trajectory of variable visibility, not a fixed consciousness: it remains active across regimes of indistinction, interrupted memory, and perceptual elevation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_07:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:HSI-03","text":"Time is a spiral of retention and virtuality in which the present exists only by prolonging a past and preparing a future differentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:HSI-04","text":"The only possible escape is not an exit from continuity, but an elevation of distinction within a perceptual activity that never absolutely ceases.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms of non-composition, internal multiplicity, continuous perception, internal causality, and qualitative gradation suffice to reconstruct the architecture of this meta-cluster.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MRT-B02","text":"The reconstruction retains the decisive generative movement: non-composite unity → represented plurality → perceptual succession → latency or distinction → oriented transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_05:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MRT-B03","text":"The force of compression resides in the integration of three exclusions: composition as the sole model of multiplicity, perceptual nothingness, and the present without antecedence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_08:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_02:MRT-B04","text":"Irreducible indeterminacy concerns the positive mechanism of enveloping, the exact threshold of apperception, and the relation between internal monadic activity and external mechanical order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_06:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L1_02:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L1 02","context":"Chapters 13–24 · Proposition 13 · Proposition 14 · Proposition 15 · Proposition 16 · Proposition 17 · Proposition 18 · Proposition 19 · Proposition 20 · Proposition 21 · Proposition 22 · Proposition 23 · Proposition 24"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L2 02","order":2,"parents":["MC_UCIC_L1_05","MC_UCIC_L1_06","MC_UCIC_L1_07","MC_UCIC_L1_08"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L2_02@R001","sha256":"c37462bd78d1ca8662cc580a2d2ba55322cbb1db65d11139c23fc6262d4c7848","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B01","text":"Le système affronte l’exigence de maintenir une pluralité de substances, de corps, de vivants et d’esprits sans admettre que leur unité dépende d’une séparation réelle, d’un transfert causal direct ou d’un commencement autonome.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B02","text":"Toute détermination est recodée comme relation fondée : la causalité devient d’abord raison et expression, puis organisation, concordance et finalement gouvernement des fonctions différenciées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B03","text":"Le mouvement général est une escalade récursive qui passe de la coordination intelligible des substances à la plénitude organisée de la matière, à la persistance des vivants, puis à la gouvernementalité providentielle des esprits.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B04","text":"Les événements visibles — action, génération, mort, changement corporel, décision ou récompense — perdent leur statut de commencements ou de clôtures et deviennent des reconfigurations d’un ordre antérieur.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B05","text":"La différence ne survit qu’en étant fonctionnelle, graduée et hiérarchisée : elle exprime un même ordre sans devenir homogénéité ni concurrence entre mondes séparés.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B06","text":"Le temps est subordonné à une logique plus profonde de sélection, de persistance organisationnelle, de parallélisme des séries et de délai rétributif ; il ne fournit plus le tribunal ultime de la causalité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B07","text":"Le sujet est produit comme opérateur local de perception, d’incorporation, d’action et de devoir, mais il demeure structurellement incapable de s’autofonder, de totaliser l’ordre ou de le réviser depuis un dehors.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B08","text":"La clôture construit une totalité sans extérieur absolu, universellement distribuée mais finiment opaque, où l’unité ne peut se donner qu’à travers des perspectives, des corps, des séries et des institutions subordonnées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Toute détermination recevable doit être rapportée à une relation de raison, de convenance, de fonction ou de finalité ; aucun fait brut ne peut porter seul l’intelligibilité du réel.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] La causalité se transforme d’un transfert supposé entre substances en une distribution de raisons, d’organisations, de correspondances et de fonctions gouvernementales.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Aucun être, phénomène, milieu ou jugement ne possède de dehors absolu à l’ordre relationnel qui le rend exprimable, organisé, persistant ou gouvernable.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] L’unité du réel ne s’obtient pas par fusion des différences, mais par leur redistribution en perspectives, degrés, séries, organes et fonctions hiérarchiquement coordonnées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Le corps organisé devient l’opérateur transversal qui convertit l’expression universelle en perspective finie, la matière en continuité identitaire et la relation au tout en position localisée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] L’identité cesse d’être propriété d’une substance, d’une matière ou d’un état ; elle devient persistance différentielle d’une organisation, d’une trajectoire vivante ou d’une fonction assignée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Aucun événement naturel ou moral ne crée ni n’abolit absolument l’être : il manifeste une disposition, une transformation ou une réarticulation déjà inscrite dans l’ordre total.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] La concordance sans transmission constitue la forme générale de l’ordre : les unités demeurent closes dans leur régime propre tout en participant à une coordination qui les dépasse.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] L’activité créée n’est recevable qu’à titre départemental : elle agit réellement dans une fonction déterminée, mais elle ne peut instituer ni évaluer souverainement la totalité qui l’emploie.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Les exclusions accumulées du simple, du vide, du commencement, de l’interaction et de l’autonomie se convertissent positivement en architecture de densification, de continuité et de gouvernement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-01","text":"La raison persiste comme refus du fait brut, mais elle mute de principe explicatif entre substances en opérateur de perfection, de sélection, puis de gouvernement de la pluralité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-02","text":"L’expression se déplace de la monade-perspective au corps organisé, du corps à la trajectoire vivante, puis de la trajectoire à la médiation cosmico-politique des esprits.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-03","text":"L’influence s’inverse durablement : ce qui semblait action transitive devient correspondance réglée, parallélisme de séries et exécution naturelle d’un gouvernement supérieur.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-04","text":"La partie, l’organisme, l’animal et l’esprit changent de fonction sans perdre leur appartenance au même schème : ils deviennent des focalisations persistantes plutôt que des unités substantielles autosuffisantes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-05","text":"La limitation cognitive passe d’une privation de distinction à une condition productive de l’ordre : l’opacité finie rend possible la perspective, la souveraineté du tout et le délai de la justice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-07","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-01","text":"[Local] Les mécanismes de machines naturelles, de semences, de préformation ou de transformations corporelles ne sont pas conservés comme explications autonomes ; ils sont absorbés comme indices d’une antériorité organisationnelle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-02","text":"[Changement d’échelle] La raison, l’expression, l’architecture et l’harmonie cessent d’être des opérations sectorielles et deviennent une grammaire unique de coordination entre les registres métaphysique, matériel, vital et politique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-03","text":"[Catalyseur] Le corps n’est plus seulement un objet de causalité ou un support de l’âme : il devient le relais par lequel la totalité se focalise, se temporalise et se différencie sans se fragmenter.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-04","text":"[Obsolescence] Les modèles de matière fixe, de partie inerte, de substance indépendante et de critique extérieure deviennent incompatibles avec une réalité définie comme organisation interne sans dehors disponible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut la causalité matérielle brute, l’influence transitive et toute relation qui traverserait directement l’intériorité d’une substance, d’un corps ou d’une série causale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut la simplicité matérielle, le vide, l’inertie et l’indistinction comme états ontologiques fondamentaux ; ces apparences doivent signaler une limite de résolution ou de composition.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut les seuils absolus de naissance, de mort, de création et d’annihilation, parce que tout changement doit être réinscrit dans une persistance antérieure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut symétriquement la fragmentation des êtres en mondes indépendants et l’unification qui abolirait leurs différences fonctionnelles ou leurs séries propres.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-03","MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut l’autonomie spirituelle, le jugement humain extérieur et la justice immédiatement vérifiable, parce que ces figures supposeraient un point d’observation ou d’action indépendant du gouvernement total.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, il doit être faux qu’une unité puisse être causalement close et ontologiquement autosuffisante, ou qu’une organisation puisse s’évanouir lorsqu’on descend dans ses parties.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-02","text":"Il doit être faux qu’une apparition, une décision ou une concordance observable fournisse sa propre explication ; l’événement ne peut être admis qu’après son inscription dans une continuité ou une harmonie antérieure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-03","text":"Il doit être faux que nature, grâce, loi, architecture, souveraineté et bonheur dérivent de principes ultimes pluriels ou soient soumis à un contre-jugement temporel durable.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-01","text":"L’absence structurante la plus profonde est celle d’une transparence finie intégrale : le tout doit être présent dans chaque position sans jamais devenir objet distinctement totalisable par elle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité radicalement indisponible est celle d’un dehors où relation, organisation, continuité et gouvernement cesseraient simultanément ; un tel dehors détruirait la condition même de toute détermination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-03","text":"Une nouveauté absolument autonome demeure impensable : la volonté, la conception, l’action et l’initiative ne peuvent apparaître que comme signatures locales d’une disposition déjà ordonnée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-01","text":"La raison suffisante, la récursion matérielle, l’antériorité organique et la Nature légiférée accomplissent une même opération : remplacer la communication directe par des médiations internes capables de produire de la concordance sans transmission.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-02","text":"L’incorporation transforme la récursion en identité persistante, mais cette persistance ne fonde aucune indépendance : elle expose au contraire chaque vivant et chaque agent à une place différenciée dans une hiérarchie fonctionnelle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-03","text":"La procédure négative produit une densification positive de l’ordre, mais son efficacité dépend de médiations dont le mécanisme reste incomplètement spécifié : expression, harmonie, élévation et rétribution sont exigées sans être entièrement opérationalisées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-05","MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-04","text":"L’actualisation du monde, la persistance du vivant et la justice providentielle relèvent d’une même reclassification : l’événement actuel n’est jamais premier, mais devient l’effet visible d’un ordre comparatif, antérieur ou différé.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-01","text":"Le réel devient une hiérarchie distribuée de médiations : raison, corps, organisme, série animale, cité et Nature n’y désignent pas des domaines séparés mais des régimes enchâssés d’une même coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-02","text":"La causalité se requalifie en administration de compatibilités : produire signifie rendre conjointement possibles des effets, des transformations, des perspectives et des sanctions sans leur attribuer une origine locale souveraine.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-03","text":"Le sujet cesse d’être un auteur autonome ou un simple réceptacle : il devient un centre incorporé de persistance, d’expérience et de devoir dont l’activité ne vaut qu’à l’intérieur d’une fonction dérivée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-04","text":"Le temps devient une stratification modale et gouvernementale : il conserve les différences par transformation, ordonne les séries parallèles et retarde la visibilité de la justice sans suspendre son efficacité postulée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-01","text":"La boucle apophatique est : exclusion d’un dehors ou d’un terme simple → découverte d’une médiation interne plus profonde → extension de l’ordre à un nouveau niveau → nouvelle exclusion de l’extériorité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-02","text":"La voie d’escalade dominante est : différence perceptive → raison comparative → organisation récursive → continuité des séries → concordance non transitive → gouvernement de la pluralité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-03","text":"L’attracteur d’unité différenciée se transforme en unité divine distribuée : il absorbe les oppositions autonomie/dépendance, vie/esprit, corps/âme et nature/grâce sans leur permettre de devenir des séparations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-05","MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-04","text":"Une boucle d’opacité soutient la clôture : l’impossibilité d’une transparence finie rend le gouvernement nécessaire, tandis que le gouvernement différé confirme l’impossibilité de juger immédiatement le tout.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B01","text":"Poser une pluralité de substances, de corps, de vivants et d’esprits dont les différences ne peuvent être expliquées ni par l’isolement, ni par la matière homogène, ni par une origine locale absolue.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B02","text":"Retirer successivement le fait brut, le vide, le simple, le seuil absolu, l’interaction transitive et le point de vue extérieur comme explications recevables.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B03","text":"Substituer à ces explications des opérateurs de relation : coordination idéale, expressivité matérielle, persistance organisée, harmonie des séries et exécution naturelle de la loi.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B04","text":"Faire de chaque unité un foyer relatif où le tout se module sans se répéter identiquement : perspective, partie organisée, animal persistant ou agent départemental.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B05","text":"Temporaliser l’ordre par sélection des possibles, renouvellement des supports, requalification des seuils et différé rétributif, afin que l’événement soit réel sans pouvoir être originaire.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B06","text":"Fermer la machine sur une totalité interne, hiérarchique et non transparente, où toute navigation consiste à changer de fonction ou de degré sans pouvoir sortir de l’architecture qui rend ce changement possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B08","MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B08","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B08","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B01","text":"Pluralité de substances, de corps et de vivants → refus de l’isolement et du fait brut → exigence d’une relation fondatrice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B02","text":"Relation fondatrice → clôture des intériorités → impossibilité du transfert direct → correspondance, expression et coordination idéales.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B03","text":"Plénitude matérielle → récursion des parties → corps comme foyer d’organisation → identité déplacée de la matière vers la continuité structurale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B02","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B04","text":"Apparence de génération, de mort ou d’influence → négation des seuils absolus → persistance organique et autonomie parallèle des séries.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B05","text":"Continuité vivante → mobilité des facultés → pluralité d’esprits → cité monarchique → Nature comme exécution du gouvernement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B06","text":"Justice immanente mais différée → activité locale du sujet → passivité devant l’issue totale → clôture providentielle sans tribunal extérieur.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B06","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-01","text":"La distinction entre causalité, intelligibilité et gouvernement est reclassée : ces termes décrivent des niveaux successifs de la même opération de mise en compatibilité des différences.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-02","text":"La matière cesse d’être support homogène et la totalité cesse d’être son contraire ; toutes deux deviennent des degrés d’emboîtement dans une profondeur organisationnelle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-03","text":"La frontière entre biologie, métaphysique et histoire s’effondre comme frontière de domaines : génération, conservation, métamorphose et temporalité deviennent des variations d’une même persistance.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04","text":"La politique devient structure ontologique et la Nature devient appareil hybride de causalité, de normativité, de Providence et de limitation de la critique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-05","text":"La lecture adéquate devient topologique et généalogique : elle doit suivre les conversions d’échelle qui transforment une apparence locale en effet d’organisation, plutôt que classer des objets isolés.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont les substances, les monades, les corps, les organismes, les animaux, les âmes, les esprits, les cités, la Nature et les sanctions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont organisés par des relations de raison, des récursions matérielles, des continuités organiques, des séries coordonnées et des médiations gouvernementales.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Le système déplace toute enquête sur des agents ou des causes isolés vers les conditions structurelles qui rendent possible l’apparence d’action, de rupture, d’autonomie ou d’injustice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est une totalité relationnelle, pleine, persistante et finalisée, dont le temps distribue les transformations et diffère les intelligibilités sans les soustraire à l’ordre.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit ce qu’elle affirme : elle retire les dehors et les termes simples, puis restitue leurs fonctions sous forme de médiations internes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-01","text":"La continuité est universalisée comme loi de l’être, mais la hiérarchie des vivants et des esprits maintient des privilèges de participation qui ne se déduisent pas entièrement d’une simple différence graduelle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-02","text":"La coordination sans transmission est indispensable à l’architecture, mais les mécanismes positifs de l’harmonie, de l’expression et de la correspondance demeurent insuffisamment déterminés après la fermeture des voies causales directes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-03","text":"La justice providentielle réclame des mécanismes naturels réels, tout en les subordonnant à une finalité qui rend incertaine la frontière entre causalité propre, exécution et discipline subjective.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-01","text":"La première mutation méta-clusterienne survient lorsque la causalité directe est définitivement remplacée par la coordination de séries closes, faisant de l’action un problème d’architecture plutôt que de transmission.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-02","text":"La seconde mutation survient lorsque l’organisation corporelle ne sert plus seulement à décrire les vivants, mais devient le modèle de leur identité à travers le renouvellement matériel.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:MP-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-03","text":"La mutation terminale survient lorsque la représentation devient capacité architectonique et lorsque l’action morale est scindée entre obligation active locale et effectivité globale reçue.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de médiations récursives : elle convertit toute frontière en changement de niveau, toute différence en fonction et toute exclusion en densification de l’ordre.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet est une focalisation incarnée et persistante, simultanément expressive, animale, cognitive, morale et civique, dont l’autonomie n’existe qu’en tant que fonction située.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-02","MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est une machine de préconfiguration, de transformation différentielle, de parallélisme et de délai rétributif ; il transforme l’ordre sans fournir de prise pour le réformer.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-04","text":"La seule navigation possible consiste à modifier une position de clarté, de puissance, de devoir ou de participation à l’intérieur du système, jamais à s’en extraire ni à le juger souverainement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante si elle conserve ensemble la raison anti-brute, la clôture des séries, la récursion matérielle, la persistance du vivant, la coordination non transitive et le gouvernement providentiel.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B02","text":"La compression demeure fidèle seulement si elle préserve les mutations entre relation, expression, organisation, continuité, harmonie et gouvernement sans les réduire à un vocabulaire invariant de l’unité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination persistante porte sur la mesure de la perfection, le mécanisme de l’expression, l’opérativité de l’harmonie, l’élévation spirituelle et les médiations concrètes de la rétribution.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence de l’ensemble dépend d’un retour récursif et non d’un séquençage simplement linéaire : chaque niveau réactive la même exigence de relation réelle sans dehors, sans rupture absolue et sans transmission autonome.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200819942901Z_99b47652","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L2 02","source_sha256":"c37462bd78d1ca8662cc580a2d2ba55322cbb1db65d11139c23fc6262d4c7848","sha256":"8124f586953af55269469bcecc4897b283ab6c3e40ce80ed1318764e13f69f89","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:08:19.944349+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B01","text":"The system confronts the requirement of maintaining a plurality of substances, bodies, living beings, and minds without admitting that their unity depends on a real separation, a direct causal transfer, or an autonomous beginning.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B02","text":"Every determination is recoded as a grounded relation: causality first becomes reason and expression, then organization, concordance, and finally governance of differentiated functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B03","text":"The general movement is a recursive escalation that proceeds from the intelligible coordination of substances to the organized fullness of matter, to the persistence of living beings, and then to the providential governmentality of minds.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B04","text":"Visible events—action, generation, death, bodily change, decision, or reward—lose their status as beginnings or closures and become reconfigurations of a prior order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B05","text":"Difference survives only by being functional, graded, and hierarchized: it expresses one and the same order without becoming either homogeneity or competition among separate worlds.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B06","text":"Time is subordinated to a deeper logic of selection, organizational persistence, parallelism of series, and retributive delay; it no longer provides the ultimate tribunal of causality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B07","text":"The subject is produced as a local operator of perception, embodiment, action, and duty, but it remains structurally incapable of self-grounding, totalizing the order, or revising it from an outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B08","text":"The closure constructs a totality without an absolute outside, universally distributed yet finitely opaque, in which unity can be given only through perspectives, bodies, series, and subordinate institutions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every admissible determination must be referred to a relation of reason, fittingness, function, or finality; no brute fact can by itself bear the intelligibility of the real.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Causality is transformed from a presumed transfer among substances into a distribution of reasons, organizations, correspondences, and governmental functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] No being, phenomenon, milieu, or judgment possesses an absolute outside to the relational order that makes it expressible, organized, persistent, or governable.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] The unity of the real is not achieved by fusion of differences, but by their redistribution into hierarchically coordinated perspectives, degrees, series, organs, and functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The organized body becomes the transversal operator that converts universal expression into finite perspective, matter into identity-continuity, and relation to the whole into localized position.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Identity ceases to be a property of a substance, matter, or state; it becomes the differential persistence of an organization, a living trajectory, or an assigned function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] No natural or moral event either absolutely creates or abolishes being: it manifests a disposition, transformation, or rearticulation already inscribed in the total order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Concordance without transmission constitutes the general form of order: units remain closed within their own regime while participating in a coordination that exceeds them.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Created activity is admissible only in a departmental capacity: it acts genuinely within a determined function, but it can neither institute nor sovereignly evaluate the totality that employs it.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The accumulated exclusions of the simple, the void, the beginning, interaction, and autonomy are converted positively into an architecture of densification, continuity, and government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-01","text":"Reason persists as a refusal of brute fact, but it mutates from an explanatory principle among substances into an operator of perfection, selection, and then governance of plurality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-02","text":"Expression shifts from the monad-perspective to the organized body, from the body to the living trajectory, then from the trajectory to the cosmico-political mediation of minds.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-03","text":"Influence is durably inverted: what seemed to be transitive action becomes regulated correspondence, parallelism of series, and natural execution of a higher government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-04","text":"The part, the organism, the animal, and the mind change function without losing their belonging to the same schema: they become persistent focalizations rather than self-sufficient substantial units.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-05","text":"Cognitive limitation passes from a privation of distinction to a productive condition of order: finite opacity makes possible perspective, the sovereignty of the whole, and the delay of justice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-07","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The mechanisms of natural machines, seeds, preformation, or bodily transformations are not retained as autonomous explanations; they are absorbed as indices of an organizational anteriority.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-02","text":"[Change of scale] Reason, expression, architecture, and harmony cease to be sectoral operations and become a single grammar of coordination among the metaphysical, material, vital, and political registers.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-03","text":"[Catalyst] The body is no longer merely an object of causality or a support of the soul: it becomes the relay through which the totality is focalized, temporalized, and differentiated without fragmenting itself.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-04","text":"[Obsolescence] Models of fixed matter, inert part, independent substance, and external critique become incompatible with a reality defined as internal organization without an available outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes brute material causality, transitive influence, and every relation that would directly traverse the interiority of a substance, body, or causal series.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-02","text":"It excludes material simplicity, the void, inertia, and indistinction as fundamental ontological states; these appearances must indicate a limit of resolution or composition.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the absolute thresholds of birth, death, creation, and annihilation, because every change must be reinscribed within a prior persistence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-04","text":"It symmetrically excludes both the fragmentation of beings into independent worlds and a unification that would abolish their functional differences or their proper series.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-03","MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-05","text":"It excludes spiritual autonomy, external human judgment, and immediately verifiable justice, because these figures would presuppose a point of observation or action independent of total government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, it must be false that a unit can be causally closed and ontologically self-sufficient, or that an organization can vanish when one descends into its parts.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that an appearance, a decision, or an observable concordance provides its own explanation; the event can be admitted only after being inscribed within a prior continuity or harmony.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that nature, grace, law, architecture, sovereignty, and happiness derive from plural ultimate principles or are subjected to a lasting temporal counter-judgment.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-01","text":"The deepest structuring absence is that of an integral finite transparency: the whole must be present in each position without ever becoming an object distinctly totalizable by it.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-02","text":"The radically unavailable possibility is that of an outside in which relation, organization, continuity, and government would simultaneously cease; such an outside would destroy the very condition of all determination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-03","text":"An absolutely autonomous novelty remains unthinkable: will, conception, action, and initiative can appear only as local signatures of an already ordered disposition.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-01","text":"Sufficient reason, material recursion, organic anteriority, and legislated Nature accomplish the same operation: replacing direct communication with internal mediations capable of producing concordance without transmission.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-02","text":"Embodiment transforms recursion into persistent identity, but this persistence grounds no independence: on the contrary, it exposes each living being and each agent to a differentiated place within a functional hierarchy.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-03","text":"The negative procedure produces a positive densification of order, but its efficacy depends on mediations whose mechanism remains incompletely specified: expression, harmony, elevation, and retribution are required without being fully operationalized.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-05","MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-04","text":"The actualization of the world, the persistence of the living being, and providential justice fall under the same reclassification: the current event is never first, but becomes the visible effect of a comparative, prior, or deferred order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-01","text":"The real becomes a distributed hierarchy of mediations: reason, body, organism, animal series, city, and Nature do not designate separate domains therein, but nested regimes of one and the same coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-02","text":"Causality is requalified as administration of compatibilities: to produce means to render effects, transformations, perspectives, and sanctions jointly possible without attributing to them a sovereign local origin.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-03","text":"The subject ceases to be an autonomous author or a mere receptacle: it becomes an embodied center of persistence, experience, and duty whose activity has value only within a derived function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-04","text":"Time becomes a modal and governmental stratification: it preserves differences through transformation, orders parallel series, and delays the visibility of justice without suspending its postulated efficacy.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-01","text":"The apophatic loop is: exclusion of an outside or a simple term → discovery of a deeper internal mediation → extension of order to a new level → renewed exclusion of exteriority.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-02","text":"The dominant escalation path is: perceptual difference → comparative reason → recursive organization → continuity of series → non-transitive concordance → governance of plurality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-03","text":"The attractor of differentiated unity is transformed into distributed divine unity: it absorbs the oppositions autonomy/dependence, life/mind, body/soul, and nature/grace without allowing them to become separations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-05","MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-04","text":"A loop of opacity sustains closure: the impossibility of finite transparency renders government necessary, while deferred government confirms the impossibility of immediately judging the whole.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B01","text":"Posit a plurality of substances, bodies, living beings, and minds whose differences can be explained neither by isolation, nor by homogeneous matter, nor by an absolute local origin.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B02","text":"Successively remove brute fact, the void, the simple, the absolute threshold, transitive interaction, and the external point of view as admissible explanations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B03","text":"Substitute for these explanations relational operators: ideal coordination, material expressivity, organized persistence, harmony of series, and natural execution of law.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B04","text":"Make each unit a relative focus in which the whole is modulated without repeating itself identically: perspective, organized part, persistent animal, or departmental agent.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B05","text":"Temporalize order through selection of possibles, renewal of supports, requalification of thresholds, and retributive deferral, so that the event is real without being able to be originary.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B06","text":"Close the machine upon an internal, hierarchical, and non-transparent totality, in which every navigation consists in changing function or degree without being able to exit the architecture that makes this change possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B08","MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B08","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B08","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B01","text":"Plurality of substances, bodies, and living beings → refusal of isolation and brute fact → requirement of a founding relation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B02","text":"Founding relation → closure of interiorities → impossibility of direct transfer → ideal correspondence, expression, and coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B03","text":"Material fullness → recursion of parts → body as a focus of organization → identity displaced from matter toward structural continuity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B02","MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B04","text":"Appearance of generation, death, or influence → negation of absolute thresholds → organic persistence and parallel autonomy of series.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B05","text":"Living continuity → mobility of faculties → plurality of minds → monarchical city → Nature as execution of government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B06","text":"Immanent but deferred justice → local activity of the subject → passivity before the total outcome → providential closure without an external tribunal.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B06","MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-01","text":"The distinction among causality, intelligibility, and government is reclassified: these terms describe successive levels of the same operation of rendering differences compatible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-02","text":"Matter ceases to be a homogeneous support and totality ceases to be its opposite; both become degrees of nesting within an organizational depth.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-03","text":"The boundary between biology, metaphysics, and history collapses as a boundary of domains: generation, preservation, metamorphosis, and temporality become variations of one and the same persistence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04","text":"Politics becomes an ontological structure and Nature becomes a hybrid apparatus of causality, normativity, Providence, and limitation of critique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-05","text":"Adequate reading becomes topological and genealogical: it must follow the conversions of scale that transform a local appearance into an organizational effect, rather than classify isolated objects.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-06","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are substances, monads, bodies, organisms, animals, souls, minds, cities, Nature, and sanctions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are organized by relations of reason, material recursions, organic continuities, coordinated series, and governmental mediations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The system displaces every inquiry into isolated agents or causes toward the structural conditions that make possible the appearance of action, rupture, autonomy, or injustice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The real is a relational, full, persistent, and finalized totality, whose time distributes transformations and defers intelligibilities without withdrawing them from order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form accomplishes what it asserts: it removes outsides and simple terms, then restores their functions in the form of internal mediations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-01","text":"Continuity is universalized as a law of being, but the hierarchy of living beings and minds maintains privileges of participation that cannot be entirely deduced from a merely gradual difference.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-02","text":"Coordination without transmission is indispensable to the architecture, but the positive mechanisms of harmony, expression, and correspondence remain insufficiently determined after the closure of direct causal paths.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-03","text":"Providential justice requires real natural mechanisms, while subordinating them to a finality that renders uncertain the boundary between proper causality, execution, and subjective discipline.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-01","text":"The first meta-cluster mutation occurs when direct causality is definitively replaced by the coordination of closed series, making action a problem of architecture rather than transmission.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-02","text":"The second mutation occurs when bodily organization no longer serves merely to describe living beings, but becomes the model of their identity through material renewal.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:MP-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-03","text":"The terminal mutation occurs when representation becomes architectonic capacity and when moral action is split between local active obligation and received global efficacy.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-01","text":"Implicit reality is a machine of recursive mediations: it converts every boundary into a change of level, every difference into function, and every exclusion into a densification of order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-02","text":"The subject is an embodied and persistent focalization, simultaneously expressive, animal, cognitive, moral, and civic, whose autonomy exists only as a situated function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-02","MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-03","text":"Time is a machine of preconfiguration, differential transformation, parallelism, and retributive delay; it transforms order without providing a grip from which to reform it.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-04","text":"The only possible navigation consists in modifying a position of clarity, power, duty, or participation within the system, never in extracting oneself from it or sovereignly judging it.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B01","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves together anti-brute reason, the closure of series, material recursion, the persistence of the living being, non-transitive coordination, and providential government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B01","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B02","text":"The compression remains faithful only if it preserves the mutations among relation, expression, organization, continuity, harmony, and government without reducing them to an invariant vocabulary of unity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B03","text":"The persistent indeterminacy concerns the measure of perfection, the mechanism of expression, the operativity of harmony, spiritual elevation, and the concrete mediations of retribution.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B04","text":"The coherence of the whole depends on a recursive return rather than on a merely linear sequencing: each level reactivates the same requirement of real relation without an outside, without absolute rupture, and without autonomous transmission.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B05","MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L2_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L2_02:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L2 02","context":"Chapters 49–90 · Proposition 49 · Proposition 50 · Proposition 51 · Proposition 52 · Proposition 53 · Proposition 54 · Proposition 55 · Proposition 56 · Proposition 57 · Proposition 58 · Proposition 59 · Proposition 60 · Proposition 61 · Proposition 62 · Proposition 63 · Proposition 64 · Proposition 65 · Proposition 66 · Proposition 67 · Proposition 68 · Proposition 69 · Proposition 70 · Proposition 71 · Proposition 72 · Proposition 73 · Proposition 74 · Proposition 75 · Proposition 76 · Proposition 77 · Proposition 78 · Proposition 79 · Proposition 80 · Proposition 81 · Proposition 82 · Proposition 83 · Proposition 84 · Proposition 85 · Proposition 86 · Proposition 87 · Proposition 88 · Proposition 89 · Proposition 90"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L1 03","order":3,"parents":["CL_UCIC_09","CL_UCIC_10","CL_UCIC_11","CL_UCIC_12"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_03@R001","sha256":"318e9f0fd4b7265dd1867527100f82b9f83d639b6f27495745daf6db6db512f2","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-01","text":"Le problème commun consiste à déterminer comment des effets ordonnés, cognitifs ou rationnels émergent de liaisons, médiations et déterminations sans pouvoir être attribués immédiatement à une cause simple, consciente ou locale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-02","text":"Le mouvement commence par défaire l’autonomie du présent : perception, action, vérité et événement sont reclassés comme effets de compositions antérieures.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-03","text":"La rationalité se détache ensuite de l’efficacité empirique : une conduite peut être orientée sans raison, tandis que la raison exige un fondement excédant la répétition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:AS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-04","text":"La fondation se déplace d’une logique de non-contradiction vers une exigence de raison suffisante qui porte simultanément sur les vérités, les faits, les existences et les déterminations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:AS-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-05","text":"La nécessité produit des arrêts analytiques locaux, mais la contingence reconduit la raison vers des séries distribuées dont aucun terme particulier ne peut être final.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:AS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-06","text":"Le système est donc spiralé : médiation corporelle, liaison mémorielle, fondation rationnelle, réflexivité et causalité sérielle requalifient successivement ce qui compte comme cause, sujet et vérité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-07","text":"La clôture n’est ni une transparence du sujet ni un premier principe isolable, mais le maintien d’une exigence d’intelligibilité à travers des seuils primitifs, des médiations inconnues et des séries infinies.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-08","text":"L’argument produit une rationalité non immédiate : elle exclut le fait brut, l’effet auto-explicatif, l’action confondue avec la raison et la clôture locale érigée en totalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Aucun effet actuel ne suffit à expliquer sa propre production : sa fonction dépend d’une composition, d’une liaison ou d’une détermination antérieure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’ordre fonctionnel ne prouve pas la présence d’une raison réflexive, mais il exige une reconstruction des médiations qui produisent son orientation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:AS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La liaison des perceptions change de statut : d’opérateur organique et mémoriel, elle devient fondement théorique de la régularité puis réseau de déterminations du contingent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] La vérité admissible doit être soustraite à la contradiction et rapportée à une raison qui explique pourquoi elle est ainsi plutôt qu’autrement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La modalité organise les régimes de justification : l’opposé impossible autorise une clôture analytique, tandis que l’opposé possible maintient une exigence de raison sans finitude locale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Le fondement ne peut plus être défini uniformément comme un terme premier : il prend la forme de primitive, de limite analytique, de condition constitutive ou d’ordre sériel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Le sujet est un relais de médiations : ses actions, ses attentes, ses connaissances et sa réflexivité convergent à partir de déterminations qui ne coïncident pas avec une initiative transparente.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] La raison suffisante absorbe progressivement la perception, la mémoire, la science, l’analyse logique et la causalité contingente sous une même exigence de non-arbitraire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] La finitude humaine cesse d’être seulement une déficience : elle devient la position réflexive depuis laquelle le sujet pense l’être, la substance et l’infini divin.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] La clôture valide n’est pas l’obtention d’un dernier objet explicatif, mais la conservation de l’intelligibilité lorsque l’analyse rencontre des primitives ou une infinité de raisons.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-01","text":"[Stable identity] La médiation persiste comme invariant : l’organe compose, la mémoire relie, la raison fonde, l’analyse décompose et la série distribue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_11:AS-04","CL_UCIC_11:AS-06","CL_UCIC_12:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] La composition quitte le seul registre sensoriel pour désigner toute conversion d’une pluralité antérieure en unité présente, qu’elle soit perceptive, cognitive, logique ou causale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-03","text":"[Escalation] La régularité se transforme d’habitude pratique en objet de fondation rationnelle, puis en différence modale entre le nécessaire analysable et le contingent à raison distribuée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-04","text":"[Reversal] L’ignorance cesse d’indiquer l’absence de fondement ; elle devient la limite d’un sujet qui reconstruit partiellement un ordre rationnel objectivement plus vaste.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_11:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-05","text":"[Absorption] Les primitives logiques, les vérités nécessaires et les séries contingentes sont absorbées dans une théorie plurielle de la clôture plutôt que réduites à une même procédure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-06","text":"[Terminal transformation] L’Esprit n’est plus un nom psychologique terminal : il condense une trajectoire où mémoire, raison, réflexivité, ontologie et théologie sont devenues co-fonctionnelles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:RMD-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-01","text":"[Local] Les mécanismes de stimulation organique, d’attente animale, d’exemple astronomique, de théorème ou d’écriture restent des cas spécialisés de liaison et de détermination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-02","text":"[Changement d’échelle] La différence entre l’humain et l’animal devient une différence de régime de fondation, non une séparation biologique ni une opposition simple entre comportement mécanique et raison.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-03","text":"[Reliaison] Les unités se raccordent lorsque la liaison perceptive, la vérité nécessaire et la causalité contingente sont comprises comme des régimes hétérogènes d’une même exigence de détermination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-04","text":"[Catalyse] Le passage décisif survient lorsque l’efficacité ne suffit plus : tout effet orienté doit être distingué de son fondement, puis rapporté à la forme de justification qui lui convient.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-05","text":"[Recodage] Devient obsolète l’idée qu’une explication adéquate doive identifier une cause singulière, présente et finie ; l’explication devient cartographie des médiations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut la réception ou l’action immédiatement auto-explicative : ni stimulus isolé, ni habitude, ni effet pratique ne constituent par eux-mêmes une raison.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’une régularité observée fournisse spontanément son principe, qu’un fait brut termine l’explication ou qu’une existence soit autojustifiée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut l’assimilation du connaissable au fondé : l’inaccessibilité humaine d’une raison ne supprime ni son objectivité ni son exigence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_11:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut une clôture unique de la raison : les primitives arrêtent certaines régressions, alors que les contingences réclament un ordre de dépendances sans dernier terme local.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, doit être faux le modèle d’un sujet central qui recevrait passivement les données, produirait souverainement ses actes et mesurerait seul la rationalité du réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:DBN-02","text":"Doit être faux le modèle d’une causalité univoque où l’intensité de l’effet, la vérité de l’énoncé ou la direction de l’action révèleraient immédiatement leur genèse.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:DBN-03","text":"Doit être faux le modèle d’un fondement totalement local : ni la primitive ni la série ne peuvent seules universaliser leur propre forme de clôture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité la plus profondément forclose est celle d’un réel sans pourquoi, dont les faits, actions et vérités seraient ultimement dépourvus de détermination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSA-02","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une médiation intégralement accessible entre les opérations finies du sujet et les principes qui fondent leur portée ontologique ou divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSA-03","text":"Le système rend indisponible un dernier fondement particulier qui convertirait l’ensemble des raisons en chose finie, simple et définitivement isolable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-01","text":"La médiation perceptive et la raison suffisante constituent deux échelles d’un même opérateur : organiser ce qui précède pour rendre possible un effet, une conduite ou une vérité présente.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08","CL_UCIC_09:XD-01","CL_UCIC_11:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-02","text":"La rationalité ne commence pas là où l’animalité cesse : elle apparaît lorsqu’une liaison efficace est reprise comme objet de fondation, de modalisation et de réflexivité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-09","CL_UCIC_10:XD-07","CL_UCIC_10:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-03","text":"Les vérités nécessaires et les vérités contingentes ne s’opposent pas comme fondé et infondé, mais comme clôture analytique locale et raison sérielle non localisable.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-10","CL_UCIC_11:XD-06","CL_UCIC_12:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-04","text":"Le sujet fini devient le lieu d’une double non-coïncidence : il ne connaît pas toutes les raisons qui le déterminent et ne peut convertir sa limitation en infinité par simple amplification.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-09","CL_UCIC_10:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-05","text":"La méthode inter-unités impose de remonter des effets actuels vers leurs conditions sans exiger que cette remontée se ferme nécessairement dans une origine unique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-10","CL_UCIC_12:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_12:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme une architecture de déterminations stratifiées où l’apparition d’un effet ne coïncide jamais avec la totalité de ses conditions de production.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-02","text":"Le temps devient une profondeur opératoire : le présent condense l’histoire des stimulations, des habitudes, des analyses et des déterminations qui le rendent possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-03","text":"La causalité cesse d’être transmission linéaire d’une force ; elle devient coordination entre médiations corporelles, psychiques, logiques et sérielles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-04","text":"L’agentivité est déplacée de l’initiative réflexive originaire vers une capacité située de reconfiguration des régimes de liaison, de justification et de lecture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-05","text":"La raison n’est pas une faculté uniforme mais la forme variable par laquelle le système refuse l’arbitraire tout en maintenant des différences irréductibles de fondation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-01","text":"Multiplicité antérieure → médiation organisatrice → effet présent → relecture de cet effet comme condition d’une médiation plus haute ; la composition réinjecte ses produits dans une nouvelle chaîne explicative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-02","text":"Régularité observée → mémoire efficace → insuffisance théorique → vérité nécessaire → réflexivité → être et Dieu ; l’escalade transforme un mécanisme pratique en architecture ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-03","text":"Proposition → exclusion de la contradiction → demande de raison → modalisation → analyse ou ouverture sérielle ; chaque réponse redéfinit le régime de la question suivante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur final est une intelligibilité sans arbitraire et sans origine locale ultime : l’absence de terme fini devient la condition de maintien de la raison pour le contingent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B01","text":"Pluralité de stimuli, perceptions, propositions ou déterminations → refus de leur autonomie explicative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B02","text":"Refus de l’autonomie → recherche d’une médiation constitutive : composition organique, liaison mémorielle, fondement rationnel ou série causale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B03","text":"Médiation constitutive → production d’un effet orienté qui peut imiter la raison sans en fournir encore le fondement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B04","text":"Effet orienté → test de contradiction, exigence de raison suffisante et détermination de son régime modal.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B05","text":"Nécessité → analyse vers les primitives ; contingence → distribution infinie des raisons ; les deux voies maintiennent l’intelligibilité par des clôtures hétérogènes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B06","text":"Clôture hétérogène → sujet reclassé comme nœud de médiations, et réel reclassé comme ordre de raisons dont aucune instance locale ne possède seule la totalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AFM-B01","text":"Effet apparemment immédiat → médiation composée → ordre fonctionnel sans raison nécessaire → exigence de fondation → vérité nécessaire ou contingente → primitive locale ou série infinie → clôture non locale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AFM-B02","text":"Mémoire et habitude → insuffisance de la répétition → raison et science → réflexivité du Moi → catégories de l’être → sujet fini rapporté à l’infini.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AFM-B03","text":"Réduction vers un fondement → découverte de seuils primitifs → extension de la raison au contingent → abandon du dernier terme particulier → intelligibilité sérielle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MME-01","text":"L’opposition entre mécanique et rationnel s’effondre : elle est remplacée par une gradation entre liaison fonctionnelle, fondation théorique, réflexivité et rationalité sérielle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MME-02","text":"L’opposition entre fini et infini est reclassée : le fini peut porter l’exigence de l’infini sans posséder le mécanisme de son accomplissement ni la totalité de ses raisons.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MME-03","text":"La distinction entre absence de preuve et absence de légitimité s’effondre pour les primitives, tandis que la distinction entre absence de terme final et absence de raison s’effondre pour la contingence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MME-04","text":"Lire le système exige de suivre les mutations de fonction d’un même terme — composition, liaison, raison, analyse, clôture — plutôt que de préserver leurs identités nominales.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets explicites sont les stimuli, les perceptions, les actions, les régularités, les propositions, les faits, les principes, le Moi, l’être et Dieu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Ces objets deviennent des nœuds de médiations où composition, mémoire, contradiction, raison suffisante, analyse et causalité coordonnent leurs effets.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — La question de la propriété d’un sujet ou d’un fait est remplacée par l’examen du régime de liaison et de fondation qui le produit.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le présent n’est jamais originaire : il est l’intersection temporelle de déterminations passées, de raisons objectives et d’orientations futures.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — La forme argumentative accomplit son objet en transformant chaque arrêt analytique ou chaque lacune explicative en indice d’un changement d’échelle de la fondation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FL-01","text":"L’exigence universelle de raison suffisante entre en tension avec l’impossibilité de fournir une raison finie, accessible ou localement terminale pour chaque vérité contingente.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FL-02","text":"La continuité entre liaisons animales et rationalité humaine demeure productive mais instable : la raison doit émerger de médiations pré-réflexives tout en ne pouvant être réduite à elles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FL-03","text":"Le passage de la réflexivité finie à l’infinité divine est affirmé comme voie générative, mais son mécanisme ne peut être assimilé à une simple généralisation quantitative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation survient lorsque le stimulus ou le fait cesse d’être une unité explicative et devient le matériau d’une médiation constitutive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MP-02","text":"Le second point de mutation survient lorsque l’efficacité pratique est recodée comme insuffisante et doit recevoir une fondation rationnelle, modale ou analytique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation survient lorsque l’infinité cesse de signifier l’échec de l’explication et devient le mode de maintien de la raison pour le contingent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est une machine de médiations stratifiées : elle produit des unités opératoires à partir de pluralités physiques, psychiques, logiques et causales sans jamais les réduire à une origine unique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet est un nœud fini de composition, de mémoire, de réflexion et de détermination, capable de reconstruire partiellement les raisons qui le traversent sans en devenir le principe total.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est compression et profondeur : le passé revient comme habitude, attente, détermination et raison non encore découverte dans le présent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-04","text":"La seule échappée disponible est méthodologique : ne pas sortir du système des médiations, mais reclassifier ses niveaux, ses voies causales et ses régimes de clôture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante si elle conserve cinq noyaux : médiation compositive, dissociation entre ordre et raison, raison suffisante, pluralité modale des clôtures et sujet comme nœud déterminé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_09:AS-06","CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_12:GA-05","CL_UCIC_12:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B02","text":"La cohérence dépend de la non-réduction réciproque des niveaux : les mécanismes perceptifs ne deviennent pas la raison, les primitives ne deviennent pas des causes contingentes, et la série n’abolit pas les arrêts locaux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:FL-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination irréductible porte sur trois passages : corps vers représentation, sujet fini vers vérités nécessaires ou infinité, et raison sérielle vers son principe unificateur.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:FL-01","CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B04","text":"La compression demeure fidèle seulement si elle préserve le mouvement mutationnel : la fondation passe de la composition locale à la justification logique, puis à une intelligibilité distribuée sans terme final particulier.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200433874848Z_2415e194","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L1 03","source_sha256":"318e9f0fd4b7265dd1867527100f82b9f83d639b6f27495745daf6db6db512f2","sha256":"b54257ec59734cbfef858404dfafee4c6dcbbbbd8a4cba0f52b98fe0514b2711","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:04:33.878445+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-01","text":"The common problem consists in determining how ordered, cognitive, or rational effects emerge from connections, mediations, and determinations without being immediately attributable to a simple, conscious, or local cause.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-02","text":"The movement begins by undoing the autonomy of the present: perception, action, truth, and event are reclassified as effects of prior compositions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-03","text":"Rationality is then detached from empirical efficacy: conduct may be oriented without reason, whereas reason requires a ground exceeding repetition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:AS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-04","text":"Grounding shifts from a logic of non-contradiction toward a requirement of sufficient reason that bears simultaneously on truths, facts, existences, and determinations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:AS-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-05","text":"Necessity produces local analytical stopping points, but contingency leads reason back toward distributed series, of which no particular term can be final.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:AS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-06","text":"The system is therefore spiral-shaped: bodily mediation, mnemonic connection, rational grounding, reflexivity, and serial causality successively requalify what counts as cause, subject, and truth.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-07","text":"Closure is neither a transparency of the subject nor an isolable first principle, but the maintenance of a requirement of intelligibility across primitive thresholds, unknown mediations, and infinite series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AS-08","text":"The argument produces a non-immediate rationality: it excludes the brute fact, the self-explanatory effect, action confused with reason, and local closure elevated into totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] No present effect suffices to explain its own production: its function depends on a prior composition, connection, or determination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:GA-13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Functional order does not prove the presence of reflexive reason, but it requires a reconstruction of the mediations that produce its orientation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:AS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The connection of perceptions changes status: from an organic and mnemonic operator, it becomes the theoretical ground of regularity and then a network of determinations of the contingent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] An admissible truth must be exempt from contradiction and referred to a reason that explains why it is thus rather than otherwise.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Modality organizes regimes of justification: the impossible opposite permits analytical closure, whereas the possible opposite sustains a requirement of reason without local finitude.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Ground can no longer be defined uniformly as a first term: it takes the form of a primitive, an analytical limit, a constitutive condition, or a serial order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The subject is a relay of mediations: its actions, expectations, knowledge, and reflexivity converge from determinations that do not coincide with a transparent initiative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Sufficient reason progressively absorbs perception, memory, science, logical analysis, and contingent causality under one and the same requirement of non-arbitrariness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Human finitude ceases to be merely a deficiency: it becomes the reflexive position from which the subject thinks being, substance, and divine infinity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Valid closure is not the attainment of a final explanatory object, but the preservation of intelligibility when analysis encounters primitives or an infinity of reasons.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-01","text":"[Stable identity] Mediation persists as an invariant: the organ composes, memory connects, reason grounds, analysis decomposes, and the series distributes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_11:AS-04","CL_UCIC_11:AS-06","CL_UCIC_12:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] Composition leaves the sensory register alone to designate every conversion of a prior plurality into a present unity, whether perceptual, cognitive, logical, or causal.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-03","text":"[Escalation] Regularity is transformed from practical habit into an object of rational grounding, then into a modal difference between analyzable necessity and contingency with distributed reason.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-04","text":"[Reversal] Ignorance ceases to indicate the absence of ground; it becomes the limit of a subject that partially reconstructs an objectively vaster rational order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_11:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-05","text":"[Absorption] Logical primitives, necessary truths, and contingent series are absorbed into a plural theory of closure rather than reduced to a single procedure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RMD-06","text":"[Terminal transformation] Spirit is no longer a terminal psychological name: it condenses a trajectory in which memory, reason, reflexivity, ontology, and theology have become co-functional.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:RMD-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The mechanisms of organic stimulation, animal expectation, astronomical example, theorem, or writing remain specialized cases of connection and determination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-02","text":"[Change of scale] The difference between the human and the animal becomes a difference in regime of grounding, not a biological separation nor a simple opposition between mechanical behavior and reason.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-03","text":"[Reconnection] The units are connected when perceptual connection, necessary truth, and contingent causality are understood as heterogeneous regimes of one and the same requirement of determination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-04","text":"[Catalysis] The decisive transition occurs when efficacy no longer suffices: every oriented effect must be distinguished from its ground, then related to the form of justification appropriate to it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:CGD-05","text":"[Recoding] The idea that an adequate explanation must identify a singular, present, and finite cause becomes obsolete; explanation becomes a mapping of mediations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes reception or action that is immediately self-explanatory: neither an isolated stimulus, nor habit, nor a practical effect by itself constitutes a reason.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that an observed regularity spontaneously provides its principle, that a brute fact terminates explanation, or that an existence is self-justified.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the assimilation of the knowable to the grounded: human inaccessibility of a reason suppresses neither its objectivity nor its requirement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_11:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:GNX-04","text":"It excludes a single closure of reason: primitives halt certain regressions, whereas contingencies require an order of dependencies without a final local term.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, the model of a central subject that would passively receive data, sovereignly produce its acts, and alone measure the rationality of the real must be false.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:DBN-02","text":"The model of a univocal causality in which the intensity of the effect, the truth of the statement, or the direction of action would immediately reveal their genesis must be false.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:DBN-03","text":"The model of a wholly local ground must be false: neither the primitive nor the series can alone universalize its own form of closure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSA-01","text":"The possibility most deeply foreclosed is that of a real without a why, whose facts, actions, and truths would ultimately lack determination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSA-02","text":"The structuring absence is that of an integrally accessible mediation between the finite operations of the subject and the principles that ground their ontological or divine scope.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSA-03","text":"The system renders unavailable a particular final ground that would convert the whole of reasons into a finite, simple, and definitively isolable thing.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-01","text":"Perceptual mediation and sufficient reason constitute two scales of one and the same operator: organizing what precedes in order to make possible a present effect, conduct, or truth.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-08","CL_UCIC_09:XD-01","CL_UCIC_11:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-02","text":"Rationality does not begin where animality ceases: it appears when an effective connection is taken up as an object of grounding, modalization, and reflexivity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-09","CL_UCIC_10:XD-07","CL_UCIC_10:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-03","text":"Necessary truths and contingent truths are not opposed as grounded and ungrounded, but as local analytical closure and non-localizable serial reason.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-10","CL_UCIC_11:XD-06","CL_UCIC_12:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-04","text":"The finite subject becomes the site of a double non-coincidence: it does not know all the reasons that determine it and cannot convert its limitation into infinity through simple amplification.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-09","CL_UCIC_10:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:XD-05","text":"The inter-unit method requires retracing present effects to their conditions without demanding that this retracing necessarily close in a single origin.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_03:GA-10","CL_UCIC_12:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_12:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-01","text":"The real is reclassified as an architecture of stratified determinations in which the appearance of an effect never coincides with the totality of its conditions of production.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-02","text":"Time becomes an operative depth: the present condenses the history of stimulations, habits, analyses, and determinations that make it possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-03","text":"Causality ceases to be the linear transmission of a force; it becomes coordination among bodily, psychic, logical, and serial mediations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-04","text":"Agency is displaced from original reflexive initiative toward a situated capacity for reconfiguring regimes of connection, justification, and reading.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:BSD-05","text":"Reason is not a uniform faculty but the variable form through which the system refuses arbitrariness while maintaining irreducible differences of grounding.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-01","text":"Prior multiplicity → organizing mediation → present effect → rereading of this effect as the condition of a higher mediation; composition reinjects its products into a new explanatory chain.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-02","text":"Observed regularity → effective memory → theoretical insufficiency → necessary truth → reflexivity → being and God; the escalation transforms a practical mechanism into an ontological architecture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-03","text":"Proposition → exclusion of contradiction → demand for reason → modalization → analysis or serial opening; each response redefines the regime of the following question.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:RLE-04","text":"The final attractor is an intelligibility without arbitrariness and without an ultimate local origin: the absence of a finite term becomes the condition for maintaining reason for the contingent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B01","text":"Plurality of stimuli, perceptions, propositions, or determinations → rejection of their explanatory autonomy.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B02","text":"Rejection of autonomy → search for a constitutive mediation: organic composition, mnemonic connection, rational ground, or causal series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B03","text":"Constitutive mediation → production of an oriented effect that can imitate reason without yet providing its ground.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B04","text":"Oriented effect → test of contradiction, requirement of sufficient reason, and determination of its modal regime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B05","text":"Necessity → analysis toward primitives; contingency → infinite distribution of reasons; both paths maintain intelligibility through heterogeneous closures.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FGS-B06","text":"Heterogeneous closure → subject reclassified as a node of mediations, and the real reclassified as an order of reasons of which no local instance alone possesses the totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AFM-B01","text":"Apparently immediate effect → composed mediation → functional order without necessary reason → requirement of grounding → necessary or contingent truth → local primitive or infinite series → non-local closure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AFM-B02","text":"Memory and habit → insufficiency of repetition → reason and science → reflexivity of the I → categories of being → finite subject related to infinity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:AFM-B03","text":"Reduction toward a ground → discovery of primitive thresholds → extension of reason to the contingent → abandonment of the particular final term → serial intelligibility.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MME-01","text":"The opposition between the mechanical and the rational collapses: it is replaced by a gradation among functional connection, theoretical grounding, reflexivity, and serial rationality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MME-02","text":"The opposition between finite and infinite is reclassified: the finite can bear the requirement of the infinite without possessing the mechanism of its fulfillment or the totality of its reasons.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MME-03","text":"The distinction between absence of proof and absence of legitimacy collapses for primitives, while the distinction between absence of a final term and absence of reason collapses for contingency.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MME-04","text":"Reading the system requires following the functional mutations of one and the same term — composition, connection, reason, analysis, closure — rather than preserving their nominal identities.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:MME-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit objects are stimuli, perceptions, actions, regularities, propositions, facts, principles, the I, being, and God.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — These objects become nodes of mediations in which composition, memory, contradiction, sufficient reason, analysis, and causality coordinate their effects.","refs":["CL_UCIC_11:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The question of the property of a subject or a fact is replaced by examination of the regime of connection and grounding that produces it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The present is never original: it is the temporal intersection of past determinations, objective reasons, and future orientations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The argumentative form accomplishes its object by transforming each analytical stopping point or each explanatory lacuna into an indication of a change in the scale of grounding.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FL-01","text":"The universal requirement of sufficient reason comes into tension with the impossibility of providing a finite, accessible, or locally terminal reason for every contingent truth.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FL-02","text":"Continuity between animal connections and human rationality remains productive but unstable: reason must emerge from pre-reflexive mediations while being unable to be reduced to them.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:FL-03","text":"The transition from finite reflexivity to divine infinity is affirmed as a generative path, but its mechanism cannot be assimilated to a simple quantitative generalization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point occurs when the stimulus or fact ceases to be an explanatory unit and becomes the material of a constitutive mediation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point occurs when practical efficacy is recoded as insufficient and must receive a rational, modal, or analytical grounding.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point occurs when infinity ceases to signify the failure of explanation and becomes the mode of maintaining reason for the contingent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-01","text":"Reality is a machine of stratified mediations: it produces operative unities from physical, psychic, logical, and causal pluralities without ever reducing them to a single origin.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a finite node of composition, memory, reflection, and determination, capable of partially reconstructing the reasons that traverse it without becoming their total principle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_10:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-03","text":"Time is compression and depth: the past returns in the present as habit, expectation, determination, and reason not yet discovered.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:HSI-04","text":"The only available escape is methodological: not to leave the system of mediations, but to reclassify its levels, its causal paths, and its regimes of closure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B01","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves five cores: compositional mediation, dissociation between order and reason, sufficient reason, modal plurality of closures, and the subject as a determined node.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_09:AS-06","CL_UCIC_11:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_12:GA-05","CL_UCIC_12:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B02","text":"Coherence depends on the reciprocal non-reduction of levels: perceptual mechanisms do not become reason, primitives do not become contingent causes, and the series does not abolish local stopping points.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:FL-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B03","text":"Irreducible indeterminacy bears on three transitions: body to representation, finite subject to necessary truths or infinity, and serial reason to its unifying principle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_09:FL-01","CL_UCIC_10:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_03:MRT-B04","text":"Compression remains faithful only if it preserves the mutational movement: grounding passes from local composition to logical justification, then to a distributed intelligibility without a particular final term.","refs":["CL_UCIC_12:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_03@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L1_03:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L1 03","context":"Chapters 25–36 · Proposition 25 · Proposition 26 · Proposition 27 · Proposition 28 · Proposition 29 · Proposition 30 · Proposition 31 · Proposition 32 · Proposition 33 · Proposition 34 · Proposition 35 · Proposition 36"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L1 04","order":4,"parents":["CL_UCIC_13","CL_UCIC_14","CL_UCIC_15","CL_UCIC_16"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_04@R001","sha256":"b2a16d58ed338f0579389e51381be2a40000d841435c702a7ed3487f84799fd7","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-01","text":"Le système convertit l’échec de toute auto-explication contingente en exigence d’un fondement nécessaire qui ne relève pas du régime qu’il fonde.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:AS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-02","text":"Ce fondement cesse d’être une simple sortie de régression lorsqu’il absorbe le possible, l’intelligible et la réalité positive dans une plénitude sans dehors indépendant.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:SP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-03","text":"La nécessité devient ainsi à la fois raison ultime du contingent, condition ontologique du possible et source de la réalité créée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-04","text":"La fermeture unitaire ne supprime pas la différence, mais la redistribue comme limitation interne, réception finie et degré d’imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-05","text":"L’argument procède par compression successive : contingence, possibilité, perfection, création et activité monadique sont recodées comme régimes distincts d’une même dépendance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-06","text":"Le mouvement est simultanément régressif, descendant et récursif : il remonte vers la nécessité, redescend vers les créatures, puis relit leur activité comme réfractedation finie de la source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-07","text":"La clôture produite est une unité divine suffisante, illimitée et productive, dont l’intériorité explique la multiplicité sans autoriser de second principe autonome.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:AS-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-08","text":"Cette clôture demeure structurellement tendue, car la source doit simultanément contenir toute réalité positive, ne pas produire la limitation comme telle, et maintenir une activité créée non primitive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Aucun ordre contingent, possible ou intelligible ne porte par lui-même la raison suffisante de son existence ou de sa réalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] La raison dernière doit être nécessaire, actuelle et interne à elle-même, plutôt qu’un terme contingent, un possible abstrait ou une extension indéfinie de la série.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La nécessité passe de fonction de clôture explicative à condition de réalité du possible, des essences, des vérités et des existences créées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RMD-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] L’unité divine exclut tout extérieur indépendant et toute pluralité de principes premiers susceptibles de limiter, compléter ou concurrencer le fondement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La plénitude divine est une totalité sans dehors dont la différence interne n’est pensable que comme limitation dérivée et non comme altérité autonome.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] La limite est exclue du principe suprême, puis réinscrite dans la créature comme condition constitutive de sa finitude, de sa réceptivité et de son degré de perfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] La causalité divine se distribue fonctionnellement : l’entendement fonde l’intelligible nécessaire, la volonté sélectionne le contingent, et la puissance actualise et soutient l’existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Toute activité créée est une dépendance productive : elle est réelle comme perception, appétition et opération finies, mais dérivative quant à son être et à son orientation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] L’unicité divine ne désigne pas seulement un être suprême ; elle désigne le point où fondement, possibilité, perfection, causalité et raison suffisante deviennent coextensifs.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] L’architecture entière converge vers une dépendance différenciée qui refuse aussi bien l’autonomie primitive de la créature que l’arbitraire indifférencié de la source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-01","text":"La contingence conserve sa fonction de symptôme de dépendance, mais cesse d’être seulement une lacune explicative pour devenir l’indice d’un ordre dérivé intégralement fondé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-02","text":"La raison suffisante migre d’une exigence négative de sortie hors série vers une fonction positive qui fonde conjointement l’être, le possible et l’intelligible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-03","text":"L’infini perd son statut de prolongement indéfini et devient l’illimitation intensive d’une totalité qui ne reçoit aucune détermination d’un dehors.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-04","text":"La perfection est déplacée d’un attribut suprême abstrait vers une règle distributive : ce qui est positif est reçu, ce qui limite procède de la nature finie du récepteur.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-05","text":"Le possible change de statut : d’abord contenu intelligible, il devient réalité dépendante, puis opérateur de démonstration de l’actualité nécessaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-06","text":"La création mute d’un commencement causal en reconduction continue de l’être, de sorte que le temps devient le rythme d’une dépendance toujours actuelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-07","text":"La Monade absorbe l’ancienne opposition entre dépendance et activité : elle est active uniquement comme traduction finie de fonctions divines qui la dépassent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-01","text":"La régression des contingences, prise isolément, appartient à une machine locale ; à l’échelle actuelle, elle devient le protocole qui interdit toute fondation interne du réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-02","text":"La non-limitation divine, prise isolément, devient ici l’opérateur transversal qui distribue plénitude suprême, finitude créaturelle et lisibilité corporelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-03","text":"La médiation de l’entendement divin et l’identité du nécessaire sont des mécanismes locaux qui, ensemble, rendent le possible à la fois intelligible et ontologiquement réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-04","text":"La distinction entendement/volonté cesse d’être une correction doctrinale locale lorsqu’elle devient la matrice générale de différenciation entre nécessité, contingence et production.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-05","text":"L’inertie corporelle et l’activité monadique changent d’échelle : elles ne sont plus des cas particuliers, mais les signatures phénoménale et dynamique de la limitation dérivée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:SP-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-06","text":"Les modèles d’un possible autonome, d’une créature auto-fondée, d’une volonté arbitraire et d’une création ponctuelle deviennent simultanément obsolètes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut qu’une succession de contingences, même infinie, puisse convertir sa dépendance en fondement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut qu’un possible, une essence ou une vérité éternelle demeure réel tout en étant extérieur à l’intelligence et à l’actualité divines.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut tout dehors indépendant de la substance suprême, qu’il soit conçu comme autre nécessité, matière autonome ou réserve de réalité positive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut que la limitation soit une détermination divine positive au même titre que la perfection, en l’attribuant à la réceptivité propre de la créature.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut qu’une vérité nécessaire procède d’une décision volontaire contingente et que la souveraineté divine soit synonyme d’arbitraire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut enfin qu’une activité créée puisse être indépendance ontologique, puisque toute opération finie demeure production soutenue et imitation graduée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-01","text":"Pour tenir, le système doit rendre impossible toute auto-suffisance de niveau : ni contingent, ni possible, ni essence, ni Monade ne peut porter sa propre raison intégrale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-02","text":"Il doit rendre faux qu’une totalité de réalités dépendantes devienne nécessaire par simple totalisation ou par clôture descriptive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-03","text":"Il doit rendre faux qu’une altérité véritablement indépendante subsiste dans une totalité divine sans dehors.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-04","text":"Il doit rendre faux qu’une création puisse être achevée une fois pour toutes, car une créature auto-maintenue échapperait à la dépendance actuelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-05","text":"Il doit rendre faux qu’une même causalité indifférenciée explique de façon homogène le nécessaire, le contingent, l’intelligible et l’activité créée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité la plus profondément indisponible est celle d’un réel qui demeurerait intelligible, modal et actif après retrait de toute source nécessaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-02","text":"L’absence structurante n’est pas seulement celle d’un dehors divin : c’est celle d’un second absolu capable de fonder la différence sans dériver d’une unité première.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-03","text":"Le système rend inadmissible une liberté créaturelle définie comme indépendance, car toute liberté recevable doit être une modalité interne de l’imitation finie.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-04","text":"L’ontologie entière est ordonnée contre l’hypothèse d’un reste positif non fondé : aucune réalité ne peut excéder le fondement sans réintroduire une rupture de suffisance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-01","text":"La raison suffisante devient une opération de totalisation interne : elle ne se contente plus d’expliquer les contingents, mais transforme leur ensemble, leurs possibles et leurs formes intelligibles en dépendances d’un même nécessaire.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-03","CL_UCIC_15:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-02","text":"L’absence de dehors et la fondation du possible produisent une transcendance sans extériorité : le suprême excède toute créature sans être séparé d’un domaine de réalité possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-05","CL_UCIC_14:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-03","text":"La limitation résout fonctionnellement la coexistence de l’unité divine et de la pluralité créée : elle différencie sans instituer de second principe.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-06","CL_UCIC_16:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-04","text":"L’attribution dissymétrique des perfections et des limites protège la plénitude divine, mais établit simultanément une causalité fragmentée dont les médiations restent sous-déterminées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07","CL_UCIC_14:FL-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-05","text":"La création continuée convertit l’activité créée en paradoxe réglé : l’être est extérieur dans son maintien, intérieur dans ses opérations, et analogue dans sa structure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08","CL_UCIC_16:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-06","text":"La différenciation des fonctions divines transforme le problème de l’arbitraire en cartographie des régimes : nécessaire, contingent, productif, normatif et monadique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-10","CL_UCIC_16:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est reclassé comme une hiérarchie sans extérieur : la différence n’y survit qu’en tant que gradation interne de réception, de perfection et d’activité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-02","text":"La causalité devient multi-régime : fonder l’intelligible, actualiser l’être, orienter le contingent et soutenir temporellement le créé ne sont pas une seule et même opération.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-03","text":"Le sujet créé n’est ni une substance indépendante ni un effet inerte, mais une micro-architecture de réceptivité, de représentation et de tendance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-04","text":"Le temps est déclassé comme fondement et reclassé comme mode de reconduction de l’existence dérivée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-05","text":"La négation devient productive : l’exclusion de l’extérieur, de l’autonomie et de l’arbitraire engendre positivement une ontologie de la plénitude différenciée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-06","text":"La rationalité métaphysique ne procède plus par preuve unique, mais par convergence de voies régressive, modale, ontologique et analogique vers le même attracteur nécessaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-01","text":"La boucle primaire est : contingence → régression → insuffisance interne → nécessité → requalification du contingent comme dépendance fondée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-02","text":"La boucle modale est : possible → exigence d’actualité → Être nécessaire → fondation renouvelée du possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-03","text":"La boucle de la limite est : absence de borne → plénitude → limitation créaturelle → visibilité physique et dynamique de la finitude → retour à l’illimitation comme critère.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-04","text":"La boucle productive est : création → maintien continu → activité monadique → dépendance reconduite, de sorte que l’effet atteste la persistance de sa source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-05","text":"La boucle analogique est : fonction divine infinie → réceptivité limitée → faculté monadique finie → mesure graduée de l’imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-06","text":"L’attracteur commun est la dépendance différenciée : toute tentative d’autonomie du possible, de la créature ou de la vérité est réabsorbée comme dépendance de régime plus profond.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B01","text":"Multiplicité contingente → régression des raisons → incapacité de la série à se fonder elle-même.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B02","text":"Insuffisance interne → coupure de niveau → nécessité d’une raison actuelle, non contingente et auto-fondée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B03","text":"Nécessité auto-fondée + absence de dehors → totalité divine de la réalité positive et du possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B04","text":"Totalité illimitée → limite réinscrite comme condition propre de la créature plutôt que comme détermination du fondement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B05","text":"Réalité modale fondée → différenciation de l’intelligible nécessaire, du contingent choisi et de l’existence effectivement produite.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B06","text":"Production continuée + réceptivité limitée → Monades actives mais dérivatives, structurées comme imitations finies de fonctions divines.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B07","text":"Dépendance différenciée + analogie graduée → clôture d’un monde unifié où la pluralité n’est admise qu որպես manifestation interne de l’unique fondement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AFM-B01","text":"Contingence régressive → insuffisance de l’infini → nécessité auto-fondée → absorption du possible → plénitude sans dehors → limitation créaturelle → différenciation entendement/volonté/puissance → création continuée → activité monadique analogue → dépendance différenciée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AFM-B02","text":"La trajectoire inverse de fermeture est : rejet du contingent auto-suffisant → rejet du possible autonome → rejet de l’extérieur indépendant → rejet de l’arbitraire → rejet de l’autonomie créaturelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-01","text":"La séparation entre transcendance et immanence s’effondre : la transcendance devient l’absence de toute dépendance envers un dehors, non une localisation extérieure au possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-02","text":"La distinction entre unité et multiplicité est redessinée : l’unité est principe de suffisance, la multiplicité est différenciation dérivée et graduée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-03","text":"La modalité cesse d’être un domaine logique séparé et devient une dimension ontologique dépendante de l’actualité nécessaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-04","text":"Le corps et l’activité monadique deviennent des objets de lecture ontologique : l’un manifeste la borne, l’autre manifeste l’imitation finie.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-05","text":"La causalité n’est plus représentable comme transmission uniforme, mais comme distribution de fonctions selon des régimes de nécessité, de choix, de puissance et de réception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-06","text":"La méthode de lecture disponible devient généalogique et différentielle : remonter les dépendances, distinguer les régimes, puis suivre leurs traductions finies sans les identifier.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont la contingence, Dieu, les possibles, les vérités éternelles, les créatures, les corps et les Monades.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont redistribués selon des relations de fondation, d’illimitation, de limitation, d’actualisation, de maintien et d’imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] La stratégie consiste à remplacer les alternatives simples — autonomie ou dépendance, nécessité ou volonté, transcendance ou immanence — par des distinctions fonctionnelles emboîtées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] La nécessité est non dérivée, la finitude est constitutive du créé, et le temps est le mode de reconduction de l’existence dépendante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit sa thèse en faisant converger des voies distinctes vers un unique fondement, puis en redistribuant ce fondement dans des différences de régime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-01","text":"La totalité divine sans dehors entre en tension avec l’attribution de la limitation à la seule nature créée, car cette nature doit être interne à la totalité tout en ne lui étant pas imputable comme imperfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-02","text":"L’identité de l’essence et de l’existence dans l’Être nécessaire stabilise le possible, mais le passage de la non-contradiction à la possibilité positive demeure insuffisamment fondé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-03","text":"La création continuée radicalise la dépendance des Monades, tandis que leur activité intérieure interdit de les réduire à de simples effets passifs.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-04","text":"L’analogie rapproche les fonctions divines et créées, mais l’infinité de la source et la limitation de la créature empêchent que cette continuité devienne identité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MP-01","text":"La régression devient mutation lorsqu’elle cesse de chercher un terme antérieur et impose une rupture de registre entre dépendance et fondement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MP-02","text":"La limite devient mutation lorsqu’elle passe de négation de la perfection suprême à principe positif de différenciation et de gradation créaturelles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MP-03","text":"Le possible devient mutation lorsqu’il passe d’objet de l’entendement divin à condition de l’actualité nécessaire et à fondement des possibilités dépendantes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MP-04","text":"La volonté devient mutation lorsqu’elle est retirée du nécessaire pour être réinscrite comme sélection normative du contingent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est une machine hiérarchique sans dehors : elle ne produit aucune indépendance, mais distribue des degrés internes de réalité, de réception et d’activité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-02","text":"Dieu est la source où raison, possibilité, perfection et production coïncident ; la créature est une répétition limitée de cette coïncidence sous forme fonctionnellement décomposée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-03","text":"Le sujet créé est un opérateur dérivé de remontée et de traduction : il perçoit, tend et produit des effets sans jamais se constituer comme principe premier.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-04","text":"La seule navigation admissible consiste à suivre les dépendances et à augmenter l’imitation dans la finitude, non à chercher une sortie hors du système de fondation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige : l’impossibilité de l’auto-fondation contingente, la nécessité actuelle, l’absence de dehors indépendant, la limite créaturelle et la dépendance productive différenciée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B02","text":"Ces cinq noyaux reconstruisent le mouvement complet, car ils relient la régression explicative, la fondation modale, la plénitude divine, la création et l’activité monadique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B03","text":"La compression reste insuffisante si elle omet la différence des régimes causaux, car l’unité du fondement ne doit pas être confondue avec l’uniformité de ses opérations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination résiduelle porte sur le mécanisme précis qui relie la plénitude au fini, l’intelligible à l’actualité, et la création continuée à l’activité propre des Monades.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B05","text":"La fidélité au système exige de conserver sa tension constitutive : une unité sans dehors doit produire des différences réelles sans autoriser leur autonomie ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200510495581Z_3bc5bbd8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L1 04","source_sha256":"b2a16d58ed338f0579389e51381be2a40000d841435c702a7ed3487f84799fd7","sha256":"3aa3d2a22f7d7a169417094ee1e0d403168079e2276b6ab9bdff3eaa2f3a281d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:05:10.498890+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-01","text":"The system converts the failure of every contingent self-explanation into the requirement of a necessary foundation that does not belong to the regime it founds.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:AS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-02","text":"This foundation ceases to be a mere escape from regress when it absorbs the possible, the intelligible, and positive reality into a plenitude without an independent outside.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:SP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-03","text":"Necessity thus becomes at once the ultimate reason of the contingent, the ontological condition of the possible, and the source of created reality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-04","text":"Unitary closure does not suppress difference, but redistributes it as internal limitation, finite reception, and degree of imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-05","text":"The argument proceeds by successive compression: contingency, possibility, perfection, creation, and monadic activity are recoded as distinct regimes of one and the same dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-06","text":"The movement is simultaneously regressive, descending, and recursive: it ascends toward necessity, descends again toward creatures, then rereads their activity as finite refractation (réfractedation) of the source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-07","text":"The closure produced is a sufficient, unlimited, and productive divine unity, whose interiority explains multiplicity without authorizing a second autonomous principle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:AS-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AS-08","text":"This closure remains structurally tense, because the source must simultaneously contain all positive reality, not produce limitation as such, and sustain a non-primitive created activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] No contingent, possible, or intelligible order bears within itself the sufficient reason for its existence or its reality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The ultimate reason must be necessary, actual, and internal to itself, rather than a contingent term, an abstract possibility, or an indefinite extension of the series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Necessity shifts from an explanatory closure function to a condition of reality for possibility, essences, truths, and created existences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RMD-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Divine unity excludes every independent outside and every plurality of first principles capable of limiting, completing, or competing with the foundation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Divine plenitude is a totality without an outside, whose internal difference can be conceived only as derived limitation and not as autonomous otherness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Limitation is excluded from the supreme principle, then reinscribed in the creature as a constitutive condition of its finitude, receptivity, and degree of perfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Divine causality is functionally distributed: the understanding grounds the necessary intelligible, the will selects the contingent, and power actualizes and sustains existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Every created activity is productive dependence: it is real as finite perception, appetition, and operation, but derivative as regards its being and orientation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] Divine uniqueness designates not merely a supreme being; it designates the point at which foundation, possibility, perfection, causality, and sufficient reason become coextensive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The entire architecture converges on a differentiated dependence that rejects both the primitive autonomy of the creature and the undifferentiated arbitrariness of the source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-01","text":"Contingency retains its function as a symptom of dependence, but ceases to be merely an explanatory gap in order to become the indication of an integrally grounded derived order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-02","text":"Sufficient reason migrates from a negative requirement of exit from the series toward a positive function that jointly grounds being, the possible, and the intelligible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-03","text":"The infinite loses its status as indefinite prolongation and becomes the intensive unlimitedness of a totality that receives no determination from an outside.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-04","text":"Perfection is displaced from an abstract supreme attribute toward a distributive rule: what is positive is received; what limits proceeds from the finite nature of the receiver.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-05","text":"The possible changes status: initially intelligible content, it becomes dependent reality, then an operator for demonstrating necessary actuality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-06","text":"Creation mutates from a causal beginning into continuous renewal of being, such that time becomes the rhythm of an ever-actual dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RMD-07","text":"The Monad absorbs the former opposition between dependence and activity: it is active solely as a finite translation of divine functions that exceed it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-01","text":"The regress of contingencies, taken in isolation, belongs to a local machine; at the current scale, it becomes the protocol that prohibits every internal grounding of the real.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-02","text":"Divine non-limitation, taken in isolation, here becomes the transversal operator that distributes supreme plenitude, creaturely finitude, and bodily legibility.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-03","text":"The mediation of the divine understanding and the identity of the necessary are local mechanisms which, together, render the possible both intelligible and ontologically real.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-04","text":"The understanding/will distinction ceases to be a local doctrinal correction when it becomes the general matrix of differentiation among necessity, contingency, and production.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-05","text":"Bodily inertia and monadic activity change scale: they are no longer particular cases, but the phenomenal and dynamic signatures of derived limitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:SP-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:CGD-06","text":"The models of an autonomous possible, a self-grounded creature, an arbitrary will, and a punctual creation simultaneously become obsolete.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that a succession of contingencies, even an infinite one, could convert its dependence into a foundation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the possibility that a possibility, an essence, or an eternal truth remains real while being external to divine intelligence and actuality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-03","text":"It excludes every outside independent of the supreme substance, whether conceived as another necessity, autonomous matter, or a reserve of positive reality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the possibility that limitation is a positive divine determination on the same footing as perfection, by attributing it to the creature's own receptivity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the possibility that a necessary truth proceeds from a contingent voluntary decision and that divine sovereignty is synonymous with arbitrariness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:GNX-06","text":"Finally, it excludes the possibility that a created activity could be ontological independence, since every finite operation remains sustained production and graded imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-01","text":"To hold, the system must render impossible every self-sufficiency of level: neither contingent, nor possible, nor essence, nor Monad can bear its own integral reason.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-02","text":"It must render false the claim that a totality of dependent realities becomes necessary through mere totalization or descriptive closure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-03","text":"It must render false the claim that a genuinely independent otherness subsists within a divine totality without an outside.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-04","text":"It must render false the claim that a creation can be completed once and for all, for a self-maintained creature would escape present dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:DBN-05","text":"It must render false the claim that one and the same undifferentiated causality homogeneously explains the necessary, the contingent, the intelligible, and created activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-01","text":"The most profoundly unavailable possibility is that of a real which would remain intelligible, modal, and active after the withdrawal of every necessary source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-02","text":"The structuring absence is not merely that of a divine outside: it is that of a second absolute capable of grounding difference without deriving from a first unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-03","text":"The system renders inadmissible a creaturely freedom defined as independence, since every admissible freedom must be an internal modality of finite imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSA-04","text":"The entire ontology is ordered against the hypothesis of an ungrounded positive remainder: no reality can exceed the foundation without reintroducing a rupture of sufficiency.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-01","text":"Sufficient reason becomes an operation of internal totalization: it no longer merely explains contingents, but transforms their ensemble, their possibilities, and their intelligible forms into dependencies of one and the same necessary being.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-03","CL_UCIC_15:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-02","text":"The absence of an outside and the grounding of the possible produce a transcendence without exteriority: the supreme exceeds every creature without being separated from a domain of possible reality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-05","CL_UCIC_14:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-03","text":"Limitation functionally resolves the coexistence of divine unity and created plurality: it differentiates without instituting a second principle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-06","CL_UCIC_16:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-04","text":"The asymmetrical attribution of perfections and limits protects divine plenitude, but simultaneously establishes a fragmented causality whose mediations remain underdetermined.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07","CL_UCIC_14:FL-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-05","text":"Continued creation converts created activity into a regulated paradox: being is external in its maintenance, internal in its operations, and analogous in its structure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-08","CL_UCIC_16:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:XD-06","text":"The differentiation of divine functions transforms the problem of arbitrariness into a mapping of regimes: necessary, contingent, productive, normative, and monadic.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_04:GA-10","CL_UCIC_16:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-01","text":"The real is reclassified as a hierarchy without an outside: difference survives within it only as an internal gradation of reception, perfection, and activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-02","text":"Causality becomes multi-regime: grounding the intelligible, actualizing being, directing the contingent, and temporally sustaining the created are not one and the same operation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-03","text":"The created subject is neither an independent substance nor an inert effect, but a micro-architecture of receptivity, representation, and tendency.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-04","text":"Time is demoted as foundation and reclassified as a mode of renewal of derived existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-05","text":"Negation becomes productive: the exclusion of exteriority, autonomy, and arbitrariness positively generates an ontology of differentiated plenitude.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:BSD-06","text":"Metaphysical rationality no longer proceeds by a single proof, but by the convergence of regressive, modal, ontological, and analogical paths toward the same necessary attractor.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-01","text":"The primary loop is: contingency → regress → internal insufficiency → necessity → requalification of the contingent as grounded dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-02","text":"The modal loop is: possible → requirement of actuality → Necessary Being → renewed grounding of the possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-03","text":"The loop of limitation is: absence of bound → plenitude → creaturely limitation → physical and dynamic visibility of finitude → return to unlimitedness as criterion.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-04","text":"The productive loop is: creation → continuous maintenance → monadic activity → renewed dependence, such that the effect attests to the persistence of its source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-05","text":"The analogical loop is: infinite divine function → limited receptivity → finite monadic faculty → graded measure of imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:RLE-06","text":"The common attractor is differentiated dependence: every attempt at autonomy of the possible, the creature, or truth is reabsorbed as dependence of a deeper regime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B01","text":"Contingent multiplicity → regress of reasons → inability of the series to ground itself.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B02","text":"Internal insufficiency → level break → necessity of an actual, non-contingent, and self-grounded reason.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B03","text":"Self-grounded necessity + absence of an outside → divine totality of positive reality and the possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B04","text":"Unlimited totality → limitation reinscribed as the creature's proper condition rather than as a determination of the foundation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B05","text":"Grounded modal reality → differentiation of the necessary intelligible, the chosen contingent, and effectively produced existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B06","text":"Continued production + limited receptivity → active but derivative Monads, structured as finite imitations of divine functions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FGS-B07","text":"Differentiated dependence + graded analogy → closure of a unified world in which plurality is admitted only as an internal manifestation of the unique foundation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AFM-B01","text":"Regressive contingency → insufficiency of the infinite → self-grounded necessity → absorption of the possible → plenitude without an outside → creaturely limitation → differentiation of understanding/will/power → continued creation → analogous monadic activity → differentiated dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:AFM-B02","text":"The inverse trajectory of closure is: rejection of the self-sufficient contingent → rejection of the autonomous possible → rejection of the independent outside → rejection of arbitrariness → rejection of creaturely autonomy.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-01","text":"The separation between transcendence and immanence collapses: transcendence becomes the absence of every dependence on an outside, not an external location relative to the possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-02","text":"The distinction between unity and multiplicity is redrawn: unity is the principle of sufficiency; multiplicity is derived and graded differentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-03","text":"Modality ceases to be a separate logical domain and becomes an ontological dimension dependent on necessary actuality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-04","text":"The body and monadic activity become objects of ontological reading: the one manifests the bound, the other manifests finite imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-05","text":"Causality can no longer be represented as uniform transmission, but as a distribution of functions according to regimes of necessity, choice, power, and reception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MME-06","text":"The available method of reading becomes genealogical and differential: ascend dependencies, distinguish regimes, then follow their finite translations without identifying them.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:BSD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are contingency, God, possibilities, eternal truths, creatures, bodies, and Monads.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are redistributed according to relations of grounding, unlimitedness, limitation, actualization, maintenance, and imitation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The strategy consists in replacing simple alternatives—autonomy or dependence, necessity or will, transcendence or immanence—with nested functional distinctions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Necessity is non-derived, finitude is constitutive of the created, and time is the mode of renewal of dependent existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form performs its thesis by making distinct paths converge toward a unique foundation, then redistributing that foundation into differences of regime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-01","text":"Divine totality without an outside comes into tension with the attribution of limitation to created nature alone, for this nature must be internal to the totality while not being imputed to it as imperfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-02","text":"The identity of essence and existence in Necessary Being stabilizes the possible, but the passage from non-contradiction to positive possibility remains insufficiently grounded.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-03","text":"Continued creation radicalizes the dependence of the Monads, while their inner activity prevents their reduction to mere passive effects.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:FL-04","text":"Analogy brings divine and created functions closer together, but the infinity of the source and the limitation of the creature prevent this continuity from becoming identity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:FL-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MP-01","text":"Regress becomes mutation when it ceases to seek an anterior term and imposes a break of register between dependence and foundation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_13:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MP-02","text":"Limitation becomes mutation when it passes from negation of supreme perfection to a positive principle of creaturely differentiation and gradation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_14:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MP-03","text":"The possible becomes mutation when it passes from object of the divine understanding to condition of necessary actuality and foundation of dependent possibilities.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MP-04","text":"Will becomes mutation when it is withdrawn from the necessary in order to be reinscribed as normative selection of the contingent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-01","text":"Reality is a hierarchical machine without an outside: it produces no independence, but distributes internal degrees of reality, reception, and activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-02","text":"God is the source in which reason, possibility, perfection, and production coincide; the creature is a limited repetition of this coincidence in a functionally decomposed form.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-03","text":"The created subject is a derivative operator of ascent and translation: it perceives, tends, and produces effects without ever constituting itself as a first principle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:HSI-04","text":"The only admissible navigation consists in following dependencies and increasing imitation in finitude, not in seeking an exit from the system of grounding.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B01","text":"Minimal reconstruction requires: the impossibility of contingent self-grounding, actual necessity, the absence of an independent outside, creaturely limitation, and differentiated productive dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B02","text":"These five cores reconstruct the complete movement, because they connect explanatory regress, modal grounding, divine plenitude, creation, and monadic activity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_15:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B03","text":"The compression remains insufficient if it omits the difference of causal regimes, for the unity of the foundation must not be confused with the uniformity of its operations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B04","text":"Residual indeterminacy concerns the precise mechanism that connects plenitude to the finite, the intelligible to actuality, and continued creation to the proper activity of the Monads.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_04:MRT-B05","text":"Fidelity to the system requires preserving its constitutive tension: a unity without an outside must produce real differences without authorizing their ontological autonomy.","refs":["CL_UCIC_16:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_04@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L1_04:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L1 04","context":"Chapters 37–48 · Proposition 37 · Proposition 38 · Proposition 39 · Proposition 40 · Proposition 41 · Proposition 42 · Proposition 43 · Proposition 44 · Proposition 45 · Proposition 46 · Proposition 47 · Proposition 48"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L1 05","order":5,"parents":["CL_UCIC_17","CL_UCIC_18","CL_UCIC_19","CL_UCIC_20"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_05@R001","sha256":"91ae17a7ea8c71cb293f613fd81c4f0ef6a92ceeeda9cb6bf46a9c308dac17eb","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-01","text":"Le problème central est de rendre pensables la pluralité réelle, la dépendance entre substances et l’unité du monde sans admettre ni transfert matériel, ni fait brut, ni extériorité absolue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:SP-01","CL_UCIC_20:SP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-02","text":"Le système recadre toute détermination comme relation de raison, de convenance, d’expression ou de degré plutôt que comme propriété isolée, force homogène ou simple succession d’états.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:AS-B02","CL_UCIC_17:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-03","text":"L’action créée est progressivement dématérialisée : elle devient d’abord priorité explicative, puis correspondance réglée, puis expression locale d’un ordre universel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:XD-01","CL_UCIC_19:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-04","text":"La pluralité cesse d’être le contraire de l’unité lorsqu’elle est redistribuée comme multiplicité de raisons, de possibilités, de substances expressives et de perspectives graduées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:RMD-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-05","text":"La causalité divine fournit la matrice de toute intelligibilité : connaître différencie les possibles, préférer les hiérarchise, produire ou régler les inscrit dans un ordre actuel et expressif.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:AS-02","CL_UCIC_19:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-06","text":"Le mouvement est récursif et ascendant : une différence interne de perception devient hiérarchie de raisons, sélection du meilleur, harmonie universelle et pluralisation perspectivale d’un même réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:SP-05","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-07","text":"La finitude n’est pas une exclusion territoriale du tout, mais une limitation graduelle de la distinction avec laquelle chaque monade exprime intégralement l’univers.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-08","text":"La clôture ne reconduit ni l’isolement ni l’unification indifférenciée : elle produit un univers unique, maximalement ordonné, distribué dans des perspectives irréductibles et non transparentes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-11","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-09","text":"L’argument entier transforme la métaphysique en machine de conversion : tout dehors causal, toute indifférence et toute fragmentation sont reconduits vers une architecture interne de coordination, de comparaison et d’expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_18:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Toute détermination intelligible requiert une raison, une comparaison ou un ordre de fondation excluant le fait brut et l’indifférence absolue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] L’action ne désigne pas un transfert de force, mais une asymétrie variable de raison, de perfection, de réglage ou d’expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_18:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Les substances restent closes à la pénétration physique tout en étant structurellement dépendantes d’un ordre relationnel qui les excède.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] La relation réelle entre substances est une correspondance idéale : elle coordonne sans transmettre, unit sans abolir les différences et produit des effets sans contact matériel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-05","CL_UCIC_17:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] La convenance opère comme principe transversal de composition : elle articule accommodation réciproque, raison suffisante, perfection graduée, harmonie et sélection du réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] La perfection passe d’un degré local de distinction à une propriété configurationnelle de l’univers, mesurée par la compatibilité entre ordre, variété, intelligibilité et expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] L’actualité n’est pas un donné autosuffisant : elle est l’effet sélectif d’un champ de possibles différenciés par leurs raisons, leurs degrés et leur convenance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-07","CL_UCIC_18:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] L’unité du réel ne subsiste qu’en étant distribuée dans une pluralité de substances, d’expressions et de perspectives qui ne constituent pas des mondes séparés.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-08","CL_UCIC_19:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] L’individualité est une localisation expressive : chaque monade contient le rapport au tout, tandis que la différence entre monades porte sur le degré de distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] La finitude est constitutive parce que la représentation universelle ne devient jamais transparence intégrale sans abolir la distinction entre créature et divinité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-09","CL_UCIC_20:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Le réel achevé est une totalité maximalement ordonnée où la variété ne survit qu’en devenant expression réciproque et différence de perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] L’unité différenciée est l’attracteur terminal : toute pluralité valide doit accroître la structure commune sans produire une réalité extérieure, isolée ou concurrente.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-12","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-01","text":"La raison persiste comme refus du fait brut, mais mute d’un critère local d’explication entre monades en principe cosmologique de sélection des possibles et d’ordonnancement du réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_18:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-02","text":"La perfection se déplace de la clarté perceptive à la supériorité explicative, puis à la convenance d’un monde et enfin à la co-maximisation de l’ordre et de la variété.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RMD-02","CL_UCIC_20:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-03","text":"L’influence s’inverse : affirmée comme action sur autrui, elle est refusée comme communication physique et conservée comme coordination idéale, expression réciproque et dépendance réglée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_20:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-04","text":"La pluralité change de valence : d’abord problème de coordination, elle devient condition de comparaison, médium de l’expression universelle et mécanisme positif de manifestation de l’unité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_19:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-05","text":"La causalité divine accomplit son travail local de médiation, puis est absorbée dans une architecture plus large où les fonctions de connaissance, préférence, production et réglage deviennent structure de l’univers exprimé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RMD-06","CL_UCIC_19:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-06","text":"La monade cesse d’être seulement intériorité close ou miroir vivant pour devenir une perspective finie qui exprime le tout sans pouvoir l’épuiser.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_19:XD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-07","text":"La limitation disparaît comme privation d’objet et reparaît comme gradation de connaissance ; le tout est représenté partout, mais distinctement nulle part hors de la divinité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:RMD-05","CL_UCIC_20:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-01","text":"[Local] Les degrés de perception distincte expliquent localement l’activité ou la passivité d’une monade, mais ne suffisent pas seuls à déterminer l’ordre global du réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-02","text":"[Local] La triade sagesse-bonté-puissance décrit directement l’opération divine, mais elle n’acquiert sa portée supérieure qu’en devenant modèle de différenciation sans séparation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_19:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-03","text":"[Changement d’échelle] La raison a priori, la raison suffisante, la convenance et l’harmonie constituent désormais une seule grammaire de conversion de la multiplicité en ordre déterminé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:CGD-03","CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-04","text":"[Catalyseur] L’impossibilité du contact physique force le passage d’une causalité de transmission à une causalité de coordination, puis rend possible la théorie d’une unité distribuée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-05","text":"[Catalyseur] La pluralité des mondes possibles transforme une comparaison locale entre substances en logique globale de sélection, de hiérarchisation et d’actualisation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-06","text":"[Recodage] Le miroir vivant et l’analogie perspectivale cessent d’être des images locales lorsqu’ils deviennent la structure ontologique selon laquelle l’unité n’existe qu’en se distribuant.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:CGD-03","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-07","text":"[Obsolescence] Les modèles de l’agent isolé, du possible indifférent, de la substance autosuffisante et du monde externe aux perspectives deviennent incompatibles avec l’architecture courante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_19:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut la causalité matérielle brute, la force unilatérale et toute transmission qui pénétrerait directement l’intériorité d’une autre substance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_18:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut les propriétés absolues d’activité, de passivité, d’existence et de perfection, parce que chacune n’est intelligible qu’à l’intérieur d’un rapport comparatif ou hiérarchique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-01","CL_UCIC_18:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut une pluralité qui serait dispersion, juxtaposition ou fragmentation ontologique, tout comme une unité qui effacerait les différences de perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_19:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut l’actualisation arbitraire et l’idée que tous les possibles puissent être indifféremment ou simultanément réalisés.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_18:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut la transparence finie au tout : représenter l’univers ne signifie ni le connaître distinctement ni occuper une position divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut tout point de vue extérieur à l’univers, qu’il prenne la forme d’un observateur absolu, d’une totalité sans expressions ou d’une perspective sans inscription relationnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_20:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-01","text":"Pour tenir, le système doit disqualifier une ontologie d’unités causalement closes et autosuffisantes ; la clôture monadique ne peut être admise qu’avec une dépendance idéale et universelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-02","text":"Il doit refuser qu’une relation intelligible puisse être sans fondement de raison, sans comparaison de degrés ou sans ordre de convenance qui rende son effectuation justifiable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_18:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-03","text":"Il doit refuser un possible plat : les possibilités ne peuvent avoir un même statut ontologique si une actualité déterminée doit être comprise comme sélection du meilleur.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:DBN-02","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-04","text":"Il doit refuser qu’une unité soit disponible hors de ses expressions, puisque l’univers n’est pensable comme un qu’à travers la multiplicité de ses manifestations situées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:DBN-03","CL_UCIC_19:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-05","text":"Il doit refuser l’équivalence entre finitude et séparation, car une monade finie demeure interne au tout et ne diffère des autres que par son degré de distinction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_20:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-01","text":"L’impossibilité la plus profonde est celle d’un extérieur absolu : aucun agent, aucun monde, aucune cause et aucune perspective ne peut subsister hors du réseau de raisons, d’expressions et de comparaisons.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_18:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-02","text":"Le système rend ontologiquement indisponible un réel composé soit de substances entièrement séparées, soit de totalités concurrentes, soit d’une unité indifférenciée sans positions singulières.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:BSA-04","CL_UCIC_19:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-03","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une transparence créaturelle intégrale : le tout doit pouvoir être universellement présent sans devenir entièrement donné à aucune de ses expressions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_20:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-04","text":"Le système contourne un critère formel entièrement explicité de la compatibilité entre maximum de variété et maximum d’ordre, dont l’absence maintient la perfection comme attracteur plutôt que comme mesure calculée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-01","text":"La coordination intermonadique et la sélection cosmologique relèvent d’une même opération : convertir une pluralité en ordre en distribuant différentiellement raisons, degrés de perfection et rapports de convenance.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-07","CL_UCIC_18:XD-01","CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-02","text":"La causalité réglée et l’expression universelle constituent deux phases d’une même dématérialisation : l’effet réel cesse d’exiger le transfert pour devenir présence structurée du tout dans ses positions locales.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","CL_UCIC_17:XD-04","CL_UCIC_19:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-03","text":"La sélection du meilleur ne clôt pas le possible ; elle conserve les possibles non actualisés comme horizon négatif et comparatif de l’ordre qui devient actuel.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-07","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_18:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-04","text":"La différence entre les substances n’est jamais une différence de monde ou de domaine ontologique : elle est une différence de fonction explicative, de degré perceptif et de position expressive.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-09","CL_UCIC_18:MME-02","CL_UCIC_20:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-05","text":"L’unité universelle est productive seulement parce qu’elle ne se présente jamais comme totalité immédiatement possédée : sa distribution perspectivale transforme l’inaccessibilité complète en condition de la pluralité ordonnée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-10","CL_UCIC_19:XD-06","CL_UCIC_20:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-06","text":"Le refus du fait brut, de l’arbitraire et de la force matérielle entraîne une dépendance systémique envers la médiation divine ou rationnelle, dont la nécessité augmente à mesure que l’autonomie locale est affirmée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:DBN-03","CL_UCIC_18:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-01","text":"Le réel devient une hiérarchie distribuée d’intelligibilités : exister, agir, exprimer et être perçu sont des positions relatives dans une même architecture de fondation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSD-04","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-02","text":"Le sujet monadique n’est ni auteur souverain ni réceptacle passif ; il est une opération locale où l’univers devient expressif selon une clarté limitée et une fonction déterminée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_20:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-03","text":"Le temps perd son privilège de succession causale et devient subordonné à des structures logiques de sélection, de réglage originaire, de perpétuité expressive et de comparaison modale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_19:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-04","text":"L’histoire du réel est une actualisation sans abolition : le monde actuel se constitue par exclusion ordonnée de possibilités qui restent actives comme mesure de sa perfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_18:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-05","text":"La méthode métaphysique adéquate consiste à rechercher non une cause isolée, mais le niveau de relation où un phénomène devient intelligible : perception, raison, convenance, expression ou limite.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSD-06","CL_UCIC_18:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-06","text":"La divinité devient moins un étant extérieur parmi d’autres qu’une fonction architectonique de comparaison, de médiation, de sélection et de seuil entre connaissance finie et transparence intégrale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:MME-04","CL_UCIC_20:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale est : perception graduée → perfection relative → priorité explicative → coordination idéale → convenance universelle → expression perspectivale → retour de la différence comme degré de perception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_20:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-02","text":"La pluralité déclenche une exigence de raison ; la raison produit une comparaison ; la comparaison hiérarchise ; la hiérarchie actualise ; l’actualité redistribue des relations qui relancent l’exigence de raison.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-03","text":"L’escalade déterminante est : clôture physique → impossibilité du contact → médiation idéale → accommodation universelle → harmonie expressive → unité différenciée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RLE-03","CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur de convenance organise le passage entre le local et le cosmologique, car il convertit tout rapport particulier en indice d’une sélection ou d’un ajustement plus général.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-09","CL_UCIC_18:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-05","text":"L’attracteur d’unité différenciée absorbe les contradictions apparentes entre autonomie et dépendance, unité et multiplicité, représentation universelle et finitude.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-07","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-06","text":"Chaque exclusion d’un dehors causal, d’un fait brut ou d’un monde séparé fonctionne comme une réentrée : ce qui était posé extérieurement est réinscrit dans l’ordre interne de la raison et de l’expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B01","text":"Poser une pluralité de substances et de possibles dont l’existence, l’activité et le rapport ne peuvent être expliqués par une propriété absolue ou un fait brut.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_18:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B02","text":"Convertir les différences internes de perception en degrés de perfection, puis les degrés de perfection en asymétries de raison et de fonction explicative.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B03","text":"Supprimer le modèle du transfert physique tout en conservant la réalité de la dépendance par une coordination idéale réglée dès l’origine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B04","text":"Généraliser la raison locale en raison suffisante, afin que la pluralité des possibles soit convertie en sélection proportionnée par convenance et perfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B05","text":"Différencier la causalité en intelligibilité, préférence et effectuation, puis distribuer l’ordre ainsi produit dans les substances qui l’expriment.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B06","text":"Perspectiviser l’expression universelle : chaque monade représente le tout, mais la différence entre monades se concentre dans la clarté et non dans l’étendue de l’objet.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B04","CL_UCIC_20:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B07","text":"Fermer la machine par une double limite : le possible borne la perfection réalisable et la distinction intégrale demeure le seuil qui sépare la créature de la divinité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B08","text":"Produire comme résultat une totalité sans extérieur, où l’unité ne survit qu’en étant maximale dans ses relations et non transparente dans aucune de ses expressions finies.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B01","text":"Pluralité de substances et de possibles → refus du fait brut → relationalisation de l’action, de la perfection et de l’existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-01","CL_UCIC_18:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B02","text":"Relationalisation des statuts → hiérarchisation des raisons → conversion de l’action en priorité explicative et de l’existence en prétention graduée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:XD-02","CL_UCIC_18:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B03","text":"Clôture physique des monades → impossibilité de l’influence directe → médiation divine, correspondance idéale et dépendance non physique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B03","CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B04","text":"Raison suffisante et convenance → sélection du meilleur → actualisation d’un ordre qui conserve les possibles exclus comme horizon comparatif.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B05","text":"Causalité différenciée → expression universelle → substances comme perspectives situées → pluralité reclassée comme différenciation d’un seul réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B03","CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B06","text":"Unité différenciée → variété et ordre maximaux → totalité interne non transparente → clôture par la limite du possible et le seuil divin.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-01","text":"L’opposition entre causalité et intelligibilité s’effondre : agir signifie ultimement occuper une fonction de fondation dans un ordre de raisons et de correspondances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MME-03","CL_UCIC_17:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-02","text":"L’opposition entre autonomie et dépendance est reclassée : l’autonomie concerne la clôture de l’intériorité, la dépendance concerne l’inscription de cette intériorité dans l’ordre universel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-03","text":"L’opposition possible/actuel devient une cartographie de prétentions graduées, de comparaisons et d’exclusions productives plutôt qu’une séparation entre irréel et réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:MME-01","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-04","text":"L’opposition unité/multiplicité est remplacée par la distinction entre référent commun, expressions distribuées et perspectives graduées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:MME-04","CL_UCIC_19:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-05","text":"La finitude est reclassée comme différence de résolution épistémique et non comme confinement d’une substance dans un fragment indépendant du réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:MME-03","CL_UCIC_20:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-06","text":"La lecture adéquate devient topologique : elle doit suivre les changements de niveau par lesquels un même terme passe de perception à raison, de causalité à expression et d’expression à perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MME-05","CL_UCIC_19:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont l’action, la passion, la causalité divine, les mondes possibles, l’harmonie, les monades et leurs perspectives sur l’univers.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont organisés par des asymétries de raison, des comparaisons de perfection, des coordinations idéales et une distribution expressive de la totalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] L’analyse substitue aux questions d’identité, de force et d’agent premier la recherche des rapports qui rendent une détermination, une sélection ou une expression intelligible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:MME-05","CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est une unité relationnelle produite par sélection logique, réglage originaire et expression perpétuelle, tandis que le temps empirique cesse d’être le support exclusif de la causalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_19:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit la machine qu’elle décrit : elle retire successivement force brute, isolement et extériorité, puis reconstruit leur fonction sous forme de relations médiatisées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-01","text":"L’architecture affirme une dépendance réelle entre monades tout en refusant tout mécanisme de transmission ; la correspondance idéale résout fonctionnellement la difficulté sans déterminer pleinement son opérativité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:FL-03","CL_UCIC_17:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-02","text":"La sélection du meilleur est déterminée par la raison suffisante, mais la teneur précise des raisons, de la comparaison et de la mesure de perfection demeure indéterminée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:FL-02","CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-03","text":"L’unité universelle exige que chaque substance exprime le tout, mais le mécanisme exact de cette expression oscille entre description ontologique et métaphore de représentation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:FL-03","CL_UCIC_19:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-04","text":"La compatibilité entre maximum de variété et maximum d’ordre est constitutive du système, mais elle reste davantage postulée que démontrée par un critère formel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FL-01","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-05","text":"L’universalité de la représentation et la limitation de la connaissance sont simultanément nécessaires ; leur tension soutient le système mais interdit une théorie pleinement univoque de l’accès au tout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FL-03","CL_UCIC_19:XD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-01","text":"La première mutation décisive survient lorsque la perfection cesse d’être une qualité perceptive interne et devient capacité de rendre raison d’un événement attribué à autrui.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MP-01","CL_UCIC_17:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-02","text":"La deuxième mutation survient lorsque l’impossibilité de la causalité physique ne détruit pas l’influence, mais oblige à la recoder comme coordination idéale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MP-03","CL_UCIC_17:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-03","text":"La troisième mutation survient lorsque la comparaison entre substances devient comparaison entre mondes, faisant de la raison un opérateur de sélection ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_18:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-04","text":"La quatrième mutation survient lorsque la production divine devient expression universelle et que l’expression devient perspective, transformant la substance en position locale du tout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_19:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-05","text":"La mutation terminale survient lorsque la limite cesse de borner l’objet représenté et devient une modulation de clarté qui protège la différence entre créature et divinité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:RMD-05","CL_UCIC_20:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de correspondances comparatives : elle produit l’ordre en répartissant raisons, degrés, expressions et perspectives sans jamais permettre leur séparation absolue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_18:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet est une chambre expressive sans dehors : causalement close, relationnellement déterminée, universellement orientée et finiment distincte.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_20:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est secondaire par rapport à une logique de préconfiguration, de sélection et de perpétuité expressive ; il est l’effet local d’un ordre modal plus profond.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_20:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-04","text":"La seule navigation possible ne consiste pas à sortir du système, mais à modifier une position de clarté, d’intelligibilité ou d’expression à l’intérieur de la totalité commune.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:HSI-04","CL_UCIC_20:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-05","text":"La divinité est l’opérateur-limite de la machine : elle rend pensable l’unité réglée, l’actualisation sélective et la distinction intégrale sans devenir une simple substance plus puissante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:MME-04","CL_UCIC_20:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale exige de conserver la raison anti-brute, la clôture physique, la coordination idéale, la sélection comparative, l’expression universelle et la finitude graduelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B02","text":"Ces opérateurs suffisent à reconstruire le mouvement supérieur parce qu’ils engendrent la chaîne complète : dépendance sans transfert, actualité sans arbitraire, unité sans homogénéité et pluralité sans fragmentation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B02","CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B03","text":"La compression demeure fidèle si elle maintient les mutations irréductibles entre perception, raison, convenance, production, expression et perspective, sans les réduire à des synonymes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B02","CL_UCIC_19:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination restante porte sur le mécanisme de l’expression universelle, la mesure de la perfection, le contenu des raisons suffisantes et la compatibilité démontrée des maxima d’ordre et de variété.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B05","text":"La cohérence dépend d’un retour récursif plutôt que d’un séquençage linéaire : chaque niveau reformule la même question, à savoir comment maintenir une relation réelle sans admettre ni séparation absolue ni transmission physique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_17:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B06","text":"Toute réduction qui réintroduirait une force matérielle autonome, un choix arbitraire, une pluralité de mondes séparés ou une transparence finie au tout détruirait l’architecture extraite.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B07","text":"La force du système réside dans sa capacité à faire de chaque limite une opération structurante, mais sa faille persistante réside dans l’absence de formalisation complète de la mesure, de la médiation et de l’expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200551219544Z_3d0cc6b3","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L1 05","source_sha256":"91ae17a7ea8c71cb293f613fd81c4f0ef6a92ceeeda9cb6bf46a9c308dac17eb","sha256":"653e4064efd4ecd51f338adeca93cb312362b16277f9c314b26ed220d4deb1b6","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:05:51.223812+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-01","text":"The central problem is to render thinkable real plurality, dependence among substances, and the unity of the world without admitting either material transfer, brute fact, or absolute exteriority.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:SP-01","CL_UCIC_20:SP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-02","text":"The system reframes every determination as a relation of reason, fittingness, expression, or degree rather than as an isolated property, homogeneous force, or mere succession of states.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:AS-B02","CL_UCIC_17:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-03","text":"Created action is progressively dematerialized: it first becomes explanatory priority, then regulated correspondence, then local expression of a universal order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:XD-01","CL_UCIC_19:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-04","text":"Plurality ceases to be the opposite of unity when it is redistributed as a multiplicity of reasons, possibilities, expressive substances, and graded perspectives.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:RMD-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-05","text":"Divine causality provides the matrix of all intelligibility: knowing differentiates possibilities, preferring hierarchizes them, producing or regulating inscribes them in an actual and expressive order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:AS-02","CL_UCIC_19:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-06","text":"The movement is recursive and ascending: an internal difference of perception becomes a hierarchy of reasons, selection of the best, universal harmony, and perspectival pluralization of one and the same reality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:SP-05","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-07","text":"Finitude is not a territorial exclusion from the whole, but a gradual limitation of the distinctness with which each monad fully expresses the universe.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-06","CL_UCIC_20:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-08","text":"Closure restores neither isolation nor undifferentiated unification: it produces a single, maximally ordered universe, distributed across irreducible and non-transparent perspectives.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-11","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ABS-09","text":"The entire argument transforms metaphysics into a conversion machine: every causal outside, every indifference, and every fragmentation are redirected toward an internal architecture of coordination, comparison, and expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_18:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Every intelligible determination requires a reason, a comparison, or an order of grounding excluding brute fact and absolute indifference.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Action does not designate a transfer of force, but a variable asymmetry of reason, perfection, regulation, or expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_18:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Substances remain closed to physical penetration while being structurally dependent on a relational order that exceeds them.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The real relation among substances is an ideal correspondence: it coordinates without transmitting, unites without abolishing differences, and produces effects without material contact.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-05","CL_UCIC_17:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-05","text":"[Attractor] Fittingness operates as a transversal principle of composition: it articulates reciprocal accommodation, sufficient reason, graded perfection, harmony, and selection of the real.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Perfection shifts from a local degree of distinctness to a configurational property of the universe, measured by compatibility among order, variety, intelligibility, and expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-02","CL_UCIC_20:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] Actuality is not a self-sufficient given: it is the selective effect of a field of possibilities differentiated by their reasons, degrees, and fittingness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-07","CL_UCIC_18:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] The unity of the real subsists only by being distributed across a plurality of substances, expressions, and perspectives that do not constitute separate worlds.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-08","CL_UCIC_19:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Individuality is an expressive localization: each monad contains the relation to the whole, while the difference among monads concerns the degree of distinctness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-10","text":"[Terminal] Finitude is constitutive because universal representation never becomes integral transparency without abolishing the distinction between creature and divinity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-09","CL_UCIC_20:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Accomplished reality is a maximally ordered totality in which variety survives only by becoming reciprocal expression and difference of perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GA-01","CL_UCIC_20:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Differentiated unity is the terminal attractor: every valid plurality must increase the common structure without producing an external, isolated, or competing reality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:GA-12","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-01","text":"Reason persists as a refusal of brute fact, but mutates from a local criterion of explanation among monads into a cosmological principle for selecting possibilities and ordering the real.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-03","CL_UCIC_18:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-02","text":"Perfection shifts from perceptual clarity to explanatory superiority, then to the fittingness of a world and finally to the co-maximization of order and variety.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RMD-02","CL_UCIC_20:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-03","text":"Influence is inverted: affirmed as action upon another, it is rejected as physical communication and retained as ideal coordination, reciprocal expression, and regulated dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_20:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-04","text":"Plurality changes valence: initially a problem of coordination, it becomes a condition of comparison, a medium of universal expression, and a positive mechanism for the manifestation of unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_19:RMD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-05","text":"Divine causality completes its local work of mediation, then is absorbed into a broader architecture in which the functions of knowledge, preference, production, and regulation become the structure of the expressed universe.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RMD-06","CL_UCIC_19:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-06","text":"The monad ceases to be merely closed interiority or a living mirror in order to become a finite perspective that expresses the whole without being able to exhaust it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_19:XD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RMD-07","text":"Limitation disappears as deprivation of an object and reappears as gradation of knowledge; the whole is represented everywhere, but distinctly nowhere outside divinity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:RMD-05","CL_UCIC_20:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-01","text":"[Local] Degrees of distinct perception explain locally the activity or passivity of a monad, but do not alone suffice to determine the global order of the real.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_20:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-02","text":"[Local] The wisdom-goodness-power triad directly describes divine operation, but acquires its higher scope only by becoming a model of differentiation without separation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_19:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-03","text":"[Change of scale] A priori reason, sufficient reason, fittingness, and harmony henceforth constitute a single grammar for converting multiplicity into determined order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:CGD-03","CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-04","text":"[Catalyst] The impossibility of physical contact compels the shift from a causality of transmission to a causality of coordination, then makes possible the theory of a distributed unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-05","text":"[Catalyst] The plurality of possible worlds transforms a local comparison among substances into a global logic of selection, hierarchization, and actualization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-06","text":"[Recoding] The living mirror and perspectival analogy cease to be local images when they become the ontological structure according to which unity exists only by distributing itself.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:CGD-03","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:CGD-07","text":"[Obsolescence] The models of the isolated agent, indifferent possibility, self-sufficient substance, and world external to perspectives become incompatible with the current architecture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_19:CGD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes brute material causality, unilateral force, and every transmission that would directly penetrate the interiority of another substance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_18:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-02","text":"It excludes absolute properties of activity, passivity, existence, and perfection, because each is intelligible only within a comparative or hierarchical relation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-01","CL_UCIC_18:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-03","text":"It excludes a plurality that would be dispersion, juxtaposition, or ontological fragmentation, as well as a unity that would erase differences of perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_19:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-04","text":"It excludes arbitrary actualization and the idea that all possibilities could be realized indifferently or simultaneously.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_18:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-05","text":"It excludes finite transparency to the whole: representing the universe means neither knowing it distinctly nor occupying a divine position.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:GNX-06","text":"It excludes every point of view external to the universe, whether it takes the form of an absolute observer, a totality without expressions, or a perspective without relational inscription.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_20:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-01","text":"To hold together, the system must disqualify an ontology of causally closed and self-sufficient units; monadic closure can be admitted only together with an ideal and universal dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-02","text":"It must reject the possibility that an intelligible relation could lack a ground of reason, a comparison of degrees, or an order of fittingness that makes its realization justifiable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_18:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-03","text":"It must reject a flat possible: possibilities cannot have the same ontological status if a determinate actuality must be understood as selection of the best.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:DBN-02","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-04","text":"It must reject the idea that unity is available apart from its expressions, since the universe is thinkable as one only through the multiplicity of its situated manifestations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:DBN-03","CL_UCIC_19:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:DBN-05","text":"It must reject the equivalence between finitude and separation, for a finite monad remains internal to the whole and differs from others only by its degree of distinctness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_20:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-01","text":"The deepest impossibility is that of an absolute outside: no agent, world, cause, or perspective can subsist outside the network of reasons, expressions, and comparisons.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_18:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-02","text":"The system renders ontologically unavailable a reality composed either of entirely separate substances, competing totalities, or an undifferentiated unity without singular positions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:BSA-04","CL_UCIC_19:GNX-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-03","text":"The structuring absence is that of integral creaturely transparency: the whole must be able to be universally present without becoming entirely given to any of its expressions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_20:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSA-04","text":"The system bypasses a fully explicated formal criterion of compatibility between maximum variety and maximum order, whose absence maintains perfection as an attractor rather than as a calculated measure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-01","text":"Intermonadic coordination and cosmological selection belong to one and the same operation: converting a plurality into order by differentially distributing reasons, degrees of perfection, and relations of fittingness.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-07","CL_UCIC_18:XD-01","CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-02","text":"Regulated causality and universal expression constitute two phases of the same dematerialization: real effect ceases to require transfer in order to become the structured presence of the whole in its local positions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","CL_UCIC_17:XD-04","CL_UCIC_19:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-03","text":"Selection of the best does not close off the possible; it preserves unactualized possibilities as the negative and comparative horizon of the order that becomes actual.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-07","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_18:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-04","text":"The difference among substances is never a difference of world or ontological domain: it is a difference of explanatory function, perceptual degree, and expressive position.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-09","CL_UCIC_18:MME-02","CL_UCIC_20:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-05","text":"Universal unity is productive only because it never presents itself as an immediately possessed totality: its perspectival distribution transforms complete inaccessibility into a condition of ordered plurality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-10","CL_UCIC_19:XD-06","CL_UCIC_20:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:XD-06","text":"The refusal of brute fact, arbitrariness, and material force entails a systemic dependence on divine or rational mediation, whose necessity increases as local autonomy is affirmed.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_05:GA-04","CL_UCIC_17:DBN-03","CL_UCIC_18:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-01","text":"The real becomes a distributed hierarchy of intelligibilities: existing, acting, expressing, and being perceived are relative positions within the same architecture of grounding.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSD-04","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-02","text":"The monadic subject is neither sovereign author nor passive receptacle; it is a local operation in which the universe becomes expressive according to a limited clarity and a determinate function.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_20:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-03","text":"Time loses its privilege as causal succession and becomes subordinate to logical structures of selection, original regulation, expressive perpetuity, and modal comparison.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_19:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-04","text":"The history of the real is an actualization without abolition: the actual world is constituted through the ordered exclusion of possibilities that remain active as the measure of its perfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_18:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-05","text":"The adequate metaphysical method consists in seeking not an isolated cause, but the level of relation at which a phenomenon becomes intelligible: perception, reason, fittingness, expression, or limit.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSD-06","CL_UCIC_18:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:BSD-06","text":"Divinity becomes less an external being among others than an architectonic function of comparison, mediation, selection, and threshold between finite knowledge and integral transparency.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:MME-04","CL_UCIC_20:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop is: graded perception → relative perfection → explanatory priority → ideal coordination → universal fittingness → perspectival expression → return of difference as degree of perception.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_20:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-02","text":"Plurality triggers a demand for reason; reason produces comparison; comparison hierarchizes; hierarchy actualizes; actuality redistributes relations that renew the demand for reason.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-03","text":"The determining escalation is: physical closure → impossibility of contact → ideal mediation → universal accommodation → expressive harmony → differentiated unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RLE-03","CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-04","text":"The attractor of fittingness organizes the passage between the local and the cosmological, because it converts every particular relation into an index of a more general selection or adjustment.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-09","CL_UCIC_18:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-05","text":"The attractor of differentiated unity absorbs the apparent contradictions between autonomy and dependence, unity and multiplicity, universal representation and finitude.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:GA-07","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:RLE-06","text":"Each exclusion of a causal outside, a brute fact, or a separate world functions as a re-entry: what was posited externally is reinscribed in the internal order of reason and expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_19:RLE-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B01","text":"Posit a plurality of substances and possibilities whose existence, activity, and relation cannot be explained by an absolute property or brute fact.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_18:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B02","text":"Convert internal differences of perception into degrees of perfection, then degrees of perfection into asymmetries of reason and explanatory function.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B03","text":"Eliminate the model of physical transfer while preserving the reality of dependence through an ideal coordination regulated from the outset.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_17:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B04","text":"Generalize local reason into sufficient reason, so that the plurality of possibilities is converted into selection proportioned by fittingness and perfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_18:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B05","text":"Differentiate causality into intelligibility, preference, and realization, then distribute the order thus produced among the substances that express it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_19:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B06","text":"Perspectivize universal expression: each monad represents the whole, but the difference among monads is concentrated in clarity and not in the extent of the object.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B04","CL_UCIC_20:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B07","text":"Close the machine through a double limit: the possible bounds realizable perfection and integral distinctness remains the threshold separating creature from divinity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_20:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FGS-B08","text":"Produce as a result a totality without outside, in which unity survives only by being maximal in its relations and non-transparent in any of its finite expressions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B07","CL_UCIC_20:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B01","text":"Plurality of substances and possibilities → refusal of brute fact → relationalization of action, perfection, and existence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:GA-01","CL_UCIC_18:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B02","text":"Relationalization of statuses → hierarchization of reasons → conversion of action into explanatory priority and of existence into graded claim.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:XD-02","CL_UCIC_18:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B03","text":"Physical closure of monads → impossibility of direct influence → divine mediation, ideal correspondence, and non-physical dependence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B03","CL_UCIC_17:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B04","text":"Sufficient reason and fittingness → selection of the best → actualization of an order that preserves excluded possibilities as a comparative horizon.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B05","text":"Differentiated causality → universal expression → substances as situated perspectives → plurality reclassified as differentiation of one reality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B03","CL_UCIC_19:AFM-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:AFM-B06","text":"Differentiated unity → maximal variety and order → non-transparent internal totality → closure through the limit of the possible and the divine threshold.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_20:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-01","text":"The opposition between causality and intelligibility collapses: to act ultimately means to occupy a grounding function within an order of reasons and correspondences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MME-03","CL_UCIC_17:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-02","text":"The opposition between autonomy and dependence is reclassified: autonomy concerns the closure of interiority; dependence concerns the inscription of that interiority in the universal order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_17:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-03","text":"The possible/actual opposition becomes a mapping of graded claims, comparisons, and productive exclusions rather than a separation between unreal and real.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:MME-01","CL_UCIC_18:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-04","text":"The unity/multiplicity opposition is replaced by the distinction among common referent, distributed expressions, and graded perspectives.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:MME-04","CL_UCIC_19:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-05","text":"Finitude is reclassified as a difference of epistemic resolution and not as the confinement of a substance within an independent fragment of the real.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:MME-03","CL_UCIC_20:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MME-06","text":"Adequate reading becomes topological: it must follow the changes of level through which a single term passes from perception to reason, from causality to expression, and from expression to perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MME-05","CL_UCIC_19:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are action, passion, divine causality, possible worlds, harmony, monads, and their perspectives on the universe.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are organized by asymmetries of reason, comparisons of perfection, ideal coordinations, and an expressive distribution of totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_19:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The analysis replaces questions of identity, force, and first agent with the search for relations that render a determination, selection, or expression intelligible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:MME-05","CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The real is a relational unity produced through logical selection, original regulation, and perpetual expression, while empirical time ceases to be the exclusive support of causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_19:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form performs the machine it describes: it successively removes brute force, isolation, and exteriority, then reconstructs their function in the form of mediated relations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_18:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-01","text":"The architecture affirms a real dependence among monads while refusing every mechanism of transmission; ideal correspondence functionally resolves the difficulty without fully determining its operativity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:FL-03","CL_UCIC_17:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-02","text":"Selection of the best is determined by sufficient reason, but the precise content of reasons, comparison, and the measure of perfection remains indeterminate.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:FL-02","CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-03","text":"Universal unity requires each substance to express the whole, but the exact mechanism of this expression oscillates between ontological description and a metaphor of representation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:FL-03","CL_UCIC_19:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-04","text":"Compatibility between maximum variety and maximum order is constitutive of the system, but remains more postulated than demonstrated by a formal criterion.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FL-01","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:FL-05","text":"The universality of representation and the limitation of knowledge are simultaneously necessary; their tension sustains the system but prevents a fully univocal theory of access to the whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:FL-03","CL_UCIC_19:XD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-01","text":"The first decisive mutation occurs when perfection ceases to be an internal perceptual quality and becomes the capacity to give a reason for an event attributed to another.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MP-01","CL_UCIC_17:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-02","text":"The second mutation occurs when the impossibility of physical causality does not destroy influence, but compels its recoding as ideal coordination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MP-03","CL_UCIC_17:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-03","text":"The third mutation occurs when comparison among substances becomes comparison among worlds, making reason an operator of ontological selection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_18:CGD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-04","text":"The fourth mutation occurs when divine production becomes universal expression and expression becomes perspective, transforming substance into a local position of the whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_19:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MP-05","text":"The terminal mutation occurs when the limit ceases to bound the represented object and becomes a modulation of clarity that protects the difference between creature and divinity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:RMD-05","CL_UCIC_20:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-01","text":"Implicit reality is a machine of comparative correspondences: it produces order by distributing reasons, degrees, expressions, and perspectives without ever allowing their absolute separation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_18:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-02","text":"The subject is an expressive chamber without outside: causally closed, relationally determined, universally oriented, and finitely distinct.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_20:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-03","text":"Time is secondary relative to a logic of preconfiguration, selection, and expressive perpetuity; it is the local effect of a deeper modal order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_20:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-04","text":"The only possible navigation does not consist in leaving the system, but in modifying a position of clarity, intelligibility, or expression within the common totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:HSI-04","CL_UCIC_20:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:HSI-05","text":"Divinity is the limit-operator of the machine: it renders thinkable regulated unity, selective actualization, and integral distinctness without becoming merely a more powerful substance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_18:MME-04","CL_UCIC_20:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B01","text":"Minimal reconstruction requires retaining anti-brute reason, physical closure, ideal coordination, comparative selection, universal expression, and gradual finitude.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B02","text":"These operators suffice to reconstruct the higher movement because they generate the complete chain: dependence without transfer, actuality without arbitrariness, unity without homogeneity, and plurality without fragmentation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B02","CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B03","text":"Compression remains faithful if it preserves the irreducible mutations among perception, reason, fittingness, production, expression, and perspective, without reducing them to synonyms.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B02","CL_UCIC_19:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B04","text":"The remaining indeterminacy concerns the mechanism of universal expression, the measure of perfection, the content of sufficient reasons, and the demonstrated compatibility of the maxima of order and variety.","refs":["CL_UCIC_19:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B05","text":"Coherence depends on recursive return rather than linear sequencing: each level reformulates the same question, namely how to maintain a real relation without admitting either absolute separation or physical transmission.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_17:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B06","text":"Any reduction that reintroduced an autonomous material force, an arbitrary choice, a plurality of separate worlds, or finite transparency to the whole would destroy the extracted architecture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_17:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_18:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_05:MRT-B07","text":"The strength of the system lies in its capacity to make every limit a structuring operation, but its persistent flaw lies in the absence of a complete formalization of measure, mediation, and expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_20:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_20:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_05@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L1_05:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L1 05","context":"Chapters 49–60 · Proposition 49 · Proposition 50 · Proposition 51 · Proposition 52 · Proposition 53 · Proposition 54 · Proposition 55 · Proposition 56 · Proposition 57 · Proposition 58 · Proposition 59 · Proposition 60"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L1 06","order":6,"parents":["CL_UCIC_21","CL_UCIC_22","CL_UCIC_23","CL_UCIC_24"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_06@R001","sha256":"c3c8801a8319dc83666ebb29c2118a8d479dd416b7f98195ec4db9e463a6374a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B01","text":"Le problème directeur consiste à penser une totalité universellement présente dans chaque réalité sans abolir la différence des corps, des parties, des vivants et des perspectives.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B02","text":"Le système remplace la matière homogène et passive par une plénitude organisée dont toute portion demeure active, composée et intérieurement différenciée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-01","CL_UCIC_23:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B03","text":"La récursion matérielle convertit la division en approfondissement : descendre vers la partie ne découvre pas un élément simple, mais une nouvelle totalité organisée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-03","CL_UCIC_23:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B04","text":"Le corps propre et l’organisme deviennent les foyers où l’expression universelle se concentre, se différencie et se stabilise provisoirement comme forme vivante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-09","CL_UCIC_24:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B05","text":"La perception finie ne révèle pas l’absence d’ordre ; elle compresse une multiplicité réelle en apparences de confusion, de vide, de distance ou de chaos.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","CL_UCIC_23:AS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B06","text":"Le flux matériel interdit de fonder l’identité sur des composants conservés et déplace la persistance vers la continuité graduelle d’une organisation incorporée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:AS-03","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B07","text":"L’argument est récursif, cumulatif et stratifié : causalité, machinicité, composition, perception, organicité et métamorphose sont autant de régimes d’une même expressivité distribuée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:AS-07","CL_UCIC_23:AS-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B08","text":"La clôture ne livre aucun fond matériel, perceptif ou organique ultime : elle établit une totalité sans dehors, finiment exprimée, continuellement transformée et jamais distinctement épuisée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-08","CL_UCIC_21:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Le réel forme une continuité pleine où aucune entité corporelle, aucun milieu et aucune partie ne peuvent être définis comme extérieurement séparés du tout qu’ils expriment.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-01","CL_UCIC_23:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Toute portion matérielle est une organisation active dont les parties reconduisent, à des échelles distinctes, une capacité de composition et d’expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-01","CL_UCIC_23:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La partie cesse d’être un résidu subordonné : elle devient successivement machine, monde interne, vivant relatif, foyer causal et totalité organisationnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] L’expression universelle n’implique jamais une identité indifférenciée entre tout et partie, mais une présence distribuée selon des degrés de distinction, de fonction et de perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-03","CL_UCIC_22:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Le corps vivant est l’opérateur de conversion entre totalité cosmique, ordre représentatif, organisation matérielle et continuité identitaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CL_UCIC_24:AS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] L’identité ne repose ni sur une matière fixe ni sur une âme détachée, mais sur la persistance graduelle d’une organisation qui traverse le renouvellement de ses supports.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-04","CL_UCIC_24:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] L’imperceptible, l’indistinct et le confus désignent des limites de résolution plutôt que des preuves d’absence, d’inertie ou de désordre réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-05","CL_UCIC_23:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] L’analyse ne peut atteindre ni matière simple, ni région vide, ni vivant purement inerte, ni âme créée absolument séparée de toute corporéité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-08","CL_UCIC_24:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] La réalité converge vers l’image d’une plénitude récursive : chaque niveau est simultanément composé, organisateur, exprimant et intégré dans une totalité plus vaste.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-09","CL_UCIC_24:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Toute négation de simplicité, de vide, de chaos ou de fixité se convertit en proposition positive de densification organisationnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MP-04","CL_UCIC_23:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-01","text":"La récursivité conserve son identité fonctionnelle lorsqu’elle passe de la machine naturelle à la portion matérielle, puis au vivant hiérarchisé : elle répète l’organisation sans répéter une unité identique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RMD-02","CL_UCIC_24:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-02","text":"Le corps mute d’objet causalement affecté en médiateur représentatif, puis en processus organique dont l’identité persiste à travers le flux de matière.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_24:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-03","text":"L’infini se déplace de la continuité de la composition vers l’impossibilité d’un terme terminal, puis devient le principe d’escalade par lequel toute réduction relance l’organisation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RMD-03","CL_UCIC_22:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-04","text":"La perception se renverse : elle n’est plus l’instance qui décide de la structure réelle, mais le lieu où la richesse du réel apparaît sous forme de compression et d’opacité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_23:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-01","text":"Les exemples locaux de machines, jardins, étangs, membres vivants ou transformations animales sont absorbés dans une loi de récursivité organisationnelle transversale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_23:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-02","text":"La distinction locale entre nature et art devient, au niveau courant, une distinction entre organisation interrompue et organisation récursivement continuée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_22:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-03","text":"La limitation perceptive change d’échelle lorsqu’elle relie l’emboîtement matériel, la contenance des milieux et l’apparence de chaos en une même théorie de la résolution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_23:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-04","text":"Le flux corporel, d’abord problème local de renouvellement, devient le catalyseur qui oblige à reformuler l’identité comme continuité organisationnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:CGD-03","CL_UCIC_24:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-05","text":"Les modèles de matière fixe, de partie inerte, de vide séparateur et de sujet désincarné deviennent obsolètes parce qu’ils interrompent artificiellement les médiations que le système généralise.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:CGD-06","CL_UCIC_23:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut une matière composée d’unités ultimes, homogènes, muettes ou dépourvues d’intériorité organisationnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_23:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut tout vide ontologique : les milieux peuvent différer de leurs contenus, mais cette différence ne constitue jamais une absence réelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-04","CL_UCIC_23:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut que l’indistinction sensible puisse valoir comme critère de l’indifférenciation ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:DBN-05","CL_UCIC_23:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut l’identité fondée sur la possession durable d’une matière assignée et la séparation de l’âme créée hors de toute corporéité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GNX-02","CL_UCIC_24:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut une opposition stable entre mécanisme et vie, puisque la machinicité devient la continuité interne de l’organisation vivante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:DBN-03","CL_UCIC_22:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, doit être faux tout modèle où l’organisation apparaît seulement au niveau du tout et s’évanouit dans les parties.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GNX-06","CL_UCIC_23:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:DBN-02","text":"Doit être faux tout modèle où la séparation spatiale, la distance ou l’imperceptibilité suffisent à produire une séparation ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_23:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:DBN-03","text":"Doit être faux tout dualisme qui ferait de l’âme une substance mobile et du corps une enveloppe contingente ou remplaçable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:DBN-03","CL_UCIC_24:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-01","text":"L’impossibilité la plus profonde est celle d’un dehors absolu où l’expression, l’organisation, la vie et la relation au tout cesseraient simultanément.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_21:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité indisponible est celle d’un observateur fini capable de convertir sans reste la présence universelle en connaissance distincte du tout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_23:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-03","text":"L’architecture ne peut admettre une créature finie totalement désincarnée, parce que l’incorporation est la condition de toute perspective, de toute organisation et de toute continuité créée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","CL_UCIC_24:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-01","text":"La plénitude matérielle et la récursion machinique impliquent que la causalité ne traverse pas des unités closes, mais se distribue dans des organisations déjà intérieurement relationnelles.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-04","CL_UCIC_21:GA-01","CL_UCIC_22:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-02","text":"La limite perceptive et la représentation universelle sont compatibles parce que la présence du tout excède sa disponibilité sous forme distincte pour une perspective finie.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-07","CL_UCIC_21:XD-03","CL_UCIC_23:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-03","text":"L’organisme constitue le point où la récursivité de la matière devient continuité d’identité : l’emboîtement ne produit pas la dispersion parce qu’une organisation dominante règle les transformations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:XD-06","CL_UCIC_24:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-04","text":"L’exclusion simultanée du simple, du vide, du chaos et de la fixité transforme les limites négatives du système en preuve cumulative d’une organisation sans dehors.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-10","CL_UCIC_23:XD-06","CL_UCIC_22:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-01","text":"Le réel est requalifié comme une topologie de totalités imbriquées où les frontières désignent des changements de niveau, de fonction ou de résolution plutôt que des séparations absolues.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:BSD-01","CL_UCIC_24:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-02","text":"Le sujet n’est ni un réceptacle isolé ni un principe désincarné : il est une focalisation organique finie, traversée par une totalité qu’il exprime sans l’expliciter entièrement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_24:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-03","text":"Le temps cesse d’être la succession de substances conservées ou remplacées ; il devient le régime de transformation graduelle par lequel l’organisation persiste dans le flux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:BSD-04","CL_UCIC_21:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-04","text":"La méthode pertinente consiste à suivre les correspondances, emboîtements et seuils de distinction plutôt qu’à rechercher des composants simples ou des perceptions immédiatement adéquates.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MME-06","CL_UCIC_24:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-01","text":"La boucle principale est : plénitude matérielle → subdivision organisée → activité interne → expression du tout → nouvelle qualification de la partie comme monde.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_21:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-02","text":"Une seconde boucle est : multiplicité vivante → flux matériel → impossibilité de propriété fixe → continuité organisationnelle → persistance de l’unité dans la métamorphose.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_24:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-03","text":"L’attracteur commun est une totalité distribuée dont chaque focalisation locale confirme à la fois l’unité du tout et l’irréductibilité de ses différenciations internes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RLE-04","CL_UCIC_21:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-04","text":"Toute tentative de réduire le réel relance le système à un niveau plus profond : la réduction devient le mécanisme même de l’escalade ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_22:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B01","text":"Poser une matière pleine, active et sans région ontologiquement vide.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B02","text":"Soumettre chaque portion à une récursion de composition qui interdit qu’elle devienne un élément matériel simple.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-02","CL_UCIC_23:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B03","text":"Convertir cette composition en expressivité différenciée : chaque partie porte le tout sans devenir identique à lui.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","CL_UCIC_21:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B04","text":"Concentrer l’expression dans des foyers corporels où l’ordre cosmique devient perception, organicité et vie hiérarchisée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CL_UCIC_24:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B05","text":"Introduire le flux des parties pour déplacer l’identité de la conservation matérielle vers la continuité graduelle de l’organisation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-05","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B06","text":"Requalifier les apparences de vide, de chaos, de rupture ou de simplicité comme effets de résolution insuffisante, de fixation abstraite ou de réduction inachevée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:XD-04","CL_UCIC_22:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AFM-B01","text":"Plénitude matérielle → composition récursive → activité interne des parties → expression universelle différenciée → focalisation corporelle → organisation du vivant.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AFM-B02","text":"Organisation vivante → pluralité de vivants subordonnés → flux matériel → continuité graduelle → identité processuelle incorporée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_24:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AFM-B03","text":"Imperceptibilité et confusion → diagnostic de compression perceptive → restitution d’une plénitude organisée → exclusion du vide, du chaos et du simple.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_23:XD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-01","text":"La matière est reclassée comme profondeur organisationnelle plutôt que comme étendue homogène, support brut ou réserve de composants fixes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MME-02","CL_UCIC_24:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-02","text":"La distinction entre partie et totalité s’effondre comme opposition rigide et devient une différence de niveau dans une architecture d’emboîtement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MME-06","CL_UCIC_24:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-03","text":"L’espace et la perception cessent de servir de tribunaux ontologiques : la distance, le milieu et l’indistinction sont reclassés comme médiations et seuils.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:MME-02","CL_UCIC_23:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-04","text":"La lecture adéquate doit cartographier les conversions entre causalité, représentation, composition, organisation et temporalité plutôt que classer des substances isolées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MME-06","CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Les objets explicites sont les corps, machines, parties matérielles, milieux, vivants, âmes, organes et transformations corporelles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ces objets sont régis par une même architecture d’emboîtement récursif, de continuité matérielle, de médiation corporelle et de flux organisationnel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Le système remplace l’analyse des unités isolées par le suivi des relations qui font d’une limite apparente une médiation, d’une partie une totalité et d’une mutation une persistance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B03","CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Le réel est continu, plein, dynamique et sans terme matériel final ; le temps y produit des transformations graduelles plutôt que des séparations absolues.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_24:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forme argumentative accomplit sa thèse en répétant le geste qui descend dans les parties, découvre davantage d’organisation et transforme chaque négation en reconstruction positive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FL-01","text":"La totalité est dite présente dans chaque réalité, mais cette présence demeure incompatible avec toute explicitation finie intégrale ; la tension entre expression et lisibilité est constitutive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:FL-01","CL_UCIC_21:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FL-02","text":"L’organisation est affirmée comme principe de persistance, mais le critère précis qui distingue une métamorphose continue d’une rupture de sujet reste partiellement sous-déterminé.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:FL-02","CL_UCIC_24:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FL-03","text":"La généralisation de la récursivité à toute matière est structurellement décisive, mais son passage de modèles locaux à une loi universelle n’est pas entièrement explicité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:FL-02","CL_UCIC_22:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MP-01","text":"Le premier point de mutation survient lorsque la causalité et la composition cessent d’être extérieures aux corps et deviennent des inscriptions expressives internes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MP-01","CL_UCIC_22:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MP-02","text":"Le second point de mutation survient lorsque la partie cesse d’être composant et devient totalité relative, monde interne ou vivant subordonné.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MP-03","CL_UCIC_23:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MP-03","text":"Le troisième point de mutation survient lorsque le flux matériel transforme le changement de corps en métamorphose organisationnelle plutôt qu’en migration d’une âme séparée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:MP-03","CL_UCIC_24:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de plénitude récursive : chaque corps est un miroir organisé, chaque partie un monde relatif, chaque monde une modulation du tout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_22:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet est une trajectoire corporelle de focalisation, continuellement modifiée par les échanges matériels sans pouvoir se soustraire à toute organisation incarnée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_24:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est une reconduction différentielle de l’organisation : il ne mène ni au chaos initial ni à un terme matériel ultime, mais à la transformation continue des formes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_23:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction est suffisante si elle conserve la plénitude sans dehors, la récursivité des parties, l’expression différenciée du tout, la médiation corporelle et la continuité identitaire dans le flux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B02","text":"La distinction entre présence universelle et explicitation perceptive finie demeure indispensable : sans elle, l’organisation totale et l’opacité locale deviennent contradictoires au lieu de se soutenir mutuellement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B02","CL_UCIC_23:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination irréductible concerne surtout le mécanisme précis reliant mouvement, représentation, entéléchie, organisation corporelle et persistance graduelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B04","text":"La compression reste fidèle tant qu’elle préserve la conversion fondamentale par laquelle toute apparence de simplicité, de vide, de chaos ou de rupture relance une organisation plus profonde.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200618611728Z_a9b5864b","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L1 06","source_sha256":"c3c8801a8319dc83666ebb29c2118a8d479dd416b7f98195ec4db9e463a6374a","sha256":"60aa26ffb7279aebad97b99b85ac6ef22452a1f1cff56ac7c2a26cc869b5b95b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:06:18.615168+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B01","text":"The guiding problem consists in thinking a totality universally present in every reality without abolishing the difference of bodies, parts, living beings, and perspectives.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B02","text":"The system replaces homogeneous and passive matter with an organized plenitude whose every portion remains active, composite, and internally differentiated.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-01","CL_UCIC_23:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B03","text":"Material recursion converts division into deepening: descending toward the part does not discover a simple element, but a new organized totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-03","CL_UCIC_23:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B04","text":"The proper body and the organism become the focal points where universal expression is concentrated, differentiated, and provisionally stabilized as a living form.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-09","CL_UCIC_24:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B05","text":"Finite perception does not reveal the absence of order; it compresses a real multiplicity into appearances of confusion, emptiness, distance, or chaos.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-06","CL_UCIC_23:AS-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B06","text":"Material flux precludes grounding identity in preserved components and shifts persistence toward the gradual continuity of an embodied organization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:AS-03","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B07","text":"The argument is recursive, cumulative, and stratified: causality, machinicity, composition, perception, organicity, and metamorphosis are so many regimes of one and the same distributed expressivity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:AS-07","CL_UCIC_23:AS-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AS-B08","text":"The conclusion yields no ultimate material, perceptual, or organic ground: it establishes a totality without an outside, finitely expressed, continually transformed, and never distinctly exhausted.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-08","CL_UCIC_21:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The real forms a full continuity in which no corporeal entity, no milieu, and no part can be defined as externally separate from the whole that they express.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-01","CL_UCIC_23:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Every material portion is an active organization whose parts reiterate, at distinct scales, a capacity for composition and expression.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-01","CL_UCIC_23:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The part ceases to be a subordinate residue: it successively becomes machine, internal world, relative living being, causal focus, and organizational totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Universal expression never implies an undifferentiated identity between whole and part, but a presence distributed according to degrees of distinction, function, and perspective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-03","CL_UCIC_22:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The living body is the operator of conversion between cosmic totality, representative order, material organization, and identity continuity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CL_UCIC_24:AS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Identity rests neither on fixed matter nor on a detached soul, but on the gradual persistence of an organization that traverses the renewal of its supports.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-04","CL_UCIC_24:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-07","text":"[Emergent] The imperceptible, the indistinct, and the confused designate limits of resolution rather than proofs of absence, inertia, or real disorder.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-05","CL_UCIC_23:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Analysis can attain neither simple matter, nor an empty region, nor a purely inert living being, nor a created soul absolutely separate from all corporeality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-08","CL_UCIC_24:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Reality converges toward the image of a recursive plenitude: each level is simultaneously composite, organizing, expressive, and integrated into a vaster totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-09","CL_UCIC_24:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Every negation of simplicity, emptiness, chaos, or fixity is converted into a positive proposition of organizational densification.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MP-04","CL_UCIC_23:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-01","text":"Recursivity retains its functional identity as it passes from the natural machine to the material portion, then to the hierarchized living being: it repeats organization without repeating an identical unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RMD-02","CL_UCIC_24:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-02","text":"The body mutates from a causally affected object into a representative mediator, then into an organic process whose identity persists through the flux of matter.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_24:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-03","text":"The infinite shifts from the continuity of composition to the impossibility of a terminal term, then becomes the principle of escalation by which every reduction relaunches organization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RMD-03","CL_UCIC_22:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RMD-04","text":"Perception is reversed: it is no longer the instance that decides real structure, but the site where the richness of the real appears in the form of compression and opacity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_23:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-01","text":"Local examples of machines, gardens, ponds, living limbs, or animal transformations are absorbed into a transversal law of organizational recursivity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_23:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-02","text":"The local distinction between nature and art becomes, at the current level, a distinction between interrupted organization and recursively continued organization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_22:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-03","text":"Perceptual limitation changes scale when it connects material nesting, the containment of milieus, and the appearance of chaos within one and the same theory of resolution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_23:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-04","text":"Corporeal flux, initially a local problem of renewal, becomes the catalyst that compels the reformulation of identity as organizational continuity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:CGD-03","CL_UCIC_24:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:CGD-05","text":"Models of fixed matter, inert part, separating void, and disembodied subject become obsolete because they artificially interrupt the mediations that the system generalizes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:CGD-06","CL_UCIC_23:GNX-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes matter composed of ultimate, homogeneous, mute units or units devoid of organizational interiority.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_23:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-02","text":"It excludes every ontological void: milieus may differ from their contents, but this difference never constitutes a real absence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-04","CL_UCIC_23:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that sensible indistinction might count as a criterion of ontological indifferentiation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:DBN-05","CL_UCIC_23:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-04","text":"It excludes identity founded on the durable possession of assigned matter and the separation of the created soul outside all corporeality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GNX-02","CL_UCIC_24:GNX-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:GNX-05","text":"It excludes a stable opposition between mechanism and life, since machinicity becomes the internal continuity of living organization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:DBN-03","CL_UCIC_22:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, every model in which organization appears only at the level of the whole and vanishes in the parts must be false.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GNX-06","CL_UCIC_23:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:DBN-02","text":"Every model in which spatial separation, distance, or imperceptibility suffices to produce an ontological separation must be false.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_23:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:DBN-03","text":"Every dualism that would make the soul a mobile substance and the body a contingent or replaceable envelope must be false.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:DBN-03","CL_UCIC_24:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-01","text":"The deepest impossibility is that of an absolute outside where expression, organization, life, and relation to the whole would simultaneously cease.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_21:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-02","text":"The unavailable possibility is that of a finite observer capable of converting without remainder universal presence into distinct knowledge of the whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_23:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSA-03","text":"The architecture cannot admit a wholly disembodied finite creature, because embodiment is the condition of every perspective, every organization, and every created continuity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-08","CL_UCIC_24:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-01","text":"Material plenitude and machinic recursion imply that causality does not traverse closed units, but is distributed within organizations already internally relational.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-04","CL_UCIC_21:GA-01","CL_UCIC_22:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-02","text":"The perceptual limit and universal representation are compatible because the presence of the whole exceeds its availability in distinct form for a finite perspective.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-07","CL_UCIC_21:XD-03","CL_UCIC_23:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-03","text":"The organism constitutes the point at which the recursivity of matter becomes continuity of identity: nesting does not produce dispersion because a dominant organization regulates transformations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-06","CL_UCIC_24:XD-06","CL_UCIC_24:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:XD-04","text":"The simultaneous exclusion of the simple, the void, chaos, and fixity transforms the negative limits of the system into cumulative proof of an organization without an outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L1_06:GA-10","CL_UCIC_23:XD-06","CL_UCIC_22:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-01","text":"The real is requalified as a topology of nested totalities in which boundaries designate changes of level, function, or resolution rather than absolute separations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:BSD-01","CL_UCIC_24:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-02","text":"The subject is neither an isolated receptacle nor a disembodied principle: it is a finite organic focalization, traversed by a totality that it expresses without fully explicating it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_24:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-03","text":"Time ceases to be the succession of preserved or replaced substances; it becomes the regime of gradual transformation by which organization persists in flux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:BSD-04","CL_UCIC_21:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:BSD-04","text":"The relevant method consists in following correspondences, nestings, and thresholds of distinction rather than seeking simple components or immediately adequate perceptions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MME-06","CL_UCIC_24:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-01","text":"The principal loop is: material plenitude → organized subdivision → internal activity → expression of the whole → new qualification of the part as world.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_21:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-02","text":"A second loop is: living multiplicity → material flux → impossibility of fixed property → organizational continuity → persistence of unity in metamorphosis.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_24:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-03","text":"The common attractor is a distributed totality whose every local focalization confirms both the unity of the whole and the irreducibility of its internal differentiations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RLE-04","CL_UCIC_21:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:RLE-04","text":"Every attempt to reduce the real relaunches the system at a deeper level: reduction becomes the very mechanism of ontological escalation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_22:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B01","text":"Posit matter that is full, active, and without an ontologically empty region.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B02","text":"Subject every portion to a recursion of composition that prevents it from becoming a simple material element.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:GA-02","CL_UCIC_23:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B03","text":"Convert this composition into differentiated expressivity: each part bears the whole without becoming identical to it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:GA-05","CL_UCIC_21:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B04","text":"Concentrate expression in corporeal focal points where cosmic order becomes perception, organicity, and hierarchized life.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:GA-07","CL_UCIC_24:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B05","text":"Introduce the flux of parts in order to shift identity from material conservation toward the gradual continuity of organization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:GA-05","CL_UCIC_24:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FGS-B06","text":"Requalify appearances of void, chaos, rupture, or simplicity as effects of insufficient resolution, abstract fixation, or unfinished reduction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:XD-04","CL_UCIC_22:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AFM-B01","text":"Material plenitude → recursive composition → internal activity of parts → differentiated universal expression → corporeal focalization → organization of the living being.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_22:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AFM-B02","text":"Living organization → plurality of subordinate living beings → material flux → gradual continuity → embodied processual identity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_24:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:AFM-B03","text":"Imperceptibility and confusion → diagnosis of perceptual compression → restoration of an organized plenitude → exclusion of void, chaos, and the simple.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_23:XD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-01","text":"Matter is reclassified as organizational depth rather than as homogeneous extension, raw support, or a reserve of fixed components.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MME-02","CL_UCIC_24:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-02","text":"The distinction between part and totality collapses as a rigid opposition and becomes a difference of level within an architecture of nesting.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MME-06","CL_UCIC_24:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-03","text":"Space and perception cease to serve as ontological tribunals: distance, milieu, and indistinction are reclassified as mediations and thresholds.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:MME-02","CL_UCIC_23:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MME-04","text":"The adequate reading must map the conversions among causality, representation, composition, organization, and temporality rather than classify isolated substances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MME-06","CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The explicit objects are bodies, machines, material parts, milieus, living beings, souls, organs, and corporeal transformations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] These objects are governed by one and the same architecture of recursive nesting, material continuity, corporeal mediation, and organizational flux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The system replaces the analysis of isolated units with the tracking of relations that make an apparent limit into a mediation, a part into a totality, and a mutation into a persistence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:ALT-B03","CL_UCIC_24:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The real is continuous, full, dynamic, and without a final material term; time produces gradual transformations therein rather than absolute separations.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_24:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The argumentative form performs its thesis by repeating the gesture that descends into the parts, discovers more organization, and transforms every negation into positive reconstruction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_23:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FL-01","text":"The totality is said to be present in every reality, but this presence remains incompatible with any integral finite explication; the tension between expression and legibility is constitutive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:FL-01","CL_UCIC_21:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FL-02","text":"Organization is affirmed as a principle of persistence, but the precise criterion distinguishing a continuous metamorphosis from a rupture of subject remains partially underdetermined.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:FL-02","CL_UCIC_24:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:FL-03","text":"The generalization of recursivity to all matter is structurally decisive, but its passage from local models to a universal law is not fully explicated.","refs":["CL_UCIC_23:FL-02","CL_UCIC_22:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MP-01","text":"The first mutation point occurs when causality and composition cease to be external to bodies and become internal expressive inscriptions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MP-01","CL_UCIC_22:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MP-02","text":"The second mutation point occurs when the part ceases to be a component and becomes a relative totality, internal world, or subordinate living being.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MP-03","CL_UCIC_23:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MP-03","text":"The third mutation point occurs when material flux transforms the change of body into organizational metamorphosis rather than into the migration of a separate soul.","refs":["CL_UCIC_24:MP-03","CL_UCIC_24:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-01","text":"Implicit reality is a machine of recursive plenitude: each body is an organized mirror, each part a relative world, each world a modulation of the whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_22:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a corporeal trajectory of focalization, continually modified by material exchanges without being able to withdraw from all embodied organization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_24:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:HSI-03","text":"Time is a differential reiteration of organization: it leads neither to initial chaos nor to an ultimate material term, but to the continuous transformation of forms.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_23:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B01","text":"The reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves plenitude without an outside, the recursivity of parts, the differentiated expression of the whole, corporeal mediation, and identity continuity in flux.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B02","text":"The distinction between universal presence and finite perceptual explication remains indispensable: without it, total organization and local opacity become contradictory instead of mutually supporting one another.","refs":["CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B02","CL_UCIC_23:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B03","text":"The irreducible indeterminacy concerns above all the precise mechanism linking movement, representation, entelechy, corporeal organization, and gradual persistence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_21:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_06:MRT-B04","text":"The compression remains faithful insofar as it preserves the fundamental conversion by which every appearance of simplicity, void, chaos, or rupture relaunches a deeper organization.","refs":["CL_UCIC_22:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_23:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_06@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L1_06:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L1 06","context":"Chapters 61–72 · Proposition 61 · Proposition 62 · Proposition 63 · Proposition 64 · Proposition 65 · Proposition 66 · Proposition 67 · Proposition 68 · Proposition 69 · Proposition 70 · Proposition 71 · Proposition 72"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L1 07","order":7,"parents":["CL_UCIC_25","CL_UCIC_26","CL_UCIC_27"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_07@R001","sha256":"03dd6a8f35808c3391165d8b9e392b573093e684870f2eb99cee6949ee085565","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B01","text":"Le système interdit de penser les vivants, leurs transformations et leurs liaisons comme des passages absolus entre présence et absence, ou comme des transmissions directes entre ordres hétérogènes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:SP-01","CL_UCIC_27:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B02","text":"La continuité organique devient d’abord antériorité préformée, puis identité persistante à travers les supports matériels, enfin coordination des séries dont les transformations concordent sans se produire mutuellement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B03","text":"Le mouvement ne convertit pas les différences en homogénéité : il maintient des trajectoires organiques inégalement distribuées, des supports matériels variables et des régimes causaux irréductibles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-07","CL_UCIC_26:GA-07","CL_UCIC_27:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B04","text":"La persistance cesse d’être une simple conservation et devient une règle de transformation : l’être demeure en changeant de forme, de support, de degré ou de mode de correspondance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-01","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B05","text":"La preuve systémique procède par exclusions cumulatives : origine absolue, mort parfaite, identité matérielle, interaction transitive et exception psychique aux invariants physiques sont successivement rendues indisponibles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_27:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B06","text":"Ces exclusions ne conduisent pas au vide mais rendent nécessaire une architecture positive de préformation, de principe animé, d’autonomie réglée et d’harmonie préétablie.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B07","text":"Le système se déploie comme une spirale mutationnelle : chaque phénomène apparent de naissance, mort, action ou influence est réinscrit dans une structure antérieure qui en retire le statut de commencement causal.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_27:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B08","text":"La clôture méta-clusterienne est une ontologie des continuités différentielles : les êtres persistent selon des séries propres, mais la totalité de leurs différences est tenue dans une concordance non transitive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Aucun vivant naturel ne commence ni ne cesse absolument ; génération et mort désignent des transformations localisées d’une persistance plus profonde.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’identité vivante ne réside ni dans l’état matériel présent ni dans la conservation numérique de la machine organique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] La continuité passe d’une antériorité organique préformée à une persistance animale, puis à une coordination intersérielle qui conserve la différence des ordres.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Les transformations corporelles sont réelles sans constituer par elles-mêmes une annihilation ou une création de l’unité animale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RMD-03","CL_UCIC_26:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] La préformation, le principe animé et l’harmonie remplissent une même fonction méta-structurelle : inscrire tout phénomène apparent dans une organisation antérieure à son apparition empirique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] L’autonomie des composantes ou des séries n’exclut pas leur concordance ; elle constitue la condition sous laquelle celle-ci peut être pensée sans fusion.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","text":"[Terminal] La causalité directe entre âme et corps est exclue parce que les invariants matériels ferment l’espace de toute intervention psychophysique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:AS-03","CL_UCIC_27:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] La concordance observable est l’attracteur qui réunit les transformations organiques, l’identité animale et les séries causales sans abolir leurs différences internes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] La conception et l’action volontaire perdent leur statut de productions inaugurales ; elles deviennent des sites phénoménaux où une organisation déjà engagée se reconfigure ou se manifeste.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-05","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] L’ordre total est différentiel plutôt qu’uniforme : les devenirs organiques sont hiérarchisés et les ordres causaux demeurent hétérogènes, mais leurs écarts sont contenus dans une même architecture de persistance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-10","CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-01","text":"Le refus de l’origine absolue demeure stable, mais change d’objet : il concerne successivement la génération organique, l’existence animale et la causalité psychophysique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RMD-01","CL_UCIC_27:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-02","text":"La mort mute d’une transformation organique terminale locale en séparation entre machine et animal, puis sert indirectement à imposer une réalité où la disparition n’est jamais l’explication ultime.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:XD-04","CL_UCIC_26:RMD-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-03","text":"La continuité organique est absorbée dans une continuité identitaire, laquelle est elle-même absorbée dans une continuité de coordination entre séries autonomes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_26:RMD-03","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-04","text":"Le corps se déplace d’un foyer de formation préexistante à un support variable de l’animal, puis à une série mécanique causalement close.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_27:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-05","text":"La conception et la volonté connaissent une inversion parallèle : ce qui paraît produire une nouveauté ou un effet devient le signe local d’une disposition ou d’une coordination déjà réglée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-06","text":"L’harmonie passe d’une réponse à l’union âme-corps à la forme générale de la concordance, tandis que son mécanisme positif demeure structurellement non spécifié.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:GA-10","CL_UCIC_27:RLE-04","CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-01","text":"Les mécanismes de semence, de préformation et de sélection relèvent de la couche organique locale ; au niveau courant, ils ne subsistent qu’en tant que principe d’antériorité et de différenciation des devenirs.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:CGD-07","CL_UCIC_25:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-02","text":"La distinction entre animal et machine change d’échelle lorsqu’elle devient une règle générale séparant l’unité persistante des supports et des manifestations qui la rendent visible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:CGD-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-03","text":"Les lois de conservation sont localement physiques, mais leur convergence devient au niveau courant une opération métaphysique de fermeture de l’interaction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:CGD-02","CL_UCIC_27:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-04","text":"La hiérarchie entre cycle ordinaire et élévation reste une différenciation organique particulière ; elle est recodée ici comme preuve que continuité et uniformité ne sont pas équivalentes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-10","CL_UCIC_25:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-05","text":"Les apparences de naissance, de mort, de rencontre et d’influence restent descriptivement valides, mais cessent d’être des descriptions ontologiquement terminales.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_27:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut les commencements et fins absolus, qu’ils prennent la forme d’une naissance ex nihilo, d’une mort parfaite ou d’un néant naturel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_26:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut l’identification du vivant à sa matière actuelle, à sa configuration organique momentanée ou à une agrégation de parties.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut qu’une concordance empirique prouve une causalité transitive entre des ordres hétérogènes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_27:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut symétriquement la fusion des causalités et leur réduction unilatérale, qu’elle soit mécaniste pour l’âme ou téléologique pour la matière.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GNX-06","CL_UCIC_27:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-01","text":"Pour que le système tienne, l’être ne peut pas être défini par opposition simple au non-être : les phénomènes naturels doivent exprimer des reconfigurations d’une persistance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-02","text":"Le modèle rival silencieusement disqualifié est celui d’un monde composé d’unités séparées, matériellement auto-suffisantes, reliées par des transmissions locales immédiatement observables.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:DBN-04","CL_UCIC_26:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-03","text":"L’harmonie ne peut pas être admise comme interaction dissimulée : elle doit demeurer coordination sans médiation causale commune.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSA-01","text":"L’absence la plus profonde est celle d’un dehors ontologique où une unité pourrait absolument surgir, absolument disparaître ou sortir de la continuité qui la constitue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_25:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSA-02","text":"La possibilité structurellement indisponible est celle d’une causalité psychophysique directe qui conserverait néanmoins l’intégrité des invariants matériels.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_27:AS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSA-03","text":"Le système refuse une totalité qui abolirait les différences : l’unité n’est recevable qu’en tant que maintien coordonné de transformations et de séries irréductibles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-01","text":"L’antériorité organique, la permanence de l’animal et l’harmonie des séries constituent trois échelles d’une même opération : retirer aux événements visibles le pouvoir d’inaugurer ou d’abolir l’être.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-05","CL_UCIC_25:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-02","text":"Lorsque l’identité est dissociée de la matière présente et que l’interaction est dissociée de la concordance, le réel devient lisible comme persistance de fonctions plutôt que comme conservation de substances ou circulation d’impulsions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-08","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-03","text":"La sélection organique et la clôture psychophysique ont une fonction commune de limitation : l’une interdit l’élévation universelle, l’autre interdit l’intervention universellement disponible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10","CL_UCIC_25:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-04","text":"La négation de l’origine absolue et la négation de la causalité transitive produisent une même architecture apophatique : aucune transformation ne peut être fondée par un commencement isolé ni par une transmission immédiate.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","CL_UCIC_27:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-05","text":"La continuité devient intrinsèquement différentielle : elle conserve les êtres à travers leurs modifications tout en distribuant inégalement leurs possibilités de changement et leurs modes de coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10","CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-01","text":"Le réel n’est plus composé d’objets qui entrent puis sortent de l’existence, mais de trajectoires organisées dont les seuils biologiques et phénoménaux sont des reconfigurations internes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-04","CL_UCIC_25:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-02","text":"Le sujet animal est reclassé comme centre de persistance et d’expérience d’une coordination, non comme propriétaire d’un corps invariable ni comme auteur d’une force transmise au corps.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","CL_UCIC_26:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-03","text":"Le temps devient stratifié et parallèle : il est à la fois profondeur d’antériorité des formes et simultanéité ordonnée de séries autonomes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-06","CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-04","text":"La causalité est déplacée de la transmission entre agents vers une distribution hiérarchisée de fonctions, de dispositions et de correspondances.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-08","CL_UCIC_25:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-05","text":"La méthode de connaissance devient une remontée des apparences locales vers les structures qui rendent ces apparences compatibles avec une permanence et une coordination préalables.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-08","CL_UCIC_25:BSD-06","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-01","text":"Apparition ou disparition apparente → exclusion du seuil absolu → découverte d’une antériorité persistante → requalification du phénomène → nouvelle apparence à expliquer.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-02","text":"Préformation → animal préexistant → dissociation de la machine → principe animé persistant : l’identité est continuellement déplacée hors de son support empirique immédiat.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-03","text":"Distinction des régimes causaux → test des possibilités d’interaction → conservation de force et de direction → fermeture de l’interaction → harmonie comme unique forme de concordance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_27:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur principal est une unité qui persiste à travers la différence, mais cet attracteur se réalise différemment comme continuité organique, identité animale et harmonie des séries.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RLE-04","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-06","CL_UCIC_27:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-05","text":"La répétition des exclusions produit un changement de phase : la négation cesse d’être défensive et devient une procédure positive de génération de l’architecture métaphysique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B01","text":"Apparence de génération, de mort ou d’action → refus de l’événement absolu comme explication ontologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:SP-02","CL_UCIC_26:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B02","text":"Refus du seuil absolu → recherche d’une organisation antérieure, d’un principe persistant ou d’une loi de coordination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B04","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B03","text":"Organisation antérieure → dissociation de l’unité et de son support matériel → transformation corporelle sans destruction de l’animal.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B04","text":"Hétérogénéité des séries → exclusion de la transmission directe → concordance devenue problème structurel plutôt qu’effet causal immédiat.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","CL_UCIC_27:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B05","text":"Fermeture des voies causales → harmonie préétablie → unité du réel comme correspondance de différences irréductibles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:XD-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B06","text":"Continuité persistante + différenciation organique + autonomie parallèle → monde de devenirs inégaux mais non discontinus.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-09","CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B01","text":"Apparence de seuil biologique → négation de la génération et de la mort absolues → continuité sous transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B02","text":"Continuité organique → préformation → antériorité du corps, de l’âme et de l’animal → conception comme disposition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B03","text":"Persistance animale → dissociation de l’animal et de la machine → identité à travers le renouvellement des supports.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B02","CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B04","text":"Hétérogénéité âme-corps → fermeture des interventions par les invariants physiques → autonomie parallèle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B05","text":"Autonomie parallèle → apparence d’influence → harmonie préétablie → concordance sans origine, annihilation ou transmission transitive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B07","CL_UCIC_27:AS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-01","text":"La frontière entre biologie et métaphysique s’effondre : génération, mort, métamorphose et union psychophysique deviennent des problèmes homologues de reclassification des apparences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-02","text":"La fausse opposition entre conservation et changement est remplacée par une continuité où conserver signifie déjà se transformer selon une règle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:MME-07","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-03","text":"La fausse opposition entre autonomie et liaison est remplacée par une coordination où l’autonomie des séries rend possible leur concordance phénoménale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-04","text":"L’analyse pertinente ne demande plus quel agent produit directement quel effet, mais quelle structure rend possible qu’une influence apparaisse sans transgression des invariants constitutifs.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:MME-06","CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets manifestes sont la génération, la mort, la semence, l’animal, la machine organique, l’âme, le corps, la force et la direction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Les phénomènes sont redistribués entre préformation, principe animé, variation des supports, invariants matériels et séries autonomes coordonnées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Les objections fondées sur l’apparence empirique sont neutralisées par déplacement vers le niveau où les conditions de possibilité de l’apparence sont déterminées.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B03","CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel est persistance organisée et simultanéité ordonnée ; le temps est profondeur d’antériorité autant que développement parallèle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — L’argument produit positivement ce qu’il affirme en retirant successivement aux phénomènes leur apparente suffisance ontologique et causale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-01","text":"La continuité est universalisée comme condition ontologique, mais les devenirs organiques demeurent hiérarchisés et inégalement accessibles.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:FL-01","CL_UCIC_25:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-02","text":"L’indestructibilité de l’animal dépend d’un passage de l’âme au vivant dont la médiation demeure insuffisamment explicitée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:FL-02","CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-03","text":"L’harmonie est exigée pour expliquer la concordance, mais le mécanisme concret qui rend cette concordance effective reste absent après la clôture de l’interaction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:FL-01","CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-01","text":"La première mutation survient lorsque génération et mort cessent d’être des limites de l’être et deviennent des orientations de la transformation continue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:MP-01","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-02","text":"La deuxième mutation survient lorsque la machine organique est déclassée de principe apparent d’identité à support remplaçable d’une unité persistante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:MP-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-03","text":"La mutation terminale survient lorsque la causalité est transférée des relations entre agents vers l’architecture de correspondances entre séries closes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:MP-01","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine de transformations stratifiées et de séries parallèles, où aucune forme ne surgit sans antériorité ni ne rejoint un néant absolu.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_27:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-02","text":"L’animal devient une unité persistante dont les corps, les formes et les apparences d’action sont les configurations variables d’un développement déjà inscrit dans un ordre plus vaste.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_26:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-03","text":"La lutte cognitive interne consiste à distinguer les effets visibles de leurs conditions structurelles, sans réduire la concordance à une interaction ni la transformation à une rupture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:HSI-04","CL_UCIC_27:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale est suffisante si elle conserve simultanément l’absence d’origine et de mort absolues, l’identité non matérielle du vivant et la coordination sans causalité transitive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B02","text":"Les axiomes peuvent reconstruire la machine méta-clusterienne sans reproduire les mécanismes locaux de semence, de sélection ou de conservation physique, à condition d’en préserver la fonction de fermeture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:CGD-07","CL_UCIC_27:CGD-02","CL_UCIC_27:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B03","text":"La compression échoue si elle transforme la continuité en homogénéité, l’harmonie en interaction déguisée ou l’identité en immobilité matérielle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B04","text":"L’indétermination irréductible porte sur les conditions positives de l’élévation organique et sur le mécanisme positif de l’harmonie ; elle ne détruit pas la clôture négative qui structure l’ensemble.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:BSA-04","CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200647155670Z_1095f869","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L1 07","source_sha256":"03dd6a8f35808c3391165d8b9e392b573093e684870f2eb99cee6949ee085565","sha256":"37acbeebd830acb969801aebc60a1f13896ee8e19c768f5415c643bbe849f77b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:06:47.263172+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B01","text":"The system prohibits thinking of living beings, their transformations, and their connections as absolute passages between presence and absence, or as direct transmissions between heterogeneous orders.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:SP-01","CL_UCIC_27:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B02","text":"Organic continuity first becomes preformed anteriority, then persistent identity across material supports, and finally coordination of series whose transformations accord without mutually producing one another.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B03","text":"Movement does not convert differences into homogeneity: it maintains unequally distributed organic trajectories, variable material supports, and irreducible causal regimes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-07","CL_UCIC_26:GA-07","CL_UCIC_27:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B04","text":"Persistence ceases to be mere conservation and becomes a rule of transformation: being remains by changing form, support, degree, or mode of correspondence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-01","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B05","text":"Systemic proof proceeds through cumulative exclusions: absolute origin, perfect death, material identity, transitive interaction, and psychic exception to physical invariants are successively rendered unavailable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_27:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B06","text":"These exclusions do not lead to emptiness but make necessary a positive architecture of preformation, animated principle, regulated autonomy, and pre-established harmony.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B07","text":"The system unfolds as a mutational spiral: every apparent phenomenon of birth, death, action, or influence is reinscribed within an anterior structure that removes from it the status of causal beginning.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_27:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AS-B08","text":"The meta-cluster closure is an ontology of differential continuities: beings persist according to their own series, but the totality of their differences is held within a non-transitive concordance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10","CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] No natural living being begins or ceases absolutely; generation and death designate localized transformations of a deeper persistence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Living identity resides neither in the present material state nor in the numerical conservation of the organic machine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] Continuity passes from a preformed organic anteriority to animal persistence, then to interserial coordination that preserves the difference of orders.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-03","CL_UCIC_27:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Bodily transformations are real without in themselves constituting an annihilation or a creation of animal unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RMD-03","CL_UCIC_26:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Preformation, the animated principle, and harmony fulfill one and the same meta-structural function: inscribing every apparent phenomenon within an organization anterior to its empirical appearance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] The autonomy of components or series does not exclude their concordance; it constitutes the condition under which this can be thought without fusion.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","text":"[Terminal] Direct causality between soul and body is excluded because material invariants close off the space of all psychophysical intervention.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:AS-03","CL_UCIC_27:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-08","text":"[Attractor] Observable concordance is the attractor that brings together organic transformations, animal identity, and causal series without abolishing their internal differences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-09","CL_UCIC_26:GA-11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-09","text":"[Mutating] Conception and voluntary action lose their status as inaugural productions; they become phenomenal sites where an already engaged organization reconfigures itself or manifests itself.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-05","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] The total order is differential rather than uniform: organic becomings are hierarchized and causal orders remain heterogeneous, but their divergences are contained within a single architecture of persistence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-10","CL_UCIC_27:GA-04","CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-01","text":"The refusal of absolute origin remains stable, but changes its object: it concerns successively organic generation, animal existence, and psychophysical causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RMD-01","CL_UCIC_27:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-02","text":"Death mutates from a local terminal organic transformation into a separation between machine and animal, then indirectly serves to impose a reality in which disappearance is never the ultimate explanation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:XD-04","CL_UCIC_26:RMD-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-03","text":"Organic continuity is absorbed into an identity continuity, which is itself absorbed into a continuity of coordination between autonomous series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_26:RMD-03","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-04","text":"The body is displaced from a locus of pre-existing formation to a variable support of the animal, then to a mechanically causally closed series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_27:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-05","text":"Conception and will undergo a parallel inversion: what appears to produce a novelty or an effect becomes the local sign of an already regulated disposition or coordination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RMD-06","text":"Harmony passes from a response to the soul-body union to the general form of concordance, while its positive mechanism remains structurally unspecified.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:GA-10","CL_UCIC_27:RLE-04","CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-01","text":"The mechanisms of seed, preformation, and selection belong to the local organic layer; at the current level, they persist only as a principle of anteriority and differentiation of becomings.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:CGD-07","CL_UCIC_25:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-02","text":"The distinction between animal and machine changes scale when it becomes a general rule separating the persistent unity from the supports and manifestations that render it visible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:CGD-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-03","text":"The laws of conservation are locally physical, but their convergence becomes, at the current level, a metaphysical operation of closure of interaction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:CGD-02","CL_UCIC_27:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-04","text":"The hierarchy between ordinary cycle and elevation remains a particular organic differentiation; it is recoded here as proof that continuity and uniformity are not equivalent.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-10","CL_UCIC_25:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:CGD-05","text":"The appearances of birth, death, encounter, and influence remain descriptively valid, but cease to be ontologically terminal descriptions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_27:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes absolute beginnings and ends, whether they take the form of a birth ex nihilo, a perfect death, or a natural nothingness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_26:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-02","text":"It excludes the identification of the living being with its current matter, its momentary organic configuration, or an aggregation of parts.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the possibility that an empirical concordance proves transitive causality between heterogeneous orders.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_27:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:GNX-04","text":"It symmetrically excludes the fusion of causalities and their unilateral reduction, whether mechanistic for the soul or teleological for matter.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GNX-06","CL_UCIC_27:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-01","text":"For the system to hold, being cannot be defined by simple opposition to non-being: natural phenomena must express reconfigurations of a persistence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-02","text":"The silently disqualified rival model is that of a world composed of separate, materially self-sufficient units, connected by immediately observable local transmissions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:DBN-04","CL_UCIC_26:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:DBN-03","text":"Harmony cannot be admitted as concealed interaction: it must remain coordination without a common causal mediation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSA-01","text":"The deepest absence is that of an ontological outside in which a unity could absolutely arise, absolutely disappear, or leave the continuity that constitutes it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_25:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSA-02","text":"The structurally unavailable possibility is that of a direct psychophysical causality that would nevertheless preserve the integrity of material invariants.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_27:AS-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSA-03","text":"The system refuses a totality that would abolish differences: unity is admissible only as the coordinated maintenance of transformations and irreducible series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_27:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-01","text":"Organic anteriority, the permanence of the animal, and the harmony of series constitute three scales of one and the same operation: removing from visible events the power to inaugurate or abolish being.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-05","CL_UCIC_25:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-02","text":"When identity is dissociated from present matter and interaction from concordance, the real becomes legible as persistence of functions rather than as conservation of substances or circulation of impulses.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-08","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-03","text":"Organic selection and psychophysical closure have a common limiting function: the former prohibits universal elevation, the latter prohibits universally available intervention.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10","CL_UCIC_25:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-04","text":"The negation of absolute origin and the negation of transitive causality produce the same apophatic architecture: no transformation can be grounded in an isolated beginning or an immediate transmission.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","CL_UCIC_27:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:XD-05","text":"Continuity becomes intrinsically differential: it preserves beings through their modifications while unequally distributing their possibilities of change and their modes of coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-10","CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-01","text":"The real is no longer composed of objects that enter and then leave existence, but of organized trajectories whose biological and phenomenal thresholds are internal reconfigurations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-04","CL_UCIC_25:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-02","text":"The animal subject is reclassified as a center of persistence and experience of a coordination, not as the owner of an invariable body nor as the author of a force transmitted to the body.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","CL_UCIC_26:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-03","text":"Time becomes stratified and parallel: it is at once the depth of the anteriority of forms and the ordered simultaneity of autonomous series.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-06","CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-04","text":"Causality is displaced from transmission between agents toward a hierarchized distribution of functions, dispositions, and correspondences.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-08","CL_UCIC_25:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:BSD-05","text":"The method of knowledge becomes an ascent from local appearances to the structures that render these appearances compatible with prior permanence and coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_07:GA-08","CL_UCIC_25:BSD-06","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-01","text":"Apparent appearance or disappearance → exclusion of the absolute threshold → discovery of a persistent anteriority → requalification of the phenomenon → new appearance to explain.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-02","text":"Preformation → pre-existing animal → dissociation from the machine → persistent animated principle: identity is continually displaced outside its immediate empirical support.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-03","text":"Distinction of causal regimes → test of possibilities of interaction → conservation of force and direction → closure of interaction → harmony as the sole form of concordance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_27:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-04","text":"The principal attractor is a unity that persists through difference, but this attractor is realized differently as organic continuity, animal identity, and harmony of series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:RLE-04","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-06","CL_UCIC_27:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:RLE-05","text":"The repetition of exclusions produces a phase change: negation ceases to be defensive and becomes a positive procedure for generating metaphysical architecture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B01","text":"Appearance of generation, death, or action → refusal of the absolute event as an ontological explanation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:SP-02","CL_UCIC_26:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B02","text":"Refusal of the absolute threshold → search for an anterior organization, a persistent principle, or a law of coordination.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B04","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B03","text":"Anterior organization → dissociation of unity and its material support → bodily transformation without destruction of the animal.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:GA-04","CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B04","text":"Heterogeneity of series → exclusion of direct transmission → concordance becomes a structural problem rather than an immediate causal effect.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:GA-01","CL_UCIC_27:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B05","text":"Closure of causal pathways → pre-established harmony → unity of the real as correspondence of irreducible differences.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:XD-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FGS-B06","text":"Persistent continuity + organic differentiation + parallel autonomy → world of unequal yet non-discontinuous becomings.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_27:GA-09","CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B01","text":"Appearance of a biological threshold → negation of absolute generation and death → continuity under transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B02","text":"Organic continuity → preformation → anteriority of body, soul, and animal → conception as disposition.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_25:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B03","text":"Animal persistence → dissociation of animal and machine → identity through the renewal of supports.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B02","CL_UCIC_26:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B04","text":"Soul-body heterogeneity → closure of interventions by physical invariants → parallel autonomy.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:AFM-B05","text":"Parallel autonomy → appearance of influence → pre-established harmony → concordance without origin, annihilation, or transitive transmission.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:FGS-B07","CL_UCIC_27:AS-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-01","text":"The boundary between biology and metaphysics collapses: generation, death, metamorphosis, and psychophysical union become homologous problems of reclassifying appearances.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-02","text":"The false opposition between conservation and change is replaced by a continuity in which to conserve already means to transform oneself according to a rule.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:MME-07","CL_UCIC_26:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-03","text":"The false opposition between autonomy and connection is replaced by a coordination in which the autonomy of series makes their phenomenal concordance possible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MME-04","text":"Relevant analysis no longer asks which agent directly produces which effect, but which structure makes it possible for an influence to appear without transgressing constitutive invariants.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:MME-06","CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The manifest objects are generation, death, seed, animal, organic machine, soul, body, force, and direction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Phenomena are redistributed among preformation, animated principle, variation of supports, material invariants, and coordinated autonomous series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Objections based on empirical appearance are neutralized by displacement to the level at which the conditions of possibility of appearance are determined.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:ALT-B03","CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The real is organized persistence and ordered simultaneity; time is depth of anteriority as much as parallel development.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The argument positively produces what it asserts by successively withdrawing from phenomena their apparent ontological and causal sufficiency.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_27:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-01","text":"Continuity is universalized as an ontological condition, but organic becomings remain hierarchized and unequally accessible.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:FL-01","CL_UCIC_25:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-02","text":"The indestructibility of the animal depends on a passage from soul to living being whose mediation remains insufficiently explicated.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:FL-02","CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:FL-03","text":"Harmony is required to explain concordance, but the concrete mechanism that makes this concordance effective remains absent after the closure of interaction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:FL-01","CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-01","text":"The first mutation occurs when generation and death cease to be limits of being and become orientations of continuous transformation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:MP-01","CL_UCIC_26:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-02","text":"The second mutation occurs when the organic machine is demoted from an apparent principle of identity to a replaceable support of a persistent unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:MP-02","CL_UCIC_26:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MP-03","text":"The terminal mutation occurs when causality is transferred from relations between agents to the architecture of correspondences between closed series.","refs":["CL_UCIC_27:MP-01","CL_UCIC_27:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-01","text":"The implicit reality is a machine of stratified transformations and parallel series, in which no form arises without anteriority nor reaches an absolute nothingness.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_27:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-02","text":"The animal becomes a persistent unity whose bodies, forms, and appearances of action are the variable configurations of a development already inscribed within a broader order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_26:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:HSI-03","text":"The internal cognitive struggle consists in distinguishing visible effects from their structural conditions, without reducing concordance to interaction or transformation to rupture.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:HSI-04","CL_UCIC_27:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction is sufficient if it simultaneously preserves the absence of absolute origin and death, the non-material identity of the living being, and coordination without transitive causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_26:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B02","text":"The axioms can reconstruct the meta-cluster machine without reproducing the local mechanisms of seed, selection, or physical conservation, provided that their function of closure is preserved.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:CGD-07","CL_UCIC_27:CGD-02","CL_UCIC_27:CGD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B03","text":"Compression fails if it transforms continuity into homogeneity, harmony into disguised interaction, or identity into material immobility.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_07:MRT-B04","text":"Irreducible indeterminacy concerns the positive conditions of organic elevation and the positive mechanism of harmony; it does not destroy the negative closure that structures the whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_25:BSA-04","CL_UCIC_27:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_27:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_07@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L1_07:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L1 07","context":"Chapters 73–81 · Proposition 73 · Proposition 74 · Proposition 75 · Proposition 76 · Proposition 77 · Proposition 78 · Proposition 79 · Proposition 80 · Proposition 81"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08","layer":"MC","title":"Ucic L1 08","order":8,"parents":["CL_UCIC_28","CL_UCIC_29","CL_UCIC_30"],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_08@R001","sha256":"3cdb97189911e361faaa2aadb5a3e22ce8c766d7f40f8a29336dda0b25665e8d","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B01","text":"Le système doit résoudre comment une vie continue peut devenir esprit, comment les esprits deviennent une cité, et comment cette cité rend la justice providentielle immanente au réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:AS-01","CL_UCIC_29:AS-01","CL_UCIC_30:BAS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B02","text":"L’argument refuse la rupture entre nature et esprit, puis refuse que l’esprit demeure une puissance privée : la participation divine doit devenir ordre relationnel, politique et cosmique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_28:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B03","text":"La puissance spirituelle locale est d’abord produite comme capacité de connaître et d’imiter l’ordre ; elle est ensuite redistribuée comme appartenance à une monarchie morale et à une Providence universelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:XD-02","CL_UCIC_30:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B04","text":"Le mouvement est une escalade de l’animation vers l’architectonique, de l’architectonique vers le gouvernement, puis du gouvernement vers la naturalisation de la justice.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B02","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B05","text":"La causalité n’est achevée qu’en devenant relation : produire un être exige de le gouverner, de recevoir sa reconnaissance et d’inscrire ses actes dans une économie de récompense et de peine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RMD-06","CL_UCIC_29:XD-03","CL_UCIC_30:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B06","text":"Le système progresse par coordination de distinctions maintenues : vivant et esprit, machine et cité, nature et grâce, devoir et effectivité ne sont pas fusionnés mais hiérarchiquement articulés.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_29:GNX-05","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B07","text":"Sa clôture produit un sujet localement actif mais globalement dessaisi : il peut imiter l’ordre, servir la cité et poursuivre le bien présumé, sans pouvoir instituer ni corriger la totalité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-07","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B08","text":"L’attracteur terminal est une gouvernementalité divine distribuée, où la continuité vitale, la pluralité spirituelle, la monarchie morale et la rétribution naturelle fonctionnent comme des régimes d’un même ordre.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_29:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La continuité du vivant interdit de penser l’esprit comme une substance sans genèse ; l’élévation spirituelle conserve donc une dépendance structurale envers la vie qu’elle transforme.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-01","CL_UCIC_28:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] La ressemblance divine mute de représentation intérieure en puissance architectonique, puis en capacité d’occuper une fonction déterminée dans un gouvernement supérieur.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-05","CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-03","text":"[Emergent] Une pluralité d’esprits ne reçoit sa forme accomplie qu’en devenant une cité politique, morale et théologique sous une souveraineté commune.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] L’unité supérieure ne résulte pas d’une indistinction des ordres, mais de leur coordination fonctionnelle sous une même source divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CL_UCIC_29:GNX-05","CL_UCIC_29:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Dieu passe du statut d’Auteur de puissances locales à celui d’architecte cosmique, de monarque des esprits et de législateur dont la justice est inscrite dans les mécanismes naturels.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_30:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] La gloire divine exige une communauté capable de connaître, d’admirer et d’incarner pratiquement les perfections qu’elle reçoit.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:XD-01","CL_UCIC_30:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] La perfection devient gouvernementale : elle organise la répartition des puissances, l’unité de la cité, l’harmonie des ordres et la rétribution des conduites.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-12","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-04","CL_UCIC_30:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] La Nature n’est ni un dehors de la grâce ni une machine autonome ; elle devient le mode opératoire par lequel le gouvernement divin rend effectives finalité, loi et justice.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:GA-01","CL_UCIC_30:GA-02","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] L’agent humain ou spirituel est actif dans son département, mais son activité reste dérivée, gouvernée et incapable de constituer un point de vue souverain sur l’ordre total.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-10","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_30:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Le temps rend compatibles l’élévation des facultés, la médiation politique et le délai rétributif en séparant l’action locale de l’intelligibilité finale du tout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_30:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-01","text":"La continuité passe du fond vital transindividuel à la cohérence d’une pluralité spirituelle, puis à l’unité cosmique d’un ordre providentiel ; elle cesse ainsi d’être seulement biologique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RMD-01","CL_UCIC_29:RMD-01","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-02","text":"L’architecture revient sous trois fonctions distinctes : imitation locale de l’ordre, organisation monarchique de la cité, puis inscription mécanique de la loi dans la Nature.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B04","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-03","text":"La relation à Dieu se déplace de la société de puissances limitées vers la reconnaissance collective de la gloire, puis vers l’acceptation subjective d’une volonté effective non totalisable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_30:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-04","text":"La perfection inverse sa fonction : puissance de participation dans l’esprit, elle devient principe de centralisation dans la cité, puis interdit toute révision humaine de l’ordre universel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_30:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-05","text":"La distinction entre nature et grâce demeure active, mais sa valence change : d’écart à harmoniser, elle devient condition d’une gouvernementalité unique à deux régimes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:MME-05","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-01","text":"Les mécanismes précis de conception, d’élection animale et d’élévation des facultés restent locaux ; au niveau courant, ils ne valent que comme matrice d’une transformation graduelle de la puissance en gouvernement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_28:CGD-02","CL_UCIC_28:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-02","text":"La distinction locale entre imitation architectonique et gouvernement princier est recodée à l’échelle courante comme passage nécessaire de la production à l’administration d’une pluralité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_28:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-03","text":"La déduction de la monarchie parfaite reste une machine interne au niveau inférieur ; sa portée actuelle est de rendre visible la politisation constitutive de toute totalité spirituelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-01","CL_UCIC_29:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-04","text":"Les catastrophes, délais corporels et mécanismes particuliers de peine demeurent locaux ; leur intégration actuelle produit une temporalité générale où l’absence de visibilité immédiate devient compatible avec la justice nécessaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_30:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_30:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-05","text":"La distinction entre volonté présomptive et volonté conséquente change d’échelle lorsqu’elle devient le protocole global qui distribue activité morale locale et passivité devant l’issue totale.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_30:XD-03","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut toute rupture absolue entre animalité, esprit et société divine, puisque l’élévation doit demeurer une transformation interne de la continuité vivante.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_28:XD-01","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut une puissance spirituelle autonome : toute capacité créatrice ou architectonique doit rester locale, dérivée et insérée dans une hiérarchie relationnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_28:GNX-05","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut une communauté spirituelle sans forme politique, ainsi qu’une perfection collective sans souveraineté organisatrice.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_29:GNX-02","CL_UCIC_29:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut la séparation durable entre mécanique naturelle, normativité morale et finalité providentielle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_30:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut enfin une critique humaine de la totalité qui prétendrait évaluer ou réformer le monde depuis un point de vue extérieur à son gouvernement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:GNX-05","CL_UCIC_30:DBN-04","CL_UCIC_30:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-01","text":"Le système ne tient que si sont simultanément rejetés le matérialisme d’une machine sans société et le spiritualisme d’une puissance sans genèse ni dépendance.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:DBN-02","CL_UCIC_28:DBN-05","CL_UCIC_28:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-02","text":"Il exige qu’une causalité adéquate soit déjà relationnelle : produire sans gouverner, gouverner sans être reconnu, ou récompenser sans médiation naturelle laisserait l’architecture inachevée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_29:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_30:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-03","text":"Il disqualifie tout pluralisme des principes ultimes : architecture, souveraineté, grâce, loi, nature et bonheur doivent relever d’une source coordonnatrice unique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GNX-06","CL_UCIC_29:BSA-04","CL_UCIC_30:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-04","text":"Il rend inadmissible une temporalité qui donnerait au sujet un contre-exemple durable à la justice ; le délai ne peut être que médiation, jamais suspension effective de l’ordre.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité la plus profondément exclue est celle d’un dehors : aucun vivant, esprit, événement naturel ou jugement humain ne peut se situer hors de l’ordre qui le produit.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_29:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_30:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-02","text":"L’absence structurante est celle d’une autonomie véritable de l’agent : l’activité n’est admise qu’à titre de fonction dérivée, départementale et orientée par une fin préalable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:DBN-04","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-03","text":"Le système rend indisponible une justice visible, immédiatement vérifiable et susceptible d’être jugée par ses effets apparents ; son efficacité dépend au contraire de l’opacité temporelle de son accomplissement.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_30:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-01","text":"La participation spirituelle devient politiquement nécessaire dès lors que la puissance locale ne peut ni s’autofonder ni coordonner par elle-même la pluralité des puissances analogues.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09","CL_UCIC_28:XD-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-02","text":"La Cité transforme la connaissance de Dieu en mécanisme de gouvernement : l’admiration collective ne s’ajoute pas à l’ordre politique, elle en réalise la fonction théologique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:XD-01","CL_UCIC_29:XD-03","CL_UCIC_29:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-03","text":"L’identification de l’architecte et du législateur absorbe la différence entre construction cosmique et jugement moral : le monde n’est pas jugé après coup, il est construit comme scène de rétribution.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-08","CL_UCIC_30:XD-04","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-04","text":"La limitation cognitive du sujet devient productive pour la souveraineté du tout : l’impossibilité de totaliser l’ordre convertit l’acceptation de l’effectivité en devoir de cohérence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-10","CL_UCIC_30:XD-05","CL_UCIC_30:XD-07","CL_UCIC_30:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-05","text":"La nature devient le relais qui ferme le circuit entre puissance divine, organisation politique et conduite individuelle, parce qu’elle exécute matériellement ce que la cité reconnaît normativement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_30:GA-03","CL_UCIC_30:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-01","text":"Ontologiquement, le réel est une hiérarchie de médiations où le vivant devient esprit, l’esprit devient membre d’une cité et la cité devient la forme morale de la machine cosmique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-02","text":"Politiquement, la souveraineté ne gouverne pas seulement des sujets ; elle détermine les conditions sous lesquelles pluralité, gloire, finalité et justice deviennent pensables comme unité.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B04","CL_UCIC_30:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-03","text":"Épistémiquement, connaître vaut lorsque la connaissance devient participation opératoire : elle reproduit localement l’ordre, reconnaît sa source et consent à ce qui excède son propre point de vue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-04","text":"Temporellement, l’histoire n’est pas un espace d’amélioration globale mais le milieu où la transformation des facultés, la maturation de la cité et le délai rétributif rendent l’ordre progressivement habitable sans le rendre révisable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-05","text":"Méthodologiquement, le système transforme chaque dualisme en relation asymétrique : l’opposition ne disparaît pas, mais devient la médiation par laquelle un ordre supérieur capture ses termes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-06","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-06","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-01","text":"Vie continue → élévation des facultés → image architectonique → société divine : la spiritualisation revient confirmer que la continuité initiale contenait déjà une capacité de participation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_28:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-02","text":"Pluralité des esprits → cité monarchique → gloire reconnue → confirmation de l’unité : le gouvernement produit la totalité dont il apparaît ensuite comme la forme nécessaire.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_29:RLE-03","CL_UCIC_29:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-03","text":"Finalité spirituelle → Nature médiatrice → rétribution différée → confirmation de la Providence : l’effet naturel redevient preuve de la cause finale qui l’ordonne.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-04","text":"L’attracteur commun est une unité divine distribuée : la différenciation des agents et des ordres augmente leur intégration au lieu de produire une autonomie concurrente.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B01","text":"Continuité vivante → mobilité des facultés → esprit comme puissance dérivée capable de connaître et d’imiter localement l’ordre.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B02","CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B02","text":"Puissances spirituelles locales → pluralité totalisée → cité morale → monarchie comme forme de coordination de la perfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:XD-06","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B03","text":"Cité monarchique → communauté connaissante et admirante → gloire divine comme réception collective des perfections divines.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B04","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B04","text":"Distinction des causes → analogie nature/grâce → double fonction architecte/monarque → coordination sans fusion des ordres.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B05","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_29:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B05","text":"Coordination cosmico-politique → Nature comme exécution de la loi → rétribution corporelle et temporelle → justice rendue immanente aux événements.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B02","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B06","text":"Justice immanente mais non immédiatement visible → sujet actif dans le devoir et passif devant l’issue → intégration pratique au gouvernement non améliorable du tout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B05","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AFM-B01","text":"Continuité vitale → différenciation des facultés → esprit-image → imitation architectonique → puissance locale relationnelle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AFM-B02","text":"Puissances locales → pluralité spirituelle → cité universelle → monarchie morale → gloire divine reconnue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B02","CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AFM-B03","text":"Monarchie coordonnatrice → Nature légiférée → rétribution différée → division active/passive du sujet → acceptation de l’optimalité providentielle.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_30:MME-03","CL_UCIC_30:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-01","text":"L’opposition animal/humain est remplacée par une cartographie graduelle des régimes de participation, allant de la sensibilité à la puissance architectonique et à l’appartenance civique divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MME-01","CL_UCIC_28:MME-05","CL_UCIC_28:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-02","text":"La politique est reclassée comme structure ontologique : une totalité d’esprits ne possède pas d’abord une forme politique, elle existe pleinement en la produisant.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:BSD-01","CL_UCIC_29:MME-01","CL_UCIC_29:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-03","text":"La Nature devient une catégorie stratégique hybride, à la fois milieu causal, appareil juridique, traduction de la Providence et limite de la critique humaine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:MME-01","CL_UCIC_30:MME-02","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-04","text":"La fausse opposition entre dépendance et activité s’effondre : l’agent n’agit correctement qu’en tant que son action est située, dérivée et orientée vers une finalité qui le dépasse.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MME-06","CL_UCIC_30:XD-03","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets explicites sont l’âme, l’esprit, la cité, la monarchie, la Nature, les corps, les catastrophes, les récompenses et les peines.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Ces objets sont organisés par une chaîne unique de médiations reliant continuité, représentation, gouvernement, causalité, finalité et rétribution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — Le système transforme les oppositions en positions intégrables, puis déplace toute contestation de l’ordre vers une correction de la position subjective qui juge.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B03","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B03","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel est une architecture finalisée dont les distinctions de niveau persistent dans le temps, tandis que la justice peut être différée sans être suspendue.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — L’argument accomplit sa thèse en reconduisant chaque séparation vers une unité supérieure, sans effacer les différences fonctionnelles dont dépend cette reconduction.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-01","text":"L’affirmation d’une continuité graduelle du vivant entre en tension avec la hiérarchie politique et spirituelle qui confère à certains êtres un privilège de participation irréductible à un simple degré.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FL-01","CL_UCIC_28:MP-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-02","text":"La puissance locale est requise pour que l’esprit participe à l’ordre, mais cette même puissance est subordonnée à une monarchie et à une Providence qui refusent tout point de vue autonome.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FL-02","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-03","text":"La justice providentielle dépend de mécanismes naturels présentés comme réels, mais leur subordination finale rend fragile la frontière entre causalité propre et simple exécution d’une volonté supérieure.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:FL-01","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-01","text":"La première mutation décisive survient lorsque l’identité persistante de l’âme devient capacité de changer de fonction, ouvrant le passage de la conservation à l’élévation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MP-01","CL_UCIC_28:RMD-02","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-02","text":"La seconde mutation survient lorsque la représentation devient architecture : connaître l’ordre ne signifie plus le refléter, mais en reproduire localement les principes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MP-02","CL_UCIC_28:MP-03","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-03","text":"La mutation terminale survient lorsque l’action morale est scindée entre devoir présumé et événement effectif, transformant l’agent en opérateur actif d’un ordre qu’il doit passivement recevoir.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:MP-03","CL_UCIC_30:XD-03","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-01","text":"La réalité est implicitement une architecture vivante et gouvernementale dont chaque niveau produit le suivant : vie, esprit, cité, nature et justice sont des régimes enchâssés d’une même machine divine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet est une puissance locale capable d’imiter et d’agir, mais sa liberté opératoire n’est admise que comme département d’une souveraineté plus vaste.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est le dispositif par lequel l’ordre transforme sans se réformer : il élève les facultés, stabilise les hiérarchies et diffère la justice afin d’empêcher que l’événement apparent devienne tribunal du réel.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-04","text":"La seule navigation admise consiste à changer de régime à l’intérieur de l’ordre — élever sa puissance, servir la cité, accomplir le devoir — jamais à sortir de la Providence ni à en reconfigurer le tout.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-04","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-04","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale est suffisante si elle conserve six invariants : continuité vivante, puissance spirituelle dérivée, politisation de la pluralité, coordination des ordres, naturalisation de la justice et dessaisissement final du sujet.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B02","text":"La cohérence dépend de trois tensions irréductibles : continuité et privilège, activité et dépendance, distinction réelle des ordres et intégration totale de leurs fonctions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B03","text":"L’indétermination persiste quant aux mécanismes concrets de l’élévation spirituelle, de l’assemblage des esprits et de la rétribution naturelle ; elle n’empêche pas de reconstruire l’architecture, mais interdit de la convertir en causalité empirique entièrement spécifiée.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B04","text":"La compression échoue si elle réduit l’ensemble à une théologie de l’ordre : il faut conserver le mouvement génératif par lequel l’ordre devient successivement capacité, cité, Nature et discipline subjective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B02","CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200721961047Z_fd8bec95","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Ucic L1 08","source_sha256":"3cdb97189911e361faaa2aadb5a3e22ce8c766d7f40f8a29336dda0b25665e8d","sha256":"6696ba5f4e4298d2fc671e37ef5d4bbd525720a484b25da4d0630b70d0565347","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:07:21.964678+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B01","text":"The system must resolve how a continuous life can become spirit, how spirits become a city, and how this city renders providential justice immanent to reality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:AS-01","CL_UCIC_29:AS-01","CL_UCIC_30:BAS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B02","text":"The argument refuses the rupture between nature and spirit, then refuses that spirit should remain a private power: divine participation must become relational, political, and cosmic order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_28:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B03","text":"Local spiritual power is first produced as the capacity to know and imitate order; it is then redistributed as membership in a moral monarchy and a universal Providence.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:XD-02","CL_UCIC_30:XD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B04","text":"The movement is an ascent from animation to architectonics, from architectonics to government, then from government to the naturalization of justice.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B02","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B05","text":"Causality is completed only by becoming relation: producing a being requires governing it, receiving its recognition, and inscribing its acts within an economy of reward and punishment.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RMD-06","CL_UCIC_29:XD-03","CL_UCIC_30:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B06","text":"The system progresses through the coordination of maintained distinctions: living being and spirit, machine and city, nature and grace, duty and actuality are not fused but hierarchically articulated.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_29:GNX-05","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B07","text":"Its closure produces a subject locally active but globally dispossessed: it can imitate order, serve the city, and pursue the presumed good, without being able to institute or correct the totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-07","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AS-B08","text":"The terminal attractor is a distributed divine governmentality, in which vital continuity, spiritual plurality, moral monarchy, and natural retribution function as regimes of one and the same order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_29:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The continuity of the living forbids conceiving spirit as a substance without genesis; spiritual elevation therefore retains a structural dependence upon the life it transforms.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-01","CL_UCIC_28:DBN-01","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Divine likeness mutates from inner representation into architectonic power, then into the capacity to occupy a determinate function within a higher government.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-05","CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_28:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-03","text":"[Emergent] A plurality of spirits receives its accomplished form only by becoming a political, moral, and theological city under a common sovereignty.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-02","CL_UCIC_29:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-04","text":"[Persistent] Higher unity does not result from an indistinction of orders, but from their functional coordination under one and the same divine source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CL_UCIC_29:GNX-05","CL_UCIC_29:XD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] God passes from the status of Author of local powers to that of cosmic architect, monarch of spirits, and legislator whose justice is inscribed in natural mechanisms.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:GA-10","CL_UCIC_30:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Divine glory requires a community capable of knowing, admiring, and practically embodying the perfections it receives.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-06","CL_UCIC_29:XD-01","CL_UCIC_30:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-07","text":"[Attractor] Perfection becomes governmental: it organizes the distribution of powers, the unity of the city, the harmony of orders, and the retribution of conduct.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-12","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-04","CL_UCIC_30:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Nature is neither an outside of grace nor an autonomous machine; it becomes the operative mode through which divine government renders purpose, law, and justice effective.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:GA-01","CL_UCIC_30:GA-02","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09","text":"[Terminal] The human or spiritual agent is active in its department, but its activity remains derived, governed, and incapable of constituting a sovereign point of view upon the total order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-10","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_30:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Time renders compatible the elevation of faculties, political mediation, and retributive delay by separating local action from the final intelligibility of the whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_30:RMD-04","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-01","text":"Continuity passes from the transindividual vital ground to the coherence of a spiritual plurality, then to the cosmic unity of a providential order; it thereby ceases to be merely biological.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RMD-01","CL_UCIC_29:RMD-01","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-02","text":"Architecture returns under three distinct functions: local imitation of order, monarchical organization of the city, then mechanical inscription of law in Nature.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B04","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-03","text":"The relation to God shifts from the society of limited powers to the collective recognition of glory, then to the subjective acceptance of an effective, non-totalizable will.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_30:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-04","text":"Perfection reverses its function: a power of participation in spirit, it becomes a principle of centralization in the city, then forbids any human revision of the universal order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_30:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RMD-05","text":"The distinction between nature and grace remains active, but its valence changes: from a gap to be harmonized, it becomes the condition of a single governmentality with two regimes.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GA-09","CL_UCIC_29:MME-05","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-01","text":"The precise mechanisms of conception, animal election, and elevation of faculties remain local; at the current level, they count only as the matrix of a gradual transformation of power into government.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_28:CGD-02","CL_UCIC_28:XD-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-02","text":"The local distinction between architectonic imitation and princely government is recoded at the current scale as the necessary passage from production to the administration of a plurality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_28:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-03","text":"The deduction of perfect monarchy remains an internal machine at the lower level; its present import is to render visible the constitutive politicization of every spiritual totality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-01","CL_UCIC_29:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-04","text":"Catastrophes, bodily delays, and particular mechanisms of punishment remain local; their current integration produces a general temporality in which the absence of immediate visibility becomes compatible with necessary justice.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:CGD-01","CL_UCIC_30:CGD-04","CL_UCIC_30:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:CGD-05","text":"The distinction between presumptive will and consequent will changes scale when it becomes the global protocol distributing local moral activity and passivity before the total outcome.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:CGD-05","CL_UCIC_30:XD-03","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes any absolute rupture between animality, spirit, and divine society, since elevation must remain an internal transformation of living continuity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_28:XD-01","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-02","text":"It excludes autonomous spiritual power: every creative or architectonic capacity must remain local, derived, and inserted within a relational hierarchy.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_28:GNX-05","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-03","text":"It excludes a spiritual community without political form, as well as a collective perfection without organizing sovereignty.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_29:GNX-02","CL_UCIC_29:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-04","text":"It excludes the enduring separation between natural mechanics, moral normativity, and providential purpose.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:GNX-01","CL_UCIC_30:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:GNX-05","text":"Finally, it excludes a human critique of the totality that would claim to assess or reform the world from a point of view external to its government.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:GNX-05","CL_UCIC_30:DBN-04","CL_UCIC_30:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-01","text":"The system holds only if both the materialism of a machine without society and the spiritualism of a power without genesis or dependence are simultaneously rejected.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:DBN-02","CL_UCIC_28:DBN-05","CL_UCIC_28:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-02","text":"It requires that adequate causality already be relational: producing without governing, governing without being recognized, or rewarding without natural mediation would leave the architecture incomplete.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:GNX-04","CL_UCIC_29:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_30:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-03","text":"It disqualifies every pluralism of ultimate principles: architecture, sovereignty, grace, law, nature, and happiness must derive from a single coordinating source.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:GNX-06","CL_UCIC_29:BSA-04","CL_UCIC_30:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:DBN-04","text":"It renders inadmissible a temporality that would give the subject a lasting counterexample to justice; delay can only be mediation, never an effective suspension of order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:GNX-03","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-01","text":"The possibility most deeply excluded is that of an outside: no living being, spirit, natural event, or human judgment can situate itself outside the order that produces it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_29:BSA-03","CL_UCIC_30:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-02","text":"The structuring absence is that of a genuine autonomy of the agent: activity is admitted only as a derived, departmental function oriented by a prior end.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:DBN-04","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSA-03","text":"The system renders unavailable a visible justice, immediately verifiable and susceptible of being judged by its apparent effects; its efficacy depends, on the contrary, upon the temporal opacity of its fulfillment.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:BSA-01","CL_UCIC_30:BSA-02","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-01","text":"Spiritual participation becomes politically necessary insofar as local power can neither ground itself nor by itself coordinate the plurality of analogous powers.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09","CL_UCIC_28:XD-06","CL_UCIC_29:GA-01","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-02","text":"The City transforms knowledge of God into a mechanism of government: collective admiration is not added to political order; it realizes its theological function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-07","CL_UCIC_29:XD-01","CL_UCIC_29:XD-03","CL_UCIC_29:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-03","text":"The identification of the architect and the legislator absorbs the difference between cosmic construction and moral judgment: the world is not judged after the fact; it is constructed as a scene of retribution.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-08","CL_UCIC_30:XD-04","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-04","text":"The subject's cognitive limitation becomes productive for the sovereignty of the whole: the impossibility of totalizing order converts the acceptance of actuality into a duty of coherence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-10","CL_UCIC_30:XD-05","CL_UCIC_30:XD-07","CL_UCIC_30:FL-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:XD-05","text":"Nature becomes the relay that closes the circuit between divine power, political organization, and individual conduct, because it materially executes what the city normatively recognizes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L1_08:GA-08","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-03","CL_UCIC_30:GA-03","CL_UCIC_30:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-01","text":"Ontologically, reality is a hierarchy of mediations in which the living becomes spirit, spirit becomes a member of a city, and the city becomes the moral form of the cosmic machine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-02","text":"Politically, sovereignty does not govern subjects alone; it determines the conditions under which plurality, glory, purpose, and justice become thinkable as unity.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B04","CL_UCIC_30:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-03","text":"Epistemically, knowing has value when knowledge becomes operative participation: it locally reproduces order, recognizes its source, and consents to what exceeds its own point of view.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-02","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-04","text":"Temporally, history is not a space of global improvement but the medium in which the transformation of faculties, the maturation of the city, and retributive delay make order progressively habitable without rendering it revisable.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:BSD-05","text":"Methodologically, the system transforms every dualism into an asymmetrical relation: opposition does not disappear, but becomes the mediation through which a higher order captures its terms.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:BSD-06","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-06","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-01","text":"Continuous life → elevation of faculties → architectonic image → divine society: spiritualization returns to confirm that initial continuity already contained a capacity for participation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_28:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-02","text":"Plurality of spirits → monarchical city → recognized glory → confirmation of unity: government produces the totality of which it subsequently appears as the necessary form.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_29:RLE-03","CL_UCIC_29:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-03","text":"Spiritual purpose → mediating Nature → deferred retribution → confirmation of Providence: the natural effect again becomes proof of the final cause that orders it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:RLE-01","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-02","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:RLE-04","text":"The common attractor is a distributed divine unity: the differentiation of agents and orders increases their integration rather than producing a competing autonomy.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:RLE-05","CL_UCIC_29:GA-11","CL_UCIC_30:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B01","text":"Living continuity → mobility of faculties → spirit as a derived power capable of knowing and locally imitating order.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B02","CL_UCIC_28:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B02","text":"Local spiritual powers → totalized plurality → moral city → monarchy as the form of coordination of perfection.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:XD-06","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B01","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B03","text":"Monarchical city → knowing and admiring community → divine glory as the collective reception of divine perfections.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B04","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B04","text":"Distinction of causes → nature/grace analogy → double architect/monarch function → coordination without fusion of orders.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B05","CL_UCIC_29:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_29:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B05","text":"Cosmico-political coordination → Nature as execution of the law → bodily and temporal retribution → justice rendered immanent to events.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B02","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B03","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FGS-B06","text":"Immanent justice but not immediately visible → subject active in duty and passive before the outcome → practical integration into the unimprovable government of the whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B05","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B06","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AFM-B01","text":"Vital continuity → differentiation of faculties → spirit-image → architectonic imitation → relational local power.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_28:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AFM-B02","text":"Local powers → spiritual plurality → universal city → moral monarchy → recognized divine glory.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B02","CL_UCIC_29:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:AFM-B03","text":"Coordinating monarchy → legislated Nature → deferred retribution → active/passive division of the subject → acceptance of providential optimality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:AFM-B01","CL_UCIC_30:MME-03","CL_UCIC_30:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-01","text":"The animal/human opposition is replaced by a gradual mapping of regimes of participation, extending from sensibility to architectonic power and divine civic membership.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MME-01","CL_UCIC_28:MME-05","CL_UCIC_28:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-02","text":"Politics is reclassified as ontological structure: a totality of spirits does not first possess a political form; it exists fully by producing one.","refs":["CL_UCIC_29:BSD-01","CL_UCIC_29:MME-01","CL_UCIC_29:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-03","text":"Nature becomes a hybrid strategic category, at once causal milieu, juridical apparatus, translation of Providence, and limit of human critique.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:MME-01","CL_UCIC_30:MME-02","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MME-04","text":"The false opposition between dependence and activity collapses: the agent acts correctly only insofar as its action is situated, derived, and oriented toward a purpose that exceeds it.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MME-06","CL_UCIC_30:XD-03","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — The explicit objects are the soul, spirit, city, monarchy, Nature, bodies, catastrophes, rewards, and punishments.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B01","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — These objects are organized by a single chain of mediations linking continuity, representation, government, causality, purpose, and retribution.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B02","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The system transforms oppositions into integrable positions, then displaces every contestation of order toward a correction of the subjective position that judges.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B03","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B03","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Reality is a purposive architecture whose distinctions of level persist over time, while justice can be deferred without being suspended.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B04","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The argument performs its thesis by leading every separation back toward a higher unity, without effacing the functional differences upon which this leading-back depends.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_29:ALT-B05","CL_UCIC_30:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-01","text":"The affirmation of a gradual continuity of the living comes into tension with the political and spiritual hierarchy that grants certain beings a privilege of participation irreducible to a mere degree.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FL-01","CL_UCIC_28:MP-01","CL_UCIC_29:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-02","text":"Local power is required for spirit to participate in order, but that same power is subordinated to a monarchy and a Providence that refuse every autonomous point of view.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:FL-02","CL_UCIC_29:BSD-05","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:FL-03","text":"Providential justice depends on natural mechanisms presented as real, but their final subordination renders fragile the boundary between proper causality and the mere execution of a higher will.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:FL-01","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_30:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-01","text":"The first decisive mutation occurs when the persistent identity of the soul becomes the capacity to change function, opening the passage from preservation to elevation.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MP-01","CL_UCIC_28:RMD-02","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-02","text":"The second mutation occurs when representation becomes architecture: to know order no longer means to reflect it, but to reproduce its principles locally.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MP-02","CL_UCIC_28:MP-03","CL_UCIC_28:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MP-03","text":"The terminal mutation occurs when moral action is split between presumed duty and effective event, transforming the agent into an active operator of an order it must passively receive.","refs":["CL_UCIC_30:MP-03","CL_UCIC_30:XD-03","CL_UCIC_30:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a living and governmental architecture in which each level produces the next: life, spirit, city, nature, and justice are nested regimes of one and the same divine machine.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-01","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a local power capable of imitating and acting, but its operative freedom is admitted only as a department of a more extensive sovereignty.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-02","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-03","text":"Time is the dispositif through which order transforms without reforming itself: it elevates faculties, stabilizes hierarchies, and defers justice in order to prevent the apparent event from becoming the tribunal of reality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-03","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:HSI-04","text":"The only navigation admitted consists in changing regime within order — elevating one's power, serving the city, fulfilling duty — never in leaving Providence or reconfiguring its whole.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:HSI-04","CL_UCIC_29:HSI-04","CL_UCIC_30:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves six invariants: living continuity, derived spiritual power, politicization of plurality, coordination of orders, naturalization of justice, and the subject's final dispossession.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B01","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B02","text":"Coherence depends on three irreducible tensions: continuity and privilege, activity and dependence, real distinction of orders and total integration of their functions.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B04","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B03","text":"Indeterminacy persists concerning the concrete mechanisms of spiritual elevation, the assemblage of spirits, and natural retribution; it does not prevent reconstructing the architecture, but forbids converting it into a fully specified empirical causality.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B03","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"MC_UCIC_L1_08:MRT-B04","text":"Compression fails if it reduces the whole to a theology of order: the generative movement through which order successively becomes capacity, city, Nature, and subjective discipline must be preserved.","refs":["CL_UCIC_28:MRT-B02","CL_UCIC_29:MRT-B05","CL_UCIC_30:MRT-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"MC_UCIC_L1_08@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:MC_UCIC_L1_08:v1","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"MC","kicker":"Meta-cluster · La Monadologie","title":"Ucic L1 08","context":"Chapters 82–90 · Proposition 82 · Proposition 83 · Proposition 84 · Proposition 85 · Proposition 86 · Proposition 87 · Proposition 88 · Proposition 89 · Proposition 90"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"WB_UCIC","layer":"WB","title":"Monadology","order":1,"parents":["MC_UCIC_L2_01","MC_UCIC_L2_02"],"revision":"WB_UCIC@R002","sha256":"7080d4cf4610811f89527fe18389df892b6b2a287baab0c3de5e7d8a8d8b1f09","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-01","text":"Le problème directeur consiste à maintenir une pluralité réelle de substances, de corps, de vivants et d’esprits tout en refusant que le composé ou l’événement puisse fonder sa propre unité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-02","text":"La thèse globale établit que toute unité dérivée doit conjuguer une différence intérieure active avec une dépendance ontologique qui lui interdit de devenir son propre principe.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-02","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-03","text":"La fermeture des substances à l’importation causale ne produit pas leur isolement, mais exige une concordance globale sans transmission directe.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-04","text":"La raison suffisante transforme progressivement la demande locale d’explication en une grammaire générale de fondation, de sélection, de coordination et de gouvernement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-05","text":"Le corps organisé matérialise cette grammaire en focalisant l’ordre total dans une perspective finie et en déplaçant l’identité vers la persistance d’une organisation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-06","text":"L’événement présent perd toute autonomie originaire : perception, action, génération, mort et sanction deviennent des effets de médiations antérieures ou des reconfigurations d’un ordre déjà constitué.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-07","text":"Le mouvement du livre est régressif vers le fondement, distributif dans les êtres dérivés, puis récursivement ascendant vers l’organisation, l’harmonie et la gouvernementalité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-08","text":"La clôture terminale est une totalité sans extérieur absolu dont l’unité dépend de la différenciation interne et dont l’opacité aux positions finies protège la souveraineté structurelle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Aucun composé, événement ou fait local ne peut constituer un fondement ultime ni porter seul la raison de son unité ou de son existence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] La simplicité passe de l’absence de parties à la concentration d’une différence active, puis s’étend en organisation capable de persister à travers la variation matérielle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] La causalité constitutive ne peut être une transmission directe de déterminations entre substances, séries ou foyers d’organisation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] La raison suffisante devient successivement principe de fondation, distribution modale, sélection de compatibilités et gouvernement de fonctions différenciées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] Le corps organisé est l’opérateur transversal qui convertit l’expression universelle en perspective localisée, continuité vivante et position fonctionnelle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] L’unité du réel ne supprime pas la différence : elle la produit et la coordonne sous forme de qualités, perceptions, degrés, séries et fonctions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] L’identité cesse d’être immobilité substantielle pour devenir cohérence temporelle d’une trajectoire, persistance organisationnelle et maintien d’une fonction.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] Aucun événement n’est absolument inaugural ou terminal : tout présent résulte de médiations antérieures et manifeste une disposition déjà inscrite dans l’ordre.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] L’activité créée est réelle mais dérivée : elle produit ses transitions propres sans instituer ni évaluer souverainement la totalité qui la rend possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] La limitation cognitive n’est pas seulement une privation ; elle constitue la perspective finie et empêche qu’une position locale ne se confonde avec le fondement total.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] La nécessité fondatrice s’accomplit en totalité providentielle sans extérieur, dans laquelle possibilité, existence, organisation et gouvernement restent différenciés mais ultimement cofondés.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-01","text":"La simplicité conserve sa fonction anti-compositionnelle, mais sa fonction positive migre de l’intériorité perceptive vers les focalisations organiques et fonctionnelles de l’ordre.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-02","text":"La clôture interne se déplace de la causalité monadique vers le parallélisme des séries : l’absence d’intrusion devient la condition d’une coordination architecturale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-03","text":"La raison suffisante mute d’une exigence régressive de fondement en opérateur positif de distribution des possibles, des perfectionnements et des fonctions gouvernementales.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-04","text":"La perception se prolonge en expression, puis l’expression migre vers le corps, la trajectoire vivante et la médiation cosmico-politique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-05","text":"L’identité trajectorielle est absorbée dans une structure d’ordre supérieur où l’organisation corporelle devient le modèle de la persistance à travers le renouvellement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-06","text":"La dépendance différenciée passe du statut d’attracteur ontologique à celui d’unité divine distribuée, capable d’intégrer sans fusion les niveaux naturels, vitaux, spirituels et politiques.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-07","text":"L’opacité finie inverse sa valence : d’abord limite de l’accès aux médiations, elle devient condition positive de la perspective et mécanisme de clôture gouvernementale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-01","text":"Les cas de sommeil, de semence, de préformation ou de transformation corporelle restent locaux ; à l’échelle du livre, ils ne valent que comme tests d’une continuité perceptive ou organisationnelle antérieure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-02","text":"Les exclusions locales de l’étendue, de l’intrusion et de l’inertie changent d’échelle lorsqu’elles deviennent une grammaire commune de causalité, de temporalité, d’organisation et de coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-03","text":"Le corps organisé relie les deux architectures inférieures : il transpose la multiplicité enveloppée de la monade en focalisation matérielle, vivante et perspectivale du tout.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-04","text":"La nécessité, d’abord terme de la régression fondatrice, change de portée lorsqu’elle devient la condition ontologique d’une Nature politiquement et providentiellement organisée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-05","text":"Les mécanismes causaux locaux deviennent obsolètes comme explications autonomes dès que l’action est recodée en problème d’architecture, de correspondance et de fonction.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-06","text":"La reconduction actuelle de l’existence et la persistance organique absorbent les seuils locaux de création, de naissance et de mort dans une continuité de transformations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-01","text":"Le système exclut que l’agrégat, la partie inerte ou la simplicité matérielle puisse produire sa propre unité explicative.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-02","text":"Il exclut toute causalité conçue comme transport, échange ou pénétration directe d’une intériorité par une autre.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-03","text":"Il exclut le fait brut et les seuils absolus, de sorte qu’aucun présent, commencement ou anéantissement ne puisse valoir comme explication terminale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-04","text":"Il exclut tout dehors principiel, tout possible autonome et toute pluralité de principes ultimes capables de concurrencer la nécessité fondatrice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-05","text":"Il exclut le sujet transparent et l’esprit souverain qui posséderaient intégralement les médiations ou jugeraient le gouvernement total depuis l’extérieur.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-06","text":"Il exclut simultanément la fragmentation en mondes indépendants et l’unification homogène qui abolirait les séries, degrés et fonctions différenciés.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-01","text":"Pour que l’architecture tienne, la différence ne peut provenir d’un second absolu ni les domaines naturels, spirituels et politiques dépendre de principes ultimes pluriels.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-02","text":"Aucune opération locale ne peut universaliser son régime ni devenir la cause ou le tribunal souverain de la totalité dont elle dépend.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-03","text":"L’organisation ne peut disparaître dans une régression indéfinie de constituants composés ; elle doit persister sous des formes plus profondes à chaque changement d’échelle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-04","text":"La médiation doit être objectivement effective sans devenir totalement transparente à la position finie, faute de quoi la perspective locale absorberait abusivement le tout.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-05","text":"La limitation réelle ne peut être ni un principe indépendant ni une imperfection de la source, alors même que la hiérarchie requiert des privilèges différenciés de participation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSA-01","text":"La possibilité la plus radicalement indisponible est un dehors où nécessité, relation, organisation et gouvernement cesseraient ensemble sans supprimer toute détermination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSA-02","text":"Une nouveauté absolument autonome est inadmissible : aucun être, acte ou vouloir ne peut ajouter au réel une détermination indépendante de l’ordre qui le rend possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSA-03","text":"La totalité interdit silencieusement le point de vue fini intégralement transparent qui pourrait totaliser l’ordre, en suspendre la juridiction et instituer un contre-jugement souverain.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-01","text":"L’intériorité causale et la concordance globale composent une action à double face : chaque foyer produit ses transitions propres tandis que leur compatibilité dépend d’une coordination qui les dépasse.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-03","WB_UCIC:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-02","text":"L’effectivité d’un mécanisme local devient l’indice, non la clôture, de son explication : toute opération observable renvoie à une antériorité organisationnelle puis à une fondation plus profonde.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-01","WB_UCIC:GA-04","WB_UCIC:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-03","text":"La simplicité active et l’organisation corporelle engendrent une identité multiscalaire où l’unité se conserve par la production de variations perceptives, matérielles et fonctionnelles.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-02","WB_UCIC:GA-05","WB_UCIC:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-04","text":"La création continuée et la négation des seuils absolus convergent vers une ontologie de la maintenance : exister signifie être reconduit à travers des transformations qui ne sont ni créations locales ni annihilations.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-08","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-05","text":"La dépendance ontologique devient assignation fonctionnelle lorsque l’activité intérieure réelle est intégrée à un ordre qui lui refuse toute souveraineté sur sa finalité totale.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-09","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-06","text":"L’opacité finie et le différé de la justice forment une boucle de légitimation : l’impossibilité de juger immédiatement le tout autorise le gouvernement, dont le délai reconfirme cette impossibilité.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-10","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-07","text":"L’accumulation des exclusions ne laisse pas un vide théorique ; elle produit positivement une architecture dense de médiations, de continuités et de fonctions coordonnées.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-01","WB_UCIC:GA-03","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-01","text":"Le réel devient une hiérarchie sans extérieur de centres perceptifs, d’organisations corporelles, de séries vivantes et de fonctions gouvernementales enchâssées dans une même coordination.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-05","WB_UCIC:GA-06","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-02","text":"La causalité devient une administration de compatibilités où constituer, percevoir, exprimer, organiser, actualiser et gouverner restent des fonctions articulées mais irréductibles à un mécanisme unique.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-03","WB_UCIC:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-03","text":"Le sujet devient un centre incorporé de perceptions, de mémoire, de persistance et de devoir, actif dans sa fonction mais incapable de posséder ou de réviser le tout.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-05","WB_UCIC:GA-09","WB_UCIC:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-04","text":"Le temps devient une profondeur stratifiée qui conjoint succession perceptive, accumulation des médiations, reconduction de l’existence, transformation organisationnelle et délai rétributif.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-07","WB_UCIC:GA-08","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-05","text":"La politique devient une dimension ontologique lorsque la Nature articule causalité, normativité et Providence tout en limitant la compétence souveraine des agents locaux.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-09","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-06","text":"La connaissance adéquate ne totalise pas le système ; elle reconstruit les régimes de liaison et suit généalogiquement les conversions d’échelle qui rendent les objets locaux possibles.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-04","WB_UCIC:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-07","text":"L’intervention admissible ne vise pas une sortie du système, mais une modification située de clarté, de puissance, de fonction ou de participation à l’intérieur de ses dépendances.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-09","WB_UCIC:GA-10","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-01","text":"La voie d’escalade dominante suit la chaîne : régression vers le fondement → simplicité active → différence perceptive → raison suffisante → expression → organisation → harmonie → gouvernement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-02","text":"La boucle apophatique retire un dehors explicatif, découvre une médiation interne plus profonde, étend l’ordre à cette médiation puis recommence l’exclusion au niveau suivant.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-03","text":"La boucle identitaire transforme la variation en conservation : la différenciation interne produit une trajectoire, l’incorporation stabilise cette trajectoire et la fonction lui assigne une position durable.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-04","text":"La clôture monadique appelle la coordination globale, tandis que cette coordination confirme que les unités n’ont pas besoin d’échanger directement leurs déterminations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-05","text":"La boucle d’opacité transforme l’incapacité de la position finie à s’autofonder en condition de la souveraineté du tout, puis utilise cette souveraineté pour confirmer la limitation locale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-06","text":"L’attracteur terminal est la dépendance différenciée devenue unité distribuée : toute autonomie apparente y est réabsorbée comme activité interne, persistance organisée ou fonction subordonnée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B01","text":"La machine conceptuelle reçoit une pluralité de réalités dérivées et retire au composé, au fait brut et à l’événement local toute capacité d’auto-fondation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B02","text":"La machine dérive une unité simple active, ferme cette unité à l’importation causale et localise son changement dans une différenciation interne.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B03","text":"La machine convertit l’insuffisance du contingent en coupure de niveau, puis absorbe les conditions de possibilité et d’intelligibilité dans une nécessité sans dehors.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-06","MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B04","text":"La machine redistribue cette fondation sous forme d’expression et de concordance, de sorte que le tout se module dans chaque unité sans communication directe ni répétition identique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B05","text":"La machine matérialise l’expression dans le corps organisé, récursive les parties et nie les seuils absolus afin de produire une persistance vivante à travers le changement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B06","text":"La machine élève la persistance jusqu’aux fonctions spirituelles et politiques, puis scinde l’action morale entre obligation locale et justice globale différée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B07","text":"La machine se ferme récursivement lorsque chaque extérieur présumé est reclassé comme médiation interne, changement de degré ou fonction d’une relation réelle sans dehors.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B01","text":"Composé manifeste → insuffisance de l’agrégat → refus du fait brut → exigence d’une relation fondatrice → unité simple active.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B02","text":"Unité simple active → différence interne → perception et appétition → succession qualitative → identité comme variation non divisante.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B03","text":"Intériorité close → impossibilité du transfert direct → expression parallèle → concordance sans transmission → ordre global coordonné.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B04","text":"Expression globale → corps comme foyer d’organisation → récursion matérielle → négation des seuils absolus → persistance organique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B05","text":"Persistance vivante → pluralité des esprits → distribution des fonctions → gouvernement naturel → justice immanente mais différée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B06","text":"Gouvernement total → activité locale subordonnée → impossibilité de sortie → retour à une architecture de dépendance différenciée sans extérieur principiel.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-01","text":"L’opposition unité/multiplicité est remplacée par une carte distinguant composition externe, différenciation interne, emboîtement organisationnel et coordination hiérarchique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-02","text":"La causalité n’est plus un transfert uniforme mais une succession de régimes de constitution, d’expression, d’organisation, de compatibilité et de gouvernement.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-03","text":"L’opposition identité/devenir s’effondre au profit d’une persistance différentielle qui traverse les perceptions, les transformations matérielles et les trajectoires vivantes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-04","text":"Le sujet est reclassé comme nœud fini d’opérations dans une architecture où la politique constitue une dimension de l’ordre ontologique plutôt qu’un domaine extérieur.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-05","text":"La méthode adéquate devient apophatico-constructive, topologique et généalogique : elle suit les exclusions, les changements d’échelle et les fonctions plutôt que des objets isolés.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-06","text":"L’événement est reclassé comme manifestation visible d’un ordre antérieur, ce qui déplace l’analyse du commencement apparent vers les conditions de sa reconfiguration.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Les objets manifestes sont le composé, la monade, la perception, le corps, les organismes, les animaux, les esprits, les cités, la Nature et les sanctions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — Ces objets sont produits par des unités simples, des médiations causales, la raison suffisante, des organisations récursives et des séries coordonnées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — L’enquête quitte les agents ou propriétés isolés pour reconstruire les régimes de liaison et les conditions structurelles de leur apparente autonomie.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — Le réel est une stratification de dépendances dont le temps distribue succession, persistance, transformation et rétribution sans produire de commencement absolu.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — L’argumentation accomplit sa thèse en transformant chaque exclusion structurale en médiation positive et en restituant les fonctions des termes qu’elle retire.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:FL-01","text":"L’activité intérieure doit être assez réelle pour éviter le passivisme, mais assez dérivée pour ne jamais menacer la souveraineté du fondement ou du gouvernement total.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FL-02","text":"La coordination sans transmission ferme les voies causales directes, mais l’expression, l’harmonie et la correspondance demeurent insuffisamment déterminées comme mécanismes positifs.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FL-03","text":"La totalité parfaite doit produire une limitation réelle et des privilèges hiérarchiques sans attribuer leur imperfection à sa propre source ni à un principe concurrent.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FL-04","text":"L’obligation morale locale exige une activité effective, tandis que la justice providentielle différée rend incertaine la frontière entre action propre, exécution et passivité devant l’issue totale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MP-01","text":"La première mutation décisive survient lorsque la simplicité cesse d’être une négation de la composition et devient la condition positive d’une intériorité différenciée.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MP-01","MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MP-02","text":"La deuxième mutation survient lorsque l’influence transitive est renversée et que l’action devient un problème d’architecture, de correspondance et de séries coordonnées.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MP-03","text":"La troisième mutation survient lorsque le corps cesse d’être un support et devient le relais organisateur de l’identité à travers le renouvellement matériel.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MP-04","text":"La mutation terminale transforme la raison explicative en gouvernement : la fondation du réel devient simultanément administration naturelle, hiérarchie politique et différé normatif.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:HSI-01","text":"La réalité implicite est une machine hiérarchique de foyers internes et de médiations récursives qui transforme toute frontière en changement de niveau.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:HSI-02","text":"Le sujet est une chambre ontologique devenue focalisation incarnée : il déploie sa différence intérieure tout en occupant une fonction perceptive, animale, morale et civique.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:HSI-03","text":"Le temps est une machine de succession, de maintenance, de préconfiguration et de délai qui transforme l’ordre sans fournir un point extérieur pour le réformer.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:HSI-04","text":"La navigation possible consiste à distinguer les régimes et à modifier une position interne de clarté, de puissance ou de participation, jamais à sortir de la totalité.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B01","text":"La reconstruction minimale est suffisante si elle conserve l’anti-composition, la simplicité active, la raison suffisante, la clôture causale, l’organisation corporelle, la persistance vivante, la coordination non transitive et le gouvernement providentiel.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B02","text":"L’indétermination irréductible concerne le mécanisme de l’enveloppement perceptif, de l’expression, de l’harmonie, du passage de la perfection à la limitation et de la rétribution concrète.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B03","text":"La compression reste fidèle seulement si elle préserve les différences entre fondation, causalité, expression, organisation, continuité et gouvernement au lieu de les réduire à un vocabulaire invariant.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B04","text":"La cohérence dépend du retour récursif de la même exigence à travers des fonctions mutantes, non d’un séquençage linéaire ni d’une identité lexicale constante.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B05","text":"La force performative de l’architecture négative résiste à la réduction axiomatique : les exclusions ne sont pas des ornements, mais les opérations qui engendrent les médiations positives du système.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"fr","language_name":"Français","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261112T200857242158Z_fe6719b8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Monadology","source_sha256":"7080d4cf4610811f89527fe18389df892b6b2a287baab0c3de5e7d8a8d8b1f09","sha256":"57afa5a925bb51dd0a06589023f3b2b693316c87987dd9f4f9583de3dd6b26c3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-11-12T20:08:57.247605+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-01","text":"The guiding problem consists in maintaining a real plurality of substances, bodies, living beings, and minds while refusing that the composite or the event can ground its own unity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-02","text":"The overall thesis establishes that every derived unity must combine an active internal difference with an ontological dependence that prevents it from becoming its own principle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-02","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-03","text":"The closure of substances to causal importation does not produce their isolation, but requires a global concordance without direct transmission.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-04","text":"Sufficient reason progressively transforms the local demand for explanation into a general grammar of grounding, selection, coordination, and government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-05","text":"The organized body materializes this grammar by focusing the total order within a finite perspective and by displacing identity toward the persistence of an organization.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-06","text":"The present event loses all originary autonomy: perception, action, generation, death, and sanction become effects of prior mediations or reconfigurations of an already constituted order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-07","text":"The movement of the book is regressive toward the ground, distributive among derived beings, then recursively ascending toward organization, harmony, and governmentality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AS-08","text":"The terminal closure is a totality without an absolute outside, whose unity depends on internal differentiation and whose opacity to finite positions protects structural sovereignty.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] No composite, event, or local fact can constitute an ultimate ground or alone bear the reason for its unity or existence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Simplicity passes from the absence of parts to the concentration of an active difference, then extends into an organization capable of persisting through material variation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Constitutive causality cannot be a direct transmission of determinations between substances, series, or centers of organization.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Sufficient reason successively becomes a principle of grounding, modal distribution, selection of compatibilities, and government of differentiated functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-05","text":"[Emergent] The organized body is the transversal operator that converts universal expression into localized perspective, living continuity, and functional position.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] The unity of the real does not suppress difference: it produces and coordinates it in the form of qualities, perceptions, degrees, series, and functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Identity ceases to be substantial immobility and becomes the temporal coherence of a trajectory, organizational persistence, and maintenance of a function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-08","text":"[Persistent] No event is absolutely inaugural or terminal: every present results from prior mediations and manifests a disposition already inscribed in the order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-09","text":"[Attractor] Created activity is real but derived: it produces its own transitions without sovereignly instituting or assessing the totality that makes it possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-10","text":"[Emergent] Cognitive limitation is not merely a privation; it constitutes finite perspective and prevents a local position from being conflated with the total ground.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Foundational necessity is fulfilled in a providential totality without an outside, in which possibility, existence, organization, and government remain differentiated but are ultimately co-grounded.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-01","text":"Simplicity retains its anti-compositional function, but its positive function migrates from perceptual interiority toward the organic and functional focalizations of order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-02","text":"Internal closure shifts from monadic causality to the parallelism of series: the absence of intrusion becomes the condition of an architectural coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-03","text":"Sufficient reason mutates from a regressive requirement of grounding into a positive operator for the distribution of possibles, perfections, and governmental functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-04","text":"Perception extends into expression, then expression migrates toward the body, the living trajectory, and cosmico-political mediation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-05","text":"Trajectorial identity is absorbed into a higher-order structure in which bodily organization becomes the model of persistence through renewal.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-09","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-06","text":"Differentiated dependence passes from the status of ontological attractor to that of distributed divine unity, capable of integrating without fusion the natural, vital, spiritual, and political levels.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RMD-07","text":"Finite opacity reverses its valence: initially a limit on access to mediations, it becomes the positive condition of perspective and a mechanism of governmental closure.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-01","text":"Cases of sleep, seed, preformation, or bodily transformation remain local; at the scale of the book, they count only as tests of a prior perceptual or organizational continuity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-02","text":"The local exclusions of extension, intrusion, and inertia change scale when they become a common grammar of causality, temporality, organization, and coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-03","text":"The organized body connects the two lower architectures: it transposes the enveloped multiplicity of the monad into a material, living, and perspectival focalization of the whole.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-04","text":"Necessity, initially the terminus of foundational regression, changes scope when it becomes the ontological condition of a politically and providentially organized Nature.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-05","text":"Local causal mechanisms become obsolete as autonomous explanations as soon as action is recoded as a problem of architecture, correspondence, and function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:CGD-06","text":"The current renewal of existence and organic persistence absorb the local thresholds of creation, birth, and death into a continuity of transformations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-01","text":"The system excludes the possibility that the aggregate, the inert part, or material simplicity can produce its own explanatory unity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-02","text":"It excludes every causality conceived as transport, exchange, or direct penetration of one interiority by another.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-03","text":"It excludes the brute fact and absolute thresholds, so that no present, beginning, or annihilation can count as a terminal explanation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-04","text":"It excludes every principial outside, every autonomous possible, and every plurality of ultimate principles capable of competing with foundational necessity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GNX-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-05","text":"It excludes the transparent subject and the sovereign mind that would possess mediations in their entirety or judge total government from outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:GNX-06","text":"It simultaneously excludes fragmentation into independent worlds and homogeneous unification that would abolish differentiated series, degrees, and functions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-01","text":"For the architecture to hold, difference cannot derive from a second absolute, nor can natural, spiritual, and political domains depend on plural ultimate principles.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-02","text":"No local operation can universalize its regime or become the sovereign cause or tribunal of the totality on which it depends.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-03","text":"Organization cannot disappear into an indefinite regress of composite constituents; it must persist under deeper forms at every change of scale.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-04","text":"Mediation must be objectively effective without becoming wholly transparent to the finite position, failing which local perspective would improperly absorb the whole.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:DBN-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:DBN-05","text":"Real limitation can be neither an independent principle nor an imperfection of the source, even though hierarchy requires differentiated privileges of participation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSA-01","text":"The most radically unavailable possibility is an outside in which necessity, relation, organization, and government would together cease without suppressing all determination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSA-02","text":"An absolutely autonomous novelty is inadmissible: no being, act, or willing can add to the real a determination independent of the order that makes it possible.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSA-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSA-03","text":"The totality silently prohibits the wholly transparent finite point of view that could totalize order, suspend its jurisdiction, and institute a sovereign counter-judgment.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-01","text":"Causal interiority and global concordance compose a two-sided action: each center produces its own transitions while their compatibility depends on a coordination that exceeds them.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-03","WB_UCIC:GA-06","MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-02","text":"The effectiveness of a local mechanism becomes the indication, not the closure, of its explanation: every observable operation refers to an organizational anteriority and then to a deeper grounding.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-01","WB_UCIC:GA-04","WB_UCIC:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_01:CGD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-03","text":"Active simplicity and bodily organization generate a multiscalar identity in which unity is preserved through the production of perceptual, material, and functional variations.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-02","WB_UCIC:GA-05","WB_UCIC:GA-07","MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-04","text":"Continued creation and the negation of absolute thresholds converge toward an ontology of maintenance: to exist means to be renewed through transformations that are neither local creations nor annihilations.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-08","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-05","text":"Ontological dependence becomes functional assignment when real inner activity is integrated into an order that refuses it all sovereignty over its total finality.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-09","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-06","text":"Finite opacity and the deferral of justice form a loop of legitimation: the impossibility of immediately judging the whole authorizes government, whose delay reconfirms this impossibility.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-10","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:XD-07","text":"The accumulation of exclusions does not leave a theoretical void; it positively produces a dense architecture of mediations, continuities, and coordinated functions.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-01","WB_UCIC:GA-03","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-01","text":"The real becomes a hierarchy without an outside of perceptual centers, bodily organizations, living series, and governmental functions nested within the same coordination.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-05","WB_UCIC:GA-06","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-02","text":"Causality becomes an administration of compatibilities in which constituting, perceiving, expressing, organizing, actualizing, and governing remain articulated functions but irreducible to a single mechanism.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-03","WB_UCIC:GA-04","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-03","text":"The subject becomes an embodied center of perceptions, memory, persistence, and duty, active in its function but incapable of possessing or revising the whole.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-05","WB_UCIC:GA-09","WB_UCIC:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-04","text":"Time becomes a stratified depth that conjoins perceptual succession, accumulation of mediations, renewal of existence, organizational transformation, and retributive delay.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-07","WB_UCIC:GA-08","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-05","text":"Politics becomes an ontological dimension when Nature articulates causality, normativity, and Providence while limiting the sovereign competence of local agents.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-09","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-06","text":"Adequate knowledge does not totalize the system; it reconstructs regimes of connection and genealogically follows the changes of scale that make local objects possible.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-04","WB_UCIC:GA-10","MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:BSD-07","text":"Admissible intervention does not aim at an exit from the system, but at a situated modification of clarity, power, function, or participation within its dependencies.","refs":["WB_UCIC:GA-09","WB_UCIC:GA-10","WB_UCIC:GA-11","MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-01","text":"The dominant escalation path follows the chain: regression toward the ground → active simplicity → perceptual difference → sufficient reason → expression → organization → harmony → government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-07","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-02","text":"The apophatic loop removes an explanatory outside, discovers a deeper internal mediation, extends order to this mediation, then begins the exclusion again at the next level.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-03","text":"The identity loop transforms variation into conservation: internal differentiation produces a trajectory, embodiment stabilizes this trajectory, and function assigns it a durable position.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-04","text":"Monadic closure calls for global coordination, while this coordination confirms that units need not directly exchange their determinations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:XD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-05","text":"The opacity loop transforms the inability of the finite position to ground itself into a condition of the sovereignty of the whole, then uses this sovereignty to confirm local limitation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:RLE-06","text":"The terminal attractor is differentiated dependence become distributed unity: every apparent autonomy is therein reabsorbed as internal activity, organized persistence, or subordinate function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B01","text":"The conceptual machine receives a plurality of derived realities and withdraws from the composite, the brute fact, and the local event every capacity for self-grounding.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B02","text":"The machine derives an active simple unity, closes this unity to causal importation, and locates its change in an internal differentiation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-02","MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B03","text":"The machine converts the insufficiency of the contingent into a break in level, then absorbs the conditions of possibility and intelligibility into a necessity without an outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-06","MC_UCIC_L2_01:FGS-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B04","text":"The machine redistributes this grounding in the form of expression and concordance, so that the whole is modulated in each unity without direct communication or identical repetition.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B05","text":"The machine materializes expression in the organized body, recursivizes the parts, and negates absolute thresholds in order to produce a living persistence through change.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B06","text":"The machine elevates persistence to spiritual and political functions, then divides moral action between local obligation and deferred global justice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FGS-B07","text":"The machine closes itself recursively when every presumed outside is reclassified as internal mediation, change of degree, or function of a real relation without an outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:FGS-B06","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B01","text":"Manifest composite → insufficiency of the aggregate → refusal of the brute fact → requirement of a grounding relation → active simple unity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B02","text":"Active simple unity → internal difference → perception and appetition → qualitative succession → identity as non-dividing variation.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:GA-05","MC_UCIC_L2_01:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B03","text":"Closed interiority → impossibility of direct transfer → parallel expression → concordance without transmission → coordinated global order.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B04","text":"Global expression → body as center of organization → material recursion → negation of absolute thresholds → organic persistence.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B05","text":"Living persistence → plurality of minds → distribution of functions → natural government → immanent but deferred justice.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:AFM-B06","text":"Total government → subordinate local activity → impossibility of exit → return to an architecture of differentiated dependence without a principial outside.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:AS-08","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-01","text":"The opposition unity/multiplicity is replaced by a map distinguishing external composition, internal differentiation, organizational nesting, and hierarchical coordination.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-02","text":"Causality is no longer a uniform transfer but a succession of regimes of constitution, expression, organization, compatibility, and government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-03","text":"The opposition identity/becoming collapses in favor of a differential persistence that traverses perceptions, material transformations, and living trajectories.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-04","text":"The subject is reclassified as a finite node of operations in an architecture in which politics constitutes a dimension of ontological order rather than an external domain.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MME-04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-05","text":"The adequate method becomes apophatico-constructive, topological, and genealogical: it follows exclusions, changes of scale, and functions rather than isolated objects.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MME-06","text":"The event is reclassified as the visible manifestation of a prior order, which displaces analysis from apparent beginning toward the conditions of its reconfiguration.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:AS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B01","text":"Surface level — Manifest objects are the composite, the monad, perception, the body, organisms, animals, minds, cities, Nature, and sanctions.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B02","text":"Structural level — These objects are produced by simple unities, causal mediations, sufficient reason, recursive organizations, and coordinated series.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B03","text":"Metastrategic level — The inquiry leaves isolated agents or properties in order to reconstruct the regimes of connection and the structural conditions of their apparent autonomy.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B04","text":"Ontological / Temporal level — The real is a stratification of dependencies, whose time distributes succession, persistence, transformation, and retribution without producing an absolute beginning.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B04","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:ALT-B05","text":"Methodological / Performative level — The argumentation performs its thesis by transforming every structural exclusion into positive mediation and by restoring the functions of the terms it removes.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:FL-01","text":"Inner activity must be real enough to avoid passivism, yet derived enough never to threaten the sovereignty of the ground or of total government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FL-02","text":"Coordination without transmission closes the paths of direct causality, but expression, harmony, and correspondence remain insufficiently determined as positive mechanisms.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FL-03","text":"The perfect totality must produce real limitation and hierarchical privileges without attributing their imperfection to its own source or to a competing principle.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:FL-04","text":"Local moral obligation requires effective activity, whereas deferred providential justice renders uncertain the boundary between proper action, execution, and passivity before the total outcome.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:FL-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:AFM-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MP-01","text":"The first decisive mutation occurs when simplicity ceases to be a negation of composition and becomes the positive condition of a differentiated interiority.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MP-01","MC_UCIC_L2_01:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MP-02","text":"The second mutation occurs when transitive influence is overturned and action becomes a problem of architecture, correspondence, and coordinated series.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MP-03","text":"The third mutation occurs when the body ceases to be a support and becomes the organizing relay of identity through material renewal.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:MP-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MP-04","text":"The terminal mutation transforms explanatory reason into government: the grounding of the real simultaneously becomes natural administration, political hierarchy, and normative deferral.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:RMD-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MME-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:HSI-01","text":"Implicit reality is a hierarchical machine of internal centers and recursive mediations that transforms every boundary into a change of level.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:HSI-02","text":"The subject is an ontological chamber become embodied focalization: it unfolds its inner difference while occupying a perceptual, animal, moral, and civic function.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:HSI-03","text":"Time is a machine of succession, maintenance, preconfiguration, and delay that transforms order without providing an external point from which to reform it.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:BSD-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:HSI-04","text":"Possible navigation consists in distinguishing regimes and modifying an internal position of clarity, power, or participation, never in leaving the totality.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:HSI-03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B01","text":"The minimal reconstruction is sufficient if it preserves anti-composition, active simplicity, sufficient reason, causal closure, bodily organization, living persistence, non-transitive coordination, and providential government.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B01","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B02","text":"Irreducible indeterminacy concerns the mechanism of perceptual envelopment, expression, harmony, the passage from perfection to limitation, and concrete retribution.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B02","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B03","text":"Compression remains faithful only if it preserves the differences between grounding, causality, expression, organization, continuity, and government instead of reducing them to an invariant vocabulary.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:MRT-B03","MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence depends on the recursive return of the same requirement through mutating functions, not on linear sequencing or constant lexical identity.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_02:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_UCIC:MRT-B05","text":"The performative force of the negative architecture resists axiomatic reduction: exclusions are not ornaments, but the operations that generate the system's positive mediations.","refs":["MC_UCIC_L2_01:ALT-B05","MC_UCIC_L2_02:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"WB_UCIC@R002","source_variant_id":"canonical:WB_UCIC:WB_UCIC@R002","source_language_code":"fr"}],"identity":{"layer":"WB","kicker":"Whole book","title":"Monadology","context":"","original_title":"La Monadologie"},"original_title":"La Monadologie","title_language_code":"en"}],"seal":"SEAL_UCIC_B06AB6DC614E946DEA71","original_title":"La Monadologie","title_language_code":"en","title_translation":{"schema":"care-title-heading-translation/1","language_code":"en","rendition_type":"machine","originals_preserved":true},"version_work_id":"WORK_STORE_CANON_PG17641","version_label":"Added 12 Nov 2026 · Run 12 Nov 2026 · gpt-5.6-terra / gpt-5.6-sol","version_revision":"425add1b43fdbd4917eee31220f18971fd84ac6e61bbe2901ab4e8dc44b0bf15"},{"id":"WORK_L_IDEA_DEL_THEATRO_DELLO_ECCELLENTE_M_GIULIO_CAMILLO","slug":"beta-ac6f7f99a63ccb92","title":"The Idea of the Theatre","author":"Giulio Camillo","edition":"","year":"1544","historical_date_label":"1544","historical_date_basis":"reviewed_original_work","original_year":1544,"publication_year":null,"description":"","cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-ac6f7f99a63ccb92-8ea87cb9e6cf152c.png","source_url":"","source_notices":{},"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","sources":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT","title":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, BY MESSER GIULIO Camillo.","order":1,"chapter_id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO,\nDI MESSER GIVLIO\nCamillo.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 8, region 2]\n\nI PIV antichi, & più ſani ſcrittori hanno ſempre hauuto in coſtume di raccomandare à loro ſcritti i ſecreti di Dio ſotto oſcuri velami, accioche nõ ſiano inteſi, ſe nõ da coloro, i quali (come dice Chriſto) hanno orecchie da udire, cioè che da Dio ſono eletti ad intendere i ſuoi ſantiſsimi miſteri. Et Meliſſo dice che le orecchie delle anime volgari non poſſono ſofferire i raggi de la diuinità. Et ciò ſi conferma con lo eſſempio di Moſe, il quale ſcendendo dal monte, ſopra il quale, egli anchor per lo mezzo dell’Angelo hauena parlato con Dio, non poteua eſſer guardato dal popolo, ſe egli il viſo co’l uelo non ſi naſ ſcondeua. Et gli apoſtoli anchora veduto Chriſto traſfigu-\nrato, ciò è quaſi partito dalla groſſezza della humanità a la quaſi gloria della diuinità, non ſufficienti a riguardarlo per la debolezza, cadderono. Et nell’Apocalipſi ſi legge. Et ſignificauit mittens per angelum ſuum ſeruo ſuo Ioanni. Doue è da notare, che anchor a Giouanni, con tutto che egli foſſe ſeruo ſuo, non aperſe l’intendimento ſuo ſe non per ſi-\ngnificationi, & per viſioni. Et ueramente ſi come nella mon dana militia ſono adoprate le uoci de Capitani, & le trom be, & le inſegne per conducere & inanimar le armate ſchiere contra i nimici, non in altra maniera nella militia\n\nDigitized by Google\n\nDI M. GIVLI CAMILLO,\n\n4\n\ndiuina habbiamo noi per la voce le parole del ſignor, le angeliche trombe, le quali ſono le voci di Propheti, & de predicatori: & le inſegne, & queſti ſono i ſegni delle viſio ni, le quali ſignificano & non eſprimono. A queſto habbia mo da aggiunger che Mercurio Triſmegillo dice, che il parlar religioso & pien di Dio vien ad eſſer violato quã do gli ſoprauiene moltitudine volgare. La onde non ſenza ragione gli antichi in ſu le porte di qualunque tempio tene uano o dipinta, o ſcolpita vna ſphinga, con quella imagine dimoſtrando che delle coſe di Dio non ſi deue ſe non con enigmi far publicamente parole. Il che in piu maniere ci e ſtato ancora inſegnato da Dio, che parola di Chriſto, e che le margarite non ſi debbiamo gittare à porci, & che à ca ni non vogliamo dar le coſe ſante. Et parlando à gli Apoſtoli ſuoi diſſe loro. Vobis datum eſt noſſe miſteria regni cælorum, cæteris in parabolis, vt videntes non videant & audientes non intelligant. Et nel quarto di Eſdra Dio parlando di Moſe fatto ſalir ſopra il monte di ce. Et detinui eum apud me diebus multis, & narraui ei mirabilia multa temporum ſecreta, & finem & dixi, hæc in palam facies, & hæc abſcondes. Et Dauid à Dio parlando dice, Reuela oculos meos, & conſiderabo mirabilia tua, doue diſſe non di douer paleſar, ma ſo lamente di conſiderar le alte marauiglie. Poi appa-\nrenendo le coſe diuine al ſopraceleſte mondo, & eſſendo quello ſeparato da noi dalla maſſa di tutti i cieli, & non potendo la lingua noſtra giunger alla eſpreſſion di quello ſe non (diro coſi) per cenni & per ſimilitudini; à fine che per lo mezzo delle coſe viſibili ſagliamo alle inuiſibili.\n\nA    iiii\n\nDigitized by Google\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nNon me è lecito anchor che Dio ci deſſe qualche gratia di ascendere al terzo cielo, & di vedere i ſuoi ſecreti, quelli di co non ci è lecito di rivelare, percioche quelli rivelando dop-\npio error ſi viene a commettere. Et cio è di ſcoprirgli a per-\nſone non degne, & di trattargli con queſta noſtra baſſa lingua, eſſendo quello il ſuggetto delle lingue delli angeli. I quali due inconvenienti volendo fuggir, Giovanni ſcriſſe le ſue viſioni ſenza cercar in altra guiſa di dichiararle. Et noi nelle coſe noſtre ci ſerviamo delle imagini, come de ſignificatrici di quelle coſe, che non ſi debbon profanare. Et quanto a Dio ſia caro che le coſe ſue ſiano tenute nella riverenza de loro velami, eſſo medeſimo ne fa fede, chiamando Moſe fedel miniſtro ſuo. Et da Cabaliſti Ezechiel vien chia-\nmato Propheta villano per hauer alla guiſa d’un’huomo di villa ſcoperto tutto quello che egli hauea veduto. Nè ta-\ncero io, che i medeſimi Cabaliſti tengono che Maria ſorel-\nla di Moſe foſſe dalla lebbra oppreſſa per hauer revelate le coſe ſecrete della divinità. Et che per lo medeſimo delitto Ammonio moriſſe di ſporca, & miſera morte. Et tanto ba-\nſtandoci di hauer detto della riverenza di quel ſilentio, nel qual ci habbiamo da tener le coſe ſante, paſſiamo col nome del ſignore a ragionar del noſtro Theatro.\n\nSalomone al nono de Proverbij dice la ſapienza hauerſi edi-\nficato caſa, & hauerla fondata ſopra ſette colonne. Queſte ſette colonne ſignificanti ſtabilſiſſima eternità habbiamo da intender che ſiano le ſette ſaphirot del ſopraceleſte mondo che ſono le ſette miſure della fabrica del celeſte & all’in-\n\niii A\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n5\n\nſeriore, nelle quali ſono compreſe le Idee di tutte le coſe al celeſte, & all’inferiore appartamenti. Di che fuori di queſto numero coſa alcuna non poſſiamo imaginare, queſto ſet tenario è numero perfetto, percioche contiene l’uno & l’al tro ſeſſo, per eſſer fatto di pari & di diſpari, onde volendo dir Virgilio perfettamente beati diſſe, terque quater-\nque. Et Mercurio Triſmegisto nel Pimandro parlando del la creation del mondo, induce ſe medeſimo à domandare. Elementa naturæ unde manarunt? Et Pimandro riſpon de. Ex voluntate Dei, quæ verbum complexa pulcherrimè que intuita mundum, ad eius exemplar reliqua ſui ipſius ele mentis, vitalibusque ſeminibus exornauit. Mens autem De us utriuſque ſexus fœcunditate pleniſſimus vita, & lux tum verbo ſuo mentem alteram opificem peperit, qui quic dem Deus ignis, atque ſpiritus ſeptem deinceps fabricauit gubernatores, qui circulis mundum ſensibilem complectun-\ntur. Et nel vero hauendo la diuinità eſplicate fuori queſte ſette miſure, ſegno è che nello biſſo della ſua diuinità ſia no anchor implicitamente contenute, percioche meno dal quod non habet, queſte colonne Eſſia le chiama femine, quã do dice. Septem mulieres apprehendent ſibi virum vnum. Et chiamale femine, che vuol dir paſſiue, cioè produtte. Ma ſe come dice Paolo: Portat omnia verbo virtutis ſuæ. Et altroue. Vnum in omnibus, & omnia in vno. Et à Coloſſen ſi. Et imago Dei in viſibilis, primogenitus omnis creaturæ, quoniam in ipſo condita ſunt vniuerſa in cœlis & in ter-\nra, viſibilia & inuiſibilia, ſiue Throni, ſiue dominationes, ſiue principatus, ſiue poteſtates, omnia per ipſum & in ipſa ſo creata ſunt. Segue che non poſſiamo trouar maggiore explici-\n\nIn ipſo\nin ipſi\ncœle.\nPer ip\nſunt. i.\nte,\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\npiù capace, che quella di Dio. Hor ſe gli antichi Oratori volendo collocar di giorno in giorno le parti delle orationi che hauerano a recitare, le affidauano a luoghi caduchi, come coſe caduche, ragione è, che volendo noi raccomandar eternalmente gli eterni di tutte le coſe, che poſſono eſſer ne ſſiti di oratione con gli eterni di eſſa oratione, che trouiamo a loro luoghi eterni. L’alta adunque fatica noſtra è ſtata di trouare ordine in queſte ſette miſure, capace baſtante, diſtin to, & che tenga ſempre il ſenſo ſuegliato, & la memoria percoſſa. Ma conſiderando che ſe uoleſſimo mettere alcuni dauanti queſte altissime miſure, & ſi lontane dalla noſtra cognitione, che ſolamente da propheti ſono ſtate anchor ne ſcoſſamente tocche, queſto ſarebbe un metter mano a coſa troppo malageuole. Per tanto in luogo di quelle piglieremo i ſette pianeti, le cui nature anchor da uolgari ſono aſſai be conoſciute, ma talmente le uſeremo, che nō ce le propognia mo come termini, fuor de quali non habbiamo ad uſcire, ma come quelli, che alle menti de ſaui ſempre rappreſentino le ſette ſopracelesti miſure. Et è ben ragione, che ſi come par lando delle coſe inferiori, la loro natura i ſette pianeti ci rappreſenta, ſecondo che queſta a quello, & quella a quel-\nl’altro è ſottopoſta, coſi anchor de pianeti parlando, ci ri-\ntorniamo alla mente quei principii, donde quelli hanno hau-\nto la loro uirtù.\n\nQueſta alta & incomparabile collocatione fa non ſolamen te officio di conſeruarci le affidate coſe parole, & arte, che a man ſalua ad ogni noſtro biſogno informati prima le potremo trouare, ma ci da anchor la uera ſapiença ne fonti di quella menendo noi in cognition delle coſe dalle cagioni, &\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\nnon da gli eſſetti. Il che piu chiaramente eſprimeremo con uno eſſempio. Se noi foſſimo in un g’ran boſcho, & haveſſi mo deſiderio di ben vederlo tutto, in quello ſtando, al deſide rio noſtro no potremmo ſodiſfare, percioche la viſta intorno volgendo, da noi non ſe ne potrebbe veder, ſe non una piccio la parte, impedendoci le piante circonuicine il veder delle lontane, ma ſe vicino a quello vi foſſe una erta, la qual ci re conduceſſe ſopra un’ alto colle, del boſco uſcendo dall’erta comincieremmo a veder in gran parte la forma di quello, poi ſopra il colle aſceſi, tutto intiero il potremmo raffigura re. Il boſco è queſto noſtro mondo inferiore, la erta ſono i Cie li, & il colle il ſopraceleſte mondo. Et a voler bene intēder queſte coſe inferiori è neceſſario di aſcendere alle ſuperio-\nri, & di alto in giù guardando, di queſte potremo haver piu certa cognitione. Di queſto modo di intender par che gli an tichi ſcrittori gentili non ne foſſero al tutto digiuni, di che Maſſimo Tirio allega Homero, che inuiaſſe Vliſſe aſceſo in alta parte conſiderare i coſtumi de gli habitanti. Et Aristotile ci laſciò ſcritto, che ſe noi foſſimo ſopra i cieli, ſi potrebb be da noi conoſcere l’Ecliſſi del Sole & della Luna per le loro cagioni, ſenza volere a quelle aſcendere da gli eſſetti. Et Cicerone nel ſogno del minore Scipione fa che di cielo lo auolo ſuo a lui dimoſtra le coſe terrene. Ma & Cicerone, Ariſtotile, come quelli che piu oltre non intendeuano, ne cie li ſi fermarono. Et noi, a cui Dio ha dato il lume della gratia ſua, non dobbiamo ſtar contenti di fermarci ne cieli, anzi co’l penſiero ci dobbiamo inalzare a quella altezza, di donde ſono diſceſe l’anime noſtre, & doue elle hanno da ri-\ntornare, che queſta è la vera via del conoſcere, & dell’in-\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\ntendere. Alla qual percio non dobbiamo preſumptuoſi penſar\n\ndi douer per noſtra virtù poter peruenire, che à queſto modo ci ſarebbe detto da Dio quello, che fu riſpoſto à Moſe nel la ſua preſuntione. Poſteriora mea videbis, faciem autem meam non videbis. Et cio è, tu vederai gli effetti delle coſ ſe, ma non le ragioni di quelle. Anzi habbiamo noi à pre-\ngar la diuina ſua Maeſtà che ci faccia degni di quella gratia, laquale quando poi piacque à lei, ella donò al medeſimo Moſe, moſtrandogli le molte ſue marauiglie, il che ſa rà quando noi ſaremo fatti tali, che annichilati & di noi ſteſſi nulla preſumendo, potremo con l’Apoſtolo dire. Iam non viuo ego, ſed viuit in me Chriſtus.\n\nOr eſſendo il proceder noſtro coſì ragioneuole, come moſtra-\nto habbiamo, del conoſcer di alto le coſe baſſe, & di pren-\nder nella fabrica noſtra ad imitation della celeſte il numero ſettenario, per venire al p:imo ordine dico che io non lo trovo ne più perfetto, ne più diuino, che per vno altro ſete-\nnario applicato à ciaſcuna delle dette colonne, o vero à ciaſcuno de detti pianeti, che dir gli uogliamo. Dicono adun que i ſecretiſſimi Theologi, i quali ſono i Cabaliſti, che Moſe ſette volte paſſò per le ſette Saphiroth ſenza poter gia-\nmai paſſar la Binà. Et dicono quello eſſer il termino, alqua le l’intelletto humano puo eſſer levato. Et benche Moſe giunto alla detta Binà hauesse di rimpetto la faccia della corona ſuperiore, & quella della Chochmà, onde è ſcritto loquebatur facie ad faciem, nondimeno veramente ad eſſo Dio non parlò ſe non per l’angelo (come ſi legge ne gli at-\nti de gli Apoſtoli) & queſto auenne, percioche. Nemo nouit filium, niſi pater, neque patrem quis nouit niſi filius, & cui\n\n[illegible]\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n7\n\nvoluſſeti: filius revelare. Et eſſendo Moſe arrivato alla Ri-\nna, nella quale è vn officio di Angelo detto Mitrathon, cio è princeps facierum, con quello hebbei ſuoi ragionamen ti. Eſſendo egli adunque ſalito ſette volte ſette ſtate, che ſo no quarantanove numero della remiſſione, alqual numero anchor Ieſu Chriſto volſe che aſcendiſſimo facendo ora tione al padre, impercioche la oratione, che Dominical chiamiamo, ſecondo l’Hebreo teſto ſcritto da Mattheo è di quaranta nove parole.\n\nL’ombra di queſte ſalite imitando noi, habbiamo dato ſet te porte, ò gradi ò diſtintioni, che dir le vogliamo à ciaſ-\nſcun pianeta.\n\nMa per dar (per coſì dir.) ordine all’ordine con tal fa-\ncilità, che facciamo gli ſtudioſi come ſpettatori, mettiamo loro dauanti le dette ſette miſure ſoſtenute dalle miſure de ſette pianeti in ſpettaculo, ò dir vogliamo in Theatro diſtin to per ſette ſalite. Et perche gli antichi Theatri erano tal mente ordinati, che ſopra i gradi allo ſpettaculo più vicini ſedeuano i più honorati, poi di mano in mano ſedeuano ne gradi aſcendenti quelli che erano di minor dignità, almen te che ne ſupremi gradi ſedeuano gli artefici, in modo che i più vicini gradi à più nobili erano aſſegnati, ſi per la vicini tà dello ſpettaculo, come anchora perche dal fiato de gli ar tefici no foſſero offeſi. Noi ſeguēdo l’ordine della creation del mondo faremo ſeder ne primi gradi le coſe più ſemplici, ò più degne, ò che poſſiamo imaginar eſſere ſtate per la diſpo ſition diuina auāti alle altre coſe create. Poi collochere mo di grado in grado quelle che appreſſo ſono ſeguite, talmente che nel ſettimo, cio è nell’vltimo grado ſuperiore ſederāne\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nnon tutte le arti & facultà, che cadono ſotto precetti, non per ragione di milità, ma per ragion di tempo, eſſendo quelle come:ultime da gli huomini ſtate ritrouate . Nel primo grado adunque ſi vedranno ſette porte di ſimili, percioche ciaſcun Pianeta in figura humana ſarà dipinto ſopra la porta della à lui deſtinata colonna, ſalvo che alla colonna del Sole, impercioche eſſendo quello il più nobil luogo di tutto il Theatro vogliamo che quello Apollo,il qual dourebbe per ſua ragione eſſer dipinto in pari grado con gli altri, cieda al continuo della latitudine de gli Enti, che è imagine della diuinità. Adunque ſotto la porta di ciaſcun pianeta ſaranno conſeruate tutte le coſe appartenenti coſì alla miſu-\nra del ſopraceleſte ſuo corriſpondente, come à quelle che ap-\npartengono ad eſſo pianeta, & alle fintion de Poeti intorno à quello. ſi come diremo hora particolarmente di ciaſcuno.\n\nSotto la porta della Luna ſi trattera del ſuo mondo ſoprace-\nleſte Marent & Gabriel.\n\nDel celeſte la Luna, la opacità, la grandezza, & la diſtan-\nza di lei. Nelle fauole Diana, le ſue inſegne, & il numero delle Diane.\n\nSotto la porta di Mercurio nel ſuo mondo ſopraceleſte ſare\nTeſſoa, & Michael.\n\nNel celeſte il ſuo pianeta.\n\nNelle fauole Mercurio meſſaggier de Dei, & ſuoi ar-\nneſi.\n\nSotto la porta di Venere nel ſopraceleſte Hod, Nizach, Ho-\nmiel.\n\nNel celeſte Venere pianeta,\n\nNelle fauole Venere Dea, Cupidine, ſuoi arneſi, il nue\n\nDIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n8\n\nnumero delle Veneri & de Cupidini.\n\nSotto la quarta porta del primo grado del Sole, [illegible] l’aqua ſe troueremo ( come è detto ) non Apolline, [illegible], ma vn conuiuio, del quale parleremo trattando del [illegible] grado. Sotto la quarta porta adunque primieramente troueremo la latitudine, ò uogliamo dir la larghezza de gli Enſ-\nti, fatta à guiſa di Piramide, ſopra la cui ſommità imagi-\nneremo vn punto indiuiſibile, che ci habbia à ſignificar la di-\nuità & ſenza relatione & con relatione. Il Padre il verbo auanti la incarnatione & da poi, & lo Spirito Santo.\n\nAppreſſo vi ſi uedrà vna imagine di Pan, il quale percioche con la teſta ſignifica il ſopraceleſte con le corna d’oro, che in ſu guardano, & con la barba i celeſti influſſi, & con la pelle ſtellata il mondo celeſte, & con le gambe caprigne l’inferiore. Sotto queſta figura ci ſaranno ſignificati i tre mondi.\n\nNel terzo luogo ſotto la porta medeſima ci ſi appreſente-\nranno le Parche ſignificatrici del fato, della cagione del principio, della coſa, dell’effetto & del fine. Et queſta iſteſſa imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà l’vo-\nmo eſſer cagione di alcuna coſa. Et ſotto i Talari ſignificherà dar cagione. Vna quarta imagine ſarà anchor ſotto queſta porta. Et queſta ſarà vn arbore con vn ramo d’oro, il quale è queſto, del qual ſcriue Virgilio, che ſenza queſto non ſi puo an-\ndar à ueder el regno dell’inferno. Et queſta imagine in queſto luogo ci ſignificherà coſe intelligibili, & che non poſſo no cader ſotto il ſenſo, ma ſolamente le poſſiamo imagina re, & intendere illuminati dallo intelletto agente. Et queſta\n\n[illegible]\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\niſteſſa imagine ſotto le Gorgoni ſigniſichera l’intelletto agente, quale parleremo al ſuo luogo. Sotto l’idea di Marte ſi tratterra nel mondo ſopraceleste Galiar, Camael. Nel celeſte Marte Pianeta, & nelle favole Marte Dio, & ſuoi arneſi. Sotto la porta di Gioue nel mondo ſopraceleste Chased, & Zadchiel. Nel celeſte Gioue Pianeta.\n\nNelle favole Gioue Dio & le ſue insegne. Sotto Saturno haueremo nel ſopraceleste Bina & Zaph-\nchiel. Nel celeſte Saturno Pianeta.\n\nNelle favole Saturno Dio & le ſue insegne. Et con queſti ſuggetti viene ad eſſer concluſo il primo grado del Theatro.\n\nIl continuo.\n\nDIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n9","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0001","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO,\nDI MESSER GIVLIO\nCamillo.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"1.1"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 8, region 2]","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"1.2"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","text":"I PIV antichi, & più ſani ſcrittori hanno ſempre hauuto in coſtume di raccomandare à loro ſcritti i ſecreti di Dio ſotto oſcuri velami, accioche nõ ſiano inteſi, ſe nõ da coloro, i quali (come dice Chriſto) hanno orecchie da udire, cioè che da Dio ſono eletti ad intendere i ſuoi ſantiſsimi miſteri. Et Meliſſo dice che le orecchie delle anime volgari non poſſono ſofferire i raggi de la diuinità. Et ciò ſi conferma con lo eſſempio di Moſe, il quale ſcendendo dal monte, ſopra il quale, egli anchor per lo mezzo dell’Angelo hauena parlato con Dio, non poteua eſſer guardato dal popolo, ſe egli il viſo co’l uelo non ſi naſ ſcondeua. Et gli apoſtoli anchora veduto Chriſto traſfigu-\nrato, ciò è quaſi partito dalla groſſezza della humanità a la quaſi gloria della diuinità, non ſufficienti a riguardarlo per la debolezza, cadderono. Et nell’Apocalipſi ſi legge.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"1.3"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004","text":"Et ſignificauit mittens per angelum ſuum ſeruo ſuo Ioanni. Doue è da notare, che anchor a Giouanni, con tutto che egli foſſe ſeruo ſuo, non aperſe l’intendimento ſuo ſe non per ſi-\ngnificationi, & per viſioni. Et ueramente ſi come nella mon dana militia ſono adoprate le uoci de Capitani, & le trom be, & le inſegne per conducere & inanimar le armate ſchiere contra i nimici, non in altra maniera nella militia","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"1.4"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0005","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"1.5"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0006","text":"DI M. GIVLI CAMILLO,","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"1.6"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","text":"4\n\ndiuina habbiamo noi per la voce le parole del ſignor, le angeliche trombe, le quali ſono le voci di Propheti, & de predicatori: & le inſegne, & queſti ſono i ſegni delle viſio ni, le quali ſignificano & non eſprimono. A queſto habbia mo da aggiunger che Mercurio Triſmegillo dice, che il parlar religioso & pien di Dio vien ad eſſer violato quã do gli ſoprauiene moltitudine volgare. La onde non ſenza ragione gli antichi in ſu le porte di qualunque tempio tene uano o dipinta, o ſcolpita vna ſphinga, con quella imagine dimoſtrando che delle coſe di Dio non ſi deue ſe non con enigmi far publicamente parole. Il che in piu maniere ci e ſtato ancora inſegnato da Dio, che parola di Chriſto, e che le margarite non ſi debbiamo gittare à porci, & che à ca ni non vogliamo dar le coſe ſante. Et parlando à gli Apoſtoli ſuoi diſſe loro.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"1.7"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","text":"Vobis datum eſt noſſe miſteria regni cælorum, cæteris in parabolis, vt videntes non videant & audientes non intelligant. Et nel quarto di Eſdra Dio parlando di Moſe fatto ſalir ſopra il monte di ce. Et detinui eum apud me diebus multis, & narraui ei mirabilia multa temporum ſecreta, & finem & dixi, hæc in palam facies, & hæc abſcondes. Et Dauid à Dio parlando dice, Reuela oculos meos, & conſiderabo mirabilia tua, doue diſſe non di douer paleſar, ma ſo lamente di conſiderar le alte marauiglie. Poi appa-\nrenendo le coſe diuine al ſopraceleſte mondo, & eſſendo quello ſeparato da noi dalla maſſa di tutti i cieli, & non potendo la lingua noſtra giunger alla eſpreſſion di quello ſe non (diro coſi) per cenni & per ſimilitudini; à fine che per lo mezzo delle coſe viſibili ſagliamo alle inuiſibili.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"1.8"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0009","text":"A    iiii","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"1.9"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0010","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"1.10"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0011","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"1.11"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","text":"Non me è lecito anchor che Dio ci deſſe qualche gratia di ascendere al terzo cielo, & di vedere i ſuoi ſecreti, quelli di co non ci è lecito di rivelare, percioche quelli rivelando dop-\npio error ſi viene a commettere. Et cio è di ſcoprirgli a per-\nſone non degne, & di trattargli con queſta noſtra baſſa lingua, eſſendo quello il ſuggetto delle lingue delli angeli. I quali due inconvenienti volendo fuggir, Giovanni ſcriſſe le ſue viſioni ſenza cercar in altra guiſa di dichiararle. Et noi nelle coſe noſtre ci ſerviamo delle imagini, come de ſignificatrici di quelle coſe, che non ſi debbon profanare. Et quanto a Dio ſia caro che le coſe ſue ſiano tenute nella riverenza de loro velami, eſſo medeſimo ne fa fede, chiamando Moſe fedel miniſtro ſuo. Et da Cabaliſti Ezechiel vien chia-\nmato Propheta villano per hauer alla guiſa d’un’huomo di villa ſcoperto tutto quello che egli hauea veduto.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"1.12"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","text":"Nè ta-\ncero io, che i medeſimi Cabaliſti tengono che Maria ſorel-\nla di Moſe foſſe dalla lebbra oppreſſa per hauer revelate le coſe ſecrete della divinità. Et che per lo medeſimo delitto Ammonio moriſſe di ſporca, & miſera morte. Et tanto ba-\nſtandoci di hauer detto della riverenza di quel ſilentio, nel qual ci habbiamo da tener le coſe ſante, paſſiamo col nome del ſignore a ragionar del noſtro Theatro.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"1.13"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","text":"Salomone al nono de Proverbij dice la ſapienza hauerſi edi-\nficato caſa, & hauerla fondata ſopra ſette colonne. Queſte ſette colonne ſignificanti ſtabilſiſſima eternità habbiamo da intender che ſiano le ſette ſaphirot del ſopraceleſte mondo che ſono le ſette miſure della fabrica del celeſte & all’in-","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"1.14"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0015","text":"iii A","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"1.15"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0016","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"1.16"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","text":"5\n\nſeriore, nelle quali ſono compreſe le Idee di tutte le coſe al celeſte, & all’inferiore appartamenti. Di che fuori di queſto numero coſa alcuna non poſſiamo imaginare, queſto ſet tenario è numero perfetto, percioche contiene l’uno & l’al tro ſeſſo, per eſſer fatto di pari & di diſpari, onde volendo dir Virgilio perfettamente beati diſſe, terque quater-\nque. Et Mercurio Triſmegisto nel Pimandro parlando del la creation del mondo, induce ſe medeſimo à domandare. Elementa naturæ unde manarunt? Et Pimandro riſpon de. Ex voluntate Dei, quæ verbum complexa pulcherrimè que intuita mundum, ad eius exemplar reliqua ſui ipſius ele mentis, vitalibusque ſeminibus exornauit.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"1.17"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","text":"Mens autem De us utriuſque ſexus fœcunditate pleniſſimus vita, & lux tum verbo ſuo mentem alteram opificem peperit, qui quic dem Deus ignis, atque ſpiritus ſeptem deinceps fabricauit gubernatores, qui circulis mundum ſensibilem complectun-\ntur. Et nel vero hauendo la diuinità eſplicate fuori queſte ſette miſure, ſegno è che nello biſſo della ſua diuinità ſia no anchor implicitamente contenute, percioche meno dal quod non habet, queſte colonne Eſſia le chiama femine, quã do dice. Septem mulieres apprehendent ſibi virum vnum. Et chiamale femine, che vuol dir paſſiue, cioè produtte. Ma ſe come dice Paolo: Portat omnia verbo virtutis ſuæ. Et altroue. Vnum in omnibus, & omnia in vno. Et à Coloſſen ſi.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"1.18"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0019","text":"Et imago Dei in viſibilis, primogenitus omnis creaturæ, quoniam in ipſo condita ſunt vniuerſa in cœlis & in ter-\nra, viſibilia & inuiſibilia, ſiue Throni, ſiue dominationes, ſiue principatus, ſiue poteſtates, omnia per ipſum & in ipſa ſo creata ſunt. Segue che non poſſiamo trouar maggiore explici-","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"1.19"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0020","text":"In ipſo\nin ipſi\ncœle.\nPer ip\nſunt. i.\nte,","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"1.20"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0021","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"1.21"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","text":"più capace, che quella di Dio. Hor ſe gli antichi Oratori volendo collocar di giorno in giorno le parti delle orationi che hauerano a recitare, le affidauano a luoghi caduchi, come coſe caduche, ragione è, che volendo noi raccomandar eternalmente gli eterni di tutte le coſe, che poſſono eſſer ne ſſiti di oratione con gli eterni di eſſa oratione, che trouiamo a loro luoghi eterni. L’alta adunque fatica noſtra è ſtata di trouare ordine in queſte ſette miſure, capace baſtante, diſtin to, & che tenga ſempre il ſenſo ſuegliato, & la memoria percoſſa. Ma conſiderando che ſe uoleſſimo mettere alcuni dauanti queſte altissime miſure, & ſi lontane dalla noſtra cognitione, che ſolamente da propheti ſono ſtate anchor ne ſcoſſamente tocche, queſto ſarebbe un metter mano a coſa troppo malageuole.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"1.22"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","text":"Per tanto in luogo di quelle piglieremo i ſette pianeti, le cui nature anchor da uolgari ſono aſſai be conoſciute, ma talmente le uſeremo, che nō ce le propognia mo come termini, fuor de quali non habbiamo ad uſcire, ma come quelli, che alle menti de ſaui ſempre rappreſentino le ſette ſopracelesti miſure. Et è ben ragione, che ſi come par lando delle coſe inferiori, la loro natura i ſette pianeti ci rappreſenta, ſecondo che queſta a quello, & quella a quel-\nl’altro è ſottopoſta, coſi anchor de pianeti parlando, ci ri-\ntorniamo alla mente quei principii, donde quelli hanno hau-\nto la loro uirtù.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"1.23"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","text":"Queſta alta & incomparabile collocatione fa non ſolamen te officio di conſeruarci le affidate coſe parole, & arte, che a man ſalua ad ogni noſtro biſogno informati prima le potremo trouare, ma ci da anchor la uera ſapiença ne fonti di quella menendo noi in cognition delle coſe dalle cagioni, &","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"1.24"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0025","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"1.25"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","text":"non da gli eſſetti. Il che piu chiaramente eſprimeremo con uno eſſempio. Se noi foſſimo in un g’ran boſcho, & haveſſi mo deſiderio di ben vederlo tutto, in quello ſtando, al deſide rio noſtro no potremmo ſodiſfare, percioche la viſta intorno volgendo, da noi non ſe ne potrebbe veder, ſe non una piccio la parte, impedendoci le piante circonuicine il veder delle lontane, ma ſe vicino a quello vi foſſe una erta, la qual ci re conduceſſe ſopra un’ alto colle, del boſco uſcendo dall’erta comincieremmo a veder in gran parte la forma di quello, poi ſopra il colle aſceſi, tutto intiero il potremmo raffigura re. Il boſco è queſto noſtro mondo inferiore, la erta ſono i Cie li, & il colle il ſopraceleſte mondo. Et a voler bene intēder queſte coſe inferiori è neceſſario di aſcendere alle ſuperio-\nri, & di alto in giù guardando, di queſte potremo haver piu certa cognitione.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"1.26"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","text":"Di queſto modo di intender par che gli an tichi ſcrittori gentili non ne foſſero al tutto digiuni, di che Maſſimo Tirio allega Homero, che inuiaſſe Vliſſe aſceſo in alta parte conſiderare i coſtumi de gli habitanti. Et Aristotile ci laſciò ſcritto, che ſe noi foſſimo ſopra i cieli, ſi potrebb be da noi conoſcere l’Ecliſſi del Sole & della Luna per le loro cagioni, ſenza volere a quelle aſcendere da gli eſſetti. Et Cicerone nel ſogno del minore Scipione fa che di cielo lo auolo ſuo a lui dimoſtra le coſe terrene. Ma & Cicerone, Ariſtotile, come quelli che piu oltre non intendeuano, ne cie li ſi fermarono. Et noi, a cui Dio ha dato il lume della gratia ſua, non dobbiamo ſtar contenti di fermarci ne cieli, anzi co’l penſiero ci dobbiamo inalzare a quella altezza, di donde ſono diſceſe l’anime noſtre, & doue elle hanno da ri-\ntornare, che queſta è la vera via del conoſcere, & dell’in-","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"1.27"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0028","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"1.28"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0029","text":"tendere. Alla qual percio non dobbiamo preſumptuoſi penſar","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"1.29"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","text":"di douer per noſtra virtù poter peruenire, che à queſto modo ci ſarebbe detto da Dio quello, che fu riſpoſto à Moſe nel la ſua preſuntione. Poſteriora mea videbis, faciem autem meam non videbis. Et cio è, tu vederai gli effetti delle coſ ſe, ma non le ragioni di quelle. Anzi habbiamo noi à pre-\ngar la diuina ſua Maeſtà che ci faccia degni di quella gratia, laquale quando poi piacque à lei, ella donò al medeſimo Moſe, moſtrandogli le molte ſue marauiglie, il che ſa rà quando noi ſaremo fatti tali, che annichilati & di noi ſteſſi nulla preſumendo, potremo con l’Apoſtolo dire. Iam non viuo ego, ſed viuit in me Chriſtus.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"1.30"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031","text":"Or eſſendo il proceder noſtro coſì ragioneuole, come moſtra-\nto habbiamo, del conoſcer di alto le coſe baſſe, & di pren-\nder nella fabrica noſtra ad imitation della celeſte il numero ſettenario, per venire al p:imo ordine dico che io non lo trovo ne più perfetto, ne più diuino, che per vno altro ſete-\nnario applicato à ciaſcuna delle dette colonne, o vero à ciaſcuno de detti pianeti, che dir gli uogliamo. Dicono adun que i ſecretiſſimi Theologi, i quali ſono i Cabaliſti, che Moſe ſette volte paſſò per le ſette Saphiroth ſenza poter gia-\nmai paſſar la Binà. Et dicono quello eſſer il termino, alqua le l’intelletto humano puo eſſer levato.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"1.31"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","text":"Et benche Moſe giunto alla detta Binà hauesse di rimpetto la faccia della corona ſuperiore, & quella della Chochmà, onde è ſcritto loquebatur facie ad faciem, nondimeno veramente ad eſſo Dio non parlò ſe non per l’angelo (come ſi legge ne gli at-\nti de gli Apoſtoli) & queſto auenne, percioche. Nemo nouit filium, niſi pater, neque patrem quis nouit niſi filius, & cui","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"1.32"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0033","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"1.33"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0034","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"1.34"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0035","text":"7\n\nvoluſſeti: filius revelare. Et eſſendo Moſe arrivato alla Ri-\nna, nella quale è vn officio di Angelo detto Mitrathon, cio è princeps facierum, con quello hebbei ſuoi ragionamen ti. Eſſendo egli adunque ſalito ſette volte ſette ſtate, che ſo no quarantanove numero della remiſſione, alqual numero anchor Ieſu Chriſto volſe che aſcendiſſimo facendo ora tione al padre, impercioche la oratione, che Dominical chiamiamo, ſecondo l’Hebreo teſto ſcritto da Mattheo è di quaranta nove parole.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"1.35"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","text":"L’ombra di queſte ſalite imitando noi, habbiamo dato ſet te porte, ò gradi ò diſtintioni, che dir le vogliamo à ciaſ-\nſcun pianeta.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"1.36"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","text":"Ma per dar (per coſì dir.) ordine all’ordine con tal fa-\ncilità, che facciamo gli ſtudioſi come ſpettatori, mettiamo loro dauanti le dette ſette miſure ſoſtenute dalle miſure de ſette pianeti in ſpettaculo, ò dir vogliamo in Theatro diſtin to per ſette ſalite. Et perche gli antichi Theatri erano tal mente ordinati, che ſopra i gradi allo ſpettaculo più vicini ſedeuano i più honorati, poi di mano in mano ſedeuano ne gradi aſcendenti quelli che erano di minor dignità, almen te che ne ſupremi gradi ſedeuano gli artefici, in modo che i più vicini gradi à più nobili erano aſſegnati, ſi per la vicini tà dello ſpettaculo, come anchora perche dal fiato de gli ar tefici no foſſero offeſi. Noi ſeguēdo l’ordine della creation del mondo faremo ſeder ne primi gradi le coſe più ſemplici, ò più degne, ò che poſſiamo imaginar eſſere ſtate per la diſpo ſition diuina auāti alle altre coſe create.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"1.37"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038","text":"Poi collochere mo di grado in grado quelle che appreſſo ſono ſeguite, talmente che nel ſettimo, cio è nell’vltimo grado ſuperiore ſederāne","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"1.38"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0039","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"1.39"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","text":"non tutte le arti & facultà, che cadono ſotto precetti, non per ragione di milità, ma per ragion di tempo, eſſendo quelle come:ultime da gli huomini ſtate ritrouate . Nel primo grado adunque ſi vedranno ſette porte di ſimili, percioche ciaſcun Pianeta in figura humana ſarà dipinto ſopra la porta della à lui deſtinata colonna, ſalvo che alla colonna del Sole, impercioche eſſendo quello il più nobil luogo di tutto il Theatro vogliamo che quello Apollo,il qual dourebbe per ſua ragione eſſer dipinto in pari grado con gli altri, cieda al continuo della latitudine de gli Enti, che è imagine della diuinità. Adunque ſotto la porta di ciaſcun pianeta ſaranno conſeruate tutte le coſe appartenenti coſì alla miſu-\nra del ſopraceleſte ſuo corriſpondente, come à quelle che ap-\npartengono ad eſſo pianeta, & alle fintion de Poeti intorno à quello. ſi come diremo hora particolarmente di ciaſcuno.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"1.40"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0041","text":"Sotto la porta della Luna ſi trattera del ſuo mondo ſoprace-\nleſte Marent & Gabriel.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"1.41"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042","text":"Del celeſte la Luna, la opacità, la grandezza, & la diſtan-\nza di lei. Nelle fauole Diana, le ſue inſegne, & il numero delle Diane.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"1.42"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0043","text":"Sotto la porta di Mercurio nel ſuo mondo ſopraceleſte ſare\nTeſſoa, & Michael.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"1.43"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0044","text":"Nel celeſte il ſuo pianeta.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"1.44"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045","text":"Nelle fauole Mercurio meſſaggier de Dei, & ſuoi ar-\nneſi.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"1.45"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0046","text":"Sotto la porta di Venere nel ſopraceleſte Hod, Nizach, Ho-\nmiel.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"1.46"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0047","text":"Nel celeſte Venere pianeta,","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"1.47"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0048","text":"Nelle fauole Venere Dea, Cupidine, ſuoi arneſi, il nue","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"1.48"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0049","text":"DIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"1.49"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0050","text":"8\n\nnumero delle Veneri & de Cupidini.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"1.50"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051","text":"Sotto la quarta porta del primo grado del Sole, [illegible] l’aqua ſe troueremo ( come è detto ) non Apolline, [illegible], ma vn conuiuio, del quale parleremo trattando del [illegible] grado. Sotto la quarta porta adunque primieramente troueremo la latitudine, ò uogliamo dir la larghezza de gli Enſ-\nti, fatta à guiſa di Piramide, ſopra la cui ſommità imagi-\nneremo vn punto indiuiſibile, che ci habbia à ſignificar la di-\nuità & ſenza relatione & con relatione. Il Padre il verbo auanti la incarnatione & da poi, & lo Spirito Santo.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"1.51"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","text":"Appreſſo vi ſi uedrà vna imagine di Pan, il quale percioche con la teſta ſignifica il ſopraceleſte con le corna d’oro, che in ſu guardano, & con la barba i celeſti influſſi, & con la pelle ſtellata il mondo celeſte, & con le gambe caprigne l’inferiore. Sotto queſta figura ci ſaranno ſignificati i tre mondi.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"1.52"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053","text":"Nel terzo luogo ſotto la porta medeſima ci ſi appreſente-\nranno le Parche ſignificatrici del fato, della cagione del principio, della coſa, dell’effetto & del fine. Et queſta iſteſſa imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà l’vo-\nmo eſſer cagione di alcuna coſa. Et ſotto i Talari ſignificherà dar cagione. Vna quarta imagine ſarà anchor ſotto queſta porta. Et queſta ſarà vn arbore con vn ramo d’oro, il quale è queſto, del qual ſcriue Virgilio, che ſenza queſto non ſi puo an-\ndar à ueder el regno dell’inferno. Et queſta imagine in queſto luogo ci ſignificherà coſe intelligibili, & che non poſſo no cader ſotto il ſenſo, ma ſolamente le poſſiamo imagina re, & intendere illuminati dallo intelletto agente. Et queſta","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"1.53"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0054","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"1.54"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0055","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"1.55"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","text":"iſteſſa imagine ſotto le Gorgoni ſigniſichera l’intelletto agente, quale parleremo al ſuo luogo. Sotto l’idea di Marte ſi tratterra nel mondo ſopraceleste Galiar, Camael. Nel celeſte Marte Pianeta, & nelle favole Marte Dio, & ſuoi arneſi. Sotto la porta di Gioue nel mondo ſopraceleste Chased, & Zadchiel. Nel celeſte Gioue Pianeta.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"1.56"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0057","text":"Nelle favole Gioue Dio & le ſue insegne. Sotto Saturno haueremo nel ſopraceleste Bina & Zaph-\nchiel. Nel celeſte Saturno Pianeta.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"1.57"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058","text":"Nelle favole Saturno Dio & le ſue insegne. Et con queſti ſuggetti viene ad eſſer concluſo il primo grado del Theatro.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"1.58"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0059","text":"Il continuo.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"1.59"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0060","text":"DIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"1.60"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0061","text":"9","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"1.61"}],"sha256":"a5a6ba05fa6ba9e1c7527ba9245f6760fe648d35572a4a1046bac166297d4087","language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261030T230046903667Z_02b95c52","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, BY MESSER GIULIO Camillo.","source_sha256":"a5a6ba05fa6ba9e1c7527ba9245f6760fe648d35572a4a1046bac166297d4087","sha256":"0402f617eb314ed30be10a35a6c2d809003436d6e2838f7a303ae7eb61d4addb","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:00:46.903724+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0001","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE,\nBY MESSER GIULIO\nCamillo.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"1.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 8, region 2]","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"1.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","text":"THE most ancient and soundest writers have always been accustomed to entrust the secrets of God to their writings beneath obscure veils, so that they may not be understood save by those who (as Christ says) have ears to hear, that is, who are chosen by God to understand His most holy mysteries. And Melissus says that the ears of vulgar souls cannot endure the rays of divinity. And this is confirmed by the example of Moses, who, descending from the mountain, upon which he had even spoken with God through the agency of the Angel, could not be looked upon by the people unless he hid his face with a veil. And the Apostles likewise, having seen Christ transfigu-\nred, that is, as though departed from the grossness of humanity into the semblance of the glory of divinity, being unable to behold Him through weakness, fell. And in the Apocalypse one reads.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"1.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004","text":"Et significauit mittens per angelum suum seruo suo Ioanni. Where it must be noted that even to John, although he was His servant, He did not open His meaning except through sig-\nnifications and visions. And truly, just as in worldly warfare the voices of captains, and trumpets, and ensigns are employed to lead and animate the armed ranks against their enemies, in no other manner in the militia","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"1.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0005","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"1.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0006","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO,","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"1.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","text":"4\n\ndivine have we, in place of voice, the words of the Lord; the angelic trumpets, which are the voices of Prophets and preachers; and the ensigns, which are the signs of visions, which signify and do not express. To this we must add that Mercury Trismegistus says that religious speech, full of God, comes to be violated when a vulgar multitude comes upon it. Whence not without reason did the ancients keep, painted or sculpted upon the doors of every temple, a sphinx, showing by that image that concerning the things of God one ought not publicly to speak save in enigmas. This too has been taught us by God in many ways: that it is a saying of Christ that pearls ought not to be cast before swine, and that we should not give holy things to dogs. And speaking to His Apostles, He said to them.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"1.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","text":"Vobis datum est nosse misteria regni cælorum, cæteris in parabolis, vt videntes non videant & audientes non intelligant. And in the Fourth Book of Ezra, God, speaking of Moses made to ascend the mountain, says: Et detinui eum apud me diebus multis, & narraui ei mirabilia multa temporum secreta, & finem & dixi, hæc in palam facies, & hæc abscondes. And David, speaking to God, says: Reuela oculos meos, & considerabo mirabilia tua, where he said not that he was to reveal, but only to consider the lofty marvels. Then, since divine things pertain to the supracelestial world, and that is separated from us by the mass of all the heavens, and since our tongue cannot attain to the expression thereof except (so to speak) by signs and similitudes, to the end that through visible things we may ascend to invisible ones.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"1.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0009","text":"A    iiii","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"1.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0010","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"1.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0011","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"1.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","text":"Nor is it lawful for me, even should God grant us some grace to ascend to the third heaven and see His secrets, to reveal those things which it is not lawful for us to reveal; for in revealing them a double error is committed. Namely, that of disclosing them to persons unworthy, and that of treating them in this low language of ours, whereas they are the subject of the tongues of angels. Wishing to avoid these two inconveniences, John wrote his visions without seeking otherwise to explain them. And in our own matters we make use of images, as signifiers of those things which ought not to be profaned. And how dear it is to God that His things should be kept under the reverence of their veils, He Himself bears witness, calling Moses His faithful minister. And by the Cabalists Ezekiel is called a rustic Prophet, because in the manner of a man of the countryside he disclosed all that he had seen.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"1.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","text":"Nor shall I be silent that the same Cabalists maintain that Mary, sister of Moses, was afflicted with leprosy for having revealed the secret things of divinity; and that for the same offence Ammonius died a foul and miserable death. And, having said enough concerning the reverence of that silence in which we must hold holy things, let us pass, in the name of the Lord, to discourse upon our Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"1.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","text":"Solomon, in the ninth chapter of Proverbs, says that wisdom has built herself a house and founded it upon seven columns. These seven columns, signifying most steadfast eternity, we must understand to be the seven saphyrot of the supracelestial world, which are the seven measures of the fabric of the celestial and in-","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"1.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0015","text":"iii A","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"1.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0016","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"1.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","text":"5\n\nferior [world], in which are comprehended the Ideas of all things belonging to the celestial and inferior regions. Beyond this number we can imagine nothing whatsoever. This septenary is a perfect number, because it contains both sexes, being made of even and odd; whence Virgil, wishing to call [men] perfectly blessed, said, terque quater-\nque. And Mercury Trismegistus in the Pimander, speaking of the creation of the world, introduces himself as asking: Elementa naturæ unde manarunt? And Pimander answers: Ex voluntate Dei, quæ verbum complexa pulcherrimè que intuita mundum, ad eius exemplar reliqua sui ipsius ele mentis, vitalibusque seminibus exornauit.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"1.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","text":"Mens autem De us utriusque sexus fœcunditate plenissimus vita, & lux tum verbo suo mentem alteram opificem peperit, qui quic dem Deus ignis, atque spiritus septem deinceps fabricauit gubernatores, qui circulis mundum sensibilem complectun-\ntur. And indeed, since divinity has unfolded outwardly these seven measures, it is a sign that in the abyss of His divinity they are still implicitly contained; for less cannot come from quod non habet. Isaiah calls these columns women, when he says: Septem mulieres apprehendent sibi virum vnum. And he calls them women, which means passive, that is, produced. But if, as Paul says: Portat omnia verbo virtutis suæ. And elsewhere: Vnum in omnibus, & omnia in vno. And to the Colossians:","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"1.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0019","text":"Et imago Dei in visibilis, primogenitus omnis creaturæ, quoniam in ipso condita sunt vniuersa in cœlis & in ter-\nra, visibilia & inuisibilia, siue Throni, siue dominationes, siue principatus, siue potestates, omnia per ipsum & in ipsa so creata sunt. It follows that we cannot find a greater explici-","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"1.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0020","text":"In ipso\nin ipsi\ncœle.\nPer ip\nsunt. i.\nte,","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"1.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0021","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"1.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","text":"tation, more capacious, than that of God. Now if the ancient Orators, wishing to place day by day the parts of the orations which they were to recite, entrusted them to perishable places, as things perishable, it is fitting that, wishing we to commit eternally the eternal things of all things which can be necessary to us in discourse, together with the eternal things of discourse itself, we should find for them eternal places. Our lofty labour, therefore, has been to find an order in these seven measures, capacious, sufficient, distinct, and such as always keeps the understanding awake and memory struck. But considering that if we wished to set someone before these most lofty measures, so far removed from our knowledge that they have been but obscurely touched even by Prophets, this would be to undertake a thing too difficult.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"1.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","text":"Therefore, in place of them we shall take the seven planets, whose natures are likewise quite well known even to common people; but we shall use them in such a manner that we do not propose them to ourselves as boundaries beyond which we ought not to go, but as those which ever represent to the minds of the wise the seven supracelestial measures. And it is fitting that, just as, in speaking of inferior things, the seven planets represent their nature to us, according as this is subject to that and that to the other, so, speaking also of the planets, our mind should return to those principles whence they have received their virtue.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"1.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","text":"This lofty and incomparable arrangement performs not only the office of preserving for us the things entrusted to us—words and art—so that, having first informed ourselves, we may safely find them at hand for every need of ours; but it also gives us true wisdom at its sources, leading us to knowledge of things through their causes, and","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"1.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0025","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"1.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","text":"not from the effects. Which we shall express more clearly by an example. If we were in a great wood, and had the desire to see it all well, while remaining in it we could not satisfy our desire; for, turning our sight about, we could see of it only a small part, the neighbouring trees preventing us from seeing those that are distant. But if near it there were a steep ascent, which led us up onto a high hill, on emerging from the wood by way of the ascent we should begin to see in great part its form; then, having climbed upon the hill, we could represent it entire. The wood is this our lower world; the steep ascent is the Heavens, and the hill the supracelestial world. And in order properly to understand these lower things, it is necessary to ascend to the higher ones;\nand, looking from on high downward, we may have a more certain knowledge of these.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"1.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","text":"Of this manner of understanding it seems that the ancient gentile writers were not altogether ignorant; concerning which Maximus Tyrius cites Homer, who sent Ulysses, having ascended to a high place, to consider the customs of the inhabitants. And Aristotle left it written for us that, if we were above the heavens, we could know the Eclipse of the Sun and of the Moon through their causes, without wishing to ascend to those causes from the effects. And Cicero, in the dream of the younger Scipio, has his grandfather show him earthly things from heaven. But Cicero and Aristotle, as those who understood no further, stopped at the heavens. And we, to whom God has given the light of His grace, ought not to be content to stop in the heavens; rather, with thought we ought to raise ourselves to that height whence our souls descended, and whither they must re-\nturn; for this is the true way of knowing and of under-","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"1.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0028","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"1.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0029","text":"standing. Wherefore we ought not presumptuously to think","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"1.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","text":"that by our own power we can attain thereto; for in this manner God would say to us that which was answered to Moses in his presumption: Posteriora mea videbis, faciem autem meam non videbis. And this is: thou shalt see the effects of things, but not their reasons. Rather, we must pray His divine Majesty to make us worthy of that grace, which, when it then pleased Him, He gave to that same Moses, showing him His many marvels; and this shall be when we have become such that, annihilated and presuming nothing of ourselves, we may say with the Apostle: Iam non vivo ego, sed vivit in me Christus.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"1.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031","text":"Now, since our procedure is as reasonable as we have shown it to be, namely, to know low things from on high, and in our structure to take, in imitation of the celestial one, the number seven, in order to come to the first order I say that I find none more perfect or more divine than another septenary applied to each of the said columns, or to each of the said planets, as we may choose to call them. The most secret theologians, who are the Kabbalists, say therefore that Moses passed seven times through the seven Saphiroth, without ever being able to pass Binà. And they say that this is the limit to which the human intellect can be raised.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"1.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","text":"And although Moses, having reached the said Binà, had opposite him the face of the higher crown, and that of Chochmà, whence it is written loquebatur facie ad faciem, nevertheless God Himself did not speak to him save through the angel (as is read in the Acts of the Apostles); and this happened because: Nemo novit filium, nisi pater, neque patrem quis novit nisi filius, & cui","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"1.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0033","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"1.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0034","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"1.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0035","text":"7\n\nvoluſſeti: filius revelare. And Moses, having arrived at the Ri-\nna, in which there is an office of Angel called Mitrathon, that is, princeps facierum, held his discourses with him. He having therefore ascended seven times seven stages, which are forty-nine, the number of remission—to which number Jesus Christ also willed that we should ascend in praying to the Father, because the prayer that we call the Lord's Prayer, according to the Hebrew text written by Matthew, consists of forty-nine words.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"1.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","text":"Imitating the shadow of these ascents, we have assigned seven doors, or steps, or distinctions, as we may choose to call them, to each planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"1.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","text":"But in order to give, so to speak, order to the order with such facility that we make students into spectators, we place before them the said seven measures, supported by the measures of the seven planets, in a spectacle—or, let us say, in a Theatre—distinguished by seven ascents. And because the ancient theatres were so ordered that, upon the steps nearest to the spectacle, the most honoured sat; then, successively, upon the ascending steps sat those who were of lesser dignity, until upon the highest steps the artisans sat, so that the nearer steps were assigned to the nobler, both on account of their proximity to the spectacle and also lest they should be offended by the breath of the artisans: we, following the order of the creation of the world, shall make the simplest, or the worthiest, things sit in the first steps, or those which we may imagine to have been, by divine disposition, before the other things created.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"1.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038","text":"Then we shall place, step by step, those which followed thereafter, so that in the seventh, that is, in the last and highest step, there shall sit","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"1.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0039","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"1.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","text":"not all the arts and faculties which fall under precepts, not by reason of worth, but by reason of time, these being as the last things discovered by men. In the first step, therefore, seven similar doors shall be seen, because each Planet in human form shall be painted above the door of the column destined for it; except at the column of the Sun, for since that is the noblest place in the whole Theatre, we wish that Apollo, who by right should be painted on an equal level with the others, yield to the continuum of the latitude of Beings, which is an image of divinity. Therefore, beneath the door of each planet shall be kept all things belonging both to the measure of its corresponding supracelestial one, and to those things which belong to that planet itself, and to the poets' fictions concerning it, as we shall now say particularly of each.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"1.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0041","text":"Beneath the door of the Moon there shall be treated its supracelestial world: Marent and Gabriel.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"1.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042","text":"Of the celestial: the Moon, its opacity, magnitude, and distance. In the fables: Diana, her insignia, and the number of Dianas.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"1.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0043","text":"Beneath the door of Mercury, in its supracelestial world, shall be Teſſoa and Michael.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"1.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0044","text":"In the celestial: its planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"1.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045","text":"In the fables: Mercury, messenger of the Gods, and his attributes.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"1.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0046","text":"Beneath the door of Venus, in the supracelestial: Hod, Nizach, Ho-\nmiel.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"1.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0047","text":"In the celestial: Venus, the planet,","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"1.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0048","text":"In the fables: Venus the Goddess, Cupid, her attributes, the clou","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"1.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0049","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"1.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0050","text":"8\n\nthe number of Venuses & Cupids.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"1.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051","text":"Under the fourth gate of the first grade of the Sun, [illegible] water we shall find (as has been said) not Apollo, [illegible], but a banquet, of which we shall speak when treating of the [illegible] grade. Under the fourth gate, therefore, we shall first find the latitude, or, let us say, the breadth of Beings, fashioned in the manner of a Pyramid, upon whose summit we shall imagine an indivisible point, which is to signify to us divinity both without relation and with relation: the Father, the Word before the incarnation and after, and the Holy Spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"1.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","text":"Next there will be seen an image of Pan, who, because with his head he signifies the supracelestial, with the golden horns that look upward, and with his beard the celestial influences, and with his starry skin the celestial world, and with his goat-like legs the lower [world]. Beneath this figure the three worlds will be signified.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"1.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053","text":"In the third place beneath the same gate there will appear to us the Fates, signifiers of fate, of the cause of the beginning, of the thing, of the effect & of the end. And this same image beneath Pasiphaë will signify man to be the cause of some thing. And beneath the Talaria it will signify to give cause. A fourth image will also be beneath this gate. And this will be a tree with a golden branch, which is that of which Virgil writes, that without this one cannot go to see the kingdom of Hell. And this image in this place will signify intelligible things, which cannot fall under sense, but we can only imagine and understand them, illuminated by the agent intellect. And this","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"1.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0054","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"1.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0055","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"1.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","text":"same image beneath the Gorgons will signify the agent intellect, of which we shall speak in its place. Under the idea of Mars, in the supracelestial world, Galiar, Camael, will be treated. In the celestial, Mars the Planet, and in the fables Mars the God, & his implements. Under the gate of Jupiter, in the supracelestial world, Chased, & Zadchiel. In the celestial, Jupiter the Planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"1.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0057","text":"In the fables, Jupiter the God & his insignia. Under Saturn we shall have, in the supracelestial, Bina & Zaphchiel. In the celestial, Saturn the Planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"1.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058","text":"In the fables, Saturn the God & his insignia. And with these subjects the first grade of the Theatre comes to be concluded.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"1.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0059","text":"The continuation.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"1.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0060","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"1.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0061","text":"9","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"1.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0061"]}],"source_digest":"b3a7a2ef26d707cfe9d9f12fbcd234a8ccc3257dc6b8ef4bcce14c1d17dd3dac","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO, DI MESSER GIVLIO Camillo."},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261031T004230991214Z_47eb935f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, BY MESSER GIULIO Camillo.","source_sha256":"a5a6ba05fa6ba9e1c7527ba9245f6760fe648d35572a4a1046bac166297d4087","sha256":"19680d345ed3a5d95c2ede4ec83b57a1b52b3515abe293854bd97483dd5479be","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-31T00:42:30.991267+00:00","translate_quotations":true,"paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0001","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE,\nBY SIR GIULIO\nCamillo.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"1.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 8, region 2]","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"1.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","text":"THE most ancient and soundest writers have always been accustomed to entrust the secrets of God to their writings beneath obscure veils, so that they may not be understood save by those who (as Christ says) have ears to hear, that is, who are chosen by God to understand His most holy mysteries. And Melissus says that the ears of vulgar souls cannot endure the rays of divinity. And this is confirmed by the example of Moses, who, descending from the mountain, upon which he had even spoken with God through the agency of the Angel, could not be looked upon by the people unless he hid his face with a veil. And the Apostles likewise, having seen Christ transfigu-\nred, that is, as though departed from the grossness of humanity into the semblance of the glory of divinity, being unable to behold Him through weakness, fell. And in the Apocalypse one reads.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"1.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004","text":"And he signified it, sending through his angel to his servant John. Where it must be noted that even to John, although he was His servant, He did not open His meaning except through sig-\nnifications and visions. And truly, just as in worldly warfare the voices of captains, and trumpets, and ensigns are employed to lead and animate the armed ranks against their enemies, in no other manner in the militia","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"1.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0005","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"1.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0006","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO,","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"1.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","text":"4\n\ndivine have we, in place of voice, the words of the Lord; the angelic trumpets, which are the voices of Prophets and preachers; and the ensigns, which are the signs of visions, which signify and do not express. To this we must add that Mercury Trismegistus says that religious speech, full of God, comes to be violated when a vulgar multitude comes upon it. Whence not without reason did the ancients keep, painted or sculpted upon the doors of every temple, a sphinx, showing by that image that concerning the things of God one ought not publicly to speak save in enigmas. This too has been taught us by God in many ways: that it is a saying of Christ that pearls ought not to be cast before swine, and that we should not give holy things to dogs. And speaking to His Apostles, He said to them.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"1.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","text":"To you it has been given to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven; to the rest, in parables, that seeing they may not see and hearing they may not understand. And in the Fourth Book of Ezra, God, speaking of Moses made to ascend the mountain, says: And I kept him with me for many days, and told him many wondrous secret things of the times, and the end, and said: these you shall make public, and these you shall hide. And David, speaking to God, says: Reveal my eyes, and I shall behold thy wonders, where he said not that he was to reveal, but only to consider the lofty marvels. Then, since divine things pertain to the supracelestial world, and that is separated from us by the mass of all the heavens, and since our tongue cannot attain to the expression thereof except (so to speak) by signs and similitudes, to the end that through visible things we may ascend to invisible ones.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"1.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0009","text":"A    iiii","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"1.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0010","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"1.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0011","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"1.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","text":"Nor is it lawful for me, even should God grant us some grace to ascend to the third heaven and see His secrets, to reveal those things which it is not lawful for us to reveal; for in revealing them a double error is committed. Namely, that of disclosing them to persons unworthy, and that of treating them in this low language of ours, whereas they are the subject of the tongues of angels. Wishing to avoid these two inconveniences, John wrote his visions without seeking otherwise to explain them. And in our own matters we make use of images, as signifiers of those things which ought not to be profaned. And how dear it is to God that His things should be kept under the reverence of their veils, He Himself bears witness, calling Moses His faithful minister. And by the Cabalists Ezekiel is called a rustic Prophet, because in the manner of a man of the countryside he disclosed all that he had seen.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"1.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","text":"Nor shall I be silent that the same Cabalists maintain that Mary, sister of Moses, was afflicted with leprosy for having revealed the secret things of divinity; and that for the same offence Ammonius died a foul and miserable death. And, having said enough concerning the reverence of that silence in which we must hold holy things, let us pass, in the name of the Lord, to discourse upon our Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"1.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","text":"Solomon, in the ninth chapter of Proverbs, says that wisdom has built herself a house and founded it upon seven columns. These seven columns, signifying most steadfast eternity, we must understand to be the seven saphyrot of the supracelestial world, which are the seven measures of the fabric of the celestial and in-","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"1.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0015","text":"iii A","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"1.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0016","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"1.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","text":"5\n\nferior [world], in which are comprehended the Ideas of all things belonging to the celestial and inferior regions. Beyond this number we can imagine nothing whatsoever. This septenary is a perfect number, because it contains both sexes, being made of even and odd; whence Virgil, wishing to call [men] perfectly blessed, said, thrice and four times. And Mercury Trismegistus in the Pimander, speaking of the creation of the world, introduces himself as asking: Whence did the elements of nature flow? And Pimander answers: From the will of God, which, having embraced the Word and most beautifully contemplated the world, adorned the remaining elements of itself after its pattern with living seeds.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"1.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","text":"Mind, however, God, most full of the fruitfulness of both sexes, being life and light, begot by his Word another mind, a craftsman; which indeed, being God of fire and spirit, thereafter fashioned seven governors, who encompass the sensible world in their circles. And indeed, since divinity has unfolded outwardly these seven measures, it is a sign that in the abyss of His divinity they are still implicitly contained; for less cannot come from what it does not have. Isaiah calls these columns women, when he says: Seven women shall take hold of one man for themselves. And he calls them women, which means passive, that is, produced. But if, as Paul says: He upholds all things by the word of his power. And elsewhere: One in all things, and all things in one. And to the Colossians:","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"1.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0019","text":"And he is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn of every creature, because in him all things were created in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, whether thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created through him and in him. It follows that we cannot find a greater explici-","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"1.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0020","text":"In ipso\nin ipsi\ncœle.\nPer ip\nsunt. i.\nte,","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"1.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0021","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"1.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","text":"tation, more capacious, than that of God. Now if the ancient Orators, wishing to place day by day the parts of the orations which they were to recite, entrusted them to perishable places, as things perishable, it is fitting that, wishing we to commit eternally the eternal things of all things which can be necessary to us in discourse, together with the eternal things of discourse itself, we should find for them eternal places. Our lofty labour, therefore, has been to find an order in these seven measures, capacious, sufficient, distinct, and such as always keeps the understanding awake and memory struck. But considering that if we wished to set someone before these most lofty measures, so far removed from our knowledge that they have been but obscurely touched even by Prophets, this would be to undertake a thing too difficult.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"1.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","text":"Therefore, in place of them we shall take the seven planets, whose natures are likewise quite well known even to common people; but we shall use them in such a manner that we do not propose them to ourselves as boundaries beyond which we ought not to go, but as those which ever represent to the minds of the wise the seven supracelestial measures. And it is fitting that, just as, in speaking of inferior things, the seven planets represent their nature to us, according as this is subject to that and that to the other, so, speaking also of the planets, our mind should return to those principles whence they have received their virtue.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"1.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","text":"This lofty and incomparable arrangement performs not only the office of preserving for us the things entrusted to us—words and art—so that, having first informed ourselves, we may safely find them at hand for every need of ours; but it also gives us true wisdom at its sources, leading us to knowledge of things through their causes, and","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"1.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0025","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"1.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","text":"not from the effects. Which we shall express more clearly by an example. If we were in a great wood, and had the desire to see it all well, while remaining in it we could not satisfy our desire; for, turning our sight about, we could see of it only a small part, the neighbouring trees preventing us from seeing those that are distant. But if near it there were a steep ascent, which led us up onto a high hill, on emerging from the wood by way of the ascent we should begin to see in great part its form; then, having climbed upon the hill, we could represent it entire. The wood is this our lower world; the steep ascent is the Heavens, and the hill the supracelestial world. And in order properly to understand these lower things, it is necessary to ascend to the higher ones;\nand, looking from on high downward, we may have a more certain knowledge of these.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"1.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","text":"Of this manner of understanding it seems that the ancient gentile writers were not altogether ignorant; concerning which Maximus Tyrius cites Homer, who sent Ulysses, having ascended to a high place, to consider the customs of the inhabitants. And Aristotle left it written for us that, if we were above the heavens, we could know the Eclipse of the Sun and of the Moon through their causes, without wishing to ascend to those causes from the effects. And Cicero, in the dream of the younger Scipio, has his grandfather show him earthly things from heaven. But Cicero and Aristotle, as those who understood no further, stopped at the heavens. And we, to whom God has given the light of His grace, ought not to be content to stop in the heavens; rather, with thought we ought to raise ourselves to that height whence our souls descended, and whither they must re-\nturn; for this is the true way of knowing and of under-","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"1.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0028","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"1.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0029","text":"standing. Wherefore we ought not presumptuously to think","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"1.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","text":"that by our own power we can attain thereto; for in this manner God would say to us that which was answered to Moses in his presumption: You shall see my back parts, but you shall not see my face. And this is: thou shalt see the effects of things, but not their reasons. Rather, we must pray His divine Majesty to make us worthy of that grace, which, when it then pleased Him, He gave to that same Moses, showing him His many marvels; and this shall be when we have become such that, annihilated and presuming nothing of ourselves, we may say with the Apostle: I no longer live, but Christ lives in me.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"1.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031","text":"Now, since our procedure is as reasonable as we have shown it to be, namely, to know low things from on high, and in our structure to take, in imitation of the celestial one, the number seven, in order to come to the first order I say that I find none more perfect or more divine than another septenary applied to each of the said columns, or to each of the said planets, as we may choose to call them. The most secret theologians, who are the Kabbalists, say therefore that Moses passed seven times through the seven Saphiroth, without ever being able to pass Binà. And they say that this is the limit to which the human intellect can be raised.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"1.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","text":"And although Moses, having reached the said Binà, had opposite him the face of the higher crown, and that of Chochmà, whence it is written he spoke face to face, nevertheless God Himself did not speak to him save through the angel (as is read in the Acts of the Apostles); and this happened because: No one knows the Son except the Father, nor does anyone know the Father except the Son, and he to whom","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"1.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0033","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"1.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0034","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"1.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0035","text":"7\n\nthe Son shall have wished to reveal. And Moses, having arrived at the Ri-\nna, in which there is an office of Angel called Mitrathon, that is, prince of faces, held his discourses with him. He having therefore ascended seven times seven stages, which are forty-nine, the number of remission—to which number Jesus Christ also willed that we should ascend in praying to the Father, because the prayer that we call the Lord's Prayer, according to the Hebrew text written by Matthew, consists of forty-nine words.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"1.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","text":"Imitating the shadow of these ascents, we have assigned seven doors, or steps, or distinctions, as we may choose to call them, to each planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"1.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","text":"But in order to give, so to speak, order to the order with such facility that we make students into spectators, we place before them the said seven measures, supported by the measures of the seven planets, in a spectacle—or, let us say, in a Theatre—distinguished by seven ascents. And because the ancient theatres were so ordered that, upon the steps nearest to the spectacle, the most honoured sat; then, successively, upon the ascending steps sat those who were of lesser dignity, until upon the highest steps the artisans sat, so that the nearer steps were assigned to the nobler, both on account of their proximity to the spectacle and also lest they should be offended by the breath of the artisans: we, following the order of the creation of the world, shall make the simplest, or the worthiest, things sit in the first steps, or those which we may imagine to have been, by divine disposition, before the other things created.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"1.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038","text":"Then we shall place, step by step, those which followed thereafter, so that in the seventh, that is, in the last and highest step, there shall sit","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"1.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0039","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"1.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","text":"not all the arts and faculties which fall under precepts, not by reason of worth, but by reason of time, these being as the last things discovered by men. In the first step, therefore, seven similar doors shall be seen, because each Planet in human form shall be painted above the door of the column destined for it; except at the column of the Sun, for since that is the noblest place in the whole Theatre, we wish that Apollo, who by right should be painted on an equal level with the others, yield to the continuum of the latitude of Beings, which is an image of divinity. Therefore, beneath the door of each planet shall be kept all things belonging both to the measure of its corresponding supracelestial one, and to those things which belong to that planet itself, and to the poets' fictions concerning it, as we shall now say particularly of each.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"1.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0041","text":"Beneath the door of the Moon there shall be treated its supracelestial world: Marent and Gabriel.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"1.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042","text":"Of the celestial: the Moon, its opacity, magnitude, and distance. In the fables: Diana, her insignia, and the number of Dianas.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"1.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0043","text":"Beneath the door of Mercury, in its supracelestial world, shall be Teſſoa and Michael.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"1.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0044","text":"In the celestial: its planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"1.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045","text":"In the fables: Mercury, messenger of the Gods, and his attributes.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"1.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0046","text":"Beneath the door of Venus, in the supracelestial: Hod, Nizach, Ho-\nmiel.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"1.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0047","text":"In the celestial: Venus, the planet,","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"1.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0048","text":"In the fables: Venus the Goddess, Cupid, her attributes, the clou","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"1.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0049","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"1.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0050","text":"8\n\nthe number of Venuses & Cupids.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"1.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051","text":"Under the fourth gate of the first grade of the Sun, [illegible] water we shall find (as has been said) not Apollo, [illegible], but a banquet, of which we shall speak when treating of the [illegible] grade. Under the fourth gate, therefore, we shall first find the latitude, or, let us say, the breadth of Beings, fashioned in the manner of a Pyramid, upon whose summit we shall imagine an indivisible point, which is to signify to us divinity both without relation and with relation: the Father, the Word before the incarnation and after, and the Holy Spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"1.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","text":"Next there will be seen an image of Pan, who, because with his head he signifies the supracelestial, with the golden horns that look upward, and with his beard the celestial influences, and with his starry skin the celestial world, and with his goat-like legs the lower [world]. Beneath this figure the three worlds will be signified.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"1.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053","text":"In the third place beneath the same gate there will appear to us the Fates, signifiers of fate, of the cause of the beginning, of the thing, of the effect & of the end. And this same image beneath Pasiphaë will signify man to be the cause of some thing. And beneath the Talaria it will signify to give cause. A fourth image will also be beneath this gate. And this will be a tree with a golden branch, which is that of which Virgil writes, that without this one cannot go to see the kingdom of Hell. And this image in this place will signify intelligible things, which cannot fall under sense, but we can only imagine and understand them, illuminated by the agent intellect. And this","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"1.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0054","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"1.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0055","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"1.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","text":"same image beneath the Gorgons will signify the agent intellect, of which we shall speak in its place. Under the idea of Mars, in the supracelestial world, Galiar, Camael, will be treated. In the celestial, Mars the Planet, and in the fables Mars the God, & his implements. Under the gate of Jupiter, in the supracelestial world, Chased, & Zadchiel. In the celestial, Jupiter the Planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"1.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0057","text":"In the fables, Jupiter the God & his insignia. Under Saturn we shall have, in the supracelestial, Bina & Zaphchiel. In the celestial, Saturn the Planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"1.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058","text":"In the fables, Saturn the God & his insignia. And with these subjects the first grade of the Theatre comes to be concluded.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"1.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0059","text":"The continuation.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"1.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0060","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"1.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0061","text":"9","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"1.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0061"]}],"source_digest":"b3a7a2ef26d707cfe9d9f12fbcd234a8ccc3257dc6b8ef4bcce14c1d17dd3dac","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO, DI MESSER GIVLIO Camillo."},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261031T001242023159Z_899f0df1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, BY MESSER GIULIO Camillo.","source_sha256":"a5a6ba05fa6ba9e1c7527ba9245f6760fe648d35572a4a1046bac166297d4087","sha256":"88efda6caaef2e2d51d29cf6e0faeb347cc2eca7d572e09d58bc7b0e87b2e38c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-31T00:12:42.023252+00:00","translate_quotations":true,"paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0001","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE,\nBY MESSER GIULIO\nCamillo.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"1.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 8, region 2]","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"1.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","text":"THE most ancient, and soundest writers have always been accustomed to entrust to their writings the secrets of God beneath obscure veils, so that they may not be understood save by those who (as Christ says) have ears to hear, that is, who are chosen by God to understand His most holy mysteries. And Melissus says that the ears of vulgar souls cannot endure the rays of divinity. And this is confirmed by the example of Moses, who, descending from the mount, upon which he had spoken with God, even through the mediation of the Angel, could not be looked upon by the people unless he hid his face with a veil. And the Apostles likewise, having seen Christ transfigu-\nred, that is, almost departed from the grossness of humanity unto the quasi-glory of divinity, being unable to behold Him because of their weakness, fell down. And in the Apocalypse one reads.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"1.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004","text":"And he made it known by sending through his angel to his servant John. Where it must be noted that even to John, although he was His servant, He did not open His understanding save through sig-\nnifications and visions. And truly, just as in worldly warfare the voices of captains, and trumpets, and standards are employed to lead and animate the armed ranks against their enemies, in no other manner in the warfare","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"1.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0005","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"1.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0006","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO,","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"1.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","text":"4\n\ndivine, we have, for the voice, the words of the Lord; the angelic trumpets, which are the voices of Prophets and preachers; and the standards, which are the signs of visi-\nons, which signify and do not express. To this we must add that Mercury Trismegistus says that speech religious and full of God comes to be violated when the vulgar multitude comes upon it. Whence, not without reason, the ancients kept, painted or carved, upon the doors of every temple a sphinx, showing by that image that one ought not publicly to speak of the things of God save by enigmas. This has also been taught us by God in several ways: that it is the saying of Christ that pearls must not be cast before swine, and that we should not give holy things to dogs. And speaking to His Apostles, He said to them.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"1.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","text":"To you it is given to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven; to the rest, in parables, so that seeing they may not see and hearing they may not understand. And in the fourth book of Ezra, God, speaking of Moses, whom He caused to ascend the mount, says: And I kept him with me for many days, and told him many wonders, secrets of the times, and the end; and I said: these things you shall make public, and these you shall hide. And David, speaking to God, says, Unveil my eyes, and I shall consider Thy wonders, where he said not that he ought to reveal, but only to consider the high marvels. Then, since divine things belong to the supercelestial world, and that world is separated from us by the mass of all the heavens, and our tongue cannot attain to the expression of it except (so to speak) by signs and similitudes; to the end that through visible things we may ascend to invisible ones.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"1.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0009","text":"A    iiii","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"1.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0010","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"1.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0011","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"1.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","text":"Nor is it permitted to me, even if God should grant us some grace to ascend to the third heaven and to see His secrets, to reveal those things which it is not permitted us to reveal; for in revealing them a dou-\nble error is committed. That is, to disclose them to un-\nworthy persons, and to treat them in this low tongue of ours, whereas that is the subject of the tongues of angels. Seeking to avoid these two inconveniences, John wrote his visions without attempting otherwise to expound them. And in our matters we make use of images, as signifiers of those things which ought not to be profaned. And how pleasing it is to God that His things be kept in the reverence of their veils, He Himself attests, calling Moses His faithful minister. And by the Kabbalists Ezekiel is called the rus-\ntic Prophet, for having, in the manner of a man of the countryside, disclosed all that he had seen.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"1.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","text":"Nor shall I be si-\nlent that the same Kabbalists maintain that Mary, the sis-\nter of Moses, was afflicted with leprosy for having revealed the secret things of divinity. And that for the same offence Ammonius died a foul and miserable death. And since it suffices us to have spoken thus much of the reverence of that silence in which we must keep holy things, let us proceed, in the name of the Lord, to speak of our Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"1.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","text":"Solomon, in the ninth of Proverbs, says that wisdom built herself a house, and founded it upon seven columns. These seven columns, signifying most steadfast eternity, we must understand to be the seven Sephiroth of the supercelestial world, which are the seven measures of the fabric of the celestial and the in-","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"1.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0015","text":"iii A","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"1.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0016","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"1.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","text":"5\n\nferior, in which are comprised the Ideas of all things belonging to the celestial and inferior regions. Beyond this number we can imagine nothing whatsoever. This septenary is a perfect number, because it contains both sexes, being made of even and odd; whence Virgil, wishing to say perfectly blessed, said, thrice and four times. And Mercury Trismegistus, in the Pimander, speaking of the creation of the world, introduces himself as asking: Whence did the elements of nature flow? And Pimander answers: From the will of God, which, having embraced the Word most beautifully, and having looked upon the world, adorned the remainder of itself with its own elements and vital seeds according to its exemplar.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"1.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","text":"But the Mind, God, most full of life and light, in the fecundity of both sexes, then by His Word begot another Mind, the craftsman, who indeed, being God of fire and spirit, thereafter made seven governors, who by their circles encompass the sensible world. And truly, since divinity has unfolded outside itself these seven measures, it is a sign that in the abyss of its divinity they are still implicitly contained; for nothing can come from that which does not have. Isaiah calls these columns women, when he says: Seven women shall lay hold of one man. And he calls them women, which means passive, that is, produced. But if, as Paul says: He bears all things by the word of His power. And elsewhere: One in all things, and all things in one. And to the Colossians:","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"1.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0019","text":"And the image of the invisible God, the firstborn of every creature, because in him all things were created, in heaven and on earth, visible and invisible, whether Thrones, or dominations, or principalities, or powers; all things were created through him and in him. It follows that we cannot find a greater expli-","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"1.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0020","text":"In him\nin him\nheaven.\nThrough him\nwere created. i.\nyou,","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"1.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0021","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"1.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","text":"cation more capacious than that of God. Now if the ancient Orators, wishing to place day by day the parts of the orations they were to recite, entrusted them to perishable places, as perishable things, it is fitting that, wishing we to entrust eternally the eternal things of all things that may be necessities of discourse, together with the eternal things of that discourse itself, we find for them eternal places. Our lofty labour, therefore, has been to find an order in these seven measures, capacious, sufficient, distinct, and such as may always keep the sense awake and memory struck. But considering that if we wished to place some persons before these most lofty measures, and so remote from our knowledge that they have only as yet been obscurely touched upon by Prophets, this would be to put hand to a matter too difficult.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"1.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","text":"Therefore, in place of them we shall take the seven planets, whose natures are also quite well known to ordinary people; but we shall use them in such a way that we do not set them before ourselves as boundaries beyond which we must not go, but as those which always represent to the minds of the wise the seven supercelestial measures. And it is quite fitting that, just as, speaking of inferior things, the seven planets represent their nature to us according as this is subject to that, and that to the other, so likewise, speaking of the planets, we return in mind to those principles whence they have received their power.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"1.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","text":"This lofty and incomparable arrangement not only performs the office of preserving for us the things, words, and arts entrusted to it, so that, having first been informed, we may find them safely at hand for every need of ours, but it also gives us true wisdom in its sources, leading us into knowledge of things from their causes, and","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"1.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0025","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"1.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","text":"not from the effects. Which we shall express more clearly by an example. If we were in a great wood, and had a desire to see it all well, while remaining in it we could not satisfy our desire; for, turning our sight about, we could see of it no more than a small part, the neighbouring trees preventing us from seeing those that are distant. But if near it there were a steep ascent, which led us up onto a high hill, on emerging from the wood at the ascent we should begin to see the form of it in large part; then, having ascended the hill, we could represent it entire. The wood is this our lower world, the steep ascent is the Heavens, and the hill the supercelestial world. And in order rightly to understand these lower things, it is necessary to ascend to the higher ones,\nand, looking from high downwards, we shall be able to have more certain knowledge of these.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"1.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","text":"Of this manner of understanding it seems that the ancient gentile writers were not altogether ignorant; concerning which Maximus Tyrius cites Homer, who sent Ulysses, having ascended to a high place, to consider the customs of the inhabitants. And Aristotle left us written that, if we were above the heavens, we could know the Eclipse of the Sun and of the Moon by their causes, without wishing to ascend to them from the effects. And Cicero, in the dream of the younger Scipio, has his grandfather show him terrestrial things from heaven. But Cicero and Aristotle, as men who understood no further, stopped at the heavens. And we, to whom God has given the light of His grace, ought not to be content to stop at the heavens; rather, with thought we must raise ourselves to that height whence our souls descended, and where they must re-\nturn, for this is the true way of knowing and of under-","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"1.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0028","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"1.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0029","text":"standing. Wherefore we ought not presumptuously to think","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"1.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","text":"that we can arrive there by our own power; for in this manner God would say to us that which was answered to Moses in his presumption: “You shall see my back parts, but you shall not see my face.” And this is: you shall see the effects of things, but not their reasons. Rather, we must pray His divine Majesty to make us worthy of that grace which, when it then pleased Him, He bestowed upon Moses himself, showing him His many marvels; and this will be when we have become such that, annihilated and presuming nothing of ourselves, we may say with the Apostle: “It is no longer I who live, but Christ lives in me.”","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"1.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031","text":"Now, since our proceeding is as reasonable as we have shown it to be, namely, to know low things from on high, and in our construction to take, in imitation of the celestial one, the number seven, in order to come to the first order I say that I find none more perfect or more divine than another sevenfold arrangement applied to each of the said columns, or indeed to each of the said planets, as we may wish to call them. Therefore the most secret theologians, who are the Kabbalists, say that Moses passed seven times through the seven Sephiroth without ever being able to pass Binà. And they say that this is the limit to which the human intellect can be raised.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"1.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","text":"And although Moses, having reached the said Binà, had facing him the face of the higher crown, and that of Chochmà, whence it is written, “he spoke face to face,” nevertheless God truly did not speak to him except through the angel (as is read in the Acts of the Apostles); and this happened because: “No one knows the Son except the Father, nor does anyone know the Father except the Son, and he to whom”","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"1.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0033","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"1.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0034","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"1.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0035","text":"7\n\n“the Son may wish to reveal [him].” And Moses, having arrived at Rinna, in which there is an office of Angel called Mitrathon, that is, “prince of faces,” held his discourses with him. Having therefore ascended seven times seven stages, which are forty-nine, the number of remission—to which number Jesus Christ also willed that we should ascend in praying to the Father, because the prayer that we call the Lord’s Prayer, according to the Hebrew text written by Matthew, consists of forty-nine words.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"1.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","text":"Imitating the shadow of these ascents, we have assigned seven gates, or degrees, or distinctions, as we may wish to call them, to each planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"1.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","text":"But in order to give, so to speak, order to the order with such ease that we make students as spectators, we set before them the said seven measures, sustained by the measures of the seven planets, in a spectacle—or, let us say, in a Theatre—distinguished into seven ascents. And because the ancient Theatres were so ordered that, upon the degrees nearest the spectacle, the most honoured persons sat, then, successively, upon the ascending degrees sat those who were of lesser dignity, so that upon the highest degrees the craftsmen sat, in such a way that the nearest degrees were assigned to the nobler persons, both because of their proximity to the spectacle and also so that they should not be offended by the breath of the craftsmen: we, following the order of the creation of the world, shall make sit on the first degrees the things more simple, or more worthy, or which we can imagine to have been, by divine disposition, before the other created things.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"1.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038","text":"Then we shall place, degree by degree, those which subsequently followed, in such a way that upon the seventh, that is, upon the last and highest degree, there shall sit","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"1.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0039","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"1.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","text":"not all the arts and faculties that fall under precepts, not by reason of rank, but by reason of time, those being as the last discovered by men. Upon the first degree, therefore, seven similar gates shall be seen, for each Planet in human figure shall be painted above the gate of the column assigned to it, save for the column of the Sun; for, that being the noblest place in the entire Theatre, we wish that Apollo, who by his nature ought to be painted on an equal degree with the others, should yield to the continuum of the latitude of Beings, which is an image of divinity. Therefore, beneath the gate of each planet shall be preserved all things belonging both to the measure of its corresponding supercelestial [world], and to those things that pertain to that planet itself, and to the fictions of the Poets concerning it, as we shall now say particularly of each.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"1.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0041","text":"Beneath the gate of the Moon there shall be treated, concerning its supercelestial world, Marent and Gabriel.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"1.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042","text":"Concerning the celestial [world]: the Moon, its opacity, magnitude, and distance. In the fables: Diana, her insignia, and the number of the Dianas.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"1.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0043","text":"Beneath the gate of Mercury, in its supercelestial world, shall be\nTessoa and Michael.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"1.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0044","text":"In the celestial [world], its planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"1.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045","text":"In the fables: Mercury, messenger of the Gods, and his emblems.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"1.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0046","text":"Beneath the gate of Venus, in the supercelestial [world]: Hod, Nizach, Ho-\nmiel.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"1.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0047","text":"In the celestial [world], Venus the planet,","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"1.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0048","text":"In the fables: Venus the Goddess, Cupid, her emblems, the clou","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"1.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0049","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"1.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0050","text":"8\n\nnumber of Venuses & Cupids.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"1.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051","text":"Under the fourth door of the first degree of the Sun, [illegible] we shall find the water (as has been said) not Apolline, [illegible], but a banquet, of which we shall speak when treating of the [illegible] degree. Under the fourth door, therefore, we shall first find the latitude, or, if we prefer to say it, the breadth of Be-\nings, made in the fashion of a Pyramid, above whose summit we shall imagine an indivisible point, which is to signify to us divin-\nity both without relation and with relation: the Father, the Word before the Incarnation and after, and the Holy Spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"1.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","text":"Beside it there will be seen an image of Pan, who, because by his head he signifies the supercelestial, by his golden horns, which look upward, and by his beard the celestial influences, by his starry skin the celestial world, and by his goat-like legs the lower world. Beneath this figure the three worlds will be signified.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"1.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053","text":"In the third place beneath the same door there will appear to us the Fates, signifying fate, the cause of the beginning, of the thing, of the effect, and of the end. And this same image beneath Pasiphaë will signify man to be the cause of some-\nthing. And beneath the Talaria it will signify to give cause. A fourth image will also be beneath this door. And this will be a tree with a golden branch, which is that of which Virgil writes, that without this one cannot go to see the kingdom of hell. And this image in this place will signify to us intelligible things, which cannot fall under sense, but which we can only imagi-\nne and understand when illuminated by the agent intellect. And this","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"1.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0054","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"1.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0055","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"1.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","text":"same image beneath the Gorgons will signify the agent intellect, of which we shall speak in its place. Under the idea of Mars, in the supercelestial world, Galiar, Camael will be treated. In the celestial, Mars the Planet, and in fables Mars the God and his accoutrements. Under the door of Jupiter, in the supercelestial world, Chased and Zadchiel. In the celestial, Jupiter the Planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"1.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0057","text":"In fables Jupiter the God & his insignia. Under Saturn we shall have in the supercelestial Bina & Zaph-\nchiel. In the celestial, Saturn the Planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"1.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058","text":"In fables Saturn the God & his insignia. And with these subjects the first degree of the Theatre comes to be concluded.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"1.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0059","text":"The continuation.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"1.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0060","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"1.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0061","text":"9","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"1.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0061"]}],"source_digest":"b3a7a2ef26d707cfe9d9f12fbcd234a8ccc3257dc6b8ef4bcce14c1d17dd3dac","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO, DI MESSER GIVLIO Camillo."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO, DI MESSER GIVLIO Camillo.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO","title":"THE BANQUET.","order":2,"chapter_id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO","text":"IL CONVIVIO.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 19, region 4]\n\nLſecondo grado del Theatro hauera le porte ſue dipin-\nte di una iſteſſa imagine, & queſta ſarà un conuinio. Finge Homero l’Oceano far un conuito à tutti i ſuoi Dei nè ſenza altiſſimo miſtero l’altiſſimo poeta fece tal fintio-\nne, intorno alla quale con la gratia di Dio noi ne diremo al-\ncuna coſa. Due ſono ſtate le produzioni, che Dio hà fatte, l’ una dentro della eſſẽza della ſua diuinità, et l’altra di fuori. La production di dentro, che è production ſenza principio, & (per dir coſi) conſuſtantiale, o co eſſentiale, & eterna è quella del verbo, della qual coſi dice Hieremia. Ego qui cæteris generationem tribuo, ſterilis ero? Et Giouanni volendo dir che foſſe coeterna diſſe. In principio erat verbum. Et per dichiarar che Dio è il principio aggiun-\nſe. Et verbum erat apud Deum. Appreſſo per farci intender la coeſſentia, perche ego in patre, & pater in me eſt, ſoggiu[n]ſe. Et Deus erat verbum. La production di fuor non è coeſſentiale, che fu fatta verbo tantum, & di nien-\nte, & in tempo. Et queſta fu la materia prima chiamata altramenti chaos, & da Platonici anima del mondo, & da Poeſti Proteo. Della quale Dio poi traſſe il cielo, la terra, & tutte le coſe. Et perche Platon nel Timeo crede queſta materia prima eſſere ſtata gemina, penſo che leſſen-\ndo Moſe in quel luogo; in principio creauit Deus cælum & terram, credeſſe Dio hauer fatto due materie, l’una del cielo, & l’altra della terra. Et qui è ben da notare; che\n\nDue pro-\nductioni\ndi Dio.\n\nIn princi-\npio. i. in\nprincipe\npatre.\n\nChaos\n\nAita del\nmondo\n\nProteo.\n\nCæli et\nterræ. i.\nmateriam\ncoeli &\nterræ.\n\nL’Idea del Theatro.\n\nB\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nSe hauessimo ad intender in queſto paſſaggio Moſe coſì ſemplicemente, cio è che Dio nell’vn giorno creaſſe il Cielo, & la Terra per Cielo formato & per Terra formata quali veggiamo,inutilmente ripiglierebbe poi, che il ſecon do giorno hauesse fatto la Rachia, che vuol dir la maſſa\nd. Cieli,& non il firmamento come dicono gli interpreti.\nEt inutilmente hauerebbe anchor meſſo il terzo giorno, nel\nqual fece apparir la terra. Ma ſi come ſe vno ſi voleſſe ve-\nſtir di lana,hauendo dauanti vna maſſa di lana non lavora\nta, potrebbe dir che quella foſſe la ſua berretta, la ſua cap-\npa,& le ſue calze,coſì diſſe Moſe che Dio creò il Cielo &\nla Terra,intendendo di quella maſſa,donde quelli ſi haue-\nuano à formare. Et Raimondo Lulio rende teſtimonio nel\nlibro,che egli chiama il ſuo teſtamento,ſcritto mentre egli\nera ritenuto in Inghilterra,che Dio creò vna materia pri-\nma,poi la diuise in tre parti,& che del fior della più eccel-\nlente fece gli angeli,& le anime noſtre,dell’altra i Cieli,\n& della terza queſto mondo inferiore. Or queſta materia\nprima appartenente & alla maſſa celeſte,& à queſto mon-\ndo inferiore, è continuamente ſotto la rota non voglio dir\ndella generatione, & della corruzzione,come ha in coſtu-\nme di ſcriver Ariſtotele, percioche queſti vocaboli di ſpica-\ntione à Mercurio Triſmegiſto,ma ſecondo la ſentenza di\nlui,della dimoſtratione,& del naſcondimento. Dice Mer-\ncurio nel Pimandro al XII. Capitolo, Sed appellationes,\nquædam falſæ homines turbant, neque enim, generatio vitæ\ncreatio eſt,ſed latentis explicatio vitæ,neque mutatio mors,\nſed occultatio potius, quum hæc igitur ita ſe habeant im-\nmortalia omnia. Et per dir in queſto ſuggetto quello che\n\nLa mate\nria prima\ntriplice.\nGenera-\ntione &\ncorruzzio\nne.\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n10\n\nal preſente ci occorre della generatione delle coſe, fanno i Pithagorici vna connumeration di ſei principij, da quali vogliono che tutte le coſe prouengano, & queſto chiamano Gamone, & queſto è tale. Sol lux lumen ſplendor calor Ge neratio. Et per lo Sole inteſero Dio padre, per la luce il figliu olo, per lo lume la mente angelica, ò il mondo intelligibi le, per lo ſplendore l’ anima del mondo, ò diciamo il Chao os, & per lo calore lo ſpirito del mondo, ò ſia il fiato dell’a nima, & coſì ſarà il Gamone.\n\nGamone.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 21, region 5]\n\nEt in queſta loro diuisione è da notar che coſì i Pithagorici come Platino trattando delle Idee non volſer collocar queſte le in Dio per eſſer ſempliciſſimo & per ciò quelle colloca-\nrono nella mente angelica. Il qual loro riſpetto fu ſouer chio, eſſendo quello, il ſopraceleſte dio, medeſimamente ſempliciſſimo, che anche il Sole è ſemplice, & moltiplici ſono i ſuoi raggi, & i ſuoi effetti. Et Dioniſio dice, che anchor che l’anima ſia ſemplice multiplici ſono le ſue ope-\nrationi, ſì come anchor ci ſi dimostra per quel luogo del Petrarca.\n\nLe Idee\ndi Dio.\n\nAnima che diuerſe coſe tante Vedi, odi, & leggi, & ſcriui, & parti, & penſi. E noi ſappiamo pur, che in Dio ſono le Idee, dicendo\n\nR  ii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nChaos:\n\nGiouanni quod factum eſt in ipſo vita erat. Non e da poſſe. ſar con ſilentio la cagione perche ſotto il nome dello ſplendore intendeſſero il Chaos. E adunque da ſapere che Or-\npheo ſcriuue il Chaos eſſer nato antiquiſſimo con l’amore nel grembo, ilquale lo riuolge alla mente, nella quale ſono impreſſe le Idee, & da quelle la forma concependo: per la lor bellezza viene ad acquiſtar ſplendore. Ma per tornare alla materia della generatione, credono i Pithagorici, & i Platonici il calor eſſere ſpirito, cio è fiato dell’anima del mondo in ogni coſa, ma occulto, & che di quel lo pregna la detta anima anelando lo partoriſca nel grembo della natura, & coſi lo coniunge col moto, & indi con giunto di eterna compagnia con maggior affetto ſoffia fuori ſpingendolo ſotto alla dimenſione, ne per tutto ciò lo ſparge, man coſal circuito. à ſe lo raccoglie. Et quan to eſſa piu ſi diffonde, tanto piu circonfonde, & manda qua ſi fuori con ogni, e muoue vn quaſi continuato ſpirito di la ſpirante. Queſta openione hanno tenuto que gli eccellenti ſpiriti, i quali non inteſero Chriſto, ma la uerita della generatione, o pur della dimoſtratione, & del naſcimento delle coſe è, che eſſendo la materia prima in ogni parte, & riducendoſi, o trouandoſi inſieme le coſe à diuersa natura come è l’acqua & la terra, eſſe mai non ſi congiuna-\nſe lo ſpirito di Chriſto non ſop-\nle coſe. aueniſſe, & in quelle entrando non le conciliaſſe ad eſſe car fuori il ſeme: orcelle dalle herbe & de fiori. Et quella ad mal gradoſſi ſi fa per l’ingroſſimento della materia, la qual poi aſſottigliandoſi, il che è lo ſecca[rſi], le coſe maniſe-\nſte ſi naſcondono, & lo ſpirito reſta & viue. Et coſi ſecono\n\nCome:\ngeneratione\n\nDIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO\tII\n\n[illegible]\n\ndo la ſentenza del Triſmegiſto immortalia omnia. Ma queſta è la [illegible] de urſi, i quali non vogliamo publicare accio che non ſi [illegible] In confermati. n della qual co ſa dice Paolo. Spiritus Chriſti, Spiritus vivificans. Et. Et al trove dice la ſcritura. Ego cœlum & terram impleo. Ego via, veritas, & vita. Et ſe queſto ſpirito non ſopraueniſſe à far la conciliatione, i contrari mai non ſi accordereb-\nbono. Et intorno a cio Mercurio ne fa un libro. Quod De us latens ſimul, ac patens ſit. Per tanto hauendo di ſopra propoſto il Canone de Pitagorini, quello riduceremo a tre capi, o vogliamo dire à tre principii in queſto mondo.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 23, region 4]\n\nChe il primo è l’autor di tutte le coſe, & il ſecondo è la vera luce, & ſapientia di Dio, in cui ſono le Idee di tutte le coſe, & il quale ſparge lo ſpirito vivificante. Et la terza è la materia nella quale ſ’imprimono le diuerſe forme del la dimoſtratione la quale coloro chiamano generatione, che viene in conſequenza, & non come principio. Et p̄ piu chiara dimoſtratione che la materia prima nō ſia coſſentiale ci piace di prouarlo per lo principio del Timeo di Plato, il qual coſi comincia. Unus, duo, tres. Unus ſigni Platon ſica Sol, Duo Lux, tres, Lumen. Poi ſoggiunge, Vel quar nel Tia tus? Et vien riſpoſto. Quartus lator at caue ſi. valetudì mea. ne. Et per queſto s’intiende la materia prima, la qual ſem\n\nB  iii\n\n11\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO:\n\npre ſi altera per le mutationi occultandoſi, & dimoſtrando ſi,& tale eſſendo, non e conſuſtantiale; & è inferma & gia tanti migliata d’anni, & per tante mutatione è da creder che vada deteriorando, & che ſi fruſtri, & quando non po tra piu, ne ſeguirà il giudicio vniuerſale.\n\nEloim i.\nVerbi.\n\nEt queſto La materia prima veramente dichiamo noi eſſer acqua, chiaramẽ percioche Moſe incontanente che hebbe fatto mention di re reſtiſſe quella, come di ſopra habbiamo detto della materia come pietro ne: ne al cielo, & alla terra, la qual diſſe eſſer inane: & vacua la ſeconda, cioè d’ogni forma, eſplicò per appoſition la ſua natura ſua eſſe. dicendo. Et Spiritus Eloim ferebatur ſuper aquas, benche il Teſto hebreo ſuoni incubabat. Et Morieno conclud[e] coſi. Er-\ndicendo. go aqua fuit antequam cœlum & terra. Et nel vero ſe la Cœli erãt prima production di dentro, che è del verbo porta il ſimbo prius & lo dell’acqua, eſſendo quello l’eſemplar di tutte le coſe, va terra de gione erà, che anchor la production di fuori fuſſe acqua aqua et p percioche, omnia per verbum fecit. Et quello fece il tutto aqua coſì conſimile. et benche dica l’acqua eſſere ſtata ſauorita dallo ſpirito di Eloim; che dee ſignificar in alcun modo calore, non ne dicendo dimeno l’humor nelle coſe diuine (come anchor proua Plo de aqua, Timo) non è ſenza calore, ne il calor ſenza l’humore, onde moſtra la egli proua in cielo non eſſer altro: che lume, & calor hude cauſa ma mido, & humor calido, ſenza la qual vnio[ne] non ſi potreb teriale. be far generatione. Et qui è da notar, che i Pithagorici nel Et p quel loro Gamone, dopo il calore mettono la generatione ſenza le, humore precedente humore, quaſi laſciandolo per inteſo ſotto il no p aqua & me del calore percioche ſono inſeparabili. La qual verità nota la, cõ facilmente conoſceremo nel ſopraceleſte. Impercioche quã efficiente. dunque dichiamo la Chochmà acquea, & la Rina ignea.\n\nal. 3. ca.\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n12\n\nNondimeno. Eſaia volendo dir, che nel ſegliuolo di Dio era ogni coſa, diſſe, Cibauit eum dominus pane vitæ, & intel lectus, & l’intelletto è dello ſpirito, & aqua ſapientiæ ſalu taris potauit illum. Et altrove. Egredietur virga de radice Ieſſe et flos de radice eius aſcendet; et requieſcet ſuper eũ ſpiritus Dei. Spũ ſapientiæ et intellectus, eſſendo pur la ſapie za della Chochmà, et l’intelletto della Binà. Et altrove an chor Eſaia. Donec abluerit ſordes filiorum Sion in ſpiritu iu dicii, & in ſpiritu ardoris. Doue è da notare, che eſſendo il giudicio del ſegliuolo, perche omne iudicium dedit mihi pater & eſſendo l’ardor dello Spirito Santo, & eſſendo la miſu ra del ſegliuolo l’acqua, vſando quel verbo abluere, dimo ſtrache l’humor con l’ardore inſieme ſiano congiunti. Et non eſſendo venuto altra perſona à lauare, che Chriſto, egli è quello, che ha fatto queſto lauamento d’humor meſco lato cō calore. Si che ſe bè Moſe diſſe, che lo ſpirito di Elo in ſuperiorità ſe acquagiò parla di coſe ſeparate, mà di coſe vnite & inſeparabili, & à queſto ſi accorda. Plotino nel libro de coelo, il qual tiene niuna altra coſa eſſere in cielo conſimile alle noſtre qualità in alcun modo, ſe non calor miſto con humor & lume. Et dice che il lume ſi ha in luogo d’intelligenza, & vuol che ’l calor ſia ſuſo ſia l’efficacia della vita et l’humor ſia il moto & il nutrimento di quel la. Ne quindi ſi ſente altramente il calor, che quaſi vn fauo re & nutrimento & ricreatione & vigore. Ne ni ſi ſente altramente l’humore, che quaſi vno aumento amplificatio ne, & ſoaue agilità, quali talhor ſentiamo appreſſo a noi. Adunque il calor del Cielo non pur dee eſſer chiamato cal do, ma anchor humido, cioè liquido, fluido, agile, lubricо et\n\nEum.i.\n\nB   iii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\npiaceuole, & al tatto della natura ſoane, diſſi al tatto della natura, percioche quello dell’huomo non vi puo arriuare, & diſſi della natura, per una total ſimilitudine al noſtro tat= to, & a noſtri oggetti. Et altrove afferma il medeſimo auſto re, il detto calore & humor celeſte eſſer molto diuerso in ge nere dal noſtro, & anchor più ch’il calor naturale in vn mi no dall’ardor di una fornace, & che la tepidezza del Sole dalle noſtre fiamme. Adunque ſi come l’humor celeſte non diſtilla per bagnare, coſì il calor celeſte non ſcalda per con= ſumare. Et eſſi fatto l’humore, è almen tanto dal noſtro humo re altero differente, quanto è differente l’humore dell’aere noſtro da quello dell’acqua, et io aggiungo alla ſotile ope nion di Plotino, che quella differenza che eſſo fa dal calor & humor celeſte a quello di queſto mondo, ſi dee intender che ſia anchor dal ſopraceleſte al celeſte. Ma tornando noi\n\nOceano.\n\nal conuito che l’Oceano fa à Dei, diciamo l’Oceano non eſſer altro, che l’acqua della ſapienza, che fu anchora auanti alla materia prima, che è la prima produzione, & i Dei conuiati non eſſer altro che le Idee nel diuino eſem= plar conſpiranti in vn medeſimo ſpirito, percioche tutto quel lo che è in Dio è eſſo Dio. Santo Agoſtino gran ſautor del le Idee, ſopra quel luogo di Giouanni. Quod factum eſt in\n\nNumero.\n\nipſo vita erat, adduce il detto di Salomone, che Dio haueua\n\nPeſo.\n\nfatte tutte le coſe in numero, in peſo, & in miſura, & con=\n\nMiſura.\n\nclude che ſi come noi in queſto mondo numerando, peſando, & miſurando non diamo co numerati peſati, & miſurati, i numeri, i peſi, & le miſure, ma ce li conſentiamo, coſì Dio ci fa veder in queſto mondo tutte le coſe ben numerate, peſa te, & miſurate, ma i numeri, i peſi, & le miſure ha voluto\n\nDI M. GEVLIO CAMILLO.  13\n\nche ſtanno fuor di quelle. Et eſſendo tutte le coſe che ſono, o Dio, o coſa produtta di fuori, & i detti numeri, peſi, & miſure non eſſendo produtti come gli altri numerali, peſati, et miſurati, ſeguita che ſtano eſſo Dio. Or di queſti numeri, peſi, & miſure ne fa mentione la ſcrittura, che nell’Euā gelo ſi legge. Capilli capitis veſtri numerati ſunt. Et nell’Apocalipſi ſi fa mention dell’Angelo con le billancie, & d’un altro che miſura con una canna. Et in Eſaia ſi legge. Ego ſum ipſe, ego ſum primus & nouiſſimus, manus mea fundauit cœlos, & dextera mea eſt cœlos, vel palmo con-\ncluſit cœlos.\n\nSono adunque le Idee forme & eſſemplari delle coſe eſſen-\ntiali nella eterna mente in quella eſſenti anchor prima che le coſe fatte foſſero, onde tutte le coſe create tirano l’eſſere, & portano come da ſigilli particolare impreſſione. Et coſi ſempre nel loro eſſere con Dio perſeuerano. Et la loro æter-\nnita fa che tutte le ſpecie rimangano eterne, anchor che gli indiuidui ſiano caduchi & mortali. Adunque quantunque gl’indiuidui ſi traſmutino, & corrompano, ouero ſi naſcon ſcano, nondimeno le ſpecie & le eterne Idee in Dio viuo ſempre viuono. Et per queſto Giovanni diſſe. Quod factum eſt in ipſo vita erat. cio è, tutto quello che è, & che noi veggiamo di fatto in queſto, o nel celeſte modo, era vita nel verbo, ne volle dir viuo, ma diede la medefima appellation del verbo, cioè è vita. & è anche ben da conſiderar quel prete-\nrito erat, che ſi contrappone à quello eſt apparente. Per le quali ragioni poſſiamo ben conſiderare il torto che hanno i Peripatetici negando le Idee, & dicendo gli uniuersi, ſali pro cedere à poſteriori, non à priori, & cio è, percioche la diuina\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nnò ſapienza va dimoſtrando loro l’ombra & i panni Ta lhor di ſe, mai’ viſo naſcondendo. Or adunque ſotto la porta del comminio appartenente à qualunque Pianeta dare mo gli elementi ſempliciſſimi, o uero coſe più vicine o al l’intelletto,o credute per autorità,che ſono poſte al ſenſo.\n\nLuna.\n\nSotto la porta del Comminio Lunare ſaranno coperte due imagini, quella di Protheo & quella di Nettuno col Tri dente.\n\nProtheo di più forme con faccia humana,ſignifica la materia prima, che fu la ſeconda produzione. Et ci auiſerà che dentro al ſuo cannone ſarà un volume ordinato per le gli,doue ſi tratterà della materia prima, o del Chaos che dire il vogliamo, & della ſua natura.capace di tutte le forme per ſucceſſione. Di eſſa forma,della priuatione, & di coſa naturale. Nettuno prometterà che nel ſuo volume ſi tratterà dell’elemento dell’ acqua puriſſimo et ſemplicis ſimo. Si dà à la Luna, per eſſer la Reina delle humidità. Queſta medeſima ſotto l’antro ſignificherà l’acquatico & ſuoi animali.\n\nSotto i Talari,tentare il guado,paſſar l’acqua, lavar con\nacqua,bagnar,bere,ſpruzzare.\n\nEt ſotto Prometheo,arti ſopra l’acque,come acquedutti,fon tane artificiate,ponti, Arzena, arte nauale, & l’arte del notare,& peſcare.\n\nMercurio\n\nSotto il Conuinio di Mercurio ſarà vna imagine di Elefan te,il quale percioche è detto da Scrittori eſſere il più reli-\ngioſo animal di tutti i bruti,vogliamo che nel volume del ſuo cannone ſi habbia à trattar della origine de Dei fauo loſi,della loro deità,& de loro nomi,& percioche dal cie-\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n14\n\nFar delle favole venne quella opinione, queſto ſuggetto a Mercurio, appartenente, come à patron della lingua & del favoleggiare queſta medesima figura ſotto Prometheo ſiè ſignifichera religione verſo i Dei favoloſi. Sotto il dominio di Venere ſarà una ſpera con dieci circo-\nli, & il decimo ſarà aureo, & carico di ſpiritelli d’aperta-\ntutto il cui volume ſarà in ſuggetto di campi Eliſii, & & dell’anime de beati, o ſtarà già in queſto mondo, o per ve-\nnire, ſecondo la openion di Platonici, & di alcuni poeti. Et in quello ſi tratterà anchor del paradijo terreſtre: & ſotto Venere ſi locarno per la dilettatione & vaghezza di quei luoghi.\n\nVenere.\n\nDel Dominio del ſole habbiamo parlato nel pri mo grado. Hor ſi come in quel luogo, dove per l’ordinario dovea eſſer Apollo, vi ſu locato il dominio, coſì in queſto luo go ordinario del dominio ſarà collocato Apollo, & ſotto la porta ſua nel mondo ſopracelleſte ſi tratterà di Tipheret, et di Raphael. Nel celeſte ſi tratterà di eſſo Sole, della lu ce, del lume, dello ſplendore & de raggi. Nelle favole di Apollo Dio & ſuoi appartenenti. Sotto il dominio di Marte ſaranno due imagini, vn Vulcano, & una bocca Tartarea aperta, & divorare anime, qual nelle pitture Fiamminghe ſi ſuol vedere. Vulcano ſignifichera ſotto queſta porta il fuoco ſemplice. Sotto l’altro l’ethere, il fuoco elementale, l’incendio vniuerſale, il fuoco no ſtro, l’incendio particolare, fauilla, fiamma, carbone, et cenere. Sotto i Tatari ſignifichera batter fuoco, ſvegliarlo nell’eſca, accenderlo, metter incendio, & eſtinguere. Sotto Prometheo conterrera tutte le arti fabricili che ſi fanno con fuoco.\n\nSole.\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nLa bocca Tartarea coprirà vn volume, doue ſi ritrerà diſ-\nſtintamente del Purgatorio, & de purgatori luoghi, ſecondo la opinione de gli ſcrittori, che ne hanno laſciato ſcritto, il qual Purgatorio diamo à Marte, percioche anchor’a il fo-\nro miſſo è martiale, & non differente dall’infernale, che ap-\npartiene à Saturno, ſe non in quanto la pena, che le anime patiſcono nel martiale, è temporale, ma quella dell’inferno & Saturnina è eterna, conueniente alla tardità di Saturno.\n\nQueſta medeſima bocca contienerà anchor quel luogo, che è chiamato limbo con tutte quelle anime che ſtanno con qual-\nche ſperanza di ſalute.\n\nSotto il Conuiuio di Gioue ſaranno due imagini, vna ſarà\nGiunon ſuſpeſa, & l’altra Europa.\n\nGiunon ſuſpeſa pigliamo da Homero, il qual finge Gioue tener quella ſuſpeſa per vna catena, & Giunone hauer à ciaſcun piede vn contrapeſo. Gioue è il tenitore di tutto l’aere. Il contrapeſo del piu ſollevato piede è l’acqua, & quello del piu baſſo è la terra. Queſta imagine adunque in queſto luogo ſignificherà l’aere ſemplice. Ma ſotto l’altro contrapeſo i quattro elementi in generale, & appreſſo l’aere in particolare con le ſue parti, & ſuoi appartenenti, come ſi dirà in quel luogo.\n\nEt ſotto i Tàari ſignificherà reſpirar, ſoſpirar vſar l’aper-\nto cielo.\n\nEt ſotto Prometheo ſignificherà qualunque arte, che per be-\nneficio dell’aere ſi faccia, come i molini da vento.\n\nEuropa rapita dal Toro, & per lo mare portata, riguardan-\ndo non la parte alla quale ella è portata, ma a quella onde ella ſi è partita, è l’anima portata dal corpo per lo pelago\n\nDIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO     15\n\ndi quello modo, la qual ſi rivolge pure a Dio terra ſopraſ-\nſelte, & queſta coprirà un volume appartenente al paradiso ſo uero & Chriſtiano, & a tutte l’anime beate già ſepara te, & queſto è dato a Gioue per eſſer pianeta di vera & ottima religione. Et queſta ſotto Prometheo ſignificherà conuerſione, conſen-\ntimento, annichilatione, ſanità, & Religione. Sotto il Conuiuio di Saturno ſaranno due imagini, di Cibele. Saturno, le una, come ella è deſcritta da Lucretio inghirlandata di Cibele, torri, & tirata da due Leoni legati al carro di lei, la quale ſignificando la terra, a noi in queſto luogo ſignificherà la terra ſemplice & uirginea. Queſta medeſima ſotto l’altro conterrà la terra et le ſue parti, & qualità, come ſi dirà nel luogo ſuo, et ſarà anchor queſta ſotto i Talari, & ſotto Prometheo. L’altra imagine di Cibele gitterà un moſtro di fuoco, & ſotto queſta ſarà il volume dell’inferno, & de nomi delle ſue magioni, & le anime dannate. Et la cagion perche deſ-\ntino l’Inferno a Saturno è detta nel conuiuio di Marte.\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0001","text":"IL CONVIVIO.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"2.1"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 19, region 4]","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"2.2"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","text":"Lſecondo grado del Theatro hauera le porte ſue dipin-\nte di una iſteſſa imagine, & queſta ſarà un conuinio. Finge Homero l’Oceano far un conuito à tutti i ſuoi Dei nè ſenza altiſſimo miſtero l’altiſſimo poeta fece tal fintio-\nne, intorno alla quale con la gratia di Dio noi ne diremo al-\ncuna coſa. Due ſono ſtate le produzioni, che Dio hà fatte, l’ una dentro della eſſẽza della ſua diuinità, et l’altra di fuori. La production di dentro, che è production ſenza principio, & (per dir coſi) conſuſtantiale, o co eſſentiale, & eterna è quella del verbo, della qual coſi dice Hieremia. Ego qui cæteris generationem tribuo, ſterilis ero? Et Giouanni volendo dir che foſſe coeterna diſſe. In principio erat verbum. Et per dichiarar che Dio è il principio aggiun-\nſe. Et verbum erat apud Deum. Appreſſo per farci intender la coeſſentia, perche ego in patre, & pater in me eſt, ſoggiu[n]ſe.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"2.3"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","text":"Et Deus erat verbum. La production di fuor non è coeſſentiale, che fu fatta verbo tantum, & di nien-\nte, & in tempo. Et queſta fu la materia prima chiamata altramenti chaos, & da Platonici anima del mondo, & da Poeſti Proteo. Della quale Dio poi traſſe il cielo, la terra, & tutte le coſe. Et perche Platon nel Timeo crede queſta materia prima eſſere ſtata gemina, penſo che leſſen-\ndo Moſe in quel luogo; in principio creauit Deus cælum & terram, credeſſe Dio hauer fatto due materie, l’una del cielo, & l’altra della terra. Et qui è ben da notare; che","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"2.4"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0005","text":"Due pro-\nductioni\ndi Dio.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"2.5"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0006","text":"In princi-\npio. i. in\nprincipe\npatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"2.6"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0007","text":"Chaos","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"2.7"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0008","text":"Aita del\nmondo","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"2.8"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0009","text":"Proteo.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"2.9"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0010","text":"Cæli et\nterræ. i.\nmateriam\ncoeli &\nterræ.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"2.10"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0011","text":"L’Idea del Theatro.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"2.11"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0012","text":"B\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"2.12"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","text":"Se hauessimo ad intender in queſto paſſaggio Moſe coſì ſemplicemente, cio è che Dio nell’vn giorno creaſſe il Cielo, & la Terra per Cielo formato & per Terra formata quali veggiamo,inutilmente ripiglierebbe poi, che il ſecon do giorno hauesse fatto la Rachia, che vuol dir la maſſa\nd. Cieli,& non il firmamento come dicono gli interpreti.\nEt inutilmente hauerebbe anchor meſſo il terzo giorno, nel\nqual fece apparir la terra. Ma ſi come ſe vno ſi voleſſe ve-\nſtir di lana,hauendo dauanti vna maſſa di lana non lavora\nta, potrebbe dir che quella foſſe la ſua berretta, la ſua cap-\npa,& le ſue calze,coſì diſſe Moſe che Dio creò il Cielo &\nla Terra,intendendo di quella maſſa,donde quelli ſi haue-\nuano à formare.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"2.13"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","text":"Et Raimondo Lulio rende teſtimonio nel\nlibro,che egli chiama il ſuo teſtamento,ſcritto mentre egli\nera ritenuto in Inghilterra,che Dio creò vna materia pri-\nma,poi la diuise in tre parti,& che del fior della più eccel-\nlente fece gli angeli,& le anime noſtre,dell’altra i Cieli,\n& della terza queſto mondo inferiore. Or queſta materia\nprima appartenente & alla maſſa celeſte,& à queſto mon-\ndo inferiore, è continuamente ſotto la rota non voglio dir\ndella generatione, & della corruzzione,come ha in coſtu-\nme di ſcriver Ariſtotele, percioche queſti vocaboli di ſpica-\ntione à Mercurio Triſmegiſto,ma ſecondo la ſentenza di\nlui,della dimoſtratione,& del naſcondimento. Dice Mer-\ncurio nel Pimandro al XII.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"2.14"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","text":"Capitolo, Sed appellationes,\nquædam falſæ homines turbant, neque enim, generatio vitæ\ncreatio eſt,ſed latentis explicatio vitæ,neque mutatio mors,\nſed occultatio potius, quum hæc igitur ita ſe habeant im-\nmortalia omnia. Et per dir in queſto ſuggetto quello che","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"2.15"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0016","text":"La mate\nria prima\ntriplice.\nGenera-\ntione &\ncorruzzio\nne.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"2.16"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0017","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"2.17"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0018","text":"10","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"2.18"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019","text":"al preſente ci occorre della generatione delle coſe, fanno i Pithagorici vna connumeration di ſei principij, da quali vogliono che tutte le coſe prouengano, & queſto chiamano Gamone, & queſto è tale. Sol lux lumen ſplendor calor Ge neratio. Et per lo Sole inteſero Dio padre, per la luce il figliu olo, per lo lume la mente angelica, ò il mondo intelligibi le, per lo ſplendore l’ anima del mondo, ò diciamo il Chao os, & per lo calore lo ſpirito del mondo, ò ſia il fiato dell’a nima, & coſì ſarà il Gamone.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"2.19"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0020","text":"Gamone.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"2.20"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0021","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 21, region 5]","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"2.21"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","text":"Et in queſta loro diuisione è da notar che coſì i Pithagorici come Platino trattando delle Idee non volſer collocar queſte le in Dio per eſſer ſempliciſſimo & per ciò quelle colloca-\nrono nella mente angelica. Il qual loro riſpetto fu ſouer chio, eſſendo quello, il ſopraceleſte dio, medeſimamente ſempliciſſimo, che anche il Sole è ſemplice, & moltiplici ſono i ſuoi raggi, & i ſuoi effetti. Et Dioniſio dice, che anchor che l’anima ſia ſemplice multiplici ſono le ſue ope-\nrationi, ſì come anchor ci ſi dimostra per quel luogo del Petrarca.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"2.22"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0023","text":"Le Idee\ndi Dio.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"2.23"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","text":"Anima che diuerſe coſe tante Vedi, odi, & leggi, & ſcriui, & parti, & penſi. E noi ſappiamo pur, che in Dio ſono le Idee, dicendo","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"2.24"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0025","text":"R  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"2.25"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0026","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"2.26"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0027","text":"Chaos:","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"2.27"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0028","text":"Giouanni quod factum eſt in ipſo vita erat. Non e da poſſe. ſar con ſilentio la cagione perche ſotto il nome dello ſplendore intendeſſero il Chaos. E adunque da ſapere che Or-\npheo ſcriuue il Chaos eſſer nato antiquiſſimo con l’amore nel grembo, ilquale lo riuolge alla mente, nella quale ſono impreſſe le Idee, & da quelle la forma concependo: per la lor bellezza viene ad acquiſtar ſplendore. Ma per tornare alla materia della generatione, credono i Pithagorici, & i Platonici il calor eſſere ſpirito, cio è fiato dell’anima del mondo in ogni coſa, ma occulto, & che di quel lo pregna la detta anima anelando lo partoriſca nel grembo della natura, & coſi lo coniunge col moto, & indi con giunto di eterna compagnia con maggior affetto ſoffia fuori ſpingendolo ſotto alla dimenſione, ne per tutto ciò lo ſparge, man coſal circuito. à ſe lo raccoglie.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"2.28"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","text":"Et quan to eſſa piu ſi diffonde, tanto piu circonfonde, & manda qua ſi fuori con ogni, e muoue vn quaſi continuato ſpirito di la ſpirante. Queſta openione hanno tenuto que gli eccellenti ſpiriti, i quali non inteſero Chriſto, ma la uerita della generatione, o pur della dimoſtratione, & del naſcimento delle coſe è, che eſſendo la materia prima in ogni parte, & riducendoſi, o trouandoſi inſieme le coſe à diuersa natura come è l’acqua & la terra, eſſe mai non ſi congiuna-\nſe lo ſpirito di Chriſto non ſop-\nle coſe. aueniſſe, & in quelle entrando non le conciliaſſe ad eſſe car fuori il ſeme: orcelle dalle herbe & de fiori. Et quella ad mal gradoſſi ſi fa per l’ingroſſimento della materia, la qual poi aſſottigliandoſi, il che è lo ſecca[rſi], le coſe maniſe-\nſte ſi naſcondono, & lo ſpirito reſta & viue. Et coſi ſecono","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"2.29"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0030","text":"Come:\ngeneratione","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"2.30"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0031","text":"DIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO\tII","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"2.31"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0032","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"2.32"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","text":"do la ſentenza del Triſmegiſto immortalia omnia. Ma queſta è la [illegible] de urſi, i quali non vogliamo publicare accio che non ſi [illegible] In confermati. n della qual co ſa dice Paolo. Spiritus Chriſti, Spiritus vivificans. Et. Et al trove dice la ſcritura. Ego cœlum & terram impleo. Ego via, veritas, & vita. Et ſe queſto ſpirito non ſopraueniſſe à far la conciliatione, i contrari mai non ſi accordereb-\nbono. Et intorno a cio Mercurio ne fa un libro. Quod De us latens ſimul, ac patens ſit. Per tanto hauendo di ſopra propoſto il Canone de Pitagorini, quello riduceremo a tre capi, o vogliamo dire à tre principii in queſto mondo.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"2.33"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0034","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 23, region 4]","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"2.34"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","text":"Che il primo è l’autor di tutte le coſe, & il ſecondo è la vera luce, & ſapientia di Dio, in cui ſono le Idee di tutte le coſe, & il quale ſparge lo ſpirito vivificante. Et la terza è la materia nella quale ſ’imprimono le diuerſe forme del la dimoſtratione la quale coloro chiamano generatione, che viene in conſequenza, & non come principio. Et p̄ piu chiara dimoſtratione che la materia prima nō ſia coſſentiale ci piace di prouarlo per lo principio del Timeo di Plato, il qual coſi comincia. Unus, duo, tres. Unus ſigni Platon ſica Sol, Duo Lux, tres, Lumen. Poi ſoggiunge, Vel quar nel Tia tus? Et vien riſpoſto. Quartus lator at caue ſi. valetudì mea. ne. Et per queſto s’intiende la materia prima, la qual ſem","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"2.35"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0036","text":"B  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"2.36"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0037","text":"11","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"2.37"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0038","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO:","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"2.38"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","text":"pre ſi altera per le mutationi occultandoſi, & dimoſtrando ſi,& tale eſſendo, non e conſuſtantiale; & è inferma & gia tanti migliata d’anni, & per tante mutatione è da creder che vada deteriorando, & che ſi fruſtri, & quando non po tra piu, ne ſeguirà il giudicio vniuerſale.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"2.39"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0040","text":"Eloim i.\nVerbi.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"2.40"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","text":"Et queſto La materia prima veramente dichiamo noi eſſer acqua, chiaramẽ percioche Moſe incontanente che hebbe fatto mention di re reſtiſſe quella, come di ſopra habbiamo detto della materia come pietro ne: ne al cielo, & alla terra, la qual diſſe eſſer inane: & vacua la ſeconda, cioè d’ogni forma, eſplicò per appoſition la ſua natura ſua eſſe. dicendo. Et Spiritus Eloim ferebatur ſuper aquas, benche il Teſto hebreo ſuoni incubabat. Et Morieno conclud[e] coſi. Er-\ndicendo. go aqua fuit antequam cœlum & terra. Et nel vero ſe la Cœli erãt prima production di dentro, che è del verbo porta il ſimbo prius & lo dell’acqua, eſſendo quello l’eſemplar di tutte le coſe, va terra de gione erà, che anchor la production di fuori fuſſe acqua aqua et p percioche, omnia per verbum fecit. Et quello fece il tutto aqua coſì conſimile.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"2.41"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","text":"et benche dica l’acqua eſſere ſtata ſauorita dallo ſpirito di Eloim; che dee ſignificar in alcun modo calore, non ne dicendo dimeno l’humor nelle coſe diuine (come anchor proua Plo de aqua, Timo) non è ſenza calore, ne il calor ſenza l’humore, onde moſtra la egli proua in cielo non eſſer altro: che lume, & calor hude cauſa ma mido, & humor calido, ſenza la qual vnio[ne] non ſi potreb teriale. be far generatione. Et qui è da notar, che i Pithagorici nel Et p quel loro Gamone, dopo il calore mettono la generatione ſenza le, humore precedente humore, quaſi laſciandolo per inteſo ſotto il no p aqua & me del calore percioche ſono inſeparabili. La qual verità nota la, cõ facilmente conoſceremo nel ſopraceleſte. Impercioche quã efficiente. dunque dichiamo la Chochmà acquea, & la Rina ignea.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"2.42"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0043","text":"al. 3. ca.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"2.43"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0044","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"2.44"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0045","text":"12","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"2.45"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0046","text":"Nondimeno. Eſaia volendo dir, che nel ſegliuolo di Dio era ogni coſa, diſſe, Cibauit eum dominus pane vitæ, & intel lectus, & l’intelletto è dello ſpirito, & aqua ſapientiæ ſalu taris potauit illum. Et altrove. Egredietur virga de radice Ieſſe et flos de radice eius aſcendet; et requieſcet ſuper eũ ſpiritus Dei. Spũ ſapientiæ et intellectus, eſſendo pur la ſapie za della Chochmà, et l’intelletto della Binà. Et altrove an chor Eſaia. Donec abluerit ſordes filiorum Sion in ſpiritu iu dicii, & in ſpiritu ardoris. Doue è da notare, che eſſendo il giudicio del ſegliuolo, perche omne iudicium dedit mihi pater & eſſendo l’ardor dello Spirito Santo, & eſſendo la miſu ra del ſegliuolo l’acqua, vſando quel verbo abluere, dimo ſtrache l’humor con l’ardore inſieme ſiano congiunti.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"2.46"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","text":"Et non eſſendo venuto altra perſona à lauare, che Chriſto, egli è quello, che ha fatto queſto lauamento d’humor meſco lato cō calore. Si che ſe bè Moſe diſſe, che lo ſpirito di Elo in ſuperiorità ſe acquagiò parla di coſe ſeparate, mà di coſe vnite & inſeparabili, & à queſto ſi accorda. Plotino nel libro de coelo, il qual tiene niuna altra coſa eſſere in cielo conſimile alle noſtre qualità in alcun modo, ſe non calor miſto con humor & lume. Et dice che il lume ſi ha in luogo d’intelligenza, & vuol che ’l calor ſia ſuſo ſia l’efficacia della vita et l’humor ſia il moto & il nutrimento di quel la. Ne quindi ſi ſente altramente il calor, che quaſi vn fauo re & nutrimento & ricreatione & vigore. Ne ni ſi ſente altramente l’humore, che quaſi vno aumento amplificatio ne, & ſoaue agilità, quali talhor ſentiamo appreſſo a noi.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"2.47"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0048","text":"Adunque il calor del Cielo non pur dee eſſer chiamato cal do, ma anchor humido, cioè liquido, fluido, agile, lubricо et","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"2.48"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0049","text":"Eum.i.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"2.49"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0050","text":"B   iii","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"2.50"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0051","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"2.51"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052","text":"piaceuole, & al tatto della natura ſoane, diſſi al tatto della natura, percioche quello dell’huomo non vi puo arriuare, & diſſi della natura, per una total ſimilitudine al noſtro tat= to, & a noſtri oggetti. Et altrove afferma il medeſimo auſto re, il detto calore & humor celeſte eſſer molto diuerso in ge nere dal noſtro, & anchor più ch’il calor naturale in vn mi no dall’ardor di una fornace, & che la tepidezza del Sole dalle noſtre fiamme. Adunque ſi come l’humor celeſte non diſtilla per bagnare, coſì il calor celeſte non ſcalda per con= ſumare. Et eſſi fatto l’humore, è almen tanto dal noſtro humo re altero differente, quanto è differente l’humore dell’aere noſtro da quello dell’acqua, et io aggiungo alla ſotile ope nion di Plotino, che quella differenza che eſſo fa dal calor & humor celeſte a quello di queſto mondo, ſi dee intender che ſia anchor dal ſopraceleſte al celeſte.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"2.52"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0053","text":"Ma tornando noi","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"2.53"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0054","text":"Oceano.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"2.54"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","text":"al conuito che l’Oceano fa à Dei, diciamo l’Oceano non eſſer altro, che l’acqua della ſapienza, che fu anchora auanti alla materia prima, che è la prima produzione, & i Dei conuiati non eſſer altro che le Idee nel diuino eſem= plar conſpiranti in vn medeſimo ſpirito, percioche tutto quel lo che è in Dio è eſſo Dio. Santo Agoſtino gran ſautor del le Idee, ſopra quel luogo di Giouanni. Quod factum eſt in","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"2.55"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0056","text":"Numero.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"2.56"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0057","text":"ipſo vita erat, adduce il detto di Salomone, che Dio haueua","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"2.57"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0058","text":"Peſo.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"2.58"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0059","text":"fatte tutte le coſe in numero, in peſo, & in miſura, & con=","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"2.59"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0060","text":"Miſura.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"2.60"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","text":"clude che ſi come noi in queſto mondo numerando, peſando, & miſurando non diamo co numerati peſati, & miſurati, i numeri, i peſi, & le miſure, ma ce li conſentiamo, coſì Dio ci fa veder in queſto mondo tutte le coſe ben numerate, peſa te, & miſurate, ma i numeri, i peſi, & le miſure ha voluto","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"2.61"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0062","text":"DI M. GEVLIO CAMILLO.  13","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"2.62"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","text":"che ſtanno fuor di quelle. Et eſſendo tutte le coſe che ſono, o Dio, o coſa produtta di fuori, & i detti numeri, peſi, & miſure non eſſendo produtti come gli altri numerali, peſati, et miſurati, ſeguita che ſtano eſſo Dio. Or di queſti numeri, peſi, & miſure ne fa mentione la ſcrittura, che nell’Euā gelo ſi legge. Capilli capitis veſtri numerati ſunt. Et nell’Apocalipſi ſi fa mention dell’Angelo con le billancie, & d’un altro che miſura con una canna. Et in Eſaia ſi legge. Ego ſum ipſe, ego ſum primus & nouiſſimus, manus mea fundauit cœlos, & dextera mea eſt cœlos, vel palmo con-\ncluſit cœlos.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"2.63"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","text":"Sono adunque le Idee forme & eſſemplari delle coſe eſſen-\ntiali nella eterna mente in quella eſſenti anchor prima che le coſe fatte foſſero, onde tutte le coſe create tirano l’eſſere, & portano come da ſigilli particolare impreſſione. Et coſi ſempre nel loro eſſere con Dio perſeuerano. Et la loro æter-\nnita fa che tutte le ſpecie rimangano eterne, anchor che gli indiuidui ſiano caduchi & mortali. Adunque quantunque gl’indiuidui ſi traſmutino, & corrompano, ouero ſi naſcon ſcano, nondimeno le ſpecie & le eterne Idee in Dio viuo ſempre viuono. Et per queſto Giovanni diſſe. Quod factum eſt in ipſo vita erat. cio è, tutto quello che è, & che noi veggiamo di fatto in queſto, o nel celeſte modo, era vita nel verbo, ne volle dir viuo, ma diede la medefima appellation del verbo, cioè è vita. & è anche ben da conſiderar quel prete-\nrito erat, che ſi contrappone à quello eſt apparente.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"2.64"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065","text":"Per le quali ragioni poſſiamo ben conſiderare il torto che hanno i Peripatetici negando le Idee, & dicendo gli uniuersi, ſali pro cedere à poſteriori, non à priori, & cio è, percioche la diuina","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"2.65"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0066","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"2.66"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","text":"nò ſapienza va dimoſtrando loro l’ombra & i panni Ta lhor di ſe, mai’ viſo naſcondendo. Or adunque ſotto la porta del comminio appartenente à qualunque Pianeta dare mo gli elementi ſempliciſſimi, o uero coſe più vicine o al l’intelletto,o credute per autorità,che ſono poſte al ſenſo.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"2.67"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0068","text":"Luna.","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"2.68"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069","text":"Sotto la porta del Comminio Lunare ſaranno coperte due imagini, quella di Protheo & quella di Nettuno col Tri dente.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"2.69"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","text":"Protheo di più forme con faccia humana,ſignifica la materia prima, che fu la ſeconda produzione. Et ci auiſerà che dentro al ſuo cannone ſarà un volume ordinato per le gli,doue ſi tratterà della materia prima, o del Chaos che dire il vogliamo, & della ſua natura.capace di tutte le forme per ſucceſſione. Di eſſa forma,della priuatione, & di coſa naturale. Nettuno prometterà che nel ſuo volume ſi tratterà dell’elemento dell’ acqua puriſſimo et ſemplicis ſimo. Si dà à la Luna, per eſſer la Reina delle humidità. Queſta medeſima ſotto l’antro ſignificherà l’acquatico & ſuoi animali.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"2.70"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","text":"Sotto i Talari,tentare il guado,paſſar l’acqua, lavar con\nacqua,bagnar,bere,ſpruzzare.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"2.71"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","text":"Et ſotto Prometheo,arti ſopra l’acque,come acquedutti,fon tane artificiate,ponti, Arzena, arte nauale, & l’arte del notare,& peſcare.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"2.72"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0073","text":"Mercurio","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"2.73"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","text":"Sotto il Conuinio di Mercurio ſarà vna imagine di Elefan te,il quale percioche è detto da Scrittori eſſere il più reli-\ngioſo animal di tutti i bruti,vogliamo che nel volume del ſuo cannone ſi habbia à trattar della origine de Dei fauo loſi,della loro deità,& de loro nomi,& percioche dal cie-","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"2.74"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0075","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"2.75"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0076","text":"14","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"2.76"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","text":"Far delle favole venne quella opinione, queſto ſuggetto a Mercurio, appartenente, come à patron della lingua & del favoleggiare queſta medesima figura ſotto Prometheo ſiè ſignifichera religione verſo i Dei favoloſi. Sotto il dominio di Venere ſarà una ſpera con dieci circo-\nli, & il decimo ſarà aureo, & carico di ſpiritelli d’aperta-\ntutto il cui volume ſarà in ſuggetto di campi Eliſii, & & dell’anime de beati, o ſtarà già in queſto mondo, o per ve-\nnire, ſecondo la openion di Platonici, & di alcuni poeti. Et in quello ſi tratterà anchor del paradijo terreſtre: & ſotto Venere ſi locarno per la dilettatione & vaghezza di quei luoghi.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"2.77"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0078","text":"Venere.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"2.78"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","text":"Del Dominio del ſole habbiamo parlato nel pri mo grado. Hor ſi come in quel luogo, dove per l’ordinario dovea eſſer Apollo, vi ſu locato il dominio, coſì in queſto luo go ordinario del dominio ſarà collocato Apollo, & ſotto la porta ſua nel mondo ſopracelleſte ſi tratterà di Tipheret, et di Raphael. Nel celeſte ſi tratterà di eſſo Sole, della lu ce, del lume, dello ſplendore & de raggi. Nelle favole di Apollo Dio & ſuoi appartenenti. Sotto il dominio di Marte ſaranno due imagini, vn Vulcano, & una bocca Tartarea aperta, & divorare anime, qual nelle pitture Fiamminghe ſi ſuol vedere. Vulcano ſignifichera ſotto queſta porta il fuoco ſemplice. Sotto l’altro l’ethere, il fuoco elementale, l’incendio vniuerſale, il fuoco no ſtro, l’incendio particolare, fauilla, fiamma, carbone, et cenere.","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"2.79"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0080","text":"Sotto i Tatari ſignifichera batter fuoco, ſvegliarlo nell’eſca, accenderlo, metter incendio, & eſtinguere. Sotto Prometheo conterrera tutte le arti fabricili che ſi fanno con fuoco.","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"2.80"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0081","text":"Sole.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"2.81"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0082","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"2.82"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","text":"La bocca Tartarea coprirà vn volume, doue ſi ritrerà diſ-\nſtintamente del Purgatorio, & de purgatori luoghi, ſecondo la opinione de gli ſcrittori, che ne hanno laſciato ſcritto, il qual Purgatorio diamo à Marte, percioche anchor’a il fo-\nro miſſo è martiale, & non differente dall’infernale, che ap-\npartiene à Saturno, ſe non in quanto la pena, che le anime patiſcono nel martiale, è temporale, ma quella dell’inferno & Saturnina è eterna, conueniente alla tardità di Saturno.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"2.83"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0084","text":"Queſta medeſima bocca contienerà anchor quel luogo, che è chiamato limbo con tutte quelle anime che ſtanno con qual-\nche ſperanza di ſalute.","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"2.84"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0085","text":"Sotto il Conuiuio di Gioue ſaranno due imagini, vna ſarà\nGiunon ſuſpeſa, & l’altra Europa.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"2.85"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0086","text":"Giunon ſuſpeſa pigliamo da Homero, il qual finge Gioue tener quella ſuſpeſa per vna catena, & Giunone hauer à ciaſcun piede vn contrapeſo. Gioue è il tenitore di tutto l’aere. Il contrapeſo del piu ſollevato piede è l’acqua, & quello del piu baſſo è la terra. Queſta imagine adunque in queſto luogo ſignificherà l’aere ſemplice. Ma ſotto l’altro contrapeſo i quattro elementi in generale, & appreſſo l’aere in particolare con le ſue parti, & ſuoi appartenenti, come ſi dirà in quel luogo.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"2.86"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0087","text":"Et ſotto i Tàari ſignificherà reſpirar, ſoſpirar vſar l’aper-\nto cielo.","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"2.87"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0088","text":"Et ſotto Prometheo ſignificherà qualunque arte, che per be-\nneficio dell’aere ſi faccia, come i molini da vento.","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"2.88"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0089","text":"Europa rapita dal Toro, & per lo mare portata, riguardan-\ndo non la parte alla quale ella è portata, ma a quella onde ella ſi è partita, è l’anima portata dal corpo per lo pelago","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"2.89"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0090","text":"DIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO     15","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"2.90"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091","text":"di quello modo, la qual ſi rivolge pure a Dio terra ſopraſ-\nſelte, & queſta coprirà un volume appartenente al paradiso ſo uero & Chriſtiano, & a tutte l’anime beate già ſepara te, & queſto è dato a Gioue per eſſer pianeta di vera & ottima religione. Et queſta ſotto Prometheo ſignificherà conuerſione, conſen-\ntimento, annichilatione, ſanità, & Religione. Sotto il Conuiuio di Saturno ſaranno due imagini, di Cibele. Saturno, le una, come ella è deſcritta da Lucretio inghirlandata di Cibele, torri, & tirata da due Leoni legati al carro di lei, la quale ſignificando la terra, a noi in queſto luogo ſignificherà la terra ſemplice & uirginea. Queſta medeſima ſotto l’altro conterrà la terra et le ſue parti, & qualità, come ſi dirà nel luogo ſuo, et ſarà anchor queſta ſotto i Talari, & ſotto Prometheo.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"2.91"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092","text":"L’altra imagine di Cibele gitterà un moſtro di fuoco, & ſotto queſta ſarà il volume dell’inferno, & de nomi delle ſue magioni, & le anime dannate. Et la cagion perche deſ-\ntino l’Inferno a Saturno è detta nel conuiuio di Marte.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"2.92"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0093","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"2.93"}],"sha256":"800a2edd014b75810be58ae561630e004d2e8ab7ce2b9e714cba70c2d8b2b488","language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261030T230207857194Z_dcdc9c50","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE BANQUET.","source_sha256":"800a2edd014b75810be58ae561630e004d2e8ab7ce2b9e714cba70c2d8b2b488","sha256":"f5ecb9f6516d153a37958c79e3c9be094b1f321647e0f135a0063b840d2a2af4","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:02:07.857262+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0001","text":"THE BANQUET.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"2.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 19, region 4]","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"2.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","text":"The second grade of the Theatre shall have its doors painted with one and the same image, and this shall be a banquet. Homer imagines Oceanus to give a feast to all his Gods; nor without the loftiest mystery did the loftiest poet make such a fiction, concerning which, with the grace of God, we shall say something. There have been two productions made by God, one within the essence of his divinity, and the other without. The production within, which is production without beginning and (so to speak) consubstantial, or coessential, and eternal, is that of the Word, of which Jeremiah thus says: Ego qui cæteris generationem tribuo, sterilis ero? And John, wishing to say that it was coeternal, said: In principio erat verbum. And to declare that God is the beginning, he added: Et verbum erat apud Deum. Thereupon, in order to make us understand the coessence, because ego in patre, & pater in me est, he added.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"2.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","text":"Et Deus erat verbum. The production without is not coessential, for it was made verbo tantum, and out of nothing, and in time. And this was the first matter, otherwise called chaos, and by the Platonists the soul of the world, and by the Poets Proteus. From this God afterwards drew heaven, earth, and all things. And because Plato in the Timaeus believes this first matter to have been twofold, I think that, reading Moses in that place, in principio creauit Deus cælum & terram, he believed God to have made two matters, one of heaven and the other of earth. And here it is well to note that","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"2.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0005","text":"Two productions\nof God.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"2.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0006","text":"In princi-\npio, i.e., in the\nfirst father.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"2.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0007","text":"Chaos","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"2.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0008","text":"Soul of the\nworld","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"2.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0009","text":"Proteus.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"2.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0010","text":"Cæli et\nterræ, i.e.,\nthe matter\nof heaven &\nearth.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"2.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0011","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"2.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0012","text":"B\n\nTHE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"2.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","text":"If we were to understand Moses in this passage so simply, that is, that God on one day created Heaven and Earth as formed Heaven and formed Earth, such as we see them, he would afterwards uselessly repeat that on the second day he made the Rachia, which means the mass of the heavens, and not the firmament, as the interpreters say. And he would uselessly also have placed the third day, on which he caused the earth to appear. But just as, if someone wished to clothe himself in wool, having before him a mass of unworked wool, he could say that it was his cap, his cloak, and his stockings, so Moses said that God created Heaven and Earth, understanding that mass from which these were to be formed.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"2.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","text":"And Raymond Lull bears witness in the book which he calls his testament, written while he was held in England, that God created one first matter, then divided it into three parts, and that from the flower of the most excellent part he made the angels and our souls, from another the Heavens, and from the third this lower world. Now this first matter, pertaining both to the heavenly mass and to this lower world, is continually under the wheel—not, I would say, of generation and corruption, as Aristotle is accustomed to write, since these terms are of explication to Hermes Trismegistus—but, according to his opinion, of manifestation and concealment. Hermes says in the Pimander, in the twelfth","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"2.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","text":"Chapter: Sed appellationes, quædam falsæ homines turbant, neque enim, generatio vitæ creatio est, sed latentis explicatio vitæ, neque mutatio mors, sed occultatio potius, quum hæc igitur ita se habeant immortalia omnia. And, to say on this subject what","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"2.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0016","text":"First matter\nthreefold.\nGenera-\ntion &\ncorruption.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"2.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0017","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"2.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0018","text":"10","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"2.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019","text":"at present occurs to us concerning the generation of things, the Pythagoreans make an enumeration of six principles, from which they wish all things to proceed, and they call this Gamone, and it is as follows: Sol lux lumen splendor calor Generatio. And by the Sun they understood God the Father; by the light, the Son; by the radiance, the angelic mind, or the intelligible world; by the splendour, the soul of the world, or, let us say, Chaos; and by the heat, the spirit of the world, or the breath of the soul; and thus shall be the Gamone.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"2.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0020","text":"Gamone.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"2.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0021","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 21, region 5]","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"2.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","text":"And in this division of theirs it is to be noted that both the Pythagoreans and Platino, in treating of the Ideas, did not wish to place them in God, because he is most simple; and for this reason they placed them in the angelic mind. Their reservation was superfluous, since that supracelestial God is likewise most simple, just as the Sun too is simple, while its rays and its effects are manifold. And Dionysius says that, although the soul is simple, its operations are manifold, as is also shown to us by that passage of Petrarch.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"2.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0023","text":"The Ideas\nof God.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"2.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","text":"Soul that so many diverse things\nSeest, hearest, and readest, and writest, and departest, and thinkest. And yet we know that the Ideas are in God, saying","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"2.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0025","text":"R  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"2.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0026","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"2.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0027","text":"Chaos:","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"2.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0028","text":"John [says]: quod factum est in ipso vita erat. Nor can the reason why they understood Chaos under the name of splendour be passed over in silence. It must therefore be known that Orpheus writes that Chaos was born most ancient with love in its bosom, which turns it toward the mind, in which the Ideas are impressed, and, conceiving form from them, through their beauty it comes to acquire splendour. But, to return to the matter of generation, the Pythagoreans and the Platonists believe heat to be spirit, that is, the breath of the soul of the world in every thing, though hidden; and that the said soul, impregnating it with that by breathing, brings it forth in the bosom of nature, and thus joins it with motion, and thence, joined in eternal companionship, with greater affection breathes it out, pushing it beneath dimension, nor for all this does it scatter it, but gathers it to itself with a circuit.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"2.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","text":"And the more it diffuses itself, the more it surrounds, and sends as it were outward with every [thing], and moves an almost continuous spirit from the one breathing. This opinion was held by those excellent spirits, who did not understand Christ, but the truth of generation, or indeed of the demonstration, and of the birth of things is [this]: that, since first matter is in every part, and things of diverse nature, such as water and earth, come or are found together, they would never be joined—\nthe spirit of Christ did not come upon—\nthe things, if it did not happen, and entering into them did not reconcile them, to draw out the seed: now from herbs and flowers. And this is done despite them through the thickening of matter, which then thinning out, which is its drying, the manifest things hide themselves, and the spirit remains and lives. And thus they dry","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"2.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0030","text":"How:\ngeneration","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"2.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0031","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO\tII","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"2.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0032","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"2.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","text":"the saying of Trismegistus: immortalia omnia. But this is the [illegible] of bears, which we do not wish to publish lest it be [illegible] confirmed. Concerning which matter Paul says: Spiritus Christi, Spiritus vivificans. And elsewhere Scripture says: Ego cœlum & terram impleo. Ego via, veritas, & vita. And if this spirit did not come upon [them] to effect reconciliation, contraries would never agree.\n\nAnd concerning this Mercury has written a book: Quod Deus latens simul, ac patens sit. Therefore, having above proposed the Canon of the Pythagoreans, we shall reduce it to three heads, or, if we wish to say, to three principles in this world.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"2.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0034","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 23, region 4]","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"2.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","text":"The first of these is the author of all things; the second is the true light and wisdom of God, in which are the Ideas of all things, and which diffuses the life-giving spirit. And the third is matter, in which are impressed the diverse forms of the demonstration, which they call generation, which comes consequently and not as a principle. And for a clearer demonstration that first matter is not consubstantial, we are pleased to prove it by the beginning of Plato's Timaeus, which begins thus: Unus, duo, tres. Unus signi Platon[sic] Sol, Duo Lux, tres, Lumen. Then he adds, Vel quar nel Tia tus? And the answer is made: Quartus lator at caue si. valetudì mea. ne. And by this is understood first matter, which alway","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"2.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0036","text":"B  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"2.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0037","text":"11","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"2.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0038","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE:","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"2.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","text":"s alters itself through mutations, hiding and showing itself; and being such, it is not consubstantial; and it is infirm and already so many thousands of years [old], and through so many mutations it is to be believed that it is growing worse, and that it will fail; and when it can no longer [do so], the universal judgment will follow.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"2.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0040","text":"Elohim, i.\nWords.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"2.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","text":"And this first matter we truly say to be water, clearly, because Moses, as soon as he had made mention of matter, as we have said above, restored it, as it were: for, having mentioned heaven and earth, which he said were void and empty—the second, that is, of every form—he explained its nature by apposition, saying: Et Spiritus Eloim ferebatur super aquas, although the Hebrew text has incubabat. And Morienus concludes thus, saying: Ergo aqua fuit antequam cœlum & terra. And indeed, if the first production within, which is of the Word, bears the symbol of water, that being the exemplar of all things, it was right that the production without should also be water, since omnia per verbum fecit. And that made the whole water thus similar.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"2.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","text":"and although it says that the water was savoured by the spirit of Elohim—which must signify heat in some way—nevertheless, saying that moisture in divine things (as Plotinus also proves de aqua, Timo) is not without heat, nor heat without moisture, it shows that in heaven there is nothing else than light, and moist heat, and warm moisture, without which union generation could not take place. And here it is to be noted that the Pythagoreans, in that their Gamone, after heat set generation without preceding moisture, as though leaving it understood under the name of heat, because they are inseparable. Which truth we shall easily recognize in the supercelestial [realm]. For when therefore we call Chochmà watery, and Rina fiery.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"2.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0043","text":"al. 3. ch.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"2.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0044","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"2.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0045","text":"12","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"2.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0046","text":"Nevertheless, Isaiah, wishing to say that in the Son of God was every thing, said: Cibauit eum dominus pane vitæ, & intellectus, and intellect is of the spirit, & aqua sapientiæ salutaris potauit illum. And elsewhere: Egredietur virga de radice Iesse et flos de radice eius ascendet; et requiescet super eum spiritus Dei. Spũ sapientiæ et intellectus, wisdom indeed being that of Chochmà, and intellect that of Binà. And again elsewhere Isaiah [says]: Donec abluerit sordes filiorum Sion in spiritu iudicii, & in spiritu ardoris. Where it is to be noted that, judgment being of the Son, because omne iudicium dedit mihi pater, and ardour being of the Holy Spirit, and the measure of the Son being water, by using that verb abluere, he shows that moisture and ardour are joined together.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"2.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","text":"And since no other person came to wash than Christ, he is the one who made this washing of moisture mingled with heat. Thus, although Moses said that the spirit of Elohim settled in superiority upon water, he speaks of things not separated, but united and inseparable; and Plotinus agrees with this in the book de coelo, who holds that there is no other thing in heaven in any way similar to our qualities, except heat mingled with moisture and light. And he says that light takes the place of intellect, and wishes heat to be, I say, the efficacy of life, and moisture to be its motion and nourishment. Nor is heat perceived otherwise there than as a kind of favour and nourishment and refreshment and vigour. Nor is moisture perceived otherwise than as a kind of increase, amplification, and gentle agility, such as we sometimes perceive near us.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"2.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0048","text":"Therefore the heat of Heaven ought not only to be called hot, but also moist, that is, liquid, fluid, agile, lubricous, and","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"2.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0049","text":"Eum. i.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"2.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0050","text":"B   iii","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"2.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0051","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"2.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052","text":"pleasant, and wholesome to the touch of nature; I said, to the touch of nature, because that of man cannot attain thereto; and I said, of nature, by a total similarity to our touch and to our objects. And elsewhere the same author affirms that the said celestial heat and moisture are very different in kind from ours, and even more so than natural heat differs in a furnace from the blaze thereof, and the warmth of the Sun from our flames. Therefore, just as celestial moisture does not distil in order to wet, so celestial heat does not warm in order to consume. And this moisture, being made, is at least as different from our other moisture as the moisture of our air differs from that of water; and I add to Plotinus's subtle opinion that the difference which he makes between celestial heat and moisture and that of this world must likewise be understood as holding between the supercelestial and the celestial.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"2.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0053","text":"But let us return","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"2.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0054","text":"Ocean.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"2.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","text":"to the banquet that Ocean gives to the Gods: let us say that Ocean is nothing other than the water of wisdom, which was also before prime matter, which is the first production; and that the invited Gods are nothing other than the Ideas in the divine exemplar, concurring in one and the same spirit, because all that is in God is God himself. Saint Augustine, great defender of the Ideas, upon that passage of John, Quod factum est in","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"2.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0056","text":"Number.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"2.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0057","text":"ipso vita erat, adduces the saying of Solomon, that God had","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"2.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0058","text":"Weight.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"2.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0059","text":"made all things in number, in weight, and in measure, and con-","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"2.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0060","text":"Measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"2.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","text":"cludes that, just as we in this world, by numbering, weighing, and measuring, do not give to numbered, weighed, and measured things the numbers, weights, and measures, but apprehend them therein, so God causes us to see in this world all things well numbered, weighed, and measured, but the numbers, weights, and measures he has willed","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"2.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0062","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  13","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"2.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","text":"to stand outside them. And since all things that are are either God or a thing produced externally, and the said numbers, weights, and measures are not produced like the other numbered, weighed, and measured things, it follows that they stand in God himself. Now Scripture makes mention of these numbers, weights, and measures, as is read in the Gospel: Capilli capitis vestri numerati sunt. And in the Apocalypse mention is made of the Angel with the balances, and of another who measures with a reed. And in Isaiah one reads: Ego sum ipse, ego sum primus & novissimus, manus mea fundavit cœlos, & dextera mea est cœlos, vel palmo con-\nclusit cœlos.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"2.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","text":"The Ideas, therefore, are forms and exemplars of essential things, existing in the eternal mind, there existing even before created things were made; whence all created things derive their being and bear, as from seals, a particular impression. And thus they always persevere in their being with God. And their eternity causes all species to remain eternal, although individuals are perishable and mortal. Therefore, although individuals are transformed and corrupted, or are born and pass away, nevertheless the species and the eternal Ideas in the living God always live. And for this reason John said: Quod factum est in ipso vita erat. That is, all that is, and that we see in actuality in this or in the celestial mode, was life in the Word; he did not wish to call it living, but gave it the very appellation of the Word, namely, it is life. And that preterite erat, which is set against the apparent est, must also be carefully considered.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"2.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065","text":"For these reasons we may well consider the error of the Peripatetics, who deny the Ideas and say that universals proceed a posteriori, not a priori; and this is because divine","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"2.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0066","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"2.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","text":"wisdom shows them its shadow and garments, sometimes concealing its face. Therefore, beneath the gate of the Common belonging to every Planet, we shall set down the most simple elements, or else things nearest either to the intellect or believed on authority, which are set before sense.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"2.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0068","text":"Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"2.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069","text":"Beneath the gate of the Lunar Common shall be covered two images: that of Proteus and that of Neptune with the Trident.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"2.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","text":"Proteus, of many forms and with a human face, signifies prime matter, which was the second production. And he will inform us that within his canon there will be a volume ordered according to the laws, where prime matter, or Chaos, if we wish to call it so, and its nature, capable of all forms in succession, will be treated. Of form itself, of privation, and of natural things. Neptune will promise that his volume shall treat of the most pure and simple element of water. It is assigned to the Moon, because she is the Queen of humidities. This same [image], beneath the cave, shall signify the aquatic and its animals.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"2.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","text":"Beneath the Winged Sandals: to try the ford, to cross the water, to wash with\nwater, to bathe, to drink, to sprinkle.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"2.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","text":"And beneath Prometheus: arts concerning waters, such as aqueducts, artificial fountains, bridges, arsenals, the art of navigation, and the art of swimming and fishing.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"2.72","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0073","text":"Mercury","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"2.73","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","text":"Under the Banquet of Mercury there shall be an image of an elephant, which, because it is said by writers to be the most reli-\ngious animal of all the brutes, we wish that in the volume of its canon there should be treatment of the origin of the fabulous gods, of their deity, & of their names, & because from hea-","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"2.74","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0075","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"2.75","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0076","text":"14","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"2.76","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","text":"ring of fables came that opinion, this subject belonging to Mercury, as patron of language & of fable-making; this same figure under Prometheus will signify religion toward the fabulous gods. Under the dominion of Venus there shall be a sphere with ten cir-\ncles, & the tenth shall be golden, & laden with little spirits open on every side, the volume of which shall concern the Elysian fields, & & the souls of the blessed, whether they be already in this world, or yet to come, according to the opinion of the Platonists, & of some poets. And therein the earthly paradise shall also be treated: & they were placed under Venus for the delight & beauty of those places.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"2.77","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0078","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"2.78","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","text":"We have spoken of the dominion of the sun in the first degree. Now, just as in that place, where ordinarily Apollo ought to have been, the dominion was placed, so in this ordinary place of the dominion Apollo shall be placed, & beneath his gate in the supercelestial world Tipheret and Raphael shall be treated. In the celestial [world] the Sun itself shall be treated, light, radiance, splendour & rays. In the fables, Apollo the god & those belonging to him. Under the dominion of Mars there shall be two images, a Vulcan, & an open Tartarean mouth, & devouring souls, such as is usually seen in Flemish paintings. Vulcan shall signify under this gate simple fire. Under the other, the ether, elemental fire, universal conflagration, our fire, particular conflagration, spark, flame, coal, and ash.","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"2.79","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0080","text":"Under the Tatari it shall signify striking fire, awakening it in tinder, kindling it, setting a fire, & extinguishing [it]. Under Prometheus it shall contain all the crafts of fabrication that are practised with fire.","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"2.80","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0081","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"2.81","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0081"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0082","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"2.82","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0082"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","text":"The Tartarean mouth shall cover a volume, where there shall be set forth dis-\ntinctly Purgatory, & purgatorial places, according to the opinion of the writers who have left writing about them; which Purgatory we assign to Mars, because the fire placed therein is martial, & no different from the infernal [fire], which belongs to Saturn, except insofar as the punishment that souls suffer in the martial [one] is temporal, whereas that of hell & Saturn is eternal, befitting the slowness of Saturn.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"2.83","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0084","text":"This same mouth shall also contain that place which is called limbo, with all those souls that remain with some hope of salvation.","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"2.84","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0084"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0085","text":"Under the Banquet of Jupiter there shall be two images, one shall be\nJuno suspended, & the other Europa.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"2.85","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0085"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0086","text":"We take Juno suspended from Homer, who feigns Jupiter to hold her suspended by a chain, & Juno to have a counterweight at each foot. Jupiter is the holder of all the air. The counterweight of the more elevated foot is water, & that of the lower is earth. This image, therefore, in this place shall signify simple air. But under the other counterweight [shall be] the four elements in general, & then air in particular with its parts, & its appurtenances, as shall be said in that place.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"2.86","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0086"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0087","text":"And under the Tàari it shall signify breathing, sighing, using the open sky.","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"2.87","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0087"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0088","text":"And under Prometheus it shall signify any art that is practised for the ben-\nefit of the air, such as windmills.","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"2.88","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0088"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0089","text":"Europa carried off by the Bull, & borne over the sea, looking not toward the part to which she is borne, but toward that whence she departed, is the soul borne from the body over the sea","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"2.89","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0089"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0090","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO     15","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"2.90","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0090"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091","text":"in that manner, which turns only toward God, the supercelestial earth, & this shall cover a volume pertaining to true or Christian paradise, & to all blessed souls already sepa-\nrated, & this is given to Jupiter for being the planet of true & excellent religion. And this, under Prometheus, shall signify conversion, assent,\nannihilation, health, & Religion. Under the Banquet of Saturn there shall be two images, of Cybele-Saturn, one, as she is described by Lucretius, garlanded with Cybele's towers, & drawn by two lions bound to her chariot; which, signifying the earth, shall signify for us in this place simple & virgin earth. This same [image] under the other shall contain the earth and its parts, & qualities, as shall be said in its place, and this too shall be under the Talari, & under Prometheus.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"2.91","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092","text":"The other image of Cybele shall cast forth a monster of fire, & beneath this shall be the volume of hell, & of the names of its abodes, & the damned souls. And the reason why I assign Hell to Saturn is stated in the banquet of Mars.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"2.92","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0093","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"2.93","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0093"]}],"source_digest":"9ef5f3a78df3330b17a17e24abab0e9b4623f36db4844f0cb1506a326127e732","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"IL CONVIVIO."},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261031T001415211308Z_f69e7fb4","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE BANQUET.","source_sha256":"800a2edd014b75810be58ae561630e004d2e8ab7ce2b9e714cba70c2d8b2b488","sha256":"c0bbafd8569625b458ad53fdac6d0806fadfd65bdb417986eceb22fb95cad0a3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-31T00:14:15.211441+00:00","translate_quotations":true,"paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0001","text":"THE BANQUET.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"2.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0002","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 19, region 4]","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"2.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","text":"The second grade of the Theatre shall have its doors painted with one and the same image, and this shall be a banquet. Homer feigns Oceanus to make a feast for all his Gods; nor without a most lofty mystery did the most lofty poet make such a fiction, concerning which, with the grace of God, we shall say something. There have been two productions that God has made: one within the essence of his divinity, and the other outside it. The production within, which is production without beginning and (so to speak) consubstantial, or coessential, and eternal, is that of the Word, of which Jeremiah thus says: “Shall I, who grant generation to others, be barren?” And John, wishing to say that it was coeternal, said: “In the beginning was the Word.” And to declare that God is the beginning he added: “And the Word was with God.” Thereupon, to make us understand the coessentiality, because “I am in the Father, and the Father is in me,” he subjoined.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"2.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","text":"“And the Word was God.” The production outside is not coessential, for it was made by the Word alone, and out of nothing, and in time. And this was prime matter, otherwise called chaos, and by the Platonists the soul of the world, and by the Poets Proteus. From this God afterwards drew forth heaven, earth, and all things. And because Plato in the Timaeus believes this prime matter to have been twin, I think that, reading Moses in that place, “In the beginning God created heaven and earth,” he believed God to have made two matters, one of heaven and the other of earth. And here it is well to note that","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"2.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0005","text":"Two productions\nof God.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"2.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0006","text":"In the begin-\nning, i.e. in\nthe first\nFather.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"2.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0007","text":"Chaos","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"2.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0008","text":"Soul of the\nworld","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"2.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0009","text":"Proteus.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"2.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0010","text":"Of heaven and\nearth, i.e.\nthe matter\nof heaven and\nearth.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"2.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0011","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"2.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0012","text":"B\n\nTHE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"2.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","text":"If in this passage we were to understand Moses so simply, namely, that God on one day created Heaven and Earth as formed Heaven and formed Earth, such as we see, he would then uselessly repeat that on the second day he made the Rachia, which means the mass of the Heavens, and not the firmament, as the interpreters say. And he would also uselessly have set down the third day, on which he made the earth appear. But just as, if one wished to clothe oneself in wool, having before oneself an unworked mass of wool, one could say that it was one’s cap, one’s cloak, and one’s stockings, so Moses said that God created Heaven and Earth, understanding that mass from which they were to be formed.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"2.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","text":"And Raymond Lull bears witness in the book which he calls his testament, written while he was detained in England, that God created one prime matter, then divided it into three parts, and that from the flower of the most excellent part he made the angels and our souls, from another the Heavens, and from the third this lower world. Now this prime matter, pertaining both to the celestial mass and to this lower world, is continually beneath the wheel—I do not mean of generation and corruption, as Aristotle is accustomed to write, since these terms belong to explication according to Hermes Trismegistus—but, according to his opinion, of manifestation and concealment. Hermes says in the twelfth chapter of the Pimander:","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"2.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","text":"“But certain false appellations trouble men; for generation is not the creation of life, but the unfolding of hidden life, nor is change death, but rather concealment; since these things are thus, all things are immortal.” And, to say on this subject what","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"2.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0016","text":"Prime matter\nthreefold.\nGenera-\ntion and\ncorruption.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"2.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0017","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"2.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0018","text":"10","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"2.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019","text":"at present occurs to us concerning the generation of things, the Pythagoreans make an enumeration of six principles from which they wish all things to proceed, and they call this Gamone, and it is as follows: Sun, light, radiance, splendour, heat, generation. And by the Sun they understood God the Father; by the light, the Son; by the radiance, the angelic mind, or the intelligible world; by the splendour, the soul of the world, or, let us say, Chaos; and by the heat, the spirit of the world, or the breath of the soul; and thus shall be the Gamone.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"2.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0020","text":"Gamone.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"2.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0021","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 21, region 5]","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"2.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","text":"And in this division of theirs it is to be noted that both the Pythagoreans and Plotinus, in treating of the Ideas, did not wish to place these in God, because he is most simple, and therefore placed them in the angelic mind. This reservation of theirs was superfluous, since that supracelestial God, who is himself most simple, is such that the sun too is simple, while its rays and its effects are manifold. And Dionysius says that, although the soul is simple, its operations are manifold, as is also shown to us by that passage of Petrarch.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"2.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0023","text":"The Ideas\nof God.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"2.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","text":"Soul, which so many diverse things you see, hear, and read, and write, and divide, and think. And yet we know that the Ideas are in God, saying","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"2.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0025","text":"R  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"2.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0026","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"2.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0027","text":"Chaos:","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"2.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0028","text":"John: what was made in him was life. Nor can the reason be passed over in silence why, under the name of splendour, they understood Chaos. It is therefore to be known that Orpheus writes that Chaos was born most ancient, with Love in its bosom, which turns it toward the Mind, in which the Ideas are impressed; and, conceiving form from them, through their beauty it comes to acquire splendour. But to return to the matter of generation, the Pythagoreans and the Platonists believe heat to be spirit, that is, the breath of the soul of the world in everything, though hidden; and that, made pregnant with it by the said soul, it brings it forth by panting in the womb of nature, and thus joins it with motion; and thence, joined in eternal companionship, with greater affection it breathes it forth, thrusting it beneath dimension, nor for all this does it scatter it everywhere, but gathers it to itself by a circuit.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"2.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","text":"And the more it diffuses itself, the more it surrounds, and sends forth, as it were, with every [thing], and moves an almost continuous spirit from the one breathing. This opinion was held by those excellent spirits, who did not understand Christ, but [held] that the truth of generation, or indeed of the demonstration and birth of things, is that, the first matter being in every part, and things of diverse nature coming together or being found together, as water and earth are, they would never be joined—\nwere the spirit of Christ not to come over—\nthe things. [if it] occurred, and, entering into them, did not reconcile them, causing them to bring forth the seed: now that of herbs and flowers. And this is done to their detriment through the thickening of matter, which then, becoming thin—that is, drying—the manifest things hide themselves, and the spirit remains and lives. And thus they dry.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"2.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0030","text":"How:\ngeneration","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"2.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0031","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO\tII","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"2.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0032","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"2.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","text":"according to the saying of Trismegistus: all things immortal. But this is the [illegible] of bears, which we do not wish to publish, lest it be [illegible] confirmed. Concerning which matter Paul says: “The Spirit of Christ, the life-giving Spirit.” And elsewhere Scripture says: “I fill heaven and earth. I am the way, truth, and life.” And if this spirit did not come upon [them] to effect the reconciliation, the contraries would never agree. And concerning this Mercury makes for us a book: “That God is at once hidden and manifest.” Therefore, having proposed above the Canon of the Pythagoreans, we shall reduce it to three heads, or, if we wish to say so, to three principles in this world.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"2.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0034","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 23, region 4]","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"2.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","text":"The first of which is the author of all things; and the second is the true light and wisdom of God, in whom are the Ideas of all things, and who pours forth the life-giving spirit. And the third is matter, in which are impressed the diverse forms of demonstration, which those call generation, which comes consequently and not as a principle. And for a clearer demonstration that first matter is not coessential, we are pleased to prove it by the beginning of Plato’s Timaeus, which begins thus: “One, two, three. One signifies Plato thus: Sun; Two, Light; three, Radiance.” Then he adds, “Or fourth in the Tia tus?” And it is answered, “The fourth bearer, but beware lest my health...”. And by this is understood first matter, which alway","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"2.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0036","text":"B  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"2.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0037","text":"11","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"2.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0038","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE:","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"2.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","text":"always alters itself through mutations, concealing and manifesting itself; and, being such, is not consubstantial; and it is infirm and already so many thousands of years [old], and through so many mutations it is to be believed that it is deteriorating and failing; and when it can no longer [do so], the universal judgment will follow.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"2.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0040","text":"Eloim i.\nOf the Word.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"2.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","text":"And this first matter we truly say to be water, clearly; for Moses, immediately after he had made mention of—\nrested it, as we have said above, of matter as Peter [says]: nor of heaven and earth, which he said to be void and empty, the second, that is, of every form, explained its nature by apposition, saying: “And the Spirit of Eloim was borne upon the waters,” although the Hebrew text sounds, “was brooding.” And Morienus concludes thus, saying: “Therefore water was before heaven and earth.” And indeed, if the first production within, which is of the Word, bears the symbol of water, that being the exemplar of all things, it was right that the production without should also be water, because “he made all things through the Word.” And that made all [things] thus similar to water.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"2.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","text":"and although he says that the water was savoured by the spirit of Eloim—which ought in some manner to signify heat—nevertheless, in saying that moisture in divine things (as Plotinus likewise proves in the Timaeus) is not without heat, nor heat without moisture, he shows that in heaven there is nothing else than light, and moist heat, and warm moisture, without which union generation could not be made. And here it is to be noted that the Pythagoreans, in their Canon, after heat place generation without preceding moisture, as though leaving it understood under the name of heat, because they are inseparable. This truth we shall easily recognize in the supercelestial realm. For when we call Chochmà watery, and Rina fiery.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"2.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0043","text":"at. 3. ch.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"2.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0044","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"2.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0045","text":"12","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"2.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0046","text":"Nevertheless, Isaiah, wishing to say that in the Son of God was everything, said: “The Lord fed him with the bread of life and understanding,” and understanding belongs to the spirit, “and gave him to drink the water of saving wisdom.” And elsewhere: “A rod shall come forth from the root of Jesse, and a flower shall rise from his root; and the Spirit of God shall rest upon him: the Spirit of wisdom and understanding,” wisdom being Chochmà and understanding Binà. And again elsewhere Isaiah: “Until he shall wash away the filth of the sons of Zion in the spirit of judgment and in the spirit of burning.” Where it is to be noted that, judgment being of the Son, because “the Father has given all judgment to me,” and burning being of the Holy Spirit, and the measure of the Son being water, by using that verb “to wash,” he shows that moisture and burning are joined together.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"2.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","text":"And since no other person came to wash than Christ, he is the one who has effected this washing of moisture mingled with heat. Thus, although Moses said that the spirit of Eloim rested upon water in superiority, he speaks not of things separated, but of things united and inseparable; and Plotinus agrees with this in the book On Heaven, in which he maintains that there is no other thing in heaven at all similar to our qualities, except heat mingled with moisture and light. And he says that light holds the place of understanding, and wishes heat to be the efficacy of life, and moisture to be its motion and nourishment. Nor is heat perceived there otherwise than as a kind of favour and nourishment and refreshment and vigour. Nor is moisture perceived otherwise than as a kind of increase, amplification, and sweet agility, such as we sometimes feel near us.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"2.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0048","text":"Therefore the heat of Heaven ought not only to be called hot, but also moist, that is, liquid, fluid, agile, slippery, and","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"2.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0049","text":"Eum.i.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"2.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0050","text":"B   iii","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"2.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0051","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"2.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052","text":"pleasant, & wholesome to nature’s touch; I said, to nature’s touch, because that of man cannot attain thereto, & I said, of nature, through a total similitude to our touch, & to our objects. And elsewhere the same author affirms the said celestial heat & moisture to be very different in kind from ours, & still more than natural heat in a minor degree from the ardour of a furnace, & than the warmth of the Sun from our flames. Therefore, just as celestial moisture does not distil in order to moisten, so celestial heat does not warm in order to consume. And that moisture, being made, is at least as different from our altered moisture as the moisture of our air is different from that of water; and I add to Plotinus’s subtle opinion that the difference which he makes between celestial heat & moisture and that of this world must be understood as extending also from the supercelestial to the celestial.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"2.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0053","text":"But let us return","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"2.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0054","text":"Ocean.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"2.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","text":"to the banquet that Ocean gives to the Gods: we say that Ocean is nothing other than the water of wisdom, which was also before prime matter, which is the first production; & that the Gods invited are nothing other than the Ideas in the divine exemplar, concurring in one and the same spirit, because all that is in God is God himself. Saint Augustine, a great supporter of the Ideas, on that passage of John, “What was made in","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"2.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0056","text":"Number.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"2.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0057","text":"him was life,” adduces the saying of Solomon, that God had made all things in","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"2.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0058","text":"Weight.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"2.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0059","text":"number, in weight, & in measure, & con=","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"2.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0060","text":"Measure.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"2.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","text":"cludes that, just as we in this world, by numbering, weighing, & measuring, do not give numbers, weights, & measures to things numbered, weighed, & measured, but obtain them from them, so God makes us see in this world all things well numbered, weighed, & measured, but the numbers, weights, & measures he has willed","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"2.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0062","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  13","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"2.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","text":"to stand outside them. And since all things that are are either God or a thing produced outwardly, & the said numbers, weights, & measures are not produced like the other numbered, weighed, and measured things, it follows that they are God himself. Now Scripture makes mention of these numbers, weights, & measures, where one reads in the Gospel: “The hairs of your head are numbered.” And in the Apocalypse mention is made of the Angel with the balances, & of another who measures with a reed. And in Isaiah one reads: “I myself am, I am the first & the last; my hand founded the heavens, & my right hand is the heavens, or enclosed the heavens with its palm.”","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"2.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","text":"The Ideas, then, are forms & exemplars of essential things, existing in the eternal mind, there existing even before things made should be; whence all created things draw their being, & bear a particular impression as from seals. And thus they always persevere in their being with God. And their eternity causes all species to remain eternal, although individuals are frail & mortal. Therefore, although individuals are transformed & corrupted, or are born, nevertheless the species & the eternal Ideas in the living God always live. And for this reason John said: “What was made in him was life”; that is, everything that is, & that we see in actuality in this, or in the celestial mode, was life in the Word. He did not wish to call it living, but gave it the very appellation of the Word, namely, it is life. & it is also well worth considering that preterite erat, which is set against the apparent est.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"2.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065","text":"For these reasons we can well consider the error of the Peripatetics, who deny the Ideas, & say that universals proceed a posteriori, not a priori; and this is because divine","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"2.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0066","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"2.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","text":"wisdom shows them the shadow & the garments of herself at times, hiding her face. Now therefore, beneath the gate of the common belonging to whatever Planet, we shall set the simplest elements, or else things nearer either to the intellect or believed on authority, which are set before sense.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"2.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0068","text":"Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"2.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069","text":"Beneath the gate of the Lunar Common there shall be covered two images: that of Proteus and that of Neptune with the Trident.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"2.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","text":"Proteus of many forms, with a human face, signifies prime matter, which was the second production. And he will inform us that within his canon there shall be a volume ordered by laws, where prime matter, or Chaos if we wish to call it so, and its nature, capable of all forms successively, shall be treated: of form itself, of privation, & of natural thing. Neptune will promise that in his volume the most pure and simplest element of water shall be treated. It is given to the Moon, because she is the Queen of moistures. This same one beneath the grotto shall signify the aquatic and its animals.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"2.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","text":"Beneath the Winged Sandals: to attempt the ford, to cross water, to wash with water, to wet, to drink, to sprinkle.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"2.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","text":"And beneath Prometheus: arts concerning waters, such as aqueducts, artificial fountains, bridges, arsenals, the naval art, & the art of swimming, & fishing.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"2.72","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0073","text":"Mercury","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"2.73","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","text":"Under the Banquet of Mercury there will be an image of an elephant, which, because writers say that it is the most religious animal of all the brutes, we wish in the volume of its canon to treat of the origin of the mythological gods, of their deity, and of their names; and because from the blind","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"2.74","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0075","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"2.75","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0076","text":"14","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"2.76","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","text":"fashioning of fables came that opinion, this subject belongs to Mercury, as patron of language and of fable-making; this same figure under Prometheus will signify religion toward the mythological gods. Under the dominion of Venus there will be a sphere with ten circles, and the tenth will be golden and filled with spirits everywhere; its volume will concern the Elysian fields, and, and the souls of the blessed, whether they are already in this world or are yet to come, according to the opinion of the Platonists and of certain poets. And therein the earthly paradise will also be treated; and it was placed under Venus because of the delight and loveliness of those places.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"2.77","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0078","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"2.78","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","text":"We have spoken of the dominion of the sun in the first grade. Now, just as in that place, where Apollo should ordinarily have been, the dominion was placed, so in this ordinary place of the dominion Apollo will be placed; and beneath his gate, in the supercelestial world, Tipheret and Raphael will be treated. In the celestial world the Sun itself will be treated, together with light, luminosity, splendour, and rays. In the fables, Apollo the god and those belonging to him. Under the dominion of Mars there will be two images: one Vulcan, and one open Tartarean mouth devouring souls, such as is customarily seen in Flemish paintings. Under this gate Vulcan will signify simple fire. Under the other, the ether, elemental fire, universal conflagration, our fire, particular conflagration, spark, flame, coal, and ash.","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"2.79","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0080","text":"Under the Winged Sandals it will signify striking fire, awakening it in tinder, kindling it, setting a fire, and extinguishing it. Under Prometheus it will contain all the crafts practised with fire.","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"2.80","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0081","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"2.81","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0081"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0082","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"2.82","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0082"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","text":"The Tartarean mouth will cover a volume in which Purgatory and places of purgation will be distinctly dealt with, according to the opinion of the writers who have left writings about it. We assign this Purgatory to Mars, because its very fire is martial and no different from the infernal fire that belongs to Saturn, except insofar as the punishment which souls suffer in the martial one is temporal, whereas that of Hell and Saturn is eternal, befitting the slowness of Saturn.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"2.83","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0084","text":"This same mouth will also contain that place which is called limbo, with all those souls that remain with some hope of salvation.","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"2.84","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0084"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0085","text":"Under the Banquet of Jupiter there will be two images: one will be Juno suspended, and the other Europa.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"2.85","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0085"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0086","text":"We take Juno suspended from Homer, who feigns that Jupiter held her suspended by a chain, and that Juno had a counterweight at each foot. Jupiter is the holder of all the air. The counterweight of the more elevated foot is water, and that of the lower one is earth. This image, therefore, in this place will signify simple air. But beneath the other counterweight, the four elements in general, and then air in particular, with its parts and its appurtenances, as will be said in that place.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"2.86","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0086"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0087","text":"And under the Winged Sandals it will signify breathing, sighing, using the open sky.","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"2.87","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0087"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0088","text":"And under Prometheus it will signify every art that is practised through the benefit of the air, such as windmills.","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"2.88","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0088"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0089","text":"Europa carried off by the Bull and borne over the sea, looking not toward the part to which she is borne but toward that from which she departed, is the soul borne from the body across the sea","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"2.89","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0089"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0090","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO     15","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"2.90","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0090"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091","text":"of this world, which turns ever toward God, the supercelestial earth; and this will cover a volume belonging to the sovereign and Christian Paradise, and to all the blessed souls already separated. And this is given to Jupiter because he is the planet of true and most excellent religion. And this under Prometheus will signify conversion, consent, annihilation, health, and Religion. Under the Banquet of Saturn there will be two images of Cybele. One of them, as she is described by Lucretius, crowned with towers and drawn by two lions bound to her chariot, signifying the earth, will in this place signify for us simple and virgin earth. This same image, under the other, will contain the earth and its parts and qualities, as will be said in its proper place; and this too will be under the Winged Sandals and under Prometheus.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"2.91","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092","text":"The other image of Cybele will cast forth a monster of fire, and beneath this will be the volume of Hell, of the names of its abodes, and of the damned souls. And the reason why I assign Hell to Saturn is stated in the Banquet of Mars.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"2.92","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0093","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"2.93","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0093"]}],"source_digest":"9ef5f3a78df3330b17a17e24abab0e9b4623f36db4844f0cb1506a326127e732","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"IL CONVIVIO."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"IL CONVIVIO.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT","title":"THE CAVE.","order":3,"chapter_id":"CH_LIDT_LANT","text":"L’ANTRO.\n\nIL Terzo grado hauera per ciaſcuna delle ſue porte di pinto vno Antro, il quale noi chiameremo l’Antro Ho= merico à differenza di quello, che Platon deſcriue nella ſua Republica. Homero adunque finge ſopra il porto di Itaca vno antro, nel quale alcune Nimphe teſſono tele purpuree, & finge api che eſcono, & tornano a fabricare i loro melli le quali teſſiture, & fabricamenti ſignificando le coſe miſ= ſte, & elementate, vogliamo che qualunque de ſette antri, ſecondo la natura del ſuo Pianeta habbia à conſeruare i miſti, & elementati à lui appartenenti. Et per hauer qual= che information delle coſe miſte & elementate, dico, che ſe= condo la diſtintion meſſa da Moſe, poiche Eloim l’un giorno creò la materia prima per fare il Cielo & la terra, perche non ſi conueniva alla materia tutto l’influſſo de ſopraceleſti ruſcelli, il ſecondo giorno formò la Rachia, ciò è la maſſa de cieli, & non il firmamento ſecondo che detto habbiamo anchora, percioche egli è ſolamente l’ottaua ſpera, & miſſe la detta maſſa diſteſa fra il mondo ſopraceleſte, & l’infe= riore, a fine che diuidiſſe l’acque de ſopraceleſti ruſcelli che non bagnano, dalle acque di queſto mondo, che bagnano, delle quali ſopraceleſti acque è ſcritto. Benedicite aquae om nes, quæ ſuper cœlos ſunt domino. Et interpoſta adunque la detta maſſa celeſte, & diſteſa, accioche non pioueſſe mag= gior l’influſſo delle acque ſuperiori, che alla capacità della materia ſi conueniſſe. Et intorno à queſte acque è da notare, che Gregorio Nazianzeno ſi inganna, intendendo per quel’\n\nI giorni\nalla crea\ntion del\nmondo.\n\nLe acque\nſopra ce=\nleſti.\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n16\n\n[illegible]\n\nSe il cielo chryſtallino, il qual nomamente è ſtato finto da alcu ni ſopra il firmamento, ma non hanno ne ragion ne fonda mento ne della ſacra, ne della prophana ſcrittura. Nel ter zo giorno dice Moſe, che Eloim comandò che ſi congregaſ ſero, le acque, che ſono ſotto il cielo in un luogo, cio è tutte le virtù germinatiue inſieme, & appareſſe fuori la terra ar rida, a fin che per le dette germinatiue virtù, raccolte eſſa dimeniſſe ſeconda, il che fatto diſſe. Produca terra herbam virentem, & lignum (ſe dir ſi poteſſe) ſeminiferum. Nel quarto giorno furono fatti i Luminari, & collocati nella maſſa de Cieli. La Luna nella prima, & il Sole nella quar-\nta Spera, per li quali ſi hauesse da diſtinguer la luce dalle te nebre, cio è le coſe, che haueano gia ricevuto forma da quel= le, che ancor informate nō erano. Nel 5 giorno parla della communication della vita in tutti gli animali, percioche vuol che le acque, cio è le germinatiue virtù producano tutte le diverſi tà de i animali coſi acquatici come volatili, et terreſtri qui a baſ ſo, a differenza di q̃lli di laſſu. Nel ſeſto di, produſſe l’homo, et nel ſettimo ripoſo. Aſſique dopo la materia prima nō veg giamo che Dio creaſſe noua materia, ma da la prima formò tutte le coſe, le quali noi chiamiamo miſte, et elementate. Et le quali habbiamo a trouar nel terzo grado de le ſette colōne ſotto la porta dell’antro, eccetto l’homo, il quale eſſendo ſtato ſeparatamente formato, et fatto ſignor de i miſti, et elementati, vogliamo c’habbia grado particolare, come poi ſi vedra. Sotto la porta adunque dell’Antro Lunare troueremo cinque imagini, Nettuno, Daphne, Diana, à cui Mercurio porge la meſſa, le ſtalle d’Augia, et Giunon fra le nubi. Ne ſi habbia il marauigliare alcuno, che Nettuno, il cui eſſer ſotto.\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nil communito ſi habbia a riueder ſotto l’Antro, ſotto i Tale-\nri, e ſotto Prometheo, il che hauerra anchor di altre ima gini & in queſto & in altri pianetti, percioche anche Ho mero dice,che Vliſſe hauua veduto Hercole & fra i Dei in Cielo,& nell’inferno, il che ſe à lui non ſi diſdice, men ſi dee diſdire à noi,quali per non aggrauar la memoria di diuerſe imagini in coſe medeſime facciamo che ſi riuegga la medeſima figura ſotto diuerſe porte. Proteo ſignifichera forma, già ſoprauenuta ſuggetto & coſa naturale.\n\nNettuno adunque ſotto il Communito ſignifica l’elemento del l’acqua ſimpliciſſimo, ma ſotto l’Antro lo ſignifichera già miſto,percioche in queſto mondo non veggiamo alcuno elemento ſi puro, che miſto non ſia ſi come lungamente ha prouato & tenuto Anaxagora.Sotto la imagine adunque di queſto Nettuno ſarà contenuto il volume, doue ſaranno ordinate diſtintamente per tagli l’acqua in genere, & l’ acqua in ſpecie, & l’acqua in genere ſi diuidera nel ſuo tutto & nelle ſue parti,il tutto è come dir acqua ſolamente,le ſue parti, come goccia.Vi ſaranno anchor le qualità delle acque, & le quantità.Le qualità, come dolce & ſal ſa,& le dolci ſtanti & correnti; & gli altri accidenti. Et oltre a ciò i lenti, le ripe, & altri appartenenti; & anchor gli animali aquatici, & ſotto queſto Nettuno non vi ſi impaccia anchor l’huomo, percioche e fu l’ultimo creato de gli animali.Ma quando troueremo Nettuno ſotto i Talari,percioche quelli ſignificano la operatione,che puo far l’huomo intorno a ciaſcuna coſa creata auanti a lui natural mente, & fuor di arte,vogliamo che egli habbia nel ſuo.\n\nCannone\n\n[illegible]\n\nDIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO.  17\n\nCannone operationi humane,& naturali intorno alle ac-\nque,come è detto anchor nel continuo.\n\nEt ſotto Prometheo ci dimostrerà le arti sopra l’acque. Daphne che ſi traſmuta in Lauro ſarà Simbolo del boſchiuo. Et qui ſi conterrà cio che già mai Theophrasto, o, altri ſcrittori hanno ſcritto de plantis co ſuoi conſeguenti, che ſono le ombre.\n\nMa ſotto i Talari Daphne ſignificherà le operationi natu rali intorno al legname,come piegar,portare. Et ſotto Prometheo conterrà i giardini,& tutte le arti in torno al legname.\n\nDaphne veramente,cio e il boſchiuo è ben dato alla Luna: cio è à Diana Dea de boſchi,percioche, è regina(come habbiamo detto)delle humidità, ſenza le quali niuna pianta creſcerebbe.La onde Virgilio nel quarto della Georgica.\n\nOceanumque patrem rerum, nymphasque sorores\nCentum quæ Syluas, centum quæ flumina ſeruant.\n\nDiana, à cui Mercurio porge la veſta è la terza imagine. Si legge fra le fauole Greche,che veggendo Gioue Diana andare ignuda eſſendo ella caſta non gli piacque, & commiſe à Mercurio che le faceſſe vna veſta. Et per mola te che egli gliene faceſſe,non ne fu mai alcuna, che le ſi poteſſe accomodare.La qual finitione ci dà ſimbolo ſignifi-\ncante le mutatione & le ſue ſpecie, cio è la generatione, la corruptione,l’augmento,la diminutione, l’alteratione, la mutatione ſecondo il luogo,& il moto con tutte le ſpecie recitate da Ariſtotele, & diſtinte per li ſuoi tagli. Queſta imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà la mutation dell’huomo o ſecondo la openione,o ſecondo la traſfigura\n\nL’Idea del Theatro.     C\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO.\n\ntione del corpo.          Et ſotto i Talari ſignificherà muouere, ò\nmutar coſa, riceuer diſporre, operation fatta roſſo ò ſubito.\n\nMa ſotto Prometheo contenerà i meſi, & le loro parti. Le Stalle di Augia coſi chiamate ſono da Greci, percioche Au gia fu un Re ricchiſſimo di poſſeſſioni & di campi, ma la grande abondantia di beſtie che tenea, ingombrò ſi il ſuo paeſe di letame, che corruppe la fertilità de campi. Adunque ſotto queſta imagine daremo un uolume, che comprehen-\nderà le ſporchezze delle coſe del mondo, le muffe, i fracidu-\nmi, le uiltà, le imperfettioni, & coſe ſimili non piaceuoli.\n\nQueſta medeſima imagine ſotto Paſiphe, contenerà le ſporchezze del corpo humano, & ſuoi eſcrementi, come quelle delle orecchie, del naſo, delle unghie, de gli occhi, il ſudore, lo ſputo, il vomito, il meſtruo, l’urina, &c.\n\nMa ſotto i Talari ſignificherà le ſporche operationi, bruta-\ntar, marchiar.&c.\n\nEt queſte Stalle ſi dàno alla Luna, percioche non ui ha ſpor-\nchezza, ſe non da humidità corrotta.\n\nGimnon fra le nubi, Gimnon ſignifica l’aere, & queſta coper-\nta di nubi ci darà ſignification di coſe naſcoſe in natura, & di quelle che da Peripatetici ſono chiamate ſcibili, ma che non ſono anchor ſapute: & ſignificherà anchor tempo brieue: & queſte coſe ſi dàno alla Luna, percioche non hab biamo Pianeta, che in più brieue tempo ci ſi naſconda.\n\nQueſta imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà l’aſcondimento\nche puo far l’huomo di ſe.\n\nMa ſotto i Talari dinoterà huomo naſconder coſa ò oltra\nperſona.\n\nSotto Mercurio ſaranno ſei imagini. Il metallo dell’Oro, gli\n\n[illegible]\n\nDI·M·GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n18\n\nAtomi, la Piramide, il nodo Gordiano implicato, il medeſimo eſplicato, Giunon finta di nubi. Il Vello dell’Oro quã tunque nella miſtica Philoſophia habbia ſignification del piu alto dono, che il Signor Dio ſoglia donare a pochi de ſuoi eletti, & che habbia gran ſignification per coſi fatto rapto la congregation de gli Heroi, la naue prima, & il perdimento che fece Iaſon del Calzaio nel fiume ſolo al mo do ſenza uento, onde per auentura è tratto l’ordine del To-\nſone, il qual conſente con la magia Zoroaſtro, la quale era la prima coſa, che inſegnar ſi doueſſe al nouello principe de Perſi, accioche ei non fuſſe Tiranno. Nondimeno tirando noi dalla altezza del ſuo miſterio queſta aurea pelle alla baſſezza del noſtro biſogno, ella ci ſeruirà per imagine di tutti gli oggetti che ſ’appartengono al giudicio de’l peſo, o del toccamento,come graue & leggiero,aſpro,molle,du ro,tenero,& ſimili, intendſi nondimeno di quelle coſe, che ſon fuor dell’huomo.\n\nQueſta medeſima imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignifichera le co\nſe medeſime del corpo humano.\n\nEt ſotto i Talari ſignifichera l’operation ſenza arte di\nfar duro,molle, aſpro.\n\nEt queſta imagine con vna tal ſignificatione ſi da a Mercurio , percioche le mani che principalmente fanno queſti giudicii ſono di Gemini, che è coſa di Mercurio.\n\nGli Atomi ci ſignificheranno tutta la quantità diſcreta nel-\nle coſe.\n\nEt ſotto Paſiphe ſignificheranno il medeſimo ne gli huo-\nmini come alcuno.\n\nC  ii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO.\n\n13\n\nMa ſotto i Talari ſignificheranno quantita discreta ſta-\nte dall’huomo ſenza arte, come far in pezzi vna coſa con lima, diſſoluere & ſpargere.\n\nEt per eſſer queſto ſuggetto della Arithmetica laquale è ſcienza di Mercurio, a lui ſi da queſta imagine.\n\nLa Piramide ſignifica quantita continua nelle coſe. Sotto Paſiphe ne gli huomini, come grande, picciolo, me-\nZano.\n\nSotto i Talari ſignifica operation ſenza arte, come alzare\nabbaſſare, ingroſſare, aſſottigliare.\n\nLe quali due quantita eſſendo l’una della Arithmetica, & l’altra della Geometria ſcienze appartenenti ad Hercule tirante la ſaetta di tre punte, ſaranno ſotto quella imagine compreſe ſotto Prometheo.\n\nIl Nodo Gordiano implicato fu porto ad Aleſſandro da eſ plicare, & egli impatiente lo tagliò. Sotto queſto ſi con-\ntenera quantita continua implicata, come vn filo, od vna faſcia.\n\nEt ſotto i Talari ſignificherà l’intricar delle coſe. Il Nodo medeſimo eſplicato dinoterà coſa continua eſpli cata.\n\nEt ſotto i Talari eſplication di coſe intricate. Giunon finta di nubi e tratta dalla favola, che eſſendo eſ-\nla ſtata da Iſſione ricercata di adulterio, gli appreſentò vn corpo di nubi ch’a lei ſi aſſimigliava, & con quello egli ſi giacque. Or per queſta beſtia fatta à colui di quella coſa finta, ſotto queſta figura ſaranno contenute le coſe appa-\nrenti ma non vere.\n\nSotto Paſiphe dinoterà natura ſimulatrice & aſtuta, &\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.  19\n\nfraudolenta.\n\nEt ſotto i Talari fingere & ingannare. Et queſta imagine diamo à Mercurio per eſſer egli l’au-\ntor de lle malitie.\n\nSotto l’Antro di Venere ſono cinque imagini. Cerbero, una Venere. fanciulla che porta in capo vn vaſo di odori, Hercule pur gãte le ſtalle d’Augia, Narciſſo, & Tantalo ſotto il ſaſſo. Cerbero è ſtato dipinto cõ tre teſte à ſignificar le tre neceſſita naturali, che ſono il mangiare, il bere, & il dormire, le quali percioche impediscono molto l’huomo dalla ſpecula-\ntione, finge Virgilio che Enea per conſiglio della Sibilla volendo paſſar alla contemplation delle coſe alte, gli git-\nta vn boccone, & di ſubito paſſa. Il che ſignifica, che quantunque noi habbiamo à ſodisfare à queſte tre neceſſità, con poco habbiamo loro à ſodisfare, ſe vogliamo hauer tẽpo di contemplare.\n\nQueſta imagine adũque ſotto l’antro conſerniera coſe appartenenti alla fame, alla ſete, & al ſonno. Vittuaglie, beueraggi, & coſe che ſonno inducono. Et à Venere ſi da queſta figura per la dilettatione.\n\nSotto Paſiphe ſignifichera fame, ſete, & ſonno ; & con ſeguenti. Sotto i Talari mangiar, bere, & dormire, & conſeguenti operationi naturali. Poi ſotto Prometheo ſignifichera la cucina, i conuiti deli-\ncioſi, & le delitie accommodate al dormire, come i ſuoni & i canti. La fanciulla portante in capo il vaſo de gli odori, quale fu treuata in Roma, nell’altro ſignifichera tutti li odori. Et\n\nC  iii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nper eſſer il vaſo di Venere, a lei ſi da. Sotto i Talari ſignifica le noſtre operationi intorno a gli odori fuor di arte, come odorare & portare odori. Ma ſotto Prometheo contie-\nne le arti pertinenti ad odori, & a perfumieri.\n\nHercole purgante le ſtalle d’Augia è indotto, percioche le fauole dicono, che quel Re vedendoſi oppreſſo dalle molte immonditie, chiamò Hercole à leuarle via: & qui ſignificherà le coſe nette per natura.\n\nSotto Paſiphe ſignificherà le nettezza del corpo humano. Sotto i Talari il nettar ſenza arte. Et ſotto Prometheo bagni & barberie. Et queſta figura à Venere ſi conuiene per la vaghezza, & delicatezza.\n\nNarciso ſi guardò nell’acqua tranſitoria di queſto mondo, & ſignifica la mortal bellezza, la cui verità a chi trouar la vuole, fa biſogno di aſcender al ſopraceleſte Tiſeret, doue Hippia Platonico la douerebbe cercare: & tutti noi anchora, percioche quiui è ferma, et immortale. Hor ſotto queſta imagine haueremo la bellezza che ci apparisce in queſto mondo nelle coſe naturali & deſiderabili. Queſta figura ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà la bellezza humana & ſuoi con ſeguenti, Morbidezza, Vaghezza, Delettatione, Diſegno, Amore, Speranza, innamorati & eſſer amato.\n\nSotto i Talari ſignificherà far bello, far innamorare, far deſiderare, far ſperare, &c. Et ſotto Prometheo con tenerà l’arte de liſci, & de belletii. Tantalo ſotto il ſaſſo ſignifica coſe vacillanti,o tremanti,o che ſta no in pendente. Sotto Paſiphe dinoterà natura timida, ſu-\nſpettoſa, dubbioſa, & marauiglioſa. Et ſotto i Talari ſar\n\n[illegible]\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n20\n\nſtamer, ſar tremar, ſar dubitar, ſar vacillar, ſar marear, [illegible]gliare,&c. Sotto l’Antro del Sole ſono cinque imagini, Sole, Argo ſolo. La Vacca guardata da Argo, Gerione vcciſa da Hercole vn Gallo & vn Leone: & Apolline che ſaet ta Giunone.\n\nArgo ſolo pieno di occhi, ſignifica tutto queſto mondo, di cui il capo ſono i Cieli, & gli occhi le ſtelle, con le quali coſì fa notiſce le coſe inferiori a venire alla apparenza della gene ratione di lontano, come lo ſtruzzo le ſue oua, dando a lo ro la vita di quello ſpirito, che è nelle ſue rote. del qual coſì parla Ezechiel. Et ſpiritus erat in rotis. Queſto come che tenga in vita tutti gli elementi, nondimeno più favoriſce il fuoco, che l’aere, & più l’aere che l’acqua, & più l’acqua che la terra: ma ſe queſta terra che è men favorita, p la vita & fecondità che le dona queſto ſpirito germina tutto di tante varietà di coſe, che debbono far gli altri elementi, la cui fecondità à noi inuiſibile favoriſce anchor la terra: Mer curio nel Pimandro dice la terra p niun modo eſſere immobile, anzi eſſere agitata da molti mouimenti. Et non dimeno à co paratione de gl’altri Elementi eſſer quaſi ſtabile: et aggiun ge che non è da creder, che eſſa, la quale è nutrice di tutte le coſe, manchi di mouimento; percioche è impoſſibil coſa, che ſen za mouimento poſſa parturire: & ſì come le ſtelle ſono gli occhi di queſto mondo, coſì gli arbori, che molto p la loro fer tilità ricevono del detto vitale ſpirito, ſono: a guiſa di peli, & di capelli del ſuo corpo, & i metalli & le pietre ſono a guiſa di oſſa. Non è adunque marauiglia, ſe i Theologhi ſim bolici hanno figurato il mondo ſotto il ſimbolo d’Argo pieno di occhi, percioche il mondo uiue. Queſta imagine adunque.\n\nLa terra\n\nC  iiii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nSi rappreſenterà il mondo tutto in vniuerſale, & in ſpecie la maſſa celeſte, & i corpi celeſti.\n\nLa Vacca guardata da Argo, anchor che ſignificaſſa poſſa la terra, nondimeno à noi ſignificherà tutti i viſibili & tut ti i colori\n\nGerione, à cui Hercule tronca le tre teſte, ſignifica il prin cipio, la conſiſtenza, & l’occaſo del tempo appartenente al Sole. Et queſta imagine ſignificherà à noi non ſolamen te le età del mondo, ma anchor le quattro ſtagioni, le quali ſi fanno per l’acceſſo & receſſo del Sole, & parimente il giorno & la notte con le ſue parti.\n\nEt ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà l’età dellhuomo.\n\nSotto i Talari operationi naturali intorno à minuti all’hore,\nall’anno, alla età, & all’horologio.\n\nEt ſotto Prometheo gli anni artificiali, minuti, hore, horolo-\ngij, & iſtrumenti di tempo.\n\nIl Gallo col Leone. Non ſolamente Plinio apre queſta ſigni ficatione, ma Iamblico Platonico anchora, & Lucretio di cono, che quantunque amendue queſti animali ſiano Solari, nondimeno il Gallo porta ne gli occhi alcun grado piu excel lente del Sole, nel quale riguardando il Leone, ſi humilia à lui. Et all’auttore di queſto Theatro auenne che ritrouando ſi egli à Parigi nel luogo detto il Tornello, con molti gen-\ntilhuomini in vna ſala ad alcune fineſtre riguardanti ſopra vn giardino, vn Leone vſcito di prigionià venne in quella ſala, & à lui di dietro accoſtandoſi con le brame che lo preſe ſenza nocumento per le coſcie, & con la lingua lo andaua leccando. Et à quel toccamento & à quel fiato eſſendoſi egli rivolto, & hauendo quello animal\n\n[illegible]\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n31\n\nVeduto , eſſendo molti gli altri chi quà & chi là fuggiti, il Leone à lui ſi humiliava , quaſi in atto di domandar mer-\ncede. Il che non è da dire che aueniſſe per altro, ſe non che quello animale iſcorgeſſe in lui eſſer molto della virtù. So-\nlare. Queſta imagine adunque con tenera la eccellenza del le coſe naturali per comparatione.\n\nSotto Paſiphe ſignifichera la eccellenza dell’huomo , la ſuperiorità , la dignità , l’autorità & dominio in coſa degna d’honore.\n\nSotto i Talari ſignifichera far ſuperiore, dar dignità, &\ngrado.\n\nMa ſotto Prometheo contenerà i Principati, & i regni -\ni quali tutti da ſcrittori ſono con precetti ſtati regolati, coſì foſſero ben ſeruati.\n\nApollo che ſaetta Giunone fra le nubi è imagine oppoſta alla Giunon naſcoſta fra le nubi, che è della Eſoda. Et ben che Homero induca queſta fauola, non è per ciò da creder che voglia introdur guerra fra i Dei, ſi come accenna So crate nel Menone , ma ſignifica coſe manifeſte.\n\nEt ſotto Paſiphe ſignifica l’huomo manifeſtarſi, & ve\nnir à luce.\n\nMa ſotto i Talari manifeſtar perſona o coſa.\n\nSotto l’Antro di Marte ſono quattro imagini; Vulcano, Marte; vna fanciulla i cui capelli ſtanno leuati verſo’l Cielo, Due ſerpi che combattono ; & Marte ſopra un Dra-\ncone.\n\nVulcano porta talmente ſeco la ſignificatione del fuoco ; che non ha meſtier di dichiaratione. Et perche il fuoco è par tito in tre maniere, conciosia coſa che la più ſottile parte ſue\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 13]\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO.\n\nſecco appunto il concauo della Luna, ha ottenuto anchor da Latini eſſer chiamato aere. La onde Cicerone de natura Deorum 44. A Ether qui conſtat ex altiſſimis ignibus me tuemur hoc quoque verbum, dicaturque tam ether latine, quàm dicitur aer. Et benche per queſto luogo alcuni l’ac= compagnerebbono cõ l’aere, che hà ſotto l’Antro di gioie nondimeno riſguardando noi alla ſua natura ſi ſeguea, che è anchor ſuperiore al fuoco, vogliamo che ſia piutoſto del fuoco che dell’aere. Et tanto più che Cicerone dice nel me deſimo à 34. Ardor cæli qui æther, vel cælum nominatur Et à 37. Tenuis ac perlucẽs, & æquabili calore ſuffuſus æther. A queſto ſeguirà il fuoco Elementale, & nel terzo luogo ſarà collocato il fuoco noſtro. Et percioche queſta ima gine è anche nel Conuiuio, & ſotto altre porte di quello habbiamo nel conuiuio detto più ampiamẽte, qui ci baſterà di tornar à dire, che Vulcano in queſto luogo ſigniſicherà, l’ethere, il fuoco elementare con l’incendio vniuerſale, & appreſſo, il fuoco noſtro con l’incendio particolare, la ſauil la, la fiamma, il carbone, & la cenere. Et q̃ſta imagine co cõtenuti da lei nõ po cõuenir ad altro pianeta, che à Marte, percioche ſolo Marte e caldo e ſecco ſi come è il fuoco, la oue il Sole è caldo, et humido, La Faciu la co capelli leuati verſo’l Cielo coſi è finta danoſi ſcioche l’huomo ſecõdo Platone è arbore riuolto, che l’arbore ha le radici all’ingiù, & l’huomo le ha all’inſù. Et Origene et Hieronimo ſuo ſeguace vogliono che quando la ſcrittura fa mention di capelli o di barba, non ſi habbia ad intender di capelli ne di barba del corpo ma dell’anima, la quale per metaphora ha capelli & barba, & occhi, & altre par\n\n[illegible]\n\nDI. M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n22\n\nti corriſpondenti al corpo. Et perche ſe’ uno ſi eſponeſſe ignudo à l’aere notturno, piu manifeſte-rebbono i capelli & la barba il contratto humore dal Cielo, che altra parte del corpo: vogliono che ſi come l’arbore p̄ le radici ſue ti ra à ſe l’humor nutritiuo dalla terra, coſì la barba & i ca pelli del noſtro huomo interiore tiri la rugiada, cio è l’hu mor viuificante da gli influſſi à ſopracелеſti canali, onde ne ſegua tutto il ſuo vigore. Et di q̃ è che ſi legge nella Caliſti ca. Come tuæ iuſtitiæ canalibus, intendendo de ſopraceleſti ruſcelli, la qual ſentenza porta ſignificatione, che quella anima foſſe piena del ſopraceleſte vigore. Et nel ſalmo ſi legge della rugiadoſa barba di Aaron; queſto medeſimo ſentimento. Adunque queſta imagine coprirà il volume ap partenente al vigor che poſſa hauer coſa in queſto mondo. Et ſignificherà coſa vigorofa ò forte, ò meriteuole. Et la verità poniamo in queſto luogo come quella della quale da ſani di Dario fu confeſſo, che ella hauesse forza ſopra tutte le altre coſe. Sotto Paſiphe queſta imagine ſignificherà natura vigoro-\nſa, forte, & verace. Et ſotto i talari dar vigor o forza, o operar ritorno al vero. Et è da notar, che la Geburà è verità: & che per quella via ſi dichiara.\n\nMisericordia & Veritas obuiaue-\nrunt ſibi. Iuſtitia & pax oſculatæ ſunt.\n\nSalmo.\n84.\n\nI due Serpenti combattenti ci rappreſentano quella favola, che ſi legge di Mercurio, che ſi incontra in due ſerpi che combattevano, ſotto la quale imagine collocheremo la dif cordanza, la differenza, & la diverſità delle coſe. Et ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà tale imagine natura con\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\ncontentioſa. Et ſotto i Talari contendere. Et ſotto Prometheo l’arte militare, & la guerra terreſ ſtra & maritima & le loro pertinenze. arte ſopra il Dragone è ſinto da noi con queſta ragione. Detto habbiamo i Pianeti ricercer le loro nature & influſſi dalle corriſpondenti Saphiroth ſopraceleſti: & perche la Gaburà che dall’influſſo a Marte, ha per ſopraſtante una angelica chiamata Zamael, che ſignifica veleno di Dio, percioche per mezzo di queſta Dio caſtiga il mondo: & percioche i Cabaliſti dicono tale intelligenza hauer figura di Dragone noi le poniamo Marte à cauallo: & a queſta imagine daremo vn volume contenente coſe nocive & ve-\nlenoſe naturali.\n\nEt ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà natura nociva, crudele, &\nvindicarice.\n\nEt ſotto i Talari, nuocere, incrudelir, vendicarſi, impedire\n\nGione.\n\nL’antro di Gione, contenerà cinque imagini, Giunon ſuſpo-\nſta, I due Fori della Lira, Il Caduceo, a cui pioue. l’Oro in grembo, & le tre Gratie.\n\nGiunon ſuſpeſa è nel Conuitio di Gione. anchora, doue ſignifica l’aere ſemplice:& qui ſignificherà i quattro elemen ti in vniuerſale,& l’aere in particolare, il quale eſſendo di uiſo in tre regioni, nella più baſſa collocheremo rugiada, brina, matina luce, freddo, freſco, caldo, & nebbia. Nella ſeconda,nubi, venti, tuoni, lampi, fulmini, pioue, gragnuola, & neue. Nella terza,& alta comete, fuochi correnti, & ſtelle cadenti in apparenza.\n\nQueſta ſarà anchor ſotto i Talari & ſotto Prometheo, co-\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n23\n\nme è detto nel Conuiuio. I due Fori della Lira habbiamo fatti per neceſſita , ma con queſta ragione,che la natura hauendo fatto gli orecchi a gli animali,& principalmente all’huomo, con vie ritorte, & accommodate a riceuer l’aere percoſſo da alcun ſuono, impercioche eſſo ſi contorce a guiſa di acqua percoſſa da pietra:& la natura per riceuerlo gli tiene apparecchiato luogo parimente contorto,queſto aere battuto,& entrato ne l’orecchia dell’animale percuote quell’aere di dentro,il qual chiamiamo connaturale,& il connaturale battuto batte alcu ni nerui di dentro,per li quali l’animale ode. Aſſi que gl’an tichi fabricatori della Lira per commodita di toccare i ner ui di quella,fecero quelli di fuora,ma i Fori ad imitation de le orecchie principalmente dell’huomo. Di che queſta imagi ne hauera il volume continente tutte le coſe udibili, et ogni ſtrepito & ſuono naturale.\n\nQueſta imagine ſotto i Talari ſignifica far ſtrepito, & ſi appartiene più a Gioue,che ad altro Pianeta, per eſſer egli patron dell’aere ſenza’l quale non ſi può far ſuono.\n\nIl Caduceo è la verga di Mercurio,la quale egli poſe (come dicono le fauole) fra i due ſerpēti,che egli trouò a combat tere,ſecondo che ſi è detto in Marte,& eſſi con perpetua unio ne intorno a quella ſi auinchiarono:& queſta imagine ci di moterà coſe vniformi,medeſime, nō differenti,et eſquivalenti,\n\nSotto Paſiphe contenerà natura amicheuole inclinata alla cura familiare,& alla republica. Et ſotto i Talari amicitia,o conuerſatione eſercitata. Sotto Prometheo,la città,et la cura familiare, laqual è di uiſa in padre di famiglia,madre di famiglia,figli, e ſerui.\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nDanae con la pioua d’oro, anchor che negli altri miſterii ſi= gniſichi quell’iſteſſo, che il vello dell’oro, & gli horti del le heſperidi, à noi qui ſignifichera buona fortuna, pienez= za, & abondanza delle coſe, che ogni plenitudine & o= gni coſa buona viene da alto.\n\nSotto Paſiphe dinotera buona fortuna, felicità, nobilità, ricchezze, ſanità, gloria ottenimento di deſiderio.\n\nSotto i Talari operatione intorno alla buona fortuna &\nalle coſe dette di ſopra.\n\nLe tre Gratie erano da gli antichi talmete dipinte che l’u= na tenea il viſo naſcoſto, & queſta ſignificaua il bene= ficio del dante, che non dee eſſer paleſato da colui che lo da. Et Ieſu Chriſto dice. Cum facis elemoſynam noli tuba canere ante te. Et altroue, Neſciat ſiniſtra tua quid fa= ciat dextera tua. L’altra il moſtraua tutto, & ſignifica il riceuitor del beneficio, a cui ſi appartiene dimoſtrare il vi= ſo, cio è paleſar la gratia riceuuta. La terza parte ne aſ= conde, & parte ne moſtra, & ſignifica il beneficio com= penſato, moſtrando il riceuuto, & celando il dato. Or que= ſta imagine in queſto ſignifichera coſe vtili.\n\nSotto Paſiphe natura benefica.\n\nSotto i Talari, dar fauor, beneficio & aiuto\n\nSaturno.\n\nL’antro di Saturno coprirà ſette imagini. Cibele. Tre cap di Lupo di Leone & di cane. L’arca del patto. Proteo legato. Vn paſſer ſolitario. Pandora. Et vna fanciulla, à cui i capelli leuati verſo’l cielo ſtano tagliati. Cibele habbiamo hauuta nel conuiiuo, & ſignifica la te ra, & per la corona turrita ſignifica le città da lei ſoſten te. Queſta è tirata da due Leoni nel carro, percioche com\n\n[illegible]\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n24\n\nIl Leone è forte davanti & debile di dietro, coſì il Sol, onde i Leoni hanno coſtal natura è più poſſente nella parte da nanti ,che in quella di dietro. Di queſta ſ’è detto anche nel conuiuio, & qui, & ne Talari, & in Prometheo non vo-\nmitera fuoco, percioche ſignifichera puramente la Terra. Et ſotto l’Antro dinoterà la Terra in Generale, con tutte le ſue ſpeci trattate da Plinio, cio è dal capitolo, che fa, de Terrarum generibus, come creata, & erme. Poi ſignifichera Terra habitata, & non habitata, piana & montuoſa. La piana contera tutti luoghi aperti. La montuoſa baua le valli, le comalli, i colli, i monti, & ſuoi appartenẽ ti, come pietre, marmi, minere di metalli,& al minerali, et a queſte coſe ſi aggiũgerãno anche gli tri animali terreſtri. Queſta imagine conterrà ſotto i Talari le operationi che puo far l’huomo naturalmente intorno alla Terra, pur che non concernano i piedi, i quali portano le ſue operationi ap preſſo ,ſi come gli altri membri. Ma ſotto Prometheo conterrà la Geometria, Geographia, Coſmographia,,& Agricultura, & le parti di lui impera ciochè queſta diſtingueremo in agricultura dintorno alla Terra,& intorno à frutti della Terra,d’ intorno à gli arbo ri,& intorno à frutti de gli arbori dintorno a gli animali,& intorno a frutti de gli animali,& in queſte ſei parti macceremo tutti gli ſcrittori della agricultura. E’ ſi dà q̃ ſta parte à Saturno p̄ eſſer freddo eſſecco,et p̄ eſſere il più immobile,eſſendo la terra di tal natura ſecondo il Triſmegisto. Le tre teſte di Lupo,di Leone et di Cane ſono tali . Scriue Macrobio che li antichi volẽdo figurare i tre tempi,cio è il paſſato,il preſente,et il futuro,dipingevano le tre predette\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nſtelle. Et quella del Lupo ſignifica il tempo paſſato , perciò cioche ha gia deuorato quella del Leone il preſente ( ſe il preſente dar ſi puo) percioche gli affanni preſenti ci ma-\ntono coſi ſatto errore, qual ci metterebbe la viſta d’un Leo ne ſe ci ſopraſſeſſe. Et quella del Cane ſignifica il tempo fu turo , percioche à guiſa di Cane adulatore il tempo futuro ci promette ſempre di meglio. Adunque queſta imagine cõ tenera queſti tre tempi Saturnini, & i loro appartenenti, percioche tutti quei tempi che non ſi comprendono per vicinanza , o lontananza del Sole , o ſono Saturnini o ſono Lu nari, Saturnini come queſti tre che habbiamo detti, i quali non ci ſi manifeſtano per lo corſo del Sole , come fa la notte & il giorno , le quattro ſtagioni, le hore , i minuti, & gli anni. La lontananza adunque di queſto pianeta fa che queſti tre predetti tempi non li conoſciamo altramente ſe non per lo paſſato , per lo preſente, & per lo futuro. I Lunari veramente ſono ſotto l’antro della Luna, & ſotto i Ta lari di quella , & ſotto Prometheo coperti dalla imagine di Diana à cui Mercurio porge la veſta.\n\nTempi.\n\nSaturni-\nni.\n\nSolari.\n\nLunari.\n\nLa medesima imagine delle tre teſte ſotto Paſiphe ſignifichera l’huomo eſſer ſottopoſto al tempo. Et ſotto i Talari tutte le operationi d’intorno al tempo non conoſciute per lontananza , o vicinanza del Sole , ne per corſo lunare, come Indugiar, far indugiar, dar termine, ò rimettere in altro tempo.\n\nL’area del patio quantunque nel ſuo alto miſterio ſignifichi i tre mondi che habbiamo dati à Pan , percioche era tale mente ſatta , che un cubito & mezo la miſuraua ſi per lungo , come per largo , Et ciaſcun cubito conſtando di\n\nſei palmi\n\n[illegible]\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO. 25\n\nſegne che noue palmi foſſe per lungo,& noue per trauerſo: il qual numero hauea da ſignificare i noue Cieli,& il deca-\ncimo era figurato per lo coperchio d’oro,ilquale non ſi ſten-\ndea ſe non ſopra la prima,& ſopra la ſeconda diuisione, & la terza rimaneua ſcoperta. Or queſta ſcoperta ſi come habbiamo ne miſteri reuelati ſignificaua queſto mondo inferiore eſpoſto à pioue,à uenti,à caldi,& à tutte le muta-\ntioni.\n\nLa ſeconda ſignificaua il celeſte mondo, & per tal cagion ne contenea vn Candelabro aureo con ſette Lucerne ſigni-\nficanti i ſette Pianeti,poi haueua vna Lucerna ſeparata con tre calami per lato,la quale anchora ſignificaua il Sole nel la ſua ſuperiorità.\n\nAppreſſo vi erano alcuni vaſi,i quali ſignificauano il rice-\nuimento,il quale faceuano i pianeti da gli influssi ſopra celeſti. Et erano figure ſperiche,le quali ſignificauano i glo bi. Eranui anchora fiori,nello ſignification de quali giace il ſecreto di tutti i ſecreti che non è lecito à riuellar ſe non a tempo,& con la uolontà di Dio. La terza diuisione era chiamata propiciatorio fauorita da due Cherubini. L’vno de quali ſignificaua la natura diuina,& l’altro la humana in vn medeſimo Chriſto per loqual propiciatorio ſi faceua remiſſion de peccati,à ſignificare che per lo uenturo Chri ſto ſi haueua à far coſi fatta remiſſione. Et queſta diuisione terza ſignificaua il ſopraceleſte. Et chiamandoſi la parte di mezzo ſancti, queſta terza chiamaua ſancti ſanctorum, ſi come à ſchior Cœli cœlo o per dir meglio,Cœli cœlorũ. Perciò che gli Hebrei nō danno ſingulare à cieli,et di queſto mõ do ci fece mentione Giouanni quando diſſe. In mundo erat,\n\nL’Idea del Theatro.    D\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\n53\n\n& mundus per ipſum factus eſt, et mundus eum non cognouit, ait, che dicendo in mōdo erat, inteſe del ſopraceleſte, & quando d.ſſe: Et mundus per ipſum factus eſt, ſignificò il te reſtre. Et in dire, Et mundus eum non cognouit, parlò del mō do inferiore.\n\nAdunque anchor che per l’Arca ci vengano ſignificati (come habbiamo detto) i tre mondi, non dimeno per hauer nō gia affidata alla guardia di Pan le ſignificationi di quelli, vogliamo che ella habbia a coprire il volume appartenente al luogo, & a tutte le ſue differenze: et quello ci par di hauer ragioneuolmente ordinato: percioche contenendo l’arca tutti i tre i mondi, dà conſequentemente luogo a tutte le coſe. Et ſi come l’Arca per contenere tutte le coſe merita la conſeruation del luogo con tutte le ſue differenze: coſì hauendo ella ad eſſer data ad uno de ſette pianeti, non puo ad altri conuenire meglio che a Saturno, ilquale per la ſua ampiezza del circulo comprende tutti gli altri. Queſta ſolo i Talari ſignificherà i monumenti che puo far l’huomo in torno al luogo, come collocar coſe quà, & là.\n\nProteo legato a differenza del Proteo ſciolto ch’è nel Conuiſio Lunare, & qui è collocato da noi per quello che appreſſo ſi dirà. E benche queſta legatura poſſa eſſer magi ca, & naturale pura, nondimeno qui intendiamo della pura naturale. Diſſi magica, percio che la legatura che fa Ariſteo di Proteo per conſiglio di Cirene ſua madre appreſſo di Homero et di Virgilio, è legatura magica. Et qui habet aures audiendi audiat, percioche appartiene al ſecreto del quale habbiamo parlato di ſopra. Ma la legatura naturale, & de la quale ſotto queſta figura intendiamo, è tale quale dire:\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.     26\n\nmo. Lo Spirito di Chriſto è quello(come habbiamo anchor\n detto nel Conuiui[o])il quale diſcendendo da ſopra celeſti coſe: natione\n dall’vniuona con la virtù ſua tutti i cieli, & porta giu tutte delle coſe\n ſe le loro impreſſioni & tutte le loro virtù & con quelle ſi\n ferma qua giù fra animali,herbe,& fiori.& ſe coſi non ſi\n rinouaſſe le coſe,tutte perirebbono. Et queſta è perauentura\n quella città,che Giouanni vide nell’Apocaliſſi ſanta diſce-\n dente piena di gioie : & per queſto Dauid canta il Cantico\n nuouo,vedendo tante coſe rinouate:et Eſaia dice,Creabo cœ-\n lum nouum,& terram nouam : & nell’Apocal. à,chora è\n ſcritto.Ecce noua facio omnia:& queſta è la ſcala di Iacob\n per la quale diſcendono & aſcendono gli ſpiriti,che lo ſce-\n dere è lo venir a far queſta rinouatione,& lo aſcendere è il\n tornare dello ſpirito a rifocillarſi co’l ſuperiore vniuerſale.\n\nMa di queſta rinouatione volendo far mentione il Petrarca\n come colui che non paſſaua il celeſte mondo fece quel Sonet-\n to,il qual comincia.\n\nQuando il Pianeta,che diſtingue. l’hore\n Ad albergar col Tauro ſi ritorna. doue dicendo.\n Cade virtù dalle celeſti come\n Che veſte il mondo di nouel colore,vien à dare a cieli que-\n ſta operatione di tornar a far bello il mondo,non intenden-\n do che l’anima del mondo piena di vinificante ſpirito che è\n Chriſto portata dal Sole giù dal concauo della Luna con\n maggior abondanza & fecondità quando il Sole comincia\n a girar ſopra di noi,che quando a più lontano,ſoprauiene a\n la miſſion,che vuol far la natura volendo far la production\n delle herbe,de fiori,& delle altre coſe elementate. Et ſe e non\n interueniffe come mediatore a conciliar le qualità contrarie\n\nD  ii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\n33\n\nne, che ſanno il miſto, le loro contrarietà non potrebbon mai ſtare in ſieme ſotto la forma di queſta o di quella herba, di quella o di quel fiore. Tale è adunque la temperan za del diuino ſpirito di Chriſto, che accorda anchora i diſ-\nſcordanti. Et è quello che dice il Propheta. Ego cælum & terram impleo, & altrove dice la Scrittura, pleni ſunt cœ li & terra gloria tua. Queſto adunque ſpirito di Chriſto, & non dell’ anima del mondo ( come dicono i Platonici) è non ſolamente mediatore, conciliatore, vinificatore, & ſoſtenito-\nre di: queſti quattro diſcordi elementi, ma moſſo dalla ſua miſericordia, è anchor mediatore & conciliatore fra la diuina giuſtitia, & la humana fragilità. Et che queſto vera mente ſia lo ſpirito vinificante tutte le coſe, habbiamo dal ſalmo. Avertente te faciem tuam turbabuntur, & omnia in pulverem reuertentur. Et, Emitte ſpiritum tuum & renouabis faciem terræ. Chiamandolo adunque ſpiritum tu um, moſtra queſto eſſere ſpirito di Dio, & non dell’ anima del mondo. Et Paolo lo chiama ſpirito vinificante. Sopraſ-\nvenendo adunque la materia prima, cio è Proteo pieno di que ſto ſpirito vinificante, alla miſtion delle herbe, & de fiori, & de gli altri miſti, ſta naturalmente tanto legato dentro da termini di queſto fiore, o di quella herba, per fin che ſi vengano à diſſoluere. Et qui è da notare vn detto di Mer curio Triſmegiſto nell’ Aſclepio. Quis quid de alto deſcen-\ndit generans eſt, quod ſurſum verſus emanat nutriens, ideſt preſtans vitam, hoc eſt vinificans. Scendendo adunque que ſto ſpirito ſoprauueniente alla miſtione, che vorrebbe far la na tura meſcolandoſi con quelli che ſarebbono ſtati diſcordi, e gli concilia & genera. Et mentre la pianta, o l’animal crea\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n27\n\nſee, lo nutriſce & vniſca. Sta adunque ſeparato in qualun que individuo per fin che uenga: il tempo della diſſolutione ne chiamata indegnamente morte ſecondo Mercurio, il qual coſì ſcriue nel Pimandro al xii. Capo. Non moritur in mun do quicquam , ſed compoſita corporea diſſoluuntur: Diſſolu tio mors non eſt , ſed miſtionis reſolutio quædam , ſoluitur autem vnio non vt ea quæ ſunt intereant, ſed vt vetera in neſcant: Per quanto tempo adunque la vnion de miſti ſta in ſieme, per tanto riman legata, & fermata, et riſtretta quel la parte di Proteo con quello ſpirito inchiuſo. Et per tal ca gione vogliamo che queſta imagine habbia à conſertar ſol to di ſe coſe immobili , fermate , o ferme.\n\nSotto Paſiphe ſignificherà natura oſtinata & immutabi\nle.\n\nEt ſotto i Talari ſar coſa alcuna immobile , come ferma-\nre, arreſtare.\n\nEt quella imagine à Saturno vien data per la ſua tar-\ndità.\n\nIl Paſſer ſolitario aſſai per ſe ſenza altra dichiara­tione mo ſtra hauere à contener coſa ſola o abbandonata.\n\nSotto Paſiphe ſignificherà natura ſolitaria, & huomo ſo\nlo, & abbandonato.\n\nMa ſotto i Talari ſignificherà andar ſolo, ſtar ſolo, abo bandonare & laſciar perſona o luogo , o coſa.\n\nEt quella imagine a Saturno ſi conuiene , come à natura Pandora nell’Antro ſignifica afflittion di coſe.\n\nSotto Paſiphe afflittion dell’huomo , & tutte le ſue male fortune infelicità , ignobilità , pouertà , infirmità, & il non ottener deſiderio.\n\nD  iii.\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO, 38\n\nSotto i Talari dar afflittione altrui. La imagine de capelli tagliati alla fanciulla, i quali vede-\nmo in Marte diſteſi verſo il cielo, porterà tutte le coſe oppo-\nſte, ciò è deboli. Ne ciò habbiamo fatto ſenza autorità, ma percioche Alceſte appreſſo Euripide non potendo morir della deſiderata morte, il mandato Mercurio le taglia il capello, & ella ſi muore: & Niſo non fu da Minos abbattuto ſe non poi che la Scilla innamorata gli tagliò il fatato capello. Ne Dido appreſſo Virgilio puo finir di morire, ſe non dapoi che Iris mandata da Giunone le ha tagliato il capello: & il conſiglio di Virgilio è, che Iris per ſignificar co colori gli elementi, ſignifichi gli elementati. Et il tagliare il capello ſia diſſolution di elementi. I quali miſteri da Poeti ſono ſtati robbati a Propheti, come da quel luogo de capelli tagliati a Sanſone.\n\nQuesta imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà debilità dello huomo, ſtanchezza, natura falſa & buggiarda. Ma ſotto i Talari ſignificherà debilitar perſona, o coſa, o mentire.\n\n[illegible]\n\nDI M. GIULIO CAMILLO\n\n28","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0001","text":"L’ANTRO.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"3.1"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","text":"IL Terzo grado hauera per ciaſcuna delle ſue porte di pinto vno Antro, il quale noi chiameremo l’Antro Ho= merico à differenza di quello, che Platon deſcriue nella ſua Republica. Homero adunque finge ſopra il porto di Itaca vno antro, nel quale alcune Nimphe teſſono tele purpuree, & finge api che eſcono, & tornano a fabricare i loro melli le quali teſſiture, & fabricamenti ſignificando le coſe miſ= ſte, & elementate, vogliamo che qualunque de ſette antri, ſecondo la natura del ſuo Pianeta habbia à conſeruare i miſti, & elementati à lui appartenenti.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"3.2"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","text":"Et per hauer qual= che information delle coſe miſte & elementate, dico, che ſe= condo la diſtintion meſſa da Moſe, poiche Eloim l’un giorno creò la materia prima per fare il Cielo & la terra, perche non ſi conueniva alla materia tutto l’influſſo de ſopraceleſti ruſcelli, il ſecondo giorno formò la Rachia, ciò è la maſſa de cieli, & non il firmamento ſecondo che detto habbiamo anchora, percioche egli è ſolamente l’ottaua ſpera, & miſſe la detta maſſa diſteſa fra il mondo ſopraceleſte, & l’infe= riore, a fine che diuidiſſe l’acque de ſopraceleſti ruſcelli che non bagnano, dalle acque di queſto mondo, che bagnano, delle quali ſopraceleſti acque è ſcritto. Benedicite aquae om nes, quæ ſuper cœlos ſunt domino. Et interpoſta adunque la detta maſſa celeſte, & diſteſa, accioche non pioueſſe mag= gior l’influſſo delle acque ſuperiori, che alla capacità della materia ſi conueniſſe.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"3.3"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0004","text":"Et intorno à queſte acque è da notare, che Gregorio Nazianzeno ſi inganna, intendendo per quel’","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"3.4"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0005","text":"I giorni\nalla crea\ntion del\nmondo.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"3.5"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0006","text":"Le acque\nſopra ce=\nleſti.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"3.6"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0007","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"3.7"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0008","text":"16","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"3.8"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0009","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"3.9"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0010","text":"Se il cielo chryſtallino, il qual nomamente è ſtato finto da alcu ni ſopra il firmamento, ma non hanno ne ragion ne fonda mento ne della ſacra, ne della prophana ſcrittura. Nel ter zo giorno dice Moſe, che Eloim comandò che ſi congregaſ ſero, le acque, che ſono ſotto il cielo in un luogo, cio è tutte le virtù germinatiue inſieme, & appareſſe fuori la terra ar rida, a fin che per le dette germinatiue virtù, raccolte eſſa dimeniſſe ſeconda, il che fatto diſſe. Produca terra herbam virentem, & lignum (ſe dir ſi poteſſe) ſeminiferum. Nel quarto giorno furono fatti i Luminari, & collocati nella maſſa de Cieli. La Luna nella prima, & il Sole nella quar-\nta Spera, per li quali ſi hauesse da diſtinguer la luce dalle te nebre, cio è le coſe, che haueano gia ricevuto forma da quel= le, che ancor informate nō erano.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"3.10"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","text":"Nel 5 giorno parla della communication della vita in tutti gli animali, percioche vuol che le acque, cio è le germinatiue virtù producano tutte le diverſi tà de i animali coſi acquatici come volatili, et terreſtri qui a baſ ſo, a differenza di q̃lli di laſſu. Nel ſeſto di, produſſe l’homo, et nel ſettimo ripoſo. Aſſique dopo la materia prima nō veg giamo che Dio creaſſe noua materia, ma da la prima formò tutte le coſe, le quali noi chiamiamo miſte, et elementate. Et le quali habbiamo a trouar nel terzo grado de le ſette colōne ſotto la porta dell’antro, eccetto l’homo, il quale eſſendo ſtato ſeparatamente formato, et fatto ſignor de i miſti, et elementati, vogliamo c’habbia grado particolare, come poi ſi vedra. Sotto la porta adunque dell’Antro Lunare troueremo cinque imagini, Nettuno, Daphne, Diana, à cui Mercurio porge la meſſa, le ſtalle d’Augia, et Giunon fra le nubi.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"3.11"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0012","text":"Ne ſi habbia il marauigliare alcuno, che Nettuno, il cui eſſer ſotto.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"3.12"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0013","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"3.13"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","text":"il communito ſi habbia a riueder ſotto l’Antro, ſotto i Tale-\nri, e ſotto Prometheo, il che hauerra anchor di altre ima gini & in queſto & in altri pianetti, percioche anche Ho mero dice,che Vliſſe hauua veduto Hercole & fra i Dei in Cielo,& nell’inferno, il che ſe à lui non ſi diſdice, men ſi dee diſdire à noi,quali per non aggrauar la memoria di diuerſe imagini in coſe medeſime facciamo che ſi riuegga la medeſima figura ſotto diuerſe porte. Proteo ſignifichera forma, già ſoprauenuta ſuggetto & coſa naturale.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"3.14"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","text":"Nettuno adunque ſotto il Communito ſignifica l’elemento del l’acqua ſimpliciſſimo, ma ſotto l’Antro lo ſignifichera già miſto,percioche in queſto mondo non veggiamo alcuno elemento ſi puro, che miſto non ſia ſi come lungamente ha prouato & tenuto Anaxagora.Sotto la imagine adunque di queſto Nettuno ſarà contenuto il volume, doue ſaranno ordinate diſtintamente per tagli l’acqua in genere, & l’ acqua in ſpecie, & l’acqua in genere ſi diuidera nel ſuo tutto & nelle ſue parti,il tutto è come dir acqua ſolamente,le ſue parti, come goccia.Vi ſaranno anchor le qualità delle acque, & le quantità.Le qualità, come dolce & ſal ſa,& le dolci ſtanti & correnti; & gli altri accidenti.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"3.15"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016","text":"Et oltre a ciò i lenti, le ripe, & altri appartenenti; & anchor gli animali aquatici, & ſotto queſto Nettuno non vi ſi impaccia anchor l’huomo, percioche e fu l’ultimo creato de gli animali.Ma quando troueremo Nettuno ſotto i Talari,percioche quelli ſignificano la operatione,che puo far l’huomo intorno a ciaſcuna coſa creata auanti a lui natural mente, & fuor di arte,vogliamo che egli habbia nel ſuo.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"3.16"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0017","text":"Cannone","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"3.17"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0018","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"3.18"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0019","text":"DIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO.  17","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"3.19"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0020","text":"Cannone operationi humane,& naturali intorno alle ac-\nque,come è detto anchor nel continuo.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"3.20"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","text":"Et ſotto Prometheo ci dimostrerà le arti sopra l’acque. Daphne che ſi traſmuta in Lauro ſarà Simbolo del boſchiuo. Et qui ſi conterrà cio che già mai Theophrasto, o, altri ſcrittori hanno ſcritto de plantis co ſuoi conſeguenti, che ſono le ombre.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"3.21"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","text":"Ma ſotto i Talari Daphne ſignificherà le operationi natu rali intorno al legname,come piegar,portare. Et ſotto Prometheo conterrà i giardini,& tutte le arti in torno al legname.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"3.22"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0023","text":"Daphne veramente,cio e il boſchiuo è ben dato alla Luna: cio è à Diana Dea de boſchi,percioche, è regina(come habbiamo detto)delle humidità, ſenza le quali niuna pianta creſcerebbe.La onde Virgilio nel quarto della Georgica.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"3.23"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0024","text":"Oceanumque patrem rerum, nymphasque sorores\nCentum quæ Syluas, centum quæ flumina ſeruant.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"3.24"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","text":"Diana, à cui Mercurio porge la veſta è la terza imagine. Si legge fra le fauole Greche,che veggendo Gioue Diana andare ignuda eſſendo ella caſta non gli piacque, & commiſe à Mercurio che le faceſſe vna veſta. Et per mola te che egli gliene faceſſe,non ne fu mai alcuna, che le ſi poteſſe accomodare.La qual finitione ci dà ſimbolo ſignifi-\ncante le mutatione & le ſue ſpecie, cio è la generatione, la corruptione,l’augmento,la diminutione, l’alteratione, la mutatione ſecondo il luogo,& il moto con tutte le ſpecie recitate da Ariſtotele, & diſtinte per li ſuoi tagli. Queſta imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà la mutation dell’huomo o ſecondo la openione,o ſecondo la traſfigura","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"3.25"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0026","text":"L’Idea del Theatro.     C","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"3.26"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0027","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"3.27"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0028","text":"tione del corpo.          Et ſotto i Talari ſignificherà muouere, ò\nmutar coſa, riceuer diſporre, operation fatta roſſo ò ſubito.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"3.28"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0029","text":"Ma ſotto Prometheo contenerà i meſi, & le loro parti. Le Stalle di Augia coſi chiamate ſono da Greci, percioche Au gia fu un Re ricchiſſimo di poſſeſſioni & di campi, ma la grande abondantia di beſtie che tenea, ingombrò ſi il ſuo paeſe di letame, che corruppe la fertilità de campi. Adunque ſotto queſta imagine daremo un uolume, che comprehen-\nderà le ſporchezze delle coſe del mondo, le muffe, i fracidu-\nmi, le uiltà, le imperfettioni, & coſe ſimili non piaceuoli.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"3.29"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0030","text":"Queſta medeſima imagine ſotto Paſiphe, contenerà le ſporchezze del corpo humano, & ſuoi eſcrementi, come quelle delle orecchie, del naſo, delle unghie, de gli occhi, il ſudore, lo ſputo, il vomito, il meſtruo, l’urina, &c.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"3.30"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0031","text":"Ma ſotto i Talari ſignificherà le ſporche operationi, bruta-\ntar, marchiar.&c.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"3.31"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0032","text":"Et queſte Stalle ſi dàno alla Luna, percioche non ui ha ſpor-\nchezza, ſe non da humidità corrotta.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"3.32"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","text":"Gimnon fra le nubi, Gimnon ſignifica l’aere, & queſta coper-\nta di nubi ci darà ſignification di coſe naſcoſe in natura, & di quelle che da Peripatetici ſono chiamate ſcibili, ma che non ſono anchor ſapute: & ſignificherà anchor tempo brieue: & queſte coſe ſi dàno alla Luna, percioche non hab biamo Pianeta, che in più brieue tempo ci ſi naſconda.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"3.33"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0034","text":"Queſta imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà l’aſcondimento\nche puo far l’huomo di ſe.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"3.34"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0035","text":"Ma ſotto i Talari dinoterà huomo naſconder coſa ò oltra\nperſona.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"3.35"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0036","text":"Sotto Mercurio ſaranno ſei imagini. Il metallo dell’Oro, gli","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"3.36"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0037","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"3.37"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0038","text":"DI·M·GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"3.38"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0039","text":"18","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"3.39"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0040","text":"Atomi, la Piramide, il nodo Gordiano implicato, il medeſimo eſplicato, Giunon finta di nubi. Il Vello dell’Oro quã tunque nella miſtica Philoſophia habbia ſignification del piu alto dono, che il Signor Dio ſoglia donare a pochi de ſuoi eletti, & che habbia gran ſignification per coſi fatto rapto la congregation de gli Heroi, la naue prima, & il perdimento che fece Iaſon del Calzaio nel fiume ſolo al mo do ſenza uento, onde per auentura è tratto l’ordine del To-\nſone, il qual conſente con la magia Zoroaſtro, la quale era la prima coſa, che inſegnar ſi doueſſe al nouello principe de Perſi, accioche ei non fuſſe Tiranno.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"3.40"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0041","text":"Nondimeno tirando noi dalla altezza del ſuo miſterio queſta aurea pelle alla baſſezza del noſtro biſogno, ella ci ſeruirà per imagine di tutti gli oggetti che ſ’appartengono al giudicio de’l peſo, o del toccamento,come graue & leggiero,aſpro,molle,du ro,tenero,& ſimili, intendſi nondimeno di quelle coſe, che ſon fuor dell’huomo.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"3.41"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0042","text":"Queſta medeſima imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignifichera le co\nſe medeſime del corpo humano.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"3.42"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0043","text":"Et ſotto i Talari ſignifichera l’operation ſenza arte di\nfar duro,molle, aſpro.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"3.43"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0044","text":"Et queſta imagine con vna tal ſignificatione ſi da a Mercurio , percioche le mani che principalmente fanno queſti giudicii ſono di Gemini, che è coſa di Mercurio.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"3.44"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0045","text":"Gli Atomi ci ſignificheranno tutta la quantità diſcreta nel-\nle coſe.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"3.45"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0046","text":"Et ſotto Paſiphe ſignificheranno il medeſimo ne gli huo-\nmini come alcuno.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"3.46"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0047","text":"C  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"3.47"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0048","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"3.48"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0049","text":"13","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"3.49"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0050","text":"Ma ſotto i Talari ſignificheranno quantita discreta ſta-\nte dall’huomo ſenza arte, come far in pezzi vna coſa con lima, diſſoluere & ſpargere.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"3.50"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0051","text":"Et per eſſer queſto ſuggetto della Arithmetica laquale è ſcienza di Mercurio, a lui ſi da queſta imagine.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"3.51"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0052","text":"La Piramide ſignifica quantita continua nelle coſe. Sotto Paſiphe ne gli huomini, come grande, picciolo, me-\nZano.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"3.52"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0053","text":"Sotto i Talari ſignifica operation ſenza arte, come alzare\nabbaſſare, ingroſſare, aſſottigliare.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"3.53"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0054","text":"Le quali due quantita eſſendo l’una della Arithmetica, & l’altra della Geometria ſcienze appartenenti ad Hercule tirante la ſaetta di tre punte, ſaranno ſotto quella imagine compreſe ſotto Prometheo.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"3.54"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0055","text":"Il Nodo Gordiano implicato fu porto ad Aleſſandro da eſ plicare, & egli impatiente lo tagliò. Sotto queſto ſi con-\ntenera quantita continua implicata, come vn filo, od vna faſcia.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"3.55"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0056","text":"Et ſotto i Talari ſignificherà l’intricar delle coſe. Il Nodo medeſimo eſplicato dinoterà coſa continua eſpli cata.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"3.56"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0057","text":"Et ſotto i Talari eſplication di coſe intricate. Giunon finta di nubi e tratta dalla favola, che eſſendo eſ-\nla ſtata da Iſſione ricercata di adulterio, gli appreſentò vn corpo di nubi ch’a lei ſi aſſimigliava, & con quello egli ſi giacque. Or per queſta beſtia fatta à colui di quella coſa finta, ſotto queſta figura ſaranno contenute le coſe appa-\nrenti ma non vere.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"3.57"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0058","text":"Sotto Paſiphe dinoterà natura ſimulatrice & aſtuta, &","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"3.58"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0059","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.  19","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"3.59"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0060","text":"fraudolenta.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"3.60"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0061","text":"Et ſotto i Talari fingere & ingannare. Et queſta imagine diamo à Mercurio per eſſer egli l’au-\ntor de lle malitie.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"3.61"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0062","text":"Sotto l’Antro di Venere ſono cinque imagini. Cerbero, una Venere. fanciulla che porta in capo vn vaſo di odori, Hercule pur gãte le ſtalle d’Augia, Narciſſo, & Tantalo ſotto il ſaſſo. Cerbero è ſtato dipinto cõ tre teſte à ſignificar le tre neceſſita naturali, che ſono il mangiare, il bere, & il dormire, le quali percioche impediscono molto l’huomo dalla ſpecula-\ntione, finge Virgilio che Enea per conſiglio della Sibilla volendo paſſar alla contemplation delle coſe alte, gli git-\nta vn boccone, & di ſubito paſſa. Il che ſignifica, che quantunque noi habbiamo à ſodisfare à queſte tre neceſſità, con poco habbiamo loro à ſodisfare, ſe vogliamo hauer tẽpo di contemplare.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"3.62"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","text":"Queſta imagine adũque ſotto l’antro conſerniera coſe appartenenti alla fame, alla ſete, & al ſonno. Vittuaglie, beueraggi, & coſe che ſonno inducono. Et à Venere ſi da queſta figura per la dilettatione.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"3.63"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","text":"Sotto Paſiphe ſignifichera fame, ſete, & ſonno ; & con ſeguenti. Sotto i Talari mangiar, bere, & dormire, & conſeguenti operationi naturali. Poi ſotto Prometheo ſignifichera la cucina, i conuiti deli-\ncioſi, & le delitie accommodate al dormire, come i ſuoni & i canti. La fanciulla portante in capo il vaſo de gli odori, quale fu treuata in Roma, nell’altro ſignifichera tutti li odori. Et","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"3.64"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0065","text":"C  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"3.65"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0066","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"3.66"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0067","text":"per eſſer il vaſo di Venere, a lei ſi da. Sotto i Talari ſignifica le noſtre operationi intorno a gli odori fuor di arte, come odorare & portare odori. Ma ſotto Prometheo contie-\nne le arti pertinenti ad odori, & a perfumieri.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"3.67"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0068","text":"Hercole purgante le ſtalle d’Augia è indotto, percioche le fauole dicono, che quel Re vedendoſi oppreſſo dalle molte immonditie, chiamò Hercole à leuarle via: & qui ſignificherà le coſe nette per natura.","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"3.68"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0069","text":"Sotto Paſiphe ſignificherà le nettezza del corpo humano. Sotto i Talari il nettar ſenza arte. Et ſotto Prometheo bagni & barberie. Et queſta figura à Venere ſi conuiene per la vaghezza, & delicatezza.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"3.69"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0070","text":"Narciso ſi guardò nell’acqua tranſitoria di queſto mondo, & ſignifica la mortal bellezza, la cui verità a chi trouar la vuole, fa biſogno di aſcender al ſopraceleſte Tiſeret, doue Hippia Platonico la douerebbe cercare: & tutti noi anchora, percioche quiui è ferma, et immortale. Hor ſotto queſta imagine haueremo la bellezza che ci apparisce in queſto mondo nelle coſe naturali & deſiderabili. Queſta figura ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà la bellezza humana & ſuoi con ſeguenti, Morbidezza, Vaghezza, Delettatione, Diſegno, Amore, Speranza, innamorati & eſſer amato.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"3.70"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0071","text":"Sotto i Talari ſignificherà far bello, far innamorare, far deſiderare, far ſperare, &c. Et ſotto Prometheo con tenerà l’arte de liſci, & de belletii. Tantalo ſotto il ſaſſo ſignifica coſe vacillanti,o tremanti,o che ſta no in pendente. Sotto Paſiphe dinoterà natura timida, ſu-\nſpettoſa, dubbioſa, & marauiglioſa. Et ſotto i Talari ſar","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"3.71"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0072","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"3.72"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0073","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"3.73"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0074","text":"20","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"3.74"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0075","text":"ſtamer, ſar tremar, ſar dubitar, ſar vacillar, ſar marear, [illegible]gliare,&c. Sotto l’Antro del Sole ſono cinque imagini, Sole, Argo ſolo. La Vacca guardata da Argo, Gerione vcciſa da Hercole vn Gallo & vn Leone: & Apolline che ſaet ta Giunone.","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"3.75"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0076","text":"Argo ſolo pieno di occhi, ſignifica tutto queſto mondo, di cui il capo ſono i Cieli, & gli occhi le ſtelle, con le quali coſì fa notiſce le coſe inferiori a venire alla apparenza della gene ratione di lontano, come lo ſtruzzo le ſue oua, dando a lo ro la vita di quello ſpirito, che è nelle ſue rote. del qual coſì parla Ezechiel. Et ſpiritus erat in rotis. Queſto come che tenga in vita tutti gli elementi, nondimeno più favoriſce il fuoco, che l’aere, & più l’aere che l’acqua, & più l’acqua che la terra: ma ſe queſta terra che è men favorita, p la vita & fecondità che le dona queſto ſpirito germina tutto di tante varietà di coſe, che debbono far gli altri elementi, la cui fecondità à noi inuiſibile favoriſce anchor la terra: Mer curio nel Pimandro dice la terra p niun modo eſſere immobile, anzi eſſere agitata da molti mouimenti.","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"3.76"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0077","text":"Et non dimeno à co paratione de gl’altri Elementi eſſer quaſi ſtabile: et aggiun ge che non è da creder, che eſſa, la quale è nutrice di tutte le coſe, manchi di mouimento; percioche è impoſſibil coſa, che ſen za mouimento poſſa parturire: & ſì come le ſtelle ſono gli occhi di queſto mondo, coſì gli arbori, che molto p la loro fer tilità ricevono del detto vitale ſpirito, ſono: a guiſa di peli, & di capelli del ſuo corpo, & i metalli & le pietre ſono a guiſa di oſſa. Non è adunque marauiglia, ſe i Theologhi ſim bolici hanno figurato il mondo ſotto il ſimbolo d’Argo pieno di occhi, percioche il mondo uiue. Queſta imagine adunque.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"3.77"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0078","text":"La terra","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"3.78"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0079","text":"C  iiii","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"3.79"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0080","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"3.80"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0081","text":"Si rappreſenterà il mondo tutto in vniuerſale, & in ſpecie la maſſa celeſte, & i corpi celeſti.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"3.81"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0082","text":"La Vacca guardata da Argo, anchor che ſignificaſſa poſſa la terra, nondimeno à noi ſignificherà tutti i viſibili & tut ti i colori","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"3.82"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0083","text":"Gerione, à cui Hercule tronca le tre teſte, ſignifica il prin cipio, la conſiſtenza, & l’occaſo del tempo appartenente al Sole. Et queſta imagine ſignificherà à noi non ſolamen te le età del mondo, ma anchor le quattro ſtagioni, le quali ſi fanno per l’acceſſo & receſſo del Sole, & parimente il giorno & la notte con le ſue parti.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"3.83"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0084","text":"Et ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà l’età dellhuomo.","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"3.84"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0085","text":"Sotto i Talari operationi naturali intorno à minuti all’hore,\nall’anno, alla età, & all’horologio.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"3.85"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0086","text":"Et ſotto Prometheo gli anni artificiali, minuti, hore, horolo-\ngij, & iſtrumenti di tempo.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"3.86"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0087","text":"Il Gallo col Leone. Non ſolamente Plinio apre queſta ſigni ficatione, ma Iamblico Platonico anchora, & Lucretio di cono, che quantunque amendue queſti animali ſiano Solari, nondimeno il Gallo porta ne gli occhi alcun grado piu excel lente del Sole, nel quale riguardando il Leone, ſi humilia à lui. Et all’auttore di queſto Theatro auenne che ritrouando ſi egli à Parigi nel luogo detto il Tornello, con molti gen-\ntilhuomini in vna ſala ad alcune fineſtre riguardanti ſopra vn giardino, vn Leone vſcito di prigionià venne in quella ſala, & à lui di dietro accoſtandoſi con le brame che lo preſe ſenza nocumento per le coſcie, & con la lingua lo andaua leccando. Et à quel toccamento & à quel fiato eſſendoſi egli rivolto, & hauendo quello animal","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"3.87"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0088","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"3.88"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0089","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"3.89"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0090","text":"31","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"3.90"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0091","text":"Veduto , eſſendo molti gli altri chi quà & chi là fuggiti, il Leone à lui ſi humiliava , quaſi in atto di domandar mer-\ncede. Il che non è da dire che aueniſſe per altro, ſe non che quello animale iſcorgeſſe in lui eſſer molto della virtù. So-\nlare. Queſta imagine adunque con tenera la eccellenza del le coſe naturali per comparatione.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"3.91"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0092","text":"Sotto Paſiphe ſignifichera la eccellenza dell’huomo , la ſuperiorità , la dignità , l’autorità & dominio in coſa degna d’honore.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"3.92"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0093","text":"Sotto i Talari ſignifichera far ſuperiore, dar dignità, &\ngrado.","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"3.93"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0094","text":"Ma ſotto Prometheo contenerà i Principati, & i regni -\ni quali tutti da ſcrittori ſono con precetti ſtati regolati, coſì foſſero ben ſeruati.","kind":"passage","sequence":94,"address":"3.94"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","text":"Apollo che ſaetta Giunone fra le nubi è imagine oppoſta alla Giunon naſcoſta fra le nubi, che è della Eſoda. Et ben che Homero induca queſta fauola, non è per ciò da creder che voglia introdur guerra fra i Dei, ſi come accenna So crate nel Menone , ma ſignifica coſe manifeſte.","kind":"passage","sequence":95,"address":"3.95"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0096","text":"Et ſotto Paſiphe ſignifica l’huomo manifeſtarſi, & ve\nnir à luce.","kind":"passage","sequence":96,"address":"3.96"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0097","text":"Ma ſotto i Talari manifeſtar perſona o coſa.","kind":"passage","sequence":97,"address":"3.97"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0098","text":"Sotto l’Antro di Marte ſono quattro imagini; Vulcano, Marte; vna fanciulla i cui capelli ſtanno leuati verſo’l Cielo, Due ſerpi che combattono ; & Marte ſopra un Dra-\ncone.","kind":"passage","sequence":98,"address":"3.98"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0099","text":"Vulcano porta talmente ſeco la ſignificatione del fuoco ; che non ha meſtier di dichiaratione. Et perche il fuoco è par tito in tre maniere, conciosia coſa che la più ſottile parte ſue","kind":"passage","sequence":99,"address":"3.99"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0100","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 13]","kind":"passage","sequence":100,"address":"3.100"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0101","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO.","kind":"passage","sequence":101,"address":"3.101"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0102","text":"ſecco appunto il concauo della Luna, ha ottenuto anchor da Latini eſſer chiamato aere. La onde Cicerone de natura Deorum 44. A Ether qui conſtat ex altiſſimis ignibus me tuemur hoc quoque verbum, dicaturque tam ether latine, quàm dicitur aer. Et benche per queſto luogo alcuni l’ac= compagnerebbono cõ l’aere, che hà ſotto l’Antro di gioie nondimeno riſguardando noi alla ſua natura ſi ſeguea, che è anchor ſuperiore al fuoco, vogliamo che ſia piutoſto del fuoco che dell’aere. Et tanto più che Cicerone dice nel me deſimo à 34. Ardor cæli qui æther, vel cælum nominatur Et à 37. Tenuis ac perlucẽs, & æquabili calore ſuffuſus æther. A queſto ſeguirà il fuoco Elementale, & nel terzo luogo ſarà collocato il fuoco noſtro.","kind":"passage","sequence":102,"address":"3.102"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0103","text":"Et percioche queſta ima gine è anche nel Conuiuio, & ſotto altre porte di quello habbiamo nel conuiuio detto più ampiamẽte, qui ci baſterà di tornar à dire, che Vulcano in queſto luogo ſigniſicherà, l’ethere, il fuoco elementare con l’incendio vniuerſale, & appreſſo, il fuoco noſtro con l’incendio particolare, la ſauil la, la fiamma, il carbone, & la cenere. Et q̃ſta imagine co cõtenuti da lei nõ po cõuenir ad altro pianeta, che à Marte, percioche ſolo Marte e caldo e ſecco ſi come è il fuoco, la oue il Sole è caldo, et humido, La Faciu la co capelli leuati verſo’l Cielo coſi è finta danoſi ſcioche l’huomo ſecõdo Platone è arbore riuolto, che l’arbore ha le radici all’ingiù, & l’huomo le ha all’inſù.","kind":"passage","sequence":103,"address":"3.103"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0104","text":"Et Origene et Hieronimo ſuo ſeguace vogliono che quando la ſcrittura fa mention di capelli o di barba, non ſi habbia ad intender di capelli ne di barba del corpo ma dell’anima, la quale per metaphora ha capelli & barba, & occhi, & altre par","kind":"passage","sequence":104,"address":"3.104"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0105","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":105,"address":"3.105"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0106","text":"DI. M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":106,"address":"3.106"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0107","text":"22","kind":"passage","sequence":107,"address":"3.107"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0108","text":"ti corriſpondenti al corpo. Et perche ſe’ uno ſi eſponeſſe ignudo à l’aere notturno, piu manifeſte-rebbono i capelli & la barba il contratto humore dal Cielo, che altra parte del corpo: vogliono che ſi come l’arbore p̄ le radici ſue ti ra à ſe l’humor nutritiuo dalla terra, coſì la barba & i ca pelli del noſtro huomo interiore tiri la rugiada, cio è l’hu mor viuificante da gli influſſi à ſopracелеſti canali, onde ne ſegua tutto il ſuo vigore. Et di q̃ è che ſi legge nella Caliſti ca. Come tuæ iuſtitiæ canalibus, intendendo de ſopraceleſti ruſcelli, la qual ſentenza porta ſignificatione, che quella anima foſſe piena del ſopraceleſte vigore. Et nel ſalmo ſi legge della rugiadoſa barba di Aaron; queſto medeſimo ſentimento. Adunque queſta imagine coprirà il volume ap partenente al vigor che poſſa hauer coſa in queſto mondo. Et ſignificherà coſa vigorofa ò forte, ò meriteuole.","kind":"passage","sequence":108,"address":"3.108"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0109","text":"Et la verità poniamo in queſto luogo come quella della quale da ſani di Dario fu confeſſo, che ella hauesse forza ſopra tutte le altre coſe. Sotto Paſiphe queſta imagine ſignificherà natura vigoro-\nſa, forte, & verace. Et ſotto i talari dar vigor o forza, o operar ritorno al vero. Et è da notar, che la Geburà è verità: & che per quella via ſi dichiara.","kind":"passage","sequence":109,"address":"3.109"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0110","text":"Misericordia & Veritas obuiaue-\nrunt ſibi. Iuſtitia & pax oſculatæ ſunt.","kind":"passage","sequence":110,"address":"3.110"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0111","text":"Salmo.\n84.","kind":"passage","sequence":111,"address":"3.111"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0112","text":"I due Serpenti combattenti ci rappreſentano quella favola, che ſi legge di Mercurio, che ſi incontra in due ſerpi che combattevano, ſotto la quale imagine collocheremo la dif cordanza, la differenza, & la diverſità delle coſe. Et ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà tale imagine natura con","kind":"passage","sequence":112,"address":"3.112"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0113","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":113,"address":"3.113"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","text":"contentioſa. Et ſotto i Talari contendere. Et ſotto Prometheo l’arte militare, & la guerra terreſ ſtra & maritima & le loro pertinenze. arte ſopra il Dragone è ſinto da noi con queſta ragione. Detto habbiamo i Pianeti ricercer le loro nature & influſſi dalle corriſpondenti Saphiroth ſopraceleſti: & perche la Gaburà che dall’influſſo a Marte, ha per ſopraſtante una angelica chiamata Zamael, che ſignifica veleno di Dio, percioche per mezzo di queſta Dio caſtiga il mondo: & percioche i Cabaliſti dicono tale intelligenza hauer figura di Dragone noi le poniamo Marte à cauallo: & a queſta imagine daremo vn volume contenente coſe nocive & ve-\nlenoſe naturali.","kind":"passage","sequence":114,"address":"3.114"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0115","text":"Et ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà natura nociva, crudele, &\nvindicarice.","kind":"passage","sequence":115,"address":"3.115"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0116","text":"Et ſotto i Talari, nuocere, incrudelir, vendicarſi, impedire","kind":"passage","sequence":116,"address":"3.116"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0117","text":"Gione.","kind":"passage","sequence":117,"address":"3.117"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0118","text":"L’antro di Gione, contenerà cinque imagini, Giunon ſuſpo-\nſta, I due Fori della Lira, Il Caduceo, a cui pioue. l’Oro in grembo, & le tre Gratie.","kind":"passage","sequence":118,"address":"3.118"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0119","text":"Giunon ſuſpeſa è nel Conuitio di Gione. anchora, doue ſignifica l’aere ſemplice:& qui ſignificherà i quattro elemen ti in vniuerſale,& l’aere in particolare, il quale eſſendo di uiſo in tre regioni, nella più baſſa collocheremo rugiada, brina, matina luce, freddo, freſco, caldo, & nebbia. Nella ſeconda,nubi, venti, tuoni, lampi, fulmini, pioue, gragnuola, & neue. Nella terza,& alta comete, fuochi correnti, & ſtelle cadenti in apparenza.","kind":"passage","sequence":119,"address":"3.119"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0120","text":"Queſta ſarà anchor ſotto i Talari & ſotto Prometheo, co-","kind":"passage","sequence":120,"address":"3.120"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0121","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":121,"address":"3.121"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0122","text":"23","kind":"passage","sequence":122,"address":"3.122"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0123","text":"me è detto nel Conuiuio. I due Fori della Lira habbiamo fatti per neceſſita , ma con queſta ragione,che la natura hauendo fatto gli orecchi a gli animali,& principalmente all’huomo, con vie ritorte, & accommodate a riceuer l’aere percoſſo da alcun ſuono, impercioche eſſo ſi contorce a guiſa di acqua percoſſa da pietra:& la natura per riceuerlo gli tiene apparecchiato luogo parimente contorto,queſto aere battuto,& entrato ne l’orecchia dell’animale percuote quell’aere di dentro,il qual chiamiamo connaturale,& il connaturale battuto batte alcu ni nerui di dentro,per li quali l’animale ode. Aſſi que gl’an tichi fabricatori della Lira per commodita di toccare i ner ui di quella,fecero quelli di fuora,ma i Fori ad imitation de le orecchie principalmente dell’huomo. Di che queſta imagi ne hauera il volume continente tutte le coſe udibili, et ogni ſtrepito & ſuono naturale.","kind":"passage","sequence":123,"address":"3.123"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0124","text":"Queſta imagine ſotto i Talari ſignifica far ſtrepito, & ſi appartiene più a Gioue,che ad altro Pianeta, per eſſer egli patron dell’aere ſenza’l quale non ſi può far ſuono.","kind":"passage","sequence":124,"address":"3.124"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0125","text":"Il Caduceo è la verga di Mercurio,la quale egli poſe (come dicono le fauole) fra i due ſerpēti,che egli trouò a combat tere,ſecondo che ſi è detto in Marte,& eſſi con perpetua unio ne intorno a quella ſi auinchiarono:& queſta imagine ci di moterà coſe vniformi,medeſime, nō differenti,et eſquivalenti,","kind":"passage","sequence":125,"address":"3.125"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0126","text":"Sotto Paſiphe contenerà natura amicheuole inclinata alla cura familiare,& alla republica. Et ſotto i Talari amicitia,o conuerſatione eſercitata. Sotto Prometheo,la città,et la cura familiare, laqual è di uiſa in padre di famiglia,madre di famiglia,figli, e ſerui.","kind":"passage","sequence":126,"address":"3.126"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0127","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":127,"address":"3.127"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0128","text":"Danae con la pioua d’oro, anchor che negli altri miſterii ſi= gniſichi quell’iſteſſo, che il vello dell’oro, & gli horti del le heſperidi, à noi qui ſignifichera buona fortuna, pienez= za, & abondanza delle coſe, che ogni plenitudine & o= gni coſa buona viene da alto.","kind":"passage","sequence":128,"address":"3.128"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0129","text":"Sotto Paſiphe dinotera buona fortuna, felicità, nobilità, ricchezze, ſanità, gloria ottenimento di deſiderio.","kind":"passage","sequence":129,"address":"3.129"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0130","text":"Sotto i Talari operatione intorno alla buona fortuna &\nalle coſe dette di ſopra.","kind":"passage","sequence":130,"address":"3.130"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0131","text":"Le tre Gratie erano da gli antichi talmete dipinte che l’u= na tenea il viſo naſcoſto, & queſta ſignificaua il bene= ficio del dante, che non dee eſſer paleſato da colui che lo da. Et Ieſu Chriſto dice. Cum facis elemoſynam noli tuba canere ante te. Et altroue, Neſciat ſiniſtra tua quid fa= ciat dextera tua. L’altra il moſtraua tutto, & ſignifica il riceuitor del beneficio, a cui ſi appartiene dimoſtrare il vi= ſo, cio è paleſar la gratia riceuuta. La terza parte ne aſ= conde, & parte ne moſtra, & ſignifica il beneficio com= penſato, moſtrando il riceuuto, & celando il dato. Or que= ſta imagine in queſto ſignifichera coſe vtili.","kind":"passage","sequence":131,"address":"3.131"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0132","text":"Sotto Paſiphe natura benefica.","kind":"passage","sequence":132,"address":"3.132"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0133","text":"Sotto i Talari, dar fauor, beneficio & aiuto","kind":"passage","sequence":133,"address":"3.133"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0134","text":"Saturno.","kind":"passage","sequence":134,"address":"3.134"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0135","text":"L’antro di Saturno coprirà ſette imagini. Cibele. Tre cap di Lupo di Leone & di cane. L’arca del patto. Proteo legato. Vn paſſer ſolitario. Pandora. Et vna fanciulla, à cui i capelli leuati verſo’l cielo ſtano tagliati. Cibele habbiamo hauuta nel conuiiuo, & ſignifica la te ra, & per la corona turrita ſignifica le città da lei ſoſten te. Queſta è tirata da due Leoni nel carro, percioche com","kind":"passage","sequence":135,"address":"3.135"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0136","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":136,"address":"3.136"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0137","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":137,"address":"3.137"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0138","text":"24","kind":"passage","sequence":138,"address":"3.138"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0139","text":"Il Leone è forte davanti & debile di dietro, coſì il Sol, onde i Leoni hanno coſtal natura è più poſſente nella parte da nanti ,che in quella di dietro. Di queſta ſ’è detto anche nel conuiuio, & qui, & ne Talari, & in Prometheo non vo-\nmitera fuoco, percioche ſignifichera puramente la Terra. Et ſotto l’Antro dinoterà la Terra in Generale, con tutte le ſue ſpeci trattate da Plinio, cio è dal capitolo, che fa, de Terrarum generibus, come creata, & erme. Poi ſignifichera Terra habitata, & non habitata, piana & montuoſa. La piana contera tutti luoghi aperti. La montuoſa baua le valli, le comalli, i colli, i monti, & ſuoi appartenẽ ti, come pietre, marmi, minere di metalli,& al minerali, et a queſte coſe ſi aggiũgerãno anche gli tri animali terreſtri.","kind":"passage","sequence":139,"address":"3.139"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0140","text":"Queſta imagine conterrà ſotto i Talari le operationi che puo far l’huomo naturalmente intorno alla Terra, pur che non concernano i piedi, i quali portano le ſue operationi ap preſſo ,ſi come gli altri membri. Ma ſotto Prometheo conterrà la Geometria, Geographia, Coſmographia,,& Agricultura, & le parti di lui impera ciochè queſta diſtingueremo in agricultura dintorno alla Terra,& intorno à frutti della Terra,d’ intorno à gli arbo ri,& intorno à frutti de gli arbori dintorno a gli animali,& intorno a frutti de gli animali,& in queſte ſei parti macceremo tutti gli ſcrittori della agricultura. E’ ſi dà q̃ ſta parte à Saturno p̄ eſſer freddo eſſecco,et p̄ eſſere il più immobile,eſſendo la terra di tal natura ſecondo il Triſmegisto. Le tre teſte di Lupo,di Leone et di Cane ſono tali .","kind":"passage","sequence":140,"address":"3.140"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0141","text":"Scriue Macrobio che li antichi volẽdo figurare i tre tempi,cio è il paſſato,il preſente,et il futuro,dipingevano le tre predette","kind":"passage","sequence":141,"address":"3.141"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0142","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":142,"address":"3.142"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0143","text":"ſtelle. Et quella del Lupo ſignifica il tempo paſſato , perciò cioche ha gia deuorato quella del Leone il preſente ( ſe il preſente dar ſi puo) percioche gli affanni preſenti ci ma-\ntono coſi ſatto errore, qual ci metterebbe la viſta d’un Leo ne ſe ci ſopraſſeſſe. Et quella del Cane ſignifica il tempo fu turo , percioche à guiſa di Cane adulatore il tempo futuro ci promette ſempre di meglio. Adunque queſta imagine cõ tenera queſti tre tempi Saturnini, & i loro appartenenti, percioche tutti quei tempi che non ſi comprendono per vicinanza , o lontananza del Sole , o ſono Saturnini o ſono Lu nari, Saturnini come queſti tre che habbiamo detti, i quali non ci ſi manifeſtano per lo corſo del Sole , come fa la notte & il giorno , le quattro ſtagioni, le hore , i minuti, & gli anni.","kind":"passage","sequence":143,"address":"3.143"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0144","text":"La lontananza adunque di queſto pianeta fa che queſti tre predetti tempi non li conoſciamo altramente ſe non per lo paſſato , per lo preſente, & per lo futuro. I Lunari veramente ſono ſotto l’antro della Luna, & ſotto i Ta lari di quella , & ſotto Prometheo coperti dalla imagine di Diana à cui Mercurio porge la veſta.","kind":"passage","sequence":144,"address":"3.144"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0145","text":"Tempi.","kind":"passage","sequence":145,"address":"3.145"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0146","text":"Saturni-\nni.","kind":"passage","sequence":146,"address":"3.146"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0147","text":"Solari.","kind":"passage","sequence":147,"address":"3.147"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0148","text":"Lunari.","kind":"passage","sequence":148,"address":"3.148"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0149","text":"La medesima imagine delle tre teſte ſotto Paſiphe ſignifichera l’huomo eſſer ſottopoſto al tempo. Et ſotto i Talari tutte le operationi d’intorno al tempo non conoſciute per lontananza , o vicinanza del Sole , ne per corſo lunare, come Indugiar, far indugiar, dar termine, ò rimettere in altro tempo.","kind":"passage","sequence":149,"address":"3.149"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0150","text":"L’area del patio quantunque nel ſuo alto miſterio ſignifichi i tre mondi che habbiamo dati à Pan , percioche era tale mente ſatta , che un cubito & mezo la miſuraua ſi per lungo , come per largo , Et ciaſcun cubito conſtando di","kind":"passage","sequence":150,"address":"3.150"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0151","text":"ſei palmi","kind":"passage","sequence":151,"address":"3.151"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0152","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":152,"address":"3.152"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0153","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO. 25","kind":"passage","sequence":153,"address":"3.153"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0154","text":"ſegne che noue palmi foſſe per lungo,& noue per trauerſo: il qual numero hauea da ſignificare i noue Cieli,& il deca-\ncimo era figurato per lo coperchio d’oro,ilquale non ſi ſten-\ndea ſe non ſopra la prima,& ſopra la ſeconda diuisione, & la terza rimaneua ſcoperta. Or queſta ſcoperta ſi come habbiamo ne miſteri reuelati ſignificaua queſto mondo inferiore eſpoſto à pioue,à uenti,à caldi,& à tutte le muta-\ntioni.","kind":"passage","sequence":154,"address":"3.154"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0155","text":"La ſeconda ſignificaua il celeſte mondo, & per tal cagion ne contenea vn Candelabro aureo con ſette Lucerne ſigni-\nficanti i ſette Pianeti,poi haueua vna Lucerna ſeparata con tre calami per lato,la quale anchora ſignificaua il Sole nel la ſua ſuperiorità.","kind":"passage","sequence":155,"address":"3.155"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","text":"Appreſſo vi erano alcuni vaſi,i quali ſignificauano il rice-\nuimento,il quale faceuano i pianeti da gli influssi ſopra celeſti. Et erano figure ſperiche,le quali ſignificauano i glo bi. Eranui anchora fiori,nello ſignification de quali giace il ſecreto di tutti i ſecreti che non è lecito à riuellar ſe non a tempo,& con la uolontà di Dio. La terza diuisione era chiamata propiciatorio fauorita da due Cherubini. L’vno de quali ſignificaua la natura diuina,& l’altro la humana in vn medeſimo Chriſto per loqual propiciatorio ſi faceua remiſſion de peccati,à ſignificare che per lo uenturo Chri ſto ſi haueua à far coſi fatta remiſſione. Et queſta diuisione terza ſignificaua il ſopraceleſte. Et chiamandoſi la parte di mezzo ſancti, queſta terza chiamaua ſancti ſanctorum, ſi come à ſchior Cœli cœlo o per dir meglio,Cœli cœlorũ.","kind":"passage","sequence":156,"address":"3.156"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0157","text":"Perciò che gli Hebrei nō danno ſingulare à cieli,et di queſto mõ do ci fece mentione Giouanni quando diſſe. In mundo erat,","kind":"passage","sequence":157,"address":"3.157"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0158","text":"L’Idea del Theatro.    D","kind":"passage","sequence":158,"address":"3.158"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0159","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":159,"address":"3.159"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0160","text":"53","kind":"passage","sequence":160,"address":"3.160"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0161","text":"& mundus per ipſum factus eſt, et mundus eum non cognouit, ait, che dicendo in mōdo erat, inteſe del ſopraceleſte, & quando d.ſſe: Et mundus per ipſum factus eſt, ſignificò il te reſtre. Et in dire, Et mundus eum non cognouit, parlò del mō do inferiore.","kind":"passage","sequence":161,"address":"3.161"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0162","text":"Adunque anchor che per l’Arca ci vengano ſignificati (come habbiamo detto) i tre mondi, non dimeno per hauer nō gia affidata alla guardia di Pan le ſignificationi di quelli, vogliamo che ella habbia a coprire il volume appartenente al luogo, & a tutte le ſue differenze: et quello ci par di hauer ragioneuolmente ordinato: percioche contenendo l’arca tutti i tre i mondi, dà conſequentemente luogo a tutte le coſe. Et ſi come l’Arca per contenere tutte le coſe merita la conſeruation del luogo con tutte le ſue differenze: coſì hauendo ella ad eſſer data ad uno de ſette pianeti, non puo ad altri conuenire meglio che a Saturno, ilquale per la ſua ampiezza del circulo comprende tutti gli altri. Queſta ſolo i Talari ſignificherà i monumenti che puo far l’huomo in torno al luogo, come collocar coſe quà, & là.","kind":"passage","sequence":162,"address":"3.162"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","text":"Proteo legato a differenza del Proteo ſciolto ch’è nel Conuiſio Lunare, & qui è collocato da noi per quello che appreſſo ſi dirà. E benche queſta legatura poſſa eſſer magi ca, & naturale pura, nondimeno qui intendiamo della pura naturale. Diſſi magica, percio che la legatura che fa Ariſteo di Proteo per conſiglio di Cirene ſua madre appreſſo di Homero et di Virgilio, è legatura magica. Et qui habet aures audiendi audiat, percioche appartiene al ſecreto del quale habbiamo parlato di ſopra. Ma la legatura naturale, & de la quale ſotto queſta figura intendiamo, è tale quale dire:","kind":"passage","sequence":163,"address":"3.163"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0164","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.     26","kind":"passage","sequence":164,"address":"3.164"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","text":"mo. Lo Spirito di Chriſto è quello(come habbiamo anchor\n detto nel Conuiui[o])il quale diſcendendo da ſopra celeſti coſe: natione\n dall’vniuona con la virtù ſua tutti i cieli, & porta giu tutte delle coſe\n ſe le loro impreſſioni & tutte le loro virtù & con quelle ſi\n ferma qua giù fra animali,herbe,& fiori.& ſe coſi non ſi\n rinouaſſe le coſe,tutte perirebbono. Et queſta è perauentura\n quella città,che Giouanni vide nell’Apocaliſſi ſanta diſce-\n dente piena di gioie : & per queſto Dauid canta il Cantico\n nuouo,vedendo tante coſe rinouate:et Eſaia dice,Creabo cœ-\n lum nouum,& terram nouam : & nell’Apocal. à,chora è\n ſcritto.Ecce noua facio omnia:& queſta è la ſcala di Iacob\n per la quale diſcendono & aſcendono gli ſpiriti,che lo ſce-\n dere è lo venir a far queſta rinouatione,& lo aſcendere è il\n tornare dello ſpirito a rifocillarſi co’l ſuperiore vniuerſale.","kind":"passage","sequence":165,"address":"3.165"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0166","text":"Ma di queſta rinouatione volendo far mentione il Petrarca\n come colui che non paſſaua il celeſte mondo fece quel Sonet-\n to,il qual comincia.","kind":"passage","sequence":166,"address":"3.166"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167","text":"Quando il Pianeta,che diſtingue. l’hore\n Ad albergar col Tauro ſi ritorna. doue dicendo.\n Cade virtù dalle celeſti come\n Che veſte il mondo di nouel colore,vien à dare a cieli que-\n ſta operatione di tornar a far bello il mondo,non intenden-\n do che l’anima del mondo piena di vinificante ſpirito che è\n Chriſto portata dal Sole giù dal concauo della Luna con\n maggior abondanza & fecondità quando il Sole comincia\n a girar ſopra di noi,che quando a più lontano,ſoprauiene a\n la miſſion,che vuol far la natura volendo far la production\n delle herbe,de fiori,& delle altre coſe elementate. Et ſe e non\n interueniffe come mediatore a conciliar le qualità contrarie","kind":"passage","sequence":167,"address":"3.167"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0168","text":"D  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":168,"address":"3.168"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0169","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":169,"address":"3.169"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0170","text":"33","kind":"passage","sequence":170,"address":"3.170"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","text":"ne, che ſanno il miſto, le loro contrarietà non potrebbon mai ſtare in ſieme ſotto la forma di queſta o di quella herba, di quella o di quel fiore. Tale è adunque la temperan za del diuino ſpirito di Chriſto, che accorda anchora i diſ-\nſcordanti. Et è quello che dice il Propheta. Ego cælum & terram impleo, & altrove dice la Scrittura, pleni ſunt cœ li & terra gloria tua. Queſto adunque ſpirito di Chriſto, & non dell’ anima del mondo ( come dicono i Platonici) è non ſolamente mediatore, conciliatore, vinificatore, & ſoſtenito-\nre di: queſti quattro diſcordi elementi, ma moſſo dalla ſua miſericordia, è anchor mediatore & conciliatore fra la diuina giuſtitia, & la humana fragilità. Et che queſto vera mente ſia lo ſpirito vinificante tutte le coſe, habbiamo dal ſalmo. Avertente te faciem tuam turbabuntur, & omnia in pulverem reuertentur. Et, Emitte ſpiritum tuum & renouabis faciem terræ.","kind":"passage","sequence":171,"address":"3.171"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","text":"Chiamandolo adunque ſpiritum tu um, moſtra queſto eſſere ſpirito di Dio, & non dell’ anima del mondo. Et Paolo lo chiama ſpirito vinificante. Sopraſ-\nvenendo adunque la materia prima, cio è Proteo pieno di que ſto ſpirito vinificante, alla miſtion delle herbe, & de fiori, & de gli altri miſti, ſta naturalmente tanto legato dentro da termini di queſto fiore, o di quella herba, per fin che ſi vengano à diſſoluere. Et qui è da notare vn detto di Mer curio Triſmegiſto nell’ Aſclepio. Quis quid de alto deſcen-\ndit generans eſt, quod ſurſum verſus emanat nutriens, ideſt preſtans vitam, hoc eſt vinificans. Scendendo adunque que ſto ſpirito ſoprauueniente alla miſtione, che vorrebbe far la na tura meſcolandoſi con quelli che ſarebbono ſtati diſcordi, e gli concilia & genera. Et mentre la pianta, o l’animal crea","kind":"passage","sequence":172,"address":"3.172"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0173","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":173,"address":"3.173"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0174","text":"27","kind":"passage","sequence":174,"address":"3.174"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","text":"ſee, lo nutriſce & vniſca. Sta adunque ſeparato in qualun que individuo per fin che uenga: il tempo della diſſolutione ne chiamata indegnamente morte ſecondo Mercurio, il qual coſì ſcriue nel Pimandro al xii. Capo. Non moritur in mun do quicquam , ſed compoſita corporea diſſoluuntur: Diſſolu tio mors non eſt , ſed miſtionis reſolutio quædam , ſoluitur autem vnio non vt ea quæ ſunt intereant, ſed vt vetera in neſcant: Per quanto tempo adunque la vnion de miſti ſta in ſieme, per tanto riman legata, & fermata, et riſtretta quel la parte di Proteo con quello ſpirito inchiuſo. Et per tal ca gione vogliamo che queſta imagine habbia à conſertar ſol to di ſe coſe immobili , fermate , o ferme.","kind":"passage","sequence":175,"address":"3.175"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0176","text":"Sotto Paſiphe ſignificherà natura oſtinata & immutabi\nle.","kind":"passage","sequence":176,"address":"3.176"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0177","text":"Et ſotto i Talari ſar coſa alcuna immobile , come ferma-\nre, arreſtare.","kind":"passage","sequence":177,"address":"3.177"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0178","text":"Et quella imagine à Saturno vien data per la ſua tar-\ndità.","kind":"passage","sequence":178,"address":"3.178"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0179","text":"Il Paſſer ſolitario aſſai per ſe ſenza altra dichiara­tione mo ſtra hauere à contener coſa ſola o abbandonata.","kind":"passage","sequence":179,"address":"3.179"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0180","text":"Sotto Paſiphe ſignificherà natura ſolitaria, & huomo ſo\nlo, & abbandonato.","kind":"passage","sequence":180,"address":"3.180"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0181","text":"Ma ſotto i Talari ſignificherà andar ſolo, ſtar ſolo, abo bandonare & laſciar perſona o luogo , o coſa.","kind":"passage","sequence":181,"address":"3.181"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0182","text":"Et quella imagine a Saturno ſi conuiene , come à natura Pandora nell’Antro ſignifica afflittion di coſe.","kind":"passage","sequence":182,"address":"3.182"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0183","text":"Sotto Paſiphe afflittion dell’huomo , & tutte le ſue male fortune infelicità , ignobilità , pouertà , infirmità, & il non ottener deſiderio.","kind":"passage","sequence":183,"address":"3.183"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0184","text":"D  iii.","kind":"passage","sequence":184,"address":"3.184"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0185","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO, 38","kind":"passage","sequence":185,"address":"3.185"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0186","text":"Sotto i Talari dar afflittione altrui. La imagine de capelli tagliati alla fanciulla, i quali vede-\nmo in Marte diſteſi verſo il cielo, porterà tutte le coſe oppo-\nſte, ciò è deboli. Ne ciò habbiamo fatto ſenza autorità, ma percioche Alceſte appreſſo Euripide non potendo morir della deſiderata morte, il mandato Mercurio le taglia il capello, & ella ſi muore: & Niſo non fu da Minos abbattuto ſe non poi che la Scilla innamorata gli tagliò il fatato capello. Ne Dido appreſſo Virgilio puo finir di morire, ſe non dapoi che Iris mandata da Giunone le ha tagliato il capello: & il conſiglio di Virgilio è, che Iris per ſignificar co colori gli elementi, ſignifichi gli elementati. Et il tagliare il capello ſia diſſolution di elementi. I quali miſteri da Poeti ſono ſtati robbati a Propheti, come da quel luogo de capelli tagliati a Sanſone.","kind":"passage","sequence":186,"address":"3.186"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0187","text":"Questa imagine ſotto Paſiphe ſignificherà debilità dello huomo, ſtanchezza, natura falſa & buggiarda. Ma ſotto i Talari ſignificherà debilitar perſona, o coſa, o mentire.","kind":"passage","sequence":187,"address":"3.187"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0188","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":188,"address":"3.188"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0189","text":"DI M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":189,"address":"3.189"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0190","text":"28","kind":"passage","sequence":190,"address":"3.190"}],"sha256":"5a8ca9af311cfec4d27db1503a7e5044ff4b06e5e0780d1ada1a732633fdb606","language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261030T230430229628Z_bc0460d8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE CAVE.","source_sha256":"5a8ca9af311cfec4d27db1503a7e5044ff4b06e5e0780d1ada1a732633fdb606","sha256":"8930b10a4d19c728a348df652fc246bce3c8e799f360d2a2298e8764d8cca1b8","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:04:30.229691+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0001","text":"THE CAVE.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"3.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","text":"The Third Grade shall have, painted for each of its doors, a Cave, which we shall call the Homeric Cave, in distinction from that which Plato describes in his Republic. Homer, therefore, imagines above the harbour of Ithaca a cave in which certain Nymphs weave purple cloths, and imagines bees which go forth and return to make their honey; which weavings and makings signifying mixed and elemental things, we intend that each of the seven caves, according to the nature of its Planet, shall preserve the mixed and elemental things belonging to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"3.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","text":"And in order to have some information concerning mixed and elemental things, I say that, according to the distinction set forth by Moses, after Elohim on the first day created prime matter in order to make Heaven and earth, because the whole influx of the supercelestial streams did not suit matter, on the second day He formed the Rachia, that is, the mass of the heavens, and not the firmament, as we have also said, since that is only the eighth sphere; and He placed the said mass, extended between the supercelestial world and the lower one, so that it might divide the waters of the supercelestial streams, which do not wet, from the waters of this world, which do wet, concerning which supercelestial waters it is written: Benedicite aquae omnes, quæ super cœlos sunt domino. And thus the said celestial mass was interposed and extended, so that there should not rain down a greater influx of the higher waters than was suited to the capacity of matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"3.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0004","text":"And concerning these waters it must be noted that Gregory Nazianzen errs, understanding by that","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"3.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0005","text":"The days\nat the crea-\ntion of the\nworld.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"3.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0006","text":"The super-\ncelestial\nwaters.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"3.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0007","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"3.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0008","text":"16","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"3.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0009","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"3.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0010","text":"the crystalline heaven, which has merely been imagined by some above the firmament, but they have neither reason nor foundation for it, whether in sacred or in profane scripture. On the third day Moses says that Elohim commanded that the waters which are beneath heaven should be gathered together in one place—that is, all the generative powers together—and that the dry earth should appear forth, so that by means of the said generative powers, gathered together, it might put forth offspring; which having been done, He said: Produca terra herbam virentem, & lignum (se dir si potesse) seminiferum. On the fourth day the Luminaries were made and placed in the mass of the Heavens: the Moon in the first sphere and the Sun in the fourth Sphere, by means of which light was to be distinguished from darkness—that is, things which had already received form from those which were not yet informed.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"3.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","text":"On the fifth day he speaks of the communication of life to all animals, for he wills that the waters—that is, the generative powers—should produce all the diversities of animals, aquatic as well as flying and terrestrial here below, in distinction from those above. On the sixth day he produced man, and on the seventh he rested. Thus, after prime matter, we do not see that God created new matter; rather, from the first He formed all things which we call mixed and elemental. And these we are to find in the third grade of the seven columns, beneath the door of the Cave, except for man, who, having been separately formed and made lord of mixed and elemental things, we intend shall have a particular grade, as shall later be seen. Beneath the door of the Lunar Cave, therefore, we shall find five images: Neptune, Daphne, Diana, to whom Mercury offers the mass, the stables of Augeas, and Juno among the clouds.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"3.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0012","text":"Nor should anyone marvel that Neptune, whose being beneath","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"3.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0013","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"3.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","text":"the Common is seen again beneath the Cave, beneath the Talaria, and beneath Prometheus; which will also occur with other images both in this and in other little planets, since Homer too says that Ulysses had seen Hercules both among the gods in Heaven and in hell. And if this is not unfitting for him, it ought still less to be unfitting for us, who, in order not to burden the memory with diverse images for the same things, cause the same figure to be seen again beneath diverse doors. Proteus shall signify form, already supervening upon a subject and natural thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"3.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","text":"Neptune, therefore, beneath the Common signifies the most simple element of water; but beneath the Cave he shall signify it already mixed, since in this world we see no element so pure that it is not mixed, as Anaxagoras has long demonstrated and maintained. Beneath the image of this Neptune, therefore, shall be contained the volume in which water in general and water in particular shall be arranged distinctly by divisions; and water in general shall be divided into its whole and its parts: the whole is, as one might say, water simply; its parts, such as a drop. There shall also be the qualities and quantities of waters: the qualities, such as sweet and salt, and sweet waters standing and running; and the other accidents.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"3.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016","text":"And, in addition, lakes, banks, and other things belonging thereto; and also aquatic animals; and beneath this Neptune man is not yet included, since he was the last of the animals created. But when we find Neptune beneath the Talaria, since these signify the operation which man can perform concerning every thing created before him naturally and apart from art, we intend that he shall have in his","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"3.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0017","text":"Canon","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"3.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0018","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"3.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0019","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  17","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"3.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0020","text":"Canon human and natural operations concerning waters, as is also said in what follows.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"3.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","text":"And beneath Prometheus it shall show us the arts concerning waters. Daphne, who is transformed into a laurel, shall be a symbol of the wood. And here shall be contained what Theophrastus or other writers have ever written de plantis, together with their consequences, which are shadows.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"3.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","text":"But beneath the Talaria Daphne shall signify natural operations concerning timber, such as bending and carrying. And beneath Prometheus it shall contain gardens, and all the arts concerning timber.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"3.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0023","text":"Daphne indeed—that is, the wood—is well assigned to the Moon, that is, to Diana, goddess of woods, since she is queen (as we have said) of humidities, without which no plant would grow. Whence Virgil in the fourth book of the Georgics:","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"3.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0024","text":"And Ocean, father of things, and the sister Nymphs,\nA hundred who guard the woods, a hundred who guard the rivers.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"3.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","text":"Diana, to whom Mercury offers the garment, is the third image. It is read among the Greek fables that, seeing Diana go naked, although she was chaste, Jove did not like it, and charged Mercury to make her a garment. And however much he made her one, there was never any that could suit her. This fiction gives us a symbol signifying change and its species, that is, generation, corruption, increase, diminution, alteration, change according to place, and motion, with all the species recounted by Aristotle and distinguished by his divisions. This image under Pasiphaë will signify the change of man, either according to opinion or according to the transfigura","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"3.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0026","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.     C","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"3.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0027","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"3.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0028","text":"tion of the body.          And under the Talaria it will signify to move, or to change a thing, to receive, to dispose, an operation done rosso or suddenly.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"3.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0029","text":"But under Prometheus it will contain the months, and their parts. The Stables of Augeas are so called by the Greeks, because Augeas was a King very rich in possessions and fields, but the great abundance of beasts that he kept so encumbered his country with dung that it corrupted the fertility of the fields. Therefore under this image we shall place a volume which will comprehend the filthinesses of the things of the world, moulds, rottennesses, vilenesses, imperfections, and similar unpleasant things.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"3.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0030","text":"This same image under Pasiphaë will contain the filthinesses of the human body and its excrements, such as those of the ears, the nose, the nails, the eyes, sweat, spit, vomit, menstruation, urine, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"3.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0031","text":"But under the Talaria it will signify filthy operations, to befoul, to stain, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"3.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0032","text":"And these Stables are given to the Moon, because there is no filthiness save from corrupted moisture.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"3.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","text":"Gimnon among the clouds: Gimnon signifies the air, and this covering of clouds will give us the signification of things hidden in nature, and of those which by the Peripatetics are called knowable, but which are not yet known; and it will also signify brief time; and these things are given to the Moon, because we have no Planet which hides itself from us in a briefer time.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"3.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0034","text":"This image under Pasiphaë will signify the hiding\nthat man can make of himself.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"3.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0035","text":"But under the Talaria it will denote a man hiding a thing or another person.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"3.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0036","text":"Under Mercury there will be six images. The metal of Gold, the","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"3.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0037","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"3.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0038","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"3.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0039","text":"18","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"3.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0040","text":"Atoms, the Pyramid, the Gordian knot entangled, the same one disentangled, Juno feigned of clouds. The Golden Fleece, although in mystical Philosophy it has the signification of the highest gift which the Lord God is wont to give to few of His elect, and although it has great signification through such an abduction—the gathering of the Heroes, the first ship, and the loss made by Jason of his shoe in the river, solely in the manner without wind—whence perhaps is drawn the Order of the Fleece, which agrees with the magic of Zoroaster, which was the first thing that ought to be taught to the new prince of the Persians, so that he should not be a Tyrant.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"3.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0041","text":"Nevertheless, drawing this golden skin down from the height of its mystery to the lowness of our need, it will serve us as an image of all the objects that pertain to the judgment of weight, or of touch, such as heavy and light, rough, soft, hard, tender, and the like; it is understood, nevertheless, of those things which are outside man.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"3.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0042","text":"This same image under Pasiphaë will signify the same things in the human body.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"3.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0043","text":"And under the Talaria it will signify the operation without art of making hard, soft, rough.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"3.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0044","text":"And this image with such a signification is given to Mercury, because the hands which chiefly make these judgments are of Gemini, which is a thing of Mercury.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"3.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0045","text":"The Atoms will signify for us all discrete quantity in things.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"3.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0046","text":"And under Pasiphaë they will signify the same in men, as someone.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"3.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0047","text":"C  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"3.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0048","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"3.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0049","text":"13","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"3.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0050","text":"But under the Talaria they will signify discrete quantity standing apart from man without art, as to break a thing into pieces with a file, to dissolve and scatter.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"3.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0051","text":"And because this is the subject of Arithmetic, which is the science of Mercury, this image is assigned to him.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"3.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0052","text":"The Pyramid signifies continuous quantity in things. Under Pasiphaë, in men, such as great, small, middling.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"3.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0053","text":"Under the Talaria it signifies operation without art, such as raising,\nlowering, thickening, thinning.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"3.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0054","text":"Which two quantities, one being of Arithmetic and the other of Geometry, sciences pertaining to Hercules drawing the three-pointed arrow, shall under that image be comprised under Prometheus.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"3.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0055","text":"The entangled Gordian Knot was brought to Alexander to be explained, and he, impatient, cut it. Under this shall be contained entangled continuous quantity, such as a thread, or a band.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"3.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0056","text":"And under the Talaria it shall signify the entangling of things. The same Knot, explained, shall denote an explained continuous thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"3.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0057","text":"And under the Talaria, the explanation of intricate things. Juno feigned of clouds and drawn from the fable, who, having\nbeen solicited to adultery by Ixion, presented him with a body of clouds that resembled her, and with that he lay. Now by this beast made for him from that feigned thing, under this figure shall be contained things appearing but not true.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"3.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0058","text":"Under Pasiphaë it shall denote a dissembling and cunning nature, and","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"3.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0059","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  19","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"3.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0060","text":"fraudulent.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"3.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0061","text":"And under the Talaria, to feign and deceive. And we assign this image to Mercury, because he is the author of\nmalices.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"3.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0062","text":"Under the Grotto of Venus are five images: Cerberus, a Venus, a maiden who bears upon her head a vessel of perfumes, Hercules cleansing the stables of Augeas, Narcissus, and Tantalus beneath the stone. Cerberus has been painted with three heads to signify the three natural necessities, which are eating, drinking, and sleeping; which, because they greatly hinder man from specula-\ntion, Virgil feigns that Aeneas, by the counsel of the Sibyl, wishing to pass to the contemplation of high things, throws him a morsel, and immediately passes. Which signifies that, although we must satisfy these three necessities, we must satisfy them with little, if we wish to have time to contemplate.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"3.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","text":"This image therefore, beneath the grotto, shall contain things pertaining to hunger, thirst, and sleep: victuals, beverages, and things that induce sleep. And this figure is assigned to Venus because of delight.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"3.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","text":"Under Pasiphaë it shall signify hunger, thirst, and sleep, and their consequences. Under the Talaria, eating, drinking, and sleeping, and consequent natural operations. Then under Prometheus it shall signify the kitchen, deli-\ncious banquets, and delights suited to sleep, such as sounds and songs. The maiden bearing upon her head the vessel of perfumes, which was found in Rome, in the other shall signify all odours. And","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"3.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0065","text":"C  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"3.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0066","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"3.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0067","text":"because the vessel is of Venus, it is assigned to her. Under the Talaria it signifies our operations concerning odours without art, such as smelling and carrying odours. But under Prometheus it con-\ntains the arts pertaining to odours and to perfumers.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"3.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0068","text":"Hercules cleansing the stables of Augeas is introduced because the fables say that that King, finding himself oppressed by the great filth, called Hercules to remove it; and here he shall signify things clean by nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"3.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0069","text":"Under Pasiphaë it shall signify the cleanliness of the human body. Under the Talaria, cleansing without art. And under Prometheus, baths and barber-shops. And this figure befits Venus for comeliness and delicacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"3.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0070","text":"Narcissus looked at himself in the transitory water of this world, and signifies mortal beauty, whose truth, for one who wishes to find it, requires ascending to the supracelestial Tiseret, where the Platonist Hippia ought to seek it; and all of us likewise, because there it is fixed and immortal. Now under this image we shall have the beauty that appears to us in this world in natural and desirable things. This figure under Pasiphaë shall signify human beauty and its consequences: Softness, Comeliness, Delight, Design, Love, Hope, lovers, and being loved.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"3.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0071","text":"Under the Talaria it shall signify making beautiful, making fall in love, making desire, making hope, etc. And under Prometheus it shall contain the art of cosmetics and of beautifying. Tantalus beneath the stone signifies things wavering, or trembling, or that stand in suspense. Under Pasiphaë it shall denote a timid, sus-\npicious, doubtful, and wonder-struck nature. And under the Talaria there shall","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"3.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0072","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"3.72","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0073","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"3.73","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0074","text":"20","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"3.74","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0075","text":"to stand, to make tremble, to make doubt, to make waver, to make seasick, [illegible]gle, etc. Beneath the Cave of the Sun are five images: the Sun, Argus alone; the Cow watched by Argus; Geryon slain by Hercules; a Cock and a Lion; and Apollo shooting Juno.","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"3.75","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0076","text":"Argus alone, full of eyes, signifies this whole world, whose head is the Heavens, and whose eyes are the stars, by means of which it thus makes the lower things known, so that they may come forth into the appearance of generation from afar, as the ostrich does its eggs, giving them the life of that spirit which is in its wheels. Of this Ezekiel speaks thus: Et spiritus erat in rotis. Although this keeps all the elements alive, it nevertheless favors fire more than air, and air more than water, and water more than earth. But if this earth, which is less favored, through the life and fecundity bestowed upon it by this spirit, brings forth all the many varieties of things that the other elements ought to produce—whose fecundity, invisible to us, also favors the earth—Mercury in the Pimander says that the earth is by no means immovable, but rather is stirred by many movements.","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"3.76","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0077","text":"And yet, in comparison with the other Elements, it is almost stable; and he adds that one must not believe that it, which is the nurse of all things, lacks movement, because it is impossible that it can bring forth without movement. And just as the stars are the eyes of this world, so trees, which through their fertility receive much of the said vital spirit, are like the hairs and locks of its body, and metals and stones are like bones. It is not therefore a wonder that symbolic Theologians have figured the world under the symbol of Argus full of eyes, because the world lives. This image, therefore.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"3.77","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0078","text":"The earth","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"3.78","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0079","text":"C  iiii","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"3.79","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0080","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"3.80","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0081","text":"The whole world shall be represented in universal terms, and in particular the celestial mass and the celestial bodies.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"3.81","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0081"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0082","text":"The Cow watched by Argus, although it may signify the earth, shall nevertheless signify for us all visible things and all colors.","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"3.82","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0082"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0083","text":"Geryon, whose three heads Hercules cuts off, signifies the beginning, the continuance, and the decline of the time belonging to the Sun. And this image shall signify for us not only the ages of the world, but also the four seasons, which are made by the Sun’s approach and recession, and likewise day and night with their parts.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"3.83","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0083"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0084","text":"And beneath Pasiphaë it shall signify the age of man.","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"3.84","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0084"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0085","text":"Beneath the Talaria, natural operations concerning minutes, hours,\nthe year, age, and the clock.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"3.85","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0085"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0086","text":"And beneath Prometheus, artificial years, minutes, hours, clocks,\nand instruments of time.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"3.86","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0086"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0087","text":"The Cock with the Lion. Not only does Pliny disclose this signification, but Iamblichus the Platonist also, and Lucretius, say that although both these animals are solar, nevertheless the Cock bears in its eyes some degree more excellent than that of the Sun, at which the Lion, looking, humbles himself. And it happened to the author of this Theatre that, finding himself in Paris in the place called the Tournelle, with many gentlemen in a hall at certain windows looking out over a garden, a Lion that had escaped from prison came into that hall, and approaching him from behind, seized him without harm by the thighs with its paws, and went about licking him with its tongue. And he, having turned at that touch and at that breath, and having that animal","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"3.87","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0087"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0088","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"3.88","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0088"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0089","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"3.89","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0089"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0090","text":"31","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"3.90","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0090"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0091","text":"seen it, while all the others had fled, some here and some there, the Lion humbled himself before him, as though in the act of asking mercy. Which must not be said to have happened for any other reason than that that animal perceived much of solar virtue to be in him. This image, therefore, shall contain the excellence of natural things by comparison.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"3.91","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0091"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0092","text":"Beneath Pasiphaë it shall signify the excellence of man, superiority, dignity, authority, and dominion in a thing worthy of honor.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"3.92","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0092"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0093","text":"Beneath the Talaria it shall signify making superior, conferring dignity, and\nrank.","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"3.93","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0093"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0094","text":"But beneath Prometheus it shall contain principalities and kingdoms—\nwhich have all been regulated by writers with precepts; would that they were well observed.","kind":"passage","sequence":94,"address":"3.94","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0094"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","text":"Apollo shooting Juno among the clouds is an image opposed to Juno hidden among the clouds, which is from Hesiod. And although Homer introduces this fable, it is not therefore to be believed that he wishes to introduce war among the Gods, as Socrates indicates in the Meno, but he signifies manifest things.","kind":"passage","sequence":95,"address":"3.95","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0096","text":"And beneath Pasiphaë it signifies man revealing himself, and coming\nto light.","kind":"passage","sequence":96,"address":"3.96","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0096"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0097","text":"But beneath the Buskins, to reveal person or thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":97,"address":"3.97","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0097"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0098","text":"Beneath the Cave of Mars are four images: Vulcan, Mars; a maiden whose hair stands raised toward Heaven; two serpents that fight; and Mars upon a Dra-\ngon.","kind":"passage","sequence":98,"address":"3.98","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0098"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0099","text":"Vulcan bears with him so much the signification of fire that he has no need of explanation. And because fire is divided into three kinds, since its most subtle part","kind":"passage","sequence":99,"address":"3.99","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0099"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0100","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 13]","kind":"passage","sequence":100,"address":"3.100","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0100"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0101","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":101,"address":"3.101","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0101"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0102","text":"precisely fills the concavity of the Moon, it has also obtained from the Latins to be called air. Whence Cicero, De natura Deorum 44: A Ether qui constat ex altissimis ignibus me tuemur hoc quoque verbum, dicaturque tam ether latine, quàm dicitur aer. And although on account of this passage some would associate it with the air that is beneath the Cave of jewels, nevertheless, considering its nature, it follows that it is also superior to fire; we wish it rather to be of fire than of air. And so much the more because Cicero says in the same [work] at 34: Ardor cæli qui æther, vel cælum nominatur. And at 37: Tenuis ac perlucens, & æquabili calore suffusus æther. Elemental fire will follow this, and in the third place our fire shall be placed.","kind":"passage","sequence":102,"address":"3.102","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0102"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0103","text":"And since this image is also in the Banquet, and beneath other gates thereof we have spoken more fully of it in the Banquet, here it will suffice us to say again that Vulcan in this place shall signify the ether, elemental fire together with the universal conflagration, and thereafter our fire together with the particular conflagration, the spark, the flame, the coal, and the ash. And this image, with the things contained by it, cannot suit another planet than Mars, because Mars alone is hot and dry, as fire is, whereas the Sun is hot and moist. The maiden with hair raised toward Heaven is thus fashioned, giving us to understand that man, according to Plato, is an inverted tree: for the tree has its roots downward, and man has them upward.","kind":"passage","sequence":103,"address":"3.103","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0103"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0104","text":"And Origen and Jerome, his follower, hold that when Scripture makes mention of hair or beard, one should not understand hair or beard of the body, but of the soul, which metaphorically has hair and beard and eyes and other parts","kind":"passage","sequence":104,"address":"3.104","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0104"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0105","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":105,"address":"3.105","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0105"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0106","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":106,"address":"3.106","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0106"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0107","text":"22","kind":"passage","sequence":107,"address":"3.107","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0107"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0108","text":"corresponding to the body. And because, if one were to expose oneself naked to the night air, the hair and beard would show more plainly the humour contracted from Heaven than any other part of the body, they hold that, just as the tree through its roots draws to itself the nutritive humour from the earth, so the beard and hair of our inner man draw the dew, that is, the life-giving humour, from the influences through supracelestial channels, whence all his vigour follows. And of this it is that one reads in the Calistica: Come tuæ iustitiæ canalibus, understanding supracelestial rivulets, which sentence bears the signification that that soul was full of supracelestial vigour. And in the psalm one reads of Aaron's dewy beard: this same meaning. Therefore this image shall cover the volume pertaining to the vigour that a thing can have in this world. And it shall signify a vigorous or strong or worthy thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":108,"address":"3.108","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0108"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0109","text":"And we place truth in this place as that of which it was confessed by Darius's sages that it had power over all other things. Beneath Pasiphaë this image shall signify a vigour-\nous, strong, and true nature. And beneath the Buskins, to give vigour or strength, or to bring about a return to truth. And it is to be noted that Geburà is truth, and that it is explained by that way.","kind":"passage","sequence":109,"address":"3.109","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0109"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0110","text":"Mercy and Truth have met\none another. Justice and peace have kissed.","kind":"passage","sequence":110,"address":"3.110","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0110"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0111","text":"Psalm.\n84.","kind":"passage","sequence":111,"address":"3.111","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0111"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0112","text":"The two fighting Serpents represent for us that fable which is read of Mercury, who comes upon two serpents that were fighting; beneath which image we shall place the dissonance, the difference, and the diversity of things. And beneath Pasiphaë such an image shall signify nature with","kind":"passage","sequence":112,"address":"3.112","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0112"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0113","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":113,"address":"3.113","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0113"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","text":"contention. And beneath the Buskins, to contend. And beneath Prometheus, the military art, and terrestrial and maritime war and their appurtenances. Mars upon the Dragon is imagined by us for this reason. We have said that the Planets seek their natures and influences from the corresponding supracelestial Sephiroth; and because the Geburà, which gives influence to Mars, has above it an angelic [being] called Zamael, which signifies the poison of God, because by means of this God chastises the world; and because the Cabalists say that such an intelligence has the figure of a Dragon, we place Mars riding it; and to this image we shall assign a volume containing harmful and poi-\nsonous natural things.","kind":"passage","sequence":114,"address":"3.114","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0115","text":"And beneath Pasiphaë it shall signify a harmful, cruel, and\nvengeful nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":115,"address":"3.115","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0115"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0116","text":"And beneath the Buskins, to harm, to become cruel, to take vengeance, to impede","kind":"passage","sequence":116,"address":"3.116","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0116"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0117","text":"Juno.","kind":"passage","sequence":117,"address":"3.117","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0117"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0118","text":"The cave of Juno shall contain five images: Juno suspen-\nded; the two Holes of the Lyre; the Caduceus, upon which it rains; Gold in the lap; and the three Graces.","kind":"passage","sequence":118,"address":"3.118","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0118"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0119","text":"Juno suspended is also in the Banquet of Juno, where she signifies simple air; and here she shall signify the four elements in general, and air in particular, which, being divided into three regions, in the lowest we shall place dew, frost, morning light, cold, coolness, heat, and mist. In the second, clouds, winds, thunders, lightnings, thunderbolts, rain, hail, and snow. In the third and highest, comets, shooting fires, and falling stars in appearance.","kind":"passage","sequence":119,"address":"3.119","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0119"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0120","text":"This shall also be beneath the Buskins and beneath Prometheus, with-","kind":"passage","sequence":120,"address":"3.120","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0120"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0121","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":121,"address":"3.121","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0121"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0122","text":"23","kind":"passage","sequence":122,"address":"3.122","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0122"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0123","text":"as is said in the Convivio. We have made the two holes of the Lyre out of necessity, but for this reason: that nature, having made the ears in animals, and principally in man, with winding passages adapted to receive the air struck by some sound—for it twists itself like water struck by a stone—and nature, in order to receive it, keeps a likewise winding place prepared for it; this beaten air, having entered the animal’s ear, strikes that air within which we call connatural; and the connatural air, once struck, strikes certain nerves within, through which the animal hears. Thus the ancient makers of the Lyre, for convenience in touching its nerves, made those on the outside, but the holes in imitation principally of the ears of man. Wherefore this image will have the volume containing all audible things, and every natural noise and sound.","kind":"passage","sequence":123,"address":"3.123","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0123"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0124","text":"This image beneath the Sandals signifies making a noise, and pertains more to Jupiter than to any other Planet, because he is lord of the air, without which sound cannot be made.","kind":"passage","sequence":124,"address":"3.124","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0124"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0125","text":"The Caduceus is Mercury’s rod, which he placed (as the fables say) between the two serpents which he found fighting, as has been said under Mars; and they entwined themselves around it in perpetual union: and this image will show us things uniform, the same, not different, and equivalent,","kind":"passage","sequence":125,"address":"3.125","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0125"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0126","text":"Under Pasiphaë it will contain a friendly nature inclined to the care of the household and of the republic. And under the Sandals, friendship, or intercourse in practice. Under Prometheus, the city and household care, which is divided into father of the household, mother of the household, children, and servants.","kind":"passage","sequence":126,"address":"3.126","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0126"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0127","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":127,"address":"3.127","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0127"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0128","text":"Danaë with the shower of gold, although in the other mysteries it signifies the same thing as the Golden Fleece and the gardens of the Hesperides, will here signify for us good fortune, fullness, and abundance of things, since every plenitude and every good thing comes from above.","kind":"passage","sequence":128,"address":"3.128","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0128"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0129","text":"Under Pasiphaë it will denote good fortune, felicity, nobility, riches, health, glory, the attainment of desire.","kind":"passage","sequence":129,"address":"3.129","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0129"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0130","text":"Under the Sandals, operation concerning good fortune and\nthe things said above.","kind":"passage","sequence":130,"address":"3.130","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0130"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0131","text":"The three Graces were painted by the ancients in such a way that one kept her face hidden, and this signified the benefit of the giver, which ought not to be disclosed by him who gives it. And Jesus Christ says: Cum facis elemoſynam noli tuba canere ante te. And elsewhere: Nesciat sinistra tua quid faciat dextera tua. The other showed all of it, and signifies the receiver of the benefit, to whom it belongs to show the face, that is, to disclose the grace received. The third partly conceals it and partly shows it, and signifies the recompensed benefit, showing what was received and concealing what was given. Now this image in this place will signify useful things.","kind":"passage","sequence":131,"address":"3.131","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0131"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0132","text":"Under Pasiphaë, beneficent nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":132,"address":"3.132","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0132"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0133","text":"Under the Sandals, to grant favour, benefit, and aid","kind":"passage","sequence":133,"address":"3.133","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0133"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0134","text":"Saturn.","kind":"passage","sequence":134,"address":"3.134","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0134"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0135","text":"Saturn’s cave will cover seven images. Cybele. Three heads of Wolf, Lion, and Dog. The ark of the covenant. Proteus bound. A solitary sparrow. Pandora. And a maiden whose hair, raised toward heaven, is cut. We have had Cybele in the banquet, and she signifies the earth; and by the turreted crown she signifies the cities sustained by her. She is drawn in a chariot by two Lions, because as","kind":"passage","sequence":135,"address":"3.135","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0135"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0136","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":136,"address":"3.136","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0136"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0137","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":137,"address":"3.137","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0137"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0138","text":"24","kind":"passage","sequence":138,"address":"3.138","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0138"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0139","text":"The Lion is strong in front and weak behind; so too is the Sun, whence Lions have this nature: they are more powerful in the part in front than in that behind. This has also been said in the banquet, and here, and under the Sandals, and under Prometheus it will not vomit fire, because it will signify purely the Earth. And beneath the Cave it will denote the Earth in general, with all its species treated by Pliny, that is, from the chapter he makes De Terrarum generibus, as created and desert. Then it will signify inhabited and uninhabited Earth, level and mountainous. The level will contain all open places. The mountainous will embrace valleys, hollows, hills, mountains, and their appurtenances, such as stones, marbles, mines of metals and minerals; and to these things will also be added terrestrial animals.","kind":"passage","sequence":139,"address":"3.139","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0139"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0140","text":"This image will contain beneath the Sandals the operations which man can naturally perform concerning the Earth, provided they do not concern the feet, which carry out their operations nearby, as do the other members. But under Prometheus it will contain Geometry, Geography, Cosmography, and Agriculture, and its parts; for we shall divide this into agriculture concerning the Earth, and concerning the fruits of the Earth, concerning trees, and concerning the fruits of trees, concerning animals, and concerning the fruits of animals; and in these six parts we shall place all the writers on agriculture. And this part is given to Saturn because he is cold and dry, and because he is the most immobile, the earth being of such a nature according to Trismegistus. The three heads of Wolf, Lion, and Dog are as follows.","kind":"passage","sequence":140,"address":"3.140","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0140"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0141","text":"Macrobius writes that the ancients, wishing to figure the three times, that is, the past, the present, and the future, painted the three aforesaid","kind":"passage","sequence":141,"address":"3.141","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0141"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0142","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":142,"address":"3.142","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0142"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0143","text":"stars. And that of the Wolf signifies past time, because it has already devoured; that of the Lion, the present (if the present can be given), because present anxieties put us into such an error as the sight of a Lion would put us into if it came upon us. And that of the Dog signifies future time, because, in the manner of a flattering Dog, future time always promises us something better. Therefore this image will contain these three Saturnine times and their appurtenances, because all those times which are not understood through the nearness or remoteness of the Sun are either Saturnine or Lunar: Saturnine, like these three which we have mentioned, which are not made manifest to us by the course of the Sun, as night and day, the four seasons, hours, minutes, and years are.","kind":"passage","sequence":143,"address":"3.143","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0143"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0144","text":"The remoteness, therefore, of this planet causes us to know these three aforesaid times in no other way than through the past, the present, and the future. The Lunar ones, truly, are beneath the cave of the Moon, and beneath her Sandals, and beneath Prometheus, covered by the image of Diana to whom Mercury offers the garment.","kind":"passage","sequence":144,"address":"3.144","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0144"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0145","text":"Times.","kind":"passage","sequence":145,"address":"3.145","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0145"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0146","text":"Saturnian.","kind":"passage","sequence":146,"address":"3.146","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0146"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0147","text":"Solar.","kind":"passage","sequence":147,"address":"3.147","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0147"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0148","text":"Lunar.","kind":"passage","sequence":148,"address":"3.148","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0148"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0149","text":"The same image of the three heads beneath Pasiphaë shall signify that man is subject to time. And beneath the Talari, all operations concerning time, known through neither the distance nor proximity of the Sun, nor through the lunar course, such as to delay, to cause delay, to set a term, or to defer to another time.","kind":"passage","sequence":149,"address":"3.149","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0149"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0150","text":"The area of the patio, although in its lofty mystery it signifies the three worlds which we have assigned to Pan, because it was so fashioned in mind that it measured a cubit and a half both in length and in breadth, and each cubit consisting of","kind":"passage","sequence":150,"address":"3.150","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0150"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0151","text":"six palms","kind":"passage","sequence":151,"address":"3.151","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0151"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0152","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":152,"address":"3.152","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0152"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0153","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO. 25","kind":"passage","sequence":153,"address":"3.153","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0153"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0154","text":"a sign that it was nine palms in length, and nine across: which number was to signify the nine Heavens, and the tenth was figured by the golden cover, which extended only over the first and over the second division, while the third remained uncovered. Now this uncovered part, as we have revealed in the mysteries, signified this lower world exposed to rains, winds, heats, and all changes.","kind":"passage","sequence":154,"address":"3.154","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0154"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0155","text":"The second signified the celestial world, and for this reason contained a golden Candlestick with seven Lamps signifying the seven Planets; then it had a separate Lamp with three reeds on either side, which also signified the Sun in its superiority.","kind":"passage","sequence":155,"address":"3.155","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0155"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","text":"Moreover, there were certain vessels, which signified the reception made by the planets of the supercelestial influences. And there were spherical figures, which signified the globes. There were also flowers, in the signification of which lies the secret of all secrets, which it is not lawful to reveal save in due time, and with God's will. The third division was called the propitiatory, favoured by two Cherubim. One of these signified the divine nature, and the other the human, in one and the same Christ, through which propitiatory remission of sins was made, to signify that through the Christ to come such remission was to be made. And this third division signified the supercelestial. And whereas the middle part was called sancti, this third was called sancti sanctorum, as Cœli cœlo, or rather, Cœli cœlorũ.","kind":"passage","sequence":156,"address":"3.156","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0157","text":"For the Hebrews do not give a singular to heavens, and John made mention to us of this world when he said, In mundo erat,","kind":"passage","sequence":157,"address":"3.157","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0157"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0158","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.    D","kind":"passage","sequence":158,"address":"3.158","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0158"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0159","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":159,"address":"3.159","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0159"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0160","text":"53","kind":"passage","sequence":160,"address":"3.160","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0160"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0161","text":"& mundus per ipſum factus eſt, et mundus eum non cognouit, that is, in saying in mundo erat, he understood the supercelestial; and when he said: Et mundus per ipsum factus est, he signified the terrestrial. And in saying, Et mundus eum non cognouit, he spoke of the lower world.","kind":"passage","sequence":161,"address":"3.161","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0161"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0162","text":"Therefore, although by the Ark the three worlds are signified to us (as we have said), nevertheless, since we have not entrusted the significations of these to Pan's keeping, we wish it to cover the volume pertaining to place, and to all its differences: and this seems to us to have been reasonably ordered; because, the Ark containing all three worlds, it consequently gives place to all things. And just as the Ark, by containing all things, merits the preservation of place with all its differences, so, since it must be assigned to one of the seven planets, it can suit none better than Saturn, who by the breadth of his circle encompasses all the others. This alone, in the Talari, shall signify the monuments that man can make concerning place, such as placing things here and there.","kind":"passage","sequence":162,"address":"3.162","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0162"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","text":"Proteus bound, as distinguished from Proteus unbound, who is in the Lunar Banquet, and is placed here by us for what shall presently be said. And although this binding may be magical and purely natural, nevertheless here we mean the purely natural. I said magical, because the binding which Aristaeus makes of Proteus, by counsel of Cyrene his mother, in Homer and Virgil, is a magical binding. Et qui habet aures audiendi audiat, because it pertains to the secret of which we have spoken above. But the natural binding, and that which we mean under this figure, is such as to say:","kind":"passage","sequence":163,"address":"3.163","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0164","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.     26","kind":"passage","sequence":164,"address":"3.164","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0164"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","text":"mo. The Spirit of Christ is that which (as we have also said in the Convivio), descending from supercelestial things: natione\nfrom the universe, with its virtue unites all the heavens, and bears down from all things their impressions and all their virtues, and with these it abides down here among animals, herbs, and flowers. And if things were not thus renewed, all would perish. And this is perhaps that holy city, full of jewels, which John saw in the Apocalypse descending: and for this David sings the new Canticle, seeing so many things renewed; and Isaiah says, Creabo cœlum nouum,& terram nouam: and in the Apocalypse, too, it is written: Ecce noua facio omnia: and this is Jacob's ladder, by which the spirits descend and ascend; the descending is coming to effect this renewal, and the ascending is the spirit's return to refresh itself with the superior universal.","kind":"passage","sequence":165,"address":"3.165","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0166","text":"But Petrarch, wishing to make mention of this renewal, as one who did not go beyond the celestial world, composed that Sonnet, which begins:","kind":"passage","sequence":166,"address":"3.166","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0166"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167","text":"When the Planet that distinguishes the hours\nReturns to lodge with Taurus. where, in saying:\nVirtue falls from the heavens as\nIt clothes the world in new colour, he comes to attribute to the heavens this operation of making the world beautiful again, not understanding that the soul of the world, full of life-giving spirit, which is Christ, borne down by the Sun from the concavity of the Moon with greater abundance and fecundity when the Sun begins to turn above us than when farther away, comes to the mission which nature intends to make when it intends the production of herbs, flowers, and the other elementary things. And if it did not intervene as mediator to reconcile the contrary qualities","kind":"passage","sequence":167,"address":"3.167","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0168","text":"D  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":168,"address":"3.168","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0168"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0169","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":169,"address":"3.169","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0169"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0170","text":"33","kind":"passage","sequence":170,"address":"3.170","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0170"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","text":"for, unless it knows the mixture, their contrarieties could never remain together under the form of this or that herb, of this or that flower. Such, therefore, is the tempering of the divine spirit of Christ, which likewise reconciles the discordant. And this is what the Prophet says: Ego cælum & terram impleo, and elsewhere Scripture says, pleni sunt cœli & terra gloria tua. This spirit of Christ, therefore, and not that of the soul of the world (as the Platonists say), is not only mediator, reconciler, vivifier, and sustainer of these four discordant elements, but, moved by His mercy, is also mediator and reconciler between divine justice and human frailty. And that this truly is the spirit vivifying all things, we have from the Psalm: Avertente te faciem tuam turbabuntur, & omnia in pulverem reuertentur. And, Emitte spiritum tuum & renouabis faciem terræ.","kind":"passage","sequence":171,"address":"3.171","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","text":"By calling it, therefore, spiritum tuum, he shows this to be the spirit of God, and not of the soul of the world. And Paul calls it the vivifying spirit. The first matter, that is Proteus, full of this vivifying spirit, supervening upon the mixture of herbs, and flowers, and other mixed things, naturally remains so bound within the limits of this flower or that herb until they come to be dissolved. And here a saying of Mercury Trismegistus in the Asclepius is to be noted. Quis quid de alto descendit generans est, quod sursum versus emanat nutriens, idest prestans vitam, hoc est vinificans. This spirit, therefore, descending and supervening upon the mixture which nature would make by mingling with those things that would have been discordant, reconciles and generates them. And while the plant, or the animal, grows","kind":"passage","sequence":172,"address":"3.172","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0173","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":173,"address":"3.173","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0173"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0174","text":"27","kind":"passage","sequence":174,"address":"3.174","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0174"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","text":"it nourishes and unites it. It therefore remains separate in every individual until the time of dissolution comes, improperly called death according to Mercury, who thus writes in the Pimander, chapter xii: Non moritur in mundo quicquam, sed composita corporea dissoluuntur: Dissolutio mors non est, sed mistionis resolutio quædam, soluitur autem vnio non vt ea quæ sunt intereant, sed vt vetera innescant: For as long as the union of mixed things remains together, for so long that part of Proteus remains bound, fixed, and constrained, with that spirit enclosed. And for this reason we wish this image to contend under itself with immovable, fixed, or firm things.","kind":"passage","sequence":175,"address":"3.175","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0176","text":"Under Pasiphaë it will signify obstinate and immutable nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":176,"address":"3.176","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0176"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0177","text":"And under the Winged Sandals it will be something immovable, such as to make firm, to arrest.","kind":"passage","sequence":177,"address":"3.177","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0177"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0178","text":"And that image is assigned to Saturn because of his slowness.","kind":"passage","sequence":178,"address":"3.178","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0178"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0179","text":"The solitary Sparrow, sufficiently by itself, without further explanation, shows that it ought to contain something solitary or abandoned.","kind":"passage","sequence":179,"address":"3.179","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0179"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0180","text":"Under Pasiphaë it will signify solitary nature, and a man alone, and abandoned.","kind":"passage","sequence":180,"address":"3.180","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0180"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0181","text":"But under the Winged Sandals it will signify to go alone, to remain alone, to abandon and leave a person, or place, or thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":181,"address":"3.181","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0181"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0182","text":"And that image befits Saturn, as Pandora in the Cave signifies affliction of things with respect to nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":182,"address":"3.182","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0182"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0183","text":"Under Pasiphaë, affliction of man, and all his ill fortunes: unhappiness, ignobility, poverty, infirmity, and not attaining desire.","kind":"passage","sequence":183,"address":"3.183","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0183"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0184","text":"D iii.","kind":"passage","sequence":184,"address":"3.184","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0184"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0185","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, 38","kind":"passage","sequence":185,"address":"3.185","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0185"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0186","text":"Under the Winged Sandals, to afflict another. The image of the hair cut from the maiden, which we see in Mars spread out toward heaven, will bear all contrary things, that is, weak things. Nor have we done this without authority, but because Alcestis in Euripides, being unable to die the desired death, Mercury, sent for that purpose, cuts her hair, and she dies; and Nisus was not overthrown by Minos until Scylla, enamoured, cut his fated lock of hair. Nor can Dido in Virgil finish dying, except after Iris, sent by Juno, has cut her hair; and Virgil’s design is that Iris, by signifying the elements through colours, should signify things composed of elements. And the cutting of the hair is the dissolution of the elements. Which mysteries have been stolen by Poets from Prophets, as from that passage concerning Samson’s cut hair.","kind":"passage","sequence":186,"address":"3.186","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0186"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0187","text":"This image under Pasiphaë will signify the weakness of man, weariness, false and lying nature. But under the Winged Sandals it will signify to weaken a person or thing, or to lie.","kind":"passage","sequence":187,"address":"3.187","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0187"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0188","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":188,"address":"3.188","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0188"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0189","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":189,"address":"3.189","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0189"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0190","text":"28","kind":"passage","sequence":190,"address":"3.190","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0190"]}],"source_digest":"14191eb683098d9c6e6ed500bb07b4be6394653772b0a0019a439b1145b402be","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"L’ANTRO."},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261031T001629489328Z_b31e00b8","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE CAVE.","source_sha256":"5a8ca9af311cfec4d27db1503a7e5044ff4b06e5e0780d1ada1a732633fdb606","sha256":"53c96dc37967251633d17621a33462ef9fd43c3448726d3dc737b578e7f2f7b6","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-31T00:16:29.489387+00:00","translate_quotations":true,"paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0001","text":"THE CAVE.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"3.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","text":"THE Third grade shall have painted, for each of its doors, a Cave, which we shall call the Homeric Cave, to distinguish it from that which Plato describes in his Republic. Homer, then, imagines above the harbour of Ithaca a cave in which certain Nymphs weave purple cloths, and imagines bees that go out and return to make their honey; which weavings and fabrications, signifying mixed and elemental things, we wish each of the seven caves, according to the nature of its Planet, to preserve the mixed and elemental things belonging to it.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"3.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","text":"And in order to have some information concerning mixed and elemental things, I say that, according to the distinction set forth by Moses, since Eloim on the first day created prime matter in order to make Heaven and earth, because the whole influx of the supercelestial streams was not fitting for matter, on the second day He formed the Rachia, that is, the mass of the heavens, and not the firmament, according to what we have also said, since it is only the eighth sphere; and He placed the said mass, extended between the supercelestial world and the lower one, so that it might divide the waters of the supercelestial streams, which do not wet, from the waters of this world, which do wet, of which supercelestial waters it is written: “All waters that are above the heavens, bless the Lord.” And thus the said celestial mass was interposed and extended, so that no greater influx of the higher waters might rain down than was fitting to the capacity of matter.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"3.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0004","text":"And concerning these waters it should be noted that Gregory Nazianzen is mistaken, understanding by that","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"3.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0005","text":"The days\nat the crea\ntion of the\nworld.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"3.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0006","text":"The waters\nabove the\nheavens.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"3.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0007","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"3.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0008","text":"16","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"3.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0009","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"3.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0010","text":"the crystalline heaven, which has merely been imagined by some above the firmament, but they have neither reason nor foundation for it in either sacred or profane writing. On the third day Moses says that Eloim commanded that the waters which are beneath heaven should be gathered into one place, that is, all the generative virtues together, and that the dry land should appear, so that, by means of the said generative virtues, gathered together, it might diminish according to [them]; which having been done, He said: “Let the earth bring forth green herb, and seed-bearing tree, if it may be so said.” On the fourth day the Luminaries were made and placed in the mass of the Heavens: the Moon in the first sphere, and the Sun in the fourth Sphere, by which light might be distinguished from darkness, that is, those things which had already received form from those which were not yet informed.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"3.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","text":"On the 5th day he speaks of the communication of life to all animals, for he wishes the waters, that is, the generative virtues, to produce all the diversities of animals, aquatic as well as flying and terrestrial, down here, unlike those up above. On the sixth day He produced man, and on the seventh He rested. Thus, after prime matter, we do not see that God created new matter, but from the first He formed all things which we call mixed and elemental. And these we are to find in the third grade of the seven columns beneath the door of the Cave, except for man, who, having been formed separately and made lord of mixed and elemental things, we wish to have a particular grade, as will later be seen. Beneath the door of the Lunar Cave, then, we shall find five images: Neptune, Daphne, Diana, to whom Mercury offers the harvest, the stables of Augeas, and Juno among the clouds.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"3.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0012","text":"Nor should anyone marvel that Neptune, whose being beneath","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"3.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0013","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"3.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","text":"the Communito, shall be seen again beneath the Cave, beneath the Talari, and beneath Prometheus; and this will also happen with other images, both in this and in other planets, since Homer too says that Ulysses had seen Hercules both among the Gods in Heaven and in Hell; and if this does not misbecome him, it ought still less to misbecome us, who, in order not to burden the memory with diverse images for the same things, cause the same figure to be seen again beneath diverse doors. Proteus shall signify form, already supervening upon subject and natural thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"3.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","text":"Neptune, then, beneath the Communito signifies the most simple element of water; but beneath the Cave he shall signify it as already mixed, since in this world we see no element so pure that it is not mixed, as Anaxagoras has long proved and maintained. Beneath the image of this Neptune, then, shall be contained the volume in which water in general and water in particular shall be arranged distinctly by sections; and water in general shall be divided into its whole and its parts: the whole is, as one might say, water alone; its parts, such as a drop. There shall also be the qualities of waters, and their quantities: the qualities, such as sweet and salty, and sweet waters standing and running, and the other accidents.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"3.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016","text":"And besides this, the still waters, the banks, and other things belonging thereto; and also aquatic animals; and beneath this Neptune man is not yet involved, since he was the last of the animals created. But when we find Neptune beneath the Talari, since these signify the operation that man can perform upon each thing created before him naturally and outside art, we wish him to have in his","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"3.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0017","text":"Canon","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"3.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0018","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"3.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0019","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  17","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"3.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0020","text":"Canon human and natural operations concerning wa-\nters, as is also said in what follows.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"3.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","text":"And beneath Prometheus he shall show us the arts concerning waters. Daphne, who is transformed into a laurel, shall be a Symbol of the woodland. And here shall be contained what Theophrastus, or other writers, have ever written On Plants, together with their consequences, which are the shadows.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"3.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","text":"But beneath the Talari Daphne shall signify natural operations concerning timber, such as bending, carrying. And beneath Prometheus she shall contain gardens, and all the arts concerning timber.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"3.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0023","text":"Daphne indeed, that is, the woodland, is aptly assigned to the Moon, that is, to Diana, goddess of woods; for she is queen, as we have said, of moistures, without which no plant would grow. Whence Virgil, in the fourth book of the Georgics:","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"3.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0024","text":"“And Ocean, father of things, and the hundred sister Nymphs,\nWho guard a hundred woods, a hundred rivers.”","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"3.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","text":"Diana, to whom Mercury offers the garment, is the third image. It is read among the Greek fables that, seeing Diana go naked, Jupiter, since she was chaste, was not pleased, and charged Mercury to make her a garment. And although he made her one, there was never any that could be fitted to her. This ending gives us a symbol signifying mutation and its species, that is, generation, corruption, increase, diminution, alteration, mutation according to place, and motion, with all the species recounted by Aristotle and distinguished according to his divisions. This image under Pasiphaë will signify the mutation of man either according to opinion, or according to the transfigura","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"3.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0026","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.     C","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"3.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0027","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"3.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0028","text":"tion of the body.          And under the Talaria it will signify to move, or\nto change a thing, to receive, to dispose, an operation done swiftly or suddenly.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"3.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0029","text":"But under Prometheus it will contain the months, and their parts. The Stables of Augeas are so called by the Greeks, because Augeas was a king exceedingly rich in possessions and fields; but the great abundance of beasts that he kept so encumbered his country with dung that it corrupted the fertility of the fields. Therefore, under this image we shall place a volume that will compreh\nend the filth of worldly things, moulds, rottenness,\nvileness, imperfections, and similar unpleasant things.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"3.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0030","text":"This same image under Pasiphaë will contain the filth of the human body and its excrements, such as those of the ears, the nose, the nails, the eyes, sweat, spittle, vomit, menses, urine, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"3.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0031","text":"But under the Talaria it will signify filthy operations, to befoul,\nto stain, etc.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"3.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0032","text":"And these Stables are assigned to the Moon, because there is no filth except from corrupted moisture.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"3.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","text":"Gymnon among the clouds: Gymnon signifies the air, and this cover\ning of clouds will give us the signification of things hidden in nature, and of those which by the Peripatetics are called knowable, but which are not yet known; and it will also signify brief time. And these things are assigned to the Moon, because we have no Planet that hides itself from us in a shorter time.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"3.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0034","text":"This image under Pasiphaë will signify the concealment\nthat a man can make of himself.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"3.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0035","text":"But under the Talaria it will denote a man hiding a thing or another\nperson.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"3.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0036","text":"Under Mercury there will be six images. The metal of Gold, the","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"3.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0037","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"3.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0038","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"3.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0039","text":"18","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"3.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0040","text":"Atoms, the Pyramid, the Gordian knot entangled, the same disentangled, Juno feigned in clouds. The Golden Fleece, although in mystical Philosophy it has the signification of the highest gift which the Lord God is wont to grant to a few of His elect, and although it has great significance for such an abduction—the gathering of the Heroes, the first ship, and the loss that Jason made of his shoe in the river, alone in the manner without wind, whence perhaps is drawn the order of the Fleeces—which accords with the magic of Zoroaster, which was the first thing that ought to be taught to the new prince of the Persians, so that he might not be a Tyrant.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"3.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0041","text":"Nevertheless, drawing this golden skin down from the height of its mystery to the lowliness of our need, it will serve us as an image of all the objects that pertain to the judgment of weight or touch, such as heavy and light, rough, soft, hard, tender, and the like; nevertheless, this is understood of those things that are outside man.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"3.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0042","text":"This same image under Pasiphaë will signify the same thin\ngs of the human body.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"3.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0043","text":"And under the Talaria it will signify the operation without art of\nmaking hard, soft, rough.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"3.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0044","text":"And this image with such a signification is assigned to Mercury, because the hands that chiefly make these judgments are those of Gemini, which is a thing of Mercury.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"3.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0045","text":"The Atoms will signify for us all discrete quantity in\nthings.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"3.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0046","text":"And under Pasiphaë they will signify the same among hu\nmans, such as someone.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"3.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0047","text":"C  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"3.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0048","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"3.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0049","text":"13","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"3.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0050","text":"But under the Sandals they will signify discrete quantity standing apart from man without art, as to break a thing into pieces with a file, to dissolve and scatter.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"3.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0051","text":"And because this is the subject of Arithmetic, which is the science of Mercury, this image is given to him.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"3.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0052","text":"The Pyramid signifies continuous quantity in things. Under Pasiphaë, in men, as great, small, middling.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"3.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0053","text":"Under the Sandals it signifies operation without art, such as raising,\nlowering, thickening, thinning.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"3.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0054","text":"And since these two quantities, one of Arithmetic and the other of Geometry, are sciences belonging to Hercules drawing the three-pointed arrow, they shall be included under that image under Prometheus.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"3.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0055","text":"The entangled Gordian Knot was brought to Alexander to be untied, and he, being impatient, cut it. Under this shall be contained entangled continuous quantity, such as a thread, or a band.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"3.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0056","text":"And under the Sandals it shall signify the entangling of things. The same Knot, untied, shall denote an unentangled continuous thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"3.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0057","text":"And under the Sandals, the untying of intricate things. Juno fashioned from clouds and drawn from the fable that, when she had been solicited for adultery by Ixion, presented to him a body of clouds resembling her, and with it he lay. Now, by this beast born to that man from that feigned thing, under this figure shall be contained things apparent but not true.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"3.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0058","text":"Under Pasiphaë it shall denote a simulating and cunning nature, and","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"3.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0059","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  19","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"3.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0060","text":"fraudulent.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"3.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0061","text":"And under the Sandals, to feign and deceive. And we give this image to Mercury because he is the author of maliciousness.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"3.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0062","text":"Under the Grotto of Venus are five images: Cerberus, a Venus, a maiden who bears on her head a vessel of scents, Hercules cleansing the stables of Augeas, Narcissus, and Tantalus beneath the stone. Cerberus was painted with three heads to signify the three natural necessities, which are eating, drinking, and sleeping; and because they greatly impede man from speculation, Virgil feigns that Aeneas, by the Sibyl's counsel, wishing to pass to contemplation of high things, throws him a morsel and immediately passes. This signifies that, although we must satisfy these three necessities, we must satisfy them with little, if we wish to have time to contemplate.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"3.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","text":"This image, therefore, under the Grotto shall contain things pertaining to hunger, thirst, and sleep: victuals, drinks, and things that induce sleep. And this figure is given to Venus because of pleasure.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"3.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","text":"Under Pasiphaë it shall signify hunger, thirst, and sleep, and their consequences. Under the Sandals, eating, drinking, and sleeping, and consequent natural operations. Then under Prometheus it shall signify cookery, delicious banquets, and delights suited to sleeping, such as sounds and songs. The maiden bearing on her head the vessel of scents, which was found in Rome, in the other shall signify all scents. And","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"3.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0065","text":"C  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"3.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0066","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"3.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0067","text":"because the vessel belongs to Venus, it is given to her. Under the Sandals it signifies our operations concerning scents without art, such as smelling and wearing scents. But under Prometheus it contains the arts pertaining to scents and perfumers.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"3.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0068","text":"Hercules cleansing the stables of Augeas is introduced because the fables say that that King, finding himself oppressed by the great amount of filth, called Hercules to remove it; and here he shall signify things clean by nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"3.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0069","text":"Under Pasiphaë it shall signify the cleanliness of the human body. Under the Sandals, cleansing without art. And under Prometheus, baths and barbers' shops. And this figure is fitting for Venus because of beauty and delicacy.","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"3.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0070","text":"Narcissus looked at himself in the transitory water of this world, and signifies mortal beauty, whose truth, for one who wishes to find it, requires ascending to the supracelestial Tiseret, where Platonic Hippia ought to seek it; and all of us likewise, because there it is steadfast and immortal. Now under this image we shall have the beauty that appears to us in this world in natural and desirable things. This figure under Pasiphaë shall signify human beauty and its consequences: Softness, Gracefulness, Pleasure, Design, Love, Hope, lovers, and being loved.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"3.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0071","text":"Under the Sandals it shall signify making beautiful, making fall in love, making desire, making hope, etc. And under Prometheus it shall contain the art of cosmetics and beautifiers. Tantalus beneath the stone signifies things wavering, or trembling, or that stand suspended. Under Pasiphaë it shall denote a timid, suspicious, doubtful, and wondering nature. And under the Sandals there shall","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"3.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0072","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"3.72","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0073","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"3.73","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0074","text":"20","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"3.74","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0075","text":"to stand, to tremble, to doubt, to waver, to become seasick, [illegible]gliare, &c. Beneath the Cave of the Sun are five images: the Sun, Argus alone; the Cow watched by Argus; Geryon slain by Hercules; a Cock and a Lion; and Apollo who shoots Juno.","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"3.75","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0076","text":"Argus alone, full of eyes, signifies this entire world, whose head is the Heavens, and whose eyes are the stars, by means of which it thus makes lower things known, bringing them from afar into the appearance of generation, as the ostrich does its eggs, giving them the life of that spirit which is in its wheels. Of this Ezekiel speaks thus: “And the spirit was in the wheels.” Although this keeps all the elements alive, it nevertheless favors fire more than air, and air more than water, and water more than earth; but if this earth, which is less favored, through the life and fecundity that this spirit bestows upon it, germinates everything with so many varieties of things as the other elements must do, whose fecundity, invisible to us, also favors the earth: Mercury in the Pimander says that the earth is by no means immovable, but rather is agitated by many movements.","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"3.76","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0077","text":"And nevertheless, in comparison with the other Elements, it is almost stable; and he adds that it is not to be believed that it, which is nurse of all things, lacks movement; for it is impossible that without movement it can give birth: and just as the stars are the eyes of this world, so the trees, which through their fertility receive much of the aforesaid vital spirit, are like the hairs and locks of its body, and metals and stones are like bones. It is therefore no wonder if the symbolic Theologians have represented the world under the symbol of Argus full of eyes, since the world lives. This image, then.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"3.77","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0078","text":"The earth","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"3.78","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0079","text":"C  iiii","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"3.79","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0080","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"3.80","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0081","text":"The whole world shall be represented in general, and in particular the celestial mass and the celestial bodies.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"3.81","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0081"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0082","text":"The Cow watched by Argus, although it may signify the earth, will nevertheless signify for us all visible things and all colours.","kind":"passage","sequence":82,"address":"3.82","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0082"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0083","text":"Geryon, whose three heads Hercules cuts off, signifies the beginning, the continuance, and the decline of time belonging to the Sun. And this image will signify for us not only the ages of the world, but also the four seasons, which are made by the approach and recession of the Sun, and likewise day and night with their parts.","kind":"passage","sequence":83,"address":"3.83","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0083"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0084","text":"And beneath Pasiphaë it will signify the age of man.","kind":"passage","sequence":84,"address":"3.84","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0084"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0085","text":"Beneath the Winged Sandals, natural operations concerning minutes, hours,\nthe year, age, and the clock.","kind":"passage","sequence":85,"address":"3.85","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0085"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0086","text":"And beneath Prometheus, artificial years, minutes, hours, clocks,\nand instruments of time.","kind":"passage","sequence":86,"address":"3.86","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0086"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0087","text":"The Cock with the Lion. Not only does Pliny disclose this signification, but Iamblichus the Platonist also, and Lucretius, say that although both these animals are solar, nevertheless the Cock bears in its eyes some degree more excellent than the Sun, upon which the Lion, gazing, humbles itself before it. And it happened to the author of this Theatre that, finding himself in Paris in the place called the Tournelle, with many gentlemen in a hall looking from certain windows over a garden, a Lion escaped from captivity came into that hall and, approaching him from behind, seized him without injury by the thighs with its paws, and went about licking him with its tongue. And at that touch and at that breath, he having turned himself about, and having that animal","kind":"passage","sequence":87,"address":"3.87","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0087"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0088","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":88,"address":"3.88","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0088"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0089","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":89,"address":"3.89","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0089"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0090","text":"31","kind":"passage","sequence":90,"address":"3.90","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0090"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0091","text":"Seen it, while many of the others had fled here and there, the Lion humbled itself before him, almost in the act of asking mercy. Nor is it to be said that this happened for any other reason than that the animal perceived much solar virtue to be in him. This image, then, will contain the excellence of natural things by comparison.","kind":"passage","sequence":91,"address":"3.91","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0091"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0092","text":"Beneath Pasiphaë it will signify the excellence of man, superiority, dignity, authority, and dominion in a thing worthy of honour.","kind":"passage","sequence":92,"address":"3.92","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0092"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0093","text":"Beneath the Winged Sandals it will signify making superior, bestowing dignity, and\ndegree.","kind":"passage","sequence":93,"address":"3.93","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0093"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0094","text":"But beneath Prometheus it will contain Principalities and kingdoms—\nwhich have all been regulated by writers with precepts, if only they were well observed.","kind":"passage","sequence":94,"address":"3.94","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0094"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","text":"Apollo shooting Juno amid the clouds is an image opposed to Juno hidden amid the clouds, which is of Esoda. And although Homer introduces this fable, it is not therefore to be believed that he wishes to introduce war among the Gods, as Socrates indicates in the Meno, but it signifies manifest things.","kind":"passage","sequence":95,"address":"3.95","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0096","text":"And beneath Pasiphaë it signifies man manifesting himself, and coming\nto light.","kind":"passage","sequence":96,"address":"3.96","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0096"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0097","text":"But beneath the Sandals, to reveal a person or thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":97,"address":"3.97","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0097"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0098","text":"Beneath the Cave of Mars are four images: Vulcan, Mars; a maiden whose hair stands raised toward Heaven, Two serpents that fight; & Mars upon a Dra-\ngon.","kind":"passage","sequence":98,"address":"3.98","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0098"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0099","text":"Vulcan carries with him so much the signification of fire that he has no need of explanation. And because fire is divided into three kinds, since its most subtle part","kind":"passage","sequence":99,"address":"3.99","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0099"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0100","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 43, region 13]","kind":"passage","sequence":100,"address":"3.100","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0100"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0101","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":101,"address":"3.101","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0101"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0102","text":"precisely fills the hollow of the Moon, it has also obtained from the Latins to be called air. Whence Cicero, On the Nature of the Gods 44. From Ether, which consists of the highest fires, we derive this word also, and ether is called in Latin just as air is called. And although from this passage some would associate it with the air, which it has beneath the Cave of jewels, nevertheless, considering its nature, it follows that it is also superior to fire; we wish it rather to be of fire than of air. And so much the more because Cicero says in the same work at 34. The burning heat of heaven, which is called ether, or heaven. And at 37. Ether, thin and transparent, and suffused with an even heat. Elementary fire shall follow this, & in the third place our fire shall be placed.","kind":"passage","sequence":102,"address":"3.102","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0102"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0103","text":"And because this im age is also in the Banquet, & beneath other doors of it we have spoken more fully in the Banquet, here it will suffice us to say again that Vulcan in this place shall signify ether, elementary fire with the universal conflagration, & moreover our fire with the particular conflagration, the spark, the flame, the coal, & the ash. And this image with the things contained by it cannot suit any planet other than Mars, because Mars alone is hot and dry, as fire is, whereas the Sun is hot and moist. The Maiden with hair raised toward Heaven is so fashioned, giving us to understand that man, according to Plato, is an inverted tree: for the tree has its roots downward, & man has them upward.","kind":"passage","sequence":103,"address":"3.103","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0103"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0104","text":"And Origen and Jerome, his follower, maintain that when Scripture makes mention of hair or beard, one must not understand hair or beard of the body, but of the soul, which metaphorically has hair & beard, & eyes, & other par","kind":"passage","sequence":104,"address":"3.104","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0104"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0105","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":105,"address":"3.105","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0105"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0106","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":106,"address":"3.106","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0106"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0107","text":"22","kind":"passage","sequence":107,"address":"3.107","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0107"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0108","text":"ts corresponding to the body. And because, if someone exposed himself naked to the night air, the hair & beard would show more clearly the humour drawn in from Heaven than any other part of the body, they maintain that, just as the tree by its roots draws to itself the nutritive humour from the earth, so the beard & hair of our inner man draw the dew, that is, the life-giving humour, from the influences of the supercelestial channels, whence all its vigour follows. And of this it is that one reads in the Callistica: As by the channels of thy justice, understanding by this the supercelestial streams, which expression bears the signification that that soul was full of supercelestial vigour. And in the psalm one reads of Aaron's dewy beard: the same meaning. Therefore this image shall cover the volume pertaining to the vigour that a thing may have in this world. And it shall signify a vigorous or strong or worthy thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":108,"address":"3.108","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0108"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0109","text":"And we place truth in this place as that of which it was confessed by the sages of Darius that it had force above all other things. Beneath Pasiphaë this image shall signify a vigorous, strong, & true na-\nture. And beneath the Sandals, to give vigour or force, or to bring about a return to truth. And it is to be noted that Geburà is truth: & that it is declared by that way.","kind":"passage","sequence":109,"address":"3.109","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0109"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0110","text":"Mercy & Truth have met\ntogether. Justice & peace have kissed.","kind":"passage","sequence":110,"address":"3.110","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0110"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0111","text":"Psalm.\n84.","kind":"passage","sequence":111,"address":"3.111","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0111"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0112","text":"The two fighting Serpents represent to us that fable which is read of Mercury, who encounters two serpents that were fighting; beneath which image we shall place the discord, the difference, & the diversity of things. And beneath Pasiphaë such an image shall signify a contentious na","kind":"passage","sequence":112,"address":"3.112","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0112"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0113","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":113,"address":"3.113","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0113"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","text":"ture. And beneath the Sandals, to contend. And beneath Prometheus, the military art, & terrestrial & maritime war and their appurtenances. Mars upon the Dragon is fashioned by us for this reason. We have said that the Planets seek their natures and influences from the corresponding supercelestial Sephiroth: & because Geburà, which gives its influence to Mars, has as its superior an angelic being called Zamael, which signifies poison of God, because by means of this God chastises the world; & because the Cabalists say that such an intelligence has the figure of a Dragon, we place Mars upon it: & to this image we shall assign a volume containing harmful & poi-\nsonous natural things.","kind":"passage","sequence":114,"address":"3.114","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0115","text":"And beneath Pasiphaë it shall signify a harmful, cruel, &\nvindictive nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":115,"address":"3.115","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0115"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0116","text":"And beneath the Sandals, to harm, to become cruel, to take revenge, to impede","kind":"passage","sequence":116,"address":"3.116","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0116"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0117","text":"Juno.","kind":"passage","sequence":117,"address":"3.117","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0117"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0118","text":"The cave of Juno shall contain five images: Juno suspen-\nded, The two Holes of the Lyre, The Caduceus, upon which it rains, Gold in the lap, & the three Graces.","kind":"passage","sequence":118,"address":"3.118","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0118"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0119","text":"Juno suspended is also in Juno's Banquet, where she signifies simple air: & here she shall signify the four elements in general, & air in particular, which being divided into three regions, in the lowest we shall place dew, hoarfrost, morning light, cold, coolness, heat, & mist. In the second, clouds, winds, thunders, lightnings, thunderbolts, rain, hail, & snow. In the third, & highest, comets, shooting fires, & stars apparently falling.","kind":"passage","sequence":119,"address":"3.119","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0119"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0120","text":"This shall also be beneath the Sandals and beneath Prometheus, co-","kind":"passage","sequence":120,"address":"3.120","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0120"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0121","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":121,"address":"3.121","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0121"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0122","text":"23","kind":"passage","sequence":122,"address":"3.122","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0122"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0123","text":"is stated to me in the Banquet. We have made the two sound-holes of the Lyre out of necessity, but for this reason: that nature, having made the ears of animals, and principally of man, with winding passages, fitted to receive the air struck by some sound—for it twists itself like water struck by a stone—and nature, in order to receive it, has prepared for it a likewise winding place; this struck air, having entered the animal's ear, strikes that inner air which we call connatural, and the connatural air, being struck, strikes certain inner nerves, through which the animal hears. Thus the ancient makers of the Lyre, for the convenience of touching its strings, made those outside, but the holes in imitation of ears, principally those of man. Hence this image will have the volume containing all audible things, and every natural noise and sound.","kind":"passage","sequence":123,"address":"3.123","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0123"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0124","text":"This image beneath the Sandals signifies making a noise, and belongs more to Jupiter than to another Planet, because he is patron of the air, without which no sound can be made.","kind":"passage","sequence":124,"address":"3.124","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0124"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0125","text":"The Caduceus is Mercury's rod, which he placed (as the fables say) between the two serpents that he found fighting, as has been said under Mars; and they entwined themselves about it in perpetual union. And this image will show us uniform, same, non-different, and equivalent things,","kind":"passage","sequence":125,"address":"3.125","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0125"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0126","text":"Under Pasiphaë it will contain a friendly nature inclined to domestic care and to the republic. And beneath the Sandals, friendship, or practiced intercourse. Under Prometheus, the city and domestic care, which is divided into father of the household, mother of the household, children, and servants.","kind":"passage","sequence":126,"address":"3.126","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0126"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0127","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":127,"address":"3.127","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0127"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0128","text":"Danaë with the shower of gold, although in the other mysteries it signifies the same thing as the Golden Fleece and the gardens of the Hesperides, will here signify for us good fortune, fullness, and abundance of things, since every plenitude and every good thing comes from above.","kind":"passage","sequence":128,"address":"3.128","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0128"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0129","text":"Under Pasiphaë it will denote good fortune, happiness, nobility, riches, health, glory, attainment of desire.","kind":"passage","sequence":129,"address":"3.129","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0129"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0130","text":"Under the Sandals, operation concerning good fortune and\nthe things stated above.","kind":"passage","sequence":130,"address":"3.130","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0130"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0131","text":"The three Graces were painted by the ancients in such a manner that one kept her face hidden, and this signified the benefit of the giver, which ought not to be made manifest by him who gives it. And Jesus Christ says: “When you give alms, do not sound a trumpet before yourself.” And elsewhere: “Let not your left hand know what your right hand does.” The other showed all of it, and signifies the receiver of the benefit, to whom it pertains to show the face, that is, to make manifest the grace received. The third partly hides it and partly shows it, and signifies the recompensed benefit, showing what has been received and concealing what has been given. Now this image in this place will signify useful things.","kind":"passage","sequence":131,"address":"3.131","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0131"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0132","text":"Under Pasiphaë, beneficent nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":132,"address":"3.132","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0132"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0133","text":"Under the Sandals, to give favour, benefit, and aid","kind":"passage","sequence":133,"address":"3.133","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0133"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0134","text":"Saturn.","kind":"passage","sequence":134,"address":"3.134","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0134"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0135","text":"Saturn's cave will cover seven images: Cybele; three heads, of Wolf, Lion, and Dog; the Ark of the Covenant; Proteus bound; a solitary sparrow; Pandora; and a maiden whose hair, raised toward heaven, is being cut. We have had Cybele in the Banquet, and she signifies the earth; and by the turreted crown she signifies the cities sustained by her. She is drawn in a chariot by two Lions, because as","kind":"passage","sequence":135,"address":"3.135","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0135"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0136","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":136,"address":"3.136","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0136"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0137","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":137,"address":"3.137","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0137"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0138","text":"24","kind":"passage","sequence":138,"address":"3.138","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0138"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0139","text":"The Lion is strong in front and weak behind; likewise the Sun, whence lions, having such a nature, are more powerful in the forepart than in the hinder part. Of this there has also been discussion in the Banquet; and here, and beneath the Sandals, and under Prometheus, it will not vomit fire, because it will signify purely the Earth. And beneath the Cave it will denote the Earth in general, with all its species treated by Pliny, that is, in the chapter which he makes, On the kinds of lands, as created and barren. Then it will signify inhabited and uninhabited Earth, level and mountainous. The level will contain all open places. The mountainous will embrace valleys, hollows, hills, mountains, and their appurtenances, such as stones, marbles, mines of metals and minerals; and to these things will also be added terrestrial animals.","kind":"passage","sequence":139,"address":"3.139","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0139"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0140","text":"This image beneath the Sandals will contain the operations that man can naturally perform concerning the Earth, provided that they do not concern the feet, which carry on their operations below, as do the other members. But under Prometheus it will contain Geometry, Geography, Cosmography, and Agriculture and its parts; for we shall distinguish this into agriculture concerning the Earth, concerning the fruits of the Earth, concerning trees, concerning the fruits of trees, concerning animals, and concerning the fruits of animals; and in these six parts we shall place all the writers on agriculture. And this part is given to Saturn because he is cold and dry, and because he is the most immobile, the earth being of such a nature according to Trismegistus. The three heads of Wolf, Lion, and Dog are such.","kind":"passage","sequence":140,"address":"3.140","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0140"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0141","text":"Macrobius writes that the ancients, wishing to represent the three times, that is, the past, the present, and the future, painted the three aforesaid","kind":"passage","sequence":141,"address":"3.141","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0141"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0142","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":142,"address":"3.142","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0142"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0143","text":"stars. And that of the Wolf signifies past time, because it has already devoured; that of the Lion, the present (if the present can be given), because present afflictions put us into such error as the sight of a Lion would put us into if it assailed us. And that of the Dog signifies future time, because, in the manner of a flattering Dog, future time always promises us better things. Therefore this image will contain these three Saturnine times and their appurtenances, because all those times which are not understood through the nearness or remoteness of the Sun are either Saturnine or Lunar: Saturnine, such as these three which we have mentioned, which do not manifest themselves to us through the course of the Sun, as do night and day, the four seasons, the hours, the minutes, and the years.","kind":"passage","sequence":143,"address":"3.143","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0143"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0144","text":"The remoteness of this planet, therefore, causes us to know these three aforesaid times in no other way than through the past, the present, and the future. The Lunar ones, indeed, are beneath the cave of the Moon, and beneath its Sandals, and under Prometheus, covered by the image of Diana to whom Mercury offers the garment.","kind":"passage","sequence":144,"address":"3.144","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0144"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0145","text":"Times.","kind":"passage","sequence":145,"address":"3.145","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0145"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0146","text":"Saturn-\nian.","kind":"passage","sequence":146,"address":"3.146","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0146"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0147","text":"Solar.","kind":"passage","sequence":147,"address":"3.147","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0147"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0148","text":"Lunar.","kind":"passage","sequence":148,"address":"3.148","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0148"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0149","text":"The same image of the three heads beneath Pasiphaë shall signify that man is subject to time. And beneath the Talaria, all operations concerning time not known through the distance or proximity of the Sun, nor through the lunar course, such as delaying, causing delay, setting a term, or postponing to another time.","kind":"passage","sequence":149,"address":"3.149","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0149"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0150","text":"The area of the court, although in its lofty mystery it signifies the three worlds which we have assigned to Pan, because it was so made that a cubit and a half measured it both in length and in breadth, and each cubit consisting of","kind":"passage","sequence":150,"address":"3.150","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0150"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0151","text":"six palms","kind":"passage","sequence":151,"address":"3.151","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0151"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0152","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":152,"address":"3.152","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0152"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0153","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO. 25","kind":"passage","sequence":153,"address":"3.153","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0153"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0154","text":"signifies that it was nine palms in length, and nine across: which number was to signify the nine Heavens, and the tenth was figured by the golden cover, which did not extend save over the first and over the second division, while the third remained uncovered. Now this uncovered part, as we have in the revealed mysteries, signified this lower world exposed to rains, winds, heats, and all changes.","kind":"passage","sequence":154,"address":"3.154","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0154"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0155","text":"The second signified the celestial world, and for this reason it contained a golden Candlestick with seven Lamps signifying the seven Planets; then it had a separate Lamp with three reeds on either side, which likewise signified the Sun in its superiority.","kind":"passage","sequence":155,"address":"3.155","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0155"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","text":"Besides, there were certain vessels, which signified the reception made by the planets of the supercelestial influences. And there were spherical figures, which signified the globes. There were also flowers, in the signification of which lies the secret of all secrets, which it is not lawful to reveal except in its time and by the will of God. The third division was called the propitiatory, attended by two Cherubim. One of these signified the divine nature, and the other the human, in one and the same Christ; through which propitiatory remission of sins was made, to signify that through the Christ to come such remission was to be made. And this third division signified the supercelestial. And the middle part being called holy, this third was called holy of holies, as Heaven of heaven, or, to say it better, Heavens of heavens.","kind":"passage","sequence":156,"address":"3.156","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0157","text":"For the Hebrews do not give the singular to heavens, and John made mention to us of this world when he said: He was in the world,","kind":"passage","sequence":157,"address":"3.157","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0157"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0158","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.    D","kind":"passage","sequence":158,"address":"3.158","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0158"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0159","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":159,"address":"3.159","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0159"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0160","text":"53","kind":"passage","sequence":160,"address":"3.160","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0160"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0161","text":"& the world was made by him, and the world knew him not, meaning that, in saying he was in the world, he understood the supercelestial world; and when he said: And the world was made by him, he signified the terrestrial. And in saying, And the world knew him not, he spoke of the lower world.","kind":"passage","sequence":161,"address":"3.161","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0161"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0162","text":"Therefore, although by the Ark the three worlds are signified to us (as we have said), nevertheless, since we have not yet entrusted to the guardianship of Pan the significations of these, we wish it to cover the volume pertaining to place and all its differences; and this seems to us to have been reasonably ordained: for, the Ark containing all three worlds, it consequently gives place to all things. And just as the Ark, by containing all things, deserves the preservation of place with all its differences, so, since it must be given to one of the seven planets, it can suit none better than Saturn, who by the extent of his circle comprehends all the others. This alone beneath the Talaria shall signify the monuments which man can make concerning place, such as placing things here and there.","kind":"passage","sequence":162,"address":"3.162","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0162"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","text":"Proteus bound, as distinct from Proteus unbound, who is in the Lunar Banquet, and is placed here by us for what shall presently be said. And although this binding may be magical and purely natural, nevertheless here we mean the purely natural. I said magical, because the binding of Proteus performed by Aristaeus on the counsel of his mother Cyrene, in Homer and Virgil, is a magical binding. And let him who has ears to hear, hear, for it pertains to the secret of which we have spoken above. But the natural binding, and that which we understand beneath this figure, is such as to say:","kind":"passage","sequence":163,"address":"3.163","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0164","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.     26","kind":"passage","sequence":164,"address":"3.164","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0164"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","text":"man. The Spirit of Christ is that which (as we have also\n said in the Banquet) descending from supercelestial things:\n nation\n from the universe, with its virtue unites all the heavens, and brings down all things\n their impressions and all their virtues, and with these it\n remains fixed down here among animals, herbs, and flowers. And if things were not thus\n renewed, all would perish. And this is perhaps\n that holy city which John saw in the Apocalypse descend-\n ing full of jewels: and for this David sings the new\n Canticle, seeing so many things renewed; and Isaiah says, I shall create a new heaven,\n and a new earth: and in the Apocalypse, it is\n written: Behold, I make all things new: and this is Jacob’s\n ladder by which spirits descend and ascend; and descent is coming to effect this\n renewal, while ascent is the return of the spirit to refresh itself with the\n higher universal.","kind":"passage","sequence":165,"address":"3.165","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0166","text":"But Petrarch, wishing to make mention of this renewal,\nlike one who did not pass beyond the celestial world, composed that Sonnet\nwhich begins:","kind":"passage","sequence":166,"address":"3.166","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0166"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167","text":"When the Planet that distinguishes the hours\nReturns to lodge with Taurus. Where, saying:\nVirtue falls from the celestial regions as\nIt clothes the world in a new colour, he comes to assign to the heavens this operation of making the world beautiful again, not understanding that the soul of the world, full of vivifying spirit, which is Christ, brought by the Sun down from the concavity of the Moon with greater abundance and fecundity when the Sun begins to turn above us than when it is farther away, comes upon the emission which nature wishes to make when it wishes to produce herbs, flowers, and the other elemental things. And if it did not intervene as mediator to reconcile the contrary qualities","kind":"passage","sequence":167,"address":"3.167","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0168","text":"D  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":168,"address":"3.168","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0168"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0169","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":169,"address":"3.169","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0169"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0170","text":"33","kind":"passage","sequence":170,"address":"3.170","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0170"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","text":"which know the composite, their contrarieties could never remain together under the form of this or that herb, of this or that flower. Such, then, is the tempering of the divine spirit of Christ, which harmonizes even the discordant. And this is what the Prophet says: “I fill heaven and earth,” and elsewhere Scripture says, “Heaven and earth are full of thy glory.” This spirit of Christ, then, and not that of the soul of the world (as the Platonists say), is not only mediator, reconciler, vivifier, and sustainer of these four discordant elements, but, moved by His mercy, is also mediator and reconciler between divine justice and human frailty. And that this truly is the spirit vivifying all things, we have from the psalm: “When thou turnest away thy face, they shall be troubled, and all shall return to dust.” And, “Send forth thy spirit and thou shalt renew the face of the earth.”","kind":"passage","sequence":171,"address":"3.171","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","text":"By calling it “thy spirit,” then, he shows this to be the spirit of God, and not of the soul of the world. And Paul calls it the vivifying spirit. Therefore, when prime matter—that is, Proteus—full of this vivifying spirit, comes upon the mixture of herbs and flowers and the other composites, it naturally remains so bound within the limits of this flower or that herb, until they come to be dissolved. And here a saying of Mercury Trismegistus in the Asclepius is to be noted: “Whatever descends from on high is generating; that which emanates upward is nourishing, that is, bestowing life; this is vivifying.” Therefore, as this spirit descends upon the mixture which nature would make by mingling itself with those things that would have been discordant, it reconciles and generates them. And while the plant, or the animal, crea","kind":"passage","sequence":172,"address":"3.172","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0173","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":173,"address":"3.173","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0173"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0174","text":"27","kind":"passage","sequence":174,"address":"3.174","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0174"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","text":"ted, it nourishes and unites it. Therefore, it remains separate in every individual until the time of dissolution comes, improperly called death according to Mercury, who thus writes in the Pimander, chapter xii: “Nothing dies in the world, but composite bodies are dissolved: dissolution is not death, but a certain resolution of mixture; union is dissolved not so that those things which are may perish, but so that they may be reborn anew.” Therefore, for as long as the union of composites remains together, for so long does that part of Proteus with that enclosed spirit remain bound, fixed, and constrained. And for this reason we wish this image to have to gather beneath itself things immobile, fixed, or firm.”","kind":"passage","sequence":175,"address":"3.175","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0176","text":"Under Pasiphaë it will signify obstinate and immutable nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":176,"address":"3.176","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0176"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0177","text":"And under the Winged Sandals it will be something immobile, such as to stop, to arrest.","kind":"passage","sequence":177,"address":"3.177","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0177"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0178","text":"And that image is assigned to Saturn because of his slowness.","kind":"passage","sequence":178,"address":"3.178","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0178"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0179","text":"The solitary Sparrow, quite by itself and without further declaration, shows that it is to contain something solitary or abandoned.","kind":"passage","sequence":179,"address":"3.179","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0179"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0180","text":"Under Pasiphaë it will signify solitary nature, and a man alone and abandoned.","kind":"passage","sequence":180,"address":"3.180","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0180"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0181","text":"But under the Winged Sandals it will signify to go alone, to remain alone, to abandon and leave a person, place, or thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":181,"address":"3.181","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0181"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0182","text":"And that image is fitting to Saturn, as to nature. Pandora in the Cave signifies affliction of things.","kind":"passage","sequence":182,"address":"3.182","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0182"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0183","text":"Under Pasiphaë, affliction of man, and all his misfortunes: unhappiness, ignobility, poverty, infirmity, and not obtaining what is desired.","kind":"passage","sequence":183,"address":"3.183","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0183"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0184","text":"D  iii.","kind":"passage","sequence":184,"address":"3.184","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0184"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0185","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, 38","kind":"passage","sequence":185,"address":"3.185","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0185"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0186","text":"Under the Winged Sandals, to inflict affliction upon another. The image of the hair cut from the maiden, which we see in Mars stretched out toward heaven, will bear all opposite things, that is, weak things. Nor have we done this without authority, but because Alcestis in Euripides, being unable to die the desired death, has her hair cut by Mercury, who was sent, and she dies; and Nisus was not overcome by Minos until Scylla, in love, cut off his fated lock of hair. Nor can Dido in Virgil finish dying except after Iris, sent by Juno, has cut off her hair; and Virgil’s intention is that Iris, in signifying the elements by colours, should signify elemental things. And the cutting of the hair is the dissolution of elements. These mysteries were stolen by Poets from the Prophets, as from that passage concerning Samson’s cut hair.","kind":"passage","sequence":186,"address":"3.186","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0186"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0187","text":"This image under Pasiphaë will signify the weakness of man, weariness, false and lying nature. But under the Winged Sandals it will signify weakening a person or thing, or lying.","kind":"passage","sequence":187,"address":"3.187","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0187"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0188","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":188,"address":"3.188","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0188"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0189","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":189,"address":"3.189","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0189"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0190","text":"28","kind":"passage","sequence":190,"address":"3.190","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0190"]}],"source_digest":"14191eb683098d9c6e6ed500bb07b4be6394653772b0a0019a439b1145b402be","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"L’ANTRO."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"L’ANTRO.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO","title":"THE GORGONS,","order":4,"chapter_id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO","text":"LE GORGONI,\n\nSAgliamo al quarto Grado appartenente all’huomo inferiore, il qual fu l’ultimo, & la più nobil creatura fatta da Dio à ſua imagine & ſimilitudine. Et qui è da no tare che nel teſto hebreo quello che è tradotto per imagi ne, è detto Celem, & quello che è detto ſimilitudine, è ſcrit to Demut. Le quali parole nel Zoar di Rabi Simeon, che ſuona illuminator, cioè dator di luce, ſono interpretate in queſto ſenſo, che Celem ſignifichi (per dir coſì) la ſtampa o uer la forma angelica, & Demut importi grado diuino. percioche vuole che Dio non ſolamente traſſe l’anima noſ tra alla eccellenza de gli Angeli ma anchor le aggiunſe eſſo il grado diuino. Et aggiunſe il detto autor del Zoar che eſſo antivedendo l’angelo, che fu poi ſcacciato, moſſo da inuidia, & dall’amor proprio, parlò contra il voler della diuina Maeſtà ma Mercurio Triſmegisto nel ſuo Pimandro prende la imagine & la ſimilitudine per vna coſa iſteſſa, & il tutto per lo grado diuino, dicendo coſì. At pater omni um intellectus, vita, & fulgor exiſtens, hominem ſibi ſimi lem procreauit, atque ei tanquam filio ſua congratulatus eſt pulcher enim erat, patriſque ſui ferebat imaginem. Deus enim re vera propria forma nimium delectatus opera eius omnia vſui conceſſit humano. Et il medefi mo nello Aſclepio. O Aſclepi magnum miraculum eſt homo, animal adorandum atque honorandum, hoc enim in naturam Dei tranſit, quaſi ipſe ſit Deus, hoc dæmonum genus nouit, vt pote qui eorum eiſdem ora.\n\nD  iii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\n3.\n\ncum eſſe cognoscat, hoc humanæ naturæ partem in ſe ipſo deſpiciat, alterius partis divinitatis confuſus. Altri ſcrittori Cabaliſti hanno laſciato ſcritto la ſimilitudine appartenersi alla operatione, quaſi volendo dir Dio hauer fatto l’huomo à fine di operar per lui: & con queſta opinione conſente la ſcrittura ſanta,doue ſi mention le opere buone,che faccia: ma non eſſer noſtre,ma di Dio, & noi eſſer ſolamente gli iſtrumenti. La onde alcuni contemplatiui chiamano queſte opere,opere eterne. Di che Paolo dice. Quid habes homo, quod non accepiſti? Et ſi accepiſti quare gloriaris quaſi nō acceperis, & è da notar che le più delle fiate quando la Scrittura fa mention dell’huomo,intende ſolamente dell’interiore,il che chiaramente ſi truoua nel libro di Moſe intito-\nlato Iob.che dice. Pelle & carnibus veſtijſti me, oſſibus & nervis compegiſti me, per le quali parole, & per quel prono me, me, dà chiaramente ad intendere altro eſſer l’huomo interiore dall’eſteriore. In queſta opinione viene Socrate nel ſuo primo Alcibiade appreſſo Platone,diſputando della na tura dell’huomo,percioche ſi come la veſta che portiamo nō è noi,ma coſa vſata da noi,coſì il corpo anchor che ſia por-\ntato da noi non è noi,ma coſa vſata da noi: per la qual coſa ſono da eſſer conſiderate le parole di Moſe nel Geneſi,facia mus hominem ad imaginem & ſimilitudinem noſtram, le quali non ſuonano ſe non l’interior huomo: & che vero ſia, aliquanto ſotto ſoggiunſe. Nondum erat homo qui operare tur in terra. Era adunque avanti nel ſopraceleſte fatto l’huo mo interiore,che Dio gli formaſſe il corpo di terra a fin che poteſſe operar in queſto mondo & eſſere iſtrumento delle opere diuine: & perciò Moſe ſoggiunſe. Plaſmauit Deus ho\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n29\n\nſimilem de limo terræ, il qual limo non ſignifica fango (come molti auuiſino) ma il fior, & (per dir coſì) il capo di lat-\nte de la terra, che era Virginale, percioche non haueua anchor contratto macchia, ſi come contraſſe quaſi famiglia di Adam doppo il peccato di lui. La qual terra virginale era chiamata Adama: onde Adam traſſe il nome. Ne queſto ta-\nccò che Chriſto per ſodisfare alla giuſtitia diuina, ſi appre-\nſentò per purgator di tutte le humane colpe in corpo con ſi-\nmile à quello che haueua Adam prima che peccaſſe, cioè in corpo fatto di terra Verginale, & di ſangue puriſſimo di Maria Vergine.\n\nAdam.\n\nA queſte coſe ſi aggiunga, poi che à parlar di Adam ſiamo entrati, che egli auanti il peccato era in due modi nell’horto delle delitie, non dico Paradiſo Terreſtre, come molti inter-\npretano quel che Moſè non diſſe già mai. Nel primo modo, Adam que era nell’horto ſopraceleſte non preſentialmente, ma terreſtre, nella gratia di Dio godendo di tutti i beati influſſi, ma come hebbe peccato coſì fu cacciato del detto horto ſopraceleſte. et ciò è, che leuati li furono i già detti influſſi, non che eſſo corporalmente foſſe mandato fuori non altramente che ſe un ſeruidor prima à Ceſare gratiſſimo in Egitto ſi ritroue-\nuaſſe, mentre egli foſſe nella gratia del Prencipe ſuo, ſi di-\nrebbe che foſſe nella ſua famiglia, ma peccando priuo della gratia ſua ſi potrebbe dir che foſſe cacciato dalla Corte. Ne ſi marauigli alcuno che io metta queſta queſtione in capo, che l’horto del quale fu cacciato Adam foſſe il ſopraceleſte giardino, percioche queſta fu opinione prima di Orige-\ngene, & poi di Hieronimo ſuo ſeguitatore. L’altro modo di dire che Adam era in paradiſo, ſare ſecondo il vocabolo,\n\nParadiſo\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nnon hebreo, ma greco, & dichiamo che Adam auanti il peccato era nella terra virginal di queſto mondo. Et mentre dimorò in quella ſenza macular il corpo ſuo di peccato era in paradiſo terreſtro. Et fatto il peccato la terra contræ heſſe macchia, & coſì venne ad eſſer cacciato del paradiſo. Auienne adunque al mondo fatto per Adam quel che potreb be auenire ad vn Baron di Ceſare, il quale ſe peccaſſe, tut-\nta la ſua famiglia verrebbe à contragger macchia anchor che ella non haueſſe peccato, & tutti la guarderebbono con occhio torto. Peccando adunque Adam peccarono tutti gli Elementi per contraction di macchia. Di che in loro non eſſendo più la prima virginità, ſi può dire che per queſta ragione Adam ſia detto eſſere ſtato cacciato dal terreſtro paradiſo.\n\nIn ani-\nme no-\nſtre.\n\nMa ſeguendo il propoſito noſtro è da ſapere che in noi ſono tre anime le quali tutte tre quantunque godano di queſto nome comune animo, nondimeno ciaſcuna ha anchor il ſuo nome particolare. Impercioche la più baſſa, & vicina, & com-\npagna del corpo noſtro è chiamata Nephes, & è queſta altramente detta da Moſe anima viuens. Et queſta percioche in lei capeno tutte le noſtre paſſioni, la habbiamo noi comune con le beſtie. Et di queſta parla Chriſto quando dice. Triſ-\nſis eſt anima mea vſque ad mortem. Et altroue, qui non ha-\nbuerit odio animam ſuam perdet eam. Al qual vocabolo, no-\naſſpirando la lingua ne greca, ne latina non ſi può rappre-\nſentar nelle traductioni la ſua ſignificatione, come (per eſ-\nempio) in quel Salmo. Lauda anima mea dominum: quantunque lo ſcrittor dello Spirito Santo habbia poſto il vocabolo di Nephes, ci fanno vſare il comune. Et fu ben ra\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n30\n\n[illegible]\n\nglione che il Propheta vſaſſe il vocabolo Nephes volendo lodar Dio con la lingua & con altri membri che formano la voce, & ſono gouernati dalla Nephes, che è più vicina alla carne. L’anima di mezo, che è la rationale, è chiamata col nome dello ſpirito, cioè Ruach. La terza è detta Neſ ſamah. Da Moſe ſpiraculo, da Dauid & da Pithagora ila me, da Apollino portio ſuperiore, da Platone mente, da Ariſtotele intelletto agente. Et ſi come la Nephes ha il dia-\nuolo, che le miniſtra dimonio per tentatore, coſì la Neſſamah ha Dio che le miniſtra l’angelo. La pouerella di mezo da amendue le parti è ſtimolata. Et ſe per diuina permiſſione ſ’inchina à far vnione cõ la Nephes, la Nephes ſi vniſce cõ la carne et la carne col dimonio, et il tutto fa traſſito et traſ mutatione in diavolo, per la qual coſa diſſe Chriſto. Ego ele gi vos duodecim, et Vnus ex vobis diabolus eſt. Ma ſe per la gratia di Chriſto(da altrui nō puo venire vn tanto benefi tio)la anima di mezo ſi diſſacca quaſi p lo taglio del coltel lo della parola di Chriſto dalla Nephes mal perſuaſa, et ſi vniſce cõ la Neſſamah, la Neſſamah,ch’è anima diuina, paſ ſa nella natura dell’angelo, et cõ ſeguẽtemẽte ſi traſmuta in Dio: p cio Chriſto aduertẽdo q̃l teſto di Malachia. Eccè ego mitto angelũ meũ, vuol che ſ’intẽda di Iouãni Battiſta traſ ſmutato in angelo nella prouidẽza diuina ab initio & ante ſecula. Ho fatto mentiōn del coltello del verbo di Chriſto, il qual ſolo col ſuo taglio diuiſde l’aia baſſa, dall’aia rationale, la quale habbiam detto hauer il nome dello ſpirito. La onde Paolo diſſe. Vivus eſt ſermo Dei, et efficax, et penetratior oĩ gladio anceps pertingens vſque ad diuisionem animae & ſpiritus & a fin che riconoſciamo le dette tre aie ciaſcuna\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO.\n\nCon nome diuerso nelle parole di Moſe ſopra ſtorche nel Geneſi, è da notare che quando diſſe, faciamus hominem, inteſe dell’ anima rationale. Et quando poſuit eum in animam viuentem, inteſe della Nephes, ma dicendo, flauit in nares eius, ſpiraculum vitæ, ſignificò la Neſſamah. Non poſſo ſar-\nch’io non metta ſopra queſti paſſaggi la openion dello ſcrittor del Zoar. La Nephes eſſer vn certo ſimulachro, o vero ombra noſtra, laqual non ſi parte mai da ſe poletri, & laſ-\nciaſi non ſolamente la notte, ma anchor di giorno da quelli a quali Dio ha aperti gli occhi. Et percioche il detto ſcrittor dimorò all’heremo per quaranta anni con ſette compagni, & con vn ſigliuolo per cagion di illuminar la ſcritttu-\nra ſanta, e dice, che vn giorno vide ad vno de ſuoi ſanti, & cari compagni diſſaccata la Nephes talmente, che gli ſtace ua di dietro ombra al capo: et poi che di qui s’auide, che queſto era il nuncio de la vicina morte di colui. ma con molti di giuni, & orationi ottenne da Dio, che la detta ſtaccata Nephes da capo al corpo ſuo ſi ricongionſe, & coſì vnita reſtò per fin al fine della impreſa. Il qual luogo da me veduto, mi fa penſare, che Virgilio toccando la vicina morte di Marcello, ſi ſia ſeruito di quello: & che o da Hebrei, o da Caldei Cabaliſti hauesse inteſo vn tal ſecreto. Appreſſo dice il detto ſcrittor del Zoar, che queſta Nephes è preſente dal principio alla formation dell’Embrione. Ma che la Ruach non entra ſe non il ſettimo giorno dopo la na-\ntiuìtà, & che perciò Dio comanda che il fanciullo ſia appre-\nſentato a lui, & alla circonciſione l’ottauo dì, ciò è vn giorno da poi che l’anima rationale ha fatta l’entrata: & quantunque la Neſſamah non entri, ſe non al trigeſimo giorno,\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n31\n\nnon ſi hauere ad aſpettar tanto à far la circonciſione, alla qual non debbono interuenir ſe non l’anima, che puo peccà-\nre, & quella che ſa peccar, che la Naſſamah eſſendo diuina nò non puo peccare: & in queſto paſſaggio coſi conſente Plotino intendendo della terza anima alta, quando dice. In anima non cadit peccatum, neque pœna. Ha ben uoluto il bello ingegno di Ariſtotele prender fatiche intorno ad una altra triplicità, che è nell’huomo interiore, ma in quella nò pone ſe non quella terza alta: impercioche diſputando dot-\ntiſſimamente de tre intelletti noſtri, chiama l’uno poſſibile, o uer paſſibile chiamato da noſtri latini, & uolgar ingé-\ngno, altramente da Cicerone intelligentiæuis. L’altro intelletto in hauere, che è l’intelletto pratico, ſignificando hauer già appreſſo, & poſſedere. Il terzo intelletto agente, & è quello per uirtù del quale noi intendiamo: et in queſto paſ-\nſo ſan Thomaſo, uolendo prouar l’intelletto agente eſſere in noi, ſe ben mi ricorda dall’eſſempio de la potenza noſtra uiſiua, & di quel raggio di fuoco, che dentro a noi riſponde all’occhio, il quale noi aſſai ſouente fregandoci alcun de gli occhi col dito ueggiamo internamente in ſimilitudine di fiamma in rota. per la qual rota fiammeggiante ſpeſſe uol-\nte auiene, che noi ſuegliati, & aprendo gli occhi nella oſcu-\nra notte per piccioliſſimo ſpatio ueggiamo, & diſcerniamo delle coſe ne la camera, la qual rota poi debilitandoſi a poco a poco perde il uigore. Adunque ſi come nell’unico occhio habbiamo il poter uedere, il uedere, & la rota che ci fa uedere, coſi è in noi non ſolamente, l’intelletto, che puo intendere, cio è l’ingegno, o l’intellettiva capacità, che dir la uo-\ngliamo, & eſſo intender, che è l’intelletto pratico, ma an-\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nper l’intelletto agente, cio è quello che fa che intendiamo. La rota di foco di che habbiamo detto ſi legge ne gli oc= chi di Tiberio eſſere ſtata ſi grande, & ſi virtuosa, che per gran pezza diſcerneua nella ſua camera la notte tutte le coſe. La onde ſeguita, che altri l’ha più, & altri meno. Et Ariſtotele quando è diuenta phiſionomiſta dice, che quan= do con difficultà affiſſiamo gli occhi altrui, quel lume da ſignification di ſuturo principe, la onde alcuni antichi han no laſciato ſcritto. gli occhi di Ieſu Chriſto eſſere ſtati coſì fatti. Ma Simplicio volendo dimoſtrare, & prouare in ogni modo queſto intelletto agente eſſer di fuori, dice che egli non altramente è fuori di noi, che è anchora il Sole fuori di noi, che è anchora il Sole fuor della potenza viſiua an= chor che eſſa per lo detto Sole vegga. Adunque ſi come nel l’occhio noſtro ſano è il poter vedere, & anchor tal’hora il vedere, ma il far vedere, che appartiene al Sole, o ad altro ſuo vicario, è di fuori dell’occhio, coſì quantunque nel no= ſtro huomo interiore ſia il poter intendere, cio è l’intelletto poſſibile, o paſſibile, & l’intendere anchor pratico, nondime= no l’intelletto agente che è il raggio diuino, o Angelo o eſſo Dio eſſer fuori di noi. Qui eſſa opinione di Simplicio par che più ſia approuata dalla ſcrittura, & maſſimamẽ te per quel luogo di Dauid. Intellectum tibi dabo, & in= ſtruam te in uia hac qua gradieris. Se adunque Dio ne è il datore, e anchor quello, che lo ſottragge o à tempo o per ſempre. Di che temendo Dauid diſſe. Et ſpiritum ſanctũ tu non ne auferas a me. Et altrove della perpetua ſottratione è ſcritto. Relinquentur domus veſtræ deſertæ. ſegue adun= que che queſto intelletto agente o raggio diuino è fuori di\n\nfuor di\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n32\n\n[illegible]\n\nnoi, & in poteſtà di Dio. Ilquale intelletto i filoſophi ignoranti di Dio il chiamarono ratione, per laquale dico: no l’huomo ſeparato dalle beſtie. Ma nel vero l’huomo è chiamato rationale, o per dir meglio intellectuale per eſſer ſolo fra gli animali capace di queſto intelletto agente, ma quando à Dio non piace darlo, colui che ſe ne uà ſenza non è differente nel dentro dalle beſtie, eſſendo ſcritto nel Salmo. Homo cum in honore eſſet non intellexit come paratus eſt iumentis inſipientibus, & ſimilis factus eſt illis. Con queſto luogo ſ’accorda quello oſcuriſſimo paſſaggio dell’Apocalipſi. Numerus hominis numerus beſtiæ, numerus autem beſtiæ ſex centi ſexaginta ſex. percioche il numero che arriva à mille per la giunta dello intelletto agente è il numero dell’huomo illuminato. Et perciò nella Cantica volendoſi deſiderar be-\nne à chi ſi parla, ſi dice nel Teſto Hebreo. Mille tibi Salo-\nmon. Il che ſignifica. Io ti deſidero non ſolamente la figura humana, ma anchor il raggio diuino. Per la qual coſa quando io ſalutero il mio Eccellentiſſimo Prencipe, in luogo di dargli il buon di, io gli dirò. Mille tibi. Ma mi ri-\nſeruo in altro tempo il dichiarar di queſti numeri. A queſta openione par che ſi conformi anchor Virgilio deſcriuendo il ſuo ramo d’oro, ilquale eſſendo di materia diuersa & molto differente dall’ albero, & non baſtando l’humano volontà ad hauerlo, moſtra che ſia coſa di fuori, & che il fauor di ſommo Dio ci ſia conuenga a conſeguir il dono di queſto noſtro intelletto. Ma tempo è hor mai che noi di-\nſcendiamo alle noſtre imagini, il che faremo ſe prima haueremmo detta una coſa non pure appartenente a i ſuoi\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO.\n\nTheologici ſimboli che ho da dare à queſta porta, ma à tut\nte le imagini del mio Theatro.\n\nAppreſſo gli antichi adunque era in coſtume, che quei philo ſophi medeſimi, i quali inſegnavano & moſtravano le profeſſio ne dottrine à cari diſcepoli, poi che haveano chiaramente, le coprivano di favole, à fin che coſì fatte coperte le teneſſero naſcoſe, & coſì non foſſero prophanate. Il qual coſtume aggiunſe in fino al tempo di Virgilio, il qual nel ſuo dottiſſimo Sileno, ſotto quel nome induce Sirone can tar, cioè manifeſtar chiaramente i principij del mondo a Chromi, & à Naſillo, cioè à Varro & ad eſſo Virgilio. Et poi che quì hà cantati entra in favole, coſa che par molto ſtrana à lettori ignoranti del detto coſtume. Ad imitatione a di quei coſì grādi philoſophi, poi che io ho chiaramente ri velato il ſecreto delle tre aië, et de tre intelletti, coſe appar tenenti all’huomo interiore, io li coprirò de debili ſimboli, à fin che nō ſieno prophanati, et ancor per deſtar la memoria Fra le favole greche adunque ſi legge di tre Sorelle cieche chiamate le Gorgoni, le quali fra loro havevano vn ſolo occhio commutabile fra loro, percioche l’una all’altra il pote va preſtare, & quella che l’haveva tanto vedeva quanto l’ haveva. Nel qual ſimbolo giace tutto il miſterio della veri tà appenta di ſopra, & ci ſi fa intender il raggio diuino eſſer di fuori, & non dentro di noi. Or queſta imagine coprirà tutto l’ordine del quarto grado contenendo ſotto le co ſe appartenenti all’huomo interiore ſecondo la natura di ciaſcun pianeta. Et per venir al particular delle porte. Sot to le Gorgoni della luna ſarà la imagine della Tazza di Bacco, la quale è fra’l Cancro & il Leone. Et ſecondo che\n\nSole,\n\ndicono\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO,\n\n33\n\ndicono i Platonici, le anime che vengono in queſto mondo. ſcendono per la porta del Cancro, & nel ritorno aſcendono per quella del Capricorno: & la porta di Cancro è detta, porta de gli huomini per ſcender l’anime ne corpi mortali, & quella di Capricorno è detta porta de Dei, per tornar el-\nle in ſu alla divinità ſecondo la natura dell’animale, che è ſegno di quella: & è il Cancro caſa della Luna, della quale la intelligenza è Gabriel: & per ſcender egli più volte mandato da Dio, la ſcrittura il chiama huomo, dicendo. Ecce vir Gabriel: & per tornare a Platonici, dicono che le anime en deſcendendo beono dalla Tazza di Bacco, & ſi dimenti-\ncano tutte le coſe di la ſù, chi più & chi meno, ſecondo che ciaſcuna più & meno ne bee. fingeremo adunque un Zodia-\nco in modo che nella ſua più alta & più viſibil parte ſi vegga il Cancro & il Leone, & la Tazza in mezzo con una Vergine inchinata à berne: & queſta imagine conſeruirà ſotto volume pertinente alla humana obliuione (quale che eſſa ſi ſia) co ſuoi conſeguenti neceſſarii, come la ignoranza, & la rozzezza: & queſta imagine alla Luna ſi appartiene per eſſer (come habbiamo detto) la caſa di lei il Cancro, intendendo queſta fanciulla per l’anima in commune di tutto quello che delle tre habbiamo detto.\n\nSotto le Gorgoni di Mercurio ſarà la imagine di una facella acceſa, la quale intendendo noi che ſia quella, che acceſe Prometheo in Cielo con l’aiuto di Pallade, vogliamo che ſignifichi lo ingegno, cio è l’intelletto poſſibile, o paſſibile, & la docilità, di cui il verbo è imparare. Di queſta facella parleremo a pieno nel ſettimo grado, dove di Prometheo tratteremo.\n\nMercurio\n\nSotto le Gorgoni di Venere ſarà coperta la imagine di Eve.\n\nVenere.\n\nL’Idea del Theatro.\n\nE\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nFelice punta nel piede Ioſeppe, & percioche il piede, & in particolare il calcagno o il talone, che dire il vogliamo, ſe gnifica i noſtri affetti gouernati dalla noſtra uolontà, uo-\ngliamo che queſta contenga la humana uolontà, che è una delle potenze dell’ anima, la quale ſi diuiderà in libera & non libera. Et conſentiremo anchor queſta la Nepheſ, & a fine che non ci fugga della memoria, habbiamo a ſaper, che gli Anatomiſti dicono dal talone ai lombi eſſere una tal corriſ-\nſpondenza di alcuni nerui, la qual fa che le ſcritture alcuna uolta piglino l’un per l’altro. Di che Chriſto volendo dir che i noſtri affetti, & la noſtra uolontà ſteſſe caſtigata & monda diſſe. Sint lumbi veſtri præcincti, et anche lauò i pie di nel ſuo partir, ciò è gli affetti à gli Apoſtoli. Alla qual dannatione non volendo conſentir Pietro, gli diſſe. Niſi laue-\nro te non habebis partem mecum. Et nel Geneſi è ſcritto. Et inſidiaberis calcaneo eius. Appreſſo ſi legge nelle fauole Greche Achille fanciullo per eſſere ſtato immerſo nelle acque Stigie, eſſer diuennuto in tutte le parti inulnerabile, ſal-\nuo che ne piedi, per li quali fu tenuto, & doue l’acque non toccarono, il che ſegnifica, che tanto huomo in tutte le parti poteua eſſer coſtante, pur che non foſſe tocco ne gli affetti. Ne ſenza miſtero Giaſone andãdo a rapire il vello dell’oro perdè l’uno de calzari nel fiume unico al mondo ſenza uen-\nto. De piedi di Antheo ripiglianti la forza dalla Terra qua lunque volta la toccaua, ne parleremo al luogo ſuo.\n\nSole.\n\nSotto le Gorgoni Solari copriràſſi la imagine del Ramo d’oro, et q̃ſta ci ſignificherà l’intelletto agente, la Neſſas mah, l’aia in generale, l’aia rationale, lo ſpirito & la vita.\n\nMarte.\n\nSotto le Gorgoni di Marte, ſarà la imagine di una fanci-\nciulla con un piede ſcalzo, & con la teſta ſcinta, & queſta\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n34\n\nſigniſicherà la deliberatione,o vero propoſito fermo, & non lo ſubito,a differenza di quella deliberatione, che è vna coſa iſteſſa co’l conſiglio,la quale è Giouiale: & l’eſſere ſan ta & ſcalza aſſai è inteſo per la dichiaratione de lombi,& del piede di Giaſone ſcalzo:et queſta figura ci eſpreſſe Vir gilio nella ſubita & ferma deliberatione di morire che fece Dido,dicendo di lei,che ella era.\n\nVnum exuta pedem,vinclis in veſte recincta,& da lei hab\nbiamo noi preſa queſta imagine.\n\nSotto le Gorgoni Giouiali,ſarà la imagine di vna Grù, Gioue, che vola verſo il Cielo,portando nel becco vn Caduceo, & laſciandoſi cader da piedi vna pharettra,della quale le ſaet te vſcendo cadono all’ingiù per l’aere ſpargendoſi, quale ho io veduto nel riuerſo d’vna antica medaglia: & la Grù ſignifica l’animo vigilante,il quale già ſtanco del mondo, & de ſuoi inganni,per hauer tranquillità vola verſo il cie lo,portando il Caduceo in bocca, cio è la pace & la tranquillità di lui:& da piedi le cade la pharettra con le ſaette, che ſignificano le cure di queſto mondo. A queſta imagine ſi conforma quel verſo del Salmo. Quis dabit mihi pennas ſi-\ncut columbæ, & volabo,& requieſcam.\n\nIl che tradusse il Petrarcha in un ſuo Sonetto, deſideran do pur l’ale della Colomba da ripoſarſi, & leuarſi di Terra. Queſta gentile imagine ci confermerà la elettione, il giudicio & il conſiglio:& ſi da queſta imagine a Gioue, ſi eſſer Pianeta quieto,benigno,& di mente compoſta.\n\nSotto le Gorgoni di Saturno,ſarà la imagine di Hercole, Saturno al quale leua Antheo ſopra il petto. Hercole è l’vmano ſpirito. Antheo è il corpo. Il petto di Hercole è la ſedia della Sapienza,& della Prudenza,queſti due(come dice Paolo)\n\nE  ii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nſanno continoua lotta, et inceſſabil guerra, percioche di con-\ntinuo la carne riſurge contra lo ſpirito,& lo ſpirito contra la carne,ne puo lo ſpirito eſſer vincitor della battaglia, ſe non leua tanto alto da la terra il corpo,che co piedi, cio e co gli affetti non poſſa ripigliar le forze dalla madre, & tanto lo tenga ſtretto,che l’uccida. doue due coſe principalmente habbiamo a conſiderare,l’una è la morte del corpo, l’altra è quaſi la traſformation di lui ne lo ſpirito:& nel vero ſe’l corpo noſtro non muore della morte de gli affetti , non ſi puo fare ſpirituale , ne farſi vno in Chriſto. Della qual morte coſì parla Paolo. Mortui eſtis,& vita veſtra abſcon-\ndita eſt cum Chriſto in Deo,& Dauid. Precioſa in conſpe-\nctu domini mors ſanctorum eius. Et nel Salmo 62. ſi legge, la carne riuolgere il deſiderio ſuo à Dio al pari dello ſpirito. Sitivit in te anima mea quàm multipliciter tibi caro mea: Et Paolo al terzo a Philippenſi. Deus reformaturus eſt cor-\npus humilitatis veſtræ configurando ipſum corpori cla-\nritatis ſuæ. Et Chriſto nella ſimilitudine della morte del grano. Niſi granum frumenti cadens ad terram mortuum fuerit, ipſum ſolum manet,ſi autem mortuum fuerit, multiù fructum affert. Et ſe ben ſarà conſiderata la noſtra interpreta-\ntione,ſi trouerà che habbiamo anchor manifeſtata la traſmutatione, la quale è l’una delle due coſe da noi propoſte: et ciò gentilmente toccò il Petrarca, quando diſſe. Volando al ciel con la terrena ſoma. Queſta traſmutatione anchora aſſai ſi manifeſta nelle tre cieche ſorelle,le quali hauendo l’occhio non loro, ma di ſuo-\nri,& preſtandoſi l’una all’altra conſentendoſi conforma-\nno inſieme,& diuengono vna coſa iſteſſa come Neſſamah tirata dall’angelo, che tira la Ruàh,& quella la Nepheſ.\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n35\n\nEt coſì ſi fà la traſformatione ſpirituale. Hor queſta imagine ne per ſignificare & tenacità nella ſtrettezza che fa Herco le, & ſollevation da terra in alto, coprirà vn volume, nel qua le ſaranno diſtinte tutte le coſe a queſte parti appartenenti, come le impreſſioni che l’anima porta dal Cielo, la me moria, la ſcienza, la openione, l’intelletto pratico, ciò è l’in tendere, il penſamento, la imaginatione, & la contempla-\ntione. Et à Saturno ſi conviene queſta imagine prima, percioche la medeſima miſura nel ſopracceleſte della Rinā cio è dell’intelletto, è commune à Saturno. Et poi per eſſer co-\nſìa ferma. Vna altra imagine ſarà anchor ſotto queſta por ta, & ciò è vna fanciulla aſcendente per lo Capricorno. Et queſta ſignificherà la aſceſſa delle anime in Cielo. Et que ſta imagine è data à Saturno, per eſſere il Capricorno caſa di lui.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0001","text":"LE GORGONI,","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"4.1"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","text":"SAgliamo al quarto Grado appartenente all’huomo inferiore, il qual fu l’ultimo, & la più nobil creatura fatta da Dio à ſua imagine & ſimilitudine. Et qui è da no tare che nel teſto hebreo quello che è tradotto per imagi ne, è detto Celem, & quello che è detto ſimilitudine, è ſcrit to Demut. Le quali parole nel Zoar di Rabi Simeon, che ſuona illuminator, cioè dator di luce, ſono interpretate in queſto ſenſo, che Celem ſignifichi (per dir coſì) la ſtampa o uer la forma angelica, & Demut importi grado diuino. percioche vuole che Dio non ſolamente traſſe l’anima noſ tra alla eccellenza de gli Angeli ma anchor le aggiunſe eſſo il grado diuino.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"4.2"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","text":"Et aggiunſe il detto autor del Zoar che eſſo antivedendo l’angelo, che fu poi ſcacciato, moſſo da inuidia, & dall’amor proprio, parlò contra il voler della diuina Maeſtà ma Mercurio Triſmegisto nel ſuo Pimandro prende la imagine & la ſimilitudine per vna coſa iſteſſa, & il tutto per lo grado diuino, dicendo coſì. At pater omni um intellectus, vita, & fulgor exiſtens, hominem ſibi ſimi lem procreauit, atque ei tanquam filio ſua congratulatus eſt pulcher enim erat, patriſque ſui ferebat imaginem. Deus enim re vera propria forma nimium delectatus opera eius omnia vſui conceſſit humano. Et il medefi mo nello Aſclepio. O Aſclepi magnum miraculum eſt homo, animal adorandum atque honorandum, hoc enim in naturam Dei tranſit, quaſi ipſe ſit Deus, hoc dæmonum genus nouit, vt pote qui eorum eiſdem ora.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"4.3"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0004","text":"D  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"4.4"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0005","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"4.5"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0006","text":"3.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"4.6"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","text":"cum eſſe cognoscat, hoc humanæ naturæ partem in ſe ipſo deſpiciat, alterius partis divinitatis confuſus. Altri ſcrittori Cabaliſti hanno laſciato ſcritto la ſimilitudine appartenersi alla operatione, quaſi volendo dir Dio hauer fatto l’huomo à fine di operar per lui: & con queſta opinione conſente la ſcrittura ſanta,doue ſi mention le opere buone,che faccia: ma non eſſer noſtre,ma di Dio, & noi eſſer ſolamente gli iſtrumenti. La onde alcuni contemplatiui chiamano queſte opere,opere eterne. Di che Paolo dice. Quid habes homo, quod non accepiſti? Et ſi accepiſti quare gloriaris quaſi nō acceperis, & è da notar che le più delle fiate quando la Scrittura fa mention dell’huomo,intende ſolamente dell’interiore,il che chiaramente ſi truoua nel libro di Moſe intito-\nlato Iob.che dice.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"4.7"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","text":"Pelle & carnibus veſtijſti me, oſſibus & nervis compegiſti me, per le quali parole, & per quel prono me, me, dà chiaramente ad intendere altro eſſer l’huomo interiore dall’eſteriore. In queſta opinione viene Socrate nel ſuo primo Alcibiade appreſſo Platone,diſputando della na tura dell’huomo,percioche ſi come la veſta che portiamo nō è noi,ma coſa vſata da noi,coſì il corpo anchor che ſia por-\ntato da noi non è noi,ma coſa vſata da noi: per la qual coſa ſono da eſſer conſiderate le parole di Moſe nel Geneſi,facia mus hominem ad imaginem & ſimilitudinem noſtram, le quali non ſuonano ſe non l’interior huomo: & che vero ſia, aliquanto ſotto ſoggiunſe. Nondum erat homo qui operare tur in terra.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"4.8"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","text":"Era adunque avanti nel ſopraceleſte fatto l’huo mo interiore,che Dio gli formaſſe il corpo di terra a fin che poteſſe operar in queſto mondo & eſſere iſtrumento delle opere diuine: & perciò Moſe ſoggiunſe. Plaſmauit Deus ho","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"4.9"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0010","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"4.10"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0011","text":"29","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"4.11"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0012","text":"ſimilem de limo terræ, il qual limo non ſignifica fango (come molti auuiſino) ma il fior, & (per dir coſì) il capo di lat-\nte de la terra, che era Virginale, percioche non haueua anchor contratto macchia, ſi come contraſſe quaſi famiglia di Adam doppo il peccato di lui. La qual terra virginale era chiamata Adama: onde Adam traſſe il nome. Ne queſto ta-\nccò che Chriſto per ſodisfare alla giuſtitia diuina, ſi appre-\nſentò per purgator di tutte le humane colpe in corpo con ſi-\nmile à quello che haueua Adam prima che peccaſſe, cioè in corpo fatto di terra Verginale, & di ſangue puriſſimo di Maria Vergine.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"4.12"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0013","text":"Adam.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"4.13"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","text":"A queſte coſe ſi aggiunga, poi che à parlar di Adam ſiamo entrati, che egli auanti il peccato era in due modi nell’horto delle delitie, non dico Paradiſo Terreſtre, come molti inter-\npretano quel che Moſè non diſſe già mai. Nel primo modo, Adam que era nell’horto ſopraceleſte non preſentialmente, ma terreſtre, nella gratia di Dio godendo di tutti i beati influſſi, ma come hebbe peccato coſì fu cacciato del detto horto ſopraceleſte. et ciò è, che leuati li furono i già detti influſſi, non che eſſo corporalmente foſſe mandato fuori non altramente che ſe un ſeruidor prima à Ceſare gratiſſimo in Egitto ſi ritroue-\nuaſſe, mentre egli foſſe nella gratia del Prencipe ſuo, ſi di-\nrebbe che foſſe nella ſua famiglia, ma peccando priuo della gratia ſua ſi potrebbe dir che foſſe cacciato dalla Corte.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"4.14"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0015","text":"Ne ſi marauigli alcuno che io metta queſta queſtione in capo, che l’horto del quale fu cacciato Adam foſſe il ſopraceleſte giardino, percioche queſta fu opinione prima di Orige-\ngene, & poi di Hieronimo ſuo ſeguitatore. L’altro modo di dire che Adam era in paradiſo, ſare ſecondo il vocabolo,","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"4.15"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0016","text":"Paradiſo","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"4.16"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0017","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"4.17"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","text":"non hebreo, ma greco, & dichiamo che Adam auanti il peccato era nella terra virginal di queſto mondo. Et mentre dimorò in quella ſenza macular il corpo ſuo di peccato era in paradiſo terreſtro. Et fatto il peccato la terra contræ heſſe macchia, & coſì venne ad eſſer cacciato del paradiſo. Auienne adunque al mondo fatto per Adam quel che potreb be auenire ad vn Baron di Ceſare, il quale ſe peccaſſe, tut-\nta la ſua famiglia verrebbe à contragger macchia anchor che ella non haueſſe peccato, & tutti la guarderebbono con occhio torto. Peccando adunque Adam peccarono tutti gli Elementi per contraction di macchia. Di che in loro non eſſendo più la prima virginità, ſi può dire che per queſta ragione Adam ſia detto eſſere ſtato cacciato dal terreſtro paradiſo.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"4.18"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0019","text":"In ani-\nme no-\nſtre.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"4.19"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","text":"Ma ſeguendo il propoſito noſtro è da ſapere che in noi ſono tre anime le quali tutte tre quantunque godano di queſto nome comune animo, nondimeno ciaſcuna ha anchor il ſuo nome particolare. Impercioche la più baſſa, & vicina, & com-\npagna del corpo noſtro è chiamata Nephes, & è queſta altramente detta da Moſe anima viuens. Et queſta percioche in lei capeno tutte le noſtre paſſioni, la habbiamo noi comune con le beſtie. Et di queſta parla Chriſto quando dice. Triſ-\nſis eſt anima mea vſque ad mortem. Et altroue, qui non ha-\nbuerit odio animam ſuam perdet eam. Al qual vocabolo, no-\naſſpirando la lingua ne greca, ne latina non ſi può rappre-\nſentar nelle traductioni la ſua ſignificatione, come (per eſ-\nempio) in quel Salmo. Lauda anima mea dominum: quantunque lo ſcrittor dello Spirito Santo habbia poſto il vocabolo di Nephes, ci fanno vſare il comune. Et fu ben ra","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"4.20"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0021","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"4.21"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0022","text":"30","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"4.22"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0023","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"4.23"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","text":"glione che il Propheta vſaſſe il vocabolo Nephes volendo lodar Dio con la lingua & con altri membri che formano la voce, & ſono gouernati dalla Nephes, che è più vicina alla carne. L’anima di mezo, che è la rationale, è chiamata col nome dello ſpirito, cioè Ruach. La terza è detta Neſ ſamah. Da Moſe ſpiraculo, da Dauid & da Pithagora ila me, da Apollino portio ſuperiore, da Platone mente, da Ariſtotele intelletto agente. Et ſi come la Nephes ha il dia-\nuolo, che le miniſtra dimonio per tentatore, coſì la Neſſamah ha Dio che le miniſtra l’angelo. La pouerella di mezo da amendue le parti è ſtimolata. Et ſe per diuina permiſſione ſ’inchina à far vnione cõ la Nephes, la Nephes ſi vniſce cõ la carne et la carne col dimonio, et il tutto fa traſſito et traſ mutatione in diavolo, per la qual coſa diſſe Chriſto. Ego ele gi vos duodecim, et Vnus ex vobis diabolus eſt.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"4.24"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","text":"Ma ſe per la gratia di Chriſto(da altrui nō puo venire vn tanto benefi tio)la anima di mezo ſi diſſacca quaſi p lo taglio del coltel lo della parola di Chriſto dalla Nephes mal perſuaſa, et ſi vniſce cõ la Neſſamah, la Neſſamah,ch’è anima diuina, paſ ſa nella natura dell’angelo, et cõ ſeguẽtemẽte ſi traſmuta in Dio: p cio Chriſto aduertẽdo q̃l teſto di Malachia. Eccè ego mitto angelũ meũ, vuol che ſ’intẽda di Iouãni Battiſta traſ ſmutato in angelo nella prouidẽza diuina ab initio & ante ſecula. Ho fatto mentiōn del coltello del verbo di Chriſto, il qual ſolo col ſuo taglio diuiſde l’aia baſſa, dall’aia rationale, la quale habbiam detto hauer il nome dello ſpirito. La onde Paolo diſſe. Vivus eſt ſermo Dei, et efficax, et penetratior oĩ gladio anceps pertingens vſque ad diuisionem animae & ſpiritus & a fin che riconoſciamo le dette tre aie ciaſcuna","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"4.25"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0026","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"4.26"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0027","text":"Con nome diuerso nelle parole di Moſe ſopra ſtorche nel Geneſi, è da notare che quando diſſe, faciamus hominem, inteſe dell’ anima rationale. Et quando poſuit eum in animam viuentem, inteſe della Nephes, ma dicendo, flauit in nares eius, ſpiraculum vitæ, ſignificò la Neſſamah. Non poſſo ſar-\nch’io non metta ſopra queſti paſſaggi la openion dello ſcrittor del Zoar. La Nephes eſſer vn certo ſimulachro, o vero ombra noſtra, laqual non ſi parte mai da ſe poletri, & laſ-\nciaſi non ſolamente la notte, ma anchor di giorno da quelli a quali Dio ha aperti gli occhi.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"4.27"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0028","text":"Et percioche il detto ſcrittor dimorò all’heremo per quaranta anni con ſette compagni, & con vn ſigliuolo per cagion di illuminar la ſcritttu-\nra ſanta, e dice, che vn giorno vide ad vno de ſuoi ſanti, & cari compagni diſſaccata la Nephes talmente, che gli ſtace ua di dietro ombra al capo: et poi che di qui s’auide, che queſto era il nuncio de la vicina morte di colui. ma con molti di giuni, & orationi ottenne da Dio, che la detta ſtaccata Nephes da capo al corpo ſuo ſi ricongionſe, & coſì vnita reſtò per fin al fine della impreſa. Il qual luogo da me veduto, mi fa penſare, che Virgilio toccando la vicina morte di Marcello, ſi ſia ſeruito di quello: & che o da Hebrei, o da Caldei Cabaliſti hauesse inteſo vn tal ſecreto. Appreſſo dice il detto ſcrittor del Zoar, che queſta Nephes è preſente dal principio alla formation dell’Embrione.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"4.28"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0029","text":"Ma che la Ruach non entra ſe non il ſettimo giorno dopo la na-\ntiuìtà, & che perciò Dio comanda che il fanciullo ſia appre-\nſentato a lui, & alla circonciſione l’ottauo dì, ciò è vn giorno da poi che l’anima rationale ha fatta l’entrata: & quantunque la Neſſamah non entri, ſe non al trigeſimo giorno,","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"4.29"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0030","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"4.30"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0031","text":"31","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"4.31"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","text":"non ſi hauere ad aſpettar tanto à far la circonciſione, alla qual non debbono interuenir ſe non l’anima, che puo peccà-\nre, & quella che ſa peccar, che la Naſſamah eſſendo diuina nò non puo peccare: & in queſto paſſaggio coſi conſente Plotino intendendo della terza anima alta, quando dice. In anima non cadit peccatum, neque pœna. Ha ben uoluto il bello ingegno di Ariſtotele prender fatiche intorno ad una altra triplicità, che è nell’huomo interiore, ma in quella nò pone ſe non quella terza alta: impercioche diſputando dot-\ntiſſimamente de tre intelletti noſtri, chiama l’uno poſſibile, o uer paſſibile chiamato da noſtri latini, & uolgar ingé-\ngno, altramente da Cicerone intelligentiæuis. L’altro intelletto in hauere, che è l’intelletto pratico, ſignificando hauer già appreſſo, & poſſedere.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"4.32"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0033","text":"Il terzo intelletto agente, & è quello per uirtù del quale noi intendiamo: et in queſto paſ-\nſo ſan Thomaſo, uolendo prouar l’intelletto agente eſſere in noi, ſe ben mi ricorda dall’eſſempio de la potenza noſtra uiſiua, & di quel raggio di fuoco, che dentro a noi riſponde all’occhio, il quale noi aſſai ſouente fregandoci alcun de gli occhi col dito ueggiamo internamente in ſimilitudine di fiamma in rota. per la qual rota fiammeggiante ſpeſſe uol-\nte auiene, che noi ſuegliati, & aprendo gli occhi nella oſcu-\nra notte per piccioliſſimo ſpatio ueggiamo, & diſcerniamo delle coſe ne la camera, la qual rota poi debilitandoſi a poco a poco perde il uigore.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"4.33"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0034","text":"Adunque ſi come nell’unico occhio habbiamo il poter uedere, il uedere, & la rota che ci fa uedere, coſi è in noi non ſolamente, l’intelletto, che puo intendere, cio è l’ingegno, o l’intellettiva capacità, che dir la uo-\ngliamo, & eſſo intender, che è l’intelletto pratico, ma an-","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"4.34"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0035","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"4.35"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0036","text":"per l’intelletto agente, cio è quello che fa che intendiamo. La rota di foco di che habbiamo detto ſi legge ne gli oc= chi di Tiberio eſſere ſtata ſi grande, & ſi virtuosa, che per gran pezza diſcerneua nella ſua camera la notte tutte le coſe. La onde ſeguita, che altri l’ha più, & altri meno. Et Ariſtotele quando è diuenta phiſionomiſta dice, che quan= do con difficultà affiſſiamo gli occhi altrui, quel lume da ſignification di ſuturo principe, la onde alcuni antichi han no laſciato ſcritto. gli occhi di Ieſu Chriſto eſſere ſtati coſì fatti. Ma Simplicio volendo dimoſtrare, & prouare in ogni modo queſto intelletto agente eſſer di fuori, dice che egli non altramente è fuori di noi, che è anchora il Sole fuori di noi, che è anchora il Sole fuor della potenza viſiua an= chor che eſſa per lo detto Sole vegga.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"4.36"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","text":"Adunque ſi come nel l’occhio noſtro ſano è il poter vedere, & anchor tal’hora il vedere, ma il far vedere, che appartiene al Sole, o ad altro ſuo vicario, è di fuori dell’occhio, coſì quantunque nel no= ſtro huomo interiore ſia il poter intendere, cio è l’intelletto poſſibile, o paſſibile, & l’intendere anchor pratico, nondime= no l’intelletto agente che è il raggio diuino, o Angelo o eſſo Dio eſſer fuori di noi. Qui eſſa opinione di Simplicio par che più ſia approuata dalla ſcrittura, & maſſimamẽ te per quel luogo di Dauid. Intellectum tibi dabo, & in= ſtruam te in uia hac qua gradieris. Se adunque Dio ne è il datore, e anchor quello, che lo ſottragge o à tempo o per ſempre. Di che temendo Dauid diſſe. Et ſpiritum ſanctũ tu non ne auferas a me. Et altrove della perpetua ſottratione è ſcritto. Relinquentur domus veſtræ deſertæ.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"4.37"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0038","text":"ſegue adun= que che queſto intelletto agente o raggio diuino è fuori di","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"4.38"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0039","text":"fuor di","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"4.39"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0040","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"4.40"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0041","text":"32","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"4.41"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0042","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"4.42"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","text":"noi, & in poteſtà di Dio. Ilquale intelletto i filoſophi ignoranti di Dio il chiamarono ratione, per laquale dico: no l’huomo ſeparato dalle beſtie. Ma nel vero l’huomo è chiamato rationale, o per dir meglio intellectuale per eſſer ſolo fra gli animali capace di queſto intelletto agente, ma quando à Dio non piace darlo, colui che ſe ne uà ſenza non è differente nel dentro dalle beſtie, eſſendo ſcritto nel Salmo. Homo cum in honore eſſet non intellexit come paratus eſt iumentis inſipientibus, & ſimilis factus eſt illis. Con queſto luogo ſ’accorda quello oſcuriſſimo paſſaggio dell’Apocalipſi. Numerus hominis numerus beſtiæ, numerus autem beſtiæ ſex centi ſexaginta ſex. percioche il numero che arriva à mille per la giunta dello intelletto agente è il numero dell’huomo illuminato. Et perciò nella Cantica volendoſi deſiderar be-\nne à chi ſi parla, ſi dice nel Teſto Hebreo.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"4.43"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","text":"Mille tibi Salo-\nmon. Il che ſignifica. Io ti deſidero non ſolamente la figura humana, ma anchor il raggio diuino. Per la qual coſa quando io ſalutero il mio Eccellentiſſimo Prencipe, in luogo di dargli il buon di, io gli dirò. Mille tibi. Ma mi ri-\nſeruo in altro tempo il dichiarar di queſti numeri. A queſta openione par che ſi conformi anchor Virgilio deſcriuendo il ſuo ramo d’oro, ilquale eſſendo di materia diuersa & molto differente dall’ albero, & non baſtando l’humano volontà ad hauerlo, moſtra che ſia coſa di fuori, & che il fauor di ſommo Dio ci ſia conuenga a conſeguir il dono di queſto noſtro intelletto. Ma tempo è hor mai che noi di-\nſcendiamo alle noſtre imagini, il che faremo ſe prima haueremmo detta una coſa non pure appartenente a i ſuoi","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"4.44"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0045","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"4.45"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0046","text":"Theologici ſimboli che ho da dare à queſta porta, ma à tut\nte le imagini del mio Theatro.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"4.46"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","text":"Appreſſo gli antichi adunque era in coſtume, che quei philo ſophi medeſimi, i quali inſegnavano & moſtravano le profeſſio ne dottrine à cari diſcepoli, poi che haveano chiaramente, le coprivano di favole, à fin che coſì fatte coperte le teneſſero naſcoſe, & coſì non foſſero prophanate. Il qual coſtume aggiunſe in fino al tempo di Virgilio, il qual nel ſuo dottiſſimo Sileno, ſotto quel nome induce Sirone can tar, cioè manifeſtar chiaramente i principij del mondo a Chromi, & à Naſillo, cioè à Varro & ad eſſo Virgilio. Et poi che quì hà cantati entra in favole, coſa che par molto ſtrana à lettori ignoranti del detto coſtume.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"4.47"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","text":"Ad imitatione a di quei coſì grādi philoſophi, poi che io ho chiaramente ri velato il ſecreto delle tre aië, et de tre intelletti, coſe appar tenenti all’huomo interiore, io li coprirò de debili ſimboli, à fin che nō ſieno prophanati, et ancor per deſtar la memoria Fra le favole greche adunque ſi legge di tre Sorelle cieche chiamate le Gorgoni, le quali fra loro havevano vn ſolo occhio commutabile fra loro, percioche l’una all’altra il pote va preſtare, & quella che l’haveva tanto vedeva quanto l’ haveva. Nel qual ſimbolo giace tutto il miſterio della veri tà appenta di ſopra, & ci ſi fa intender il raggio diuino eſſer di fuori, & non dentro di noi. Or queſta imagine coprirà tutto l’ordine del quarto grado contenendo ſotto le co ſe appartenenti all’huomo interiore ſecondo la natura di ciaſcun pianeta. Et per venir al particular delle porte.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"4.48"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0049","text":"Sot to le Gorgoni della luna ſarà la imagine della Tazza di Bacco, la quale è fra’l Cancro & il Leone. Et ſecondo che","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"4.49"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0050","text":"Sole,","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"4.50"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0051","text":"dicono","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"4.51"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0052","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO,","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"4.52"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0053","text":"33","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"4.53"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0054","text":"dicono i Platonici, le anime che vengono in queſto mondo. ſcendono per la porta del Cancro, & nel ritorno aſcendono per quella del Capricorno: & la porta di Cancro è detta, porta de gli huomini per ſcender l’anime ne corpi mortali, & quella di Capricorno è detta porta de Dei, per tornar el-\nle in ſu alla divinità ſecondo la natura dell’animale, che è ſegno di quella: & è il Cancro caſa della Luna, della quale la intelligenza è Gabriel: & per ſcender egli più volte mandato da Dio, la ſcrittura il chiama huomo, dicendo. Ecce vir Gabriel: & per tornare a Platonici, dicono che le anime en deſcendendo beono dalla Tazza di Bacco, & ſi dimenti-\ncano tutte le coſe di la ſù, chi più & chi meno, ſecondo che ciaſcuna più & meno ne bee.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"4.54"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055","text":"fingeremo adunque un Zodia-\nco in modo che nella ſua più alta & più viſibil parte ſi vegga il Cancro & il Leone, & la Tazza in mezzo con una Vergine inchinata à berne: & queſta imagine conſeruirà ſotto volume pertinente alla humana obliuione (quale che eſſa ſi ſia) co ſuoi conſeguenti neceſſarii, come la ignoranza, & la rozzezza: & queſta imagine alla Luna ſi appartiene per eſſer (come habbiamo detto) la caſa di lei il Cancro, intendendo queſta fanciulla per l’anima in commune di tutto quello che delle tre habbiamo detto.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"4.55"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056","text":"Sotto le Gorgoni di Mercurio ſarà la imagine di una facella acceſa, la quale intendendo noi che ſia quella, che acceſe Prometheo in Cielo con l’aiuto di Pallade, vogliamo che ſignifichi lo ingegno, cio è l’intelletto poſſibile, o paſſibile, & la docilità, di cui il verbo è imparare. Di queſta facella parleremo a pieno nel ſettimo grado, dove di Prometheo tratteremo.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"4.56"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0057","text":"Mercurio","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"4.57"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058","text":"Sotto le Gorgoni di Venere ſarà coperta la imagine di Eve.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"4.58"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0059","text":"Venere.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"4.59"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0060","text":"L’Idea del Theatro.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"4.60"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0061","text":"E\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"4.61"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062","text":"Felice punta nel piede Ioſeppe, & percioche il piede, & in particolare il calcagno o il talone, che dire il vogliamo, ſe gnifica i noſtri affetti gouernati dalla noſtra uolontà, uo-\ngliamo che queſta contenga la humana uolontà, che è una delle potenze dell’ anima, la quale ſi diuiderà in libera & non libera. Et conſentiremo anchor queſta la Nepheſ, & a fine che non ci fugga della memoria, habbiamo a ſaper, che gli Anatomiſti dicono dal talone ai lombi eſſere una tal corriſ-\nſpondenza di alcuni nerui, la qual fa che le ſcritture alcuna uolta piglino l’un per l’altro. Di che Chriſto volendo dir che i noſtri affetti, & la noſtra uolontà ſteſſe caſtigata & monda diſſe. Sint lumbi veſtri præcincti, et anche lauò i pie di nel ſuo partir, ciò è gli affetti à gli Apoſtoli. Alla qual dannatione non volendo conſentir Pietro, gli diſſe. Niſi laue-\nro te non habebis partem mecum.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"4.62"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0063","text":"Et nel Geneſi è ſcritto. Et inſidiaberis calcaneo eius. Appreſſo ſi legge nelle fauole Greche Achille fanciullo per eſſere ſtato immerſo nelle acque Stigie, eſſer diuennuto in tutte le parti inulnerabile, ſal-\nuo che ne piedi, per li quali fu tenuto, & doue l’acque non toccarono, il che ſegnifica, che tanto huomo in tutte le parti poteua eſſer coſtante, pur che non foſſe tocco ne gli affetti. Ne ſenza miſtero Giaſone andãdo a rapire il vello dell’oro perdè l’uno de calzari nel fiume unico al mondo ſenza uen-\nto. De piedi di Antheo ripiglianti la forza dalla Terra qua lunque volta la toccaua, ne parleremo al luogo ſuo.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"4.63"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0064","text":"Sole.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"4.64"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065","text":"Sotto le Gorgoni Solari copriràſſi la imagine del Ramo d’oro, et q̃ſta ci ſignificherà l’intelletto agente, la Neſſas mah, l’aia in generale, l’aia rationale, lo ſpirito & la vita.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"4.65"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0066","text":"Marte.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"4.66"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067","text":"Sotto le Gorgoni di Marte, ſarà la imagine di una fanci-\nciulla con un piede ſcalzo, & con la teſta ſcinta, & queſta","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"4.67"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0068","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"4.68"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0069","text":"34","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"4.69"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070","text":"ſigniſicherà la deliberatione,o vero propoſito fermo, & non lo ſubito,a differenza di quella deliberatione, che è vna coſa iſteſſa co’l conſiglio,la quale è Giouiale: & l’eſſere ſan ta & ſcalza aſſai è inteſo per la dichiaratione de lombi,& del piede di Giaſone ſcalzo:et queſta figura ci eſpreſſe Vir gilio nella ſubita & ferma deliberatione di morire che fece Dido,dicendo di lei,che ella era.","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"4.70"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0071","text":"Vnum exuta pedem,vinclis in veſte recincta,& da lei hab\nbiamo noi preſa queſta imagine.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"4.71"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072","text":"Sotto le Gorgoni Giouiali,ſarà la imagine di vna Grù, Gioue, che vola verſo il Cielo,portando nel becco vn Caduceo, & laſciandoſi cader da piedi vna pharettra,della quale le ſaet te vſcendo cadono all’ingiù per l’aere ſpargendoſi, quale ho io veduto nel riuerſo d’vna antica medaglia: & la Grù ſignifica l’animo vigilante,il quale già ſtanco del mondo, & de ſuoi inganni,per hauer tranquillità vola verſo il cie lo,portando il Caduceo in bocca, cio è la pace & la tranquillità di lui:& da piedi le cade la pharettra con le ſaette, che ſignificano le cure di queſto mondo. A queſta imagine ſi conforma quel verſo del Salmo. Quis dabit mihi pennas ſi-\ncut columbæ, & volabo,& requieſcam.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"4.72"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0073","text":"Il che tradusse il Petrarcha in un ſuo Sonetto, deſideran do pur l’ale della Colomba da ripoſarſi, & leuarſi di Terra. Queſta gentile imagine ci confermerà la elettione, il giudicio & il conſiglio:& ſi da queſta imagine a Gioue, ſi eſſer Pianeta quieto,benigno,& di mente compoſta.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"4.73"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074","text":"Sotto le Gorgoni di Saturno,ſarà la imagine di Hercole, Saturno al quale leua Antheo ſopra il petto. Hercole è l’vmano ſpirito. Antheo è il corpo. Il petto di Hercole è la ſedia della Sapienza,& della Prudenza,queſti due(come dice Paolo)","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"4.74"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0075","text":"E  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"4.75"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0076","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"4.76"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","text":"ſanno continoua lotta, et inceſſabil guerra, percioche di con-\ntinuo la carne riſurge contra lo ſpirito,& lo ſpirito contra la carne,ne puo lo ſpirito eſſer vincitor della battaglia, ſe non leua tanto alto da la terra il corpo,che co piedi, cio e co gli affetti non poſſa ripigliar le forze dalla madre, & tanto lo tenga ſtretto,che l’uccida. doue due coſe principalmente habbiamo a conſiderare,l’una è la morte del corpo, l’altra è quaſi la traſformation di lui ne lo ſpirito:& nel vero ſe’l corpo noſtro non muore della morte de gli affetti , non ſi puo fare ſpirituale , ne farſi vno in Chriſto. Della qual morte coſì parla Paolo. Mortui eſtis,& vita veſtra abſcon-\ndita eſt cum Chriſto in Deo,& Dauid. Precioſa in conſpe-\nctu domini mors ſanctorum eius. Et nel Salmo 62. ſi legge, la carne riuolgere il deſiderio ſuo à Dio al pari dello ſpirito.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"4.77"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","text":"Sitivit in te anima mea quàm multipliciter tibi caro mea: Et Paolo al terzo a Philippenſi. Deus reformaturus eſt cor-\npus humilitatis veſtræ configurando ipſum corpori cla-\nritatis ſuæ. Et Chriſto nella ſimilitudine della morte del grano. Niſi granum frumenti cadens ad terram mortuum fuerit, ipſum ſolum manet,ſi autem mortuum fuerit, multiù fructum affert. Et ſe ben ſarà conſiderata la noſtra interpreta-\ntione,ſi trouerà che habbiamo anchor manifeſtata la traſmutatione, la quale è l’una delle due coſe da noi propoſte: et ciò gentilmente toccò il Petrarca, quando diſſe. Volando al ciel con la terrena ſoma. Queſta traſmutatione anchora aſſai ſi manifeſta nelle tre cieche ſorelle,le quali hauendo l’occhio non loro, ma di ſuo-\nri,& preſtandoſi l’una all’altra conſentendoſi conforma-\nno inſieme,& diuengono vna coſa iſteſſa come Neſſamah tirata dall’angelo, che tira la Ruàh,& quella la Nepheſ.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"4.78"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0079","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"4.79"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0080","text":"35","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"4.80"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","text":"Et coſì ſi fà la traſformatione ſpirituale. Hor queſta imagine ne per ſignificare & tenacità nella ſtrettezza che fa Herco le, & ſollevation da terra in alto, coprirà vn volume, nel qua le ſaranno diſtinte tutte le coſe a queſte parti appartenenti, come le impreſſioni che l’anima porta dal Cielo, la me moria, la ſcienza, la openione, l’intelletto pratico, ciò è l’in tendere, il penſamento, la imaginatione, & la contempla-\ntione. Et à Saturno ſi conviene queſta imagine prima, percioche la medeſima miſura nel ſopracceleſte della Rinā cio è dell’intelletto, è commune à Saturno. Et poi per eſſer co-\nſìa ferma. Vna altra imagine ſarà anchor ſotto queſta por ta, & ciò è vna fanciulla aſcendente per lo Capricorno. Et queſta ſignificherà la aſceſſa delle anime in Cielo. Et que ſta imagine è data à Saturno, per eſſere il Capricorno caſa di lui.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"4.81"}],"sha256":"80f6e97fb40a8b7738785f65128dbefd0cf3dfb106bb21336f87a44a7cbb7b43","language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261030T230613212029Z_ece4ebea","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE GORGONS,","source_sha256":"80f6e97fb40a8b7738785f65128dbefd0cf3dfb106bb21336f87a44a7cbb7b43","sha256":"248f6a0f58bcb5b1973c984a0ded7b47755e7e8ae2bfb3a9eb8fa7d6d5c9966e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:06:13.212098+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0001","text":"THE GORGONS,","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"4.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","text":"Let us ascend to the fourth Grade belonging to the lower man, which was the last, and the noblest creature made by God in His image and likeness. And here it should be noted that in the Hebrew text that which is translated as image is called Celem, and that which is called likeness is written Demut. These words in the Zoar of Rabbi Simeon, which means illuminator, that is, giver of light, are interpreted in this sense: that Celem signifies (so to speak) the imprint or angelic form, and Demut imports divine grade; for he would have it that God not only drew our soul up to the excellence of the Angels, but Himself also added to it the divine grade.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"4.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","text":"And the said author of the Zoar added that He foresaw the angel who was afterwards cast out, moved by envy and self-love, speaking against the will of the divine Majesty. But Mercurius Trismegistus, in his Pimander, takes image and likeness as one and the same thing, and all of it as the divine grade, saying thus: At pater omni um intellectus, vita, & fulgor exiſtens, hominem ſibi ſimi lem procreauit, atque ei tanquam filio ſua congratulatus eſt pulcher enim erat, patriſque ſui ferebat imaginem. Deus enim re vera propria forma nimium delectatus opera eius omnia vſui conceſſit humano. And the same in the Asclepius: O Aſclepi magnum miraculum eſt homo, animal adorandum atque honorandum, hoc enim in naturam Dei tranſit, quaſi ipſe ſit Deus, hoc dæmonum genus nouit, vt pote qui eorum eiſdem ora.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"4.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0004","text":"D iii","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"4.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0005","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"4.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0006","text":"3.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"4.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","text":"cum eſſe cognoscat, hoc humanæ naturæ partem in ſe ipſo deſpiciat, alterius partis divinitatis confuſus. Other Cabalistic writers have left it written that likeness belongs to operation, as though wishing to say that God made man in order to operate through him; and with this opinion Holy Scripture agrees, where mention is made of the good works that he performs: but that they are not ours, but God's, and that we are merely the instruments. Whence some contemplatives call these works eternal works. Of which Paul says: Quid habes homo, quod non accepiſti? Et ſi accepiſti quare gloriaris quaſi nō acceperis, and it should be noted that most often, when Scripture makes mention of man, it understands only the inner man; which is clearly found in the book of Moses entitled Job, which says:","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"4.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","text":"Pelle & carnibus veſtijſti me, oſſibus & nervis compegiſti me, by which words, and by that repeated me, me, it clearly gives to understand that the inner man is other than the outer. Socrates comes to this opinion in his First Alcibiades in Plato, disputing concerning the nature of man; for just as the garment that we wear is not us, but a thing used by us, so too the body, although it is borne by us, is not us, but a thing used by us. For which reason the words of Moses in Genesis are to be considered: facia mus hominem ad imaginem & ſimilitudinem noſtram, which signify none other than the inner man; and that this is true, a little below he adds: Nondum erat homo qui operare tur in terra.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"4.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","text":"Therefore, the inner man was first made in the supercelestial realm, before God formed for him a body of earth, so that he might operate in this world and be an instrument of divine works; and therefore Moses added: Plaſmauit Deus ho","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"4.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0010","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"4.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0011","text":"29","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"4.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0012","text":"ſimilem de limo terræ, which limo does not signify mud (as many suppose), but the flower and (so to speak) the cream of the earth, which was virginal, because it had not yet contracted a stain, as almost Adam's whole family contracted it after his sin. This virginal earth was called Adama, whence Adam drew his name. Nor does this touch upon the fact that Christ, in order to satisfy divine justice, presented Himself as the purifier of all human sins in a body similar to that which Adam had before he sinned; that is, in a body made of virginal earth and of the most pure blood of the Virgin Mary.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"4.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0013","text":"Adam.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"4.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","text":"To these things let there be added, since we have entered upon speaking of Adam, that before sin he was in the garden of delights in two ways; I do not mean the Terrestrial Paradise, as many interpret what Moses never at all said. In the first way, Adam, who was in the supercelestial garden not bodily but terrestrially, enjoying in the grace of God all the blessed influences; but as soon as he had sinned, he was cast out of the said supercelestial garden. And this means that the aforesaid influences were taken away from him, not that he was bodily sent out; no otherwise than if a servant, most pleasing to Caesar, found himself in Egypt: while he was in the grace of his Prince, he would be said to be in his household; but, sinning and deprived of his grace, he could be said to be cast out from the Court.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"4.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0015","text":"Nor should anyone marvel that I raise this question, that the garden from which Adam was cast out was the supercelestial garden, for this was first the opinion of Origen, and then of Jerome, his follower. The other way of saying that Adam was in paradise would be according to the word,","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"4.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0016","text":"Paradise","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"4.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0017","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"4.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","text":"not Hebrew, but Greek; and we say that before sin Adam was in the virginal earth of this world. And while he remained therein without staining his body with sin, he was in the terrestrial paradise. And once sin had been committed, the earth contracted a stain, and thus he came to be cast out of paradise. Therefore, what might happen to a Baron of Caesar happened to the world on account of Adam: if he sinned, all his household would come to contract a stain, although it had not sinned, and everyone would look upon it askance. Therefore, Adam sinning, all the Elements sinned through the contraction of a stain. Since the first virginity was no longer in them, it may be said that for this reason Adam is said to have been cast out of the terrestrial paradise.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"4.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0019","text":"In our\nsouls.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"4.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","text":"But, following our purpose, it should be known that there are in us three souls, all three of which, although they enjoy this common name, soul, nevertheless each also has its particular name. For the lowest, and nearest, and companion of our body is called Nephes, and this is otherwise called by Moses the living soul. And since all our passions are contained in it, we have it in common with the beasts. And Christ speaks of this when He says: Triſſis eſt anima mea vſque ad mortem. And elsewhere: qui non haſbuerit odio animam ſuam perdet eam. To this term, since neither the Greek nor the Latin tongue aspires, its signification cannot be represented in translations, as, for example, in that Psalm: Lauda anima mea dominum: although the writer of the Holy Spirit has set down the term Nephes, they make us use the common one. And it was right","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"4.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0021","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"4.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0022","text":"30","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"4.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0023","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"4.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","text":"that the Prophet should use the term Nephes, wishing to praise God with the tongue and with the other members that form the voice and are governed by Nephes, which is nearer to the flesh. The middle soul, which is the rational, is called by the name of spirit, that is, Ruach. The third is called Nessamah. By Moses, breath; by David and Pythagoras, ila me; by Apollonius, higher portion; by Plato, mind; by Aristotle, active intellect. And just as Nephes has the devil, who ministers to it a demon as tempter, so Nessamah has God, who ministers to it the angel. The poor middle one is stimulated from both sides. And if, by divine permission, it inclines to make union with Nephes, Nephes unites with the flesh and the flesh with the demon, and the whole makes transition and transformation into devil; for which reason Christ said: Ego ele gi vos duodecim, et Vnus ex vobis diabolus eſt.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"4.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","text":"But if, through the grace of Christ (so great a benefit cannot come from another), the middle soul detaches itself, as it were by the cut of the knife of the word of Christ, from the ill-persuaded Nephes, and unites itself with the Nessamah—the Nessamah, which is a divine soul—it passes into the nature of the angel, and consequently is transmuted into God: wherefore Christ, having regard to that text of Malachi, Ecce ego mitto angelum meum, wills it to be understood of John the Baptist, transmuted into an angel in divine providence ab initio & ante saecula. I have made mention of the knife of Christ's word, which alone by its cut divides the lower soul from the rational soul, which we have said bears the name of spirit. Whence Paul said: Vivus est sermo Dei, et efficax, et penetratior omni gladio anceps pertingens usque ad divisionem animae & spiritus; and in order that we may recognize the aforesaid three souls, each one","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"4.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0026","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"4.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0027","text":"Under diverse names in the words of Moses recounted above in Genesis, it is to be noted that when he said, faciamus hominem, he understood the rational soul. And when [he said] posuit eum in animam viventem, he understood the Nephes; but in saying, flauit in nares eius, spiraculum vitae, he signified the Nessamah. I cannot but set down upon these passages the opinion of the writer of the Zohar. The Nephes is a certain simulacrum, or rather our shadow, which never departs from its own [unclear], and shows itself not only by night, but also by day, to those whose eyes God has opened.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"4.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0028","text":"And because the said writer dwelt in the desert for forty years with seven companions, and with a son, for the purpose of illuminating Holy Scripture, he says that one day he saw the Nephes of one of his holy and dear companions so detached that it stood behind his head as a shadow; and thereafter he became aware that this was the messenger of that man's approaching death. But with many fasts and prayers he obtained from God that the said detached Nephes should be rejoined from the head to his body, and thus united it remained until the end of the undertaking. Which passage, having been seen by me, makes me think that Virgil, in touching upon the approaching death of Marcellus, made use of it; and that he had understood such a secret either from Hebrews or from Chaldaean Kabbalists. Thereupon the said writer of the Zohar says that this Nephes is present from the beginning at the formation of the embryo.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"4.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0029","text":"But that the Ruach does not enter until the seventh day after birth, and that therefore God commands that the child be presented to Him, and to circumcision on the eighth day, that is, one day after the rational soul has made its entrance; and although the Nessamah does not enter until the thirtieth day,","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"4.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0030","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"4.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0031","text":"31","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"4.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","text":"one must not wait so long to perform circumcision, at which there should intervene only the soul that can sin, and that which knows how to sin; for the Nassamah, being divine, cannot sin: and in this passage Plotinus likewise agrees, speaking of the third high soul, when he says: In anima non cadit peccatum, neque poena. Aristotle's fine intelligence indeed chose to labour over another triplicity which is in the inner man, but therein he posits only that third high [principle]; for, disputing most learnedly concerning our three intellects, he calls one possible, or passive, as it is called by our Latins, and in the vernacular ingegno, otherwise by Cicero intelligentiae vis. The other intellect in possession, which is the practical intellect, signifying already to have apprehended and to possess.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"4.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0033","text":"The third, the active intellect, is that by whose virtue we understand: and in this passage Saint Thomas, wishing to prove that the active intellect is in us, if I remember rightly, draws [his proof] from the example of our visual power, and of that ray of fire which within us answers to the eye, which we very often see internally, when rubbing one of our eyes with a finger, in the likeness of a wheel of flame. By means of which flaming wheel it often happens that, upon awakening and opening our eyes in the dark night, for a very brief space we see and discern things in the chamber; then, as that wheel gradually weakens, it loses its force.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"4.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0034","text":"Therefore, just as in the single eye we have the power of seeing, the seeing, and the wheel that makes us see, so in us there is not only the intellect which can understand—that is, the ingegno, or intellectual capacity, as we may call it—and understanding itself, which is the practical intellect, but al-","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"4.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0035","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"4.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0036","text":"so the active intellect, that is, that which makes us understand. The wheel of fire of which we have spoken is said to have been so great and powerful in the eyes of Tiberius that for a long while at night he discerned all things in his chamber. Whence it follows that one has more of it and another less. And Aristotle, when he becomes a physiognomist, says that when with difficulty we fix our eyes upon others, that light signifies a future prince; whence some ancients have left it written that the eyes of Jesus Christ were such. But Simplicius, wishing by every means to demonstrate and prove this active intellect to be outside, says that it is outside us no otherwise than the Sun too is outside us, and outside the visual power, although it is by means of the said Sun that it sees.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"4.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","text":"Therefore, just as in our sound eye there is the power of seeing, and at times seeing itself as well, but the making to see, which belongs to the Sun or to some other of its deputies, is outside the eye; so, although in our inner man there is the power of understanding—that is, the possible or passive intellect—and practical understanding as well, nevertheless the active intellect, which is the divine ray, or Angel, or God Himself, is outside us. Here this opinion of Simplicius seems to be more approved by Scripture, and most especially by that passage of David: Intellectum tibi dabo, & instruam te in via hac qua gradieris. If therefore God is its giver, He is also He who withdraws it, either for a time or forever. Fearing this, David said: Et spiritum sanctum tu non auferas a me. And elsewhere it is written of perpetual withdrawal: Relinquentur domus vestrae desertae.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"4.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0038","text":"It follows therefore that this active intellect or divine ray is outside of","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"4.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0039","text":"outside of","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"4.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0040","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"4.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0041","text":"32","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"4.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0042","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"4.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","text":"us, and in the power of God. This intellect philosophers ignorant of God called reason, by which, I say, man is separated from beasts. But in truth man is called rational, or rather intellectual, because he alone among animals is capable of this active intellect; but when it does not please God to give it, he who goes without it is not inwardly different from beasts, as is written in the Psalm: Homo cum in honore esset non intellexit come paratus est iumentis insipientibus, & similis factus est illis. With this passage agrees that most obscure passage of the Apocalypse: Numerus hominis numerus bestiae, numerus autem bestiae sex centi sexaginta sex. For the number which reaches a thousand through the addition of the active intellect is the number of the illuminated man. And therefore in the Canticle, when good is to be wished to him who is addressed, it is said in the Hebrew text:","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"4.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","text":"Mille tibi Salomon. Which signifies: I wish you not only the human figure, but also the divine ray. For which reason, when I greet my Most Excellent Prince, instead of giving him good day, I shall say to him: Mille tibi. But I reserve for another time the explanation of these numbers. Virgil too seems to conform to this opinion in describing his golden branch, which, being of a diverse matter and very different from the tree, and not being obtainable by human will, shows itself to be something outside, and that the favour of the supreme God must be with us if we are to obtain the gift of this our intellect. But now it is time that we descend to our images, which we shall do if first we have said one thing pertaining not only to the","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"4.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0045","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"4.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0046","text":"theological symbols that I am to give to this gate, but to all the images of my Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"4.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","text":"Among the ancients, therefore, it was the custom that those same philosophers who taught and showed learned doctrines openly to dear disciples, after they had [thus] made them clear, covered them with fables, so that, thus covered, they might be kept hidden and might not be profaned. This custom endured until the time of Virgil, who in his most learned Silenus, under that name, introduces Siro as singing—that is, as clearly making manifest—the principles of the world to Chromis and Nasillus, that is, to Varro and to Virgil himself. And after he has sung them here, he enters into fables, a thing which seems very strange to readers ignorant of the said custom.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"4.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","text":"In imitation of those so great philosophers, after I have clearly revealed the secret of the three souls and of the three intellects, matters pertaining to the inner man, I shall cover them with weak symbols, lest they be profaned, and also in order to awaken memory. Among Greek fables, therefore, one reads of three blind Sisters called the Gorgons, who had among themselves one eye, interchangeable between them, because one could lend it to another, and she who had it saw only so much as she had it. In this symbol lies the entire mystery of the truth set forth above, and it is made understood to us that the divine ray is outside and not within us. Now this image shall cover the whole order of the fourth grade, containing beneath it the things pertaining to the inner man according to the nature of each planet. And to come to the particular of the gates.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"4.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0049","text":"Under the Gorgons of the Moon shall be the image of Bacchus’s Cup, which is between Cancer and Leo. And according as","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"4.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0050","text":"Sun,","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"4.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0051","text":"they say","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"4.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0052","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO,","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"4.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0053","text":"33","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"4.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0054","text":"the Platonists say, the souls that come into this world descend through the gate of Cancer, and on their return ascend through that of Capricorn: and the gate of Cancer is called the gate of men, for souls to descend into mortal bodies, and that of Capricorn is called the gate of the Gods, for them to return up to divinity according to the nature of the animal that is its sign: and Cancer is the house of the Moon, whose intelligence is Gabriel: and because, in descending, he was many times sent by God, Scripture calls him man, saying, Ecce vir Gabriel: and, to return to the Platonists, they say that souls, in descending, drink from Bacchus’s Cup, and forget all the things up there, some more and some less, according as each drinks more or less of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"4.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055","text":"We shall therefore fashion a Zodiac in such a manner that, in its highest and most visible part, Cancer and Leo may be seen, and the Cup in the middle, with a Virgin bent over to drink from it: and this image shall preserve beneath it a volume pertaining to human forgetfulness (whatever that may be), with its necessary consequences, such as ignorance and rudeness: and this image belongs to the Moon, because (as we have said) Cancer is her house, understanding this maiden as the soul in common, in all that we have said of the three.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"4.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056","text":"Under the Gorgons of Mercury shall be the image of a lighted torch, which, understanding it to be that which Prometheus kindled in Heaven with the aid of Pallas, we wish to signify ingenuity, that is, the possible or passive intellect, and docility, whose verb is to learn. We shall speak fully of this torch in the seventh grade, where we shall treat of Prometheus.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"4.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0057","text":"Mercury","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"4.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058","text":"Under the Gorgons of Venus shall be covered the image of Eve.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"4.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0059","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"4.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0060","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"4.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0061","text":"E\n\nTHE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"4.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062","text":"Felice points Joseph in the foot, and because the foot, and in particular the heel or the talon, as we may call it, signifies our affections governed by our will, we wish this to contain the human will, which is one of the powers of the soul, and which shall be divided into free and non-free. And we shall also allow this to be the Nefesh, and lest it escape our memory, we must know that anatomists say that from the heel to the loins there is such a correspondence of certain nerves that the Scriptures sometimes take one for the other. Thus Christ, wishing to say that our affections, and our very will, should be chastened and cleansed, said: Sint lumbi vestri præcincti, and also washed the feet at his departure, that is, the affections, of the Apostles. Peter, not wishing to consent to that damnation, said to him: Nisi lavero te non habebis partem mecum.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"4.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0063","text":"And in Genesis it is written: Et insidiaberis calcaneo eius. Further on, one reads in the Greek fables that Achilles, as a child, having been immersed in the Stygian waters, became invulnerable in all parts, except in the feet, by which he was held, and where the waters did not touch; which signifies that a man could be constant in all parts, provided that he were not touched in his affections. Nor without mystery did Jason, going to seize the Golden Fleece, lose one of his shoes in the river unique in the world without wind. Of the feet of Antaeus, regaining their strength from the Earth whenever he touched it, we shall speak in their proper place.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"4.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0064","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"4.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065","text":"Under the Solar Gorgons shall be covered the image of the Golden Bough, and this shall signify for us the active intellect, the Nessas mah, the aia in general, the rational aia, spirit, and life.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"4.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0066","text":"Mars.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"4.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067","text":"Under the Gorgons of Mars shall be the image of a maiden with one bare foot, and with her head unbound, and this","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"4.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0068","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"4.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0069","text":"34","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"4.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070","text":"shall signify deliberation, or rather firm resolve, and not the sudden [resolve], in distinction from that deliberation which is one and the same thing as counsel, which is Jovial: and her being unbound and barefoot is sufficiently understood from the explanation of the loins and of Jason’s bare foot: and Virgil expressed this figure for us in the sudden and firm resolve to die that Dido made, saying of her that she was:","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"4.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0071","text":"Vnum exuta pedem, vinclis in veste recincta, and from her we have taken this image.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"4.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072","text":"Under the Jovial Gorgons shall be the image of a crane, Jupiter, that flies toward Heaven, carrying in its beak a caduceus, and letting fall from its feet a quiver, from which the arrows, coming forth, fall downward through the air, scattering themselves, as I have seen on the reverse of an ancient medal: and the crane signifies the vigilant mind, which, now weary of the world and of its deceits, flies toward Heaven in order to have tranquillity, carrying the caduceus in its mouth, that is, its peace and tranquillity: and from its feet falls the quiver with the arrows, which signify the cares of this world. To this image conforms that verse of the Psalm: Quis dabit mihi pennas sicut columbæ, & volabo, & requiescam.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"4.72","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0073","text":"Which Petrarch translated in one of his Sonnets, desiring only the wings of the Dove in order to rest himself, and rise from the Earth. This gentle image will confirm choice, judgment, and counsel: and from this image to Jupiter, as being a tranquil, benign Planet, and of composed mind.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"4.73","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074","text":"Under the Gorgons of Saturn shall be the image of Hercules, Saturn, who lifts Antaeus upon his breast. Hercules is the human spirit. Antaeus is the body. The breast of Hercules is the seat of Wisdom and Prudence; these two (as Paul says)","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"4.74","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0075","text":"E  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"4.75","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0076","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"4.76","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","text":"make continual struggle and unceasing war, because the flesh continually rises against the spirit, and the spirit against the flesh; nor can the spirit be victor in the battle unless it lifts the body so high from the earth that with its feet—that is, with its affections—it cannot regain strength from its mother, and holds it so tightly that it kills it. Here we have principally to consider two things: one is the death of the body, the other is, as it were, its transformation into the spirit. And indeed, if our body does not die the death of the affections, it cannot become spiritual, nor become one in Christ. Of which death Paul speaks thus: “You are dead, and your life is hidden with Christ in God”; and David: “Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his saints.” And in Psalm 62 one reads that the flesh turns its desire toward God equally with the spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"4.77","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","text":"“My soul thirsted for thee; how manifoldly my flesh for thee.” And Paul, in the third to the Philippians: “God is to reform the body of your humility, conforming it to the body of his glory.” And Christ, in the similitude of the death of the grain: “Unless a grain of wheat, falling to the earth, shall have died, it remains alone; but if it shall have died, it bears much fruit.” And if our interpretation shall be well considered, it will be found that we have also made manifest the transmutation, which is one of the two things proposed by us; and Petrarch gently touched upon this when he said: “Flying to heaven with the earthly burden.” This transmutation is likewise sufficiently made manifest in the three blind sisters, who, having the eye not their own but that of their sisters, and lending themselves one to another, by consenting conform together, and become one and the same thing, like Nessamah drawn by the angel, which draws the Ruàh, and that the Nephesh.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"4.78","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0079","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"4.79","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0080","text":"35","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"4.80","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","text":"And thus spiritual transformation is effected. Now this image, in order to signify both tenacity in the tightness that Hercules makes, and elevation upward from the earth, shall cover a volume in which all the things belonging to these parts shall be distinguished, such as the impressions that the soul bears from Heaven, memory, knowledge, opinion, practical intellect—that is, understanding—thought, imagination, and contemplation. And this first image befits Saturn, because the same measure in the supercelestial of the Rinā, that is, of the intellect, is common to Saturn. And then because it is so firm. Another image shall likewise be beneath this gate, namely, a maiden ascending through Capricorn. And this shall signify the ascent of souls into Heaven. And this image is given to Saturn, because Capricorn is his house.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"4.81","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081"]}],"source_digest":"91e502ac584524d10cf142d770b68ea5c74d40688ac4f9a91462fcc6794bb551","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"LE GORGONI,"},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261031T001809997430Z_e40204a2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE GORGONS,","source_sha256":"80f6e97fb40a8b7738785f65128dbefd0cf3dfb106bb21336f87a44a7cbb7b43","sha256":"fd54eb39c41201fd11eb452e7cf7ecb4f18a7c896dafb7b342ea506855e2bc74","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-31T00:18:09.997519+00:00","translate_quotations":true,"paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0001","text":"THE GORGONS,","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"4.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","text":"Let us ascend to the fourth Grade belonging to the inner man, which was the last, and the noblest creature made by God in His image and likeness. And here it should be noted that in the Hebrew text that which is translated as image is called Celem, and that which is called likeness is written Demut. Which words in the Zohar of Rabbi Simeon, which means illuminator, that is, giver of light, are interpreted in this sense: that Celem signifies (so to speak) the impress or rather the angelic form, and Demut imports a divine grade. For it holds that God not only raised our soul to the excellence of the Angels, but Himself further added to it the divine grade.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"4.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","text":"And the said author of the Zohar added that He, foreseeing the angel who was afterwards cast out, moved by envy and self-love, spoke against the will of the divine Majesty. But Mercurius Trismegistus in his Pimander takes image and likeness as one and the same thing, and the whole as the divine grade, saying thus: “But the Father of all, being intellect, life, and radiance, begot a man like unto Himself, and rejoiced in him as in a son; for he was beautiful and bore the image of his Father. For God, truly delighted exceedingly with His own form, granted all His works for human use.” And the same in the Asclepius: “O Asclepius, man is a great miracle, an animal to be adored and honoured; for he passes into the nature of God, as though he himself were God; he knows this race of daemons, as being of their same countenance.”","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"4.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0004","text":"D  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"4.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0005","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"4.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0006","text":"3.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"4.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","text":"when he knows himself to be, he may despise this part of human nature in himself, ashamed of the divinity of the other part. Other Cabalistic writers have left it written that likeness pertains to operation, as though wishing to say that God made man in order that he might work for Him; and Holy Scripture agrees with this opinion, where mention is made of the good works that he performs: but that they are not ours, but God’s, and that we are only the instruments. Whence certain contemplatives call these works eternal works. Of this Paul says: “What hast thou, O man, that thou hast not received? And if thou hast received it, why dost thou glory as though thou hadst not received it?” And it should be noted that most often, when Scripture mentions man, it understands only the inner man; which is clearly found in the book of Moses entitled Job, which says:","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"4.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","text":"“Thou hast clothed me with skin and flesh; thou hast compacted me with bones and sinews”; by which words, and by that pronoun “me, me,” he clearly gives us to understand that the inner man is other than the outer. Socrates takes this view in his First Alcibiades in Plato, disputing concerning the nature of man; for just as the garment that we wear is not ourselves, but a thing used by us, so the body, although it is borne by us, is not ourselves, but a thing used by us. For which reason the words of Moses in Genesis are to be considered: “Let us make man in our image and likeness,” which signify nothing but the inner man; and that this is true, a little below he added: “There was not yet a man to work the earth.”","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"4.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","text":"Therefore the inner man had first been made in the supercelestial realm, before God formed for him a body of earth, so that he might be able to work in this world and be an instrument of divine works; and therefore Moses added: “God formed a hu","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"4.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0010","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"4.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0011","text":"29","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"4.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0012","text":"similar out of the clay of the earth,” which clay does not signify mud (as many suppose), but the flower, and (so to speak) the head of the milk of the earth, which was virginal, because it had not yet contracted a stain, as almost all Adam’s family contracted one after his sin. This virginal earth was called Adama, whence Adam took his name. Nor did it escape notice that Christ, in order to satisfy divine justice, presented Himself as the purifier of all human faults in a body similar to that which Adam had before he sinned, that is, in a body made of virginal earth and of the most pure blood of the Virgin Mary.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"4.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0013","text":"Adam.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"4.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","text":"To these things let it be added, since we have entered upon speaking of Adam, that before sin he was in the garden of delights in two ways; I do not say the Terrestrial Paradise, as many interpret that which Moses never said. In the first way, Adam, who was in the supercelestial garden not bodily present there, but earthly, enjoying in the grace of God all the blessed influences; but as soon as he sinned, he was cast out of the said supercelestial garden. And this means that the aforesaid influences were taken away from him, not that he was bodily sent forth; no otherwise than if a servant most dear to Caesar should be found in Egypt: while he remained in the favour of his Prince, he would be said to be in his household; but, sinning and deprived of his favour, he could be said to have been cast out from the Court.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"4.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0015","text":"Nor should anyone marvel that I advance this question, that the garden from which Adam was cast out was the supercelestial garden; for this was first the opinion of Origen, and then of Jerome, his follower. The other way of saying that Adam was in paradise would be according to the word,","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"4.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0016","text":"Paradise","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"4.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0017","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"4.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","text":"not Hebrew, but Greek; and we say that Adam before sin was in the virginal earth of this world. And while he remained in it without staining his body by sin, he was in the terrestrial paradise. And when sin had been committed, the earth contracted a stain, and thus he came to be cast out of paradise. There befell the world, therefore, on Adam’s account, what might befall a Baron of Caesar, who, if he sinned, would cause all his household to contract a stain, although it had not sinned, and all would look upon it askance. Therefore, when Adam sinned, all the Elements sinned by contraction of stain. Since, then, their first virginity was no longer in them, it may be said that for this reason Adam is said to have been cast out of the terrestrial paradise.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"4.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0019","text":"In our\nsouls.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"4.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","text":"But, pursuing our purpose, it must be known that there are in us three souls, all three of which, although they enjoy this common name of soul, nevertheless each also has its particular name. For the lowest, and nearest, and companion of our body is called Nephes, and this is otherwise called by Moses the living soul. And because all our passions are contained in it, we have it in common with the beasts. And Christ speaks of this when He says: “My soul is sorrowful unto death.” And elsewhere: “He who has not hated his soul shall lose it.” To which word, since neither the Greek nor the Latin tongue aspires, its meaning cannot be represented in translations, as, for example, in that Psalm: “Praise the Lord, O my soul”; although the writer of the Holy Spirit has used the word Nephes, they make us use the common term. And it was quite rea","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"4.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0021","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"4.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0022","text":"30","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"4.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0023","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"4.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","text":"son that the Prophet should use the word Nephes, wishing to praise God with the tongue and with the other members that form the voice, and are governed by Nephes, which is nearer to the flesh. The middle soul, which is the rational, is called by the name of spirit, that is, Ruach. The third is called Nessamah: by Moses, breath; by David and Pythagoras, Ilame; by Apollonius, the higher portion; by Plato, mind; by Aristotle, the active intellect. And just as Nephes has the devil, who supplies it with a demon as tempter, so Nessamah has God, who supplies it with the angel. The poor middle one is stimulated from both sides. And if, by divine permission, it inclines to make union with Nephes, Nephes unites with the flesh, and the flesh with the demon, and the whole makes passage and transformation into devil; for which reason Christ said: “I have chosen you twelve, and one of you is a devil.”","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"4.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","text":"But if through the grace of Christ (so great a benefit cannot come from another) the middle soul detaches itself, almost by the cut of the knife of the word of Christ, from the ill-persuaded Nephes, and joins itself with the Nessamah, the Nessamah, which is a divine soul, passes into the nature of the angel, and consequently is transformed into God: therefore Christ, observing that text of Malachi, “Behold, I send my angel,” wishes it to be understood of John the Baptist, transformed into an angel in divine providence from the beginning & before the ages. I have made mention of the knife of the word of Christ, which alone by its cut divides the lower threshing-floor from the rational threshing-floor, which we have said bears the name of spirit. Whence Paul said: “The word of God is living and efficacious, and more penetrating than every two-edged sword, reaching as far as the division of soul and spirit,” and in order that we may recognize the said three threshing-floors, each","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"4.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0026","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"4.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0027","text":"Under a different name, in the words of Moses set out above in Genesis, it is to be noted that when he said, “Let us make man,” he understood the rational soul. And when [he said], “he placed him in a living soul,” he understood the Nephes; but in saying, “he breathed into his nostrils the breath of life,” he signified the Nessamah. I cannot help\nbut set down upon these passages the opinion of the writer of the Zohar. The Nephes is a certain simulacrum, or rather our shadow, which never departs from its bodies, and aban-\ndons itself not only at night, but even by day, to those whose eyes God has opened.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"4.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0028","text":"And because the said writer remained in the wilderness for forty years with seven companions, and with one son, for the purpose of illuminating the holy Scrip-\nture, he says that one day he saw the Nephes of one of his holy and dear companions so detached that it stood behind his head as a shadow; and afterwards he perceived from this that it was the messenger of that man’s approaching death. But by many fasts and prayers he obtained from God that the said Nephes, detached from the head of his body, should be rejoined to it, and thus united it remained until the end of the undertaking. Which passage, having been seen by me, makes me think that Virgil, in touching upon the approaching death of Marcellus, made use of it; and that either from Hebrew or from Chaldean Kabbalists he had learned such a secret. Thereupon the said writer of the Zohar says that this Nephes is present from the beginning at the formation of the Embryo.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"4.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0029","text":"But that the Ruach enters only on the seventh day after birth, & that therefore God commands that the child be pre-\nsented to him, and to circumcision on the eighth day, that is, one day after the rational soul has made its entry; and although the Nessamah enters only on the thirtieth day,","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"4.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0030","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"4.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0031","text":"31","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"4.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","text":"one ought not to wait so long to perform circumcision, at which none ought to be present save the soul that can sin, and that which knows how to sin, since the Nassamah, being divine, cannot sin: and in this passage Plotinus likewise agrees, understanding the third high soul, when he says: “In the soul there is no sin, nor punishment.” Aristotle’s fine intellect has indeed wished to take pains over another triplicity that is in the inner man, but in it he posits only that third high [soul]: for, disputing most learnedly concerning our three intellects, he calls one possible, or passive, as it is called by our Latins, and in the vulgar tongue wit, otherwise by Cicero the power of understanding. The other is intellect in possession, which is the practical intellect, signifying already to have near at hand, and to possess.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"4.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0033","text":"The third intellect is agent, and it is that by whose virtue we understand: and in this pas-\nsage Saint Thomas, wishing to prove that the agent intellect is in us, if I remember rightly, [argues] from the example of our visual power and of that ray of fire which within us corresponds to the eye, which we very often see inwardly, on rubbing one of our eyes with a finger, in the likeness of a wheel of flame. By means of this flaming wheel it often hap-\npens that, when awake and opening our eyes in the dark night, for a very small space we see and discern things in the chamber; and then, as this wheel gradually weakens, it loses its force.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"4.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0034","text":"Therefore, just as in the single eye we have the power to see, the seeing, and the wheel that makes us see, so in us there are not only the intellect that can understand, that is, wit, or intellectual capacity, whichever we wish to call it, and understanding itself, which is the practical intellect, but al-","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"4.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0035","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"4.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0036","text":"so the agent intellect, that is, that which causes us to understand. The wheel of fire of which we have spoken is said to have been so great and powerful in the eyes of Tiberius that for a long while at night he discerned all things in his chamber. Whence it follows that one has more of it and another less. And Aristotle, when he becomes a physiognomist, says that when we fix our eyes upon others with difficulty, that light signifies a future prince; whence certain ancients have left it written that the eyes of Jesus Christ were such. But Simplicius, wishing by every means to demonstrate and prove that this agent intellect is outside, says that it is no more outside us than the Sun too is outside us, and is outside the visual power, although by means of the said Sun it sees.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"4.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","text":"Therefore, just as in our sound eye there is the power to see, and sometimes also the seeing, but the making to see, which belongs to the Sun or to another of its deputies, is outside the eye, so, although in our inner man there is the power to understand, that is, the possible or passive intellect, and practical understanding too, nevertheless the agent intellect, which is the divine ray, or Angel, or God himself, is outside us. Here this opinion of Simplicius seems to be the more approved by Scripture, and especially by that passage of David: “I will give thee understanding, and will instruct thee in this way in which thou shalt walk.” Therefore, if God is its giver, he is also the one who withdraws it, either for a time or forever. Fearing this, David said: “And do not take thy holy spirit from me.” And elsewhere, concerning perpetual withdrawal, it is written: “Your houses shall be left desolate.”","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"4.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0038","text":"there follows there-\nfore that this agent intellect or divine ray is outside","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"4.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0039","text":"outside of","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"4.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0040","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"4.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0041","text":"32","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"4.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0042","text":"[illegible]","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"4.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","text":"us, & in the power of God. This intellect philosophers ignorant of God called reason, by which, I say, man [is] separated from beasts. But in truth man is called rational, or rather intellectual, because he alone among animals is capable of this agent intellect; but when it does not please God to grant it, he who goes without it is not inwardly different from beasts, it being written in the Psalm: “Man, when he was in honour, did not understand; he was compared to senseless beasts, and was made like unto them.” With this passage agrees that most obscure passage of the Apocalypse: “The number of man [is] the number of the beast; but the number of the beast [is] six hundred and sixty-six.” For the number that reaches a thousand by the addition of the agent intellect is the number of enlightened man. And therefore in the Canticle, when one wishes well to the person addressed, it is said in the Hebrew Text.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"4.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","text":"“A thousand to thee, Solo-\nmon.” This signifies: I desire for thee not only the human figure, but also the divine ray. For which reason, when I greet my Most Excellent Prince, instead of bidding him good day, I shall say to him: “A thousand to thee.” But I reserve for another time the explanation of these numbers. To this opinion Virgil too seems to conform in describing his golden bough, which, being of a diverse matter and very different from the tree, and not being obtainable by human will, shows that it is something external, and that we need the favour of the supreme God in order to obtain the gift of this our intellect. But it is now time for us to de-\nscend to our images, which we shall do if first we have said one thing belonging not only to the","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"4.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0045","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"4.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0046","text":"Theological symbols that I am to give to this gate, but to all\nthe images of my Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"4.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","text":"Among the ancients, therefore, it was the custom that those same philosophers who taught and showed learned doctrines to dear disciples, after they had clearly [expounded them], covered them with fables, so that, thus covered, they might keep them hidden and thus might not be profaned. This custom continued down to the time of Virgil, who, in his most learned Silenus, under that name introduces Siro to sing—that is, to manifest clearly—the principles of the world to Chromis and Nasillus, that is, to Varro and to Virgil himself. And after he has sung them here, he enters into fables, a thing that seems very strange to readers ignorant of the said custom.","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"4.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","text":"In imitation of those such great philosophers, after I have clearly revealed the secret of the three threshing-floors, and of the three intellects, things belonging to the inner man, I shall cover them with weak symbols, so that they may not be profaned, and also in order to awaken memory. Among Greek fables, therefore, one reads of three blind Sisters called the Gorgons, who had among themselves a single eye exchangeable between them, because one could lend it to another, and she who had it saw only so much as she had it. In this symbol lies the whole mystery of the truth expounded above, and it makes us understand that the divine ray is outside, and not within us. Now this image shall cover the whole order of the fourth degree, containing beneath it the things belonging to the inner man according to the nature of each planet. And to come to the particulars of the gates.","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"4.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0049","text":"Under the Gorgons of the Moon shall be the image of Bacchus’ Cup, which is between Cancer & Leo. And according as","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"4.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0050","text":"Sun,","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"4.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0051","text":"they say","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"4.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0052","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO,","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"4.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0053","text":"33","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"4.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0054","text":"the Platonists say, the souls that come into this world descend through the gate of Cancer, & on their return ascend through that of Capricorn: & the gate of Cancer is called the gate of men, for the souls to descend into mortal bodies, & that of Capricorn is called the gate of the Gods, for them to return on high to divinity according to the nature of the animal which is its sign: & Cancer is the house of the Moon, whose intelligence is Gabriel: & because, in descending, he was many times sent by God, Scripture calls him man, saying: Behold the man Gabriel: & to return to the Platonists, they say that souls, in descending, drink from Bacchus’ Cup, & forget all the things above, some more & some less, according as each drinks more or less of it.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"4.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055","text":"We shall therefore fashion a Zodiac in such a way that in its highest & most visible part Cancer & Leo may be seen, & the Cup in the middle with a Virgin bent down to drink from it: & this image shall preserve beneath it a volume pertaining to human forgetfulness (whatever it may be), with its necessary consequences, such as ignorance & rudeness: & this image belongs to the Moon because (as we have said) Cancer is her house, understanding this maiden as the soul in common, in all that we have said concerning the three.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"4.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056","text":"Under the Gorgons of Mercury shall be the image of a lighted torch, which, understanding it to be that which Prometheus kindled in Heaven with the aid of Pallas, we wish to signify ingenuity, that is, the possible, or passive, intellect, & teachability, whose verb is to learn. We shall speak fully of this torch in the seventh grade, where we shall treat of Prometheus.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"4.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0057","text":"Mercury","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"4.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058","text":"Under the Gorgons of Venus shall be covered the image of Eve.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"4.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0059","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"4.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0060","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"4.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0061","text":"E\n\nTHE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"4.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062","text":"Joseph’s foot happily pricks, & since the foot, & in particular the heel, or the talon, whichever we wish to call it, signifies our affections governed by our will, we wish this to contain the human will, which is one of the powers of the soul, and which shall be divided into free & non-free. And we shall also grant this to be the Nephesh, & lest it escape our memory, we must know that the anatomists say that from the heel to the loins there is such a correspondence of certain nerves that the Scriptures sometimes take one for the other. Thus Christ, wishing to say that our affections, & our will itself, should be chastised & cleansed, said: Let your loins be girded; and he also washed the feet at his departure, that is, the affections, of the Apostles. Peter, not wishing to consent to that cleansing, said to him: Unless I wash you, you shall have no part with me.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"4.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0063","text":"And in Genesis it is written: And you shall lie in wait for his heel. Moreover, one reads in the Greek fables that Achilles, as a child, because he had been immersed in the Stygian waters, became invulnerable in all parts, except in the feet, by which he was held, & where the waters did not touch; which signifies that a man could be steadfast in all his parts, provided he were not touched in his affections. Nor without mystery did Jason, going to seize the Golden Fleece, lose one of his sandals in the only river in the world without wind. Of the feet of Antaeus, recovering strength from the Earth whenever he touched it, we shall speak in its proper place.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"4.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0064","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"4.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065","text":"Under the Solar Gorgons shall be covered the image of the Golden Bough, and this shall signify for us the active intellect, the Nessas mah, the aia in general, the rational aia, spirit & life.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"4.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0066","text":"Mars.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"4.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067","text":"Under the Gorgons of Mars shall be the image of a maiden with one bare foot, & with her head ungirded, & this","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"4.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0068","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":68,"address":"4.68","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0068"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0069","text":"34","kind":"passage","sequence":69,"address":"4.69","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0069"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070","text":"shall signify deliberation, or rather firm resolve, & not the sudden kind, in distinction from that deliberation which is one and the same thing as counsel, which is Jovial: & her being ungirded & barefoot is sufficiently understood from the explanation of the loins, & of Jason’s bare foot: and Virgil expressed this figure for us in Dido’s sudden & firm resolve to die, saying of her that she was:","kind":"passage","sequence":70,"address":"4.70","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0071","text":"With one foot bare, her garment ungirded by clasps, & from her have we taken this image.","kind":"passage","sequence":71,"address":"4.71","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0071"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072","text":"Under the Jovial Gorgons shall be the image of a Crane, Jupiter, flying toward Heaven, carrying a Caduceus in its beak, & letting fall from its feet a quiver, from which, as the arrows emerge, they fall downward through the air, scattering themselves, as I have seen on the reverse of an ancient medal: & the Crane signifies the vigilant soul, which, now weary of the world & its deceptions, flies toward heaven in order to have tranquillity, bearing the Caduceus in its mouth, that is, its peace & tranquillity: & from its feet falls the quiver with the arrows, which signify the cares of this world. To this image conforms that verse of the Psalm: Who will give me wings like a dove, & I shall fly, & I shall rest.","kind":"passage","sequence":72,"address":"4.72","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0073","text":"Which Petrarch rendered in one of his Sonnets, desiring only the wings of the Dove in order to rest, and to rise from the Earth. This graceful image will confirm election, judgment, and counsel: and from this image Jupiter is given to be a quiet, benign Planet, and of composed mind.","kind":"passage","sequence":73,"address":"4.73","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0073"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074","text":"Under the Gorgons of Saturn shall be the image of Hercules, who lifts Antaeus, Saturn, upon his breast. Hercules is the human spirit. Antaeus is the body. The breast of Hercules is the seat of Wisdom and Prudence; these two (as Paul says)","kind":"passage","sequence":74,"address":"4.74","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0075","text":"E  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":75,"address":"4.75","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0075"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0076","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":76,"address":"4.76","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0076"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","text":"wage continual struggle and unceasing war, because continually the flesh rises up against the spirit, and the spirit against the flesh; nor can the spirit be victor in the battle unless it raises the body so high from the earth that with its feet—that is, with its affections—it cannot recover strength from its mother, and holds it so tightly that it kills it. Wherein we chiefly have two things to consider: one is the death of the body, the other is, as it were, its transformation into the spirit. And indeed, if our body does not die the death of the affections, it cannot become spiritual, nor become one in Christ. Of which death Paul thus speaks: You are dead, and your life is hidden with Christ in God; and David: Precious in the sight of the Lord is the death of his saints. And in Psalm 62 one reads that the flesh turns its desire toward God equally with the spirit.","kind":"passage","sequence":77,"address":"4.77","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","text":"My soul has thirsted for thee; how greatly my flesh [has thirsted] for thee: And Paul, in the third [chapter] to the Philippians: God is about to reform the body of your humility, fashioning it like unto the body of his glory. And Christ, in the similitude of the death of the grain: Unless a grain of wheat, falling into the earth, has died, it remains itself alone; but if it has died, it bears much fruit. And if our interpretation be well considered, it will be found that we have also made manifest the transmutation, which is one of the two things proposed by us: and Petrarch touched upon this gracefully when he said: Flying to heaven with the earthly burden. This transmutation is likewise greatly manifested in the three blind sisters, who, having an eye not their own but that of others, and lending themselves to one another, conform together, and become one and the same thing, like Nessamah drawn by the angel, which draws the Ruàh, and that the Nephesh.","kind":"passage","sequence":78,"address":"4.78","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0079","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":79,"address":"4.79","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0079"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0080","text":"35","kind":"passage","sequence":80,"address":"4.80","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0080"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","text":"And thus the spiritual transformation is made. Now this image, to signify for us both the tenacity in the tightness exerted by Hercules, and the lifting up from the earth on high, will cover a volume in which all the things belonging to these parts shall be distinguished, such as the impressions that the soul bears from Heaven, memory, knowledge, opinion, practical intellect—that is, understanding—thought, imagination, and contemplation. And this first image is fitting to Saturn, because the same measure in the supercelestial Rina, that is, of the intellect, is common to Saturn. And then because it is so steadfast. Another image shall also be under this door, namely, a maiden ascending through Capricorn. And this shall signify the ascent of souls into Heaven. And this image is given to Saturn, because Capricorn is his house.","kind":"passage","sequence":81,"address":"4.81","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081"]}],"source_digest":"91e502ac584524d10cf142d770b68ea5c74d40688ac4f9a91462fcc6794bb551","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"LE GORGONI,"}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"LE GORGONI,","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI","title":"PASIPHAË","order":5,"chapter_id":"CH_LIDT_PASI","text":"PASIPHE\n\nDicono i Platonici le anime noſtre la ſuſo hauere vn vehiculo igneo, o vero ethereo, percioche altramente non hauerebbono mouimento, percioche coſa non ſi muoue ſe non per mezo del corpo. Il che è comprobato negli angeli da Dauid quãdo dice. Qui facit Angelos ſuos ſpiritus, & miniſtros ſuos flammam ignis vel ventum. Et aggiungono i Platonici, che quando à ciaſcuna delle dette anime è ap-\nparecchiato nel ventre materno il vehiculo terreno, ſe ben la anima, che è nel ſottiliſſimo vehiculo igneo ſi voleſſe copular col corpo, cioè vehiculo terreno, non potrebbe, per cioche tanta ſottilità, con tanta groſſezza non potrebbe con uenir ſenza vn mezo che teneſſe della natura dell’vno, &\n\nE  iii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\ndell’alto,& che per tanto ſcendendo ella di Cielo, in Cie lo,& di ſpera di elemento in ſpera di elemento, va tanto ingroſſandoſi, che acquiſta vn vehiculo aereo, il qual tenendo della natura di amendue viene à farſi copulatione. Que ſta opinion tenne anchor Virgilio nel ſeſto,doue dice che le anime peccatrici partendoſi da queſto corpo,anchor che eſſe le dal terren vehiculo ſiano liberate, per tutto ciò non ſono libere dell’aereo,& per tal cagioni vanno à luoghi purga torii,doue tanto dimorano,che dell’aereo vehiculo ſono libe re,& ritornate nel puro igneo, nel quale al terzo luogo aſcendono. Queſta alla philoſophia a fin che non foſſe პრო phanata fu coperta nella Theologia ſimbolica dalla fauo-\nla di Paſiphe. Perciochè ella del Toro innamorata ſignifica l’anima laqual ſecondo i Platonici cade in cupidita del cor po. Et non ſi poſſendo per queſta copula di coſa tanto ſottile & tanto groſſa, la noua Vaccha finta, che ſignifica il finto corpo aereo, con il quale venuta a congiungimento, con-\ncepiſce & partoriſce vn moſtro chiamato Minotauro, del quale al ſuo luogo parleremo. Queſta imagine adunque di Paſiphe ſopra qualunque porta del quinto Grado del Thea tro coprirà tutte quelle imagini, alle quali ſaranno raccomã dati volumi contenenti coſe,& parole appartenenti non al l’huomo interior: ſolamente, ma à quello, che è coper-\nto anchor dallo eſteriore & appreſſo alle membra particolari del corpo ſecondo la natura di ciaſcun pianeta, legati membra particolari, & ſoggette alla natura del continente vol pianeta ſaranno ſempre ſotto la ultima imagine, che ſa rà vn toro ſolo.\n\nLuna.\n\nSotto la Paſiphe della Luna ſaranno ſei imagini, Vna fanciulla ſcendente per lo Cancro. Et queſta ſi=\n\nDIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n36\n\nſignifica l’anima ſcender dal cielo, la entrata ſua nel corpo, la dimora di quella nel corpo auanti il naſcimento & il naſcimento co loro appartenenti.\n\nDiana à cui Mercurio porge la meſſa ſignifica mutation di\nanimo ò di figura di corpo.\n\nLe Stelle d’Angui ſignificano le ſporchezze del corpo, & i\nſuoi eſcrementi.\n\nGiunon fra le nubi ſignificano aſcondimento di perſona.\n\nPrometheo appreſſo un monte, il quale ſi mette in dito uno anello d’una catena attaccata al detto monte: & è da ſa-\npere che nelle antiche fauole ſi legge, che per lo furto che Prometheo fece del fuoco, Gioue lo legò, ò dannò ad eſſer legato con una Catena al monte Caucaſo, da poi moſſo dalla ſua pietà lo liberò. Et egli grato di tal beneficio pre-\nſe uno anello della catena, & un poco di ſaſſo del Caucaſo, & l’uno & l’altro ſi legò ad un dio, Onde dicono eſ-\nſere ad un tempo nata la inuention dello anello, & il pro-\nuerbio di hauerla ſi legata al dito. Queſta imagine conſer-\nuera la gratitudine, la obligatione, & il debito, & ſimili. Et s’appartiene alla Luna per l’apparente beneficio, che tanto di riceue dal Sole più che alcun altro pianeta.\n\nUn Tauro ſolo, ilquale hà à contener(ſi come in ogni altra Paſiphe) alcuni membri del corpo humano. Et di quelli alcuni eſtraordinarii, & alcuni ordinarii. Eſtra ordinarii chia-\nmo, percioche eſſendo tutto il capo dell’huomo ſecondo gli Aſtrologi conſegnato all’ariete, che è uno de ſegni del Zo-\ndiaco, ragioneuolmente va tutto ſotto il Tauro della Paſiphe di Marte, per eſſer l’ariete la ſua caſa. Nondimeno le-\nuiamo fuori del detto capo i capelli, la barba, & tutti i pe-\nli del corpo, & anche il ceruello Et gli conſegniamo per la\n\nE\n\niiii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nloro humidità, o per la attrattion di quella a membri eſtra ordinarii della Luna, la quale per membri ordinarii ha il petto, & le poppe, percioche tutta la parte del petto è ſecon do gli Aſtrologi del Cancro, che è caſa della Luna.\n\nMercu-\nrio.\n\nSotto la Paſſiphe di Mercurio ſono imagini. Il Vello dell’oro ilqual contiene la grandezza, & legge rezza del corpo humano, la aſprezza, la mollitie, & la ſolidezza di quello. Gli Atomi ſignificheranno quantita di ſcrete ne gli huomini, come alcuno. La piramide ſignifichera quantita continua ne gli huomini come grande, picciolo, di mezana ſtatura. Giunon cinta di nubi, ſimulatore & diſſimulatore, aſtuta & inganneuol natura. Iſione legato ad una ruota ſignifica ſecondo la openione di Lucretio le mortali cure. Et à queſta imagine ſarà dato in guardia la natura negozioſa, faticoſa, & induſtrioſa. Un Toro. Queſta haurà per membri eſtraordinarii la lin= gua con le ſue parti & conſequenti, come i linguaggi, & il parlar ordinato per li ſuoi capi ben diſtinti, coſi tanto ma rauiglioſa, quanto ſi vedrà per li fogli del ſuo volume. I membri ordinarii ſaranno di due maniere, per hauer Mer curio due caſe, cio è Gemini & Vergine. Et per conto di Ge mini haurà gli homeri, le braccia & le mani per Vergine hauerà.\n\nVenere.\n\nSotto la Paſſiphe di Venere ſaranno ſette imagini. Cerbero ſignifichera fame, ſete, & ſonno. Hercule purgante le ſtalle di Augia conterrà le nettezza del corpo. Narciso conterrà bellezza, vaghezza, leggiadria, amor;\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n37\n\ndiſegno, inamorarsi , deſiderio, ſperanza &c. & haura\ndue catene.\n\nBacco con l’Haſta in mano veſtita di hedera ſigniſichera lui non voler combattere, ma darſi buon tempo. Et per tanto ha hauera volume pertinente all’otio, & alla tranquillita dell’a= nimo, dinotando natura allegra, ſollazzeuole, & che atte ſia à darſi buon tempo.\n\nVn Minotauro. Queſto è il parto di Paſiphe ſecondo i poe ti, congiunta co’l Toro. Et qui è da notar che la Theologia ſimbolica non ſenza miſterio ha introdutto non pure il Mi= notauro, ma i Centauri, & i Satiri, & Fauni, & ſimili che portano la figura humana inſino al bilico , & dal bilico in giu la portano di beſtia: percioche gli huomini che ſono vi= tioſi, & che non ſono partecipi del raggio diuino (del qual s’è detto) hanno ſolamente la figura humana, ma nel rima= nente ſono da eſſer comparati alle beſtie. Scriue Platon nel Timeo la parte iraſcibile noſtra eſſer da dare al cuore , & che la concupiſcibile è ſotto la cartilagine chiamata dia= phragma, ſotto la quale ſono tutte le paſſioni & queſta di= uide quaſi noi da noi medeſimi: & hauendo noi queſta parte piu baſſa comune con le beſtie, ſe le compiacciamo, diueni= mo beſtie. Con graue ragione adunque gli antichi hanno fin to l’huomo traſformato in beſtia da quella parte in giu.\n\nAdunque à queſta imagine daremo natura inclinata al vi= tio, quantunque non ſi eſercitaſſe, qual fu quella di Socra= te per la confeſſion di lui medeſimo. Et queſto dico, perciò che il vitio eſercitato ſi tratterà ne Talari.\n\nTantalo ſotto il ſaſſo dinoterà natura timida, & ſoſpeſa,\n& dubioſa, & marauiglioſa.\n\nVn Toro per membri eſtraordinarij hauera il naſo et la vir\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nſù odoratina, percioche venere ha anchora gli odori. Et ha vna anchora le guance, le labbra, e’l diuorare, & per la Libra lezza. Per membri ordinarii hauera per Tauro hauera il collo la gola, l’inghiottire, e’l diuorare, & per la Libra hauera la parte di dietro, che è la groppa.\n\nSole.\n\nSotto la Paſiphe del Sole ſaranno cinque imagini. Gerione vcciſo da Hercole ſignifichera l’età dell’huomo. Il Gallo col Leone ſignifichera eccellenza, ſuperiorità, de gnità, authorità, dominio dell’huomo in coſe di honore. Le Parche ſignifichera l’huomo eſſer Re, e ſignor di alcuna coſa. La Vacca guardata da Argo hauera i colori del corpo humano. Apollo che feriſce Giunon fra le nubi ſignifichera la mani ſtation dell’huomo, & il venir à luce. Un Tauro per membri eſtraordinarii hauera gli orecchi con le loro operationi, come ſono il mirare, & il vedere, & per membri ordinarii hauera la ſchiena, & i fianchi, per eſ ſer quelli del Leone, che è caſa del Sole. Sotto Marte ſaranno ſei imagini.\n\nMorte.\n\nIſione che vuol abbracciar la Giunon finta di nubi, che ſi legge nelle antiche fauole, che Iſione fu sì ſuperbo di na tura, & sì arrogante, & sì preſuntuoso, che ſenza hauer a Gioue alcun riſpetto non ſolamente ſi diede ad amar Giu none, mà anchora de ſuoi abbracciamenti la richiede. Diſſe che ella ſdegnata, per iſchermirſi finſe vna Giunon di Nu bi, con la quale Iſione ſi giacque, & di quella giacitura ne naſquero i Centauri. Queſta imagine adunque hauera ſot to di ſe nello aſſo; lo volume due catene, l’una appartenen te alla preſuntione di Iſione & l’altra allo ſdegno di Giu none. La prima hauera per auelli natura orgoglioſa, ſuper\n\nv.\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO  38\n\nbe, nuotatrice, preſuntuosa, arrogante, & ſimili. Et l’alma natura ſdegnosa, & ſchermiſtrice, & beſſatrice. Due ſerpi combattenti ſignificheranno natura contentioſa. Vna fanciulla co capelli leuati verſo il cielo contenerà na-\ntura forte, vigorosa, & nerbace.     Marte ſopra il Dragone\nſignificherà natura nociva. Vn huomo ſenza capo, cioè ſen za ceruello, il quale è il ſetto dell’intelletto, & per queſta imagine ci ſarà ſignificata natura furioſa, o pazza. Vn Tauro. Queſto non haurà membra eſtraordinarie, ma per ordinario per l’Ariete haurà la teſta, et per lo Scorpione haurà le parti genitale con le loro operationi.\n\nSotto la Paſſiphe di Gioue ſaranno ſei imagini.\n\nGioue.\n\nIl Leone vcciſo da Hercole.\n\nA la dichiaration di queſta ſa uola ci ſa biſogno intendere, che quel luogo della Scrittura Iſrael ſi me audieris, non adorabis Deos alienos, neque erit in te Deus recens, ci ſa intender che poſſiamo far due gra-\nuiſſimi peccati, l’uno di non adorar Dio vero & ſolo, l’altro di commetter maggiore Idolatria, che non faceua l’antica ſim plicita Imperoche quella adoraua Dei fuor di ſe, ma i piu di noi adoriamo i Dei, che ci facciamo dentro di noi. Percio che de capi ſacrati ne monſtreri molti hanno fatto dentro di ſe vno idolo della loro cõtinenza, & caſtità. Et nō ſolamēte eſſi la adorano, ma vorrebbono p̄ gli altri deſſal riuerire ado rati, & coſi hanno dirizzato dentro della loro fantaſia vna dea Veſta, et i piu literati hanno dirizzato Vna Pallade, la qual non ſolamente eſſi adorano, ma vorrebbono ancor che foſſe da tutti eſtimata & adorata. I Prencipe de gli eſſerciti hanno dirizzata nel cuore la Deità di marte. Ne ſolamente eſſi la reputano, & adorano, ma vorrebbono che tutti a quel la s’inchinaſſero. Et per dir briue, tutti habbiamo dentro\n\nL’ IDEAL THEATRO\n\nVn fiero & ſuperbo leone, che ſignifica la noſtra malvagità, & indomita ambitione. Et è il recente Dio, che ci habbiamo dentro. Se adunque il noſtro ſpirito diventa vn Hercole fortiſſimo, vcciderà queſto leone, il quale vcciſo, ne ſeguirà la humilità, nella qual ſola poſſiamo piacere à Dio diuene-\ndo pargoli, & poveri di ſpirito Queſta imagine adunque ſotto la paſiphe di Gioue ci ſignifichera natura humile, ver-\ngognoſa, & inclinata alla bontà, & a tutte quelle coſe che ſe ben da Philoſophi non ſono chiamate virtù, ſono non dimeno di ſpoſitione à quella, come habbiamo detto della vergogna.\n\nMa ſotto i Talari ſignifichera eſercitatione di tal bon-\nta, o buona diſpoſitione. Il Minotauro vcciſo da Teſeo nel Labirintho darà ſignificatione di inclinatione alla virtù. Ma ſotto i talari ſignifichera qualunque delle virtù nelle ſue attioni che altramente non ſarebbono virtù, che molti ſanno la diffinitione della virtù ſenza hauerla. Et queſta da Cicerone è virtù chiamata attuoſa & da Virgilio arde-\nte, & coſi dal Petr. Et nel vero ſe il Minotauro vivo ſignifica vitio, morto dee ſignificar virtù.\n\nIl Caduceo ſignifichera natura amicheuole, & inchinata alla cura familiare, & alla republica. Danae ſignifica bona fortuna, felicità, ſanità, richez-\nza nobilità, & ottenimento di deſideria. Le Gratie ſignificano natura benefica. Vn Tauro hà per membra eſtraordinarie gli orecchi, et le loro operationi, vdire & aſcoltare & anche la paſſione come la ſordezza, ordinaria per lo Sagittario le coſce, per li Peſci i Piedi & loro operationi,\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.  39\n\nSotto la Paſſphe di Saturno ſono ſette imagini. I tre capi, del lupo, del leone, & del cane ſignificano huomo eſſer ſottopoſto al tempo.\n\nProteo legato ſignifica natura oſtinata & immutabi-\nle.\n\nIl paſſer ſolitario ſignifica natura ſolitaria o huomo ſo-\nlo o abbandonato.\n\nPandora malvagia fortuna, infelicita, ignobilita,\npoverta, infamia, infermita non ottener deſiderio.\n\nLa fanciulla co capelli tagliati dinotera debilita dell’huo\nmo, ſtanchezza, & menzogna.\n\nEndimione addormentato ſopra un monte, & baſciato da Diana. Si legge appreſſo Cabaliſti, che ſenza la morte del baſcio non ci poſſiamo vnir di vera vniōne co celeſti, ne cō Dio. Queſto dico, percioche fra il numero di piu morti, nelle quali entra anchor quella, che dicemmo di Anteo, è que ſta del baſcio, della quale Salomone coſi fa mentione nel principio della Cantica. Oſculetur me oſculo oris ſui. Il= qual ſenſo per altre parole è piu apertamente detto da Pao lo, quando dice, Cupio diſſolui, & eſſe con Chriſto. il qual deſiderio non è eſpreſſo da Salomone ne la ſignificatione del verbo, come da Paolo, ma ſi nel modo deſideratiuo. Et il Petrarca lo miſe nell’indeclinabile quando diſſe.\n\nO felice quel di che dal terreno Carcere uſcendo, laſci rotta & ſparta Queſta mia graue, & frale, & mortal gonna, Et da ſi lunghe tenebre mi parta Volando tanto in ſu nel bel ſereno, Ch’io vegga il mio ſignore & la mia donna.\n\nAdunque il corpo eſſendo quello, che ci tien ſeparati da\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nla vnion vera , & dal baſcio che vorrebbeno fare le coſe celeſti , alle anime noſtre raccogliendole a loro , ſegue che per la diſſolution di quello ſi verrebe a queſto baſcio. Il che i Theologhi ſimbolici volendo aprire hanno laſciato nelle lor fauole,che Diana(la qual tenendo il regno di tut= te le miſure ſopraceleſti,& per lei paſſando tutti gli influſſi ſuperiori,è vicaria & luogotenente di tutte le coſe ſupe= riori,)hanno finto dico,che queſta innamorata di Endimione cio è dell’anima noſtra,la quale ſi aſpetta la ſua,deſideroſa di poterlo laſciare mentre ſugge, l’addormenta di ſonno perpetuo ſopra un monte,& hauendolo addormentato,puo nel baſciarlo ſatiar le ſue voglie.Il qual ſonno perpetuo ſi= gnificando la morte;queſta imagine contenerà l’eſſer mor= tale,la morte,& tutti gli anelli a lei appartenenti come la pompa funebre.\n\nVn Toro.Quеſto per membra eſtraordinarie haurà i pe ti canuti,& le creſpe:& per ordinario per conto di Capri corno le ginocchia,& per Aquario le gambe.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0001","text":"PASIPHE","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"5.1"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","text":"Dicono i Platonici le anime noſtre la ſuſo hauere vn vehiculo igneo, o vero ethereo, percioche altramente non hauerebbono mouimento, percioche coſa non ſi muoue ſe non per mezo del corpo. Il che è comprobato negli angeli da Dauid quãdo dice. Qui facit Angelos ſuos ſpiritus, & miniſtros ſuos flammam ignis vel ventum. Et aggiungono i Platonici, che quando à ciaſcuna delle dette anime è ap-\nparecchiato nel ventre materno il vehiculo terreno, ſe ben la anima, che è nel ſottiliſſimo vehiculo igneo ſi voleſſe copular col corpo, cioè vehiculo terreno, non potrebbe, per cioche tanta ſottilità, con tanta groſſezza non potrebbe con uenir ſenza vn mezo che teneſſe della natura dell’vno, &","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"5.2"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0003","text":"E  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"5.3"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0004","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"5.4"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","text":"dell’alto,& che per tanto ſcendendo ella di Cielo, in Cie lo,& di ſpera di elemento in ſpera di elemento, va tanto ingroſſandoſi, che acquiſta vn vehiculo aereo, il qual tenendo della natura di amendue viene à farſi copulatione. Que ſta opinion tenne anchor Virgilio nel ſeſto,doue dice che le anime peccatrici partendoſi da queſto corpo,anchor che eſſe le dal terren vehiculo ſiano liberate, per tutto ciò non ſono libere dell’aereo,& per tal cagioni vanno à luoghi purga torii,doue tanto dimorano,che dell’aereo vehiculo ſono libe re,& ritornate nel puro igneo, nel quale al terzo luogo aſcendono. Queſta alla philoſophia a fin che non foſſe პრო phanata fu coperta nella Theologia ſimbolica dalla fauo-\nla di Paſiphe. Perciochè ella del Toro innamorata ſignifica l’anima laqual ſecondo i Platonici cade in cupidita del cor po.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"5.5"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","text":"Et non ſi poſſendo per queſta copula di coſa tanto ſottile & tanto groſſa, la noua Vaccha finta, che ſignifica il finto corpo aereo, con il quale venuta a congiungimento, con-\ncepiſce & partoriſce vn moſtro chiamato Minotauro, del quale al ſuo luogo parleremo. Queſta imagine adunque di Paſiphe ſopra qualunque porta del quinto Grado del Thea tro coprirà tutte quelle imagini, alle quali ſaranno raccomã dati volumi contenenti coſe,& parole appartenenti non al l’huomo interior: ſolamente, ma à quello, che è coper-\nto anchor dallo eſteriore & appreſſo alle membra particolari del corpo ſecondo la natura di ciaſcun pianeta, legati membra particolari, & ſoggette alla natura del continente vol pianeta ſaranno ſempre ſotto la ultima imagine, che ſa rà vn toro ſolo.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"5.6"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0007","text":"Luna.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"5.7"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0008","text":"Sotto la Paſiphe della Luna ſaranno ſei imagini, Vna fanciulla ſcendente per lo Cancro. Et queſta ſi=","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"5.8"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0009","text":"DIM. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"5.9"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0010","text":"36","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"5.10"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0011","text":"ſignifica l’anima ſcender dal cielo, la entrata ſua nel corpo, la dimora di quella nel corpo auanti il naſcimento & il naſcimento co loro appartenenti.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"5.11"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0012","text":"Diana à cui Mercurio porge la meſſa ſignifica mutation di\nanimo ò di figura di corpo.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"5.12"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0013","text":"Le Stelle d’Angui ſignificano le ſporchezze del corpo, & i\nſuoi eſcrementi.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"5.13"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0014","text":"Giunon fra le nubi ſignificano aſcondimento di perſona.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"5.14"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0015","text":"Prometheo appreſſo un monte, il quale ſi mette in dito uno anello d’una catena attaccata al detto monte: & è da ſa-\npere che nelle antiche fauole ſi legge, che per lo furto che Prometheo fece del fuoco, Gioue lo legò, ò dannò ad eſſer legato con una Catena al monte Caucaſo, da poi moſſo dalla ſua pietà lo liberò. Et egli grato di tal beneficio pre-\nſe uno anello della catena, & un poco di ſaſſo del Caucaſo, & l’uno & l’altro ſi legò ad un dio, Onde dicono eſ-\nſere ad un tempo nata la inuention dello anello, & il pro-\nuerbio di hauerla ſi legata al dito. Queſta imagine conſer-\nuera la gratitudine, la obligatione, & il debito, & ſimili. Et s’appartiene alla Luna per l’apparente beneficio, che tanto di riceue dal Sole più che alcun altro pianeta.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"5.15"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","text":"Un Tauro ſolo, ilquale hà à contener(ſi come in ogni altra Paſiphe) alcuni membri del corpo humano. Et di quelli alcuni eſtraordinarii, & alcuni ordinarii. Eſtra ordinarii chia-\nmo, percioche eſſendo tutto il capo dell’huomo ſecondo gli Aſtrologi conſegnato all’ariete, che è uno de ſegni del Zo-\ndiaco, ragioneuolmente va tutto ſotto il Tauro della Paſiphe di Marte, per eſſer l’ariete la ſua caſa. Nondimeno le-\nuiamo fuori del detto capo i capelli, la barba, & tutti i pe-\nli del corpo, & anche il ceruello Et gli conſegniamo per la","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"5.16"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0017","text":"E\n\niiii","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"5.17"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0018","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"5.18"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","text":"loro humidità, o per la attrattion di quella a membri eſtra ordinarii della Luna, la quale per membri ordinarii ha il petto, & le poppe, percioche tutta la parte del petto è ſecon do gli Aſtrologi del Cancro, che è caſa della Luna.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"5.19"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0020","text":"Mercu-\nrio.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"5.20"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","text":"Sotto la Paſſiphe di Mercurio ſono imagini. Il Vello dell’oro ilqual contiene la grandezza, & legge rezza del corpo humano, la aſprezza, la mollitie, & la ſolidezza di quello. Gli Atomi ſignificheranno quantita di ſcrete ne gli huomini, come alcuno. La piramide ſignifichera quantita continua ne gli huomini come grande, picciolo, di mezana ſtatura. Giunon cinta di nubi, ſimulatore & diſſimulatore, aſtuta & inganneuol natura. Iſione legato ad una ruota ſignifica ſecondo la openione di Lucretio le mortali cure. Et à queſta imagine ſarà dato in guardia la natura negozioſa, faticoſa, & induſtrioſa. Un Toro. Queſta haurà per membri eſtraordinarii la lin= gua con le ſue parti & conſequenti, come i linguaggi, & il parlar ordinato per li ſuoi capi ben diſtinti, coſi tanto ma rauiglioſa, quanto ſi vedrà per li fogli del ſuo volume.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"5.21"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","text":"I membri ordinarii ſaranno di due maniere, per hauer Mer curio due caſe, cio è Gemini & Vergine. Et per conto di Ge mini haurà gli homeri, le braccia & le mani per Vergine hauerà.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"5.22"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0023","text":"Venere.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"5.23"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0024","text":"Sotto la Paſſiphe di Venere ſaranno ſette imagini. Cerbero ſignifichera fame, ſete, & ſonno. Hercule purgante le ſtalle di Augia conterrà le nettezza del corpo. Narciso conterrà bellezza, vaghezza, leggiadria, amor;","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"5.24"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0025","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"5.25"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0026","text":"37","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"5.26"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0027","text":"diſegno, inamorarsi , deſiderio, ſperanza &c. & haura\ndue catene.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"5.27"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0028","text":"Bacco con l’Haſta in mano veſtita di hedera ſigniſichera lui non voler combattere, ma darſi buon tempo. Et per tanto ha hauera volume pertinente all’otio, & alla tranquillita dell’a= nimo, dinotando natura allegra, ſollazzeuole, & che atte ſia à darſi buon tempo.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"5.28"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","text":"Vn Minotauro. Queſto è il parto di Paſiphe ſecondo i poe ti, congiunta co’l Toro. Et qui è da notar che la Theologia ſimbolica non ſenza miſterio ha introdutto non pure il Mi= notauro, ma i Centauri, & i Satiri, & Fauni, & ſimili che portano la figura humana inſino al bilico , & dal bilico in giu la portano di beſtia: percioche gli huomini che ſono vi= tioſi, & che non ſono partecipi del raggio diuino (del qual s’è detto) hanno ſolamente la figura humana, ma nel rima= nente ſono da eſſer comparati alle beſtie. Scriue Platon nel Timeo la parte iraſcibile noſtra eſſer da dare al cuore , & che la concupiſcibile è ſotto la cartilagine chiamata dia= phragma, ſotto la quale ſono tutte le paſſioni & queſta di= uide quaſi noi da noi medeſimi: & hauendo noi queſta parte piu baſſa comune con le beſtie, ſe le compiacciamo, diueni= mo beſtie.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"5.29"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0030","text":"Con graue ragione adunque gli antichi hanno fin to l’huomo traſformato in beſtia da quella parte in giu.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"5.30"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","text":"Adunque à queſta imagine daremo natura inclinata al vi= tio, quantunque non ſi eſercitaſſe, qual fu quella di Socra= te per la confeſſion di lui medeſimo. Et queſto dico, perciò che il vitio eſercitato ſi tratterà ne Talari.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"5.31"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0032","text":"Tantalo ſotto il ſaſſo dinoterà natura timida, & ſoſpeſa,\n& dubioſa, & marauiglioſa.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"5.32"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0033","text":"Vn Toro per membri eſtraordinarij hauera il naſo et la vir","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"5.33"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0034","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"5.34"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0035","text":"ſù odoratina, percioche venere ha anchora gli odori. Et ha vna anchora le guance, le labbra, e’l diuorare, & per la Libra lezza. Per membri ordinarii hauera per Tauro hauera il collo la gola, l’inghiottire, e’l diuorare, & per la Libra hauera la parte di dietro, che è la groppa.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"5.35"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0036","text":"Sole.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"5.36"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0037","text":"Sotto la Paſiphe del Sole ſaranno cinque imagini. Gerione vcciſo da Hercole ſignifichera l’età dell’huomo. Il Gallo col Leone ſignifichera eccellenza, ſuperiorità, de gnità, authorità, dominio dell’huomo in coſe di honore. Le Parche ſignifichera l’huomo eſſer Re, e ſignor di alcuna coſa. La Vacca guardata da Argo hauera i colori del corpo humano. Apollo che feriſce Giunon fra le nubi ſignifichera la mani ſtation dell’huomo, & il venir à luce. Un Tauro per membri eſtraordinarii hauera gli orecchi con le loro operationi, come ſono il mirare, & il vedere, & per membri ordinarii hauera la ſchiena, & i fianchi, per eſ ſer quelli del Leone, che è caſa del Sole. Sotto Marte ſaranno ſei imagini.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"5.37"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0038","text":"Morte.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"5.38"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0039","text":"Iſione che vuol abbracciar la Giunon finta di nubi, che ſi legge nelle antiche fauole, che Iſione fu sì ſuperbo di na tura, & sì arrogante, & sì preſuntuoso, che ſenza hauer a Gioue alcun riſpetto non ſolamente ſi diede ad amar Giu none, mà anchora de ſuoi abbracciamenti la richiede. Diſſe che ella ſdegnata, per iſchermirſi finſe vna Giunon di Nu bi, con la quale Iſione ſi giacque, & di quella giacitura ne naſquero i Centauri. Queſta imagine adunque hauera ſot to di ſe nello aſſo; lo volume due catene, l’una appartenen te alla preſuntione di Iſione & l’altra allo ſdegno di Giu none. La prima hauera per auelli natura orgoglioſa, ſuper","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"5.39"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0040","text":"v.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"5.40"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0041","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO  38","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"5.41"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0042","text":"be, nuotatrice, preſuntuosa, arrogante, & ſimili. Et l’alma natura ſdegnosa, & ſchermiſtrice, & beſſatrice. Due ſerpi combattenti ſignificheranno natura contentioſa. Vna fanciulla co capelli leuati verſo il cielo contenerà na-\ntura forte, vigorosa, & nerbace.     Marte ſopra il Dragone\nſignificherà natura nociva. Vn huomo ſenza capo, cioè ſen za ceruello, il quale è il ſetto dell’intelletto, & per queſta imagine ci ſarà ſignificata natura furioſa, o pazza. Vn Tauro. Queſto non haurà membra eſtraordinarie, ma per ordinario per l’Ariete haurà la teſta, et per lo Scorpione haurà le parti genitale con le loro operationi.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"5.42"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0043","text":"Sotto la Paſſiphe di Gioue ſaranno ſei imagini.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"5.43"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0044","text":"Gioue.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"5.44"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0045","text":"Il Leone vcciſo da Hercole.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"5.45"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","text":"A la dichiaration di queſta ſa uola ci ſa biſogno intendere, che quel luogo della Scrittura Iſrael ſi me audieris, non adorabis Deos alienos, neque erit in te Deus recens, ci ſa intender che poſſiamo far due gra-\nuiſſimi peccati, l’uno di non adorar Dio vero & ſolo, l’altro di commetter maggiore Idolatria, che non faceua l’antica ſim plicita Imperoche quella adoraua Dei fuor di ſe, ma i piu di noi adoriamo i Dei, che ci facciamo dentro di noi. Percio che de capi ſacrati ne monſtreri molti hanno fatto dentro di ſe vno idolo della loro cõtinenza, & caſtità. Et nō ſolamēte eſſi la adorano, ma vorrebbono p̄ gli altri deſſal riuerire ado rati, & coſi hanno dirizzato dentro della loro fantaſia vna dea Veſta, et i piu literati hanno dirizzato Vna Pallade, la qual non ſolamente eſſi adorano, ma vorrebbono ancor che foſſe da tutti eſtimata & adorata.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"5.46"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","text":"I Prencipe de gli eſſerciti hanno dirizzata nel cuore la Deità di marte. Ne ſolamente eſſi la reputano, & adorano, ma vorrebbono che tutti a quel la s’inchinaſſero. Et per dir briue, tutti habbiamo dentro","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"5.47"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0048","text":"L’ IDEAL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"5.48"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","text":"Vn fiero & ſuperbo leone, che ſignifica la noſtra malvagità, & indomita ambitione. Et è il recente Dio, che ci habbiamo dentro. Se adunque il noſtro ſpirito diventa vn Hercole fortiſſimo, vcciderà queſto leone, il quale vcciſo, ne ſeguirà la humilità, nella qual ſola poſſiamo piacere à Dio diuene-\ndo pargoli, & poveri di ſpirito Queſta imagine adunque ſotto la paſiphe di Gioue ci ſignifichera natura humile, ver-\ngognoſa, & inclinata alla bontà, & a tutte quelle coſe che ſe ben da Philoſophi non ſono chiamate virtù, ſono non dimeno di ſpoſitione à quella, come habbiamo detto della vergogna.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"5.49"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","text":"Ma ſotto i Talari ſignifichera eſercitatione di tal bon-\nta, o buona diſpoſitione. Il Minotauro vcciſo da Teſeo nel Labirintho darà ſignificatione di inclinatione alla virtù. Ma ſotto i talari ſignifichera qualunque delle virtù nelle ſue attioni che altramente non ſarebbono virtù, che molti ſanno la diffinitione della virtù ſenza hauerla. Et queſta da Cicerone è virtù chiamata attuoſa & da Virgilio arde-\nte, & coſi dal Petr. Et nel vero ſe il Minotauro vivo ſignifica vitio, morto dee ſignificar virtù.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"5.50"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051","text":"Il Caduceo ſignifichera natura amicheuole, & inchinata alla cura familiare, & alla republica. Danae ſignifica bona fortuna, felicità, ſanità, richez-\nza nobilità, & ottenimento di deſideria. Le Gratie ſignificano natura benefica. Vn Tauro hà per membra eſtraordinarie gli orecchi, et le loro operationi, vdire & aſcoltare & anche la paſſione come la ſordezza, ordinaria per lo Sagittario le coſce, per li Peſci i Piedi & loro operationi,","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"5.51"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0052","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.  39","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"5.52"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0053","text":"Sotto la Paſſphe di Saturno ſono ſette imagini. I tre capi, del lupo, del leone, & del cane ſignificano huomo eſſer ſottopoſto al tempo.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"5.53"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0054","text":"Proteo legato ſignifica natura oſtinata & immutabi-\nle.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"5.54"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0055","text":"Il paſſer ſolitario ſignifica natura ſolitaria o huomo ſo-\nlo o abbandonato.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"5.55"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0056","text":"Pandora malvagia fortuna, infelicita, ignobilita,\npoverta, infamia, infermita non ottener deſiderio.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"5.56"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0057","text":"La fanciulla co capelli tagliati dinotera debilita dell’huo\nmo, ſtanchezza, & menzogna.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"5.57"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","text":"Endimione addormentato ſopra un monte, & baſciato da Diana. Si legge appreſſo Cabaliſti, che ſenza la morte del baſcio non ci poſſiamo vnir di vera vniōne co celeſti, ne cō Dio. Queſto dico, percioche fra il numero di piu morti, nelle quali entra anchor quella, che dicemmo di Anteo, è que ſta del baſcio, della quale Salomone coſi fa mentione nel principio della Cantica. Oſculetur me oſculo oris ſui. Il= qual ſenſo per altre parole è piu apertamente detto da Pao lo, quando dice, Cupio diſſolui, & eſſe con Chriſto. il qual deſiderio non è eſpreſſo da Salomone ne la ſignificatione del verbo, come da Paolo, ma ſi nel modo deſideratiuo. Et il Petrarca lo miſe nell’indeclinabile quando diſſe.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"5.58"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","text":"O felice quel di che dal terreno Carcere uſcendo, laſci rotta & ſparta Queſta mia graue, & frale, & mortal gonna, Et da ſi lunghe tenebre mi parta Volando tanto in ſu nel bel ſereno, Ch’io vegga il mio ſignore & la mia donna.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"5.59"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","text":"Adunque il corpo eſſendo quello, che ci tien ſeparati da","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"5.60"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0061","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"5.61"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","text":"la vnion vera , & dal baſcio che vorrebbeno fare le coſe celeſti , alle anime noſtre raccogliendole a loro , ſegue che per la diſſolution di quello ſi verrebe a queſto baſcio. Il che i Theologhi ſimbolici volendo aprire hanno laſciato nelle lor fauole,che Diana(la qual tenendo il regno di tut= te le miſure ſopraceleſti,& per lei paſſando tutti gli influſſi ſuperiori,è vicaria & luogotenente di tutte le coſe ſupe= riori,)hanno finto dico,che queſta innamorata di Endimione cio è dell’anima noſtra,la quale ſi aſpetta la ſua,deſideroſa di poterlo laſciare mentre ſugge, l’addormenta di ſonno perpetuo ſopra un monte,& hauendolo addormentato,puo nel baſciarlo ſatiar le ſue voglie.Il qual ſonno perpetuo ſi= gnificando la morte;queſta imagine contenerà l’eſſer mor= tale,la morte,& tutti gli anelli a lei appartenenti come la pompa funebre.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"5.62"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0063","text":"Vn Toro.Quеſto per membra eſtraordinarie haurà i pe ti canuti,& le creſpe:& per ordinario per conto di Capri corno le ginocchia,& per Aquario le gambe.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"5.63"}],"sha256":"b272f37d8856970061c6cdd29f9099139c5130b17919506ff8bcda3133b058ec","language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261030T230714512885Z_b77c59b5","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"PASIPHAË","source_sha256":"b272f37d8856970061c6cdd29f9099139c5130b17919506ff8bcda3133b058ec","sha256":"7be8c6f5086192922e1e376598fe1a96d23ec047d66f64dc23d4a4e036d1d686","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:07:14.512958+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0001","text":"PASIPHAË","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"5.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","text":"The Platonists say that our souls above have a fiery, or indeed ethereal, vehicle, because otherwise they would have no movement, since nothing moves except by means of a body. This is proved in the angels by David when he says: Qui facit Angelos suos spiritus, & ministros suos flammam ignis vel ventum. And the Platonists add that, when for each of the said souls the terrestrial vehicle is prepared in the maternal womb, although the soul, which is in the most subtle fiery vehicle, should wish to join with the body, that is, the terrestrial vehicle, it could not do so, because such subtlety could not agree with such grossness without a medium that partook of the nature of the one, &","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"5.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0003","text":"E  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"5.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0004","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"5.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","text":"of the other, and therefore, descending from Heaven, into Heaven, and from sphere of element into sphere of element, it becomes so much thickened that it acquires an aerial vehicle, which, partaking of the nature of both, comes to effect the conjunction. Virgil too held this opinion in the sixth [book], where he says that sinful souls, departing from this body, although they are freed from the terrestrial vehicle, nevertheless are not free from the aerial one; and for such reasons they go to purgatorial places, where they remain so long that they are freed from the aerial vehicle, and, having returned to the pure fiery one, ascend to the third place. This philosophy, lest it should be profaned, was concealed in symbolic Theology by the fable of Pasiphaë. For she, being in love with the Bull, signifies the soul which, according to the Platonists, falls into desire for the body.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"5.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","text":"And since, through this coupling of a thing so subtle and so gross, [she] could not [conceive], the feigned new Cow, which signifies the feigned aerial body, with which, having come to conjunction, she conceives and gives birth to a monster called the Minotaur, of whom we shall speak in his place. This image, then, of Pasiphaë above every gate of the fifth Grade of the Theatre shall cover all those images to which volumes containing things and words pertaining not only to the inner man shall be entrusted, but to that which is also covered by the exterior and belongs to the particular members of the body according to the nature of each planet; particular members bound and subject to the nature of the containing planet shall always be under the final image, which shall be a bull alone.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"5.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0007","text":"Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"5.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0008","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of the Moon there shall be six images. A maiden descending through Cancer. And this sig=","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"5.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0009","text":"OF M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"5.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0010","text":"36","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"5.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0011","text":"nifies the soul's descent from heaven, its entry into the body, its dwelling in the body before birth, and birth with their appurtenances.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"5.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0012","text":"Diana, to whom Mercury offers the message, signifies a change of\nmind or of bodily form.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"5.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0013","text":"The Stars of Serpents signify the filthiness of the body, & its\nexcrements.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"5.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0014","text":"Juno among the clouds signifies concealment of the person.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"5.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0015","text":"Prometheus beside a mountain, who places upon his finger a ring from a chain fastened to the said mountain: and it should be known that in the ancient fables one reads that, for the theft Prometheus made of fire, Jupiter bound him, or condemned him to be bound, with a Chain to Mount Caucasus; afterwards, moved by pity for him, he freed him. And he, grateful for such a benefit, took a ring from the chain and a little stone from Caucasus, and bound both the one and the other to a finger. Whence they say that at one time were born the invention of the ring and the proverb of having it bound to one's finger. This image shall preserve gratitude, obligation, and debt, and the like. And it belongs to the Moon on account of the apparent benefit which it receives from the Sun more than any other planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"5.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","text":"A Bull alone, which is to contain (as in every other Pasiphaë) certain members of the human body. And of these, some extraordinary and some ordinary. I call them extraordinary because, since the whole head of man is, according to the Astrologers, assigned to Aries, which is one of the signs of the Zodiac, it reasonably falls entirely under the Bull of the Pasiphaë of Mars, because Aries is its house. Nevertheless, let us remove from the said head the hair, the beard, and all the hairs of the body, and also the brain, and assign them, on account of their","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"5.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0017","text":"E\n\niiii","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"5.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0018","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"5.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","text":"moisture, or because of the attraction thereof, to the extraordinary members of the Moon, which among its ordinary members has the chest and the breasts, because the whole part of the chest is, according to the Astrologers, under Cancer, which is the house of the Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"5.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0020","text":"Mercu-\nry.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"5.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of Mercury are images. The Golden Fleece, which contains the largeness and lightness of the human body, its roughness, softness, and solidity. The Atoms shall signify discrete quantity in men, as someone. The pyramid shall signify continuous quantity in men, such as great, small, of middle stature. Juno girded with clouds: a simulator and dissembler, a cunning and deceitful nature. Ixion bound to a wheel signifies, according to the opinion of Lucretius, mortal cares. And to this image shall be entrusted a busy, laborious, and industrious nature. A Bull. This shall have as extraordinary members the tongue with its parts and consequences, such as languages, and speech ordered according to its well-distinguished heads, so very marvellous, as shall be seen from the leaves of its volume.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"5.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","text":"The ordinary members shall be of two kinds, because Mercury has two houses, namely Gemini and Virgo. And on account of Gemini it shall have the shoulders, the arms, and the hands; for Virgo it shall have.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"5.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0023","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"5.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0024","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of Venus there shall be seven images. Cerberus shall signify hunger, thirst, and sleep. Hercules cleansing the stables of Augeas shall contain bodily cleanliness. Narcissus shall contain beauty, comeliness, gracefulness, love;","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"5.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0025","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"5.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0026","text":"37","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"5.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0027","text":"design, falling in love, desire, hope, etc., and it will have\ntwo chains.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"5.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0028","text":"Bacchus with the spear in his hand clothed in ivy will signify that he does not wish to fight, but to enjoy himself. And therefore he will have a volume pertaining to leisure, and to tranquillity of mind, denoting a cheerful, playful nature, and one suited to enjoying itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"5.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","text":"A Minotaur. This is the offspring of Pasiphaë, according to the poets, joined with the Bull. And here it should be noted that symbolic Theology has not without mystery introduced not only the Mi-\notaur, but the Centaurs, and the Satyrs, and Fauns, and the like, which bear the human figure down to the waist, and from the waist down bear that of a beast: for men who are vi-\ntious, and who do not partake of the divine ray (of which has been spoken), have only the human figure, but in the re-\nmainder are to be compared with beasts. Plato writes in the Timaeus that our irascible part is to be assigned to the heart, and that the concupiscible part is beneath the cartilage called the dia-\nphragm, beneath which are all the passions; and this di-\nvides us almost from ourselves: and since we have this lower part in common with beasts, if we please it, we become beasts.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"5.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0030","text":"With grave reason, therefore, the ancients have feigned man transformed into a beast from that part downward.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"5.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","text":"Therefore, to this image we shall assign a nature inclined to vice, even though it were not exercised, such as that of Socra-\ntes, by his own confession. And I say this because exercised vice will be treated among the Talari.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"5.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0032","text":"Tantalus beneath the stone will denote a timid, suspended,\nand doubtful, and wonder-struck nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"5.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0033","text":"A Bull, for extraordinary members, will have the nose and the facul","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"5.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0034","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"5.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0035","text":"ty of smell, because Venus also has odours. And it also has the cheeks, the lips, and devouring, and through Libra, grace. For ordinary members, through Taurus it will have the neck, the throat, swallowing, and devouring; and through Libra it will have the hinder part, which is the rump.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"5.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0036","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"5.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0037","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of the Sun there will be five images. Geryon slain by Hercules will signify the age of man. The Cock with the Lion will signify excellence, superiority, dig-\nnity, authority, the dominion of man in matters of honour. The Fates will signify man to be King and lord of some thing. The Cow guarded by Argus will have the colours of the human body. Apollo striking Juno among the clouds will signify the mani-\nfestation of man, and his coming to light. A Bull, for extraordinary members, will have the ears with their operations, such as looking and seeing; and for ordinary members it will have the back and the flanks, because they are those of the Lion, which is the house of the Sun. Under Mars there will be six images.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"5.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0038","text":"Death.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"5.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0039","text":"Ixion, who wishes to embrace Juno feigned from clouds: it is read in the ancient fables that Ixion was so proud by na-\nture, and so arrogant, and so presumptuous, that, without having any respect for Jove, he not only gave himself to loving Ju-\nno, but also sought her for his embraces. It is said that she, indignant, in order to shield herself, feigned a Juno of Clo-\nuds, with whom Ixion lay, and from that lying together the Centaurs were born. This image, therefore, will have be-\nneath itself on the axis two chains, one belonging to the presumption of Ixion and the other to the indignation of Ju-\nno. The first will have, for avelli, a proud nature, super","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"5.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0040","text":"v.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"5.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0041","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO  38","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"5.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0042","text":"b, boastful, presumptuous, arrogant, and the like. And the other, an indignant, defensive, and mocking nature. Two fighting serpents will signify a contentious nature. A maiden with her hair raised toward heaven will contain a na-\nture strong, vigorous, and sinewy. Mars above the Dragon\nwill signify a harmful nature. A man without a head, that is, without a brain, which is the seat of the intellect, and by this image a furious or mad nature will be signified. A Bull. This will not have extraordinary members, but as ordinary ones, through Aries it will have the head, and through Scorpio it will have the genitals with their operations.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"5.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0043","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of Jove there will be six images.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"5.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0044","text":"Jove.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"5.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0045","text":"The Lion slain by Hercules.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"5.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","text":"For the explanation of this fable, it is necessary for us to understand that that passage of Scripture, Israel si me audieris, non adorabis Deos alienos, neque erit in te Deus recens, makes us understand that we can commit two most grave sins: one, not to worship the true and only God; the other, to commit a greater idolatry than did ancient sim-\nplicity. For that worshipped Gods outside itself, but most of us worship the Gods that we make within ourselves. For among consecrated heads, in monasteries, many have made within themselves an idol of their continence and chastity. And not only do they worship it, but they would have others revere it as worshipped; and thus they have set up within their imagination a goddess Vesta, and the more learned have set up a Pallas, whom not only do they worship, but they would also have her esteemed and worshipped by all.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"5.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","text":"The princes of armies have set up in their heart the Deity of Mars. Nor do they only esteem and worship it, but they would have everyone bow to that one. And, to speak briefly, we all have within","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"5.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0048","text":"THE IDEAL THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"5.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","text":"A fierce and proud lion, which signifies our wickedness, and untamed ambition. And it is the resistant God whom we have within us. If therefore our spirit becomes a most strong Hercules, it will kill this lion; which, once killed, will be followed by humility, in which alone we can please God, becoming little children and poor in spirit. This image, therefore, under the Pasiphaë of Jupiter, will signify a humble nature, shamefaced, and inclined to goodness, and to all those things which, although they are not called virtues by Philosophers, are nevertheless a disposition toward it, as we have said of shame.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"5.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","text":"But under the Talars it will signify the exercise of such goodness, or good disposition. The Minotaur killed by Theseus in the Labyrinth will give the signification of inclination toward virtue. But under the talars it will signify any of the virtues in their actions, which otherwise would not be virtues, since many know the definition of virtue without possessing it. And this is called by Cicero active virtue, and by Virgil ardent, and likewise by Petrarch. And indeed, if the living Minotaur signifies vice, dead it must signify virtue.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"5.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051","text":"The Caduceus will signify a friendly nature, and one inclined to domestic care and to the republic. Danaë signifies good fortune, happiness, health, wealth, nobility, and the obtaining of desires. The Graces signify a beneficent nature. A Bull has as extraordinary members the ears, and their operations, hearing and listening, and also the passion, such as deafness; ordinarily, for Sagittarius, the thighs; for Pisces, the feet and their operations,","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"5.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0052","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  39","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"5.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0053","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of Saturn are seven images. The three heads, of the wolf, the lion, and the dog, signify man being subject to time.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"5.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0054","text":"Proteus bound signifies an obstinate and immutable nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"5.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0055","text":"The solitary sparrow signifies a solitary man, or a man alone or abandoned.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"5.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0056","text":"Pandora: evil fortune, unhappiness, ignobility, poverty, infamy, infirmity, not obtaining desire.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"5.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0057","text":"The maiden with her hair cut off will denote the weakness of man, weariness, and falsehood.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"5.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","text":"Endymion asleep upon a mountain, and kissed by Diana. One reads among the Cabalists that without the death of the kiss we cannot unite ourselves in true union with the celestial beings, nor with God. I say this because among the number of several deaths, among which enters also that which we spoke of concerning Antaeus, is this one of the kiss, of which Solomon thus makes mention at the beginning of the Canticle. Osculetur me osculo oris sui. Which sense is more openly expressed in other words by Paul, when he says, Cupio dissolui, & esse cum Christo. Which desire is not expressed by Solomon in the signification of the verb, as by Paul, but rather in the desiderative mode. And Petrarch put it in the indeclinable when he said.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"5.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","text":"O happy that day when, leaving the earthly\nPrison, I leave broken and scattered\nThis my heavy, frail, and mortal garment,\nAnd depart from such long shadows,\nFlying so high into the fair serenity,\nThat I may see my lord and my lady.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"5.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","text":"Therefore the body being that which keeps us separate from","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"5.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0061","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"5.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","text":"true union, and from the kiss which the celestial things would make to our souls, drawing them back to themselves, it follows that through its dissolution one would come to this kiss. Which the symbolic Theologians, wishing to explain, have left in their fables: that Diana (who, holding the reign over all the supracelestial measures, and through whom all the higher influences pass, is vicar and lieutenant of all higher things), they have feigned, I say, that she, being in love with Endymion—that is, with our soul, which awaits her own, desirous of being able to leave it while it sucks—puts him into perpetual sleep upon a mountain; and having put him to sleep, can, in kissing him, satisfy her desires. Which perpetual sleep signifying death, this image will contain mortality, death, and all the links belonging to it, such as the funeral pomp.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"5.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0063","text":"A Bull. This, as extraordinary members, will have its grey breast and its curls; and ordinarily, by reason of Capricorn, the knees, and by Aquarius, the legs.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"5.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0063"]}],"source_digest":"3d9fad6598146d1d69c2c73ea3a7f21eb3a7ce70f832f42cca34a8e713d30be6","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"PASIPHE"},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261031T001904076367Z_f985f488","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"PASIPHAË","source_sha256":"b272f37d8856970061c6cdd29f9099139c5130b17919506ff8bcda3133b058ec","sha256":"a15f0846511085063998da16c5e7f7e8dd5accc113362613679d8477311f62de","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-31T00:19:04.076427+00:00","translate_quotations":true,"paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0001","text":"PASIPHE","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"5.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","text":"The Platonists say that our souls above have a fiery, or indeed ethereal, vehicle, because otherwise they would have no movement, since a thing does not move except by means of a body. This is confirmed concerning the angels by David when he says: “Who makes his Angels spirits, and his ministers a flame of fire or wind.” And the Platonists add that, when the earthly vehicle is prepared for each of the said souls in the maternal womb, although the soul that is in the most subtle fiery vehicle should wish to unite with the body, that is, the earthly vehicle, it could not, because such subtlety could not come together with such grossness without a medium that partook of the nature of the one, &","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"5.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0003","text":"E  iii","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"5.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0004","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"5.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","text":"of the other; and therefore, descending from Heaven, into Heaven, and from sphere of element into sphere of element, it becomes so much grosser that it acquires an aerial vehicle, which, partaking of the nature of both, comes to make the union. This opinion was also held by Virgil in the sixth [book], where he says that sinful souls, departing from this body, although they are freed from the earthly vehicle, are nevertheless not free of the aerial one; and for this reason they go to purgatorial places, where they remain until they are free of the aerial vehicle, and, having returned to the pure fiery [vehicle], ascend to the third place. This [matter] was covered in symbolic Theology by the fable of Pasiphaë, so that philosophy might not be profaned. For she, in love with the Bull, signifies the soul which, according to the Platonists, falls into desire for the body.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"5.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","text":"And since it is not possible through this union of something so subtle and something so gross, the feigned new Cow, which signifies the feigned aerial body, having come to union with it, conceives and gives birth to a monster called the Minotaur, of whom we shall speak in his place. This image, then, of Pasiphaë above every door of the fifth Grade of the Theatre shall cover all those images to which volumes shall be entrusted containing things and words pertaining not only to the inner man, but to that which is also covered by the outer [man]; and, with respect to the particular members of the body according to the nature of each planet, the particular members bound and subject to the nature of the containing planet shall always be beneath the last image, which shall be a Bull alone.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"5.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0007","text":"Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"5.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0008","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of the Moon there shall be six images. A maiden descending through Cancer. And this sig=","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"5.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0009","text":"BY GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"5.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0010","text":"36","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"5.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0011","text":"nifies the soul’s descent from heaven, its entry into the body, its stay in the body before birth, and birth with their appurtenances.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"5.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0012","text":"Diana, to whom Mercury offers the message, signifies alteration of mind or of bodily form.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"5.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0013","text":"The Stars of Serpents signify the filth of the body, & its excrements.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"5.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0014","text":"Juno among the clouds signifies concealment of person.","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"5.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0015","text":"Prometheus beside a mountain, who puts on his finger a ring from a chain attached to the said mountain: & it is to be known that in the ancient fables one reads that, because of the theft that Prometheus made of fire, Jupiter bound him, or condemned him to be bound with a Chain to Mount Caucasus; afterwards, moved by pity for him, he freed him. And he, grateful for such a benefit, took a ring from the chain and a little stone from Caucasus, and bound both the one and the other to one finger. Whence they say that the invention of the ring and the proverb of having it bound to one’s finger were born at the same time. This image shall preserve gratitude, obligation, and debt, and the like. And it pertains to the Moon because of the evident benefit that it receives from the Sun more than any other planet.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"5.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","text":"A Bull alone, which is to contain (as in every other Pasiphaë) certain members of the human body. And of these, some extraordinary and some ordinary. I call them extraordinary because, although the entire head of man is, according to the Astrologers, assigned to Aries, which is one of the signs of the Zodiac, it properly falls wholly under the Bull of the Pasiphaë of Mars, because Aries is its house. Nevertheless, we remove from the said head the hair, the beard, and all the hairs of the body, and also the brain, and assign them, on account of their","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"5.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0017","text":"E\n\niiii","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"5.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0018","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"5.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","text":"moisture, or by attraction of it, to the extraordinary members of the Moon, which among its ordinary members has the breast and the breasts, because the whole region of the breast is, according to the Astrologers, [under] Cancer, which is the house of the Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"5.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0020","text":"Mercu-\nry.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"5.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of Mercury there are images. The Golden Fleece, which contains the greatness and lightness of the human body, its roughness, softness, and solidity. The Atoms shall signify discrete quantity in men, such as one. The pyramid shall signify continuous quantity in men, such as great, small, of middling stature. Juno girded with clouds: a simulating and dissimulating, crafty and deceitful nature. Ixion bound to a wheel signifies, according to the opinion of Lucretius, mortal cares. And to this image shall be entrusted the busy, laborious, and industrious nature. A Bull. This shall have as extraordinary members the tongue with its parts and consequences, such as languages, and speech ordered according to its well-distinguished heads, so very marvellous as shall be seen in the leaves of its volume.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"5.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","text":"The ordinary members shall be of two kinds, since Mercury has two houses, namely Gemini and Virgo. And on account of Gemini it shall have the shoulders, arms, and hands; for Virgo it shall have.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"5.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0023","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"5.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0024","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of Venus there shall be seven images. Cerberus shall signify hunger, thirst, & sleep. Hercules cleansing the stables of Augeas shall contain the cleanliness of the body. Narcissus shall contain beauty, loveliness, gracefulness, love;","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"5.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0025","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"5.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0026","text":"37","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"5.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0027","text":"design, falling in love, desire, hope, etc. and it will have\ntwo chains.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"5.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0028","text":"Bacchus with the Spear in his hand, clothed in ivy, will signify that he does not wish to fight, but to enjoy himself. And therefore he will have a volume pertaining to leisure, and to tranquillity of the mind, denoting a cheerful, sportive nature, and one fit to enjoy itself.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"5.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","text":"A Minotaur. This is the offspring of Pasiphaë, according to the poets, joined with the Bull. And here it is to be noted that symbolic Theology has not without mystery introduced not only the Minotaur, but the Centaurs, and the Satyrs, and Fauns, and the like, which bear the human figure down to the waist, and from the waist downward bear that of a beast: because men who are vicious, and who do not partake of the divine ray (of which it has been spoken) have only the human figure, but in the rest are to be compared to beasts. Plato writes in the Timaeus that our irascible part is to be assigned to the heart, and that the concupiscible is beneath the cartilage called the diaphragm, beneath which are all the passions, and this divides us, as it were, from ourselves: and since we have this lower part in common with beasts, if we please it, we become beasts.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"5.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0030","text":"With grave reason, therefore, the ancients have feigned man transformed into a beast from that part downward.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"5.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","text":"Therefore, to this image we shall assign a nature inclined to vice, although it may not be exercised, such as was that of Socrates by his own confession. And I say this because exercised vice will be treated in the Talari.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"5.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0032","text":"Tantalus beneath the rock will denote a timid, suspended,\nand doubtful, and wondering nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"5.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0033","text":"A Bull, for extraordinary members, will have the nose and the vir","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"5.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0034","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"5.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0035","text":"tue of smell, because Venus also has smells. And it also has the cheeks, the lips, and devouring, and through Libra lightness. For ordinary members, through Taurus it will have the neck, the throat, swallowing, and devouring, and through Libra it will have the hind part, which is the rump.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"5.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0036","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"5.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0037","text":"Beneath the Pasiphaë of the Sun there will be five images. Geryon slain by Hercules will signify the age of man. The Cock with the Lion will signify the excellence, superiority, dignity, authority, dominion of man in matters of honour. The Fates will signify man to be King and lord of some thing. The Cow guarded by Argus will have the colours of the human body. Apollo wounding Juno amid the clouds will signify the manifestation of man, and his coming to light. A Bull, for extraordinary members, will have the ears with their operations, such as looking and seeing, and for ordinary members it will have the back and the flanks, because they are those of the Lion, which is the house of the Sun. Beneath Mars there will be six images.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"5.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0038","text":"Death.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"5.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0039","text":"Ixion who wishes to embrace Juno feigned of clouds: it is read in the ancient fables that Ixion was so proud by nature, and so arrogant, and so presumptuous, that without having any respect for Jupiter he not only set himself to love Juno, but even asked her for her embraces. It is said that she, indignant, in order to defend herself, feigned a Juno of Clouds, with whom Ixion lay, and from that lying together the Centaurs were born. This image, therefore, will have beneath itself on the axis the volume, two chains, one pertaining to the presumption of Ixion and the other to the indignation of Juno. The first will have, as avelli, a proud, haughty","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"5.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0040","text":"v.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"5.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0041","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO  38","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"5.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0042","text":"swimming, presumptuous, arrogant nature, and the like. And the soul, an indignant, defensive, and mocking nature. Two fighting serpents will signify a contentious nature. A maiden with her hair raised toward the sky will contain a strong, vigorous, and sinewy nature. Mars upon the Dragon will signify a harmful nature. A man without a head, that is, without a brain, which is the seat of the intellect, and by this image a furious, or mad nature will be signified. A Bull. This will not have extraordinary members, but for the ordinary, through Aries it will have the head, and through Scorpio it will have the genital parts with their operations.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"5.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0043","text":"Beneath the Pasiphaë of Jupiter there will be six images.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"5.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0044","text":"Jupiter.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"5.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0045","text":"The Lion slain by Hercules.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"5.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","text":"For the explanation of this fable, we need to understand that that passage of Scripture, “Israel, if you shall hear me, you shall not worship foreign Gods, nor shall there be in you a new God,” makes us understand that we can commit two most grave sins: the one, not to worship the true and only God; the other, to commit a greater idolatry than ancient simplicity did. For that worshipped Gods outside itself, but most of us worship the Gods that we make within ourselves. Therefore many of the sacred heads that we shall show have made within themselves an idol of their continence and chastity. And not only do they worship it, but they would wish to be revered and worshipped for it by others, and thus they have erected within their imagination a goddess Vesta; and the most learned have erected a Pallas, whom not only do they worship, but they would also wish her to be esteemed and worshipped by all.","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"5.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","text":"The commanders of armies have erected in their heart the Deity of Mars. Not only do they esteem and worship it, but they would wish all to bow down to it. And, to speak briefly, we all have within","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"5.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0048","text":"THE IDEAL THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"5.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","text":"A fierce & proud lion, which signifies our wickedness, & untamed ambition. And it is the recent God, whom we have within us. If therefore our spirit becomes a most strong Hercules, it will slay this lion, which, once slain, will be followed by humility, in which alone we can please God, becoming children, & poor in spirit. This image therefore, under the Pasiphaë of Jupiter, will signify a humble, bashful nature, & inclined to goodness, & to all those things which, although they are not called virtues by Philosophers, are nevertheless a disposition toward it, as we have said of bashfulness.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"5.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","text":"But under the Talari it will signify the exercise of such good-\nness, or good disposition. The Minotaur slain by Theseus in the Labyrinth will give the signification of inclination toward virtue. But under the talari it will signify any one of the virtues in its actions, which otherwise would not be virtues; for many know the definition of virtue without possessing it. And this is called by Cicero active virtue, & by Virgil burn-\ning, & likewise by Petrarch. And indeed, if the living Minotaur signifies vice, when dead it must signify virtue.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"5.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051","text":"The Caduceus will signify an amicable nature, & inclined to the care of the household, & of the republic. Danaë signifies good fortune, happiness, health, wealth,\nnobility, & the attainment of desires. The Graces signify a beneficent nature. A Bull has as extraordinary members the ears, and their operations, to hear & to listen, and also the passion, such as deafness; ordinarily, for Sagittarius the thighs, for Pisces the Feet & their operations,","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"5.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0052","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  39","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"5.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0053","text":"Under the Pasiphaë of Saturn are seven images. The three heads, of the wolf, the lion, & the dog, signify that man is subject to time.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"5.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0054","text":"Proteus bound signifies an obstinate & unchange-\nable nature.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"5.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0055","text":"The solitary sparrow signifies a solitary nature, or a man a-\nlone or abandoned.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"5.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0056","text":"Pandora: evil fortune, unhappiness, ignobility,\npoverty, infamy, infirmity, not attaining desire.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"5.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0057","text":"The maiden with her hair cut will denote the weakness of man,\nweariness, & falsehood.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"5.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","text":"Endymion asleep upon a mountain, & kissed by Diana. One reads among the Kabbalists that without the death of the kiss we cannot unite ourselves in true union with the heavenly things, nor with God. I say this because, among the number of several deaths, among which also enters that which we mentioned of Antaeus, is this one of the kiss, of which Solomon thus makes mention at the beginning of the Song. “Let him kiss me with the kiss of his mouth.” This meaning is more openly expressed in other words by Paul, when he says, “I desire to be dissolved, & to be with Christ.” This desire is not expressed by Solomon in the signification of the verb, as by Paul, but rather in the desiderative mood. And Petrarch placed it in the indeclinable when he said:","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"5.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","text":"O happy that day when, leaving the earthly\nPrison, I leave broken & scattered\nThis my heavy, & frail, & mortal garment,\nAnd depart from such long shadows,\nFlying so high into the fair serenity,\nThat I may see my lord & my lady.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"5.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","text":"Therefore the body, being that which keeps us separate from","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"5.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0061","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"5.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","text":"the true union, & from the kiss which the heavenly things would make with our souls, gathering them unto themselves, it follows that through the dissolution of that body one would come to this kiss. Which the symbolic Theologians, wishing to make clear, have left in their fables: that Diana (who, holding the kingdom of all the supra-celestial measures, & through whom all the higher influences pass, is vicar & lieutenant of all the higher things), have feigned, I say, that she, being in love with Endymion, that is, with our soul, which awaits her own, desirous of being able to leave it while it sucks, puts it to sleep with perpetual sleep upon a mountain, & having put it to sleep, can in kissing it satisfy her desires. This perpetual sleep signi-\nfying death, this image will contain mortality, death, & all the links belonging to it, such as the funeral pomp.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"5.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0063","text":"A Bull. This, as extraordinary members, will have gray hairs,& curls: and ordinarily, on account of Capricorn, the knees, & on account of Aquarius, the legs.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"5.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0063"]}],"source_digest":"3d9fad6598146d1d69c2c73ea3a7f21eb3a7ce70f832f42cca34a8e713d30be6","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"PASIPHE"}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"PASIPHE","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL","title":"ITALARIANS.","order":6,"chapter_id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL","text":"ITALARI.\n\nIl ſeſto grado del Theatro hà ſopra la porta di qua= lunque pianeta i Talari , & altri guarnimenti , che Mercurio ſi mette quando va ad eſeguir la volontà de Dei,ſi come fauoleggiano i Poeti.La onde ci ſueglieran= no la memoria à ritrouar ſotto coſi fatte porte tutte le ope= rationi che puo far l’Huomo dintorno à gradi ſottopoſti na= turalmente,& fuor d’ogni arte.\n\nLuna.\n\nSotto i Talari della Luna ſaranno ſette imagini.\nLa fanciulla ſceſa dal Cancro ſignificherà la tornare che\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n40\n\nſeno i ſegliuo i, & l’officio de’lazzari.\n\nNettuno dinoterà il guado, paſſar l’acqua, lavar con ac-\nqua, bagnar bere, ſpruzzare.\n\nDaphne operationi naturali intorno alle piante.\n\nDiana a cui Mercurio porge la veſſa, muouer, o mutar coſa, riceuer, dipingere, operation fatta toſto, o ſubito.\n\nLe Stalle d’Augia, bruttar, ſporcare, o macchiare. Giun-\nnon ſtrale nubi, aſconder perſona, o caſa.\n\nPrometheo con l’anello, operatione intorno alla gratitu-\ndine, o obligatione.\n\nSotto i Talari di Mercurio ſaranno ſette imagini.\n\nMercurio\n\nIl Vello dell’oro dinoterà aggrauar, alleggerir, indurir,\nintenerir, inuiaſprar, liſciare.\n\nGli Aromi ſignificheranno minuzzar, diſcontinuar, ſpar-\ngere, diſſoluere.\n\nLa Piramide, alzare, abbaſſare.\n\nIl Nodo Gordiano ineſplicato ſignificherà implicar, in-\ntricar, annodare.\n\nIl Nodo Gordiano eſplicato, ſpiegar, diſſoluere, diſtricare.\n\nGiunon cinta di nubi dimostra, uſar ſimulation, o diſſimu-\nlatione, aſtutia, o inganno.\n\nIſſion legato alla Rota ſignifica dar, o riceuer negocio, fornire, inueſtigare, vigilanẓa, induſtria, diligenẓa, perſeue-\nranza, fatica.\n\nSotto Venere ſaranno ſette imagini.\n\nVenere.\n\nCerbero ſignifica mangiar, bere, dormire,\n\nHercule purgàte le ſtalle di Augia, purgare, & nettare.\n\nNarciso ſar bello, ſar inamorare, ſar deſiderar, ſar ſperar.\n\nLa fanciulla col vaſo d’odori, per fumare.\n\nBacco con l’hoſtia veſtita d’hedera, darſi buon tempo, giu\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nbiſar,rider, far ridere,conſolar, far allegrare.\nTantalo ſotto il ſaſſo,far vacillar,far tremar, far dubbiō\nſtar,far temere.\nIl Mino: auro,operation di vitij.\n\nSole.\n\nSotto il Sole ſaranno cinque imagini. La Catena d’oro ſigniſichera andare al Sole, pigliare il Sole,ſtendere al Sole. Gerione veciſo dinoterà operationi intorno à minuti, all’ hore,all’anno,alle ſue parti,& all’età naturalmente. Il Gallo col leone, far ſuperiore, honorar, dar luogo. Le Parche,dar cagione,incominciar , menar à fine. Apollo che ſaetta Giunone ſignifica manifeſtar perſona,o coſa.\n\nMarte.\n\nSotto i Talari di Marte ſaranno cinque imagini. Vulcano dinoterà batter foco,pigliarlo nell’eſca,accen-\nderlo,mettere incendio,eſtinguerlo. Iſione ſchernito da Giunone havrà due Catene. l’vno conterrà l’inſuperbirſi,& ſar inſuperbire, preſumer & ſar preſumptuoſo,vantarſi,& ſar vantaſe,arrogàrſi,& ſar arrogante,& l’altra haver à ſdegno,beffare,& ſcher-\nnire.\n\n[Visual material: PDF page 82, region 7]\n\nLa fanciulla co capelli dirizzati al cielo, dar vigore, o fortezza, o nero operare intorno al nero. Due ſerpenti combattenti,contendere. Marte ſopra il Dracone,nuocer increduli,vendicarſi,im pedire. Sotto i Talari di Giove ſaranno ſette imagini. Giunone ſuſpeſa ſigniſichera reſpirare,ſuſpirare, vſar l’aperto cielo. I due fori della lira, fare ſtrepito. Il Leone veciſo da Hercole,eſercitar la humilità, bontà, ſemplicità,\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n41\n\nſemplicità, & vergogna.\n\nIl Minutauro ucciſo da Theſeo,eſercitar virtù.\nIl Caduceo,eſercitar amicitia o converſatione.\nDonne operatione & conſecution di buona fortuna.\nLe gratie,dar favor,beneficio & aiuto.\nSotto i Talari di Saturno ſaranno ſette imagini.\n\nSaturno.\n\nCibele dinoterà operation fuor di arte intorno alla terra. I tre capi di animali,indugiarſi,ſar indugiare, dar ter-\nmino,rimettere in alcun tempo. L’arca del paio,locar,& collocare. Proteo legato,ſtar coſa immobile. Il Paſſer ſolitario,andar ſolo,abbandonare &c. Pandora dar tribulationi. La fanciulla co capelli tagliati,debilitar coſa,o metter.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0001","text":"ITALARI.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"6.1"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","text":"Il ſeſto grado del Theatro hà ſopra la porta di qua= lunque pianeta i Talari , & altri guarnimenti , che Mercurio ſi mette quando va ad eſeguir la volontà de Dei,ſi come fauoleggiano i Poeti.La onde ci ſueglieran= no la memoria à ritrouar ſotto coſi fatte porte tutte le ope= rationi che puo far l’Huomo dintorno à gradi ſottopoſti na= turalmente,& fuor d’ogni arte.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"6.2"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0003","text":"Luna.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"6.3"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","text":"Sotto i Talari della Luna ſaranno ſette imagini.\nLa fanciulla ſceſa dal Cancro ſignificherà la tornare che","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"6.4"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0005","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"6.5"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0006","text":"40","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"6.6"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0007","text":"ſeno i ſegliuo i, & l’officio de’lazzari.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"6.7"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","text":"Nettuno dinoterà il guado, paſſar l’acqua, lavar con ac-\nqua, bagnar bere, ſpruzzare.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"6.8"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0009","text":"Daphne operationi naturali intorno alle piante.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"6.9"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","text":"Diana a cui Mercurio porge la veſſa, muouer, o mutar coſa, riceuer, dipingere, operation fatta toſto, o ſubito.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"6.10"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0011","text":"Le Stalle d’Augia, bruttar, ſporcare, o macchiare. Giun-\nnon ſtrale nubi, aſconder perſona, o caſa.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"6.11"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012","text":"Prometheo con l’anello, operatione intorno alla gratitu-\ndine, o obligatione.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"6.12"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","text":"Sotto i Talari di Mercurio ſaranno ſette imagini.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"6.13"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0014","text":"Mercurio","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"6.14"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","text":"Il Vello dell’oro dinoterà aggrauar, alleggerir, indurir,\nintenerir, inuiaſprar, liſciare.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"6.15"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0016","text":"Gli Aromi ſignificheranno minuzzar, diſcontinuar, ſpar-\ngere, diſſoluere.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"6.16"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0017","text":"La Piramide, alzare, abbaſſare.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"6.17"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0018","text":"Il Nodo Gordiano ineſplicato ſignificherà implicar, in-\ntricar, annodare.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"6.18"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0019","text":"Il Nodo Gordiano eſplicato, ſpiegar, diſſoluere, diſtricare.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"6.19"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","text":"Giunon cinta di nubi dimostra, uſar ſimulation, o diſſimu-\nlatione, aſtutia, o inganno.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"6.20"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021","text":"Iſſion legato alla Rota ſignifica dar, o riceuer negocio, fornire, inueſtigare, vigilanẓa, induſtria, diligenẓa, perſeue-\nranza, fatica.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"6.21"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","text":"Sotto Venere ſaranno ſette imagini.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"6.22"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0023","text":"Venere.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"6.23"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","text":"Cerbero ſignifica mangiar, bere, dormire,","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"6.24"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0025","text":"Hercule purgàte le ſtalle di Augia, purgare, & nettare.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"6.25"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026","text":"Narciso ſar bello, ſar inamorare, ſar deſiderar, ſar ſperar.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"6.26"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0027","text":"La fanciulla col vaſo d’odori, per fumare.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"6.27"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0028","text":"Bacco con l’hoſtia veſtita d’hedera, darſi buon tempo, giu","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"6.28"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0029","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"6.29"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0030","text":"biſar,rider, far ridere,conſolar, far allegrare.\nTantalo ſotto il ſaſſo,far vacillar,far tremar, far dubbiō\nſtar,far temere.\nIl Mino: auro,operation di vitij.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"6.30"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0031","text":"Sole.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"6.31"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","text":"Sotto il Sole ſaranno cinque imagini. La Catena d’oro ſigniſichera andare al Sole, pigliare il Sole,ſtendere al Sole. Gerione veciſo dinoterà operationi intorno à minuti, all’ hore,all’anno,alle ſue parti,& all’età naturalmente. Il Gallo col leone, far ſuperiore, honorar, dar luogo. Le Parche,dar cagione,incominciar , menar à fine. Apollo che ſaetta Giunone ſignifica manifeſtar perſona,o coſa.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"6.32"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0033","text":"Marte.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"6.33"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","text":"Sotto i Talari di Marte ſaranno cinque imagini. Vulcano dinoterà batter foco,pigliarlo nell’eſca,accen-\nderlo,mettere incendio,eſtinguerlo. Iſione ſchernito da Giunone havrà due Catene. l’vno conterrà l’inſuperbirſi,& ſar inſuperbire, preſumer & ſar preſumptuoſo,vantarſi,& ſar vantaſe,arrogàrſi,& ſar arrogante,& l’altra haver à ſdegno,beffare,& ſcher-\nnire.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"6.34"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0035","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 82, region 7]","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"6.35"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036","text":"La fanciulla co capelli dirizzati al cielo, dar vigore, o fortezza, o nero operare intorno al nero. Due ſerpenti combattenti,contendere. Marte ſopra il Dracone,nuocer increduli,vendicarſi,im pedire. Sotto i Talari di Giove ſaranno ſette imagini. Giunone ſuſpeſa ſigniſichera reſpirare,ſuſpirare, vſar l’aperto cielo. I due fori della lira, fare ſtrepito. Il Leone veciſo da Hercole,eſercitar la humilità, bontà, ſemplicità,","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"6.36"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0037","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"6.37"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0038","text":"41","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"6.38"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0039","text":"ſemplicità, & vergogna.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"6.39"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","text":"Il Minutauro ucciſo da Theſeo,eſercitar virtù.\nIl Caduceo,eſercitar amicitia o converſatione.\nDonne operatione & conſecution di buona fortuna.\nLe gratie,dar favor,beneficio & aiuto.\nSotto i Talari di Saturno ſaranno ſette imagini.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"6.40"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0041","text":"Saturno.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"6.41"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","text":"Cibele dinoterà operation fuor di arte intorno alla terra. I tre capi di animali,indugiarſi,ſar indugiare, dar ter-\nmino,rimettere in alcun tempo. L’arca del paio,locar,& collocare. Proteo legato,ſtar coſa immobile. Il Paſſer ſolitario,andar ſolo,abbandonare &c. Pandora dar tribulationi. La fanciulla co capelli tagliati,debilitar coſa,o metter.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"6.42"}],"sha256":"c66a3584c1f7b0accedf336fb45180997b8bec2b559011eb540817f1915fdc42","language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261030T230738809098Z_07da4a8a","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"ITALARIANS.","source_sha256":"c66a3584c1f7b0accedf336fb45180997b8bec2b559011eb540817f1915fdc42","sha256":"3053915d0f433e1a87449571a6989c2e13e9a3d1fbd8a1b2926868256253a892","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:07:38.809154+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0001","text":"THE TALARIA.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"6.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","text":"The sixth grade of the Theatre has above the door of each planet the Talaria, and other ornaments that Mercury puts on when he goes to execute the will of the Gods, as the Poets fabulate. Whence they will awaken our memory to find beneath such doors all the operations that Man can perform concerning grades naturally subordinate, and outside every art.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"6.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0003","text":"Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"6.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","text":"Beneath the Talaria of the Moon there shall be seven images.\nThe maiden descended from Cancer will signify the returning that","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"6.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0005","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"6.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0006","text":"40","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"6.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0007","text":"be the followers, and the office of the lazari.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"6.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","text":"Neptune will denote the ford, crossing water, washing with wa-\nter, bathing, drinking, sprinkling.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"6.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0009","text":"Daphne, natural operations concerning plants.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"6.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","text":"Diana, to whom Mercury offers the vessa: moving, or changing a thing, receiving, painting, an operation done quickly, or immediately.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"6.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0011","text":"The Stables of Augeas: befouling, soiling, or staining. Juno\namong clouds: concealing a person, or a house.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"6.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012","text":"Prometheus with the ring, an operation concerning gratitude,\nor obligation.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"6.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","text":"Beneath the Talaria of Mercury there shall be seven images.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"6.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0014","text":"Mercury","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"6.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","text":"The Golden Fleece will denote making heavy, making light, hardening,\nsoftening, making rough, smoothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"6.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0016","text":"The Aromas will signify mincing, discontinuing, scatter-\ning, dissolving.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"6.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0017","text":"The Pyramid: raising, lowering.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"6.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0018","text":"The Gordian Knot unexplained will signify implicating, en-\ntangling, knotting.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"6.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0019","text":"The Gordian Knot explained: unfolding, dissolving, disentangling.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"6.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","text":"Juno girded with clouds shows the use of simulation, or dissimu-\nlation, cunning, or deceit.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"6.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021","text":"Ixion bound to the Wheel signifies giving, or receiving business, providing, investigating, vigilance, industry, diligence, perseve-\nrance, toil.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"6.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","text":"Beneath Venus there shall be seven images.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"6.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0023","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"6.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","text":"Cerberus signifies eating, drinking, sleeping,","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"6.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0025","text":"Hercules cleansed the stables of Augeas, to cleanse, & to make clean.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"6.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026","text":"Narcissus, to be beautiful, to make [someone] fall in love, to desire, to hope.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"6.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0027","text":"The maiden with the vessel of perfumes, for fumigating.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"6.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0028","text":"Bacchus with the victim clothed in ivy, to enjoy oneself, to rejoice","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"6.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0029","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"6.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0030","text":"to jest, to laugh, to make laugh, to console, to make glad.\nTantalus beneath the stone, to make waver, to make tremble, to make doubtful\nremain, to make fear.\nThe Minotaur: operation of vices.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"6.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0031","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"6.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","text":"Beneath the Sun there shall be five images. The golden Chain shall signify going to the Sun, taking the Sun, stretching out toward the Sun. Geryon slain shall denote operations concerning minutes, hours, the year, its parts, & age naturally. The Cock with the lion, to make superior, to honour, to give place. The Fates, to give cause, to begin, to bring to an end. Apollo shooting Juno signifies manifesting a person, or thing.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"6.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0033","text":"Mars.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"6.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","text":"Beneath the Talaria of Mars there shall be five images. Vulcan shall denote striking fire, taking it in the tinder, kindling\nit, setting fire, extinguishing it. Ixion mocked by Juno shall have two Chains. The one shall contain becoming proud, & making [someone] proud, presuming & being presumptuous, boasting, & being boastful, arrogating to oneself, & being arrogant, & the other, taking offence, mocking, & deriding.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"6.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0035","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 82, region 7]","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"6.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036","text":"The maiden with hair raised toward heaven, to give vigour, or strength, or black operation concerning black. Two serpents fighting, to contend. Mars above the Dragon, to harm unbelievers, to take vengeance, to hinder. Beneath the Talaria of Jupiter there shall be seven images. Juno suspended shall signify breathing, sighing, using the open sky. The two holes of the lyre, to make noise. The Lion slain by Hercules, to practise humility, goodness, simplicity,","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"6.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0037","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"6.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0038","text":"41","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"6.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0039","text":"simplicity, & shame.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"6.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","text":"The Minotaur slain by Theseus, to practise virtue.\nThe Caduceus, to practise friendship or conversation.\nWomen, operation & attainment of good fortune.\nThe Graces, to give favour, benefit & aid.\nBeneath the Talaria of Saturn there shall be seven images.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"6.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0041","text":"Saturn.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"6.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","text":"Cybele shall denote operation outside art concerning the earth. The three heads of animals, to delay, to make delay, to give ter-\nmination, to defer to some time. The ark of the pair, to place, & to set in place. Proteus bound, for a thing to remain motionless. The solitary Sparrow, to go alone, to abandon &c. Pandora, to give tribulations. The maiden with shorn hair, to weaken a thing, or to put.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"6.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042"]}],"source_digest":"d96593fe8a539a7aa1e1e87cfe3971644d3623d0132c90c822d23877cd8b576b","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"ITALARI."},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261031T001924668126Z_7a82572f","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"ITALARIANS.","source_sha256":"c66a3584c1f7b0accedf336fb45180997b8bec2b559011eb540817f1915fdc42","sha256":"db7cebd5210a26f7c65ac1e416884a6dc9f08b4b2fb855510cb3938136ee1437","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-31T00:19:24.668214+00:00","translate_quotations":true,"paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0001","text":"WINGED SANDALS.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"6.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","text":"The sixth grade of the Theatre has above the door of every planet the winged sandals, and other ornaments, which Mercury puts on when he goes to execute the will of the Gods, as the Poets fabulously relate. Whence they will awaken our memory to find beneath such doors all the operations that Man can perform concerning grades naturally subject, and apart from every art.","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"6.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0003","text":"Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"6.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","text":"Beneath the winged sandals of the Moon there will be seven images.\nThe maiden descended from Cancer will signify the return that","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"6.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0005","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"6.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0006","text":"40","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"6.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0007","text":"bosom, the following ones, and the office of nurses.","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"6.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","text":"Neptune will denote the ford, crossing water, washing with wa-\nter, bathing, drinking, sprinkling.","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"6.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0009","text":"Daphne, natural operations concerning plants.","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"6.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","text":"Diana, to whom Mercury offers the bladder: to move, or change a thing, to receive, to paint, an operation done quickly, or immediately.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"6.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0011","text":"The Stables of Augeas: to befoul, soil, or stain. Ju-\nno among clouds: to conceal a person, or a house.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"6.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012","text":"Prometheus with the ring: an operation concerning gratitude,\nor obligation.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"6.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","text":"Beneath the winged sandals of Mercury there will be seven images.","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"6.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0014","text":"Mercury","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"6.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","text":"The Golden Fleece will denote making heavy, making light, hardening,\nsoftening, roughening, smoothing.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"6.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0016","text":"Aromatics will signify mincing, discontinuing, scat-\ntering, dissolving.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"6.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0017","text":"The Pyramid: raising, lowering.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"6.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0018","text":"The unloosed Gordian Knot will signify involving, en-\ntangling, knotting.","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"6.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0019","text":"The loosed Gordian Knot: unfolding, dissolving, disentangling.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"6.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","text":"Juno girded with clouds shows the use of simulation, or dissimu-\nlation, cunning, or deception.","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"6.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021","text":"Ixion bound to the Wheel signifies giving, or receiving business, furnishing, investigating, vigilance, industry, diligence, perseve-\nrance, labour.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"6.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","text":"Beneath Venus there will be seven images.","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"6.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0023","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"6.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","text":"Cerberus signifies eating, drinking, sleeping,","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"6.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0025","text":"Hercules cleansed the stables of Augeas: to cleanse, & to make clean.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"6.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026","text":"Narcissus: to be handsome, to make fall in love, to desire, to hope.","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"6.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0027","text":"The maiden with the vessel of scents, for fumigating.","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"6.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0028","text":"Bacchus with the victim clothed in ivy: to enjoy oneself, to re","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"6.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0029","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"6.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0030","text":"joice, to laugh, to make laugh, to console, to make glad.\nTantalus beneath the stone: to waver, to tremble, to remain\nuncertain, to fear.\nMinos: gold, operation of vices.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"6.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0031","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"6.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","text":"Beneath the Sun there shall be five images. The golden Chain shall signify going to the Sun, taking the Sun, extending into the Sun. Geryon slain shall denote operations concerning minutes, hours, the year, its parts, & age naturally. The Cock with the lion: to make superior, to honour, to give place. The Fates: to give cause, to begin, to bring to an end. Apollo shooting Juno signifies making a person or thing manifest.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"6.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0033","text":"Mars.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"6.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","text":"Beneath the Talaria of Mars there shall be five images. Vulcan shall denote striking fire, taking it in tinder, kind-\nling it, setting a fire, extinguishing it. Ixion mocked by Juno shall have two Chains. The one shall contain becoming proud, & making proud, presuming & being presumptuous, boasting, & being boastful, arrogating to oneself, & being arrogant, & the other, taking offence, mocking, & scoff-\ning.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"6.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0035","text":"[Visual material: PDF page 82, region 7]","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"6.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036","text":"The maiden with her hair standing upright toward heaven: to give vigour, or strength, or black operation concerning black. Two serpents fighting: to contend. Mars above the Dragon: to harm unbelievers, to avenge oneself, to im pede. Beneath the Talaria of Jupiter there shall be seven images. Juno suspended shall signify breathing, sighing, using the open sky. The two holes of the lyre: to make noise. The Lion slain by Hercules: to exercise humility, goodness, simplicity,","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"6.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0037","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"6.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0038","text":"41","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"6.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0039","text":"simplicity, & shame.","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"6.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","text":"The Minotaur slain by Theseus: to exercise virtue.\nThe Caduceus: to exercise friendship or conversation.\nWomen: operation & attainment of good fortune.\nThe Graces: to give favour, benefit & help.\nBeneath the Talaria of Saturn there shall be seven images.","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"6.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0041","text":"Saturn.","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"6.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","text":"Cybele shall denote operation outside art concerning the earth. The three heads of animals: to delay, to make delay, to give a ter-\nminus, to postpone for some time. The ark of the pair: to place, & to set in place. Proteus bound: for a thing to remain motionless. The solitary Sparrow: to go alone, to abandon &c. Pandora: to give tribulations. The maiden with cut hair: to weaken a thing, or to put.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"6.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042"]}],"source_digest":"d96593fe8a539a7aa1e1e87cfe3971644d3623d0132c90c822d23877cd8b576b","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"ITALARI."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"ITALARI.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM","title":"PROMETHEUS.","order":7,"chapter_id":"CH_LIDT_PROM","text":"PROMETHEO.\n\nIL ſettimo Grado è aſſignato a tutte le arti coſi nobili come vili,le quali hanno ſopra ciaſcuna porta Prometheo con la facella acceſa. Et accioche ſ’intenda la cagion,per la quale vogliamo,che egli ci ſia il ſimbolo delle arti, fa biſogno intender quello che dice Socrate nel Protagora di Pla-\ntone. Dice egli adunque che eſſendo venuto il tempo fatal de la creatione de gli animali, i Dei, che all’hora erano ſoli for marono eſſi animali nelle viſcere della terra di fuoco, et di terra,& di quelle coſe che col fuoco, & con la terra ſono meſcolate:& mentre erano in volontà di mettergli in luce, commiſſero à Prometheo,& ad Epimetheo,che diſtribuiſſe-\nro a ciaſcuno le convenevoli forze. Et Epimetheo pregò Pro metheo,che à lui laſciaſſe far coſi fatta diſtributione, &\n\nL’Idea del Theatro.\n\nR\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nche egli ſolamente ſi ſteſſe a porui mente. conſenti Prometheo, & Epimetheo fece la diſtributione. Ad alcuni adunque diede robuſtezza ſenza celerità, & ad alcuni più deboli die de velocità, alcuni armò, & à quelli che mancauano di ar-\nme trouo alcuna coſa accommodata alla lor ſalute: & di quelli che erano chiuſi in picciol corpo, parte ne fece leuar per l’ae re dalle piume, & parte ſerper per la terra. Et quelle che erano di ampia grandezza volle, che eſſa grandezza deſſe loro forza per la loro ſalute. Et poi che Socrate ha molto va gato intorno alla varietà de gli animali bruti, dice che Epi metheo poco ſauio conſumò tutte le doti nele beſtie, & non auerſi di laſciar parte di tanta larghezza da donare all’hu mana ſpecie. Reſtaua adunque la ſpecie humana vota & priua de ogni dote. Ma Prometheo vedendo la mala distribu tion fatta da Epimetheo, & gia vicinarſi il giorno fatale, nel qual faceua biſogno far uſcir in luce gli animali, no tro uando altra via da poter alla humana ſalute prouedere, na ſcoſamente col fuoco furò l’artificio, la ſapienza di Vulcano & di Minerua. percioche non ſi poteua far che alcuno ſen za fuoco, cio è ſenza acutezza di ingegno la poteſſe ne con ſeguir, ne vſare. Queſta adunque miſe Prometheo ne gli huomini, la qual appartiene ſolamente al viuere, ma la ciuile mancaua, la quale era bene appreſſo Gioue. Ma non fu leci to à Prometheo aſcender tanto alto, percioche horribil cuſto die, che ſtauano intorno alla rocca di Gioue ne lo ſpauentaua no. Per quel furto adunque l’huomo ſolo fra gli animali fat to partecipe della diuina ſorte; hebbe cognition de Dei da principio, per la qual cognitione diuenne religioso, & à lo ro dedicò altari & ſtatue. Diſtinſe con arte articolatamen te la voce in parole, ediſicò caſe, fece ueſtimenti, letti & rote\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO\n\n42\n\ncoſe nutrimenti della terra. Ma pur gli huomini ſparſame re vagauano dal principio, percioche non anchora erano edi ficate le citta, donde aueniua che gli huomini eſſendo piu de boli delle fere, erano da quelle per tutto diſſipati. Bene era trouata la facultà appartenente all’apparecchio del viuere, ma da combatter contra le fere non haueuano il modo, per= cioche la ciuil facultà, della qual la militia n’è vna, parte, non era fra loro. Pur per poterſi gli huomini dalle fere dif= ſendere, ſi congregarono & edificarono le citta. Ma ohimè che coſi congregati non ſi poteuano l’vn l’altro comporta= re, & tra loro ſi faceuano di mille oltraggi, percioche della ciuil facultà non erano partecipi. la onde ſforzati ad vſcir delle citta tornarono a diu enir paſtura delle fere. Alla fin Gio ue moſſo a pietà dell’humana infelicità, mandò Mercurio, che portaſſe a gli huomini il pudore, & la giuſtitia, à fin che queſte due coſe ornaſſero talmente le citta, che gli huo= mini ſi conciliaſſero cõ beniuolẽza. Mercurio hauẽdo da por tar queſti due ornamenti, interrogò il Padre ſe hauea da di ſtribuir queſti due doni nella maniera che erano ſtate diſtri= buite le arti, delle quali l’vno ne hauea l’vna, l’altro l’altra o ſe pur le haueſſe da dare à tutti egualmẽte. A tutti riſpo= ſe Gioue, percioche tutti li huomini ne debbono eſſer partecipi che altramente le citta conſeruar nõ ſi potrebbono, che ſe be ne un Medico, o un calzolajo in una citta poteſſe ſodiſfare a molti nõ medici, et a molti nõ calzolai, vno nõdimeno di pu dore & di giuſtitia ornato fra molti che ne puden, ne giuſti tia non haueſſero non ſi porebbe conſeruare. Appreſſo Gio= ue commiſe, che da ſua parte ſacreſſe una legge, che qual ſi trouaſſe nudo di pudore & di giuſtitia, foſſe come peſte de la citta con eſtremo ſupplicio tolto dal numero de viui.\n\nF  ii\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nMa noi vogliamo che il noſtro Prometheo non ſolamente contenga tutte le arti nobili & ignobili, che da lui furono diſtribuite, ma anchor la ciuile & la militar facultà, per non leuar il Theatro a più alto grado.\n\nLuna.\n\nSotto il Prometheo della Luna ſaranno cinque imagini Diana a cui Mercurio porge la veſta contenerà i meſi & le lor parti. Nettuno ci darà le arti ſopra le acque , come acquedutti fontane artificiate,ponti porti, Arzane,arte nauale & del peſcare. Daphne contenerà i giardini , & l’arti intorno al le-\ngname. Himeneo ſignificherà nozze & parentadi. Diana con l’arco dinoterà la cacciagione.\n\nMercu\n\nSotto il Prometheo di Mercurio ſaranno ſei imagini. Vn orio, Elephante. Si come queſta imagine ſotto il Conuiuio ſignifi ca fauoloſa Deità, coſì qui dinoterà fauoloſa religione, riti & cerimonie co ſuoi appartenenti. Hercole che tira una ſaetta con tre punte è nobilissima imagine di tutte le ſcienze pertinenti alle coſe celeſti , à queſto mondo,& all’abiſſo.percioche i Theologi ſimboliza ti vogliono che Hercole ſignifichi l’humano ſpirito,il quale come ſaetta di tre punte poſſa penetrar con l’vna i ſecreti celeſti con l’altra quelli di queſto mondo. E con la terza quelli dell’abiſſo. Adunque contenerà vn volume molto ben diſtinto,nel qual ſi vederanno ordinate ſenza eccettione tut te le ſcienze con tutti gli anelli appartenenti alle loro par ticolari catene. Et finalmente la eloquenza,come ricetto & ornamento di tutte, la eloquenza dico appartenente alla oratione ſciolta,in tutte le ſue ſpecie , percioche il poema è\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.\n\n43\n\nſolare. Et andra alla imagine di Apollo fra le Muſe, & ſotto queſto Hercole anchor fara compreſſa la libreria. L’Arco celeſte con Mercurio. Per eſſer Iris meſſaggiera di Giunone & Mercurio de Dei. Queſta imagine haurà il volume delle ambaſſerie del nuncio privato, & del man= dato ſotto mano. Et il primo contenerà i pertinenti alle let tere che ſi mandano, & che ſi ricevono.\n\nTre Pallidi. vna edificante città, l’altra che teſſa te la figurata, la terza che faccia vna ſtatua. dell’edificar hab= biamo Virgilio Pallas quas condidit artes ipſa colat. Della tela figurata ne teſtifica il congresſo con Arachne. Et che ella foſſe ſtatuaria di Plaſtica il ci poſſiamo perſuader dal le coſe dette di ſopra. Et dalla fauola di Socrate di ſopra da noi recitata, quando dice che i Dei formarono tutti gli ani mali ſenza nominare alcuno in particolare. queſta imagine adunque con ſeruera volume appartenente al diſegno, al l’architettura alla pittura, alla proſpettiva, alla plaſtica, & alla ſtatuaria, & a tutti i loro appartenenti. Et la diſtintion ſarà tale ne tagli che farà apparir marauiglioſo l’ordine.\n\nMercurio con vn Gallo, ſignificherà la mercatura, & Mercu ſuoi appartenenti. ne ſo onde Landino ſe l’habbia tratto. rio. Ma à me baſta il teſtimonio ſuo nelle ſue allegorie, nelle quali e dice l’antichità hauere vſato coſi fatto ſimbolo per la mercatura, aggiungendo non ſo che ragione della gar rulità di Mercurio rappreſentante quella de mercatanti Prometheo con la facella, come è anchor in ſu la porta rappreſenterà arti & artefici in generale. Ne cio paia nuo uo, che anchor Ariſtotele nella ſua Priora dice eſſer lecito per difetto di vocaboli dar tal’hora alla ſpecie il nome del genere.\n\nDigitized by Google\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nVenere.\n\nSotto Venere ſaranno ſette imagini.\nCerbero contiene la cucina , & appartamenti a conviti, &\nal dormir ſolenne.\n\nI vermi che fan la ſeta conterrà il Ginecio, con la veſtia ria con gli antecedenti, & conſeguenti. Antecedenti, come filar, teſſere , ſartoria , tintoria. Conſeguenti veſtirſi, ſpo gliarſi, reſarcire,& la guardaroba.\n\nHercole purgante le ſtalle d’Augia conterrà bagni &\nbarberie.\n\nLa fanciulla col vaſo d’odori ſignificherà la perfumeria. Il Minotauro qui è arte vitioſa, ruffianeſmo, bordello,& arte meretricia.\n\nBacco cõ l’aſta coperta di hedera, muſica et arti di giochi.\nNarciso conterrà l’arte de bellezzi.\n\nSole.\n\nSotto il Prometheo del Sole ſaranno ſette imagini. Gerion ucciſo da Hercole conterrà minuti,hore,anno,horo logio.\n\nIl Gallo col Leone conterrà il principato,& ſuoi appara-\ntenenti.\n\nLa Sibilla col tripode ſignificherà la divinatione,& le\nſue ſpeci ,& la prophetia.\n\nApollo fra le muſe dinoterà la poeſia. Apollo che uccide il ſerpente , cioè i veleni delle infirmi-\ntà , haurà tutta la medicina. Apollo paſtore ci darà l’arte paſtorale.\n\nVn huomo à cauallo con vn logoro in mano conterrà la caccia dello ſparuiere & del falcone eſercitij nobili. Et ben che appreſſo gli antichi non foſſero in coſtume, nondimeno potendoſi per perplexionem accomodar molti modi di parla re , & acciochè volendoſi aſſoluer le nouelle del Boccac-\n\nDigitized by Google\n\nDI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.  44\n\ncio accioche buchi non manchino, habbiam dato queſto luogo . Et qui diro quattro parole della vtilità della mia fatica, che proponendomi lo ſtato di queſta età, & della no ſtra religione, ho cercato di accomodar molte coſe al noſtro coſtume, come per eſempio. Quantunque Cicerone non hab bia mai parlato di Chriſto, ne dello Spirito Santo, conſideran do io il biſogno noſtro del parlare , & dello ſcriuer delle perſone diuine ſotto la imagine della latitudine de gli en= ti, ho apparecchiato gran ſelua tratta da gli ſcritti di Cice rone, con la qual ciceronianamente ſi potra veſtire il nome del figliuolo & dello ſpirito ſanto. Et quello del figliuolo ha due ſelue ſeparate, l’vna per veſtire il ſuo ſantiſſimo no me, come verbo & ſapienza. l’altra come verbo incarnato cio è Chriſto, & Chriſto crucifiſſo per noi. Queſta dico per cioche molti de Cabaliſti Hebrei hanno conoſciuto la ſapie za & il verbo, ma non hanno creduto quella eſſerſi incar= nata, & hauer per noi patito. Il che vedendo Paolo dice vn ſottiſſimo paſſaggio. Non per ſapientiam verbi, ne crux Chri ſti euacuantur. Di che ſe eſſo geloſiſſimo Paolo hauſſe hau to a ſcriuer l’Euangelio di Giovanni, hauerebbe perauentura detto. In principio erat Chriſtus, & Chriſtus erat apud Deum, & Deus erat Chriſtus. benche Giovanni diede il ri medio quando diſſe. Et verbum caro factum eſt.\n\nSotto Marte ſaranno ſette imagini.\n\nMarte.\n\nVulcano ci dara l’arti fabrili di fuoco. Vn Centauro, benche nella natura delle coſe non ſiano mai ſtati i centauri, pur leggendoſi, che quando ſi comincia rono a domare i caualli, a coloro che di lõtano mirauano pareua che il cauallo & caualcatore foſſe vna coſa iſteſſa. Sotto queſta imagine copriremo le arti al cauallo, & al ſuo\n\nDigitized by Google\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO\n\nbeneficio appartenenti: & ſi da a Marte, per eſſer il cauallo\nanimal Martiale.\n\nDue ſerpenti combattenti: conteneranno l’arte militare,\n& la guerra terreſtre & nauale.\n\nDue giuocatori di Ceſti conteneranno tutti i giuochi Mar\ntiali.\n\nRhadamanto giudicante le anime hauerà il foro crimi=\nnale diſtinto.\n\nLe furie infernali per eſſere eſecutrici delle pene, contene= ranno il bargellato, cattura, carcere, tortura, ſupplicii.\n\nMarſia ſcorticato da Apollo ci darà il macello.\n\nSotto il Prometheo di Gioue ſaranno cinque imagini.\n\nGioue.\n\nGiuno ſuſpeſa contenerà arti fatte per beneficio di aere,\ncome molini da vento.\n\nEuropa ſopra il Toro ſignifica la conuerſione, il conſen timento, la ſanità, la annichilatione, & la religione.\n\nIl giudicio di Paris hauerà il foro ciuile.\n\nLa ſpera dinoterà l’Aſtrologia.\n\nSotto il Prometheo di Saturno ſaranno cinque imagini.\n\nCibele contenerà la Geometria, Geographia, Coſmogra\nphia, & Agricoltura.\n\nUn fanciullo ſopra la tauola dell’Alphabeto ci darà la\nGrammatica.\n\nLa pelle di Marſia conſeruerà l’arti d’intorno a cuoi,\n& pelli.\n\nUna ſfera contenerà l’uccellagioni co notturni uccelli.\n\nVno aſino, per eſſer animal Saturnino, & nato alle fa= tiche, ſignificherà vetture, ſacchini, piſtrino, & ſerui a quel lo condannati.\n\nIL FINE.","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0001","text":"PROMETHEO.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"7.1"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","text":"IL ſettimo Grado è aſſignato a tutte le arti coſi nobili come vili,le quali hanno ſopra ciaſcuna porta Prometheo con la facella acceſa. Et accioche ſ’intenda la cagion,per la quale vogliamo,che egli ci ſia il ſimbolo delle arti, fa biſogno intender quello che dice Socrate nel Protagora di Pla-\ntone. Dice egli adunque che eſſendo venuto il tempo fatal de la creatione de gli animali, i Dei, che all’hora erano ſoli for marono eſſi animali nelle viſcere della terra di fuoco, et di terra,& di quelle coſe che col fuoco, & con la terra ſono meſcolate:& mentre erano in volontà di mettergli in luce, commiſſero à Prometheo,& ad Epimetheo,che diſtribuiſſe-\nro a ciaſcuno le convenevoli forze. Et Epimetheo pregò Pro metheo,che à lui laſciaſſe far coſi fatta diſtributione, &","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"7.2"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0003","text":"L’Idea del Theatro.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"7.3"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0004","text":"R\n\nL’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"7.4"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","text":"che egli ſolamente ſi ſteſſe a porui mente. conſenti Prometheo, & Epimetheo fece la diſtributione. Ad alcuni adunque diede robuſtezza ſenza celerità, & ad alcuni più deboli die de velocità, alcuni armò, & à quelli che mancauano di ar-\nme trouo alcuna coſa accommodata alla lor ſalute: & di quelli che erano chiuſi in picciol corpo, parte ne fece leuar per l’ae re dalle piume, & parte ſerper per la terra. Et quelle che erano di ampia grandezza volle, che eſſa grandezza deſſe loro forza per la loro ſalute. Et poi che Socrate ha molto va gato intorno alla varietà de gli animali bruti, dice che Epi metheo poco ſauio conſumò tutte le doti nele beſtie, & non auerſi di laſciar parte di tanta larghezza da donare all’hu mana ſpecie. Reſtaua adunque la ſpecie humana vota & priua de ogni dote.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"7.5"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","text":"Ma Prometheo vedendo la mala distribu tion fatta da Epimetheo, & gia vicinarſi il giorno fatale, nel qual faceua biſogno far uſcir in luce gli animali, no tro uando altra via da poter alla humana ſalute prouedere, na ſcoſamente col fuoco furò l’artificio, la ſapienza di Vulcano & di Minerua. percioche non ſi poteua far che alcuno ſen za fuoco, cio è ſenza acutezza di ingegno la poteſſe ne con ſeguir, ne vſare. Queſta adunque miſe Prometheo ne gli huomini, la qual appartiene ſolamente al viuere, ma la ciuile mancaua, la quale era bene appreſſo Gioue. Ma non fu leci to à Prometheo aſcender tanto alto, percioche horribil cuſto die, che ſtauano intorno alla rocca di Gioue ne lo ſpauentaua no. Per quel furto adunque l’huomo ſolo fra gli animali fat to partecipe della diuina ſorte; hebbe cognition de Dei da principio, per la qual cognitione diuenne religioso, & à lo ro dedicò altari & ſtatue.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"7.6"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0007","text":"Diſtinſe con arte articolatamen te la voce in parole, ediſicò caſe, fece ueſtimenti, letti & rote","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"7.7"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0008","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"7.8"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0009","text":"42","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"7.9"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","text":"coſe nutrimenti della terra. Ma pur gli huomini ſparſame re vagauano dal principio, percioche non anchora erano edi ficate le citta, donde aueniua che gli huomini eſſendo piu de boli delle fere, erano da quelle per tutto diſſipati. Bene era trouata la facultà appartenente all’apparecchio del viuere, ma da combatter contra le fere non haueuano il modo, per= cioche la ciuil facultà, della qual la militia n’è vna, parte, non era fra loro. Pur per poterſi gli huomini dalle fere dif= ſendere, ſi congregarono & edificarono le citta. Ma ohimè che coſi congregati non ſi poteuano l’vn l’altro comporta= re, & tra loro ſi faceuano di mille oltraggi, percioche della ciuil facultà non erano partecipi. la onde ſforzati ad vſcir delle citta tornarono a diu enir paſtura delle fere.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"7.10"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","text":"Alla fin Gio ue moſſo a pietà dell’humana infelicità, mandò Mercurio, che portaſſe a gli huomini il pudore, & la giuſtitia, à fin che queſte due coſe ornaſſero talmente le citta, che gli huo= mini ſi conciliaſſero cõ beniuolẽza. Mercurio hauẽdo da por tar queſti due ornamenti, interrogò il Padre ſe hauea da di ſtribuir queſti due doni nella maniera che erano ſtate diſtri= buite le arti, delle quali l’vno ne hauea l’vna, l’altro l’altra o ſe pur le haueſſe da dare à tutti egualmẽte. A tutti riſpo= ſe Gioue, percioche tutti li huomini ne debbono eſſer partecipi che altramente le citta conſeruar nõ ſi potrebbono, che ſe be ne un Medico, o un calzolajo in una citta poteſſe ſodiſfare a molti nõ medici, et a molti nõ calzolai, vno nõdimeno di pu dore & di giuſtitia ornato fra molti che ne puden, ne giuſti tia non haueſſero non ſi porebbe conſeruare.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"7.11"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","text":"Appreſſo Gio= ue commiſe, che da ſua parte ſacreſſe una legge, che qual ſi trouaſſe nudo di pudore & di giuſtitia, foſſe come peſte de la citta con eſtremo ſupplicio tolto dal numero de viui.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"7.12"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0013","text":"F  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"7.13"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0014","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"7.14"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","text":"Ma noi vogliamo che il noſtro Prometheo non ſolamente contenga tutte le arti nobili & ignobili, che da lui furono diſtribuite, ma anchor la ciuile & la militar facultà, per non leuar il Theatro a più alto grado.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"7.15"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0016","text":"Luna.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"7.16"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","text":"Sotto il Prometheo della Luna ſaranno cinque imagini Diana a cui Mercurio porge la veſta contenerà i meſi & le lor parti. Nettuno ci darà le arti ſopra le acque , come acquedutti fontane artificiate,ponti porti, Arzane,arte nauale & del peſcare. Daphne contenerà i giardini , & l’arti intorno al le-\ngname. Himeneo ſignificherà nozze & parentadi. Diana con l’arco dinoterà la cacciagione.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"7.17"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0018","text":"Mercu","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"7.18"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","text":"Sotto il Prometheo di Mercurio ſaranno ſei imagini. Vn orio, Elephante. Si come queſta imagine ſotto il Conuiuio ſignifi ca fauoloſa Deità, coſì qui dinoterà fauoloſa religione, riti & cerimonie co ſuoi appartenenti. Hercole che tira una ſaetta con tre punte è nobilissima imagine di tutte le ſcienze pertinenti alle coſe celeſti , à queſto mondo,& all’abiſſo.percioche i Theologi ſimboliza ti vogliono che Hercole ſignifichi l’humano ſpirito,il quale come ſaetta di tre punte poſſa penetrar con l’vna i ſecreti celeſti con l’altra quelli di queſto mondo. E con la terza quelli dell’abiſſo. Adunque contenerà vn volume molto ben diſtinto,nel qual ſi vederanno ordinate ſenza eccettione tut te le ſcienze con tutti gli anelli appartenenti alle loro par ticolari catene.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"7.19"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0020","text":"Et finalmente la eloquenza,come ricetto & ornamento di tutte, la eloquenza dico appartenente alla oratione ſciolta,in tutte le ſue ſpecie , percioche il poema è","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"7.20"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0021","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"7.21"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0022","text":"43","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"7.22"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0023","text":"ſolare. Et andra alla imagine di Apollo fra le Muſe, & ſotto queſto Hercole anchor fara compreſſa la libreria. L’Arco celeſte con Mercurio. Per eſſer Iris meſſaggiera di Giunone & Mercurio de Dei. Queſta imagine haurà il volume delle ambaſſerie del nuncio privato, & del man= dato ſotto mano. Et il primo contenerà i pertinenti alle let tere che ſi mandano, & che ſi ricevono.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"7.23"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","text":"Tre Pallidi. vna edificante città, l’altra che teſſa te la figurata, la terza che faccia vna ſtatua. dell’edificar hab= biamo Virgilio Pallas quas condidit artes ipſa colat. Della tela figurata ne teſtifica il congresſo con Arachne. Et che ella foſſe ſtatuaria di Plaſtica il ci poſſiamo perſuader dal le coſe dette di ſopra. Et dalla fauola di Socrate di ſopra da noi recitata, quando dice che i Dei formarono tutti gli ani mali ſenza nominare alcuno in particolare. queſta imagine adunque con ſeruera volume appartenente al diſegno, al l’architettura alla pittura, alla proſpettiva, alla plaſtica, & alla ſtatuaria, & a tutti i loro appartenenti. Et la diſtintion ſarà tale ne tagli che farà apparir marauiglioſo l’ordine.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"7.24"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","text":"Mercurio con vn Gallo, ſignificherà la mercatura, & Mercu ſuoi appartenenti. ne ſo onde Landino ſe l’habbia tratto. rio. Ma à me baſta il teſtimonio ſuo nelle ſue allegorie, nelle quali e dice l’antichità hauere vſato coſi fatto ſimbolo per la mercatura, aggiungendo non ſo che ragione della gar rulità di Mercurio rappreſentante quella de mercatanti Prometheo con la facella, come è anchor in ſu la porta rappreſenterà arti & artefici in generale. Ne cio paia nuo uo, che anchor Ariſtotele nella ſua Priora dice eſſer lecito per difetto di vocaboli dar tal’hora alla ſpecie il nome del genere.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"7.25"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0026","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"7.26"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0027","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"7.27"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0028","text":"Venere.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"7.28"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0029","text":"Sotto Venere ſaranno ſette imagini.\nCerbero contiene la cucina , & appartamenti a conviti, &\nal dormir ſolenne.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"7.29"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0030","text":"I vermi che fan la ſeta conterrà il Ginecio, con la veſtia ria con gli antecedenti, & conſeguenti. Antecedenti, come filar, teſſere , ſartoria , tintoria. Conſeguenti veſtirſi, ſpo gliarſi, reſarcire,& la guardaroba.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"7.30"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0031","text":"Hercole purgante le ſtalle d’Augia conterrà bagni &\nbarberie.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"7.31"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","text":"La fanciulla col vaſo d’odori ſignificherà la perfumeria. Il Minotauro qui è arte vitioſa, ruffianeſmo, bordello,& arte meretricia.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"7.32"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0033","text":"Bacco cõ l’aſta coperta di hedera, muſica et arti di giochi.\nNarciso conterrà l’arte de bellezzi.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"7.33"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0034","text":"Sole.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"7.34"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0035","text":"Sotto il Prometheo del Sole ſaranno ſette imagini. Gerion ucciſo da Hercole conterrà minuti,hore,anno,horo logio.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"7.35"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0036","text":"Il Gallo col Leone conterrà il principato,& ſuoi appara-\ntenenti.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"7.36"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0037","text":"La Sibilla col tripode ſignificherà la divinatione,& le\nſue ſpeci ,& la prophetia.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"7.37"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0038","text":"Apollo fra le muſe dinoterà la poeſia. Apollo che uccide il ſerpente , cioè i veleni delle infirmi-\ntà , haurà tutta la medicina. Apollo paſtore ci darà l’arte paſtorale.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"7.38"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","text":"Vn huomo à cauallo con vn logoro in mano conterrà la caccia dello ſparuiere & del falcone eſercitij nobili. Et ben che appreſſo gli antichi non foſſero in coſtume, nondimeno potendoſi per perplexionem accomodar molti modi di parla re , & acciochè volendoſi aſſoluer le nouelle del Boccac-","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"7.39"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0040","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"7.40"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0041","text":"DI M. GIVLIO CAMILLO.  44","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"7.41"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","text":"cio accioche buchi non manchino, habbiam dato queſto luogo . Et qui diro quattro parole della vtilità della mia fatica, che proponendomi lo ſtato di queſta età, & della no ſtra religione, ho cercato di accomodar molte coſe al noſtro coſtume, come per eſempio. Quantunque Cicerone non hab bia mai parlato di Chriſto, ne dello Spirito Santo, conſideran do io il biſogno noſtro del parlare , & dello ſcriuer delle perſone diuine ſotto la imagine della latitudine de gli en= ti, ho apparecchiato gran ſelua tratta da gli ſcritti di Cice rone, con la qual ciceronianamente ſi potra veſtire il nome del figliuolo & dello ſpirito ſanto. Et quello del figliuolo ha due ſelue ſeparate, l’vna per veſtire il ſuo ſantiſſimo no me, come verbo & ſapienza. l’altra come verbo incarnato cio è Chriſto, & Chriſto crucifiſſo per noi.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"7.42"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","text":"Queſta dico per cioche molti de Cabaliſti Hebrei hanno conoſciuto la ſapie za & il verbo, ma non hanno creduto quella eſſerſi incar= nata, & hauer per noi patito. Il che vedendo Paolo dice vn ſottiſſimo paſſaggio. Non per ſapientiam verbi, ne crux Chri ſti euacuantur. Di che ſe eſſo geloſiſſimo Paolo hauſſe hau to a ſcriuer l’Euangelio di Giovanni, hauerebbe perauentura detto. In principio erat Chriſtus, & Chriſtus erat apud Deum, & Deus erat Chriſtus. benche Giovanni diede il ri medio quando diſſe. Et verbum caro factum eſt.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"7.43"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0044","text":"Sotto Marte ſaranno ſette imagini.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"7.44"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0045","text":"Marte.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"7.45"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046","text":"Vulcano ci dara l’arti fabrili di fuoco. Vn Centauro, benche nella natura delle coſe non ſiano mai ſtati i centauri, pur leggendoſi, che quando ſi comincia rono a domare i caualli, a coloro che di lõtano mirauano pareua che il cauallo & caualcatore foſſe vna coſa iſteſſa. Sotto queſta imagine copriremo le arti al cauallo, & al ſuo","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"7.46"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0047","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"7.47"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0048","text":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"7.48"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0049","text":"beneficio appartenenti: & ſi da a Marte, per eſſer il cauallo\nanimal Martiale.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"7.49"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","text":"Due ſerpenti combattenti: conteneranno l’arte militare,\n& la guerra terreſtre & nauale.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"7.50"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0051","text":"Due giuocatori di Ceſti conteneranno tutti i giuochi Mar\ntiali.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"7.51"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","text":"Rhadamanto giudicante le anime hauerà il foro crimi=\nnale diſtinto.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"7.52"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","text":"Le furie infernali per eſſere eſecutrici delle pene, contene= ranno il bargellato, cattura, carcere, tortura, ſupplicii.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"7.53"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0054","text":"Marſia ſcorticato da Apollo ci darà il macello.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"7.54"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0055","text":"Sotto il Prometheo di Gioue ſaranno cinque imagini.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"7.55"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0056","text":"Gioue.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"7.56"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0057","text":"Giuno ſuſpeſa contenerà arti fatte per beneficio di aere,\ncome molini da vento.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"7.57"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0058","text":"Europa ſopra il Toro ſignifica la conuerſione, il conſen timento, la ſanità, la annichilatione, & la religione.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"7.58"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0059","text":"Il giudicio di Paris hauerà il foro ciuile.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"7.59"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0060","text":"La ſpera dinoterà l’Aſtrologia.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"7.60"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0061","text":"Sotto il Prometheo di Saturno ſaranno cinque imagini.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"7.61"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0062","text":"Cibele contenerà la Geometria, Geographia, Coſmogra\nphia, & Agricoltura.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"7.62"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0063","text":"Un fanciullo ſopra la tauola dell’Alphabeto ci darà la\nGrammatica.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"7.63"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0064","text":"La pelle di Marſia conſeruerà l’arti d’intorno a cuoi,\n& pelli.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"7.64"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0065","text":"Una ſfera contenerà l’uccellagioni co notturni uccelli.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"7.65"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0066","text":"Vno aſino, per eſſer animal Saturnino, & nato alle fa= tiche, ſignificherà vetture, ſacchini, piſtrino, & ſerui a quel lo condannati.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"7.66"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0067","text":"IL FINE.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"7.67"}],"sha256":"1c56cc5d24eef4a7317af708416721ee7f5e660119aac4375d521117212168a9","language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261030T230827211996Z_56d389d9","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"PROMETHEUS.","source_sha256":"1c56cc5d24eef4a7317af708416721ee7f5e660119aac4375d521117212168a9","sha256":"6de69754c568fe5f57408f51c05f63194751fbd715c721dcb566daac4cbd02f3","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:08:27.212059+00:00","paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0001","text":"PROMETHEUS.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"7.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","text":"The seventh Grade is assigned to all the arts, both noble and vile, which have above each door Prometheus with the torch lit. And in order that the reason may be understood for which we wish him to be the symbol of the arts, it is necessary to understand what Socrates says in Plato's Prota-\ngoras. He says, then, that when the fated time for the creation of animals had come, the Gods, who were then alone, formed these animals in the bowels of the earth out of fire, and earth, and those things that are mingled with fire and earth; and while they were intending to bring them into light, they entrusted to Prometheus and Epimetheus that they should distribu-\nte to each the suitable powers. And Epimetheus begged Pro-\nmetheus to leave to him the making of such a distribution, and","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"7.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0003","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"7.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0004","text":"R\n\nTHE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"7.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","text":"that he himself should merely attend to it. Prometheus consented, and Epimetheus made the distribution. To some, therefore, he gave strength without swiftness, and to some weaker ones he gave swiftness; some he armed, and for those who lacked ar-\nms he found some thing suited to their safety; and of those enclosed in a small body, some he made to fly through the air by means of feathers, and some to creep through the earth. And those that were of great size, he wished that size itself should give them strength for their safety. And after Socrates has ranged widely over the variety of brute animals, he says that Epimetheus, being little wise, consumed all the gifts upon the beasts, and had not left himself a portion of such abundance to bestow upon the human species. The human species therefore remained empty and deprived of every gift.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"7.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","text":"But Prometheus, seeing the bad distribu-\ntion made by Epimetheus, and that the fated day was already drawing near on which it was necessary to bring the animals forth into the light, finding no other way to provide for human safety, secretly stole, together with fire, the artifice, the wisdom of Vulcan and Minerva. For no one could either acquire or use it without fire, that is, without keenness of intellect. This, then, Prometheus placed in men, which pertains only to living; but the civil [art] was lacking, which was indeed with Jupiter. But Prometheus was not permitted to ascend so high, for the terrible guards who stood about Jupiter's citadel frightened him. By that theft, therefore, man alone among animals, having been made a participant in the divine lot, had from the beginning knowledge of the Gods; through which knowledge he became religious, and dedicated altars and statues to them.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"7.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0007","text":"With art he distinctly articulated the voice into words, built houses, made garments, beds, and wheeled","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"7.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0008","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"7.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0009","text":"42","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"7.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","text":"things, nourishments of the earth. Yet men wandered scatteredly at the beginning, for cities had not yet been built; whence it came about that men, being weaker than beasts, were everywhere destroyed by them. The faculty pertaining to the provision of living had indeed been discovered, but they had no means of fighting against the beasts, be-\ncause the civil faculty, of which military art is one part, was not among them. Yet, in order that men might defend themselves against beasts, they gathered together and built cities. But alas, being thus gathered together they could not endure one another, and among themselves they committed a thousand outrages, because they did not partake of the civil faculty. Whereupon, forced to leave the cities, they again became food for the beasts.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"7.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","text":"At last Ju-\npiter, moved to pity by human unhappiness, sent Mercury to bring men shame and justice, so that these two things might so adorn the cities that men might be united with goodwill. Mercury, having to bring these two ornaments, asked the Father whether he was to distribute these two gifts in the manner in which the arts had been distributed, of which one man had one and another another; or whether indeed he should give them equally to all. To all, Jupiter answered, for all men must partake of them, since otherwise cities could not be preserved: for although one physician, or one cobbler, in a city might suffice for many non-physicians and many non-cobblers, nevertheless one man adorned with shame and justice among many who possessed neither shame nor justice could not be preserved.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"7.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","text":"Moreover Ju-\npiter commanded that a law be ordained in his name: that whoever should be found naked of shame and justice should, as a pest of the city, be removed from the number of the living by extreme punishment.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"7.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0013","text":"F  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"7.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0014","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"7.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","text":"But we wish that our Prometheus should contain not only all the noble and ignoble arts that were distributed by him, but also the civil and military faculty, so as not to raise the Theatre to a higher grade.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"7.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0016","text":"Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"7.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","text":"Under the Prometheus of the Moon there shall be five images. Diana, to whom Mercury offers the garment, shall contain the months and their parts. Neptune shall give us the arts upon the waters, such as aqueducts, artificial fountains, bridges, ports, arsenals, the art of navigation and of fishing. Daphne shall contain gardens and the arts concerning ti-\nmber. Hymenaeus shall signify marriages and kinships. Diana with the bow shall denote hunting.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"7.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0018","text":"Mercury","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"7.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","text":"Under the Prometheus of Mercury there shall be six images. An elephant, as this image beneath the Banquet signifies fabulous Deity, so here it shall denote fabulous religion, rites and ceremonies with their appurtenances. Hercules, who draws an arrow with three points, is a most noble image of all the sciences pertaining to celestial things, to this world, and to the abyss; for the symbolizing Theologians wish Hercules to signify the human spirit, which, like an arrow with three points, can penetrate with one the celestial secrets, with another those of this world, and with the third those of the abyss. Therefore it shall contain a volume very well distinguished, in which shall be seen arranged without exception all the sciences with all the rings belonging to their particular chains.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"7.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0020","text":"And finally eloquence, as the receptacle and ornament of them all—I mean eloquence belonging to unbound discourse, in all its species—for the poem is","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"7.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0021","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"7.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0022","text":"43","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"7.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0023","text":"solar. And it shall go to the image of Apollo among the Muses; and under this Hercules the library too shall be included. The celestial Bow with Mercury. Since Iris is messenger of Juno and Mercury of the Gods. This image shall have the volume of embassies, of the private messenger, and of the mandate underhand. And the first shall contain matters pertaining to letters that are sent and received.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"7.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","text":"Three Pallas figures: one building a city, another weaving the figured web, the third making a statue. Of building we have Virgil: Pallas quas condidit artes ipsa colat. Of the figured web, her contest with Arachne bears witness to us. And that she was a statuary in Plastic art, we can persuade ourselves from the things said above, and from the fable of Socrates recounted above by us, when he says that the Gods formed all the ani-\nmals without naming any one in particular. This image, therefore, shall preserve the volume pertaining to design, to architecture, to painting, to perspective, to plastic art, and to statuary, and to all their appurtenances. And the distinction shall be such in the divisions that it shall make the order appear marvellous.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"7.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","text":"Mercury with a Cock will signify commerce, and things pertaining to Mercury. I know not whence Landino drew it. But for me his testimony in his allegories suffices, in which he says that antiquity used such a symbol for commerce, adding I know not what reason concerning Mercury’s garrulity, representing that of merchants. Prometheus with the torch, as he is also upon the gate, will represent arts and artificers in general. Nor should this seem new, since Aristotle too in his Prior Analytics says that, for want of words, it is permissible sometimes to give the species the name of the genus.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"7.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0026","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"7.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0027","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"7.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0028","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"7.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0029","text":"Under Venus there shall be seven images.\nCerberus comprises the kitchen, and apartments for banquets, and for solemn sleeping.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"7.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0030","text":"The worms that make silk shall contain the gynaeceum, with clothing and its antecedents and consequents. Antecedents, such as spinning, weaving, tailoring, dyeing. Consequents: dressing oneself, undressing oneself, mending, and the wardrobe.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"7.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0031","text":"Hercules cleansing the stables of Augeas shall contain baths and\nbarbers’ shops.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"7.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","text":"The maiden with the vessel of scents shall signify perfumery. The Minotaur here is the vicious art: procuring, the brothel, and the art of prostitution.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"7.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0033","text":"Bacchus with the staff covered in ivy: music and the arts of games.\nNarcissus shall contain the art of beautification.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"7.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0034","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"7.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0035","text":"Under the Prometheus of the Sun there shall be seven images. Geryon slain by Hercules shall contain minutes, hours, year, clock.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"7.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0036","text":"The Cock with the Lion shall contain principality, and its appur-\ntenances.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"7.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0037","text":"The Sibyl with the tripod shall signify divination, and its\nspecies, and prophecy.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"7.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0038","text":"Apollo among the Muses shall denote poetry. Apollo who slays the serpent, that is, the poisons of infirmi-\nties, shall have all medicine. Apollo the shepherd shall give us the pastoral art.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"7.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","text":"A man on horseback with a lure in his hand shall contain hunting with the sparrowhawk and the falcon, noble exercises. And although among the ancients these were not customary, nevertheless, since by perplexionem many modes of speech can be accommodated, and so that, should one wish to complete Boccac-","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"7.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0040","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"7.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0041","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  44","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"7.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","text":"cio, no gaps may be lacking, we have assigned this place. And here I shall say four words about the usefulness of my labour: proposing to myself the condition of this age, and of our religion, I have sought to accommodate many things to our custom, as for example. Although Cicero never spoke of Christ, nor of the Holy Spirit, considering our need to speak and write of the divine persons under the image of the latitude of beings, I have prepared a great forest drawn from Cicero’s writings, with which the name of the Son and of the Holy Spirit may be clad in Ciceronian fashion. And that of the Son has two separate forests, one for clothing his most holy name, as Word and Wisdom; the other as the incarnate Word, that is Christ, and Christ crucified for us.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"7.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","text":"I say this because many of the Hebrew Kabbalists have known Wisdom and the Word, but have not believed that it was incarnate and suffered for us. Seeing which, Paul says a most subtle passage: Non per sapientiam verbi, ne crux Christi euacuantur. Wherefore, if Paul, most zealous as he was, had had to write the Gospel of John, he would perhaps have said: In principio erat Christus, & Christus erat apud Deum, & Deus erat Christus. Although John provided the remedy when he said: Et verbum caro factum est.","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"7.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0044","text":"Under Mars there shall be seven images.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"7.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0045","text":"Mars.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"7.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046","text":"Vulcan shall give us the mechanical arts of fire. A Centaur—although in the nature of things centaurs have never existed, yet it being read that, when men first began to tame horses, to those who beheld them from afar the horse and rider seemed to be one and the same thing. Under this image we shall cover the arts pertaining to the horse, and to its","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"7.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0047","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"7.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0048","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"7.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0049","text":"belonging to benefit: & it is given to Mars, because the horse is a\nMartial animal.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"7.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","text":"Two fighting serpents: shall contain the military art,\n& war by land & sea.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"7.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0051","text":"Two players of Cesti shall contain all the Martial games.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"7.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","text":"Rhadamanthus judging souls shall have the criminal court\ndistinguished.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"7.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","text":"The infernal Furies, being executors of punishments, shall con=\ntain the office of the bargello, arrest, prison, torture, punishments.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"7.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0054","text":"Marsyas flayed by Apollo shall give us the slaughterhouse.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"7.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0055","text":"Under the Prometheus of Jupiter there shall be five images.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"7.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0056","text":"Jupiter.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"7.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0057","text":"Juno suspended shall contain arts made for the benefit of air,\nsuch as windmills.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"7.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0058","text":"Europa upon the Bull signifies conversion, consent,\nhealth, annihilation, & religion.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"7.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0059","text":"The judgement of Paris shall have the civil court.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"7.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0060","text":"The sphere shall denote Astrology.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"7.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0061","text":"Under the Prometheus of Saturn there shall be five images.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"7.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0062","text":"Cybele shall contain Geometry, Geography, Cosmogra\nphy, & Agriculture.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"7.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0063","text":"A child upon the table of the Alphabet shall give us\nGrammar.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"7.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0064","text":"The skin of Marsyas shall preserve the arts concerning hides,\n& skins.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"7.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0065","text":"A sphere shall contain bird-catching with nocturnal birds.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"7.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0066","text":"One ass, being a Saturnine animal, & born to labours, shall\nsignify conveyances, porters, the mill, & servants condemned to that.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"7.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0067","text":"THE END.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"7.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0067"]}],"source_digest":"28cc06385f363f35f629375dc3e678b8884fc34fb6af4de5f9a51b5b58f3883e","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"PROMETHEO."},{"id":"SOURCE_TR_20261031T002018430919Z_b7dc9bb5","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"PROMETHEUS.","source_sha256":"1c56cc5d24eef4a7317af708416721ee7f5e660119aac4375d521117212168a9","sha256":"e127b67f235331c2b9ca87f976996a006422f41eaf86abd5264164954bb5cb64","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-31T00:20:18.430984+00:00","translate_quotations":true,"paragraphs":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0001","text":"PROMETHEUS.","kind":"passage","sequence":1,"address":"7.1","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0001"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","text":"The seventh Grade is assigned to all the arts, both noble and base, which have above each door Prometheus with the lighted torch. And in order that the reason may be understood for which we wish him to be the symbol of the arts, it is necessary to understand what Socrates says in Plato's Protagoras. He says, then, that when the fated time for the creation of animals had come, the Gods, who at that time were alone, formed those animals in the bowels of the earth out of fire, and earth, and those things which are mixed with fire and earth; and while they intended to bring them forth into the light, they entrusted to Prometheus and Epimetheus the task of distributing to each its suitable powers. And Epimetheus begged Prometheus to let him make such a distribution, and","kind":"passage","sequence":2,"address":"7.2","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0003","text":"The Idea of the Theatre.","kind":"passage","sequence":3,"address":"7.3","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0003"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0004","text":"R\n\nTHE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":4,"address":"7.4","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0004"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","text":"that he himself should merely attend to it. Prometheus consented, and Epimetheus made the distribution. To some, then, he gave strength without swiftness, and to some weaker ones he gave swiftness; he armed some, and for those who lacked arms he found something suited to their safety; and of those enclosed in a small body, he caused some to fly through the air by means of feathers, and others to crawl upon the earth. And those that were of great size, he wished that size itself should give them strength for their safety. And after Socrates has dwelt at length upon the variety of brute animals, he says that Epimetheus, being not very wise, consumed all the gifts upon the beasts, and had not left himself any part of so great abundance to bestow upon the human species. Thus the human species remained empty and deprived of every gift.","kind":"passage","sequence":5,"address":"7.5","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","text":"But Prometheus, seeing the bad distribution made by Epimetheus, and that the fated day was already drawing near, on which it was necessary to bring the animals forth into the light, finding no other way of providing for human safety, secretly stole, together with fire, the artifice, the wisdom of Vulcan and Minerva. For it could not be that anyone without fire—that is, without sharpness of intellect—could either attain or use it. This, then, Prometheus placed among men, which belongs only to living; but the civic art was lacking, which was indeed with Jupiter. But it was not permitted to Prometheus to ascend so high, because the terrible guards who stood around Jupiter's fortress frightened him. By that theft, therefore, man alone among animals, having become a participant in the divine lot, had knowledge of the Gods from the beginning; by which knowledge he became religious, and dedicated to them altars and statues.","kind":"passage","sequence":6,"address":"7.6","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0007","text":"He distinguished the voice articulately into words by art, built houses, made garments, beds, and roots,","kind":"passage","sequence":7,"address":"7.7","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0007"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0008","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO","kind":"passage","sequence":8,"address":"7.8","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0008"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0009","text":"42","kind":"passage","sequence":9,"address":"7.9","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0009"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","text":"things that are the nourishment of the earth. Yet men wandered scattered about at first, because cities had not yet been built; whence it came about that men, being weaker than wild beasts, were everywhere destroyed by them. The faculty belonging to the provision of life had indeed been found, but they had no means of fighting against the wild beasts, because the civic faculty, of which military science is one part, was not among them. Yet, so that men might defend themselves against the wild beasts, they gathered together and built cities. But alas, being thus gathered, they could not endure one another, and committed a thousand outrages among themselves, because they did not partake of the civic faculty. Wherefore, compelled to leave the cities, they returned to becoming food for the wild beasts.","kind":"passage","sequence":10,"address":"7.10","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","text":"At last Jupiter, moved to pity by human unhappiness, sent Mercury to bring men shame and justice, so that these two things might so adorn the cities that men should reconcile themselves with goodwill. Mercury, having to carry these two ornaments, asked the Father whether he was to distribute these two gifts in the manner in which the arts had been distributed, of which one had one and another another, or whether rather he was to give them equally to all. To all, Jupiter replied, for all men must partake of them, since otherwise cities could not be preserved; for although one physician or one shoemaker in a city could satisfy many non-physicians and many non-shoemakers, yet one adorned with shame and justice among many who had neither shame nor justice could not be preserved.","kind":"passage","sequence":11,"address":"7.11","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","text":"Moreover, Jupiter commanded that a law should be proclaimed on his behalf: that whoever should be found naked of shame and justice should, as a pest of the city, be removed from the number of the living by the most extreme punishment.","kind":"passage","sequence":12,"address":"7.12","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0013","text":"F  ii","kind":"passage","sequence":13,"address":"7.13","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0013"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0014","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":14,"address":"7.14","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0014"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","text":"But we wish our Prometheus to contain not only all the noble and ignoble arts that were distributed by him, but also the civic and military faculty, so as not to raise the Theatre to a higher grade.","kind":"passage","sequence":15,"address":"7.15","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0016","text":"Moon.","kind":"passage","sequence":16,"address":"7.16","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0016"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","text":"Under the Prometheus of the Moon there will be five images. Diana, to whom Mercury offers the garment, will contain the months and their parts. Neptune will give us the arts concerning waters, such as aqueducts, artificial fountains, bridges, ports, arsenals, the art of navigation and of fishing. Daphne will contain gardens, and the arts concerning wood. Hymenaeus will signify marriages and kinships. Diana with the bow will denote hunting.","kind":"passage","sequence":17,"address":"7.17","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0018","text":"Mercu","kind":"passage","sequence":18,"address":"7.18","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0018"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","text":"Under the Prometheus of Mercury there will be six images. An orio, Elephant. Just as this image under the Banquet signifies fabulous Deity, so here it will denote fabulous religion, rites and ceremonies with their appurtenances. Hercules, who draws an arrow with three points, is a most noble image of all the sciences pertaining to celestial things, to this world, and to the abyss. For the symbolizing Theologians wish Hercules to signify the human spirit, which, like a three-pointed arrow, can penetrate with one point the celestial secrets, with another those of this world, and with the third those of the abyss. It will therefore contain a very well distinguished volume, in which all the sciences will be seen ordered without exception, with all the rings belonging to their particular chains.","kind":"passage","sequence":19,"address":"7.19","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0020","text":"And finally eloquence, as the receptacle and ornament of them all—I mean the eloquence belonging to prose discourse, in all its kinds, for the poem is","kind":"passage","sequence":20,"address":"7.20","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0020"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0021","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.","kind":"passage","sequence":21,"address":"7.21","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0021"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0022","text":"43","kind":"passage","sequence":22,"address":"7.22","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0022"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0023","text":"solar. And it will go to the image of Apollo among the Muses; and under this Hercules the library will also be included. The heavenly bow with Mercury. Since Iris is the messenger of Juno and Mercury of the Gods. This image will have the volume of embassies, of the private envoy, and of the clandestine mandate. And the first will contain those matters pertaining to letters that are sent and received.","kind":"passage","sequence":23,"address":"7.23","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0023"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","text":"Three Pallas figures: one building a city, another weaving figured cloth, the third making a statue. Of building we have Virgil: “Pallas herself cultivates the arts which she founded.” Of figured cloth her contest with Arachne bears witness to us. And that she was a maker of statues and of plastic art, we may persuade ourselves from the things said above, and from the fable of Socrates recited above by us, when he says that the Gods formed all the animals without naming any in particular. This image, therefore, will preserve the volume pertaining to design, architecture, painting, perspective, plastic art, and statuary, and to all their appurtenances. And the distinction in the divisions will be such as to make the order appear marvellous.","kind":"passage","sequence":24,"address":"7.24","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","text":"Mercury with a Cock will signify commerce, and the things pertaining to Mercury. I do not know whence Landino has drawn it. But for me his testimony in his allegories suffices, in which he says that antiquity used such a symbol for commerce, adding I know not what reason concerning the loquacity of Mercury, representing that of merchants. Prometheus with the torch, as also upon the door, will represent arts and craftsmen in general. Nor should this seem new, since Aristotle too in his Prior Analytics says that, through lack of terms, it is permissible sometimes to give the species the name of the genus.","kind":"passage","sequence":25,"address":"7.25","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0026","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":26,"address":"7.26","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0026"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0027","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":27,"address":"7.27","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0027"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0028","text":"Venus.","kind":"passage","sequence":28,"address":"7.28","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0028"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0029","text":"Under Venus there will be seven images.\nCerberus contains the kitchen, and apartments for banquets, and\nfor solemn sleeping.","kind":"passage","sequence":29,"address":"7.29","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0029"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0030","text":"The worms that make silk will contain the gynaeceum, with clothing and its antecedents and consequences. Antecedents, such as spinning, weaving, tailoring, dyeing. Consequences: dressing oneself, undressing oneself, mending, and the wardrobe.","kind":"passage","sequence":30,"address":"7.30","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0030"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0031","text":"Hercules cleansing the stables of Augeas will contain baths and\nbarbershops.","kind":"passage","sequence":31,"address":"7.31","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0031"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","text":"The maiden with the vase of perfumes will signify perfumery. The Minotaur here is a vicious art: procuring, brothel-keeping, and the art of prostitution.","kind":"passage","sequence":32,"address":"7.32","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0033","text":"Bacchus with the staff covered in ivy: music and the arts of games.\nNarcissus will contain the art of beautification.","kind":"passage","sequence":33,"address":"7.33","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0033"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0034","text":"Sun.","kind":"passage","sequence":34,"address":"7.34","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0034"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0035","text":"Under the Prometheus of the Sun there will be seven images. Geryon slain by Hercules will contain minutes, hours, year, clock.","kind":"passage","sequence":35,"address":"7.35","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0035"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0036","text":"The Cock with the Lion will contain principality, and its appur-\ntenances.","kind":"passage","sequence":36,"address":"7.36","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0036"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0037","text":"The Sibyl with the tripod will signify divination, and its\nspecies, and prophecy.","kind":"passage","sequence":37,"address":"7.37","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0037"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0038","text":"Apollo among the Muses will denote poetry. Apollo who kills the serpent, that is, the poisons of infirmi-\nties, will have all medicine. Apollo the shepherd will give us the pastoral art.","kind":"passage","sequence":38,"address":"7.38","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0038"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","text":"A man on horseback with a lure in his hand will contain the hunting of the sparrowhawk and the falcon, noble exercises. And although among the ancients these were not customary, nevertheless, since by interweaving many modes of speaking can be accommodated, and so that, when wishing to complete the tales of Boccac-","kind":"passage","sequence":39,"address":"7.39","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0040","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":40,"address":"7.40","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0040"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0041","text":"BY M. GIULIO CAMILLO.  44","kind":"passage","sequence":41,"address":"7.41","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0041"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","text":"cio, so that holes may not be lacking, we have given this place. And here I shall say four words concerning the usefulness of my labour: setting before myself the state of this age and of our religion, I have sought to accommodate many things to our custom, as for example. Although Cicero never spoke either of Christ or of the Holy Spirit, considering our need to speak and write of the divine Persons under the image of the latitude of beings, I have prepared a great forest drawn from Cicero's writings, with which, in Ciceronian fashion, the name of the Son and of the Holy Spirit may be clothed. And that of the Son has two separate forests: one to clothe his most holy name, as Word and Wisdom; the other as the incarnate Word, that is Christ, and Christ crucified for us.","kind":"passage","sequence":42,"address":"7.42","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","text":"I say this because many of the Hebrew Cabalists have known Wisdom and the Word, but have not believed that it had become incarnate and suffered for us. Seeing which, Paul speaks a most subtle passage: “Not through the wisdom of the Word, nor is the cross of Christ emptied.” Wherefore, if that most zealous Paul had had to write the Gospel of John, he would perhaps have said: “In the beginning was Christ, and Christ was with God, and God was Christ.” Although John supplied the remedy when he said: “And the Word was made flesh.”","kind":"passage","sequence":43,"address":"7.43","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0044","text":"Under Mars there will be seven images.","kind":"passage","sequence":44,"address":"7.44","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0044"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0045","text":"Mars.","kind":"passage","sequence":45,"address":"7.45","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0045"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046","text":"Vulcan will give us the fiery crafts. A Centaur—although in the nature of things centaurs have never existed—yet, since it is read that, when horses first began to be tamed, to those who watched from afar it seemed that horse and rider were one and the same thing. Under this image we shall cover the arts pertaining to the horse, and to its","kind":"passage","sequence":46,"address":"7.46","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0047","text":"Digitized by Google","kind":"passage","sequence":47,"address":"7.47","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0047"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0048","text":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE","kind":"passage","sequence":48,"address":"7.48","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0048"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0049","text":"belonging to him: & sacred to Mars, because the horse is a\nMartial animal.","kind":"passage","sequence":49,"address":"7.49","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0049"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","text":"Two fighting serpents: shall contain the military art,\n& warfare by land & sea.","kind":"passage","sequence":50,"address":"7.50","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0051","text":"Two players of Cesti shall contain all Martial games.","kind":"passage","sequence":51,"address":"7.51","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0051"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","text":"Rhadamanthus judging souls shall have the criminal\ncourt distinguished.","kind":"passage","sequence":52,"address":"7.52","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","text":"The infernal Furies, being executors of punishments, shall con=\ntain the office of the bargello, arrest, prison, torture, punishments.","kind":"passage","sequence":53,"address":"7.53","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0054","text":"Marsyas flayed by Apollo shall give us the slaughterhouse.","kind":"passage","sequence":54,"address":"7.54","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0054"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0055","text":"Beneath the Prometheus of Jupiter there shall be five images.","kind":"passage","sequence":55,"address":"7.55","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0055"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0056","text":"Jupiter.","kind":"passage","sequence":56,"address":"7.56","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0056"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0057","text":"Juno suspended shall contain arts made for the benefit of air,\nsuch as windmills.","kind":"passage","sequence":57,"address":"7.57","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0057"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0058","text":"Europa upon the Bull signifies conversion, consent,\nhealth, annihilation, & religion.","kind":"passage","sequence":58,"address":"7.58","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0058"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0059","text":"The judgement of Paris shall have the civil court.","kind":"passage","sequence":59,"address":"7.59","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0059"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0060","text":"The sphere shall denote Astrology.","kind":"passage","sequence":60,"address":"7.60","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0060"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0061","text":"Beneath the Prometheus of Saturn there shall be five images.","kind":"passage","sequence":61,"address":"7.61","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0061"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0062","text":"Cybele shall contain Geometry, Geography, Cosmography,\n& Agriculture.","kind":"passage","sequence":62,"address":"7.62","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0062"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0063","text":"A child upon the table of the Alphabet shall give us\nGrammar.","kind":"passage","sequence":63,"address":"7.63","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0063"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0064","text":"The skin of Marsyas shall preserve the arts concerning hides,\n& skins.","kind":"passage","sequence":64,"address":"7.64","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0064"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0065","text":"A sphere shall contain bird-catching with nocturnal birds.","kind":"passage","sequence":65,"address":"7.65","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0065"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0066","text":"An ass, being a Saturnine animal, & born for labours, shall\nsignify conveyances, porters, the mill, & servants condemned to that.","kind":"passage","sequence":66,"address":"7.66","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0066"]},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0067","text":"THE END.","kind":"passage","sequence":67,"address":"7.67","source_paragraph_ids":["RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0067"]}],"source_digest":"28cc06385f363f35f629375dc3e678b8884fc34fb6af4de5f9a51b5b58f3883e","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"PROMETHEO."}],"passage_basis":"frozen-grounding","original_title":"PROMETHEO.","title_language_code":"en"}],"units":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT","layer":"CH","title":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, BY MESSER GIULIO Camillo.","order":1,"parents":["RAW_LIDT_LIDT"],"revision":"CH_LIDT_LIDT@R001","sha256":"6902728d2168cf1608d322d18441e4b4dcc0689a771097e59c6d881e566c91cc","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS1","text":"Il problema consiste nel rendere conoscibili e memorizzabili le cose senza profanare ciò che eccede la capacità del linguaggio e dell’intelletto umano.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","text":"Il sapere divino deve essere comunicato attraverso veli, immagini, visioni e similitudini, poiché il segno può indicare ciò che non può esprimere direttamente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS3","text":"La conoscenza certa delle realtà inferiori procede dall’ascesa alle loro cause superiori, fino al mondo sopraceleste da cui derivano.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS4","text":"Il Theatro traduce l’ordine eterno delle sette misure sopracelesti in un dispositivo sensibile di sette pianeti, sette colonne, sette porte e sette gradi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS5","text":"Il movimento argomentativo conduce dal divieto della rivelazione diretta alla costruzione di una memoria ordinata che conserva, orienta e riallaccia il molteplice visibile alla sua causa invisibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A1","text":"Le realtà divine eccedono l’espressione della lingua umana e sono accessibili soltanto mediante significazioni, visioni, cenni e similitudini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2","text":"La rivelazione dei misteri è legittima soltanto per soggetti resi degni da Dio e deve restare velata per non essere profanata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","text":"Le sette Saphiroth costituiscono le misure eterne nelle quali sono comprese le Idee di tutte le realtà celesti e inferiori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","text":"Le misure esplicate nella creazione sono contenute implicitamente nell’abisso della divinità da cui procedono.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A5","text":"Le realtà inferiori sono conosciute più certamente dalle loro cause superiori che dai loro effetti immediati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A6","text":"L’intelletto umano non raggiunge autonomamente la causa divina ultima, ma dipende dalla grazia, dalla rivelazione e dall’annichilimento della presunzione soggettiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","text":"I sette pianeti sono segni sensibili e accessibili delle sette misure sopracelesti, non termini ultimi della conoscenza.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8","text":"Una memoria adeguata alle cose eterne richiede luoghi stabili, distinti e ordinati secondo l’architettura eterna del cosmo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A9","text":"L’ordine della creazione dispone le realtà secondo anteriorità ontologica e temporale, dalle cose semplici alle arti e facoltà ritrovate più tardi dagli uomini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10","text":"Le immagini del Theatro sono significanti polivalenti: ciascuna connette una realtà sopraceleste, una realtà celeste, una finzione poetica e una funzione intellettuale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX1","text":"Il mistero divino non è oggetto di esposizione letterale, trasparente o pubblicamente indiscriminata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX2","text":"Il linguaggio umano non è misura sufficiente della realtà sopraceleste, poiché questa appartiene propriamente alle “lingue delli angeli”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX3","text":"La divulgazione del sacro non è innocua, perché produce insieme indegnità del destinatario e degradazione del contenuto rivelato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX4","text":"I pianeti non sono confini autosufficienti del sapere, ma mediatori che rinviano ai principii superiori da cui ricevono virtù.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX5","text":"La conoscenza delle cause non deriva dalla semplice accumulazione degli effetti visibili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX6","text":"L’accesso al sapere superiore non è conquista della virtù individuale né effetto della presunzione intellettuale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX7","text":"Il Theatro non riproduce un ordine sociale umano di dignità, poiché i suoi gradi seguono l’ordine della creazione e del tempo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX8","text":"Apollo non occupa il luogo supremo della colonna solare, perché l’immagine della divinità deve eccedere la figura mitologica del dio solare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D1","text":"La figurazione simbolica diventa la sola mediazione legittima tra l’invisibile divino e l’intelletto umano.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A1","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D2","text":"Il Theatro può presentare il sapere senza esaurirlo, poiché mostra segni che rinviano oltre la loro presenza sensibile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A1","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D3","text":"La memoria ordinata acquista funzione epistemica: il recupero delle cose coincide con la risalita dalle apparenze alle cause.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A5","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D4","text":"La disposizione settenaria del Theatro non è una convenzione mnemonica arbitraria, ma un’imitazione della struttura causale della creazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D5","text":"L’uso dei pianeti universalizza l’accesso iniziale alla struttura senza rendere universale il possesso del suo significato superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A6","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D6","text":"La progressione dai gradi inferiori alle arti finali riclassifica le discipline umane come effetti tardivi di un ordine creaturale preesistente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7","text":"La funzione di una singola immagine dipende dalla sua collocazione nell’ordine, non da un significato fisso indipendente dal luogo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD1","text":"Il Theatro trasforma l’arte della memoria in una macchina di conversione ontologica, nella quale ricordare correttamente significa reinserire ogni cosa nella sua derivazione dal divino.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A5","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD2","text":"La mediazione figurale svolge una doppia funzione strutturale: rende il sapere praticabile e contemporaneamente ne preserva l’inaccessibilità ultima.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A1","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD3","text":"Il sistema subordina astronomia, mitologia, cabala, teologia cristiana e arti umane a una sola gerarchia emanativa di origine divina.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A9","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD4","text":"Il soggetto conoscente è strutturalmente decentrato: non fonda il sapere, ma può soltanto ricevere e percorrere un ordine già disposto.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A6","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD5","text":"Il privilegio della porta solare stabilisce che la totalità dell’essere precede e domina ogni rappresentazione mitica, cosmica o disciplinare.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX1","text":"Non è vero che il sapere più alto possa essere pienamente contenuto in una proposizione, poiché il segreto permane oltre ogni dichiarazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX2","text":"Non è vero che il soggetto umano disponga di un accesso cognitivo autonomo alla realtà ultima, poiché l’ascesa dipende da grazia e rivelazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX3","text":"Non è vero che il sensibile costituisca un piano epistemico autosufficiente, poiché esso ottiene intelligibilità soltanto come traccia del sopraceleste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX4","text":"Non è vero che gli ordini mitologico, astronomico e artificiale siano piani indipendenti, poiché sono validi solo come articolazioni simboliche dell’ordine divino.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX5","text":"Non è vero che la memoria sia un deposito neutrale di contenuti, poiché la sua validità dipende dalla conformità fra luogo mnemonico e ordine cosmico.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX1","text":"È preclusa una conoscenza della divinità “facie ad faciem” posseduta e amministrata dall’intelletto umano.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX2","text":"È preclusa una comunicazione del sacro che sia insieme integralmente pubblica, letterale e non profanatrice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX3","text":"È preclusa una enciclopedia orizzontale nella quale tutte le arti, immagini e discipline possiedano pari statuto causale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX4","text":"È preclusa una separazione stabile tra dispositivo tecnico della memoria e disciplina spirituale dell’accesso al sapere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS1","text":"Eccedenza divina rispetto alla lingua umana → necessità di veli, immagini e significanti indiretti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS2","text":"Segretezza del mistero → selezione del destinatario e interdizione della divulgazione letterale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS3","text":"Emanazione della creazione nelle sette misure → fondazione di un ordine settenario universale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS4","text":"Inaccessibilità immediata delle Saphiroth → sostituzione pedagogica con i sette pianeti come segni mediatori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS5","text":"Corrispondenza tra cose eterne e luoghi eterni → costruzione del Theatro come architettura di memoria ordinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS6","text":"Collocazione gerarchica di immagini polivalenti → conservazione mnemonica, lettura causale e risalita dal visibile all’invisibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS7","text":"Limite dell’intelletto umano → chiusura del sistema nella dipendenza dalla grazia e nell’umiltà del soggetto conoscente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF1","text":"L’indicibilità del sacro → la legittimazione del velo simbolico → la condanna della rivelazione indiscriminata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF2","text":"Le sette misure sopracelesti → i pianeti come mediazione accessibile → le sette colonne e le sette salite del Theatro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF3","text":"La critica della conoscenza dagli effetti → l’ascesa alle cause superiori → la memoria come accesso ordinato alla sapienza.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF4","text":"L’ordine della creazione → la graduazione delle realtà e delle arti → la distribuzione delle immagini nelle porte planetarie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF5","text":"La pluralità di immagini, miti e saperi → la loro subordinazione a una sola architettura divina → la chiusura gerarchica del sistema.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME1","text":"La distinzione tra segno e termine diventa decisiva: pianeti, figure e miti non sono oggetti finali di sapere, ma vettori verso cause superiori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME2","text":"La memoria viene riclassificata da tecnica di conservazione contingente a dispositivo di ordinamento cosmologico e spirituale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME3","text":"Il mondo visibile diventa leggibile come superficie derivata, nella quale ogni realtà inferiore rinvia a una disposizione sopraceleste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME4","text":"Le discipline umane perdono autonomia originaria e vengono ordinate come ritrovamenti temporalmente tardi entro una genealogia della creazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME5","text":"La mitologia non viene espulsa dalla teologia, ma riconfigurata come repertorio subordinato di immagini capaci di veicolare rapporti metafisici.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT1","text":"Surface — Il testo istituisce un Theatro composto da colonne planetarie, porte, gradi, immagini e contenuti da collocare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT2","text":"Structural — Il Theatro organizza corrispondenze tra ordine sopraceleste, ordine celeste, mondo inferiore, memoria, poesia e sapere disciplinare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’argomentazione converte il problema della trasmissione del sapere in una politica del velo, nella quale il mostrare deve insieme nascondere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La realtà procede per emanazione gerarchica dal divino verso il creato e si dispone nel tempo dalle realtà semplici alle arti umane più tarde.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT5","text":"Epistemic — Il conoscere valido procede dall’alto al basso, dalle cause agli effetti, ma la sua possibilità resta dipendente da una grazia non producibile dal soggetto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT1","text":"Gli assiomi sono sufficienti per ricostruire il passaggio dalla teologia della segretezza alla macchina mnemonico-cosmologica del Theatro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT2","text":"Resta sottodeterminato il criterio operativo che stabilisce quando un’immagine conservi il velo del mistero e quando invece lo esponga impropriamente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT3","text":"La struttura è coerente se il simbolo è assunto come mediazione reale ma non esaustiva tra sensibile e sopraceleste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT4","text":"La sua maggiore forza generativa consiste nel legare una tecnica locale di memoria a un ordine totale di causalità, tempo e creazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT5","text":"Il sistema dipende dall’elisione della distanza fra corrispondenza simbolica, derivazione ontologica e validità conoscitiva.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT6","text":"Una tensione centrale permane tra l’apertura spettacolare del Theatro agli “studioſi” e la restrizione del sapere autentico ai destinatari resi degni dalla grazia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT7","text":"Un’ulteriore tensione deriva dal fatto che le immagini sono necessarie per conoscere l’invisibile ma sono anche il mezzo attraverso cui l’invisibile resta sottratto al possesso diretto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT8","text":"La ricostruzione conserva il movimento effettivo del testo se mantiene inseparabili segretezza, gerarchia cosmica, mediazione figurale, memoria ordinata e limite del soggetto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T231024651470Z_1182878c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, BY MESSER GIVLIO Camillo.","source_sha256":"6902728d2168cf1608d322d18441e4b4dcc0689a771097e59c6d881e566c91cc","sha256":"66920d67c38b3db237620794ce0e725afe1d6e86ddda3e7e10c2ca78b4aff08b","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:10:24.654341+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS1","text":"The problem consists in making things knowable and memorable without profaning that which exceeds the capacity of human language and intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","text":"Divine knowledge must be communicated through veils, images, visions, and similitudes, since the sign can indicate what it cannot express directly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS3","text":"Certain knowledge of lower realities proceeds by ascent to their higher causes, as far as the supercelestial world from which they derive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS4","text":"The Theatro translates the eternal order of the seven supercelestial measures into a sensible device of seven planets, seven columns, seven gates, and seven grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS5","text":"The argumentative movement leads from the prohibition of direct revelation to the construction of an ordered memory that preserves, guides, and reconnects the visible manifold to its invisible cause.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A1","text":"Divine realities exceed the expression of human language and are accessible only through significations, visions, signs, and similitudes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2","text":"The revelation of mysteries is legitimate only for subjects made worthy by God and must remain veiled so as not to be profaned.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","text":"The seven Saphiroth constitute the eternal measures in which the Ideas of all celestial and lower realities are comprised.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","text":"The measures unfolded in creation are implicitly contained in the abyss of divinity from which they proceed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A5","text":"Lower realities are known more certainly through their higher causes than through their immediate effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A6","text":"The human intellect does not autonomously attain the ultimate divine cause, but depends on grace, revelation, and the annihilation of subjective presumption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","text":"The seven planets are sensible and accessible signs of the seven supercelestial measures, not ultimate termini of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8","text":"A memory adequate to eternal things requires stable, distinct places ordered according to the eternal architecture of the cosmos.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A9","text":"The order of creation arranges realities according to ontological and temporal priority, from simple things to the arts and faculties discovered later by human beings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10","text":"The images of the Theatro are polyvalent signifiers: each connects a supercelestial reality, a celestial reality, a poetic fiction, and an intellectual function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX1","text":"The divine mystery is not an object of literal, transparent, or publicly indiscriminate exposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX2","text":"Human language is not a sufficient measure of supercelestial reality, since the latter properly belongs to the “lingue delli angeli”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX3","text":"The divulgation of the sacred is not innocuous, because it produces both the unworthiness of the recipient and the degradation of the revealed content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX4","text":"The planets are not self-sufficient boundaries of knowledge, but mediators that refer back to the higher principles from which they receive virtue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX5","text":"Knowledge of causes does not derive from the mere accumulation of visible effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX6","text":"Access to higher knowledge is not an achievement of individual virtue nor an effect of intellectual presumption.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX7","text":"The Theatro does not reproduce a human social order of dignity, since its grades follow the order of creation and of time.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX8","text":"Apollo does not occupy the supreme place of the solar column, because the image of divinity must exceed the mythological figure of the solar god.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D1","text":"Symbolic figuration becomes the sole legitimate mediation between the invisible divine and the human intellect.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A1","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D2","text":"The Theatro can present knowledge without exhausting it, since it shows signs that refer beyond their sensible presence.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A1","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D3","text":"Ordered memory acquires an epistemic function: the recovery of things coincides with ascent from appearances to causes.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A5","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D4","text":"The sevenfold arrangement of the Theatro is not an arbitrary mnemonic convention, but an imitation of the causal structure of creation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D5","text":"The use of planets universalizes initial access to the structure without making possession of its higher meaning universal.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A6","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D6","text":"The progression from the lower grades to the final arts reclassifies human disciplines as late effects of a pre-existing created order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7","text":"The function of a single image depends on its placement within the order, not on a fixed meaning independent of place.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD1","text":"The Theatro transforms the art of memory into a machine of ontological conversion, in which remembering correctly means reinserting each thing into its derivation from the divine.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A5","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD2","text":"Figural mediation performs a double structural function: it makes knowledge practicable and at the same time preserves its ultimate inaccessibility.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A1","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD3","text":"The system subordinates astronomy, mythology, cabala, Christian theology, and the human arts to a single emanative hierarchy of divine origin.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A9","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD4","text":"The knowing subject is structurally decentered: it does not found knowledge, but can only receive and traverse an order already arranged.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A6","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD5","text":"The privilege of the solar gate establishes that the totality of being precedes and dominates every mythic, cosmic, or disciplinary representation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX1","text":"It is not true that the highest knowledge can be fully contained in a proposition, since the secret remains beyond every declaration.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX2","text":"It is not true that the human subject possesses autonomous cognitive access to ultimate reality, since ascent depends on grace and revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX3","text":"It is not true that the sensible constitutes a self-sufficient epistemic plane, since it obtains intelligibility only as a trace of the supercelestial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX4","text":"It is not true that the mythological, astronomical, and artificial orders are independent planes, since they are valid only as symbolic articulations of the divine order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX5","text":"It is not true that memory is a neutral repository of contents, since its validity depends on the conformity between mnemonic place and cosmic order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX1","text":"A knowledge of divinity “facie ad faciem,” possessed and administered by the human intellect, is precluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX2","text":"A communication of the sacred that is at once wholly public, literal, and non-profaning is precluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX3","text":"A horizontal encyclopedia in which all arts, images, and disciplines possess equal causal status is precluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX4","text":"A stable separation between the technical device of memory and the spiritual discipline of access to knowledge is precluded.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS1","text":"Divine excess over human language → necessity of veils, images, and indirect signifiers.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS2","text":"Secrecy of the mystery → selection of the recipient and prohibition of literal divulgation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS3","text":"Emanation of creation in the seven measures → foundation of a universal sevenfold order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS4","text":"Immediate inaccessibility of the Saphiroth → pedagogical substitution with the seven planets as mediating signs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS5","text":"Correspondence between eternal things and eternal places → construction of the Theatro as an architecture of ordered memory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS6","text":"Hierarchical placement of polyvalent images → mnemonic preservation, causal reading, and ascent from the visible to the invisible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS7","text":"Limit of the human intellect → closure of the system in dependence on grace and in the humility of the knowing subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF1","text":"The ineffability of the sacred → the legitimization of the symbolic veil → the condemnation of indiscriminate revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF2","text":"The seven supercelestial measures → the planets as accessible mediation → the seven columns and the seven ascents of the Theatro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF3","text":"The critique of knowledge from effects → ascent to higher causes → memory as ordered access to wisdom.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF4","text":"The order of creation → the gradation of realities and arts → the distribution of images in the planetary gates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0038","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:AF5","text":"The plurality of images, myths, and knowledges → their subordination to a single divine architecture → the hierarchical closure of the system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME1","text":"The distinction between sign and terminus becomes decisive: planets, figures, and myths are not final objects of knowledge, but vectors toward higher causes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME2","text":"Memory is reclassified from a technique of contingent preservation into a device of cosmological and spiritual ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME3","text":"The visible world becomes legible as a derived surface, in which every lower reality refers to a supercelestial disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME4","text":"Human disciplines lose their original autonomy and are ordered as temporally late discoveries within a genealogy of creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME5","text":"Mythology is not expelled from theology, but reconfigured as a subordinate repertory of images capable of conveying metaphysical relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0045","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text establishes a Theatro composed of planetary columns, gates, grades, images, and contents to be placed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0036","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT2","text":"Structural — The Theatro organizes correspondences among supercelestial order, celestial order, the lower world, memory, poetry, and disciplinary knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The argument converts the problem of the transmission of knowledge into a politics of the veil, in which showing must at once conceal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Reality proceeds by hierarchical emanation from the divine toward the created and is arranged in time from simple realities to the later human arts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT5","text":"Epistemic — Valid knowing proceeds from above to below, from causes to effects, but its possibility remains dependent on a grace not producible by the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0030","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the transition from the theology of secrecy to the mnemonic-cosmological machine of the Theatro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0007","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT2","text":"The operative criterion that establishes when an image preserves the veil of mystery and when it instead exposes it improperly remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT3","text":"The structure is coherent if the symbol is assumed as a real but non-exhaustive mediation between the sensible and the supercelestial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT4","text":"Its greatest generative force consists in binding a local technique of memory to a total order of causality, time, and creation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT5","text":"The system depends on the elision of the distance among symbolic correspondence, ontological derivation, and cognitive validity.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0023","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0040","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT6","text":"A central tension remains between the spectacular opening of the Theatro to the “studioſi” and the restriction of authentic knowledge to recipients made worthy by grace.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT7","text":"A further tension derives from the fact that images are necessary in order to know the invisible but are also the means through which the invisible remains withdrawn from direct possession.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0012","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the text's actual movement if it keeps secrecy, cosmic hierarchy, figural mediation, ordered memory, and the limit of the subject inseparable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0027","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LIDT:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_LIDT_LIDT@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_LIDT_LIDT:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 01","title":"THE IDEA OF THE THEATRE, BY MESSER GIULIO Camillo.","context":"Chapter 01","original_title":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO, DI MESSER GIVLIO Camillo."},"original_title":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO, DI MESSER GIVLIO Camillo.","title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO","layer":"CH","title":"Il Convivio.","order":2,"parents":["RAW_LIDT_ILCO"],"revision":"CH_LIDT_ILCO@R001","sha256":"0bc1e6d0388b41142aa131379095ee61784c0a5f7ddedc600f29176377c7075b","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS1","text":"Il convito omerico viene convertito da finzione poetica in figura dell’acqua sapienziale e della convocazione delle Idee divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS2","text":"La cosmogonia viene fondata sulla distinzione fra la produzione interna, eterna e coessenziale del Verbo, e la produzione esterna, temporale e non coessenziale della materia prima.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS3","text":"La generazione viene riformulata come manifestazione di vita latente e la corruzione come suo occultamento, sotto l’azione dello spirito vivificante che concilia i contrari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS4","text":"Le Idee, i numeri, i pesi e le misure vengono collocati nella mente divina come esemplari anteriori alle cose create e causa della permanenza delle specie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS5","text":"L’ordine metafisico viene tradotto in una macchina mnemonico-enciclopedica nella quale immagini, porte, pianeti e luoghi teatrali rendono recuperabili i gradi della realtà.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS6","text":"La distribuzione planetaria organizza in un solo sistema gli elementi, le arti, le favole, le anime, i luoghi ultraterreni e le operazioni naturali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","text":"Dio è principio di una produzione interna e di una produzione esterna.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","text":"Il Verbo costituisce la produzione interna, eterna, senza principio e coessenziale a Dio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","text":"La materia prima costituisce la produzione esterna, creata nel tempo, non coessenziale e capace di ricevere le forme.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","text":"Il Gamone viene ridotto alla triade Artifex, Exemplar e Hyle, nella quale la generazione è conseguenza e non principio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","text":"Le Idee sono nell’eterna mente divina e precedono le cose create come loro forme esemplari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6","text":"La generazione è esplicazione del vivente nascosto e la corruzione è occultamento, non annientamento della vita.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","text":"Lo spirito vivificante di Cristo rende conciliabili i contrari e rende possibile la produzione delle forme nella materia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A8","text":"L’umore e il calore sono inseparabili e la loro unione costituisce la condizione della generazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9","text":"Numero, peso e misura non sono prodotti insieme alle cose numerate, pesate e misurate, ma sussistono in Dio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","text":"Il sensibile manifesta la sapienza divina soltanto attraverso ombre, panni, effetti e immagini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11","text":"Le immagini teatrali sono dispositivi semantici che collegano un principio, un volume dottrinale, un dominio naturale, un’azione e un’arte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX1","text":"La materia prima non è coessenziale, coeterna o autosussistente come il Verbo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX2","text":"Il primo atto della Genesi non designa il cielo e la terra già formati, ma la massa dalla quale essi devono essere formati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX3","text":"La semplicità divina non esclude la pluralità delle Idee e dei loro effetti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX4","text":"Generazione e corruzione non sono rispettivamente creazione assoluta e morte assoluta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX5","text":"Il calore e l’umore celesti non coincidono univocamente con il calore, l’umidità e il fuoco terrestri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX6","text":"Gli universali non procedono soltanto a posteriori dagli individui, come sostengono i Peripatetici criticati dal testo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX7","text":"Il convito degli dèi non è assunto come avvenimento mitologico autonomo, poiché Oceano significa sapienza e gli dèi invitati significano Idee.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX8","text":"Il Purgatorio marziale non coincide con l’Inferno saturnino, poiché la pena del primo è temporale e quella del secondo è eterna.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D1","text":"La mutazione degli individui non compromette la permanenza delle specie, poiché le specie perseverano nelle Idee divine.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D2","text":"La materia non può produrre da sé l’unità dei contrari, poiché richiede lo spirito vivificante come principio di conciliazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D3","text":"L’ordine creato riceve la propria intelligibilità da un esemplare divino che precede la materia e ne determina le forme possibili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D4","text":"L’ordine sensibile può essere conosciuto soltanto come impronta, segno o immagine di principi che non si esauriscono nella percezione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D5","text":"Un’immagine teatrale può distribuire simultaneamente un’essenza, le sue manifestazioni naturali, le sue azioni pratiche e le arti che la impiegano.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D6","text":"La degradazione progressiva della materia prima rende possibile una temporalità escatologica culminante nel giudizio universale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD1","text":"Il sistema istituisce una catena discendente da Dio al Verbo, dal Verbo alle Idee, dalle Idee alle specie, dalle specie agli individui e dagli individui alle immagini teatrali.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2","text":"Il teatro rende possibile il movimento inverso dall’immagine sensibile verso il principio metafisico che l’immagine conserva e nasconde.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD3","text":"Le fonti platoniche, pitagoriche, ermetiche e poetiche sono mantenute come repertori di segni, ma vengono ordinate sotto la causalità cristologica del Verbo e dello spirito di Cristo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD4","text":"La permanenza appartiene agli esemplari e alle specie, mentre il deterioramento appartiene alla materia e agli individui che essa sostiene.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX1","text":"Non esiste un principio materiale concorrente con Dio, poiché la materia è derivata, temporale e incapace di autosostituirsi allo spirito vivificante.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX2","text":"Non esiste una molteplicità che obblighi a moltiplicare i principi primi, poiché il semplice divino può contenere Idee ed effetti molteplici.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX3","text":"Il sensibile non possiede criteri propri e autosufficienti di intelligibilità, poiché la sua forma, misura e permanenza dipendono da modelli anteriori.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX4","text":"Il mito non costituisce una sfera di verità indipendente, poiché le sue figure devono essere risolte nei loro corrispettivi teologici, cosmologici e morali.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX5","text":"L’individuo caduco non può essere il portatore ultimo dell’essere, poiché la sua stabilità ontologica appartiene alla specie e all’Idea.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX1","text":"È precluso un universo di enti finiti pienamente autonomi, perché l’essere creato resta dipendente dall’esemplare, dalla misura e dalla conciliazione spirituale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX2","text":"È preclusa una presenza immediata della sapienza divina al sapere sensibile, perché il visibile offre soltanto ombre, panni, impronte e figure.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX3","text":"È precluso un archivio neutrale di cose e immagini, perché ogni collocazione teatrale deriva il proprio senso da una gerarchia ontologica verticale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS1","text":"La produzione interna del Verbo genera l’Exemplar eterno, mentre la produzione esterna fornisce la Hyle temporale capace di ricevere forma.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS2","text":"Lo spirito vivificante entra nella materia, concilia i contrari, unisce calore e umore e trasforma la potenza materiale in manifestazione formale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS3","text":"Le Idee divine imprimono specie nelle cose create, mentre numero, peso e misura ne regolano l’ordine senza confondersi con gli oggetti ordinati.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS4","text":"Il principio invisibile viene assegnato a un pianeta, condensato in un’immagine, distribuito nei luoghi del teatro e riaperto come dottrina, azione naturale e arte.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF1","text":"La finzione del convito omerico viene convertita nell’enigma che apre la distinzione fra le due produzioni divine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF2","text":"La distinzione delle produzioni conduce alla ridefinizione della materia prima come massa informe, acquosa e non coessenziale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF3","text":"La materia informe conduce alla riformulazione della generazione come manifestazione e alla necessità dello spirito conciliatore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF4","text":"La causalità spirituale conduce alla dottrina delle Idee, delle specie eterne e delle misure divine anteriori al sensibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF5","text":"La dottrina degli esemplari invisibili conduce alla loro codifica planetaria mediante immagini, porte, arti, elementi e luoghi ultraterreni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME1","text":"Il racconto della creazione viene riclassificato come passaggio dalla materia informe alle forme, non come apparizione immediata di enti già compiuti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME2","text":"Il mutamento viene riclassificato come alternanza di manifestazione e occultamento, anziché come successione di essere e non-essere assoluti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME3","text":"L’universale viene riclassificato da astrazione posteriore a esemplare divino anteriore che garantisce la permanenza delle specie.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME4","text":"La favola, l’elemento, l’arte, la religione e l’escatologia vengono riclassificati come registri diversi di uno stesso ordine di corrispondenze.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME5","text":"Il teatro viene riclassificato da sede di rappresentazione a macchina di risalita interpretativa dal segno sensibile al suo principio invisibile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT1","text":"Surface — Le porte del secondo grado presentano immagini planetarie che designano acqua, fuoco, aria, terra, favole, anime, paradisi, purgatorio e inferno.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT2","text":"Structural — La realtà è ordinata dalla sequenza Dio, Verbo, Idee, spirito, materia, forme, specie, individui e loro manifestazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — L’interpretazione valida deve convertire il dato poetico, naturale e sensibile in accesso mediato a un ordine esemplare superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’eternità appartiene al Verbo, alle Idee e alle specie, mentre la temporalità, l’alterazione, il deterioramento e il giudizio appartengono all’ordine materiale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT1","text":"Gli assiomi estratti sono sufficienti a ricostruire il passaggio dalla teologia della produzione alla classificazione teatrale delle immagini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT2","text":"La distribuzione concreta delle immagini fra i pianeti resta parzialmente sottodeterminata, poiché il testo espone le assegnazioni ma non fornisce una regola unica capace di dedurle tutte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT3","text":"La struttura è coerente finché ogni livello inferiore è trattato come impronta, manifestazione o veicolo di un principio superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT4","text":"Il punto di massima forza strutturale è la conversione dell’ontologia emanativa in un meccanismo di memoria che rende leggibile il passaggio fra metafisica, natura e arte.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT5","text":"Il sistema dipende da una compressione che assimila fonti bibliche, platoniche, pitagoriche, ermetiche e poetiche senza formalizzare un criterio generale di arbitraggio fra esse.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT6","text":"Rimane una tensione fra la ridefinizione della corruzione come occultamento della vita e la rappresentazione della materia come sostanza che si deteriora fino al giudizio universale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT7","text":"Rimane una tensione fra l’inaccessibilità del calore e dell’umore celesti al tatto umano e il loro uso come analoghi ordinatori dell’esperienza naturale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A8","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT8","text":"La ricostruzione preserva il movimento effettivo del testo se mantiene inseparabili la gerarchia causale, la semantica delle immagini e la funzione classificatoria del teatro.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T230850272665Z_1dd514ec","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE BANQUET.","source_sha256":"0bc1e6d0388b41142aa131379095ee61784c0a5f7ddedc600f29176377c7075b","sha256":"0520e0e0ca5a9b12dbcda69576804efaaa5a53abb112985b7e43eadec53377c2","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:08:50.275892+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS1","text":"The Homeric banquet is converted from poetic fiction into a figure of sapiential water and of the convocation of divine Ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS2","text":"Cosmogony is grounded in the distinction between the internal, eternal, and coessential production of the Word, and the external, temporal, and non-coessential production of prime matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS3","text":"Generation is reformulated as the manifestation of latent life and corruption as its concealment, under the action of the life-giving spirit that reconciles contraries.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS4","text":"Ideas, numbers, weights, and measures are placed in the divine mind as exemplars prior to created things and as the cause of the permanence of species.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS5","text":"The metaphysical order is translated into a mnemonic-encyclopedic machine in which images, gates, planets, and theatrical places render the degrees of reality retrievable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS6","text":"The planetary distribution organizes into a single system the elements, arts, fables, souls, supraterrestrial places, and natural operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","text":"God is the principle of an internal production and an external production.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","text":"The Word constitutes the internal, eternal production, without beginning and coessential with God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","text":"Prime matter constitutes the external production, created in time, non-coessential, and capable of receiving forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","text":"The Gamone is reduced to the triad Artifex, Exemplar, and Hyle, in which generation is a consequence and not a principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","text":"Ideas are in the eternal divine mind and precede created things as their exemplary forms.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6","text":"Generation is the explication of hidden life and corruption is concealment, not annihilation of life.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","text":"The life-giving spirit of Christ renders contraries reconcilable and makes possible the production of forms in matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A8","text":"Moisture and heat are inseparable, and their union constitutes the condition of generation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9","text":"Number, weight, and measure are not produced together with numbered, weighed, and measured things, but subsist in God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0059","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","text":"The sensible manifests divine wisdom only through shadows, veils, effects, and images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11","text":"Theatrical images are semantic devices that connect a principle, a doctrinal volume, a natural domain, an action, and an art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX1","text":"Prime matter is not coessential, coeternal, or self-subsisting like the Word.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX2","text":"The first act of Genesis does not designate heaven and earth already formed, but the mass from which they must be formed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX3","text":"Divine simplicity does not exclude the plurality of Ideas and their effects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX4","text":"Generation and corruption are not, respectively, absolute creation and absolute death.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX5","text":"Celestial heat and moisture do not coincide univocally with terrestrial heat, moisture, and fire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX6","text":"Universals do not proceed solely a posteriori from individuals, as maintained by the Peripatetics criticized by the text.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX7","text":"The banquet of the gods is not taken as an autonomous mythological event, since Ocean signifies wisdom and the invited gods signify Ideas.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX8","text":"Martial Purgatory does not coincide with Saturnian Hell, since the punishment of the former is temporal and that of the latter eternal.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D1","text":"The mutation of individuals does not compromise the permanence of species, since species persevere in divine Ideas.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D2","text":"Matter cannot produce the unity of contraries by itself, since it requires the life-giving spirit as a principle of reconciliation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D3","text":"The created order receives its intelligibility from a divine exemplar that precedes matter and determines its possible forms.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D4","text":"The sensible order can be known only as an imprint, sign, or image of principles that are not exhausted in perception.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D5","text":"A theatrical image can simultaneously distribute an essence, its natural manifestations, its practical actions, and the arts that employ it.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:D6","text":"The progressive degradation of prime matter makes possible an eschatological temporality culminating in the universal judgment.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD1","text":"The system establishes a descending chain from God to the Word, from the Word to Ideas, from Ideas to species, from species to individuals, and from individuals to theatrical images.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2","text":"The theater makes possible the inverse movement from the sensible image toward the metaphysical principle that the image preserves and conceals.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD3","text":"Platonic, Pythagorean, Hermetic, and poetic sources are retained as repertories of signs, but are ordered under the Christological causality of the Word and the spirit of Christ.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0028","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD4","text":"Permanence belongs to exemplars and species, whereas deterioration belongs to matter and the individuals it sustains.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX1","text":"There is no material principle competing with God, since matter is derived, temporal, and incapable of replacing the life-giving spirit by itself.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX2","text":"There is no multiplicity that compels the multiplication of first principles, since the divine simple can contain multiple Ideas and effects.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX3","text":"The sensible does not possess its own self-sufficient criteria of intelligibility, since its form, measure, and permanence depend on prior models.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX4","text":"Myth does not constitute an independent sphere of truth, since its figures must be resolved into their theological, cosmological, and moral counterparts.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX5","text":"The perishable individual cannot be the ultimate bearer of being, since its ontological stability belongs to the species and the Idea.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX1","text":"A universe of fully autonomous finite entities is precluded, because created being remains dependent on the exemplar, measure, and spiritual reconciliation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX2","text":"An immediate presence of divine wisdom to sensible knowledge is precluded, because the visible offers only shadows, veils, imprints, and figures.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX3","text":"A neutral archive of things and images is precluded, because every theatrical placement derives its meaning from a vertical ontological hierarchy.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS1","text":"The internal production of the Word generates the eternal Exemplar, whereas external production provides the temporal Hyle capable of receiving form.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS2","text":"The life-giving spirit enters matter, reconciles contraries, joins heat and moisture, and transforms material potency into formal manifestation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS3","text":"Divine Ideas imprint species upon created things, whereas number, weight, and measure regulate their order without being confused with the ordered objects.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS4","text":"The invisible principle is assigned to a planet, condensed into an image, distributed among the places of the theater, and reopened as doctrine, natural action, and art.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0069","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0071","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0072","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF1","text":"The fiction of the Homeric banquet is converted into the enigma that opens the distinction between the two divine productions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF2","text":"The distinction of productions leads to the redefinition of prime matter as an unformed, aqueous, and non-coessential mass.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF3","text":"Unformed matter leads to the reformulation of generation as manifestation and to the necessity of the reconciling spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0033","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF4","text":"Spiritual causality leads to the doctrine of Ideas, eternal species, and divine measures prior to the sensible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0061","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF5","text":"The doctrine of invisible exemplars leads to their planetary codification by means of images, gates, arts, elements, and supraterrestrial places.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME1","text":"The account of creation is reclassified as a passage from unformed matter to forms, not as the immediate appearance of entities already complete.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0041","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME2","text":"Change is reclassified as an alternation of manifestation and concealment, rather than as a succession of absolute being and non-being.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME3","text":"The universal is reclassified from a posterior abstraction to a prior divine exemplar that guarantees the permanence of species.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME4","text":"Fable, element, art, religion, and eschatology are reclassified as different registers of one and the same order of correspondences.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME5","text":"The theater is reclassified from a site of representation into a machine of interpretive ascent from the sensible sign to its invisible principle.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT1","text":"Surface — The gates of the second degree present planetary images that designate water, fire, air, earth, fables, souls, paradises, purgatory, and hell.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0077","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0079","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0083","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0091","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0092","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT2","text":"Structural — Reality is ordered by the sequence God, Word, Ideas, spirit, matter, forms, species, individuals, and their manifestations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Valid interpretation must convert poetic, natural, and sensible data into mediated access to a higher exemplary order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0055","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Eternity belongs to the Word, Ideas, and species, whereas temporality, alteration, deterioration, and judgment belong to the material order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage from the theology of production to the theatrical classification of images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT2","text":"The concrete distribution of images among the planets remains partially underdetermined, since the text sets forth the assignments but does not provide a single rule capable of deducing them all.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT3","text":"The structure is coherent insofar as every lower level is treated as an imprint, manifestation, or vehicle of a higher principle.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT4","text":"The point of greatest structural strength is the conversion of emanative ontology into a mechanism of memory that renders legible the passage between metaphysics, nature, and art.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT5","text":"The system depends on a compression that assimilates biblical, Platonic, Pythagorean, Hermetic, and poetic sources without formalizing a general criterion for adjudication among them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT6","text":"A tension remains between the redefinition of corruption as the concealment of life and the representation of matter as a substance that deteriorates until the universal judgment.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0015","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT7","text":"A tension remains between the inaccessibility of celestial heat and moisture to human touch and their use as ordering analogues of natural experience.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A8","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0052","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the effective movement of the text if it keeps inseparable the causal hierarchy, the semantics of images, and the classificatory function of the theater.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0035","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0067","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0070","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ILCO:P0074","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_LIDT_ILCO@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_LIDT_ILCO:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 02","title":"Il Convivio.","context":"Chapter 02"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT","layer":"CH","title":"L’Antro.","order":3,"parents":["RAW_LIDT_LANT"],"revision":"CH_LIDT_LANT@R001","sha256":"5db837eaed1ad3143eb0a842e893f01abb88a29db353649dfb619a24ba44333b","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS1","text":"La molteplicità delle cose miste ed elementate deve essere ordinata senza moltiplicare indefinitamente le immagini necessarie alla memoria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS2","text":"Il terzo grado del Teatro assegna ogni cosa mista a uno dei sette Antri planetari secondo la natura cui essa appartiene.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS3","text":"La classificazione è fondata sulla derivazione di tutte le forme naturali da un’unica materia prima sottoposta a influssi sopracelesti mediati dalla massa celeste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS4","text":"Le immagini mitiche vengono convertite in contenitori tassonomici, ciascuno associato a un volume internamente articolato per divisioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS5","text":"Il significato di un’immagine dipende dalla sua posizione e viene trasposto dalla cosa naturale alla natura umana, all’operazione non artificiale e infine all’arte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS6","text":"La stabilità dei misti viene ricondotta allo Spirito vivificante di Cristo, che concilia i contrari e lega la materia alla forma fino alla dissoluzione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS7","text":"Il procedimento avanza dalla cosmologia creazionale alla ripartizione planetaria, quindi alla codificazione combinatoria e infine alla chiusura cristologica del sistema naturale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","text":"Il terzo grado dell’Antro ha per oggetto le cose miste ed elementate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","text":"La materia prima è l’unica materia creata, mentre tutte le cose successive sono sue formazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","text":"La Rachia media l’influsso sopraceleste affinché esso non ecceda la capacità della materia inferiore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A4","text":"Nel mondo inferiore nessun elemento naturale sussiste in purezza, ma ogni elemento è mescolato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","text":"L’uomo, formato separatamente e posto sopra i misti, richiede un grado distinto dall’Antro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","text":"Le sette nature planetarie, ricevute dalle corrispondenti Saphiroth sopracelesti, ripartiscono le classi delle cose inferiori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","text":"Ogni immagine simbolica conserva un volume concettuale articolato per generi, specie, parti, qualità, quantità, accidenti o relazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","text":"Il significato dell’immagine è determinato dalla collocazione, così che una stessa figura può essere riutilizzata senza identità di contenuto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","text":"L’Antro traduce la categoria simbolica in cosa naturale mista o elementata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","text":"Pasiphe traduce la categoria simbolica in natura, corpo, stato o disposizione dell’uomo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","text":"I Talari traducono la categoria simbolica in operazione umana naturale e non artificiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A12","text":"Prometheo traduce la categoria simbolica in arte, scienza, tecnica o istituzione artificiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","text":"Il mondo è vivente e mobile perché gli influssi celesti comunicano vita e fecondità agli elementi inferiori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","text":"Lo Spirito di Cristo concilia le qualità contrarie, genera, nutre, vivifica e rinnova i composti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","text":"Ogni individuo misto lega entro i propri termini una porzione di materia prima e lo spirito vivificante fino alla dissoluzione della forma.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A16","text":"La morte del composto è risoluzione della mistura e non annientamento di ciò che è.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX1","text":"L’Antro del terzo grado non è l’antro platonico della Repubblica, ma l’Antro Homerico delle tessiture e dei fabricamenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX2","text":"La Rachia non è il firmamento, identificato invece con l’ottava sfera.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX3","text":"Il cielo cristallino posto sopra il firmamento è respinto come costruzione priva di fondamento scritturale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX4","text":"Dopo la materia prima non viene creata alcuna nuova materia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX5","text":"Gli elementi del mondo inferiore non sono empiricamente puri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX6","text":"L’uomo non appartiene al catalogo naturale dell’Antro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX7","text":"Le operazioni dei Talari non sono arti, poiché le arti appartengono a Prometheo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX8","text":"Una figura ricorrente non conserva necessariamente lo stesso significato in porte o gradi differenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX9","text":"Le favole relative agli dèi non devono essere assunte letteralmente come narrazioni di conflitti divini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX10","text":"Il Proteo legato dell’Antro saturnino designa una legatura naturale e non la legatura magica di Aristeo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX11","text":"Il principio vivificante non è l’anima del mondo intesa platonicamente come causa autonoma, ma lo Spirito di Cristo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX12","text":"La dissoluzione del composto non è morte intesa come cessazione assoluta dell’essere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D1","text":"L’ordine causale del cosmo viene convertito direttamente in ordine della memoria.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D2","text":"La variazione posizionale consente di ridurre il numero delle immagini senza ridurre il numero delle categorie rappresentabili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D3","text":"Ogni categoria può essere trasformata secondo quattro registri coordinati: cosa naturale, determinazione umana, operazione non artificiale e arte.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D4","text":"L’Antro ordina composti concreti, qualità e accidenti anziché essenze elementari isolate.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A4","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D5","text":"L’esclusione dell’uomo dal terzo grado non interrompe il sistema, ma prepara la trasposizione antropologica e operativa delle categorie naturali.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D6","text":"La porta planetaria funziona simultaneamente come indice mnemonico e come dichiarazione della causa o affinità cosmica della categoria.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D7","text":"Il volume associato all’immagine può espandersi senza nuove immagini mediante successive divisioni tassonomiche.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D8","text":"L’individuo possiede una stabilità formale temporanea, mentre materia e principio vivificante eccedono la durata della singola composizione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1","text":"Il Teatro costituisce un’interfaccia isomorfa fra causalità cosmica, tassonomia concettuale e recupero mnemonico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2","text":"Un inventario finito di immagini genera una copertura estesa del sapere mediante la combinazione di figura, porta planetaria e grado operativo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD3","text":"La cristologia fornisce la chiusura causale della fisica dei misti, poiché rende possibile la coesistenza delle qualità contrarie che la classificazione presuppone.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD4","text":"L’uomo è ontologicamente distinto dalle cose dell’Antro ma operativamente dipendente da esse, perché le assume come materia di azione, arte e istituzione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD5","text":"Dopo la creazione della materia prima, la novità naturale consiste in formazione, mistura, rinnovazione e ricomposizione, non in nuova creazione materiale o annientamento.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD6","text":"Il sistema incorpora anche ciò che resta nascosto, non ancora saputo o non rivelabile, trasformando l’assenza di conoscenza in una posizione classificata.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX1","text":"La materia inferiore non può formarsi, vivificarsi o sostenersi autonomamente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX2","text":"Non esiste nel Teatro un segno semanticamente autosufficiente e indipendente dalla propria collocazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX3","text":"La natura inferiore non costituisce un ordine causalmente chiuso rispetto al sopraceleste.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX4","text":"L’uomo non è riducibile a un elemento interno della serie dei misti, benché il suo corpo e le sue operazioni ne riprendano le categorie.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX5","text":"Cosmologia, antropologia, operazione e arte non formano inventari indipendenti, ma trasformazioni coordinate di una medesima matrice.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX1","text":"L’inclassificabile assoluto è escluso, poiché ogni cosa mista deve poter ricevere una sede planetaria e un contenitore figurale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX2","text":"Un mondo inferiore autosufficiente è impossibile, perché la sua generazione e conservazione dipendono da una mediazione discendente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX3","text":"La morte assoluta è preclusa: può cessare l’unione individuale, non la continuità della materia e del principio vivificante.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4","text":"La trasparenza totale del sapere è preclusa, perché il sistema conserva luoghi per gli scibili non ancora saputi e per segreti rivelabili soltanto a tempo e con volontà divina.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS1","text":"La catena ontologica è: materia prima → mediazione della Rachia → influsso sopraceleste → informazione e mistura → cosa elementata.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS2","text":"La catena classificatoria è: cosa mista → affinità planetaria → porta dell’Antro → immagine simbolica → volume → divisioni tassonomiche.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS3","text":"La trasduzione verticale è: categoria naturale → disposizione umana → operazione non artificiale → arte o istituzione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS4","text":"La compressione mnemonica è: figura ricorrente + nuova collocazione → nuova funzione semantica senza nuova immagine.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS5","text":"La chiusura dinamica è: Spirito vivificante → conciliazione dei contrari → legatura individuale → nutrizione e rinnovazione → dissoluzione → nuova disponibilità della materia.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AF1","text":"Molteplicità dei misti → fondazione creazionale → esclusione dell’uomo → ripartizione planetaria → assegnazione delle immagini → articolazione dei volumi → chiusura cristologica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AF2","text":"Favola o figura → estrazione del significato → giustificazione planetaria → delimitazione della categoria → trasposizione sotto Pasiphe, Talari e Prometheo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AF3","text":"Stabilità apparente del composto → Proteo legato → mediazione vivificante → permanenza individuale temporanea → dissoluzione non annientante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1","text":"I pianeti cessano di essere soltanto corpi celesti e diventano coordinate generali per l’ordinamento del sapere naturale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME2","text":"Il mito viene riclassificato da narrazione a operatore di indicizzazione concettuale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME3","text":"La collocazione spaziale diventa una componente costitutiva del significato.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4","text":"Cosa naturale, natura umana, azione e arte diventano registri trasformativi di un’unica categoria invece di domini separati.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME5","text":"Il terreno empirico della natura viene riclassificato come dominio di misture, forme e accidenti, non di elementi puri.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A4","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME6","text":"La morte viene riclassificata da cessazione dell’essere a dissoluzione di una configurazione materiale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME7","text":"La funzione cosmologica dell’anima del mondo viene subordinata o sostituita dallo Spirito di Cristo come principio effettivamente vivificante.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME8","text":"Il tempo viene pluralizzato in regime solare misurabile, regime lunare della mutazione e regime saturnino del passato, presente e futuro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0144","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT1","text":"Surface — Il capitolo assegna immagini, categorie e volumi ai sette Antri planetari del terzo grado.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT2","text":"Structural — Il sistema opera come matrice composta da porta planetaria, immagine, volume, divisione interna e registro di trasposizione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — La variazione posizionale e la suddivisione dei volumi riducono il carico mnemonico rendendo produttivamente riutilizzabile ogni figura.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — La realtà consiste in materia unica, influsso discendente, composizione temporanea, vivificazione cristologica, rinnovazione e dissoluzione non annientante.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT1","text":"Gli assiomi estratti sono sufficienti a ricostruire la funzione dell’Antro, la matrice planetaria e la trasposizione fra natura, uomo, operazione e arte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT2","text":"Restano sottodeterminate le assegnazioni locali di ogni immagine, le suddivisioni complete dei singoli volumi e alcuni segmenti testuali illeggibili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT3","text":"La struttura è coerente finché la posizione viene accettata come principio semantico e la corrispondenza planetaria come principio causale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT4","text":"Il sistema è più forte nella reiterazione della grammatica Antro–Pasiphe–Talari–Prometheo e nella distinzione fra immagine e significato posizionale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT5","text":"La giustificazione delle singole corrispondenze dipende da un montaggio di autorità scritturali, mitiche, aristoteliche, platoniche, ermetiche e cabalistiche non ridotto a una sola procedura dimostrativa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT6","text":"Permane una tensione fra la pretesa necessità cosmica delle assegnazioni e il loro carattere talvolta dichiaratamente pragmatico, convenzionale o imposto dal bisogno mnemonico.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7","text":"La pretesa di copertura universale coesiste con scibili non ancora saputi e con segreti che il testo dichiara indisponibili alla rivelazione presente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT8","text":"L’anima del mondo è respinta come fonte autonoma della vita, ma riappare funzionalmente come veicolo riempito e mosso dallo Spirito di Cristo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT9","text":"La ricostruzione conserva il movimento effettivo dal fondamento cosmologico alla macchina tassonomico-mnemonica e da questa alla spiegazione della stabilità e dissoluzione dei misti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T230934116222Z_acfef28d","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE CAVE.","source_sha256":"5db837eaed1ad3143eb0a842e893f01abb88a29db353649dfb619a24ba44333b","sha256":"5a537b5ff582adf62819d620a6fd2eb754eefbd3b7fae8a24065f3a779fd48ca","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:09:34.119621+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS1","text":"The multiplicity of mixed and elemental things must be ordered without indefinitely multiplying the images necessary for memory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS2","text":"The third degree of the Theatre assigns every mixed thing to one of the seven planetary Caves according to the nature to which it belongs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS3","text":"The classification is founded on the derivation of all natural forms from a single prime matter subjected to supracelestial influences mediated by the celestial mass.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS4","text":"Mythic images are converted into taxonomic containers, each associated with a volume internally articulated by divisions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS5","text":"The meaning of an image depends on its position and is transposed from the natural thing to human nature, to non-artificial operation, and finally to art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS6","text":"The stability of mixed things is traced back to the life-giving Spirit of Christ, which reconciles contraries and binds matter to form until dissolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AS7","text":"The procedure advances from creational cosmology to planetary distribution, then to combinatorial codification, and finally to the Christological closure of the natural system.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","text":"The third degree of the Cave has mixed and elemental things as its object.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","text":"Prime matter is the only created matter, whereas all subsequent things are its formations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","text":"The Rachia mediates supracelestial influence so that it does not exceed the capacity of lower matter.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A4","text":"In the lower world no natural element subsists in purity, but every element is mixed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","text":"Man, formed separately and placed above mixed things, requires a degree distinct from the Cave.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","text":"The seven planetary natures, received from the corresponding supracelestial Saphiroth, distribute the classes of lower things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","text":"Every symbolic image retains a conceptual volume articulated by genera, species, parts, qualities, quantities, accidents, or relations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","text":"The meaning of the image is determined by placement, so that the same figure can be reused without identity of content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","text":"The Cave translates the symbolic category into a mixed or elemental natural thing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","text":"Pasiphe translates the symbolic category into man's nature, body, state, or disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0071","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","text":"The Talari translate the symbolic category into natural and non-artificial human operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A12","text":"Prometheo translates the symbolic category into art, science, technique, or artificial institution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0054","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0094","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","text":"The world is living and mobile because celestial influences communicate life and fecundity to the lower elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0076","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","text":"The Spirit of Christ reconciles contrary qualities, generates, nourishes, vivifies, and renews compounds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","text":"Every mixed individual binds within its own limits a portion of prime matter and the life-giving spirit until the dissolution of form.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:A16","text":"The death of the compound is the resolution of the mixture and not the annihilation of what is.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX1","text":"The Cave of the third degree is not the Platonic cave of the Republic, but the Homeric Cave of weavings and fabrications.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX2","text":"The Rachia is not the firmament, which is instead identified with the eighth sphere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX3","text":"The crystalline heaven placed above the firmament is rejected as a construction lacking scriptural foundation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX4","text":"After prime matter, no new matter is created.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX5","text":"The elements of the lower world are not empirically pure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX6","text":"Man does not belong to the natural catalogue of the Cave.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX7","text":"The operations of the Talari are not arts, since the arts belong to Prometheo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0016","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX8","text":"A recurring figure does not necessarily retain the same meaning in different doors or degrees.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX9","text":"Fables concerning the gods must not be taken literally as narratives of divine conflicts.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX10","text":"The bound Proteus of the Saturnine Cave designates a natural binding and not the magical binding of Aristeo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX11","text":"The life-giving principle is not the soul of the world understood Platonically as an autonomous cause, but the Spirit of Christ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:NX12","text":"The dissolution of the compound is not death understood as the absolute cessation of being.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D1","text":"The causal order of the cosmos is directly converted into an order of memory.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D2","text":"Positional variation makes it possible to reduce the number of images without reducing the number of representable categories.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D3","text":"Every category can be transformed according to four coordinated registers: natural thing, human determination, non-artificial operation, and art.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D4","text":"The Cave orders concrete compounds, qualities, and accidents rather than isolated elemental essences.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A4","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D5","text":"The exclusion of man from the third degree does not interrupt the system, but prepares the anthropological and operative transposition of natural categories.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D6","text":"The planetary door functions simultaneously as a mnemonic index and as a declaration of the cosmic cause or affinity of the category.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D7","text":"The volume associated with the image can expand without new images through successive taxonomic divisions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:D8","text":"The individual possesses temporary formal stability, whereas matter and the life-giving principle exceed the duration of the single composition.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1","text":"The Theatre constitutes an isomorphic interface between cosmic causality, conceptual taxonomy, and mnemonic retrieval.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2","text":"A finite inventory of images generates extended coverage of knowledge through the combination of figure, planetary door, and operative degree.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD3","text":"Christology provides the causal closure of the physics of mixed things, since it makes possible the coexistence of contrary qualities presupposed by classification.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD4","text":"Man is ontologically distinct from the things of the Cave but operationally dependent on them, because he takes them up as the matter of action, art, and institution.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD5","text":"After the creation of prime matter, natural novelty consists in formation, mixture, renewal, and recomposition, not in new material creation or annihilation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SD6","text":"The system also incorporates what remains hidden, not yet known, or unrevealable, transforming the absence of knowledge into a classified position.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX1","text":"Lower matter cannot form, vivify itself, or sustain itself autonomously.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX2","text":"There exists in the Theatre no semantically self-sufficient sign independent of its own placement.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX3","text":"Lower nature does not constitute a causally closed order with respect to the supracelestial.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX4","text":"Man is not reducible to an internal element of the series of mixed things, although his body and his operations reproduce their categories.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX5","text":"Cosmology, anthropology, operation, and art do not form independent inventories, but coordinated transformations of one and the same matrix.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX1","text":"The absolute unclassifiable is excluded, since every mixed thing must be able to receive a planetary seat and a figural container.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX2","text":"A self-sufficient lower world is impossible, because its generation and preservation depend on a descending mediation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX3","text":"Absolute death is precluded: individual union may cease, but not the continuity of matter and of the life-giving principle.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4","text":"The total transparency of knowledge is precluded, because the system preserves places for knowables not yet known and for secrets revealable only in time and by divine will.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS1","text":"The ontological chain is: prime matter → mediation of the Rachia → supracelestial influence → information and mixture → elemental thing.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS2","text":"The classificatory chain is: mixed thing → planetary affinity → door of the Cave → symbolic image → volume → taxonomic divisions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS3","text":"The vertical transduction is: natural category → human disposition → non-artificial operation → art or institution.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS4","text":"Mnemonic compression is: recurring figure + new placement → new semantic function without new image.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS5","text":"The dynamic closure is: life-giving Spirit → reconciliation of contraries → individual binding → nourishment and renewal → dissolution → renewed availability of matter.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0165","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AF1","text":"Multiplicity of mixed things → creational foundation → exclusion of man → planetary distribution → assignment of images → articulation of volumes → Christological closure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AF2","text":"Fable or figure → extraction of meaning → planetary justification → delimitation of category → transposition under Pasiphe, Talari, and Prometheo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:AF3","text":"Apparent stability of the compound → bound Proteus → life-giving mediation → temporary individual permanence → non-annihilating dissolution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1","text":"The planets cease to be merely celestial bodies and become general coordinates for the ordering of natural knowledge.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME2","text":"Myth is reclassified from narrative into an operator of conceptual indexing.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME3","text":"Spatial placement becomes a constitutive component of meaning.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4","text":"Natural thing, human nature, action, and art become transformative registers of a single category instead of separate domains.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME5","text":"The empirical terrain of nature is reclassified as a domain of mixtures, forms, and accidents, not of pure elements.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A4","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME6","text":"Death is reclassified from cessation of being into the dissolution of a material configuration.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME7","text":"The cosmological function of the soul of the world is subordinated or replaced by the Spirit of Christ as the effectively life-giving principle.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A13","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ME8","text":"Time is pluralized into a measurable solar regime, a lunar regime of mutation, and a Saturnine regime of past, present, and future.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0083","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0143","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0144","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT1","text":"Surface — The chapter assigns images, categories, and volumes to the seven planetary Caves of the third degree.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A1","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT2","text":"Structural — The system operates as a matrix composed of planetary door, image, volume, internal division, and register of transposition.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:A9","CH_LIDT_LANT:A10","CH_LIDT_LANT:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Positional variation and the subdivision of volumes reduce the mnemonic burden by making every figure productively reusable.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Reality consists in single matter, descending influence, temporary composition, Christological vivification, renewal, and non-annihilating dissolution.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14","CH_LIDT_LANT:A15","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0172","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the function of the Cave, the planetary matrix, and the transposition between nature, man, operation, and art.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT2","text":"The local assignments of each image, the complete subdivisions of individual volumes, and some illegible textual segments remain underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0136","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT3","text":"The structure is coherent so long as position is accepted as a semantic principle and planetary correspondence as a causal principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT4","text":"The system is stronger in the reiteration of the Cave–Pasiphe–Talari–Prometheo grammar and in the distinction between image and positional meaning.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0063","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0064","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"low","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT5","text":"The justification of individual correspondences depends on an assemblage of scriptural, mythic, Aristotelian, Platonic, Hermetic, and Kabbalistic authorities not reduced to a single demonstrative procedure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0095","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0103","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT6","text":"A tension remains between the claimed cosmic necessity of the assignments and their character, at times explicitly declared, as pragmatic, conventional, or imposed by mnemonic need.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0041","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0114","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7","text":"The claim to universal coverage coexists with knowables not yet known and with secrets that the text declares unavailable to present revelation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0033","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0156","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT8","text":"The soul of the world is rejected as an autonomous source of life, but functionally reappears as a vehicle filled and moved by the Spirit of Christ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0167","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT9","text":"The reconstruction preserves the effective movement from cosmological foundation to the taxonomic-mnemonic machine and from this to the explanation of the stability and dissolution of mixed things.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0163","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0171","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LANT:P0175","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_LIDT_LANT@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_LIDT_LANT:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 03","title":"L’Antro.","context":"Chapter 03"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO","layer":"CH","title":"Le Gorgoni,","order":4,"parents":["RAW_LIDT_LEGO"],"revision":"CH_LIDT_LEGO@R001","sha256":"7afd803a972890c88eb101b72cffac04c287824402ab35659cb8879c84d5aad6","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS1","text":"Il quarto grado deve rendere intelligibile l’uomo interiore come immagine divina, distinguendolo dal corpo senza separarlo dalla sua funzione mondana.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS2","text":"La tesi centrale identifica il principio propriamente intellettuale con un’illuminazione divina esterna, ricevibile ma non posseduta autonomamente dall’uomo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS3","text":"Il procedimento è esegetico, concordistico e ricostruttivo: Scrittura, Cabala, filosofia e mito vengono correlati come formulazioni convergenti di una stessa antropologia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS4","text":"L’argomentazione procede dalla creazione e dalla caduta alla tripartizione dell’anima, quindi alla tripartizione dell’intelletto e all’esteriorità del principio illuminante.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS5","text":"Il simbolo delle tre Gorgoni trasforma la dottrina in una struttura visibile: tre potenze cieche dipendono da un unico occhio esterno e comunicabile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS6","text":"L’ordine planetario distribuisce infine le facoltà dell’uomo interiore in immagini capaci di occultare, indicizzare e riattivare mnemonicamene la dottrina.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","text":"Nel lessico dominante della Scrittura, l’uomo propriamente detto è l’uomo interiore, non il corpo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","text":"Immagine e somiglianza designano l’elevazione angelico-divina dell’uomo, sebbene le autorità citate le articolino come due gradi, un solo grado o una destinazione operativa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","text":"Le opere buone appartengono causalmente a Dio, mentre l’uomo ne è lo strumento.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","text":"Il corpo terrestre è formato affinché l’uomo interiore possa operare nel mondo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","text":"La condizione adamitica originaria consiste insieme nella partecipazione agli influssi sopracelesti e nell’integrità della terra virginale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6","text":"Il peccato produce la sottrazione degli influssi divini e la contrazione della macchia nella terra e negli elementi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","text":"L’uomo interiore comprende tre anime distinte: Nephes, Ruach e Nessamah.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","text":"La Nephes è la potenza inferiore, comune alle bestie, prossima al corpo e ricettacolo delle passioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","text":"La Ruach è l’anima razionale intermedia, esposta alle sollecitazioni dei poli inferiore e superiore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","text":"La Nessamah è la parte divina e impeccabile dell’anima, associata alla mente superiore, all’angelo e all’intelletto agente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","text":"L’unione della Ruach con la Nephes o con la Nessamah determina l’assimilazione dell’intero composto al polo inferiore o superiore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","text":"La separazione della Ruach dalla Nephes e la sua unione con la Nessamah dipendono dalla grazia e dalla parola di Cristo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","text":"L’intellezione comprende una capacità possibile, un intendere pratico e un principio agente che rende possibile l’atto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","text":"La soluzione infine preferita, attribuita a Simplicio e confermata mediante la Scrittura, colloca l’intelletto agente fuori dell’uomo come raggio divino, angelo o Dio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15","text":"L’uomo si distingue dalle bestie perché è capace di ricevere l’intelletto agente, non perché lo possieda necessariamente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","text":"La dottrina chiaramente esposta deve essere ricoperta da favole per impedirne la profanazione e sostenerne la memoria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","text":"Le tre Gorgoni cieche e il loro unico occhio esterno simbolizzano la triplicità interiore dipendente da una sola illuminazione comunicabile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18","text":"Le porte planetarie distribuiscono le facoltà, gli stati e i movimenti dell’uomo interiore in immagini ordinate.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX1","text":"L’uomo non coincide con il corpo che usa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX2","text":"Le opere buone non sono proprietà autonoma del soggetto umano.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX3","text":"La cacciata dal paradiso non è riducibile a uno spostamento corporeo fuori da un giardino terrestre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX4","text":"L’anima non è una sostanza interiormente indifferenziata designabile senza residui da un unico nome.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX5","text":"L’intelletto agente non è un possesso stabile e autosufficiente dell’individuo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX6","text":"L’appartenenza alla figura umana non garantisce la differenza interiore dalla bestia.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX7","text":"La Nessamah non è soggetta al peccato né alla pena.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX8","text":"La volontà umana non può procurarsi da sola l’illuminazione o l’ascesa spirituale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX9","text":"La favola non è ornamento arbitrario né finzione priva di contenuto dottrinale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX10","text":"La spiritualizzazione non può avvenire lasciando immutato il radicamento corporeo negli affetti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D1","text":"Le letture concorrenti di immagine e somiglianza convergono sull’eccedenza divina dell’uomo, ma non risolvono se tale eccedenza sia ontologica, unitaria o operativa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D2","text":"Il corpo rende possibile l’operazione mondana dell’uomo interiore senza conferirgli l’autorialità ultima delle opere.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D3","text":"La cacciata dal paradiso sopraceleste equivale alla perdita della grazia, mentre la cacciata dal paradiso terrestre equivale alla perdita della verginità cosmica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D4","text":"Il corpo verginale di Cristo ricapitola la materialità incorrotta di Adamo e rende possibile la purgazione della macchia introdotta dalla caduta.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","text":"L’unione della Ruach con la Nephes genera la catena Ruach–Nephes–carne–demonio e culmina nella trasmutazione inferiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D6","text":"La grazia separa la Ruach dalla Nephes, la unisce alla Nessamah e genera la catena ascendente Ruach–Nessamah–angelo–Dio.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D7","text":"La triplicità aristotelica non aggiunge tre anime, ma articola entro il livello superiore la capacità di intendere, l’atto d’intendere e il principio che fa intendere.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","text":"L’umanità intellettuale è uno stato contingente di illuminazione: senza il raggio agente resta la forma umana, ma viene meno la differenza interiore dalla bestia.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D9","text":"L’occhio condiviso delle Gorgoni codifica simultaneamente l’esteriorità dell’intelletto agente e la possibile unificazione delle tre anime mediante un’unica luce.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D10","text":"Le immagini di Luna, Mercurio e Venere classificano rispettivamente oblio e ignoranza, intelletto possibile e docilità, volontà e affetti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D11","text":"Le immagini del Sole, di Marte e di Giove classificano rispettivamente intelletto agente, deliberazione ferma, elezione, giudizio e consiglio.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D12","text":"L’immagine saturnina di Ercole e Anteo converte il conflitto tra spirito e corpo nella necessità di recidere la forza terrestre degli affetti e trasformare il corpo nello spirito.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","text":"Le immagini planetarie funzionano come indici di volumi nei quali vengono ordinate memoria, scienza, opinione, intelletto pratico, pensiero, immaginazione e contemplazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","text":"Il soggetto umano non è una sostanza chiusa, ma un dispositivo ricettivo la cui identità dipende dal polo con cui entra in unione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD2","text":"Conoscenza, conversione morale e salvezza condividono la medesima struttura: ricezione di una luce esterna, separazione dal polo inferiore e riallineamento ascendente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD3","text":"Bestialità, diabolicità, angelicità e divinizzazione operano come esiti dinamici dell’allineamento umano, non soltanto come classi ontologiche separate.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","text":"Il Theatro rende isomorfi antropologia, cosmologia e memoria, perché le gerarchie dell’anima vengono ordinate mediante porte planetarie e immagini mitiche.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD5","text":"Caduta e redenzione sono strutturate come modificazioni della partecipazione: la prima sottrae l’influsso superiore e intensifica il legame terrestre, la seconda ripristina l’orientamento ascendente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX1","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea di un soggetto umano autosufficiente, proprietario delle proprie opere e della propria luce intellettuale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX2","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea che la ragione naturale basti a produrre l’intellezione superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX3","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea che uomo, bestia, angelo e demonio siano identità interiori assolutamente impermeabili alla trasformazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX4","text":"Deve essere insufficiente ogni lettura meramente letterale del paradiso, del corpo, delle favole e delle immagini cosmiche.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX5","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea che la verità profonda possa restare indiscriminatamente pubblica senza degradarsi in profanazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX6","text":"Deve essere falsa l’incommensurabilità radicale tra Scrittura, Cabala, platonismo, aristotelismo e mito, poiché il sistema dipende dalla loro traducibilità reciproca.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX1","text":"L’assenza terminale attorno a cui ruota il sistema è quella di un occhio intellettuale posseduto stabilmente dall’uomo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX2","text":"La possibilità preclusa è l’autoredensione: nessuna capacità, volontà o deliberazione umana può sostituire il dono della grazia e dell’intelletto agente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX3","text":"L’assenza temporale che struttura caduta e desiderio di ritorno è la perduta integrità adamitica, insieme sopraceleste e terrestre.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX4","text":"È esclusa una conciliazione stabile tra ascesa spirituale e permanenza incontestata del corpo sotto il dominio degli affetti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX5","text":"È esclusa una verità simultaneamente profonda, totalmente scoperta e immune dalla profanazione; il simbolo occupa precisamente questa impossibilità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS1","text":"Immagine e somiglianza divina → costituzione dell’uomo interiore → formazione del corpo strumentale → operazione nel mondo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS2","text":"Partecipazione adamitica → peccato → sottrazione degli influssi e macchia cosmica → duplice espulsione dal paradiso.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS3","text":"Nephes inferiore + Nessamah superiore → Ruach intermedia → necessità di un orientamento decisivo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS4","text":"Unione con la Nephes → carne e demonio → trasmutazione inferiore; separazione dalla Nephes → unione con la Nessamah → trasmutazione superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS5","text":"Potenza d’intendere → intendere pratico → intelletto agente esterno → umanità intellettuale condizionata dal dono divino.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS6","text":"Esposizione dottrinale → ricopertura favolosa → protezione dalla profanazione → riattivazione mnemonica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS7","text":"Triplicità interiore + illuminazione esterna → simbolo delle Gorgoni → distribuzione planetaria → indicizzazione delle facoltà.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","text":"Recisione degli affetti terrestri → morte simbolica del corpo → trasformazione spirituale → ascesa dell’anima.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF1","text":"Immagine e somiglianza → eccedenza angelico-divina → definizione dell’uomo interiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF2","text":"Uomo interiore → corpo strumentale → stato adamitico → caduta come perdita d’influsso e integrità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF3","text":"Tripartizione dell’anima → centralità della Ruach → biforcazione tra assimilazione inferiore e superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF4","text":"Tripartizione dell’intelletto → distinzione del principio agente → esteriorità del raggio divino → umanità condizionale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF5","text":"Esteriorità della luce → occhio condiviso delle Gorgoni → copertura simbolica della dottrina.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF6","text":"Gorgoni → sette articolazioni planetarie → classificazione delle facoltà → mortificazione degli affetti → ascesa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME1","text":"L’uomo viene riclassificato da composto corporeo autosufficiente a struttura interiore che usa il corpo e riceve dall’esterno il proprio compimento intellettuale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME2","text":"La razionalità cessa di essere un possesso naturale garantito e diventa un evento revocabile di illuminazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME3","text":"Il paradiso viene riclassificato da luogo esclusivamente geografico a stato di partecipazione sopraceleste e integrità cosmica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME4","text":"Le facoltà dell’anima vengono riclassificate da inventario statico a sistema direzionale nel quale la potenza intermedia può essere catturata dal basso o attratta dall’alto.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME5","text":"Il mito viene riclassificato da racconto profano a dispositivo di occultamento, memoria e trasmissione dottrinale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME6","text":"I pianeti cessano di essere soltanto oggetti cosmologici e diventano coordinate classificatorie delle operazioni interiori.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","text":"Il corpo assume una doppia posizione: è lo strumento necessario dell’operazione divina e, quando resta radicato negli affetti, il principale vincolo dell’ascesa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT1","text":"Sul piano di superficie, il capitolo assegna al quarto grado del Theatro le Gorgoni e le immagini subordinate alle sette porte planetarie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT2","text":"Sul piano strutturale, il capitolo costruisce un apparato tripartito dell’anima e dell’intelletto governato da mediazione, illuminazione e conflitto tra carne e spirito.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT3","text":"Sul piano metastrategico, la dottrina viene convertita in simboli che ne regolano accesso, memorizzazione e ordinamento.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT4","text":"Sul piano ontologico e temporale, l’uomo è una realtà pre-corporea poi incarnata, caduta per sottrazione d’influsso e capace di trasformazione soltanto mediante un principio superiore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT1","text":"Gli assiomi estratti sono sufficienti a ricostruire la sequenza fondamentale: uomo interiore, caduta, tripartizione, illuminazione esterna, simbolo gorgonico e ordinamento planetario.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT2","text":"Resta sottodeterminato se Celem e Demut designino due gradi distinti, un solo grado divino o una relazione operativa tra Dio e l’uomo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT3","text":"La Nessamah è presentata come una delle anime presenti nell’uomo e insieme assimilata a un intelletto agente collocato fuori dell’uomo; la distinzione tra presenza, partecipazione e fonte non viene pienamente formalizzata.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT4","text":"La classificazione della volontà come libera e non libera resta in tensione con la dipendenza dell’ascesa dalla grazia, dalla permissione divina e dall’operatività di Dio.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT5","text":"Il simbolo deve simultaneamente nascondere la dottrina e renderla memorabile, lasciando irrisolta la soglia precisa tra protezione, rivelazione e accessibilità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT6","text":"La deliberazione marziale viene distinta dall’atto subito, ma è esemplificata mediante la deliberazione insieme subita e ferma di Didone.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT7","text":"La massima forza generativa risiede nell’occhio esterno delle Gorgoni, che unifica antropologia, teoria dell’intelletto, trasformazione spirituale e tecnica mnemonica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT8","text":"La ricostruzione preserva il movimento effettivo del testo, ma la sua coerenza dipende dalla compressione analogica di autorità eterogenee e dall’equivalenza non dimostrata tra categorie cabalistiche, cristiane, platoniche e aristoteliche.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T231000786151Z_3e30c8b2","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"THE GORGONS,","source_sha256":"7afd803a972890c88eb101b72cffac04c287824402ab35659cb8879c84d5aad6","sha256":"0ec02160a9d7e7790b40a7835dcf78387aba9e9d8ba6426ff6c795584079f4c9","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:10:00.789423+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS1","text":"The fourth degree must render the inner man intelligible as a divine image, distinguishing him from the body without separating him from his worldly function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS2","text":"The central thesis identifies the properly intellectual principle with an external divine illumination, receivable but not autonomously possessed by man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS3","text":"The procedure is exegetical, concordist, and reconstructive: Scripture, Kabbalah, philosophy, and myth are correlated as convergent formulations of the same anthropology.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS4","text":"The argument proceeds from creation and the fall to the tripartition of the soul, then to the tripartition of the intellect and the exteriority of the illuminating principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS5","text":"The symbol of the three Gorgons transforms the doctrine into a visible structure: three blind powers depend on a single external and communicable eye.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS6","text":"The planetary order finally distributes the faculties of the inner man into images capable of concealing, indexing, and mnemonically reactivating the doctrine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","text":"In the dominant lexicon of Scripture, man properly so called is the inner man, not the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","text":"Image and likeness designate the angelic-divine elevation of man, although the cited authorities articulate them as two degrees, a single degree, or an operative destination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","text":"Good works belong causally to God, while man is their instrument.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","text":"The terrestrial body is formed so that the inner man may operate in the world.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","text":"The original Adamic condition consists both in participation in supracelestial influences and in the integrity of the virginal earth.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6","text":"Sin produces the withdrawal of divine influences and the contraction of stain in the earth and the elements.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","text":"The inner man comprises three distinct souls: Nephes, Ruach, and Nessamah.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","text":"Nephes is the lower power, common to beasts, close to the body and the receptacle of passions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","text":"Ruach is the intermediate rational soul, exposed to the solicitations of the lower and higher poles.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","text":"Nessamah is the divine and impeccable part of the soul, associated with the higher mind, the angel, and the agent intellect.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","text":"The union of Ruach with Nephes or with Nessamah determines the assimilation of the entire composite to the lower or higher pole.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","text":"The separation of Ruach from Nephes and its union with Nessamah depend on the grace and word of Christ.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","text":"Intellection comprises a possible capacity, a practical understanding, and an agent principle that makes the act possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0033","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","text":"The solution ultimately preferred, attributed to Simplicius and confirmed through Scripture, places the agent intellect outside man as a divine ray, angel, or God.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15","text":"Man is distinguished from beasts because he is capable of receiving the agent intellect, not because he necessarily possesses it.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","text":"Clearly expounded doctrine must be covered over with fables in order to prevent its profanation and sustain its memory.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","text":"The three blind Gorgons and their single external eye symbolize the inner triplicity dependent upon a single communicable illumination.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18","text":"The planetary gates distribute the faculties, states, and movements of the inner man into ordered images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX1","text":"Man does not coincide with the body that he uses.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX2","text":"Good works are not the autonomous property of the human subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX3","text":"Expulsion from paradise is not reducible to a bodily displacement outside a terrestrial garden.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX4","text":"The soul is not an inwardly undifferentiated substance designable without remainder by a single name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX5","text":"The agent intellect is not a stable and self-sufficient possession of the individual.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX6","text":"Belonging to the human form does not guarantee an inner difference from the beast.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX7","text":"Nessamah is subject neither to sin nor to punishment.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX8","text":"The human will cannot by itself procure illumination or spiritual ascent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX9","text":"The fable is neither arbitrary ornament nor a fiction devoid of doctrinal content.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX10","text":"Spiritualization cannot occur while leaving unchanged the bodily rootedness in the affections.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D1","text":"The competing readings of image and likeness converge on man's divine excess, but do not resolve whether this excess is ontological, unitary, or operative.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D2","text":"The body makes possible the worldly operation of the inner man without conferring on him the ultimate authorship of works.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D3","text":"Expulsion from the supracelestial paradise is equivalent to the loss of grace, whereas expulsion from the terrestrial paradise is equivalent to the loss of cosmic virginity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D4","text":"The virginal body of Christ recapitulates Adam's incorrupt materiality and makes possible the purgation of the stain introduced by the fall.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","text":"The union of Ruach with Nephes generates the chain Ruach–Nephes–flesh–demon and culminates in lower transmutation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D6","text":"Grace separates Ruach from Nephes, unites it with Nessamah, and generates the ascending chain Ruach–Nessamah–angel–God.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D7","text":"The Aristotelian triplicity does not add three souls, but articulates within the higher level the capacity to understand, the act of understanding, and the principle that causes understanding.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","text":"Intellectual humanity is a contingent state of illumination: without the agent ray, the human form remains, but the inner difference from the beast fails.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D9","text":"The shared eye of the Gorgons simultaneously encodes the exteriority of the agent intellect and the possible unification of the three souls through a single light.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D10","text":"The images of the Moon, Mercury, and Venus classify respectively oblivion and ignorance, possible intellect and docility, will and affections.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D11","text":"The images of the Sun, Mars, and Jupiter classify respectively agent intellect, firm deliberation, choice, judgment, and counsel.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0073","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D12","text":"The Saturnine image of Hercules and Antaeus converts the conflict between spirit and body into the necessity of severing the terrestrial force of the affections and transforming the body into spirit.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","text":"The planetary images function as indices of volumes in which memory, science, opinion, practical intellect, thought, imagination, and contemplation are ordered.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0055","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","text":"The human subject is not a closed substance, but a receptive apparatus whose identity depends on the pole with which it enters into union.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD2","text":"Knowledge, moral conversion, and salvation share the same structure: reception of an external light, separation from the lower pole, and ascending realignment.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD3","text":"Bestiality, diabolicity, angelicity, and divinization operate as dynamic outcomes of human alignment, not merely as separate ontological classes.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","text":"The Theatro renders anthropology, cosmology, and memory isomorphic, because the hierarchies of the soul are ordered through planetary gates and mythical images.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD5","text":"Fall and redemption are structured as modifications of participation: the former withdraws the higher influence and intensifies the terrestrial bond, the latter restores the ascending orientation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX1","text":"The idea of a self-sufficient human subject, proprietor of its own works and its own intellectual light, must be false.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX2","text":"The idea that natural reason suffices to produce higher intellection must be false.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX3","text":"The idea that man, beast, angel, and demon are inner identities absolutely impermeable to transformation must be false.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX4","text":"Every merely literal reading of paradise, the body, fables, and cosmic images must be insufficient.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX5","text":"The idea that profound truth can remain indiscriminately public without degrading into profanation must be false.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX6","text":"The radical incommensurability of Scripture, Kabbalah, Platonism, Aristotelianism, and myth must be false, since the system depends on their reciprocal translatability.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX1","text":"The terminal absence around which the system revolves is that of an intellectual eye stably possessed by man.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX2","text":"The precluded possibility is self-redemption: no human capacity, will, or deliberation can replace the gift of grace and the agent intellect.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0044","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX3","text":"The temporal absence structuring the fall and the desire to return is lost Adamic integrity, at once supracelestial and terrestrial.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX4","text":"A stable reconciliation between spiritual ascent and the uncontested persistence of the body under the dominion of the affections is excluded.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX5","text":"A truth simultaneously profound, wholly uncovered, and immune from profanation is excluded; the symbol precisely occupies this impossibility.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS1","text":"Divine image and likeness → constitution of the inner man → formation of the instrumental body → operation in the world.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS2","text":"Adamic participation → sin → withdrawal of influences and cosmic stain → twofold expulsion from paradise.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS3","text":"Lower Nephes + higher Nessamah → intermediate Ruach → necessity of a decisive orientation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS4","text":"Union with Nephes → flesh and demon → lower transmutation; separation from Nephes → union with Nessamah → higher transmutation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS5","text":"Capacity to understand → practical understanding → external agent intellect → intellectual humanity conditioned by the divine gift.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS6","text":"Doctrinal exposition → fabulous covering → protection from profanation → mnemonic reactivation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS7","text":"Inner triplicity + external illumination → symbol of the Gorgons → planetary distribution → indexing of faculties.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","text":"Severance of terrestrial affections → symbolic death of the body → spiritual transformation → ascent of the soul.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF1","text":"Image and likeness → angelic-divine excess → definition of the inner man.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF2","text":"Inner man → instrumental body → Adamic state → fall as loss of influence and integrity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF3","text":"Tripartition of the soul → centrality of Ruach → bifurcation between lower and higher assimilation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A9","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF4","text":"Tripartition of the intellect → distinction of the agent principle → exteriority of the divine ray → conditional humanity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF5","text":"Exteriority of light → shared eye of the Gorgons → symbolic covering of doctrine.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:AF6","text":"Gorgons → seven planetary articulations → classification of faculties → mortification of the affections → ascent.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME1","text":"Man is reclassified from a self-sufficient bodily composite to an inner structure that uses the body and receives from without its own intellectual fulfillment.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME2","text":"Rationality ceases to be a guaranteed natural possession and becomes a revocable event of illumination.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A15"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME3","text":"Paradise is reclassified from an exclusively geographical place to a state of supracelestial participation and cosmic integrity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0018","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME4","text":"The faculties of the soul are reclassified from a static inventory to a directional system in which the intermediate power may be captured from below or drawn from above.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME5","text":"Myth is reclassified from a profane tale to a device of concealment, memory, and doctrinal transmission.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME6","text":"The planets cease to be merely cosmological objects and become classificatory coordinates of inner operations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","text":"The body assumes a double position: it is the necessary instrument of divine operation and, when it remains rooted in the affections, the principal constraint upon ascent.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A8","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT1","text":"At the surface level, the chapter assigns to the fourth degree of the Theatro the Gorgons and the images subordinate to the seven planetary gates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0056","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0065","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0067","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0072","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0074","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT2","text":"At the structural level, the chapter constructs a tripartite apparatus of soul and intellect governed by mediation, illumination, and conflict between flesh and spirit.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0077","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT3","text":"At the metastrategic level, doctrine is converted into symbols that regulate its access, memorization, and ordering.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0081","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT4","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, man is a pre-corporeal reality subsequently incarnated, fallen through withdrawal of influence and capable of transformation only through a higher principle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0009","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT1","text":"The extracted axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the fundamental sequence: inner man, fall, tripartition, external illumination, Gorgonic symbol, and planetary ordering.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A6","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0014","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT2","text":"It remains underdetermined whether Celem and Demut designate two distinct degrees, a single divine degree, or an operative relation between God and man.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT3","text":"Nessamah is presented as one of the souls present in man and at the same time assimilated to an agent intellect situated outside man; the distinction between presence, participation, and source is not fully formalized.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT4","text":"The classification of the will as free and unfree remains in tension with the dependence of ascent on grace, divine permission, and the operation of God.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0007","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0025","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0062","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT5","text":"The symbol must simultaneously conceal doctrine and render it memorable, leaving unresolved the precise threshold between protection, revelation, and accessibility.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0047","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT6","text":"Martial deliberation is distinguished from the immediate act, but is exemplified through Dido's deliberation, at once undergone and firm.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0070","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT7","text":"The greatest generative force resides in the external eye of the Gorgons, which unifies anthropology, theory of intellect, spiritual transformation, and mnemonic technique.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0037","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0078","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the effective movement of the text, but its coherence depends on the analogical compression of heterogeneous authorities and on the unproven equivalence among Kabbalistic, Christian, Platonic, and Aristotelian categories.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A10","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0003","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_LEGO:P0048","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_LIDT_LEGO@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_LIDT_LEGO:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 04","title":"Le Gorgoni,","context":"Chapter 04"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI","layer":"CH","title":"Pasiphe","order":5,"parents":["RAW_LIDT_PASI"],"revision":"CH_LIDT_PASI@R001","sha256":"7535fcbe22d0e7f94e4515b18fb9071db99cbd7d841ac55656575c4893cb06ed","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS1","text":"Il testo risolve il problema della congiunzione fra anima sottile e corpo grossolano mediante la postulazione di un veicolo aereo intermedio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS2","text":"La favola di Pasiphe viene riformulata come teologia simbolica della caduta dell’anima nella cupidità del corpo e della mediazione che rende possibile tale caduta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS3","text":"Il quinto grado del Theatro trasforma la mediazione anima-corpo in un sistema di collocazione mnemonica per affetti, disposizioni, funzioni corporee e condizioni umane.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS4","text":"La pluralità delle immagini planetarie scompone l’uomo in corrispondenze fra natura morale, parte corporea, influsso astrale e figura mitica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS5","text":"Il Minotauro istituisce il discrimine fra inclinazione bestiale ancora non esercitata, vizio attuato e virtù come distruzione o conversione della disposizione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS6","text":"Il movimento procede da cosmologia della discesa → allegorizzazione mitica → tassonomia planetaria dell’umano → distinzione operativa fra disposizione, esercizio, morte e ricongiunzione celeste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A1","text":"Ogni movimento dell’anima richiede un corpo o veicolo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A2","text":"L’anima ignea e il corpo terreno non possono congiungersi immediatamente perché la loro differenza di sottigliezza e grossezza esige un termine medio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","text":"La discesa dell’anima attraverso cieli ed elementi produce un veicolo aereo capace di partecipare della natura dell’anima e del corpo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A4","text":"La teologia simbolica custodisce in forma favolosa una filosofia alta che non deve essere esposta senza velamento.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A5","text":"Pasiphe significa l’anima che cade nella cupidità del corpo, mentre la vacca finta significa il corpo aereo mediatore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A6","text":"Il Minotauro è il prodotto della copula fra anima desiderante, mediazione aerea e corporeità bestiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","text":"Il quinto grado del Theatro raccoglie ciò che appartiene all’uomo non soltanto interiore ma ancora rivestito di esteriorità corporea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A8","text":"Le immagini planetarie ordinano le qualità umane, le condizioni di vita, le passioni e le membra secondo corrispondenze astrologiche.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A9","text":"La parte concupiscibile, comune all’uomo e alle bestie, può ridurre l’uomo a bestia quando viene compiaciuta e non partecipa del raggio divino.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","text":"L’inclinazione al vizio o al bene non coincide con il suo esercizio, che è assegnato al grado successivo dei Talari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A11","text":"La virtù esiste propriamente nelle azioni e non nella sola definizione, conoscenza o disposizione ad agire bene.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A12","text":"Il corpo separa l’anima dalla vera unione con le realtà celesti, e la morte ne rende possibile la dissoluzione liberatrice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A13","text":"L’ambizione indomita costituisce un idolo interno che deve essere ucciso perché si produca umiltà e disposizione al bene.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX1","text":"L’anima non è un principio motore pienamente disincarnato, poiché il movimento richiede un veicolo corporeo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX2","text":"La congiunzione fra anima e corpo non è immediata, naturale né possibile senza mediazione aerea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX3","text":"La favola non è assunta come racconto letterale, ma come involucro di una struttura filosofico-teologica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX4","text":"Il quinto grado non riguarda l’uomo puramente interiore, poiché registra ciò che resta avvolto nell’esteriorità e nelle membra.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX5","text":"La forma umana non garantisce la partecipazione al divino, poiché il vizioso può conservare figura umana e risultare bestiale nella parte inferiore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX6","text":"L’inclinazione non è vizio esercitato, né disposizione al bene è virtù attuosa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX7","text":"La conoscenza della definizione della virtù non è possesso della virtù.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX8","text":"L’idolatria non consiste soltanto nell’adorazione di dèi esterni, poiché la forma più grave è la divinizzazione interna di castità, sapere, potere o ambizione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX9","text":"La morte non è soltanto cessazione biologica, poiché viene configurata come condizione della ricongiunzione dell’anima con il celeste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D1","text":"Il corpo aereo acquisisce una funzione ambivalente: rende possibile l’incarnazione dell’anima e conserva, dopo la morte terrena, il residuo che impedisce la piena liberazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A2","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D2","text":"La narrazione di Pasiphe traduce una necessità cosmologica in una genealogia morale della cupidità e della mostruosità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4","CH_LIDT_PASI:A5","CH_LIDT_PASI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D3","text":"Il Minotauro funziona come segno reversibile: vivo designa il vizio o la disposizione bestiale, ucciso designa l’inclinazione alla virtù.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A6","CH_LIDT_PASI:A9","CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D4","text":"Il sistema planetario non descrive un uomo unitario, ma distribuisce le sue proprietà in serie eterogenee di membra, passioni, sorti, attitudini e relazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D5","text":"Il giudizio morale viene spostato dall’aspetto esterno e dalla dichiarazione interiore all’uso effettivo delle facoltà inferiori e alle azioni che ne seguono.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A9","CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D6","text":"L’umiltà non è una virtù autosufficiente ma l’effetto della distruzione dell’idolo interiore dell’ambizione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A11","CH_LIDT_PASI:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D7","text":"La morte integra la tassonomia del quinto grado come fatto corporeo e, simultaneamente, oltrepassa tale grado come scioglimento della prigionia corporea.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1","text":"Il Theatro converte una cosmologia verticale della discesa e dell’ascesa in una macchina classificatoria orizzontale capace di archiviare l’intero composto umano.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4","CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2","text":"La corporeità è insieme condizione indispensabile del movimento dell’anima, sede della sua caduta e ostacolo terminale alla sua unione superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A1","CH_LIDT_PASI:A2","CH_LIDT_PASI:A5","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD3","text":"La distinzione fra disposizione ed esercizio introduce una temporalità morale: nessuna natura è pienamente classificabile come virtù o vizio prima dell’atto che la realizza.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A9","CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD4","text":"L’ordine astrologico organizza il materiale umano senza eliminare il problema della responsabilità, poiché la disposizione planetaria deve ancora essere convertita, esercitata o repressa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A8","CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11","CH_LIDT_PASI:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD5","text":"Il dispositivo simbolico lega antropologia, morale, fisiologia, politica domestica e destino in una sola grammatica di immagini.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A4","CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX1","text":"Deve essere falsa l’autosufficienza dell’anima pura, poiché anima, movimento e incarnazione dipendono da una serie di supporti veicolari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX2","text":"Deve essere falsa l’identità immediata dell’uomo con la propria figura razionale, poiché la sua parte desiderante può renderlo strutturalmente bestiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX3","text":"Deve essere falsa l’equivalenza fra sapere morale e vita virtuosa, poiché la virtù richiede attualizzazione nelle opere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX4","text":"Deve essere falsa l’esteriorità dell’idolatria, poiché il nemico decisivo viene insediato nell’immaginazione e nell’ambizione del soggetto.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX5","text":"Deve essere falsa la pienezza del corpo mortale, poiché il corpo viene pensato come carcere e come separazione dalla vera unione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX1","text":"L’unità immediata fra spirituale e corporeo è indisponibile: ogni passaggio richiede degradazione, mediazione e residuo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX2","text":"La vera unione con il celeste è preclusa alla persistenza integrale del corpo vivente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX3","text":"Non esiste innocenza garantita dalla natura umana, perché la forma dell’uomo può coprire una vita dominata dalla parte bestiale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX4","text":"Non esiste un bene spirituale non esposto alla trasformazione in idolo interno quando viene assunto come oggetto di autoesaltazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS1","text":"Differenza ontologica anima ignea / corpo terreno → impossibilità della copula immediata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS2","text":"Impossibilità della copula immediata → produzione del veicolo aereo come medio partecipante di entrambi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS3","text":"Mediazione aerea + desiderio dell’anima per il corpo → allegoria di Pasiphe e generazione del Minotauro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS4","text":"Allegoria velata → traduzione in immagini mnemoniche del quinto grado.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS5","text":"Ordine planetario + zodiaco + corpo umano → distribuzione di membra, affetti, stati, qualità e destini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS6","text":"Parte concupiscibile + adesione alle passioni → bestializzazione e vizio potenziale o attuato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS7","text":"Distruzione dell’idolo interno o del Minotauro → umiltà e inclinazione alla virtù.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS8","text":"Inclinazione buona + esercizio nei Talari → virtù attuosa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9","text":"Dissoluzione del corpo e del residuo veicolare → possibilità della riunione dell’anima con il celeste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF1","text":"Movimento dell’anima → necessità di un veicolo → incompatibilità fra igneo e terreno.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF2","text":"Incompatibilità fra igneo e terreno → veicolo aereo → discesa dell’anima nel corpo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF3","text":"Veicolo aereo → Pasiphe e vacca finta → Minotauro come figura della copula degradata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF4","text":"Favola simbolica → quinto grado del Theatro → repertorio planetario dell’uomo esteriorizzato.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF5","text":"Repertorio planetario → distinzione fra natura, inclinazione, passione, parte corporea e condotta.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF6","text":"Minotauro vivo e idolo interno → vizio, ambizione e bestialità → necessità di uccisione o conversione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF7","text":"Disposizione al bene → esercizio nei Talari → virtù attuosa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF8","text":"Corpo come separazione → morte e dissoluzione → unione con il celeste.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME1","text":"La favola viene riclassificata da finzione poetica a tecnologia di custodia e trasmissione di dottrina filosofica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME2","text":"Il corpo viene riclassificato da semplice supporto dell’anima a sistema pluristratificato di mediazione, prigionia, memoria e corrispondenza astrale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME3","text":"La differenza fra vizio e virtù viene spostata dalla mera proprietà interiore alla relazione fra inclinazione, esercizio e trasformazione simbolica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME4","text":"Le membra corporee cessano di essere elementi anatomici isolati e diventano nodi di un reticolo che collega pianeti, segni zodiacali, passioni e operazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME5","text":"L’idolatria viene ricollocata dall’errore cultuale esterno alla costruzione psichica di dèi interiori fondati sull’autoaffermazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT1","text":"Surface — Pasiphe, Toro, Minotauro, figure mitiche e animali fungono da immagini di collocazione per contenuti umani determinati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT2","text":"Structural — Il quinto grado organizza una tassonomia planetaria che connette corpo, passioni, qualità morali, sorti e azioni possibili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Il testo converte simboli mitici in indirizzi mnemonici e distingue ciò che deve essere ricordato come disposizione da ciò che deve essere ricordato come azione esercitata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’anima discende attraverso gradi di densificazione, dimora nel corpo, conserva residui veicolari e si riunisce al celeste soltanto attraverso un processo di liberazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT5","text":"Ethical-Political — La cura di sé, della famiglia e della republica viene situata sullo stesso piano classificatorio delle inclinazioni, delle passioni e della lotta contro l’idolo dell’ambizione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT1","text":"Gli assiomi ricostruiscono sufficientemente la catena necessità del veicolo → mediazione aerea → allegoria di Pasiphe → organizzazione del quinto grado.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT2","text":"La distinzione fra inclinazione ed esercizio ricostruisce il passaggio decisivo dal repertorio di Pasiphe alla funzione futura dei Talari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT3","text":"La struttura conserva la coerenza interna soltanto assumendo come validi il platonismo veicolare, il simbolismo teologico e la corrispondenza astrologica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT4","text":"Resta sottodeterminato il criterio che assegna precisamente ciascuna immagine a un pianeta, salvo il rinvio a corrispondenze astrologiche e simboliche già presupposte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT5","text":"La tensione principale oppone il determinismo classificatorio delle nature planetarie alla richiesta morale di trasformare, frenare o attuare tali nature.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT6","text":"Una seconda tensione concentra nel corpo funzioni incompatibili ma simultanee: condizione del movimento, oggetto della cupidità, sede della bestialità e ostacolo alla vera unione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT7","text":"Una terza tensione rende il Minotauro semanticamente reversibile, poiché la stessa figura passa da prodotto della caduta a segno della virtù quando viene uccisa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT8","text":"La ricostruzione preserva il movimento effettivo del testo perché mantiene la conversione di metafisica, etica e anatomia in un unico dispositivo simbolico-mnemonico.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T231047862886Z_5656f5be","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"PASIPHAË","source_sha256":"7535fcbe22d0e7f94e4515b18fb9071db99cbd7d841ac55656575c4893cb06ed","sha256":"1e5378825934fdb7f8a8ab7a1f88e043271f4fec656ffdf250b126cba8fdfb0d","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:10:47.865697+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS1","text":"The text resolves the problem of the conjunction between subtle soul and gross body by postulating an intermediate aerial vehicle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS2","text":"The fable of Pasiphe is reformulated as a symbolic theology of the soul’s fall into the cupidity of the body and of the mediation that makes such a fall possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS3","text":"The fifth degree of the Theatro transforms soul-body mediation into a system of mnemonic placement for affects, dispositions, bodily functions, and human conditions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS4","text":"The plurality of planetary images breaks man down into correspondences among moral nature, bodily part, astral influence, and mythical figure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0037","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS5","text":"The Minotaur establishes the distinction between bestial inclination not yet exercised, actualized vice, and virtue as the destruction or conversion of disposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AS6","text":"The movement proceeds from cosmology of descent → mythical allegorization → planetary taxonomy of the human → operative distinction among disposition, exercise, death, and celestial reunion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A1","text":"Every movement of the soul requires a body or vehicle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A2","text":"The fiery soul and the earthly body cannot be conjoined immediately because their difference in subtlety and grossness requires a middle term.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","text":"The descent of the soul through heavens and elements produces an aerial vehicle capable of participating in the nature of soul and body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A4","text":"Symbolic theology preserves, in fabulous form, a lofty philosophy that must not be expounded without veiling.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A5","text":"Pasiphe signifies the soul that falls into the cupidity of the body, whereas the false cow signifies the mediating aerial body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A6","text":"The Minotaur is the product of the copulation between desiring soul, aerial mediation, and bestial corporeality.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","text":"The fifth degree of the Theatro gathers what belongs to man not merely as interior but as still clothed in bodily exteriority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A8","text":"Planetary images order human qualities, conditions of life, passions, and limbs according to astrological correspondences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A9","text":"The concupiscible part, common to man and beasts, can reduce man to a beast when it is gratified and does not participate in the divine ray.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","text":"The inclination toward vice or good does not coincide with its exercise, which is assigned to the subsequent degree of the Talari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A11","text":"Virtue properly exists in actions and not in mere definition, knowledge, or disposition to act well.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A12","text":"The body separates the soul from true union with celestial realities, and death makes its liberating dissolution possible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:A13","text":"Untamed ambition constitutes an internal idol that must be killed for humility and disposition toward the good to arise.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX1","text":"The soul is not a fully disembodied moving principle, since movement requires a bodily vehicle.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX2","text":"The conjunction between soul and body is neither immediate nor natural, nor possible without aerial mediation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX3","text":"The fable is not taken as a literal account, but as the envelope of a philosophical-theological structure.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX4","text":"The fifth degree does not concern purely interior man, since it records what remains enveloped in exteriority and limbs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX5","text":"Human form does not guarantee participation in the divine, since the vicious person may retain human figure and be bestial in the lower part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX6","text":"Inclination is not exercised vice, nor is disposition toward the good active virtue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX7","text":"Knowledge of the definition of virtue is not possession of virtue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX8","text":"Idolatry does not consist solely in the worship of external gods, since its gravest form is the internal divinization of chastity, knowledge, power, or ambition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:NX9","text":"Death is not merely biological cessation, since it is configured as the condition for the soul’s reunion with the celestial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D1","text":"The aerial body acquires an ambivalent function: it makes possible the soul’s incarnation and preserves, after earthly death, the residue that prevents full liberation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A2","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D2","text":"The narrative of Pasiphe translates a cosmological necessity into a moral genealogy of cupidity and monstrosity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4","CH_LIDT_PASI:A5","CH_LIDT_PASI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D3","text":"The Minotaur functions as a reversible sign: alive, it designates vice or bestial disposition; killed, it designates inclination toward virtue.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A6","CH_LIDT_PASI:A9","CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D4","text":"The planetary system does not describe a unitary man, but distributes his properties into heterogeneous series of limbs, passions, fortunes, aptitudes, and relations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D5","text":"Moral judgment is shifted from external appearance and inner declaration to the effective use of the lower faculties and the actions that follow from them.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A9","CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D6","text":"Humility is not a self-sufficient virtue but the effect of the destruction of the internal idol of ambition.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A11","CH_LIDT_PASI:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:D7","text":"Death integrates the taxonomy of the fifth degree as a bodily fact and, simultaneously, surpasses that degree as the dissolution of bodily imprisonment.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1","text":"The Theatro converts a vertical cosmology of descent and ascent into a horizontal classificatory machine capable of archiving the entire human composite.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4","CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2","text":"Corporeality is at once the indispensable condition of the soul’s movement, the seat of its fall, and the final obstacle to its higher union.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A1","CH_LIDT_PASI:A2","CH_LIDT_PASI:A5","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD3","text":"The distinction between disposition and exercise introduces a moral temporality: no nature is fully classifiable as virtue or vice before the act that realizes it.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A9","CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD4","text":"The astrological order organizes human material without eliminating the problem of responsibility, since planetary disposition must still be converted, exercised, or repressed.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A8","CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11","CH_LIDT_PASI:A13"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SD5","text":"The symbolic apparatus binds anthropology, morality, physiology, domestic politics, and destiny into a single grammar of images.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A4","CH_LIDT_PASI:A7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX1","text":"The self-sufficiency of the pure soul must be false, since soul, movement, and incarnation depend on a series of vehicular supports.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX2","text":"The immediate identity of man with his own rational figure must be false, since his desiring part can render him structurally bestial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX3","text":"The equivalence between moral knowledge and virtuous life must be false, since virtue requires actualization in deeds.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX4","text":"The externality of idolatry must be false, since the decisive enemy is installed in the imagination and ambition of the subject.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX5","text":"The fullness of the mortal body must be false, since the body is conceived as prison and as separation from true union.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX1","text":"Immediate unity between spiritual and corporeal is unavailable: every passage requires degradation, mediation, and residue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX2","text":"True union with the celestial is precluded by the integral persistence of the living body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX3","text":"There is no innocence guaranteed by human nature, because the form of man may cover a life dominated by the bestial part.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX4","text":"There is no spiritual good not exposed to transformation into an internal idol when it is taken as an object of self-exaltation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS1","text":"Ontological difference fiery soul / earthly body → impossibility of immediate copulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS2","text":"Impossibility of immediate copulation → production of the aerial vehicle as a middle participant in both.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS3","text":"Aerial mediation + the soul’s desire for the body → allegory of Pasiphe and generation of the Minotaur.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS4","text":"Veiled allegory → translation into mnemonic images of the fifth degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS5","text":"Planetary order + zodiac + human body → distribution of limbs, affects, states, qualities, and destinies.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS6","text":"Concupiscible part + adherence to passions → bestialization and potential or actualized vice.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS7","text":"Destruction of the internal idol or of the Minotaur → humility and inclination toward virtue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS8","text":"Good inclination + exercise in the Talari → active virtue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9","text":"Dissolution of the body and vehicular residue → possibility of the soul’s reunion with the celestial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF1","text":"Movement of the soul → necessity of a vehicle → incompatibility between fiery and earthly.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF2","text":"Incompatibility between fiery and earthly → aerial vehicle → descent of the soul into the body.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF3","text":"Aerial vehicle → Pasiphe and false cow → Minotaur as figure of degraded copulation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF4","text":"Symbolic fable → fifth degree of the Theatro → planetary repertory of exteriorized man.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF5","text":"Planetary repertory → distinction among nature, inclination, passion, bodily part, and conduct.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF6","text":"Living Minotaur and internal idol → vice, ambition, and bestiality → necessity of killing or conversion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF7","text":"Disposition toward the good → exercise in the Talari → active virtue.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:AF8","text":"Body as separation → death and dissolution → union with the celestial.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME1","text":"The fable is reclassified from poetic fiction into a technology for the preservation and transmission of philosophical doctrine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME2","text":"The body is reclassified from a simple support of the soul into a multilayered system of mediation, imprisonment, memory, and astral correspondence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME3","text":"The difference between vice and virtue is shifted from mere inner property to the relation among inclination, exercise, and symbolic transformation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME4","text":"The bodily limbs cease to be isolated anatomical elements and become nodes of a network connecting planets, zodiacal signs, passions, and operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ME5","text":"Idolatry is relocated from external cultic error to the psychic construction of interior gods founded upon self-assertion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0046","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0047","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT1","text":"Surface — Pasiphe, Bull, Minotaur, mythical and animal figures function as images of placement for determinate human contents.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT2","text":"Structural — The fifth degree organizes a planetary taxonomy connecting body, passions, moral qualities, fortunes, and possible actions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0021","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text converts mythical symbols into mnemonic addresses and distinguishes what must be remembered as disposition from what must be remembered as exercised action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — The soul descends through degrees of densification, dwells in the body, retains vehicular residues, and reunites with the celestial only through a process of liberation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0058","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0059","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT5","text":"Ethical-Political — Care of the self, the family, and the republic is situated on the same classificatory plane as inclinations, passions, and the struggle against the idol of ambition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0051","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT1","text":"The axioms sufficiently reconstruct the chain necessity of vehicle → aerial mediation → allegory of Pasiphe → organization of the fifth degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT2","text":"The distinction between inclination and exercise reconstructs the decisive passage from the repertory of Pasiphe to the future function of the Talari.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT3","text":"The structure preserves internal coherence only by assuming as valid vehicular Platonism, theological symbolism, and astrological correspondence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT4","text":"The criterion that precisely assigns each image to a planet remains underdetermined, except for reference to already presupposed astrological and symbolic correspondences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT5","text":"The principal tension opposes the classificatory determinism of planetary natures to the moral demand to transform, restrain, or actualize such natures.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT6","text":"A second tension concentrates incompatible yet simultaneous functions in the body: condition of movement, object of cupidity, seat of bestiality, and obstacle to true union.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0060","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT7","text":"A third tension renders the Minotaur semantically reversible, since the same figure passes from product of the fall to sign of virtue when it is killed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0031","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT8","text":"The reconstruction preserves the effective movement of the text because it maintains the conversion of metaphysics, ethics, and anatomy into a single symbolic-mnemonic apparatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0016","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0029","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0049","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PASI:P0062","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_LIDT_PASI@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_LIDT_PASI:v1","source_language_code":"it","original_title":"PASIPHE"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 05","title":"Pasiphe","context":"Chapter 05"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL","layer":"CH","title":"Italari.","order":6,"parents":["RAW_LIDT_ITAL"],"revision":"CH_LIDT_ITAL@R001","sha256":"da0d17777348b8725b1bd512b35de138460860eb2c1f4c108b4fcd82f2d6fbac","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS1","text":"Il testo affronta il problema di rendere memorizzabili tutte le operazioni che l’Uomo può compiere nei gradi inferiori del Teatro.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS2","text":"Il problema viene riformulato mediante il sesto grado, dove i Talari e gli altri guarnimenti di Mercurio sono disposti sopra le porte dei pianeti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS3","text":"La struttura assume come dispositivo mnemonico l’immaginario di Mercurio che esegue la volontà degli Dei, secondo ciò che “fauoleggiano i Poeti”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS4","text":"La dimostrazione consiste nell’assegnare a ogni pianeta una serie finita di immagini, ciascuna correlata a una o più operazioni verbali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS5","text":"Il movimento generativo procede dalla porta planetaria all’immagine, dall’immagine all’operazione e dall’insieme delle operazioni a un repertorio umano naturale e “fuor d’ogni arte”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A1","text":"Il Teatro è organizzato secondo gradi sovrapposti e porte associate ai pianeti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A2","text":"Il sesto grado reca sopra ogni porta planetaria i Talari e gli altri guarnimenti attribuiti a Mercurio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A3","text":"Mercurio costituisce il modello simbolico dell’esecuzione della volontà divina attraverso immagini mitiche.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","text":"Le immagini collocate sotto i Talari planetari hanno una funzione mnemonica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5","text":"La funzione mnemonica consiste nel far ritrovare le operazioni che l’Uomo può compiere nei gradi inferiori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A6","text":"Le operazioni rappresentate appartengono all’ambito del naturale e sono dichiarate “fuor d’ogni arte”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7","text":"Ogni pianeta possiede una serie delimitata di immagini operative.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","text":"Le serie planetarie contengono sette immagini sotto Luna, Mercurio, Venere, Giove e Saturno, e cinque immagini sotto Sole e Marte.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","text":"Ogni immagine significa una o più operazioni espresse mediante verbi o serie verbali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A10","text":"Una singola immagine può rappresentare l’azione, l’azione causata, la ricezione, la trasformazione o la variazione d’intensità di una stessa operazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A11","text":"Le immagini possono assumere forma mitologica, umana, animale, naturale o oggettuale senza perdere la funzione operativa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A12","text":"La distribuzione planetaria organizza insieme operazioni materiali, naturali, affettive, temporali, sociali, morali, conflittuali e patitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX1","text":"Il repertorio non descrive un’arte produttrice delle operazioni, poiché le operazioni sono collocate “fuor d’ogni arte”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX2","text":"Il repertorio non è una raccolta indifferenziata di immagini, poiché ogni immagine è collocata sotto una porta planetaria determinata.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX3","text":"Le immagini non sono offerte come semplici illustrazioni narrative dei miti, ma come segni di operazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX4","text":"Il rapporto fra immagine e operazione non è necessariamente uno-a-uno, poiché una figura può condensare una pluralità di verbi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX5","text":"Il sistema non limita le operazioni ai soli atti nobili o intellettuali, ma comprende atti corporei, vizi, impurità, timore, tribolazione e indebolimento.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX6","text":"La disposizione planetaria non viene presentata come una dimostrazione causale del prodursi delle operazioni, ma come una sede di significazione e recupero mnemonico.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX7","text":"La memoria non è affidata alla sola interiorità del soggetto, ma viene esteriorizzata in immagini, porte e gradi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX8","text":"Il catalogo non offre una tassonomia omogenea delle operazioni, poiché accosta mutamenti materiali, condotte, stati affettivi, virtù, relazioni e processi temporali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D1","text":"Le porte planetarie trasformano la disposizione spaziale del Teatro in un indice di accesso alle operazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D2","text":"La figura mitica o scenica funziona come un operatore mnemonico capace di richiamare una famiglia di azioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A3","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D3","text":"Il repertorio converte immagini in sequenze verbali, facendo passare il segno figurativo nell’azione praticabile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D4","text":"Le varianti causative, ricettive, trasformative e reversibili ampliano il valore di ogni immagine oltre l’atto singolo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D5","text":"La struttura del sesto grado collega l’apparato simbolico superiore alla memoria delle operazioni contenute nei gradi inferiori.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A2","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D6","text":"La partizione planetaria rende recuperabili operazioni eterogenee senza ricondurle a un unico genere materiale o morale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD1","text":"Il Teatro diventa un lessico eseguibile nel quale la memoria non conserva soltanto immagini, ma procedure d’azione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD2","text":"Una pluralità potenzialmente illimitata di operazioni umane viene resa enumerabile mediante un numero finito di nuclei figurativi.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD3","text":"La naturalità delle operazioni viene resa accessibile attraverso una mediazione simbolica e artificiale, creando una tensione fra contenuto naturale e forma mnemotecnica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A6","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD4","text":"La coordinata planetaria agisce come principio di recupero e distribuzione, non come spiegazione causale autonoma delle operazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7","CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD5","text":"Il sistema unifica sotto una stessa architettura figurale livelli che normalmente apparirebbero separati: materia, corpo, affetto, tempo, relazione, virtù, conflitto e sofferenza.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A12","CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX1","text":"Il sistema esclude tacitamente una memoria priva di supporto spaziale, figurativo e ordinativo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX2","text":"Il sistema esclude che il significato operativo possa essere ricavato dalla sola forma letterale dell’immagine.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX3","text":"Il sistema esclude una separazione stabile fra operazioni fisiche, morali, sociali e affettive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX4","text":"Il sistema esclude che la totalità delle operazioni debba essere esposta mediante spiegazione discorsiva continua.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX5","text":"Il sistema esclude una distinzione netta fra contenuto mitologico e funzione pratica, poiché la scena mitica viene utilizzata come veicolo di operazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX1","text":"È precluso l’accesso immediato alla totalità delle operazioni umane: l’accesso passa necessariamente attraverso porte e immagini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX2","text":"È preclusa una classificazione puramente concettuale delle operazioni, sostituita da una distribuzione figurativa e planetaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX3","text":"È resa indisponibile la separazione fra dispositivo mnemonico, cosmologia simbolica e repertorio operativo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX4","text":"Rimane strutturalmente assente una regola generale che deduca perché ogni singola figura significhi proprio quella determinata serie di operazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS1","text":"Il sistema prende come input la necessità di ricordare le operazioni umane e la colloca nella struttura gerarchica del sesto grado.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS2","text":"Il sesto grado distribuisce il materiale mnemonico secondo la sequenza porta planetaria → Talari di Mercurio → serie figurativa.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS3","text":"Ogni figura viene convertita nella sequenza immagine → significazione → verbo operativo → famiglia di varianti dell’azione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS4","text":"L’insieme delle serie planetarie produce una mappa finita di recupero per operazioni naturali, corporee, affettive, temporali, sociali, morali e conflittuali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AF1","text":"Necessità di ricordare le operazioni → istituzione del sesto grado → collocazione dei Talari sulle porte planetarie → inserimento delle immagini → conversione delle immagini in operazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AF2","text":"Distribuzione planetaria → repertori figurativi delimitati → associazioni verbali plurime → recupero ordinato della varietà dell’agire umano.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME1","text":"La memoria viene riclassificata da facoltà interna a topologia operativa fatta di porte, gradi e immagini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME2","text":"Le immagini mitiche vengono riclassificate da contenuti narrativi a segni verbali e operatori d’azione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME3","text":"La distinzione fra azione materiale, condotta morale, stato affettivo e relazione sociale perde il ruolo di separazione primaria.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME4","text":"La categoria di “operazione” viene ampliata fino a includere non soltanto il fare, ma anche il subire, il ricevere, il mutare, il ritardare, il manifestare e il causare.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME5","text":"Il terreno strategico della memoria viene spostato dalla ripetizione di elenchi alla riattivazione di un repertorio mediante coordinate cosmologiche.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — Il livello immediato consiste nelle immagini poste sotto i Talari di ciascun pianeta e nelle operazioni loro attribuite.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — Il livello strutturale è costituito dalla relazione stabile fra porta planetaria, serie figurativa e famiglia di operazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — Il livello metastrategico trasforma la memoria delle azioni in un sistema di reperimento spaziale, figurativo e associativo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — Il livello ontologico e temporale definisce l’agire umano come insieme naturale di trasformazioni, stati, relazioni, durate, età, ritardi, fortune, tribolazioni e indebolimenti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT1","text":"Gli assiomi sono sufficienti per ricostruire il funzionamento centrale: un grado superiore organizza immagini planetarie che richiamano operazioni dei gradi inferiori.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT2","text":"Rimane sottodeterminato il criterio generale mediante cui una specifica figura viene associata a una specifica serie di operazioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT3","text":"Rimane inoltre non spiegata la ragione della diversa quantità di immagini assegnata ai pianeti e della distribuzione dei domini operativi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT4","text":"La struttura è coerente come dispositivo catalogico e mnemonico, ma non come sistema deduttivo che dimostri le proprie corrispondenze.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT5","text":"La tensione principale oppone operazioni dichiarate naturali e “fuor d’ogni arte” alla loro necessaria accessibilità mediante un apparato figurativo e ordinativo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT6","text":"Una seconda tensione oppone la finitezza delle immagini alla pretesa di comprendere tutte le operazioni che l’Uomo può compiere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT7","text":"La ricostruzione preserva il movimento effettivo del testo perché mantiene la sequenza porta planetaria → immagine → significazione → repertorio operativo, lasciando irrisolta la genesi particolare delle corrispondenze.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T230909147410Z_02bd6040","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"TALARIA.","source_sha256":"da0d17777348b8725b1bd512b35de138460860eb2c1f4c108b4fcd82f2d6fbac","sha256":"3c058f73de8b48c5771967aa5959c8108015e68790621b03285327d5dafb6d35","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:09:09.151059+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS1","text":"The text addresses the problem of making memorable all the operations that Man can perform in the lower grades of the Theatre.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS2","text":"The problem is reformulated by means of the sixth grade, where the Talaria and the other accoutrements of Mercury are arranged above the doors of the planets.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS3","text":"The structure adopts as a mnemonic device the imagery of Mercury carrying out the will of the Gods, according to what “fauoleggiano i Poeti”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS4","text":"The demonstration consists in assigning to each planet a finite series of images, each correlated with one or more verbal operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS5","text":"The generative movement proceeds from the planetary door to the image, from the image to the operation, and from the set of operations to a natural human repertoire “fuor d’ogni arte”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A1","text":"The Theatre is organized according to superimposed grades and doors associated with the planets.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A2","text":"The sixth grade bears above each planetary door the Talaria and the other accoutrements attributed to Mercury.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A3","text":"Mercury constitutes the symbolic model of the execution of divine will through mythical images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","text":"The images placed beneath the planetary Talaria have a mnemonic function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5","text":"The mnemonic function consists in making it possible to retrieve the operations that Man can perform in the lower grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A6","text":"The operations represented belong to the domain of the natural and are declared “fuor d’ogni arte”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7","text":"Each planet possesses a delimited series of operative images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","text":"The planetary series contain seven images under the Moon, Mercury, Venus, Jupiter, and Saturn, and five images under the Sun and Mars.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","text":"Each image signifies one or more operations expressed by means of verbs or verbal series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A10","text":"A single image can represent the action, the caused action, reception, transformation, or variation in intensity of one and the same operation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A11","text":"The images can take mythological, human, animal, natural, or objectual form without losing their operative function.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:A12","text":"The planetary distribution organizes together material, natural, affective, temporal, social, moral, conflictual, and passive operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX1","text":"The repertoire does not describe an art that produces operations, since the operations are situated “fuor d’ogni arte”.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX2","text":"The repertoire is not an undifferentiated collection of images, since each image is situated beneath a determined planetary door.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX3","text":"The images are not offered as mere narrative illustrations of myths, but as signs of operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX4","text":"The relation between image and operation is not necessarily one-to-one, since a figure can condense a plurality of verbs.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX5","text":"The system does not limit operations to noble or intellectual acts alone, but includes bodily acts, vices, impurities, fear, tribulation, and weakening.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX6","text":"The planetary arrangement is not presented as a causal demonstration of the production of operations, but as a site of signification and mnemonic retrieval.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX7","text":"Memory is not entrusted to the subject's interiority alone, but is externalized in images, doors, and grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX8","text":"The catalogue does not offer a homogeneous taxonomy of operations, since it juxtaposes material changes, conduct, affective states, virtues, relations, and temporal processes.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D1","text":"The planetary doors transform the spatial arrangement of the Theatre into an index of access to operations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D2","text":"The mythical or scenic figure functions as a mnemonic operator capable of recalling a family of actions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A3","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D3","text":"The repertoire converts images into verbal sequences, carrying the figurative sign into practicable action.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D4","text":"Causative, receptive, transformative, and reversible variants extend the value of each image beyond the single act.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D5","text":"The structure of the sixth grade connects the upper symbolic apparatus to the memory of the operations contained in the lower grades.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A2","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:D6","text":"The planetary partition makes heterogeneous operations retrievable without reducing them to a single material or moral genus.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0036","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD1","text":"The Theatre becomes an executable lexicon in which memory preserves not only images, but procedures of action.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD2","text":"A potentially unlimited plurality of human operations is made enumerable by means of a finite number of figurative nuclei.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD3","text":"The naturalness of operations is made accessible through symbolic and artificial mediation, creating a tension between natural content and mnemonic form.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A6","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD4","text":"The planetary coordinate acts as a principle of retrieval and distribution, not as an autonomous causal explanation of operations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A7","CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD5","text":"The system unifies under the same figural architecture levels that would normally appear separate: matter, body, affect, time, relation, virtue, conflict, and suffering.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A12","CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX1","text":"The system tacitly excludes a memory devoid of spatial, figurative, and ordering support.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX2","text":"The system excludes the possibility that operative meaning can be derived from the image's literal form alone.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX3","text":"The system excludes a stable separation between physical, moral, social, and affective operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0020","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX4","text":"The system excludes the requirement that the totality of operations be set forth by means of continuous discursive explanation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX5","text":"The system excludes a sharp distinction between mythological content and practical function, since the mythical scene is used as a vehicle of operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX1","text":"Immediate access to the totality of human operations is precluded: access necessarily passes through doors and images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX2","text":"A purely conceptual classification of operations is precluded, replaced by a figurative and planetary distribution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX3","text":"The separation between mnemonic device, symbolic cosmology, and operative repertoire is rendered unavailable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX4","text":"A general rule that deduces why each individual figure signifies precisely that determinate series of operations remains structurally absent.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS1","text":"The system takes as input the necessity of remembering human operations and places it within the hierarchical structure of the sixth grade.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS2","text":"The sixth grade distributes mnemonic material according to the sequence planetary door → Talaria of Mercury → figurative series.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS3","text":"Each figure is converted into the sequence image → signification → operative verb → family of variants of the action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0021","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS4","text":"The set of planetary series produces a finite map of retrieval for natural, bodily, affective, temporal, social, moral, and conflictual operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AF1","text":"Necessity of remembering operations → institution of the sixth grade → placement of the Talaria upon the planetary doors → insertion of images → conversion of images into operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:AF2","text":"Planetary distribution → delimited figurative repertoires → multiple verbal associations → ordered retrieval of the variety of human action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME1","text":"Memory is reclassified from an internal faculty into an operative topology made of doors, grades, and images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME2","text":"Mythical images are reclassified from narrative contents into verbal signs and operators of action.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME3","text":"The distinction between material action, moral conduct, affective state, and social relation loses its role as primary separation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0026","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0040","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME4","text":"The category of “operation” is broadened to include not only doing, but also undergoing, receiving, changing, delaying, manifesting, and causing.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME5","text":"The strategic terrain of memory is shifted from the repetition of lists to the reactivation of a repertoire by means of cosmological coordinates.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT1","text":"**Surface** — The immediate level consists in the images placed beneath the Talaria of each planet and in the operations attributed to them.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0022","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT2","text":"**Structural** — The structural level consists in the stable relation between planetary door, figurative series, and family of operations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT3","text":"**Metastrategic** — The metastrategic level transforms the memory of actions into a system of spatial, figurative, and associative retrieval.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT4","text":"**Ontological/Temporal** — The ontological and temporal level defines human action as a natural set of transformations, states, relations, durations, ages, delays, fortunes, tribulations, and weakenings.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0008","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0034","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the central functioning: a higher grade organizes planetary images that recall operations of the lower grades.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT2","text":"The general criterion by which a specific figure is associated with a specific series of operations remains underdetermined.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT3","text":"Moreover, the reason for the differing number of images assigned to the planets and for the distribution of operative domains remains unexplained.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT4","text":"The structure is coherent as a catalogical and mnemonic device, but not as a deductive system that demonstrates its own correspondences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT5","text":"The principal tension opposes operations declared natural and “fuor d’ogni arte” to their necessary accessibility by means of a figurative and ordering apparatus.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT6","text":"A second tension opposes the finitude of images to the claim of comprising all the operations that Man can perform.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0013","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the actual movement of the text because it maintains the sequence planetary door → image → signification → operative repertoire, while leaving unresolved the particular genesis of the correspondences.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0004","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_ITAL:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_LIDT_ITAL@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_LIDT_ITAL:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 06","title":"Italari.","context":"Chapter 06"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM","layer":"CH","title":"Prometheo.","order":7,"parents":["RAW_LIDT_PROM"],"revision":"CH_LIDT_PROM@R001","sha256":"ed8d14df1e706a44d54832caf18415f97a21e46e6777b8ea168209a818f0522a","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS1","text":"Il settimo grado deve rendere tutte le arti, nobili e vili, riconoscibili entro una sola architettura simbolica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS2","text":"Il mito prometeico viene assunto come genealogia della differenza fra la dotazione tecnica necessaria alla vita e la facoltà civile necessaria alla convivenza.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS3","text":"La carenza originaria dell’uomo viene trasformata in principio di classificazione: le arti compensano l’indigenza naturale, mentre pudore e giustizia rendono stabile la città.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS4","text":"Prometeo diviene il segno generale che raccoglie arti, artefici, facoltà civili e facoltà militari senza trasferire il Theatro a un grado ulteriore.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS5","text":"La classificazione mitologica viene adattata ai bisogni del presente, includendo oggetti moderni, costumi posteriori e lessico cristiano mediante trasposizione simbolica e retorica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","text":"L’uomo è originariamente privo delle difese naturali distribuite agli altri animali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A2","text":"Il furto prometeico di fuoco, artificio e sapienza fornisce all’uomo l’acutezza d’ingegno necessaria per acquisire e usare le arti del vivere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","text":"La facoltà tecnica assicura l’apparecchio del vivere ma non contiene da sé la facoltà civile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","text":"La città non può conservarsi se pudore e giustizia non sono partecipati universalmente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","text":"La facoltà civile include la milizia, la difesa, la giurisdizione e l’esecuzione delle pene.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A6","text":"Le arti possono essere distribuite in modo differenziale, mentre i requisiti della convivenza civile devono essere comuni a tutti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","text":"Un’immagine mitologica può contenere una serie di pratiche, saperi, istituzioni e loro appartenenze mediante analogia simbolica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","text":"Prometeo con la facella designa genericamente arti e artefici, perché un nome di specie può operare come nome di genere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A9","text":"L’ordine del Theatro deve comprendere tanto le arti nobili quanto quelle ignobili, incluse le pratiche viziose, servili, punitive e coercitive.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","text":"La memoria classificatoria può accogliere materiali estranei all’antichità mediante accomodamento ai costumi e ai bisogni dell’età presente.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A11","text":"La traduzione del sapere classico nella religione cristiana richiede di distinguere il Verbo e la sapienza dall’incarnazione e dalla passione di Cristo.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX1","text":"L’uomo non è definito da una sufficienza naturale, poiché la sua condizione iniziale è «vota & priua de ogni dote».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX2","text":"L’arte non coincide con la facoltà civile, poiché il possesso di tecniche non impedisce la dissoluzione violenta della comunità.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX3","text":"Pudore e giustizia non sono arti specialistiche distribuibili a pochi, perché la loro distribuzione diseguale rende impossibile la conservazione della città.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX4","text":"Il simbolo mitologico non è vincolato alla realtà letterale dell’oggetto figurato, come mostra il Centauro dichiarato inesistente nella natura.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX5","text":"L’ordinamento del Theatro non è una riproduzione archeologica dei costumi antichi, perché include pratiche non anticamente consuete per evitare lacune classificatorie.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX6","text":"Il sapere classico non basta integralmente al discorso cristiano, poiché il lessico ciceroniano deve essere adattato e non può sostituire la verità dell’incarnazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX7","text":"L’inclusione enciclopedica non equivale ad approvazione morale, poiché bordello, ruffianesmo, tortura, carcere e servitù sono classificati senza essere assolti.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D1","text":"La tecnica costituisce una compensazione artificiale della vulnerabilità umana, non una proprietà naturale dell’uomo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D2","text":"La fondazione della città richiede un secondo dono rispetto all’invenzione delle arti, perché la capacità di vivere non produce automaticamente la capacità di convivere.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D3","text":"Il potere politico appare come condizione di continuità dell’ordine civile, poiché universalizza le virtù civiche e sanziona la loro assenza.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D4","text":"Ogni immagine del Theatro opera come nodo di condensazione che connette una figura, un dominio pratico e una catena di saperi subordinati.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D5","text":"La distinzione fra arti liberali, arti meccaniche, pratiche vili e apparati coercitivi perde funzione escludente e diviene distinzione interna alla medesima mappa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D6","text":"L’accomodamento al presente è una condizione di completezza del sistema, poiché l’assenza di posto per nuovi oggetti produrrebbe «buchi» nella memoria ordinata.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D7","text":"L’uso cristiano delle risorse classiche è subordinato a una differenza teologica che il solo vocabolario della sapienza non può cancellare.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SD1","text":"Il Theatro si costituisce come dispositivo di governo cognitivo: ordina simultaneamente i mezzi della sopravvivenza, le forme della vita sociale, le istituzioni del comando e le pratiche della punizione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SD2","text":"La totalità enciclopedica non è ottenuta eliminando l’eterogeneo, ma assegnando a ogni eterogeneità una collocazione simbolica e una catena di appartenenze.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SD3","text":"Il mito di Prometeo legittima il passaggio dalla povertà naturale dell’uomo alla centralità dell’arte, ma il mito di Mercurio e Giove subordina tale centralità a un ordine civile universale e punitivo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SD4","text":"L’adattamento cristiano conserva l’autorità formale del patrimonio pagano soltanto rendendolo materiale retorico subordinato alla specificità dell’incarnazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX1","text":"È falsa l’idea che l’autoconservazione umana possa fondarsi esclusivamente su forza, tecnica o aggregazione spontanea.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX2","text":"È falsa l’idea che le arti possano rimanere conoscenze isolate, poiché ciascuna deve essere inserita in una catena ordinata di appartenenze.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX3","text":"È falsa l’idea che una classificazione completa debba limitarsi a oggetti leciti, nobili o teoricamente puri.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX4","text":"È falsa l’idea che l’antico possa parlare immediatamente il cristiano senza una mediazione retorica e dottrinale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5","text":"È falsa l’idea che il Verbo inteso come sapienza esaurisca il Cristo, poiché l’incarnazione e la passione costituiscono una differenza non assorbibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1","text":"Nessuna pratica umana deve restare senza luogo nel Theatro, perché l’assenza di collocazione è trattata come lacuna dell’ordine stesso.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX2","text":"Nessun ordine politico può tollerare la non-partecipazione a pudore e giustizia, perché il soggetto privo di entrambi è costruito come «peste de la città» ed espulso dal numero dei viventi.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX3","text":"Nessun sapere simbolicamente ordinato può restare esterno alla mediazione figurale, poiché anche scienza, legge, commercio, artigianato e religione diventano pensabili nel sistema solo come contenuti di immagini.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX4","text":"Nessuna universalità profana del sapere può chiudersi su se stessa, perché la pienezza cristiana esige un evento incarnativo che eccede sapienza, verbo e repertorio classico.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS1","text":"Indigenza naturale → furto prometeico → acquisizione di fuoco, ingegno e arti → sopravvivenza umana incompleta.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS2","text":"Aggregazione difensiva → conflitto reciproco → insufficienza della sola città materiale → distribuzione universale di pudore e giustizia → ordine civile sanzionato.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS3","text":"Figura mitologica → analogia funzionale → raccolta di pratiche e saperi → articolazione in appartenenze e catene → memoria enciclopedica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS4","text":"Generalità di Prometeo → inclusione di arti nobili, vili, civili e militari → chiusura del settimo grado senza elevazione del Theatro.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS5","text":"Lacuna fra repertorio antico e bisogno presente → accomodamento simbolico e retorico → integrazione di nuovi costumi e materia cristiana → riserva dell’incarnazione contro la riduzione alla sola sapienza.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AF1","text":"Privazione umana originaria → invenzione tecnica prometeica → insufficienza della vita tecnica → dono universale di pudore e giustizia → stabilizzazione della città.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AF2","text":"Genealogia mitica delle facoltà → Prometeo come genere delle arti → immagini planetarie come nodi classificatori → distribuzione dei saperi nel settimo grado.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AF3","text":"Pretesa di completezza → inclusione di pratiche nobili, ignobili, coercitive e viziose → eliminazione dei vuoti del repertorio.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AF4","text":"Distanza fra antico e presente → accomodamento ai costumi moderni → impiego del patrimonio ciceroniano → delimitazione cristologica del traducibile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME1","text":"La distinzione fra natura e arte viene riorganizzata: l’arte appare come condizione compensativa dell’umanità anziché come supplemento accidentale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME2","text":"La distinzione fra sapere tecnico e ordine politico diviene visibile come separazione costitutiva fra vivere e convivere.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME3","text":"La distinzione fra arte nobile e arte vile cessa di essere un criterio di esclusione e diventa un criterio interno di collocazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME4","text":"Le immagini mitologiche cessano di funzionare soltanto come ornamenti narrativi e diventano operatori di indicizzazione per domini di conoscenza.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME5","text":"Il rapporto fra antico e moderno viene riclassificato come rapporto di adattamento controllato, non di fedeltà antiquaria né di sostituzione integrale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME6","text":"La religione cristiana viene collocata insieme entro e oltre il repertorio classico: traducibile sul piano retorico, irriducibile sul piano dell’incarnazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT1","text":"Surface — Il testo assegna a Prometeo e alle immagini subordinate serie determinate di arti, mestieri, saperi, istituzioni e pratiche.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT2","text":"Structural — Il testo distingue il circuito della tecnica dal circuito della cittadinanza e fa della giustizia universale la condizione di conservazione della città.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — Il testo converte il mito in una tecnologia di ordinamento mnemonico, capace di assorbire materiali eterogenei mediante simboli e partizioni.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — L’uomo è pensato come essere naturalmente deficitario, artificialmente compensato e storicamente bisognoso di ritraduzione dei repertori ereditati.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT5","text":"Theological — Il sistema presuppone che il linguaggio della sapienza possa essere riusato cristianamente ma non possa annullare la differenza dell’incarnazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT1","text":"Gli assiomi sono sufficienti a ricostruire il passaggio dalla vulnerabilità umana alla necessità delle arti e dalla tecnica alla necessità dell’ordine civile.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT2","text":"Gli assiomi sono sufficienti a ricostruire la funzione di Prometeo quale principio generale di raccolta delle arti nel settimo grado.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT3","text":"Rimane sottodeterminato il criterio rigoroso che assegna ogni arte a una figura particolare, poiché molte associazioni operano per analogia contingente o autorità allegorica.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT4","text":"La struttura è coerente nel distinguere distribuzione differenziale delle arti e universalità delle virtù civili.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT5","text":"La struttura dipende da una tensione non risolta fra pretesa di ordine totale e necessità di accomodamenti contingenti per includere oggetti posteriori, moderni o marginali.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT6","text":"La struttura dipende da una seconda tensione fra traducibilità retorica del cristianesimo nel repertorio classico e irriducibilità dottrinale dell’incarnazione.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT7","text":"La ricostruzione preserva il movimento effettivo del testo se mantiene inseparabili genealogia antropologica, fondazione politica, classificazione mnemonica e adattamento confessionale.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T231109730471Z_d0a53165","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"PROMETHEUS.","source_sha256":"ed8d14df1e706a44d54832caf18415f97a21e46e6777b8ea168209a818f0522a","sha256":"f53f3c6d09f7fa9564bb0ae2cae42be8532f73a1d3288d4771cda0241bd5758e","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:11:09.734276+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS1","text":"The seventh degree must render all arts, noble and vile, recognizable within a single symbolic architecture.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS2","text":"The Promethean myth is taken up as a genealogy of the difference between the technical endowment necessary for life and the civil faculty necessary for coexistence.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS3","text":"Man's original deficiency is transformed into a principle of classification: the arts compensate for natural indigence, while shame and justice make the city stable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS4","text":"Prometheus becomes the general sign that gathers arts, artificers, civil faculties, and military faculties without transferring the Theatro to a further degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AS5","text":"Mythological classification is adapted to the needs of the present, including modern objects, later customs, and Christian vocabulary through symbolic and rhetorical transposition.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","text":"Man is originally deprived of the natural defenses distributed among the other animals.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A2","text":"Prometheus's theft of fire, artifice, and wisdom provides man with the acuity of intellect necessary to acquire and use the arts of living.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","text":"Technical faculty secures the apparatus of living but does not in itself contain civil faculty.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","text":"The city cannot preserve itself unless shame and justice are universally shared.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","text":"Civil faculty includes military service, defense, jurisdiction, and the execution of punishments.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A6","text":"The arts may be distributed differentially, whereas the requirements of civil coexistence must be common to all.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","text":"A mythological image can contain a series of practices, forms of knowledge, institutions, and their affiliations by means of symbolic analogy.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","text":"Prometheus with the torch generically designates arts and artificers, because a species-name can operate as a genus-name.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A9","text":"The order of the Theatro must encompass both noble and ignoble arts, including vicious, servile, punitive, and coercive practices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","text":"Classificatory memory can accommodate materials foreign to antiquity by adapting them to the customs and needs of the present age.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:A11","text":"The translation of classical knowledge into the Christian religion requires distinguishing the Word and wisdom from Christ's incarnation and passion.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX1","text":"Man is not defined by natural self-sufficiency, since his initial condition is «vota & priua de ogni dote».","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX2","text":"Art does not coincide with civil faculty, since the possession of techniques does not prevent the violent dissolution of the community.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX3","text":"Shame and justice are not specialized arts distributable to a few, because their unequal distribution makes the preservation of the city impossible.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX4","text":"The mythological symbol is not bound to the literal reality of the depicted object, as the Centaur, declared nonexistent in nature, shows.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX5","text":"The ordering of the Theatro is not an archaeological reproduction of ancient customs, because it includes practices not customarily ancient in order to avoid classificatory lacunae.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX6","text":"Classical knowledge is not wholly sufficient for Christian discourse, since Ciceronian vocabulary must be adapted and cannot replace the truth of the incarnation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:NX7","text":"Encyclopedic inclusion does not amount to moral approval, since brothel, pimping, torture, prison, and servitude are classified without being absolved.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"4","name":"Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D1","text":"Technique constitutes an artificial compensation for human vulnerability, not a natural property of man.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D2","text":"The foundation of the city requires a second gift in addition to the invention of the arts, because the capacity to live does not automatically produce the capacity to coexist.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D3","text":"Political power appears as a condition for the continuity of civil order, since it universalizes civic virtues and sanctions their absence.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D4","text":"Every image of the Theatro operates as a node of condensation that connects a figure, a practical domain, and a chain of subordinate forms of knowledge.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D5","text":"The distinction between liberal arts, mechanical arts, vile practices, and coercive apparatuses loses its excluding function and becomes a distinction internal to the same map.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D6","text":"Accommodation to the present is a condition of the system's completeness, since the absence of a place for new objects would produce «buchi» in ordered memory.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:D7","text":"The Christian use of classical resources is subordinated to a theological difference that the vocabulary of wisdom alone cannot erase.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"5","name":"Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SD1","text":"The Theatro constitutes itself as a device of cognitive government: it simultaneously orders the means of survival, the forms of social life, the institutions of command, and the practices of punishment.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0052","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SD2","text":"Encyclopedic totality is not attained by eliminating the heterogeneous, but by assigning each heterogeneity a symbolic location and a chain of affiliations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SD3","text":"The myth of Prometheus legitimates the passage from man's natural poverty to the centrality of art, but the myth of Mercury and Jupiter subordinates this centrality to a universal and punitive civil order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SD4","text":"Christian adaptation preserves the formal authority of the pagan heritage only by making it rhetorical material subordinate to the specificity of the incarnation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX1","text":"The idea that human self-preservation can be founded exclusively on force, technique, or spontaneous aggregation is false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX2","text":"The idea that the arts can remain isolated bodies of knowledge is false, since each must be inserted into an ordered chain of affiliations.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX3","text":"The idea that a complete classification must limit itself to lawful, noble, or theoretically pure objects is false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX4","text":"The idea that antiquity can speak immediately to the Christian without rhetorical and doctrinal mediation is false.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5","text":"The idea that the Word understood as wisdom exhausts Christ is false, since the incarnation and passion constitute a difference that cannot be absorbed.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Negative","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Deep Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1","text":"No human practice must remain without a place in the Theatro, because the absence of placement is treated as a lacuna in order itself.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX2","text":"No political order can tolerate non-participation in shame and justice, because the subject lacking both is constructed as «peste de la città» and expelled from the number of the living.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX3","text":"No symbolically ordered knowledge can remain external to figural mediation, since even science, law, commerce, craftsmanship, and religion become thinkable in the system only as contents of images.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX4","text":"No profane universality of knowledge can close itself upon itself, because Christian fullness requires an incarnative event that exceeds wisdom, word, and the classical repertoire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics"},{"number":"8","name":"Formal Generative Schema","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS1","text":"Natural indigence → Promethean theft → acquisition of fire, ingenuity, and arts → incomplete human survival.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS2","text":"Defensive aggregation → reciprocal conflict → insufficiency of the material city alone → universal distribution of shame and justice → sanctioned civil order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS3","text":"Mythological figure → functional analogy → collection of practices and forms of knowledge → articulation into affiliations and chains → encyclopedic memory.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS4","text":"Generality of Prometheus → inclusion of noble, vile, civil, and military arts → closure of the seventh degree without elevation of the Theatro.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0050","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS5","text":"Lacuna between ancient repertoire and present need → symbolic and rhetorical accommodation → integration of new customs and Christian matter → reservation of the incarnation against reduction to wisdom alone.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"From","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema"},{"number":"9","name":"Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AF1","text":"Original human deprivation → Promethean technical invention → insufficiency of technical life → universal gift of shame and justice → stabilization of the city.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AF2","text":"Mythic genealogy of faculties → Prometheus as genus of the arts → planetary images as classificatory nodes → distribution of forms of knowledge in the seventh degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AF3","text":"Claim to completeness → inclusion of noble, ignoble, coercive, and vicious practices → elimination of gaps in the repertoire.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0053","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:AF4","text":"Distance between antiquity and the present → accommodation to modern customs → use of the Ciceronian heritage → Christological delimitation of what is translatable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"10","name":"Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME1","text":"The distinction between nature and art is reorganized: art appears as a compensatory condition of humanity rather than as an accidental supplement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Composite","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME2","text":"The distinction between technical knowledge and political order becomes visible as a constitutive separation between living and coexisting.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME3","text":"The distinction between noble art and vile art ceases to be a criterion of exclusion and becomes an internal criterion of placement.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0002","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0032","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME4","text":"Mythological images cease to function merely as narrative ornaments and become indexing operators for domains of knowledge.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME5","text":"The relation between ancient and modern is reclassified as one of controlled adaptation, not of antiquarian fidelity nor of integral substitution.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ME6","text":"The Christian religion is situated both within and beyond the classical repertoire: translatable at the rhetorical level, irreducible at the level of incarnation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Map-Effects"},{"number":"11","name":"Altitude Levels","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT1","text":"Surface — The text assigns to Prometheus and subordinate images determinate series of arts, trades, forms of knowledge, institutions, and practices.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT2","text":"Structural — The text distinguishes the circuit of technique from the circuit of citizenship and makes universal justice the condition for the preservation of the city.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0012","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT3","text":"Metastrategic — The text converts myth into a technology of mnemonic ordering, capable of absorbing heterogeneous materials by means of symbols and partitions.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT4","text":"Ontological/Temporal — Man is conceived as a being naturally deficient, artificially compensated, and historically in need of retranslating inherited repertoires.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT5","text":"Theological — The system presupposes that the language of wisdom can be reused Christianly but cannot annul the difference of the incarnation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Altitude Levels"},{"number":"12","name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT1","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage from human vulnerability to the necessity of the arts and from technique to the necessity of civil order.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT2","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the function of Prometheus as a general principle for gathering the arts in the seventh degree.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Direct","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT3","text":"The rigorous criterion assigning each art to a particular figure remains underdetermined, since many associations operate through contingent analogy or allegorical authority.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0017","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0024","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0046","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"medium","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT4","text":"The structure is coherent in distinguishing the differential distribution of arts from the universality of civic virtues.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0019","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT5","text":"The structure depends on an unresolved tension between the claim to total order and the necessity of contingent accommodations to include later, modern, or marginal objects.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT6","text":"The structure depends on a second tension between the rhetorical translatability of Christianity into the classical repertoire and the doctrinal irreducibility of the incarnation.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Tension","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]},{"id":"CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT7","text":"The reconstruction preserves the text's actual movement if it keeps anthropological genealogy, political foundation, mnemonic classification, and confessional adaptation inseparable.","refs":[],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0005","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0006","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0010","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0011","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0015","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0025","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0039","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0042","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"},{"id":"RAW_LIDT_PROM:P0043","trace_type":"Structural","confidence":"high","alignment_provenance":"frozen-grounding"}]}],"original_name":"Minimal Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CH_LIDT_PROM@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CH_LIDT_PROM:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CH","kicker":"Chapter 07","title":"Prometheo.","context":"Chapter 07"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 01–03","order":1,"parents":["CH_LIDT_LIDT","CH_LIDT_ILCO","CH_LIDT_LANT"],"revision":"CL_LIDT_01@R001","sha256":"c7f3e8feebd0a6fff98071bba760d70291dd3ec92c9f9860cd97ef218a8bd222","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-01","text":"Il problema sistemico è rendere il molteplice integralmente indirizzabile dalla memoria senza convertire l’eccedenza divina in contenuto trasparente né proliferare indefinitamente i segni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS1","CH_LIDT_LANT:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-02","text":"Il Teatro opera come trasduttore bidirezionale: converte la gerarchia causale in immagini ordinate e riapre dalle immagini una risalita verso i principi invisibili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-03","text":"L’argomentazione diventa una macchina teologico-cosmologica, semiotica e tassonomica che subordina domini eterogenei a una sola architettura di causalità e recupero.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD3","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-04","text":"Il movimento è ricorsivo e spiraliforme: ogni ritorno della stessa figura sotto una nuova posizione modifica la funzione, amplia la copertura e riduce il carico mnemonico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7","CH_LIDT_LANT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-05","text":"La chiusura è simultaneamente cristologica e apofatica: lo Spirito garantisce la coesione dinamica del creato, mentre il non ancora saputo impedisce alla totalità classificata di diventare trasparenza esaustiva.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD3","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] L’ordine sopraceleste ed esemplare precede causalmente le realtà create e ne rende possibile tanto la formazione quanto la classificazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Il sensibile comunica il divino soltanto mediante veli, immagini, ombre ed effetti che indicano senza esaurire.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Il Teatro traduce l’ordine causale in un’architettura spaziale di pianeti, porte, gradi e immagini capace di organizzare il recupero mnemonico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS5","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] I pianeti mutano da segni accessibili delle misure superiori a coordinate generali per distribuire classi naturali, dottrinali e operative.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] L’immagine passa dalla corrispondenza polivalente alla funzione posizionale: il suo significato dipende dall’intersezione fra principio, luogo, volume e grado.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] La materia e la natura inferiori non costituiscono un ordine autonomo, ma ricevono forma, capacità e intelligibilità attraverso mediazioni superiori.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Generazione e corruzione vengono ricodificate come manifestazione, occultamento, composizione e dissoluzione, non come produzione e annientamento assoluti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] Un inventario finito di figure può sostenere una copertura estesa del sapere mediante variazione posizionale, volumi interni e divisioni tassonomiche.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:AS1","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Una medesima categoria può essere trasdotta fra cosa naturale, determinazione umana, operazione spontanea e arte senza perdere la propria continuità strutturale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:D3","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Il conoscere valido consiste nella risalita ordinata dai segni sensibili alle cause che essi conservano e occultano.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] Lo Spirito di Cristo chiude il sistema causale conciliando i contrari e rendendo possibili generazione, stabilità e rinnovazione dei composti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] L’assenza di conoscenza non resta esterna al sistema, ma viene localizzata come riserva di scibili e segreti non ancora disponibili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD6","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-01","text":"[Identità stabile] La priorità delle Idee e delle misure divine permane come fondamento della formazione, della permanenza e dell’ordinamento delle cose inferiori.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-02","text":"[Ricorrenza funzionale] L’immagine ricorre prima come velo dell’eccedenza e poi come contenitore tassonomico; conserva la mediazione ma cambia operazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","CH_LIDT_LANT:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-03","text":"[Mutazione] Il pianeta cessa di essere soltanto segno sensibile del sopraceleste e diventa coordinata produttiva per l’ordinamento generale del sapere.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-04","text":"[Spostamento] Il mito migra dalla funzione di repertorio subordinato alla funzione tecnica di operatore d’indicizzazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME5","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-05","text":"[Intensificazione] La memoria passa da un insieme di luoghi stabili a una matrice combinatoria capace di espandere il sapere senza moltiplicare le figure.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-06","text":"[Rovesciamento] Morte e corruzione perdono la valenza di cessazione assoluta e diventano occultamento della vita o dissoluzione di una configurazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-07","text":"[Assorbimento] L’esclusione dell’uomo dal catalogo dei misti prepara il suo riassorbimento superiore come luogo di trasposizione antropologica, operativa e artificiale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-08","text":"[Trasformazione terminale] La restrizione iniziale della rivelazione diventa una riserva interna di luoghi per segreti e conoscenze non ancora disponibili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-01","text":"[Locale] Saphiroth, Gamone e Rachia restano articolazioni specifiche del livello inferiore; a questa scala convergono nella funzione comune di mediare fra principio superiore e molteplicità formata.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-02","text":"[Esteso] La priorità epistemica delle cause e la natura segnica del sensibile attraversano tutte le articolazioni e diventano una regola globale di intelligibilità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:D4","CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-03","text":"[Ponte] Lo schema planetario collega cosmologia, memoria e tassonomia convertendo la mediazione celeste in criterio stabile di collocazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-04","text":"[Catalizzatore] La distinzione fra produzione interna ed esterna fornisce il fondamento metafisico che la conciliazione cristologica trasforma in dinamica dei misti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS2","CH_LIDT_LANT:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-05","text":"[Ricodificato] Il modello di un significato fisso dell’immagine viene superato dalla semantica della collocazione e del riuso differenziale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7","CH_LIDT_LANT:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-06","text":"[Ricodificato] Purezza elementare e morte assoluta diventano modelli obsoleti rispetto a una natura composta di misture temporanee e dissoluzioni non annientanti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A4","CH_LIDT_LANT:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-01","text":"Il sacro non ammette esposizione integralmente letterale né presenza immediata entro il sapere sensibile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-02","text":"L’accumulazione degli effetti e i criteri interni al sensibile non bastano a produrre conoscenza causale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-03","text":"La materia non è coeterna né capace di formarsi, vivificarsi o sostenersi autonomamente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-04","text":"Nessun segno teatrale possiede un significato autosufficiente e indipendente dalla collocazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX2","CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-05","text":"Il mito non costituisce una sfera narrativa autonoma e non deve essere assunto come cronaca letterale del divino.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX7","CH_LIDT_LANT:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-06","text":"Il sapere non forma un’enciclopedia orizzontale né un archivio neutrale di arti, immagini e discipline.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-07","text":"Il mondo inferiore non contiene elementi empiricamente puri né consente che la dissoluzione individuale equivalga a non-essere assoluto.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:NX5","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-01","text":"Deve essere falso che una proposizione o un’immagine possa contenere integralmente il principio che manifesta.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-02","text":"Deve essere falso che l’universale e l’ordine intelligibile derivino esclusivamente dall’astrazione posteriore degli effetti sensibili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-03","text":"Deve essere falso che il soggetto fondi autonomamente il sapere attraverso virtù o potenza intellettuale proprie.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX6","CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-04","text":"Deve essere falso che cosmologia, antropologia, operazione e arte costituiscano domini ontologicamente indipendenti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD3","CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-05","text":"Il sistema deve negare che le collocazioni siano radicalmente arbitrarie, benché la pretesa necessità cosmica ceda localmente alla convenzione e al bisogno mnemonico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT6","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSA-01","text":"La possibilità indisponibile che organizza il sistema è il possesso immediato e amministrabile della divinità da parte dell’intelletto umano.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSA-02","text":"L’inclassificabile assoluto è reso inammissibile, ma il non ancora saputo sopravvive come casella vuota interna alla classificazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSA-03","text":"Il non-essere assoluto è ontologicamente indisponibile: può cessare la legatura individuale, non la continuità dei suoi principi.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSA-04","text":"Una totalità simultaneamente pubblica, letterale, esaustiva e non profanatrice resta impossibile; il sistema può soltanto localizzare i propri residui di opacità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX2","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-01","text":"L’opacità simbolica diventa una condizione positiva di indirizzabilità: ciò che non può essere espresso direttamente può tuttavia ricevere posizione, figura e riserva classificatoria.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-02","CL_LIDT_01:GA-05","CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-02","text":"La discesa ontologica e la risalita mnemonica formano un solo circuito: il Teatro codifica la derivazione delle cose e consente di percorrerla inversamente.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-01","CL_LIDT_01:GA-03","CL_LIDT_01:GA-10","CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2","CH_LIDT_LANT:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-03","text":"La semantica teatrale non è lessicale ma coordinativa: una figura significa attraverso il nodo formato da pianeta, posizione, volume e registro di trasposizione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-04","CL_LIDT_01:GA-05","CL_LIDT_01:GA-08","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-04","text":"L’identità durevole viene trasferita dall’individuo materiale all’esemplare, alla specie e alla configurazione formale che può manifestarsi in composti successivi.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-01","CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_01:GA-07","CH_LIDT_ILCO:D1","CH_LIDT_LANT:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-05","text":"Il sistema può rivendicare copertura universale senza possesso esaustivo perché converte l’ignoto in una posizione disponibile per espansioni future.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-08","CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD6","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-06","text":"La tassonomia presuppone un’ontologia dinamica: le categorie naturali sono classificabili perché lo Spirito rende temporaneamente coesistenti qualità contrarie nella materia.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_01:GA-07","CL_LIDT_01:GA-11","CH_LIDT_LANT:AS6","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-07","text":"I pianeti costituiscono lo strato d’interfaccia fra misure sopracelesti e classificazione inferiore, unendo accessibilità sensibile e capacità distributiva.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-03","CL_LIDT_01:GA-04","CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-01","text":"La memoria diventa un motore inferenziale: recuperare un elemento significa ricostruirne posizione, dipendenze causali e possibilità di trasposizione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME5","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-02","text":"La realtà viene resa indirizzabile come sistema di trasformazioni coordinate, non come collezione di sostanze o discipline isolate.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-03","text":"Il significato diventa relazionale e spaziale: la collocazione non accompagna il contenuto, ma contribuisce a costituirlo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-04","text":"Il soggetto conoscente viene riclassificato come navigatore decentrato di un ordine preesistente, non come produttore sovrano dei principi.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-05","text":"Il tempo si divide fra eternità degli esemplari, alterazione dei composti e regimi planetari distinti di misura, mutazione e successione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-06","text":"L’accessibilità dell’interfaccia non universalizza il possesso del significato: apertura spettacolare e restrizione spirituale coesistono come politica strutturale della trasmissione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-07","text":"L’unità metodologica non deriva da un criterio dimostrativo comune, ma dalla sincronizzazione operativa di autorità eterogenee entro la macchina delle corrispondenze.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT5","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-01","text":"La discesa da Dio alle immagini e la risalita dalle immagini al principio costituiscono il circuito ricorsivo fondamentale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-02","text":"Il circuito immagine–posizione–volume–divisione consente a ogni figura di riaprirsi in classificazioni ulteriori senza richiedere nuovi segni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS4","CH_LIDT_LANT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-03","text":"L’intensificazione procede dalla cosa naturale alla disposizione umana, quindi all’operazione e infine all’arte, trasformando una categoria in una matrice transdominio.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:D3","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-04","text":"L’attrattore nascosto è l’unità divina anteriore alla molteplicità, verso cui convergono causalità, rappresentazione e classificazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-05","text":"Il passaggio dai pianeti-segni ai pianeti-coordinate costituisce un cambiamento di fase: la mediazione contemplativa diventa infrastruttura classificatoria.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-06","text":"Il circuito vitale procede per formazione, mistura, rinnovazione e dissoluzione, restituendo la materia a nuove configurazioni senza annientarla.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD5","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-07","text":"L’ignoto alimenta un circuito espansivo: l’assenza riceve una sede, la sede autorizza future integrazioni e l’integrazione preserva l’aspirazione alla totalità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD6","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B01","text":"Eccedenza divina → insufficienza del linguaggio → necessità del velo figurale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B02","text":"Dio → Verbo → Idee → spirito → materia → forme → specie → individui → immagini.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B03","text":"Influsso sopraceleste → attenuazione mediatrice → natura planetaria → ripartizione delle classi inferiori.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B04","text":"Categoria → immagine mitica → posizione planetaria → volume concettuale → divisioni tassonomiche.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:AS4","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B05","text":"Figura ricorrente + nuova collocazione → nuova funzione semantica → trasduzione fra natura, uomo, operazione e arte.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS4","CH_LIDT_LANT:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B06","text":"Recupero mnemonico → risalita all’invisibile → dipendenza dalla grazia → chiusura cristologica senza trasparenza totale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS6","CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS7","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AFM-B01","text":"Eccedenza divina → velo simbolico → gerarchia causale → mediazione planetaria → codifica teatrale → trasduzione dei domini → risalita mnemonica → limite apofatico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF5","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AFM-B02","text":"Materia derivata → influsso vivificante → mistura → stabilità individuale temporanea → dissoluzione → disponibilità per nuove formazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD5","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-01","text":"La distinzione fra tecnica mnemonica e ontologia crolla: la memoria diventa l’interfaccia operativa della causalità cosmica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME2","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-02","text":"La distinzione fra contenuto e collocazione crolla: lo spazio teatrale entra nella costituzione del significato.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:ME3","CH_LIDT_LANT:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-03","text":"Teologia, mito, cosmologia, natura e arte vengono riclassificati come registri subordinati e trasformativi di una sola matrice.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-04","text":"La natura empirica diventa un campo di misture, forme e accidenti, non un inventario di elementi puri.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:ME5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-05","text":"L’uomo appare simultaneamente distinto dal catalogo naturale e capace di trasporne le categorie in operazioni, arti e istituzioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD4","CH_LIDT_LANT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-06","text":"La totalità diventa indicizzabile senza diventare trasparente: persino ciò che manca riceve una posizione strutturale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B01","text":"Al livello di superficie, il sistema dispone colonne, porte, gradi, Antri, immagini e volumi entro una geometria planetaria.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT1","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B02","text":"Al livello strutturale, la geometria visibile coordina ordine sopraceleste, ordine celeste, natura inferiore e matrice tassonomica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT2","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B03","text":"Al livello metastrategico, l’accesso al sapere viene ridefinito come navigazione regolata fra occultamento, posizione e compressione mnemonica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT3","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B04","text":"Al livello ontologico e temporale, esemplari eterni governano composti sottoposti a influsso, alterazione, durata temporanea e dissoluzione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B05","text":"Al livello metodologico e performativo, la forma ricorsiva mette in atto la propria tesi riutilizzando figure identiche per produrre funzioni differenti e copertura crescente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-01","text":"L’apertura spettacolare del Teatro agli studiosi resta in tensione con la restrizione del sapere autentico ai destinatari resi degni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-02","text":"La necessità cosmica delle assegnazioni entra in tensione con il loro carattere pragmatico, convenzionale o imposto dall’economia mnemonica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT6","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-03","text":"La validità del sistema dipende dall’assimilazione non dimostrata fra corrispondenza simbolica, impronta epistemica e derivazione ontologica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-04","text":"La chiusura unitaria della macchina convive con un montaggio di autorità eterogenee privo di un criterio generale di arbitraggio.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT5","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-05","text":"La pretesa di classificabilità universale coesiste con scibili non saputi e segreti indisponibili, rendendo la totalità strutturalmente incompleta.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MP-01","text":"Il pianeta muta da segno contemplativo del sopraceleste a coordinata generale della tassonomia.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MP-02","text":"L’immagine muta da velo rappresentativo a operatore d’indicizzazione, senza perdere la propria funzione mediatrice.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MP-03","text":"La corruzione oscilla fra occultamento della vita, deterioramento materiale e dissoluzione della configurazione individuale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT6","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MP-04","text":"L’anima del mondo viene respinta come causa autonoma, ma la sua funzione mediatrice riappare nel veicolo cosmico mosso dallo Spirito.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:NX11","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:HSI-01","text":"La realtà è implicitamente una macchina di trasduzione annidata, nella quale ogni livello riceve, attenua, forma e ritrasmette la causalità superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:HSI-02","text":"Il soggetto è un lettore-operatore decentrato: distinto dagli oggetti classificati, ma dipendente dall’ordine che percorre e trasforma.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD4","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:HSI-03","text":"Il tempo combina eternità esemplare, successione planetaria, mutazione materiale e ricomposizione non annientante.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:HSI-04","text":"L’azione possibile non è il possesso dell’origine, ma la navigazione disciplinata di veli, posizioni e trasformazioni che comprimono il sapere senza abolirne il segreto.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B01","text":"Gli assiomi estratti sono sufficienti a ricostruire il passaggio dalla segretezza teologica alla matrice planetaria e alla trasposizione fra natura, uomo, operazione e arte.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT1","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B02","text":"Restano sottodeterminate le assegnazioni locali delle immagini, le divisioni complete dei volumi e i segmenti testuali non leggibili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT2","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B03","text":"Il sistema è coerente a questa scala se il simbolo resta mediazione non esaustiva e la posizione viene accettata come principio semantico-causale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT3","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B04","text":"L’architettura è più forte nella conversione dell’ordine totale di causalità in un’interfaccia mnemonica capace di collegare ontologia, tassonomia e recupero.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT4","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B05","text":"La ricostruzione dipende dalla compressione di autorità eterogenee e dall’omissione di un criterio unitario che ne risolva i conflitti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT5","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B06","text":"Resistono alla riduzione assiomatica la dipendenza dalla grazia, il tempo della rivelazione e la riserva di segreti non ancora disponibili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B07","text":"La ricostruzione preserva il movimento effettivo soltanto mantenendo inseparabili segretezza, gerarchia causale, mediazione figurale, mutazione posizionale e chiusura cristologica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT8","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T231140520414Z_5c91dbe1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 01–03","source_sha256":"c7f3e8feebd0a6fff98071bba760d70291dd3ec92c9f9860cd97ef218a8bd222","sha256":"de20448ce847decbbafbe36909007c22fa048e992ea41951895c387bff8a8123","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:11:40.523151+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-01","text":"The systemic problem is to make the multiple fully addressable by memory without converting divine excess into transparent content or indefinitely proliferating signs.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS1","CH_LIDT_LANT:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-02","text":"The Theatre operates as a bidirectional transducer: it converts the causal hierarchy into ordered images and reopens, from the images, an ascent toward invisible principles.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-03","text":"The argument becomes a theological-cosmological, semiotic, and taxonomic machine that subordinates heterogeneous domains to a single architecture of causality and retrieval.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD3","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-04","text":"The movement is recursive and spiral-shaped: each return of the same figure under a new position modifies its function, broadens coverage, and reduces mnemonic load.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7","CH_LIDT_LANT:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AS-05","text":"The closure is simultaneously Christological and apophatic: the Spirit guarantees the dynamic cohesion of creation, while what is not yet known prevents the classified totality from becoming exhaustive transparency.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD3","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] The supracelestial and exemplary order causally precedes created realities and makes possible both their formation and their classification.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The sensible communicates the divine only through veils, images, shadows, and effects that indicate without exhausting.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] The Theatre translates causal order into a spatial architecture of planets, gates, degrees, and images capable of organizing mnemonic retrieval.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS5","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] The planets change from accessible signs of higher measures into general coordinates for distributing natural, doctrinal, and operative classes.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] The image passes from polyvalent correspondence to positional function: its meaning depends on the intersection between principle, place, volume, and degree.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A10","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","text":"[Persistent] Lower matter and nature do not constitute an autonomous order, but receive form, capacity, and intelligibility through higher mediations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Generation and corruption are recoded as manifestation, concealment, composition, and dissolution, not as absolute production and annihilation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:A16"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-08","text":"[Emergent] A finite inventory of figures can sustain extensive coverage of knowledge through positional variation, internal volumes, and taxonomic divisions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:AS1","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] One and the same category can be transduced between natural thing, human determination, spontaneous operation, and art without losing its structural continuity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:D3","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] Valid knowing consists in the ordered ascent from sensible signs to the causes that they preserve and conceal.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-11","text":"[Terminal] The Spirit of Christ closes the causal system by reconciling contraries and making possible generation, stability, and renewal of composites.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] The absence of knowledge does not remain external to the system, but is localized as a reserve of knowables and secrets not yet available.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD6","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-01","text":"[Stable identity] The priority of Ideas and divine measures remains as the foundation of the formation, persistence, and ordering of lower things.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-02","text":"[Functional recurrence] The image recurs first as a veil of excess and then as a taxonomic container; it retains mediation but changes operation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","CH_LIDT_LANT:AS4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-03","text":"[Mutation] The planet ceases to be merely a sensible sign of the supracelestial and becomes a productive coordinate for the general ordering of knowledge.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-04","text":"[Displacement] Myth migrates from the function of a subordinate repertoire to the technical function of an indexing operator.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME5","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-05","text":"[Intensification] Memory passes from a set of stable places to a combinatorial matrix capable of expanding knowledge without multiplying figures.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-06","text":"[Reversal] Death and corruption lose the value of absolute cessation and become concealment of life or dissolution of a configuration.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-07","text":"[Absorption] The exclusion of man from the catalogue of mixtures prepares his higher reabsorption as a site of anthropological, operative, and artificial transposition.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A5","CH_LIDT_LANT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RMD-08","text":"[Terminal transformation] The initial restriction of revelation becomes an internal reserve of places for secrets and knowledge not yet available.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-01","text":"[Local] Saphiroth, Gamone, and Rachia remain specific articulations of the lower level; at this scale, they converge in the common function of mediating between higher principle and formed multiplicity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A4","CH_LIDT_LANT:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-02","text":"[Extended] The epistemic priority of causes and the sign-character of the sensible traverse all articulations and become a global rule of intelligibility.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:D4","CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-03","text":"[Bridge] The planetary schema links cosmology, memory, and taxonomy by converting celestial mediation into a stable criterion of placement.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-04","text":"[Catalyst] The distinction between internal and external production provides the metaphysical foundation that Christological reconciliation transforms into the dynamics of mixtures.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:AS2","CH_LIDT_LANT:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-05","text":"[Recoded] The model of a fixed meaning of the image is superseded by the semantics of placement and differential reuse.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7","CH_LIDT_LANT:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:CGD-06","text":"[Recoded] Elemental purity and absolute death become obsolete models in relation to a nature composed of temporary mixtures and non-annihilating dissolutions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A4","CH_LIDT_LANT:NX12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-01","text":"The sacred admits neither wholly literal exposition nor immediate presence within sensible knowledge.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-02","text":"The accumulation of effects and criteria internal to the sensible do not suffice to produce causal knowledge.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-03","text":"Matter is neither coeternal nor capable of forming, vivifying, or sustaining itself autonomously.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-04","text":"No theatrical sign possesses a self-sufficient meaning independent of placement.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX2","CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-05","text":"Myth does not constitute an autonomous narrative sphere and must not be taken as a literal chronicle of the divine.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:NX7","CH_LIDT_LANT:NX9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-06","text":"Knowledge does not form a horizontal encyclopedia or a neutral archive of arts, images, and disciplines.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:GNX-07","text":"The lower world contains no empirically pure elements, nor does it allow individual dissolution to be equivalent to absolute non-being.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:NX5","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-01","text":"It must be false that a proposition or an image can contain in its entirety the principle that it manifests.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:DNX1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-02","text":"It must be false that the universal and intelligible order derive exclusively from the subsequent abstraction of sensible effects.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that the subject autonomously founds knowledge through its own virtue or intellectual power.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:NX6","CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that cosmology, anthropology, operation, and art constitute ontologically independent domains.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD3","CH_LIDT_LANT:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:DBN-05","text":"The system must deny that placements are radically arbitrary, although the claimed cosmic necessity locally yields to convention and mnemonic need.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT6","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSA-01","text":"The unavailable possibility that organizes the system is the immediate and manageable possession of divinity by the human intellect.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSA-02","text":"The absolute unclassifiable is rendered inadmissible, but what is not yet known survives as an empty slot internal to classification.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSA-03","text":"Absolute non-being is ontologically unavailable: the individual bond may cease, but not the continuity of its principles.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSA-04","text":"A totality simultaneously public, literal, exhaustive, and non-profane remains impossible; the system can only localize its own residues of opacity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX2","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-01","text":"Symbolic opacity becomes a positive condition of addressability: what cannot be expressed directly can nevertheless receive a position, figure, and classificatory reserve.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-02","CL_LIDT_01:GA-05","CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-02","text":"Ontological descent and mnemonic ascent form a single circuit: the Theatre encodes the derivation of things and makes it possible to traverse it inversely.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-01","CL_LIDT_01:GA-03","CL_LIDT_01:GA-10","CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2","CH_LIDT_LANT:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-03","text":"Theatrical semantics is not lexical but coordinative: a figure signifies through the node formed by planet, position, volume, and register of transposition.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-04","CL_LIDT_01:GA-05","CL_LIDT_01:GA-08","CH_LIDT_ILCO:A11","CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-04","text":"Durable identity is transferred from the material individual to the exemplar, the species, and the formal configuration that can manifest itself in successive composites.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-01","CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_01:GA-07","CH_LIDT_ILCO:D1","CH_LIDT_LANT:D8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-05","text":"The system can claim universal coverage without exhaustive possession because it converts the unknown into a position available for future expansions.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-08","CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD6","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-06","text":"Taxonomy presupposes a dynamic ontology: natural categories are classifiable because the Spirit makes contrary qualities temporarily coexist in matter.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_01:GA-07","CL_LIDT_01:GA-11","CH_LIDT_LANT:AS6","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:XD-07","text":"The planets constitute the interface layer between supracelestial measures and lower classification, joining sensible accessibility and distributive capacity.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-03","CL_LIDT_01:GA-04","CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-01","text":"Memory becomes an inferential engine: retrieving an element means reconstructing its position, causal dependencies, and possibilities of transposition.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME5","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-02","text":"Reality is made addressable as a system of coordinated transformations, not as a collection of isolated substances or disciplines.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-03","text":"Meaning becomes relational and spatial: placement does not accompany content, but contributes to constituting it.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-04","text":"The knowing subject is reclassified as a decentered navigator of a preexisting order, not as a sovereign producer of principles.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-05","text":"Time is divided between the eternity of exemplars, the alteration of composites, and distinct planetary regimes of measure, mutation, and succession.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-06","text":"The accessibility of the interface does not universalize possession of meaning: spectacular openness and spiritual restriction coexist as a structural politics of transmission.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:BSD-07","text":"Methodological unity derives not from a common demonstrative criterion, but from the operative synchronization of heterogeneous authorities within the machine of correspondences.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT5","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-01","text":"The descent from God to images and the ascent from images to the principle constitute the fundamental recursive circuit.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-02","text":"The image–position–volume–division circuit enables every figure to reopen into further classifications without requiring new signs.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:FGS4","CH_LIDT_LANT:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-03","text":"Intensification proceeds from the natural thing to human disposition, then to operation and finally to art, transforming a category into a cross-domain matrix.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:D3","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-04","text":"The hidden attractor is the divine unity anterior to multiplicity, toward which causality, representation, and classification converge.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A4","CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-05","text":"The passage from planets-as-signs to planets-as-coordinates constitutes a phase change: contemplative mediation becomes classificatory infrastructure.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-06","text":"The vital circuit proceeds through formation, mixture, renewal, and dissolution, returning matter to new configurations without annihilating it.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD5","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:RLE-07","text":"The unknown feeds an expansive circuit: absence receives a seat, the seat authorizes future integrations, and integration preserves the aspiration to totality.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD6","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B01","text":"Divine excess → insufficiency of language → necessity of the figural veil.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B02","text":"God → Word → Ideas → spirit → matter → forms → species → individuals → images.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B03","text":"Supracelestial influence → mediating attenuation → planetary nature → distribution of lower classes.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A3","CH_LIDT_LANT:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B04","text":"Category → mythical image → planetary position → conceptual volume → taxonomic divisions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:AS4","CH_LIDT_LANT:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B05","text":"Recurring figure + new placement → new semantic function → transduction between nature, man, operation, and art.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:FGS4","CH_LIDT_LANT:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B06","text":"Mnemonic retrieval → ascent to the invisible → dependence on grace → Christological closure without total transparency.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS6","CH_LIDT_LIDT:FGS7","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AFM-B01","text":"Divine excess → symbolic veil → causal hierarchy → planetary mediation → theatrical encoding → transduction of domains → mnemonic ascent → apophatic limit.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS5","CH_LIDT_ILCO:AF5","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:AFM-B02","text":"Derived matter → vivifying influence → mixture → temporary individual stability → dissolution → availability for new formations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD5","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-01","text":"The distinction between mnemonic technique and ontology collapses: memory becomes the operative interface of cosmic causality.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ME2","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-02","text":"The distinction between content and placement collapses: theatrical space enters into the constitution of meaning.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:ME3","CH_LIDT_LANT:NX8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-03","text":"Theology, myth, cosmology, nature, and art are reclassified as subordinate and transformative registers of a single matrix.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD3","CH_LIDT_ILCO:ME4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-04","text":"Empirical nature becomes a field of mixtures, forms, and accidents, not an inventory of pure elements.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:ME5","CH_LIDT_LANT:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-05","text":"Man appears simultaneously distinct from the natural catalogue and capable of transposing its categories into operations, arts, and institutions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD4","CH_LIDT_LANT:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MME-06","text":"Totality becomes indexable without becoming transparent: even what is missing receives a structural position.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, the system arranges columns, gates, degrees, Caves, images, and volumes within a planetary geometry.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT1","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, visible geometry coordinates supracelestial order, celestial order, lower nature, and taxonomic matrix.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT2","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, access to knowledge is redefined as regulated navigation among concealment, position, and mnemonic compression.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:ALT3","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological and temporal level, eternal exemplars govern composites subject to influence, alteration, temporary duration, and dissolution.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological and performative level, the recursive form enacts its own thesis by reusing identical figures to produce different functions and increasing coverage.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:A8","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-01","text":"The Theatre's spectacular openness to scholars remains in tension with the restriction of authentic knowledge to recipients rendered worthy.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-02","text":"The cosmic necessity of assignments enters into tension with their pragmatic, conventional, or mnemonic-economy-imposed character.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT6","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-03","text":"The validity of the system depends on the undemonstrated assimilation between symbolic correspondence, epistemic imprint, and ontological derivation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-04","text":"The unitary closure of the machine coexists with an assemblage of heterogeneous authorities lacking a general criterion of arbitration.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT5","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:FL-05","text":"The claim of universal classifiability coexists with unknown knowables and unavailable secrets, rendering totality structurally incomplete.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MP-01","text":"The planet changes from a contemplative sign of the supracelestial to a general coordinate of taxonomy.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A7","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MP-02","text":"The image changes from representational veil to indexing operator, without losing its mediating function.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:AS2","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MP-03","text":"Corruption oscillates between concealment of life, material deterioration, and dissolution of the individual configuration.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT6","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MP-04","text":"The soul of the world is rejected as an autonomous cause, but its mediating function reappears in the cosmic vehicle moved by the Spirit.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:NX11","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a nested transduction machine, in which each level receives, attenuates, forms, and retransmits higher causality.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1","CH_LIDT_ILCO:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a decentered reader-operator: distinct from classified objects, but dependent on the order that it traverses and transforms.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SD4","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:HSI-03","text":"Time combines exemplary eternity, planetary succession, material mutation, and non-annihilating recomposition.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:ALT4","CH_LIDT_LANT:ME8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:HSI-04","text":"Possible action is not possession of the origin, but the disciplined navigation of veils, positions, and transformations that compress knowledge without abolishing its secrecy.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:SNX1","CH_LIDT_LANT:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the passage from theological secrecy to the planetary matrix and to transposition between nature, man, operation, and art.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT1","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B02","text":"The local assignments of images, the complete divisions of volumes, and unreadable textual segments remain underdetermined.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT2","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B03","text":"The system is coherent at this scale if the symbol remains non-exhaustive mediation and position is accepted as a semantic-causal principle.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT3","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B04","text":"The architecture is strongest in converting the total order of causality into a mnemonic interface capable of linking ontology, taxonomy, and retrieval.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT4","CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT4","CH_LIDT_LANT:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction depends on the compression of heterogeneous authorities and on the omission of a unitary criterion that resolves their conflicts.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ILCO:MRT5","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B06","text":"Dependence on grace, the time of revelation, and the reserve of secrets not yet available resist axiomatic reduction.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:A6","CH_LIDT_LANT:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B07","text":"The reconstruction preserves the effective movement only by keeping secrecy, causal hierarchy, figural mediation, positional mutation, and Christological closure inseparable.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LIDT:MRT8","CH_LIDT_LANT:MRT9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_LIDT_01@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_LIDT_01:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · The Idea of the Theatre","title":"Chapters 01–03","context":"L’IDEA DEL THEATRO, DI MESSER GIVLIO Camillo. · Il Convivio. · L’Antro."},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 04–05","order":2,"parents":["CH_LIDT_LEGO","CH_LIDT_PASI"],"revision":"CL_LIDT_02@R001","sha256":"7684013434e7c49ad3afdfbbd84e76c58480cac486c8f03fbb92b50be740dcbe","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-01","text":"Il sistema deve rendere intelligibile come l’uomo interiore, dipendente da un’illuminazione divina, possa congiungersi al corpo e operare attraverso di esso senza ridursi alla corporeità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS1","CH_LIDT_PASI:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-02","text":"L’uomo emerge come struttura stratificata e ricettiva, costituita dall’interazione fra luce esterna, mediazione veicolare, corpo e orientamento morale, non come sostanza autosufficiente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-03","text":"L’argomentazione assume forma concordistica e simbolica, traducendo Scrittura, filosofia, mito e astrologia in registri convergenti di una medesima antropologia operativa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-04","text":"Il movimento procede dall’architettura interiore e dalla sua illuminazione alla discesa nel composto corporeo, convertendo infine la verticalità cosmologica in un archivio planetario delle facoltà e delle disposizioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-05","text":"La chiusura rimane condizionata e transitiva: la disposizione deve ancora diventare azione, mentre la ricongiunzione superiore richiede il superamento del vincolo corporeo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] L’identità umana è relazionale e ricettiva: dipende da principi, influssi e supporti che non possiede autonomamente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] Il corpo è simultaneamente strumento dell’operazione, medio dell’incarnazione, sede della cattura affettiva e ostacolo alla riunione superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Nessuna congiunzione decisiva è immediata: l’intellezione richiede una luce agente esterna e l’incarnazione richiede un veicolo intermedio.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] L’umanità non è garantita dalla figura corporea, ma varia secondo la partecipazione alla luce e l’uso della potenza concupiscibile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] La tripartizione interiore viene espansa in una tassonomia distribuita di facoltà, membra, passioni, condizioni e destini.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Il mito passa dall’occultamento mnemonico di una struttura intellettuale alla genealogia simbolica della discesa, della cupidità e della mostruosità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME5","CH_LIDT_PASI:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Le immagini planetarie costituiscono indirizzi mnemonici che rendono navigabile la distribuzione cosmica e antropologica delle facoltà.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] La trasformazione dipende prima dalla grazia e dall’illuminazione, quindi dall’attualizzazione operativa della disposizione, senza che i due regimi vengano pienamente conciliati.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD2","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Il Theatro trasduce una cosmologia verticale di discesa e ascesa in una superficie classificatoria orizzontale che ne conserva la direzionalità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] La macchina converge sulla liberazione dal radicamento affettivo e corporeo come condizione di un riallineamento ascendente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Il male viene interiorizzato come circuito di allineamento inferiore, concupiscenza e autoidolatria prima di manifestarsi nell’azione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] Il cluster termina distinguendo disposizione ed esercizio e rinvia al grado successivo il compimento effettivo della virtù o del vizio.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-01","text":"L’identità stabile del simbolo consiste nel non essere finzione ornamentale: esso vela, conserva e trasmette una struttura dottrinale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX9","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-02","text":"La ricorrenza funzionale della mediazione cambia direzione: la luce esterna rende possibile l’ascesa intellettuale, mentre il veicolo aereo rende possibile la discesa corporea.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-03","text":"Il corpo muta da strumento esterno dell’uomo interiore a complesso pluristratificato che consente l’incarnazione e prolunga la prigionia dell’anima.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D2","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-04","text":"La bestialità si intensifica da privazione contingente dell’illuminazione a processo morale temporalizzato attraverso inclinazione, compiacimento e azione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-05","text":"L’ordine planetario migra dall’indicizzazione delle facoltà interiori alla distribuzione di membra, passioni, condizioni sociali e destini.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","CH_LIDT_PASI:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-06","text":"La morte subisce una trasformazione terminale: dalla recisione simbolica degli affetti passa alla dissoluzione corporea e veicolare richiesta dalla ricongiunzione celeste.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-07","text":"La figura delle Gorgoni scompare come contenuto dominante dopo aver condensato la dipendenza dalla luce; la sua funzione viene assorbita dal Minotauro come condensazione ibrida e reversibile della mediazione degradata.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D9","CH_LIDT_PASI:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-01","text":"Restano locali al quarto grado la nomenclatura Nephes–Ruach–Nessamah e l’occhio condiviso delle Gorgoni come formalizzazione specifica della triplicità interiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-02","text":"Restano locali al quinto grado il veicolo aereo, Pasiphe e il Minotauro come genealogia specifica della congiunzione fra anima desiderante e corporeità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-03","text":"Si estende al livello corrente la negazione del soggetto autosufficiente, perché tanto l’intellezione quanto l’incarnazione dipendono da condizioni esterne o intermedie.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-04","text":"Il simbolismo mitico e la distribuzione planetaria collegano le unità traducendo strutture invisibili in coordinate mnemoniche ordinabili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-05","text":"Il passaggio dall’ordinamento delle facoltà interiori alla classificazione dell’uomo corporeamente rivestito catalizza la transizione fra quarto e quinto grado.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS6","CH_LIDT_PASI:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-06","text":"L’opposizione semplice fra interiorità e corpo viene ricodificata in una serie di mediazioni corporee con funzioni simultaneamente operative, mnemoniche e carcerarie.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_PASI:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-07","text":"La distinzione fra inclinazione ed esercizio funziona da soglia terminale del cluster e rende obsoleta ogni classificazione morale fondata sulla sola disposizione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-01","text":"L’uomo non coincide con il corpo né la figura umana garantisce che il composto partecipi effettivamente dell’ordine divino.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX1","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-02","text":"Né l’intellezione né il movimento dell’anima sono potenze autonome esercitabili senza illuminazione o supporto veicolare.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX5","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-03","text":"La congiunzione fra spirituale e corporeo non è diretta, perché richiede termini medi ontologicamente partecipi dei poli congiunti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:NX2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-04","text":"La forma umana, l’inclinazione e la conoscenza della virtù non equivalgono rispettivamente a umanità interiore, vizio esercitato o vita virtuosa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX6","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-05","text":"La favola non è né racconto letterale né ornamento arbitrario, ma una delimitazione operativa dell’accesso alla dottrina.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX9","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-06","text":"Il corpo non può essere definito univocamente come bene, male o supporto neutro, poiché rende possibile l’operazione e produce simultaneamente cattura.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-01","text":"Deve essere falsa ogni ontologia del soggetto come centro chiuso, proprietario della propria luce, delle proprie opere e del proprio movimento.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX1","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-02","text":"Deve essere falsa l’efficacia immediata: conoscere, incarnarsi, ricordare e ascendere richiedono sempre influssi, veicoli, immagini o trasformazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX2","CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-03","text":"Deve essere falsa la fissità delle identità ontologiche e morali, poiché bestialità, angelicità, vizio e virtù dipendono da allineamenti e attualizzazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX3","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-04","text":"Deve essere falsa la localizzazione esclusivamente esterna del male, perché la cattura inferiore culmina nell’idolo installato dentro il soggetto.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-05","text":"Deve essere falsa la neutralità del dispositivo mnemonico: l’archivio simbolico non registra soltanto l’uomo, ma ne organizza le possibilità di orientamento e trasformazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-01","text":"L’assenza strutturante è quella di una conciliazione integra e durevole fra corpo vivente, liberazione dagli affetti e vera unione celeste.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-02","text":"La possibilità indisponibile è l’autogenerazione del bene: la disposizione, il sapere e la volontà non possono produrre autonomamente illuminazione o virtù attuosa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX2","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-03","text":"Per l’anima umana è inammissibile una pura efficacia disincarnata, ma il supporto corporeo necessario al movimento diventa anche ciò che impedisce l’unione finale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A1","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-04","text":"È impossibile una verità simultaneamente profonda, totalmente trasparente, indiscriminatamente accessibile e immune dalla profanazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX5","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-05","text":"Il sistema ruota attorno all’assenza di un’umanità intrinseca e stabilmente posseduta, sostituita da una condizione sempre esposta alla ricezione o alla degradazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX1","CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-01","text":"Il soggetto è doppiamente eccentrico: riceve dall’esterno il principio della propria intellezione e acquisisce mediante un veicolo la possibilità della propria incorporazione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-01","CL_LIDT_02:GA-03","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-02","text":"Il corpo costituisce la cerniera produttivamente contraddittoria del sistema, perché rende possibile l’operazione mondana e rende necessaria la successiva liberazione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-02","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D2","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-03","text":"La bestialità non designa una specie separata, ma un processo che comincia con la mancata partecipazione alla luce e si determina nell’uso effettivo delle facoltà inferiori.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-04","CL_LIDT_02:GA-08","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-04","text":"L’opacità simbolica e l’accessibilità mnemonica non sono funzioni opposte: la dottrina viene resa trasmissibile precisamente attraverso il velamento che ne regola l’accesso.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-06","CL_LIDT_02:GA-07","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-05","text":"L’azione è necessaria alla virtù ma non basta a fondarne l’autorialità, poiché il sistema attribuisce a Dio la causalità superiore delle opere.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-08","CL_LIDT_02:GA-12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-06","text":"Il Theatro opera come trasduttore: converte gerarchie ontologiche verticali in una superficie spaziale capace di archiviare e riattivare il composto umano.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-05","CL_LIDT_02:GA-09","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-07","text":"La conversione non coincide con un unico evento, ma articola grazia, distruzione dell’idolo, esercizio operativo e dissoluzione del vincolo corporeo.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-10","CL_LIDT_02:GA-11","CL_LIDT_02:GA-12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D6","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-01","text":"Ontologicamente, l’uomo diventa una pila di ricezioni e veicoli nella quale nessuno strato isolato può rivendicare l’identità dell’intero.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-02","text":"Temporalmente, l’esistenza assume la forma discesa–incorporazione–disposizione–azione–mortificazione–dissoluzione, sostituendo alla natura statica una sequenza trasformativa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD5","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD3","CH_LIDT_PASI:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-03","text":"Epistemicamente, la razionalità cessa di essere proprietà naturale e la conoscenza dottrinale diventa ricezione indicizzata da dispositivi simbolici.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME2","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-04","text":"Eticamente, la responsabilità si situa nell’attualizzazione di disposizioni non auto-prodotte, entro un campo condizionato da grazia, influssi e corrispondenze astrali.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-05","text":"Politicamente, la lotta contro l’idolo interno può essere estesa dalla cura del soggetto alla famiglia e alla repubblica perché tutti questi domini sono collocati nella medesima grammatica classificatoria.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A13","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-06","text":"Metodologicamente, l’analogia diventa un operatore costitutivo che comprime antropologia, cosmologia, fisiologia e morale, pur lasciando indimostrata la piena equivalenza dei loro lessici.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT8","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-01","text":"La luce esterna produce orientamento, l’orientamento viene archiviato in immagini e l’archivio mnemonico rende nuovamente disponibile la struttura dell’orientamento.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD2","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-02","text":"L’allineamento inferiore alimenta un circuito di concupiscenza, bestializzazione e azione che consolida ulteriormente la cattura nel corpo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-03","text":"Il corpo genera il circuito più instabile: permette l’operazione, suscita cupidità, rafforza il vincolo e rende necessaria la propria trasformazione o dissoluzione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D2","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-04","text":"L’esposizione dottrinale ritorna come favola, la favola diventa indice mnemonico e l’indice permette di riattivare ciò che era stato ricoperto.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-05","text":"La discesa verticale viene spazializzata nel Theatro e la navigazione orizzontale del Theatro rende nuovamente leggibile la direzione della discesa e dell’ascesa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-06","text":"L’attrattore terminale è la ricongiunzione celeste, raggiungibile non evitando le mediazioni ma attraversandole, convertendole e infine dissolvendone i residui.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D6","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-07","text":"Il passaggio dall’occhio delle Gorgoni al Minotauro segna un cambiamento di fase dalla dipendenza cognitiva da una luce condivisa alla produzione corporea di una forma ibrida da convertire.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D9","CH_LIDT_PASI:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B01","text":"Immagine divina ricevuta → costituzione dell’uomo interiore → soggetto aperto a principi non posseduti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B02","text":"Capacità intellettuale → intervento della luce agente esterna → umanità intellettuale condizionale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B03","text":"Incompatibilità fra anima ignea e corpo terreno → produzione del veicolo aereo → possibilità dell’incarnazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A2","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B04","text":"Orientamento verso il polo inferiore → concupiscenza corporea → composizione ibrida e bestializzazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_PASI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B05","text":"Struttura invisibile → condensazione mitica → distribuzione planetaria → archivio di facoltà, membra e condizioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B06","text":"Grazia e distruzione dell’idolo → disposizione superiore → esercizio nelle opere → virtù attuosa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B07","text":"Recisione degli affetti → dissoluzione corporea e veicolare → possibilità, non garanzia, della riunione celeste.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:AFM-B01","text":"Immagine divina ricevuta → tripartizione interiore → illuminazione esterna → mediazione veicolare → incorporazione desiderante → distribuzione planetaria → disposizione morale → esercizio differito → mortificazione e dissoluzione → ricongiunzione celeste condizionata.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS4","CH_LIDT_PASI:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:AFM-B02","text":"Dottrina esplicita → ricopertura mitica → indirizzamento planetario → riattivazione mnemonica → discriminazione degli allineamenti → conversione operativa → nuova disponibilità alla luce superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","CH_LIDT_PASI:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-01","text":"L’uomo viene riclassificato da composto bipartito a rete stratificata di anima, facoltà, luce, veicolo, corpo e influssi.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME1","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-02","text":"La corporeità viene sottratta all’opposizione semplice fra strumento e carcere e ridefinita come medio che produce entrambe le funzioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-03","text":"La mappa morale distingue ora natura, inclinazione, allineamento, esercizio e trasformazione, facendo crollare l’equivalenza fra disposizione e condotta.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME4","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-04","text":"Mito e favola diventano tecnologie epistemiche che occultano selettivamente, trasmettono e rendono memorizzabili strutture altrimenti astratte.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME5","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-05","text":"Pianeti e membra cessano di appartenere a inventari separati e diventano nodi di un unico reticolo fra cosmologia e operazioni umane.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME6","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-06","text":"La falsa opposizione fra minaccia esterna e corruzione interna si indebolisce, perché il decisivo circuito inferiore attraversa affetti, demonizzazione e autoidolatria.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B01","text":"Al livello superficiale, Gorgoni, Pasiphe, Toro, Minotauro, animali e figure planetarie costituiscono immagini di collocazione per contenuti antropologici determinati.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT1","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B02","text":"Al livello strutturale, tripartizioni, luce esterna, veicolo aereo e corrispondenze planetarie organizzano una rete di mediazioni e biforcazioni direzionali.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT2","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B03","text":"Al livello metastrategico, leggere significa tradurre immagini mitiche in indirizzi mnemonici e distinguere capacità, disposizioni e azioni senza confonderle.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT3","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B04","text":"Al livello ontologico-temporale, la realtà è composta da gradi di partecipazione e densificazione, mentre il tempo assume la forma di discesa, dimora corporea, conversione e liberazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT4","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B05","text":"Al livello metodologico-performativo, l’accostamento di autorità eterogenee e la proliferazione delle immagini mettono in atto la stessa macchina di traduzione e archiviazione che il sistema teorizza.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS3","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-01","text":"La necessità del corpo e la necessità di liberarsene costituiscono una tensione produttiva e non eliminabile: senza corpo non vi è operazione, ma con la sua persistenza non vi è unione superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-02","text":"La dipendenza da grazia e illuminazione resta irrisolta rispetto alla richiesta che la virtù esista soltanto nell’azione e che le disposizioni siano moralmente trasformabili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT4","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-03","text":"La Nessamah è interna alla tripartizione e assimilata a un principio agente esterno, mentre il veicolo aereo aggiunge un’ulteriore mediazione senza formalizzare i rapporti fra presenza, fonte e supporto.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT3","CH_LIDT_PASI:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-04","text":"Il simbolo deve nascondere la dottrina e renderla accessibile alla memoria; l’assenza di una soglia precisa fra protezione e rivelazione è costitutiva della sua efficacia.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT5","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-05","text":"La classificazione astrologica tende al determinismo, mentre l’etica richiede conversione, repressione o attualizzazione delle nature classificate.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MP-01","text":"Il concetto di mediazione muta dall’illuminazione esterna che eleva l’intelletto al veicolo intermedio che rende possibile la discesa dell’anima.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MP-02","text":"La bestialità muta da stato prodotto dall’assenza della luce a figura reversibile di una disposizione che può essere esercitata, distrutta o convertita.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MP-03","text":"La morte muta da mortificazione simbolica degli affetti a dissoluzione effettiva del composto corporeo e dei suoi residui veicolari.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MP-04","text":"La mappa planetaria muta da ordinamento delle facoltà interiori a dispositivo esteso che distribuisce parti corporee, passioni, condizioni e relazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","CH_LIDT_PASI:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:HSI-01","text":"La realtà è implicitamente un teatro stratificato di raggi, veicoli, porte e corrispondenze, nel quale ogni livello traduce e ridistribuisce quello superiore.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:HSI-02","text":"Il soggetto è un relè ricettivo e potenzialmente ibrido, la cui configurazione dipende dagli influssi ricevuti, dai mediatori attraversati e dal polo a cui aderisce.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:HSI-03","text":"Il tempo è una spirale di partecipazione, caduta, densificazione, esercizio e liberazione, non una successione neutra di stati indipendenti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD5","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:HSI-04","text":"La lotta possibile consiste nel riallineare le mediazioni, distruggere gli idoli interni, attualizzare il bene e attraversare la dissoluzione senza presumere una fuga immediata.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D6","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B01","text":"Gli assiomi sono sufficienti a ricostruire il cluster come passaggio dall’uomo interiore illuminato al composto veicolare e corporeo organizzato simbolicamente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT1","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B02","text":"Rimangono sottodeterminati il rapporto preciso fra Nessamah e intelletto agente e il criterio che assegna le singole immagini alle corrispondenze planetarie.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT3","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B03","text":"L’architettura è più forte nella trasduzione di antropologia e cosmologia in un dispositivo simbolico-mnemonico capace di preservare differenze direzionali.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT7","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B04","text":"La coerenza dipende dalla compressione analogica di tradizioni eterogenee, dal simbolismo teologico e dal sequenziamento fra quarto grado, quinto grado e Talari.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT8","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B05","text":"La ricostruzione preserva il movimento effettivo soltanto mantenendo irrisolte le tensioni fra grazia e azione, necessità e prigionia del corpo, determinazione astrologica e trasformazione morale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT4","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT6","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T231216491185Z_5dac4b4c","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 04–05","source_sha256":"7684013434e7c49ad3afdfbbd84e76c58480cac486c8f03fbb92b50be740dcbe","sha256":"7f9f8b8b857d8e23d9fd23b2c3b194aed770c39ac1299e773d8c05a5546c1ba0","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:12:16.494026+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-01","text":"The system must make intelligible how the inner man, dependent on a divine illumination, can join with the body and operate through it without being reduced to corporeality.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS1","CH_LIDT_PASI:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-02","text":"Man emerges as a stratified and receptive structure, constituted by the interaction of external light, vehicular mediation, body, and moral orientation, not as a self-sufficient substance.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-03","text":"The argumentation takes a concordistic and symbolic form, translating Scripture, philosophy, myth, and astrology into convergent registers of one and the same operative anthropology.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-04","text":"The movement proceeds from the inner architecture and its illumination to descent into the corporeal composite, finally converting cosmological verticality into a planetary archive of faculties and dispositions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BAS-05","text":"The closure remains conditional and transitive: disposition must still become action, while the higher reconjunction requires overcoming the bodily bond.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Human identity is relational and receptive: it depends on principles, influences, and supports that it does not autonomously possess.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-02","text":"[Mutating] The body is simultaneously the instrument of operation, the medium of incarnation, the seat of affective capture, and an obstacle to higher reunion.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] No decisive conjunction is immediate: intellection requires an external agent light and incarnation requires an intermediate vehicle.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] Humanity is not guaranteed by bodily form, but varies according to participation in light and the use of the concupiscible power.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] The inner tripartition is expanded into a distributed taxonomy of faculties, limbs, passions, conditions, and destinies.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-06","text":"[Mutating] Myth passes from the mnemonic concealment of an intellectual structure to the symbolic genealogy of descent, cupidity, and monstrosity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME5","CH_LIDT_PASI:D2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Planetary images constitute mnemonic addresses that make the cosmic and anthropological distribution of faculties navigable.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Transformation depends first on grace and illumination, then on the operative actualization of disposition, without the two regimes being fully reconciled.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD2","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] The Theatro transduces a vertical cosmology of descent and ascent into a horizontal classificatory surface that preserves its directionality.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-10","text":"[Attractor] The machine converges upon liberation from affective and bodily rootedness as the condition of an ascending realignment.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-11","text":"[Emergent] Evil is internalized as a circuit of lower alignment, concupiscence, and self-idolatry before manifesting itself in action.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GA-12","text":"[Terminal] The cluster ends by distinguishing disposition and exercise and defers to the next degree the effective fulfillment of virtue or vice.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-01","text":"The stable identity of the symbol consists in not being ornamental fiction: it veils, preserves, and transmits a doctrinal structure.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX9","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-02","text":"The functional recurrence of mediation changes direction: external light makes intellectual ascent possible, whereas the aerial vehicle makes corporeal descent possible.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-03","text":"The body mutates from the external instrument of the inner man into a multilayered complex that permits incarnation and prolongs the soul's imprisonment.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D2","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-04","text":"Bestiality intensifies from a contingent deprivation of illumination into a moral process temporalized through inclination, complacency, and action.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-05","text":"The planetary order migrates from the indexing of inner faculties to the distribution of limbs, passions, social conditions, and destinies.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","CH_LIDT_PASI:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-06","text":"Death undergoes a terminal transformation: from the symbolic severance of the affections it passes to the corporeal and vehicular dissolution required by celestial reconjunction.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RMD-07","text":"The figure of the Gorgons disappears as dominant content after having condensed dependence on light; its function is absorbed by the Minotaur as a hybrid and reversible condensation of degraded mediation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D9","CH_LIDT_PASI:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-01","text":"The nomenclature Nephes–Ruach–Nessamah and the shared eye of the Gorgons as a specific formalization of inner triplicity remain local to the fourth degree.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A7","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A17"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-02","text":"The aerial vehicle, Pasiphe, and the Minotaur as a specific genealogy of the conjunction between desiring soul and corporeality remain local to the fifth degree.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-03","text":"The negation of the self-sufficient subject extends to the current level, because both intellection and incarnation depend on external or intermediate conditions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-04","text":"Mythic symbolism and planetary distribution connect the units by translating invisible structures into orderable mnemonic coordinates.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-05","text":"The passage from the ordering of inner faculties to the classification of corporeally clad man catalyzes the transition between the fourth and fifth degrees.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS6","CH_LIDT_PASI:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-06","text":"The simple opposition between interiority and body is recoded into a series of corporeal mediations with simultaneously operative, mnemonic, and carceral functions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A4","CH_LIDT_PASI:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:CGD-07","text":"The distinction between inclination and exercise functions as the terminal threshold of the cluster and renders obsolete every moral classification founded on disposition alone.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A10","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-01","text":"Man does not coincide with the body, nor does human form guarantee that the composite effectively participates in the divine order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX1","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-02","text":"Neither intellection nor the movement of the soul are autonomous powers exercisable without illumination or vehicular support.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX5","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-03","text":"The conjunction between spiritual and corporeal is not direct, because it requires mediating terms ontologically participant in the conjoined poles.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:NX2","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-04","text":"Human form, inclination, and knowledge of virtue do not correspond respectively to inner humanity, exercised vice, or virtuous life.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX6","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-05","text":"The fable is neither a literal account nor arbitrary ornament, but an operative delimitation of access to doctrine.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:NX9","CH_LIDT_PASI:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:GNX-06","text":"The body cannot be defined univocally as good, evil, or neutral support, since it makes operation possible and simultaneously produces capture.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-01","text":"Every ontology of the subject as a closed center, owner of its own light, its own works, and its own movement, must be false.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX1","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-02","text":"Immediate efficacy must be false: knowing, incarnating, remembering, and ascending always require influences, vehicles, images, or transformations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX2","CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-03","text":"The fixity of ontological and moral identities must be false, since bestiality, angelicity, vice, and virtue depend on alignments and actualizations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:DNX3","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-04","text":"The exclusively external localization of evil must be false, because lower capture culminates in the idol installed within the subject.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:DBN-05","text":"The neutrality of the mnemonic device must be false: the symbolic archive does not merely record man, but organizes his possibilities of orientation and transformation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-01","text":"The structuring absence is that of an integral and enduring reconciliation between the living body, liberation from the affections, and true celestial union.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-02","text":"The unavailable possibility is the self-generation of the good: disposition, knowledge, and will cannot autonomously produce illumination or enacted virtue.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX2","CH_LIDT_PASI:DNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-03","text":"For the human soul, a purely disincarnate efficacy is inadmissible, but the bodily support necessary for movement also becomes that which prevents final union.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A1","CH_LIDT_PASI:A12"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-04","text":"A truth that is simultaneously profound, wholly transparent, indiscriminately accessible, and immune from profanation is impossible.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX5","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSA-05","text":"The system revolves around the absence of an intrinsic and stably possessed humanity, replaced by a condition always exposed to reception or degradation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SNX1","CH_LIDT_PASI:SNX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-01","text":"The subject is doubly eccentric: it receives from outside the principle of its own intellection and acquires through a vehicle the possibility of its own incorporation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-01","CL_LIDT_02:GA-03","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-02","text":"The body constitutes the productively contradictory hinge of the system, because it makes worldly operation possible and makes subsequent liberation necessary.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-02","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D2","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-03","text":"Bestiality does not designate a separate species, but a process that begins with the failure to participate in light and is determined in the effective use of the lower faculties.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-04","CL_LIDT_02:GA-08","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-04","text":"Symbolic opacity and mnemonic accessibility are not opposed functions: doctrine is made transmissible precisely through the veiling that regulates access to it.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-06","CL_LIDT_02:GA-07","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-05","text":"Action is necessary to virtue but does not suffice to ground its authorship, since the system attributes to God the higher causality of works.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-08","CL_LIDT_02:GA-12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-06","text":"The Theatro operates as a transducer: it converts vertical ontological hierarchies into a spatial surface capable of archiving and reactivating the human composite.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-05","CL_LIDT_02:GA-09","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:XD-07","text":"Conversion does not coincide with a single event, but articulates grace, destruction of the idol, operative exercise, and dissolution of the bodily bond.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-10","CL_LIDT_02:GA-11","CL_LIDT_02:GA-12","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D6","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-01","text":"Ontologically, man becomes a stack of receptions and vehicles in which no isolated layer can claim the identity of the whole.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-02","text":"Temporally, existence takes the form descent–incorporation–disposition–action–mortification–dissolution, replacing static nature with a transformative sequence.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD5","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD3","CH_LIDT_PASI:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-03","text":"Epistemically, rationality ceases to be a natural property and doctrinal knowledge becomes reception indexed by symbolic devices.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME2","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-04","text":"Ethically, responsibility is situated in the actualization of non-self-produced dispositions, within a field conditioned by grace, influences, and astral correspondences.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A3","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-05","text":"Politically, the struggle against the internal idol can be extended from the care of the subject to the family and the republic because all these domains are situated within the same classificatory grammar.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A13","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT5","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:BSD-06","text":"Methodologically, analogy becomes a constitutive operator that compresses anthropology, cosmology, physiology, and morality, while leaving the full equivalence of their lexicons unproven.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT8","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-01","text":"External light produces orientation, orientation is archived in images, and the mnemonic archive makes the structure of orientation available again.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD2","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-02","text":"Lower alignment feeds a circuit of concupiscence, bestialization, and action that further consolidates capture in the body.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-03","text":"The body generates the most unstable circuit: it permits operation, arouses cupidity, reinforces the bond, and makes its own transformation or dissolution necessary.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D2","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-04","text":"Doctrinal exposition returns as fable, the fable becomes a mnemonic index, and the index makes it possible to reactivate what had been covered over.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-05","text":"Vertical descent is spatialized in the Theatro, and the horizontal navigation of the Theatro makes the direction of descent and ascent legible again.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-06","text":"The terminal attractor is celestial reconjunction, attainable not by avoiding mediations but by passing through them, converting them, and finally dissolving their residues.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D6","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:RLE-07","text":"The passage from the eye of the Gorgons to the Minotaur marks a phase change from cognitive dependence on a shared light to the corporeal production of a hybrid form to be converted.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D9","CH_LIDT_PASI:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B01","text":"Received divine image → constitution of the inner man → subject open to unpossessed principles.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A1","CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B02","text":"Intellectual capacity → intervention of external agent light → conditional intellectual humanity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A13","CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B03","text":"Incompatibility between fiery soul and earthly body → production of the aerial vehicle → possibility of incarnation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:A2","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B04","text":"Orientation toward the lower pole → corporeal concupiscence → hybrid composition and bestialization.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A11","CH_LIDT_PASI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B05","text":"Invisible structure → mythic condensation → planetary distribution → archive of faculties, limbs, and conditions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A18","CH_LIDT_PASI:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B06","text":"Grace and destruction of the idol → higher disposition → exercise in works → enacted virtue.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A12","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FGS-B07","text":"Severance of the affections → corporeal and vehicular dissolution → possibility, not guarantee, of celestial reunion.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:AFM-B01","text":"Received divine image → inner tripartition → external illumination → vehicular mediation → desiring incorporation → planetary distribution → moral disposition → deferred exercise → mortification and dissolution → conditional celestial reconjunction.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS4","CH_LIDT_PASI:AS6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:AFM-B02","text":"Explicit doctrine → mythic covering → planetary addressing → mnemonic reactivation → discrimination of alignments → operative conversion → renewed availability to higher light.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A16","CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","CH_LIDT_PASI:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-01","text":"Man is reclassified from a bipartite composite into a stratified network of soul, faculties, light, vehicle, body, and influences.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME1","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-02","text":"Corporeality is removed from the simple opposition between instrument and prison and redefined as a medium that produces both functions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-03","text":"The moral map now distinguishes nature, inclination, alignment, exercise, and transformation, collapsing the equivalence between disposition and conduct.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME4","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-04","text":"Myth and fable become epistemic technologies that selectively conceal, transmit, and render memorable otherwise abstract structures.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME5","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-05","text":"Planets and limbs cease to belong to separate inventories and become nodes of a single network between cosmology and human operations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME6","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MME-06","text":"The false opposition between external threat and internal corruption is weakened, because the decisive lower circuit traverses affections, demonization, and self-idolatry.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D5","CH_LIDT_PASI:ME5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B01","text":"At the surface level, Gorgons, Pasiphe, Bull, Minotaur, animals, and planetary figures constitute images of placement for determinate anthropological contents.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT1","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B02","text":"At the structural level, tripartitions, external light, aerial vehicle, and planetary correspondences organize a network of mediations and directional bifurcations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT2","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B03","text":"At the metastrategic level, reading means translating mythic images into mnemonic addresses and distinguishing capacities, dispositions, and actions without confusing them.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT3","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B04","text":"At the ontological-temporal level, reality is composed of degrees of participation and densification, while time takes the form of descent, bodily dwelling, conversion, and liberation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ALT4","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B05","text":"At the methodological-performative level, the juxtaposition of heterogeneous authorities and the proliferation of images enact the very machine of translation and archiving that the system theorizes.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:AS3","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-01","text":"The necessity of the body and the necessity of freeing oneself from it constitute a productive and irreducible tension: without body there is no operation, but with its persistence there is no higher union.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:ME7","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-02","text":"Dependence on grace and illumination remains unresolved in relation to the requirement that virtue exist only in action and that dispositions be morally transformable.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT4","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-03","text":"Nessamah is internal to the tripartition and assimilated to an external agent principle, while the aerial vehicle adds a further mediation without formalizing the relations among presence, source, and support.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT3","CH_LIDT_PASI:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-04","text":"The symbol must conceal doctrine and render it accessible to memory; the absence of a precise threshold between protection and revelation is constitutive of its efficacy.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT5","CH_LIDT_PASI:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:FL-05","text":"Astrological classification tends toward determinism, whereas ethics requires the conversion, repression, or actualization of classified natures.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PASI:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MP-01","text":"The concept of mediation mutates from external illumination that elevates the intellect to the intermediate vehicle that makes the descent of the soul possible.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:A14","CH_LIDT_PASI:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MP-02","text":"Bestiality mutates from a state produced by the absence of light into a reversible figure of a disposition that can be exercised, destroyed, or converted.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MP-03","text":"Death mutates from symbolic mortification of the affections into effective dissolution of the corporeal composite and its vehicular residues.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:FGS8","CH_LIDT_PASI:D7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MP-04","text":"The planetary map mutates from an ordering of inner faculties into an extended device that distributes bodily parts, passions, conditions, and relations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D13","CH_LIDT_PASI:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:HSI-01","text":"Reality is implicitly a stratified theater of rays, vehicles, gates, and correspondences, in which each level translates and redistributes the superior one.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD4","CH_LIDT_PASI:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a receptive and potentially hybrid relay, whose configuration depends on the influences received, the mediators traversed, and the pole to which it adheres.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD1","CH_LIDT_PASI:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:HSI-03","text":"Time is a spiral of participation, fall, densification, exercise, and liberation, not a neutral succession of independent states.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:SD5","CH_LIDT_PASI:ALT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:HSI-04","text":"The possible struggle consists in realigning mediations, destroying internal idols, actualizing the good, and passing through dissolution without presuming an immediate escape.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:D6","CH_LIDT_PASI:FGS7","CH_LIDT_PASI:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the cluster as a passage from the illuminated inner man to the symbolically organized vehicular and corporeal composite.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT1","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B02","text":"The precise relation between Nessamah and agent intellect, and the criterion assigning individual images to planetary correspondences, remain underdetermined.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT3","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B03","text":"The architecture is stronger in the transduction of anthropology and cosmology into a symbolic-mnemonic device capable of preserving directional differences.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT7","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B04","text":"Coherence depends on the analogical compression of heterogeneous traditions, theological symbolism, and the sequencing between fourth degree, fifth degree, and Talari.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT8","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction preserves the effective movement only by leaving unresolved the tensions between grace and action, necessity and imprisonment of the body, astrological determination and moral transformation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_LEGO:MRT4","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT6","CH_LIDT_PASI:MRT8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_LIDT_02@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_LIDT_02:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · The Idea of the Theatre","title":"Chapters 04–05","context":"Le Gorgoni, · Pasiphe"},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03","layer":"CL","title":"Chapters 06–07","order":3,"parents":["CH_LIDT_ITAL","CH_LIDT_PROM"],"revision":"CL_LIDT_03@R001","sha256":"edd63053fc502edd85e422eb0e002d38b00a43d77a17d4bc95936a865b8e25ca","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-01","text":"Il problema del cluster consiste nel rendere richiamabile una totalità eterogenea di operazioni, arti, istituzioni e pratiche senza dissolverla in un elenco indifferenziato.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS1","CH_LIDT_PROM:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-02","text":"La tesi globale è che il Theatro converte immagini mitiche e coordinate spaziali in nodi di accesso a sequenze operative, tecniche e civili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-03","text":"L’argomento collega l’agire naturale, dichiarato non prodotto dall’arte, alla compensazione artificiale dell’indigenza umana e alla successiva necessità dell’ordine civile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-04","text":"Il sistema procede mediante una doppia conversione: la figura diventa repertorio di azioni, mentre la vulnerabilità umana diventa genealogia delle arti e delle istituzioni di convivenza.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-05","text":"Il movimento è ricorsivo e cumulativo: porta, immagine, verbo e pratica producono recupero; il recupero si amplia attraverso accomodamenti storici, ma incontra un limite terminale nella differenza dell’incarnazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] La memoria è una struttura esterna di porte, gradi, immagini e serie associative, non una facoltà autosufficiente dell’interiorità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] L’immagine simbolica è un nodo polisemico che condensa operazioni, pratiche, saperi e appartenenze senza coincidere con una semplice illustrazione narrativa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","CH_LIDT_PROM:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] L’ordinamento planetario-mitico muta da dispositivo di recupero delle operazioni naturali a principio di raccolta delle arti, degli artefici e degli apparati civili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] Il Theatro organizza un continuum fra azione naturale, trasformazione subita, tecnica compensativa, pratica sociale e istituzione politica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A12","CH_LIDT_PROM:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] La completezza classificatoria richiede l’inclusione delle pratiche nobili, vili, corporee, viziose, punitive e coercitive come differenze interne alla mappa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Ogni pratica e sapere devono ricevere una collocazione, poiché la lacuna non è un margine tollerabile ma un difetto dell’ordine enciclopedico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] Le arti possono essere distribuite differenzialmente, ma la conservazione civile esige la partecipazione universale a pudore, giustizia e dispositivi di difesa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] Il patrimonio classico può essere tradotto e riusato soltanto come materiale subordinato, poiché la differenza dell’incarnazione non viene assorbita dalla sapienza figurabile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX6","CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-01","text":"[Identità stabile] L’immagine conserva la funzione di supporto mnemonico e di indice ordinativo nei due gradi.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-02","text":"[Mutazione] Il mito passa dall’esecuzione mercuriale della volontà divina alla genealogia prometeica dell’arte, spostando il centro dalla sequenza operativa alla compensazione antropologica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-03","text":"[Rovesciamento] Il naturale non appare più soltanto come repertorio di operazioni “fuor d’ogni arte”, ma come insufficienza che rende necessaria l’arte.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-04","text":"[Intensificazione] La categoria di operazione si estende dal fare al subire, al trasformarsi, al ricevere, al causare e infine alla pratica istituzionale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-05","text":"[Assorbimento] La serie finita di figure diviene una procedura di espansione controllata, capace di accogliere costumi moderni senza rinunciare alla chiusura ordinativa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-06","text":"[Trasformazione terminale] La traducibilità simbolica del classico viene interrotta dove la dottrina cristiana richiede una differenza non riducibile al repertorio allegorico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SD4","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-01","text":"[Locale] Il numero delle immagini assegnate ai singoli pianeti e la loro distribuzione quantitativa restano determinazioni locali non elevate ad assiomi del cluster.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-02","text":"[Locale] Le corrispondenze puntuali fra una figura e una serie specifica di azioni o arti rimangono parzialmente contingenti e non dedotte da una regola generale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX4","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-03","text":"[Scala cluster] La funzione delle immagini si generalizza: esse non conservano soltanto operazioni, ma organizzano l’intero passaggio fra azione, tecnica, sapere, istituzione e governo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD1","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-04","text":"[Collegamento] Il nesso fra sesto e settimo grado è costituito dalla conversione di una disposizione figurale in una classificazione operativa di capacità umane e forme sociali.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-05","text":"[Catalizzatore] L’indigenza naturale catalizza il passaggio dalla memoria delle operazioni alla necessità di arti, città, difesa, giurisdizione e sanzione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D1","CH_LIDT_PROM:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-06","text":"[Ricodifica] La distinzione fra arti nobili e ignobili perde funzione escludente, mentre la differenza cristologica conserva funzione limitativa e terminale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D5","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-01","text":"Il sistema rifiuta una memoria puramente interiore, poiché il recupero dipende da supporti spaziali, figurativi e ordinativi.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-02","text":"Il sistema rifiuta tanto il mito come descrizione letterale quanto la classificazione puramente concettuale, imponendo una mediazione figurale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-03","text":"Il sistema rifiuta l’autosufficienza naturale e l’equivalenza fra capacità tecnica e ordine civile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-04","text":"Il sistema rifiuta una classificazione moralmente selettiva, perché il vizio, la coercizione, la servitù e la punizione devono essere mappati senza diventare approvati.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-05","text":"Il sistema rifiuta l’antiquaria come criterio di completezza, poiché l’ordine deve assorbire materiali posteriori e bisogni presenti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX5","CH_LIDT_PROM:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-01","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea che la forma letterale di una figura basti a produrne il significato operativo: la significazione richiede una catena associativa esterna alla figura.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX2","CH_LIDT_PROM:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-02","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea che la tecnica, una volta acquisita, produca spontaneamente città stabile, perché il vivere tecnico non genera da sé il convivere civile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-03","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea che l’universalità significhi distribuzione uniforme di ogni facoltà, poiché le arti restano differenziali mentre le virtù civili devono essere comuni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-04","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea che una totalità ordinata possa espellere il marginale, il basso o il coercitivo senza produrre un vuoto interno alla propria pretesa enciclopedica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX3","CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-05","text":"Deve essere falsa l’idea che la traduzione simbolica del classico possa chiudersi in una sintesi teologica autosufficiente.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSA-01","text":"È precluso un accesso immediato, non mediato e trasparente alla totalità dell’agire umano: la totalità diventa accessibile soltanto come percorso fra porte, immagini e catene di appartenenza.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSA-02","text":"È inammissibile una totalità priva di luogo, perché ciò che non viene situato nel Theatro si presenta come lacuna strutturale dell’ordine.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSA-03","text":"È indisponibile una chiusura simbolica assoluta: la macchina enciclopedica tende alla completezza, ma la differenza dell’incarnazione impedisce che il suo repertorio diventi totalità teologica conclusa.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT5","CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-01","text":"La memoria delle operazioni e la classificazione delle arti convergono in un dispositivo di governo cognitivo che rende recuperabili insieme capacità corporee, tecniche, civili e punitive.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-01","CL_LIDT_03:GA-02","CL_LIDT_03:GA-04","CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD5","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-02","text":"Natura e arte non costituiscono poli semplicemente opposti: il repertorio naturale fornisce il campo dell’operare, mentre l’arte appare come compensazione organizzata della vulnerabilità.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-03","CL_LIDT_03:GA-04","CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD3","CH_LIDT_PROM:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-03","text":"La topologia figurale diventa una macchina di aggiornamento storico: assorbe materiali estranei all’antichità senza abbandonare il principio che ogni contenuto deve essere collocato.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-02","CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-04","text":"La distinzione fra distribuzione differenziale delle arti e partecipazione universale alle virtù civili converte la classificazione in una teoria implicita delle condizioni della convivenza.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-07","CH_LIDT_PROM:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-05","text":"L’attrattore della completezza produce inclusione crescente, ma la riserva cristologica impedisce che tale inclusione equivalga a una piena assimilazione semantica di ogni contenuto.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08","CH_LIDT_PROM:D6","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSD-01","text":"Il soggetto umano viene ricostruito come essere naturalmente insufficiente le cui capacità diventano effettive soltanto attraverso mediazioni tecniche, mnemoniche e civili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSD-02","text":"La conoscenza non opera come contemplazione di generi puri, ma come collocazione di differenze eterogenee in una rete di immagini, pratiche e appartenenze.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SD2","CH_LIDT_ITAL:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSD-03","text":"Il tempo storico non distrugge il Theatro, ma ne obbliga l’espansione mediante accomodamenti; tuttavia l’evento incarnativo introduce una discontinuità non pienamente traducibile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:AS5","CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSD-04","text":"La causalità cosmologica viene subordinata a una causalità operativa e istituzionale: pianeti e miti non spiegano direttamente gli eventi, ma ne ordinano il recupero, l’uso e la distribuzione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD4","CH_LIDT_PROM:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RLE-01","text":"Il circuito mnemonico procede da porta a immagine, da immagine a verbo, da verbo a famiglia d’azioni e da famiglia d’azioni a recupero ordinato.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS2","CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RLE-02","text":"Il circuito antropologico procede da indigenza a tecnica, da tecnica a insufficienza civile, da insufficienza a giustizia universale e da giustizia a ordine sanzionato.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS1","CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RLE-03","text":"Il circuito enciclopedico procede dalla minaccia del vuoto all’accomodamento di nuovi materiali e ritorna alla pretesa di completezza attraverso la loro nuova collocazione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D6","CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RLE-04","text":"L’attrattore centrale è l’assenza di lacune; il suo limite è la differenza cristologica, che non distrugge il repertorio ma impedisce la sua autochiusura assoluta.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B01","text":"La macchina riceve una pluralità di operazioni umane e una condizione di vulnerabilità naturale che non può essere mantenuta come dato immediato.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B02","text":"La pluralità viene esteriorizzata in gradi, porte e figure, così che la differenza diventi localizzabile e richiamabile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B03","text":"Ogni figura viene convertita in una catena di verbi, operazioni, arti, saperi e appartenenze, producendo nuclei finiti di recupero per materiali eterogenei.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B04","text":"Le arti compensano l’insufficienza del vivere, ma la loro distribuzione viene subordinata a una seconda macchina civile fondata sull’universalità di pudore e giustizia.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B05","text":"La macchina estende il repertorio mediante accomodamento storico, conservando tuttavia una riserva terminale contro la riduzione della differenza cristologica a sola sapienza.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B01","text":"Pluralità delle operazioni e indigenza naturale → necessità di un ordinamento esterno e compensativo.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS1","CH_LIDT_PROM:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B02","text":"Ordinamento esterno → porte planetarie e figure mitiche → repertori di significazioni operative.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A2","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B03","text":"Repertori operativi → arti e artefici → apparati della sopravvivenza e della vita sociale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B04","text":"Vita tecnica → insufficienza della sola tecnica → universalizzazione di pudore, giustizia, difesa e sanzione.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B05","text":"Pretesa di completezza → accomodamento ai materiali presenti → inclusione senza autochiusura teologica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:AF3","CH_LIDT_PROM:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-01","text":"La memoria viene riclassificata come topologia operativa capace di distribuire accessi, non come deposito interno di rappresentazioni.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-02","text":"La distinzione fra natura e arte viene ridisegnata come rapporto fra repertorio dell’agire e compensazione dell’insufficienza umana.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-03","text":"Le opposizioni fra atto, passione, trasformazione, mestiere, virtù e istituzione cessano di essere separazioni primarie e diventano differenze mappabili.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME4","CH_LIDT_PROM:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-04","text":"La distinzione fra arte nobile e arte vile viene sostituita dalla distinzione fra contenuti differenziati ma ugualmente collocabili nell’ordine enciclopedico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:ME3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-05","text":"Il rapporto fra antico, moderno e cristiano viene reso pensabile come adattamento controllato con un limite dottrinale non convertibile in semplice retorica.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:ME5","CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Il livello immediato è composto da porte, Talari, figure mitiche, serie di operazioni, arti, mestieri, istituzioni e pratiche coercitive.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A2","CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Il livello strutturale consiste nella relazione fra collocazione figurale, catena di significazioni, recupero mnemonico e distribuzione delle capacità.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT2","CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Il livello metastrategico converte l’eterogeneità in governabilità cognitiva, impedendo che pratiche, saperi e istituzioni restino privi di posto.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME5","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Il livello ontologico e temporale definisce l’umano come deficitario, artificialmente compensato e soggetto alla ritraduzione storica dei repertori.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] La forma catalogica mette in atto la propria tesi: l’ordine non viene soltanto enunciato, ma prodotto dalla distribuzione spaziale e figurale del materiale.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS4","CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FL-01","text":"Le operazioni vengono dette naturali e “fuor d’ogni arte”, ma sono accessibili soltanto mediante un apparato artificiale di immagini, porte e ordinamenti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT5","CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FL-02","text":"La pretesa di comprendere tutte le operazioni e tutte le arti entra in tensione con la finitezza delle immagini e con la necessità di accomodamenti contingenti.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT6","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FL-03","text":"La macchina tende a integrare ogni contenuto, ma la differenza dell’incarnazione richiede un resto che non può diventare soltanto elemento del repertorio.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX4","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MP-01","text":"L’immagine muta da scena mitologica a segno operativo e infine a nodo generale di raccolta per pratiche, saperi, istituzioni e appartenenze.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX3","CH_LIDT_PROM:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MP-02","text":"L’universalità muta da pretesa di repertorio totale a condizione selettiva della cittadinanza: non tutto deve essere condiviso, ma pudore e giustizia sì.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD2","CH_LIDT_PROM:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:HSI-01","text":"La realtà appare come una macchina di soglie e conversioni in cui immagini, coordinate e catene di appartenenze trasformano differenze eterogenee in accessi ordinati.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:D1","CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:HSI-02","text":"Il soggetto appare come essere non autosufficiente, capace di agire soltanto attraverso protesi tecniche, supporti mnemonici e condizioni civili condivise.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:HSI-03","text":"Il tempo appare come ritorno ricorsivo del repertorio attraverso adattamenti successivi, interrotto da una soglia teologica che non può essere integralmente tradotta.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:AS5","CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:HSI-04","text":"La lotta possibile nel sistema è una lotta contro il vuoto classificatorio, l’insufficienza tecnica isolata e la dissoluzione dell’ordine civile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B01","text":"Gli assiomi del cluster sono sufficienti a ricostruire il nucleo del sistema: esteriorizzazione mnemonica dell’agire, conversione figurale delle arti e subordinazione della tecnica alla continuità civile.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT1","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B02","text":"Rimangono sottodeterminati il criterio che assegna ogni figura a una serie determinata e la ragione della distribuzione quantitativa e planetaria dei repertori.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT2","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B03","text":"La ricostruzione è coerente come macchina catalogica, mnemonica e civile, ma dipende strutturalmente dalle tensioni fra finitezza e totalità, accomodamento e limite cristologico.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT4","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T231244428085Z_f8c5e889","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"Chapters 06–07","source_sha256":"edd63053fc502edd85e422eb0e002d38b00a43d77a17d4bc95936a865b8e25ca","sha256":"9300550ad39fb446f60bec819ae7ff54850e0a0d309b35a8d8c57b4d8b95bd7c","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:12:44.431043+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-01","text":"The problem of the cluster consists in making recallable a heterogeneous totality of operations, arts, institutions, and practices without dissolving it into an undifferentiated list.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS1","CH_LIDT_PROM:AS1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-02","text":"The global thesis is that the Theatro converts mythical images and spatial coordinates into nodes of access to operational, technical, and civil sequences.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-03","text":"The argument links natural action, declared not to be produced by art, to the artificial compensation for human indigence and to the subsequent necessity of civil order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-04","text":"The system proceeds through a double conversion: the figure becomes a repertory of actions, while human vulnerability becomes a genealogy of the arts and institutions of coexistence.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AS-05","text":"The movement is recursive and cumulative: gate, image, verb, and practice produce retrieval; retrieval expands through historical accommodations, but encounters a terminal limit in the difference of the incarnation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Memory is an external structure of gates, degrees, images, and associative series, not a self-sufficient faculty of interiority.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] The symbolic image is a polysemic node that condenses operations, practices, forms of knowledge, and affiliations without coinciding with a simple narrative illustration.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9","CH_LIDT_PROM:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-03","text":"[Mutating] The planetary-mythical ordering changes from a device for retrieving natural operations into a principle for gathering arts, artisans, and civil apparatuses.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A8"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-04","text":"[Emergent] The Theatro organizes a continuum between natural action, undergone transformation, compensatory technique, social practice, and political institution.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A12","CH_LIDT_PROM:A2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-05","text":"[Persistent] Classificatory completeness requires the inclusion of noble, vile, bodily, vicious, punitive, and coercive practices as internal differences within the map.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","text":"[Attractor] Every practice and form of knowledge must receive a placement, since the gap is not a tolerable margin but a defect of encyclopedic order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-07","text":"[Mutating] The arts may be distributed differentially, but civil preservation requires universal participation in shame, justice, and devices of defense.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GA-08","text":"[Terminal] The classical heritage may be translated and reused only as subordinate material, since the difference of the incarnation is not absorbed by figurative wisdom.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX6","CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-01","text":"[Stable identity] The image retains the function of mnemonic support and ordering index in the two degrees.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A4","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] Myth passes from the Mercurial execution of divine will to the Promethean genealogy of art, shifting the center from the operational sequence to anthropological compensation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:AS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-03","text":"[Reversal] The natural no longer appears merely as a repertory of operations “fuor d’ogni arte,” but as an insufficiency that makes art necessary.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-04","text":"[Intensification] The category of operation extends from doing to undergoing, becoming transformed, receiving, causing, and finally to institutional practice.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-05","text":"[Absorption] The finite series of figures becomes a procedure of controlled expansion, capable of accommodating modern customs without relinquishing ordering closure.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RMD-06","text":"[Terminal transformation] The symbolic translatability of the classical is interrupted where Christian doctrine requires a difference irreducible to the allegorical repertory.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SD4","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-01","text":"[Local] The number of images assigned to individual planets and their quantitative distribution remain local determinations not elevated to axioms of the cluster.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A8","CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-02","text":"[Local] The specific correspondences between a figure and a particular series of actions or arts remain partially contingent and are not deduced from a general rule.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX4","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-03","text":"[Cluster scale] The function of images is generalized: they do not merely preserve operations, but organize the entire passage between action, technique, knowledge, institution, and government.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD1","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-04","text":"[Connection] The link between the sixth and seventh degrees consists in the conversion of a figural arrangement into an operational classification of human capacities and social forms.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-05","text":"[Catalyst] Natural indigence catalyzes the passage from the memory of operations to the necessity of arts, cities, defense, jurisdiction, and sanction.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D1","CH_LIDT_PROM:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:CGD-06","text":"[Recoding] The distinction between noble and ignoble arts loses its excluding function, while the Christological difference retains a limiting and terminal function.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D5","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-01","text":"The system rejects a purely interior memory, since retrieval depends on spatial, figural, and ordering supports.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-02","text":"The system rejects both myth as literal description and purely conceptual classification, imposing figural mediation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX4","CH_LIDT_ITAL:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-03","text":"The system rejects natural self-sufficiency and the equivalence between technical capacity and civil order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:NX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-04","text":"The system rejects a morally selective classification, because vice, coercion, servitude, and punishment must be mapped without thereby becoming approved.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX7","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:GNX-05","text":"The system rejects antiquarianism as a criterion of completeness, since order must absorb later materials and present needs.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:NX5","CH_LIDT_PROM:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-01","text":"The idea that the literal form of a figure suffices to produce its operational meaning must be false: signification requires an associative chain external to the figure.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:DNX2","CH_LIDT_PROM:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-02","text":"The idea that technique, once acquired, spontaneously produces a stable city must be false, because technical living does not of itself generate civil coexistence.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-03","text":"The idea that universality means the uniform distribution of every faculty must be false, since the arts remain differential while civil virtues must be common.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-04","text":"The idea that an ordered totality can expel the marginal, the low, or the coercive without producing a void internal to its own encyclopedic claim must be false.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX3","CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:DBN-05","text":"The idea that the symbolic translation of the classical can close itself within a self-sufficient theological synthesis must be false.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSA-01","text":"Immediate, unmediated, and transparent access to the totality of human action is foreclosed: the totality becomes accessible only as a path among gates, images, and chains of affiliation.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSA-02","text":"A totality without place is inadmissible, because what is not situated in the Theatro presents itself as a structural gap in the order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSA-03","text":"Absolute symbolic closure is unavailable: the encyclopedic machine tends toward completeness, but the difference of the incarnation prevents its repertory from becoming a concluded theological totality.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT5","CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-01","text":"The memory of operations and the classification of the arts converge in a device of cognitive governance that renders bodily, technical, civil, and punitive capacities retrievable together.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-01","CL_LIDT_03:GA-02","CL_LIDT_03:GA-04","CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD5","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-02","text":"Nature and art do not constitute simply opposed poles: the natural repertory provides the field of operating, while art appears as the organized compensation of vulnerability.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-03","CL_LIDT_03:GA-04","CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD3","CH_LIDT_PROM:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-03","text":"Figural topology becomes a machine of historical updating: it absorbs materials foreign to antiquity without abandoning the principle that every content must be placed.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-02","CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME5","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-04","text":"The distinction between the differential distribution of the arts and universal participation in civil virtues converts classification into an implicit theory of the conditions of coexistence.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-07","CH_LIDT_PROM:A6","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:XD-05","text":"The attractor of completeness produces increasing inclusion, but the Christological reservation prevents such inclusion from amounting to a full semantic assimilation of every content.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08","CH_LIDT_PROM:D6","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSD-01","text":"The human subject is reconstructed as a naturally insufficient being whose capacities become effective only through technical, mnemonic, and civil mediations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSD-02","text":"Knowledge does not operate as contemplation of pure genera, but as the placement of heterogeneous differences in a network of images, practices, and affiliations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SD2","CH_LIDT_ITAL:D6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSD-03","text":"Historical time does not destroy the Theatro, but compels its expansion through accommodations; yet the incarnative event introduces a discontinuity not fully translatable.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:AS5","CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:BSD-04","text":"Cosmological causality is subordinated to operational and institutional causality: planets and myths do not directly explain events, but order their retrieval, use, and distribution.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD4","CH_LIDT_PROM:D3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RLE-01","text":"The mnemonic circuit proceeds from gate to image, from image to verb, from verb to family of actions, and from family of actions to ordered retrieval.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS2","CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RLE-02","text":"The anthropological circuit proceeds from indigence to technique, from technique to civil insufficiency, from insufficiency to universal justice, and from justice to sanctioned order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS1","CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RLE-03","text":"The encyclopedic circuit proceeds from the threat of void to the accommodation of new materials and returns to the claim of completeness through their new placement.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D6","CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:RLE-04","text":"The central attractor is the absence of gaps; its limit is the Christological difference, which does not destroy the repertory but prevents its absolute self-closure.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B01","text":"The machine receives a plurality of human operations and a condition of natural vulnerability that cannot be maintained as immediate datum.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B02","text":"The plurality is externalized into degrees, gates, and figures, so that difference becomes localizable and recallable.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B03","text":"Each figure is converted into a chain of verbs, operations, arts, forms of knowledge, and affiliations, producing finite nuclei of retrieval for heterogeneous materials.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B04","text":"The arts compensate for the insufficiency of living, but their distribution is subordinated to a second civil machine founded on the universality of shame and justice.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B05","text":"The machine extends the repertory through historical accommodation, while nevertheless retaining a terminal reservation against reducing the Christological difference to wisdom alone.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A10","CH_LIDT_PROM:A11"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B01","text":"Plurality of operations and natural indigence → necessity of an external and compensatory ordering.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:AS1","CH_LIDT_PROM:AS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B02","text":"External ordering → planetary gates and mythical figures → repertories of operational significations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A2","CH_LIDT_ITAL:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B03","text":"Operational repertories → arts and artisans → apparatuses of survival and social life.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:A8","CH_LIDT_PROM:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B04","text":"Technical life → insufficiency of technique alone → universalization of shame, justice, defense, and sanction.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D2","CH_LIDT_PROM:A5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B05","text":"Claim of completeness → accommodation to present materials → inclusion without theological self-closure.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:AF3","CH_LIDT_PROM:AF4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-01","text":"Memory is reclassified as an operational topology capable of distributing accesses, not as an internal repository of representations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME1","CH_LIDT_ITAL:D1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-02","text":"The distinction between nature and art is redrawn as the relation between a repertory of action and compensation for human insufficiency.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:ME1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-03","text":"The oppositions between act, passion, transformation, trade, virtue, and institution cease to be primary separations and become mappable differences.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME4","CH_LIDT_PROM:D5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-04","text":"The distinction between noble art and vile art is replaced by the distinction between contents differentiated but equally placeable within encyclopedic order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:ME3","CH_LIDT_PROM:A9"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MME-05","text":"The relation between ancient, modern, and Christian is made thinkable as controlled adaptation with a doctrinal limit not convertible into mere rhetoric.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:ME5","CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] The immediate level is composed of gates, Talari, mythical figures, series of operations, arts, trades, institutions, and coercive practices.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:A2","CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] The structural level consists in the relation between figural placement, chain of significations, mnemonic retrieval, and distribution of capacities.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:ALT2","CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] The metastrategic level converts heterogeneity into cognitive governability, preventing practices, forms of knowledge, and institutions from remaining without a place.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:ME5","CH_LIDT_PROM:SD1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] The ontological and temporal level defines the human as deficient, artificially compensated, and subject to the historical retranslation of repertories.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:ALT4","CH_LIDT_PROM:A10"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] The catalogic form enacts its own thesis: order is not merely stated, but produced by the spatial and figural distribution of the material.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:FGS4","CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FL-01","text":"Operations are said to be natural and “fuor d’ogni arte,” but are accessible only through an artificial apparatus of images, gates, and orderings.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT5","CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FL-02","text":"The claim to comprehend all operations and all arts comes into tension with the finitude of images and with the necessity of contingent accommodations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT6","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:FL-03","text":"The machine tends to integrate every content, but the difference of the incarnation requires a remainder that cannot become merely an element of the repertory.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX4","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT6"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MP-01","text":"The image changes from mythological scene to operational sign and finally to a general node of collection for practices, forms of knowledge, institutions, and affiliations.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:NX3","CH_LIDT_PROM:D4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MP-02","text":"Universality changes from a claim of total repertory to a selective condition of citizenship: not everything must be shared, but shame and justice must be.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:SD2","CH_LIDT_PROM:NX3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:HSI-01","text":"Reality appears as a machine of thresholds and conversions in which images, coordinates, and chains of affiliations transform heterogeneous differences into ordered accesses.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:D1","CH_LIDT_PROM:FGS3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:HSI-02","text":"The subject appears as a non-self-sufficient being, capable of acting only through technical prostheses, mnemonic supports, and shared civil conditions.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:D1","CH_LIDT_PROM:A4"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:HSI-03","text":"Time appears as the recursive return of the repertory through successive adaptations, interrupted by a theological threshold that cannot be integrally translated.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:AS5","CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX5"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:HSI-04","text":"The possible struggle in the system is a struggle against classificatory void, isolated technical insufficiency, and the dissolution of civil order.","refs":["CH_LIDT_PROM:DNX1","CH_LIDT_PROM:SNX2"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B01","text":"The axioms of the cluster are sufficient to reconstruct the nucleus of the system: mnemonic externalization of action, figural conversion of the arts, and subordination of technique to civil continuity.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT1","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT1"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B02","text":"The criterion that assigns each figure to a determinate series and the reason for the quantitative and planetary distribution of the repertories remain underdetermined.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT2","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT3"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B03","text":"The reconstruction is coherent as a catalogic, mnemonic, and civil machine, but depends structurally on the tensions between finitude and totality, accommodation and Christological limit.","refs":["CH_LIDT_ITAL:MRT4","CH_LIDT_PROM:MRT7"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"CL_LIDT_03@R001","source_variant_id":"canonical:CL_LIDT_03:v1","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"CL","kicker":"Cluster · The Idea of the Theatre","title":"Chapters 06–07","context":"Italari. · Prometheo."},"title_language_code":"en"},{"id":"WB_LIDT","layer":"WB","title":"The Idea of the Theatre","order":1,"parents":["CL_LIDT_01","CL_LIDT_02","CL_LIDT_03"],"revision":"WB_LIDT@R002","sha256":"299214dd6dd0f201188d32b9de7d635b8d49a219c7ecbb85dda2363760c6f706","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-01","text":"Il problema globale consiste nel rendere indirizzabile la molteplicità cosmica, antropologica, tecnica e civile senza ridurla a un elenco piano né trasformare l’eccedenza divina in possesso trasparente.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-01","CL_LIDT_03:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-02","text":"Il Theatro risolve il problema traducendo la derivazione causale in una topologia esterna di immagini e riconvertendo tale topologia in percorsi di recupero, operazione e risalita.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-02","CL_LIDT_03:AS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-03","text":"Il fondamento è una realtà gerarchica nella quale ordine esemplare, soggetto ricettivo e pratiche umane appartengono a un solo continuum mediato.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-01","CL_LIDT_02:GA-01","CL_LIDT_03:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-04","text":"L’argomentazione assume la forma di una macchina teologico-cosmologica, antropologica, mnemonica e civile che concorda registri eterogenei subordinandoli a una sola architettura trasformativa.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-03","CL_LIDT_02:BAS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-05","text":"Il movimento discende dai principi alle forme, interiorizza la gerarchia nell’uomo, la esteriorizza in azioni e istituzioni e rende infine il percorso inversamente navigabile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:XD-02","CL_LIDT_02:RLE-05","CL_LIDT_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-06","text":"La progressione è ricorsiva, spiraliforme e cumulativa: ogni ritorno di immagini e coordinate conserva la mediazione ma ne amplia il dominio operativo.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-04","CL_LIDT_03:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-07","text":"L’attrattore direzionale è la risalita ordinata verso l’unità superiore mediante attraversamento, conversione e dissoluzione delle mediazioni, non mediante loro elusione immediata.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-10","CL_LIDT_02:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-08","text":"La chiusura è cristologica e apofatica: Cristo garantisce coesione e orientamento, ma l’ignoto e la differenza dell’incarnazione impediscono l’autoesaurimento della macchina classificatoria.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-05","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] L’ordine esemplare precede causalmente forme, soggetti e operazioni e rende possibile la loro continuità entro una medesima architettura.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] Nessun passaggio decisivo è immediato: conoscenza, incarnazione, memoria, azione e ascesa richiedono immagini, influssi, veicoli o istituzioni.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-03","CL_LIDT_02:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] Il Theatro è un dispositivo topologico esterno che converte gerarchie invisibili e pluralità operative in collocazioni recuperabili.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-03","CL_LIDT_03:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] L’immagine conserva la funzione mediatrice ma muta da velo dell’eccedenza a coordinata posizionale, indice antropologico e nodo operativo-civile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-02","CL_LIDT_03:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] Il pianeta passa da segno dell’ordine superiore a infrastruttura distributiva di nature, facoltà, membra, arti e apparati sociali.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-04","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-05","CL_LIDT_03:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Cosmologia, antropologia, tecnica e politica costituiscono fasi trasducibili di un continuum che procede dalla formazione alla pratica istituzionale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-09","CL_LIDT_03:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] Il soggetto è relazionale, ricettivo e non autosufficiente: riceve luce, forma, capacità e condizioni operative che non può fondare autonomamente.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-01","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Materia e corpo sono mediazioni necessarie che ricevono forma e consentono l’azione, ma introducono anche composizione, cattura, vulnerabilità e bisogno di trasformazione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_02:GA-02","CL_LIDT_02:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] Un repertorio finito di figure può sostenere un’espansione indefinita regolata mediante variazione posizionale, suddivisione e accomodamento storico.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-08","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Capacità, disposizione, azione e appartenenza civile sono livelli distinti: nessuna potenza diventa virtù o ordine comune senza attualizzazione e regolazione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-12","CL_LIDT_03:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] La macchina tende a collocare ogni realtà, pratica e sapere, convertendo lacune e differenze in posizioni interne all’ordine.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","CL_LIDT_01:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Il conoscere e l’agire validi consistono nel ripercorrere ordinatamente le mediazioni, riallineandole alla causalità superiore.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-10","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Cristo opera insieme come principio di coesione interna e come differenza terminale non assorbibile dalla traducibilità simbolica generale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-11","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-14","text":"[Emergent] L’ignoto viene interiorizzato come riserva di espansione, ma la totalità resta non autochiudibile perché non ogni differenza può diventare repertorio disponibile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","CL_LIDT_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-01","text":"[Identità stabile] Il simbolo permane come mediazione non ornamentale che vela, conserva e trasmette una struttura eccedente la propria forma sensibile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-02","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-01","CL_LIDT_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-02","text":"[Mutazione] L’immagine passa dal rappresentare velatamente una causa al produrre accessi differenziali a facoltà, azioni, arti e istituzioni.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-02","CL_LIDT_03:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-03","text":"[Spostamento] Il pianeta migra dalla mediazione contemplativa alla coordinazione tassonomica, antropologica e sociale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-03","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-05","CL_LIDT_03:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-04","text":"[Mutazione] Il mito passa da velo dottrinale a genealogia della discesa e infine a repertorio operativo dell’invenzione tecnica.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-04","CL_LIDT_02:GA-06","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-05","text":"[Ricorrenza funzionale] La mediazione cambia direzione e supporto: attenua la causalità cosmica, rende possibile illuminazione e incarnazione, quindi riappare come protesi tecnica e civile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RMD-02","CL_LIDT_02:MP-01","CL_LIDT_03:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-06","text":"[Rovesciamento] La natura inferiore passa dall’essere ordine derivato all’apparire come condizione insufficiente che richiede corpo, arte e istituzione senza diventare autonoma.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-07","text":"[Intensificazione] La memoria evolve da disposizione di luoghi a matrice combinatoria e infine a topologia esterna capace di governare il recupero dell’intero campo operativo.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-05","CL_LIDT_03:GA-01","CL_LIDT_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-08","text":"[Assorbimento] L’uomo, inizialmente distinto dal catalogo naturale, viene riassorbito come nodo deficitario che trasforma categorie cosmiche in disposizioni, tecniche e forme civili.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-04","CL_LIDT_03:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-09","text":"[Trasformazione terminale] L’ignoto passa da riserva interna collocabile a limite della pretesa di eliminare ogni lacuna, culminando nella differenza cristologica non assimilabile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","CL_LIDT_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-10","text":"[Spostamento] La dissoluzione migra dalla ricomposizione cosmica dei misti alla liberazione antropologica dai residui corporei e veicolari.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-06","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-01","text":"[Locale] Nomi cabalistici, figure mitiche determinate e quantità planetarie restano articolazioni locali; alla scala del libro valgono soltanto come realizzazioni della mediazione generale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:CGD-01","CL_LIDT_02:CGD-01","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-02","text":"[Locale] Le assegnazioni puntuali fra figura, pianeta e contenuto restano sottodeterminate e non possono essere elevate a necessità globale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B02","CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-03","text":"[Esteso] La necessità di mediazione e la non autosufficienza di materia, soggetto e tecnica attraversano tutte le unità e diventano leggi globali.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-03","CL_LIDT_02:CGD-03","CL_LIDT_03:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-04","text":"[Ponte] La topologia planetaria collega causalità cosmica, struttura umana e distribuzione delle pratiche rendendole registri di un’unica matrice.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:CGD-03","CL_LIDT_02:MP-04","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-05","text":"[Catalizzatore] L’incorporazione trasforma la gerarchia cosmica in problema morale, mentre l’indigenza trasforma il problema morale-operativo in tecnica e ordine civile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:CGD-05","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-06","text":"[Ponte] Il corpo collega ricezione ontologica e operazione mondana; l’arte estende questa funzione mediatrice oltre l’organismo verso istituzioni condivise.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:XD-02","CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-07","text":"[Ricodificato] Il significato fisso dell’immagine, il soggetto bipartito e l’opposizione semplice fra natura e arte vengono superati da semantiche posizionali e continuità mediate.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:CGD-05","CL_LIDT_02:MME-01","CL_LIDT_03:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-08","text":"[Terminale] La differenza cristologica non è un contenuto locale aggiuntivo, ma il limite globale che impedisce alla traducibilità universale di chiudersi su sé stessa.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:CGD-06","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-01","text":"Il divino non può essere esposto, posseduto o amministrato integralmente mediante forme letterali e sensibili.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-01","CL_LIDT_01:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-02","text":"Materia e natura non possiedono autonomia formativa, vitale o intelligibile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-03","CL_LIDT_03:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-03","text":"Il soggetto non è proprietario della propria luce, del proprio movimento o dell’efficacia delle proprie opere.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:DBN-03","CL_LIDT_02:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-04","text":"Nessuna immagine possiede un significato letterale, fisso o autosufficiente indipendente dalla posizione e dalla catena associativa.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-04","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-05","text":"La memoria non è deposito interiore né enciclopedia orizzontale, ma dipende da un ordine esterno differenziale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-06","CL_LIDT_03:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-06","text":"La natura, la disposizione e la tecnica non bastano rispettivamente a produrre arte, virtù e convivenza stabile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GNX-04","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-07","text":"La completezza non autorizza l’espulsione del basso, del vizioso o del coercitivo, che devono essere collocati senza essere normativamente approvati.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GNX-04","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-08","text":"Né la dissoluzione equivale a non-essere assoluto né la classificazione equivale a trasparenza esaustiva.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-07","CL_LIDT_01:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-01","text":"Deve essere falsa ogni efficacia immediata, perché l’intera macchina dipende dall’interposizione produttiva di segni, veicoli, corpi e ordinamenti.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:DBN-02","CL_LIDT_02:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-02","text":"Deve essere falsa l’indipendenza ontologica di cosmologia, antropologia, arte e politica, poiché la trasduzione fra domini costituisce l’unità del libro.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:DBN-04","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-03","text":"Deve essere falso che le corrispondenze siano radicalmente arbitrarie, sebbene il sistema non dimostri pienamente la loro necessità.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-04","text":"Deve essere falso che universalità significhi trasparenza simultanea, poiché la totalità dipende da velamento, differenziazione e accesso regolato.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSA-04","CL_LIDT_02:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-05","text":"Deve essere falsa l’autosufficienza dell’umano naturale o tecnico, perché ricezione, artificio e istituzione rimediano a insufficienze senza abolirle definitivamente.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSA-02","CL_LIDT_03:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-06","text":"Deve essere falsa la piena assimilabilità dell’incarnazione al repertorio classico, altrimenti il limite terminale verrebbe ridotto a un’ulteriore equivalenza figurale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-01","text":"La possibilità assolutamente indisponibile è il possesso immediato dell’origine divina da parte del soggetto o del dispositivo mnemonico.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSA-01","CL_LIDT_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-02","text":"L’assenza strutturante è una conciliazione stabile fra corporeità operativa, liberazione dagli affetti e unione superiore.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSA-01","CL_LIDT_02:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-03","text":"Il sistema non ammette un oggetto assolutamente privo di luogo, ma incontra una differenza che non può essere ridotta a semplice collocazione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:BSA-02","CL_LIDT_03:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-04","text":"L’auto-chiusura assoluta della totalità resta vietata: l’ignoto alimenta l’espansione e l’incarnazione ne interrompe l’assimilazione completa.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RLE-07","CL_LIDT_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-05","text":"Manca un metalinguaggio capace di arbitrare definitivamente le autorità e le analogie eterogenee sincronizzate dalla macchina.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:FL-04","CL_LIDT_02:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-01","text":"La derivazione cosmica si prolunga nell’antropologia e nell’ordine civile: forme, facoltà, operazioni e istituzioni sono stadi differenziati di una stessa causalità mediata.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-01","WB_LIDT:GA-05","WB_LIDT:GA-06","WB_LIDT:GA-10","CL_LIDT_01:XD-02","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-02","text":"La memoria diventa causalmente informata perché la topologia teatrale codifica la discesa delle realtà e permette di ripercorrerla in senso inverso.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-03","WB_LIDT:GA-12","CL_LIDT_01:MME-01","CL_LIDT_02:XD-06","CL_LIDT_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-03","text":"L’opacità simbolica produce accessibilità regolata: la variazione posizionale consente a un repertorio finito di indirizzare contenuti che non può esporre integralmente.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-02","WB_LIDT:GA-04","WB_LIDT:GA-09","WB_LIDT:GA-11","CL_LIDT_01:XD-01","CL_LIDT_02:XD-04","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-04","text":"L’insufficienza umana è una forma locale della non autonomia cosmica: luce, corpo, arte e città compensano dipendenze che nessun soggetto può auto-fondare.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-07","WB_LIDT:GA-08","WB_LIDT:GA-10","CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_02:XD-01","CL_LIDT_03:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-05","text":"Corpo e arte sono mediazioni omologhe: entrambi rendono possibile l’operazione, ma generano un problema secondario di cattura, insufficienza o regolazione.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-06","WB_LIDT:GA-08","WB_LIDT:GA-10","CL_LIDT_02:XD-02","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-06","text":"Ignoto e accomodamento storico rendono la totalità espandibile, mentre la differenza cristologica impedisce che espansione significhi assimilazione illimitata.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-09","WB_LIDT:GA-11","WB_LIDT:GA-13","WB_LIDT:GA-14","CL_LIDT_01:RLE-07","CL_LIDT_03:XD-03","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-07","text":"La conversione morale traduce la verticalità cosmica in azione e la prolunga politicamente nelle condizioni universali della convivenza.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-10","WB_LIDT:GA-12","CL_LIDT_02:GA-11","CL_LIDT_02:XD-05","CL_LIDT_03:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-08","text":"La dissoluzione antropologica costituisce una specializzazione della ricomposizione cosmica: la perdita del composto non annienta i principi, ma può liberarli per un nuovo allineamento.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-01","WB_LIDT:GA-08","WB_LIDT:GA-12","CL_LIDT_01:RMD-06","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-01","text":"Ontologicamente, la realtà diventa una rete di ricezioni, attenuazioni e ritrasmissioni nella quale nessun livello inferiore è autosufficiente.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-01","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-02","text":"Il soggetto diventa un relè decentrato che riceve orientamenti, attraversa supporti e converte la propria posizione in pratica.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSD-04","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-03","text":"Epistemicamente, conoscere significa navigare relazioni posizionali e ricostruire dipendenze, non possedere contenuti isolati.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSD-01","CL_LIDT_01:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-04","text":"Il tempo si articola in eternità esemplare, discesa, incorporazione, azione, dissoluzione e aggiornamento storico dei repertori.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSD-05","CL_LIDT_02:BSD-02","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-05","text":"L’agire resta reale ma derivato: consiste nell’attualizzare e riallineare capacità ricevute entro vincoli corporei, astrali, tecnici e civili.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSD-04","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-06","text":"Politicamente, la tecnica non fonda da sola la convivenza; la continuità civile richiede disposizioni comuni, difesa, giurisdizione e sanzione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:DBN-02","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-07","text":"Metodologicamente, analogia e catalogo non descrivono soltanto il sistema, ma producono operativamente la continuità fra domini eterogenei.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSD-06","CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-08","text":"La totalità assume forma asintotica: può estendere indefinitamente la propria indirizzabilità senza raggiungere trasparenza o chiusura teologica assoluta.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:XD-05","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-01","text":"Causalità superiore → immagini → recupero mnemonico → risalita causale costituisce il circuito ricorsivo fondamentale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RLE-01","CL_LIDT_01:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-02","text":"Figura → posizione → divisione → nuova funzione produce espansione combinatoria senza proliferazione illimitata dei segni.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RLE-02","CL_LIDT_01:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-03","text":"La discesa verticale viene spazializzata e la navigazione orizzontale riattiva la direzione verticale, facendo del Theatro una spirale fra livelli.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RLE-05","CL_LIDT_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-04","text":"Luce → orientamento → immagine → memoria → nuovo orientamento forma il circuito cognitivo che mantiene il soggetto dipendente dall’esterno.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RLE-01","CL_LIDT_02:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-05","text":"Corpo → concupiscenza → azione inferiore → cattura → mortificazione intensifica la mediazione fino a renderne necessaria la conversione o dissoluzione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RLE-02","CL_LIDT_02:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-06","text":"Indigenza → tecnica → insufficienza civile → giustizia comune → ordine sanzionato costituisce il circuito politico di compensazione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:RLE-02","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-07","text":"Lacuna → collocazione provvisoria → accomodamento → nuova completezza riapre continuamente l’enciclopedia senza abbandonarne l’attrattore totalizzante.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:RLE-03","CL_LIDT_03:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-08","text":"Cristo è l’attrattore-limite: garantisce la convergenza delle mediazioni e simultaneamente impedisce che la macchina si dichiari autosufficiente.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-11","CL_LIDT_03:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B01","text":"Eccedenza divina → impossibilità dell’esposizione diretta → necessità del velo simbolico.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:DBN-01","CL_LIDT_01:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B02","text":"Ordine esemplare → mediazioni cosmiche → forme naturali → composti temporanei.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-01","CL_LIDT_01:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B03","text":"Gerarchia causale → pianeti-coordinate → spazio teatrale → recuperabilità mnemonica.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:XD-07","CL_LIDT_01:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B04","text":"Luce ricevuta → facoltà interiori → orientamento → umanità condizionale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BAS-02","CL_LIDT_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B05","text":"Mediazione veicolare → incorporazione → desiderio → disposizione morale → azione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RMD-03","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B06","text":"Operazione naturale → indigenza → arte compensativa → repertorio tecnico-sociale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:AS-03","CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B07","text":"Tecnica distribuita → insufficienza della coesistenza → virtù civili comuni → difesa e sanzione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-07","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B08","text":"Navigazione delle mediazioni → riallineamento → dissoluzione dei vincoli → risalita condizionata → chiusura cristologica non esaustiva.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-04","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-06","CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:AFM-B01","text":"Eccedenza divina → causalità esemplare → mediazione planetaria → codifica figurale → interiorizzazione antropologica → incorporazione → operazione → arte → istituzione civile → limite cristologico.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MME-03","CL_LIDT_02:MME-01","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:AFM-B02","text":"Molteplicità dispersa → collocazione teatrale → recupero relazionale → discriminazione degli allineamenti → conversione dell’azione → risalita attraverso le mediazioni → unità senza trasparenza totale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSD-02","CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B03","CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-01","text":"La separazione fra ontologia e memoria crolla: ricordare significa navigare la struttura causale e operativa della realtà.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MME-01","CL_LIDT_01:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-02","text":"La distinzione fra contenuto e collocazione crolla, perché posizione e catena associativa partecipano alla produzione del significato.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MME-02","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-03","text":"Il soggetto viene riclassificato da sostanza autonoma a rete di ricezioni, supporti, allineamenti e pratiche.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSD-01","CL_LIDT_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-04","text":"Natura, corpo, arte e città cessano di essere domini separati e diventano fasi di una medesima compensazione trasformativa.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-04","CL_LIDT_03:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-05","text":"La totalità viene ridefinita come indirizzabilità espandibile anziché possesso esaustivo, rendendo strutturalmente compatibili classificazione e opacità.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:XD-01","CL_LIDT_01:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-06","text":"La classificazione diventa governo cognitivo e civile, poiché distribuire luoghi significa organizzare possibilità operative, appartenenze e condizioni della convivenza.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:XD-01","CL_LIDT_03:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-07","text":"Il rapporto fra classico e cristiano viene ridisegnato come riuso subordinato interrotto da una differenza non integralmente traducibile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:RMD-06","CL_LIDT_03:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Pianeti, porte, gradi, immagini mitiche, facoltà, membra, arti e istituzioni costituiscono gli oggetti espliciti della distribuzione teatrale.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B01","CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B01","CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Ricezione, attenuazione, collocazione, trasduzione e recupero coordinano i domini come livelli di una sola macchina mediatrice.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-01","CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] Interpretare e intervenire significa localizzare differenze, distinguere potenze da atti e riallineare le mediazioni anziché cercare accesso immediato.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] La realtà è gerarchica e relazionale, mentre il tempo è una spirale di discesa, densificazione, esercizio, dissoluzione e aggiornamento.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:HSI-03","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] Ricorrenza figurale, montaggio di autorità e catalogazione spaziale mettono in atto l’espansione ordinata che il sistema afferma.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B05","CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-01","text":"La necessità cosmica delle collocazioni resta in tensione con la loro dipendenza da convenzione, economia mnemonica e accomodamento storico.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:FL-02","CL_LIDT_03:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-02","text":"La pretesa di classificabilità universale richiede l’eliminazione delle lacune, ma ignoto e incarnazione preservano residui non assimilabili.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:FL-05","CL_LIDT_03:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-03","text":"Grazia, influssi e determinazioni astrali condizionano il soggetto, mentre l’etica e la politica richiedono azione, conversione e responsabilità.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:FL-02","CL_LIDT_02:FL-05","CL_LIDT_02:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-04","text":"Il corpo è simultaneamente necessario all’operazione e incompatibile con la piena riunione superiore.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:FL-01","CL_LIDT_02:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-05","text":"L’inclusione enciclopedica di pratiche vili e coercitive entra in tensione con la subordinazione normativa dell’agire a virtù e ordine civile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-05","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-06","text":"L’unità della macchina dipende da autorità e analogie eterogenee senza disporre di un criterio generale che ne risolva i conflitti.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:FL-04","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-01","text":"L’immagine muta da velo rappresentativo a operatore posizionale e infine a nodo generale di pratiche e istituzioni.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MP-02","CL_LIDT_03:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-02","text":"Il pianeta muta da segno contemplativo a coordinata tassonomica e poi a distributore antropologico-operativo.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MP-01","CL_LIDT_02:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-03","text":"La mediazione muta da attenuazione cosmica a illuminazione, veicolo corporeo, protesi tecnica e condizione civile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:MP-01","CL_LIDT_03:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-04","text":"La natura muta da ordine derivato a repertorio operativo e infine a insufficienza che rende necessaria l’arte.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RLE-03","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-05","text":"La morte muta da occultamento e dissoluzione cosmica a mortificazione affettiva e liberazione dai residui corporei.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MP-03","CL_LIDT_02:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:HSI-01","text":"La realtà è una macchina di trasduzione annidata composta da soglie, raggi, veicoli, immagini e istituzioni che ricevono e ridistribuiscono causalità.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-01","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-01","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:HSI-02","text":"Il soggetto è un relè ricettivo e operativo, incapace di possedere l’origine ma capace di convertire influssi ricevuti in memoria, azione e convivenza.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:HSI-02","CL_LIDT_01:HSI-02","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:HSI-03","text":"Il tempo è una spirale che intreccia eternità esemplare, discesa, incorporazione, trasformazione, dissoluzione e riapertura storica del repertorio.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-03","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-03","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:HSI-04","text":"La lotta possibile consiste nel navigare le mediazioni, impedire la cattura inferiore, colmare lacune operative e civili e risalire senza pretendere accesso immediato.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-04","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-04","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B01","text":"Gli assiomi estratti sono sufficienti a ricostruire la macchina come discesa causale, spazializzazione mnemonica, interiorizzazione antropologica, esteriorizzazione operativa e regolazione civile.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B01","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B01","CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B02","text":"Restano sottodeterminati i criteri delle assegnazioni figurali, le distribuzioni quantitative e il rapporto preciso fra alcune mediazioni teologiche e antropologiche.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B02","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B02","CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B03","text":"Il sistema è coerente a questa scala se simbolo, posizione e analogia vengono accettati come mediazioni reali ma non esaustive.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B03","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B04","text":"L’architettura è più forte nella conversione di causalità, soggettività e azione in una topologia comune capace di preservarne le differenze direzionali.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B04","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B05","text":"La ricostruzione dipende dalla ricorrenza spiraliforme, dalla compressione di autorità eterogenee e dalla tensione produttiva fra totalità finita ed espansione.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B05","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B05","CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B06","text":"Resistono alla riduzione assiomatica la grazia, la necessità non dimostrata delle corrispondenze e la differenza cristologica; eliminarle distruggerebbe il movimento effettivo del sistema.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B06","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"language_code":"it","language_name":"Italiano","translations":[{"id":"CAREVAR_20261030T231319243458Z_d62597c1","language_code":"en","language_name":"English","title":"The Idea of the Theatre","source_sha256":"299214dd6dd0f201188d32b9de7d635b8d49a219c7ecbb85dda2363760c6f706","sha256":"b05449862532e3fadee7ad1feb3d5af16853208016ecfef00fe1eb3522392c91","rendition_type":"machine","review_status":"machine","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","created":"2026-10-30T23:13:19.246861+00:00","sections":[{"number":"1","name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-01","text":"The global problem consists in making cosmic, anthropological, technical, and civil multiplicity addressable without reducing it to a flat list or transforming divine excess into transparent possession.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-01","CL_LIDT_03:AS-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-02","text":"The Theatro resolves the problem by translating causal derivation into an external topology of images and reconverting that topology into paths of retrieval, operation, and ascent.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-02","CL_LIDT_03:AS-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-03","text":"The foundation is a hierarchical reality in which exemplary order, receptive subject, and human practices belong to a single mediated continuum.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-01","CL_LIDT_02:GA-01","CL_LIDT_03:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-04","text":"The argument takes the form of a theological-cosmological, anthropological, mnemonic, and civil machine that harmonizes heterogeneous registers by subordinating them to a single transformative architecture.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-03","CL_LIDT_02:BAS-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-05","text":"The movement descends from principles to forms, interiorizes hierarchy in the human being, exteriorizes it in actions and institutions, and finally makes the path navigable in reverse.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:XD-02","CL_LIDT_02:RLE-05","CL_LIDT_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-06","text":"The progression is recursive, spiraliform, and cumulative: each recurrence of images and coordinates preserves mediation while expanding its operational domain.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-04","CL_LIDT_03:AS-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-07","text":"The directional attractor is the ordered ascent toward higher unity through traversal, conversion, and dissolution of mediations, not through their immediate evasion.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-10","CL_LIDT_02:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BAS-08","text":"The closure is Christological and apophatic: Christ guarantees cohesion and orientation, but the unknown and the difference of incarnation prevent the classificatory machine from exhausting itself.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:AS-05","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Argumental Spine"},{"number":"2","name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-01","text":"[Persistent] Exemplary order causally precedes forms, subjects, and operations and makes their continuity possible within one and the same architecture.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-02","text":"[Persistent] No decisive passage is immediate: knowledge, incarnation, memory, action, and ascent require images, influences, vehicles, or institutions.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-03","CL_LIDT_02:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-03","text":"[Persistent] The Theatro is an external topological device that converts invisible hierarchies and operational pluralities into retrievable placements.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-03","CL_LIDT_03:GA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-04","text":"[Mutating] The image retains its mediating function but changes from a veil of excess into a positional coordinate, anthropological index, and operational-civil node.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-02","CL_LIDT_03:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-05","text":"[Mutating] The planet shifts from a sign of higher order to a distributive infrastructure of natures, faculties, members, arts, and social apparatuses.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-04","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-05","CL_LIDT_03:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-06","text":"[Emergent] Cosmology, anthropology, technique, and politics constitute transducible phases of a continuum proceeding from formation to institutional practice.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-09","CL_LIDT_03:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-07","text":"[Persistent] The subject is relational, receptive, and non-self-sufficient: it receives light, form, capacity, and operational conditions that it cannot autonomously ground.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-01","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-08","text":"[Mutating] Matter and body are necessary mediations that receive form and enable action, but they also introduce composition, capture, vulnerability, and the need for transformation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_02:GA-02","CL_LIDT_02:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-09","text":"[Emergent] A finite repertoire of figures can sustain a regulated indefinite expansion through positional variation, subdivision, and historical accommodation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-08","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-10","text":"[Mutating] Capacity, disposition, action, and civil belonging are distinct levels: no potentiality becomes virtue or common order without actualization and regulation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-12","CL_LIDT_03:GA-07"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-11","text":"[Attractor] The machine tends to place every reality, practice, and body of knowledge, converting gaps and differences into positions internal to order.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","CL_LIDT_01:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-12","text":"[Attractor] Valid knowing and acting consist in orderly retracing mediations, realigning them with higher causality.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-10","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-13","text":"[Terminal] Christ operates both as a principle of internal cohesion and as a terminal difference not absorbable by general symbolic translatability.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-11","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GA-14","text":"[Emergent] The unknown is internalized as a reserve of expansion, but totality remains incapable of self-closure because not every difference can become an available repertoire.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","CL_LIDT_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Load-Bearing Axioms"},{"number":"3","name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-01","text":"[Stable identity] The symbol endures as non-ornamental mediation that veils, preserves, and transmits a structure exceeding its own sensible form.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-02","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-01","CL_LIDT_03:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-02","text":"[Mutation] The image shifts from veiled representation of a cause to producing differential accesses to faculties, actions, arts, and institutions.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-02","CL_LIDT_03:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-03","text":"[Displacement] The planet migrates from contemplative mediation to taxonomic, anthropological, and social coordination.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-03","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-05","CL_LIDT_03:GA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-04","text":"[Mutation] Myth shifts from doctrinal veil to genealogy of descent and finally to an operational repertoire of technical invention.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-04","CL_LIDT_02:GA-06","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-05","text":"[Functional recurrence] Mediation changes direction and support: it attenuates cosmic causality, makes illumination and incarnation possible, then reappears as a technical and civil prosthesis.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RMD-02","CL_LIDT_02:MP-01","CL_LIDT_03:RLE-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-06","text":"[Reversal] Lower nature shifts from being derived order to appearing as an insufficient condition requiring body, art, and institution without becoming autonomous.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-07","text":"[Intensification] Memory evolves from an arrangement of places into a combinatorial matrix and finally into an external topology capable of governing retrieval of the entire operational field.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-05","CL_LIDT_03:GA-01","CL_LIDT_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-08","text":"[Absorption] The human being, initially distinct from the natural catalogue, is reabsorbed as a deficient node that transforms cosmic categories into dispositions, techniques, and civil forms.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GA-04","CL_LIDT_03:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-09","text":"[Terminal transformation] The unknown shifts from a placeable internal reserve to a limit on the claim to eliminate every gap, culminating in the non-assimilable Christological difference.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-12","CL_LIDT_03:GA-06","CL_LIDT_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RMD-10","text":"[Displacement] Dissolution migrates from the cosmic recomposition of mixtures to anthropological liberation from bodily and vehicular residues.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-06","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recurrence, Mutation, and Displacement Matrix"},{"number":"4","name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-01","text":"[Local] Kabbalistic names, determinate mythical figures, and planetary quantities remain local articulations; at the scale of the book they count only as realizations of general mediation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:CGD-01","CL_LIDT_02:CGD-01","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-02","text":"[Local] Specific assignments among figure, planet, and content remain underdetermined and cannot be elevated to global necessity.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B02","CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-03","text":"[Extended] The necessity of mediation and the non-self-sufficiency of matter, subject, and technique run through all units and become global laws.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-03","CL_LIDT_02:CGD-03","CL_LIDT_03:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-04","text":"[Bridge] Planetary topology connects cosmic causality, human structure, and the distribution of practices, making them registers of a single matrix.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:CGD-03","CL_LIDT_02:MP-04","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-05","text":"[Catalyst] Incorporation transforms cosmic hierarchy into a moral problem, while indigence transforms the moral-operational problem into technique and civil order.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:CGD-05","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-06","text":"[Bridge] The body connects ontological reception and worldly operation; art extends this mediating function beyond the organism toward shared institutions.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:XD-02","CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-07","text":"[Recoded] The fixed meaning of the image, the bipartite subject, and the simple opposition between nature and art are superseded by positional semantics and mediated continuities.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:CGD-05","CL_LIDT_02:MME-01","CL_LIDT_03:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:CGD-08","text":"[Terminal] Christological difference is not an additional local content, but the global limit preventing universal translatability from closing upon itself.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:CGD-06","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Lower-Layer vs Current-Level Distinction"},{"number":"5","name":"Global Apophatic Structure","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-01","text":"The divine cannot be fully exposed, possessed, or administered through literal and sensible forms.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-01","CL_LIDT_01:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-02","text":"Matter and nature possess no formative, vital, or intelligible autonomy.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-03","CL_LIDT_03:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-03","text":"The subject is not the owner of its own light, movement, or the efficacy of its works.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:DBN-03","CL_LIDT_02:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-04","text":"No image possesses a literal, fixed, or self-sufficient meaning independent of position and associative chain.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-04","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-05","text":"Memory is neither an inner repository nor a horizontal encyclopedia, but depends on an external differential order.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-06","CL_LIDT_03:GNX-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-06","text":"Nature, disposition, and technique are respectively insufficient to produce art, virtue, and stable coexistence.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:GNX-04","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-07","text":"Completeness does not authorize the expulsion of the base, the vicious, or the coercive, which must be placed without being normatively approved.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GNX-04","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:GNX-08","text":"Neither does dissolution amount to absolute non-being, nor does classification amount to exhaustive transparency.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GNX-07","CL_LIDT_01:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Global Apophatic Structure"},{"number":"6","name":"Deep Book Apophatics","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-01","text":"Every immediate efficacy must be false, because the entire machine depends on the productive interposition of signs, vehicles, bodies, and orderings.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:DBN-02","CL_LIDT_02:GNX-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-02","text":"The ontological independence of cosmology, anthropology, art, and politics must be false, since transduction among domains constitutes the unity of the book.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:DBN-04","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-03","text":"It must be false that correspondences are radically arbitrary, although the system does not fully demonstrate their necessity.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-04","text":"It must be false that universality means simultaneous transparency, since totality depends on veiling, differentiation, and regulated access.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSA-04","CL_LIDT_02:BSA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-05","text":"The self-sufficiency of the natural or technical human being must be false, because reception, artifice, and institution remedy insufficiencies without definitively abolishing them.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSA-02","CL_LIDT_03:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:DBN-06","text":"The full assimilability of incarnation to the classical repertoire must be false; otherwise the terminal limit would be reduced to a further figural equivalence.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:DBN-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Deep Book Apophatics"},{"number":"7","name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-01","text":"The absolutely unavailable possibility is the immediate possession of divine origin by the subject or the mnemonic device.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSA-01","CL_LIDT_03:BSA-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-02","text":"The structuring absence is a stable reconciliation between operative corporeality, liberation from affects, and higher union.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSA-01","CL_LIDT_02:FL-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-03","text":"The system admits no object absolutely devoid of place, but encounters a difference that cannot be reduced to mere placement.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:BSA-02","CL_LIDT_03:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-04","text":"The absolute self-closure of totality remains prohibited: the unknown fuels expansion, and incarnation interrupts its complete assimilation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RLE-07","CL_LIDT_03:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Negative","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSA-05","text":"There is no metalanguage capable of definitively arbitrating the heterogeneous authorities and analogies synchronized by the machine.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:FL-04","CL_LIDT_02:BSD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Super-Apophatics of the Whole"},{"number":"8","name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-01","text":"Cosmic derivation extends into anthropology and civil order: forms, faculties, operations, and institutions are differentiated stages of the same mediated causality.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-01","WB_LIDT:GA-05","WB_LIDT:GA-06","WB_LIDT:GA-10","CL_LIDT_01:XD-02","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-02","text":"Memory becomes causally informed because theatrical topology encodes the descent of realities and makes it possible to retrace it in the inverse direction.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-03","WB_LIDT:GA-12","CL_LIDT_01:MME-01","CL_LIDT_02:XD-06","CL_LIDT_03:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-03","text":"Symbolic opacity produces regulated accessibility: positional variation enables a finite repertoire to address contents that it cannot fully expose.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-02","WB_LIDT:GA-04","WB_LIDT:GA-09","WB_LIDT:GA-11","CL_LIDT_01:XD-01","CL_LIDT_02:XD-04","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-04","text":"Human insufficiency is a local form of cosmic non-autonomy: light, body, art, and city compensate for dependencies that no subject can self-ground.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-07","WB_LIDT:GA-08","WB_LIDT:GA-10","CL_LIDT_01:GA-06","CL_LIDT_02:XD-01","CL_LIDT_03:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-05","text":"Body and art are homologous mediations: both make operation possible, but generate a secondary problem of capture, insufficiency, or regulation.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-06","WB_LIDT:GA-08","WB_LIDT:GA-10","CL_LIDT_02:XD-02","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-06","text":"The unknown and historical accommodation make totality expandable, while Christological difference prevents expansion from meaning unlimited assimilation.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-09","WB_LIDT:GA-11","WB_LIDT:GA-13","WB_LIDT:GA-14","CL_LIDT_01:RLE-07","CL_LIDT_03:XD-03","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-07","text":"Moral conversion translates cosmic verticality into action and politically extends it into the universal conditions of coexistence.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-10","WB_LIDT:GA-12","CL_LIDT_02:GA-11","CL_LIDT_02:XD-05","CL_LIDT_03:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:XD-08","text":"Anthropological dissolution constitutes a specialization of cosmic recomposition: the loss of the compound does not annihilate principles, but can free them for a new alignment.","refs":["WB_LIDT:GA-01","WB_LIDT:GA-08","WB_LIDT:GA-12","CL_LIDT_01:RMD-06","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Composite","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Cross-Unit Derivative Propositions"},{"number":"9","name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-01","text":"Ontologically, reality becomes a network of receptions, attenuations, and retransmissions in which no lower level is self-sufficient.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-01","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-02","text":"The subject becomes a decentered relay that receives orientations, traverses supports, and converts its own position into practice.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSD-04","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-03","text":"Epistemically, knowing means navigating positional relations and reconstructing dependencies, not possessing isolated contents.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSD-01","CL_LIDT_01:BSD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-04","text":"Time is articulated into exemplary eternity, descent, incorporation, action, dissolution, and historical updating of repertoires.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSD-05","CL_LIDT_02:BSD-02","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-05","text":"Acting remains real but derived: it consists in actualizing and realigning received capacities within bodily, astral, technical, and civil constraints.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSD-04","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-06","text":"Politically, technique alone does not ground coexistence; civil continuity requires common dispositions, defense, jurisdiction, and sanction.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:DBN-02","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-07","text":"Methodologically, analogy and catalogue do not merely describe the system, but operationally produce continuity among heterogeneous domains.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSD-06","CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:BSD-08","text":"Totality assumes an asymptotic form: it can indefinitely extend its own addressability without attaining transparency or absolute theological closure.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:XD-05","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Book-Scale Super-Derivatives"},{"number":"10","name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-01","text":"Higher causality → images → mnemonic retrieval → causal ascent constitutes the fundamental recursive circuit.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RLE-01","CL_LIDT_01:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-02","text":"Figure → position → division → new function produces combinatorial expansion without unlimited proliferation of signs.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RLE-02","CL_LIDT_01:RMD-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-03","text":"Vertical descent is spatialized, and horizontal navigation reactivates vertical direction, making the Theatro a spiral among levels.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RLE-05","CL_LIDT_02:GA-09"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-04","text":"Light → orientation → image → memory → new orientation forms the cognitive circuit that keeps the subject dependent on the external.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RLE-01","CL_LIDT_02:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-05","text":"Body → concupiscence → lower action → capture → mortification intensifies mediation until its conversion or dissolution becomes necessary.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RLE-02","CL_LIDT_02:RLE-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-06","text":"Indigence → technique → civil insufficiency → common justice → sanctioned order constitutes the political circuit of compensation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:RLE-02","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-07","text":"Gap → provisional placement → accommodation → new completeness continually reopens the encyclopedia without abandoning its totalizing attractor.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:RLE-03","CL_LIDT_03:RLE-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:RLE-08","text":"Christ is the limit-attractor: he guarantees the convergence of mediations and simultaneously prevents the machine from declaring itself self-sufficient.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:GA-11","CL_LIDT_03:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Recursive Loops, Escalation Paths, and Conceptual Attractors"},{"number":"11","name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B01","text":"Divine excess → impossibility of direct exposition → necessity of the symbolic veil.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:DBN-01","CL_LIDT_01:GA-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B02","text":"Exemplary order → cosmic mediations → natural forms → temporary compounds.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RMD-01","CL_LIDT_01:RLE-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B03","text":"Causal hierarchy → planets-coordinates → theatrical space → mnemonic retrievability.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:XD-07","CL_LIDT_01:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B04","text":"Received light → inner faculties → orientation → conditional humanity.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BAS-02","CL_LIDT_02:GA-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B05","text":"Vehicular mediation → incorporation → desire → moral disposition → action.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:RMD-03","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B06","text":"Natural operation → indigence → compensatory art → technical-social repertoire.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:AS-03","CL_LIDT_03:FGS-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B07","text":"Distributed technique → insufficiency of coexistence → common civil virtues → defense and sanction.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-07","CL_LIDT_03:AFM-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FGS-B08","text":"Navigation of mediations → realignment → dissolution of constraints → conditioned ascent → non-exhaustive Christological closure.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-04","CL_LIDT_02:RMD-06","CL_LIDT_01:FGS-B06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Formal Generative Schema of the Whole Book"},{"number":"12","name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:AFM-B01","text":"Divine excess → exemplary causality → planetary mediation → figural encoding → anthropological interiorization → incorporation → operation → art → civil institution → Christological limit.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MME-03","CL_LIDT_02:MME-01","CL_LIDT_03:CGD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:AFM-B02","text":"Dispersed multiplicity → theatrical placement → relational retrieval → discrimination of alignments → conversion of action → ascent through mediations → unity without total transparency.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:BSD-02","CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B03","CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Whole-Book Argument Flow Map"},{"number":"13","name":"Macro Map-Effects","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-01","text":"The separation between ontology and memory collapses: remembering means navigating the causal and operational structure of reality.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MME-01","CL_LIDT_01:BSD-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-02","text":"The distinction between content and placement collapses, because position and associative chain participate in the production of meaning.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MME-02","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-03","text":"The subject is reclassified from autonomous substance into a network of receptions, supports, alignments, and practices.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:BSD-01","CL_LIDT_02:MME-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-04","text":"Nature, body, art, and city cease to be separate domains and become phases of one and the same transformative compensation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-04","CL_LIDT_03:MME-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-05","text":"Totality is redefined as expandable addressability rather than exhaustive possession, making classification and opacity structurally compatible.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:XD-01","CL_LIDT_01:MME-06"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-06","text":"Classification becomes cognitive and civil governance, since distributing places means organizing operational possibilities, belongings, and conditions of coexistence.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:XD-01","CL_LIDT_03:XD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MME-07","text":"The relation between the classical and the Christian is redrawn as subordinate reuse interrupted by a difference not wholly translatable.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:RMD-06","CL_LIDT_03:MME-05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Macro Map-Effects"},{"number":"14","name":"Altitude Integration","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B01","text":"[Surface level] Planets, gates, degrees, mythical images, faculties, members, arts, and institutions constitute the explicit objects of theatrical distribution.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B01","CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B01","CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B02","text":"[Structural level] Reception, attenuation, placement, transduction, and retrieval coordinate domains as levels of a single mediating machine.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-01","CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B03","text":"[Metastrategic level] To interpret and intervene means to locate differences, distinguish potentialities from acts, and realign mediations rather than seek immediate access.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:ALT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B04","text":"[Ontological / Temporal level] Reality is hierarchical and relational, while time is a spiral of descent, densification, exercise, dissolution, and updating.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:HSI-03","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:ALT-B05","text":"[Methodological / Performative level] Figural recurrence, montage of authorities, and spatial cataloguing enact the ordered expansion that the system asserts.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:ALT-B05","CL_LIDT_03:ALT-B05"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Altitude Integration"},{"number":"15","name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-01","text":"The cosmic necessity of placements remains in tension with their dependence on convention, mnemonic economy, and historical accommodation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:FL-02","CL_LIDT_03:XD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-02","text":"The claim of universal classificability requires the elimination of gaps, but the unknown and incarnation preserve non-assimilable residues.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:FL-05","CL_LIDT_03:FL-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-03","text":"Grace, influences, and astral determinations condition the subject, while ethics and politics require action, conversion, and responsibility.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:FL-02","CL_LIDT_02:FL-05","CL_LIDT_02:BSD-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-04","text":"The body is simultaneously necessary to operation and incompatible with full higher reunion.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:FL-01","CL_LIDT_02:BSA-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-05","text":"The encyclopedic inclusion of base and coercive practices enters into tension with the normative subordination of action to virtue and civil order.","refs":["CL_LIDT_03:GA-05","CL_LIDT_03:DBN-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:FL-06","text":"The unity of the machine depends on heterogeneous authorities and analogies without having a general criterion capable of resolving their conflicts.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:FL-04","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-01","text":"The image changes from representative veil to positional operator and finally to a general node of practices and institutions.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MP-02","CL_LIDT_03:MP-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-02","text":"The planet changes from contemplative sign to taxonomic coordinate and then to anthropological-operative distributor.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MP-01","CL_LIDT_02:MP-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-03","text":"Mediation changes from cosmic attenuation to illumination, bodily vehicle, technical prosthesis, and civil condition.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:MP-01","CL_LIDT_03:XD-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-04","text":"Nature changes from derived order to operational repertoire and finally to an insufficiency that makes art necessary.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:RLE-03","CL_LIDT_03:RMD-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MP-05","text":"Death changes from cosmic concealment and dissolution to affective mortification and liberation from bodily residues.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MP-03","CL_LIDT_02:MP-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"Tension","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Internal Tensions, Mutation Points, and Fault Lines"},{"number":"16","name":"Hidden System Image","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:HSI-01","text":"Reality is a nested transduction machine composed of thresholds, rays, vehicles, images, and institutions that receive and redistribute causality.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-01","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-01","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:HSI-02","text":"The subject is a receptive and operative relay, incapable of possessing the origin but capable of converting received influences into memory, action, and coexistence.","refs":["CL_LIDT_02:HSI-02","CL_LIDT_01:HSI-02","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:HSI-03","text":"Time is a spiral that intertwines exemplary eternity, descent, incorporation, transformation, dissolution, and the historical reopening of the repertoire.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-03","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-03","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:HSI-04","text":"The possible struggle consists in navigating mediations, preventing lower capture, filling operational and civil gaps, and ascending without claiming immediate access.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:HSI-04","CL_LIDT_02:HSI-04","CL_LIDT_03:HSI-04"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Hidden System Image"},{"number":"17","name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test","items":[{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B01","text":"The extracted axioms are sufficient to reconstruct the machine as causal descent, mnemonic spatialization, anthropological interiorization, operative exteriorization, and civil regulation.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B01","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B01","CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B01"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B02","text":"The criteria of figural assignments, quantitative distributions, and the precise relation between certain theological and anthropological mediations remain underdetermined.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B02","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B02","CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B02"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B03","text":"The system is coherent at this scale if symbol, position, and analogy are accepted as real but non-exhaustive mediations.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B03","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B04","text":"The architecture is stronger in converting causality, subjectivity, and action into a common topology capable of preserving their directional differences.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B04","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B05","text":"The reconstruction depends on spiraliform recurrence, the compression of heterogeneous authorities, and the productive tension between finite totality and expansion.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B05","CL_LIDT_02:MRT-B05","CL_LIDT_03:MRT-B03"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]},{"id":"WB_LIDT:MRT-B06","text":"Grace, the unproven necessity of correspondences, and Christological difference resist axiomatic reduction; eliminating them would destroy the system's actual movement.","refs":["CL_LIDT_01:MRT-B06","CL_LIDT_03:GA-08"],"deep_refs":[],"trace_type":"","passages":[]}],"original_name":"Minimal Whole-Book Reconstruction Test"}],"revision":"WB_LIDT@R002","source_variant_id":"canonical:WB_LIDT:WB_LIDT@R002","source_language_code":"it"}],"identity":{"layer":"WB","kicker":"Whole book","title":"The Idea of the Theatre","context":""},"title_language_code":"en"}],"seal":"SEAL_LIDT_55A20D3B2AE773FCCF3B","title_language_code":"en","title_translation":{"schema":"care-title-heading-translation/1","language_code":"en","rendition_type":"machine","originals_preserved":true},"version_work_id":"WORK_L_IDEA_DEL_THEATRO_DELLO_ECCELLENTE_M_GIULIO_CAMILLO","version_label":"Added 30 Oct 2026 · Run 30 Oct 2026 · gpt-5.6-terra / gpt-5.6-sol","version_revision":"dc612115e0c1a8ec3476242b957c8233d3a5f6a7b9a775048c6a8c5005fdd850"}],"fields":[{"id":"FIELD:lateral:32b23876456807","entity_id":"32b23876456807","field":"lateral","item_type":"lateral","title":"The Critique of Pure Reason × A Treatise of Human Nature","author":"Laterals","description":"Diagnosis, reframings, strange child and audit, with their declared sources","year":"","cloth":"#665077","foil":"#eee7d6","has_care":true,"has_source":true,"members":[{"id":"WORK_KANT_PURE_REASON","work_id":"WORK_KANT_PURE_REASON","title":"The Critique of Pure Reason","author":"Immanuel Kant","cloth":"#35442f","foil":"#ba8e54","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","CL","CH","NUMO"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_KPR"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-73b8664b61f6f07f-e4b1ac743ae9ce7e.png"},{"id":"WORK_A_TREATISE_OF_HUMAN_NATURE_DAVID_HUME","work_id":"WORK_A_TREATISE_OF_HUMAN_NATURE_DAVID_HUME","title":"A Treatise of Human Nature","author":"David Hume","cloth":"#35442f","foil":"#ba8e54","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH","NUMO"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_THN"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-d0138d38bb5ad732-8308e15450bed635.png"}],"member_count":2,"member_titles":["The Critique of Pure Reason","A Treatise of Human Nature"],"layers":["XR"],"cover_url":"","format":"care-beta-fields/1.0","revision":"6a2677acc8e311e399e6984b41c2b90f624712b527a386a0104c647c4659af97","bundle_sha256":"6a2677acc8e311e399e6984b41c2b90f624712b527a386a0104c647c4659af97","bundle_url":"./data/fields/c42a9648b8605e31-6a2677acc8e311e3.json"},{"id":"FIELD:corpus:CB_CORPUS_I_D01E832B","entity_id":"CB_CORPUS_I_D01E832B","field":"corpus","item_type":"corpus","title":"Corpus I","author":"Corpus","description":"14 source books · whole corpus and its member layers","year":"v2","cloth":"#94723f","foil":"#eee7d6","has_care":true,"has_source":true,"members":[{"id":"WORK_STORE_PERSEUS_GREEK_TLG0059_TLG031_PERSEUS_GRC2","work_id":"WORK_STORE_PERSEUS_GREEK_TLG0059_TLG031_PERSEUS_GRC2","title":"Timaeus","author":"Plato","cloth":"#33353c","foil":"#bd8156","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_JP8E"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-8805fe2c663d049f-ba5df89a85e8d5ea.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_PERSEUS_GREEK_TLG0086_TLG025_PERSEUS_GRC2","work_id":"WORK_STORE_PERSEUS_GREEK_TLG0086_TLG025_PERSEUS_GRC2","title":"Metaphysica","author":"Aristotle","cloth":"#35442f","foil":"#ba8e54","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_DAZY"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-223fa1fddd7cddd2-8bbd0ab3c2fb0bf2.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_PERSEUS_LATIN_PHI0550_PHI001_PERSEUS_LAT1","work_id":"WORK_STORE_PERSEUS_LATIN_PHI0550_PHI001_PERSEUS_LAT1","title":"De Rerum Natura","author":"Lucretius","cloth":"#6f2f2a","foil":"#b98655","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_0T6T"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-f7e0ff97940e1001-24de84d5b17d77d2.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_CANON_PG33849","work_id":"WORK_STORE_CANON_PG33849","title":"Confessiones","author":"Augustine of Hippo","cloth":"#6a4b27","foil":"#d2ad72","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_5P0L"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-181820be1428d1b8-f9c3234dca0ae23f.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_THOMISTICUM_SUMMA_PRIMA","work_id":"WORK_STORE_THOMISTICUM_SUMMA_PRIMA","title":"Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","author":"Thomas Aquinas","cloth":"#35442f","foil":"#ba8e54","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_GGVC"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-ef18241e546d391b-d0a1f05565a51515.png"},{"id":"WORK_MONAS_HIEROGLYPHICA_JOHN_DEE","work_id":"WORK_MONAS_HIEROGLYPHICA_JOHN_DEE","title":"Monas Hieroglyphica","author":"John Dee","cloth":"#33353c","foil":"#bd8156","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_MHON"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-eb6edcaef3392c37-df4a27ed9967941c.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_EUROPEAN_SPINOZA_ETHICA","work_id":"WORK_STORE_EUROPEAN_SPINOZA_ETHICA","title":"Ethica","author":"Baruch Spinoza","cloth":"#35442f","foil":"#ba8e54","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_QGOH"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-cb20d40c005d7d22-d25aa60e1847c527.png"},{"id":"WORK_A_TREATISE_OF_HUMAN_NATURE_DAVID_HUME","work_id":"WORK_A_TREATISE_OF_HUMAN_NATURE_DAVID_HUME","title":"A Treatise of Human Nature","author":"David Hume","cloth":"#35442f","foil":"#ba8e54","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH","NUMO"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_THN"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-d0138d38bb5ad732-8308e15450bed635.png"},{"id":"WORK_TRIAL_84B8A4537CF74654B5E46D40D58586CB","work_id":"WORK_TRIAL_84B8A4537CF74654B5E46D40D58586CB","title":"The Critique of Pure Reason","author":"Immanuel Kant","cloth":"#224b43","foil":"#bca16b","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_BA94"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-d17c4d1cf7669949-e4b1ac743ae9ce7e.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_CANON_PG6729","work_id":"WORK_STORE_CANON_PG6729","title":"Science of Logic","author":"Georg Wilhelm Friedrich Hegel","cloth":"#5b343b","foil":"#c38a68","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_GB18"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-f03cac44c6d2d3c9-d925a75208887813.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_HISTORICAL_MARX_CAPITAL_I_1867","work_id":"WORK_STORE_HISTORICAL_MARX_CAPITAL_I_1867","title":"Capital Volume 1","author":"Karl Marx","cloth":"#33353c","foil":"#bd8156","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_V4GB"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-8e3d28d7330b7735-341d9cd9d3110f51.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_CANON_PG7205","work_id":"WORK_STORE_CANON_PG7205","title":"Also sprach Zarathustra","author":"Friedrich Nietzsche","cloth":"#253f46","foil":"#c59657","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","MC","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_97E9"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-b01befca9f426e10-4818676456175297.png"},{"id":"WORK_MATIERE_ET_MEMOIRE_HENRI_BERGSON","work_id":"WORK_MATIERE_ET_MEMOIRE_HENRI_BERGSON","title":"Matiere Et Memoire","author":"Henri Bergson","cloth":"#47364f","foil":"#c49a63","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_MEMA"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-78523a9a70580441-cf0cd733b25b678d.png"},{"id":"WORK_STORE_HISTORICAL_FREUD_UNBEHAGEN_1930","work_id":"WORK_STORE_HISTORICAL_FREUD_UNBEHAGEN_1930","title":"Das Unbehagen in der Kultur","author":"Sigmund Freud","cloth":"#47364f","foil":"#c49a63","has_source":true,"layers":["WB","CL","CH"],"source_unit_ids":["WB_R2TV"],"cover_url":"./assets/covers/beta-9fdf3655cf91ced9-367cb556593641b7.png"}],"member_count":14,"member_titles":["Timaeus","Metaphysica","De Rerum Natura","Confessiones","Summa Theologiae · Prima pars","Monas Hieroglyphica","Ethica","A Treatise of Human Nature","The Critique of Pure Reason","Science of Logic","Capital Volume 1","Also sprach Zarathustra","Matiere Et Memoire","Das Unbehagen in der Kultur"],"layers":["CB","CL","MC"],"cover_url":"","format":"care-beta-fields/1.0","revision":"0dd0640f5bec4dfe749fb0199d5a8a6e29a0416c491891566492299850c390ab","bundle_sha256":"0dd0640f5bec4dfe749fb0199d5a8a6e29a0416c491891566492299850c390ab","bundle_url":"./data/fields/406de238c542e8aa-0dd0640f5bec4dfe.json","preview_depth":"WB"}],"featured_reading":{"type":"field","id":"FIELD:lateral:32b23876456807"}}